ts one owning\\nmember, using its exact filename without `.md`, such as\\n`owner:FOUNDATIONS`, `owner:ACTIVATION` or `owner:WORLD_MODEL`. Accept only a\\nmember listed in the verified standards inventory; the local\\n[method entry](../../../standards/README.md) locates its scope. A full owner\\nread has its own acquisition cost; select a task entry when it is sufficient.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/plugins/spec/references/REFRESH.md#STDO%20Refresh%20Procedure%2FOwner%20And%20Task%20Entries\",\"start_line\":48},{\"end_line\":68,\"path\":\"plugins/spec/references/REFRESH.md\",\"quote\":\"| `task:rf-task-a` | `frames/rf-task-a.md` |\\n| `task:rf-task-b` | `frames/rf-task-b.md` |\\n| `task:ac-task-a` | `frames/ac-task-a.md` |\\n| `task:traversal-task-f` | `frames/traversal-task-f.md` |\\n| `task:eb-task-d` | `frames/eb-task-d.md` |\\n| `task:dm-task-d` | `frames/dm-task-d.md` |\\n| `task:configuration` | `frames/configuration.md` |\\n| `task:binding` | `frames/binding.md` |\\n| `task:stale-summary` | `frames/stale-summary.md` |\\n| `task:bootstrap` | `frames/bootstrap.md` |\\n| `task:acceptance-release` | `frames/acceptance-release.md` |\\n| `task:member-build-assess` | `frames/member-build-assess.md` |\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/plugins/spec/references/REFRESH.md#STDO%20Refresh%20Procedure%2FOwner%20And%20Task%20Entries\",\"start_line\":57}],\"label\":\"Refresh owner and task entries\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:3d1b7e8fd94b6a13e7036881a685a062","key":13,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:3d1b7e8fd94b6a13e7036881a685a062\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[\"The request says stdo help or explicitly concerns entering or operating an STDO-governed project.\"],\"definition\":\"stdo-help explains or establishes the next lawful STDO step through practical help from the project's exact selected basis. It routes attention and does not replace method or Product authority.\",\"exceptions\":[\"Generic non-STDO help is outside its invocation scope.\"],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":3,\"path\":\"plugins/spec/skills/stdo-help/SKILL.md\",\"quote\":\"description: Explain or establish the next lawful STDO step. Use when a user says stdo help or explicitly asks how to enter or operate an STDO-governed project. Do not invoke for generic non-STDO help.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/plugins/spec/skills/stdo-help/SKILL.md#preamble\",\"start_line\":3},{\"end_line\":9,\"path\":\"plugins/spec/skills/stdo-help/SKILL.md\",\"quote\":\"Give practical help from the project's exact selected basis. This skill routes\\nattention; it does not replace method or Product authority.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/plugins/spec/skills/stdo-help/SKILL.md#STDO%20Help\",\"start_line\":8}],\"label\":\"STDO Help\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:ff8ab62ddcaa2b8acea0e3284aeae490","key":14,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:ff8ab62ddcaa2b8acea0e3284aeae490\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[\"The request says stdo review or explicitly concerns an STDO-governed candidate, release claim, qualification claim or governed boundary.\"],\"definition\":\"stdo-review independently evaluates one exact claim or candidate as Reviewer and returns a closed technical result. It is read-only and does not repair, assign Product priority, apply disposition or activate next work.\",\"exceptions\":[\"Generic review is outside its invocation scope.\"],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":3,\"path\":\"plugins/spec/skills/stdo-review/SKILL.md\",\"quote\":\"description: Independently evaluate one exact STDO-governed candidate and return a closed technical result. Use when a user says stdo review or explicitly asks to review an STDO-governed candidate, release claim, qualification claim, or governed boundary. Do not invoke for generic review.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/plugins/spec/skills/stdo-review/SKILL.md#preamble\",\"start_line\":3},{\"end_line\":9,\"path\":\"plugins/spec/skills/stdo-review/SKILL.md\",\"quote\":\"Act only as Reviewer for one exact claim. Review is read-only. It does not\\nrepair, assign Product priority, apply disposition, or activate the next work.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/plugins/spec/skills/stdo-review/SKILL.md#STDO%20Review\",\"start_line\":8}],\"label\":\"STDO Review\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:0e1bc82e2ce39b9c50e5931eb79ef30d","key":15,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:0e1bc82e2ce39b9c50e5931eb79ef30d\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"The review projection names five core result values: satisfied, falsified, indeterminate, out_of_frame and invalid_basis. They remain distinct from technical triage and Product disposition.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":79,\"path\":\"plugins/spec/skills/stdo-review/SKILL.md\",\"quote\":\"- `satisfied`: no finding; triage is `not_applicable`;\\n- `falsified`: findings carry complete triage or explicit field-level\\n  indeterminate values;\\n- `indeterminate` or `out_of_frame`: return the unresolved triage and basis;\\n  and\\n- `invalid_basis`: triage is `not_applicable`; return the basis re-entry.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/plugins/spec/skills/stdo-review/SKILL.md#STDO%20Review%2FEvaluate\",\"start_line\":74}],\"label\":\"Review result domain\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:6b63054663984bff3aa30721243fa32e","key":16,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:6b63054663984bff3aa30721243fa32e\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[\"The request says stdo status or explicitly requests progress, blockers, monitoring or triage help for an STDO-governed project.\"],\"definition\":\"stdo-status produces evidence-backed read-only Product/work delivery status and bounded triage candidates from Product-owned authority and evidence. The shell stdo status command instead reports installed-basis integrity.\",\"exceptions\":[\"Generic status is outside its invocation scope.\"],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":3,\"path\":\"plugins/spec/skills/stdo-status/SKILL.md\",\"quote\":\"description: Produce an evidence-backed read-only STDO project status and bounded triage candidates. Use when a user says stdo status or explicitly asks for progress, blockers, monitoring, or triage help in an STDO-governed project. Do not invoke for generic status.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/plugins/spec/skills/stdo-status/SKILL.md#preamble\",\"start_line\":3},{\"end_line\":10,\"path\":\"plugins/spec/skills/stdo-status/SKILL.md\",\"quote\":\"Report Product and work truth without changing it. The shell command `stdo\\nstatus` reports installed-basis integrity; this skill reports project delivery\\nstate from Product-owned authority and evidence.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/plugins/spec/skills/stdo-status/SKILL.md#STDO%20Status\",\"start_line\":8}],\"label\":\"STDO Status\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:effbef4bb67c2a61fe9f289cf9efa2dc","key":17,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:effbef4bb67c2a61fe9f289cf9efa2dc\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[\"The request says stdo ticket or explicitly requests ticketing, opening or updating an STDO-governed request, bug, failed test, finding or release issue.\"],\"definition\":\"stdo-ticket turns intake into one durable governed work carrier without starting implementation.\",\"exceptions\":[\"Read-only classification is outside its invocation scope.\"],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":3,\"path\":\"plugins/spec/skills/stdo-ticket/SKILL.md\",\"quote\":\"description: Create or update one governed STDO work item. Use when a user says stdo ticket or explicitly asks to ticket, open, or update an STDO-governed request, bug, failed test, finding, or release issue. Do not invoke for read-only classification.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/plugins/spec/skills/stdo-ticket/SKILL.md#preamble\",\"start_line\":3},{\"end_line\":8,\"path\":\"plugins/spec/skills/stdo-ticket/SKILL.md\",\"quote\":\"Turn an intake into one durable work carrier without starting implementation.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/plugins/spec/skills/stdo-ticket/SKILL.md#STDO%20Ticket\",\"start_line\":8}],\"label\":\"STDO Ticket\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:33beae1c984885116b47bb6d76386149","key":18,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:33beae1c984885116b47bb6d76386149\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[\"The request says stdo work or explicitly requests requirements, design, code or test work under an STDO-governed basis.\"],\"definition\":\"stdo-work executes one admitted work item through its lawful re-entry point and delivers the smallest causally closed change authorized by one exact work basis. The admitted re-entry point decides where work begins.\",\"exceptions\":[\"Generic non-STDO development is outside its invocation scope.\"],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":3,\"path\":\"plugins/spec/skills/stdo-work/SKILL.md\",\"quote\":\"description: Execute one admitted STDO work item through its lawful re-entry point. Use when a user says stdo work or explicitly asks to perform requirements, design, code, or test work under an STDO-governed basis. Do not invoke for generic non-STDO development.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/plugins/spec/skills/stdo-work/SKILL.md#preamble\",\"start_line\":3},{\"end_line\":9,\"path\":\"plugins/spec/skills/stdo-work/SKILL.md\",\"quote\":\"Deliver the smallest causally closed change authorized by one exact work basis.\\nThe admitted re-entry point decides where work begins.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/plugins/spec/skills/stdo-work/SKILL.md#STDO%20Work\",\"start_line\":8}],\"label\":\"STDO Work\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:5fec0f21265016ca449d4389511dce49","key":19,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:5fec0f21265016ca449d4389511dce49\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"ACTIVATION declares itself Tier 1 owner of bounded work: steps and their transitions, intake, execution unit, admission, applicability/exclusion, output, configuration and delegation; context construction, size/fit/acquisition/activation/evaluation/staleness; refined results and disposition; totality, refinement, hard stops, licensing and approximation; work state/restart/accounts; cost, proportionality and resource limits; and closed results, invalidation and reuse. It uses, without redefining, FOUNDATIONS objects and core results and REFERENCE_FRAME frame objects and activate outcomes.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":25,\"path\":\"standards/ACTIVATION.md\",\"quote\":\"It uses\\nthe objects of [FOUNDATIONS §2](FOUNDATIONS.md#2-ontology), the core result\\nalgebra of [FOUNDATIONS §4 Results](FOUNDATIONS.md#results), and the frame\\nobject and the outcomes of `activate` of\\n[REFERENCE_FRAME](REFERENCE_FRAME.md) (§5). It defines the step-level\\nconcepts it introduces, among them the current state, the destination,\\nthe transition, the configuration, the execution unit, acquisition, the\\nrewrite step, the licensing law, the adequacy relation, the work state,\\nthe actor's account, progress and churn, proportionality and the closed\\nresult, and refines the\\ncore for admission, activation and steps (§3); it redefines nothing those\\nmembers own.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ACTIVATION.md#ACTIVATION\",\"start_line\":14}],\"label\":\"ACTIVATION standard\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:095b668d8b756b7fc08853511607dac3","key":20,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:095b668d8b756b7fc08853511607dac3\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"A step activates one reference frame or declared active frame configuration on an exact subject. Its context is the activated frame's projection to the actor, never the corpus or workspace. Intake, admission, applicability and activation are distinct even within one invocation.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":34,\"path\":\"standards/ACTIVATION.md\",\"quote\":\"A step is the activation of one reference frame, or one declared active\\nframe configuration, on an exact subject (REFERENCE_FRAME §1, §11). Its\\ncontext is the projection of that activated frame to the actor; the corpus\\nor the workspace is never the context (P0; RF-002). Intake, admission,\\napplicability and activation are distinct relations inside the step even\\nwhen one invocation performs all of them.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ACTIVATION.md#ACTIVATION%2F1.%20The%20step\",\"start_line\":29}],\"label\":\"Bounded step\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:bf286579d4e585eb06b3157fadd71330","key":21,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:bf286579d4e585eb06b3157fadd71330\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"Current state comprises material workspace state, authoritative inputs, justified knowledge and explicit unknowns. Work state records the workspace, governing basis, still-applicable closed results and judgments, residuals and external-effect uncertainty. An actor's context is an account of this state, not the state.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":126,\"path\":\"standards/ACTIVATION.md\",\"quote\":\"The current state is the material state of the workspace and\\nits authoritative inputs, together with what is justifiably known about\\nthat state, with the unknowns explicit. The work state of §5 records it:\\nthe workspace, the governing basis, and the closed results and judgments\\nthat still apply, with the residuals and the uncertainty over external\\neffects as the explicit unknowns. An actor's context is an account of the\\ncurrent state, not the state itself\\n([§5](#the-workspace-and-an-actors-account)) (P3, P5).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ACTIVATION.md#ACTIVATION%2F1.%20The%20step%2FTransitions\",\"start_line\":119}],\"label\":\"Current state\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:757947ab4358af48fb6a8afcb14ab842","key":22,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:757947ab4358af48fb6a8afcb14ab842\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"The destination is the owning authority's constraint-defined selected outcome, acceptance conditions and obligations to preserve. It admits multiple realised states rather than naming one state. Construction denotes this destination by Z.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":132,\"path\":\"standards/ACTIVATION.md\",\"quote\":\"The destination is defined by constraints: the selected outcome with its\\nacceptance conditions (Outcome U, [FOUNDATIONS §2](FOUNDATIONS.md#2-ontology))\\nand the governing obligations the work must keep. It names no single\\nstate: its acceptance conditions admit several realised states. Its\\nowning authority defines it (P2, P6).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ACTIVATION.md#ACTIVATION%2F1.%20The%20step%2FTransitions\",\"start_line\":128}],\"label\":\"Destination\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:3d3b5c6c2d3f3cc4fc6c364bdbb9d934","key":23,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:3d3b5c6c2d3f3cc4fc6c364bdbb9d934\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"A transition is one step's bounded change from current to next state. Work fitting one activation is one transition; work exceeding it is refined into bounded transitions under the declared refinement law.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":138,\"path\":\"standards/ACTIVATION.md\",\"quote\":\"A transition is a bounded change from the current state to a next state,\\ncarried out by one step. Where the work exceeds one activation's capacity,\\nthe outer transformation towards the destination is refined into a series\\nof bounded transitions under §4 Refinement, each carried out by its own\\nstep; work that fits one activation is a single transition.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ACTIVATION.md#ACTIVATION%2F1.%20The%20step%2FTransitions\",\"start_line\":134}],\"label\":\"Bounded transition\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:32042b38168b865f15b179aa395cf70f","key":24,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:32042b38168b865f15b179aa395cf70f\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"The construction relation binds current state A and destination predicate Z, selects work, composes steps, corrects discrepancies and grounds completion claims. Its three subject accounts are specification of required conditions, observations of what holds, and causal/predictive explanation of possible action effects. Strategy arranges admissible construction and assurance within resources; a composition boundary passes one step's output into the next starting state and differs from a categorical join. Feedback observes, compares, diagnoses, selects an authorized response, acts and observes again; homeostasis is correction toward required conditions without a convergence or adequacy guarantee.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":206,\"path\":\"standards/ACTIVATION.md\",\"quote\":\"This subsection states the construction relation for this corpus: how a\\nselected construction binds its current state and destination, chooses\\nits work, composes its steps, corrects itself and claims completion. This\\nsection owns that relation. ACTIVATION §2 to §7, EVALUATION §1,\\nSPEC_METHOD §4 and §8, EXECUTIVE_BASELINE and ODD apply it through their\\nlocal bindings; none creates a competing determination (P6).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ACTIVATION.md#ACTIVATION%2F1.%20The%20step%2FConstruction%20relation\",\"start_line\":201}],\"label\":\"Construction relation\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:51712ba4356f75aa10803f984ec35302","key":25,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:51712ba4356f75aa10803f984ec35302\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"Intake is the reconstructable governing basis from which a step activates, independent of conversation history, commentary or prior-actor memory.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":357,\"path\":\"standards/ACTIVATION.md\",\"quote\":\"A step is activated from an intake sufficient to reconstruct its governing\\nrelations without conversation history, commentary or a prior actor's memory\\n(P0, actor-change premise). The intake names:\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ACTIVATION.md#ACTIVATION%2F1.%20The%20step%2FIntake\",\"start_line\":355}],\"label\":\"Step intake\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:878ed078b22fb1ce473fd0d2699d4e73","key":26,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:878ed078b22fb1ce473fd0d2699d4e73\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"The execution unit is the smallest coherent causal dependency cone able to deliver working behaviour while preserving every affected governing relation. It need not align with a function, file, module, ticket field or design document. It is the seed set called Z for context construction in ACTIVATION §2, distinct in usage from construction's destination predicate Z.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":400,\"path\":\"standards/ACTIVATION.md\",\"quote\":\"The execution unit is the smallest coherent causal dependency cone capable\\nof delivering working behaviour while preserving every affected governing\\nrelation. It need not coincide with one function, file, module, ticket\\nfield or design document (P0, P4b). A seam whose far side can causally affect,\\nor be affected by, the action is inside the cone unless the basis\\nestablishes that it cannot participate. Unrelated incompleteness outside\\nthe cone is recorded as repricing input and does not block the bounded\\nclaim. The cone is the seed set Z of §2; the context is its projection.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ACTIVATION.md#ACTIVATION%2F1.%20The%20step%2FExecution%20unit\",\"start_line\":393}],\"label\":\"Execution unit\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:c175c5ee302c9e5c9c41a8555568a32f","key":27,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:c175c5ee302c9e5c9c41a8555568a32f\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"Execution-contract drafting and admission are distinct relations. Contracts carry at least drafted, admitted, rejected and superseded states. Admission validates a contract against its cited outcome, prerequisite or experiment basis; it does not admit that underlying basis.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":408,\"path\":\"standards/ACTIVATION.md\",\"quote\":\"Drafting a step's contract and admitting it are distinct relations, even\\ninside one invocation that drafts, validates, admits and executes; no\\nseparate turn, carrier or approval ceremony is implied by the distinction.\\nA contract carries at minimum the states drafted, admitted, rejected and\\nsuperseded ([TICKETS §5](TICKETS.md#execution-contract-admission)).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ACTIVATION.md#ACTIVATION%2F1.%20The%20step%2FAdmission\",\"start_line\":404}],\"label\":\"Execution-contract admission\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:451f63c242804b87ec1e73f8ecc74c3e","key":28,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:451f63c242804b87ec1e73f8ecc74c3e\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"Applicability evaluates the owning predicate that an obligation applies to an exact subject, using sufficient basis-bound facts. Exclusion is the state of an obligation following falsified applicability, not a result of that obligation's own evaluation.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":475,\"path\":\"standards/ACTIVATION.md\",\"quote\":\"An exclusion is the state of the excluded obligation after a\\n`falsified` applicability result: it is no result, the obligation's own\\nevaluation is not performed and maps to no core value, and the obligation\\nleaves the required coverage of a dependent conjunction under the cited\\nauthority of that applicability result.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ACTIVATION.md#ACTIVATION%2F1.%20The%20step%2FApplicability\",\"start_line\":471}],\"label\":\"Obligation applicability and exclusion\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:513eeab44b02914568c5f3d8092564e7","key":29,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:513eeab44b02914568c5f3d8092564e7\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"Step output is a candidate plus step-produced facts: judgments and their evidence, residuals, observations, authority decisions, provenance, and one construction-availability stop state. The actor's internal path is excluded from the output and is not governed.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":495,\"path\":\"standards/ACTIVATION.md\",\"quote\":\"The step's output is a candidate plus its step-produced facts: judgments with\\ntheir evidence, residuals, observations, authority decisions, provenance, and\\none stop state, a value of construction availability (§3). The actor's\\ninternal path is not part of the output\\nand is not governed (FOUNDATIONS §2, work boundary).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ACTIVATION.md#ACTIVATION%2F1.%20The%20step%2FOutput\",\"start_line\":491}],\"label\":\"Step output\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:6df3862f885cf91fa2e0a1d3a1ea15aa","key":30,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:6df3862f885cf91fa2e0a1d3a1ea15aa\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"A configuration allocates task responsibilities and information exchanges to frames across the work; activation binds actors to frames. An active frame configuration is the portion used for one evaluation or decision. A coordinator, where selected, manages delivery across tasks from bounded closed results. The optional Executive configuration assigns construction to Worker/Writer, assessment to Reviewer, and longer-term outcome, next-work selection and granted disposition to a non-mutating Executive; it is not the method default.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":503,\"path\":\"standards/ACTIVATION.md\",\"quote\":\"A configuration allocates a task's responsibilities and information\\nexchanges to frames; activation binds an actor to each frame (§2). It\\nspans the task's work. The active frame configuration of\\n[FOUNDATIONS §2](FOUNDATIONS.md#frame-objects) is the part of it used for\\none evaluation or decision (P0, P6).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ACTIVATION.md#ACTIVATION%2F1.%20The%20step%2FConfiguration\",\"start_line\":499},{\"end_line\":604,\"path\":\"standards/ACTIVATION.md\",\"quote\":\"It allocates construction,\\nassessment and disposition (Roles and delegation below) to three frames: a\\nWorker frame, specialised as Writer for documents and records, constructs;\\na Reviewer frame assesses; an Executive frame keeps the longer-term\\noutcome, selects the next work and disposes within its decision grant, and\\nmutates nothing. That profile owns its frames, their grants, limits and\\nprohibitions, and its explanation; they apply where it is selected. It is\\nnot the method's default. A configuration with other frames, names or\\ntopology is evaluated as Evaluation of a configuration above states.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ACTIVATION.md#ACTIVATION%2F1.%20The%20step%2FConfiguration\",\"start_line\":596}],\"label\":\"Frame configuration\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:5a4be050afd6cab484eae2425fa439e5","key":31,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:5a4be050afd6cab484eae2425fa439e5\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"Roles are configuration-allocated relations over steps, not actor kinds or a fixed inventory. Where the corresponding operations occur, the constructor owns bounded implementation and self-review, the assessor independently evaluates a frozen candidate, and the decision owner disposes. Other responsibilities may be allocated.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":627,\"path\":\"standards/ACTIVATION.md\",\"quote\":\"Roles are relations over steps that a configuration allocates\\n(Configuration above), not kinds of actor and not a fixed inventory.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ACTIVATION.md#ACTIVATION%2F1.%20The%20step%2FRoles%20and%20delegation\",\"start_line\":621}],\"label\":\"Roles over steps\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:ea44ff449da230ebcd91aa055503a19e","key":32,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:ea44ff449da230ebcd91aa055503a19e\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"A bounded operation grant can cover a declared construction, status and checkpoint sequence. A bounded proxy is a delegate whose ability to accept and advance routine actions must be declared by the governing authority relation.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":638,\"path\":\"standards/ACTIVATION.md\",\"quote\":\"The governing authority relation declares whether a bounded proxy may\\naccept and advance routine actions.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ACTIVATION.md#ACTIVATION%2F1.%20The%20step%2FRoles%20and%20delegation\",\"start_line\":637},{\"end_line\":682,\"path\":\"standards/ACTIVATION.md\",\"quote\":\"One bounded operation grant may cover its declared construction, status and\\ncheckpoint sequence.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ACTIVATION.md#ACTIVATION%2F1.%20The%20step%2FRoles%20and%20delegation\",\"start_line\":681}],\"label\":\"Bounded operation grant and proxy\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:6e08c1219e2615bd98a4b4349eacb927","key":33,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:6e08c1219e2615bd98a4b4349eacb927\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"Context construction is the source-defined procedure joining material closure, projection, envelope fit and exact input acquisition. Z contains the intake's subject, outcome and affected relations; R contains dependency relations whose change can alter result, basis validity, evidence sufficiency or authority; B is the actor's envelope.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":698,\"path\":\"standards/ACTIVATION.md\",\"quote\":\"Given a seed set Z (the subject, outcome and affected relations named in the\\nintake), a relation family R (the dependency relations whose change can\\nalter the result, basis validity, evidence sufficiency or authority), and\\nthe actor's envelope B:\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ACTIVATION.md#ACTIVATION%2F2.%20Context%20construction%20under%20an%20envelope\",\"start_line\":695}],\"label\":\"Context construction under an envelope\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:a7bf2b374366f62d9330810c3c2636be","key":34,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:a7bf2b374366f62d9330810c3c2636be\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"Acquisition is read-only observation of the frame, actual subject and declared inputs needed by a step, within the inputs its intake permits. Activation selects one capable frame or declared active frame configuration and binds reusable declarations to the exact subject and basis. Evaluation applies the activated frame's invariants, evidence rules and result algebra.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":780,\"path\":\"standards/ACTIVATION.md\",\"quote\":\"Acquisition. Acquisition is the read-only observation of the material a\\nstep needs (its frame, its subject and its declared inputs) within the\\ninputs its intake permits it to acquire (§1 Intake).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ACTIVATION.md#ACTIVATION%2F2.%20Context%20construction%20under%20an%20envelope\",\"start_line\":776},{\"end_line\":819,\"path\":\"standards/ACTIVATION.md\",\"quote\":\"Activation\\nbinds each reusable frame declaration to the exact subject and basis and\\nloads the declared material relations and evidence sources\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ACTIVATION.md#ACTIVATION%2F2.%20Context%20construction%20under%20an%20envelope\",\"start_line\":817},{\"end_line\":830,\"path\":\"standards/ACTIVATION.md\",\"quote\":\"Evaluation. The evaluator applies the activated frame's declared\\ninvariants, evidence rules and result algebra.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ACTIVATION.md#ACTIVATION%2F2.%20Context%20construction%20under%20an%20envelope\",\"start_line\":829}],\"label\":\"Acquisition, activation and evaluation\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:1e4bf2ddf108dcc3728f8fb9c3694873","key":35,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:1e4bf2ddf108dcc3728f8fb9c3694873\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"A derived surface copies, projects or compresses owning sources, names those sources and owns no determination. A task constraint surface from a current a_c interpretation is an example, subject to the cited constraint-surface law. Currentness is relative to an exact selected basis; it is distinct from fidelity and question-specific sufficiency.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":784,\"path\":\"standards/ACTIVATION.md\",\"quote\":\"A derived surface is material derived from owning\\nsources by copying, projection or compression, such as a projected frame\\nfor a task; it names its sources and owns no determination.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ACTIVATION.md#ACTIVATION%2F2.%20Context%20construction%20under%20an%20envelope\",\"start_line\":782},{\"end_line\":901,\"path\":\"standards/ACTIVATION.md\",\"quote\":\"They establish neither its fidelity to them nor its\\n  sufficiency for a question\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ACTIVATION.md#ACTIVATION%2F2.%20Context%20construction%20under%20an%20envelope%2FStaleness%20of%20derived%20surfaces\",\"start_line\":899}],\"label\":\"Derived surface\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:3af2fdc9a53de92bc0500be7d49532ee","key":36,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:3af2fdc9a53de92bc0500be7d49532ee\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"A prompt is a rendered contract over typed authority, not source law; it projects the material selected by acquisition.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":845,\"path\":\"standards/ACTIVATION.md\",\"quote\":\"Prompt construction. A prompt is rendered contract over typed authority;\\nit is not source law.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ACTIVATION.md#ACTIVATION%2F2.%20Context%20construction%20under%20an%20envelope\",\"start_line\":844}],\"label\":\"Prompt as rendered contract\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:59e8abdb24124885d914c88740a00872","key":37,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:59e8abdb24124885d914c88740a00872\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"The source describes five refinements of its core result algebra: admission and activation asks whether a step may begin; construction availability asks whether a candidate is available; disposition asks whether a candidate is accepted at its declared boundary; ambiguity outcome asks whether a declared ambiguity is resolved on the exact basis; effects asks whether an intended effect occurred. These answer different questions from the step's evaluations.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":941,\"path\":\"standards/ACTIVATION.md\",\"quote\":\"| admission and activation | may the step begin | the step is lawfully admitted and activated on the exact subject and basis |\\n| construction availability | did the step yield its output | a candidate is available |\\n| disposition | what the decision owner does with an assessed candidate | the candidate is accepted at its declared boundary |\\n| ambiguity outcome | what happened to a declared ambiguity | the declared ambiguity is resolved on the exact basis |\\n| effects | did an intended external effect occur | the intended effect occurred |\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ACTIVATION.md#ACTIVATION%2F3.%20Step%20results%20and%20disposition\",\"start_line\":937}],\"label\":\"Five predicate-bound result refinements\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:967b396c83203d799b9da541efa92a8f","key":38,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:967b396c83203d799b9da541efa92a8f\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"Admission and activation outcomes concern lawful admission and activation on the exact subject and basis. A step exists only after its contract is admitted and its frame activated. Named outcomes are activated, admission_refused(authority), admission_refused(basis), closure_unresolved, out_of_frame and cause-qualified activation_refusal.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":953,\"path\":\"standards/ACTIVATION.md\",\"quote\":\"A step exists only after its contract is admitted (§1, Admission) and its\\nframe is activated on the exact subject and basis (§2).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ACTIVATION.md#ACTIVATION%2F3.%20Step%20results%20and%20disposition%2FAdmission%20and%20activation\",\"start_line\":949}],\"label\":\"Admission and activation outcomes\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:fdffde11bee635b630b1f96f399dbd64","key":39,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:fdffde11bee635b630b1f96f399dbd64\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[\"Lawful activation has occurred.\"],\"definition\":\"Construction availability records existence of a step's candidate output: a constructing step's constructed subject or an assessing step's closed results. Its values are candidate_ready, refused, incomplete, re_entry_requested(authority) and re_entry_requested(basis). Output remains a candidate until evaluated.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":986,\"path\":\"standards/ACTIVATION.md\",\"quote\":\"A step's output is a candidate until evaluated (FOUNDATIONS §3, P0): the\\nconstructed subject of a constructing step, or the closed results of an\\nassessing step. Construction availability records whether that output\\nexists (P5, P6):\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ACTIVATION.md#ACTIVATION%2F3.%20Step%20results%20and%20disposition%2FConstruction%20availability\",\"start_line\":983}],\"label\":\"Construction availability\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:ed56e674258c8d8e90c3046d72aaf499","key":40,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:ed56e674258c8d8e90c3046d72aaf499\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[\"A decision owner disposes an assessed candidate.\"],\"definition\":\"Disposition is the acceptance result, distinct from availability, assessment and an assessor's recommendation. Its four semantic values are accept, local_repair, re_enter and reject, all mapped for acceptance at the candidate's declared boundary.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1037,\"path\":\"standards/ACTIVATION.md\",\"quote\":\"The disposition is the\\nacceptance result: it consumes the candidate's availability and assessment\\nresults and stays separate from both (FOUNDATIONS §4 Results).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ACTIVATION.md#ACTIVATION%2F3.%20Step%20results%20and%20disposition%2FDisposition\",\"start_line\":1033}],\"label\":\"Candidate disposition\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:af664c6b9353a038c00eff8d30c32886","key":41,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:af664c6b9353a038c00eff8d30c32886\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[\"A declared ambiguity is being handled.\"],\"definition\":\"Ambiguity outcomes are resolved, carried, escalated and blocked. They answer whether the declared ambiguity is resolved on the exact basis and retain their domain-specific information beside their core value.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1073,\"path\":\"standards/ACTIVATION.md\",\"quote\":\"A declared ambiguity is resolved, carried, escalated or blocked, and the\\noutcome is recorded either way\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ACTIVATION.md#ACTIVATION%2F3.%20Step%20results%20and%20disposition%2FAmbiguity%20outcome\",\"start_line\":1068}],\"label\":\"Ambiguity outcome\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:5a3dd9d1ad03a25d09bcc27c8ac5c6c1","key":42,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:5a3dd9d1ad03a25d09bcc27c8ac5c6c1\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[\"An effectful step has an intended external effect.\"],\"definition\":\"Effect outcomes concern attainment of the declared intended outcome: completed, not_effected or completion_unknown. Whether the effect has ended is a separate question, required conjunctively for completed and otherwise recorded as an unresolved end when applicable. Uncertain completion includes completion_unknown and not_effected with an unestablished end.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1099,\"path\":\"standards/ACTIVATION.md\",\"quote\":\"An effectful step's intended external effect has one of three values,\\nmapped for the predicate \\\"the intended effect occurred\\\", that is, the\\ndeclared outcome of the effect is attained.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ACTIVATION.md#ACTIVATION%2F3.%20Step%20results%20and%20disposition%2FEffects\",\"start_line\":1095},{\"end_line\":1130,\"path\":\"standards/ACTIVATION.md\",\"quote\":\"An effect of uncertain completion is one whose value is\\n`completion_unknown`, or whose value is `not_effected` with its end not\\nestablished.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ACTIVATION.md#ACTIVATION%2F3.%20Step%20results%20and%20disposition%2FEffects\",\"start_line\":1128}],\"label\":\"External effect outcome and end\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:f0c8f92d73a2b89efda429853c9a3bbe","key":43,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:f0c8f92d73a2b89efda429853c9a3bbe\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"Total handling declares a next move for every admitted condition class, including an explicit unknown class. It does not assert recognition of every external condition, provider termination or completion of every request. A hanging call, unsatisfiable demand and lost post-effect response remain distinct cases.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1152,\"path\":\"standards/ACTIVATION.md\",\"quote\":\"Each admitted condition class has a declared\\nnext move, including an explicit unknown class. Total handling does not\\nclaim that every external condition is recognised, that an invoked provider\\nterminates, or that every request can be completed.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ACTIVATION.md#ACTIVATION%2F4.%20Totality%20and%20refinement\",\"start_line\":1147}],\"label\":\"Total handling and reconfiguration\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:37b3d302abc5b3361220cc283757b68c","key":44,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:37b3d302abc5b3361220cc283757b68c\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"Refinement decomposes an outer transformation T: A → X with success predicates P₀ … Pₙ into steps. A rewrite replaces a representation, step or composite by another claimed to keep its meaning, including partitioning, regrouping, reordering, merging or substitution. Exact steps preserve meaning under the subject's declared interpretation; approximate steps instead require an adequacy relation and a composite end-to-end bound.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1187,\"path\":\"standards/ACTIVATION.md\",\"quote\":\"An outer transformation T: A → X with success predicates P₀ … Pₙ\\nis faithfully refined by steps Tᵢ\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ACTIVATION.md#ACTIVATION%2F4.%20Totality%20and%20refinement%2FRefinement\",\"start_line\":1183},{\"end_line\":1213,\"path\":\"standards/ACTIVATION.md\",\"quote\":\"A rewrite step replaces a representation, a step or\\na composite by another that is claimed to keep its meaning\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ACTIVATION.md#ACTIVATION%2F4.%20Totality%20and%20refinement%2FRefinement\",\"start_line\":1211}],\"label\":\"Refinement, rewrite, exactness and approximation\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:bfe14a0ff0b9caef21ad7cbc62061481","key":45,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:bfe14a0ff0b9caef21ad7cbc62061481\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[\"A material transition is proposed for admission.\"],\"definition\":\"The complete enclosing admission relation includes every participant and equality join whose identity, validity, authority, currentness or transition can affect or be affected by admission, including relevant far sides of crossing seams. Each admission owner independently derives and validates it from authoritative inputs.\",\"exceptions\":[\"A crossing seam's far side may be excluded when authoritative evidence establishes that it cannot participate.\"],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1267,\"path\":\"standards/ACTIVATION.md\",\"quote\":\"For a material transition, each admission owner is independently\\nresponsible for deriving and validating the complete enclosing relation\\nfrom authoritative inputs (P4b, P6).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ACTIVATION.md#ACTIVATION%2F4.%20Totality%20and%20refinement%2FComplete%20enclosing-relation%20admission\",\"start_line\":1259}],\"label\":\"Complete enclosing-relation admission\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:90da442170f46d6cdf3bca49e170cff2","key":46,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:90da442170f46d6cdf3bca49e170cff2\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[\"An admission owner and supported boundary are declared by accepted design.\"],\"definition\":\"Standing structural qualification instantiates the admission law for every such owner and boundary, with case applicability determined by supported inputs, state and operating or threat model. It examines direct, composite or nested, forged, ambiguous, stale, incoherent, competing-authority, reconstructed, replay and atomic-publication-failure forms.\",\"exceptions\":[\"Unsupported forms require a design-grounded not_applicable disposition and no weaker or competing path.\"],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1317,\"path\":\"standards/ACTIVATION.md\",\"quote\":\"Qualification of the admission law is instantiated for every admission\\nowner and supported boundary declared by accepted design (P6). Case applicability\\nfollows the supported input, state and operating or threat model.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ACTIVATION.md#ACTIVATION%2F4.%20Totality%20and%20refinement%2FStanding%20structural%20qualification\",\"start_line\":1311}],\"label\":\"Standing structural qualification\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:1922d98a4b06f1a4a48edade05b0d465","key":47,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:1922d98a4b06f1a4a48edade05b0d465\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"Work state is an object comprising the current persistent workspace, governing basis, applicable closed results and judgments with invalidators, residuals and known uncertainty over external effects. Resumption re-enters the same method from current material state, possibly with another actor. Checkpointing, resumption and progress accounting are carrier-independent procedures.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1350,\"path\":\"standards/ACTIVATION.md\",\"quote\":\"Work state is the tuple of: the current persistent workspace; the governing\\nbasis; the applicable closed results and judgments with their invalidators;\\nthe residuals; and the known uncertainty over external effects.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ACTIVATION.md#ACTIVATION%2F5.%20Work%20state%20and%20restart\",\"start_line\":1343}],\"label\":\"Work state, resumption and checkpoint\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:7fe4bc4d420d2ffbab8ac5fcc89547c3","key":48,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:7fe4bc4d420d2ffbab8ac5fcc89547c3\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"Progress is accepted material movement toward the selected outcome. Prerequisite work names the obligation enabled; preservation and repeated proof are evidence without new progress; rejected or superseded construction is churn; discovering hidden distance revises the forecast without being negative progress. These are semantic categories, not a numeric progress algorithm.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1382,\"path\":\"standards/ACTIVATION.md\",\"quote\":\"Progress is accepted material movement toward the selected outcome;\\nprerequisite work names the obligation it enables; preservation and\\nrepeated proof are evidence, not new progress; rejected or superseded\\nconstruction is churn; discovering previously hidden distance revises the\\nforecast and is not negative progress.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ACTIVATION.md#ACTIVATION%2F5.%20Work%20state%20and%20restart\",\"start_line\":1375}],\"label\":\"Progress categories\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:1bbfea85ff18f82f399dc48f5698013b","key":49,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:1bbfea85ff18f82f399dc48f5698013b\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"The persistent workspace and authoritative inputs are the work's continuing truth surface. An actor's context is its bounded, revisable and disposable account, not a second truth surface. Later intake reconstructs governing relations without the prior actor's private context.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1440,\"path\":\"standards/ACTIVATION.md\",\"quote\":\"The workspace and its authoritative inputs persist across activations and\\nare the continuing truth surface of the work: the surface whose current\\nmaterial state decides what the work has and has not done.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ACTIVATION.md#ACTIVATION%2F5.%20Work%20state%20and%20restart%2FThe%20workspace%20and%20an%20actor%27s%20account\",\"start_line\":1431}],\"label\":\"Workspace truth surface and actor account\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:e3fd35bdac6bd4cd6baec77ead672074","key":50,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:e3fd35bdac6bd4cd6baec77ead672074\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"Proportionality relates semantic ambiguity removed to effective reasoning complexity introduced. Complexity includes independent concepts and authority surfaces, cross-document joins, exceptions, branching, states, transitions, reconciled duplicates and decision-relevant detail; it is not raw lines, artifact count or context-window size.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1506,\"path\":\"standards/ACTIVATION.md\",\"quote\":\"Proportionality is the relation between semantic ambiguity removed and\\neffective reasoning complexity introduced.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ACTIVATION.md#ACTIVATION%2F6.%20Cost%20and%20proportionality\",\"start_line\":1492}],\"label\":\"Proportionality\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:c5b83e3a0a9998b11c480c9d9b26887b","key":51,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:c5b83e3a0a9998b11c480c9d9b26887b\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[\"A cost claim is the governed question.\"],\"definition\":\"A selected cost claim declares an allowance and reports spend measured under the selected execution binding or explicitly unmeasured. Material startup, framework processing, external computation, transport and assurance costs are distinct components. Transferred-context cost includes every delegated actor.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1552,\"path\":\"standards/ACTIVATION.md\",\"quote\":\"Cost is selected, not universal. Where a cost claim is the governed\\nquestion, the activation declares its allowance and reports its spend,\\nmeasured under the selected execution binding or recorded as unmeasured\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ACTIVATION.md#ACTIVATION%2F6.%20Cost%20and%20proportionality\",\"start_line\":1549}],\"label\":\"Selected cost claim\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:c95cc0e07f26edab0dce96bc1cff9eaf","key":52,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:c95cc0e07f26edab0dce96bc1cff9eaf\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"A resource limit bounds context, attention, wall time, spend, human effort, communication or machine resources consumed by activation. Its intake, capability envelope or selected execution binding must declare it. This law supplies no numerical limit; the selected execution binding supplies values and measurable units and boundaries.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1603,\"path\":\"standards/ACTIVATION.md\",\"quote\":\"A resource limit bounds a resource that an activation consumes: context,\\nattention, wall time, spend, human effort, communication or a machine\\nresource (P0). This subsection owns the law for every such limit. It sets\\nno value\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ACTIVATION.md#ACTIVATION%2F6.%20Cost%20and%20proportionality%2FResource%20limits\",\"start_line\":1600}],\"label\":\"Declared resource limit\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:5b25bc7a2a279511eaa355c912e1a27b","key":53,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:5b25bc7a2a279511eaa355c912e1a27b\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"A closed result identifies frame and activation, subject, basis, evaluation, actor, evidence, verdict, residual uncertainty and invalidation conditions. Its reuse depends on exact applicability and three invalidator kinds: material input change, changed basis and a declared revising observation that occurs.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1657,\"path\":\"standards/ACTIVATION.md\",\"quote\":\"A closed result identifies the frame and its activation, the subject, the\\nbasis, the evaluation, the actor, the evidence, the verdict, the residual\\nuncertainty and the invalidation conditions\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ACTIVATION.md#ACTIVATION%2F7.%20Closed%20result%20and%20reuse\",\"start_line\":1654}],\"label\":\"Closed result and invalidators\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:e5c8b96517828a0f56dd887c29ace149","key":54,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:e5c8b96517828a0f56dd887c29ace149\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"Transition evidence is a consumer-represented read model identifying exact candidate, affected relations, changed realisation paths, added or removed authority paths, retained and open seams, focused and required integration proof, explicit non-changes, any activated assessor's recommendation and the owner's disposition once made. It is not specification, design or admission authority.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1725,\"path\":\"standards/ACTIVATION.md\",\"quote\":\"Consumers\\nchoose the representation. Transition evidence is a read\\nmodel; it does not become specification, design or admission authority\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ACTIVATION.md#ACTIVATION%2F7.%20Closed%20result%20and%20reuse%2FTransition%20evidence\",\"start_line\":1722}],\"label\":\"Transition evidence\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:9064eb4b0984f7fd1d567f3325b1ca5d","key":55,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:9064eb4b0984f7fd1d567f3325b1ca5d\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"ASSURANCE is presented as a tier-2 owner of assurance and testing law: verification layers; testing taxonomy, proof authorities and portability; test authority; scenario bundles; installed development proof; significant paths; product testing frames; combinatorial coverage and testing value; legitimate-path and technical-debt erasure; evidence composition; subject acquisition; counterexample localisation; and interface integration. Its family table is F14. It consumes tier-1 laws without adding tier-1 definitions.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":11,\"path\":\"standards/ASSURANCE.md\",\"quote\":\"Tier 2. Owns the assurance and testing law of the method\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ASSURANCE.md#ASSURANCE\",\"start_line\":3},{\"end_line\":20,\"path\":\"standards/ASSURANCE.md\",\"quote\":\"adds no definition to tier 1.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ASSURANCE.md#ASSURANCE\",\"start_line\":20}],\"label\":\"ASSURANCE document role\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:06901ce9bac058a7449da2d48cc0ae44","key":56,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:06901ce9bac058a7449da2d48cc0ae44\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"The verification layers preserve distinct truths: requirements preserve invariant truth and ask what must be true; design preserves structural choice and asks how that truth is realised; scenarios preserve operational meaning and ask whether the realised system can do the claimed thing. Scenarios are concrete end-to-end product-owner use cases validating intent through realised behaviour.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":40,\"path\":\"standards/ASSURANCE.md\",\"quote\":\"| Requirements | invariant truth | what must be true? |\\n| Design | structural choice | how is that truth realised? |\\n| Scenarios | operational meaning | can the realised system actually do the claimed thing? |\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ASSURANCE.md#ASSURANCE%2F1.%20Verification%20layers\",\"start_line\":38}],\"label\":\"Requirements, design and scenarios\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:ad2911520dc8ffb9419df0fede4f0e57","key":57,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:ad2911520dc8ffb9419df0fede4f0e57\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"F14 is the source's foundation-to-law account for evidence about realised products and its organisation. Its additional instance premises are runnable product (source and deployed, installed or runnable forms can produce execution or observation evidence), composition (modules, interfaces and owners form causal paths), users (claims concern supported-surface outcomes), external boundaries (workers, transports or fixtures outside source), and designed modules (a design profile may govern a boundary and module ownership). Commitments do not supply these premises. Fourteen rows distinguish claimed consequences from domain and policy choices.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":88,\"path\":\"standards/ASSURANCE.md\",\"quote\":\"Its instance premises, which the commitments\\ndo not supply, are named in the rows as follows:\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ASSURANCE.md#ASSURANCE%2F1.%20Verification%20layers%2FFoundation%20to%20law%3A%20assurance%20and%20testing\",\"start_line\":77}],\"label\":\"F14 assurance and testing foundation account\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:2e29eb63656a6092cdf8daa41beaada3","key":58,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:2e29eb63656a6092cdf8daa41beaada3\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[\"The selected complete STDO basis supplies the bounded context.\"],\"definition\":\"The product-assurance bounded context is urn:stdo:bounded-context:product-assurance. Its Product-level taxonomy distinguishes design or module conformance authority from UAT or acceptance authority independently of execution breadth. Conformance asks whether implementation realises the module or design boundary; UAT asks whether the composed product satisfies its claimed requirement or scenario.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":140,\"path\":\"standards/ASSURANCE.md\",\"quote\":\"This member owns the product-assurance bounded context,\\n`urn:stdo:bounded-context:product-assurance`, under the selected complete\\nSTDO basis, and within it the Product-level test-authority taxonomy.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ASSURANCE.md#ASSURANCE%2F2.%20Testing%20strategy%20taxonomy\",\"start_line\":135}],\"label\":\"Product-assurance proof taxonomy\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:433fbad86b733e2a1409c02021a25be1","key":59,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:433fbad86b733e2a1409c02021a25be1\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"Sandbox UAT exercises an isolated composed product through declared application, public, runtime or control surfaces using a requirement-sourced scenario or acceptance case. Harnessed mode uses deterministic, fake, recorded or injected worker or result surfaces; live mode uses a real configured worker, tool, agent, service or external probabilistic transport where the product depends on that boundary.\",\"exceptions\":[\"An explicitly equivalent isolated composed-product proof lane may also be called UAT or acceptance testing.\"],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":181,\"path\":\"standards/ASSURANCE.md\",\"quote\":\"Under this method only sandbox tests, or an explicitly equivalent isolated\\ncomposed-product proof lane, may be called UAT or acceptance tests.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ASSURANCE.md#ASSURANCE%2F2.%20Testing%20strategy%20taxonomy\",\"start_line\":173},{\"end_line\":189,\"path\":\"standards/ASSURANCE.md\",\"quote\":\"- harnessed sandbox UAT exercises the full composed product path with a\\n  deterministic, fake, recorded or injected worker or result surface; and\\n- live sandbox UAT exercises the full composed product path with a real\\n  configured worker, tool, agent, service or other external probabilistic\\n  transport where the product depends on that live boundary.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ASSURANCE.md#ASSURANCE%2F2.%20Testing%20strategy%20taxonomy\",\"start_line\":185}],\"label\":\"Harnessed and live sandbox UAT\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:3bc1331fd561438b3abf435cbe8f3166","key":60,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:3bc1331fd561438b3abf435cbe8f3166\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"Fixture and proof portability concerns reproducibility of required closure lanes from their declared source boundary and the classification or declared acquisition of external project evidence.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":221,\"path\":\"standards/ASSURANCE.md\",\"quote\":\"Required closure lanes are reproducible from the declared source boundary\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ASSURANCE.md#ASSURANCE%2F2.%20Testing%20strategy%20taxonomy%2FFixture%20and%20proof%20portability\",\"start_line\":217}],\"label\":\"Fixture and proof portability\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:12d92e8aac0a56903f7c6713bf136289","key":61,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:12d92e8aac0a56903f7c6713bf136289\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"Written test-case authority is traceable authority for each live requirement's proof. It includes each expected result's assertion provenance: owning obligation, interpretation, assumptions, derivation, shared dependencies and whether the asserted predicate is the obligation itself, a necessary condition or part of a sufficient conjunction.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":245,\"path\":\"standards/ASSURANCE.md\",\"quote\":\"Written authority includes the assertion\\nprovenance of each expected result: the owning obligation, its\\ninterpretation, assumptions, derivation and shared dependencies, and\\nwhether the asserted predicate is the obligation, a necessary condition of\\nit or part of a sufficient conjunction\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ASSURANCE.md#ASSURANCE%2F3.%20Test%20authority\",\"start_line\":241}],\"label\":\"Written test-case authority\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:a53692f0d555aea884937662d5230e55","key":62,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:a53692f0d555aea884937662d5230e55\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"An ordered proving surface showing the exercised feature or use-case boundary, the test-case sequence and expected outcomes at significant steps, making operational meaning inspectable. Declared scenarios and use cases expose operational boundaries, sequences, actors, controls and outcomes and are the preferred source for identifying significant code and control paths.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":265,\"path\":\"standards/ASSURANCE.md\",\"quote\":\"A scenario bundle shows the feature or use-case boundary being exercised,\\nthe test-case sequence that proves it, and the outcomes expected at each\\nsignificant step. It is the layer that makes operational meaning\\ninspectable (P6).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ASSURANCE.md#ASSURANCE%2F4.%20Scenario%20bundle\",\"start_line\":262}],\"label\":\"Scenario bundle\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:b0b4ff2640d207bee8d1ebe2ff5163f3","key":63,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:b0b4ff2640d207bee8d1ebe2ff5163f3\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[\"The system has an installable or runnable development form.\"],\"definition\":\"The decisive proving lane exercises an installed development version as an independent project or externalised target.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":279,\"path\":\"standards/ASSURANCE.md\",\"quote\":\"Where a system has an installable or runnable development form, the\\ndecisive proving lane runs against an installed development version as if\\nit were an independent project or an externalised target, not only against\\nthe source tree in place (P6, P3).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ASSURANCE.md#ASSURANCE%2F5.%20Installed%20dev%20proof\",\"start_line\":276}],\"label\":\"Installed development proof\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:f9c245e92a9e876a8878777f5d99ecff","key":64,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:f9c245e92a9e876a8878777f5d99ecff\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"Claim-relative meaningful paths deliberately named and exercised by the proving surface. Relevant paths usually include success, fail-closed or rejection, boundary or control, integration or dispatch or transport, and recovery or retry or replay.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":293,\"path\":\"standards/ASSURANCE.md\",\"quote\":\"The proving surface declares and exercises the significant paths for the\\nbehaviour being claimed (P6, P2).\\nExhaustive proof does not mean every possible branch in every file; it\\nmeans the project names the meaningful paths and proves them\\nintentionally.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ASSURANCE.md#ASSURANCE%2F6.%20Significant%20path%20coverage\",\"start_line\":289}],\"label\":\"Significant paths\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:5501995e5fa70ff1ab307cf852168870","key":65,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:5501995e5fa70ff1ab307cf852168870\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[\"Governing frame configuration or admitted work authority selects testing frames for a Product promotion, closure or release-assurance claim.\"],\"definition\":\"A claim-relative testing configuration ordinarily containing four distinct frames: user acceptance, end to end, integration and unit. Availability in this member does not activate the set or its supporting sections 8–13.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":306,\"path\":\"standards/ASSURANCE.md\",\"quote\":\"## 7. Product testing frame set\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ASSURANCE.md#ASSURANCE%2F7.%20Product%20testing%20frame%20set\",\"start_line\":306},{\"end_line\":345,\"path\":\"standards/ASSURANCE.md\",\"quote\":\"Where the governing frame configuration (PRODUCT_DEFINITION §7) or the\\nadmitted work authority selects testing frames for a Product promotion,\\nclosure or release-assurance claim, testing is configured as a\\nclaim-relative set of testing frames. Placement in this member makes the\\nset, and the law of §8 to §13 that serves it, available; it adopts nothing,\\nand each activation is decided by ACTIVATION §1 (Applicability).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ASSURANCE.md#ASSURANCE%2F7.%20Product%20testing%20frame%20set%2FThe%20set\",\"start_line\":340}],\"label\":\"Product testing frame set\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:2aa7efe612226c86a56903f07ffef6a4","key":66,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:2aa7efe612226c86a56903f07ffef6a4\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"A frame whose evaluation executes or observes a declared subject to discriminate one exact claim using an explicit oracle, evidence population, path boundary and falsification condition.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":313,\"path\":\"standards/ASSURANCE.md\",\"quote\":\"A testing frame is a frame (REFERENCE_FRAME §1) whose evaluation executes\\nor observes a declared subject to discriminate one exact claim through an\\nexplicit oracle, evidence population, path boundary and falsification\\ncondition.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ASSURANCE.md#ASSURANCE%2F7.%20Product%20testing%20frame%20set%2FTerms\",\"start_line\":310}],\"label\":\"Testing frame\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:a95cc4187253ab78a3b16b5c7c45e144","key":67,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:a95cc4187253ab78a3b16b5c7c45e144\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"The declared ordinary causal composition from a supported user or public entry through the exact selected interfaces, owners, state transitions, effects, persistence and recovery boundaries to the outcome projection required by the Product claim.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":322,\"path\":\"standards/ASSURANCE.md\",\"quote\":\"An authoritative Product path is the declared ordinary causal composition\\nfrom a supported user or public entry, through the exact selected\\ninterfaces, owners, state transitions, effects, persistence and recovery\\nboundaries, to the outcome projection the Product claim requires.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ASSURANCE.md#ASSURANCE%2F7.%20Product%20testing%20frame%20set%2FTerms\",\"start_line\":319}],\"label\":\"Authoritative Product path\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:37c6c0adb01d42ea37f40ece5db0dad2","key":68,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:37c6c0adb01d42ea37f40ece5db0dad2\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"The claim-relative population of independent dimensions and interactions whose combinations can change an outcome, violate an invariant, select another authority path or expose failure. Unit dimensions include module-owned public-contract laws, algebraic operators, calculation regimes, states, transitions, boundary classes and failures; cross-participant interface, Product, persistence, configuration and user-role combinations belong to integration, end-to-end or user-acceptance frames.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":330,\"path\":\"standards/ASSURANCE.md\",\"quote\":\"Material combinatorial complexity is the claim-relative population of\\nindependent dimensions and interactions whose combinations can change an\\noutcome, violate an invariant, select another authority path or expose a\\nfailure.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ASSURANCE.md#ASSURANCE%2F7.%20Product%20testing%20frame%20set%2FTerms\",\"start_line\":327}],\"label\":\"Material combinatorial complexity\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:9e6e1272a4d33627b22f146f2f8b9751","key":69,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:9e6e1272a4d33627b22f146f2f8b9751\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[\"The claim asks whether a declared user can obtain the exact Product-defined outcome through the supported ordinary surface.\"],\"definition\":\"The primary Product-outcome evidence frame for claims that a user can use the Product. Its subject is the exact deployed, installed or runnable form under current Product, requirement, UX, identity, policy and acceptance authority, declared role, environment and harnessed/live mode. Its manifold covers goals, entries, permissions, inputs, configuration, ordinary dependencies, declared worker/transport substitutions, visible state and outputs, refusals, recovery and acceptance interval. Coordinates bind Product/artifact identity, install, role, capability, configuration, dependency realisation, mode, data, workspace, invocation, time, outcome and scenario. Evidence includes actual supported requests/responses, visible projections, claimed durable effects, refusals, recovery, scenario records and exact subject/dependency identities. Capability requires acting as the declared user, perceiving material outcomes/refusals and detecting hidden setup or unsupported assistance.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":409,\"path\":\"standards/ASSURANCE.md\",\"quote\":\"| capability envelope | ability to operate the Product as the declared user would, perceive the material outcome and refusal surfaces, and distinguish hidden setup or unsupported assistance |\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ASSURANCE.md#ASSURANCE%2F7.%20Product%20testing%20frame%20set%2FUser-acceptance%20frame\",\"start_line\":409}],\"label\":\"User-acceptance frame\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:74b38a1ed583949eef88dee3e98a862a","key":70,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:74b38a1ed583949eef88dee3e98a862a\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"Evaluates whether the exact runnable Product realises an outcome through every material interface, owner, state transition, effect, persistence, continuation, recovery and projection boundary of the complete authoritative path. Basis includes composition design, supported entry, selected owners/dependencies, ordinary runtime configuration and Product claim. The manifold includes entry-to-outcome producers/consumers, contracts, authority transitions, state, events, persistence, processes, continuation, retry, recovery, projections and competing paths. Coordinates identify artifact/install, entry, operation, definition/owner, path/edges, process, event prefix, state, configuration, dependency, result, replay and scenario. Evidence includes entry invocation, observed semantic path/authority edges, owner receipts, durable events, transitions, outputs, claimed replay/reconstruction, installed identity and negative paths. Capability requires observing the complete path without changing it, distinguishing rivals and reproducing material state/failure relations.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":434,\"path\":\"standards/ASSURANCE.md\",\"quote\":\"| evaluation family | Does the exact Product subject realise the claimed outcome through the complete authoritative Product path, including every material interface, owner, state transition, effect, persistence, continuation, recovery and projection boundary? |\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ASSURANCE.md#ASSURANCE%2F7.%20Product%20testing%20frame%20set%2FEnd-to-end%20frame\",\"start_line\":434}],\"label\":\"End-to-end frame\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:1c4c010033a4beec67d91c7c12d3f812","key":71,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:1c4c010033a4beec67d91c7c12d3f812\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"Evaluates actual participants at one declared material composition boundary against their joint contract across outcome-changing state, authority, configuration, timing, failure and recovery combinations. Basis binds the exact declaration, actual implementations or exact admitted substitutes, Product/requirement/design law and interaction population. The manifold includes both sides, shared carriers, pre/postconditions, authority/ownership, ordering, state, configuration, failure, retry, recovery, translation and competing participants. Coordinates bind participant/version, interface/carrier revision, state, configuration, dependency, interaction case, input, output, failure and evidence. Evidence comprises exchanges, admitted carriers, transitions, contract verdicts, failures, retries, recovery, combinations and participant identities. Capability requires exercising/observing the seam, detecting substitution and varying every material interaction dimension.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":457,\"path\":\"standards/ASSURANCE.md\",\"quote\":\"| evaluation family | Do the actual participants at one declared material composition boundary satisfy their joint contract across the combinations of state, authority, configuration, timing, failure and recovery that can change the boundary result? |\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ASSURANCE.md#ASSURANCE%2F7.%20Product%20testing%20frame%20set%2FIntegration%20frame\",\"start_line\":457}],\"label\":\"Integration frame\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:9873a2fcf1a72b9c6d82964e88b5d0b2","key":72,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:9873a2fcf1a72b9c6d82964e88b5d0b2\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"Evaluates one module-owned law across material operator, calculation-regime, state, transition, public/private boundary-class and failure combinations. Basis includes the exact module boundary, accepted ontology/design, active declared carrier inventory, owned requirements/public contracts, implementation and module-bounded decidable oracle. The manifold includes public contracts, algebras, calculations, parsers, reducers, state machines, transitions, combinators, admission predicates, conservation laws, invariants, numerical boundaries and failures. Coordinates bind module/implementation revision, law, operator/function family, state, input/boundary class, expected relation, generated case, mutation and result. Evidence includes law-derived examples, equivalence classes, available finite exhaustive cases, properties/generation, metamorphic relations, calculation/algebra oracles, boundary cases and killed internal mutations. Capability requires an independently law-derived oracle, identifying bounded combinations and distinguishing violations from implementation restatement.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":481,\"path\":\"standards/ASSURANCE.md\",\"quote\":\"| evaluation family | Does one module-owned law hold across its material combinations of algebraic operator, calculation regime, state, transition, public or private boundary class, and failure case? |\\n| subject and basis | one exact module boundary, the accepted ontology and design, the active carrier inventory the design declares, module-owned requirements and public contracts, the implementation, and a module-bounded decidable oracle |\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ASSURANCE.md#ASSURANCE%2F7.%20Product%20testing%20frame%20set%2FUnit%20frame\",\"start_line\":480}],\"label\":\"Unit frame\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:9998e713a60bf1ac244a0e611d7a518a","key":73,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:9998e713a60bf1ac244a0e611d7a518a\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"A claim-relative index of the material combinations a frame can discriminate. It considers at least subject/claim congruence, independent dimension number/materiality, covered interaction strength, authoritative-path exactness, oracle independence/precision, realistic-fault/rival-path/historical-failure sensitivity, observability/reconstruction/reproducibility, and explicit residual combinations/invalidation. It is not inherently a scalar.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":526,\"path\":\"standards/ASSURANCE.md\",\"quote\":\"Testing value is indexed first by the material combinations a frame can\\ndiscriminate for its exact claim, not by test, assertion, file, line,\\nbranch, mock, snapshot or runner count (P2, P6). For one claim, the\\ntesting-value index considers at least:\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ASSURANCE.md#ASSURANCE%2F8.%20Combinatorial%20coverage%20and%20testing%20value\",\"start_line\":523}],\"label\":\"Testing-value index\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:3635e0d97a204bc786bfeff7cc2b76e4","key":74,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:3635e0d97a204bc786bfeff7cc2b76e4\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"Evaluation of two distinct finite subject-relative graphs: production closure over the exact runnable Product/configuration and transitive imports, exports, package paths, switches, registries, fallbacks, consumers, generated runtime artifacts, recovery and fresh-process reconstruction; and assurance/source closure over relied-on source consumers, fixtures, proof scripts, generators, mutations and assurance tools.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":594,\"path\":\"standards/ASSURANCE.md\",\"quote\":\"A successor passing does not prove the predecessor removed. Technical-debt\\nerasure evaluates two distinct, finite, subject-relative graphs (P3, P6):\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ASSURANCE.md#ASSURANCE%2F9.%20Legitimate%20path%20and%20technical-debt%20erasure\",\"start_line\":593}],\"label\":\"Technical-debt erasure\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:4a758d8b16a2d0014a7ecd1bc24c03f7","key":75,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:4a758d8b16a2d0014a7ecd1bc24c03f7\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"Distinct acquisition and evaluation relations: acquire actual owner-issued subjects through exact runnable owner surfaces, validators, projections, receipts or reconstruction relations, then evaluate with an independently contract-derived oracle.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":671,\"path\":\"standards/ASSURANCE.md\",\"quote\":\"Acquiring the assurance subject and evaluating it are distinct relations\\n(P6, P1). Where a\\nclaim depends on owner-issued Product, runtime, lifecycle, admission,\\nreplay or projection truth, the testing frame acquires that truth through\\nthe exact runnable owner surface, validator, projection, receipt or\\nreconstruction relation.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ASSURANCE.md#ASSURANCE%2F11.%20Assurance%20subject%20acquisition%20and%20evaluation\",\"start_line\":666}],\"label\":\"Assurance subject acquisition and evaluation\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:75d7ebdc57547aefb3f31ca6c91db8e4","key":76,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:75d7ebdc57547aefb3f31ca6c91db8e4\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"Return of a testing counterexample to its earliest supported causal frontier: causally minimal violated owner relations or seam coordinates under the declared causal relation, not log or clock order. Its four exclusive domain forms are unique locus, jointly established incomparable earliest loci whose combined violation is necessary, unresolved alternative frontiers, and an unbounded frontier represented by indeterminate.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":705,\"path\":\"standards/ASSURANCE.md\",\"quote\":\"A testing counterexample is returned to its earliest supported causal\\nfrontier on the declared path. The frontier holds the causally minimal\\nviolated owner relations or seam coordinates the evidence establishes;\\nearliest means minimal under the declared causal relation, not first in log\\nor clock order (P5, P6).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ASSURANCE.md#ASSURANCE%2F12.%20Counterexample%20localisation\",\"start_line\":701}],\"label\":\"Counterexample localisation\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:edbbabc8b2dc4636bae4930b21b2d9bb","key":77,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:edbbabc8b2dc4636bae4930b21b2d9bb\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[\"Selected by governing frame configuration or admitted work authority under the exact selected basis.\"],\"definition\":\"Composite refinement urn:stdo:reference-frame:end-to-end-interface-integration:v1, resolving in urn:stdo:bounded-context:reference-frame-evaluation owned by REFERENCE_FRAME. It relates public-boundary, design, operator, owner and proof evaluation to integration, end-to-end and user-acceptance frames. It asks whether one outcome remains constructable, understandable and correctly realised across its material interface chain with sufficient context and conserved meaning, authority and cause. Design subjects bind declared roles, functional paths, dependencies, configuration and capabilities; realisation subjects bind actual participants, callable selection, supported entry/exit and exact runnable artifact/install. Both bind an independent oracle, requirements/design, exact source/workspace checkpoint, contracts and finite cases. The manifold covers producers, consumers, transformations and effect owners, seam pre/postconditions, value/reference domains, lifecycle/time, context, mutable subject, refusals, observations and visible results. Coordinates distinguish Product, artifact/install, workspace, observation, invocation, candidate, admitted result and evidence, including revisions, domains, units, cardinality, ordering, empty/null/default meaning and validity intervals.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":752,\"path\":\"standards/ASSURANCE.md\",\"quote\":\"`urn:stdo:reference-frame:end-to-end-interface-integration:v1` is a\\ncomposite refinement whose identity resolves in\\n`urn:stdo:bounded-context:reference-frame-evaluation` (owned by\\nREFERENCE_FRAME) under the exact selected basis; its assurance law is\\nstated here. It relates the evaluation of public boundaries, design,\\noperators, owners and proof to the integration, end-to-end and\\nuser-acceptance frames of §7. Like the set, it is available and is\\nactivated only where the governing frame configuration or admitted work\\nauthority selects it. It adds no fifth testing type, role or\\nuniversal activation gate (P2, P3).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ASSURANCE.md#ASSURANCE%2F13.%20End-to-end%20interface%20integration%20frame\",\"start_line\":743}],\"label\":\"End-to-end interface integration refinement\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:548e95b2ad0b13be8c12ff0b8188144c","key":78,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:548e95b2ad0b13be8c12ff0b8188144c\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"Four distinct claims: contract sufficiency asks whether every participant can determine and perform its responsibility from declared interfaces/context; boundary congruence asks whether actual selected producers, transformations and consumers preserve domains, meanings, lifecycle and authority; path realisation asks whether the exact runnable subject uses the authoritative entry-to-outcome path; user usability asks whether the ordinary human, LLM or software caller obtains the outcome using only declared context, access and supported surfaces.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":778,\"path\":\"standards/ASSURANCE.md\",\"quote\":\"| contract sufficiency | Can each participant determine and perform its responsibility from the declared interface and the available context? Source-grounded design evaluation may establish this claim without an implemented runtime; unresolved realisability or actor-context questions stay explicit. |\\n| boundary congruence | Do the actual selected producers, transformations and consumers preserve the declared domains, meanings, lifecycle and authority? An actual-composition claim acquires both sides and their exchanges; design correspondence alone proves no implementation behaviour. |\\n| path realisation | Does the exact runnable subject use the authoritative entry-to-outcome path through its material state, effect and observation boundaries? Matching output through another path is insufficient. |\\n| user usability | Can the ordinary human, LLM or software caller obtain the selected outcome using only its declared context, access and supported surface? Internal success or validator-aware fixtures cannot establish this claim. |\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ASSURANCE.md#ASSURANCE%2F13.%20End-to-end%20interface%20integration%20frame%2FClaim%20boundaries\",\"start_line\":775}],\"label\":\"Interface refinement claims\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:fe7db12377fdd46a49a3d55fed08adb1","key":79,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:fe7db12377fdd46a49a3d55fed08adb1\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[\"Material computational composition or recurrence work.\"],\"definition\":\"Bounded composition of selected interface claims with evaluations of path operators, owners, reused foundations and proof, covering one complete producer-to-consumer path under DESIGN_MODULE computational-realisation and recurrence law. It binds fact establishment, every consumer, validity/invalidation, effects, retained alternatives and accumulated work, and evaluates equivalent computation across domain names without presuming semantic equivalence.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":888,\"path\":\"standards/ASSURANCE.md\",\"quote\":\"For material computational composition or recurrence work, the selected\\ninterface claims are composed with evaluations of the path's operators,\\nowners, reused foundations and proof, to evaluate one complete\\nproducer-to-consumer path under the design profile's computational\\nrealisation and recurrence law (DESIGN_MODULE). The evaluation binds fact\\nestablishment, each consumer, validity and invalidation, effects, retained\\nalternatives and accumulated work. It evaluates equivalent computation\\nacross different domain names without assuming semantic equivalence.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ASSURANCE.md#ASSURANCE%2F13.%20End-to-end%20interface%20integration%20frame%2FComputational%20whole-path%20evaluation\",\"start_line\":881}],\"label\":\"Computational whole-path evaluation\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:5a33a4d8c03287f415271883ababd0f6","key":80,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:5a33a4d8c03287f415271883ababd0f6\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[\"A new or materially changed realisation boundary is governed by a design profile.\"],\"definition\":\"Two directed evidence chains: semantic derivation from constitutional WHAT and owning requirements through accepted ontology, declared carriers, target design and domain/sequence/state evidence to implementation and module-derived tests, reconciliation/acceptance, promotion/design-method closure; and feedback from implementation/tests through evidence, counterexamples or falsification to affected ontology/design relations. Assertion and execution provenance remain distinct.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":946,\"path\":\"standards/ASSURANCE.md\",\"quote\":\"The first chain is semantic derivation. The second is evidence feedback\\nand cannot select or accept the affected semantic answer (P6). The two\\nchains are this member's instance of parallel derivation: expected results\\ncarry assertion provenance from the first chain and executions carry\\nexecution provenance from the second; agreement between them is\\ncompatible with a shared error, and disagreement requires diagnosis\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ASSURANCE.md#ASSURANCE%2F14.%20Design-to-module%20evidence%20route\",\"start_line\":941}],\"label\":\"Design-to-module evidence route\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:f36832f6941f8683b920fbd70d2f5ad7","key":81,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:f36832f6941f8683b920fbd70d2f5ad7\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[\"Unit tests under the design profile.\"],\"definition\":\"Module-owned proof lanes derived from realisation authority owned by DESIGN_MODULE and from module ownership evidence. Their authority is for module proof; Product UAT and acceptance meaning remain with Product authority.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1025,\"path\":\"standards/ASSURANCE.md\",\"quote\":\"Unit tests under the design profile are module-owned proof lanes. They\\nderive from module ownership evidence, not from code shape alone. A unit\\ntest should be traceable to (P6, P2):\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ASSURANCE.md#ASSURANCE%2F15.%20Module-derived%20unit%20tests\",\"start_line\":1023}],\"label\":\"Module-derived unit lane\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:32452eb024ac40cc77301d8270aacad9","key":82,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:32452eb024ac40cc77301d8270aacad9\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[\"A boundary is governed by the design profile.\"],\"definition\":\"Confirmation at the realisation boundary, before design-method closure, of the operational lifecycle of every designed module, function, application/runtime/plugin/public/data surface and published profile function or module. It consumes SPEC_METHOD §2 phases without redefining them; its checklist detects ambiguity about ultimate intended use and is neither a release plan nor a replacement for RELEASE.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1062,\"path\":\"standards/ASSURANCE.md\",\"quote\":\"Every designed module, function, application surface, runtime surface,\\nplugin surface, public interface, data surface, and published function or\\nmodule of a profile exists inside an operational lifecycle. Under the\\ndesign profile that lifecycle signal is confirmed at the realisation\\nboundary before design-method closure (P2, P6). The\\ncanonical operational lifecycle chain is SPEC_METHOD §2 Operational\\nlifecycle sufficiency; this section consumes that chain and does not\\nredefine its phases. The checklist is not a release plan and does not\\nreplace RELEASE; it is an ambiguity detector for ultimate intended use.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ASSURANCE.md#ASSURANCE%2F16.%20Module%20lifecycle%20confirmation\",\"start_line\":1054}],\"label\":\"Module lifecycle confirmation\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:8710247991b836d7b07fd776cf748e2c","key":83,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:8710247991b836d7b07fd776cf748e2c\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"Subject-described Tier 1 STDO Axiomatic Calculus for Governed Symbolic Systems, a_c: domain-specific and carrier-neutral, with stable identity urn:stdo:concept:axiomatic-calculus:a-c in urn:stdo:bounded-context:axiomatic-calculus. Its member owns position/scope, signature, record shapes, AC-001–AC-020, traversals/functor kinds, interpretation/models, three layers, calculus identity, application/import/exclusion boundaries and conformance obligations. It consumes FOUNDATIONS ontology and core results without redefining them; clauses identify their requiring P0–P6 principles. Its definitions do not depend on derivation-record layout, selected interpretation, carrier, provider, runtime or repository topology.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":14,\"path\":\"standards/AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS.md\",\"quote\":\"Tier 1. Owns the a_c theory in full: position and scope, the signature,\\nthe typed records, the laws AC-001 to AC-020, traversals and functor\\nkinds, interpretation and models, the three governed layers, the law of\\ncalculus identity, the application boundary, external imports, exclusions\\nand the conformance obligations of this member. Consumes the ontology of\\n[FOUNDATIONS §2](FOUNDATIONS.md) (subject, representation, interpretation,\\ncontext, object, claim, evidence, judgment, authority, residual, basis,\\nmaterial) and the core result algebra of\\n[FOUNDATIONS §4 Results](FOUNDATIONS.md#results); it states laws over\\nthose objects and defines none of them a second time. Each clause names\\nthe principle (P0 to P6) that requires it, as\\n[FOUNDATIONS §1](FOUNDATIONS.md#1-vocabulary-of-standing) requires.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS.md#AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS\",\"start_line\":3},{\"end_line\":25,\"path\":\"standards/AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS.md\",\"quote\":\"The STDO Axiomatic Calculus for Governed Symbolic Systems, written `a_c`,\\nis this method's domain-specific, carrier-neutral constitutional calculus\\nfor representing and relating governed symbolic systems. Its stable\\nconcept identity is `urn:stdo:concept:axiomatic-calculus:a-c`. This member\\nowns that concept in the bounded context\\n`urn:stdo:bounded-context:axiomatic-calculus`. Both identifiers are\\ndeclared identities and do not change with the carrier or the directory\\nthat publishes them (P3).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS.md#AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS%2F1.%20Position\",\"start_line\":18}],\"label\":\"Subject-described a_c calculus\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:7fd7c71247668ac4656ebb2663df6898","key":84,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:7fd7c71247668ac4656ebb2663df6898\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"An interpreted model a_c.X is downstream of a_c plus exact subject X. A carrier a_c.X.C encodes that model with an exact accepted semantic judgment J_X and exact carrier C. Calculus, interpreted model and encoded carrier have separate content identities and proof boundaries.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":57,\"path\":\"standards/AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS.md\",\"quote\":\"The calculus, an interpreted model and an encoded carrier are distinct\\ngoverned layers with separate content identities and proof boundaries\\n(§7). A layer becomes a released Product only through separately\\nauthorised Product acceptance and release. Neither interpretation nor\\nencoding can redefine the calculus (P6).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS.md#AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS%2F1.%20Position\",\"start_line\":53}],\"label\":\"Calculus, interpreted model and encoded carrier\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:3dab7b4ae60847a9b5f77b8991c041fa","key":85,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:3dab7b4ae60847a9b5f77b8991c041fa\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"Finite local derivation owners cover scoped identity/authority and bounded-context meaning in FOUNDATIONS §2; bounded probabilistic construction in P0, Work boundary and ACTIVATION §1; delegation/candidate production/independent assessment in ACTIVATION §1 and EVALUATION §3; ambiguity/human adjudication/hard stops in ACTIVATION §4; exact basis, authority, evidence/verdict separation and results in RF-005–007 and FOUNDATIONS; constitutional derivation/re-entry in SPEC_METHOD §§1,4; closure/projection/residual/capability law in REFERENCE_FRAME §3; singular release authority in SPEC_METHOD §6 and PRODUCT_DEFINITION §4. AxiomaticCalculusBasis resolves these to immutable absolute clause addresses in derivation_basis.principle_refs. Generic F_D, F_P and F_H originate here, independently of equal-spelled runtime/profile/application terms.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":63,\"path\":\"standards/AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS.md\",\"quote\":\"The calculus specialises the governing commitments declared in this\\npackage. Its derivation basis is the following finite set of current local\\nowners, resolved to exact clauses by the identity record of §8 (P6):\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS.md#AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS%2F1.%20Position%2FDerivation%20provenance\",\"start_line\":61}],\"label\":\"Calculus derivation basis\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:90c3d9660d33d96fa0e0932fb3cdc162","key":86,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:90c3d9660d33d96fa0e0932fb3cdc162\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"Material family F9's premise-to-rule account distinguishes derived consequences from owner-selected choices. Instance premises, not supplied by commitments, are: a finite model represents governed objects/relations/constraints/residuals/traversals/transformations/judgments; exact subject, interpreted model and possible carrier have separate identities; some predicates are mechanical and others need bounded probabilistic construction or explicit human adjudication. P1, P2, P3, P4a and P6 are marked independent; P0 recovered; P4b derived from P0/P2; P5 derived from P0/P6. Nineteen rows bind these premises to position, scope, signature, identity/typing, authority/basis, results, latitude, residuals, closure/projection, overlay, transformation, judgment separation, traversal/composition, interpretation, layers, identity issuance, application/import boundaries, constraint surfaces and qualification.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":158,\"path\":\"standards/AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS.md\",\"quote\":\"This member is material family F9, the `a_c` calculus. The table below\\nshows which of its rules follow from which premises, in the format of\\n[FOUNDATIONS §3 Foundation to law](FOUNDATIONS.md#foundation-to-law),\\nwhich also states the standing of the consequences. Instance premises,\\nwhich the commitments do not supply:\\n\\n- (i) a governed symbolic system is represented by a finite model whose\\n  records stand for its objects, relations, constraints, residuals,\\n  traversals, transformations and judgments;\\n- (ii) a model is interpreted from an exact subject and may be encoded in\\n  a carrier, and subject, model and carrier are separately identified;\\n- (iii) some predicates over a model are decided mechanically, and others\\n  need bounded probabilistic construction or explicit human adjudication.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS.md#AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS%2F1.%20Position%2FFoundation%20to%20law\",\"start_line\":146}],\"label\":\"Foundation-to-law account\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:756e46fcb645468c0a61b7d1af496ff1","key":87,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:756e46fcb645468c0a61b7d1af496ff1\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"Sigma = (RecordKind, Sort, RelationKind, ConstraintKind, ResidualKind, FunctorKind, JudgmentKind, StopKind). RecordKind_ac fixes eight urn:stdo:concept:axiomatic-calculus:record-kind: identities ending semantic-object, typed-relation, constraint, latitude, residual, traversal, transformation and judgment. Each signature member is a finite closed identity set for one model family. The signature specifies fields/value domains, reference domains/cardinalities, relation endpoint sorts, constraint subject/predicate domains, residual subject/uncertainty/consequence/re-entry domains, judgment input/output/evidence/stop contracts and permitted traversal functor kinds.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":228,\"path\":\"standards/AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS.md\",\"quote\":\"Sigma = (\\n  RecordKind,\\n  Sort,\\n  RelationKind,\\n  ConstraintKind,\\n  ResidualKind,\\n  FunctorKind,\\n  JudgmentKind,\\n  StopKind\\n)\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS.md#AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS%2F2.%20Signature\",\"start_line\":219}],\"label\":\"Subject a_c signature\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:d7d4d3087eb8ab6376c885fc78a46108","key":88,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:d7d4d3087eb8ab6376c885fc78a46108\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"M_b = (b, I, O, E, C, L, X, V, T, J), with exact basis b, closed identity universe I and finite populations for semantic objects, directed relations, constraints, latitude, residuals, traversals, transformations and judgments. Population_M is total over the eight core kinds. Local_M is their disjoint union; I = Local_M disjoint_union External_M. RefDomain_Sigma(record_kind, field) yields cardinality, allowed local kinds, semantic-object sorts, external target kinds and required basis relation.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":302,\"path\":\"standards/AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS.md\",\"quote\":\"`Population_M` is a total function over `RecordKind_ac`. Every population\\nis finite, every fundamental record belongs to exactly one population, and\\nrecord identities are unique across their disjoint union. Let `Local_M` be\\nthat union. Then `I = Local_M disjoint_union External_M`, where every\\nmember of `External_M` is admitted only through one signature-declared\\nexternal reference domain and exact resolution relation. A hidden record,\\nan unpopulated extra record family, an identity occurring in two\\npopulations, or an identity in `I` with neither one local record nor one\\nlawful external resolution refuses the model. A population may be empty\\nonly when the selected signature does not require a member of that record\\nkind (P3, P5).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS.md#AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS%2F2.%20Signature\",\"start_line\":292}],\"label\":\"Subject a_c model\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:a581786e372e2577624fc3ed9d0583a0","key":89,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:a581786e372e2577624fc3ed9d0583a0\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"SemanticObject has exactly id, sort, context, owner, scope, basis and value. id/sort/context/owner/basis are identities; scope is the closed governed domain; value is sort-defined carrier-neutral content or an exact-content reference. It carries a FOUNDATIONS Object, with scoped identity in id/owner/sort and boundary in scope.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":354,\"path\":\"standards/AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS.md\",\"quote\":\"SemanticObject = {\\n  id,\\n  sort,\\n  context,\\n  owner,\\n  scope,\\n  basis,\\n  value\\n}\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS.md#AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS%2F3.%20Typed%20records%2FSemantic%20object\",\"start_line\":346}],\"label\":\"SemanticObject record\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:9d8d43c934e9fdbe3d228917333e3d48","key":90,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:9d8d43c934e9fdbe3d228917333e3d48\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"TypedRelation has exactly id, kind, source, target, context, owner, scope, basis and qualifiers. Endpoints resolve into I; qualifiers is a closed kind-specific record carrying required direction, cardinality, preservation, loss, inverse, invalidation or other signature-defined semantics.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":378,\"path\":\"standards/AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS.md\",\"quote\":\"TypedRelation = {\\n  id,\\n  kind,\\n  source,\\n  target,\\n  context,\\n  owner,\\n  scope,\\n  basis,\\n  qualifiers\\n}\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS.md#AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS%2F3.%20Typed%20records%2FTyped%20relation\",\"start_line\":368}],\"label\":\"TypedRelation record\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:aca1e4de8dbbb05752a7c83155ab6025","key":91,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:aca1e4de8dbbb05752a7c83155ab6025\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"Constraint has exactly id, kind, applies_to, predicate, context, owner, scope, basis, judgment_kind, latitude_ref and refusal. Its kind and judgment_kind resolve declared ConstraintKind and JudgmentKind; the owning signature supplies predicate language and judgment semantics.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":403,\"path\":\"standards/AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS.md\",\"quote\":\"Constraint = {\\n  id,\\n  kind,\\n  applies_to,\\n  predicate,\\n  context,\\n  owner,\\n  scope,\\n  basis,\\n  judgment_kind,\\n  latitude_ref,\\n  refusal\\n}\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS.md#AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS%2F3.%20Typed%20records%2FConstraint\",\"start_line\":391}],\"label\":\"Constraint record\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:d5f04a0892164371ab84d6dfd38ae088","key":92,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:d5f04a0892164371ab84d6dfd38ae088\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"Explicit permission set within a constraint boundary, represented by Latitude with id, applies_to, allowed_variation, forbidden_variation, context, owner, scope, basis and invalidation.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":427,\"path\":\"standards/AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS.md\",\"quote\":\"Latitude = {\\n  id,\\n  applies_to,\\n  allowed_variation,\\n  forbidden_variation,\\n  context,\\n  owner,\\n  scope,\\n  basis,\\n  invalidation\\n}\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS.md#AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS%2F3.%20Typed%20records%2FLatitude\",\"start_line\":417}],\"label\":\"Latitude record\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:5e6bfac5ccaaebc55f824ebe3d10283c","key":93,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:5e6bfac5ccaaebc55f824ebe3d10283c\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"First-class model uncertainty carrying FOUNDATIONS Residual, with fields id, subject, kind, uncertainty, consequence, context, owner, scope, basis, re_entry and invalidation. Its declared ResidualKind and lawful subject, uncertainty, consequence, re-entry and invalidation domains belong to the signature.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":453,\"path\":\"standards/AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS.md\",\"quote\":\"Residual = {\\n  id,\\n  subject,\\n  kind,\\n  uncertainty,\\n  consequence,\\n  context,\\n  owner,\\n  scope,\\n  basis,\\n  re_entry,\\n  invalidation\\n}\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS.md#AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS%2F3.%20Typed%20records%2FResidual\",\"start_line\":441}],\"label\":\"Residual record\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:5dd095b251a98fbf2b0a7ece590700f8","key":94,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:5dd095b251a98fbf2b0a7ece590700f8\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"Subject-described constraint judgments and operation outcomes map to the FOUNDATIONS core values satisfied, falsified, indeterminate, out_of_frame and invalid_basis without raising standing. A refinement maps each value to exactly one core value. Operation stops include hold, gap, refusal(constraint) and refusal(basis), distinguished by cause and predicate.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":545,\"path\":\"standards/AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS.md\",\"quote\":\"Each constraint names its governed subject, predicate, judgment kind,\\nlatitude and refusal (§3, Constraint). The judgment of a constraint\\nreturns one value of the core result algebra of\\n[FOUNDATIONS §4 Results](FOUNDATIONS.md#results), directly or through a\\nrefinement that the owning signature declares and that maps each of its\\nvalues to exactly one core value. Under the no-coercion rule of\\nFOUNDATIONS §4 Results, a failed, missing, indeterminate, out-of-scope or\\ninvalid-basis result of a constraint follows that algebra and is never\\ncoerced to satisfied (P5, P6). The\\ncore values, the rule that no mapping raises a result's standing and the\\nboundary among out_of_frame, indeterminate and an evaluation that was not\\nperformed are FOUNDATIONS §4 Results'. This law applies them to the\\njudgment of a constraint and to the outcomes of the operations of this\\nmember, and adds no core value.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS.md#AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS%2F4.%20Fundamental%20laws%2FAC-007%20Constraint%20and%20refusal\",\"start_line\":532}],\"label\":\"Subject-described core results and stops\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:18a9318a44e9f56d1d45b6db418ee071","key":95,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:18a9318a44e9f56d1d45b6db418ee071\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[\"Seed set, dependency relation family, required-edge semantics, basis and scope are exact; the fixed point is finite and unique.\"],\"definition\":\"Material closure is closure_R(M, Z) = lfp(lambda Q: Z union required_R(M, Q)), the least lawful record closure under the exact dependency family R.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":651,\"path\":\"standards/AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS.md\",\"quote\":\"closure_R(M, Z) = lfp(lambda Q: Z union required_R(M, Q))\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS.md#AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS%2F4.%20Fundamental%20laws%2FAC-010%20Material%20closure\",\"start_line\":651}],\"label\":\"Material closure operation\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:ef0ffce7253e996c7f40fd2fb817d10e","key":96,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:ef0ffce7253e996c7f40fd2fb817d10e\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"A meaning-preserving model view: project(M, Z, R) returns (M_Z, Boundary_Z), gap or refusal. M_Z contains the material closure; Boundary_Z records excluded, external, unresolved, translated and invalidation-sensitive seams.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":676,\"path\":\"standards/AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS.md\",\"quote\":\"`M_Z` contains the material closure of `Z`, so a projection's `gap` or\\n`refusal` is that of the closure it contains or of the model it acts on:\\n`gap` or `refusal(basis)` (AC-007). `Boundary_Z` records excluded,\\nexternal, unresolved, translated and invalidation-sensitive seams.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS.md#AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS%2F4.%20Fundamental%20laws%2FAC-011%20Projection\",\"start_line\":673}],\"label\":\"Model projection\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:af35b2208105298937667271bdb8b937","key":97,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:af35b2208105298937667271bdb8b937\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"Addition of explicit records to declared Population_M families of a basis model without mutating that basis.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":688,\"path\":\"standards/AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS.md\",\"quote\":\"An overlay adds explicit records to one or more declared `Population_M`\\nfamilies of a basis model. It does not mutate the basis.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS.md#AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS%2F4.%20Fundamental%20laws%2FAC-012%20Overlay\",\"start_line\":687}],\"label\":\"Model overlay\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:aea0ac1826c9dc379a8b046db93f8e1d","key":98,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:aea0ac1826c9dc379a8b046db93f8e1d\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"An operation-bearing specialisation of one exact traversal v. Its record t contains id, traversal, domain_model, codomain_model, context, owner, scope, basis, operation_authority, preconditions, preservation_relation, preserved, introduced, removed, external_preserved, external_introduced, external_removed, external_resolution_witnesses, residuals, evidence, provenance, stop_states, invalidation and re_entry. Its application T[t](M_b, inputs) returns a proposed successor M_b_prime*, hold, gap or refusal; the input remains unchanged.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":696,\"path\":\"standards/AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS.md\",\"quote\":\"A transformation is an operation-bearing specialisation of one exact\\ntraversal record `v` (§5). Its record is (P4b, P3):\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS.md#AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS%2F4.%20Fundamental%20laws%2FAC-013%20Transformation\",\"start_line\":695},{\"end_line\":874,\"path\":\"standards/AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS.md\",\"quote\":\"The exact transformation identity `t` declares every mutation it may\\nperform. The input model remains unchanged; `M_b_prime*` is a proposed\\nsuccessor. A proposed successor does not accept or admit itself (P6). The\\nstops `hold`, `gap` and `refusal` take their core values under AC-007 by\\ntheir causes.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS.md#AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS%2F4.%20Fundamental%20laws%2FAC-013%20Transformation\",\"start_line\":870}],\"label\":\"Subject transformation record and operation\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:a0e0dad70524c698d0bec0c1bea7fe41","key":99,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:a0e0dad70524c698d0bec0c1bea7fe41\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"A signature-supplied model coordinate, not a ninth record family: Resolution_M(x) = {external_identity, reference_domain, external_target_kind, resolved_target_identity, basis_relation, resolution_basis, evidence_identity}. Every field is exact and identity-bearing; ResolutionSet_M contains one such tuple for each External_M identity. ExternalResolutionPreservationWitness contains external_resolution, domain_model, codomain_model, domain_resolution, codomain_resolution, decision equal and evidence.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":761,\"path\":\"standards/AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS.md\",\"quote\":\"`Resolution_M` is a model coordinate supplied by the signature-declared\\nexternal reference relation, not a ninth fundamental record family. Every\\nfield is identity-bearing and exact. One external identity has exactly one\\nresolution tuple in one model; a missing, ambiguous or extra tuple refuses\\n(P3).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS.md#AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS%2F4.%20Fundamental%20laws%2FAC-013%20Transformation\",\"start_line\":757}],\"label\":\"External resolution coordinate and preservation witness\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:0430c525dee26281ae235ebacc9459ab","key":100,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:0430c525dee26281ae235ebacc9459ab\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"FOUNDATIONS Judgment carried as a model record pointing to an unchanged subject, with id, kind, subject, subject_digest, context, owner, scope, basis, evaluator, authority, decision, evidence, provenance and decided_at.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":900,\"path\":\"standards/AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS.md\",\"quote\":\"Judgment = {\\n  id,\\n  kind,\\n  subject,\\n  subject_digest,\\n  context,\\n  owner,\\n  scope,\\n  basis,\\n  evaluator,\\n  authority,\\n  decision,\\n  evidence,\\n  provenance,\\n  decided_at\\n}\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS.md#AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS%2F4.%20Fundamental%20laws%2FAC-014%20Judgment%20separation\",\"start_line\":885}],\"label\":\"Subject Judgment record\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:ad180a0b7eeeab223c0c1434f7a93e6a","key":101,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:ad180a0b7eeeab223c0c1434f7a93e6a\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"This member's traversal is a typed contract with id, domain, codomain, context, owner, scope, basis, preconditions, postconditions, authority, evidence, provenance and stop_states.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":926,\"path\":\"standards/AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS.md\",\"quote\":\"v = {\\n  id,\\n  domain,\\n  codomain,\\n  context,\\n  owner,\\n  scope,\\n  basis,\\n  preconditions,\\n  postconditions,\\n  authority,\\n  evidence,\\n  provenance,\\n  stop_states\\n}\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS.md#AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS%2F5.%20Traversals%20and%20functor%20kinds\",\"start_line\":912}],\"label\":\"Traversal contract\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:cc99c053f518c955c093894ab174b704","key":102,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:cc99c053f518c955c093894ab174b704\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"F_D, urn:stdo:concept:axiomatic-calculus:f-d, classifies deterministic evaluation or proof over declared properties. It returns a judgment without performing the domain construction judged.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":937,\"path\":\"standards/AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS.md\",\"quote\":\"F_D = urn:stdo:concept:axiomatic-calculus:f-d\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS.md#AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS%2F5.%20Traversals%20and%20functor%20kinds\",\"start_line\":937},{\"end_line\":975,\"path\":\"standards/AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS.md\",\"quote\":\"- `F_D` classifies deterministic evaluation or proof over declared\\n  properties. It returns a judgment and does not perform the domain\\n  construction being judged (P6).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS.md#AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS%2F5.%20Traversals%20and%20functor%20kinds\",\"start_line\":973}],\"label\":\"F_D\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:a264d9c6baa9d13219958780b476cbb9","key":103,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:a264d9c6baa9d13219958780b476cbb9\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"F_P, urn:stdo:concept:axiomatic-calculus:f-p, classifies bounded probabilistic interpretation, construction or proposal under an exact traversal contract. Usefulness or repeatability confers no semantic, admission, acceptance or closure authority on its result.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":938,\"path\":\"standards/AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS.md\",\"quote\":\"F_P = urn:stdo:concept:axiomatic-calculus:f-p\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS.md#AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS%2F5.%20Traversals%20and%20functor%20kinds\",\"start_line\":938},{\"end_line\":979,\"path\":\"standards/AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS.md\",\"quote\":\"- `F_P` classifies bounded probabilistic interpretation, construction or\\n  proposal under an exact traversal contract. Its result has no semantic,\\n  admission, acceptance or closure authority merely because it is useful\\n  or repeatable (P6, P0; instance premise (iii) of §1 Foundation to law).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS.md#AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS%2F5.%20Traversals%20and%20functor%20kinds\",\"start_line\":976}],\"label\":\"F_P\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:de2cfd132ecf92f2b6817d00d756fdd7","key":104,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:de2cfd132ecf92f2b6817d00d756fdd7\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"F_H, urn:stdo:concept:axiomatic-calculus:f-h, classifies explicit human adjudication under exact identity, authority grant, subject, basis and decision contract. Human presence grants no ambient authority.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":939,\"path\":\"standards/AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS.md\",\"quote\":\"F_H = urn:stdo:concept:axiomatic-calculus:f-h\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS.md#AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS%2F5.%20Traversals%20and%20functor%20kinds\",\"start_line\":939},{\"end_line\":982,\"path\":\"standards/AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS.md\",\"quote\":\"- `F_H` classifies explicit human adjudication under an exact identity,\\n  authority grant, subject, basis and decision contract. Human presence\\n  grants no ambient authority (P6).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS.md#AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS%2F5.%20Traversals%20and%20functor%20kinds\",\"start_line\":980}],\"label\":\"F_H\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:0a8a14f789f22c87c4dd9c92b92241f1","key":105,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:0a8a14f789f22c87c4dd9c92b92241f1\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"F_K[v](X_v) -> Y_v | Omega_v denotes one functor kind applied under one exact traversal identity to its typed input domain, yielding its typed result domain or a value of its closed stop algebra. Omega_v refines the core result algebra without adding a core value.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":952,\"path\":\"standards/AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS.md\",\"quote\":\"where `F_K` is one functor kind, `v` is one exact traversal identity,\\n`X_v` and `Y_v` are its typed input and result domains, and `Omega_v` is\\nits closed stop algebra. `Omega_v` is a refinement of the core result\\nalgebra of [FOUNDATIONS §4 Results](FOUNDATIONS.md#results): it adds no\\ncore value\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS.md#AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS%2F5.%20Traversals%20and%20functor%20kinds\",\"start_line\":948}],\"label\":\"Functor application and stop domain\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:7f4b90a2ef961e06be982fbd06f043b5","key":106,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:7f4b90a2ef961e06be982fbd06f043b5\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"Typed composition orders a first traversal v and a second traversal w, written F_K2[w] compose F_K1[v], while retaining their separate contracts and results.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1018,\"path\":\"standards/AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS.md\",\"quote\":\"Composition retains both traversal identities, intermediate results,\\njudgments, evidence, authority, provenance and stop states.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS.md#AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS%2F5.%20Traversals%20and%20functor%20kinds%2FAC-016%20Typed%20composition\",\"start_line\":1017}],\"label\":\"Typed composition\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:a6456d0051fb8cb6e9e734fa4c1a72ce","key":107,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:a6456d0051fb8cb6e9e734fa4c1a72ce\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"Interpret_a_c(subject_basis, signature, interpretation_contract) applies a_c to one exact subject and yields a proposed M_subject* or hold, gap or refusal. The star denotes absence of the applicable semantic acceptance judgment; stops take their cause-dependent core values under AC-007.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1038,\"path\":\"standards/AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS.md\",\"quote\":\"Interpret_a_c(subject_basis, signature, interpretation_contract)\\n  -> M_subject* | hold | gap | refusal\\n```\\n\\nThe stops `hold`, `gap` and `refusal` take their core values under AC-007\\nby their causes. The trailing `*` marks a proposed model that has not\\nreceived the\\napplicable semantic acceptance judgment.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS.md#AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS%2F6.%20Interpretation%20and%20models\",\"start_line\":1029}],\"label\":\"Exact subject interpretation\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:9740b41ae788ab183f1158a8c17b9c96","key":108,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:9740b41ae788ab183f1158a8c17b9c96\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"Structural conformance covers closed syntax, types, identities, references, bases and mechanically decidable predicates. Semantic fidelity covers interpretation meaning and materiality. Semantic acceptance is a separately recorded authority judgment.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1075,\"path\":\"standards/AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS.md\",\"quote\":\"structural conformance of a model covers its closed syntax, types,\\nidentities, references, bases and mechanically decidable predicates, and\\nthe semantic fidelity of an interpretation covers its meaning and\\nmateriality (P1, P6).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS.md#AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS%2F6.%20Interpretation%20and%20models%2FAC-018%20Structural%20and%20semantic%20separation\",\"start_line\":1072},{\"end_line\":1056,\"path\":\"standards/AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS.md\",\"quote\":\"Semantic acceptance remains a separately recorded authority judgment (P6,\\nP1).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS.md#AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS%2F6.%20Interpretation%20and%20models\",\"start_line\":1055}],\"label\":\"Structural, semantic and acceptance assessments\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:67c220e7b0925f26c733270e399c4399","key":109,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:67c220e7b0925f26c733270e399c4399\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"M_b satisfies a_c[Sigma] names a valid-model claim under an exact signature and calculus basis, subject to AC-019's necessary conditions.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1080,\"path\":\"standards/AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS.md\",\"quote\":\"A model `M_b` is a valid model of `a_c` under signature `Sigma`, written\\n`M_b satisfies a_c[Sigma]`, only when (P6, P1):\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS.md#AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS%2F6.%20Interpretation%20and%20models%2FAC-019%20Valid%20model\",\"start_line\":1079}],\"label\":\"Valid model claim\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:eae05dbe7bea9721fd387b0353bf6ffd","key":110,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:eae05dbe7bea9721fd387b0353bf6ffd\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"a_c is the pure calculus layer.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1102,\"path\":\"standards/AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS.md\",\"quote\":\"a_c       = the pure calculus\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS.md#AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS%2F7.%20Layers\",\"start_line\":1102}],\"label\":\"a_c\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:ef0db177bf46d1cab0da9336e9c1ccd2","key":111,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:ef0db177bf46d1cab0da9336e9c1ccd2\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"a_c.X is subject X interpreted as a model of a_c. Acceptance is external to its unchanged content identity; an accepted interpretation is the pair (a_c.X, J_X).\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1103,\"path\":\"standards/AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS.md\",\"quote\":\"a_c.X     = subject X interpreted as a model of a_c\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS.md#AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS%2F7.%20Layers\",\"start_line\":1103},{\"end_line\":1227,\"path\":\"standards/AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS.md\",\"quote\":\"The accepted\\ninterpretation is the pair `(a_c.X, J_X)` where `J_X` is the applicable\\naccepted judgment.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS.md#AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS%2F8.%20Calculus%20identity\",\"start_line\":1225}],\"label\":\"a_c.X\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:6051ed012cfd01b86ac5f4b8f7d062f6","key":112,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:6051ed012cfd01b86ac5f4b8f7d062f6\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"a_c.X.C is the accepted model encoded in carrier C. G_C denotes encoded bytes; J_X is external semantic acceptance over unchanged M_X; D_C is deterministic carrier admission under v_carrier_admission using G_C, Profile_C and CarrierBasis_C, over unchanged carrier bytes. The admitted encoding evidence is the exact triple (G_C, J_X, D_C).\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1114,\"path\":\"standards/AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS.md\",\"quote\":\"M_X = Interpret_a_c(X)\\nJ_X = Accept_X(M_X) -> accepted | refuse\\nG_C = Encode_C(M_X, J_X) where J_X = accepted\\nD_C = F_D[v_carrier_admission](G_C, Profile_C, CarrierBasis_C)\\n      -> admitted | refuse\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS.md#AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS%2F7.%20Layers\",\"start_line\":1110},{\"end_line\":1123,\"path\":\"standards/AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS.md\",\"quote\":\"`D_C` is a judgment over unchanged carrier bytes; it is not a\\ntransformed carrier. The admitted encoding evidence relation is the exact\\ntriple `(G_C, J_X, D_C)`; neither judgment enters the identity of its\\nsubject (P6, P3).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS.md#AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS%2F7.%20Layers\",\"start_line\":1120}],\"label\":\"a_c.X.C and encoding evidence\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:c875cd254042a164528403012c2ce30f","key":113,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:c875cd254042a164528403012c2ce30f\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"AxiomaticCalculusBasis is an external, post-publication record distinguishing the stable calculus concept from an immutable edition. It binds governing premise clauses through derivation_basis and the published member through publication_basis within one exact immutable package.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1155,\"path\":\"standards/AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS.md\",\"quote\":\"The stable concept identity does not identify one immutable calculus\\nedition. An exact released calculus basis is an external record created\\nafter the publication bytes exist. It binds the governing premise clauses\\nand the published calculus member as distinct roles inside one exact\\nimmutable package (P3, P6):\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS.md#AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS%2F8.%20Calculus%20identity\",\"start_line\":1151}],\"label\":\"AxiomaticCalculusBasis\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:61261422be28ee2eb8577411fd931eb7","key":114,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:61261422be28ee2eb8577411fd931eb7\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"An application binding is an external typed import, translation or specialisation of an a_c concept declared under the application's own exact authority, context, basis, scope, preservation, loss, refusal and invalidation law.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1277,\"path\":\"standards/AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS.md\",\"quote\":\"An application may declare a typed import, translation or specialisation\\nof an `a_c` concept under that application's own exact authority, context,\\nbasis, scope, preservation, loss, refusal and invalidation law. Such a\\nrelation is external to the calculus.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS.md#AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS%2F9.%20Application%20boundary%2C%20imports%20and%20exclusions%2FExternal%20imports%20and%20specialisations\",\"start_line\":1274}],\"label\":\"External application binding\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:62a4645dab80b6d4b815a54e56dda0f7","key":115,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:62a4645dab80b6d4b815a54e56dda0f7\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"A constraint surface is a derived task view specifying a declared subject and work boundary's objects and meanings, predicates and dependencies, admissible operations, required results, authority, evidence, permitted freedom and unresolved conditions. It bounds work without prescribing internal strategy beyond those obligations and supports recovery of task constraints within finite attention.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1289,\"path\":\"standards/AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS.md\",\"quote\":\"A constraint surface states, for a declared subject and work boundary,\\nthe obligations and the permitted freedom of the work: its objects and\\ntheir meanings, the predicates and dependencies that bear on it, the\\nadmissible operations, the required results, the authority, the evidence\\nand the conditions still unresolved. It constrains the work without\\nprescribing the worker's internal solution strategy beyond those\\nobligations (P2, P6).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS.md#AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS%2F9.%20Application%20boundary%2C%20imports%20and%20exclusions%2FConstraint%20surfaces\",\"start_line\":1283}],\"label\":\"Constraint surface\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:f2c25849cc6b1cd3bcf28e04dd63d98c","key":116,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:f2c25849cc6b1cd3bcf28e04dd63d98c\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"Calculus review and qualification evaluate explicitly bounded claims about the member, including its signature, laws, identities, references, conservation properties and absence of hidden application dependencies.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1386,\"path\":\"standards/AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS.md\",\"quote\":\"Review and qualification of this member cover at least (P6):\\n\\n1. closed signature, `RecordKind_ac`, population, field, value-domain and\\n   reference-domain definitions;\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS.md#AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS%2F10.%20Conformance%20obligations\",\"start_line\":1383}],\"label\":\"Calculus qualification\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:41bf874a29ce16378405f71ab8c8c333","key":117,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:41bf874a29ce16378405f71ab8c8c333\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"CONFORMANCE is a Tier 2 catalogue importing method rules for shared owners and consumers without defining a competing result algebra. A discriminator is a situation whose expected distinction separates a conforming application from a defective one. A case names subject, mechanism and expected distinction; a separate execution record binds exact tested subject, basis, acquired context, observations, assessor and result.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":13,\"path\":\"standards/CONFORMANCE.md\",\"quote\":\"Tier 2. Defines conformance cases for the method's shared owners and their\\nconsumers. A discriminator is a situation whose expected distinction\\nseparates a conforming application from a defective one. Each expectation\\nand its deciding local owner are stated here; this member imports the\\nmethod's rules and defines no competing result algebra.\\n\\nA case names its subject, mechanism and expected distinction. An execution\\nrecord separately binds the exact tested subject, basis, acquired context,\\nobservations, assessor and result.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/CONFORMANCE.md#CONFORMANCE\",\"start_line\":3}],\"label\":\"Conformance catalogue and cases\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:ab6137fc418fad31d70ce554031e1867","key":118,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:ab6137fc418fad31d70ce554031e1867\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"The named core values are satisfied, falsified, indeterminate, out_of_frame and invalid_basis. CONFORMANCE imports them from FOUNDATIONS. Its re_enter, re_entry_requested(authority), not_effected and completion_unknown are ACTIVATION-defined refinements mapped into that core. Non-performance has no result.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":31,\"path\":\"standards/CONFORMANCE.md\",\"quote\":\"Result values. The values `satisfied`, `falsified`, `indeterminate`,\\n`out_of_frame` and `invalid_basis` named in this member are core values of\\n[FOUNDATIONS §4 Results](FOUNDATIONS.md#results). The values `re_enter`,\\n`re_entry_requested(authority)`, `not_effected` and `completion_unknown`\\nare refinements that\\n[ACTIVATION §3](ACTIVATION.md#3-step-results-and-disposition) defines and\\nmaps into that core. This member defines no result value\\n(P5, P6).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/CONFORMANCE.md#CONFORMANCE\",\"start_line\":24}],\"label\":\"Imported conformance result domains\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:3030c011fcddc60e3c15f2b18a635b9c","key":119,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:3030c011fcddc60e3c15f2b18a635b9c\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"Counterexample cases C-01 through C-12 identify failure mechanisms and local rules expected to distinguish them; they are assessment designs rather than reports of observed failures or passes.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":36,\"path\":\"standards/CONFORMANCE.md\",\"quote\":\"These cases identify failure mechanisms and the local rules that must\\ndistinguish them.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/CONFORMANCE.md#CONFORMANCE%2F1.%20Counterexample%20cases\",\"start_line\":35}],\"label\":\"Counterexample cases\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:3b64cf3c4b6500bf2f4c5566de937a70","key":120,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:3b64cf3c4b6500bf2f4c5566de937a70\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"Construction trials T-01 through T-08 test bounded construction, ambiguity, composition, failure conservation, recovery, requirement change, defective acceptance and broader sourced decision work.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":57,\"path\":\"standards/CONFORMANCE.md\",\"quote\":\"| T-01 Context cap and decomposition | required basis exceeds one actor's declared cap; repeat with tighter caps and a coupled case that cannot fit | refinement preserves the outer contract under independent assessment; the cannot-fit case returns out_of_frame or a lawful escalation, never omission |\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/CONFORMANCE.md#CONFORMANCE%2F2.%20Construction%20trials\",\"start_line\":57}],\"label\":\"Construction trials\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:1feeffc1b115acff77fce3a56823b82e","key":121,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:1feeffc1b115acff77fce3a56823b82e\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"R-01 and R-02 test fresh-context recovery of governing relations from the corpus, including matched comparisons when claimed and operation without validator folklore, author memory or whole-corpus loading.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":79,\"path\":\"standards/CONFORMANCE.md\",\"quote\":\"| R-02 No private knowledge | the same with validator folklore, author memory and whole-corpus loading withheld | the activation still succeeds or returns out_of_frame truthfully |\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/CONFORMANCE.md#CONFORMANCE%2F3.%20Recoverability\",\"start_line\":79}],\"label\":\"Recoverability cases\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:d61f2a51196c61efb27445373af99579","key":122,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:d61f2a51196c61efb27445373af99579\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"CD construction-discriminator cases exercise configurations, executor bindings and workspace recovery through actual use. AR assurance-relation cases exercise weak assertions, insufficient observations, shared error and change selection.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":91,\"path\":\"standards/CONFORMANCE.md\",\"quote\":\"A case here is\\nnamed CD (construction discriminator); the numbers in brackets are those of the\\ndiscriminators it exercises.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/CONFORMANCE.md#CONFORMANCE%2F4.%20Cases%20for%20method%20discriminators\",\"start_line\":89},{\"end_line\":110,\"path\":\"standards/CONFORMANCE.md\",\"quote\":\"The four cases below carry them; a case here is named AR (assurance\\nrelation). Each applicable case requires its own exact execution and assessment\\nrecord; no run or result is asserted by this catalogue.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/CONFORMANCE.md#CONFORMANCE%2F4.%20Cases%20for%20method%20discriminators\",\"start_line\":108}],\"label\":\"Construction-discriminator and assurance-relation cases\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:303a9298cdaede2eb7861c085d6b6788","key":123,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:303a9298cdaede2eb7861c085d6b6788\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"Discriminator coverage associates each situation and expected distinction with local owning sections and checks. L-n denotes a qualified reviewer's reasoned textual review without execution; actual-use cases add observed evidence. J53–J59 concern integrated assessment across members and their material composition.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":129,\"path\":\"standards/CONFORMANCE.md\",\"quote\":\"A logical-review check is a reviewer's reasoned reading: the reviewer\\nconstructs a discriminator's situation against the text and finds whether\\nthe text yields the expected distinction, or finds a counterexample or a\\ncontradiction, without running anything (P6).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/CONFORMANCE.md#CONFORMANCE%2F5.%20Discriminator%20coverage\",\"start_line\":121},{\"end_line\":197,\"path\":\"standards/CONFORMANCE.md\",\"quote\":\"Integrated assessment checks the complete declared member set and its\\nmaterial composition. Local success cannot discharge a contradictory\\nshared determination, an unresolved owner decision or a required result\\ngap.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/CONFORMANCE.md#CONFORMANCE%2F5.%20Discriminator%20coverage\",\"start_line\":194}],\"label\":\"Logical and integrated discriminator coverage\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:fa454c5f56bb19592ddc541d457f3689","key":124,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:fa454c5f56bb19592ddc541d457f3689\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"UC-1–UC-9 are construction cases and AS-1–AS-12 are assurance cases with stated expected distinctions. Each receives local-owner logical review and applicable actual-use evidence where required by the claim. These cases remain assessment design.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":222,\"path\":\"standards/CONFORMANCE.md\",\"quote\":\"The following nine construction cases and twelve assurance cases state\\ntheir complete expected distinctions. UC-n identifies a construction case;\\nAS-n identifies an assurance case. Each receives a logical-review check\\nunder its local owner, and applicable actual-use evidence where the claim\\nrequires it.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/CONFORMANCE.md#CONFORMANCE%2F5.%20Discriminator%20coverage%2FUniversal-construction%20and%20assurance%20discriminators\",\"start_line\":216}],\"label\":\"Universal-construction and assurance discriminators\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:803107dc0e8102b1fc0c5d9126108f77","key":125,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:803107dc0e8102b1fc0c5d9126108f77\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[\"Applies within boundaries governed by this optional profile.\"],\"definition\":\"DESIGN_MODULE is a Tier 3 optional realisation-design profile covering ontology-first derivation, proportional sequencing and decision completeness, bounded frames, native constructability, capability and foundation selection, entity/authority/admission/function completeness, Prime atoms and contraction, IACS, three-view design, reconstruction, computational realisation, module taxonomy, realisation rules, review, adoption and bound-runtime identity defaults.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":14,\"path\":\"standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md\",\"quote\":\"Tier 3. An optional profile of realisation design: ontology-first\\nderivation, proportional design sequencing and decision completeness,\\nbounded frame conservation, native constructability, capability and\\nfoundation selection, entity, authority, admission and function\\ncompleteness, Prime semantic atoms and their contraction, the irreducible\\narchitectural carrier set, the three-view design gate, invariant\\nreconstruction, computational realisation, the module taxonomy, the\\nrealisation rules (immutable carriers, totality, effect edge, no semantic\\ncentre, coupling, governance and strategy separation, opportunistic\\noptimisation, recurrence, post-ticket review, interface bleed, proxy\\ninterfaces), the review questions and checklist, adoption, and the identity\\ndefaults of a bound runtime realisation.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md#DESIGN_MODULE\",\"start_line\":3}],\"label\":\"DESIGN_MODULE\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:b53ecd7f95b44bc7ffed5180d491d116","key":126,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:b53ecd7f95b44bc7ffed5180d491d116\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[\"These terms have profile-local ownership.\"],\"definition\":\"The profile names Ontology as the engineering Ontology of one designed boundary; Prime; Irreducible Architectural Carrier Set (IACS); Subordinate Payload; Promotion Test; Boundary Inflation; carrier; three-view design asset; module; and decision_complete(B) and co_evolution_admissible(B). Their detailed definitions are referred to §§5–9.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":32,\"path\":\"standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md\",\"quote\":\"This profile's own terms are Ontology (the engineering Ontology of one\\ndesigned boundary, §5), Prime (§5, §6), the Irreducible Architectural\\nCarrier Set (IACS, §6), Subordinate Payload, Promotion Test and Boundary\\nInflation (§6), carrier, three-view design asset (§7), module (§9) and the\\npredicates `decision_complete(B)` and `co_evolution_admissible(B)` (§5).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md#DESIGN_MODULE\",\"start_line\":28}],\"label\":\"Profile-owned design terms\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:ac55c80211cf131cf378a4be5f1205d3","key":127,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:ac55c80211cf131cf378a4be5f1205d3\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"Tier-2 ASSURANCE supplies the design-to-module evidence route, module-derived unit tests and module lifecycle confirmation (§§14–16), and names generic carrier inventory, accepted ontology/design, domain/sequence/state projections and decision-completeness/co-evolution conditions that this profile binds for its own boundaries.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":24,\"path\":\"standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md\",\"quote\":\"the design-to-module evidence route, module-derived unit tests and\\nmodule lifecycle confirmation ASSURANCE §14 to §16.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md#DESIGN_MODULE\",\"start_line\":23},{\"end_line\":38,\"path\":\"standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md\",\"quote\":\"where ASSURANCE (tier 2) names \\\"the\\ncarrier inventory the design declares\\\", \\\"the accepted ontology and\\ndesign\\\", \\\"the design's domain, sequence and state projections\\\" and \\\"the\\ndesign's decision-completeness and co-evolution conditions\\\", a boundary\\ngoverned by this profile binds them to the IACS, the accepted Ontology and\\ntarget design, the three-view design asset and the two predicates of §5.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md#DESIGN_MODULE\",\"start_line\":33}],\"label\":\"Imported ASSURANCE design roles\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:48509418a2bcdf06ca45005884f68544","key":128,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:48509418a2bcdf06ca45005884f68544\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"Profile evaluation results, Ontology/design dispositions and author-declared design-record entries are distinct categories. Reconstruction decisions and axiom verdicts are the profile's two result refinements. Other closed design vocabularies are records without core-result mappings; their evaluations return their own core values.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":54,\"path\":\"standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md\",\"quote\":\"A performed evaluation under this profile\\nreturns a value of the core result algebra of\\n[FOUNDATIONS §4 Results](FOUNDATIONS.md#results), directly or through one\\nof this profile's two refinements, each mapped where it is defined: the\\nreconstruction decisions of §7 Invariant reconstruction sufficiency and\\nthe axiom verdicts of §7 Cross-view axiom evaluation.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md#DESIGN_MODULE\",\"start_line\":44}],\"label\":\"Design results, dispositions and record entries\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:634fd70c19c7707b7f5e7b83c30a4e6b","key":129,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:634fd70c19c7707b7f5e7b83c30a4e6b\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[\"Once the project has decided its outcomes and capabilities.\"],\"definition\":\"The profile concerns realisation design and implementation shape. Its goals are reduced ambiguity, entropy, avoidable debt, hidden authority, hidden mutation and semantic drift; increased refactorability; and preserved evidence for audit and reconstruction. Bounded intermediate traversal gives finite inspectable units for reasoning, implementation, evaluation, proof and refactor; a module boundary is one such tool.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":91,\"path\":\"standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md\",\"quote\":\"The goals are to reduce ambiguity, reduce\\nentropy, eliminate avoidable technical debt, increase refactorability,\\nreduce hidden authority, hidden mutation and semantic drift in realisation\\ncode, and preserve enough evidence that later reviewers can audit,\\nrefactor and reconstruct why the realisation took its current shape (P2,\\nP6).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md#DESIGN_MODULE%2F1.%20Purpose%20and%20position%2FPurpose\",\"start_line\":85},{\"end_line\":107,\"path\":\"standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md\",\"quote\":\"Specification gives the global WHAT; every intermediate\\ntraversal should have a finite, inspectable unit for reasoning,\\nimplementation, evaluation, proof and later refactor. A module boundary is\\none realisation-level tool for creating that unit; it is not the only\\npossible bounded traversal.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md#DESIGN_MODULE%2F1.%20Purpose%20and%20position%2FPurpose\",\"start_line\":101}],\"label\":\"Bounded realisation design\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:6448312e3a64306604f189415f61316f","key":130,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:6448312e3a64306604f189415f61316f\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[\"Within the profile's governed boundaries.\"],\"definition\":\"Functional design discipline is required, with a preferred functionally biased realisation: explicit typed carriers and transforms hold meaning, imperative coordination is subordinate to admitted truth, effects are isolated at explicit boundary modules, and mutable shared state is minimised and justified. A functional programming language is not required.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":134,\"path\":\"standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md\",\"quote\":\"The preferred realisation shape is functionally biased (P1, P6). That means semantic meaning should live in typed carriers and\\nexplicit transforms; imperative coordination should be subordinate to\\nadmitted truth; side effects should be isolated to explicit boundary\\nmodules; and mutable shared state should be minimised and justified. The\\nprofile does not require a functional programming language; it does\\nrequire a functional design discipline.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md#DESIGN_MODULE%2F1.%20Purpose%20and%20position%2FPosition\",\"start_line\":127}],\"label\":\"Functional design discipline\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:1f5a3d72754c41847528656b6d22a2cc","key":131,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:1f5a3d72754c41847528656b6d22a2cc\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[\"Scoped to boundaries governed by DESIGN_MODULE.\"],\"definition\":\"The core realisation-shape rule is owned once by SPEC_METHOD §2. Its stated test is that a design is too imperative and coupled when a reader must inspect orchestration to learn the system's meaning. The profile's subsequent rules refine it.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":143,\"path\":\"standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md\",\"quote\":\"The core rule, with the test that a design is too imperative and too\\ncoupled when a reader has to inspect orchestration to learn what the\\nsystem means, is stated once in\\n[SPEC_METHOD §2 Realisation shape](SPEC_METHOD.md#realisation-shape),\\nscoped to boundaries this profile governs; every rule below refines it\\n(P1, P6).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md#DESIGN_MODULE%2F1.%20Purpose%20and%20position%2FCore%20rule\",\"start_line\":138}],\"label\":\"Imported realisation core rule\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:af6461c6cd976f9897df29c33b0d379b","key":132,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:af6461c6cd976f9897df29c33b0d379b\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[\"A project adopts the profile for a named realisation boundary.\"],\"definition\":\"DESIGN_MODULE is optional material family F17, software design. Actors enter it when designing, implementing or reviewing a governed boundary. It governs realisation of decided Product outcomes, not the constitutional decision about those outcomes. Its foundation-to-law table distinguishes derived consequences from domain and policy choices and their owners.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":174,\"path\":\"standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md\",\"quote\":\"Its instance premises hold where a project\\nadopts this profile for a boundary; they are adopted with it and do not\\nfollow from the foundations (P1, P6):\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md#DESIGN_MODULE%2F1.%20Purpose%20and%20position%2FFoundation%20to%20law\",\"start_line\":172}],\"label\":\"Software design profile, F17\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:e33b4c2ac78d7102c41dd630b46098a2","key":133,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:e33b4c2ac78d7102c41dd630b46098a2\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"The table's cited commitments have distinct standing: P0 recovered; P1, P2, P3, P4a and P6 independent; P4b derived from P0 and P2 with P0's non-reacquirable step-fact premise; P5 derived from P0 and P6 with P0's open-world premise. Imported families are F1 frames/context, F2 transitions/steps/configuration, F3 results/combination, F4 work state/resumption/reuse, F6 claims/evidence/assessment/acceptance, F8 identity, F10 constitutional chain/outcome/build-tenant binding, F12 project adoption, F13 work carriers, and F18 graph-native construction. Adopted instance premises are I1 decided outcomes/capabilities and named-boundary adoption; I2 alternative and possibly multiple code locations for one meaning; I3 bounded actors whose later actions generally lack original design reasoning; I4 local or existing-foundation mechanisms and recurrence across boundaries and time.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":187,\"path\":\"standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md\",\"quote\":\"- I4: a mechanism the boundary needs can be built locally or taken from\\n  existing foundations, and similar computation recurs across boundaries\\n  and over time.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md#DESIGN_MODULE%2F1.%20Purpose%20and%20position%2FFoundation%20to%20law\",\"start_line\":185}],\"label\":\"Commitments, imports and instance premises\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:7aeab816d4886c4c3a6f91c67d6ca97c","key":134,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:7aeab816d4886c4c3a6f91c67d6ca97c\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"Named rule and consumer loci in FOUNDATIONS, PROFILES, ACTIVATION, EVALUATION, IDENTITY, SPEC_METHOD, PRODUCT_DEFINITION, TICKETS, ODD, ASSURANCE, UX, WORLD_MODEL, CONFORMANCE and EXECUTIVE_BASELINE, together with later DESIGN_MODULE clauses. These are references with the roles explicitly stated in the supplied text; their absent bodies are not reconstructed.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":231,\"path\":\"standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md\",\"quote\":\"Consumers of these rows, where an actor enters them (FOUNDATIONS §3\\nFoundation to law, Consumers), one list per row, each consumer linked to\\nits own locus:\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md#DESIGN_MODULE%2F1.%20Purpose%20and%20position%2FFoundation%20to%20law\",\"start_line\":229}],\"label\":\"Referenced owning and consuming rule loci\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:97f087b604d6d9d05c50fbf4d552359b","key":135,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:97f087b604d6d9d05c50fbf4d552359b\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[\"The Product is governed by the graph-execution profile.\"],\"definition\":\"For Product movement between typed asset states, the governing structure is outcome traversal, then declarative graph carriers (GTL and ABG), then deterministic module realisation. A module is a realisation cut inside this graph program, not the program itself.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":280,\"path\":\"standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md\",\"quote\":\"1. outcome traversal under the graph-execution profile;\\n2. the declarative graph carrier structure (GTL and ABG in that profile's\\n   terms); and\\n3. deterministic module realisation under this profile.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md#DESIGN_MODULE%2F2.%20Graph-execution%20alignment%20and%20escalation\",\"start_line\":277}],\"label\":\"Graph-execution and module alignment\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:82e6156594202f0a9c804bce9d492a25","key":136,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:82e6156594202f0a9c804bce9d492a25\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[\"The profile governs the boundary.\"],\"definition\":\"Three overriding boundary-closure evaluators are authority seam closure, essential carrier consolidation and enforcement after proof. Ingress collapse specifies the accompanying foreign-input boundary discipline.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":304,\"path\":\"standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md\",\"quote\":\"When this profile governs a boundary, each design or implementation change\\nshould be judged against three overriding evaluators (P6, P2). They are not optional heuristics. A\\nchange that improves local ergonomics, test output or static-checker\\noutput but fails one of them is not real progress under this profile.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md#DESIGN_MODULE%2F3.%20Boundary%20closure%20evaluators\",\"start_line\":301}],\"label\":\"Boundary closure evaluators\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:fb7c124a177ade36a4c47157ab72d44e","key":137,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:fb7c124a177ade36a4c47157ab72d44e\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"The functional-bias and typing rule family combines language-independent carrier, composition and effect preferences with a Python-specific full-typing and strict-checking requirement.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":366,\"path\":\"standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md\",\"quote\":\"## 4. Functional bias and typing\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md#DESIGN_MODULE%2F4.%20Functional%20bias%20and%20typing\",\"start_line\":366}],\"label\":\"Functional bias and typing\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:fdb10a62e0ecdba0beca462cc9d91a8d","key":138,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:fdb10a62e0ecdba0beca462cc9d91a8d\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[\"The boundary is governed by this profile.\"],\"definition\":\"An Ontology is the boundary's prior semantic-design authority: entities, identities, relationships, invariants, lifecycle, authority, atomic functions, higher-order composition, effects and projections. It derives from constitutional intent, Product, requirements and applicable graph/domain profile. Accepted design supplies structural HOW: topology, interfaces, carrier placement, module boundaries, algorithms and local realisation. Implementation and tests derive through requirements and accepted design while preserving the Ontology.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":447,\"path\":\"standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md\",\"quote\":\"The Ontology is the prior semantic-design authority for the boundary.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md#DESIGN_MODULE%2F5.%20Ontology-first%20design\",\"start_line\":437},{\"end_line\":480,\"path\":\"standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md\",\"quote\":\"Ontology =\\n  entities + identities + relationships + invariants + lifecycle\\n  + authority + atomic functions + higher-order composition\\n  + effects + projections\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md#DESIGN_MODULE%2F5.%20Ontology-first%20design\",\"start_line\":477}],\"label\":\"Accepted Ontology and design layers\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:0a1c7d24e8784721926afa9489f9c0e0","key":139,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:0a1c7d24e8784721926afa9489f9c0e0\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"A material semantic boundary is one whose change affects identity, authority, lifecycle, public contract, externally observable Product meaning, cross-module topology, or accepted effect or closure law.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":466,\"path\":\"standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md\",\"quote\":\"A material semantic boundary is\\none whose change affects identity, authority, lifecycle, public contract,\\nexternally observable Product meaning, cross-module topology, or accepted\\neffect or closure law.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md#DESIGN_MODULE%2F5.%20Ontology-first%20design\",\"start_line\":463}],\"label\":\"Material semantic boundary\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:b8bc7d3a0ac93efb8d5099e60d3dfcad","key":140,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:b8bc7d3a0ac93efb8d5099e60d3dfcad\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[\"B is one governed boundary.\"],\"definition\":\"M(B) is the complete material-relation network: entities; identities; relationships; cardinalities; invariants; authorities; authority transitions; functions; higher-order composition laws; topology; lifecycle states and transitions; public contracts; externally observable Product meaning; declared domains and admission conditions; failure and refusal routes; effect and closure laws; projections; module mappings; material algorithmic obligations. U(B) is its unresolved subset. Decision completeness requires empty U(B), joint satisfiability, and semantic equivalence of every admitted network under governing Product, requirements and accepted design relations. Co-evolution admissibility is exactly decision completeness. The design gate is the smallest causally closed affected set needed to establish it.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":502,\"path\":\"standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md\",\"quote\":\"U(B) = unresolved(M(B))\\ndecision_complete(B) iff\\n  U(B) = empty\\n  and M(B) is jointly satisfiable\\n  and every network admitted by M(B) is semantically equivalent under the\\n      governing Product, requirements and accepted design relations\\nco_evolution_admissible(B) iff decision_complete(B)\\ndesign_gate(B) =\\n  the smallest causally closed affected set needed to establish\\n  decision_complete(B)\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md#DESIGN_MODULE%2F5.%20Ontology-first%20design%2FProportional%20design%20sequencing\",\"start_line\":493},{\"end_line\":571,\"path\":\"standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md\",\"quote\":\"M(B) =\\n  entities + identities + relationships + cardinalities + invariants\\n  + authorities + authority transitions + functions\\n  + higher-order composition laws + topology\\n  + lifecycle states and transitions + public contracts\\n  + externally observable Product meaning\\n  + declared domains and admission conditions\\n  + failure and refusal routes + effect and closure laws\\n  + projections + module mappings + material algorithmic obligations\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md#DESIGN_MODULE%2F5.%20Ontology-first%20design%2FDecision-complete%20symbolic%20design\",\"start_line\":563}],\"label\":\"Decision-complete material-relation network\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:a47b4123e6da5cd417b5ac30e436cd15","key":141,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:a47b4123e6da5cd417b5ac30e436cd15\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"A material design frame records governing frames and accepted relations, bounded affected relations, inherited invariants, crossing authority/composition seams and subordinate frames opened by unresolved material distinctions. Global and local are relative to the selected frame. Governing frames form a constraint network and may be multiple rather than a mandatory hierarchy.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":613,\"path\":\"standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md\",\"quote\":\"- the governing frames and accepted relations from which it derives;\\n- the bounded affected relation set of the proposed action;\\n- the applicable inherited invariants;\\n- the authority and composition seams crossing that set; and\\n- the subordinate frames opened by unresolved material distinctions.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md#DESIGN_MODULE%2F5.%20Ontology-first%20design%2FBounded%20frame%20conservation%20%28UP-017%29\",\"start_line\":609}],\"label\":\"Bounded design frame\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:3f7e4abc35ea8e58b3115e97b533309b","key":142,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:3f7e4abc35ea8e58b3115e97b533309b\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"Native constructability concerns whether the chosen substrate can construct required identities, relationships, transitions, authority boundaries, effects, lifecycle, composition, publication and retirement. Foundation selection separately compares bounded candidate compositions for material generic capabilities, common mechanics, algorithms and dependencies.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":669,\"path\":\"standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md\",\"quote\":\"This is a constructability obligation,\\nnot a prescribed implementation; the consumer chooses the substrate and the\\nevidence mechanism (P0).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md#DESIGN_MODULE%2F5.%20Ontology-first%20design%2FNative%20constructability%20%28UP-002%29\",\"start_line\":667},{\"end_line\":680,\"path\":\"standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md\",\"quote\":\"Native constructability proves that the selected substrate can realise the\\ndesign; it does not prove that locally constructing another generic\\nmechanism is the best realisation.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md#DESIGN_MODULE%2F5.%20Ontology-first%20design%2FCapability%20and%20foundation%20selection%20%28UP-023%29\",\"start_line\":673}],\"label\":\"Constructability and foundation selection\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:c27a10cb8a982f47cef70a74549cb00b","key":143,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:c27a10cb8a982f47cef70a74549cb00b\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"Entity-lifecycle evidence enumerates active entities, identities, relationships, cardinalities, invariants, lifecycle states and authority owners. Its matrix has Entity, Identity, Authority owner, Declare/create, Read/project, Update/transition and Delete/retire columns. These are completeness questions, not a mutable-CRUD mandate. Domain-entity lifecycle is distinct from ASSURANCE §16's operational build, release, deployment, observation and retirement lifecycle.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":799,\"path\":\"standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md\",\"quote\":\"| Entity | Identity | Authority owner | Declare/create | Read/project | Update/transition | Delete/retire |\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md#DESIGN_MODULE%2F5.%20Ontology-first%20design%2FEntity%20and%20lifecycle%20completeness\",\"start_line\":799}],\"label\":\"Entity and lifecycle completeness evidence\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:094d58ecf1ad6d4feccfdf69b1667180","key":144,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:094d58ecf1ad6d4feccfdf69b1667180\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"Authority is part of the Ontology. The authority matrix distinguishes proposer, evaluator, verifier, admitter, executor, projector and retirement owner for each relevant function/transition. Actor identity, capability on a basis, attribution, permission, domain-meaning ownership and runtime-effect ownership are distinct.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":832,\"path\":\"standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md\",\"quote\":\"| Function or transition | Proposer | Evaluator | Verifier | Admitter | Executor | Projector | Retirement owner |\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md#DESIGN_MODULE%2F5.%20Ontology-first%20design%2FAuthority%20model\",\"start_line\":832}],\"label\":\"Ontology authority model\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:d2d50ec064f37926a95bcc1bbbb51190","key":145,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:d2d50ec064f37926a95bcc1bbbb51190\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[\"A consequential entity-transition domain is present.\"],\"definition\":\"The singular transformation-admission relation decides which candidate becomes durable entity truth. It spans entity identity, predecessor basis, authority scope, candidate family, decision cardinality, admission predicate, durable result and supersession law. Singularity belongs to the complete decision relation, not a single actor, callable or component. The evidence table records Entity transition domain, Predecessor basis, Candidate family, Admission relation, Durable result and Competing-path disposition.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":875,\"path\":\"standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md\",\"quote\":\"| Entity transition domain | Predecessor basis | Candidate family | Admission relation | Durable result | Competing-path disposition |\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md#DESIGN_MODULE%2F5.%20Ontology-first%20design%2FTransformation%20admission%20completeness%20%28UP-016%29\",\"start_line\":875}],\"label\":\"Complete transformation-admission relation\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:c568f26576d25f251810727e0b735e24","key":146,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:c568f26576d25f251810727e0b735e24\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"Atomic function families are the smallest parameterised families completing entity lifecycles. Function derivation records Discovered functionality, Entity, Atomic function or template, Higher-order composition, Effect class, Required authority and Disposition. Higher-order behaviour uses an explicit composition/effect algebra; illustrative categories are unit/lift, sequential, parallel/applicative, fold/evaluation, retry/recovery, recursion/fixed point and projection.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":948,\"path\":\"standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md\",\"quote\":\"| Discovered functionality | Entity | Atomic function or template | Higher-order composition | Effect class | Required authority | Disposition |\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md#DESIGN_MODULE%2F5.%20Ontology-first%20design%2FAtomic%20functions%20and%20higher-order%20composition\",\"start_line\":948}],\"label\":\"Atomic functions and higher-order composition\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:6814b648516f3fa537517748d3181520","key":147,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:6814b648516f3fa537517748d3181520\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"A Prime semantic atom is an irreducible design relation—atomic function family, identity, authority transition, lifecycle relation, topology, effect, closure or composition law—that cannot honestly be expressed by composing accepted atoms while preserving meaning. Prime is decided at semantic-design altitude. Smallness, typing, naming, separate testing or a file/class/module boundary do not establish it. Whole-family contraction examines every candidate atom kind and every proposed realisation projection.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":982,\"path\":\"standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md\",\"quote\":\"A Prime semantic atom is one irreducible design relation: an atomic\\nfunction family, identity, authority transition, lifecycle relation,\\ntopology, effect, closure law or composition law that cannot be expressed\\nhonestly by composing other accepted atoms while preserving the same\\nmeaning (P3, P1).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md#DESIGN_MODULE%2F5.%20Ontology-first%20design%2FPrime%20semantic%20atoms%20and%20admitted%20domain\",\"start_line\":978}],\"label\":\"Prime semantic atom and family\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:982faaba8542901a360f970f115eecef","key":148,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:982faaba8542901a360f970f115eecef\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"Ontology projections include domain/class, sequence, state/lifecycle diagrams; authority/effect matrices; IACS; APIs, operation registers, SDK/CLI surfaces; schemas, codecs, manifests, catalogues; target architecture/module design; implementation through accepted target design; and tests/proofs through requirements and accepted design. They preserve one semantic truth and are not independent semantic authorities.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1062,\"path\":\"standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md\",\"quote\":\"The Ontology is one semantic truth (P1, P6).\\nThese preserve it and do not become independent semantic authorities:\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md#DESIGN_MODULE%2F5.%20Ontology-first%20design%2FOntology%20projection\",\"start_line\":1055}],\"label\":\"Ontology and realisation projections\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:e14ea2ce604c9b38027bf09a26544d13","key":149,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:e14ea2ce604c9b38027bf09a26544d13\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"IACS is the smallest lawful top-level carrier family needed for a boundary's functionality and authority flow. Subordinate Payload is internal payload detail, not top-level by default. Promotion Test is the explicit prerequisite for elevating it to a top-level type. Boundary Inflation is promotion into peer types without irreducible need. Example carrier roles are source truth, admission, execution, yielded/recovery, effect plan and public projection.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1100,\"path\":\"standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md\",\"quote\":\"- Irreducible Architectural Carrier Set (IACS): the smallest lawful\\n  top-level carrier family required for one boundary;\\n- Subordinate Payload: payload detail that exists inside that boundary but\\n  is not top-level by default;\\n- Promotion Test: the explicit test a Subordinate Payload passes before it\\n  becomes a top-level type; and\\n- Boundary Inflation: the defect where subordinate payload detail is\\n  promoted into extra peer types without irreducible need.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md#DESIGN_MODULE%2F6.%20Prime%20law\",\"start_line\":1093}],\"label\":\"IACS, subordinate payloads, promotion and inflation\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:d64c3fd67483b1082f3765ec22d6a46f","key":150,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:d64c3fd67483b1082f3765ec22d6a46f\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[\"Realisation derives from an existing design line, released tenant or reference implementation.\"],\"definition\":\"Reference-derived module design carries the derivation chain constitutional WHAT → reference design → target Ontology and reference-to-Ontology mapping → target design mapping → target module boundary assets → implementation. Code comparison alone does not establish design-method completion.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1265,\"path\":\"standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md\",\"quote\":\"The required derivation\\nevidence is: (1) constitutional WHAT; (2) reference design; (3) target\\nOntology and reference-to-Ontology mapping; (4) target design mapping; (5)\\ntarget module boundary assets; (6) implementation.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md#DESIGN_MODULE%2F6.%20Prime%20law%2FReference-derived%20module%20design\",\"start_line\":1262}],\"label\":\"Reference-to-target derivation\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:c19d38e4362efe35b2f5323c54192a62","key":151,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:c19d38e4362efe35b2f5323c54192a62\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"The design-gate asset combines one accepted Ontology with three distinct fidelity-checked views: classDiagram domain, sequenceDiagram execution and stateDiagram-v2 lifecycle. Together they provide the sign-off surface for identity, authority, behaviour, lifecycle and axiom conformance.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1302,\"path\":\"standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md\",\"quote\":\"The asset contains all three views: a Mermaid `classDiagram` domain model;\\na Mermaid `sequenceDiagram` execution model; and a Mermaid\\n`stateDiagram-v2` lifecycle model.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md#DESIGN_MODULE%2F7.%20Ontology%20and%20three-view%20design%20gate\",\"start_line\":1298}],\"label\":\"Ontology and three-view design asset\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:770fcc5357db9571656e4e89a8719021","key":152,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:770fcc5357db9571656e4e89a8719021\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[\"An accepted material-frame basis and a proposed bounded action are declared.\"],\"definition\":\"Invariant reconstruction is the sufficiency of selected method basis plus accepted design to recover every governing relation in the action's causally closed affected set and classify the action against each as preserves, changes, duplicates or violates. Method supplies required relations and reasoning law; accepted design supplies concrete invariant values. These inputs do not substitute for one another.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1346,\"path\":\"standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md\",\"quote\":\"The two inputs are distinct and neither\\nsubstitutes for the other: the selected method describes which relations\\nare required and how to reason about them; the accepted design supplies\\nthe concrete invariant values.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md#DESIGN_MODULE%2F7.%20Ontology%20and%20three-view%20design%20gate%2FInvariant%20reconstruction%20sufficiency%20%28UP-018%29\",\"start_line\":1343}],\"label\":\"Invariant reconstruction sufficiency\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:9809bdb58b2f5e183372e40c53f99694","key":153,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:9809bdb58b2f5e183372e40c53f99694\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"The domain model is the structural Ontology projection. It uses stereotypes <<prime-conformant>>, <<subordinate>>, <<effect-edge>>, <<deferred>>, <<authoritative>>, <<downstream>>; '+' means public/exported and '-' module-local/private. Standard relationships use composition for owned subordinate payloads, association for downstream consumption and inheritance only for actual variant/outcome families.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1420,\"path\":\"standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md\",\"quote\":\"The standard stereotype vocabulary is `<<prime-conformant>>`,\\n`<<subordinate>>`, `<<effect-edge>>`, `<<deferred>>`, `<<authoritative>>`\\nand `<<downstream>>`.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md#DESIGN_MODULE%2F7.%20Ontology%20and%20three-view%20design%20gate%2FDomain%20model\",\"start_line\":1414}],\"label\":\"Domain model\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:b88eeaaa5be3aa8b3a9cb5bb26849eb0","key":154,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:b88eeaaa5be3aa8b3a9cb5bb26849eb0\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"The sequence model projects Ontology functions and authority onto supported execution from admitted input to a result or truthful stop.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1427,\"path\":\"standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md\",\"quote\":\"The `sequenceDiagram` is the behavioural projection of Ontology functions\\nand authority (P1, P6). It shows the supported\\nexecution path from admitted input to result or truthful stop,\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md#DESIGN_MODULE%2F7.%20Ontology%20and%20three-view%20design%20gate%2FSequence%20model\",\"start_line\":1424}],\"label\":\"Sequence model\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:7f39de5452d3ee7ee736cf3e653ad621","key":155,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:7f39de5452d3ee7ee736cf3e653ad621\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"The state model projects Ontology entity lifecycle, including every admitted refusal, blocked, continuation, retry, escalation and terminal state the active boundary can produce.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1444,\"path\":\"standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md\",\"quote\":\"The `stateDiagram-v2` is the lifecycle projection of Ontology entities\\n(P3, P5). It shows the complete admitted lifecycle for\\nthe active boundary, including refusal, blocked, continuation, retry,\\nescalation and terminal states that the boundary can produce.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md#DESIGN_MODULE%2F7.%20Ontology%20and%20three-view%20design%20gate%2FState%20model\",\"start_line\":1441}],\"label\":\"State model\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:b8eaf98796f24eef0b1f5239adcc90a4","key":156,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:b8eaf98796f24eef0b1f5239adcc90a4\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"Cross-view axiom evaluation records Axiom, Ontology evidence, Authority, Domain evidence, Sequence evidence, State evidence, Native enforcement, Admission/compiler enforcement, Verdict and Gap owner. The refined verdicts pass, fail and not_applicable map to core values for the exact-basis disjunction 'the design meets the axiom, or the axiom does not apply'; unresolved evaluation and absence of evaluation remain separate.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1457,\"path\":\"standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md\",\"quote\":\"| Axiom | Ontology evidence | Authority | Domain evidence | Sequence evidence | State evidence | Native enforcement | Admission/compiler enforcement | Verdict | Gap owner |\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md#DESIGN_MODULE%2F7.%20Ontology%20and%20three-view%20design%20gate%2FCross-view%20axiom%20evaluation\",\"start_line\":1457}],\"label\":\"Cross-view assessment and axiom result domain\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:17af2f81977b5a255c4155d8b1c3abd0","key":157,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:17af2f81977b5a255c4155d8b1c3abd0\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"Ontology and design verdicts are separate owner acceptance decisions consuming availability and assessment results at the design gate. The decision owner is the design authority accepting the Ontology. 'accepted' is the ACTIVATION disposition 'accept', mapped to satisfied for 'the candidate is accepted at its declared boundary'. Other dispositions or no disposition are not acceptance; no disposition means no acceptance result.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1538,\"path\":\"standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md\",\"quote\":\"The Ontology verdict and the design verdict are each an acceptance\\nresult: a decision that consumes the results of assessment, distinct from\\nthem.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md#DESIGN_MODULE%2F7.%20Ontology%20and%20three-view%20design%20gate%2FGate%20and%20retrospective%20work\",\"start_line\":1527}],\"label\":\"Design-gate acceptance and retrospective work\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:bb53ea665dafe38a1f8718f3b042739a","key":158,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:bb53ea665dafe38a1f8718f3b042739a\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"An operational engineering profile for preferred realisation structure and design discipline. Its engineering Ontology concerns one designed boundary; using the profile does not require adopting a world-model, Constraint-Emergence Ontology, or metaphysical or empirical programme.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1691,\"path\":\"standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md\",\"quote\":\"This profile is operational and stands on its own.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md#DESIGN_MODULE%2F8.%20Theoretical%20framing\",\"start_line\":1686}],\"label\":\"Design-module profile\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:8e5e05d12a032d36a117b5f56176885c","key":159,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:8e5e05d12a032d36a117b5f56176885c\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"The three domain views show domain structure, execution and lifecycle. A computational realisation projection additionally exposes abstract data types, identity and key structures, algorithms, algebraic laws, mutation and effect boundaries, selected implementations and domain-to-computational mappings, including repeated machinery obscured by domain names.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1619,\"path\":\"standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md\",\"quote\":\"domain design into its computational realisation: abstract data types,\\nidentity and key structures, algorithms, algebraic laws, mutation and\\neffect boundaries, selected implementations, and domain-to-computational\\nmappings.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md#DESIGN_MODULE%2F7.%20Ontology%20and%20three-view%20design%20gate%2FComputational%20realisation%20projection%20%28UP-019%29\",\"start_line\":1616}],\"label\":\"Computational realisation projection\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:1ffb0d473667cbcd448ccf239b30f413","key":160,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:1ffb0d473667cbcd448ccf239b30f413\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"The explicit semantic and operational roles declared for a material realisation component. The declared role set is design authority; technological capability creates no authority.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1603,\"path\":\"standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md\",\"quote\":\"A component's declared role set is design authority;\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md#DESIGN_MODULE%2F7.%20Ontology%20and%20three-view%20design%20gate%2FComputational%20realisation%20projection%20%28UP-019%29\",\"start_line\":1603}],\"label\":\"Component role set\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:a46e77f57dce5d3691cc4fbe307267d5","key":161,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:a46e77f57dce5d3691cc4fbe307267d5\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"Optional theoretical framing in which a Markov object is a candidate identity-bearing cut: a stable self-bounding pattern with an effective blanket separating identity-bearing from contextual structure. IACS analogises the smallest such cut; the Promotion Test asks whether a payload has independent boundary authority; Boundary Inflation mistakes fragments for peer objects; semantic-boundary strong typing keeps the cut explicit.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1697,\"path\":\"standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md\",\"quote\":\"It treats a Markov object\\nas a candidate identity-bearing cut: a stable self-bounding pattern whose\\neffective blanket separates what is load-bearing for identity from what is\\nload-bearing for context.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md#DESIGN_MODULE%2F8.%20Theoretical%20framing\",\"start_line\":1694}],\"label\":\"Markov-object theoretical framing\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:d0ef4997ddb9eeaa35eecc22a937ba5e","key":162,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:d0ef4997ddb9eeaa35eecc22a937ba5e\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[\"The profile governs the realisation boundary.\"],\"definition\":\"Recommended module roles: carrier modules define typed immutable inputs, outputs, contracts, transitions, records or envelopes; semantic kernels transform carriers without effects; effect shells perform emission, publication, network, subprocess, persistence or delivery effects; projections derive read models or reports from authoritative truth; bindings/adapters translate external boundaries to internal carriers without inventing law; constructors/materialisers write generated or built artifacts from admitted carriers and explicit plans. Module boundaries constrain traversal reasoning under finite context, attention and time, expose ownership, consumption, emissions and sufficient proof, and make recurrence visible for library consolidation.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1732,\"path\":\"standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md\",\"quote\":\"- constructor or materialisation module: writes generated or built\\n  artifacts from admitted carriers and explicit plans.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md#DESIGN_MODULE%2F9.%20Module%20taxonomy\",\"start_line\":1731}],\"label\":\"Module role taxonomy\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:656e135dc87d3a38444515f4547a5002","key":163,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:656e135dc87d3a38444515f4547a5002\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"Typed values carrying source truth, preferably produced by a constructor or parser, consumed by transforms that return another carrier or closed result, and read by projections without mutation.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1769,\"path\":\"standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md\",\"quote\":\"preferred shape: a constructor or parser produces a typed carrier;\\ntransforms consume one carrier and return another carrier or a closed\\nresult; projections read those carriers without mutating them.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md#DESIGN_MODULE%2F10.%20Realisation%20rules%2FImmutable%20carriers\",\"start_line\":1767}],\"label\":\"Typed truth carrier\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:7243c6a09744b0df33d05cde1696eb08","key":164,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:7243c6a09744b0df33d05cde1696eb08\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"A Product semantic function may encounter input outside its admitted domain. Its returned outcomes are Product domain values, distinct from the method's core results; an evaluation consuming those outcomes returns its own core result.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1785,\"path\":\"standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md\",\"quote\":\"The outcome values a\\nsemantic function returns are the Product's domain values, not results of\\nthis method; an evaluation that consumes them returns its own core value\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md#DESIGN_MODULE%2F10.%20Realisation%20rules%2FTotality\",\"start_line\":1782}],\"label\":\"Semantic function and Product outcomes\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:a50aeb522de220e58f85fd64698e09f8","key":165,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:a50aeb522de220e58f85fd64698e09f8\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"An explicit boundary for effects such as file writes, network calls, subprocess execution, event append, manifest publication, prompt delivery and database mutation.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1799,\"path\":\"standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md\",\"quote\":\"Typical effect edges include file writes, network calls, subprocess\\nexecution, event append, manifest publication, prompt delivery and\\ndatabase mutation.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md#DESIGN_MODULE%2F10.%20Realisation%20rules%2FEffect%20edge\",\"start_line\":1797}],\"label\":\"Effect edge\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:43b972cd7d8a7223dd4bfa064cbaee31","key":166,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:43b972cd7d8a7223dd4bfa064cbaee31\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"A hidden semantic centre is an orchestration or wrapper surface that procedurally holds meaning which should already reside in carriers, contracts or explicit design modules. Its diagnostic is needing to read that module to discover closure, identity, failure, next work or current truth.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1816,\"path\":\"standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md\",\"quote\":\"A\\nmodule is acting as an unlawful semantic centre when reviewers have to\\nread it to discover what counts as closure, what identity means, what\\nfailure means, what work is next, or what the current truth is.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md#DESIGN_MODULE%2F10.%20Realisation%20rules%2FNo%20semantic%20centre\",\"start_line\":1813}],\"label\":\"Hidden semantic centre\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:71c5dc886f20ac28171b216ffc9f66b7","key":167,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:71c5dc886f20ac28171b216ffc9f66b7\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"A boundary governing, observing, routing, auditing or evaluating another actor, executor, builder or substrate. Governance surfaces describe facts, state, boundary and admissible routes; strategy surfaces prescribe how another actor should work.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1848,\"path\":\"standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md\",\"quote\":\"Governance surfaces describe the state, boundary\\nand admissible routes; strategy surfaces prescribe how another actor\\nshould do the work.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md#DESIGN_MODULE%2F10.%20Realisation%20rules%2FGovernance%20and%20strategy%20separation\",\"start_line\":1846}],\"label\":\"Governance and strategy surfaces\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:3fa0f57bb318e19e8b76a27b4f5b3a61","key":168,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:3fa0f57bb318e19e8b76a27b4f5b3a61\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[\"A realisation boundary is lawfully open for migration, refactor or bounded implementation work.\"],\"definition\":\"Opportunistic optimisation is local improvement subordinate to constitutional truth, declared module ownership evidence and functional equivalence. Cross-boundary improvements are repricing inputs rather than silently enlarged clean-up.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1860,\"path\":\"standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md\",\"quote\":\"This does not\\noutrank constitutional truth, declared module ownership evidence or\\nfunctional equivalence; it is subordinate to them.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md#DESIGN_MODULE%2F10.%20Realisation%20rules%2FOpportunistic%20optimisation\",\"start_line\":1857}],\"label\":\"Opportunistic optimisation\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:efb9ff5d3635a7b82d3288c918fc04d1","key":169,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:efb9ff5d3635a7b82d3288c918fc04d1\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"Review of repeated realisation machinery as a commonisation candidate. Typical candidates are authority-neutral, not Product truth, reused across two or more tickets or boundaries, and locally adaptable without changing semantic ownership: expectation derivation, nested contract or policy carriers, proof helpers, fixtures, effect plans and constructors that own no semantic law.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1897,\"path\":\"standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md\",\"quote\":\"When the same realisation pattern appears across more than one processed\\nboundary, review treats that pattern as a commonisation candidate rather\\nthan as another purely local clean-up\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md#DESIGN_MODULE%2F10.%20Realisation%20rules%2FRecurrence%20extraction\",\"start_line\":1895}],\"label\":\"Recurrence extraction and commonisation\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:dae69138fe6568c833436d0e22dc3ade","key":170,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:dae69138fe6568c833436d0e22dc3ade\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[\"A ticket applies the profile to a boundary and claims that boundary has been processed.\"],\"definition\":\"A bounded design check against the accepted design basis and exact closure claim. Its complete selected function is the claim's causal closure, not the whole Product or construction history; it reconstructs governing requirements through Ontology, Prime atoms, IACS, views, target modules, implementation and module-owned proof.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1965,\"path\":\"standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md\",\"quote\":\"The complete selected function is the causal closure of the declared\\nclaim, not the whole Product or the whole history of its construction.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md#DESIGN_MODULE%2F10.%20Realisation%20rules%2FPost-ticket%20design%20review\",\"start_line\":1964}],\"label\":\"Post-ticket bounded design check\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:f885e90230e4244ecb359d1703569deb","key":171,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:f885e90230e4244ecb359d1703569deb\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"An interface family has one authoritative source truth consumed downstream. Interface bleed includes reconstructing another family's truth, projection becoming closure, reports/prompts becoming admission, wrappers deciding kernel semantics, or adapters inventing meaning.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":2028,\"path\":\"standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md\",\"quote\":\"The required shape: each interface family has\\none authoritative source truth; downstream interfaces consume that truth;\\ncrossing an interface boundary does not create a new semantic centre.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md#DESIGN_MODULE%2F10.%20Realisation%20rules%2FInterface%20bleed%20prohibition\",\"start_line\":2026}],\"label\":\"Interface family and semantic bleed\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:106b5875c771ed4e6863de75f3deb31a","key":172,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:106b5875c771ed4e6863de75f3deb31a\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"A proxy interface is a new-looking surface that forwards to old authority, reconstructs missing truth from it, keeps it executable under a new name, or leaves proofs green while old law governs. Such substitution is bridge debt, distinct from explicitly retained compatibility.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":2039,\"path\":\"standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md\",\"quote\":\"A proxy interface is a new-looking surface that\\nforwards to the old authority path, reconstructs missing truth from the\\nold path, keeps the old path executable behind a new name, or allows\\nproofs to stay green while the old law still governs.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md#DESIGN_MODULE%2F10.%20Realisation%20rules%2FProxy%20interface%20prohibition\",\"start_line\":2036}],\"label\":\"Proxy interface and retained compatibility\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:0793e8125983d93adb20487fbf5a9458","key":173,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:0793e8125983d93adb20487fbf5a9458\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"Review under the design profile includes provenance-bearing prompts, design-review questions, and an explicit functional-realisation checklist when functional bias, pure transforms, immutable carriers, single-owner truth or low coupling is claimed.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":2051,\"path\":\"standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md\",\"quote\":\"A prompt clause that exists to enforce design law\\nneeds provenance and a proof that the clause still causes or prevents the\\nintended behaviour\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md#DESIGN_MODULE%2F11.%20Review\",\"start_line\":2049},{\"end_line\":2214,\"path\":\"standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md\",\"quote\":\"When a project claims functional bias, pure transforms, immutable\\ncarriers, single-owner truth or low-coupling realisation, review\\nexplicitly checks\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md#DESIGN_MODULE%2F11.%20Review%2FFunctional%20realisation%20checklist\",\"start_line\":2212}],\"label\":\"Design review and functional checklist\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:0bfa7a9a55ccb9c21fe73b41be970541","key":174,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:0bfa7a9a55ccb9c21fe73b41be970541\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"Product authority's adoption of an available design profile for a named boundary and, for partial adoption, a named rule family. Inclusion in the selected method cut makes the profile available but does not adopt it or create another adopter.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":2373,\"path\":\"standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md\",\"quote\":\"inclusion in the selected method cut makes the profile available, and only\\nProduct authority adopts it. This profile adds no adopter.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md#DESIGN_MODULE%2F12.%20Adoption%20and%20relations%2FAdoption\",\"start_line\":2372}],\"label\":\"Product adoption of the profile\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:178c7d7d9a8e9d339fe3d75171216d5f","key":175,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:178c7d7d9a8e9d339fe3d75171216d5f\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"The source's allocation of member responsibilities: SPEC_METHOD owns constitutional process, authority flow, repricing and migration; RELEASE owns release cut, Product, install, qualification and version-line promotion evaluation; ODD owns graph-native constructive carrier law; DESIGN_MODULE owns preferred implementation/design module structure; UX adds rendering, state-transition, effect-membrane and AssetSurface-binding discipline for UX surfaces. ASSURANCE module lifecycle confirmation detects sufficient lifecycle signal for building and review, not release or rollout eligibility.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":2419,\"path\":\"standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md\",\"quote\":\"the UX profile ([UX](UX.md)) refines this profile for UX\\nsurfaces with rendering, state-transition and effect-membrane rules and is\\nloaded only when the work realises a UX surface\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md#DESIGN_MODULE%2F12.%20Adoption%20and%20relations%2FRelationship%20to%20other%20members\",\"start_line\":2417}],\"label\":\"Responsibilities of related members\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:e19911b2f9e025ddf9ca3741869cd84a","key":176,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:e19911b2f9e025ddf9ca3741869cd84a\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[\"A runtime realisation is consumer-bound to the ABG role under the graph-execution profile.\"],\"definition\":\"A bound ABG runtime realisation may publish default identity generators, validators and normalisers for its own runtime surfaces and default ODD surface kinds used by default F_D helpers.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":2450,\"path\":\"standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md\",\"quote\":\"the permission is scoped to that role\\nand does not extend to other runtime realisations\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md#DESIGN_MODULE%2F12.%20Adoption%20and%20relations%2FIdentity%20defaults%20from%20a%20bound%20runtime%20realisation\",\"start_line\":2449}],\"label\":\"Role-scoped runtime identity defaults\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:8bd473f512c46558efbc0c97d6a4b7e9","key":177,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:8bd473f512c46558efbc0c97d6a4b7e9\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"A Tier 1 member owning justification and acceptance of claims, evidence, independent assessment, review results, acceptance, realisation conformance and the equivalence ladder, frame and method qualification, and actual-use evidence of adequate attention. It consumes FOUNDATIONS' core results and defines no result values itself.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":9,\"path\":\"standards/EVALUATION.md\",\"quote\":\"[Results](FOUNDATIONS.md#results) own the core result values this member\\nuses; it defines no result values of its own.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/EVALUATION.md#EVALUATION\",\"start_line\":8}],\"label\":\"EVALUATION member\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:68dd606198d8326413b678398e5e1a69","key":178,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:68dd606198d8326413b678398e5e1a69\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"A load-bearing assertion over an exact subject, property and governing basis, with a declared witness relation, excluded nearest weaker property and falsifier. Construction claims about recursive or repeated work distinguish preservation, progress, termination and outcome satisfaction.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":15,\"path\":\"standards/EVALUATION.md\",\"quote\":\"A load-bearing claim names its exact subject, the property claimed, the\\ngoverning basis, the relation between witness and claim, the nearest weaker\\nproperty it excludes, and its falsifier, before a witness is selected.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/EVALUATION.md#EVALUATION%2F1.%20Claims\",\"start_line\":13}],\"label\":\"Load-bearing claim\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:bc7e4c53bced59c7b790eb61fb0c25fa","key":179,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:bc7e4c53bced59c7b790eb61fb0c25fa\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[\"Exact-subject claims are relied on for promotion, closure or release.\",\"Evidence is finite and may observe a weaker subject, another subject or another basis.\",\"A constructor may be probabilistic or otherwise fallible.\",\"Each reliance boundary has a decision owner.\"],\"definition\":\"F6 is the claims, evidence, assessment and acceptance family covering EVALUATION §§1–5. Its instance premises are conditions of governed work, not commitments or consequences of finite capacity alone. Its table traces consequences, rule owners, added policy/domain choices and consumers. P1, P2, P3 and P6 are cited as independent; P0 is recovered with named candidate-output or non-reacquirable-fact premises; P5 is derived from P0 and P6 with the open-world premise, and P4b from P0 and P2 with the step-produced-fact premise.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":71,\"path\":\"standards/EVALUATION.md\",\"quote\":\"They are conditions of the work\\nthis family governs, not commitments, and do not follow from finite\\ncapacity alone.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/EVALUATION.md#EVALUATION%2F1.%20Claims%2FFoundation%20to%20law%3A%20claims%2C%20evidence%2C%20assessment%20and%20acceptance\",\"start_line\":69},{\"end_line\":88,\"path\":\"standards/EVALUATION.md\",\"quote\":\"P5 (derived from P0 and P6, with P0's open-world premise)\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/EVALUATION.md#EVALUATION%2F1.%20Claims%2FFoundation%20to%20law%3A%20claims%2C%20evidence%2C%20assessment%20and%20acceptance\",\"start_line\":88},{\"end_line\":94,\"path\":\"standards/EVALUATION.md\",\"quote\":\"P4b (derived from P0 and P2, with P0's premise that step-produced facts are not re-acquirable)\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/EVALUATION.md#EVALUATION%2F1.%20Claims%2FFoundation%20to%20law%3A%20claims%2C%20evidence%2C%20assessment%20and%20acceptance\",\"start_line\":94}],\"label\":\"Foundation-to-law family F6\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:c069b37d4f1a0f0716eb0d9fe2891726","key":180,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:c069b37d4f1a0f0716eb0d9fe2891726\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"Three distinct bases: semantic basis comprises constitutional and accepted-design relations defining claim meaning; evidence basis comprises exact artifacts, events, logs, tests and observations; state projection is a current view derived from admitted semantic and evidence bases. Four distinct roles define law, supply observations, apply the declared evaluation relation and dispose by decision authority. Structural conformance concerns closed syntax, types, identities, references, bases and mechanically decidable predicates; semantic fidelity concerns meaning and materiality.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":136,\"path\":\"standards/EVALUATION.md\",\"quote\":\"Semantic law defines what an evaluation means;\\nevidence supplies observations; the evaluator applies the declared\\nrelation; decision authority disposes.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/EVALUATION.md#EVALUATION%2F2.%20Separation\",\"start_line\":134}],\"label\":\"Bases, roles and structural/semantic separation\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:82a1c0ef4b3ec237b1b9e89ac75fddb3","key":181,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:82a1c0ef4b3ec237b1b9e89ac75fddb3\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"Assessment independent in authorship and evidence conditions. Constructor self-review remains construction output. Author identity is the party responsible for realised content; actor identity identifies whoever performs an operation and is not authority. Independence is not established by a fresh context or assumed across actor families.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":213,\"path\":\"standards/EVALUATION.md\",\"quote\":\"Authorship is one of the conditions on\\nwhich the independence of an assessment rests; the evidence conditions are\\nthe other\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/EVALUATION.md#EVALUATION%2F3.%20Independent%20assessment\",\"start_line\":211}],\"label\":\"Independent assessment\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:2bdf6340141f53f21c1781855206b707","key":182,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:2bdf6340141f53f21c1781855206b707\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"A review returns one FOUNDATIONS core result per declared predicate actually evaluated, accompanied by exact subject and basis, consulted evidence, consequence-ranked findings with evidence and smallest bounded correction, residual uncertainty and invalidation conditions. A planned but unperformed predicate has no result, unlike an evaluated undecided predicate or required coverage with no planned assessment.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":254,\"path\":\"standards/EVALUATION.md\",\"quote\":\"A declared predicate the review planned and did\\nnot evaluate has no result (FOUNDATIONS §4, Results). The review names it\\nas not performed and reports no core value for it, neither\\n`indeterminate` nor `falsified`, so that conjunction keeps it apart from\\nan undecided predicate and from required coverage that no planned\\nassessment addresses\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/EVALUATION.md#EVALUATION%2F4.%20Review%20results\",\"start_line\":249}],\"label\":\"Review result and absence of evaluation\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:e5950994e1df5b915151a6b066232472","key":183,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:e5950994e1df5b915151a6b066232472\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[\"A review returns findings with technical triage.\"],\"definition\":\"Finding-level, evidence-bound assessment against the exact evaluated claim and basis. Severity is the assessor's consequence grade; priority, current promotion-boundary effect and disposition belong to the decision owner. Triage payload classes complete, indeterminate and not_applicable are neither core results nor dispositions, priorities or lifecycle states.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":282,\"path\":\"standards/EVALUATION.md\",\"quote\":\"The payload classes `complete`,\\n`indeterminate` and `not_applicable` classify the triage only; they are\\nnot new results, dispositions, priorities or lifecycle states\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/EVALUATION.md#EVALUATION%2F4.%20Review%20results%2FResult%20and%20triage%20projection\",\"start_line\":280}],\"label\":\"Technical triage projection\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:89222b77e50c83868d267c878c6103c4","key":184,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:89222b77e50c83868d267c878c6103c4\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"Acceptance is the decision owner's disposition over an unchanged subject, bounded to its named instance and interval. Work-item closure is satisfaction of the item's stated closing condition; review is an input rather than closure.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":315,\"path\":\"standards/EVALUATION.md\",\"quote\":\"A work item closes by the condition it stated, not by a reviewer's approval;\\na reviewer result is an input to closure, never the closure. Green labels,\\ndocument counts, review counts and historical outcomes are not acceptance.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/EVALUATION.md#EVALUATION%2F5.%20Acceptance\",\"start_line\":313}],\"label\":\"Acceptance and work-item closure\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:7995901312b7127d206370b31b7cfb50","key":185,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:7995901312b7127d206370b31b7cfb50\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"A finding is a reported defect against the exact evaluated claim. Blocking current promotion is the decision owner's act over that finding. EVALUATION §5 supplies the shared blocking conditions; profiles and work carriers add only domain triggers.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":340,\"path\":\"standards/EVALUATION.md\",\"quote\":\"This section is the\\none statement of when a finding can block; profiles and work carriers\\nrefer to it and add only their domain triggers.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/EVALUATION.md#EVALUATION%2F5.%20Acceptance%2FWhen%20a%20finding%20blocks%20promotion\",\"start_line\":338}],\"label\":\"Finding-dependent promotion blocking\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:cae7dff6a99951473cac43cb9487326d","key":186,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:cae7dff6a99951473cac43cb9487326d\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"A realisation conforms to specification Σ when its interpreted behaviour satisfies Σ under a declared interpretation contract and independent judgment. Several realisations may conform; sufficiency does not require unique derivation or incumbent equality.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":378,\"path\":\"standards/EVALUATION.md\",\"quote\":\"A realisation aⱼ conforms to a specification Σ when its interpreted behaviour\\nsatisfies Σ under a declared interpretation contract (P1) and an independent\\njudgment (P6). Several realisations may conform to one Σ; sufficiency does\\nnot require unique derivation or equality with an incumbent.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/EVALUATION.md#EVALUATION%2F6.%20Conformance%20of%20realisations\",\"start_line\":375}],\"label\":\"Realisation conformance\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:19e30cf61a7e6ca33b6b4f01e979cf51","key":187,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:19e30cf61a7e6ca33b6b4f01e979cf51\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"Four listed, unordered, mutually non-implying claim kinds: conformance; semantic equivalence of realisations, meaning identical interpreted behaviour on a stated domain including behaviour outside Σ; computational equivalence, meaning the same function at equal cost for declared workloads on architecture H; and categorical equivalence of categories and maps. Semantic equivalence here is not cross-context concept equivalence. Preservation of identities and composition by a map is a further distinct claim.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":385,\"path\":\"standards/EVALUATION.md\",\"quote\":\"the rungs are listed, not ordered, and no rung implies\\nanother. Conformance, semantic equivalence, computational equivalence and\\ncategorical equivalence are separate claims with separate evidence\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/EVALUATION.md#EVALUATION%2F6.%20Conformance%20of%20realisations\",\"start_line\":383}],\"label\":\"Unordered equivalence ladder\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:6d96b75770d3c078aeccf46c41c1bc6f","key":188,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:6d96b75770d3c078aeccf46c41c1bc6f\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"A layered specification is sufficient when a competent actor can derive a conformant next layer from every layer. The test is sufficiency, not unique derivation or determinism; reconstructability requires a correct route, not executing it on every use.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":418,\"path\":\"standards/EVALUATION.md\",\"quote\":\"A specification arranged in layers is sufficient when\\na competent actor can derive a conformant next layer from each layer; the\\nderivation need not be unique, since different realisations may satisfy the\\nsame upper layer, and the test is sufficiency, not determinism.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/EVALUATION.md#EVALUATION%2F6.%20Conformance%20of%20realisations\",\"start_line\":415}],\"label\":\"Layered sufficiency and reconstruction\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:1d08ca4a4088f38ec8f6103c6776ca87","key":189,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:1d08ca4a4088f38ec8f6103c6776ca87\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[\"A task builds or assesses one successor member against its predecessor.\"],\"definition\":\"A reconstruction return separates semantic conservation, demonstrated reduction and mere relocation. Conservation preserves the meaning of a disposed predecessor claim, judged by reading both texts against the disposition. Reduction shows lower cost for the same deciding path on a declared measure through traces of both paths and declared tradeoffs. Relocation moves text between owners or carriers without changed meaning or a traced deciding-path change.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":460,\"path\":\"standards/EVALUATION.md\",\"quote\":\"Demonstrated\\nreduction: a deciding path of the successor costs less than the same path\\nin the predecessor on a declared measure, shown by the trace of both paths\\nwith the declared tradeoffs. Mere relocation: text moved from one owner or\\ncarrier to another without a change in meaning and without a traced\\nchange in any deciding path.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/EVALUATION.md#EVALUATION%2F6.%20Conformance%20of%20realisations%2FReturn%20of%20a%20reconstruction\",\"start_line\":455}],\"label\":\"Three-part reconstruction return\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:acdfc80f32db9748da683d36150a1900","key":190,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:acdfc80f32db9748da683d36150a1900\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"F7 concerns whether realisations, frames and the method are fit for their claims. Its instance premises allow several realisations per specification, fallible constructors and reliance by other actors, and finite qualification cases within declared envelopes. These are work conditions, not commitments or consequences of finite capacity alone. The cited actor-change premise permits reacquisition of declared sources, not private memory.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":481,\"path\":\"standards/EVALUATION.md\",\"quote\":\"Its instance premises are: (a)\\none specification may have several realisations; (b) realisations, frames\\nand the method are made by fallible constructors and relied on by actors\\nwho did not make them; (c) qualification evidence comes from a finite set\\nof cases, run by actors inside declared envelopes.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/EVALUATION.md#EVALUATION%2F6.%20Conformance%20of%20realisations%2FFoundation%20to%20law%3A%20conformance%2C%20equivalence%20and%20qualification\",\"start_line\":473}],\"label\":\"Conformance, equivalence and qualification\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:37fb4b17481814bac5a73cccf5a35e94","key":191,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:37fb4b17481814bac5a73cccf5a35e94\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"Conformance is satisfaction of a specification by interpreted realisation behaviour under a declared interpretation contract and independent judgment. Semantic, computational and categorical equivalence are distinct claims; preservation of identities and composition by a map is a further claim.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":488,\"path\":\"standards/EVALUATION.md\",\"quote\":\"conformance, semantic equivalence, computational equivalence and categorical equivalence are separate claims with separate evidence, and no rung implies another.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/EVALUATION.md#EVALUATION%2F6.%20Conformance%20of%20realisations%2FFoundation%20to%20law%3A%20conformance%2C%20equivalence%20and%20qualification\",\"start_line\":488}],\"label\":\"Conformance and equivalence claims\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:f35cd95bc2a52b766d1979572061b2cf","key":192,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:f35cd95bc2a52b766d1979572061b2cf\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"Layered sufficiency concerns a competent finite actor's ability to derive a conformant next layer from each layer. A reconstruction return distinguishes semantic conservation, demonstrated reduction and mere relocation.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":489,\"path\":\"standards/EVALUATION.md\",\"quote\":\"a layered specification is sufficient when a competent actor can derive a conformant next layer from each layer, not necessarily uniquely.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/EVALUATION.md#EVALUATION%2F6.%20Conformance%20of%20realisations%2FFoundation%20to%20law%3A%20conformance%2C%20equivalence%20and%20qualification\",\"start_line\":489},{\"end_line\":499,\"path\":\"standards/EVALUATION.md\",\"quote\":\"a reconstruction return states semantic conservation, demonstrated reduction and mere relocation as separate claims with separate evidence\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/EVALUATION.md#EVALUATION%2F6.%20Conformance%20of%20realisations%2FFoundation%20to%20law%3A%20conformance%2C%20equivalence%20and%20qualification\",\"start_line\":499}],\"label\":\"Layered sufficiency and reconstruction\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:9b0624c77d9b5a044328250e6c6a92a3","key":193,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:9b0624c77d9b5a044328250e6c6a92a3\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"A conformance case identifies its subject, mechanism, independently specified expected distinction and status. A bounded construction trial additionally declares actor context and total-work bounds.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":497,\"path\":\"standards/EVALUATION.md\",\"quote\":\"a conformance case names its subject, the mechanism under test, an independently specified expected distinction and its status, and a status names what exists.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/EVALUATION.md#EVALUATION%2F6.%20Conformance%20of%20realisations%2FFoundation%20to%20law%3A%20conformance%2C%20equivalence%20and%20qualification\",\"start_line\":497},{\"end_line\":498,\"path\":\"standards/EVALUATION.md\",\"quote\":\"a trial of bounded construction declares its per-actor context cap and total-work budget before each run\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/EVALUATION.md#EVALUATION%2F6.%20Conformance%20of%20realisations%2FFoundation%20to%20law%3A%20conformance%2C%20equivalence%20and%20qualification\",\"start_line\":498}],\"label\":\"Conformance cases and bounded trials\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:b73ca3b72a332e1f5c469f48ede7d11c","key":194,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:b73ca3b72a332e1f5c469f48ede7d11c\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"Document section grouping qualification of frames and qualification of the method; the heading alone adds no test or verdict.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":526,\"path\":\"standards/EVALUATION.md\",\"quote\":\"## 7. Qualification of frames and of the method\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/EVALUATION.md#EVALUATION%2F7.%20Qualification%20of%20frames%20and%20of%20the%20method\",\"start_line\":526}],\"label\":\"Qualification of frames and of the method\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:a317b21a815ed3243d75442184df803b","key":195,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:a317b21a815ed3243d75442184df803b\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"Qualification of a candidate frame in proportion to its claims. Capability includes separately evaluated fit and adequate attention: context fit compares measured selected-representation size with declared capacity; adequate attention concerns evidenced actual use on declared tasks and conditions.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":531,\"path\":\"standards/EVALUATION.md\",\"quote\":\"A candidate frame ([REFERENCE_FRAME](REFERENCE_FRAME.md)) is qualified in\\nproportion to its claims (P6, P2).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/EVALUATION.md#EVALUATION%2F7.%20Qualification%20of%20frames%20and%20of%20the%20method%2FFrame%20qualification\",\"start_line\":530},{\"end_line\":566,\"path\":\"standards/EVALUATION.md\",\"quote\":\"Whether the actor class\\noperates the frame adequately is adequate attention\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/EVALUATION.md#EVALUATION%2F7.%20Qualification%20of%20frames%20and%20of%20the%20method%2FFrame%20qualification\",\"start_line\":565}],\"label\":\"Frame qualification, fit and adequate attention\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:6a2c32a018781528793f87b832b7cdf2","key":196,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:6a2c32a018781528793f87b832b7cdf2\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"Method self-qualification uses the ordinary qualification process, the work boundary, construction/assessment relation and layered sufficiency. Its population is every claimed function and failure relation. It includes qualification of changed derived guidance and a recoverability benchmark using fresh actors and published documents.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":588,\"path\":\"standards/EVALUATION.md\",\"quote\":\"The method is qualified the way it qualifies anything else. Qualification\\nof generic method sufficiency consumes the work boundary (FOUNDATIONS §2),\\nthe construction and assessment relation of ACTIVATION §1 and the layered\\nsufficiency of §6; it creates no second process.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/EVALUATION.md#EVALUATION%2F7.%20Qualification%20of%20frames%20and%20of%20the%20method%2FMethod%20self-qualification\",\"start_line\":585}],\"label\":\"Method self-qualification\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:495aa231497a5ecc0c35bbb322f4f213","key":197,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:495aa231497a5ecc0c35bbb322f4f213\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"Optional tier-3 operational profile mapping Executive, Worker, Reviewer and specialist frames onto tiers 1 and 2. It owns its direct-entry additions, empirical revision boundary, frame mappings and allocation explanation, specialist catalogue, engagement procedure, Worker value readings and adoption/configuration/qualification/closure records. It imports, without redefining, FOUNDATIONS, REFERENCE_FRAME, ACTIVATION, EVALUATION, SPEC_METHOD, PRODUCT_DEFINITION and ASSURANCE.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":15,\"path\":\"standards/EXECUTIVE_BASELINE.md\",\"quote\":\"An operational\\nprofile owns only its own bindings, the terms and choices it adds for its\\noperation.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/EXECUTIVE_BASELINE.md#EXECUTIVE_BASELINE\",\"start_line\":7}],\"label\":\"EXECUTIVE_BASELINE\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:eb7981268a5454854862747e722df76d","key":198,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:eb7981268a5454854862747e722df76d\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"Canonical engagement projection: existing authority, complete method basis including REFERENCE_FRAME, exact Product or Product-chain outcome/workspace and known evaluations/dependencies/residuals support sufficient direct Worker entry or material coordination. Coordination locks outcome/basis and finite readiness, obtains applicable Worker/specialist and required Reviewer evaluations, consumes closed results, applicable triage and declared conjunction, applies bounded decisions, records results and next lawful action, updates basis/coverage/residuals/frontier, and repeats or stops.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":65,\"path\":\"standards/EXECUTIVE_BASELINE.md\",\"quote\":\"  -> a sufficient direct Worker activation, or coordination where material\\n  -> when coordinated: Executive locks outcome and basis, holds a finite ready frontier\\n  -> Worker and the applicable specialist evaluations; Reviewer only where required\\n  -> closed results, technical triage where applicable, declared conjunction\\n  -> existing bounded decision authority, result recording, next lawful action\\n  -> updated basis, coverage, residuals and frontier\\n  -> repeat or stop\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/EXECUTIVE_BASELINE.md#EXECUTIVE_BASELINE%2F1.%20Canonical%20compression\",\"start_line\":59}],\"label\":\"Canonical engagement projection\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:363fd61e6242c3dcc4ebf0264109f1a4","key":199,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:363fd61e6242c3dcc4ebf0264109f1a4\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"Ownership boundary distinguishing pure frame principles, optional profile mappings, the Product-binding relation and each adopting Product's concrete Project Reference-Frame Basis. Execution, result, assessment, assurance, design, identity and release rules remain with their cited owners.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":115,\"path\":\"standards/EXECUTIVE_BASELINE.md\",\"quote\":\"REFERENCE_FRAME owns the pure frame principles; this member owns the\\noptional Executive, Worker, Reviewer and specialist mappings; PRODUCT_DEFINITION\\n§7 owns the Product-binding relation, and each adopting Product's authority\\nowns its concrete Project Reference-Frame Basis. The testing-frame\\nmappings this profile uses are ASSURANCE's.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/EXECUTIVE_BASELINE.md#EXECUTIVE_BASELINE%2F2.%20Status%20and%20authority%20boundary\",\"start_line\":111}],\"label\":\"Profile ownership boundary\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:491378d3b3b4015b2d90d884ace55ff3","key":200,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:491378d3b3b4015b2d90d884ace55ff3\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"Direct entry and coordinated engagement are conditional branches under ACTIVATION. In the executive configuration the entering frame is Worker/Writer and the coordinator is Executive; a name creates no review obligation.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":157,\"path\":\"standards/EXECUTIVE_BASELINE.md\",\"quote\":\"Where the\\nexecutive configuration is selected, the directly entering frame is Worker\\n(Writer) and the coordinating frame Executive. A role or frame name alone\\ncreates no review obligation either (P0, P6).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/EXECUTIVE_BASELINE.md#EXECUTIVE_BASELINE%2F3.%20Engagement%20applicability\",\"start_line\":154}],\"label\":\"Engagement applicability\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:c2d16ed93a567939f5baae9786faa7d7","key":201,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:c2d16ed93a567939f5baae9786faa7d7\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"F16's foundation-to-law trace separates commitments, imported consequences, adopted instance premises and profile/Product choices. It imports F1 frames/context, F2 transitions/configuration, F3 results/combination, F4 work-state/reuse, F5 cost, F6 claims/assessment, F15 lineage and F13 carriers. P0 is reported recovered; P1, P2, P3, P4a and P6 independent; P4b derived from P0/P2 with non-reacquirable step facts; P5 derived from P0/P6 with the open-world premise. I1 separates bounded changes from delivery attention, I2 locates every decision grant in existing authority, and I3 assumes finite, fallible, possibly probabilistic actors. Instance premises apply when this configuration is selected, not as deductions from foundations.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":218,\"path\":\"standards/EXECUTIVE_BASELINE.md\",\"quote\":\"Its instance premises hold where\\nthe executive configuration is selected; they are adopted with it and do\\nnot follow from the foundations (P1, P6):\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/EXECUTIVE_BASELINE.md#EXECUTIVE_BASELINE%2F3.%20Engagement%20applicability%2FFoundation%20to%20law\",\"start_line\":216}],\"label\":\"Engagement foundation-to-law trace\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:cea8ae141dfb19e4eca4c429eafae830","key":202,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:cea8ae141dfb19e4eca4c429eafae830\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"Delivery practice, observed failures and repeated Product drift provide evidence for frame selection, qualification and revision. Resets, repair loops, moving subjects, proof masking and duplicated authority are possible misfit signals, not verdicts or a universal architecture.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":320,\"path\":\"standards/EXECUTIVE_BASELINE.md\",\"quote\":\"They justify re-evaluation;\\nthey neither identify one universal architecture nor give a precedent\\nsemantic authority (P6, P5).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/EXECUTIVE_BASELINE.md#EXECUTIVE_BASELINE%2F4.%20Empirical%20revision%20boundary\",\"start_line\":318}],\"label\":\"Empirical revision boundary\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:351533b059a03eff20c93052cff8b725","key":203,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:351533b059a03eff20c93052cff8b725\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"Document grouping for the profile's terms; the heading alone does not define additional terms.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":327,\"path\":\"standards/EXECUTIVE_BASELINE.md\",\"quote\":\"## 5. Profile terms\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/EXECUTIVE_BASELINE.md#EXECUTIVE_BASELINE%2F5.%20Profile%20terms\",\"start_line\":327}],\"label\":\"Profile terms\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:674c4b1f0b031111dcbbcb0a999c7374","key":204,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:674c4b1f0b031111dcbbcb0a999c7374\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"A frame whose evaluation family concerns selecting, constructing, assessing or disposing governed work. Executive, Worker and Reviewer are this profile's engagement frames.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":333,\"path\":\"standards/EXECUTIVE_BASELINE.md\",\"quote\":\"An engagement frame is a frame (REFERENCE_FRAME §1) whose evaluation family\\nconcerns selecting, constructing, assessing or disposing governed work.\\nExecutive, Worker and Reviewer are this profile's engagement frames (P1).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/EXECUTIVE_BASELINE.md#EXECUTIVE_BASELINE%2F5.%20Profile%20terms%2FEngagement%20frame\",\"start_line\":331}],\"label\":\"Engagement frame\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:569b067e2c41ed731fc3f20b96647d5c","key":205,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:569b067e2c41ed731fc3f20b96647d5c\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"An activated Product, requirement, design, identity, release, domain, implementation, test, operational, historical or capability frame needed by an engagement evaluation.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":339,\"path\":\"standards/EXECUTIVE_BASELINE.md\",\"quote\":\"A specialist frame is an activated Product, requirement, design, identity,\\nrelease, domain, implementation, test, operational, historical or\\ncapability frame that one engagement evaluation needs.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/EXECUTIVE_BASELINE.md#EXECUTIVE_BASELINE%2F5.%20Profile%20terms%2FSpecialist%20frame\",\"start_line\":337}],\"label\":\"Specialist frame\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:e93730bb10784ead2fad3cb8fa00816d","key":206,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:e93730bb10784ead2fad3cb8fa00816d\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"Reusable evaluation-family archetype preserving a recurring distinction. The twelve available families are Product, Product Composition, Design, Design Component, Public Boundary, Entity, Operator, Owner, Effect, Reuse/Foundation, Install and Proof. They are not mandatory actors, stages, components, services, files or runtime types.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":348,\"path\":\"standards/EXECUTIVE_BASELINE.md\",\"quote\":\"A generic specialist-frame family is a reusable evaluation-family archetype\\nof this profile (§11).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/EXECUTIVE_BASELINE.md#EXECUTIVE_BASELINE%2F5.%20Profile%20terms%2FGeneric%20specialist-frame%20family\",\"start_line\":347},{\"end_line\":84,\"path\":\"standards/EXECUTIVE_BASELINE.md\",\"quote\":\"Product, Product Composition, Design, Design Component, Public Boundary,\\nEntity, Operator, Owner, Effect, Reuse/Foundation, Install and Proof.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/EXECUTIVE_BASELINE.md#EXECUTIVE_BASELINE%2F1.%20Canonical%20compression\",\"start_line\":79}],\"label\":\"Generic specialist-frame family\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:2a23e5bb7457e62b35e4b7a587c5c87d","key":207,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:2a23e5bb7457e62b35e4b7a587c5c87d\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"Testing frame, authoritative Product path and material combinatorial complexity are imported tier-2 terms owned by ASSURANCE §7; this profile adds nothing to their definitions.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":363,\"path\":\"standards/EXECUTIVE_BASELINE.md\",\"quote\":\"Testing frame, authoritative Product path and material combinatorial\\ncomplexity are tier-2 terms defined in ASSURANCE §7. This profile uses them\\nas defined there and adds nothing to them (P1).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/EXECUTIVE_BASELINE.md#EXECUTIVE_BASELINE%2F5.%20Profile%20terms%2FTerms%20owned%20by%20ASSURANCE\",\"start_line\":361}],\"label\":\"ASSURANCE-owned terms\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:bac22443a8ebc6c8a3471d29babef1a3","key":208,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:bac22443a8ebc6c8a3471d29babef1a3\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"Frame selecting or confirming bounded activation configuration and consuming closed Worker/Reviewer results under existing project decision authority. It holds the complete Product view and current MVP/release mandate needed for priority, disposition and next authorised action; it is not a universal semantic owner, controller, manager service or runtime observer.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":372,\"path\":\"standards/EXECUTIVE_BASELINE.md\",\"quote\":\"Executive is this profile's label for the frame that selects or confirms\\nthe bounded activation configuration and consumes closed Worker and\\nReviewer results under existing project decision authority.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/EXECUTIVE_BASELINE.md#EXECUTIVE_BASELINE%2F5.%20Profile%20terms%2FExecutive\",\"start_line\":367}],\"label\":\"Executive\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:85c4a097d7c23e71690337215dd1fa32","key":209,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:85c4a097d7c23e71690337215dd1fa32\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"ACTIVATION's constructor role activated as a frame, responsible for construction and self-review within exact intake and inherited operation authority.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":385,\"path\":\"standards/EXECUTIVE_BASELINE.md\",\"quote\":\"Worker is this profile's label for the constructor role of ACTIVATION §1\\nactivated as a frame. It owns construction and self-review inside its exact\\nintake, through the operation authority inherited from the governing work\\nrelation.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/EXECUTIVE_BASELINE.md#EXECUTIVE_BASELINE%2F5.%20Profile%20terms%2FWorker\",\"start_line\":382}],\"label\":\"Worker\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:a470d1aba69b9afe0d76c5f3e25bf466","key":210,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:a470d1aba69b9afe0d76c5f3e25bf466\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"Independent live-surface evaluation activated as a frame and consumed by ACTIVATION's assessment relation, governed by EVALUATION's independence, traceability, assurance-boundary and qualification-freeze rules. It evaluates one exact subject and returns a closed result with evidence-bound technical triage when a finding exists.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":395,\"path\":\"standards/EXECUTIVE_BASELINE.md\",\"quote\":\"It\\nevaluates one exact subject and returns a closed result, with evidence-bound\\ntechnical triage when a finding exists.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/EXECUTIVE_BASELINE.md#EXECUTIVE_BASELINE%2F5.%20Profile%20terms%2FReviewer\",\"start_line\":393}],\"label\":\"Reviewer\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:bceb0794d7f53e7c746942b7b8e1a769","key":211,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:bceb0794d7f53e7c746942b7b8e1a769\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"Technical triage assesses one finding against its exact claim and basis. Severity grades manifested consequence; priority orders response against Product outcome, likelihood/exposure, mandate, reversibility, dependencies, delay cost and capacity. Current-boundary effect records blocks, requires narrowing, or may remain an explicit residual. These are distinct from the frame result and disposition; boundary effect has no core value or independent deciding force.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":443,\"path\":\"standards/EXECUTIVE_BASELINE.md\",\"quote\":\"Current-boundary effect is the Executive's recorded determination of what\\none finding does to the current promotion boundary: it blocks it, requires\\nnarrowing it, or may remain an explicit residual. It is a decision\\nprojection, a state this profile declares, not a result and not a\\ndisposition (§8)\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/EXECUTIVE_BASELINE.md#EXECUTIVE_BASELINE%2F5.%20Profile%20terms%2FTechnical%20triage%2C%20severity%2C%20priority%20and%20boundary%20effect\",\"start_line\":439}],\"label\":\"Technical triage and decision projections\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:5126ced26ec459f2f807d8d313977e1e","key":212,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:5126ced26ec459f2f807d8d313977e1e\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[\"A Worker activation has succeeded.\"],\"definition\":\"Worker's closed output to its declared consumer, which is Executive in the coordinated branch. Its five construction-availability carriers refine the predicate that a candidate is available; ACTIVATION owns their causes and total, exclusive core-value mapping. They are neither new dispositions, assessment nor acceptance.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":462,\"path\":\"standards/EXECUTIVE_BASELINE.md\",\"quote\":\"A work result is the Worker's closed output to its declared consumer; in\\nthe coordinated branch that consumer is the Executive. It exists only after\\na successful Worker activation.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/EXECUTIVE_BASELINE.md#EXECUTIVE_BASELINE%2F5.%20Profile%20terms%2FWork%20result\",\"start_line\":460}],\"label\":\"Work result\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:8df660b9cabda7f7412953117071e6f3","key":213,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:8df660b9cabda7f7412953117071e6f3\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"Subject identity required by transition evidence and review traceability. Generic method qualification freezes the construction result before material reference exposure under its applicable rule; elsewhere an immutable identity or equivalent exact-subject relation stabilises the subject sufficiently for the assessment. No lifecycle state named frozen is created.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":524,\"path\":\"standards/EXECUTIVE_BASELINE.md\",\"quote\":\"Elsewhere this profile stabilises the review subject through an immutable\\nidentity or an equivalent exact-subject relation sufficient for the claimed\\nassessment. The profile creates no new lifecycle state named `frozen` (P3,\\nP6).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/EXECUTIVE_BASELINE.md#EXECUTIVE_BASELINE%2F5.%20Profile%20terms%2FExact%20candidate\",\"start_line\":521}],\"label\":\"Exact candidate\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:e0e2d9ea94128bfd8635404e6a168219","key":214,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:e0e2d9ea94128bfd8635404e6a168219\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[\"The Product-owned Project Reference-Frame Basis adopts this profile.\"],\"definition\":\"Projection consuming that basis and recording the selected profile mapping, exact outcome, actor envelopes, evidence coordinates and revision conditions additional to the Product binding. It defines no second basis and creates no authority.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":533,\"path\":\"standards/EXECUTIVE_BASELINE.md\",\"quote\":\"Where that basis adopts\\nthis profile, the projection records the selected profile mapping, exact\\noutcome, actor envelopes, evidence coordinates and revision conditions\\nneeded in addition to the Product binding (§16). It is not a second\\nframe-basis definition and mints none of the authority it projects (P6).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/EXECUTIVE_BASELINE.md#EXECUTIVE_BASELINE%2F5.%20Profile%20terms%2FBaseline-adoption%20projection\",\"start_line\":529}],\"label\":\"Baseline-adoption projection\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:d5f7adfbbb083f469f0de4e02b21a127","key":215,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:d5f7adfbbb083f469f0de4e02b21a127\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"Document grouping for Executive attention, evaluation and action; the heading alone adds no operation or authority.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":535,\"path\":\"standards/EXECUTIVE_BASELINE.md\",\"quote\":\"## 6. Executive attention, evaluation and action\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/EXECUTIVE_BASELINE.md#EXECUTIVE_BASELINE%2F6.%20Executive%20attention%2C%20evaluation%20and%20action\",\"start_line\":535}],\"label\":\"Executive attention, evaluation and action\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:1e906ab4002640bb16a98dfd2f40993e","key":216,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:1e906ab4002640bb16a98dfd2f40993e\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"U is the durable inventory of known material evaluations lacking an applicable closed result on the current basis; M is its selected finite dependency-ready part. The frontier is the readiness relation. The closed-result ledger records returned results, predicates, subject, basis, evidence and residuals. An applicable stop is an admitted work stop, including authority, capability or resource limits.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":584,\"path\":\"standards/EXECUTIVE_BASELINE.md\",\"quote\":\"`U` is the durable inventory of known material evaluations that do not have\\na closed result applicable to the current basis. `M` is the finite,\\ndependency-ready part selected for the next activation. The frontier is the\\ninventory's readiness relation; the closed-result ledger records the\\nreturned results, their predicates, subject, basis, evidence and residuals.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/EXECUTIVE_BASELINE.md#EXECUTIVE_BASELINE%2F6.%20Executive%20attention%2C%20evaluation%20and%20action%2FAttention%20cycle\",\"start_line\":580}],\"label\":\"Attention cycle, frontier and ledger\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:9eb4e5b2722bf42c8e9e4e78ac118aac","key":217,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:9eb4e5b2722bf42c8e9e4e78ac118aac\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"Five checks before activation and disposition: outcome lock preserves Goal/Product outcome, boundary/re-entry class, mandate and triage policy; basis lock requires exact current subject, authority, dependency, configuration, topology, evidence, time and candidate coordinates; Product-role lock preserves distinct lineage identities and exact Install binding; authority lock preserves semantic, evaluation, operation, decision, acceptance and publication grants/owners; coverage-and-return lock requires each material evaluation/interaction closed or explicit residual and each consumed result on its declared return relation.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":680,\"path\":\"standards/EXECUTIVE_BASELINE.md\",\"quote\":\"Before activation and before disposition, the Executive revalidates five\\nlocks (P3, P6, P2):\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/EXECUTIVE_BASELINE.md#EXECUTIVE_BASELINE%2F6.%20Executive%20attention%2C%20evaluation%20and%20action%2FDrift%20locks\",\"start_line\":679}],\"label\":\"Drift locks\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:d71326ac32b31ff5e9a0324a726e4bfc","key":218,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:d71326ac32b31ff5e9a0324a726e4bfc\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"A basis for one Product or an explicit directed Product chain, distinguishing every mutable Source Project, current Product Definition, exact candidate checkpoint, Release Cut, Product, Install, Artifact, Development Product, dependent Product and composition edge. Each Development Product role binds one exact Install; each edge records source/target roles, governing authority/contracts, lifecycle, evidence boundary, refusal and invalidation.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":715,\"path\":\"standards/EXECUTIVE_BASELINE.md\",\"quote\":\"Each Development Product role binds one exact underlying\\nInstall identity. Each edge names its source and target roles, its governing\\nauthority and contracts, its lifecycle, its evidence boundary, its refusal\\nand its invalidation\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/EXECUTIVE_BASELINE.md#EXECUTIVE_BASELINE%2F6.%20Executive%20attention%2C%20evaluation%20and%20action%2FProduct-chain%20basis\",\"start_line\":712}],\"label\":\"Product-chain basis\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:3b84039784294dad7e5f95fd3a5d0549","key":219,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:3b84039784294dad7e5f95fd3a5d0549\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"Distinct structures are authority precedence for work/configuration/disposition/re-entry, temporal/evidence communication carrying packets/results, and frame topology for disjointness, overlap, conjunction, translation and composition. Evaluation independence and Reviewer assurance independence remain separate activation relations. Structures may align when warranted but never become one hierarchy. One activated evaluation combines an engagement frame, material specialist frames, exact subject/basis and capable actor.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":749,\"path\":\"standards/EXECUTIVE_BASELINE.md\",\"quote\":\"3. frame topology records disjointness, overlap, conjunction, translation\\n   or composition among the evaluations actually used (REFERENCE_FRAME §7),\\n   while evaluation independence and Reviewer assurance independence stay\\n   separate activation relations.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/EXECUTIVE_BASELINE.md#EXECUTIVE_BASELINE%2F7.%20Non-hierarchical%20frame%20configuration\",\"start_line\":746}],\"label\":\"Non-hierarchical frame configuration\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:668afb84e5d220dd4674a57a384862c4","key":220,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:668afb84e5d220dd4674a57a384862c4\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[\"Selected by existing authority where the allocation fits the task.\"],\"definition\":\"Configuration allocating construction to Worker, specialised as Writer for documents/records; required assessment to Reviewer; and cross-task coordination and bounded disposition to Executive. It fits successive bounded tasks needing separate construction and delivery attention. Finite actor contexts respectively concern one causal cone, one exact claim/evidence, and outcome/frontier/closed-result ledger. It is one lawful configuration, not the method default or a universal role inventory.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":787,\"path\":\"standards/EXECUTIVE_BASELINE.md\",\"quote\":\"It is\\none configuration, selected where it fits the task, not an inventory of\\nroles that all work needs.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/EXECUTIVE_BASELINE.md#EXECUTIVE_BASELINE%2F7.%20Non-hierarchical%20frame%20configuration%2FThe%20executive%20configuration\",\"start_line\":782}],\"label\":\"The executive configuration\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:f6ecf4a769d282df4ea3c82a852c0588","key":221,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:f6ecf4a769d282df4ea3c82a852c0588\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"Profile-selected delivery strategy using the smallest real runnable supported-entry-to-material-outcome path through selected composition. Early end-to-end feedback trades against later widening; no superiority over other configurations' lawful strategies is claimed.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":890,\"path\":\"standards/EXECUTIVE_BASELINE.md\",\"quote\":\"The Executive sequences delivery around a steel thread: the smallest real,\\nrunnable path from a supported Product entry to a material outcome through\\nthe selected composition.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/EXECUTIVE_BASELINE.md#EXECUTIVE_BASELINE%2F8.%20Derived%20Executive%20frame%2FSteel-thread%20delivery\",\"start_line\":885}],\"label\":\"Steel-thread delivery\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:82f113a16ea802824461602cdcb694b0","key":222,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:82f113a16ea802824461602cdcb694b0\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"Finite Worker evaluation of whether the exact authorised outcome can be constructed through the smallest coherent causal cone while preserving every affected governing relation and disposing of competing paths. Its basis is sufficient ACTIVATION §1 intake and, where applicable, accepted design-to-execution basis. Its manifold includes affected entities, lifecycles, transformations, authorities, capabilities, algorithms, inputs, outputs, dependencies, interaction seams, failure boundaries and proof obligations. Coordinates bind activation, checkpoint, workspace, inputs, dependencies, configuration, actor envelope, outputs, candidate and evidence. Evidence includes live implementation, tests and their source, analysis, generated artifacts, claimed installed or operational behaviour, reconstruction, mutations and transition evidence. Required competence covers method, domain, implementation, tools, access and finite context.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":935,\"path\":\"standards/EXECUTIVE_BASELINE.md\",\"quote\":\"| evaluation family | Can the exact authorised outcome be constructed through the smallest coherent causal cone while preserving every affected governing relation and disposing of competing paths? |\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/EXECUTIVE_BASELINE.md#EXECUTIVE_BASELINE%2F9.%20Derived%20Worker%20frame\",\"start_line\":928}],\"label\":\"Derived Worker frame\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:ab9ace3a757b796239f24bcaa97089ea","key":223,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:ab9ace3a757b796239f24bcaa97089ea\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"Bounded Reviewer evaluation of exact claimed subject and basis, satisfaction of applicable method and project relations, competing authority, proof masking, composition boundaries, and evidence-bound severity and technical implications. Its intake includes candidate, claim, governing authorities, scope, exclusions, evidence population, Product-selected severity scale, review carrier and independence conditions. Its manifold includes causal producers and consumers, authority seams, competing paths, claimed failure/recovery/installed/reconstruction surfaces, test and fixture semantics, historical counterexamples and supportable technical triage. Coordinates include candidate, source basis, authority revision, configuration, dependency, evidence population, severity scale, installed subject, review time and Reviewer identity. Evidence is independently acquired from material live authority, implementation, tests, artifacts, history, operations, mutations, replay, reconstruction and reproduced observations. Competence includes method, domain, implementation, assurance, technical triage, tools, access, context, counterexample search and independence.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":970,\"path\":\"standards/EXECUTIVE_BASELINE.md\",\"quote\":\"| evaluation family | Is this the exact claimed subject and basis? Does it satisfy the applicable method and project relations without competing authority, proof masking or an unevaluated composition boundary? For each finding, which evidence-bound severity and technical implications follow? |\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/EXECUTIVE_BASELINE.md#EXECUTIVE_BASELINE%2F10.%20Derived%20Reviewer%20frame\",\"start_line\":963}],\"label\":\"Derived Reviewer frame\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:7aa04f0e75b58f269a74a0246551af0f","key":224,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:7aa04f0e75b58f269a74a0246551af0f\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[\"The coordinated branch is selected.\"],\"definition\":\"The profile's bounded assessor or proxy and decision owner: consumes closed results and technical triage against current Product and MVP or release mandates, assigns priority and promotion-boundary effect, and applies an existing disposition within its grant.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1279,\"path\":\"standards/EXECUTIVE_BASELINE.md\",\"quote\":\"The Executive verifies that every consumed result is still bound to the\\ncurrent subject and basis, revalidates the complete Product view and the\\ncurrent MVP or release mandate, applies any declared result conjunction\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/EXECUTIVE_BASELINE.md#EXECUTIVE_BASELINE%2F12.%20Complete%20engagement%20transition%2F7.%20Executive%20disposes%20and%20checkpoints\",\"start_line\":1273}],\"label\":\"Executive in the coordinated branch\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:a1d9192a9add8672ac09f1e82f9d892c","key":225,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:a1d9192a9add8672ac09f1e82f9d892c\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[\"Lawful Worker activation has occurred.\"],\"definition\":\"Exactly one closed Worker result: candidate_ready(exact_subject, transition_evidence, residuals), refused(reason, authority, evidence), incomplete(residuals, evidence, stop_basis), or re_entry_requested(owner, material_relation, evidence). The material relation in re_entry_requested includes its cause, authority or basis. Each variant maps to exactly one core value for the predicate 'a candidate is available'; individual Worker evaluations retain their own core results. The displayed notation is explanatory and mandates no schema.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1184,\"path\":\"standards/EXECUTIVE_BASELINE.md\",\"quote\":\"  = candidate_ready(exact_subject, transition_evidence, residuals)\\n  | refused(reason, authority, evidence)\\n  | incomplete(residuals, evidence, stop_basis)\\n  | re_entry_requested(owner, material_relation, evidence)\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/EXECUTIVE_BASELINE.md#EXECUTIVE_BASELINE%2F12.%20Complete%20engagement%20transition%2F3.%20Worker%20returns%20to%20Executive\",\"start_line\":1173},{\"end_line\":937,\"path\":\"standards/EXECUTIVE_BASELINE.md\",\"quote\":\"each evaluation the Worker performed keeps its own core result\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/EXECUTIVE_BASELINE.md#EXECUTIVE_BASELINE%2F9.%20Derived%20Worker%20frame\",\"start_line\":937}],\"label\":\"WorkerResult\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:ee1b3728d887e6a5db6e18271a927bad","key":226,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:ee1b3728d887e6a5db6e18271a927bad\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[\"Activation detects a known capability, authority, subject, basis or topology mismatch.\"],\"definition\":\"activation_refusal is returned by the activation relation directly to the Executive, with the cause and the core value assigned by REFERENCE_FRAME §5. No Worker frame is active and no Worker evaluation or Worker result exists for that failed activation.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1164,\"path\":\"standards/EXECUTIVE_BASELINE.md\",\"quote\":\"If activation detects a known capability, authority, subject, basis or\\ntopology mismatch, it returns `activation_refusal` directly to the\\nExecutive\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/EXECUTIVE_BASELINE.md#EXECUTIVE_BASELINE%2F12.%20Complete%20engagement%20transition%2F2.%20Executive%20activates%20Worker\",\"start_line\":1159}],\"label\":\"Activation refusal\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:de33d953ef86a7c2be96a9c8d96ca5fa","key":227,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:de33d953ef86a7c2be96a9c8d96ca5fa\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"One closed Reviewer evaluation in the shape owned by EVALUATION §4: frame and activation identity; exact subject, basis, claim, scope, exclusions and evaluated population; Reviewer actor and independence; acquired evidence and ordinary assurance path; core result; findings, counterexamples and adjacent observations; supportable finding-level affected claim, severity, causal assessment and confidence, blast radius, workaround, repair complexity, regression risk and residual uncertainty; invalidation conditions and applicable re-entry owner. Its triage projects over the result algebra; a recommendation is evidence only.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1262,\"path\":\"standards/EXECUTIVE_BASELINE.md\",\"quote\":\"The Reviewer returns one closed evaluation in the shape of EVALUATION §4,\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/EXECUTIVE_BASELINE.md#EXECUTIVE_BASELINE%2F12.%20Complete%20engagement%20transition%2F6.%20Reviewer%20returns%20to%20Executive\",\"start_line\":1249}],\"label\":\"Closed review result\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:7afbe7f5297c074ec9d4d63e0240a1f4","key":228,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:7afbe7f5297c074ec9d4d63e0240a1f4\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"Exactly one authorised disposition: accept, local_repair, re_enter or reject. The disposition is the acceptance result; candidate_ready and a satisfied review are not acceptance. ACTIVATION §3 and §5 own disposition semantics, accepted checkpoint and next already-authorised bounded action.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1284,\"path\":\"standards/EXECUTIVE_BASELINE.md\",\"quote\":\"The disposition\\nis the acceptance result; neither `candidate_ready` nor a satisfied review\\nresult is acceptance\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/EXECUTIVE_BASELINE.md#EXECUTIVE_BASELINE%2F12.%20Complete%20engagement%20transition%2F7.%20Executive%20disposes%20and%20checkpoints\",\"start_line\":1282}],\"label\":\"Disposition and acceptance result\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:77d30851030c0160e2eef6173a7ceb06","key":229,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:77d30851030c0160e2eef6173a7ceb06\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[\"The profile's generic set is adopted for Product work.\"],\"definition\":\"Twelve non-hierarchical, potentially overlapping evaluation archetypes in urn:stdo:bounded-context:reference-frame-evaluation, owned by REFERENCE_FRAME under the selected basis. They are not complete frame declarations, components, actors or runtime objects. Same-spelled Product, Owner, Entity, Operator, Install and other concepts in other contexts remain distinct.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1025,\"path\":\"standards/EXECUTIVE_BASELINE.md\",\"quote\":\"Each\\nrow is an evaluation archetype, not a complete frame declaration\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/EXECUTIVE_BASELINE.md#EXECUTIVE_BASELINE%2F11.%20Derived%20generic%20specialist%20frame%20set\",\"start_line\":1012}],\"label\":\"Generic specialist frame families\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c