n and revision.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1487,\"path\":\"standards/EXECUTIVE_BASELINE.md\",\"quote\":\"A project may define different frames, names, overlaps, sequences and actor\\nbindings.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/EXECUTIVE_BASELINE.md#EXECUTIVE_BASELINE%2F16.%20Adoption%20or%20project-defined%20configuration%2FDefine%20a%20project%20configuration\",\"start_line\":1469}],\"label\":\"Project-defined configuration\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:28256ef3aca6996af0b7c43465583b7b","key":255,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:28256ef3aca6996af0b7c43465583b7b\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[\"The baseline is adopted.\"],\"definition\":\"Profile-specific template additions to the Product Definition §7 basis and §16 adoption record: profile identity; role declarations or acquisition references; role capability, authority and independence bindings; Product-selected severity and priority scales, cutoff, hard stops and triage relation; referenced work-to-core mapping and each refinement's parent core value; twelve-family dispositions; testing claims, topology, populations, scenario matrix, oracles and required/forbidden authoritative paths; activation refusal, closed-result, conjunction and return relations; qualification evidence and residuals.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1668,\"path\":\"standards/EXECUTIVE_BASELINE.md\",\"quote\":\"# Executive Baseline Adoption Additions\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/EXECUTIVE_BASELINE.md#EXECUTIVE_BASELINE%2F19.%20Baseline-specific%20basis%20and%20activation%20additions%2FProject-basis%20additions\",\"start_line\":1650}],\"label\":\"Executive Baseline Adoption Additions template\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:a601044bc31703ab025ff339f4d17598","key":256,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:a601044bc31703ab025ff339f4d17598\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"Qualification of the profile and its declared composition with exact REFERENCE_FRAME basis through EVALUATION §7 frame qualification and method self-qualification. No new protocol or peer authority is created. Pure-method trials do not prove this profile; profile trials do not prove the complete method function population. Claims are limited to evaluated frame revisions, actor envelopes, result branches and evidence populations.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1548,\"path\":\"standards/EXECUTIVE_BASELINE.md\",\"quote\":\"A valid pure-method trial does not prove this profile, and a\\nvalid profile trial does not prove the method's complete function\\npopulation\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/EXECUTIVE_BASELINE.md#EXECUTIVE_BASELINE%2F18.%20Profile%20qualification\",\"start_line\":1546}],\"label\":\"Profile qualification\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:4cf9bc8bd98b23b5fc036cefad9bae4d","key":257,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:4cf9bc8bd98b23b5fc036cefad9bae4d\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"Observation-to-first-diagnosis routing table. Its classifications guide evaluation and do not predetermine verdicts.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1683,\"path\":\"standards/EXECUTIVE_BASELINE.md\",\"quote\":\"The table routes evaluation; it does not predetermine a verdict\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/EXECUTIVE_BASELINE.md#EXECUTIVE_BASELINE%2F20.%20Failure%20classification\",\"start_line\":1683}],\"label\":\"Failure classification\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:f8dada96e1fc49226a473a335e1d40b9","key":258,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:f8dada96e1fc49226a473a335e1d40b9\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[\"An exact selected outcome and engagement branch determine applicability.\"],\"definition\":\"Condition-based closure owned by TICKETS §7, applied to the selected branch. Available frames and testing families do not by themselves make claims applicable. A review event or closed indeterminate result cannot satisfy an unresolved obligation; indeterminate never maps to satisfied. A project-defined configuration may close against REFERENCE_FRAME, complete selected method and existing project authorities without claiming this optional profile.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1804,\"path\":\"standards/EXECUTIVE_BASELINE.md\",\"quote\":\"a closed\\n`indeterminate` result or a review event does not satisfy an unresolved\\nobligation\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/EXECUTIVE_BASELINE.md#EXECUTIVE_BASELINE%2F22.%20Closure\",\"start_line\":1800}],\"label\":\"Applicable condition-based closure\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:6ec8a2077a8e4407dbae4ef32cd2e567","key":259,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:6ec8a2077a8e4407dbae4ef32cd2e567\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"Subject document described as Tier 1 owner of standing vocabulary; ontology, frame, authority, lineage and work-boundary objects; construction accounts and imports; commitments P0–P6 and foundation-to-law traces; composition, conservation, core result and conjunction algebras; categorical demonstration requirements; and hypotheses. Other members import or refine these definitions.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":13,\"path\":\"standards/FOUNDATIONS.md\",\"quote\":\"Tier 1. Owns the vocabulary of standing (§1);\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/FOUNDATIONS.md#FOUNDATIONS\",\"start_line\":3}],\"label\":\"FOUNDATIONS subject document\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:bba66a69742d9ed73c7869959fc063e7","key":260,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:bba66a69742d9ed73c7869959fc063e7\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"Each foundational claim, whether commitment or hypothesis, has exactly one standing: recovered is an adopted premise consolidating named source rules without treating them as proof; independent is an adopted premise argued by a case where other commitments hold and it fails; derived is a consequence with named premises; hypothesis is unestablished by the method, not law, and held for falsification. This differs from result standing and successor disposition.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":31,\"path\":\"standards/FOUNDATIONS.md\",\"quote\":\"Each has exactly one of four standings:\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/FOUNDATIONS.md#FOUNDATIONS%2F1.%20Vocabulary%20of%20standing\",\"start_line\":21}],\"label\":\"Foundational claim standing\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:55b15bfe765ffb98681bf2644b322028","key":261,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:55b15bfe765ffb98681bf2644b322028\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"Four distinct uses of join: categorical join is a map between categories; composition boundary joins successive steps; join of results combines closed results under one decision rule; relation join is equality join of participants in an enclosing relation. Unqualified join in a result context means join of results.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":50,\"path\":\"standards/FOUNDATIONS.md\",\"quote\":\"An\\nunqualified \\\"join\\\" in a result context means the join of results\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/FOUNDATIONS.md#FOUNDATIONS%2F1.%20Vocabulary%20of%20standing\",\"start_line\":49}],\"label\":\"Four context-dependent meanings of join\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:7d30c17505ac92c5cce93774e45e6626","key":262,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:7d30c17505ac92c5cce93774e45e6626\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"Ontology categories: Subject is the exact thing a claim, representation or transformation concerns, identified by inventory and bytes or semantic addresses. Representation is bytes, text, model or program standing for a subject. Interpretation is a declared context-bound representation-to-meaning contract identifying reliable distinctions and residuals. Context declares subject, definitions, basis and admissible observations. Outcome U is an owner-selected directly verifiable state with acceptance interval. Object O has scoped identity (authority, kind, value), boundary, state and material relations. Actor performs a step within context, attention, time and capability limits; role is an occupied relation selected by configuration. Step is bounded intake, selected context, grant, execution and output. Step-produced fact is a judgment, residual, observation or authority decision that cannot be reacquired from declared sources; reproducible observations are excluded. Claim binds subject, property, basis, witness relation and falsifier. Evidence comprises admitted exact observations/artifacts with provenance, subject identity, basis and scope. Judgment is recorded evaluation over unchanged subject, with evaluator, decision, evidence, scope and revising observation. Authority is identity-bearing scoped permission to operate or dispose acceptance. Residual is material uncertainty, omission, loss or unproven relation awaiting authorised disposition. Basis is every exact version, identity, time, topology, authority, configuration or evidence coordinate whose change can alter the bound step, claim, result or evaluation. Materiality is evaluation-relative potential to change result, basis validity, admissible evidence, operation performer or decision owner, including uncertainty and closure.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":71,\"path\":\"standards/FOUNDATIONS.md\",\"quote\":\"| Subject | the thing a claim, representation or transformation is about; exact, with inventory and bytes or semantic addresses | P3 |\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/FOUNDATIONS.md#FOUNDATIONS%2F2.%20Ontology\",\"start_line\":56}],\"label\":\"Foundational ontology objects\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:a31aad4a23047f64dc2ae6c9cc88ecd9","key":263,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:a31aad4a23047f64dc2ae6c9cc88ecd9\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"Frame objects: Evaluation is a declared question with known result family, evidence basis, decision authority and material-operation authority where needed, admitting judgment, prediction, construction, comparison, proof, refusal, classification or action recommendation. Evaluation family shares required manifold, authority basis and result algebra. Workspace is bounded reasoned-over or acted-on material, potentially broader than a repository. Material-relation manifold is the finite jointly interpretable variables, entities, identities, states, relations, invariants, authorities, observations and exclusions needed by a family, allowing overlapping coordinate charts without implied geometry or runtime. Coordinate is complete locally required basis, identity, lineage, input, evidence and authority information. Topology is the material relation structure visible at one basis, not necessarily complete workspace topology. Capability envelope is required competence, context capacity, tools, access, independence and configuration. Reference frame specifies finite attention, coordinates, authority, evidence and result relations for a family and basis. Activated frame binds declaration to exact evaluation, workspace subject, basis, actor and evidence-acquisition boundary. Frame set is a human-declared available family permitting overlaps, alternatives, specialists, exploration and separate assurance. Active frame configuration is activations and declared result relations for one evaluation or decision. Lens is a reusable question family, becoming a frame only on full bounded instantiation. Role allocates responsibility/authority; persona changes approach/salience; abstraction hides/contracts detail; component is structural. None is a frame merely by identity.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":94,\"path\":\"standards/FOUNDATIONS.md\",\"quote\":\"The reference frame and the objects it binds are first-class in this\\ncorpus.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/FOUNDATIONS.md#FOUNDATIONS%2F2.%20Ontology%2FFrame%20objects\",\"start_line\":75}],\"label\":\"Reference-frame ontology\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:cdbc87d83c3a1d696b268a09e5c6e022","key":264,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:cdbc87d83c3a1d696b268a09e5c6e022\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"Distinct kinds: frame-set authority is human declaration/acceptance of a project frame set; semantic authority owns meaning of a material relation; evaluation authority permits evaluation; operation authority is an owner-issued grant to construct, transform, admit, publish or mutate a material subject; decision authority permits accepting, rejecting or otherwise disposing results. Actor identity identifies the human, agent, tool or process and is not authority. These may lawfully coincide but never collapse by default.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":109,\"path\":\"standards/FOUNDATIONS.md\",\"quote\":\"These may coincide in a lawful case and\\nnever collapse by default.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/FOUNDATIONS.md#FOUNDATIONS%2F2.%20Ontology%2FAuthority%20kinds\",\"start_line\":106}],\"label\":\"Authority kinds and actor identity\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:8e88edc4965cafedcab2959b65acc4cc","key":265,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:8e88edc4965cafedcab2959b65acc4cc\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"Frame disjointness is structural absence of shared material variable, coordinate, evidence or result dependency for declared evaluations. Evaluation independence is procedural separation of activations that neither consume nor influence one another's unclosed working results; they may share subject or manifold and later contribute closed results to one conjunction. Assurance independence is claim-relative separation prescribed by assurance law, including non-authorship, acquisition, exposure, actor and configuration conditions. Disjointness does not imply independent evaluation, independent activation does not imply disjointness, and the unqualified word independent establishes none of the three.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":174,\"path\":\"standards/FOUNDATIONS.md\",\"quote\":\"Three relations stay distinct\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/FOUNDATIONS.md#FOUNDATIONS%2F2.%20Ontology%2FDisjointness%20and%20independence\",\"start_line\":162}],\"label\":\"Disjointness, evaluation independence and assurance independence\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:028479125fd2aebd66e8dbd97b743e8c","key":266,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:028479125fd2aebd66e8dbd97b743e8c\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"Reference frame F = ⟨Q, B, M, C, I, A, E, X, R, J, K, D⟩: evaluation family; workspace/topology basis; manifold; coordinate/equality law; invariants; authority; evidence/provenance law; exclusions/prohibited assumptions; closed core result algebra or mapped refinement; invalidation/rechart condition; capability envelope; optional declared dependencies, overlaps, inputs and outputs. This relation is an evaluation contract, not a required schema/runtime carrier. Prompt, context packet, symbolic program or other representation projects an activated frame rather than being the frame.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":196,\"path\":\"standards/FOUNDATIONS.md\",\"quote\":\"A reference frame F is the tuple ⟨Q, B, M, C, I, A, E, X, R, J, K, D⟩\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/FOUNDATIONS.md#FOUNDATIONS%2F2.%20Ontology%2FThe%20frame%20tuple\",\"start_line\":178}],\"label\":\"Frame tuple\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:557308c7c90ed316b3c85ed43c6bcb23","key":267,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:557308c7c90ed316b3c85ed43c6bcb23\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"Distinct identities in FOUNDATIONS-owned urn:stdo:bounded-context:recursive-product-taxonomy, with corresponding urn:stdo:concept:recursive-product-taxonomy:<name> identities: substrate is a lower product/runtime used to build products; development-product is the role of one exact released-product install acting as builder for a source project, creating no new Product identity or authority transfer; source-project is mutable workspace building the next release cut; release-cut is immutable annotated candidate boundary over a published feature set; product is the immutable released thing after cut acceptance; install is a stamped workspace instance; artifact is published output built by a source project or configured install; product-definition is present-tense source-project WHAT authority, conventionally PRODUCT.md, not released artifact. Separate release neighbours are candidate source, a mutable successor-building state non-operative for released consumers; release subject, the exact member set/artifact bound by cut-scoped claims; and version-line selector, a mutable alias for the highest-ordinal published cut on one project's version line, useful for discovery but insufficient as exact immutable basis.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":247,\"path\":\"standards/FOUNDATIONS.md\",\"quote\":\"Each role is an\\nobject with its own identity\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/FOUNDATIONS.md#FOUNDATIONS%2F2.%20Ontology%2FProduct%20lineage%20objects\",\"start_line\":203}],\"label\":\"Recursive product taxonomy and release neighbours\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:06f029793a578b1e4a299a7a0f429e20","key":268,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:06f029793a578b1e4a299a7a0f429e20\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"Boundary object around a probabilistic, agentic or delegated work unit. Live specification and design should declare six parts: input/output contract; required context; capability/role expectation; admissible evidence/evaluator regime; provenance obligation; lawful stop, hold, gap, continuation or completion states. ACTIVATION §1 makes this unit's intake, context and result algebra exact.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":262,\"path\":\"standards/FOUNDATIONS.md\",\"quote\":\"the\\nlive specification and design should declare\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/FOUNDATIONS.md#FOUNDATIONS%2F2.%20Ontology%2FWork%20boundary\",\"start_line\":254}],\"label\":\"Declared work boundary\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:3a838f9d52d7a26394e4a485e996ad42","key":269,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:3a838f9d52d7a26394e4a485e996ad42\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"Construction realises a selected outer contract through steps. Three independently variable accounts remain distinct: algorithmic description of steps; informational interpretation of data under an Interpretation contract; computational realisation by people, machines or mixtures in a declared execution environment, with build-tenant environment owned by SPEC_METHOD §11. A construction may need all three; none is a corpus tier. This distinction is an added choice, not a commitment, and has none of the foundational claim standings.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":285,\"path\":\"standards/FOUNDATIONS.md\",\"quote\":\"This section owns the distinction as an added\\nchoice in the sense of §3 Foundation to law, not a commitment;\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/FOUNDATIONS.md#FOUNDATIONS%2F2.%20Ontology%2FAccounts%20of%20a%20construction\",\"start_line\":280}],\"label\":\"Three accounts of construction\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:b0d28fcdc19fd68081f6b530c2780343","key":270,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:b0d28fcdc19fd68081f6b530c2780343\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"Reference-only import carries identical owner-qualified meaning from named source to importing context, with no loss, translation, ownership transfer or authority. It takes either a collected declaration or a point-of-use reference naming the owning section. Adoption is the target's use of an imported concept under source-owned adoption premises; lifecycle remains source-owned.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":297,\"path\":\"standards/FOUNDATIONS.md\",\"quote\":\"An import is\\nreference-only. Source and target meanings are identical owner-qualified\\nreferences, not new local definitions.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/FOUNDATIONS.md#FOUNDATIONS%2F2.%20Ontology%2FImports%20between%20members\",\"start_line\":290}],\"label\":\"Import and adoption between members\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:6fa6231a6a9a8b9b410e028e53f394b4","key":271,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:6fa6231a6a9a8b9b410e028e53f394b4\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"P0 Bounded construction is recovered: finite actors realise selected outer contracts through fitting steps, owning their internal path; actors may change and reacquire declared sources but not private memory, step-produced facts are not reacquirable, the world is open and output is candidate until evaluated. P1 Interpretation is independent: subject, representation and context-bound meaning differ; structural success is not fidelity and semantic decisions require exact contracts. P2 Purpose is independent: selected outcome defines adequacy and interface obligations derive from the served transformation. P3 Identity is independent: declared authority/kind/value identity survives admissible change and boundaries carry proof obligations. P4a Typed composition is independent: prior type and judgment must satisfy the next exact domain and preconditions, retaining identities, intermediate results, judgments, evidence, authority, provenance and stop states. P4b Conservation is derived from P0 and P2 plus non-reacquirability: producing steps record outer-contract-needed judgments, residuals, observations and authority decisions; reacquirable sources follow sufficiency rather than conservation. P5 Totality is derived from P0 and P6 plus open-world premise: no success on outside-context conditions, first-class non-success and named next moves. P6 Justification and authority is independent: definitions, assumptions, observations, candidate judgments and accepted claims have distinct standing; evidence supports basis-bound claims and authority permits or disposes only within scope.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":365,\"path\":\"standards/FOUNDATIONS.md\",\"quote\":\"| P4b Conservation of step-produced facts | derived from P0 and P2, with P0's premise that step-produced facts are not re-acquirable | sources a later step can re-acquire are governed by sufficiency, not conservation |\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/FOUNDATIONS.md#FOUNDATIONS%2F3.%20Commitments\",\"start_line\":363}],\"label\":\"P0–P6 commitments\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:2951160ca2da445ee90413367849a4a5","key":272,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:2951160ca2da445ee90413367849a4a5\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"Derived consequence synthesising commitments for movement from observed current state to acceptable destination under finite resources; not a further commitment. P0 bounds acquisition/work and preserves internal strategy; P1 preserves comparison meaning among conditions, observations and predictions; P2 selects destination Z and adequacy criteria; P3 separates persistent subject, observations and dependencies from accounts; P4a carries obligations through steps/refinement/boundaries; P4b conserves non-reacquirable facts through observation/correction/reuse; P5 accounts for resource tradeoffs, recursion, recovery and truthful undecided stops; P6 establishes support and authority without minting either. ACTIVATION §1 owns the construction relation.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":490,\"path\":\"standards/FOUNDATIONS.md\",\"quote\":\"It is derived, not a further\\ncommitment, and has the standing of a consequence\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/FOUNDATIONS.md#FOUNDATIONS%2F3.%20Commitments%2FConstruction%20synthesis\",\"start_line\":477}],\"label\":\"Construction synthesis\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:e5540e29232bd5affc66513f588ca970","key":273,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:e5540e29232bd5affc66513f588ca970\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"A material family groups deciding rules whose outcomes matter to the selected method outcome. Its owner-located entry table traces labelled instance premises and one row per consequence using five columns: premises with standing; consequence; linked owning rule; only additional domain/policy choice with owner or none; pillar contributions. Ten numbered contributions are specification/project structure; world models/identity/Markov objects; algebraic calculus; functional design; outcome-driven development; information/interpretation; reference frames; computational calculus/execution binding; evidence/correction/authority; axiomatic calculus. Tables, consumer paragraphs and family index are traces, not owners, added determinations, new authority or proofs of entire rules.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":553,\"path\":\"standards/FOUNDATIONS.md\",\"quote\":\"A family table is a trace.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/FOUNDATIONS.md#FOUNDATIONS%2F3.%20Commitments%2FFoundation%20to%20law\",\"start_line\":551}],\"label\":\"Foundation-to-law family traces and index\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:03892680a0099e23b65aaa50c3aad6e6","key":274,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:03892680a0099e23b65aaa50c3aad6e6\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"Subject-defined algebra of typed step composition, conservation accounting, sufficient references, explicit latitude, shared implementation without identity/authority merger, and conditional demonstration requirements for categorical claims. These are descriptions of the supplied subject's calculus and create no operation in this interpretation.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":638,\"path\":\"standards/FOUNDATIONS.md\",\"quote\":\"Composition. For steps s₁: X → Y and s₂: Y → Z, s₂ ∘ s₁ exists only under P4a.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/FOUNDATIONS.md#FOUNDATIONS%2F4.%20Algebra\",\"start_line\":636}],\"label\":\"Subject algebra and formal fragment\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:4bc9faf98ce709b8d6d49d1eb9109591","key":275,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:4bc9faf98ce709b8d6d49d1eb9109591\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"H1 proposes 𝒜 as the free category on typed primitives, ℐ as selected carrier sets with total functions, and 𝒞_H as function pairs with additive costs; S: 𝒜 → ℐ and R_H: 𝒜 → 𝒞_H would be functors, with S neither faithful nor an equivalence. H names architecture, never runtime. The source explicitly leaves the whole claim unsupported and unresolved.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":712,\"path\":\"standards/FOUNDATIONS.md\",\"quote\":\"It has no supporting\\nevidence and the whole claim is unresolved:\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/FOUNDATIONS.md#FOUNDATIONS%2F4.%20Algebra\",\"start_line\":706}],\"label\":\"H1 categorical-structure hypothesis\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:73f26e79b171732285e45607615def72","key":276,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:73f26e79b171732285e45607615def72\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"The single core result domain for every performed evaluation, directly or through refinement: satisfied means the declared predicate holds on the exact basis; falsified means a declared counterexample defeats it; indeterminate means available admissible evidence cannot decide it; out_of_frame means a required material relation or capability is undeclared; invalid_basis means the subject or basis cannot support evaluation. Constraints, judgments, frame evaluations, stops, work steps and effects use this core or a refinement mapped into it.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":729,\"path\":\"standards/FOUNDATIONS.md\",\"quote\":\"| `satisfied` | the declared predicate holds on the exact basis |\\n| `falsified` | a declared counterexample defeats it |\\n| `indeterminate` | the available admissible evidence cannot decide it |\\n| `out_of_frame` | the evaluation requires an undeclared material relation or capability |\\n| `invalid_basis` | the subject or basis cannot support the evaluation |\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/FOUNDATIONS.md#FOUNDATIONS%2F4.%20Algebra%2FResults\",\"start_line\":721}],\"label\":\"Core result algebra\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:9f8b2905240c9cb93ab890acc6dd7e24","key":277,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:9f8b2905240c9cb93ab890acc6dd7e24\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"A finer outcome vocabulary defined by a member, profile or adopting Product for a named question and mapping predicate. Each refined value has exactly one core value; cause-dependent alternatives are separate refined values. Further refinement by a member, profile, project or adopting Product splits parent values by named causes while retaining each parent's core value.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":791,\"path\":\"standards/FOUNDATIONS.md\",\"quote\":\"each child value names its parent value and its cause and keeps its\\nparent's core value; a child that needs a different core value needs a\\ndifferent parent value, which only the owner of the parent declares; and\\nno child takes `satisfied` from a parent that is not `satisfied`.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/FOUNDATIONS.md#FOUNDATIONS%2F4.%20Algebra%2FResults\",\"start_line\":788}],\"label\":\"Result refinement and parent-value rule\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:1e617d4a71ceb9be3d7c064bf93039d6","key":278,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:1e617d4a71ceb9be3d7c064bf93039d6\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[\"An evaluation was required or planned but was not performed.\"],\"definition\":\"Absence of a closed evaluation result, distinct from every core value, undecidable evidence, a step's stop state and unresolved work. In conjunction it is a planned-assessment gap when assessment was planned; required coverage with no planned assessment is uncovered coverage.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":771,\"path\":\"standards/FOUNDATIONS.md\",\"quote\":\"a missing result, being no result, enters every\\nconjunction over it as a gap: a planned assessment without a closed result\\nwhere an assessment was planned, and uncovered coverage where none was.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/FOUNDATIONS.md#FOUNDATIONS%2F4.%20Algebra%2FResults\",\"start_line\":769}],\"label\":\"Evaluation not performed\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:87a70139cbc7ea84f5c9fa15ac690645","key":279,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:87a70139cbc7ea84f5c9fa15ac690645\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"Three separate results with separate predicates: availability establishes that a step produced a candidate; assessment addresses whether the candidate meets declared criteria; acceptance addresses whether the decision owner accepts it at its boundary. Candidate production and successful work do not establish fitness or acceptance.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":807,\"path\":\"standards/FOUNDATIONS.md\",\"quote\":\"Availability, assessment and acceptance are separate results, each with its\\nown predicate: that a step produced a candidate; that the candidate meets\\nits declared criteria; and that the\\n[decision owner](ACTIVATION.md#roles-and-delegation) accepts it at its\\nboundary. A step having produced a candidate never maps to the candidate's\\nfitness or acceptance, and acceptance is never inferred from a successful\\nstep\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/FOUNDATIONS.md#FOUNDATIONS%2F4.%20Algebra%2FResults\",\"start_line\":801}],\"label\":\"Availability, assessment and acceptance\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:065709d4630efac07de8bfd91abef267","key":280,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:065709d4630efac07de8bfd91abef267\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"The source's family F3 trace register connects result and combination rules to commitments, added choices, owners and consumers. Its instance premises are declaration of predicate, subject and basis; combination of evaluations, steps or members into a decision; and a need for finer outcomes. P0 is recovered; P1, P2, P3, P4a and P6 are treated as independent; P5 is derived from P0 and P6, and P4b from P0 and P2. The register attributes the core names and non-success division to Results; refined meanings to their definers; conjunction choices to its applying member/profile; acceptance to EVALUATION §5; step stops to ACTIVATION §3; transformation record fields to AC-013; composition-law need to the governing evaluation under RF-010; latitude to the contract owner; shared implementation to accepted design; categorical claims to their claimant.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":864,\"path\":\"standards/FOUNDATIONS.md\",\"quote\":\"Instance premises, which the commitments do not supply:\\n(i) an evaluation declares its predicate, subject and basis; (ii) results\\nof several evaluations, steps or members are combined into one decision;\\n(iii) members, profiles and adopting Products need outcomes finer than the\\ncore.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/FOUNDATIONS.md#FOUNDATIONS%2F4.%20Algebra%2FResults\",\"start_line\":860},{\"end_line\":918,\"path\":\"standards/FOUNDATIONS.md\",\"quote\":\"Each consumer applies the rule and decides nothing the owning section does\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/FOUNDATIONS.md#FOUNDATIONS%2F4.%20Algebra%2FResults\",\"start_line\":918}],\"label\":\"Result rules, owners and consumer register\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:27e46433dafe1a605ba0856f6d082557","key":281,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:27e46433dafe1a605ba0856f6d082557\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"Combination of component results into one result for a composite predicate, a decision over evaluations, or the outer contract of composed steps. Its three distinct inputs are returned closed results with predicates and domain outcomes; planned assessments lacking an applicable closed result; and required coverage R minus coverage C admitted by planned assessments. Missing applicable results include non-performance, absence, staleness, another subject or basis, or inability to establish the required claim.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":943,\"path\":\"standards/FOUNDATIONS.md\",\"quote\":\"1. the closed results returned, each a core value with its predicate and\\n   domain outcome;\\n2. the planned assessments that have no closed result applicable to the\\n   composite: evaluations the composite requires that were not performed,\\n   or whose result is absent, stale, bound to another subject or basis, or\\n   incapable of establishing its claim;\\n3. the required coverage that no planned assessment addresses: for a\\n   required obligation set R and the coverage C that the planned\\n   assessments admit, the uncovered coverage R minus C.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/FOUNDATIONS.md#FOUNDATIONS%2F4.%20Algebra%2FConjunction%20of%20results\",\"start_line\":935}],\"label\":\"Conjunction of results\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:efae46f9c8f159bf2892e36617e85953","key":282,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:efae46f9c8f159bf2892e36617e85953\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"The rule for a particular conjunction declares mandatory results, conflict and indeterminacy handling, basis relations required to agree, a coherent composite basis for different bases, the owning decision authority, treatment of nonmandatory results, and any veto or deferral. It supplies the ordering or choice among non-satisfied returned values; no universal such order is supplied.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1029,\"path\":\"standards/FOUNDATIONS.md\",\"quote\":\"A conjunction declares which results are mandatory; how\\nconflict and indeterminacy are handled; which basis relations must agree,\\nresults on different bases combining only under a declared coherent\\ncomposite basis (§2, Basis); which decision authority owns the\\nconjunction; how results that are not mandatory count; and whether any\\nresult may veto or defer the decision.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/FOUNDATIONS.md#FOUNDATIONS%2F4.%20Algebra%2FConjunction%20of%20results\",\"start_line\":1024}],\"label\":\"Declared conjunction rule\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:a69423fbd046a97b345dff84e7d2be8f","key":283,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:a69423fbd046a97b345dff84e7d2be8f\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[\"Applicable instance premises are a construction with intake-bound governing basis and material assumptions Γ; a declared case domain Ω including material inputs, behaviour and environment; and a checker with declared observations and an admitted evaluation relation.\"],\"definition\":\"Shared source-owned preservation, assertion, provenance, quantified-assurance, reuse and formal-representation obligations connecting construction to supporting claims and evidence. The family table explains the six following owners and adds no separate decision. Its instance premises are conditions of governed situations, not commitments. ACTIVATION, EVALUATION, ASSURANCE, RELEASE, SPEC_METHOD and a_c interpretations apply these relations without declaring a second relation.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1056,\"path\":\"standards/FOUNDATIONS.md\",\"quote\":\"They are the shared owner for\\nthe preservation, assertion, provenance, quantified-assurance, reuse and\\nformal-representation obligations in this corpus; ACTIVATION §1, §4, §5 and §7, EVALUATION §1 and §3,\\nASSURANCE §3, §10, §11 and §14, RELEASE §8 and §9, SPEC_METHOD §4 and\\nany a_c interpretation apply them and state no second relation (P6).\\nA tenant chooses its representation and execution within these obligations. The notation\\nstates proof obligations; writing an implication does not discharge it.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/FOUNDATIONS.md#FOUNDATIONS%2F4.%20Algebra%2FAssurance%20relations\",\"start_line\":1050}],\"label\":\"Assurance relations and family trace\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:bcbce5d0a737828a451a5a279b5244d0","key":284,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:bcbce5d0a737828a451a5a279b5244d0\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"A construction binds starting state A, required outcome Z and Γ, its intake-bound governing basis plus material assumptions. Z includes required effects and trace properties where material. For boundary state or trace domains X_i, declared transitions F_i ⊆ X_i × X_(i+1), and properties P_i, preservation states: for all x and x', P_i(x) and F_i(x,x') implies P_(i+1)(x'). This is a proof obligation, separate from real execution's conformance. Algorithmic, informational and computational accounts respectively state required operation, retained meaning/distinctions, and realisation of work/observations.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1107,\"path\":\"standards/FOUNDATIONS.md\",\"quote\":\"For all x, x':  P_i(x) and F_i(x, x')  implies  P_(i+1)(x').\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/FOUNDATIONS.md#FOUNDATIONS%2F4.%20Algebra%2FPreservation%20through%20construction\",\"start_line\":1107},{\"end_line\":1138,\"path\":\"standards/FOUNDATIONS.md\",\"quote\":\"The algorithmic account states the required operation, the informational\\naccount the meaning and distinctions retained, and the computational\\nbinding how work and observations are realised\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/FOUNDATIONS.md#FOUNDATIONS%2F4.%20Algebra%2FPreservation%20through%20construction\",\"start_line\":1136}],\"label\":\"Construction preservation\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:8c9bb8ca53b69dcc2598cbba518b1faa","key":285,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:8c9bb8ca53b69dcc2598cbba518b1faa\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"For a selected obligation r, Q_r = interpret(r, Γ, Ω) is its required predicate over declared cases Ω. An assertion targets q_t and identifies whether it expresses the full obligation or a narrower claim. Conditional on Γ and Ω, Q_r implies q_t makes q_t necessary; q_t implies Q_r makes q_t sufficient; a stated conjunction q_1 and ... and q_n implying Q_r is sufficient collectively.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1159,\"path\":\"standards/FOUNDATIONS.md\",\"quote\":\"Q_r implies q_t                   : q_t is a necessary condition of Q_r.\\nq_t implies Q_r                   : establishing q_t is sufficient for Q_r.\\n(q_1 and ... and q_n) implies Q_r : the stated conjunction is sufficient.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/FOUNDATIONS.md#FOUNDATIONS%2F4.%20Algebra%2FAssertions%20and%20observation\",\"start_line\":1157}],\"label\":\"Obligation interpretation and assertion direction\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:c6397a5cd31d7e801c41504d6a8621df","key":286,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:c6397a5cd31d7e801c41504d6a8621df\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"A checker has observation map π: Ω → O and admitted evaluation relation T ⊆ O × R, where R is the core result domain. Deterministic checking is a functional special case; human or probabilistic checking may admit different conclusions for identical observations. Universal soundness covers every admitted conclusion: for every s in Ω, (π(s), sat) in T implies q_t(s), and (π(s), fal) in T implies not q_t(s). sat and fal denote judgments about q_t, not execution states.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1173,\"path\":\"standards/FOUNDATIONS.md\",\"quote\":\"Let `π: Ω → O` describe the observations available to a checker and\\n`T ⊆ O × R` its admitted evaluation relation, where R is the core result\\nalgebra of Results above. A deterministic checker is a functional special\\ncase. A human or probabilistic checker can admit different conclusions on\\nthe same observations; a universal soundness claim covers all admitted\\nconclusions, not a favourable selected run.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/FOUNDATIONS.md#FOUNDATIONS%2F4.%20Algebra%2FAssertions%20and%20observation\",\"start_line\":1167},{\"end_line\":1184,\"path\":\"standards/FOUNDATIONS.md\",\"quote\":\"For every s in Ω:\\n  (π(s), sat) in T  implies  q_t(s).\\n  (π(s), fal) in T  implies  not q_t(s).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/FOUNDATIONS.md#FOUNDATIONS%2F4.%20Algebra%2FAssertions%20and%20observation\",\"start_line\":1182}],\"label\":\"Observation and admitted checking relation\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:17185edeb211602f3f2cb3d5ef889e0f","key":287,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:17185edeb211602f3f2cb3d5ef889e0f\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"Assertion provenance comprises the owning obligation, interpretation, assumptions, derivation and shared dependencies. Execution provenance comprises actual checker, exact subject, applicable environment, inputs, observations and result. Authentication binds a returned assessment to producer, subject, basis and evidence but establishes neither provenance. Construction and assurance may derive along different paths from a common obligation, such as requirement → refinement → realisation; these example roles prescribe no stage names or test classes.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1238,\"path\":\"standards/FOUNDATIONS.md\",\"quote\":\"An expected result or acceptance predicate has assertion provenance: the\\nowning obligation, its interpretation, assumptions, derivation and shared\\ndependencies, which give it meaning. An execution has execution\\nprovenance: the actual checker, exact subject, applicable environment,\\ninputs, observations and result. Both are needed for the claims they\\nsupport; execution records alone cannot establish that the expected\\nanswer follows from the requirement. Authentication of a returned\\nassessment, which binds a result to its producer, subject, basis and\\nevidence ([EVALUATION §3](EVALUATION.md#3-independent-assessment)), is a\\nthird thing and establishes neither provenance (P6, P3).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/FOUNDATIONS.md#FOUNDATIONS%2F4.%20Algebra%2FParallel%20derivation%20and%20mutual%20assurance\",\"start_line\":1229}],\"label\":\"Assertion provenance, execution provenance and authentication\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:4530a9f715df287b4ea597f2bbf43a15","key":288,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:4530a9f715df287b4ea597f2bbf43a15\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"Comparison of independently justified constructions or assertions within declared scope. Agreement is compatible with correctness or shared error; disagreement calls for diagnosis and does not identify the faulty party. Material shared causes include specifications, interpretations, tools, fixtures, observations and copied material.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1256,\"path\":\"standards/FOUNDATIONS.md\",\"quote\":\"Mutual assurance compares independently justified constructions or\\nassertions within their stated scope. Agreement is compatible with both\\nbeing correct and with a shared error; disagreement requires diagnosis\\n([ACTIVATION §1 Feedback and diagnosis](ACTIVATION.md#construction-relation))\\nand does not identify the faulty party by itself. Assurance accounts for\\nshared specifications, interpretations, tools, fixtures, observations,\\ncopied material and other material failure causes. Different actors,\\nmodel families or codebases do not establish statistical independence.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/FOUNDATIONS.md#FOUNDATIONS%2F4.%20Algebra%2FParallel%20derivation%20and%20mutual%20assurance\",\"start_line\":1249}],\"label\":\"Mutual assurance\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:cc5f5776011ad47b85c4351075c214f5","key":289,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:cc5f5776011ad47b85c4351075c214f5\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[\"Quantified assurance is claimed.\"],\"definition\":\"A model of a specified population or uncertainty with prior information, likelihoods, shared causes and calibration limits. For violation V and evidence E, P(V | E, Γ) = P(E | V, Γ) P(V | Γ) / [P(E | V, Γ) P(V | Γ) + P(E | not V, Γ) P(not V | Γ)]. For check misses M_i under specified conditions, P(M_1 and ... and M_n | V, Γ) = product over i of P(M_i | V, Γ, M_1, ..., M_(i-1)). These are model-conditional claims, not truth values for the whole Product.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1290,\"path\":\"standards/FOUNDATIONS.md\",\"quote\":\"P(V | E, Γ) =\\n  P(E | V, Γ) P(V | Γ)\\n  / [P(E | V, Γ) P(V | Γ) + P(E | not V, Γ) P(not V | Γ)].\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/FOUNDATIONS.md#FOUNDATIONS%2F4.%20Algebra%2FQuantified%20assurance\",\"start_line\":1288},{\"end_line\":1304,\"path\":\"standards/FOUNDATIONS.md\",\"quote\":\"P(M_1 and ... and M_n | V, Γ)\\n  = product over i of P(M_i | V, Γ, M_1, ..., M_(i-1)).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/FOUNDATIONS.md#FOUNDATIONS%2F4.%20Algebra%2FQuantified%20assurance\",\"start_line\":1303}],\"label\":\"Quantified assurance\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:5a25ded62c9539a0ed3a79b1b0ff63bb","key":290,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:5a25ded62c9539a0ed3a79b1b0ff63bb\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"Assertion justification explains why a check expresses an obligation; evidence validity identifies dependencies affecting behaviour, conclusion or applicability, including implementation, libraries, data, instruments, environments and governing assumptions. For a material change Δ, including discovery of an invalid assumption, I(Δ) conservatively covers changed facts and affected dependents; D*(t) covers transitive dependencies material to assertion, execution and evidence use. Candidate selection is S_Δ = { t : D*(t) intersects I(Δ) }. For a new subject and basis, E_new = retain_applicable(E_old, new_subject, new_basis) union E_reassessed.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1331,\"path\":\"standards/FOUNDATIONS.md\",\"quote\":\"Assertion justification and evidence validity are related but distinct\\ndependency relations. The former explains why a check expresses an\\nobligation. The latter identifies what can affect the check's behaviour,\\nconclusion or applicability: implementation, shared libraries, data,\\ninstruments, environments and governing assumptions. A\\nrequirements-to-test link alone is not a complete impact model (P3, P6).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/FOUNDATIONS.md#FOUNDATIONS%2F4.%20Algebra%2FChange%20impact%20and%20evidence%20reuse\",\"start_line\":1326},{\"end_line\":1362,\"path\":\"standards/FOUNDATIONS.md\",\"quote\":\"E_new = retain_applicable(E_old, new_subject, new_basis) union E_reassessed.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/FOUNDATIONS.md#FOUNDATIONS%2F4.%20Algebra%2FChange%20impact%20and%20evidence%20reuse\",\"start_line\":1362}],\"label\":\"Change impact and evidence reuse\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:cffbc4e797362ee75c9acc3609227c21","key":291,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:cffbc4e797362ee75c9acc3609227c21\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"An a_c interpretation represents material assurance obligations and dependencies while distinguishing five support kinds: stated formula, discharged mathematical argument, mechanically checked structure, externally assessed predicate and execution evidence. Mathematical proof, exhaustive finite-model checks, sampled tests and observed use retain distinct scopes; source semantics, formal fidelity and actual use retain separate evidence.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1420,\"path\":\"standards/FOUNDATIONS.md\",\"quote\":\"It distinguishes five kinds of support for a statement: a\\nstated formula, a discharged mathematical argument, mechanically checked\\nstructure, an externally assessed predicate, and evidence from execution.\\nAn external predicate retains the source, scope and evidence required to\\nestablish it; an arbitrary truth label does not discharge the obligation.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/FOUNDATIONS.md#FOUNDATIONS%2F4.%20Algebra%2FFormal%20representation\",\"start_line\":1416}],\"label\":\"Formal representation and support kinds\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:44f67134d32e1310c5a17534a999d67f","key":292,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:44f67134d32e1310c5a17534a999d67f\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"Claims carried for falsification, expressly not law: categorical equivalence of 𝒜 and ℐ under some reformulation; universal algorithmic capture of meaning; the statistical Markov boundary with candidate status referenced to WORLD_MODEL §4; and traversal composition laws of any runtime.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1452,\"path\":\"standards/FOUNDATIONS.md\",\"quote\":\"Not law; carried for falsification: categorical equivalence of 𝒜 and ℐ under\\nsome reformulation; universal algorithmic capture of meaning; the statistical\\nMarkov boundary (candidate status under\\n[WORLD_MODEL §4](WORLD_MODEL.md#epistemic-status));\\ntraversal composition laws of any runtime.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/FOUNDATIONS.md#FOUNDATIONS%2F5.%20Hypotheses\",\"start_line\":1448}],\"label\":\"Foundational hypotheses\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:a159dd754aa9500e917e52db5c007d60","key":293,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:a159dd754aa9500e917e52db5c007d60\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"A guide and non-deciding locator index from indexed spellings to corpus clauses declaring bounded contexts and owning concepts. It realises the glossary named by PRODUCT_DEFINITION §5, adds no law, and names P0–P6 principles for its clauses. It supplies no semantic definitions, contexts, imports, translations, equivalences, disambiguations or authority.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":8,\"path\":\"standards/GLOSSARY.md\",\"quote\":\"Guide. A non-deciding locator index from indexed spellings to the clauses\\nof this corpus that declare their bounded contexts and own their concepts.\\nIt realises the glossary that\\n[PRODUCT_DEFINITION §5](PRODUCT_DEFINITION.md#5-bounded-context-semantic-resolution)\\nnames and adds nothing to that law. Every clause names the principle that\\nrequires it (P0 to P6, FOUNDATIONS §3).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/GLOSSARY.md#GLOSSARY\",\"start_line\":3}],\"label\":\"GLOSSARY locator index\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:19d24390af542ec401ed7241d9526db2","key":294,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:19d24390af542ec401ed7241d9526db2\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"A normal glossary row records spelling, cited owner's bounded-context identity and exact owning concept clause. The alternate §17 row records a shared label, a use locator and owning clause. A locator only identifies where to look. Owner clause plus selected basis identifies candidate meaning; the occurrence supplies governed scope. Unresolved context or owning clause makes a row invalid and cannot be repaired by the index.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":28,\"path\":\"standards/GLOSSARY.md\",\"quote\":\"The owning clause together with the selected basis identifies the candidate meaning;\\nthe occurrence being resolved still supplies its own governed scope (P1,\\nP3). A row whose context or owning clause does not resolve is invalid, and\\nthis index cannot repair it (P5, P6).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/GLOSSARY.md#GLOSSARY%2F1.%20Index%20contract\",\"start_line\":25}],\"label\":\"Index row and occurrence resolution\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:b333d837ab9e156928c31281a56e5a0e","key":295,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:b333d837ab9e156928c31281a56e5a0e\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"Every locus is an owning corpus clause. A concept's defining section supplies its owning clause, with context ownership supplied directly or by its member. Imported concepts cite the defining section and identify the importing declaration or stated owner relation in the relation clause; otherwise that clause only locates an externally stated relationship. A concept outside all bounded contexts declared by its member uses the member as source context; §16 indexes it without declaring a new context. An index watch separately records locator path and digest from deciding sources, and locator drift makes dependent surfaces or frames stale without making the index a meaning owner.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":60,\"path\":\"standards/GLOSSARY.md\",\"quote\":\"A concept defined outside every bounded context its member declares has\\nthat member as its source context\\n([FOUNDATIONS §2 Imports between members](FOUNDATIONS.md#imports-between-members)).\\n§16 indexes those concepts with the member in place of a bounded-context\\nidentity. Such a row declares no context, and a context holds one of those\\nconcepts only by its own import (P1, P3).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/GLOSSARY.md#GLOSSARY%2F2.%20Locator%20law\",\"start_line\":55},{\"end_line\":71,\"path\":\"standards/GLOSSARY.md\",\"quote\":\"Index watch. A derived surface or projected frame that relies on this\\nindex to locate meaning watches it through the index's path and digest,\\nrecorded separately from the deciding sources it was derived from. Locator\\ndrift in this index then makes that surface or frame stale\\n([PRODUCT_DEFINITION §11](PRODUCT_DEFINITION.md#11-one-constitutional-surface-and-version-boundary),\\nstaleness binding), and the watch does not make this index an owner of\\nmeaning (P3, P6).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/GLOSSARY.md#GLOSSARY%2F2.%20Locator%20law\",\"start_line\":65}],\"label\":\"Locator ownership, imports and staleness watch\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:632d2f88164206c41df4869d221ebff2","key":296,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:632d2f88164206c41df4869d221ebff2\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"Locator category urn:stdo:bounded-context:method-identity, whose declaration and both owning concept clauses are SPEC_METHOD.md#method-identity. Indexed entries are STDO, with no relation clause, and O pillar symbol, with relation locator ODD.md#1-position. These are locators, not supplied definitions.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":81,\"path\":\"standards/GLOSSARY.md\",\"quote\":\"| `STDO` | `urn:stdo:bounded-context:method-identity` | [`SPEC_METHOD.md#method-identity`](SPEC_METHOD.md#method-identity) | none |\\n| `O` pillar symbol | `urn:stdo:bounded-context:method-identity` | [`SPEC_METHOD.md#method-identity`](SPEC_METHOD.md#method-identity) | [`ODD.md#1-position`](ODD.md#1-position) |\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/GLOSSARY.md#GLOSSARY%2F3.%20Method%20identity\",\"start_line\":80}],\"label\":\"Method identity locators\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identi