fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"EVALUATION owns Equivalence Ladder, semantic equivalence of realisations, Computational Equivalence and Categorical Equivalence at Conformance of realisations, linked to FOUNDATIONS Algebra; Semantic Equivalence of concepts in glossary §5 is explicitly another concept. EVALUATION also owns Adequate Attention and Actual-Use Evidence at Frame qualification, linked to ACTIVATION context construction. CONFORMANCE owns Discriminator and Common Discriminators at Conformance, linked to Discriminator coverage, and Logical-Review Check at Discriminator coverage, linked to EVALUATION review results. PROFILES owns the profile import rule at The boundary, linked to FOUNDATIONS imports.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":357,\"path\":\"standards/GLOSSARY.md\",\"quote\":\"| `Equivalence Ladder`; semantic equivalence of realisations; `Computational Equivalence`; `Categorical Equivalence` | EVALUATION | [`EVALUATION.md#6-conformance-of-realisations`](EVALUATION.md#6-conformance-of-realisations) | [`FOUNDATIONS.md#4-algebra`](FOUNDATIONS.md#4-algebra); `Semantic Equivalence` of concepts in §5 is another concept |\\n| `Adequate Attention`; `Actual-Use Evidence` | EVALUATION | [`EVALUATION.md#frame-qualification`](EVALUATION.md#frame-qualification) | [`ACTIVATION.md#2-context-construction-under-an-envelope`](ACTIVATION.md#2-context-construction-under-an-envelope) |\\n| `Discriminator`; `Common Discriminators` | CONFORMANCE | [`CONFORMANCE.md#conformance`](CONFORMANCE.md#conformance) | [`CONFORMANCE.md#5-discriminator-coverage`](CONFORMANCE.md#5-discriminator-coverage) |\\n| `Logical-Review Check` | CONFORMANCE | [`CONFORMANCE.md#5-discriminator-coverage`](CONFORMANCE.md#5-discriminator-coverage) | [`EVALUATION.md#4-review-results`](EVALUATION.md#4-review-results) |\\n| profile import rule | PROFILES | [`PROFILES.md#1-the-boundary`](PROFILES.md#1-the-boundary) | [`FOUNDATIONS.md#imports-between-members`](FOUNDATIONS.md#imports-between-members) |\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/GLOSSARY.md#GLOSSARY%2F16.%20Concepts%20of%20members%20without%20a%20declared%20context\",\"start_line\":353}],\"label\":\"Assessment and profile concept inventory\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:a2f107acde99288ef9dd2a88dd1b0877","key":313,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:a2f107acde99288ef9dd2a88dd1b0877\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"Separate indexed result domains: DESIGN_MODULE cross-view axiom verdict has pass, fail and not_applicable and relates to FOUNDATIONS Results; DESIGN_MODULE ontology and design verdicts use accepted at Gate and retrospective work and relate to ACTIVATION Disposition. UX Results of this profile owns four distinct domains, each linked to FOUNDATIONS Results: surface review {compliant, violation, design_module_incomplete}; replay proof {replay_passes, replay_fails}; closure obligations {closure_obligations_met, closure_unproven}; carrier admission {carrier_admitted, carrier_missing}. No evaluation is performed by listing them.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":363,\"path\":\"standards/GLOSSARY.md\",\"quote\":\"| axiom verdict: `pass`; `fail`; `not_applicable` | DESIGN_MODULE | [`DESIGN_MODULE.md#cross-view-axiom-evaluation`](DESIGN_MODULE.md#cross-view-axiom-evaluation) | [`FOUNDATIONS.md#results`](FOUNDATIONS.md#results) |\\n| Ontology verdict and design verdict: `accepted` | DESIGN_MODULE | [`DESIGN_MODULE.md#gate-and-retrospective-work`](DESIGN_MODULE.md#gate-and-retrospective-work) | [`ACTIVATION.md#disposition`](ACTIVATION.md#disposition) |\\n| surface review: `compliant`; `violation`; `design_module_incomplete` | UX | [`UX.md#15-results-of-this-profile`](UX.md#15-results-of-this-profile) | [`FOUNDATIONS.md#results`](FOUNDATIONS.md#results) |\\n| replay proof: `replay_passes`; `replay_fails` | UX | [`UX.md#15-results-of-this-profile`](UX.md#15-results-of-this-profile) | [`FOUNDATIONS.md#results`](FOUNDATIONS.md#results) |\\n| closure obligations: `closure_obligations_met`; `closure_unproven` | UX | [`UX.md#15-results-of-this-profile`](UX.md#15-results-of-this-profile) | [`FOUNDATIONS.md#results`](FOUNDATIONS.md#results) |\\n| carrier admission: `carrier_admitted`; `carrier_missing` | UX | [`UX.md#15-results-of-this-profile`](UX.md#15-results-of-this-profile) | [`FOUNDATIONS.md#results`](FOUNDATIONS.md#results) |\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/GLOSSARY.md#GLOSSARY%2F16.%20Concepts%20of%20members%20without%20a%20declared%20context\",\"start_line\":358}],\"label\":\"Indexed design and UX verdict domains\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:13b6172ff45e0c256887788162a4e35c","key":314,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:13b6172ff45e0c256887788162a4e35c\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"A sense locator rather than a definition catalogue. indeterminate: FOUNDATIONS Results core value when admissible evidence cannot decide; EVALUATION Result and triage projection payload class, not a result. not_applicable: EVALUATION triage class, not a result; RELEASE §9 successor disposition with bounded reason; SPEC_METHOD lifecycle phase declared inapplicable with reason; DESIGN_MODULE head/state-model and ACTIVATION §4 design-grounded exclusion/entity-lifecycle matrix entry; TRAVERSAL_OCCURRENCE judgment value. refusal/refused: REFERENCE_FRAME §5 method-function activation or translation refusal; AC-007 a_c constraint or basis refusal; TRAVERSAL_OCCURRENCE judgment decision and stop; ACTIVATION admission refusal of a work contract. gap: AC-007 stop with a core value; FOUNDATIONS conjunction gap without its own value. disposition: ACTIVATION boundary acceptance; RELEASE predecessor-claim successor disposition; TICKETS obligation repricing; PROJECT_REFERENCE_FRAME_BASIS_TEMPLATE Coverage And Residuals planning choice for an evaluation, not coverage status. missing: absence of a closed result, FOUNDATIONS Results/Not performed. adoption: PRODUCT_DEFINITION §7 adoption of an available profile; SPEC_METHOD §6 shared method lesson adoption; RELEASE §4 consumer release-basis adoption. Closed/closed: POSTING_GUIDE §7 discussion state; TICKETS §4 ticket or sprint status.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":371,\"path\":\"standards/GLOSSARY.md\",\"quote\":\"Some labels name different things in different clauses. Each row below\\nlocates one sense with the clause that owns it; the label's meaning at an\\noccurrence is the sense its owning clause gives, and the occurrence\\nqualifies the label or states its predicate where it is used. Equal\\nspelling across these rows establishes no equivalence (§1; P1, P3).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/GLOSSARY.md#GLOSSARY%2F17.%20Labels%20with%20several%20senses\",\"start_line\":367},{\"end_line\":394,\"path\":\"standards/GLOSSARY.md\",\"quote\":\"| disposition | a planning choice for an evaluation in a basis inventory, not a coverage status | `templates/PROJECT_REFERENCE_FRAME_BASIS_TEMPLATE.md`, Coverage And Residuals |\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/GLOSSARY.md#GLOSSARY%2F17.%20Labels%20with%20several%20senses\",\"start_line\":394}],\"label\":\"Clause-owned senses of shared labels\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:856015343871c433411a25f5b43fe66d","key":315,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:856015343871c433411a25f5b43fe66d\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"Tier 1 member owning identity law: scoped uniqueness, type, stability, readable/opaque forms, hierarchy, engine/domain split, authority conservation, default-format overrides and publication, parsing, object/release boundary, minimum questions, examples and implementation consequences. It consumes FOUNDATIONS §2 Object, Authority and Basis without redefining them. AC-002 applies scoped identity to every calculus identity with a coordinate map; calculus-edition identity remains owned by AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS §8 and release names/forms by RELEASE. Clauses name their requiring P0–P6 principles; identity is P3's commitment and authority P6's.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":23,\"path\":\"standards/IDENTITY.md\",\"quote\":\"identity is P3's commitment and authority P6's.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/IDENTITY.md#IDENTITY\",\"start_line\":23},{\"end_line\":13,\"path\":\"standards/IDENTITY.md\",\"quote\":\"Object (a subject with scoped identity of authority, kind and value),\\nAuthority with its kinds, and Basis are defined once, and adds no\\ndefinition to tier 1.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/IDENTITY.md#IDENTITY\",\"start_line\":11}],\"label\":\"IDENTITY member\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:592f428587096675d25235df24f32725","key":316,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:592f428587096675d25235df24f32725\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"Object identity is always scoped and typed, unique in its lawful scope and stable enough for its governed purpose. Its minimum semantic model is authority + kind + value, through which identity should be interpretable. It is not a universal naked-string convention.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":105,\"path\":\"standards/IDENTITY.md\",\"quote\":\"identity = authority + kind + value\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/IDENTITY.md#IDENTITY%2F2.%20Core%20law%2FScoped%20identity\",\"start_line\":105},{\"end_line\":29,\"path\":\"standards/IDENTITY.md\",\"quote\":\"Identity is scoped, typed, unique, and stable enough for the governed\\npurpose. Identity is not a flat global string convention; it is made\\nunique by hierarchy and type (P3).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/IDENTITY.md#IDENTITY%2F1.%20Position\",\"start_line\":27}],\"label\":\"Scoped object identity\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:628ebb39e8881c3e537451819d0b33f2","key":317,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:628ebb39e8881c3e537451819d0b33f2\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"A useful identity hierarchy is authority / kind / value / revision. Examples distinguish product-authority requirement REQ-F-CAPABILITY-001, product-authority requirement_family REQ-F-CAPABILITY, runtime-authority run UUID and release-authority release 1.0.0-rc.1. Family/member and runtime/domain identities remain different semantic kinds even when serialised as strings.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":201,\"path\":\"standards/IDENTITY.md\",\"quote\":\"The important point is that `REQ-F-CAPABILITY` and `REQ-F-CAPABILITY-001`\\nare not the same kind of identity, and that a runtime `run_id` and a\\ndomain requirement identity do not belong to the same semantic category\\neven if both serialise as strings (P3).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/IDENTITY.md#IDENTITY%2F4.%20Identity%20hierarchy\",\"start_line\":198}],\"label\":\"Identity hierarchy\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:66dfe66094c11997c7f30e2adfcebb0c","key":318,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:66dfe66094c11997c7f30e2adfcebb0c\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"An object's boundary states what belongs to it and what its identity does not depend on. It is an evidence- and basis-bounded claim with a proof obligation, not something established by storage, schema or name.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":151,\"path\":\"standards/IDENTITY.md\",\"quote\":\"An object's boundary, what belongs to the object and what its identity\\ndoes not depend on, is a claim with a proof obligation\\n([FOUNDATIONS §3](FOUNDATIONS.md#3-commitments), P3), not a property that\\nits storage, schema or name establishes. A boundary claim names its\\nobject, the evidence that supports it and the basis it holds on, and it\\nholds only as far as that evidence goes (P3, P6).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/IDENTITY.md#IDENTITY%2F2.%20Core%20law%2FBoundaries%20and%20sufficiency%20claims\",\"start_line\":146}],\"label\":\"Object boundary claim\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:56f840f046c75cbe5f578321eada0403","key":319,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:56f840f046c75cbe5f578321eada0403\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"Material sufficiency under RF-003 is a claim that observed boundary state suffices for a particular task. Statistical Markov boundary is the stronger hypothesis that the boundary screens the interior from everything outside it. Task sufficiency establishes neither completeness nor that stronger claim.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":160,\"path\":\"standards/IDENTITY.md\",\"quote\":\"A claim that an\\nobject's observed boundary state is sufficient for a task is a material\\nsufficiency claim of\\n[RF-003](REFERENCE_FRAME.md#rf-003-material-sufficiency), bounded by\\nthat task: it is not completeness, and it does not establish that the\\nboundary screens the object's interior from everything outside it. That\\nstronger claim, a statistical Markov boundary, is a hypothesis\\n([FOUNDATIONS §5](FOUNDATIONS.md#5-hypotheses)); no work relies on it as\\nestablished, and a profile that uses such a construct states its\\nepistemic status (P5).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/IDENTITY.md#IDENTITY%2F2.%20Core%20law%2FBoundaries%20and%20sufficiency%20claims\",\"start_line\":151}],\"label\":\"Task sufficiency and Markov hypothesis\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:0fa83fdec596671a1df9bd98f5348022","key":320,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:0fa83fdec596671a1df9bd98f5348022\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"Identity for runtime-owned objects, including runs, function calls, jobs, execution frames, continuations and events. The substrate/runtime may provide defaults, opaque forms and engine-local generation rules.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":210,\"path\":\"standards/IDENTITY.md\",\"quote\":\"The substrate or runtime may define default identities for runtime-owned\\nobjects, such as runs, function calls, jobs, execution frames,\\ncontinuations and events. For these, the engine may use opaque identities and engine-local\\ngeneration rules.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/IDENTITY.md#IDENTITY%2F5.%20Authority%20split%2FEngine-owned%20identity\",\"start_line\":207}],\"label\":\"Engine-owned identity\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:006ca6488f42ba4e76c541e522c13142","key":321,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:006ca6488f42ba4e76c541e522c13142\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"Derived domains own semantic identity grammar for their constitutional objects, including requirements, requirement families, acceptance criteria, scenarios, ADRs/design decisions and published domain assets. The domain defines kinds, distinctions, uniqueness and parsing/reading.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":221,\"path\":\"standards/IDENTITY.md\",\"quote\":\"Derived domains own the semantic identity grammar for their own\\nconstitutional objects, such as requirements, requirement families,\\nacceptance criteria, scenarios, ADRs or design decisions, and published\\ndomain assets. The domain defines which identity kinds exist, how they\\nare distinguished, what makes them unique, and how they are parsed or\\nread.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/IDENTITY.md#IDENTITY%2F5.%20Authority%20split%2FDomain-owned%20identity\",\"start_line\":216}],\"label\":\"Domain-owned identity\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:413efc4ed18e10f86b5c76f1f98556e0","key":322,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:413efc4ed18e10f86b5c76f1f98556e0\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"Authority is an identity-bearing semantic relation preserving owner, kind, governed subject, scope and governing basis. It is not a display label, capability string, actor identity or reachable code path. FOUNDATIONS §2 owns Authority and its kinds.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":230,\"path\":\"standards/IDENTITY.md\",\"quote\":\"Authority is an identity-bearing semantic relation, not a display label,\\ncapability string, actor identity or reachable code path. Its identity\\npreserves owner, kind, governed subject, scope and governing basis (P6,\\nP3; the Authority\\nobject and its kinds are FOUNDATIONS §2).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/IDENTITY.md#IDENTITY%2F6.%20Authority%20identity%20and%20conservation%20%28STDO-UP-004%29\",\"start_line\":226}],\"label\":\"Authority identity\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:0ed41260452a87de6836fa5047cb79ce","key":323,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:0ed41260452a87de6836fa5047cb79ce\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[\"Human authority acts through an explicitly admitted bounded proxy.\"],\"definition\":\"A proxy grant names grantor, actor, subject, scope, permitted and excluded decisions, validity, delegation rights, revocation and provenance. Proxy actor identity remains distinct from human-authority identity.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":245,\"path\":\"standards/IDENTITY.md\",\"quote\":\"Human authority may act directly or through an explicitly admitted\\nbounded proxy. Proxy actor identity and human-authority identity remain\\ndistinct; a profile's own surfaces may project the human-authority\\nrelation under that profile's term (PROFILES). A proxy grant names its\\ngrantor, actor, subject, scope, permitted and excluded decisions,\\nvalidity, delegation rights, revocation and provenance (P6, P3).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/IDENTITY.md#IDENTITY%2F6.%20Authority%20identity%20and%20conservation%20%28STDO-UP-004%29\",\"start_line\":240}],\"label\":\"Bounded proxy grant\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:487b998011fc8bbf86f5688efd791a52","key":324,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:487b998011fc8bbf86f5688efd791a52\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"A derived domain's published replacement of format or structure defaults supplied by its bound runtime realisation for the domain's own kinds. Defaults are starter conventions and convenience contracts; the realisation's actual default surfaces belong to DESIGN_MODULE §12 realisation law.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":270,\"path\":\"standards/IDENTITY.md\",\"quote\":\"Default identity formats that a bound runtime realisation publishes are\\nstarter conventions and convenience contracts, not universal doctrine;\\nthey are lawful only so long as derived domains may override them (P3,\\nP6). What such a realisation publishes, and for which surfaces, is\\nrealisation law outside this member\\n([DESIGN_MODULE §12](DESIGN_MODULE.md#identity-defaults-from-a-bound-runtime-realisation)).\\n\\nDerived domains may override identity format and structure for their own\\nkinds.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/IDENTITY.md#IDENTITY%2F7.%20Default%20formats%20and%20overrides%2FDerived%20domain%20overrides\",\"start_line\":262}],\"label\":\"Domain identity override\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:0d44548345ed4f30503f0de96135ec17","key":325,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:0d44548345ed4f30503f0de96135ec17\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"An identity reader/parser operating under published identity law. Regex over prose is at most a provisional extractor over a surface with identity law defined elsewhere; it is not a complete identity model.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":314,\"path\":\"standards/IDENTITY.md\",\"quote\":\"Regex extraction from prose is not a complete identity model. At most,\\nregex may be a provisional extractor over a surface whose identity law is\\nalready defined elsewhere (P3, P1).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/IDENTITY.md#IDENTITY%2F8.%20Parsing\",\"start_line\":312}],\"label\":\"Identity parsing\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:159bec39f19aa215b9d76120e9fe9081","key":326,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:159bec39f19aa215b9d76120e9fe9081\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"Distinct coordinates: object identity, release identity, publication/revision coordinates and mutable discovery selectors. An immutable release cut is the only exact operative release identifier; a mutable version-line selector names only the highest-ordinal published immutable cut on its line. Release version is a release-process fact, not the live constitutional identity of every project object.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":345,\"path\":\"standards/IDENTITY.md\",\"quote\":\"- an immutable release cut is the only exact operative release\\n  identifier;\\n- the mutable version-line selector only names the highest-ordinal\\n  published immutable cut on its line (FOUNDATIONS §2);\\n- release version is a release-process fact; and\\n- release version is not the live constitutional identity of every\\n  object in the project.\\n\\nSo the method distinguishes object identity, release identity,\\npublication or revision coordinates, and mutable discovery selectors.\\nThese may relate, but they are not interchangeable (P3, P6).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/IDENTITY.md#IDENTITY%2F9.%20Release%20version%20boundary\",\"start_line\":335}],\"label\":\"Release and object identity coordinates\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:3cbeb196d9da340381b2cca3bb1e434d","key":327,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:3cbeb196d9da340381b2cca3bb1e434d\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"A surface defining or exposing identity, whose adequacy is tested by seven questions about owning authority, denoted kind, uniqueness scope, lifecycle stability, over-trust in readability, unambiguous parsing of families/members/aliases/revisions, and runtime/domain/release category.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":362,\"path\":\"standards/IDENTITY.md\",\"quote\":\"If those questions cannot be answered, the identity surface is\\nunder-defined (P3).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/IDENTITY.md#IDENTITY%2F10.%20Minimum%20questions\",\"start_line\":361}],\"label\":\"Identity surface\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:8b02973e1156879c7d2e0e2a6c603ecd","key":328,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:8b02973e1156879c7d2e0e2a6c603ecd\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"F8 identity's authored foundation-to-law table distinguishes consequences from owned choices. Instance premises not supplied by commitments: (i) many object kinds with runtime/domain owners; (ii) serialised/readable forms read by people/parsers; (iii) release versions belong to releases, not every object. Premise/standing map: scoped/type/uniqueness P3 independent+i; stability P3 independent and P4b derived from P0/P2; boundaries P3/P6 independent, P5 derived from P0/P6 with P0 open-world premise+i; readability P3/P1 independent+ii; hierarchy P3+i,ii; authority split P3/P6+i; authority conservation P6/P3/P4b; defaults P3/P6; parsing P3/P1+ii; release boundary P3/P6+iii; minimum questions P3/P6; implementation policy P3/P1 independent and P0 recovered. Choice ownership remains with the stated owner: object owner for extra coordinates/kinds/form/visible segments; runtime for its generation/defaults; domain for semantic grammar, overrides and family need; WORLD_MODEL/RF-003 for their refinements; issuing authority for grants/decisions; IDENTITY for hierarchy model, grant fields, seven questions and enduring-repair policy; RELEASE for release forms. Examples add no decisions. Consumer applications add no authority beyond their owning rule.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":47,\"path\":\"standards/IDENTITY.md\",\"quote\":\"This member is material family F8, identity. The table below shows which\\nof its rules follow from which premises, in the format of\\n[FOUNDATIONS §3 Foundation to law](FOUNDATIONS.md#foundation-to-law),\\nwhich also states the standing of the consequences. Instance premises,\\nwhich the commitments do not supply:\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/IDENTITY.md#IDENTITY%2F1.%20Position%2FFoundation%20to%20law\",\"start_line\":43},{\"end_line\":95,\"path\":\"standards/IDENTITY.md\",\"quote\":\"Each consumer applies the rule and decides nothing the owning section does\\nnot (P2, P6).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/IDENTITY.md#IDENTITY%2F1.%20Position%2FFoundation%20to%20law\",\"start_line\":94}],\"label\":\"F8 foundation-to-law derivation\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:d95615227f8fdfe4b3e7141e3ba237e3","key":329,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:d95615227f8fdfe4b3e7141e3ba237e3\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"Tier 3 Outcome-Driven Development profile for graph-native product authoring over a declared asset graph. It owns graph-native terms in urn:stdo:bounded-context:graph-native-odd under the selected complete STDO basis, imports listed families by reference and restates none. Its traversal and F_D/F_P/F_H shorthands are distinct from a_c traversal records and functor kinds. Executive, Worker and Reviewer are roles over steps; actor, executor, domain operation and functor kind are distinct coordinates. It owns structural traversal-governance and product-authoring law, not consuming-domain semantics or same-spelled runtime carriers.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":21,\"path\":\"standards/ODD.md\",\"quote\":\"This profile's graph traversal and its F_D, F_P and F_H shorthands are its\\nown concepts and are not those records by spelling. The Executive, Worker\\nand Reviewer of [EXECUTIVE_BASELINE](EXECUTIVE_BASELINE.md) are roles, and roles\\nare relations over steps in which no role name confers an operation\\n([ACTIVATION §1](ACTIVATION.md#roles-and-delegation)); the actor, the\\nexecutor, the domain operation and the functor kind are different\\ncoordinates (AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS §5) (P3, P6).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ODD.md#ODD\",\"start_line\":15},{\"end_line\":60,\"path\":\"standards/ODD.md\",\"quote\":\"This profile owns those concepts in the graph-native bounded context\\n`urn:stdo:bounded-context:graph-native-odd` under the selected complete\\nSTDO basis. The context covers the ODD product shape, the GTL language\\nrole, the ABG method role, graph assets, vectors, functions, traversals and\\nthe graph and runtime worker and evaluator shorthands defined here. It does\\nnot absorb a consuming Product's domain semantics, nor a concrete runtime's\\ncarriers that happen to share a spelling (P1, P3).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ODD.md#ODD%2F1.%20Position\",\"start_line\":54}],\"label\":\"Outcome-Driven Development profile\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:b45635a1f0ea19b2701d9a88aa71857a","key":330,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:b45635a1f0ea19b2701d9a88aa71857a\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"GTL, Graph Transformation Language, is the capability role of a typed declarative graph language and the language expression of ODD. It does not require a particular repository, package, vendor or implementation.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":52,\"path\":\"standards/ODD.md\",\"quote\":\"ODD, GTL and ABG name normative capability roles and a construction\\nalgebra, not a required repository, package, vendor or concrete\\nimplementation. ODD, Outcome-Driven Development, names the graph-native\\nproduct-authoring profile. GTL, Graph Transformation Language, names the\\nrole of the typed declarative graph language. ABG names the role of the\\nsingular traversal-governance and runtime-truth authority (P1, P6).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ODD.md#ODD%2F1.%20Position\",\"start_line\":47}],\"label\":\"GTL role\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:7401bbbf535fd5e1e16b14036ff56999","key":331,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:7401bbbf535fd5e1e16b14036ff56999\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"ABG is the singular traversal-governance and runtime-truth role. Its owned operations and facts include traversal, dispatch, actor invocation, process supervision, graph-call realisation, runtime facts, event emission/replay, frames, continuations, retry/correction control, closure folds, re-entry after publish boundaries, lineage and provenance. This describes source-defined authority, not an authority granted by this interpretation.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":585,\"path\":\"standards/ODD.md\",\"quote\":\"ABG owns traversal; dispatch; actor invocation; process supervision;\\ngraph-call realisation; runtime facts; runtime event emission and replay;\\nframes; continuations; retry and correction control; closure folds over\\nruntime truth; re-entry after publish boundaries; lineage and provenance\\n(P6).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ODD.md#ODD%2F10.%20What%20an%20ODD%20product%20is%2FABG\",\"start_line\":581}],\"label\":\"ABG role\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:dfebaec0e3fc6f2d93521655089f3a54","key":332,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:dfebaec0e3fc6f2d93521655089f3a54\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"Configured GTL/ABG domain product whose published graph functions construct typed domain assets. Its ten-part application boundary comprises Bootstrap Surface, Initialization Surface, Domain Configuration, Typed Domain Assets/Nodes, GTL Function Catalog, GTL Module, Policy Hook Bindings, ABG Runtime, Projection/Query Surface and Proof Surface. The product owns domain asset and graph-function meaning, catalogue, policy overlays, domain projections and domain closure/gap interpretation.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":547,\"path\":\"standards/ODD.md\",\"quote\":\"App\\n= Bootstrap Surface\\n+ Initialization Surface\\n+ Domain Configuration\\n+ Typed Domain Assets / Nodes\\n+ GTL Function Catalog\\n+ GTL Module\\n+ Policy Hook Bindings\\n+ ABG Runtime\\n+ Projection / Query Surface\\n+ Proof Surface\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ODD.md#ODD%2F10.%20What%20an%20ODD%20product%20is\",\"start_line\":537},{\"end_line\":591,\"path\":\"standards/ODD.md\",\"quote\":\"The ODD product owns domain asset meaning, graph-function meaning, the\\npublished function catalogue, policy overlays, domain query projections,\\nand closure and gap interpretation for its domain (P6, P1).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ODD.md#ODD%2F10.%20What%20an%20ODD%20product%20is%2FODD%20product\",\"start_line\":589}],\"label\":\"ODD domain product\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:f4ab02ff3778dca8d3f25b278e550a77","key":333,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:f4ab02ff3778dca8d3f25b278e550a77\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"Declared asset graph over state transitions relevant to the product's work; it is the product's process model and declared program space.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":274,\"path\":\"standards/ODD.md\",\"quote\":\"The product is expressed as a declared asset graph over the state\\ntransitions relevant to the product's work (P0, P3).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ODD.md#ODD%2F5.%20Graph%20model\",\"start_line\":273}],\"label\":\"Declared asset graph\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:845e0e60b60e69f173452f33a26b882d","key":334,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:845e0e60b60e69f173452f33a26b882d\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"Durable truth surface or product asset naming a bounded state of truth. Illustrative software-product names are intent, product, requirements, design, module_decomp, code, uat_testcases, integration_tests, bootloader and build targets; these names are product-local.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":283,\"path\":\"standards/ODD.md\",\"quote\":\"Nodes are durable truth surfaces or product assets; each names a bounded\\nstate of truth. In one software-development ODD product the nodes include\\n`intent`, `product`, `requirements`, `design`, `module_decomp`, `code`,\\n`uat_testcases`, `integration_tests`, `bootloader` and build targets. Those\\nnames are illustrative and product-local; the law is that nodes name\\nbounded states (P3).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ODD.md#ODD%2F5.%20Graph%20model%2FNodes\",\"start_line\":278}],\"label\":\"ODD node\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:4affde1b64c0d4f4480ba70fa8f30aea","key":335,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:4affde1b64c0d4f4480ba70fa8f30aea\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"A lawful admissible transition between nodes. Its declaration gives required upstream assets, target asset, governing evaluators/gates and output contract; the probabilistic-work boundary additionally declares required context, role/capability expectation, provenance obligation and lawful stop, hold, gap, continuation or completion states.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":290,\"path\":\"standards/ODD.md\",\"quote\":\"Vectors are the lawful transitions between nodes and are the admissible\\ntransitions of the product. Each vector declares its required upstream\\nassets, its target asset, its governing evaluators and gates, and its\\noutput contract (P4a, P6).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ODD.md#ODD%2F5.%20Graph%20model%2FVectors\",\"start_line\":287},{\"end_line\":315,\"path\":\"standards/ODD.md\",\"quote\":\"The vector declares the admissible external traversal space: required\\nupstream assets; target asset or output contract; required context; role\\nor capability expectation; governing evaluators and gates; provenance\\nobligation; and the lawful stop, hold, gap, continuation or completion\\nstates.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ODD.md#ODD%2F5.%20Graph%20model%2FProbabilistic%20compute\",\"start_line\":311}],\"label\":\"ODD vector\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:dd4c6b532dec6f332c60a24617ffac0a","key":336,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:dd4c6b532dec6f332c60a24617ffac0a\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"Source-described workflow over the graph: bind current target, locate admissible vectors, traverse one vector, materialise next asset, prove that vector closed and continue until the selected target closes. One declared vector/edge traversal is the profile's bounded unit of probabilistic compute.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":406,\"path\":\"standards/ODD.md\",\"quote\":\"The workflow is a traversal over the graph: bind the current target;\\nlocate the next admissible vectors; traverse one vector; materialise the\\nnext asset; prove the vector closed; continue until the selected target\\ncloses. The graph is the declared program space of the product (P0, P5).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ODD.md#ODD%2F5.%20Graph%20model%2FTraversal\",\"start_line\":403}],\"label\":\"ODD graph traversal\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:7041e57978eba9d41b7f61db1ca3b4ed","key":337,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:7041e57978eba9d41b7f61db1ca3b4ed\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"FOUNDATIONS P0's bounded step, referenced here as the source of ODD's binding: selected context fits the actor's envelope, internal path belongs to the actor, and traversal supplies admissible external space. Its full foundational definition is not supplied.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":309,\"path\":\"standards/ODD.md\",\"quote\":\"Direction: from the step of\\nFOUNDATIONS P0 to one declared ODD vector or edge traversal. Preserved\\nmeaning: the step's selected context fits the actor's envelope, the\\nactor's internal path within the step is its own, and the traversal is\\nthe admissible external space. Narrowed scope: one declared vector or edge\\ntraversal of a published graph. Invalidation: a change to FOUNDATIONS P0,\\nto the vector's declaration or to the selected basis invalidates the\\nbinding until it is evaluated again (P0, P1).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ODD.md#ODD%2F5.%20Graph%20model%2FProbabilistic%20compute\",\"start_line\":302}],\"label\":\"Referenced foundational bounded step\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:eac7cf8a2799092be0571f0c747f7bb9","key":338,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:eac7cf8a2799092be0571f0c747f7bb9\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"urn:stdo:concept:graph-native-odd:f-p: bounded probabilistic worker turn preserving bounded non-human construction under declared policy and narrowing it to one graph traversal contract.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":330,\"path\":\"standards/ODD.md\",\"quote\":\"- `F_P` (`urn:stdo:concept:graph-native-odd:f-p`) is the shorthand for the\\n  bounded probabilistic worker turn. It specialises substrate-neutral\\n  lawful probabilistic processing: it keeps bounded non-human construction\\n  under declared policy and narrows that meaning to one graph traversal\\n  contract.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ODD.md#ODD%2F5.%20Graph%20model%2FProbabilistic%20compute\",\"start_line\":326}],\"label\":\"ODD F_P\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:aeb3b76829c62d92d2421634121dbe87","key":339,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:aeb3b76829c62d92d2421634121dbe87\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"urn:stdo:concept:graph-native-odd:f-d: deterministic evaluation or proof over declared traversal properties. It may optimise or validate a domain-local path where the domain makes work precise, without moving domain HOW into GTL, ABG or the framework.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":335,\"path\":\"standards/ODD.md\",\"quote\":\"- `F_D` (`urn:stdo:concept:graph-native-odd:f-d`) is the shorthand for\\n  deterministic evaluation or proof over declared properties of the\\n  traversal. F_D may optimise or validate a domain-local path where the\\n  domain can make part of the work precise; it does not move domain HOW\\n  into GTL, ABG or the framework.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ODD.md#ODD%2F5.%20Graph%20model%2FProbabilistic%20compute\",\"start_line\":331}],\"label\":\"ODD F_D\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:f688644e4a37c1669dd925477341038c","key":340,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:f688644e4a37c1669dd925477341038c\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"urn:stdo:concept:graph-native-odd:f-h: explicit human adjudication invoked under the traversal's declared authority and ambiguity policy. It grants no ambient traversal, semantic or closure authority.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":340,\"path\":\"standards/ODD.md\",\"quote\":\"- `F_H` (`urn:stdo:concept:graph-native-odd:f-h`) is the shorthand for\\n  explicit human adjudication invoked under the traversal's declared\\n  authority and ambiguity policy. It specialises the substrate-neutral\\n  human-adjudication concept and grants a human no ambient traversal,\\n  semantic or closure authority.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ODD.md#ODD%2F5.%20Graph%20model%2FProbabilistic%20compute\",\"start_line\":336}],\"label\":\"ODD F_H\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:c4e137050be29b55e509bb3284c7bad0","key":341,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:c4e137050be29b55e509bb3284c7bad0\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"Referenced source concept urn:stdo:concept:ambiguity-governance:lawful-probabilistic-processing, owned with its context by SPEC_METHOD §5. Only its preserved meaning of bounded non-human construction under declared policy is supplied here.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":350,\"path\":\"standards/ODD.md\",\"quote\":\"The F_P\\nspecialisation runs from\\n`urn:stdo:concept:ambiguity-governance:lawful-probabilistic-processing` to\\n`urn:stdo:concept:graph-native-odd:f-p`; the F_H specialisation runs from\\n`urn:stdo:concept:ambiguity-governance:human-adjudication` to\\n`urn:stdo:concept:graph-native-odd:f-h`. The source concepts and their\\ncontext are owned by\\n[SPEC_METHOD §5](SPEC_METHOD.md#5-ambiguity-governance-and-lifecycle); this\\nprofile owns the targets in the graph-native ODD context (P1, P6).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ODD.md#ODD%2F5.%20Graph%20model%2FProbabilistic%20compute\",\"start_line\":342}],\"label\":\"Referenced lawful probabilistic processing\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:aeb8d30e922b74cb3478814dc61ad20c","key":342,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:aeb8d30e922b74cb3478814dc61ad20c\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"Referenced substrate-neutral source concept urn:stdo:concept:ambiguity-governance:human-adjudication, owned with its context by SPEC_METHOD §5; the complete source definition is not supplied.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":350,\"path\":\"standards/ODD.md\",\"quote\":\"`urn:stdo:concept:ambiguity-governance:human-adjudication` to\\n`urn:stdo:concept:graph-native-odd:f-h`. The source concepts and their\\ncontext are owned by\\n[SPEC_METHOD §5](SPEC_METHOD.md#5-ambiguity-governance-and-lifecycle); this\\nprofile owns the targets in the graph-native ODD context (P1, P6).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ODD.md#ODD%2F5.%20Graph%20model%2FProbabilistic%20compute\",\"start_line\":346}],\"label\":\"Referenced human adjudication\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:8a952a4985c21b8548d5a4551258e042","key":343,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:8a952a4985c21b8548d5a4551258e042\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"Named constructive program realising a vector: directly, through a small inner workflow refining one outer vector, or as a reusable higher-order library function. The outer vector remains its constitutional callable contract.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":374,\"path\":\"standards/ODD.md\",\"quote\":\"Graph functions are named constructive programs that realise vectors. A\\ngraph function may realise one outer vector directly, refine one outer\\nvector into a small inner workflow, or act as a reusable higher-order\\nlibrary function. The outer vector remains the constitutional contract;\\nthe graph function is the constructive realisation of that contract (P4a,\\nP0).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ODD.md#ODD%2F5.%20Graph%20model%2FGraph%20functions\",\"start_line\":369}],\"label\":\"GraphFunction\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:b4bfe7d8f52830a21e97ccd74cb89f5f","key":344,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:b4bfe7d8f52830a21e97ccd74cb89f5f\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"Referenced ACTIVATION §4 typed refinement allows earlier outputs to reach later steps only through a declared adapter or specialised contract whose declared domain names them. ODD binds it to a graph function refining one outer vector; the full general law is external.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":382,\"path\":\"standards/ODD.md\",\"quote\":\"[ACTIVATION §4](ACTIVATION.md#4-totality-and-refinement) generalises the\\nrefinement of one outer vector into an inner workflow to any realisation,\\nlets a refinement carry an earlier output to a later step only through a\\ndeclared adapter or specialised contract whose declared domain names it,\\nand names [PROFILES §2](PROFILES.md#2-graph-execution), which indexes this\\nprofile, as the keeper of the ODD binding.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ODD.md#ODD%2F5.%20Graph%20model%2FGraph%20functions\",\"start_line\":377}],\"label\":\"Referenced typed refinement\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:bf756d2b9147004f7d63d89815cb85ca","key":345,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:bf756d2b9147004f7d63d89815cb85ca\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"ODD §11.8's specialised cumulative carried environment, conserved as profile law rather than generalised into the core. A later function's declared domain is environment.requires and may require any typed binding available in the cumulative environment, not only the preceding output. Retained functions should declare environment.requires, environment.provides and environment.carries.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":397,\"path\":\"standards/ODD.md\",\"quote\":\"Narrowed scope: one published outer\\nvector and its declared inner workflow, whose retained functions should\\ndeclare `environment.requires`, `environment.provides` and\\n`environment.carries` (§11.8); a later function's declared domain is its\\n`environment.requires`, which may require any typed binding available in\\nthe cumulative carried environment, not only the immediately previous\\noutput.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ODD.md#ODD%2F5.%20Graph%20model%2FGraph%20functions\",\"start_line\":391}],\"label\":\"Cumulative carried environment\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:a1ff9d15d7f9cef03b4fc72c204cdd04","key":346,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:a1ff9d15d7f9cef03b4fc72c204cdd04\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"The mutable source library authors a future method release; consumers select one complete immutable release distributed in the shared versioned STDO store. Both libraries contain method members, guides and templates. Only README-designated method members—tier 1, tier 2 and selected tier 3 profiles—are constitutional method surfaces. *_GUIDE.md documents refine application; *_TEMPLATE.md files are reusable starter forms/examples and convenience artifacts only.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":269,\"path\":\"standards/ODD.md\",\"quote\":\"Both the authoring library and an installed distribution contain three\\nclasses of document. Method members are the constitutional method\\nsurfaces, the members that [README](README.md#documents) names as method\\nmembers: the tier 1 and tier 2 standards and, when a\\nproject selects them, the tier 3 profiles. Guides (`*_GUIDE.md`) are operational guides and application standards\\nthat refine application of the method. Templates (`*_TEMPLATE.md`) are\\nreusable starter forms and examples and are convenience artifacts only.\\nOnly method members are constitutional method surfaces (P6, P3).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ODD.md#ODD%2F4.%20Method%20library%20classes\",\"start_line\":262}],\"label\":\"Method library and document classes\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:7b9b61c944808f060ef20bc9a9b82c30","key":347,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:7b9b61c944808f060ef20bc9a9b82c30\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"The installed graph-native product supplies the method, runtime and carrier surfaces, owning traversal-control substrate, runtime/control/command surfaces, release-managed methodology and scaffold templates. It is distinct from the target project and, in self-hosting, from the next version under development.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":424,\"path\":\"standards/ODD.md\",\"quote\":\"The installed product owns the graph-native method and its\\ntraversal-control substrate, the runtime and control surfaces, the command\\nsurfaces, the release-managed methodology surfaces and the project\\nscaffold templates (P6).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ODD.md#ODD%2F6.%20Product%20boundary\",\"start_line\":421}],\"label\":\"Installed ODD builder\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:796a8085272464e74aa0b22d9354d8cb","key":348,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:796a8085272464e74aa0b22d9354d8cb\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"The project built with an installed ODD product owns its business domain; one stdo_<label>.json definition per distinct product WHAT locating constitutional, local/collective reference-frame basis, realisation, work and composition surfaces; constitutional surfaces; one or more how.build_tenants realisation roots; domain outputs and evidence. Software examples include design, code, tests, documents and proof surfaces; other domains name their own artifacts.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":438,\"path\":\"standards/ODD.md\",\"quote\":\"- one `stdo_<label>.json` definition for each distinct product WHAT,\\n  locating its constitutional, local and collective reference-frame\\n  basis, realisation, work and composition surfaces;\\n- its constitutional surfaces under SPEC_METHOD, where `GOALS.md`,\\n  `INTENT.md`, `PRODUCT.md` and `requirements/` are the default\\n  software-development scaffold and not mandatory names;\\n- one or more realisation roots bound through `how.build_tenants`, where\\n  `build_tenants/` is the default root name for software-development ODD\\n  products and existing projects and other domain types may use their own\\n  locations;\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ODD.md#ODD%2F6.%20Product%20boundary\",\"start_line\":429}],\"label\":\"Target project\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:84dcf51004fa90f680da8c7bf39066d9","key":349,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:84dcf51004fa90f680da8c7bf39066d9\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"A structural responsibility layer expresses one capability class, which the product binds to local domain semantics and the GTL carrier exposes through lawful transitions. Examples are bootstrap/intake, design, implementation, qualification, release, operational transition and retrofit; they are not mandatory instance names.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":469,\"path\":\"standards/ODD.md\",\"quote\":\"This profile governs structural responsibility layers and their required\\npublication shape. It does not freeze one product's local asset names as\\nuniversal ODD doctrine. A responsibility layer expresses one capability\\nclass; the product binds that capability to its own local domain\\nsemantics; the GTL carrier publishes the lawful transitions for that bound\\ncapability (P1, P3).\\n\\nCapability classes may include bootstrap or intake, design,\\nimplementation, qualification, release, operational transition and\\nretrofit. They are responsibility-layer ideas, not mandatory universal\\ninstance names (P1).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ODD.md#ODD%2F8.%20Responsibility%20layers%20and%20local%20binding\",\"start_line\":459}],\"label\":\"Responsibility layer\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:f410088881523b5ea81f03f38d542d3b","key":350,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:f410088881523b5ea81f03f38d542d3b\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"Source-defined evaluation of a move against the current ODD profile. For the predicate 'the move complies with the current profile', compliant maps to satisfied; non-compliant maps to falsified with the violated law as counterexample; valid and worth incorporating maps to out_of_frame because current law lacks what the move needs. Incorporation names the needed law, profile owner and update, and is neither compliance nor failure.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":523,\"path\":\"standards/ODD.md\",\"quote\":\"| compliant | satisfied | the move meets the law of the current profile |\\n| non-compliant | falsified | the law of this profile that the move violates is the counterexample |\\n| valid and worth incorporating | out_of_frame | the current profile does not declare the law the move needs; the outcome names that law, this profile as its owner and the update it requires, which is the reconfiguration pressure of out_of_frame ([FOUNDATIONS §4 Results](FOUNDATIONS.md#results), Out of frame or indeterminate) |\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ODD.md#ODD%2F9.%20Method%20governance%20and%20audit\",\"start_line\":521}],\"label\":\"ODD method audit and outcome domain\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:34566a52e8fcda8cee3d666e0e57e8ae","key":351,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:34566a52e8fcda8cee3d666e0e57e8ae\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"Downstream read models over admitted carrier, runtime, event or source truth; visible current state is projected constructive history. Possible views include assets, catalogue, checkpoint/provenance overlays and domain explainability.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":673,\"path\":\"standards/ODD.md\",\"quote\":\"Visible current state is a projection and does not replace runtime truth.\\nThe ODD query lane may expose asset views, function catalogue views,\\ncheckpoint overlays, provenance overlays and domain-specific\\nexplainability overlays; it must not redefine ABG runtime facts (P3, P6).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ODD.md#ODD%2F11.%20Core%20law%2F11.5%20Current%20state%20is%20a%20projection%20over%20constructive%20history\",\"start_line\":670}],\"label\":\"ODD projection and query lane\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:68488250933586b7cf75d39d4f345fde","key":352,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:68488250933586b7cf75d39d4f345fde\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"Authoritative WHAT located by product-definition what bindings; specification/ is the default software-development location. It defines intent, product position, goals, requirements and scenarios.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":571,\"path\":\"standards/ODD.md\",\"quote\":\"The product definition's `what` bindings locate the authoritative WHAT;\\n`specification/` is the default software-development location. It defines\\nintent, product position, goals, requirements and scenarios (P6).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ODD.md#ODD%2F10.%20What%20an%20ODD%20product%20is%2FProduct%20specification%20%28software-development%20topology%29\",\"start_line\":569}],\"label\":\"Product specification\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:e8fba98a082000f2293a25bde2a6c895","key":353,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:e8fba98a082000f2293a25bde2a6c895\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"Authoritative HOW located by product-definition how bindings; build_tenants/ is the default software-development location. It carries design, GTL publications, code, tests and local proof surfaces.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":577,\"path\":\"standards/ODD.md\",\"quote\":\"The product definition's `how` bindings locate the authoritative HOW;\\n`build_tenants/` is the default software-development location. It carries\\ndesign, GTL publications, code, tests and local proof surfaces (P6).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ODD.md#ODD%2F10.%20What%20an%20ODD%20product%20is%2FProduct%20realisation%20%28software-development%20topology%29\",\"start_line\":575}],\"label\":\"Product realisation\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:66f74c8f29b280b5c3f16e2a8b3d89fe","key":354,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:66f74c8f29b280b5c3f16e2a8b3d89fe\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"Service/query layers may own transport, sessions, routing, browser-safe projection and APIs; they own neither runtime truth nor continuation truth.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":598,\"path\":\"standards/ODD.md\",\"quote\":\"Service or query layers may own transport, sessions, routing,\\nbrowser-safe projection and API surfaces. They own neither runtime truth\\nnor continuation truth. The real constructive carrier is never hidden\\nbehind the word service (P6).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ODD.md#ODD%2F10.%20What%20an%20ODD%20product%20is%2FQuery%20and%20service%20layers\",\"start_line\":595}],\"label\":\"Service and query layers\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:39e42e814d731b3e0b9630ddf1b8e191","key":355,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:39e42e814d731b3e0b9630ddf1b8e191\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"Machine-readable catalogue of retained graph functions on the live line; recommended minimum fields are name, inputs, outputs, intent and public/helper role.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":653,\"path\":\"standards/ODD.md\",\"quote\":\"The live line must publish a machine-readable function catalogue. At\\nminimum each retained function should expose its name, inputs, outputs,\\nintent, and public or helper role. A callable surface that exists only in\\nprose or in prompt memory leaves the product under-built (P6, P3).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ODD.md#ODD%2F11.%20Core%20law%2F11.3%20The%20function%20catalogue%20is%20published\",\"start_line\":650}],\"label\":\"Function catalogue\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:81f6906b71f893b3c94e1dfc03ff9522","key":356,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:81f6906b71f893b3c94e1dfc03ff9522\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"Operative publication surface for public graph-function carriers, traversed graphs, typed node/vector surfaces and bound semantic jobs or equivalent outer callable contracts. Refined live inner boundaries have lawful GTL boundary surfaces such as RefinementBoundary or CandidateFamily.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":666,\"path\":\"standards/ODD.md\",\"quote\":\"Where a public carrier refines into inner executable structure, the live\\ntraversal boundaries are published explicitly through lawful GTL boundary\\nsurfaces such as `RefinementBoundary` or `CandidateFamily`. The outer\\npublic carrier remains the callable contract (P4a, P3).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ODD.md#ODD%2F11.%20Core%20law%2F11.4%20The%20GTL%20module%20is%20the%20operative%20publication%20surface\",\"start_line\":663}],\"label\":\"GTL module\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:38deb25eaedf22835dddaba18b4d70a8","key":357,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:38deb25eaedf22835dddaba18b4d70a8\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"Audit of the unique execution authority for an affected ODD traversal, including traversal selection/advance; invocation/supervision; retry/correction/continuation/re-entry; runtime event emission/append/replay/projection; and closure fold/assurance gate. It examines authority-bearing implementation surfaces, not artifacts alone.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":737,\"path\":\"standards/ODD.md\",\"quote\":\"Reviewing produced artifacts alone does not satisfy the audit. It must\\ninclude a code, call-graph or static-surface review appropriate to the\\nlanguage and tenant, and it must name the evidence used to rule out hidden\\nexecution authority (P6).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ODD.md#ODD%2F11.%20Core%20law%2F11.5B%20Execution%20authority%20audit\",\"start_line\":734}],\"label\":\"Execution-authority audit\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:a5d43a54e9b6c1b4035264da5197bcbd","key":358,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:a5d43a54e9b6c1b4035264da5197bcbd\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[\"A product is built with the ODD profile.\"],\"definition\":\"F18's authored foundation-to-law table imports F1 frames/context, F2 transitions/steps/configuration, F3 results, F4 work-state/resumption/reuse, F6 claims/evidence/assessment/acceptance, F9 a_c, F10 constitutional chain/outcome/build tenants, F11 change/ambiguity, F12 project binding, F13 work carriers and F15 release/successor conservation; rules and choices retain their owners. Adopted instance premises, not foundational deductions: I1 externally admitted selected Product outcome; I2 mutable workspace beside immutable ledger/event log; I3 bounded probabilistic workers whose reports/artifacts are observations; I4 installed method-product release, possibly an earlier self release. The 25 rows distinguish derived consequences from profile/product/consumer/other-member choices. Standing includes P0 recovered; P1/P2/P3/P4a/P6 independent; P4b derived from P0/P2; P5 derived from P0/P6. Consumer applications decide nothing beyond rule owners. §1's opening, §16 failure patterns, §19 checklist and §20 compression add no independent law; §11 decides built correctness and §9 move compliance.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":82,\"path\":\"standards/ODD.md\",\"quote\":\"This member is material family F18, outcome-driven development. The table\\nbelow shows which of its rules follow from which premises, in the format\\nof [FOUNDATIONS §3 Foundation to law](FOUNDATIONS.md#foundation-to-law),\\nwhich also states the standing of the consequences. Under\\n[PROFILES §1](PROFILES.md#1-the-boundary) the family imports the families\\nits rows rest on; their rules and choices keep their owners:\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ODD.md#ODD%2F1.%20Position%2FFoundation%20to%20law\",\"start_line\":77},{\"end_line\":109,\"path\":\"standards/ODD.md\",\"quote\":\"Its instance premises hold where a product is built with this profile;\\nthey are adopted with it and do not follow from the foundations (P1, P6):\\n\\n- I1: a selected Product outcome is admitted as external authority for\\n  the work;\\n- I2: the work changes a mutable workspace, beside which an immutable\\n  ledger and event log record the admitted work;\\n- I3: bounded probabilistic workers carry out the constructive actions,\\n  and their reports and artifacts are observations;\\n- I4: the product is built with an installed release of a method product,\\n  which may be an earlier release of the product itself.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ODD.md#ODD%2F1.%20Position%2FFoundation%20to%20law\",\"start_line\":99}],\"label\":\"F18 foundation-to-law derivation\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:ccf788aa3cfe567da2d3eff370213cba","key":359,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:ccf788aa3cfe567da2d3eff370213cba\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"Source-described constructive evaluation loop, referenced through §11.5D: separate authorities for synthesize_model, eval_gap, evaluate_next and evaluate_action; immutable ledger/event log admitting observations; closure fold; replay; lawful yield; selected-outcome-bounded action selection. Closure decisions form a closed sum type with seven decisions and cause-dependent core mappings; evaluate_next is total. The supplied table names only some states and does not supply the full operational algebra.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":123,\"path\":\"standards/ODD.md\",\"quote\":\"the four functions `synthesize_model`, `eval_gap`, `evaluate_next` and `evaluate_action`, and the duty of a design, ticket, module or proof to name the one it implements or consumes\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ODD.md#ODD%2F1.%20Position%2FFoundation%20to%20law\",\"start_line\":123},{\"end_line\":128,\"path\":\"standards/ODD.md\",\"quote\":\"the seven closure decisions, their causes, the two causes of a typed no-action and the default of graph following in A4\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ODD.md#ODD%2F1.%20Position%2FFoundation%20to%20law\",\"start_line\":128}],\"label\":\"Referenced constructive evaluation and yield loop\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:bcaa8a8d820aec2a089181d683a453df","key":360,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:bcaa8a8d820aec2a089181d683a453df\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[\"Applies to every ODD product over GTL/ABG.\"],\"definition\":\"The profile's constructive homeostasis loop runs from intent lineage and model synthesis through observation to the next lawful action. Its operative functions are synthesize_model, eval_gap, evaluate_next and evaluate_action. It corrects toward required conditions as observations arrive, without guaranteeing convergence or the adequacy of those conditions.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":788,\"path\":\"standards/ODD.md\",\"quote\":\"it corrects towards the required conditions as observations arrive,\\nguarantees neither convergence nor the adequacy of those conditions, and\\nits diagnoses distinguish the four causes named there (P2, P6).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ODD.md#ODD%2F11.%20Core%20law%2F11.5D%20Constructive%20evaluation%20and%20yield%20loop\",\"start_line\":786}],\"label\":\"Constructive evaluation and yield loop\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:3c87e88b6006249dbc37ff1e00860b70","key":361,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:3c87e88b6006249dbc37ff1e00860b70\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"Loop carrier vocabulary: IntentLineage is admitted source intent and lineage from a human, imported source, prior product, intent engine or prior synthesized construction intent, backed by ABG event-log truth. ProductAssetModel is desired and known typed asset truth synthesized from lineage, prior model and admitted product truth, with admitted-event and product-projection publication refs; it is neither runtime fact nor action authority. Worksite is the observable workspace, runtime archive, transform assets, product asset root, profile and file/process state. RuntimeEventLog is append-only admitted runtime facts; RuntimeProjection is replay-derived runtime state over event log and execution basis. ObservationSnapshot is a read-only runtime/worksite view; GapPressureRow represents missing, partial, blocked, waiting or ambiguous asset/evidence pressure. TargetObligationBinding binds pressure to the exact selected outcome, admitted prerequisite/experiment basis, assets, roles, evidence and admissible outcomes. ActionCatalog publishes lawful graph functions, vectors, targets, inputs and eligible outcomes. NextActionBasis is the dispatch sum initial_selection, post_yield_resume, post_close_graph_continuation, post_retry, post_repair, post_reenter, post_reprice or post_block, not a controller. PriorityProjection deterministically ranks bound lawful actions under visible policy. ConstructionIntent is an admitted selected action for one bounded invocation preserving outcome/basis refs. AdmittedEvidence includes worker, process, product, execution, materialization, liveness and postflight evidence, without worker self-closure. EdgeFulfillmentLedger carries evidence and convergence for one edge attempt/version. EdgeClosureDecision carries closure truth. NextActionProjection reads current truth and NextActionBasis and selects only when lawful.\",\"exceptions\":[\"post_reprice carries a re-entry request and no action-selection authority.\"],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":847,\"path\":\"standards/ODD.md\",\"quote\":\"| `NextActionProjection` | Read model that observes `NextActionBasis` plus current truth and selects a next graph action only when lawful. | ABG next-action evaluation projection with product policy. |\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ODD.md#ODD%2F11.%20Core%20law%2F11.5D%20Constructive%20evaluation%20and%20yield%20loop\",\"start_line\":847},{\"end_line\":839,\"path\":\"standards/ODD.md\",\"quote\":\"| `TargetObligationBinding` | Exact binding from gap pressure to the selected Product outcome, any admitted prerequisite or experiment basis, target assets, required roles, evidence refs, and admissible graph outcomes. | Product domain binding over GTL/ABG action authority. |\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ODD.md#ODD%2F11.%20Core%20law%2F11.5D%20Constructive%20evaluation%20and%20yield%20loop\",\"start_line\":839}],\"label\":\"Constructive loop carriers\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:43f24abc172ed34fa00c9cdc0a76989f","key":362,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:43f24abc172ed34fa00c9cdc0a76989f\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"The selected Product outcome is external authority for the loop under SPEC_METHOD §3. An admitted bounded prerequisite or experiment can also supply a bounded work basis. Models, gaps, assurance, ledgers and projections interpret these bases but do not author, select or enlarge the outcome.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":795,\"path\":\"standards/ODD.md\",\"quote\":\"Product models, gaps, assurance, ledgers and\\nprojections may interpret that outcome but cannot author, select or\\nenlarge it. `evaluate_next` may select material work only within that\\noutcome or within an admitted bounded prerequisite or experiment.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ODD.md#ODD%2F11.%20Core%20law%2F11.5D%20Constructive%20evaluation%20and%20yield%20loop\",\"start_line\":792}],\"label\":\"Selected outcome and admitted bounded basis\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:505ca2ca015711bae0650516cdea1113","key":363,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:505ca2ca015711bae0650516cdea1113\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"Four separate authority functions: synthesize_model takes IntentLineage, prior ProductAssetModel and admitted product truth and produces ProductAssetModel; eval_gap takes ProductAssetModel, RuntimeEventLog, RuntimeProjection and Worksite and produces ObservationSnapshot and GapPressureRow; evaluate_next takes NextActionBasis, fresh eval_gap, TargetObligationBinding, ActionCatalog and Policy and produces PriorityProjection, NextActionProjection and selected_action, plus its own core result for typed no-action; evaluate_action takes ConstructionIntent, AdmittedEvidence, TargetObligationBinding and Policy and produces EdgeFulfillmentLedger and EdgeClosureDecision.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":851,\"path\":\"standards/ODD.md\",\"quote\":\"The loop has one model-synthesis function and three distinct evaluation\\nfunctions. They may share underlying libraries; they must not share\\nauthority (P6):\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ODD.md#ODD%2F11.%20Core%20law%2F11.5D%20Constructive%20evaluation%20and%20yield%20loop\",\"start_line\":849}],\"label\":\"Model synthesis and three evaluation functions\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:5656d4fa0bbe717157f7717db2dae858","key":364,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:5656d4fa0bbe717157f7717db2dae858\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"The governed work pair comprises mutable workspace W and immutable ledger L of closure-relevant work over W, anchored and ordered by immutable event spine E. Evaluator work Ev evaluates declared L snapshots. L records admitted callout basis, observed deltas, file refs, digests, execution evidence, touched obligations, claims, evaluator inputs/outputs and admission status, rather than copying W. Ledger attention is a structural analogy: typed, immutable, lineage-constrained, policy-bounded and replayable, without a transformer-attention implementation dependency.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":928,\"path\":\"standards/ODD.md\",\"quote\":\"F_P acts in W.\\nAdmission records governed facts in L.\\nE orders and anchors L entries with predecessor refs.\\nEv evaluates a declared L snapshot, not ambient W.\\nEv output is itself F_P work and is admitted back into L/E.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ODD.md#ODD%2F11.%20Core%20law%2F11.5D%20Constructive%20evaluation%20and%20yield%20loop\",\"start_line\":924}],\"label\":\"Workspace, ledger and evaluator attention\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:34ccd9efb88618a7ee79652a99297483","key":365,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:34ccd9efb88618a7ee79652a99297483\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"The closed closure-decision vocabulary is close, yield, retry, repair, re-enter, reprice and block. These evaluate the predicate that the edge's obligations are fulfilled on the exact basis. Cause refinements map each refined value to exactly one core result without adding decisions or core values. Selection results evaluate whether a published lawful action can be selected for the current gap on the exact basis. Candidate availability, candidate acceptance and edge fulfillment are distinct predicates; ACTIVATION acceptance dispositions accept, local_repair, re_enter and reject are not closure decisions.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1178,\"path\":\"standards/ODD.md\",\"quote\":\"A closure decision is not a disposition and is never recorded\\nas one, and no disposition is a closure decision: `repair` is not\\n`local_repair`, and `re-enter` is not `re_enter`. Edge closure is\\nevidence toward acceptance and never acceptance itself\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ODD.md#ODD%2F11.%20Core%20law%2F11.5D%20Constructive%20evaluation%20and%20yield%20loop\",\"start_line\":1175}],\"label\":\"Closure, selection, availability and acceptance results\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:790dc2b2d5efd074ca29cd1903ea9f8d","key":366,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:790dc2b2d5efd074ca29cd1903ea9f8d\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"ODD supplies structural product shape; each domain product owns its asset meanings, proof lanes and query overlays. The same structural law can build different domain products.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1409,\"path\":\"standards/ODD.md\",\"quote\":\"This profile gives the product shape, not the domain semantics. The same\\nODD structural law can build many different domain products, and each\\nproduct defines its own asset meanings, proof lanes and query overlays.\\nStructural GTL law and product-specific semantic law are never confused\\n(P1).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ODD.md#ODD%2F11.%20Core%20law%2F11.6%20Product-specific%20semantics%20sit%20above%20the%20shared%20carrier\",\"start_line\":1405}],\"label\":\"Structural profile and product semantic law\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:c268d2b1bafeebb5b3c54ed7be08bb2e","key":367,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:c268d2b1bafeebb5b3c54ed7be08bb2e\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[\"The operator uses only declared authority surfaces.\"],\"definition\":\"A manual walkthrough identifies current asset/node state, the next lawful vector and its public graph-function carrier, required inputs/evaluators/output contract/carried environment, constructs or assesses the next asset/checkpoint, and repeats to target-relative closure. A vector is the constitutional transition contract; its graph function is the published constructive program realizing it.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1424,\"path\":\"standards/ODD.md\",\"quote\":\"3. determine the required inputs, evaluators, output contract and carried\\n   environment;\\n4. construct or assess the next asset, a produced asset or checkpoint;\\n5. repeat until target-relative closure is reached.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ODD.md#ODD%2F11.%20Core%20law%2F11.7%20Manual%20walkthrough%20must%20still%20be%20lawful\",\"start_line\":1421}],\"label\":\"Lawful manual traversal\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:26c627c4204c2f1f3b1820e20d788928","key":368,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:26c627c4204c2f1f3b1820e20d788928\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"Agentic conformance has two halves: an F_P walkthrough proves the constitutional process can be followed on real work from declared authority, and an F_D deterministic gate admits produced artifacts. The walkthrough covers intake triage, smallest lawful re-entry, specification/requirement/design/ticket chain, constructive evaluation and closure proof. A minimal authority packet carries input/output contract, required context, role, evaluator regime, provenance and the smallest sufficient declared authority with source refs.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1452,\"path\":\"standards/ODD.md\",\"quote\":\"Conformance has two halves: an F_P proof that the process can be followed,\\nand an F_D gate that admits the produced artifacts (P6).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ODD.md#ODD%2F11.%20Core%20law%2F11.7A%20Conforming%20agentic%20development\",\"start_line\":1451}],\"label\":\"Agentic walkthrough and artifact admission\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:b6360702187f5ffc1352d86f863767c8","key":369,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:b6360702187f5ffc1352d86f863767c8\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[\"Applies to an ODD or graph-native boundary.\"],\"definition\":\"Real authority-path negative proof exercises the supported Product authority path. Closure-grade evidence identifies entry and authority, invalidates the actual authority-bearing input, exercises that path, proves refusal before the prohibited effect and establishes that no legacy, fallback, reconstruction or parallel path succeeds. Source, packaged, installed and runtime absence are distinct claims.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1536,\"path\":\"standards/ODD.md\",\"quote\":\"Closure-grade negative evidence identifies the supported entry and the\\ngoverning authority; invalidates the real authority-bearing input;\\nexercises the supported path; proves refusal before the prohibited\\neffect; and establishes that no legacy, fallback, reconstruction or\\nparallel path succeeds. Source, packaged, installed and runtime absence\\nare distinct claims (P6, P3).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ODD.md#ODD%2F11.%20Core%20law%2F11.7B%20Real%20authority-path%20negative%20proof%20%28STDO-UP-010%29\",\"start_line\":1531}],\"label\":\"Real authority-path negative proof\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:6fdea63aaeebf1d9349b481121a8bf88","key":370,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:6fdea63aaeebf1d9349b481121a8bf88\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"Graph composition uses a cumulative typed environment. A later function can require any typed binding available in that carried environment. Each retained GraphFunction should declare environment.requires, environment.provides and environment.carries.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1563,\"path\":\"standards/ODD.md\",\"quote\":\"Each retained `GraphFunction` should declare `environment.requires`,\\n`environment.provides` and `environment.carries`. A later function may\\nrequire any typed binding available in the cumulative carried\\nenvironment, not only the immediately previous output (P4a, P4b).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ODD.md#ODD%2F11.%20Core%20law%2F11.8%20Cumulative%20environment%20law%20is%20mandatory\",\"start_line\":1560}],\"label\":\"Cumulative typed environment\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:0ca7e123739fe9e8cd201c94ddb48a7c","key":371,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:0ca7e123739fe9e8cd201c94ddb48a7c\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"Global convergence requires lawful inner closure, preservation of the enclosing coarse contract after fold-back and agreement between zoomed and unzoomed open/closed status. Current requirement proof is proof-lane aware: a governed realized witness appropriate to the requirement class is required; realized testcases or archived test evidence are the usual immediate pressure for an active software line.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1575,\"path\":\"standards/ODD.md\",\"quote\":\"When an outer public carrier is refined\\ninto inner executable structure, the refined inner chain must close\\nlawfully; the enclosing coarse contract must also stay true after\\nfold-back; and zoomed and unzoomed views must agree on whether the\\nenclosing carrier is open or closed (P4a, P2).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ODD.md#ODD%2F11.%20Core%20law%2F11.9%20Global%20convergence%20must%20be%20stable%20under%20zoom\",\"start_line\":1571}],\"label\":\"Global convergence under refinement\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:4e9e4a92055d8fabb6a672153a494baa","key":372,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:4e9e4a92055d8fabb6a672153a494baa\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"Scenarios are graph-native proving surfaces. A bundle should identify the exercised feature/use-case boundary, pre-existing assets, expected vectors, significant paths and closure evidence. Declared scenarios and use cases are preferred sources for selecting significant code/control proving paths because they pressure feature intent and design decisions.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1592,\"path\":\"standards/ODD.md\",\"quote\":\"Scenarios are graph-native proving surfaces, not only test\\ndocumentation. A scenario bundle should make clear which feature or\\nuse-case boundary is exercised; which assets are expected to exist before\\nthe scenario starts; which vectors are expected to be traversed; which\\nsignificant paths are expected to be exercised; and what evidence closes\\nthe scenario (P2, P6).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ODD.md#ODD%2F12.%20Scenario%20rule\",\"start_line\":1587}],\"label\":\"Scenario bundle\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:e22ced7f66cd72435a045f8206873289","key":373,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:e22ced7f66cd72435a045f8206873289\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[\"The product has an installable development form.\"],\"definition\":\"Installed-development proof is decisive proof run against that installed form in isolation. For graph-native ODD products the proving lane should exercise installation, project bootstrap, graph traversal, evidence collection and target-relative closure. ASSURANCE §5 owns this rule.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1608,\"path\":\"standards/ODD.md\",\"quote\":\"Where the product has an installable development form, decisive proof\\nruns against that installed development form in an isolated environment.\\nFor a graph-native ODD product the proving lane should exercise install,\\nproject bootstrap, graph traversal, evidence collection and\\ntarget-relative closure. Direct source checks stay useful and do not\\nreplace installed-dev proof (P6, P3). This rule is the profile's binding of\\n[ASSURANCE §5 Installed dev proof](ASSURANCE.md#5-installed-dev-proof), which\\nowns it.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ODD.md#ODD%2F13.%20Installed-dev%20rule\",\"start_line\":1601}],\"label\":\"Installed-dev proof\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:1a237778b4d22a437e7c3d2c0bd6aca4","key":374,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:1a237778b4d22a437e7c3d2c0bd6aca4\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"ODD dogfooding is development through the graph-native method the product provides, increasingly using explicit assets, vectors, graph functions, scenario bundles and target-relative closure.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1618,\"path\":\"standards/ODD.md\",\"quote\":\"The project should therefore increasingly describe and\\nbuild itself through explicit assets, explicit vectors, explicit graph\\nfunctions, explicit scenario bundles and explicit target-relative closure.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ODD.md#ODD%2F14.%20Dogfooding%20rule\",\"start_line\":1616}],\"label\":\"ODD dogfooding\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:1970c5a23af72944a34f6f82fdce4f4f","key":375,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:1970c5a23af72944a34f6f82fdce4f4f\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"Release versions belong to release process/metadata, not constitutional graph truth. Graph-native method concerns current assets, vectors, closures and authority; immutable RC publication, version-line selector advancement and exact-cut acceptance belong to the separate RELEASE process surface.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1628,\"path\":\"standards/ODD.md\",\"quote\":\"A release version is not constitutional graph truth; it belongs to the\\nrelease process and release metadata. The graph-native method concerns\\ncurrent assets, current vectors, current closures and current authority.\\nImmutable RC publication, version-line selector advancement and exact-cut\\nacceptance stay a separate process surface, [RELEASE](RELEASE.md) (P3,\\nP6).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ODD.md#ODD%2F15.%20Release%20boundary\",\"start_line\":1623}],\"label\":\"Graph truth and release process boundary\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:e7edc30111d4c0953afc57895e74e66f","key":376,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:e7edc30111d4c0953afc57895e74e66f\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[\"An agent or designer is instructed to build a product using ODD.\"],\"definition\":\"The expected invocation sequence is: read SPEC_METHOD; read an existing product-specific method; read local Intent, Product, relevant requirements and active design; identify source-to-outcome semantic chain, typed assets and public graph functions; define the machine-readable catalogue; define/update GTL outer callable carriers and live traversal boundaries; define scale-consistent coarse/inner/proof closure; complete the execution-authority audit for affected runtime/plugin/worker/event/projection/assurance/closure/continuation surfaces; define the constructive loop and closure vocabulary including lawful yield; define projection/query over admitted history with source coherence; only then implement code, policy and transport.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1695,\"path\":\"standards/ODD.md\",\"quote\":\"13. define the projection and query lane as a projection over admitted\\n    constructive history, including the structural coherence rule between\\n    the read model and its source carrier;\\n14. only then implement code, policy and transport surfaces.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ODD.md#ODD%2F17.%20Invocation%20rule\",\"start_line\":1692}],\"label\":\"ODD product-authoring sequence\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:1e047b6ff0b6ea833072e579043bf818","key":377,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:1e047b6ff0b6ea833072e579043bf818\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[\"Starting cold in a concrete ODD product.\"],\"definition\":\"Cold-start reading is ordered. General route: SPEC_METHOD; ODD; product stdo_<label>.json; applicable bound project reference-frame basis and authorized activation packet; bound Intent; bound Product; relevant bound requirements; active bound design; GTL module, catalogue and queries. World-model route inserts WORLD_MODEL after ODD, uses relevant bound requirement families and current bound design, and includes the proof lane with the final GTL/catalogue/query surfaces. ODD sets structural expectations, the product method sets domain law and local surfaces set the current build line. Skipping the order usually risks missing domain meaning or realizing it through the wrong carrier.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1703,\"path\":\"standards/ODD.md\",\"quote\":\"Starting cold in a concrete ODD product, read in the order below (P1, P2).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ODD.md#ODD%2F18.%20Cold-start%20reading%20order\",\"start_line\":1703},{\"end_line\":1716,\"path\":\"standards/ODD.md\",\"quote\":\"9. the GTL module, function catalogue and query surfaces.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ODD.md#ODD%2F18.%20Cold-start%20reading%20order%2FGeneral%20ODD%20product\",\"start_line\":1716},{\"end_line\":1730,\"path\":\"standards/ODD.md\",\"quote\":\"10. the GTL module, function catalogue, query surfaces and proof lane.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ODD.md#ODD%2F18.%20Cold-start%20reading%20order%2FWorld-model%20product\",\"start_line\":1730}],\"label\":\"General and world-model cold-start routes\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:e185446f4b1c692b239122ba48b7c9d5","key":378,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:e185446f4b1c692b239122ba48b7c9d5\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"ODD's canonical compression describes graph-native GTL/ABG product authoring: typed assets, named functions, published catalogue, operative GTL module, ABG execution authority, one constructive loop, current-state projections over constructive history, lawful manual explainability, outcome-first framework realization and agentic walkthrough plus deterministic admission. It is a derived acquisition surface with no determination of its own; its declared sources are same-digest §§1, 2, 11.1–11.5D, 11.7 and 11.7A.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1790,\"path\":\"standards/ODD.md\",\"quote\":\"This section is a compression of this member, a derived surface in the\\nsense of [ACTIVATION §2](ACTIVATION.md#2-context-construction-under-an-envelope),\\nAcquisition. Its sources are §1, §2, §11.1 to §11.5D, §11.7 and §11.7A of\\nthis member at the same digest, and it owns no determination. Where it and\\na source section differ, the source section decides\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ODD.md#ODD%2F20.%20Canonical%20compression\",\"start_line\":1786}],\"label\":\"ODD derived canonical compression\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:273ec344d475ed17ef6961eeeb518c2f","key":379,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:273ec344d475ed17ef6961eeeb518c2f\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"POSTING_GUIDE owns the governed project's commentary layer: post purpose, authority boundary, location, identity, categories, structure, discussion state, posting rules and ratification. It consumes PRODUCT_DEFINITION §8 ticketing.comments, TICKETS §1 work carriers, SPEC_METHOD §2 authority surfaces and EVALUATION §1 claims/evidence without redefining them; SPEC_METHOD §6 owns shared-method adoption. Clauses cite FOUNDATIONS principles P0–P6.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":6,\"path\":\"standards/POSTING_GUIDE.md\",\"quote\":\"Guide. Owns the commentary layer of a governed project: what a post is\\nfor, its boundary with authority, where posts live, their identity,\\ncategories and structure, their discussion state, the posting rules and\\nratification. Consumes\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/POSTING_GUIDE.md#POSTING_GUIDE\",\"start_line\":3}],\"label\":\"POSTING_GUIDE\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:43a55d217680888d5abfc84ed0225020","key":380,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:43a55d217680888d5abfc84ed0225020\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"A post is working commentary for analysis, criticism, proposed changes, handoff or repricing confidence. It may influence later specification/design but is not constitutional truth. Its category is one of REVIEW (critique), STRATEGY (proposed technical/method direction), GAP (precise insufficiency/contradiction), SCHEMA (data/event/interface/contract shape), HANDOFF (bounded context/task-state transfer) or MATRIX (explicit decision-option comparison).\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":28,\"path\":\"standards/POSTING_GUIDE.md\",\"quote\":\"A post is not constitutional truth. It is working commentary, and it may\\nlater influence specification or design (P6).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/POSTING_GUIDE.md#POSTING_GUIDE%2F1.%20Position\",\"start_line\":27},{\"end_line\":85,\"path\":\"standards/POSTING_GUIDE.md\",\"quote\":\"- `REVIEW`: critique of code, specification, design or another post;\\n- `STRATEGY`: a proposed technical or methodological direction;\\n- `GAP`: a precise insufficiency or contradiction;\\n- `SCHEMA`: the shape of a data model, event model, interface or contract;\\n- `HANDOFF`: a bounded transfer of context or task state; and\\n- `MATRIX`: an explicit comparison of options for a decision.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/POSTING_GUIDE.md#POSTING_GUIDE%2F5.%20Categories\",\"start_line\":80}],\"label\":\"Post and category vocabulary\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:39bdea0a1e0944501e86c53001a7d5cb","key":381,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:39bdea0a1e0944501e86c53001a7d5cb\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"A post carrier is bound by ticketing.comments.root, defaulting locally to .ai-workspace/comments/<agent>/. Default file identity is YYYYMMDDTHHMMSS_CATEGORY_SUBJECT.md; 20260327T120000_REVIEW_bootloader-boundary.md is an example, not a required post. Non-file carriers preserve equivalent stable identity, publication time, category, subject, author, discussion state and supersession history.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":43,\"path\":\"standards/POSTING_GUIDE.md\",\"quote\":\"Posts live at the location the product definition binds as\\n`ticketing.comments.root` (P6, P3). The default local-file\\nbinding is:\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/POSTING_GUIDE.md#POSTING_GUIDE%2F3.%20Location\",\"start_line\":41},{\"end_line\":74,\"path\":\"standards/POSTING_GUIDE.md\",\"quote\":\"A carrier that is not a file must preserve an equivalent stable post\\nidentity, publication time, category, subject, author, discussion state\\nand supersession history (P3, P4b).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/POSTING_GUIDE.md#POSTING_GUIDE%2F4.%20Carrier%20identity\",\"start_line\":72}],\"label\":\"Commentary carrier and post identity\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:38b9914ee8bbc6790e310e2774932d74","key":382,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:38b9914ee8bbc6790e310e2774932d74\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"The post template has title CATEGORY: Subject; Author; ISO 8601 Date; Addresses identifying the artifact/issue/boundary; Status initially Draft; optional ISO 8601 Updated; Summary; Analysis; and Recommended Action. MATRIX uses a central decision table instead of free prose. Discussion states are Draft (author shaping), Open (published active discussion) and Closed (discussion concluded).\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":98,\"path\":\"standards/POSTING_GUIDE.md\",\"quote\":\"# {CATEGORY}: {Subject}\\n\\n**Author**: {agent}\\n**Date**: {ISO 8601}\\n**Addresses**: {artifact, issue, or boundary under discussion}\\n**Status**: Draft\\n**Updated**: {ISO 8601, optional}\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/POSTING_GUIDE.md#POSTING_GUIDE%2F6.%20Structure\",\"start_line\":92},{\"end_line\":120,\"path\":\"standards/POSTING_GUIDE.md\",\"quote\":\"- `Draft`: the author is still shaping the post;\\n- `Open`: the post is published into an active discussion; and\\n- `Closed`: the discussion has concluded.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/POSTING_GUIDE.md#POSTING_GUIDE%2F7.%20Discussion%20state%20and%20mutability\",\"start_line\":118}],\"label\":\"Post structure and discussion state\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:91a6d5513e1d5d62fed15c7f4838d766","key":383,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:91a6d5513e1d5d62fed15c7f4838d766\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"PRODUCT_DEFINITION is a tier-2 member owning project binding through the overlay, definition relations, constitutional-set sufficiency, installed release/toolchain management, semantic resolution, local binding, collective frame basis, WHAT/HOW/work carriers, discovery/composition, conformance cases, STDO-SURFACE-001 and bootstrap. It consumes tier-1 FOUNDATIONS, REFERENCE_FRAME, ACTIVATION and EVALUATION without adding tier-1 definitions. Its contexts are product-definition-routing (§§1–4, 9, 12), semantic-resolution (§§5, 6, 10) and build-tenancy (§8). Generic WHAT/HOW, lineage, build-tenant, release and assurance law remain with the cited owners. Its schemas/templates/filenames/fields/commands are Product realization shapes accepted as interoperability boundaries, not profile terms.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":30,\"path\":\"standards/PRODUCT_DEFINITION.md\",\"quote\":\"The schemas, templates, filenames, manifest\\nfields and commands named here are this Product's own realisation shapes,\\naccepted as interoperability boundaries under §11; they are not profile\\nterms. Three bounded contexts are\\nowned here: product-definition-routing (§1 to §4, §9, §12),\\nsemantic-resolution (§5, §6, §10) and build-tenancy (§8).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/PRODUCT_DEFINITION.md#PRODUCT_DEFINITION\",\"start_line\":25}],\"label\":\"PRODUCT_DEFINITION member\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:8048859bf02f15f5c3158d9ca21e6198","key":384,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:8048859bf02f15f5c3158d9ca21e6198\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[\"Under the selected complete STDO basis.\"],\"definition\":\"The product-definition-routing context, urn:stdo:bounded-context:product-definition-routing, owns overlay, definition, discovery, locator and composition meanings. A product definition is a JSON locator/relation overlay for one continuing product WHAT, independent of existing layout. Its definition root is its containing directory; relative URI references resolve against the definition file's retrieval URI. product.source_project locates a source-project root that may be elsewhere. The conventional filename is stdo_<label>.json, with stdo_default.json the single-definition source-project default.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":41,\"path\":\"standards/PRODUCT_DEFINITION.md\",\"quote\":\"This member owns the product-definition-routing bounded context,\\n`urn:stdo:bounded-context:product-definition-routing`, under the selected\\ncomplete STDO basis, and defines that context's overlay, definition,\\ndiscovery, locator and composition concepts. The JSON schema named below\\nrealises the accepted interoperability shape of the overlay and is not a\\nsecond semantic owner (P6).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/PRODUCT_DEFINITION.md#PRODUCT_DEFINITION%2F1.%20Overlay%20and%20layout%20independence\",\"start_line\":36}],\"label\":\"Product definition overlay\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:c1ed13a1e7694716094389e56c921b63","key":385,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:c1ed13a1e7694716094389e56c921b63\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"Definition Label is a stable lowercase ASCII-letter/digit/hyphen/underscore discovery label unique only within a directory, not Product identity. Product-Definition Identity is product.definition_id, a stable URI for the mutable definition line, unique within the discovered workspace definition set. Immutable Products/releases retain separate identities. The normative JSON schema is schemas/product-definition.schema.json and the single fill-in form is templates/PRODUCT_DEFINITION_TEMPLATE.json; they standardize identity/location/relation/discovery fields without absorbing referenced meaning.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":58,\"path\":\"standards/PRODUCT_DEFINITION.md\",\"quote\":\"The suffix `<label>` is the Definition Label: a stable lowercase local\\ndiscovery label of ASCII letters, digits, hyphens or underscores, unique\\nonly among the definitions in the same directory. It is not Product\\nidentity. The `product.definition_id` URI inside the definition is the\\nProduct-Definition Identity: the stable identity of the mutable\\nproduct-definition line, unique within the discovered workspace definition\\nset. It identifies one continuing WHAT definition, not one immutable\\nreleased Product (P3).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/PRODUCT_DEFINITION.md#PRODUCT_DEFINITION%2F1.%20Overlay%20and%20layout%20independence\",\"start_line\":51}],\"label\":\"Definition identities, schema and template\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:4650f9cc9cfd8d82c104f3c11bf25352","key":386,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:4650f9cc9cfd8d82c104f3c11bf25352\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"F12 traces project-binding rules to foundational commitments plus instance premises: independent project authorities; chosen existing layout; shared workspace/machine; recurring terms with different context meanings; and immutable released method versions selected, installed and replaced by projects. P1, P2, P3 and P6 are independent; P0 is recovered; P5 derives from P0/P6 with the open-world premise; P4b derives from P0/P2 with the premise that step-produced facts are not re-acquirable. The family traces imports without owning that law, distinguishes consequences from member-owned interoperability/domain choices and supplies a per-row consumer-locus index.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":105,\"path\":\"standards/PRODUCT_DEFINITION.md\",\"quote\":\"The index also assigns to this family the rule of\\n[FOUNDATIONS §2 Imports between members](FOUNDATIONS.md#imports-between-members);\\nthe table traces that rule in its sixth row, whose rule column names that\\nsection, and owns none of it. Each commitment's standing is written as the\\ntable of commitments in FOUNDATIONS §3 states it.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/PRODUCT_DEFINITION.md#PRODUCT_DEFINITION%2F1.%20Overlay%20and%20layout%20independence%2FFoundation%20to%20law%3A%20binding%20a%20project%20to%20the%20method\",\"start_line\":101}],\"label\":\"F12 foundation-to-law family\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:cd46ea3f9d64e23d695883c0d8fb98b2","key":387,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:cd46ea3f9d64e23d695883c0d8fb98b2\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"A Constitutional Set is the complete selected governing document set for a product, with no prescribed file count. It collectively makes recoverable axioms (starting truths, invariants, refusal conditions), ontology (real kinds, identities, relations, boundaries, lifecycle), epistemology (evidence, observation, uncertainty, falsification, acceptability and decision authority), taxonomy (classifications preventing category collapse), and semantics (governed meanings of terms, relations, states, operations and outcomes). These are sufficiency dimensions, not filename classes or folders.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":191,\"path\":\"standards/PRODUCT_DEFINITION.md\",\"quote\":\"A Constitutional Set is the complete set of governing documents selected\\nfor a product, not a prescribed number of files. Collectively the selected\\nset makes five things recoverable for the governed scope (P2, P1):\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/PRODUCT_DEFINITION.md#PRODUCT_DEFINITION%2F3.%20Constitutional-set%20sufficiency\",\"start_line\":189}],\"label\":\"Constitutional Set\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:395e42597f3b0df9d733f31d1b45bed9","key":388,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:395e42597f3b0df9d733f31d1b45bed9\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[\"Within product-definition-routing.\"],\"definition\":\"Installed Release Basis is the pair of immutable stdo://releases/<cut>/ URI and installed-manifest SHA-256. The URI identifies an annotated immutable RC cut; the deterministic manifest binds tag object, commit, repository tree, standards subtree, exact standards inventory, member bytes and admitted auxiliary payloads. Its schema is schemas/installed-release-manifest.schema.json. The manifest is transport/integrity evidence, not a replacement constitution.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":239,\"path\":\"standards/PRODUCT_DEFINITION.md\",\"quote\":\"The URI identifies one immutable annotated RC cut. The digest identifies\\nthe deterministic installed-release manifest, which binds the cut's tag\\nobject, commit, repository tree, standards subtree, exact standards\\ninventory, member bytes and admitted auxiliary payloads. The manifest shape\\nis owned by `schemas/installed-release-manifest.schema.json`. The manifest\\nis transport and integrity evidence, not a replacement constitution (P6).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/PRODUCT_DEFINITION.md#PRODUCT_DEFINITION%2F4.%20Shared%20installed%20release%20basis%20and%20toolchain%20manager\",\"start_line\":234}],\"label\":\"Installed Release Basis\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:af0ac7f76ba62dab9f89ee2789b6ecd2","key":389,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:af0ac7f76ba62dab9f89ee2789b6ecd2\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"An Adoption Plan is a read-only deterministic acceptance object binding current Product Definition identity/bytes/current basis to one resolved immutable target cut, tag object, commit, tree and manifest digest. Its SHA-256 is an operator-presentable acceptance token, whose possession alone grants no authority. A Fleet Adoption Plan binds an authorized fleet root and the complete ordered per-definition plan-digest set.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":249,\"path\":\"standards/PRODUCT_DEFINITION.md\",\"quote\":\"Its SHA-256 is the\\noperator-presentable acceptance token. Possession of the token alone grants\\nno authority; a mismatch proves that the presented subject is no longer the\\nsubject being mutated (P6, P3). A Fleet Adoption Plan binds an authorised\\nfleet root and the complete ordered set of per-definition plan digests\\nunder the same law.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/PRODUCT_DEFINITION.md#PRODUCT_DEFINITION%2F4.%20Shared%20installed%20release%20basis%20and%20toolchain%20manager\",\"start_line\":244}],\"label\":\"Adoption and Fleet Adoption Plans\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:f5ea64751cc1eb33ef2ae5a9bbc3b09a","key":390,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:f5ea64751cc1eb33ef2ae5a9bbc3b09a\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"The STDO Toolchain Manager is a bounded executable realization that installs each immutable cut once in a shared versioned store, resolves logical release URIs to verified bytes, inventories/verifies complete distributions, synchronizes selected exact bases, plans and explicitly acceptedly performs adoption, manages declared marker-bounded agent bootstrap and applies operations to an explicitly discovered fleet. The store registry maps release URIs to paths/digests and owns neither Product selection nor method meaning.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":270,\"path\":\"standards/PRODUCT_DEFINITION.md\",\"quote\":\"- emits an exact digest-bound adoption plan from a mutable version-line\\n  selector and performs adoption only when that plan is explicitly\\n  accepted;\\n- manages the stable marker-bounded bootstrap in declared agent files; and\\n- applies those operations to an explicitly discovered fleet of Product\\n  Definitions.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/PRODUCT_DEFINITION.md#PRODUCT_DEFINITION%2F4.%20Shared%20installed%20release%20basis%20and%20toolchain%20manager\",\"start_line\":265}],\"label\":\"STDO Toolchain Manager\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:22c3599132a83101cd9b734284661c93","key":391,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:22c3599132a83101cd9b734284661c93\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"A Complete Consumer Update Plan binds one explicitly selected Product Definition and the complete companion population of one exact upstream release-matched cohort to owner-selected consumer bindings. Its invocation/plan/result are operation evidence, not a persistent dependency declaration, registry or lock. cohort-update presents a whole plan binding effect destinations, preimages, exact cohort bytes, companion tags/commits/subtrees/inventories, replacement dependency locators, native routes and declared derived-source observations. Product Definition owns composition; upstream cohort and Product release records own release/member identities.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":363,\"path\":\"standards/PRODUCT_DEFINITION.md\",\"quote\":\"The caller selects every native route and derived context\\nfor the claimed update scope; directory proximity or an empty discovery\\nresult cannot supply that selection, and an empty derived-context\\npopulation means the owner selected none, not that the manager established\\nthe absence of semantic context (P6, P3).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/PRODUCT_DEFINITION.md#PRODUCT_DEFINITION%2F4.%20Shared%20installed%20release%20basis%20and%20toolchain%20manager%2FExplicit%20complete%20consumer%20update\",\"start_line\":359}],\"label\":\"Complete consumer update\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:523af2ab7853a047877a596bb6f7f95e","key":392,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:523af2ab7853a047877a596bb6f7f95e\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"Toolchain outcomes are cause-refined core results for separate predicates: external effect occurrence; lawful admission/activation on an exact subject and basis; candidate availability after commencement; and a read-only command's own evaluated condition. Completion status, effect-end establishment, refusal cause and partial effects remain distinct data.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":410,\"path\":\"standards/PRODUCT_DEFINITION.md\",\"quote\":\"Outcomes as results. The outcomes of the manager's operations in §4,\\nits refusals, its reported completion and the recovery that\\nloss requires, are stated in the core result algebra of\\n[FOUNDATIONS §4 Results](FOUNDATIONS.md#results) through the refinements\\nof [ACTIVATION §3](ACTIVATION.md#3-step-results-and-disposition), each\\nfor its own predicate; the cause of an outcome selects its value, and the\\nmapping adds no core value (P5, P6):\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/PRODUCT_DEFINITION.md#PRODUCT_DEFINITION%2F4.%20Shared%20installed%20release%20basis%20and%20toolchain%20manager%2FExplicit%20complete%20consumer%20update\",\"start_line\":404}],\"label\":\"Toolchain effect and refusal result domains\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:c92508f838e93201cd94c393f5aefdbd","key":393,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:c92508f838e93201cd94c393f5aefdbd\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[\"Under the selected complete STDO basis.\"],\"definition\":\"Semantic-resolution law is owned in urn:stdo:bounded-context:semantic-resolution. A term is a lexical label in an occurrence. A bounded context is an explicitly identified semantic scope whose vocabulary, concepts and relations are jointly interpretable under named authority. A concept reference exactly locates an authority-owned meaning on a selected basis without minting meaning or authority. Every material occurrence's semantic address is (term, bounded-context identity, owning authority, selected basis, governed scope).\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":490,\"path\":\"standards/PRODUCT_DEFINITION.md\",\"quote\":\"A term is a lexical label used in an occurrence, not a context-free concept\\nidentity. A bounded context is an explicitly identified semantic scope in\\nwhich a governed vocabulary, concept set and relation set are jointly\\ninterpretable under named authority. A concept reference is an exact,\\nresolvable reference to a meaning owned by an authority under a selected\\nbasis; the reference locates that meaning and mints neither the meaning nor\\nits authority (P1, P3, P6).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/PRODUCT_DEFINITION.md#PRODUCT_DEFINITION%2F5.%20Bounded-context%20semantic%20resolution\",\"start_line\":484}],\"label\":\"Bounded-context semantic resolution\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:54629b053141a69765f840b7f0c3f90c","key":394,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:54629b053141a69765f840b7f0c3f90c\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"Four owner-authorized cross-context relation kinds: Semantic Import applies unchanged source meaning in declared target scope under FOUNDATIONS import law; Semantic Translation declares directional meaning change and loss and is not an import; Semantic Equivalence is an equality established by governing authorities while both concepts retain owners/contexts and neither adopts the other's meaning; Semantic Disambiguation selects one meaning for one scope without equating alternatives, using a declared import/translation/equivalence if the selected meaning is external. Specialisation is directional translation preserving declared source meaning while narrowing admissible instances or adding target constraints.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":598,\"path\":\"standards/PRODUCT_DEFINITION.md\",\"quote\":\"A specialisation is a directional translation whose target preserves the\\ndeclared source meaning while narrowing its admissible instances or adding\\ntarget-context constraints. It identifies the exact target concept, the\\npreserved and narrowed meaning, the excluded source instances, and the\\nabsence or law of any inverse. Calling a term a specialisation without\\nthose coordinates establishes nothing (P1, P3).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/PRODUCT_DEFINITION.md#PRODUCT_DEFINITION%2F5.%20Bounded-context%20semantic%20resolution\",\"start_line\":593}],\"label\":\"Semantic relations and specialisation\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:b698ebbf7b1bde39a0a5b16677367aa6","key":395,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:b698ebbf7b1bde39a0a5b16677367aa6\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"Local constitutional entries locate local axioms, overrides and disambiguations whose authority belongs to an existing lawful owner. A local disambiguation carrier owns the resolution; overlay metadata only makes its exact context, candidates, selected concept, bases, authority and scope discoverable/checkable.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":629,\"path\":\"standards/PRODUCT_DEFINITION.md\",\"quote\":\"The referenced `uri` owns the resolution. When the candidates cross bounded\\ncontexts, that carrier also declares the complete import, translation or\\nequivalence relation §5 requires. The overlay metadata makes the relation\\ndiscoverable and checkable; it neither restates the source-owned meanings\\nnor mints the decision (P6).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/PRODUCT_DEFINITION.md#PRODUCT_DEFINITION%2F6.%20Local%20constitutional%20binding\",\"start_line\":625}],\"label\":\"Local constitutional binding\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:24eaed2b3ae25fcb1bde979499653b21","key":396,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:24eaed2b3ae25fcb1bde979499653b21\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"A Project Reference-Frame Basis is a Product-owned accepted declaration of the shared frame set through which finite actors engage a governed scope/outcome. It binds exact frame law and optional profile basis, admitting authorities/scopes, frame declarations/evaluation inventory, actor-binding rules/capability envelopes, semantic/evaluation/operation/decision grants, result/conjunction/translation/coverage relations, lifecycle triggers and invalidation. REFERENCE_FRAME supplies principles/declaration shape and the Executive baseline supplies an optional profile; Product authority owns the concrete declaration and every grant.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":650,\"path\":\"standards/PRODUCT_DEFINITION.md\",\"quote\":\"Project Reference-Frame Basis\\n  = exact reference-frame law and optional profile basis\\n  + admitting authorities and governed scopes\\n  + frame declarations and evaluation inventory\\n  + actor-binding rules and capability envelopes\\n  + semantic, evaluation, operation and decision grants\\n  + result, conjunction, translation and coverage relations\\n  + lifecycle activation triggers and invalidation law\\n```\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/PRODUCT_DEFINITION.md#PRODUCT_DEFINITION%2F7.%20Collective%20reference-frame%20basis\",\"start_line\":642}],\"label\":\"Project Reference-Frame Basis\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:6e2b00300849fee60f54d5d16d37822d","key":397,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:6e2b00300849fee60f54d5d16d37822d\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"Agent Frame Activation is an execution-scoped binding of one agent to an applicable frame/configuration, exact evaluation, subject, basis, evidence boundary and capability envelope. Its packet is carried by a ticket or other authorized work instruction, while the Product Definition locates the durable shared frame basis. Profile availability, Product adoption and execution activation are distinct relations.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":680,\"path\":\"standards/PRODUCT_DEFINITION.md\",\"quote\":\"Profile availability, Product adoption and execution-scoped activation are\\nthree distinct relations. Inclusion in a selected method cut makes a\\nprofile available; only Product authority may adopt it; only an exact\\nauthorised work instruction may activate one bound frame for an actor and\\nsubject (P6, P3).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/PRODUCT_DEFINITION.md#PRODUCT_DEFINITION%2F7.%20Collective%20reference-frame%20basis\",\"start_line\":676}],\"label\":\"Agent Frame Activation\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:1d16434fac1e65d9e2c7122fb8b5e138","key":398,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:1d16434fac1e65d9e2c7122fb8b5e138\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[\"Under the selected complete STDO basis.\"],\"definition\":\"The build-tenancy context is urn:stdo:bounded-context:build-tenancy. Build tenancy is one constitutional WHAT realized by one or more independent project-owned HOW tenants: one is the singleton case; multiple independent realizations of the same WHAT constitute multi-build-tenancy. SPEC_METHOD §11 owns build-tenant meanings/bindings, and TICKETS §4 owns the multi-tenant work-item relation through explicit owner relations.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":744,\"path\":\"standards/PRODUCT_DEFINITION.md\",\"quote\":\"In this context build tenancy is that one-or-more relation; one tenant is\\nits singleton case, and multi-build-tenancy begins when the same WHAT has\\nmore than one independent realisation (P3, P2).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/PRODUCT_DEFINITION.md#PRODUCT_DEFINITION%2F8.%20WHAT%2C%20HOW%20and%20work%20carriers\",\"start_line\":742}],\"label\":\"Build tenancy\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:71e0e361793d1a2f94d72888e297322b","key":399,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:71e0e361793d1a2f94d72888e297322b\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"Tenant Registry is canonical how.build_tenants, identifying independent HOW realizations by stable identity and locating roots/design/implementation; tenant surfaces declare bindings under SPEC_METHOD §11. how.common locates common realization law explicitly adopted across multiple tenants. WHAT bindings locate current Intent, Product and specifications. ticketing.goals locates the work wave; ticketing.tickets locates durable tickets with backlog/active/completed lanes; ticketing.comments locates commentary; optional ticketing.sprints locates bounded execution-batch manifests.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":759,\"path\":\"standards/PRODUCT_DEFINITION.md\",\"quote\":\"The Tenant Registry is the canonical `how.build_tenants` collection for the\\nproduct's independent HOW realisations. Each entry has stable identity and\\nlocates its root, design and implementation surfaces; the tenant's\\nbinding, which those surfaces declare, is governed by SPEC_METHOD §11.\\nThe Common Build-Tenant Surface is the realisation law bound by `how.common` and\\nexplicitly adopted across more than one tenant. A separate\\n`TENANT_REGISTRY.md` may remain as a human-readable companion or generated\\nprojection and cannot become a second tenant-identity or location\\nauthority (P3, P6).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/PRODUCT_DEFINITION.md#PRODUCT_DEFINITION%2F8.%20WHAT%2C%20HOW%20and%20work%20carriers\",\"start_line\":751}],\"label\":\"WHAT, tenant registry and work-carrier bindings\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:ec08ef0caf1ef5504b20e94591bbea9d","key":400,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:ec08ef0caf1ef5504b20e94591bbea9d\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"A mutable Product Definition discovered as stdo_*.json within a selected workspace boundary, including its root and arbitrarily deep project roots. Its stable product.definition_id is distinct from its locator and from immutable Product or release identities.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":776,\"path\":\"standards/PRODUCT_DEFINITION.md\",\"quote\":\"Tools discover `stdo_*.json` recursively within the selected workspace\\nboundary: definitions at the workspace root and definitions at arbitrarily\\ndeep nested project roots (P3).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/PRODUCT_DEFINITION.md#PRODUCT_DEFINITION%2F9.%20Recursive%20discovery%20and%20explicit%20composition\",\"start_line\":774}],\"label\":\"Product Definition\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:8bdd42573e0cb3dc879df6ffa3bb6827","key":401,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:8bdd42573e0cb3dc879df6ffa3bb6827\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"An explicit directed composition entry containing product_definition as target locator, target_definition_id as expected stable identity, relation as the authority defining composition kind, source and target roles, owner, scope, lifecycle and invalidation, and contracts as one or more exact governing interface, capability, identity, lifecycle, data, evidence or other contract references consumed by the relation.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":795,\"path\":\"standards/PRODUCT_DEFINITION.md\",\"quote\":\"- `relation`: the authority defining the directed composition kind, the\\n  source and target roles, owner, scope, lifecycle and invalidation\\n  conditions; and\\n- `contracts`: one or more exact interface, capability, identity,\\n  lifecycle, data, evidence or other governing contract references\\n  consumed by that relation.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/PRODUCT_DEFINITION.md#PRODUCT_DEFINITION%2F9.%20Recursive%20discovery%20and%20explicit%20composition\",\"start_line\":790}],\"label\":\"Explicit product composition\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:d9ee38b33be5ec7706f3f3ad6cfcdc0c","key":402,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:d9ee38b33be5ec7706f3f3ad6cfcdc0c\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"The discovered definition set is a conformance subject with separate structural and semantic claims. Draft 2020-12 JSON Schema establishes structural shape; required semantic and cross-file checks remain separate.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":835,\"path\":\"standards/PRODUCT_DEFINITION.md\",\"quote\":\"constitutional sufficiency, semantic-resolution and cross-context-relation\\ncompleteness, and authority-congruence checks. The structural subset and\\nthe semantic subset of these checks are distinct claims\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/PRODUCT_DEFINITION.md#PRODUCT_DEFINITION%2F9.%20Recursive%20discovery%20and%20explicit%20composition\",\"start_line\":833}],\"label\":\"Discovered-set conformance\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:ea41d0e99982e9880a7fa88c1f2c15a4","key":403,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:ea41d0e99982e9880a7fa88c1f2c15a4\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"Semantic-resolution conformance covers uniquely resolved occurrences and material collisions under an exact selected basis. Its named collision cases are Frame, Owner, Product, Tenant and User.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":841,\"path\":\"standards/PRODUCT_DEFINITION.md\",\"quote\":\"Conformance covers both uniquely resolved use and material collision. At\\nminimum it establishes these cases under an exact selected basis (P1, P6):\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/PRODUCT_DEFINITION.md#PRODUCT_DEFINITION%2F10.%20Semantic-resolution%20conformance%20cases\",\"start_line\":840}],\"label\":\"Semantic-resolution conformance\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:70f67311f73a19765787897dfa4176f1","key":404,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:70f67311f73a19765787897dfa4176f1\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"One complete released version is the operative shared methodology and sole publication authority. Its cut identifies the exact member set, member digests, review basis, human acceptance and immutable identity. Each law has one owning member; other members consume it by reference.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":869,\"path\":\"standards/PRODUCT_DEFINITION.md\",\"quote\":\"STDO-SURFACE-001. The shared methodology is modular in authorship and\\nsingular in authority. Each law has one owning member; other members\\nconsume it by reference. The members become operative only as one complete\\nreleased version of the method (P6, P3).\\n\\nA released cut identifies its exact member set, member digests, review\\nbasis, human acceptance and immutable identity.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/PRODUCT_DEFINITION.md#PRODUCT_DEFINITION%2F11.%20One%20constitutional%20surface%20and%20version%20boundary\",\"start_line\":863}],\"label\":\"Released method cut\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:05c1a265f04949108de6c22b4ed5d7b2","key":405,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:05c1a265f04949108de6c22b4ed5d7b2\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"Compressions, templates, comments, candidate work, installed copies and mutable source are derived, evidential or authoring surfaces. Released or installed derived carriers include bootstraps, indexes and projected frames; they preserve source meaning without acquiring ownership.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":872,\"path\":\"standards/PRODUCT_DEFINITION.md\",\"quote\":\"Compressions, templates,\\ncomments, candidate work, installed copies and mutable source are derived,\\nevidential or authoring surfaces. They cannot become a selectable partial\\nconstitution and cannot reinterpret the owning members (P3, P6).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/PRODUCT_DEFINITION.md#PRODUCT_DEFINITION%2F11.%20One%20constitutional%20surface%20and%20version%20boundary\",\"start_line\":869}],\"label\":\"Derived methodology surface\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:95866066e6bc25e27771686a22cc6e9e","key":406,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:95866066e6bc25e27771686a22cc6e9e\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"Consumer-owned concrete Product realisation comprises instantiated types and schemas, files, tools, runtime, orchestration machinery, tests and executable conformance implementation. The method instead owns construction algebra, authority relations, abstract states and transitions, admissibility, necessary causal order and evidence invariants.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":904,\"path\":\"standards/PRODUCT_DEFINITION.md\",\"quote\":\"The method owns normative construction algebra, authority relations,\\nabstract state and transition laws, admissibility conditions, necessary\\ncausal order and evidence invariants. Consumers own concrete Product\\nrealisation: instantiated types and schemas, files, tools, runtime and\\norchestration machinery, tests and executable conformance implementation.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/PRODUCT_DEFINITION.md#PRODUCT_DEFINITION%2F11.%20One%20constitutional%20surface%20and%20version%20boundary\",\"start_line\":900}],\"label\":\"Concrete Product realisation\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:3add3b1f83bc954a23767c8b23298c71","key":407,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:3add3b1f83bc954a23767c8b23298c71\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"The source-described bootstrap begins every product from templates/PRODUCT_DEFINITION_TEMPLATE.json copied from its exact selected cut to its definition root as stdo_default.json for a singleton default project or stdo_<label>.json for a named definition. This is a represented adoption procedure, not an execution by this interpretation.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":927,\"path\":\"standards/PRODUCT_DEFINITION.md\",\"quote\":\"Every product defined under this method begins from\\n`templates/PRODUCT_DEFINITION_TEMPLATE.json`, copied to the product's\\ndefinition root as `stdo_default.json` for a singleton default project or\\nas `stdo_<label>.json` for a named product definition. An existing project\\nfills the URI bindings over its current layout; adoption requires no\\nmoving, renaming or duplicating of existing authority or realisation\\nsurfaces (P2, P3).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/PRODUCT_DEFINITION.md#PRODUCT_DEFINITION%2F12.%20Bootstrap\",\"start_line\":921}],\"label\":\"Product bootstrap\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:1948ec4783ac3e1560e6eed4e2e68e9d","key":408,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:1948ec4783ac3e1560e6eed4e2e68e9d\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"The starter scaffold binds the shared versioned store through constitution.stdo.basis; specification/GOALS.md to work-wave orientation; INTENT.md to domain direction; PRODUCT.md to current product definition; requirements/ to live requirements; build_tenants/ to shared and tenant-local realisation; and .ai-workspace/ to sprint, ticket and comment carriers. The depicted children are build_tenants/common and default, and .ai-workspace/sprints, tickets/backlog, active, completed, and comments. These paths and topology are defaults, not universal path or conformance law.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":943,\"path\":\"standards/PRODUCT_DEFINITION.md\",\"quote\":\"These are template defaults, not universal path law; the definition's URI\\nbindings select the actual project carriers (P2).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/PRODUCT_DEFINITION.md#PRODUCT_DEFINITION%2F12.%20Bootstrap\",\"start_line\":942},{\"end_line\":998,\"path\":\"standards/PRODUCT_DEFINITION.md\",\"quote\":\".ai-workspace/\\n├── sprints/\\n├── tickets/\\n│   ├── backlog/\\n│   ├── active/\\n│   └── completed/\\n└── comments/\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/PRODUCT_DEFINITION.md#PRODUCT_DEFINITION%2F12.%20Bootstrap\",\"start_line\":992}],\"label\":\"Default scaffold and carriers\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:fcb3e9e8bb4e4ab57ffef14f92ab3625","key":409,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:fcb3e9e8bb4e4ab57ffef14f92ab3625\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"PROFILES is a tier-3 member owning the core/profile boundary, declared-binding rule and common import rule, and indexing profiles. A profile is a domain or operational specialisation; tiers 1 and 2 are the core.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":7,\"path\":\"standards/PROFILES.md\",\"quote\":\"Tier 3. Owns the boundary between the core and the profiles, the\\ndeclared-binding rule and the import rule that every profile applies\\n(§1), and indexes the profiles (§2 to §6). A profile is a domain or\\noperational specialisation of the method; the members of tiers 1 and 2\\nare the core.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/PROFILES.md#PROFILES\",\"start_line\":3}],\"label\":\"PROFILES member and profile category\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:a8af91d16de288148f9b593e559aa36d","key":410,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:a8af91d16de288148f9b593e559aa36d\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"The tier-1 and tier-2 core names no runtime, carrier or executor. Its calculus vocabulary includes traversal records and functor kinds F_D, F_P and F_H owned by AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS §5; module is a generic ASSURANCE term. These are not excluded by the profile vocabulary boundary.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":17,\"path\":\"standards/PROFILES.md\",\"quote\":\"The traversal record and the functor kinds F_D,\\nF_P and F_H are tier-1 calculus terms owned by AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS §5, and\\n\\\"module\\\" is a generic term under [ASSURANCE](ASSURANCE.md); neither is\\nrestricted here.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/PROFILES.md#PROFILES%2F1.%20The%20boundary\",\"start_line\":14}],\"label\":\"Method core\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:d855004b5d8379de384a5375291dfc0c","key":411,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:d855004b5d8379de384a5375291dfc0c\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"A profile's declared binding specialises a core mechanism with explicit direction, preserved meaning, narrowed scope and invalidation. It differs from Product adoption binding under PRODUCT_DEFINITION §7 and carrier-to-typed-contract binding under UX §7; the three senses are not interchangeable.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":23,\"path\":\"standards/PROFILES.md\",\"quote\":\"the binding is declared in the profile with its direction, preserved\\nmeaning, narrowed scope and invalidation. In this member \\\"binding\\\" means\\nthat declared binding of a core mechanism; a Product's adoption binding is\\n[PRODUCT_DEFINITION §7](PRODUCT_DEFINITION.md#7-collective-reference-frame-basis)'s,\\nand a carrier binding to a typed contract is [UX §7](UX.md#7-carrier-binding)'s;\\nthe three are not interchanged\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/PROFILES.md#PROFILES%2F1.%20The%20boundary\",\"start_line\":18}],\"label\":\"Declared profile binding\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:d9237cdda330747e7521d91a94f9903d","key":412,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:d9237cdda330747e7521d91a94f9903d\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"Graph execution is indexed through two tier-3 owning members. ODD binds the P0 bounded step to one vector or edge traversal; supplies graph-native F_P, F_D and F_H shorthands, with F_P and F_H declared specialisations of SPEC_METHOD §5; and refines ACTIVATION §4 to graph functions with §11.8's cumulative-environment contract for earlier outputs. TRAVERSAL_OCCURRENCE supplies an optional closed model-family signature over one exact a_c basis for immutable occurrence histories over a mutable subject, with OP-001 to OP-007. ODD §10 owns runtime/product/service layer separation; ODD §5 leaves worker internal solution strategy outside the framework.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":55,\"path\":\"standards/PROFILES.md\",\"quote\":\"Graph execution is two tier-3 members, indexed here; each states its\\nlaw in full and declares its bindings under §1 (P0 boundary, P1):\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/PROFILES.md#PROFILES%2F2.%20Graph%20execution\",\"start_line\":54},{\"end_line\":60,\"path\":\"standards/PROFILES.md\",\"quote\":\"| [TRAVERSAL_OCCURRENCE](TRAVERSAL_OCCURRENCE.md) | an optional closed model-family signature over one exact `a_c` basis of AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS for immutable occurrence histories over a mutable subject, with OP-001 to OP-007 |\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/PROFILES.md#PROFILES%2F2.%20Graph%20execution\",\"start_line\":60}],\"label\":\"Graph-execution profiles\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:bff1d9cf01a51b82efe1da37919b576e","key":413,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:bff1d9cf01a51b82efe1da37919b576e\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"DESIGN_MODULE imports the core and binds ontology-first derivation of operation identities from discovered functionality through logical completeness, Prime contraction, irreducible architectural carriers and projections; proportional sequencing and a decision-complete gate; bounded frame conservation; native constructability; capability and foundation selection; transformation admission completeness; invariant reconstruction; computational realisation projection; module taxonomy and realisation rules; and review questions/checklists. ASSURANCE §§14–16 own design-to-module evidence, module-derived unit tests and lifecycle confirmation; SPEC_METHOD §2 owns its core rule and non-goals. DESIGN_MODULE §§5 and 7 decide per-boundary derivation cost.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":85,\"path\":\"standards/PROFILES.md\",\"quote\":\"Its design-to-module evidence\\nroute, module-derived unit tests and module lifecycle confirmation are\\nASSURANCE §14 to §16, and its core rule and non-goals SPEC_METHOD §2\\nRealisation shape. The per-boundary cost of the derivation chain is\\ndecided there (DESIGN_MODULE §5 Proportional design sequencing, §7 Gate\\nand retrospective work) (P2, P0).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/PROFILES.md#PROFILES%2F3.%20Software%20design\",\"start_line\":80}],\"label\":\"Software-design profile\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:7bad658d82a142e3a12d7ef3dd5f3e8e","key":414,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:7bad658d82a142e3a12d7ef3dd5f3e8e\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[\"Applies as a refinement of DESIGN_MODULE to modules realising a UX surface.\"],\"definition\":\"UX imports the core and binds the Elm process model's typed State, Msg, Update, View, Cmd and Sub; UX-message/admitted-carrier boundary; state transition law; effect membrane; AssetSurface or equivalent typed-contract binding; continuation and Msg-replay proof; view shape; shared types with runtime validation at untrusted seams; accessibility minimum; realisation discretion; adoption scaffold/exemption law and UX sprint compliance escrow; failures and review questions; and result refinements each mapped to one core value. Its lead declares the binding of TICKETS §3's generalised escrow terms.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":93,\"path\":\"standards/PROFILES.md\",\"quote\":\"[UX](UX.md) is the UX profile. It refines DESIGN_MODULE for modules that\\nrealise a UX surface, imports the core, and binds: the Elm process model\\nwith typed State, Msg, Update, View, Cmd and Sub; the boundary between UX\\nmessages and admitted product carriers; the state transition law; the\\neffect membrane; binding to AssetSurface or an equivalent typed contract;\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/PROFILES.md#PROFILES%2F4.%20UX\",\"start_line\":89}],\"label\":\"UX profile\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:3a7dbc4ecae4b3f5cc41c0adb447df38","key":415,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:3a7dbc4ecae4b3f5cc41c0adb447df38\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"WORLD_MODEL imports the core and binds product-lineage concepts and Builder Project specialisation; a candidate-status Markov-object construct with effective blanket, working refinements, epistemic status and promotion gate; claims and units; entity recovery and the published identity-bearing entity cut with admissibility, discrimination and publication law; attribute ledger; representation/materialisation/publication laws; Markov-object overlays; saturation; local-artifact composition; projection; control/data planes; proof and world-model-driven development; and result refinements each mapped to one core value. Its lead binds FOUNDATIONS §2 Object and P3's boundary claim to the entity cut. Nothing in the core depends on establishment of the construct.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":118,\"path\":\"standards/PROFILES.md\",\"quote\":\"Its\\nbinding of FOUNDATIONS §2 Object\\nand P3's boundary claim to the entity cut is declared in its lead.\\nNothing in the core depends on the construct being established (P3, P6).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/PROFILES.md#PROFILES%2F5.%20World%20model\",\"start_line\":115}],\"label\":\"World-model profile\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:fc43c65ddaf2dfc761ac15a3bf6c1f3e","key":416,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:fc43c65ddaf2dfc761ac15a3bf6c1f3e\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[\"Adoption is optional.\"],\"definition\":\"EXECUTIVE_BASELINE imports the core and describes one executive configuration under ACTIVATION §1, comprising Executive, Worker and Reviewer engagement frames and a specialist-frame catalogue mapped to tiers 1 and 2. Frame names bind responsibilities allocated by that configuration under Roles and delegation, not roles imported by spelling.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":130,\"path\":\"standards/PROFILES.md\",\"quote\":\"[EXECUTIVE_BASELINE](EXECUTIVE_BASELINE.md) is the optional\\nengagement-baseline profile. It imports the core and describes the\\nexecutive configuration, one configuration in the sense of\\n[ACTIVATION §1 Configuration](ACTIVATION.md#configuration), with three\\nengagement frames (Executive, Worker, Reviewer) and a catalogue of\\nspecialist frames, mapped onto the law of tiers 1 and 2. Its frame names\\nbind the responsibilities that configuration allocates under\\n[ACTIVATION §1 Roles and delegation](ACTIVATION.md#roles-and-delegation),\\nnot roles imported by spelling, as its lead declares (P1, P6).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/PROFILES.md#PROFILES%2F6.%20Engagement%20baseline\",\"start_line\":122}],\"label\":\"Engagement-baseline profile\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:bccbbb08ac621eb8a23669f1ff45717a","key":417,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:bccbbb08ac621eb8a23669f1ff45717a\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"The subject's STDO V3 methodology addresses construction and evaluation by actors with finite context, attention, time and capability: interpret a scoped subject, select purpose and governing contract, transform within admitted authority while conserving material relations, evaluate resulting claims, then continue, recover or conclude from current state under explicit uncertainty.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":8,\"path\":\"standards/README.md\",\"quote\":\"This specification methodology is for construction and evaluation by\\nactors with finite context, attention, time and capability. Its core\\nstatement: interpret a scoped subject; select a purpose and governing\\ncontract; transform within admitted authority while conserving its material\\nrelations; evaluate the resulting claims; continue, recover or conclude from\\ncurrent state under explicit uncertainty.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/README.md#STDO%20V3\",\"start_line\":3}],\"label\":\"Subject methodology\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:0b861da646df218c18f157e8c069d3be","key":418,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:0b861da646df218c18f157e8c069d3be\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"An ordered reading-route index, not an execution grant. Routes are: understand→FOUNDATIONS, REFERENCE_FRAME, ACTIVATION, EVALUATION, AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS, SPEC_METHOD; bind a project→SPEC_METHOD §1 then PRODUCT_DEFINITION; realise WHAT→SPEC_METHOD §11 then PRODUCT_DEFINITION §8; triage→SPEC_METHOD §§4–5 then TICKETS §4; migrate/reset→SPEC_METHOD §7 then TICKETS §6; prove realisation→EVALUATION §§1–2,6 then ASSURANCE; model/project/encode→AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS §§2–4,6–8 then EVALUATION §2; bounded work→ACTIVATION §§1–3, FOUNDATIONS §4 result mapping, REFERENCE_FRAME §11 then SPEC_METHOD §4; frame-set work→REFERENCE_FRAME §§4,8,10 then EVALUATION §7; resume→ACTIVATION §§5,7 then TICKETS §7; carry work→TICKETS §§5,4,7; review→EVALUATION including §5 then nearest CONFORMANCE case; acceptance/release→EVALUATION §5, SPEC_METHOD §6, RELEASE §§8–9; publication/qualification/selection→RELEASE §§1–4 then PRODUCT_DEFINITION §4; identity→IDENTITY §§2–4,8,10,6 and boundary/sufficiency rules with or without WORLD_MODEL; coordinate→ACTIVATION configuration then, if executive configuration is chosen, EXECUTIVE_BASELINE §§3,7,6,12,16; software design→DESIGN_MODULE §§5–7,11 then ASSURANCE §§14–16; profiles→PROFILES §§1–6 with UX §§4,8,12 or WORLD_MODEL §§7,9–10 as applicable; ODD construction→ODD §§17–18; occurrence histories→TRAVERSAL_OCCURRENCE authority/adoption; specification writing→WRITING_GUIDE then SPEC_METHOD §2; publish analysis/review/handoff/proposal→POSTING_GUIDE then SPEC_METHOD §6; locate term→GLOSSARY including §17 then PRODUCT_DEFINITION §5; trace commitments→FOUNDATIONS §3 then indexed family table; acquire context→ACTIVATION §2, preferring a current derived surface that serves the task, otherwise deciding owner sections, including verbatim frames or current a_c constraint projections.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":14,\"path\":\"standards/README.md\",\"quote\":\"| You want to | Read, in order |\\n|---|---|\\n| understand the method | [FOUNDATIONS](FOUNDATIONS.md) → [REFERENCE_FRAME](REFERENCE_FRAME.md) → [ACTIVATION](ACTIVATION.md) → [EVALUATION](EVALUATION.md) → [AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS](AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS.md) → [SPEC_METHOD](SPEC_METHOD.md) |\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/README.md#STDO%20V3%2FRoutes\",\"start_line\":12},{\"end_line\":38,\"path\":\"standards/README.md\",\"quote\":\"Acquisition: a derived surface whose sources are current where one serves the task, otherwise the deciding owner sections;\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/README.md#STDO%20V3%2FRoutes\",\"start_line\":38}],\"label\":\"Ordered task reading routes\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:f701f72fd1de2cad38030bb4061e3655","key":419,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:f701f72fd1de2cad38030bb4061e3655\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"The document catalogue attributes ownership, without supplying the referenced laws. Tier 1: FOUNDATIONS—standing, ontology/imports, P0–P6, foundation-to-law, composition/conservation, results/conjunction, categorical demonstration and hypotheses; REFERENCE_FRAME—frame context/imports, RF-001–017, sets/functions/outcomes, conjunction/relations, coverage/revision, packets/declarations; ACTIVATION—bounded steps, intake/admission/applicability/configuration/delegation, context/acquisition/size, result refinements/disposition, totality/hard stops/licensing, restart/accounts, proportionality and reuse; AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS—signature, records, AC-001–020, traversals/functors, interpretation/models/layers/identity, exclusions/conformance; IDENTITY—scoping, uniqueness/type/stability, readable/opaque/hierarchical/engine/domain identities, authority conservation, overrides/publication, parsing/version boundary/questions/examples; EVALUATION—claims/evidence/independent assessment/review/acceptance, realisation conformance/equivalence and actual-use frame/method qualification. Tier 2: SPEC_METHOD—process constitution/identity, constitutional chain and surfaces, requirements/classification/trace/lifecycle/immutability, outcome conservation, triage/classes/gates/sprints/carriers, ambiguity, lineage/releases/migrations, execution/priorities/ADRs; PRODUCT_DEFINITION—overlay, required relations, constitutional sufficiency, installed basis/manager, semantic resolution, local bindings, frame basis, WHAT/HOW/work, discovery/composition, conformance cases, singular surface and bootstrap; ASSURANCE—verification/taxonomy/portability, test authority/scenarios/installed proof/path coverage, testing frames/combinatorics/debt/evidence, acquisition/localisation/integration, module evidence/tests/lifecycle; TICKETS—goals/tickets/sprints/comments/contracts/milestones, layout/substitution, escrow, fields/classification/triage/status, admission/criteria/terms, migration, judgments/rulings/closure/test authority, recommended shapes and operating relations; RELEASE—identities/refs/subtrees/history, construction/publication/qualification/advancement, selectors/adoption/naming, assets/cohorts, acceptance/dependencies, successor conservation and open questions; CONFORMANCE—qualification cases and discriminator distinctions/routes. Tier 3: PROFILES—boundary/import rule/index; EXECUTIVE_BASELINE—optional executive configuration, roles/frames/duties/drift locks, specialist families, transitions/handoff/coverage/re-entry/adoption/qualification/failures; DESIGN_MODULE—optional design profile, closure/ingress, functional bias/typing, derivation/completeness/conservation/Prime, gates/projections/taxonomy/realisation/review/adoption; ODD—graph profile, libraries/model/compute, product/self-host boundaries/layers/governance, laws, execution audit, constructive loop, cumulative environment, proof/release/failures/invocation/ramp-up; TRAVERSAL_OCCURRENCE—optional mutable-subject occurrence profile, signature/reference domains/events/relations/constraints/judgments/residuals/stops, identity/admission/causality/lineage/effects/frontiers, OP laws/adoption/exclusions/conformance; UX—optional Elm/carrier/state/effect/continuation/type/accessibility/adoption/escrow/review/result profile; WORLD_MODEL—optional Builder/candidate Markov/entity-cut/ledger/overlay/composition/projection/planes/proof/result profile. Guides: POSTING_GUIDE—commentary purpose/boundary/location/identity/categories/structure/discussion/rules/ratification; WRITING_GUIDE—writing discipline, style, authority-layer tone and artifact/current-surface practice; GLOSSARY—non-deciding locator index by bounded context or undeclared context.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":43,\"path\":\"standards/README.md\",\"quote\":\"| File | Tier | Owns |\\n|---|---|---|\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/README.md#STDO%20V3%2FDocuments\",\"start_line\":42},{\"end_line\":65,\"path\":\"standards/README.md\",\"quote\":\"| [GLOSSARY.md](GLOSSARY.md) | guide | the non-deciding locator index: index contract, locator law, rows by bounded context, and rows for concepts whose member declares no context |\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/README.md#STDO%20V3%2FDocuments\",\"start_line\":65}],\"label\":\"Document tiers and ownership catalogue\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:0c4adf064c8a053607896be69a4fb6ac","key":420,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:0c4adf064c8a053607896be69a4fb6ac\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"Task excerpts in frames/, inventoried by frames/FRAME_INPUTS.json, copy needed owner sections byte for byte and cite source digests; they own no determination. Indexed tasks: bootstrap—unspecified-task entry, basis/definition/admission/results/acquisition; rf-task-a—declare/activate/evaluate one frame and distinguish result from owner disposition; rf-task-b—coverage, diagnosis and revision; ac-task-a—transformation record, successor judgment and promotion; traversal-task-f—causality/corrections/lineage/precedence/stops; eb-task-d—Executive drift locks, candidate_ready, finding dimensions and disposition; dm-task-d—accepted/new boundary design completeness, sequencing, gate/promotion/retained code/substrate/Prime; configuration—multi-actor configuration, capabilities/capacities and optimality/check claims; binding—software/human-process tenants, author/actor/operation distinctions, structural versus conformance results; stale-summary—workspace disagreement, changed-dependency reuse and next action; acceptance-release—assessment, blocking findings/disposition, condition closure, exact-cut acceptance and successor dispositions; member-build-assess—family table, ownership/refinement, predecessor claims and local discriminators without substituting self-review for independent review.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":80,\"path\":\"standards/README.md\",\"quote\":\"The verbatim frames live in `frames/`, with their manifest\\n`frames/FRAME_INPUTS.json`. Each frame copies, byte for byte, the owning\\nsections that one task needs and names each source with its digest; the\\nowning sections decide, and a frame owns no determination. A frame whose\\nsource digests no longer match the members is stale\\n([PRODUCT_DEFINITION §11](PRODUCT_DEFINITION.md#11-one-constitutional-surface-and-version-boundary)).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/README.md#STDO%20V3%2FDocuments\",\"start_line\":75}],\"label\":\"Task-frame excerpt catalogue\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:b6c2d02f1f961be2126e685d026c926b","key":421,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:b6c2d02f1f961be2126e685d026c926b\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"A selectable STDO Product's constitutional member set is one complete immutable standards cut. A cut carries tiers 1–2, carrier-neutral a_c theory separate from subject models and encodings, optional application-neutral TRAVERSAL_OCCURRENCE on an exact basis, derived application profiles, companion guides, non-deciding GLOSSARY, task frames with source identity and permitted excerpt transformations, normative interoperability schemas including definition overlay and deterministic installed manifest, and starter product/specification/frame-basis/agent-bootstrap templates. It may also carry subordinate executable and interaction tooling.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":104,\"path\":\"standards/README.md\",\"quote\":\"One complete immutable release cut of this standards tree is the\\nconstitutional member set of the selectable STDO Product. The release may\\nalso carry subordinate executable and interaction tooling (P6, P3). A cut carries (P3, P2):\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/README.md#STDO%20V3%2FLibrary%20and%20installed%20basis\",\"start_line\":102}],\"label\":\"Release library and installed distribution\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:35f1f9ede029690551cd65423de48e25","key":422,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:35f1f9ede029690551cd65423de48e25\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"The tier-1 REFERENCE_FRAME member owns engagement laws: declaring/selecting frame sets, frame relations and joint use, bounded workspace coverage audits, revision and activation packets. It imports frame objects, activating steps, core results/conjunction and qualification unchanged from their owners. Each clause names its requiring principle P0–P6.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":11,\"path\":\"standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md\",\"quote\":\"Tier 1. Owns the reference frame as a first-class object of engagement:\\nthe laws every frame obeys, how a frame set is declared and selected, how\\nframes relate and act together, how coverage of a workspace is audited and\\nbounded, how a frame set is revised, and what an actor receives when it is\\nactivated on a frame. The frame objects, the step that activates a frame,\\nthe core result algebra with its conjunction, and qualification belong to\\nother members; this member imports them unchanged and defines none of them\\n(§1, Imports into this context). Each clause names the principle that\\nrequires it (P0 to P6, FOUNDATIONS §3), as FOUNDATIONS §1 requires.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md#REFERENCE_FRAME\",\"start_line\":3}],\"label\":\"REFERENCE_FRAME member\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:395652cb307f9e3aec1351f1377975e4","key":423,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:395652cb307f9e3aec1351f1377975e4\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[\"Human, agentic, deterministic, probabilistic, assurance or mixed work is covered wherever its governing product or method permits it.\"],\"definition\":\"A reference frame is one atomic engagement unit activated and evaluated as a bounded context. An activated frame combines declared evaluation family, exact workspace/topology basis, finite material relations/coordinates, invariants/authorities, admissible evidence/exclusions and actor envelope, leading to one closed core result when evaluation is performed. Engagement atomicity does not imply semantic irreducibility. The member owns urn:stdo:bounded-context:reference-frame-evaluation under its exact publication basis, with local frame declaration/activation/evaluation/basis/relation/result/coverage/revision/qualification concepts and unchanged owner-defined imports.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":53,\"path\":\"standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md\",\"quote\":\"The reference frame is the atomic engagement unit: the unit that is\\nactivated and evaluated as one bounded context. Frame-set selection,\\nactivation, evaluation, conjunction, translation, coverage and revision are\\nseparate functions over it (§5). A frame supports a bounded evaluation\\nwithout first containing a universal theory of its possible relationships.\\n\\\"Atomic\\\" is said at engagement altitude only. It does not assert that every\\nrelation inside the frame is one irreducible semantic atom; a frame may\\ncarry several semantic atoms and several owner relations without merging\\ntheir meaning or authority (P1, P3).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md#REFERENCE_FRAME%2F1.%20The%20frame%20as%20the%20engagement%20unit\",\"start_line\":45}],\"label\":\"Reference frame and activated frame\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:6f930ad8904d0b79e414891042c6c678","key":424,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:6f930ad8904d0b79e414891042c6c678\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"A declared frame set supports bounded evaluations of a workspace and governed outcome using accumulated practice/failures, available actor capability and human judgment; required conjunction/translation leads to a coverage ledger, residual uncertainty and empirical revision. Selection, activation, evaluation, conjunction, translation, coverage and revision are distinct functions, not implied callable interfaces.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":42,\"path\":\"standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md\",\"quote\":\"workspace and governed outcome\\n  + accumulated practice and historical failures\\n  + available actor capabilities\\n  + human judgment\\n  -> declared frame set\\n  -> bounded evaluations\\n  -> conjunction or translation where required\\n  -> coverage ledger and residual uncertainty\\n  -> empirical frame-set revision\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md#REFERENCE_FRAME%2F1.%20The%20frame%20as%20the%20engagement%20unit\",\"start_line\":34}],\"label\":\"Frame set\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:aa239bec637e6fe48df5a9c006edecbb","key":425,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:aa239bec637e6fe48df5a9c006edecbb\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"The reference-frame context declares lossless imports from FOUNDATIONS, ACTIVATION and EVALUATION; these sources declare no bounded-context identity, so each source context is its member. FOUNDATIONS supplies frame objects, ontology, authority kinds/actor identity, disjointness/independence, the tuple ⟨Q, B, M, C, I, A, E, X, R, J, K, D⟩, core results including non-performance and refinements, and result conjunction/composition. ACTIVATION supplies intake/admission/applicability/context size/activation/evaluation, step result refinements/disposition and closed-result reuse. EVALUATION supplies frame/method qualification.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":91,\"path\":\"standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md\",\"quote\":\"the direction is from each source member named below to\\nthis context, and the loss is none, for every concept in the table; the\\ntarget context is `urn:stdo:bounded-context:reference-frame-evaluation`,\\nowned by this member as Scope above declares. FOUNDATIONS, ACTIVATION and\\nEVALUATION declare no bounded-context identity, so each row's source\\ncontext is its member (P1, P3).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md#REFERENCE_FRAME%2F1.%20The%20frame%20as%20the%20engagement%20unit%2FImports%20into%20this%20context\",\"start_line\":86}],\"label\":\"Declared reference-frame imports\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:544a4e40a3d742a6d00a0bffa1b08fbd","key":426,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:544a4e40a3d742a6d00a0bffa1b08fbd\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"Family F1, frames and context, traces bounded-frame engagement across this member, ACTIVATION §2 and FOUNDATIONS §2 frame objects, authorities, independence and tuple. The table owns none of the rules it names. Instance premises are workspace material exceeding one actor's competence/context/tools/access; declared outcome questions; possibly overlapping frames/actors; changing workspace/topology/capabilities; and actor use of owning and derived sources. These are work conditions, not foundational commitments or consequences of finite capacity alone. P0 is recovered; P1, P2, P3, P4a and P6 are cited as independent; P4b is derived from P0/P2 with non-reacquirable step facts; P5 is derived from P0/P6 with the open-world premise. P0 also includes actor change with declared-source reacquisition rather than private memory. Rows distinguish consequences, owning rules, additional choices/owners and pillars; RF-012 and result mappings are traced in F3, imports in F12. Core claims and violation lists add no independent rules.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":146,\"path\":\"standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md\",\"quote\":\"They are conditions of the work this family governs, not\\ncommitments, and do not follow from finite capacity alone. Two of P0's\\npremises are cited by name: its actor-change premise, that the actor of one\\nstep need not be the actor of the next and may re-acquire declared sources\\nbut not private memory; and its open-world premise, that the world is open.\\nThe standing of the consequences below is stated in\\n[FOUNDATIONS §3 Foundation to law](FOUNDATIONS.md#foundation-to-law).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md#REFERENCE_FRAME%2F1.%20The%20frame%20as%20the%20engagement%20unit%2FFoundation%20to%20law\",\"start_line\":140}],\"label\":\"F1 frames-and-context foundation table\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:f09c3ecfad4a4003e555be971583654b","key":427,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:f09c3ecfad4a4003e555be971583654b\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"Coverage is an audit relative to an exact workspace, governed outcome, basis, evaluation inventory, frame set and time. Its ledger and statuses concern coverage predicates and are distinct from results of the covered evaluations. Operational full coverage remains relative to that tuple and an explicit residual boundary.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":176,\"path\":\"standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md\",\"quote\":\"coverage is evaluated against an exact tuple of workspace, governed outcome, basis, evaluation inventory, frame set and time, and a change of any material member may invalidate it.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md#REFERENCE_FRAME%2F1.%20The%20frame%20as%20the%20engagement%20unit%2FFoundation%20to%20law\",\"start_line\":176}],\"label\":\"Frame coverage audit\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:525a659feca950ea645bdcfeb6f5d581","key":428,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:525a659feca950ea645bdcfeb6f5d581\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[\"Evaluation is performed.\"],\"definition\":\"A frame evaluation returns one closed result in its declared algebra: the FOUNDATIONS §4 core values satisfied, falsified, indeterminate, out_of_frame and invalid_basis, or a refinement mapped into that algebra. The owning core meanings and standing are imported, not redefined by REFERENCE_FRAME.\",\"exceptions\":[\"An evaluation not performed has no evaluation result; its stop state belongs to ACTIVATION §3.\"],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":402,\"path\":\"standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md\",\"quote\":\"Every performed evaluation of a frame returns one closed result in the\\nframe's declared result algebra: the core algebra of\\n[FOUNDATIONS §4 Results](FOUNDATIONS.md#results), or a refinement mapped\\ninto it under that section. That section owns the five core values\\n(`satisfied`, `falsified`, `indeterminate`, `out_of_frame` and\\n`invalid_basis`), their meanings and the rules over them: that nothing is\\ncoerced to success; that a refinement adds no core value, keeps\\nindeterminate, out-of-frame and invalid-basis pressure explicit and raises\\nno result's standing; and that an evaluation not performed has no result,\\nits stop state being\\n[ACTIVATION §3](ACTIVATION.md#3-step-results-and-disposition). This law\\napplies them to every frame and defines none of them (P5).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md#REFERENCE_FRAME%2F3.%20Laws%2FRF-012%20Closed%20results\",\"start_line\":391}],\"label\":\"Frame result domain\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:e12ad01daa78bc629c9782979e182c88","key":429,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:e12ad01daa78bc629c9782979e182c88\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"A semantic atom concerns irreducible meaning; an engagement atom concerns one bounded activation/evaluation. One frame may contain several semantic atoms and one semantic atom may participate in several frames. An adopting domain method's semantic-contraction law governs its domain atom family, not frame-set contraction by default.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":455,\"path\":\"standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md\",\"quote\":\"A reference frame is atomic at engagement altitude: it is activated and\\nevaluated as one bounded attention unit. Semantic irreducibility is a\\nseparate question: one frame may contain several semantic atoms, and one\\nsemantic atom may take part in several frames (P1, P3). Where an adopting\\nmethod supplies a semantic-contraction law for its domain atoms, that law\\ngoverns the domain atom family.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md#REFERENCE_FRAME%2F3.%20Laws%2FEngagement%20atom%20and%20semantic%20atom\",\"start_line\":450}],\"label\":\"Semantic atom\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:58a83663d990ad5bb6ebf276fd62dec9","key":430,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:58a83663d990ad5bb6ebf276fd62dec9\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"A declared bounded evaluation family with stable local identity; subject and exact basis; material manifold; coordinates and equality; invariants; authorities; admissible evidence; capability envelope; boundaries; optional relations actually used; invalidation and recharting conditions; and qualification cases, counterexamples and residuals.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1055,\"path\":\"standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md\",\"quote\":\"# Frame: <stable local identity>\\n\\n## Evaluation Family\\n<questions, predicates, and closed result algebra>\\n\\n## Subject And Basis\\n<workspace boundary, exact identity, version/time/topology coordinates>\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md#REFERENCE_FRAME%2F13.%20Minimal%20declarations%2FMinimal%20frame%20declaration\",\"start_line\":1049}],\"label\":\"Reference frame\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:51a5f7e39586744f57d4c28f2d03a6d3","key":431,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:51a5f7e39586744f57d4c28f2d03a6d3\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"A stable locally identified declaration of governed workspace, outcome, basis and time; human declaration and acceptance authority; known evaluation inventory and provenance; selected frame identities, revisions and capability envelopes; coverage mapping; intentional overlap; required conjunction and translation; residual uncertainty; and revision triggers.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1103,\"path\":\"standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md\",\"quote\":\"## Evaluation Inventory\\n<known material evaluations and provenance>\\n\\n## Selected Frames\\n<frame identities, revisions, and capability envelopes>\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md#REFERENCE_FRAME%2F13.%20Minimal%20declarations%2FMinimal%20frame-set%20declaration\",\"start_line\":1099}],\"label\":\"Frame set\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:9a8783a2b29a0621f74aa70f7d3ee135","key":432,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:9a8783a2b29a0621f74aa70f7d3ee135\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"Relations distinct from the frame: declare(human_authority, workspace, outcome, practices, capabilities) → frame_set; activate(frame, evaluation, subject, basis, actor) → activated_frame | activation_refusal; evaluate(activated_frame, admissible_evidence) → result + evidence + residuals; conjoin(decision_rule, frame_results) → decision | conflict | indeterminate; translate(source_frame, target_frame, value_or_evidence, mapping) → translated_value | declared_loss | refusal; audit_coverage(workspace, outcome, evaluation_inventory, frame_set) → coverage_ledger; revise(frame_set, new_evidence, failures, capability_change, topology_change) → proposed_frame_set_delta. Later text additionally specifies direct core-value returns absent from the signatures.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":517,\"path\":\"standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md\",\"quote\":\"The frame and the functions over it remain distinct. An application may\\nrealise the following relations in any conforming form; the signatures\\ndescribe relations, not callable software interfaces (P2; RF-016):\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md#REFERENCE_FRAME%2F5.%20Method%20functions\",\"start_line\":515}],\"label\":\"Method functions\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:8a4b3e0b01733e1d2848d3e37a77872b","key":433,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:8a4b3e0b01733e1d2848d3e37a77872b\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[\"An evaluation requires the relation.\"],\"definition\":\"Frames act together through four distinct relations: independently activated co-evaluation, result conjunction, evidence or coordinate translation, and material composition.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":600,\"path\":\"standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md\",\"quote\":\"Frames act together through four distinct relations, and only where the\\nevaluation requires one (P4a; RF-010).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md#REFERENCE_FRAME%2F6.%20Frames%20in%20conjunction\",\"start_line\":599}],\"label\":\"Frames acting together\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:195629e9ad706d9544c0aecd154fcd87","key":434,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:195629e9ad706d9544c0aecd154fcd87\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"Several frames may separately activate on the same subject and return closed results, serving assurance independence, different evidence altitudes and distinct failure perspectives.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":609,\"path\":\"standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md\",\"quote\":\"Several frames may evaluate the same subject through separate activations\\nand return closed results. They may overlap in subject, manifold or\\nevidence sources; neither evaluation consumes or influences the other's\\nunclosed working result. This serves assurance independence, different\\nevidence altitudes and distinct failure perspectives (P6; FOUNDATIONS §2,\\nevaluation independence).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md#REFERENCE_FRAME%2F6.%20Frames%20in%20conjunction%2FIndependently%20activated%20co-evaluation\",\"start_line\":604}],\"label\":\"Independently activated co-evaluation\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:db936e60348cd5ddfbe90eadaba01749","key":435,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:db936e60348cd5ddfbe90eadaba01749\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"A declared decision rule consumes several frames' closed results using the core conjunction and rule requirements owned by FOUNDATIONS §4. REFERENCE_FRAME defines no separate conjunction.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":618,\"path\":\"standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md\",\"quote\":\"A declared decision rule consumes the closed results of several frames.\\nThe rule, what it must state, and the conjunction it computes are\\n[FOUNDATIONS §4 Conjunction of results](FOUNDATIONS.md#conjunction-of-results),\\nover the core values of [FOUNDATIONS §4 Results](FOUNDATIONS.md#results);\\nthis member defines no conjunction of its own. The outcomes of `conjoin`\\nmap to the core as §5 states (P4a, P5, P6).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md#REFERENCE_FRAME%2F6.%20Frames%20in%20conjunction%2FResult%20conjunction\",\"start_line\":613}],\"label\":\"Result conjunction\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:a18aa4716c81ba6c7558cbd669733f84","key":436,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:a18aa4716c81ba6c7558cbd669733f84\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"One frame supplies evidence or a value consumed inside another through a translation declaring source and target coordinates, preserved meaning, accepted loss, provenance, equality law and refusal conditions.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":624,\"path\":\"standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md\",\"quote\":\"One frame supplies evidence or a value consumed inside another. The\\ntranslation declares source and target coordinates, preserved meaning,\\naccepted loss, provenance, equality law and refusal conditions (P1, P4b).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md#REFERENCE_FRAME%2F6.%20Frames%20in%20conjunction%2FEvidence%20or%20coordinate%20translation\",\"start_line\":622}],\"label\":\"Evidence or coordinate translation\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:a8dda0745628627da84c7c6f067aa78a","key":437,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:a8dda0745628627da84c7c6f067aa78a\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[\"The evaluation requires composition.\"],\"definition\":\"Several frame-governed operations form one material execution or reasoning relation, declared by the owning application with shared invariants, material effect or decision order, closure, failure and conservation of semantic, operation and decision authority.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":642,\"path\":\"standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md\",\"quote\":\"Several frame-governed operations form one material execution or reasoning\\nrelation. The owning application declares the composition, the shared\\ninvariants, the effect or decision order where material, closure, failure,\\nand the conservation of semantic, operation and decision authority.\\nComposition is introduced only when the evaluation requires it; a possible\\nfuture interaction does not require a general composition law in every\\nframe (P4a, P6, P2).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md#REFERENCE_FRAME%2F6.%20Frames%20in%20conjunction%2FMaterial%20composition\",\"start_line\":636}],\"label\":\"Material composition\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:cff170c9e1941f9081b9f3ff23444d52","key":438,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:cff170c9e1941f9081b9f3ff23444d52\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"Permitted relation categories: disjoint means no shared material variable, coordinate, evidence or result dependency for the declared evaluations; overlapping shares material variables, evidence or entities; complementary jointly informs one decision through distinct evaluations; alternative evaluates the same claim under declared capability or evidence conditions; refinement resolves a distinction another frame aggregates; restriction evaluates a lawful subset of another domain; translated moves values or evidence through a declared coordinate map; temporally successive evaluates a changed basis later; composed combines frame relations into one governed evaluation or action; governing/subordinate inherits declared constraints where real authority or decomposition exists.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":663,\"path\":\"standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md\",\"quote\":\"- governing and subordinate: one frame inherits declared constraints from\\n  another where a real authority or decomposition relation exists.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md#REFERENCE_FRAME%2F7.%20Frame%20relations\",\"start_line\":662}],\"label\":\"Frame relation categories\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:72de70c8d4e8e6e465a75397655a737d","key":439,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:72de70c8d4e8e6e465a75397655a737d\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"Coverage(W, G, B, E, S, T): workspace W, governed outcome G, exact basis B, known evaluation inventory E, declared frame set S, and the claim's time or immutable checkpoint T.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":676,\"path\":\"standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md\",\"quote\":\"Coverage is evaluated against the tuple Coverage(W, G, B, E, S, T): the\\nworkspace W, the governed outcome G, the exact basis B, the known\\nevaluation inventory E, the declared frame set S and the time or immutable\\ncheckpoint T of the claim.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md#REFERENCE_FRAME%2F8.%20Workspace%20coverage%2FCoverage%20basis\",\"start_line\":673}],\"label\":\"Coverage basis\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:7729b386c86d4a0bdcd75f325e1923cf","key":440,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:7729b386c86d4a0bdcd75f325e1923cf\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"Known material evaluations derived by the coverage evaluator from every material available source, recording provenance and materiality.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":685,\"path\":\"standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md\",\"quote\":\"The coverage evaluator derives the known evaluation inventory from every\\nmaterial available source, including where applicable:\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md#REFERENCE_FRAME%2F8.%20Workspace%20coverage%2FEvaluation%20inventory\",\"start_line\":684}],\"label\":\"Evaluation inventory\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:b5ad6b84b70663c91207ead9c9b5ef6d","key":441,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:b5ad6b84b70663c91207ead9c9b5ef6d\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"Cross-cutting audit lenses, typically outcome/capability, identity/authority, lifecycle/temporal behaviour, topology/interactions, transport/representation, evidence/proof, change/failure/recovery/rollback, historical regression, and actor capability/context fit. A lens becomes a frame only through separate instantiation as a bounded evaluation family.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":707,\"path\":\"standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md\",\"quote\":\"These are lenses (FOUNDATIONS §2): they become frames only when separately\\ninstantiated as bounded evaluation families (P2).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md#REFERENCE_FRAME%2F8.%20Workspace%20coverage%2FCoverage%20dimensions\",\"start_line\":706}],\"label\":\"Coverage dimensions\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:873d4a144c22169c04cc15288c18fb86","key":442,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:873d4a144c22169c04cc15288c18fb86\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"Per-evaluation ledger of coverage obligations. Baseline statuses are covered, separately_covered, conditionally_covered, conflicted, uncovered, unknown and excluded_by_authority. Their predicate is coverage by a capable frame of S on the declared tuple without unresolved conflict among covering frames, results or authorities, or exclusion by the governing authority cited by the row.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":739,\"path\":\"standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md\",\"quote\":\"whether a row's coverage obligation is met, for the predicate \\\"on the\\ndeclared coverage tuple, a capable frame of S covers the evaluation with\\nno unresolved conflict among the frames, results or authorities that\\ncover it, or a governing authority the row cites excludes it\\\". Each status\\nmaps to exactly one core value, and the value travels with that predicate\\nand with the status, whose meaning stays here (P5, P6):\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md#REFERENCE_FRAME%2F8.%20Workspace%20coverage%2FCoverage%20ledger\",\"start_line\":734}],\"label\":\"Coverage ledger\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:41719079da7311bbe57eb93d596d2793","key":443,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:41719079da7311bbe57eb93d596d2793\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"Ordered investigation of activation, exact basis, actor capability, evidence, missing material distinctions, missing conjunction/translation, evaluation-family adequacy and need for another frame.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":869,\"path\":\"standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md\",\"quote\":\"1. Was the correct declared frame activated?\\n2. Were the subject and basis exact?\\n3. Was the actor inside the capability envelope?\\n4. Was admissible evidence available?\\n5. Is a material variable or invariant missing from the frame?\\n6. Is a required conjunction or translation missing?\\n7. Is the evaluation family itself wrong or incomplete?\\n8. Is another frame required?\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md#REFERENCE_FRAME%2F10.%20Discovery%20and%20revision%2FDiagnostic%20order\",\"start_line\":862}],\"label\":\"Frame diagnosis\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:c8d1bd7d867c78286170d056a942c518","key":444,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:c8d1bd7d867c78286170d056a942c518\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"Revision of frame declarations or frame-set organisation, distinguished from reconsideration of closed-result validity. A material frame revision creates a new revision coordinate; a change to no frame declaration needs no new coordinate.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":914,\"path\":\"standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md\",\"quote\":\"Whether a revision needs a new frame revision coordinate turns on the\\nframe's declarations; whether a result already closed stays valid is a\\nseparate question. A revision is material when it changes a frame\\ndeclaration in a way that is material under\\n[FOUNDATIONS §2](FOUNDATIONS.md#2-ontology). A revision that changes no\\ndeclaration of the frame needs no new coordinate. That answer decides\\nnothing about any result: an unchanged declaration is no ground for\\nkeeping a result closed.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md#REFERENCE_FRAME%2F10.%20Discovery%20and%20revision%2FRevision%20actions\",\"start_line\":907}],\"label\":\"Frame revision\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:1d204a797802b5261b6acecea9ea1275","key":445,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:1d204a797802b5261b6acecea9ea1275\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"The actor's received activated frame or declared active frame configuration, with minimum identity/revision, evaluation/result algebra, exact subject/basis, material relations/invariants, authorities, admissible evidence/tools, capability/context envelope, exclusions/prohibited assumptions, dependencies/conjunction outputs, and invalidation/stop/reconfiguration conditions.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":938,\"path\":\"standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md\",\"quote\":\"An actor receives one activated frame or one declared active frame\\nconfiguration, never an implied demand to reconstruct the complete\\nworkspace from ambient context (P0). The minimum\\nactivation packet contains:\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md#REFERENCE_FRAME%2F11.%20The%20activation%20packet\",\"start_line\":935}],\"label\":\"Activation packet\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:2d2745cd8eece9f0ad7fb3c267b65b08","key":446,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:2d2745cd8eece9f0ad7fb3c267b65b08\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"Carrier-neutral template sufficient to bind one declared frame for one evaluation: stable activation identity; declaration identity/revision and exact evaluation/closed algebra; exact subject or candidate and workspace/authority/dependency/configuration/time basis; material relations/invariants, source/semantic references, exclusions; actor/envelope; semantic/evaluation authority, material operation authority/subject/territory, decision/acceptance/publication authority; admissible evidence/acquisition, used dependency/overlap/input/conjunction/translation relations, result consumer/return; invalidation, stop, residual, re-entry and reconfiguration conditions.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":965,\"path\":\"standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md\",\"quote\":\"The following carrier-neutral content is sufficient to bind one declared\\nframe for one evaluation. It may be written in Markdown, structured data, a\\nprompt or another consumer-selected carrier without changing the relation\\n(P0, RF-016).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md#REFERENCE_FRAME%2F11.%20The%20activation%20packet%2FMinimal%20activation%20binding\",\"start_line\":962}],\"label\":\"Minimal activation binding\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:1fbf69d69e14a78abead83b3babfa8aa","key":447,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:1fbf69d69e14a78abead83b3babfa8aa\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"Three carrier-neutral shapes supply the least content declaring a frame, frame set and evaluation result, sufficient in Markdown or another consumer-selected carrier.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1044,\"path\":\"standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md\",\"quote\":\"The three carrier-neutral shapes below are the least content that declares\\na frame, a frame set and an evaluation result. Each is sufficient as\\nwritten in Markdown or any other consumer-selected carrier (P0, P2;\\nRF-016).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md#REFERENCE_FRAME%2F13.%20Minimal%20declarations\",\"start_line\":1041}],\"label\":\"Minimal declarations\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:4e34ff185f118a1294229a41556d8e43","key":448,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:4e34ff185f118a1294229a41556d8e43\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"Result record containing frame identity/revision, activation identity, evaluation, subject/basis, actor/envelope, semantic/evaluation/material operation/decision authorities, admissible evidence, result, inference relation, residual uncertainty, out_of_frame residual, invalidation conditions and consuming decision or conjunction.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1138,\"path\":\"standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md\",\"quote\":\"- result:\\n- inference relation:\\n- residual uncertainty:\\n- out_of_frame residual (missing relation or capability, owner, reconfiguration pressure):\\n- invalidation conditions:\\n- consuming decision or conjunction:\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md#REFERENCE_FRAME%2F13.%20Minimal%20declarations%2FMinimal%20evaluation%20result\",\"start_line\":1133}],\"label\":\"Minimal evaluation result\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:47f5a07e664b149bf807f7c0c22cd554","key":449,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:47f5a07e664b149bf807f7c0c22cd554\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"Tier-2 RELEASE owns release publication, identities, project-qualified refs/subtrees, historical conservation, candidate/publication/qualification phases, monotonic selectors, naming, release-scoped assets and Product subject, coordinated cohorts, acceptance, external qualification dependencies and successor conservation. It consumes rather than redefines lineage, result, effect, identity, claim, acceptance, layer, calculus-identity, installed-basis and adoption laws.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":11,\"path\":\"standards/RELEASE.md\",\"quote\":\"Tier 2. Owns release publication: the release-publication bounded\\ncontext, release identities, project-qualified refs and the project\\nsubtree, historical ref conservation, the three phases with candidate\\nconstruction, immutable RC publication, exact-cut qualification and\\nmonotonic version-line advancement, the selector and its relation to\\nconsumer adoption, naming, release-scoped assets and the Product subject,\\ncoordinated release-matched asset cohorts, acceptance, external\\nqualification dependencies and successor baseline conservation\\n(STDO-UP-015) with its disposition values.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/RELEASE.md#RELEASE\",\"start_line\":3}],\"label\":\"Release-publication member\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:99876a10de367b85603c3ed68656e593","key":450,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:99876a10de367b85603c3ed68656e593\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"Seven distinct identities: Project Release Namespace, a stable repository-local authority-assigned project key; Project Subtree, exact repository-relative root and Git tree for a cut; Candidate Source, mutable source state constructing a possible successor; RC Branch, mutable project-qualified candidate-window carrier; Immutable RC Cut, annotated project-qualified tag plus exact Product release subject, naming a published candidate and, once accepted, a released Product; Version-Line Selector, mutable project-qualified tag alias for the highest published ordinal on that project/version line; optional Release Branch, mutable convenience carrier aligned to the selector's latest-published commit.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":177,\"path\":\"standards/RELEASE.md\",\"quote\":\"Equal version text does not collapse these identities. Branches and the\\nversion-line selector may move. An immutable RC tag never moves (P3).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/RELEASE.md#RELEASE%2F2.%20Release%20identities\",\"start_line\":176}],\"label\":\"Release identities\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:b6b525988325f2bf81fd5df06a4e1be9","key":451,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:b6b525988325f2bf81fd5df06a4e1be9\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"Evaluation bound to an exact immutable cut and member set, exact claim bytes, governing Product/release basis, each property's observation boundary, evidence subjects, owner verdicts, gaps and complete successor relation.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":339,\"path\":\"standards/RELEASE.md\",\"quote\":\"- the exact release-scoped claim bytes;\\n- the governing Product and release basis;\\n- each claimed property and its observation boundary;\\n- evidence subjects, owner verdicts and unresolved gaps; and\\n- the complete successor relation to the declared predecessor (§9).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/RELEASE.md#RELEASE%2F3.%20Phases%2FExact-cut%20qualification\",\"start_line\":335}],\"label\":\"Exact-cut qualification\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:ab9e1240d741031d3f1aaabda745554e","key":452,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:ab9e1240d741031d3f1aaabda745554e\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"Separate explicit Product-Definition transition that resolves, presents, installs, verifies and pins a selected immutable RC. Its operative basis is the exact release URI and installed-manifest digest; a channel is discovery only.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":399,\"path\":\"standards/RELEASE.md\",\"quote\":\"A Product Definition may retain `stdo://channels/<version>` as its\\ndiscovery selector, but its operative basis is the exact\\n`stdo://releases/v<version>-rc.<n>/` URI and installed-manifest digest,\\nthe installed release basis of PRODUCT_DEFINITION §4. Moving the Git\\nversion-line selector does not update any consumer. Adoption is a separate\\nexplicit Product-Definition transition that resolves, presents, installs,\\nverifies and pins the selected immutable RC.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/RELEASE.md#RELEASE%2F4.%20Selector%20and%20consumer%20adoption\",\"start_line\":393}],\"label\":\"Consumer adoption\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:fa247d55722088d1c8208111b982761e","key":453,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:fa247d55722088d1c8208111b982761e\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[\"A Product authority explicitly declares the relation when a source corpus and required distributed or derived assets need to be usable as one versioned set.\"],\"definition\":\"Cross-Product Release-Matched Asset Cohort naming every required Product and asset, exact source dependency, owning authorities, qualification boundary and publication transaction. The STDO stack cohort contains the exact standards cut, its distributed spec plugin/host assets, exact Axiom Indexer mechanics Product, exact STDO Representation Product, and its released a_c.STDO program/logical constraint map or equivalent semantic index with complete source member inventory, member digests, member-set digest and exact derivation cut.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":505,\"path\":\"standards/RELEASE.md\",\"quote\":\"A Product authority may declare an explicit cross-Product Release-Matched\\nAsset Cohort when one source corpus and its required distributed or\\nderived assets need to remain usable as one versioned set. The declaring\\nrelation names every required Product and asset, the exact source\\ndependency, its owning authorities, the qualification boundary and the\\npublication transaction. Path co-location, equal version text or a common\\nactor cannot infer the relation (P3, P6).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/RELEASE.md#RELEASE%2F7.%20Coordinated%20release-matched%20asset%20cohorts\",\"start_line\":499}],\"label\":\"Release-Matched Asset Cohort\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:d6c44732513e57f9b82a2af8b45fb479","key":454,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:d6c44732513e57f9b82a2af8b45fb479\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[\"A predecessor claim is capable of affecting the successor.\"],\"definition\":\"One semantic claim about that predecessor claim: conserved means retained; superseded means replaced by an accepted successor relation; intentionally removed means removed by current Product authority; not applicable means no successor effect with bounded reason. These are predicates to evaluate, not core result values or the decision owner's acceptance disposition. Unresolved states no claim and has no result.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":661,\"path\":\"standards/RELEASE.md\",\"quote\":\"- conserved: the successor retains the claim;\\n- superseded: an accepted successor relation replaces it;\\n- intentionally removed: current Product authority removes it; or\\n- not applicable: it has no successor effect, with a bounded reason.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/RELEASE.md#RELEASE%2F9.%20Successor%20baseline%20conservation%20%28STDO-UP-015%29\",\"start_line\":658}],\"label\":\"Successor semantic disposition\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:7b19e39be9fd85c952d4163c0c025b77","key":455,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:7b19e39be9fd85c952d4163c0c025b77\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"F15 traces release and successor-conservation laws from commitments plus explicitly additional instance premises: recursive products, published cuts, mutable carriers, derived assets, external services and successor lines. It traces but does not own FOUNDATIONS lineage objects. P1/P3/P6 are cited as independent, P0 as recovered, P4b as derived from P0/P2 with non-reacquirable step-produced facts, and P5 as derived from P0/P6 with the open-world premise. Domain choices and their owners are distinct from consequences.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":111,\"path\":\"standards/RELEASE.md\",\"quote\":\"the table traces that section in its first two rows, whose rule column\\nnames it, and owns none of it. Each commitment's standing is written as\\nthe table of commitments in FOUNDATIONS §3 states it.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/RELEASE.md#RELEASE%2F1.%20Context%20and%20position%2FFoundation%20to%20law%3A%20release%20and%20successor%20conservation\",\"start_line\":109}],\"label\":\"F15 release and successor conservation\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:894323f233349c5a81fd1da1c9c828ba","key":456,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:894323f233349c5a81fd1da1c9c828ba\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"Tier-2 particular method owning position/identity, constitutional chain and surfaces, manifesto/litmus tests, requirement/design/trace/live-surface laws, outcome conservation, change management/triage/classification/consistency/sprint boundaries, ambiguity/lifecycle, lineage/release boundary, migration/procedures/design records and build-tenant binding. It is a realisation of FOUNDATIONS, REFERENCE_FRAME, ACTIVATION and EVALUATION, not itself foundational; other Tier-2 members own project binding, testing, work carriers and release mechanics.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":16,\"path\":\"standards/SPEC_METHOD.md\",\"quote\":\"It is realised from [FOUNDATIONS](FOUNDATIONS.md),\\n[REFERENCE_FRAME](REFERENCE_FRAME.md), [ACTIVATION](ACTIVATION.md) and\\n[EVALUATION](EVALUATION.md): nothing here is foundational, every clause\\nnames the principle that requires it (P0 to P6, FOUNDATIONS §3), and each\\nmechanism could be realised differently under the same principles.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/SPEC_METHOD.md#SPEC_METHOD\",\"start_line\":12}],\"label\":\"SPEC_METHOD\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:7b52a0bef35a63b536af6e7f80726a0a","key":457,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:7b52a0bef35a63b536af6e7f80726a0a\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"Meta-constitutional process for spec-driven projects defining relations among goals, intent, product, requirements, design, code, evidence and repricing; specification sufficiency; kinds of requirement truth; and authority during iterative delivery. The method should bootstrap a new process if implementation disappears; method plus surviving domain specification can reconstruct the project.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":52,\"path\":\"standards/SPEC_METHOD.md\",\"quote\":\"Its role is meta-constitutional: it defines how goals, intent, product,\\nrequirements, design, code, evidence and repricing relate; what counts as\\nspecification sufficiency; what kinds of requirement truth exist; and how\\nauthority flows during iterative delivery. If a project's implementation\\ndisappears, the method should still be sufficient to bootstrap a new\\nspec-driven project process from scratch; the method plus the surviving domain specification\\ncan reconstruct the project (P2, P0).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/SPEC_METHOD.md#SPEC_METHOD%2F1.%20Position%20and%20identity%2FProcess%20constitution\",\"start_line\":46}],\"label\":\"Process constitution\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:867a67ed8bb9b0e5119339afe287cda0","key":458,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:867a67ed8bb9b0e5119339afe287cda0\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[\"Within urn:stdo:bounded-context:method-identity under the selected complete basis.\"],\"definition\":\"STDO names four method-law areas: S Specification owned by SPEC_METHOD; T Ticketing owned by TICKETS; D Design owned by DESIGN_MODULE; O Outcome-Driven Development, whose complete identity and realisation meaning are owned by ODD.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":95,\"path\":\"standards/SPEC_METHOD.md\",\"quote\":\"S,\\nSpecification, owned by this member; T, Ticketing, owned by\\n[TICKETS](TICKETS.md); D, Design, owned by the design profile member\\n[DESIGN_MODULE](DESIGN_MODULE.md); and O, Outcome-Driven Development, the\\ncomplete area whose identity and realisation meaning are owned by its\\nprofile member [ODD](ODD.md).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/SPEC_METHOD.md#SPEC_METHOD%2F1.%20Position%20and%20identity%2FMethod%20identity\",\"start_line\":90}],\"label\":\"STDO method identity\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:fc18dcf616a3cdc09fa46a6044df9951","key":459,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:fc18dcf616a3cdc09fa46a6044df9951\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"Homeostatic responsibility chain: Goals → Intent → Product Definition → Requirements → Design → Code → Events → Projection → Delta → Scenarios → Gap analysis → Repricing at the layer named by change class. Goals name current work-wave concerns; intent purpose/direction; Product Definition the current mutable source project's terms, boundaries and end-state shape; requirements invariant obligations; design structural decisions/interfaces/carriers/topology; Code realisation in software, human procedure or both; Events retained happenings; Projection reconstructs current truth from sufficient retained records; Delta exposes intended/realised drift; Scenarios test operational meaning; Gap analysis finds model insufficiency; Repricing changes the appropriate layer and generates new goals/intent when work-wave, direction or scope changes.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":212,\"path\":\"standards/SPEC_METHOD.md\",\"quote\":\"Goals → Intent → Product Definition → Requirements → Design → Code\\n  → Events → Projection → Delta → Scenarios → Gap analysis\\n  → Repricing at the layer its change class names\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/SPEC_METHOD.md#SPEC_METHOD%2F2.%20The%20chain%2FConstitutional%20chain\",\"start_line\":210}],\"label\":\"Constitutional chain\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:26a8936b7793bf1681e921b95ed4987b","key":460,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:26a8936b7793bf1681e921b95ed4987b\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"F10 traces how specification governs realisations from owned layers, layered surfaces, several changing realisations and immutable releases as instance premises not supplied by commitments. Commitment standings are P0 recovered; P1/P2/P3/P4a/P6 independent; P4b derived from P0/P2 with non-reacquirable step-produced facts; P5 derived from P0/P6 with the open-world premise. It distinguishes consequences, owning rules, domain/policy choices and consumers.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":158,\"path\":\"standards/SPEC_METHOD.md\",\"quote\":\"Standing of the commitments cited (FOUNDATIONS §3): P0\\nrecovered; P1, P2, P3, P4a and P6 independent; P4b derived from P0 and\\nP2, with P0's premise that step-produced facts are not re-acquirable; P5\\nderived from P0 and P6, with P0's open-world premise.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/SPEC_METHOD.md#SPEC_METHOD%2F2.%20The%20chain%2FFoundation%20to%20law%3A%20chain%2C%20outcome%20and%20build-tenant%20binding\",\"start_line\":155}],\"label\":\"F10 chain, outcome and build-tenant binding\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:f80d75c7a70cd53604f225c790e0cbea","key":461,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:f80d75c7a70cd53604f225c790e0cbea\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"Specification-driven development is a governed derivation and disambiguation method: current goals precede deeper repricing, intent precedes implementation, product definition precedes detailed requirements, and design explicitly bridges requirements to code.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":288,\"path\":\"standards/SPEC_METHOD.md\",\"quote\":\"The method commits to these (P2, P6). It defines the\\ncurrent goals for the active body of work before repricing deeper\\nconstitutional layers. It works from intent before implementation. It\\ndefines the current product definition in explicit present-tense terms\\nbefore decomposing it into detailed requirements. It defines the full\\nconstitutional what in requirements, not merely a feature list. It prefers\\ndeclaring desired truth and lawful boundaries over prescribing step-by-step\\nimperative procedure. It makes design the explicit structural bridge\\nbetween requirements and code. It requires code to be derivable from\\nrequirements and design, not defended as accidental precedent. It treats\\nspec-driven development as a disambiguation pipeline: each major gate\\nreduces the space of lawful interpretations before downstream realisation\\nproceeds.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/SPEC_METHOD.md#SPEC_METHOD%2F2.%20The%20chain%2FManifesto\",\"start_line\":276}],\"label\":\"Specification-driven method\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:0fba6006fc3beaeee2b2da0429d2ebd5","key":462,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:0fba6006fc3beaeee2b2da0429d2ebd5\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"Goals orient the current bounded work wave; they do not substitute for requirements.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":407,\"path\":\"standards/SPEC_METHOD.md\",\"quote\":\"Goals orient the current bounded work\\nwave and are not a substitute requirement surface.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/SPEC_METHOD.md#SPEC_METHOD%2F2.%20The%20chain%2FSpecification%20surface%20rule\",\"start_line\":406}],\"label\":\"Goals surface\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:6aa1c6f8fac3acabc7f9abbc957c9418","key":463,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:6aa1c6f8fac3acabc7f9abbc957c9418\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"Intent states why the system exists and which directional change is in or out of scope.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":409,\"path\":\"standards/SPEC_METHOD.md\",\"quote\":\"Intent states why the\\nsystem exists and what directional change is in or out of scope; it carries\\nno optional realisation detail unless that detail is itself constitutional.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/SPEC_METHOD.md#SPEC_METHOD%2F2.%20The%20chain%2FSpecification%20surface%20rule\",\"start_line\":407}],\"label\":\"Intent surface\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:b468f75bb4237ed72bce6a9a5f81fb40","key":464,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:b468f75bb4237ed72bce6a9a5f81fb40\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"Product definition is the current concrete, present-tense bridge from intent to requirements, including lifecycle signal material to product meaning; it is not release notes.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":415,\"path\":\"standards/SPEC_METHOD.md\",\"quote\":\"Product states the current concrete product definition and bridges intent\\nto requirements; it is not a release-note surface; it carries enough\\noperational lifecycle signal for downstream requirements and design to\\nunderstand intended use, release and install posture, live-use posture,\\nobservability posture, and retirement or supersession posture where those\\nmaterially affect product meaning.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/SPEC_METHOD.md#SPEC_METHOD%2F2.%20The%20chain%2FSpecification%20surface%20rule\",\"start_line\":410}],\"label\":\"Product definition\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:9f2f38ea41a0381a444a2592fc8caaaa","key":465,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:9f2f38ea41a0381a444a2592fc8caaaa\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"Requirements state the full constitutional WHAT as stable obligations with explicit acceptance criteria, sufficient for downstream design derivation.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":420,\"path\":\"standards/SPEC_METHOD.md\",\"quote\":\"Requirements state stable obligations\\nthat must be true; they carry explicit acceptance criteria and remain\\nsufficient for downstream design derivation, including lifecycle\\nobligations or named lifecycle ambiguity gaps where build, assurance,\\nrelease, deployment, live usage, telemetry or retirement materially affect\\nthe obligation.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/SPEC_METHOD.md#SPEC_METHOD%2F2.%20The%20chain%2FSpecification%20surface%20rule\",\"start_line\":415}],\"label\":\"Requirements surface\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:d9ba6983a42a941491c1518a443a52cf","key":466,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:d9ba6983a42a941491c1518a443a52cf\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"Design is the downstream structural HOW that realises requirement truth and chooses lawful mechanisms, structures, interfaces, carriers, packaging and tenant boundaries.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":423,\"path\":\"standards/SPEC_METHOD.md\",\"quote\":\"Design states how requirement truth is realised; it is\\ndownstream of requirements and may choose structure, interfaces, carriers,\\npackaging and tenant boundaries. ADRs are durable design memory, not a\\nsecond requirement surface.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/SPEC_METHOD.md#SPEC_METHOD%2F2.%20The%20chain%2FSpecification%20surface%20rule\",\"start_line\":420}],\"label\":\"Design surface\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:f696d7d5c8744e38d05c8d6dc1e2fd47","key":467,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:f696d7d5c8744e38d05c8d6dc1e2fd47\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"Code is executable realisation derived from requirements and design, rather than a source of authority through accidental precedent.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":285,\"path\":\"standards/SPEC_METHOD.md\",\"quote\":\"It requires code to be derivable from\\nrequirements and design, not defended as accidental precedent.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/SPEC_METHOD.md#SPEC_METHOD%2F2.%20The%20chain%2FManifesto\",\"start_line\":284}],\"label\":\"Code realisation\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:f8a1b1b5f801b47764b6f0c9f0a8473d","key":468,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:f8a1b1b5f801b47764b6f0c9f0a8473d\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"Reconstruction sufficiency is competent reconstruction of conformant downstream layers in order. It is not determinism and cannot depend on hiding major ambiguity.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":337,\"path\":\"standards/SPEC_METHOD.md\",\"quote\":\"The generic law, that a layered specification is sufficient when a competent\\nactor can derive each layer from the one above, that sufficiency is not\\ndeterminism, that a boundary crossed only by hiding a major ambiguity is not\\nsufficient, and that an accepted relation may be reused on its exact basis\\nafter checking applicability and invalidation, is EVALUATION §6.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/SPEC_METHOD.md#SPEC_METHOD%2F2.%20The%20chain%2FReconstruction%20litmus\",\"start_line\":333}],\"label\":\"Reconstruction sufficiency\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:5901946aac03404c647b37dbf3bfb477","key":469,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:5901946aac03404c647b37dbf3bfb477\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"Renewal is the cumulative feedback cycle from current specification through real-world use case and explicit gap analysis to lawful re-entry and forward repricing.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":380,\"path\":\"standards/SPEC_METHOD.md\",\"quote\":\"current specification → real-world use case → gap analysis → re-entry at the layer its change class names\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/SPEC_METHOD.md#SPEC_METHOD%2F2.%20The%20chain%2FRenewal%20path\",\"start_line\":380}],\"label\":\"Renewal cycle\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:55a257d3aa9a5758b48bd07e923451f9","key":470,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:55a257d3aa9a5758b48bd07e923451f9\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[\"The tier-3 DESIGN_MODULE profile governs the boundary under its own adoption rule.\"],\"definition\":\"The design profile's realisation shape makes meaning readable as transforms over admitted truth and locates effects explicitly at the edge.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":469,\"path\":\"standards/SPEC_METHOD.md\",\"quote\":\"For a realisation boundary that the design profile governs (DESIGN_MODULE,\\ntier 3, adopted under its own adoption rule), the core rule is: semantic\\nsteps should read as transforms over admitted truth; effects should be\\nexplicit and pushed to the edge. If a reader has to inspect orchestration\\ncode, mutable workspace state, service methods or fallback defaults to\\ndetermine what the system means, the design is too imperative and too\\ncoupled (P1, P6).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/SPEC_METHOD.md#SPEC_METHOD%2F2.%20The%20chain%2FRealisation%20shape\",\"start_line\":463}],\"label\":\"Profile-governed realisation shape\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:7d0a9c90f5f4ae3de1e1726cf6d1423f","key":471,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:7d0a9c90f5f4ae3de1e1726cf6d1423f\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"Requirement category and lifecycle status are independent declared-state domains. Categories are Capability (required behaviour/function/surface), Constraint / Guarantee (invariant, law, safety, portability or semantic bound), Governance (lifecycle, authority, visibility, release or operator policy), and Verification (tests, evidence, traceability, qualification or forensic obligations). Statuses are Active, Deferred, Superseded and Orphaned.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":492,\"path\":\"standards/SPEC_METHOD.md\",\"quote\":\"| Capability | a behaviour, function or surface the system must provide | what can the system do |\\n| Constraint / Guarantee | an invariant, law, safety property, portability rule or semantic guarantee that bounds how the system may behave | what must always remain true |\\n| Governance | a policy or control rule over lifecycle, authority, visibility, release or operator action | what governs use and change |\\n| Verification | a requirement on tests, evidence, traceability, qualification or forensic surfaces | how do we know the claim is true |\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/SPEC_METHOD.md#SPEC_METHOD%2F2.%20The%20chain%2FRequirement%20categories%20and%20classification\",\"start_line\":489},{\"end_line\":509,\"path\":\"standards/SPEC_METHOD.md\",\"quote\":\"Every live requirement family is classified on two independent axes (P3,\\nP1): lifecycle status (Active,\\nDeferred, Superseded, Orphaned) and requirement category (the four above).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/SPEC_METHOD.md#SPEC_METHOD%2F2.%20The%20chain%2FRequirement%20categories%20and%20classification\",\"start_line\":507}],\"label\":\"Requirement classifications\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:d8b080fae05d72da046074755cfaa758","key":472,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:d8b080fae05d72da046074755cfaa758\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"Constitutional trace closure closes the constitution over realised behaviour and is stricter than documentation completeness.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":566,\"path\":\"standards/SPEC_METHOD.md\",\"quote\":\"Spec-driven development requires constitutional trace closure: the rule\\nthat closes the constitution over realised behaviour, stricter than\\ndocumentation completeness (P6, P4b).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/SPEC_METHOD.md#SPEC_METHOD%2F2.%20The%20chain%2FTrace%20closure%20and%20anti-drift\",\"start_line\":564}],\"label\":\"Constitutional trace closure\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:ed7ff9285b162fceacac9fd577163485","key":473,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:ed7ff9285b162fceacac9fd577163485\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[\"A domain artifact has been published as a live constitutional surface.\"],\"definition\":\"A live domain surface is versioned constitutional history, immutable in place; a project may accumulate multiple such surfaces.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":610,\"path\":\"standards/SPEC_METHOD.md\",\"quote\":\"A project may accumulate multiple live domain surfaces over time. A live\\nsurface is versioned constitutional history, not scratch space (P3). Engine code, design documents, tests and\\ntooling may be refactored aggressively while they remain mutable\\nimplementation surfaces. Live domain artifacts, once published as live\\nconstitutional surfaces, are immutable in place; if one is wrong, the valid\\nactions are to supersede it with a new version or to withdraw or delete it\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/SPEC_METHOD.md#SPEC_METHOD%2F2.%20The%20chain%2FLive%20surface%20immutability\",\"start_line\":605}],\"label\":\"Live domain surface\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:7e3dd4056d50d0eb1d1209f1d770b654","key":474,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:7e3dd4056d50d0eb1d1209f1d770b654\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[\"The designed product, application, module, function, runtime surface, plugin surface, public interface, data surface or capability is material.\"],\"definition\":\"The canonical operational lifecycle is intent, requirement, build, assurance, release, deployment, live usage, observed telemetry and retirement. A phase has one declared answer: answered; not applicable with reason; or a named Gap:/Unanswered: marker.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":627,\"path\":\"standards/SPEC_METHOD.md\",\"quote\":\"Any material\\nproduct, application, module, function, runtime surface, plugin\\nsurface, public interface, data surface or capability has an operational\\nlifecycle, whose canonical chain is intent, requirement, build, assurance,\\nrelease, deployment, live usage, observed telemetry, retirement.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/SPEC_METHOD.md#SPEC_METHOD%2F2.%20The%20chain%2FOperational%20lifecycle%20sufficiency\",\"start_line\":623},{\"end_line\":648,\"path\":\"standards/SPEC_METHOD.md\",\"quote\":\"Each phase has one of three answers, and this\\nsection owns them: the phase is answered by the surface; if a phase is\\nnot applicable, the surface says why; if it is unknown, a named gap such\\nas `Gap:` or `Unanswered:` is recorded.\\nSilent absence is not a valid lifecycle answer.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/SPEC_METHOD.md#SPEC_METHOD%2F2.%20The%20chain%2FOperational%20lifecycle%20sufficiency\",\"start_line\":644}],\"label\":\"Operational lifecycle\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:7e174d80769b16059837b8b7bff5ce16","key":475,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:7e174d80769b16059837b8b7bff5ce16\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[\"The work wave bears a product outcome.\"],\"definition\":\"A work wave binds one explicitly selected, unresolved, directly verifiable product-defined outcome instance and its declared acceptance interval.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":672,\"path\":\"standards/SPEC_METHOD.md\",\"quote\":\"Every product-outcome-bearing work wave identifies one explicitly selected,\\nunresolved, directly verifiable product-defined outcome and declares the\\nacceptance interval for that instance. Product-progress claims and\\npromotion onto the supported product path are judged against that same\\noutcome (P2; FOUNDATIONS §2\\nOutcome U is the generic object).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/SPEC_METHOD.md#SPEC_METHOD%2F3.%20Outcome%20conservation\",\"start_line\":667}],\"label\":\"Selected product outcome\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:e4591f6921a4ff4e2ea685314fb47f04","key":476,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:e4591f6921a4ff4e2ea685314fb47f04\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"Product-outcome evidence distinguishes material advance, prerequisite readiness, preservation and regression. These are declared classifications rather than evaluation core values.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":685,\"path\":\"standards/SPEC_METHOD.md\",\"quote\":\"Evidence distinguishes material advance, prerequisite readiness,\\npreservation and regression. The four refine the progress\\ncategories of [ACTIVATION §5](ACTIVATION.md#5-work-state-and-restart)\\n(Progress) for a product outcome: material advance is progress there,\\naccepted material movement toward the selected product outcome, and only\\nmaterial advance projects product progress; prerequisite readiness is\\nits prerequisite work, which names the product obligation it enables and\\nhere also remains bounded; preservation is its preservation and repeated\\nproof, useful evidence, not progress; regression maps to evidence that\\nis not new progress, and this member adds one need to it: the promotion\\nblock in the last paragraph of this section. Churn and the revision of the forecast are\\nACTIVATION §5's, unchanged here.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/SPEC_METHOD.md#SPEC_METHOD%2F3.%20Outcome%20conservation\",\"start_line\":674}],\"label\":\"Outcome evidence classes\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:d1c14012a50c7c8714ad1601967bfdee","key":477,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:d1c14012a50c7c8714ad1601967bfdee\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[\"Within a product-outcome-bearing work wave.\"],\"definition\":\"Material growth has a live basis in the selected unresolved outcome, an admitted named bounded prerequisite, or an admitted named bounded experiment whose stated observation discriminates a stated decision for that outcome.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":719,\"path\":\"standards/SPEC_METHOD.md\",\"quote\":\"Within a product-outcome-bearing work wave, material realisation growth\\nderives its authority from the selected unresolved product outcome, an\\nadmitted named bounded prerequisite to it, or an admitted named bounded\\nexperiment whose stated observation discriminates a stated decision for it.\\nA prerequisite or experiment authorises only its declared provisional\\nbound; it does not select or enlarge the product outcome, authorise\\ndownstream work, confer promotion or closure, or waive applicable design,\\nsafety, authority or release law, including the prime law of a design\\nprofile where one applies.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/SPEC_METHOD.md#SPEC_METHOD%2F3.%20Outcome%20conservation\",\"start_line\":711}],\"label\":\"Bounded growth basis\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:26bbc9cba5e07244353a82f9765fde0a","key":478,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:26bbc9cba5e07244353a82f9765fde0a\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"Change management routes reports through intake triage, owning-layer change classification, separation of computed treatment from judgment and owner decisions, and affected-span consistency closure.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":761,\"path\":\"standards/SPEC_METHOD.md\",\"quote\":\"For an arriving report, start at [Universal intake triage](#universal-intake-triage).\\n[Change classes](#change-classes) locates the owning layer;\\n[Computed classification and treatment](#computed-classification-and-treatment)\\nseparates what rules decide from judgment and owner decisions;\\n[Consistency gate](#consistency-gate) decides closure over the affected span.\\nThe family table traces those rules and creates no second decision path.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/SPEC_METHOD.md#SPEC_METHOD%2F4.%20Change%20management\",\"start_line\":756}],\"label\":\"Change management\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:13bc06c340699b069791c359438dbd42","key":479,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:13bc06c340699b069791c359438dbd42\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"F11 is the foundation-to-law family accounting for change entry, computed classification and reuse, ambiguity governance and shared-interface migration. Its instance premises are changing specification, one front door, shared interfaces with multiple producers/consumers, and decisions either under declared policy or reserved to human authority. It reports P0 recovered; P1, P2, P3, P4a and P6 independent; P4b derived from P0/P2 with non-reacquirable step facts; and P5 derived from P0/P6 with an open-world premise.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":782,\"path\":\"standards/SPEC_METHOD.md\",\"quote\":\"This family (F11 in the index of\\n[FOUNDATIONS §3 Foundation to law](FOUNDATIONS.md#foundation-to-law))\\ndecides how a change enters the chain, how its classification is computed\\nand reused, how ambiguity is governed and how a shared interface is\\nmigrated. Its instance premises, which the commitments do not supply, are\\nnamed in the rows as follows: changing specification, the specification\\nchanges while work proceeds; one front door, reports of every kind arrive\\nat one product; shared interfaces, a shared interface has several\\nproducers and consumers; reserved decisions, a decision may be taken\\nunder declared policy or be reserved to a human authority. Standing of\\nthe commitments cited (FOUNDATIONS §3): P0 recovered; P1, P2, P3, P4a and\\nP6 independent; P4b derived from P0 and P2, with P0's premise that\\nstep-produced facts are not re-acquirable; P5 derived from P0 and P6,\\nwith P0's open-world premise.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/SPEC_METHOD.md#SPEC_METHOD%2F4.%20Change%20management%2FFoundation%20to%20law%3A%20change%20management%20and%20ambiguity\",\"start_line\":769}],\"label\":\"F11 foundation-to-law family\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:fc60a58521409c90ecb8c28db3403f83","key":480,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:fc60a58521409c90ecb8c28db3403f83\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"Universal intake triage is the single entry for substantive change, determining substance, affected product boundary/scope, lawful class, re-entry point, affected downstream surfaces/evidence, and release-scope fit or repricing.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":835,\"path\":\"standards/SPEC_METHOD.md\",\"quote\":\"Intake triage determines six things: whether the report represents a\\nsubstantive change at all; the affected product boundary and intended\\nscope; the lawful change class; the lawful re-entry point into the\\nconstitutional chain; the downstream surfaces and evidence that must be\\nrepriced, re-derived or re-proved, a determination whose evidence part is\\nthe selection `S_Δ` over the impact cover `I(Δ)` of the affected surfaces\\n([FOUNDATIONS §4 Change impact and evidence reuse](FOUNDATIONS.md#change-impact-and-evidence-reuse));\\nand whether the work remains within the\\ncurrently declared release scope or requires repricing of that release\\nplan.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/SPEC_METHOD.md#SPEC_METHOD%2F4.%20Change%20management%2FUniversal%20intake%20triage\",\"start_line\":826}],\"label\":\"Universal intake triage\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:1a5f8a4248ff79a871f4360d85c0c3f0","key":481,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:1a5f8a4248ff79a871f4360d85c0c3f0\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"The minimum lawful declared change classes are goal_reprice, intent_reprice, product_reprice, requirement_reprice, design_reframe and realization_refactor. Each identifies changed meaning, lawful re-entry and downstream flow; a declared class is not an evaluation result.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":881,\"path\":\"standards/SPEC_METHOD.md\",\"quote\":\"| `goal_reprice` | current bounded work-wave focus changes | Goals | Intent, Product, Requirements, Design, Code and Evidence where that focus changes deeper constitutional truth |\\n| `intent_reprice` | directional or scope change | Intent | Product, Requirements, Design, Code, Evidence |\\n| `product_reprice` | current product realisation changes while directional intent stays stable | Product | Requirements, Design, Code, Evidence |\\n| `requirement_reprice` | constitutional truth changes while project direction stays stable | Requirements | Design, Code, Evidence |\\n| `design_reframe` | realisation structure changes while active intent and requirement truth stay stable | Design | Code, Evidence |\\n| `realization_refactor` | local code, configuration or attribute change with no intended constitutional or structural change | the realised surface only | nothing upstream; it must prove no upstream drift |\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/SPEC_METHOD.md#SPEC_METHOD%2F4.%20Change%20management%2FChange%20classes\",\"start_line\":876}],\"label\":\"Change classes\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:e21989c4cfce457542b5b0140e63807c","key":482,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:e21989c4cfce457542b5b0140e63807c\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"Reusable intake classification distinguishes C, reproducible facts and declared-rule application; J, residual semantic/materiality judgment; and O, a ruling reserved to its actual owner. These annotations create no authority, calculus kind, runtime, classifier interface or mandatory document.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":913,\"path\":\"standards/SPEC_METHOD.md\",\"quote\":\"Intake supplies one reusable classification result rather than requiring\\neach role to reconstruct the same facts (P4b, P6, P1). Three annotations keep the kinds\\nof determination apart: C denotes reproducible facts and declared rule\\napplication; J denotes residual semantic or materiality judgment; O denotes\\na ruling reserved to its actual owner. The annotations grant no authority,\\nan instance of\\n[FOUNDATIONS §2 Authority kinds](FOUNDATIONS.md#authority-kinds), What\\ncreates no authority, and introduce no calculus kind, runtime, classifier interface or mandatory\\ndocument.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/SPEC_METHOD.md#SPEC_METHOD%2F4.%20Change%20management%2FComputed%20classification%20and%20treatment\",\"start_line\":905}],\"label\":\"Computed classification and C/J/O\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:ab6da5130acf85f9459ce4914e1db565","key":483,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:ab6da5130acf85f9459ce4914e1db565\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"The consistency gate applies the externally owned condition-based closure rule to obligations of a declared change span, requiring upstream sufficiency, downstream consistency and evidence of active intended behaviour.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1019,\"path\":\"standards/SPEC_METHOD.md\",\"quote\":\"No gate closes while the affected active surfaces are internally\\ninconsistent (P6, P4b). For the declared\\nchange span the framework proves that the upstream surface remains\\nsufficient for the downstream surface, that downstream artifacts do not\\ncontradict active upstream truth, and that tests and qualification prove\\nthe active intended behaviour rather than stale precedent. If that proof is\\nmissing the change remains open even if one local artifact already looks\\ncorrect.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/SPEC_METHOD.md#SPEC_METHOD%2F4.%20Change%20management%2FConsistency%20gate\",\"start_line\":1012}],\"label\":\"Consistency gate\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:34a40dd5a86c3b8c493c9326a6d886d9","key":484,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:34a40dd5a86c3b8c493c9326a6d886d9\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"A sprint is a bounded execution-control surface under existing constitutional authority, allowing batching, coordination, proof-cost pricing and close review without becoming a constitutional layer.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1048,\"path\":\"standards/SPEC_METHOD.md\",\"quote\":\"A sprint is a bounded execution-control surface, not a new layer in the\\nconstitutional chain (P6, P2). It may\\nbatch work, coordinate tickets or iteration entries, price proof cost and\\nforce close review under existing goals, intent, product definition,\\nrequirements and design authority; it does not create, supersede, weaken\\nor override that authority.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/SPEC_METHOD.md#SPEC_METHOD%2F4.%20Change%20management%2FSprint%20execution%20boundary\",\"start_line\":1043}],\"label\":\"Sprint execution boundary\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:5b910fcb1a1702f5d09d1acaec26b473","key":485,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:5b910fcb1a1702f5d09d1acaec26b473\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"Work-carrier selection follows required lifetime: durable ticket for cross-session identity; sprint-local entry for within-batch traceability only; run/return record for one activation.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1091,\"path\":\"standards/SPEC_METHOD.md\",\"quote\":\"The carrier of a work item is selected for its required lifetime: a\\ndurable ticket where the work needs identity across sessions; a\\nsprint-local entry where its only value is traceability inside a batch; a\\nrun or return record where the work lives and dies with one activation.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/SPEC_METHOD.md#SPEC_METHOD%2F4.%20Change%20management%2FCarriers\",\"start_line\":1088}],\"label\":\"Work-carrier selection\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:8454481b045e2d4a4564c3e00b3dca1d","key":486,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:8454481b045e2d4a4564c3e00b3dca1d\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"The method describes procedures for substantive intake, feature introduction/change, project bootstrap or requirement repricing, and use-case gaps. They preserve triage-first re-entry and downstream consistency.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1105,\"path\":\"standards/SPEC_METHOD.md\",\"quote\":\"When any substantive intake arrives (P2, P4b): enter\\n[Universal intake triage](#universal-intake-triage), keeping classification\\nunresolved until the evidence supports a lawful class; determine the lawful\\nre-entry point into the constitutional chain when that class is established; identify the affected downstream span that must\\nremain consistent; only then treat the work as implementation, repricing or\\nrelease-bound change.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/SPEC_METHOD.md#SPEC_METHOD%2F4.%20Change%20management%2FProcedures\",\"start_line\":1100}],\"label\":\"Method procedures\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:286649052d4f3d74e1c0094c628bac34","key":487,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:286649052d4f3d74e1c0094c628bac34\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"The substrate-neutral context urn:stdo:bounded-context:ambiguity-governance progressively narrows goals, direction/scope, product shape/terms, obligations, executable class, structure and local implementation. Major ambiguity materially affects architecture, stack, product boundary, execution/deployment admissibility, public contracts or downstream law; micro ambiguity is local choice within an already-governed design boundary.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1178,\"path\":\"standards/SPEC_METHOD.md\",\"quote\":\"This member owns the substrate-neutral ambiguity-governance bounded context\\n`urn:stdo:bounded-context:ambiguity-governance` under the selected complete\\nbasis; a profile's runtime shorthands for its own frames stay in that\\nprofile's context unless an explicit relation imports or translates them\\n(P3, P1).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/SPEC_METHOD.md#SPEC_METHOD%2F5.%20Ambiguity%20governance%20and%20lifecycle\",\"start_line\":1174},{\"end_line\":1193,\"path\":\"standards/SPEC_METHOD.md\",\"quote\":\"Major ambiguity materially changes\\narchitecture, stack, product boundary, execution or deployment\\nadmissibility, public contract shape or other downstream realisation law;\\nmicro ambiguity is a local implementation choice inside an already-governed\\ndesign boundary.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/SPEC_METHOD.md#SPEC_METHOD%2F5.%20Ambiguity%20governance%20and%20lifecycle\",\"start_line\":1189}],\"label\":\"Ambiguity governance\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:21feeb8c6dd7e2109f1517741510bd3b","key":488,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:21feeb8c6dd7e2109f1517741510bd3b\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[\"Declared policy permits bounded handling of declared ambiguity.\"],\"definition\":\"urn:stdo:concept:ambiguity-governance:lawful-probabilistic-processing names bounded non-human processing permitted to carry or resolve declared ambiguity. The source also places a person's policy-permitted decision without human-adjudication admission under this processing's policy and recording rules.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1211,\"path\":\"standards/SPEC_METHOD.md\",\"quote\":\"Lawful probabilistic processing\\n(`urn:stdo:concept:ambiguity-governance:lawful-probabilistic-processing`)\\nis bounded non-human processing permitted by declared policy to carry or\\nresolve declared ambiguity.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/SPEC_METHOD.md#SPEC_METHOD%2F5.%20Ambiguity%20governance%20and%20lifecycle\",\"start_line\":1208}],\"label\":\"Lawful probabilistic processing\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:7a473adb85314975c9d0699a47c00191","key":489,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:7a473adb85314975c9d0699a47c00191\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[\"Human judgment is explicitly admitted by authority where policy or risk appetite requires it.\"],\"definition\":\"urn:stdo:concept:ambiguity-governance:human-adjudication names admitted human judgment resolving declared ambiguity. Admission, not the performer's identity or participation elsewhere, makes the operation human adjudication.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1219,\"path\":\"standards/SPEC_METHOD.md\",\"quote\":\"Human adjudication\\n(`urn:stdo:concept:ambiguity-governance:human-adjudication`) is explicit\\nhuman judgment admitted by authority to resolve declared ambiguity where\\npolicy or risk appetite requires it. That admission makes an operation\\nhuman adjudication. A person who relays, records or carries out a step\\ndoes not adjudicate by doing so, and a person who carries or decides a\\ndeclared ambiguity where policy permits it, without that admission, acts\\nunder the policy and recording that govern lawful probabilistic\\nprocessing; who performs an operation does not decide its kind\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/SPEC_METHOD.md#SPEC_METHOD%2F5.%20Ambiguity%20governance%20and%20lifecycle\",\"start_line\":1211}],\"label\":\"Human adjudication\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:691f85265c6da81d5a46b1d99e177c71","key":490,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:691f85265c6da81d5a46b1d99e177c71\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"Lineage distinguishes substrate, development product, source project, release cut, product, install, artifact and product definition. A release cut v<version>-rc.<n> is immutable point-in-time release identity; mutable v<version> is a discovery selector for the highest-ordinal published cut.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1250,\"path\":\"standards/SPEC_METHOD.md\",\"quote\":\"The roles are distinct objects with distinct identities,\\nsubstrate, development product, source project, release cut, product,\\ninstall, artifact and product definition, defined once in FOUNDATIONS §2\\n(product lineage objects) with their governing rules and the compiler\\nanalogy; the product definition is the source project's present-tense\\nsurface, not the released artifact and not the builder that happens to be\\nrunning the build (P3).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/SPEC_METHOD.md#SPEC_METHOD%2F6.%20Lineage%20and%20release\",\"start_line\":1244},{\"end_line\":1259,\"path\":\"standards/SPEC_METHOD.md\",\"quote\":\"The only exact operative release identifier is the immutable release-cut\\ntag `v<version>-rc.<n>` (P3). That cut is a\\npoint-in-time release identity, a boundary over the feature set accepted\\nfor that cut, and part of release metadata and release-process evaluation;\\nit is not part of the live project specification. The mutable `v<version>`\\ntag is a version-line discovery selector to the highest-ordinal published\\nimmutable cut; it is not an exact dependency, evidence or constitutional\\nbasis and cannot silently change a consumer selection.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/SPEC_METHOD.md#SPEC_METHOD%2F6.%20Lineage%20and%20release\",\"start_line\":1252}],\"label\":\"Lineage and release identities\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:7a15f604d594ccb443f28aaff58f7767","key":491,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:7a15f604d594ccb443f28aaff58f7767\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[\"A reusable change to the shared method is proposed.\"],\"definition\":\"Shared-method adoption preserves authority causality from incident/review evidence through shared intake, one owning standard, consistency and independent review, human-authority acceptance, one complete released STDO version, explicit consumer selection, and consumer-owned realisation/evidence.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1294,\"path\":\"standards/SPEC_METHOD.md\",\"quote\":\"incident or review evidence\\n  -> shared-method intake\\n  -> one owning standard\\n  -> consistency and independent review\\n  -> human-authority acceptance\\n  -> one complete released STDO version\\n  -> explicit consumer selection\\n  -> consumer-owned realisation and evidence\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/SPEC_METHOD.md#SPEC_METHOD%2F6.%20Lineage%20and%20release%2FShared%20method%20adoption%20and%20propagation%20%28STDO-UP-012%29\",\"start_line\":1287}],\"label\":\"Shared method adoption and propagation\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:84561c6c35c47be892577620d26f84f9","key":492,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:84561c6c35c47be892577620d26f84f9\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"Migration is the document's section grouping for changes of constitutional or implementation basis.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1306,\"path\":\"standards/SPEC_METHOD.md\",\"quote\":\"## 7. Migration\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/SPEC_METHOD.md#SPEC_METHOD%2F7.%20Migration\",\"start_line\":1306}],\"label\":\"Migration section\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:65b6437bbefcb9936036eaeba32cf1f7","key":493,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:65b6437bbefcb9936036eaeba32cf1f7\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"A core interface is any shared contract/carrier materially governing runtime closure, reporting/status truth, topology/frame progression, proof/qualification, event/projection semantics, identity/binding resolution or provider/resolver behaviour. A change affecting how multiple surfaces decide current truth is a core-interface change.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1408,\"path\":\"standards/SPEC_METHOD.md\",\"quote\":\"A core interface is any shared contract or carrier that materially governs\\nruntime closure, reporting or status truth, topology or frame progression,\\nproof or qualification outcome, event or projection semantics, identity or\\nbinding resolution, or provider or resolver behaviour. If changing the\\ninterface can alter how multiple surfaces decide what is true now, it is a\\ncore interface change (P3).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/SPEC_METHOD.md#SPEC_METHOD%2F7.%20Migration%2FWhat%20counts%20as%20a%20core%20interface\",\"start_line\":1403}],\"label\":\"Core interface\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:ae116d98f8db6a1aeaa78cdaaeb00dfc","key":494,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:ae116d98f8db6a1aeaa78cdaaeb00dfc\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[\"A change alters a load-bearing shared contract, carrier, resolver, provider, projection law, closure law or other interface depended on by multiple surfaces.\"],\"definition\":\"Constitutional migration replaces shared authority across the affected interface family; it is not ordinary incremental local patching.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1314,\"path\":\"standards/SPEC_METHOD.md\",\"quote\":\"Core interface changes are not ordinary local patches. Where a change\\nalters a load-bearing contract, carrier, resolver, provider, projection\\nlaw, closure law or other shared interface that multiple surfaces depend\\non, the work is handled as a constitutional migration, not as incremental\\npatching (P3, P6).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/SPEC_METHOD.md#SPEC_METHOD%2F7.%20Migration%2FCore%20interface%20migration\",\"start_line\":1310}],\"label\":\"Constitutional migration\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:0ac47d0a931c315a32966d607562e1c0","key":495,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:0ac47d0a931c315a32966d607562e1c0\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"Two lawful strategies are inside-out hard-break migration on the same implementation line, replacing authoritative source truth from its carrier outward, and fundamental re-adoption for intentional major re-derivation on a materially different implementation basis. Bounded evolution is a rebuttable selection presumption, not a third strategy.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1342,\"path\":\"standards/SPEC_METHOD.md\",\"quote\":\"Core interface and major implementation replacement work has two lawful\\nconstitutional strategies (P3, P6).\\nInside-out hard-break migration applies when the project remains on the\\nsame implementation line and the authoritative source truth is being\\nreplaced in place; the work proceeds from the source carrier outward\\nthrough a sequence of deliberate breaks and repairs. Fundamental\\nre-adoption migration applies when the rewrite is major and the project is\\nintentionally re-deriving itself on a materially different implementation\\nbasis, such as a new runtime model, carrier model, type system, execution\\nsubstrate or realisation tree; the prior implementation is moved sideways\\nand treated as reference material, not live authority.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/SPEC_METHOD.md#SPEC_METHOD%2F7.%20Migration%2FConstitutional%20migration%20options\",\"start_line\":1332}],\"label\":\"Constitutional migration strategies\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:609c724f3e72ded60af13a3da3caf985","key":496,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:609c724f3e72ded60af13a3da3caf985\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"An affected outcome's acceptance path is its full causal closure: every admitted entrypoint, producer, consumer, resolver, fallback, shared state, event, projection and proof surface capable of changing, interpreting or closing it.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1383,\"path\":\"standards/SPEC_METHOD.md\",\"quote\":\"For this rule the affected acceptance path is the full causal closure of\\nthe outcome: every admitted entrypoint, producer, consumer, resolver,\\nfallback, shared state surface, event, projection and proof surface capable\\nof changing, interpreting or closing the outcome. Singular authority means\\none governing authority across that closure, not one selected successful\\ntrace. If the same request, fact, identity, state or projection is\\nadmissible to old and new authority, authority is competing and promotion\\nblocks (P3).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/SPEC_METHOD.md#SPEC_METHOD%2F7.%20Migration%2FConstitutional%20migration%20options\",\"start_line\":1376}],\"label\":\"Affected acceptance path\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:9cabea2f5cca79b57c9d7036eae01d55","key":497,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:9cabea2f5cca79b57c9d7036eae01d55\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"Projections, reports, status views and topology views are downstream reflections of an authoritative carrier, not independent closure surfaces.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1441,\"path\":\"standards/SPEC_METHOD.md\",\"quote\":\"Projections, reports, status views and topology views may reflect the\\nauthoritative carrier; they do not become a second closure surface (P6,\\nP1).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/SPEC_METHOD.md#SPEC_METHOD%2F7.%20Migration%2FProjection%20discipline\",\"start_line\":1439}],\"label\":\"Projection read model\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:4db287e299d86eb8953d36f89d7b0b07","key":498,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:4db287e299d86eb8953d36f89d7b0b07\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[\"The project intentionally abandons its prior constitutional shape and re-derives on a new branch, version line or methodology basis.\"],\"definition\":\"Fundamental migration is a constitutional reset through explicit adoption. Inherited constitutional material is classified adopted, superseded, deferred or orphaned; implementation is carry_across, redundant or rewrite.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1534,\"path\":\"standards/SPEC_METHOD.md\",\"quote\":\"A fundamental migration is a constitutional reset, not an in-place\\nrefactor. It applies when a project intentionally abandons a prior\\nconstitutional shape and re-derives itself on a new branch, version line or\\nmethodology basis (P3, P6). In that case:\\ninherited constitutional documents from the prior line become migration\\nsource material, not live authority in the new line; it is lawful to zero\\ninherited constitutional surfaces on the migration line and rebuild them\\nfrom first principles; nothing carries forward by default, and every\\nretained statement, requirement, design choice or guide rule must be\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/SPEC_METHOD.md#SPEC_METHOD%2F7.%20Migration%2FFundamental%20migration\",\"start_line\":1526}],\"label\":\"Fundamental migration\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:737fbdeb1271e076ee2a5b4f8cf1e047","key":499,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:737fbdeb1271e076ee2a5b4f8cf1e047\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"A transformation wave describes refactor/migration over mutable implementation surfaces, with bounded non-authoritative transitional plumbing during the wave and one current operative surface for its affected scope when it lands.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1609,\"path\":\"standards/SPEC_METHOD.md\",\"quote\":\"Refactor and migration should be understood as a transformation wave over\\nmutable\\nimplementation surfaces (P3, P6). While\\nthe wave is in flight: temporary mixed-state implementation may exist only\\nbelow the current break boundary and only as explicitly non-authoritative\\nplumbing; transitional adapters or scaffolds may exist only when they are\\nnamed, bounded and outside the acceptance path; refactor state may still\\ncarry traces of the prior operative model, never as competing or ambiguous\\ndual authority over the same request, fact, identity, state or projection.\\nExplicitly specified, deterministically routed, non-overlapping product or\\ncompatibility scopes are not competing authority under this rule; they may\\ncoexist while the enclosing migration remains visibly open.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/SPEC_METHOD.md#SPEC_METHOD%2F7.%20Migration%2FTransformation%20wave\",\"start_line\":1598}],\"label\":\"Transformation wave\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:730ea09d59cbd3d5c5d2f2393282f546","key":500,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:730ea09d59cbd3d5c5d2f2393282f546\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[\"Construction is delegated to a probabilistic or agentic worker.\"],\"definition\":\"The method applies ACTIVATION's bounded construction step: accepted basis, affected relation set, selected computations, delegated execution/decision authority, construction/self-review, independent assessment where required, owner disposition accept/local_repair/re_enter/reject, exact accepted checkpoint and next already-authorised action. Candidate availability, assessment and owner disposition are separate results.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1630,\"path\":\"standards/SPEC_METHOD.md\",\"quote\":\"Construction delegated to a probabilistic or agentic worker is governed as\\nthe step of ACTIVATION: the execution relation from accepted governing\\nbasis through bounded affected relation set, selected computational\\nrelations, delegated execution and decision authority, construction and\\nself-review, independent live-surface assessment where required, one of\\naccept, local repair, re-enter or reject, the exact accepted checkpoint,\\nand the next already-authorised bounded action (ACTIVATION §1, §3, §5 and\\n§7). The\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/SPEC_METHOD.md#SPEC_METHOD%2F8.%20Bounded%20execution%20in%20this%20method\",\"start_line\":1623}],\"label\":\"Bounded execution\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:e9e4bace23b4c2d17586434a8f7540df","key":501,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:e9e4bace23b4c2d17586434a8f7540df\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"Realisation evidence serves existing closure law with authority trace, realisation proof, negative proof where drift is plausible and a present-tense statement of residual open pressure.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1705,\"path\":\"standards/SPEC_METHOD.md\",\"quote\":\"For a realisation claim, the evidence that the closure condition of\\n[TICKETS §7 Condition-based closure and reuse](TICKETS.md#condition-based-closure-and-reuse)\\nrequires includes an authority trace, realisation proof, negative proof\\nwhere drift is plausible, and a present-tense statement of the residual\\nopen pressure; this section adds no second closure condition (P6, P4b,\\nP5).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/SPEC_METHOD.md#SPEC_METHOD%2F9.%20Evidence\",\"start_line\":1700}],\"label\":\"Realisation evidence\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:1b1081fd5b172df398ec35893fd08af7","key":502,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:1b1081fd5b172df398ec35893fd08af7\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"An ADR is durable design memory per decision boundary: the choice making acceptance criteria true. Its declared statuses are active, superseded and retired; it is an authoritative design file, while templates and optional registries project its rules.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1718,\"path\":\"standards/SPEC_METHOD.md\",\"quote\":\"Each ADR explicitly includes `Status:` (`active`, `superseded` or\\n`retired`); `Implements:` (the requirement identifiers the ADR makes true);\\n`Derives from:` (the intent identifier or strategy document that motivated\\nthe decision); `Supersedes:` (the prior ADR or doctrine it replaces);\\n`Superseded by:` (the successor ADR when its status is superseded); and\\n`Retained special case:` (when earlier behaviour is intentionally retained\\nas a special case of the current surface) (P6, P4b).\\nADRs are written per decision boundary, not per requirement file; the\\nboundary is the question \\\"what design choice makes these acceptance\\ncriteria true\\\".\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/SPEC_METHOD.md#SPEC_METHOD%2F10.%20Design%20records\",\"start_line\":1709}],\"label\":\"Architecture decision record\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:c273a437cbb3bf7285b6040216d5722e","key":503,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:c273a437cbb3bf7285b6040216d5722e\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"A build tenant is one independent, project-owned HOW realisation of a product's WHAT, located by the product definition's tenant registry.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1767,\"path\":\"standards/SPEC_METHOD.md\",\"quote\":\"- A build tenant is one independent, project-owned HOW realisation of a\\n  product's WHAT. The build-tenancy context of\\n  [PRODUCT_DEFINITION §8](PRODUCT_DEFINITION.md#8-what-how-and-work-carriers)\\n  names it, and the product definition's tenant registry locates each one.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/SPEC_METHOD.md#SPEC_METHOD%2F11.%20Build-tenant%20binding\",\"start_line\":1764}],\"label\":\"Build tenant\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:b24ab29ed2af1879ab09c354e892e5be","key":504,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:b24ab29ed2af1879ab09c354e892e5be\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"A product's requirements calculus comprises its WHAT obligations, permitted outcomes and rules for refining/composing realising work.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1770,\"path\":\"standards/SPEC_METHOD.md\",\"quote\":\"- The requirements calculus of a product is the set of obligations its\\n  WHAT states, the outcomes it permits, and its rules for refining and\\n  composing the work that realises it.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/SPEC_METHOD.md#SPEC_METHOD%2F11.%20Build-tenant%20binding\",\"start_line\":1768}],\"label\":\"Requirements calculus\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:99af08784eea240f27b803be49f856e2","key":505,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:99af08784eea240f27b803be49f856e2\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"A computational calculus declares executable operations, composition laws, permitted transformations, effects and resource behaviour insofar as material to obligations.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1774,\"path\":\"standards/SPEC_METHOD.md\",\"quote\":\"- A computational calculus is a declared set of executable operations,\\n  with the laws by which they compose, the transformations they permit,\\n  and their effects and resource behaviour, as far as these are material\\n  to the obligations.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/SPEC_METHOD.md#SPEC_METHOD%2F11.%20Build-tenant%20binding\",\"start_line\":1771}],\"label\":\"Computational calculus\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:088223e4b5ad7c379a6722a6b1aca800","key":506,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:088223e4b5ad7c379a6722a6b1aca800\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"An execution environment performs operations through a technology stack, a human process comprising people/roles/documents/channels/decision procedures, or both.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1778,\"path\":\"standards/SPEC_METHOD.md\",\"quote\":\"- An execution environment is the concrete means that performs those\\n  operations: a technology stack; a human process, made of people, roles,\\n  documents, communication channels and decision procedures; or a\\n  combination of the two.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/SPEC_METHOD.md#SPEC_METHOD%2F11.%20Build-tenant%20binding\",\"start_line\":1775}],\"label\":\"Execution environment\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:152d2a8a64bd069bdea1135af24a3c80","key":507,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:152d2a8a64bd069bdea1135af24a3c80\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"Build-tenant binding comprises calculus binding from requirements calculus to computational calculus and execution binding from computational calculus to execution environment. A registry entry locates a tenant but is not its binding.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1783,\"path\":\"standards/SPEC_METHOD.md\",\"quote\":\"- A tenant's build-tenant binding has two parts: its calculus binding,\\n  from the requirements calculus to its computational calculus, and its\\n  execution binding, from that computational calculus to its execution\\n  environment. A tenant's registry entry locates the tenant; it is not the\\n  binding.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/SPEC_METHOD.md#SPEC_METHOD%2F11.%20Build-tenant%20binding\",\"start_line\":1779}],\"label\":\"Build-tenant binding\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:89a8456fc34b22ab5de4993cf6bc5b8a","key":508,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:89a8456fc34b22ab5de4993cf6bc5b8a\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"TICKETS is the tier-2 owner of the work-carrier model, layout/bindings, sprint/ticket mechanics, triage/class recording/upward propagation, smallest lawful carrier and carrier-side execution-contract admission, execution/verification separation, judgment/ruling continuity, condition-based closure/reuse, test-case authority, migration-ticket rules, one-truth projection, recommended shapes and operating mode. It derives from FOUNDATIONS, ACTIVATION and EVALUATION rather than establishing foundational law.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":18,\"path\":\"standards/TICKETS.md\",\"quote\":\"Tier 2. Owns the work carriers of the method: goals, tickets, sprints,\\ncomments and execution contracts as one model; the default layout and the\\nbindings that locate the carriers; the sprint rules; the ticket rules,\\nincluding triage-first intake, the change class the ticket records and the\\nupward propagation check; the selection of the smallest lawful carrier for\\na piece of work and the carrier side of execution-contract admission; the\\nseparation of execution from verification authority; the continuity of\\nrecorded judgment and owner rulings; condition-based closure and reuse;\\ntest case authority; the implementation-migration ticket category with its\\ndeclaration, checklist and review rules; one-truth state projection; the\\nrecommended ticket and sprint shape; the operating mode. It is realised\\nfrom [FOUNDATIONS](FOUNDATIONS.md), [ACTIVATION](ACTIVATION.md) and\\n[EVALUATION](EVALUATION.md) and is the T area named by\\n[SPEC_METHOD §1](SPEC_METHOD.md#method-identity): nothing here is\\nfoundational, every clause names the principle that requires it (P0 to P6,\\nFOUNDATIONS §3), and each mechanism could be realised differently under the\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/TICKETS.md#TICKETS\",\"start_line\":3}],\"label\":\"TICKETS standard\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:ce23ea4563ef04c3464f33bbdbb73062","key":509,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:ce23ea4563ef04c3464f33bbdbb73062\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"Work carriers is the TICKETS section grouping its carrier roles.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":27,\"path\":\"standards/TICKETS.md\",\"quote\":\"## 1. Work carriers\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/TICKETS.md#TICKETS%2F1.%20Work%20carriers\",\"start_line\":27}],\"label\":\"TICKETS work-carrier section\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:b6a5459977c02c1a9ee67655ab021547","key":510,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:b6a5459977c02c1a9ee67655ab021547\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"In TICKETS, Goals is the current epic layer located by ticketing.goals, with GOALS.md as default. Broader than one ticket and narrower/more current than intent, it states the active wave and current priorities, not durable execution tracking.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":35,\"path\":\"standards/TICKETS.md\",\"quote\":\"The product definition's `ticketing.goals` binding locates the current epic\\nlayer; `GOALS.md` is the default file (PRODUCT_DEFINITION §1). Goals are\\nbroader than one ticket, narrower and more current than the intent surface,\\nand the place to state the active work wave and what matters now. Goals are\\nnot the durable unit of execution tracking (P2, P3).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/TICKETS.md#TICKETS%2F1.%20Work%20carriers%2FGoals\",\"start_line\":31}],\"label\":\"TICKETS goals carrier\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:b643fdd62b3be8f761bafff726c6c232","key":511,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:b643fdd62b3be8f761bafff726c6c232\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[\"Work needs independent durable identity, including feature work, bugs, spikes and chores.\"],\"definition\":\"A ticket is one enduring, typed source-of-truth work record durable across sessions; one Markdown file is the default carrier and bugs/features share one system.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":43,\"path\":\"standards/TICKETS.md\",\"quote\":\"Tickets are the enduring work records. Each ticket is one durable record,\\none markdown file being the default carrier; the source of truth for that\\nunit of work; durable across sessions; and typed, so that bugs and features\\nshare one system. A ticket is used when work needs independent durable\\nidentity: feature work, bug tracking, spikes and chores (P3, P4b).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/TICKETS.md#TICKETS%2F1.%20Work%20carriers%2FTicket%20records\",\"start_line\":39}],\"label\":\"Ticket record\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:d2a79ed2fdb131ad2ae0e382dc22ee38","key":512,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:d2a79ed2fdb131ad2ae0e382dc22ee38\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"In TICKETS, a sprint is one bounded-batch manifest under optional ticketing.sprints.root, default .ai-workspace/sprints/, batching authority references, closure law, evidence expectations and deferred local compliance debt and closing by explicit review.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":55,\"path\":\"standards/TICKETS.md\",\"quote\":\"Sprints are bounded execution batches. Each sprint is one manifest under\\nthe product definition's optional `ticketing.sprints.root` binding,\\n`.ai-workspace/sprints/` being the default; a control surface for a bounded\\nbody of work; a place to batch repeated authority references, closure law,\\nevidence expectations and deferred local compliance debt; and closed by an\\nexplicit sprint-close review. Sprints are not constitutional authority: they\\noperate under SPEC_METHOD and the project surfaces they cite\\n([SPEC_METHOD §4](SPEC_METHOD.md#sprint-execution-boundary) states the\\nsprint boundary; this member states the mechanics) (P2, P6).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/TICKETS.md#TICKETS%2F1.%20Work%20carriers%2FSprints\",\"start_line\":47}],\"label\":\"TICKETS sprint manifest\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:fd968916f08ade55608ac7b3f7f0511e","key":513,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:fd968916f08ade55608ac7b3f7f0511e\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"Comments are POSTING_GUIDE posts for ideas, strategy, reviews, handoffs, closure summaries and reasoned decisions, located by ticketing.comments.root with .ai-workspace/comments/ as default. They have neither task-status authority nor independent decision authority.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":74,\"path\":\"standards/TICKETS.md\",\"quote\":\"The product definition's `ticketing.comments.root` binding is the message\\nboard; `.ai-workspace/comments/` is the default. Comments are for publishing\\nideas, strategy notes, reviews, handoffs, closure summaries, and decisions\\nwith their reasoning. Comments are not task status authority. A comment\\nis a post of [POSTING_GUIDE](POSTING_GUIDE.md), which states what it\\ncarries, its structure and its discussion state. A decision recorded in a\\ncomment takes its authority from the surface that owns the decision, once\\nit is adopted there ([POSTING_GUIDE §9](POSTING_GUIDE.md#9-ratification)),\\nand has none of its own (P6, P3).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/TICKETS.md#TICKETS%2F1.%20Work%20carriers%2FComments\",\"start_line\":66}],\"label\":\"Comment carrier\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:d852d15950483fab7f616afd7b72e49a","key":514,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:d852d15950483fab7f616afd7b72e49a\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"A durable authoritative work record that survives sessions and work waves. Its carrier defaults to one Markdown file; its identity and authority are distinct from a run-scoped execution contract.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":85,\"path\":\"standards/TICKETS.md\",\"quote\":\"ticket survives sessions and work waves;\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/TICKETS.md#TICKETS%2F1.%20Work%20carriers%2FExecution%20contracts\",\"start_line\":82},{\"end_line\":330,\"path\":\"standards/TICKETS.md\",\"quote\":\"Each ticket has one durable authoritative record; the default carrier is\\none markdown file.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/TICKETS.md#TICKETS%2F4.%20Ticket%20rules%2FOne%20durable%20record%20per%20ticket\",\"start_line\":329}],\"label\":\"Ticket\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:04e341b6732269d66c8ea0de2a25c61d","key":515,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:04e341b6732269d66c8ea0de2a25c61d\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"The current admitted execution function for one run, derived from a ticket, a sprint manifest with an included ticket or iteration entry, or drafted during intake when no durable or sprint-local work identity is required. Drafting, admission, rejection and supersession remain distinct states.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":85,\"path\":\"standards/TICKETS.md\",\"quote\":\"An execution contract is the run-scoped\\nadmitted work surface\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/TICKETS.md#TICKETS%2F1.%20Work%20carriers%2FExecution%20contracts\",\"start_line\":78},{\"end_line\":683,\"path\":\"standards/TICKETS.md\",\"quote\":\"(drafted, admitted, rejected, superseded).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/TICKETS.md#TICKETS%2F5.%20From%20carrier%20to%20execution%2FExecution%20contract%20admission\",\"start_line\":683}],\"label\":\"Execution contract\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:c91d96dbd8d81139a3066db234ad87a7","key":516,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:c91d96dbd8d81139a3066db234ad87a7\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"A subordinate closure-bearing work claim with stable identity, bounded claim, relevant dependencies, current state, required evidence and an explicit relation to ticket closure. Several milestones may belong to one ticket.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":106,\"path\":\"standards/TICKETS.md\",\"quote\":\"Each milestone has stable identity, a bounded claim,\\nrelevant dependencies, current state, required evidence, and an explicit\\nrelation to ticket closure (P3).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/TICKETS.md#TICKETS%2F1.%20Work%20carriers%2FMilestones%20and%20phase-scoped%20truth%20%28UP-006%29\",\"start_line\":104}],\"label\":\"Milestone\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:5f7af811df86c66a0f026fe690dc0a23","key":517,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:5f7af811df86c66a0f026fe690dc0a23\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"Product-definition locations for work carriers: ticketing.goals locates the epic layer; optional ticketing.sprints.root locates bounded execution batches and sprint-close review; ticketing.tickets.lanes.backlog, .active and .completed locate ticket authority; ticketing.comments.root locates discussion and publication. The definition locates carriers without owning their ticket or comment content.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":157,\"path\":\"standards/TICKETS.md\",\"quote\":\"The definition locates these carriers and\\ndoes not own their ticket or comment content.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/TICKETS.md#TICKETS%2F2.%20Layout%20and%20authority%2FBindings%20and%20projections\",\"start_line\":156}],\"label\":\"Work-carrier binding\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:6df0210aa0cfac994dc829752b179bc7","key":518,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:6df0210aa0cfac994dc829752b179bc7\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"A generated board or other derived presentation of work authority. Comments, dashboards, registers, indexes and summaries are projections; visibility, repetition and recency do not confer authority.\",\"exceptions\":[\"A board becomes the ticket authority only through explicit product-definition rebinding with no rival remaining.\"],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":163,\"path\":\"standards/TICKETS.md\",\"quote\":\"that board is a projection only and does not become the source of truth\\nunless the product definition explicitly rebinds the ticket authority to\\nthat carrier and no rival remains (§7).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/TICKETS.md#TICKETS%2F2.%20Layout%20and%20authority%2FBindings%20and%20projections\",\"start_line\":161},{\"end_line\":1269,\"path\":\"standards/TICKETS.md\",\"quote\":\"Comments,\\ndashboards, registers, indexes and generated summaries are projections\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/TICKETS.md#TICKETS%2F7.%20Authority%2C%20judgment%2C%20closure%20and%20state%2FOne-truth%20state%20projection%20and%20drift%20refusal%20%28UP-009%29\",\"start_line\":1267}],\"label\":\"Work-state projection\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:7da6fbd5a21c446b21dde647032e07d7","key":519,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:7da6fbd5a21c446b21dde647032e07d7\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"The one durable record of a sprint, whose lifetime covers one bounded execution batch and its close review. A local Markdown file is the default carrier.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":84,\"path\":\"standards/TICKETS.md\",\"quote\":\"a sprint survives one bounded\\nexecution batch and its close review;\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/TICKETS.md#TICKETS%2F1.%20Work%20carriers%2FExecution%20contracts\",\"start_line\":82},{\"end_line\":185,\"path\":\"standards/TICKETS.md\",\"quote\":\"Each sprint has one durable manifest record; the default carrier is one\\nmarkdown file.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/TICKETS.md#TICKETS%2F3.%20Sprint%20rules%2FOne%20durable%20record%20per%20sprint\",\"start_line\":183}],\"label\":\"Sprint manifest\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:0584fc4e2fd93e2660fcdd839ddc7ea2","key":520,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:0584fc4e2fd93e2660fcdd839ddc7ea2\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"Declared sprint states minimally comprise active, closing, closed and superseded. Active admits iteration within the boundary; closing freezes new iteration during review and paydown classification; closed denotes finished review with all remaining debt accepted, ticketed, repriced or removed; superseded denotes replacement of an incorrect boundary by a new authority surface, sprint or ticket set.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":217,\"path\":\"standards/TICKETS.md\",\"quote\":\"The minimum sprint status model is `active`, `closing`, `closed` and\\n`superseded`\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/TICKETS.md#TICKETS%2F3.%20Sprint%20rules%2FSprint%20status\",\"start_line\":211}],\"label\":\"Sprint status\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:b58b9bef6638581a1adfc8e2f24b5cd4","key":521,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:b58b9bef6638581a1adfc8e2f24b5cd4\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"A result for one reviewed item, separate from the core assessment it consumes. For the predicate that the item is accepted as compliant under sprint authority: accepted maps to accept/satisfied; local_paydown maps to local_repair/falsified; design_reframe, requirement_reprice and product_reprice map to re_enter/invalid_basis; remove maps to falsified with no matching disposition. Debt outcomes map correspondingly: accepted to accept/satisfied, ticketed to local_repair/falsified, repriced to re_enter/invalid_basis, removed to falsified with no matching disposition.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":294,\"path\":\"standards/TICKETS.md\",\"quote\":\"Each classification\\ntakes exactly one core value, for the predicate \\\"the reviewed item is\\naccepted as compliant under the sprint authority\\\"\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/TICKETS.md#TICKETS%2F3.%20Sprint%20rules%2FClose%20review\",\"start_line\":291},{\"end_line\":316,\"path\":\"standards/TICKETS.md\",\"quote\":\"accepted matches `accept` (`satisfied`), ticketed\\nmatches `local_repair` (`falsified`), removed takes `falsified` with no\\nmatching disposition, and repriced matches `re_enter`\\n(`invalid_basis`)\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/TICKETS.md#TICKETS%2F3.%20Sprint%20rules%2FClose%20review\",\"start_line\":313}],\"label\":\"Sprint-close classification and debt outcome\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:a41b7a918702f428860acb628ab48df5","key":522,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:a41b7a918702f428860acb628ab48df5\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"The kind of work record. The minimum common types are feature, bug, spike and chore; the source expects this default set to suffice for most cases.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":412,\"path\":\"standards/TICKETS.md\",\"quote\":\"The minimum common set of ticket types is `feature`, `bug`, `spike` and\\n`chore`.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/TICKETS.md#TICKETS%2F4.%20Ticket%20rules%2FTypes\",\"start_line\":410}],\"label\":\"Ticket type\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:4f444a4cc883ac93d02be4653b6ab221","key":523,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:4f444a4cc883ac93d02be4653b6ab221\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"The execution or migration discipline governing a ticket, orthogonal to its type and change class. The minimum categories are ordinary and implementation_migration; feature, bug, spike and chore may each carry either.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":421,\"path\":\"standards/TICKETS.md\",\"quote\":\"category answers what execution or migration\\ndiscipline governs the ticket\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/TICKETS.md#TICKETS%2F4.%20Ticket%20rules%2FCategory\",\"start_line\":418}],\"label\":\"Ticket category\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:a9a45cc30fc2d890d88c8a17834de609","key":524,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:a9a45cc30fc2d890d88c8a17834de609\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"The intake-triage declaration of lawful constitutional re-entry, distinct from ticket type and execution discipline. Named classes include goal_reprice, intent_reprice, product_reprice, requirement_reprice, design_reframe and realization_refactor. Common pairings are illustrative: feature with the first five, bug with requirement_reprice/design_reframe/realization_refactor, chore with design_reframe/realization_refactor; a spike still carries its current triage class.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":452,\"path\":\"standards/TICKETS.md\",\"quote\":\"change class answers where the change lawfully\\nre-enters the constitutional chain.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/TICKETS.md#TICKETS%2F4.%20Ticket%20rules%2FChange%20class\",\"start_line\":449}],\"label\":\"Change class\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:5f68ddf5dc5c4ea4e2e1746d8627d2d6","key":525,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:5f68ddf5dc5c4ea4e2e1746d8627d2d6\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"Intake classification consuming the computed result for the declared owner/layer traversal, complete relevant public membership and value delta, accepted-design scope and trace coverage, and rule-determined treatment. The owning carrier references that exact result and its residuals.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":476,\"path\":\"standards/TICKETS.md\",\"quote\":\"The owning work carrier references that\\nexact result and its residuals; a new role does not repeat an unchanged\\nwalk\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/TICKETS.md#TICKETS%2F4.%20Ticket%20rules%2FUpward%20propagation%20check\",\"start_line\":474}],\"label\":\"Intake triage and upward propagation\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:1906988707368f41598a83175d808b93","key":526,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:1906988707368f41598a83175d808b93\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"Declared ticket states minimally comprise backlog, active and completed. Their corresponding lanes mean accepted durable work outside current execution focus, the current bounded execution set, and closed work retained as history. State labels are not evaluation results.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":521,\"path\":\"standards/TICKETS.md\",\"quote\":\"The minimum ticket status model is `backlog`, `active` and `completed`.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/TICKETS.md#TICKETS%2F4.%20Ticket%20rules%2FStatus\",\"start_line\":519},{\"end_line\":546,\"path\":\"standards/TICKETS.md\",\"quote\":\"`backlog`\\nis accepted durable work that should remain visible but is not part of the\\ncurrent execution focus; `active` is the current bounded execution set;\\n`completed` is closed work retained as history.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/TICKETS.md#TICKETS%2F4.%20Ticket%20rules%2FLanes\",\"start_line\":543}],\"label\":\"Ticket status and lane\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:2269e5c21dad5030dba9012113f88134","key":527,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation