 not adoption.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/TRAVERSAL_OCCURRENCE.md#TRAVERSAL_OCCURRENCE%2FPosition\",\"start_line\":47}],\"label\":\"Traversal occurrence profile\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:b791117709f1f0565ea01a996a54f5e1","key":545,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:b791117709f1f0565ea01a996a54f5e1\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[\"The Product adopts the profile and its instance premises.\"],\"definition\":\"Material family F19 imports F3 results/combination and F9 a_c under PROFILES §1. Adopted premises are I1 externally changing subject reality with stable binding, I2 one exact a_c basis, and I3 separately identified effects under owner-issued grants; these premises do not follow from foundations. Reported commitment standing is P0 recovered; P1/P3/P6 independent; P4b derived from P0/P2; P5 derived from P0/P6. The table separates consequences, profile policy choices and adopting-Product choices, with an internal consumer index.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":72,\"path\":\"standards/TRAVERSAL_OCCURRENCE.md\",\"quote\":\"Its instance premises hold where a Product adopts the profile; they are\\nadopted with it and do not follow from the foundations\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/TRAVERSAL_OCCURRENCE.md#TRAVERSAL_OCCURRENCE%2FPosition%2FFoundation%20to%20law\",\"start_line\":61}],\"label\":\"F19 premises, consequences and owners\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:7c694b903339568539f5073b033755b9","key":546,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:7c694b903339568539f5073b033755b9\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"The profile represents an immutable occurrence per exact traversal application; stable external subject binding; bounded pre/post observations; intended typed outcomes; separately authorized operations/evidence; immutable admitted framework-event facts; candidate claims, judgments and materialized typed relations; explicit frontiers and frontier-bound projections; distinct identity dependency, causal subgraphs and wider typed lineage.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":122,\"path\":\"standards/TRAVERSAL_OCCURRENCE.md\",\"quote\":\"- distinct identity dependency, causal subgraphs and wider typed lineage.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/TRAVERSAL_OCCURRENCE.md#TR