asis\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:5364ed6b537f501c3e9da24b34e62cd8","key":597,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:5364ed6b537f501c3e9da24b34e62cd8\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"Optional Tier 3 UX profile, material family F20, refining DESIGN_MODULE for UX modules. Its own terms include UX surface, State, Msg, Update, View, ViewTree, Cmd, Sub, view-local ephemera, effect membrane, product-truth-changing message, admitted product carrier, Msg-replay test/proof, scaffold, exemption record, UX sprint and its refined result values. It imports FOUNDATIONS, ACTIVATION, EVALUATION, SPEC_METHOD and TICKETS under PROFILES without redefining their objects. Graph function and ABG remain graph-execution terms; AssetSurface and workorder remain Product-design carriers.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":44,\"path\":\"standards/UX.md\",\"quote\":\"Tier 3. An optional profile for realising UX surfaces:\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/UX.md#UX\",\"start_line\":3},{\"end_line\":107,\"path\":\"standards/UX.md\",\"quote\":\"This member is material family F20, UX.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/UX.md#UX%2F1.%20Position%2FFoundation%20to%20law\",\"start_line\":89}],\"label\":\"UX profile\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:7a9d378573708e829488aa2ffbb49efa","key":598,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:7a9d378573708e829488aa2ffbb49efa\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"UX surfaces project and control admitted Product truth by rendering it and emitting typed messages. They supplement module realization discipline with render purity, state-transition algebra, effect-membrane discipline and accessibility minimums. In graph-execution Products they are projection and query surfaces.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":218,\"path\":\"standards/UX.md\",\"quote\":\"UX surfaces are projection and control surfaces: they render admitted\\ntruth and emit typed messages (P6, P0).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/UX.md#UX%2F3.%20Product%20truth%20and%20admitted%20carriers\",\"start_line\":214}],\"label\":\"UX surface\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:c9843b48485016f674dd3003449d040f","key":599,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:c9843b48485016f674dd3003449d040f\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"Elm Architecture is the UX constitutional process model: typed runtime-owned State; typed Msg algebra naming every user/system action; pure Update:(Msg,State)→(State,Cmd); pure View:State→ViewTree, producing the same output for the same State; typed Cmd descriptions of scheduled effects and Sub descriptions of external subscriptions interpreted at the runtime's effect membrane. Runtime loop: current State→render View→user Msg→Update produces State and Cmds→runtime interprets Cmds→repeat.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":261,\"path\":\"standards/UX.md\",\"quote\":\"- Update: the pure reducer of signature `(Msg, State) → (State, Cmd)`; it\\n  describes side effects as Cmd values and does not perform them;\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/UX.md#UX%2F4.%20Process%20model\",\"start_line\":243}],\"label\":\"Elm Architecture and typed UX process coordinates\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:593429f1fa25b744fdcf828e4235cd1c","key":600,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:593429f1fa25b744fdcf828e4235cd1c\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"Admitted Product carrier for a truth-changing UX message: an AssetSurface action; published graph function or lawful composition; Product-design-admitted workorder, job or runtime command; ABG event/command boundary where ABG is runtime authority; or another typed Product contract named by the design module. AssetSurface or its named equivalent supplies shared typed projections and action contracts.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":234,\"path\":\"standards/UX.md\",\"quote\":\"Such a message maps to one admitted product carrier (P6, P4a):\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/UX.md#UX%2F3.%20Product%20truth%20and%20admitted%20carriers\",\"start_line\":228}],\"label\":\"Admitted UX Product carrier\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:b3ee6d135ca780f28776d4755a5fbf1b","key":601,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:b3ee6d135ca780f28776d4755a5fbf1b\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"Declared effect boundary interpreting reducer-produced Cmd values and returning outcomes as typed Msg values. It is the permitted location for I/O, external subscriptions and imperative host-platform interop, rather than a controller or owner of business decisions.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":384,\"path\":\"standards/UX.md\",\"quote\":\"The membrane has one job: interpret declared Cmd values.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/UX.md#UX%2F6.%20Effect%20membrane\",\"start_line\":372}],\"label\":\"UX effect membrane\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:38bc94913c88b810c504dd4ecae182ca","key":602,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:38bc94913c88b810c504dd4ecae182ca\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"Msg-replay test asks whether the view's behavior can be reproduced by replaying its Msg log against empty State. Executable Msg-replay proof is recorded work-state resumption evidence that the view owns no hidden continuation. It includes initial State fixture, ordered Msg log, expected final State, expected ordered Cmds, typed Cmd outcome Msgs including every materially possible unresolved outcome and recovery messages, and injected deterministic time, randomness, generated ids and external payloads.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":456,\"path\":\"standards/UX.md\",\"quote\":\"The discipline test is the Msg-replay test: can the view's\\nbehaviour be replayed by replaying its Msg log against an empty State?\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/UX.md#UX%2F8.%20Continuation%20and%20replay\",\"start_line\":454},{\"end_line\":478,\"path\":\"standards/UX.md\",\"quote\":\"- an initial State fixture;\\n- an ordered Msg log;\\n- the expected final State;\\n- the expected ordered Cmd values;\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/UX.md#UX%2F8.%20Continuation%20and%20replay%2FMsg-replay%20proof\",\"start_line\":471}],\"label\":\"Msg-replay test and proof\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:2baee2e53c0d830eab71c96035503953","key":603,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:2baee2e53c0d830eab71c96035503953\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"Shared front-end/back-end typed contract is the source of UX-consumed types and Product record shapes. A project-local typed-schema mechanism produces both compile-time types and runtime validators from the same definition.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":544,\"path\":\"standards/UX.md\",\"quote\":\"The project uses a typed-schema mechanism so that the same type\\ndefinition is the source of both compile-time types and runtime\\nvalidators; the mechanism choice is project-local.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/UX.md#UX%2F10.%20Type%20sharing\",\"start_line\":539}],\"label\":\"Shared UX type contract\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:a5c323426e83c24d36ee5025b541da67","key":604,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:a5c323426e83c24d36ee5025b541da67\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"Referenced upstream roles: SPEC_METHOD owns constitutional process, authority flow, lawful re-entry, repricing and migration; ODD/graph-execution owns graph-native constructive carrier law; DESIGN_MODULE owns deterministic module realization discipline, including immutability, totality, effect edges, no semantic centre and coupling; TICKETS owns ticket/sprint lifecycle and generic escrow; WORLD_MODEL owns world-model semantic law for Products with that dimension. These are referenced document roles, not imported full definitions.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":174,\"path\":\"standards/UX.md\",\"quote\":\"SPEC_METHOD defines constitutional process and lawful re-entry; the\\ngraph-execution profile defines graph-native constructive carrier law;\\nDESIGN_MODULE defines deterministic module-level realisation discipline\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/UX.md#UX%2F2.%20Role%20and%20composition\",\"start_line\":163},{\"end_line\":202,\"path\":\"standards/UX.md\",\"quote\":\"TICKETS governs ticket and sprint lifecycle;\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/UX.md#UX%2F2.%20Role%20and%20composition%2FRelationship%20to%20other%20members\",\"start_line\":192}],\"label\":\"UX upstream document roles\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:ac03acbc25d43f1c4cec70fe0b4cab0a","key":605,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:ac03acbc25d43f1c4cec70fe0b4cab0a\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"The UX profile governs UX surfaces within its adopted or default scope. Product authority adopts it per project, with adoption and any restricted surface scope recorded in design modules.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":571,\"path\":\"standards/UX.md\",\"quote\":\"Product authority adopts this profile for a project (§1 Authority), and\\nthe adoption is recorded by (P6, P4b):\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/UX.md#UX%2F12.%20Adoption\",\"start_line\":570}],\"label\":\"UX profile\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:254e32e899936a647b4a4ae7b911dd86","key":606,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:254e32e899936a647b4a4ae7b911dd86\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"A UX interaction surface, including public product capabilities and potentially internal debug, scaffold, prototype or temporary proof surfaces; applicability and exemptions depend on declared scope and the profile's default triggers.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":549,\"path\":\"standards/UX.md\",\"quote\":\"A UX surface that is the public face of a product capability declares\\n(P2, P6):\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/UX.md#UX%2F11.%20Accessibility%20minimum\",\"start_line\":548}],\"label\":\"UX surface\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:f07b5194dc5c79f56d598c615a03f3b1","key":607,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:f07b5194dc5c79f56d598c615a03f3b1\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"The design document carrying UX adoption, architecture, surface shapes, contracts, proof references, accessibility refinements and exemptions. Answerability from this document is a basis condition for surface review.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":579,\"path\":\"standards/UX.md\",\"quote\":\"4. declaring the State, Msg, Update, Cmd and Sub shapes for each UX\\n   surface in the design module before implementation;\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/UX.md#UX%2F12.%20Adoption\",\"start_line\":578}],\"label\":\"UX design module\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:fba38b75e6777b991248c792e3cacb39","key":608,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:fba38b75e6777b991248c792e3cacb39\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"A short UX iteration window permitting specified local compliance proof to be deferred when per-change proof cost exceeds expected correction cost, followed by forensic close review.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":629,\"path\":\"standards/UX.md\",\"quote\":\"A UX sprint may defer local UX\\ncompliance proof during a short iteration window when per-change proof\\ncost is higher than expected correction cost. This is a cost-optimisation\\nrule; it does not weaken the UX process model (P2).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/UX.md#UX%2F12.%20Adoption%2FUX%20sprint%20compliance%20escrow\",\"start_line\":626}],\"label\":\"UX sprint compliance escrow\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:0248d4f244332b39c63670566a866da5","key":609,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:0248d4f244332b39c63670566a866da5\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"Four predicate-specific result refinements: surface review, replay proof, closure obligations and carrier admission. Their values map individually to core results and combine with other members' results only in the core.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":770,\"path\":\"standards/UX.md\",\"quote\":\"Purpose and material relation: this profile's verdicts decide closure of a UX surface\\nand enter conjunctions with the results of other members, which combine\\nonly in the core, so a review, a proof, a closure claim and a carrier\\ncheck are each read for their own predicate and none is read as another\\n(P5, P6).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/UX.md#UX%2F15.%20Results%20of%20this%20profile\",\"start_line\":766}],\"label\":\"UX result refinements\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:3cd931c3ed7a9f280b50fe22580e8256","key":610,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:3cd931c3ed7a9f280b50fe22580e8256\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"Optional Tier 3 profile, material family F21, for constructing and publishing bounded world-model artifacts over sovereign source systems. Its declared scope includes position, constitutional intents, manifesto, imports and Builder Project specialisation, world-model objectives and evidence hierarchy, candidate Markov theory, units, fourteen-stage flow, representation/materialisation/publication/ledger laws, entity and overlay construction, saturation/composition/projection, planes, proof, development, outputs, companions and result refinements. It imports other members without redefining their objects.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":5,\"path\":\"standards/WORLD_MODEL.md\",\"quote\":\"Tier 3. An optional profile for world-model construction: building a\\ngoverned semantic layer over sovereign source systems and publishing\\nbounded world-model artifacts.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/WORLD_MODEL.md#WORLD_MODEL\",\"start_line\":3}],\"label\":\"WORLD_MODEL profile\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:e39b94f9c23281964c94da96edfba0a6","key":611,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:e39b94f9c23281964c94da96edfba0a6\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"Governed semantic layer over existing source systems, descriptive before generative. Its primary published semantic unit is the entity cut; generic world-model-object references denote that unit unless explicitly identifying looser candidates or intermediates.\",\"exceptions\":[\"Explicit references to a looser candidate or intermediate surface do not denote a published entity cut.\"],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":306,\"path\":\"standards/WORLD_MODEL.md\",\"quote\":\"A world model is a governed semantic layer built over existing source\\nsystems. It is descriptive before it is generative (P3, P6). Its primary semantic unit is the published\\nentity cut (§6 Units). Generic references to a \\\"world-model object\\\" are\\nshorthand for this unit unless the text explicitly names a looser\\ncandidate or intermediate surface.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/WORLD_MODEL.md#WORLD_MODEL%2F3.%20What%20a%20world%20model%20is\",\"start_line\":302}],\"label\":\"World model\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:87e03ae16d8303ea92b9eeaa8b53070b","key":612,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:87e03ae16d8303ea92b9eeaa8b53070b\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"Authoritative operational systems enacting bounded domain function through code paths, events, records, APIs, schedules, configuration, documents and downstream obligations. They retain sovereignty for operational truth.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":69,\"path\":\"standards/WORLD_MODEL.md\",\"quote\":\"World-model work builds a governed semantic\\nlayer over authoritative source systems, which enact bounded domain\\nfunction through code paths, events, records, APIs, schedules,\\nconfigurations, documents and downstream obligations (P1, P6). The profile starts from these claims:\\n\\n- source systems enact domain function and remain sovereign for\\n  operational truth;\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/WORLD_MODEL.md#WORLD_MODEL%2F1.%20Position\",\"start_line\":63}],\"label\":\"Source systems\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:5b76634cadf8409273f4834fa26ac392","key":613,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:5b76634cadf8409273f4834fa26ac392\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"A bounded functional and authoritative surface characterised by what enters, changes, is owned, is guaranteed, leaves and can be relied on by adjacent domains.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":516,\"path\":\"standards/WORLD_MODEL.md\",\"quote\":\"Domains are functional surfaces. A domain is defined by coherent\\nfunction: what enters, what changes, what is owned, what is guaranteed,\\nwhat leaves, and what adjacent domains can rely on (P3).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/WORLD_MODEL.md#WORLD_MODEL%2F5.%20Core%20claims\",\"start_line\":514}],\"label\":\"Domain\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:9732f555ffd02a5cb722940a58180d9b","key":614,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:9732f555ffd02a5cb722940a58180d9b\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"The profile-owned bounded context urn:stdo:bounded-context:world-model under the selected complete method basis; narrower Product-owned contexts do not alter it by proximity.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":222,\"path\":\"standards/WORLD_MODEL.md\",\"quote\":\"It owns\\nthe world-model bounded context `urn:stdo:bounded-context:world-model`\\nunder the selected complete method basis. A consuming Product may declare\\nnarrower Product-owned contexts without changing this profile's context by\\nproximity (P1, P6).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/WORLD_MODEL.md#WORLD_MODEL%2F2.%20Role%20and%20imports\",\"start_line\":218}],\"label\":\"World-model bounded context\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:71122f9461dadc023581a2b25fd7b04d","key":615,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:71122f9461dadc023581a2b25fd7b04d\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"Source Project, urn:stdo:concept:recursive-product-taxonomy:source-project, owned by FOUNDATIONS §2 in urn:stdo:bounded-context:recursive-product-taxonomy: a mutable workspace building the next release cut. PRODUCT.md is its product-definition surface, not a released Product.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":259,\"path\":\"standards/WORLD_MODEL.md\",\"quote\":\"- Source Project retains the\\n  mutable-workspace-building-the-next-release-cut meaning;\\n- Artifact retains the published-output meaning; and\\n- `PRODUCT.md` remains the product-definition surface of a mutable Source\\n  Project, not the released Product artifact itself.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/WORLD_MODEL.md#WORLD_MODEL%2F2.%20Role%20and%20imports\",\"start_line\":255}],\"label\":\"Source Project\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:60576aa2140b8aef363512775cb7cbce","key":616,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:60576aa2140b8aef363512775cb7cbce\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"Three distinct FOUNDATIONS-owned imported identities in the recursive-product-taxonomy context: urn:stdo:concept:recursive-product-taxonomy:product is the released immutable thing, potentially a builder or runtime; urn:stdo:concept:recursive-product-taxonomy:install is its stamped workspace instance; urn:stdo:concept:recursive-product-taxonomy:artifact is a published output. This grouped inventory does not identify the three concepts with one another.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":240,\"path\":\"standards/WORLD_MODEL.md\",\"quote\":\"- `urn:stdo:concept:recursive-product-taxonomy:product`;\\n- `urn:stdo:concept:recursive-product-taxonomy:install`; and\\n- `urn:stdo:concept:recursive-product-taxonomy:artifact`.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/WORLD_MODEL.md#WORLD_MODEL%2F2.%20Role%20and%20imports\",\"start_line\":238},{\"end_line\":257,\"path\":\"standards/WORLD_MODEL.md\",\"quote\":\"- Product retains the released immutable-thing meaning; a builder or\\n  runtime may be one such Product;\\n- Install retains the stamped-workspace-instance meaning;\\n- Source Project retains the\\n  mutable-workspace-building-the-next-release-cut meaning;\\n- Artifact retains the published-output meaning; and\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/WORLD_MODEL.md#WORLD_MODEL%2F2.%20Role%20and%20imports\",\"start_line\":252}],\"label\":\"Imported Product, Install and Artifact identities\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:43f89028fb972707e26975d939e746bb","key":617,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:43f89028fb972707e26975d939e746bb\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"World-model-owned concept urn:stdo:concept:world-model:builder-project: a mutable workspace configured for a world-model builder application, owning source inputs, settings and publication lane. It specialises Source Project and may use an installed builder Product as substrate.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":282,\"path\":\"standards/WORLD_MODEL.md\",\"quote\":\"- target concept: `urn:stdo:concept:world-model:builder-project`, term\\n  Builder Project, in `urn:stdo:bounded-context:world-model`, owned by\\n  this member's §6 Units, Builder Project;\\n- direction: source to target only; no inverse, equivalence, or\\n  assertion that every Source Project is a Builder Project;\\n- preserved meaning: a mutable workspace builds a next release cut and\\n  remains distinct from a Release Cut, Product, Install and Artifact;\\n- changed and narrowed meaning: the workspace is configured for a\\n  world-model builder application and owns its source inputs, settings\\n  and publication lane; it may use an installed builder Product as\\n  substrate;\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/WORLD_MODEL.md#WORLD_MODEL%2F2.%20Role%20and%20imports%2FBuilder%20Project%20specialisation\",\"start_line\":272}],\"label\":\"Builder Project\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:8b5b1ad1ac3b2d75baf19fd2e7853cdb","key":618,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:8b5b1ad1ac3b2d75baf19fd2e7853cdb\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"An App is a world-model builder application. A Published Domain Artifact is its builder project's immutable published world-model output; a Fragment is a bounded published slice within such an artifact. These are distinct application, output and containment roles.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":572,\"path\":\"standards/WORLD_MODEL.md\",\"quote\":\"| App | a world-model builder application | P3 |\\n| Builder Project | concept identity `urn:stdo:concept:world-model:builder-project`; a configured project instance of the builder with its own source inputs, settings and publication lane; its relation to Source Project is the directional specialisation of §2 Builder Project specialisation, and this clause is not read as an unchanged import or general equivalence | P3, P1 |\\n| Published Domain Artifact | a published immutable world-model output built by a builder project | P3, P4b |\\n| Fragment | a bounded published slice inside a published domain artifact | P3 |\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/WORLD_MODEL.md#WORLD_MODEL%2F6.%20Units\",\"start_line\":569}],\"label\":\"App, Published Domain Artifact and Fragment\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:0bbd894b080148e4f1a5c1c827e9d6f2","key":619,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:0bbd894b080148e4f1a5c1c827e9d6f2\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"Generic shorthand for something treated as real in an institutional operating model, intentionally weaker than Markov Object and useful during observation, extraction, review and discussion; not the preferred name after a governed identity-bearing cut is constructed.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":573,\"path\":\"standards/WORLD_MODEL.md\",\"quote\":\"| World Model Object | a generic shorthand for something treated as real in the institutional operating model; intentionally weaker than Markov Object; useful during observation, extraction, review and discussion; not the preferred name for the primary published semantic unit once the builder has constructed a governed identity-bearing cut | P3, P1 |\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/WORLD_MODEL.md#WORLD_MODEL%2F6.%20Units\",\"start_line\":573}],\"label\":\"World Model Object\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:3faa4fb493acae06174655ecb783af0f","key":620,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:3faa4fb493acae06174655ecb783af0f\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"Governed basis qualifying a traced source observation as an accepted semantic claim, explaining why it is lawful world-model truth rather than a raw observation.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":574,\"path\":\"standards/WORLD_MODEL.md\",\"quote\":\"| Assurance | the governed basis on which a traced source observation is accepted as a qualified semantic claim; it answers why a claim is lawful world-model truth rather than merely a raw observation | P6 |\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/WORLD_MODEL.md#WORLD_MODEL%2F6.%20Units\",\"start_line\":574}],\"label\":\"Assurance\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:861bbbd5b7d29d5df06de8f92d683ed1","key":621,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:861bbbd5b7d29d5df06de8f92d683ed1\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"Append-only ordered record of qualified attribute claims over stable object identity, potentially recording observed or derived values, interpreted meanings, rules, constraints, topology, relations, provenance, authority and effective/observed/publication coordinates.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":575,\"path\":\"standards/WORLD_MODEL.md\",\"quote\":\"| Attribute Ledger | an append-only ordered record of qualified attribute claims over a stable object identity; entries may carry observed values, derived values, interpreted meanings, rule or constraint claims, topology or relation claims, provenance and authority claims, and effective, observed and publication coordinates | P4b, P3 |\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/WORLD_MODEL.md#WORLD_MODEL%2F6.%20Units\",\"start_line\":575}],\"label\":\"Attribute Ledger\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:ea7976cc8986c83e51397ea3c9641497","key":622,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:ea7976cc8986c83e51397ea3c9641497\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"Primary published semantic unit: an identity-bearing, bounded, evidence-backed cut of a recovered entity projected from an attribute ledger. Its eight surfaces are identity, boundary, authority, state, evidence, treatment, covariance and ambiguity, traced to ledger entries and assurance. It can be lawful without an identity direction.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":610,\"path\":\"standards/WORLD_MODEL.md\",\"quote\":\"Entity Cut. The primary published semantic unit: an identity-bearing,\\nbounded, evidence-backed cut of a recovered entity, projected from the\\nattribute ledger (P3, P6). An entity cut is lawful\\nwithout an identity direction. It publishes identity, boundary,\\nauthority, state, evidence, treatment, covariance and ambiguity, each\\ntraced to ledger entries and their assurance basis.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/WORLD_MODEL.md#WORLD_MODEL%2F6.%20Units\",\"start_line\":605}],\"label\":\"Entity Cut\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:f0813b08ad22c7e3d02e681158434ded","key":623,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:f0813b08ad22c7e3d02e681158434ded\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"Load-bearing candidate construct: a stable self-bounding pattern in a constraint structure, with internal state reasoned about through an effective blanket. Its substrate-neutral propagation across biology, language traces, learned representations and engineered institutions is a working claim. Published Markov-object language denotes an immutable ledger-derived cut with identity direction and distributed evidence, while recovered entities can be published as entity cuts independently.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":381,\"path\":\"standards/WORLD_MODEL.md\",\"quote\":\"A Markov object is\\na stable self-bounding pattern in a constraint structure whose internal\\nstate can be reasoned about through its effective blanket. The term is\\nsubstrate-neutral: the same topology is expected wherever a constraint\\nstructure admits stable configurations, in biological systems, in the natural-language traces those systems emit, in\\nlearned representations built over those traces (LLMs), and in the\\nengineered institutional systems descended from both. The working claim\\nis that world-model construction is possible because this topology\\npropagates across substrates: what domain experts recognise as \\\"objects\\\"\\nin an institutional system is the same kind of stable constraint\\nstructure hypothesised for biological systems, re-expressed through\\nanother substrate.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/WORLD_MODEL.md#WORLD_MODEL%2F4.%20The%20Markov-object%20construct\",\"start_line\":369},{\"end_line\":592,\"path\":\"standards/WORLD_MODEL.md\",\"quote\":\"The\\npublished Markov object is an immutable object cut projected from the\\nattribute ledger, not an in-place mutable record; the cut is an identity\\ndirection together with the distributed attribute evidence that supports\\nit, not an enumeration of member columns (P3, P4b).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/WORLD_MODEL.md#WORLD_MODEL%2F6.%20Units\",\"start_line\":588}],\"label\":\"Markov Object\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:4945be8fe304fdd50b4910957a8aeb30","key":624,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:4945be8fe304fdd50b4910957a8aeb30\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"Working geometric reading of an effective blanket: a low-rank projection preserving identity under treatment. The distributed attribute basis evidences the projection rather than constituting column membership. An identity direction is a geometric combination over columns in a declared representation space.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":407,\"path\":\"standards/WORLD_MODEL.md\",\"quote\":\"- the effective blanket is a low-rank projection in the representation\\n  space along which object identity is preserved under treatment;\\n- the attribute basis is evidence for that projection; the projection is\\n  not a column-membership predicate;\\n- a published Markov-object overlay is an identity direction together\\n  with the distributed attribute evidence supporting it.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/WORLD_MODEL.md#WORLD_MODEL%2F4.%20The%20Markov-object%20construct%2FEffective%20blanket\",\"start_line\":402}],\"label\":\"Effective blanket and identity direction\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:c143b6f091bd0e5b8b35148ab55197eb","key":625,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:c143b6f091bd0e5b8b35148ab55197eb\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[\"A declared representation space exists.\"],\"definition\":\"Optional geometric overlay on an entity cut, adding identity direction, projection support and effective coordinate, constructed and verified under §10. It strengthens a cut; its absence does not weaken the cut. It retains candidate-class standing independently of publication verification.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":578,\"path\":\"standards/WORLD_MODEL.md\",\"quote\":\"| Markov-Object Overlay | an optional geometric overlay on an entity cut, admissible only where a declared representation space exists; it adds an identity direction, projection support and effective coordinate, constructed and verified under §10; the overlay strengthens an entity cut, and its absence does not weaken one | P3, P6 |\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/WORLD_MODEL.md#WORLD_MODEL%2F6.%20Units\",\"start_line\":578}],\"label\":\"Markov-Object Overlay\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:22a6fe3d61f766946bb29c4e77059644","key":626,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:22a6fe3d61f766946bb29c4e77059644\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"Related but distinct semantic units: Treatment Surface reinterprets one domain into another; Covariance Edge declares how changes in one object correspond to another; Adjoint Mapping is a treatment's interpret-back contract; Temporal Reference Artifact is a changing value list, code set or classification whose semantics affect interpretation.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":582,\"path\":\"standards/WORLD_MODEL.md\",\"quote\":\"| Treatment Surface | a semantic reinterpretation from one domain into another | P1 |\\n| Covariance Edge | a declared relation showing how changes in one object correspond to changes in another | P1, P3 |\\n| Adjoint Mapping | the interpret-back contract for a treatment | P1 |\\n| Temporal Reference Artifact | a changing value list, code set or classification set whose semantics matter for object interpretation | P3, P1 |\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/WORLD_MODEL.md#WORLD_MODEL%2F6.%20Units\",\"start_line\":579}],\"label\":\"Treatment, covariance, adjoint and temporal reference units\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:47e7639a8632c2097cf426c2201bade1","key":627,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:47e7639a8632c2097cf426c2201bade1\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"Higher-order world model built by referencing and stitching published domain artifacts while preserving their identity, version and local authority.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":583,\"path\":\"standards/WORLD_MODEL.md\",\"quote\":\"| Composed World Model | a higher-order world model built by referencing and stitching published domain artifacts while preserving their identity, version and local authority | P4a, P6 |\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/WORLD_MODEL.md#WORLD_MODEL%2F6.%20Units\",\"start_line\":583}],\"label\":\"Composed World Model\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:a7d93851d417c75f3d15373901149cb8","key":628,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:a7d93851d417c75f3d15373901149cb8\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"A Projection is a user- or downstream-facing artifact derived from the semantic kernel. A Query Plane is an optional downstream serving surface for querying or traversing published domain artifacts and composed models without constitutional publication authority.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":585,\"path\":\"standards/WORLD_MODEL.md\",\"quote\":\"| Projection | a user-facing or downstream-facing artifact derived from the semantic kernel | P1 |\\n| Query Plane | an optional downstream serving surface that makes published domain artifacts or composed world models queryable or traversable without becoming the constitutional publication authority | P6 |\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/WORLD_MODEL.md#WORLD_MODEL%2F6.%20Units\",\"start_line\":584}],\"label\":\"Projection and Query Plane\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:61857acd4f5f365bed011dce43b5991a","key":629,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:61857acd4f5f365bed011dce43b5991a\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"The sole constitutional semantic truth surface consists of published domain artifacts, bounded fragments, entity cuts, explicit treatments, covariance edges, adjoint mappings, temporal reference artifacts and models composed by reference. Epistemic overlays, query planes, mapping reports and compiled execution artifacts are downstream or supporting.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":347,\"path\":\"standards/WORLD_MODEL.md\",\"quote\":\"World-model work has one constitutional truth surface: the published\\nsemantic layer (P6). That layer consists of\\npublished domain artifacts; their bounded fragments and published entity\\ncuts; explicit treatments, covariance edges, adjoint mappings and\\ntemporal reference artifacts; and composed world models built by\\nreference from those published artifacts. Everything else is downstream\\nor supporting: epistemic overlays, query planes, mapping reports and\\ncompiled deterministic execution artifacts. Those surfaces may be\\nimportant; they do not create a second truth surface (P6, P1).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/WORLD_MODEL.md#WORLD_MODEL%2F3.%20What%20a%20world%20model%20is%2FSingle%20truth%20surface\",\"start_line\":339}],\"label\":\"Published semantic layer\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:63dba586b5a95104e1ecff3442d0c5f0","key":630,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:63dba586b5a95104e1ecff3442d0c5f0\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"Probabilistic uncertainty, ranking, anomaly and alignment surface, potentially containing correspondence candidates, confidence, ambiguity registers, surprise signals and suggested mappings or treatments. Distinct from accepted semantic treatments, published domain artifacts and deterministic compiled artifacts.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":556,\"path\":\"standards/WORLD_MODEL.md\",\"quote\":\"Probability belongs in the epistemic overlay. The canonical published\\nentity cut should remain semantic and bounded. Probability belongs in\\nuncertainty, ranking, anomaly and alignment overlays, not in the\\nontological identity of the published object itself (P3, P6). That overlay may\\ninclude correspondence candidates; confidence and ranking; ambiguity\\nregisters; anomaly and surprise signals; and candidate mappings or\\ntreatment suggestions.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/WORLD_MODEL.md#WORLD_MODEL%2F5.%20Core%20claims\",\"start_line\":550}],\"label\":\"Epistemic overlay\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:0a85925cde6108a838ebe8913e3afc63","key":631,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:0a85925cde6108a838ebe8913e3afc63\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"Publication record of immutable domain-artifact cuts and object projections, distinct from the attribute ledger of qualified claims. Git and the filesystem suffice in the initial publication lane; a later database complements them as query plane.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":749,\"path\":\"standards/WORLD_MODEL.md\",\"quote\":\"Git is the publication ledger; a database is the query plane\\n(P6). This publication ledger is distinct from the attribute ledger: the\\nattribute ledger records qualified semantic claims over object identity,\\nand the publication ledger records immutable published cuts of domain\\nartifacts and object projections. Both should remain append-only and\\nreplayable (P4b).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/WORLD_MODEL.md#WORLD_MODEL%2F8.%20Representation%20and%20publication%2FPublication%20law\",\"start_line\":744}],\"label\":\"Publication ledger\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:d346a1dbfeb78b1415d50ab61ce48315","key":632,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:d346a1dbfeb78b1415d50ab61ce48315\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"Source-defined fourteen-stage construction flow: Observe, Trace, Extract, Assure, Ledger, Bound, Materialise, Relate, Publish, Compose, optional Align, Project, optional Compile, optional Serve or query.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":620,\"path\":\"standards/WORLD_MODEL.md\",\"quote\":\"The profile proceeds through these stages (P4b, P6):\\n\\n1. Observe.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/WORLD_MODEL.md#WORLD_MODEL%2F7.%20Flow\",\"start_line\":618}],\"label\":\"World-model construction flow\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:fa21a8371950f5ec05eb0e10d057e58b","key":633,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:fa21a8371950f5ec05eb0e10d057e58b\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"Semantic control plane contains published artifacts, composed models, treatments, covariance edges, adjoint mappings and epistemic overlays. The high-volume data plane contains deterministic executable artifacts compiled from accepted semantic understanding. The split distinguishes truth, probabilistic correspondence and runtime behaviour without creating another truth surface.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1026,\"path\":\"standards/WORLD_MODEL.md\",\"quote\":\"The semantic\\ncontrol plane consists of published domain artifacts; composed world\\nmodels; treatments, covariance edges and adjoint mappings; and epistemic\\noverlays for correspondence, ranking and ambiguity. The high-volume data\\nplane consists of deterministic executable artifacts compiled from\\naccepted semantic understanding. That means: world-model artifacts carry\\nsemantic truth; epistemic overlays carry probabilistic correspondence and\\nuncertainty; compiled execution artifacts carry deterministic runtime\\nbehaviour. This is a plane split, not a truth split; the semantic truth\\nsurface remains the published world-model layer (§3 Single truth\\nsurface) (P6).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/WORLD_MODEL.md#WORLD_MODEL%2F12.%20Planes%2C%20proof%20and%20development%2FControl%20plane%20and%20data%20plane\",\"start_line\":1016}],\"label\":\"Control plane and data plane\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:fc9b41e078bad0f2e87fffa996874467","key":634,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:fc9b41e078bad0f2e87fffa996874467\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"Seven predicate-specific refinements: cut admissibility, direction acceptance, overlay publication, overlay storage, null-peer discrimination, promotion-gate run and saturation. Each value maps to exactly one core value without raising standing or satisfying another predicate.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1118,\"path\":\"standards/WORLD_MODEL.md\",\"quote\":\"Each refinement names\\nthe question it answers and the predicate its mapping is for, and maps\\neach of its values to exactly one core value. The predicate travels with\\nthe value, so a `satisfied` for one predicate never counts toward another\\n([FOUNDATIONS §4 Conjunction of results](FOUNDATIONS.md#conjunction-of-results)),\\nand no mapping raises a result's standing: nothing is coerced to\\n`satisfied` (P5, P6).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/WORLD_MODEL.md#WORLD_MODEL%2F14.%20Results%20of%20this%20profile\",\"start_line\":1112}],\"label\":\"World-model result refinements\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:07fe88a2a6a0523330a19d0977d0c575","key":635,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:07fe88a2a6a0523330a19d0977d0c575\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"Practical writing guide for method surfaces: claim-and-reason writing, style, prose quality, authority-layer tone, specification-artifact discipline, layer checks and current-surface writing. It consumes SPEC_METHOD's chain and release boundary and POSTING_GUIDE's commentary layer without defining them.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":12,\"path\":\"standards/WRITING_GUIDE.md\",\"quote\":\"Guide. Owns the practical writing discipline for this method's surfaces:\\nthe core rule, style rules, habits to remove, the marks of good and bad\\nprose, alignment of tone with the authority layer, practice for\\nspecification artifacts, the layer checks and present-tense writing of the\\ncurrent surface. Consumes [SPEC_METHOD §2](SPEC_METHOD.md#2-the-chain)\\n(the chain, its layers and the specification surface rule) and\\n[§6](SPEC_METHOD.md#6-lineage-and-release) (the release version boundary),\\nand [POSTING_GUIDE](POSTING_GUIDE.md) (the commentary layer); defines none\\nof them. Every clause names the principle that requires it (P0 to P6,\\nFOUNDATIONS §3).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/WRITING_GUIDE.md#WRITING_GUIDE\",\"start_line\":3}],\"label\":\"WRITING_GUIDE\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:4fde8cb332e23c5fd70f410d41046ae4","key":636,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:4fde8cb332e23c5fd70f410d41046ae4\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[],\"definition\":\"Specification-layer document whose roles and closure are owned by SPEC_METHOD §2; the writing guide governs its practical prose discipline.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":81,\"path\":\"standards/WRITING_GUIDE.md\",\"quote\":\"[SPEC_METHOD §2](SPEC_METHOD.md#2-the-chain) is the constitutional\\nauthority for the roles and closure of the specification layers; this\\nguide supplies the practical writing discipline for those artifacts (P6).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/WRITING_GUIDE.md#WRITING_GUIDE%2F7.%20Specification%20artifact%20practice\",\"start_line\":79}],\"label\":\"Specification artifact\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:d4026128310a589d335a770c7ceb2679","key":637,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c: