":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:00da0796474a9e6a7531f014f8132c66","key":747,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:00da0796474a9e6a7531f014f8132c66\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:relation-kind:governing:governs_format\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"qualifiers\":{\"conditions\":[\"The overridden kinds belong to the derived domain and all preservation/publication conditions hold.\"],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":270,\"path\":\"standards/IDENTITY.md\",\"quote\":\"Derived domains may override identity format and structure for their own\\nkinds. An override is lawful only if it preserves (P3):\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/IDENTITY.md#IDENTITY%2F7.%20Default%20formats%20and%20overrides%2FDerived%20domain%20overrides\",\"start_line\":269}],\"kind\":\"governs_format\",\"meaning\":\"A lawful domain-published override governs format and structure for that domain's own identity kinds.\"},\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"source\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:487b998011fc8bbf86f5688efd791a52\",\"target\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:006ca6488f42ba4e76c541e522c13142\"}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"relations","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:cab1ec7733972caf0edd5b55395db179","key":748,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:cab1ec7733972caf0edd5b55395db179\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:relation-kind:discovery:transition_between\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"qualifiers\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":290,\"path\":\"standards/ODD.md\",\"quote\":\"Vectors are the lawful transitions between nodes and are the admissible\\ntransitions of the product. Each vector declares its required upstream\\nassets, its target asset, its governing evaluators and gates, and its\\noutput contract (P4a, P6).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ODD.md#ODD%2F5.%20Graph%20model%2FVectors\",\"start_line\":287}],\"kind\":\"transition_between\",\"meaning\":\"A vector links declared upstream assets to its target node/asset through an admissible transition. This category-level relation does not select or execute a concrete edge.\"},\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"source\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:4affde1b64c0d4f4480ba70fa8f30aea\",\"target\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:845e0e60b60e69f173452f33a26b882d\"}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"relations","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:bcb5caaa1193d2f3fb0301e262cf5adb","key":749,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:bcb5caaa1193d2f3fb0301e262cf5adb\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:relation-kind:governing:declared_binding\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"qualifiers\":{\"conditions\":[\"One declared vector or edge traversal of a published graph.\",\"The selected context fits the actor's envelope.\",\"The binding has not been invalidated, or has been evaluated again after change.\"],\"exceptions\":[\"Changes to FOUNDATIONS P0, vector declaration or selected basis invalidate the binding until re-evaluation.\"],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":309,\"path\":\"standards/ODD.md\",\"quote\":\"Direction: from the step of\\nFOUNDATIONS P0 to one declared ODD vector or edge traversal. Preserved\\nmeaning: the step's selected context fits the actor's envelope, the\\nactor's internal path within the step is its own, and the traversal is\\nthe admissible external space. Narrowed scope: one declared vector or edge\\ntraversal of a published graph. Invalidation: a change to FOUNDATIONS P0,\\nto the vector's declaration or to the selected basis invalidates the\\nbinding until it is evaluated again (P0, P1).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ODD.md#ODD%2F5.%20Graph%20model%2FProbabilistic%20compute\",\"start_line\":302}],\"kind\":\"declared_binding\",\"meaning\":\"Direction is foundational bounded step to ODD edge traversal, preserving actor-owned internal path and externally bounded admissible space. PROFILES §2 indexes the binding; this is a described binding, not a traversal occurrence.\"},\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"source\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:7041e57978eba9d41b7f61db1ca3b4ed\",\"target\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:dd4c6b532dec6f332c60a24617ffac0a\"}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"relations","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:4017b7e5758fd54465a17101f370d214","key":750,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:4017b7e5758fd54465a17101f370d214\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:relation-kind:governing:declared_specialisation\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"qualifiers\":{\"conditions\":[\"Source and target basis are the selected complete STDO release.\",\"Governed scope is one declared ODD traversal.\",\"The supplied Probabilistic compute clause is the provenance carrier.\"],\"exceptions\":[\"Processing outside the traversal is excluded.\",\"There is no implied inverse.\",\"A change to either concept/context, basis, scope, preserved/narrowed meaning or control contract invalidates the affected specialisation until re-evaluated.\"],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":345,\"path\":\"standards/ODD.md\",\"quote\":\"The F_P\\nspecialisation runs from\\n`urn:stdo:concept:ambiguity-governance:lawful-probabilistic-processing` to\\n`urn:stdo:concept:graph-native-odd:f-p`;\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ODD.md#ODD%2F5.%20Graph%20model%2FProbabilistic%20compute\",\"start_line\":342},{\"end_line\":361,\"path\":\"standards/ODD.md\",\"quote\":\"Both relations preserve the source meaning and authority, narrow scope to\\na declared ODD traversal, and add graph-contract and runtime-control\\ncoordinates. They exclude processing or adjudication outside that\\ntraversal, refuse ambient worker or human authority, and have no implied\\ninverse. Their source and target basis is the selected complete STDO\\nrelease, their governed scope is ODD traversal, and this clause is their\\nprovenance carrier. A change to either concept or context, to the basis,\\nto the scope, to the preserved or narrowed meaning or to the control\\ncontract invalidates the affected specialisation until it is evaluated\\nagain (P1, P3, P6).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ODD.md#ODD%2F5.%20Graph%20model%2FProbabilistic%20compute\",\"start_line\":352}],\"kind\":\"declared_specialisation\",\"meaning\":\"Source lawful probabilistic processing specialises directionally into ODD F_P, preserving bounded non-human construction under policy and source authority, narrowing to the traversal contract and adding graph-contract/runtime-control coordinates. It grants no ambient worker authority.\"},\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"source\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:c4e137050be29b55e509bb3284c7bad0\",\"target\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:eac7cf8a2799092be0571f0c747f7bb9\"}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"relations","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:4b929bd92e9a2ead6dad1b83ea7106ed","key":751,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:4b929bd92e9a2ead6dad1b83ea7106ed\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:relation-kind:governing:declared_specialisation\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"qualifiers\":{\"conditions\":[\"Source and target basis are the selected complete STDO release.\",\"Governed scope is one declared ODD traversal.\",\"The supplied Probabilistic compute clause is the provenance carrier.\"],\"exceptions\":[\"Adjudication outside the traversal is excluded.\",\"There is no implied inverse.\",\"A change to either concept/context, basis, scope, preserved/narrowed meaning or control contract invalidates the affected specialisation until re-evaluated.\"],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":350,\"path\":\"standards/ODD.md\",\"quote\":\"the F_H specialisation runs from\\n`urn:stdo:concept:ambiguity-governance:human-adjudication` to\\n`urn:stdo:concept:graph-native-odd:f-h`. The source concepts and their\\ncontext are owned by\\n[SPEC_METHOD §5](SPEC_METHOD.md#5-ambiguity-governance-and-lifecycle); this\\nprofile owns the targets in the graph-native ODD context (P1, P6).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ODD.md#ODD%2F5.%20Graph%20model%2FProbabilistic%20compute\",\"start_line\":345},{\"end_line\":361,\"path\":\"standards/ODD.md\",\"quote\":\"A change to either concept or context, to the basis,\\nto the scope, to the preserved or narrowed meaning or to the control\\ncontract invalidates the affected specialisation until it is evaluated\\nagain (P1, P3, P6).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ODD.md#ODD%2F5.%20Graph%20model%2FProbabilistic%20compute\",\"start_line\":358}],\"kind\":\"declared_specialisation\",\"meaning\":\"Source human adjudication specialises directionally into ODD F_H, preserving source meaning/authority while narrowing invocation to declared traversal authority and ambiguity policy and adding graph/runtime-control coordinates. It grants no ambient human traversal, semantic or closure authority.\"},\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"source\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:aeb8d30e922b74cb3478814dc61ad20c\",\"target\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:f688644e4a37c1669dd925477341038c\"}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"relations","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:f907be66c4917c59efe0bb0d8bf7d717","key":752,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:f907be66c4917c59efe0bb0d8bf7d717\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:relation-kind:governing:governing_contract\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"qualifiers\":{\"conditions\":[\"The function realises the outer vector directly or through refinement.\"],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":374,\"path\":\"standards/ODD.md\",\"quote\":\"The outer vector remains the constitutional contract;\\nthe graph function is the constructive realisation of that contract (P4a,\\nP0).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ODD.md#ODD%2F5.%20Graph%20model%2FGraph%20functions\",\"start_line\":372}],\"kind\":\"governing_contract\",\"meaning\":\"The outer vector governs its constructive graph-function realisation and remains the callable contract.\"},\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"source\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:4affde1b64c0d4f4480ba70fa8f30aea\",\"target\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:8a952a4985c21b8548d5a4551258e042\"}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"relations","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:31591c3d84d1ea89565004b1b7295b63","key":753,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:31591c3d84d1ea89565004b1b7295b63\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:relation-kind:governing:declared_binding\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"qualifiers\":{\"conditions\":[\"One published outer vector and its declared inner workflow.\",\"The cumulative carried environment is the specialised contract.\",\"Inner inputs satisfy their declared domains/preconditions and inner steps preserve the outer contract and applicable invariants.\"],\"exceptions\":[\"Changes to ACTIVATION §4, ODD §11.8, the outer vector or a function environment declaration invalidate the binding until re-evaluated.\"],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":388,\"path\":\"standards/ODD.md\",\"quote\":\"Direction: from the typed refinement of ACTIVATION §4 to a graph\\nfunction that refines one outer vector, with the §11.8 environment as its\\nspecialised contract.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ODD.md#ODD%2F5.%20Graph%20model%2FGraph%20functions\",\"start_line\":386}],\"kind\":\"declared_binding\",\"meaning\":\"General typed refinement binds directionally to an ODD graph function refining one outer vector through the profile-specific cumulative environment; this does not generalise §11.8 into the core.\"},\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"source\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:b4bfe7d8f52830a21e97ccd74cb89f5f\",\"target\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:8a952a4985c21b8548d5a4551258e042\"}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"relations","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:ef7fd6c4e356998b4a1bba39acb625fb","key":754,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:ef7fd6c4e356998b4a1bba39acb625fb\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:relation-kind:governing:owns_execution_governance\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"qualifiers\":{\"conditions\":[\"The consumer has bound the ABG role for this traversal.\"],\"exceptions\":[\"A different realisation requires explicitly ratified non-overlapping runtime scope.\"],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":585,\"path\":\"standards/ODD.md\",\"quote\":\"ABG owns traversal; dispatch; actor invocation; process supervision;\\ngraph-call realisation; runtime facts; runtime event emission and replay;\\nframes; continuations; retry and correction control; closure folds over\\nruntime truth; re-entry after publish boundaries; lineage and provenance\\n(P6).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ODD.md#ODD%2F10.%20What%20an%20ODD%20product%20is%2FABG\",\"start_line\":581}],\"kind\":\"owns_execution_governance\",\"meaning\":\"ABG owns traversal control and runtime truth, including lifecycle, continuation, event/replay and closure responsibilities; product domain interpretation remains separately owned.\"},\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"source\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:7401bbbf535fd5e1e16b14036ff56999\",\"target\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:dd4c6b532dec6f332c60a24617ffac0a\"}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"relations","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:5bde76b23f98844933de81b83ec0665d","key":755,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:5bde76b23f98844933de81b83ec0665d\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:relation-kind:governing:owns_domain_meaning\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"qualifiers\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":591,\"path\":\"standards/ODD.md\",\"quote\":\"The ODD product owns domain asset meaning, graph-function meaning, the\\npublished function catalogue, policy overlays, domain query projections,\\nand closure and gap interpretation for its domain (P6, P1).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ODD.md#ODD%2F10.%20What%20an%20ODD%20product%20is%2FODD%20product\",\"start_line\":589}],\"kind\":\"owns_domain_meaning\",\"meaning\":\"The product owns its graph-function semantics, independently of ABG runtime control and closure-fold ownership.\"},\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"source\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:dfebaec0e3fc6f2d93521655089f3a54\",\"target\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:8a952a4985c21b8548d5a4551258e042\"}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"relations","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:59027f5b0ac03b221b96dcad2d716f7d","key":756,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:59027f5b0ac03b221b96dcad2d716f7d\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:relation-kind:governing:constrains_projection\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"qualifiers\":{\"conditions\":[\"The view describes an admitted GTL module or public carrier.\"],\"exceptions\":[\"Missing, stale or structurally divergent described carriers require domain overlays to fail closed.\"],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":769,\"path\":\"standards/ODD.md\",\"quote\":\"function catalogue views must reconcile to the\\nadmitted GTL module or public carrier; asset ownership and start-target\\nviews must be derived from, or structurally compared against, the admitted\\ncarrier they expose; runtime status views must derive from ABG runtime\\nfacts, events, replay or projection truth; domain query overlays must fail\\nclosed when the carrier they describe is missing, stale or structurally\\ndivergent (P3, P6).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ODD.md#ODD%2F11.%20Core%20law%2F11.5C%20Projection-source%20coherence\",\"start_line\":763}],\"kind\":\"constrains_projection\",\"meaning\":\"The admitted carrier constrains downstream catalogue/asset/start-target views through derivation or structural reconciliation; the projection cannot become a rival authority.\"},\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"source\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:81f6906b71f893b3c94e1dfc03ff9522\",\"target\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:34566a52e8fcda8cee3d666e0e57e8ae\"}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"relations","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:f5d2af48071f739a45a144ce36ff4207","key":757,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:f5d2af48071f739a45a144ce36ff4207\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:relation-kind:governing:external_authority\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"qualifiers\":{\"conditions\":[\"The selected outcome and any bounded prerequisite/experiment basis are admitted.\"],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":794,\"path\":\"standards/ODD.md\",\"quote\":\"The selected Product outcome under\\n[SPEC_METHOD §3 Outcome conservation](SPEC_METHOD.md#3-outcome-conservation) is external\\nauthority for this loop. Product models, gaps, assurance, ledgers and\\nprojections may interpret that outcome but cannot author, select or\\nenlarge it.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ODD.md#ODD%2F11.%20Core%20law%2F11.5D%20Constructive%20evaluation%20and%20yield%20loop\",\"start_line\":790}],\"kind\":\"external_authority\",\"meaning\":\"The selected Product outcome limits the loop's material work and is preserved through target binding and construction intent; interpretation does not confer outcome-selection authority.\"},\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"source\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:43f24abc172ed34fa00c9cdc0a76989f\",\"target\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:bcaa8a8d820aec2a089181d683a453df\"}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"relations","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:a00cf903fcbedc17ce9b5cb2d9a73238","key":758,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:a00cf903fcbedc17ce9b5cb2d9a73238\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:relation-kind:discovery:declared_output\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"qualifiers\":{\"conditions\":[\"Each function uses only its declared input and authority boundary.\"],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":858,\"path\":\"standards/ODD.md\",\"quote\":\"| `evaluate_action` | `ConstructionIntent + AdmittedEvidence + TargetObligationBinding + Policy` | `EdgeFulfillmentLedger + EdgeClosureDecision` | Action-result evaluation. It decides close, yield, retry, repair, re-enter, reprice, or block for the action just taken. It does not choose the next graph action. |\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ODD.md#ODD%2F11.%20Core%20law%2F11.5D%20Constructive%20evaluation%20and%20yield%20loop\",\"start_line\":858}],\"kind\":\"declared_output\",\"meaning\":\"The four functions produce the specifically named model, observation/gap, priority/next-action, or ledger/closure carriers recorded in evaluation_functions; this is a source-described producer relation, not execution or acceptance.\"},\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"source\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:505ca2ca015711bae0650516cdea1113\",\"target\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:3c87e88b6006249dbc37ff1e00860b70\"}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"relations","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:4542a2dfbc99aad92ec6e97c17fd65ac","key":759,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:4542a2dfbc99aad92ec6e97c17fd65ac\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:relation-kind:discovery:conformance_evidence\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"qualifiers\":{\"conditions\":[\"The walkthrough is agentic, end-to-end, on real work and uses only declared authority.\"],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1457,\"path\":\"standards/ODD.md\",\"quote\":\"The walkthrough is the conformance proof. §11.7 requires automation to\\nstay true for a manual walkthrough; its agentic form is a conformance test\\nof the method itself. An agentic coder executes the constitutional process\\nend to end on real work, using only the declared authority surfaces:\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ODD.md#ODD%2F11.%20Core%20law%2F11.7A%20Conforming%20agentic%20development\",\"start_line\":1454}],\"kind\":\"conformance_evidence\",\"meaning\":\"The agentic form of manual traversal supplies the F_P process-followability half of conformance; it neither substitutes for deterministic artifact admission nor ratifies method change.\"},\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"source\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:c268d2b1bafeebb5b3c54ed7be08bb2e\",\"target\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:26c627c4204c2f1f3b1820e20d788928\"}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"relations","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:563ab357e4f4bd32a598de736408ec11","key":760,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:563ab357e4f4bd32a598de736408ec11\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:relation-kind:discovery:interoperability_realization\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"qualifiers\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":85,\"path\":\"standards/PRODUCT_DEFINITION.md\",\"quote\":\"The normative schema is `schemas/product-definition.schema.json`; the\\nsingle fill-in form is `templates/PRODUCT_DEFINITION_TEMPLATE.json`. This\\nconcrete JSON shape is an accepted interoperability boundary under\\nSTDO-SURFACE-001 (§11). It standardises only identity, location, relation\\nand discovery fields and absorbs no meaning owned by a referenced\\nconstitutional, Product, requirement, design, ticket or commentary surface\\n(P6, P2).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/PRODUCT_DEFINITION.md#PRODUCT_DEFINITION%2F1.%20Overlay%20and%20layout%20independence\",\"start_line\":79}],\"kind\":\"interoperability_realization\",\"meaning\":\"The schema and fill-in template realize the overlay's accepted JSON boundary without becoming a second semantic owner or creating a populated Product definition.\"},\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"source\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:c1ed13a1e7694716094389e56c921b63\",\"target\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:8048859bf02f15f5c3158d9ca21e6198\"}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"relations","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:9d02daced031ce99443603f04576f073","key":761,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:9d02daced031ce99443603f04576f073\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:relation-kind:discovery:locates\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"qualifiers\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":211,\"path\":\"standards/PRODUCT_DEFINITION.md\",\"quote\":\"`constitution.stdo.basis` locates the complete selected STDO constitutional\\nset; `constitution.additional_authorities` locates every additional\\nconstitutional set or source.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/PRODUCT_DEFINITION.md#PRODUCT_DEFINITION%2F3.%20Constitutional-set%20sufficiency\",\"start_line\":209}],\"kind\":\"locates\",\"meaning\":\"Definition basis/additional-authority fields locate complete selected governing sources; location transfers neither content ownership nor constitutional authority to the overlay.\"},\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"source\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:8048859bf02f15f5c3158d9ca21e6198\",\"target\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:cd46ea3f9d64e23d695883c0d8fb98b2\"}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"relations","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:2b6cc9f130ddf982864952b0ae6f7041","key":762,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:2b6cc9f130ddf982864952b0ae6f7041\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:relation-kind:discovery:bounded_realization\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"qualifiers\":{\"conditions\":[\"An exact basis is selected and the applicable operation is authorized.\"],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":264,\"path\":\"standards/PRODUCT_DEFINITION.md\",\"quote\":\"- installs each immutable cut once in a shared, versioned release store;\\n- resolves logical `stdo://releases/...` URIs to verified installed bytes;\\n- inventories and verifies complete installed distributions;\\n- synchronises the exact basis already selected by a Product Definition;\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/PRODUCT_DEFINITION.md#PRODUCT_DEFINITION%2F4.%20Shared%20installed%20release%20basis%20and%20toolchain%20manager\",\"start_line\":261}],\"kind\":\"bounded_realization\",\"meaning\":\"The manager installs, resolves, verifies and synchronizes the exact selected release basis; it does not independently select Product law or redefine method meaning.\"},\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"source\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:f5ea64751cc1eb33ef2ae5a9bbc3b09a\",\"target\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:395e42597f3b0df9d733f31d1b45bed9\"}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"relations","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:42788e5395da7b8e0d8e33a1ff86e000","key":763,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:42788e5395da7b8e0d8e33a1ff86e000\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:relation-kind:governing:required_semantic_contract\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"qualifiers\":{\"conditions\":[\"Local disambiguation candidates cross bounded contexts.\"],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":627,\"path\":\"standards/PRODUCT_DEFINITION.md\",\"quote\":\"The referenced `uri` owns the resolution. When the candidates cross bounded\\ncontexts, that carrier also declares the complete import, translation or\\nequivalence relation §5 requires.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/PRODUCT_DEFINITION.md#PRODUCT_DEFINITION%2F6.%20Local%20constitutional%20binding\",\"start_line\":625}],\"kind\":\"required_semantic_contract\",\"meaning\":\"The cross-context relation contract governs the resolution carrier: it must declare a complete import, translation or equivalence rather than relying on overlay metadata or nominal matching.\"},\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"source\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:54629b053141a69765f840b7f0c3f90c\",\"target\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:b698ebbf7b1bde39a0a5b16677367aa6\"}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"relations","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:2dca9845199515030e038f5b67784fcb","key":764,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:2dca9845199515030e038f5b67784fcb\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:relation-kind:discovery:execution_scoped_binding\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"qualifiers\":{\"conditions\":[\"An exact authorized work instruction activates an applicable bound frame for an agent and subject.\"],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":689,\"path\":\"standards/PRODUCT_DEFINITION.md\",\"quote\":\"The collective basis and an actor activation are distinct. An Agent Frame\\nActivation is the execution-scoped binding of one agent to an applicable\\nframe declaration or active configuration, an exact evaluation, subject,\\nbasis, evidence boundary and capability envelope; what the agent receives\\nis the activation packet of REFERENCE_FRAME §11, and the step it performs\\nis ACTIVATION §1. The Product Definition records the durable shared basis;\\na ticket or other authorised work instruction carries the activation\\npacket.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/PRODUCT_DEFINITION.md#PRODUCT_DEFINITION%2F7.%20Collective%20reference-frame%20basis\",\"start_line\":682}],\"kind\":\"execution_scoped_binding\",\"meaning\":\"An activation binds an agent to an applicable declaration/configuration from the collective frame basis without mutating that durable basis or the overlay.\"},\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"source\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:6e2b00300849fee60f54d5d16d37822d\",\"target\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:24eaed2b3ae25fcb1bde979499653b21\"}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"relations","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:d1ac691cfbb3e871de089ea17a46e1c9","key":765,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:d1ac691cfbb3e871de089ea17a46e1c9\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:relation-kind:discovery:explicit_carrier_binding\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"qualifiers\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":765,\"path\":\"standards/PRODUCT_DEFINITION.md\",\"quote\":\"`ticketing.comments` locates the\\ncommentary root. `ticketing.sprints` optionally locates bounded\\nexecution-batch manifests.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/PRODUCT_DEFINITION.md#PRODUCT_DEFINITION%2F8.%20WHAT%2C%20HOW%20and%20work%20carriers\",\"start_line\":763},{\"end_line\":42,\"path\":\"standards/POSTING_GUIDE.md\",\"quote\":\"Posts live at the location the product definition binds as\\n`ticketing.comments.root` (P6, P3).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/POSTING_GUIDE.md#POSTING_GUIDE%2F3.%20Location\",\"start_line\":41}],\"kind\":\"explicit_carrier_binding\",\"meaning\":\"The expressly shared ticketing.comments binding locates the post carrier while preserving commentary's non-authoritative role; this link follows explicit source references, not label matching.\"},\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"source\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:71e0e361793d1a2f94d72888e297322b\",\"target\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:39bdea0a1e0944501e86c53001a7d5cb\"}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"relations","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:5c0de7fab8d7dec07b6e698ac62c37a0","key":766,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:5c0de7fab8d7dec07b6e698ac62c37a0\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:relation-kind:governing:requires_identity_resolved_target\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"qualifiers\":{\"conditions\":[\"An explicit composition entry is declared.\"],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":823,\"path\":\"standards/PRODUCT_DEFINITION.md\",\"quote\":\"- every composition target resolves to another product definition whose\\n  `product.definition_id` equals `target_definition_id`, and every\\n  relation and non-empty contract set resolves; and\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/PRODUCT_DEFINITION.md#PRODUCT_DEFINITION%2F9.%20Recursive%20discovery%20and%20explicit%20composition\",\"start_line\":821}],\"kind\":\"requires_identity_resolved_target\",\"meaning\":\"The declared entry requires a target definition whose stable ID matches its expected ID, together with resolving relation authority and non-empty contracts. This is a type-level requirement, not an asserted concrete product edge.\"},\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"source\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:8bdd42573e0cb3dc879df6ffa3bb6827\",\"target\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:ec08ef0caf1ef5504b20e94591bbea9d\"}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"relations","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:6710171b00464b0b2afe61b407fa2e73","key":767,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:6710171b00464b0b2afe61b407fa2e73\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:relation-kind:governing:defers_deciding_authority_to\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"qualifiers\":{\"conditions\":[\"The derived surface is carried by a released cut or installation.\"],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":898,\"path\":\"standards/PRODUCT_DEFINITION.md\",\"quote\":\"The raw owning members of the same\\nselected cut remain the deciding authority: a question that a stale or\\ninsufficient carrier cannot decide is decided from them, as ACTIVATION\\n§2 states (P3, P5, P6).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/PRODUCT_DEFINITION.md#PRODUCT_DEFINITION%2F11.%20One%20constitutional%20surface%20and%20version%20boundary\",\"start_line\":895}],\"kind\":\"defers_deciding_authority_to\",\"meaning\":\"Derived surfaces remain subordinate to owning members of the same selected cut; stale or insufficient representations cannot replace their deciding authority.\"},\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"source\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:05c1a265f04949108de6c22b4ed5d7b2\",\"target\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:70f67311f73a19765787897dfa4176f1\"}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"relations","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:c211220136bc060ebb5d5c1e8241726e","key":768,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:c211220136bc060ebb5d5c1e8241726e\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:relation-kind:governing:requires_reference_import_from\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"qualifiers\":{\"conditions\":[\"A profile uses a core concept or rests on a generic family.\"],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":34,\"path\":\"standards/PROFILES.md\",\"quote\":\"A profile imports the generic families of tiers 1 and 2 that\\nits rules rest on, and owns only its own bindings: the terms and choices\\nit adds for its domain or operation, among them the declared bindings\\nabove (P1, P6). It imports each concept it uses from a member of tiers 1\\nand 2 under\\n[FOUNDATIONS §2 Imports between members](FOUNDATIONS.md#imports-between-members),\\nwhich states what an import is, and restates none of that member's rules.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/PROFILES.md#PROFILES%2F1.%20The%20boundary\",\"start_line\":28}],\"kind\":\"requires_reference_import_from\",\"meaning\":\"Profiles must import their used core concepts and relied-on families while retaining source ownership and without restating core rules.\"},\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"source\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:fcb3e9e8bb4e4ab57ffef14f92ab3625\",\"target\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:a8af91d16de288148f9b593e559aa36d\"}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0