, APIs, schedules,\\nconfigurations, documents and downstream obligations (P1, P6). The profile starts from these claims:\\n\\n- source systems enact domain function and remain sovereign for\\n  operational truth;\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/WORLD_MODEL.md#WORLD_MODEL%2F1.%20Position\",\"start_line\":63}],\"kind\":\"derived_semantic_layer_over\",\"meaning\":\"The world model interprets authoritative sources while their operational sovereignty remains intact; derivation does not transfer operational authority.\"},\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"source\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:e39b94f9c23281964c94da96edfba0a6\",\"target\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:87e03ae16d8303ea92b9eeaa8b53070b\"}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"relations","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:57e95ae4e3ea710dc2b05793bb593c23","key":832,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:57e95ae4e3ea710dc2b05793bb593c23\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:relation-kind:governing:semantic_import_into_context\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"qualifiers\":{\"conditions\":[\"Selected complete method basis and declared source/target contexts remain valid.\"],\"exceptions\":[\"Material changes invalidate the import until re-evaluation.\"],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":250,\"path\":\"standards/WORLD_MODEL.md\",\"quote\":\"For each\\nimport the source and target concept reference is the same listed\\nidentity; the relation expands applicability into the target context and\\nmints no alias or new semantic owner (P1, P6).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/WORLD_MODEL.md#WORLD_MODEL%2F2.%20Role%20and%20imports\",\"start_line\":247}],\"kind\":\"semantic_import_into_context\",\"meaning\":\"Source Project's unchanged FOUNDATIONS-owned identity gains applicability in the world-model context; the target endpoint is the applicability context, not a newly minted concept.\"},\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"source\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:71122f9461dadc023581a2b25fd7b04d\",\"target\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:9732f555ffd02a5cb722940a58180d9b\"}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"relations","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:0ad8fbfe87899ee399bd16db9ac6df29","key":833,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:0ad8fbfe87899ee399bd16db9ac6df29\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:relation-kind:governing:semantic_import_inventory_into_context\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"qualifiers\":{\"conditions\":[\"Selected complete method basis and declared source/target contexts remain valid.\"],\"exceptions\":[\"Material changes invalidate each import until re-evaluation.\"],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":246,\"path\":\"standards/WORLD_MODEL.md\",\"quote\":\"The meanings are adopted unchanged for this profile's scope under the\\nselected complete method basis. Their owner in FOUNDATIONS §2 is\\nretained, and a change to either context, any cited concept or taxonomy\\nclause, or the selected method basis invalidates the import until it is\\nreevaluated.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/WORLD_MODEL.md#WORLD_MODEL%2F2.%20Role%20and%20imports\",\"start_line\":242}],\"kind\":\"semantic_import_inventory_into_context\",\"meaning\":\"Each separately named Product, Install and Artifact identity is imported unchanged into world-model applicability; no ownership transfer or same-spelling import is licensed.\"},\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"source\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:60576aa2140b8aef363512775cb7cbce\",\"target\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:9732f555ffd02a5cb722940a58180d9b\"}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"relations","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:b3f85230412a35633ff0c88744f9410d","key":834,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:b3f85230412a35633ff0c88744f9410d\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:relation-kind:governing:directional_semantic_specialisation\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"qualifiers\":{\"conditions\":[\"Workspace has world-model-builder configuration and owns its source inputs, settings and publication lane.\",\"Both clauses are in the same selected complete method release and governed scope is world-model construction.\"],\"exceptions\":[\"General Source Projects outside the configuration are excluded.\",\"Changes to concepts, contexts, basis, configuration relation or scope invalidate the translation pending owner re-evaluation.\"],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":278,\"path\":\"standards/WORLD_MODEL.md\",\"quote\":\"- direction: source to target only; no inverse, equivalence, or\\n  assertion that every Source Project is a Builder Project;\\n- preserved meaning: a mutable workspace builds a next release cut and\\n  remains distinct from a Release Cut, Product, Install and Artifact;\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/WORLD_MODEL.md#WORLD_MODEL%2F2.%20Role%20and%20imports%2FBuilder%20Project%20specialisation\",\"start_line\":275}],\"kind\":\"directional_semantic_specialisation\",\"meaning\":\"Source Project→Builder Project preserves mutable next-cut workspace meaning and narrows configuration. It is not identity, general equivalence or inverse translation, and grants no authority over source taxonomy.\"},\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"source\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:71122f9461dadc023581a2b25fd7b04d\",\"target\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:43f89028fb972707e26975d939e746bb\"}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"relations","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:f1e119d02d958ef814a38c009d7ecaee","key":835,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:f1e119d02d958ef814a38c009d7ecaee\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:relation-kind:discovery:downstream_of\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"qualifiers\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":347,\"path\":\"standards/WORLD_MODEL.md\",\"quote\":\"Everything else is downstream\\nor supporting: epistemic overlays, query planes, mapping reports and\\ncompiled deterministic execution artifacts. Those surfaces may be\\nimportant; they do not create a second truth surface (P6, P1).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/WORLD_MODEL.md#WORLD_MODEL%2F3.%20What%20a%20world%20model%20is%2FSingle%20truth%20surface\",\"start_line\":344}],\"kind\":\"downstream_of\",\"meaning\":\"Projections and query facilities are downstream or supporting surfaces, without a second constitutional truth surface.\"},\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"source\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:a7d93851d417c75f3d15373901149cb8\",\"target\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:61857acd4f5f365bed011dce43b5991a\"}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"relations","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:7b8f782af895b6ab6417a6f237784fe9","key":836,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:7b8f782af895b6ab6417a6f237784fe9\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:relation-kind:governing:inherits_epistemic_standing_from\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"qualifiers\":{\"conditions\":[\"No promotion-gate result meets the exact subject/basis predicate.\"],\"exceptions\":[\"Formally closed publication kinds require real promotion-gate backing; independent entity cuts do not inherit this status.\"],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":479,\"path\":\"standards/WORLD_MODEL.md\",\"quote\":\"This status attaches to the construct and to overlays built on it. A\\npublished Markov-object overlay is a candidate-class overlay of a\\ncandidate construct, not a certified blanket of a formally established\\nobject. It does not attach to entity cuts: an entity cut is lawful\\npublished truth on its own admissibility test (§9) and does not inherit\\nthe construct's candidate status. A candidate entity that has not met\\nthat test is a candidate; a published entity cut is not (P3, P6).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/WORLD_MODEL.md#WORLD_MODEL%2F4.%20The%20Markov-object%20construct%2FEpistemic%20status\",\"start_line\":473}],\"kind\":\"inherits_epistemic_standing_from\",\"meaning\":\"Overlays inherit candidate-class standing from the construct; verification for publication does not promote the theory.\"},\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"source\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:c143b6f091bd0e5b8b35148ab55197eb\",\"target\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:f0813b08ad22c7e3d02e681158434ded\"}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"relations","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:a9b090ed67b1d377d90dec638d476262","key":837,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:a9b090ed67b1d377d90dec638d476262\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:relation-kind:discovery:optional_geometric_overlay_on\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"qualifiers\":{\"conditions\":[\"A declared representation space exists.\"],\"exceptions\":[\"Overlay absence does not weaken the entity cut.\"],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":578,\"path\":\"standards/WORLD_MODEL.md\",\"quote\":\"| Markov-Object Overlay | an optional geometric overlay on an entity cut, admissible only where a declared representation space exists; it adds an identity direction, projection support and effective coordinate, constructed and verified under §10; the overlay strengthens an entity cut, and its absence does not weaken one | P3, P6 |\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/WORLD_MODEL.md#WORLD_MODEL%2F6.%20Units\",\"start_line\":578}],\"kind\":\"optional_geometric_overlay_on\",\"meaning\":\"The overlay adds verified geometry to an independently admissible semantic cut.\"},\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"source\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:c143b6f091bd0e5b8b35148ab55197eb\",\"target\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:ea7976cc8986c83e51397ea3c9641497\"}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b