:"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:b065f2c12d6837b3e57a061fc9ea0131\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:relation-kind:governing:conditionally_governs_by_adoption\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"qualifiers\":{\"conditions\":[\"The tenant declares adoption of exact shared design surfaces.\"],\"exceptions\":[\"If none is adopted, the tenant explicitly declares none.\"],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":18,\"path\":\"standards/templates/build_tenants/variant/design/README_TEMPLATE.md\",\"quote\":\"List the exact shared surfaces from `build_tenants/common/` that this tenant\\nadopts.\\n\\n- Shared design law under `build_tenants/common/design/`\\n- Shared qualification law under `build_tenants/common/qualification/` when it\\n  constrains tenant-local tests or evidence\\n\\nIf no common surface is currently adopted, say that explicitly.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/templates/build_tenants/variant/design/README_TEMPLATE.md#Tenant%20Design%2FAdopted%20Common%20Surfaces\",\"start_line\":11}],\"kind\":\"conditionally_governs_by_adoption\",\"meaning\":\"Exact adopted common design law governs the tenant's local design only under the declared adoption; proximity to common is insufficient.\"},\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"source\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:f1ae4372889c4213ac98c1d03a4317b8\",\"target\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:f3ceb5e45f636cbf468d85358c2cad82\"}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"relations","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:4acea888079c765c762351ced00e662b","key":849,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:4acea888079c765c762351ced00e662b\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:relation-kind:governing:constrains_document_shape\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"qualifiers\":{\"conditions\":[\"The override shape is resolved from the applicable Product Definition's exact installed basis.\"],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":8,\"path\":\"standards/templates/build_tenants/variant/design/fp/README_TEMPLATE.md\",\"quote\":\"Resolve\\n`standards/templates/build_tenants/variant/design/fp/edge-overrides/EDGE_OVERRIDE_TEMPLATE.json`\\nfrom the exact installed STDO basis in the applicable Product Definition and\\nuse it as the authoritative template shape for edge override files.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/templates/build_tenants/variant/design/fp/README_TEMPLATE.md#Tenant%20F_P%20Customization\",\"start_line\":5}],\"kind\":\"constrains_document_shape\",\"meaning\":\"The exact installed edge-override template constrains override-file shape for tenant F_P customization; it does not authorize or execute constructive work.\"},\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"source\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:9863f4ace5b88bce6ff8db5d105f0561\",\"target\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:ee07b57051997beacd910a40317b1de5\"}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:c9d8734f75ab2b25090e86c2baa6fe67","key":850,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:88c24e636e936c1563b71094f6254158\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:c9d8734f75ab2b25090e86c2baa6fe67\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"Entering an existing STDO-governed project.\"],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":78,\"path\":\"plugins/spec/references/GETTING_STARTED.md\",\"quote\":\"`sync` may install bytes. It never follows the moving selector or edits the\\nProduct Definition. The shell command `stdo status` reports basis and install\\nhealth; it is not a Product-delivery status report.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/plugins/spec/references/GETTING_STARTED.md#Using%20STDO%2F1.%20Get%20Ready%20To%20Work%2FExisting%20STDO-Governed%20Project\",\"start_line\":76},{\"end_line\":94,\"path\":\"plugins/spec/references/GETTING_STARTED.md\",\"quote\":\"Acquire item 7 under the basis's `ACTIVATION.md` section 2, Acquisition: a\\nderived surface whose sources are current where one serves the task,\\notherwise the owning sections that decide it. Do not bulk-load the\\nstandards corpus. A new LLM should be able to state this\\ncompact basis before it changes anything:\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/plugins/spec/references/GETTING_STARTED.md#Using%20STDO%2F1.%20Get%20Ready%20To%20Work%2FExisting%20STDO-Governed%20Project\",\"start_line\":90}],\"statement\":\"Require exactly one applicable stdo_<label>.json for the requested Product scope; nesting implies no governance. Start read-only with stdo status --definition <path-to-definition> --verify. Only if the cut is absent and installation authorized, sync that exact pinned basis and verify again; sync neither follows a moving selector nor edits the definition. Before acting resolve bootstrap, accepted Product-owned frame basis, current Goals, Intent/Product, only affected requirements/accepted design, admitted work carrier, and only the exact needed owner standard. Acquire current derived surfaces when sufficient, otherwise deciding owner sections under ACTIVATION §2; do not bulk-load standards. A new LLM should be able to state definition identity/path, cut/manifest digest, current outcome, carrier/re-entry, actor/operation/subject/write territory, claim/evidence boundary, stop/re-entry conditions, then one bounded ACTION. Action comes last; this context qualifies work without prescribing irrelevant internals.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:7ab26fc33bc8886838b7936453ff592c","key":851,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:88c24e636e936c1563b71094f6254158\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:7ab26fc33bc8886838b7936453ff592c\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"The host loads a separate plugin copy.\"],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":122,\"path\":\"plugins/spec/references/GETTING_STARTED.md\",\"quote\":\"Basis verification checks the selected installed method. If the host loads a\\nseparate copy of this plugin, also compare that actual loaded root against\\n`auxiliary.plugin.members` in the verified installed-release manifest. Check\\nevery managed member's relative path and SHA-256, including both host plugin\\nmanifests and all referenced skill and guidance files. Missing, changed or\\nunexpected managed files are a mismatch. A matching plugin version string,\\nname, repository or advertised install location does not establish identity.\\nRecord the host-selected plugin root and the exact manifest used for this\\ncomparison; if the host cannot identify that root, installed-plugin identity\\nis unresolved. Keep host-managed caches or metadata outside the compared\\nplugin member tree.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/plugins/spec/references/GETTING_STARTED.md#Using%20STDO%2F1.%20Get%20Ready%20To%20Work%2FVerify%20The%20Host%27s%20Plugin%20Copy\",\"start_line\":112}],\"statement\":\"Compare the actual host-loaded root to auxiliary.plugin.members in the verified installed-release manifest, checking every managed relative path and SHA-256, both host manifests and all referenced skills/guidance. Missing, changed or unexpected managed files mismatch; version, name, repository or advertised location does not establish identity. Record actual root and exact manifest; inability to identify the root leaves identity unresolved. Keep host caches/metadata outside the compared tree. Resolve actual method members and anchors through Product Basis Selection before a skill route; installation and skill names do not change the selected Product basis.\",\"uncertainty\":\"No actual loaded root or manifest is supplied.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:7e4fc69050e7b5a79a9d6958367a1263","key":852,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:e951012fd928af6b3146db11b940936a\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:7e4fc69050e7b5a79a9d6958367a1263\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"Coordinated distribution has been published and placeholders bound at its RC cut under RELEASE §§6–7.\"],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":177,\"path\":\"plugins/spec/references/GETTING_STARTED.md\",\"quote\":\"The exact qualified cut install is the missing-tool path. The explicit\\n`pipx install --force` branch upgrades an older installation. Do not continue\\nto `stdo install` unless the final version check accepts `stdo-toolchain\\n<toolchain-minimum>` or newer.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/plugins/spec/references/GETTING_STARTED.md#Using%20STDO%2F1.%20Get%20Ready%20To%20Work%2FNew%20Project\",\"start_line\":174}],\"statement\":\"Select one immutable cut v<version>-rc.<n> and qualified ref specification_methodology/v<version>-rc.<n>, with toolchain minimum and Git installation spec bound to that ref and specification_methodology subdirectory. The example installs via pipx if stdo is absent and forces installation if the version comparison fails for an existing tool. Its parser requires three numeric components with optional suffix, rejects invalid versions and compares numeric tuples. Report and recheck the resulting version; do not proceed to stdo install unless it meets the minimum. Then install and verify the exact cut.\",\"uncertainty\":\"The concrete release, qualified ref and minimum are unbound placeholders.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:19b70ffd5be9726933bb5a45e2be3922","key":853,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:e951012fd928af6b3146db11b940936a\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:19b70ffd5be9726933bb5a45e2be3922\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":223,\"path\":\"plugins/spec/references/GETTING_STARTED.md\",\"quote\":\"# Preflight every source and target before creating a directory or file.\\nprepared = []\\nfor source, target in pairs:\\n    if not source.is_file():\\n        raise SystemExit(f\\\"missing STDO setup source: {source}\\\")\\n    payload = source.read_bytes()\\n    if target.exists() or target.is_symlink():\\n        raise SystemExit(\\n            f\\\"refusing to overwrite existing STDO setup file: {target}\\\"\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/plugins/spec/references/GETTING_STARTED.md#Using%20STDO%2F1.%20Get%20Ready%20To%20Work%2FNew%20Project\",\"start_line\":215},{\"end_line\":299,\"path\":\"plugins/spec/references/GETTING_STARTED.md\",\"quote\":\"    # Each replacement is an atomic rename into a name reserved by this run.\\n    for stage, (target, _, _) in zip(staged.copy(), prepared, strict=True):\\n        stat = stage.stat()\\n        remember_owned(target, (stat.st_dev, stat.st_ino))\\n        os.replace(stage, target)\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/plugins/spec/references/GETTING_STARTED.md#Using%20STDO%2F1.%20Get%20Ready%20To%20Work%2FNew%20Project\",\"start_line\":295}],\"statement\":\"Resolve both templates from the installed cut; example destinations are ./stdo_default.json and ./specification/REFERENCE_FRAME_BASIS.md. The copy program requires a nonempty even sequence of source/target arguments, rejects duplicate absolute targets, preflights every source as a file and every target as absent including symlinks, reads source bytes and permission bits, and requires the nearest existing/symlink ancestor to be a directory before creating anything. It creates missing parents, tolerating a racing existing directory only if it is a directory; stages bytes in target-parent temporary files with source permission bits, flush and fsync; reserves every final path with exclusive creation at mode 0600; remembers device/inode ownership; and individually atomically replaces reserved names. On BaseException it removes final paths only while their identities match owned identities, removes remaining stages, attempts reverse removal of created directories while ignoring OSError, and reraises.\",\"uncertainty\":\"This describes example control flow, not successful execution, whole-operation atomicity or verified concurrency safety.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:f5c89e6b7f7cbbb5f0b792a9f530fe36","key":854,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:e951012fd928af6b3146db11b940936a\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:f5c89e6b7f7cbbb5f0b792a9f530fe36\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":322,\"path\":\"plugins/spec/references/GETTING_STARTED.md\",\"quote\":\"Use the installed cut's `templates/README.md` to fill the definition over the\\nexisting layout. Bind a real Product-owned reference-frame basis, `WHAT`,\\n`HOW`, work carriers, and every known Product composition edge. Replace every\\nplaceholder. A delegated agent may draft a complete provisional basis, but it\\nmust return that exact draft and stop for Product-owner ratification. The\\nProduct owner records and admits acceptance; the drafting agent cannot record,\\nadmit, or infer that acceptance itself. A copied or completed template is not\\naccepted merely because it exists.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/plugins/spec/references/GETTING_STARTED.md#Using%20STDO%2F1.%20Get%20Ready%20To%20Work%2FNew%20Project\",\"start_line\":315}],\"statement\":\"Use the installed template guide over the existing layout, bind a real Product-owned frame basis, WHAT, HOW, work carriers and every known composition edge, and replace every placeholder. A delegated drafter may produce a complete provisional basis but must return that exact draft and stop for Product-owner ratification; only the owner records and admits acceptance, which copying or completing a template does not establish. Then sync and verify the definition, preview bootstrap with --dry-run, and install only marker-owned bootstrap. The packaged guide supplies field bindings and the frame template supplies the declaration.\",\"uncertainty\":\"Template contents and Product ratification are not supplied.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:083ae9afa4f96024b543648ddff9ef8a","key":855,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:88c24e636e936c1563b71094f6254158\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:083ae9afa4f96024b543648ddff9ef8a\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"Install examples apply after coordinated publication.\"],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":343,\"path\":\"plugins/spec/references/GETTING_STARTED.md\",\"quote\":\"The following install commands apply after coordinated publication.\\nThe `spec` plugin version and immutable repository cut are aligned at\\n`<version>-rc.<n>`, bound at the RC cut under `RELEASE.md` section 7. An\\nearlier cut retains its own plugin payload and never moves. The Specification Stack marketplace name is `specification_stack`.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/plugins/spec/references/GETTING_STARTED.md#Using%20STDO%2F1.%20Get%20Ready%20To%20Work%2FInstall%20The%20Shared%20Skills\",\"start_line\":340},{\"end_line\":376,\"path\":\"plugins/spec/references/GETTING_STARTED.md\",\"quote\":\"Natural-language invocation remains valid. In chat, `stdo status` requests\\nProduct/work status through the skill. In a shell, `stdo status --definition\\n...` remains the toolchain command for installed-basis health.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/plugins/spec/references/GETTING_STARTED.md#Using%20STDO%2F1.%20Get%20Ready%20To%20Work%2FInstall%20The%20Shared%20Skills\",\"start_line\":374}],\"statement\":\"Align spec plugin version and immutable repository cut at the RC version under RELEASE §7; earlier cuts retain unmoving payloads. Marketplace identity is specification_stack. Claude's example adds foolishimp/specification_methodology@<qualified-ref> then installs spec@specification_stack; Codex's adds that repository with --ref <qualified-ref> then adds the same plugin. Both hosts consume identical workflow skill bytes. For each of help, ticket, work, review and status, conversational 'stdo <verb>' maps to portable stdo-<verb>, Claude /spec:stdo-<verb> and Codex $spec:stdo-<verb>. Natural-language invocation remains valid. Chat status means Product/work status; shell status means basis health.\",\"uncertainty\":\"The release placeholder is not a resolved published ref.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:2c944816a4d279b5813e38f7eeaeac72","key":856,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:88c24e636e936c1563b71094f6254158\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:9a04da2e6f16b4be2e53345a44c2c932\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:2c944816a4d279b5813e38f7eeaeac72\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":393,\"path\":\"plugins/spec/references/GETTING_STARTED.md\",\"quote\":\"Reuse it while the question, subject,\\nbasis and supporting premises still apply; a role change alone is no reason to\\nrepeat the classification. The owning rule is `SPEC_METHOD.md` section 4,\\nComputed classification and treatment, in a basis that contains that successor rule.\\nOn an earlier basis, re-enter its owning intake and construction law; this\\nguide does not adopt a successor.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/plugins/spec/references/GETTING_STARTED.md#Using%20STDO%2F2.%20Iterate%20Requirements\",\"start_line\":388}],\"statement\":\"Every feature, bug, failed test, operator finding, scenario failure and release concern begins with intake triage; its label does not choose re-entry. Start with declared authority/owner routes, complete relevant Public serialization changes and accepted-design trace coverage, retaining exact tool inputs/outputs and unknowns. Judge residual meaning/materiality and record support in the existing carrier; reuse while question, subject, basis and premises hold, regardless of role change. Use the successor computed-classification rule only in a basis containing it; earlier bases retain their own intake/construction law. Repair a helper violating unchanged requirements within its grant; reprice only when the selected outcome needs new governing meaning. Candidate bytes do not choose that outcome. Keep unclear owner choices explicit and resolve only what the next action needs.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:ade3866f1d81c35f603c8a936944524f","key":857,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:9a04da2e6f16b4be2e53345a44c2c932\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:ade3866f1d81c35f603c8a936944524f\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"Before substantive execution.\"],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":437,\"path\":\"plugins/spec/references/GETTING_STARTED.md\",\"quote\":\"`Ticket-shaped` describes required execution-contract fields; it does not mean\\n“create a ticket.” Drafting, admission, and execution may occur in the same\\ninvocation. A drafted or rejected contract stops before construction, while an\\nadmitted one does not require another ticket, turn, or approval ceremony.\\nThe admitted result names the Product-bound mechanism and authority, exact\\ncontract identity or digest, decision, and evidence; the drafting model cannot\\nsupply those coordinates by assertion. The contract also names an authorized\\nProduct-bound durable result/evidence surface. Every result, withheld closure,\\nand residual is recorded there before return; a conversation return alone is\\nnot durable evidence.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/plugins/spec/references/GETTING_STARTED.md#Using%20STDO%2F2.%20Iterate%20Requirements%2FFind%20The%20First%20Changed%20Layer\",\"start_line\":428}],\"statement\":\"Establish upstream authority before selecting a carrier and derive/admit one run contract from the first matching carrier row. Without authority stop or re-enter; no substitute ticket. Reuse an exact admitted ticket if it covers the work. Otherwise use a durable ticket plus contract under ticket-state authority only for independent state beyond the admitted sprint, or beyond the run without a sprint; use a manifest-local iteration entry for work ending in its sprint; otherwise an intake-drafted contract for authorized work ending in the run. Ticket-shaped means fields, not compulsory ticket creation. Drafting/admission/execution may share an invocation; drafted/rejected stops construction, admitted requires no extra turn/ticket/ceremony. Bind mechanism/authority, contract identity or digest, decision/evidence and authorized durable result surface; assertion is insufficient. Record every result, withheld closure and residual before return. Cite an existing exact grant once without renewed authorization. For discovered obligations beyond the local boundary, mutate ticket state only if already granted; otherwise retain in authorized durable evidence/enclosing carrier, withhold closure and return re-entry plus an uninvoked stdo ticket route.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:f4c1301f673fa91e1df2cef24cde5298","key":858,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:9a04da2e6f16b4be2e53345a44c2c932\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:f4c1301f673fa91e1df2cef24cde5298\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":454,\"path\":\"plugins/spec/references/GETTING_STARTED.md\",\"quote\":\"The base ticket fields are exactly `id`, `title`, `type`, `ticket_category`,\\n`status`, `goal`, `change_intent`, `change_class`, `re_entry_point`,\\n`triaged_at`, `created_at`, and `updated_at`. Execution admission additionally\\nbinds `target_truth`, relevant `superseded_truth`, `closure_law`,\\n`evaluation_criteria`, `non_closure_conditions`, and `proof_surface`. Record\\ndependencies where applicable. The Product Definition locates the actual\\nlanes; `.ai-workspace/tickets/` is only the default.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/plugins/spec/references/GETTING_STARTED.md#Using%20STDO%2F2.%20Iterate%20Requirements%2FFind%20The%20First%20Changed%20Layer\",\"start_line\":448}],\"statement\":\"Base ticket fields are exactly id, title, type, ticket_category, status, goal, change_intent, change_class, re_entry_point, triaged_at, created_at and updated_at. Execution admission also binds target_truth, relevant superseded_truth, closure_law, evaluation_criteria, non_closure_conditions and proof_surface. Record applicable dependencies. Actual lanes come from the Product Definition; .ai-workspace/tickets/ is only a default.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:985f509fcbc0f35a7a352d97de2b754e","key":859,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:9a04da2e6f16b4be2e53345a44c2c932\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:985f509fcbc0f35a7a352d97de2b754e\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"The selected class is requirement_reprice.\"],\"exceptions\":[\"An existing requirement lacking structural realization re-enters design.\",\"Current requirements/design with deviating code uses realization_refactor.\"],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":473,\"path\":\"plugins/spec/references/GETTING_STARTED.md\",\"quote\":\"1. confirm that Goals, Intent, and Product still support the requirement;\\n2. establish the new present-tense requirement version as the sole operative\\n   truth; supersede or withdraw a published live domain artifact instead of\\n   silently correcting it in place;\\n3. give each requirement family `Family`, lifecycle `Status`, and `Category`;\\n4. state stable obligations and explicit acceptance criteria;\\n5. provide written testcase or other proof authority;\\n6. expose lifecycle gaps rather than letting design or code decide them;\\n7. leave incidental realization choice in design; and\\n8. re-derive affected design, scenarios, code, and proof.\\n\\nIf the requirement already exists but its structural realization is missing,\\nre-enter design. If requirements and design are current and code deviated, use\\n`realization_refactor`. Current code is evidence, not authority.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/plugins/spec/references/GETTING_STARTED.md#Using%20STDO%2F2.%20Iterate%20Requirements%2FChange%20Requirement%20Truth\",\"start_line\":460}],\"statement\":\"Confirm Goals/Intent/Product support; establish a present-tense successor as sole operative truth, superseding or withdrawing published live domain artifacts instead of silently editing them. Each family receives Family, lifecycle Status and Category, stable obligations, explicit acceptance criteria and written testcase or other proof authority. Expose lifecycle gaps; design/code cannot decide them. Leave incidental realization choices in design and rederive affected design, scenarios, code and proof. Current code is evidence, not authority.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:cc1c6d275b00dd4fef453231ceb34cff","key":860,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:88c24e636e936c1563b71094f6254158\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:cc1c6d275b00dd4fef453231ceb34cff\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":486,\"path\":\"plugins/spec/references/GETTING_STARTED.md\",\"quote\":\"Raw prompt wording does not authorize implementation. Code work begins when an\\nadmitted work carrier supplies a reconstructable basis:\\n\\n- selected Product outcome;\\n- lawful re-entry point and target truth;\\n- governing requirement and accepted design where required;\\n- smallest coherent affected relation set;\\n- exact operation grant, mutation subject, and write territory;\\n- closure law, evaluation criteria, and non-closure conditions; and\\n- proof, review, stop, and upstream re-entry conditions.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/plugins/spec/references/GETTING_STARTED.md#Using%20STDO%2F3.%20Start%20Code%20Development%20And%20Testing\",\"start_line\":477}],\"statement\":\"Raw prompt wording is insufficient for implementation: an admitted carrier must reconstruct Product outcome, lawful re-entry/target truth, required requirement/accepted design, smallest coherent affected relation set, exact grant/subject/write territory, closure/evaluation/non-closure law and proof/review/stop/upstream re-entry conditions. Under an adopted optional Executive profile, Executive owns bounded attention, activation, consumption, Product priority/boundary effect, disposition, checkpoint and next already-authorized action without automatic implementation/publication/new decision authority; Worker owns bounded construction/tests/self-review without automatic acceptance/independent review/continuation; Reviewer owns exact-claim independent evaluation/technical triage without repair/priority/disposition/next activation. Labels grant nothing. Accepted frame basis binds actors, capabilities, authorities, results, scales, cutoff, hard stops and invalidation. An actor may span frames across claims only with valid grants and independence. False applicability omits, true requires an exact result, unknown remains unresolved; a caller list proves no coverage. Use a sufficient basis-permitted direct Writer; material dependency/authority/context boundaries can require coordination and independence can require Reviewer, neither automatically. Executive must enter separately bound Writer activation before file or Git edits.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:c6f18d114d986302003a57b694db7e26","key":861,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:88c24e636e936c1563b71094f6254158\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:c6f18d114d986302003a57b694db7e26\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":549,\"path\":\"plugins/spec/references/GETTING_STARTED.md\",\"quote\":\"Closure means all applicable obligations are satisfied, supporting evidence\\nis valid, required judgments and owner rulings are present, and no active\\nnon-closure condition remains. Review checks those conditions; holding a review\\ndoes not close the work. Record state only under the existing mutation grant.\\nRepair invalidates affected claims and support, while unrelated valid results\\nremain usable. Candidate qualification, publication and adoption are distinct\\noutcomes with their own conditions.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/plugins/spec/references/GETTING_STARTED.md#Using%20STDO%2F3.%20Start%20Code%20Development%20And%20Testing%2FDerive%20Tests%20From%20Authority\",\"start_line\":543}],\"statement\":\"Derive expected results through carrier → triage → re-entry → requirement/design/module/closure law. Match proof breadth to claim: unit/module law, integration/participating boundaries, harnessed sandbox UAT/deterministic composed path, live sandbox UAT/real external service or worker when claimed, installed-development/built or installed Product's declared public path. Begin with the cheapest adequate focused falsifier; broaden at candidate boundary or earlier for risk. Green evidence on the wrong subject, fixture, route, authority or substitute boundary does not close a claim. Delegated Worker returns one exact candidate/evidence and stops; Product authority decides required assessment, Reviewer when required returns a closed result for authorized disposition, and sufficient direct Writer records without adding review. Closure is all applicable obligations satisfied, valid support, required judgments/rulings and no active non-closure condition; review occurrence is not closure. State changes require existing grants; repair invalidates only affected claims/support. Qualification, publication and adoption retain separate conditions.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:57f777c9ee4744ac0e7e854d8777e4c7","key":862,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:88c24e636e936c1563b71094f6254158\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:57f777c9ee4744ac0e7e854d8777e4c7\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"Monitoring or helping triage.\"],\"exceptions\":[\"State change requires separate user authorization.\"],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":561,\"path\":\"plugins/spec/references/GETTING_STARTED.md\",\"quote\":\"Monitoring is read-only unless the user separately authorizes a state change.\\nRead in this order:\\n\\n1. verify the selected STDO basis;\\n2. read current Goals;\\n3. read authoritative active, backlog, and completed work state;\\n4. identify the accepted checkpoint and current workspace delta;\\n5. inspect observed tests, installed/runtime evidence, and exact reviews; and\\n6. compare claims only when they share the same subject and basis.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/plugins/spec/references/GETTING_STARTED.md#Using%20STDO%2F4.%20Monitor%20And%20Help%20Triage\",\"start_line\":553}],\"statement\":\"Monitor read-only in order: verify basis, read Goals, authoritative active/backlog/completed state, accepted checkpoint/workspace delta, tests/runtime/installed evidence/exact reviews, then compare only same-subject/same-basis claims. Tools supply identity/state/delta/freshness; missing producer/input stays unknown and semantic sufficiency remains supported judgment. Continuation consumes existing outcome/grant/facts/judgments/rulings and refreshes only changed inputs/affected support. Preserve original rulings separately; existing carriers retain reusable judgment question, exact subject/basis, evidence, actor/authority, conclusion, uncertainty and revising observation. Recovery separates requested outcome, observed effects and owner retry rule; refusal/no effect proves neither completion nor need to retry, and unknown effects remain unknown. Suspension/conclusion records actual outcome and surviving obligations under existing grant. Default shell examples apply only to definition-bound default layout. Status should lead with outcome and include basis health, accepted movement, active work/dependencies, exact proof/review, blockers/residuals/drift/uncertainty, triage/decisions and next already-authorized action; counts or prose alone prove no progress. Under optional Executive profile Reviewer may supply technical severity, impact, confidence, blast radius, workaround, repair complexity, regression risk and uncertainty; Executive combines these with complete Product/release/MVP view for priority, boundary effect, disposition/action. Frame basis owns scales/cutoff/hard stops; no universal P2 cutoff. Proposed class/re-entry does not silently ticket, widen release boundary, reprioritize or dispose.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:b891ca82d4491af6f0d3d127f22b85f3","key":863,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:88c24e636e936c1563b71094f6254158\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:b891ca82d4491af6f0d3d127f22b85f3\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"A listed stop condition is encountered.\"],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":627,\"path\":\"plugins/spec/references/GETTING_STARTED.md\",\"quote\":\"| zero or several Product Definitions apply | stop and disambiguate Product scope |\\n| installed cut or manifest does not verify | stop; never substitute mutable source |\\n| reference-frame basis is missing or a placeholder | return the missing Product-owned acceptance basis |\\n| no admitted run-scoped execution contract exists | select the smallest carrier, draft and validate the contract, then continue in the same invocation only if admitted |\\n| requirement truth is missing | re-enter requirements, not code |\\n| structural decision is missing | re-enter design |\\n| code and test disagree | reconcile through governing authority |\\n| independent review is required (the boundaries TICKETS §7 names) | stabilise one exact review subject as EVALUATION §3 Protocol states (frozen before material reference exposure where method qualification requires it; otherwise an immutable identity or an equivalent exact-subject relation sufficient for the claim) and activate Reviewer |\\n| a finding is adjacent to the current claim | return it as triage input; do not automatically block |\\n| requested effect exceeds the grant | refuse and return to Product-owned decision authority |\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/plugins/spec/references/GETTING_STARTED.md#Using%20STDO%2FCommon%20Stops\",\"start_line\":618}],\"statement\":\"Zero/several definitions → stop and disambiguate; unverifiable cut/manifest → stop without mutable replacement; missing/placeholder frame basis → return missing Product acceptance basis; missing admitted run contract → smallest carrier, draft/validate and continue same invocation only on admission; missing requirement truth → requirements; missing structure → design; code/test disagreement → governing authority. When TICKETS §7 requires independence, stabilize the exact review subject under EVALUATION §3: freeze before material reference exposure where method qualification requires, otherwise use immutable identity or sufficient equivalent exact-subject relation, then activate Reviewer. Adjacent findings are triage input, not automatic blockers. Effects exceeding grant are refused and returned to Product decision authority.\",\"uncertainty\":\"The referenced review-boundary and protocol owners are not supplied.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:f424e4a7622b9910fb1142c12ab9fe2d","key":864,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:a12d6bbf803663ff616848a01e97de98\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:f424e4a7622b9910fb1142c12ab9fe2d\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":655,\"path\":\"plugins/spec/references/GETTING_STARTED.md\",\"quote\":\"The Claude host provides a manual-only `refresh` loader for the full exact\\nowning members of one registry entry. The Codex host resolves and reads those\\nexact installed members directly; the five daily workflow skills remain\\nbyte-shared. Daily work should read the smallest relevant source surface.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/plugins/spec/references/GETTING_STARTED.md#Using%20STDO%2FOwning%20References\",\"start_line\":652}],\"statement\":\"Resolve owning references from the exact installed basis selected by the Product Definition. Claude's full-entry loader is manual-only; Codex directly resolves and reads exact installed members. Five daily skills remain byte-shared. Daily work should acquire the smallest relevant surface.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:2f42334e56485edb10f9ac7c8ebab113","key":865,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:c80654beefe2552a98ab1258d238ff01\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:2f42334e56485edb10f9ac7c8ebab113\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":41,\"path\":\"plugins/spec/references/PRODUCT_BASIS.md\",\"quote\":\"Zero definitions, multiple applicable definitions, failed verification, or any\\nidentity, path, basis, manifest, installation, or validity mismatch stops the\\ncalling skill before effects. Report the exact candidates or mismatch and the\\nrequired re-entry; do not repair it implicitly.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/plugins/spec/references/PRODUCT_BASIS.md#Product%20Basis%20Selection%2FProcedure\",\"start_line\":38}],\"statement\":\"State requested scope from the exact request and Product identities/claims; insufficient distinction leaves scope unresolved. Discover candidate definitions only within the authorized workspace search boundary. Filename/current directory/nearest file/nesting are discovery only, not selection or composition. Determine applicability from definition identity and owned what/how/ticketing/bounded-context/explicit-composition bindings; paths select only when explicitly scope-bound. Require exactly one: zero returns unresolved scope, multiple returns every remaining identity/path and requests disambiguation; never choose by proximity, familiarity, recency or label. Read-only status verification must report matching definition identity/path, immutable basis URI and manifest SHA-256, installed:true, valid:true and no failures. Do not sync/adopt/install, substitute mutable source or nearby Product. Return scope, identity/path, URI/cut, digest and result; only then may caller continue under its own authority/effect boundary. Any listed mismatch stops before effects and reports exact candidates/mismatch and re-entry without implicit repair.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:22cc4a1bcc96864f59611fca934c9b5a","key":866,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:5f470cb500e8e3245082004482b762e6\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:22cc4a1bcc96864f59611fca934c9b5a\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"The Product basis has verified.\"],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":70,\"path\":\"plugins/spec/references/PRODUCT_BASIS.md\",\"quote\":\"Resolve the member without its fragment, then locate the exact anchor in\\nthose verified bytes; for example, `#7-closed-result-and-reuse` selects\\nACTIVATION's reuse owner. A missing member, anchor, manifest mismatch or\\ncontent mismatch leaves the route unresolved. Acquire no replacement from a\\ncheckout, moving selector, later cut or neighbouring Product. A frame is a\\nmember too: verify its own bytes and the local sources and section digests\\nlisted in `standards/frames/FRAME_INPUTS.json` before treating it as current.\\nThis identity check does not establish semantic fidelity or task sufficiency.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/plugins/spec/references/PRODUCT_BASIS.md#Product%20Basis%20Selection%2FRead%20A%20Member%20From%20That%20Basis\",\"start_line\":63}],\"statement\":\"Use the verified definition's basis URI and manifest matching manifest_sha256. Require ACTIVATION.md in standards inventory and its resolved SHA-256 equal to the declared member digest; apply equivalent checks to every selected member. Returned URI must equal requested URI and path lie in the verified installation; path alone proves neither membership nor bytes. Resolve without fragment, then find exact anchor in verified bytes. Missing member/anchor or digest/content mismatch leaves the route unresolved; no checkout, moving-selector, later-cut or neighboring-Product replacement. For frames also verify local sources/section digests in FRAME_INPUTS.json before currency claims. Identity checking proves neither fidelity nor sufficiency. Return exact basis URI/manifest digest, member digest, selected anchor and unresolved dependencies for every acquired member; caller keeps its authority/effect boundary.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:f874cef10f960b10d24293548d7688b4","key":867,"