 and design trace coverage; bind inputs, producer, outputs and freshness. File diff alone is not Public comparison and trace presence is not sufficiency. Missing targets/serialization/mappings stay unknown; invent no result and do not treat distribution manager as worksite analyzer. Reuse applicable facts/judgments after checking question, subject, basis, support and revising observation; role change alone needs no reclassification. Judge only residual needed for smallest lawful path, recording once; unresolved choices remain with owners. Use one bounded discriminator when sufficient. Reject/repair helper violations of unchanged Public requirements inside grant; changed governing meaning requires requirement-owner re-entry. Bytes choose no outcome and enlarge no grant.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:0b8263a2955e6b922c0edc25d331eb82","key":888,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:33beae1c984885116b47bb6d76386149\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:0b8263a2955e6b922c0edc25d331eb82\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":90,\"path\":\"plugins/spec/skills/stdo-work/SKILL.md\",\"quote\":\"3. Validate and admit or reject that exact contract. Drafting, admission, and\\n   execution may occur in the same invocation, but ticket presence, `active`\\n   status, a generic work request, or the model's own draft cannot supply\\n   admission. Continue only after deterministic admission or an exact human\\n   override of the bounded contract. Record the Product-bound admitting\\n   mechanism and authority, exact contract identity or digest, decision, and\\n   evidence. If those coordinates are absent, return the missing authority and\\n   stop.\\n   Consume an existing exact owner instruction or admitted grant when it\\n   already covers this contract; cite it instead of requesting the same\\n   authorization again. Record the binding, not another approval round.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/plugins/spec/skills/stdo-work/SKILL.md#STDO%20Work%2FEstablish%20The%20Work%20Basis\",\"start_line\":80}],\"statement\":\"Establish upstream work authority first or stop before carrier selection. Select first applicable source: covering exact admitted durable ticket; otherwise authorized durable ticket for independent state beyond sprint or run; otherwise admitted sprint plus local iteration for work ending by sprint close; otherwise current-run intake draft. Do not automatically invoke ticketing; absence neither requires nor authorizes it. Bind Goal/exact instruction, change_intent/class/re-entry, target_truth/relevant superseded_truth, closure_law, governing requirement/design, checkpoint, affected relation set/write territory, criteria/non-closure/proof and authorized available Product durable result surface; absent surface refuses admission. Validate exact contract; only deterministic admission or exact human override permits continuation, supported by mechanism/authority, identity/digest, decision/evidence. Presence, active status, generic request and self-draft are insufficient; missing coordinates stop. Cite covering existing exact grants without new approval. Re-enter first changed layer: requirement successor becomes sole truth with published predecessor superseded/withdrawn; structural design admitted before reliance; realization proves unchanged Goals/Intent/Product/requirements/design. New beyond-boundary obligations get ticket mutation only under exact grant; otherwise retain in authorized durable evidence/enclosing carrier, withhold closure and return re-entry/uninvoked stdo-ticket route. Chat alone is not durable evidence.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:f6e89f9abf6d2c8110aed8ede403b13a","key":889,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:33beae1c984885116b47bb6d76386149\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:f6e89f9abf6d2c8110aed8ede403b13a\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":128,\"path\":\"plugins/spec/skills/stdo-work/SKILL.md\",\"quote\":\"When that basis permits direct Writer use and one sufficient context/grant\\ncovers the outcome, construct directly without an additional coordinating\\nactivation, Reviewer or durable ticket. Activate the coordination the\\napplicable configuration selects for a material dependency, authority or\\ncontext boundary. While occupying Executive, do not edit files or\\nGit state; the same actor must first enter a separately bound Writer activation.\\nAn actual independence requirement still needs an independent capable actor.\\nOne exact Writer grant may cover its declared construction, status and checkpoint\\nsequence. Record actual role transitions; unchanged status alone does not need\\na new activation or wholesale rehash. Refresh bindings on material change.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/plugins/spec/skills/stdo-work/SKILL.md#STDO%20Work%2FConstruct%20And%20Prove\",\"start_line\":119}],\"statement\":\"Use accepted frame basis and affected-owner conditions for required evaluations. Known false omits; unknown requires bounded resolution or explicit residual and withholds dependent claim until evidence/owner decision; absent required results never satisfy, and frame availability never mandates activation. Use direct Writer without added coordinator/Reviewer/durable ticket when basis and sufficient context/grant permit. Material dependency/authority/context boundaries activate configured coordination; Executive edits no files/Git before separately bound Writer activation, and real independence requires independent capable actor. One exact Writer grant may cover declared construction/status/checkpoint; record actual transitions, refresh on material change, and do not reactivate or rehash for unchanged status. Work in smallest coherent causal cone and exact write territory, reading material producers/consumers/owners across the cone within access grant; narrow writes do not narrow reasoning. Return cross-territory repairs to owners and preserve variation unable to change governed properties.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:5778eac61ae8916b15dae89806db03c4","key":890,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:33beae1c984885116b47bb6d76386149\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:5778eac61ae8916b15dae89806db03c4\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":158,\"path\":\"plugins/spec/skills/stdo-work/SKILL.md\",\"quote\":\"   Retire superseded responsibility; retained mechanisms need a supported\\n   obligation, owner, purpose, scope and cost, and temporary ones a removal\\n   trigger. Audit affected test predicates against the supported operating and\\n   threat model; an excluded threat cannot require a replacement guard.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/plugins/spec/skills/stdo-work/SKILL.md#STDO%20Work%2FConstruct%20And%20Prove\",\"start_line\":155},{\"end_line\":185,\"path\":\"plugins/spec/skills/stdo-work/SKILL.md\",\"quote\":\"Evaluate closure as the conjunction of satisfied applicable obligations,\\nvalid supporting evidence, required judgments/rulings and absence of an active\\nnon-closure condition. A review event is not completion. Record a satisfied\\nbounded result under the existing state-mutation grant; withhold only the\\naffected claim when a condition is missing. Qualification, publication and\\nconsumer adoption retain their separate conditions.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/plugins/spec/skills/stdo-work/SKILL.md#STDO%20Work%2FConstruct%20And%20Prove\",\"start_line\":180}],\"statement\":\"Implement/self-review bounded change; derive tests via carrier→triage→re-entry→requirement/design/module/closure law. Use cheapest adequate focused falsifier and add integration/installed-development/harnessed/live sandbox only as claimed; real probabilistic boundaries require live lanes. Reconcile authority/design/implementation/tests/displaced rivals before candidate claim. Reuse facts only with applicable subject/basis/scope/provenance/validity; function boundaries alone do not invalidate but mutation/rollback/authority-basis changes/trust boundaries retain checks. Material composition/recurrence requires complete-path and accumulated-work inspection under owning design/optional refinement and qualification of declared workload/operational assumptions, not local green. Retire superseded responsibility; retained mechanisms require obligation/owner/purpose/scope/cost and temporary ones removal triggers; excluded threats require no replacement guard. Delegated candidate return stops; Product authority or adopted authorized Executive separately determines independence under Product/qualification/release/risk/work law and activates review. Existing carriers store judgments with question/subject-basis/evidence/actor-authority/conclusion/scope/uncertainty/revising observation, separating owner rulings; invalidate affected support only, never manufacture rulings or independent assessment by reuse. Repricing retains/supersedes/defers/withdraws every affected obligation with links and consequence delta; continue accepts no hidden architecture. Authorized preservation checkpoint retains unfinished work with predecessor, territory, concurrent-writer disposition and durable evidence, claiming neither acceptance nor publication. Closure requires all applicable obligations, valid evidence, required rulings/judgments and no active non-closure; review event is insufficient. Record under mutation grant, withholding only affected claims. Qualification/publication/adoption remain distinct.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:0c6f9cba7d0d965bfd26af1c7cd50e5c","key":891,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:33beae1c984885116b47bb6d76386149\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:0c6f9cba7d0d965bfd26af1c7cd50e5c\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":193,\"path\":\"plugins/spec/skills/stdo-work/SKILL.md\",\"quote\":\"Return the exact candidate/checkpoint, changed paths, affected authority,\\nexecution-contract admission mechanism/result/evidence, focused and broader\\nproof, non-changes, residuals, and closed or withheld work result. Do not\\nclaim acceptance beyond the grant, discard a surviving obligation, or silently\\ncontinue beyond a delegated return boundary.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/plugins/spec/skills/stdo-work/SKILL.md#STDO%20Work%2FReturn\",\"start_line\":189}],\"statement\":\"Return exact candidate/checkpoint, changed paths, affected authority, admission mechanism/result/evidence, focused/broader proof, non-changes, residuals and closed/withheld result. Claim no acceptance beyond grant, discard no surviving obligation and never silently cross delegated return boundary.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:19b4c5a745c38c2a66b08e2cb2daf1de","key":892,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:095b668d8b756b7fc08853511607dac3\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:19b4c5a745c38c2a66b08e2cb2daf1de\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"Construction is delegated to a probabilistic or agentic worker.\"],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":45,\"path\":\"standards/ACTIVATION.md\",\"quote\":\"When construction is delegated to a probabilistic or agentic worker, the\\nmethod governs the execution relation without prescribing the worker's\\nmodel, prompt, tools, internal search, process topology, repository layout\\nor orchestration runtime (P0; the work boundary of FOUNDATIONS §2). The\\nnormative relation runs: accepted governing basis; bounded affected\\nrelation set; selected computational relations; delegated execution and\\ndecision authority; construction and self-review; independent live-surface\\nassessment where required; one of accept, local repair, re-enter or reject\\n(§3); the exact accepted checkpoint; the next already-authorised bounded\\naction (§5).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ACTIVATION.md#ACTIVATION%2F1.%20The%20step\",\"start_line\":36}],\"statement\":\"Govern the relation accepted basis → bounded affected relations → selected computational relations → delegated execution/decision authority → construction/self-review → independent live-surface assessment where required → accept/local repair/re-enter/reject → exact accepted checkpoint → next already-authorised bounded action. This does not prescribe worker model, prompt, tools, search, topology, layout or runtime.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:6ff08d40322c4fa9cf9183ea1146ae0e","key":893,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:095b668d8b756b7fc08853511607dac3\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:32042b38168b865f15b179aa395cf70f\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:6df3862f885cf91fa2e0a1d3a1ea15aa\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:6ff08d40322c4fa9cf9183ea1146ae0e\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"The foundation-to-law family applies with its stated instance premises, not from finite capacity alone.\"],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":59,\"path\":\"standards/ACTIVATION.md\",\"quote\":\"Foundation to law. This family, transitions, steps and configuration,\\ncovers this section and §4. Its instance premises are: (a) a selected\\noutcome with its acceptance conditions; (b) work that may exceed one\\nactivation's capacity; (c) actors with declared capability envelopes; (d)\\nan admitted grant. They are conditions of the work this family governs,\\nnot commitments, and do not follow from finite capacity alone. The\\nstanding of the consequences below is stated in\\n[FOUNDATIONS §3 Foundation to law](FOUNDATIONS.md#foundation-to-law).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ACTIVATION.md#ACTIVATION%2F1.%20The%20step\",\"start_line\":52},{\"end_line\":114,\"path\":\"standards/ACTIVATION.md\",\"quote\":\"Each consumer applies the rule and decides nothing the owning section does\\nnot (P2, P6).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ACTIVATION.md#ACTIVATION%2F1.%20The%20step\",\"start_line\":113}],\"statement\":\"The authored family covers step §1 and refinement §4, with premises a=selected outcome/acceptance, b=possibly over-capacity work, c=declared actor envelopes, d=admitted grant. It labels P0 recovered; P1/P2/P3/P4a/P6 independent; P4b derived from P0/P2 with unreacquirable step-facts premise; P5 derived from P0/P6 with open-world premise. Its 14 traces are: P0/P2+a,b→bounded transitions binding state/destination/obligations (pillars1,5); P0/P4b/P6+d→history-independent intake, non-self-certified admission and candidate/facts (5,9); P1/P6/P5+a→evidence-bound applicability, unresolved withholding and exclusion/disjunction distinctions (9,6); P0/P2/P4a/P5/P6+b,c,d→capability/dependency/assurance-based configuration preserving obligations/effects/authority/independence (7,9); P6/P2/P0+d→grant-holder durable recording without added assessment/acceptance where neither required/reserved, no disposition/waiver (9,1); P2/P6/P4b/P5+a→evidence-based completion and cause-preserving stops (1,5,9); P5/P2/P6+d→named next moves including explicit unknown class for every non-satisfied result, cause-based reconfiguration and non-waivable hard stops (5); P4a/P1/P6+b→subject-declared refinement/rewrite law, layer preservation, exact/domain-compatible faithful refinement and bounded adequacy for approximation (3,4); P4b/P3/P6+d→complete enclosing material-transition relation validated on one basis, all-or-none admission and every owner/supported boundary qualified (4,9); P2/P3/P1/P6+a→explicit A/Z and distinct specification/observation/model accounts under declared calculi (1,5,6,8); P0/P2/P5/P6+b,c→resource-bounded strategy with material rationale, no imposed preference (5,7,9); P4a/P1/P6+b→compatible composition preserving outer obligations, local success only with coverage/compatibility/outcome evidence (3,4,7); P1/P2/P6/P5+a→four-cause diagnosis preserving alternatives and owner-routed repair (5,9); P5/P2/P6+a,b→separate preservation/progress/termination/satisfaction claims, exhaustion proving neither completion nor impossibility (5,7,9). Added choices retain their owners: outcome authority for destination/acceptance, TICKETS for carriers, evaluation/scope owner for applicability/disjunction, design for configuration and declared subject laws, applicable law/grant for assessment/reserved acceptance, disposition owner for completion acceptance, Product policy for ambiguity/risk, accepted design for supported boundaries/threat model, specification owner for Z, tenant law for calculi, realization/granted actor for strategy, strategy owner for decomposition/order/concurrency, Product carriers for severity/priority and mandate owner for ongoing completion. SPEC_METHOD §8 applies these traces but retains ownership; its priority traces to F5/§6, results to F3/§3 and tenant binding to F10/§11. Consumers apply the owning rule without extending its determinations.\",\"uncertainty\":\"This preserves the source's claimed derivation standing without independently proving it; cited owners and consumer loci are largely unsupplied.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:43aacce1d3f718320440fc9987a05d82","key":894,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:3d3b5c6c2d3f3cc4fc6c364bdbb9d934\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:bf286579d4e585eb06b3157fadd71330\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:757947ab4358af48fb6a8afcb14ab842\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:43aacce1d3f718320440fc9987a05d82\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":182,\"path\":\"standards/ACTIVATION.md\",\"quote\":\"Stops. Work that cannot continue ends in an explicit stop that names its\\ncause: a step that cannot deliver its output stops with a value of\\nconstruction availability other than `candidate_ready`, and a declared\\nambiguity that halts the work or exceeds the step's authority stops it\\nwith `blocked` or `escalated` (§3). A refused admission or activation\\nstops the work without creating a step (§3 Admission and activation).\\nThe work state (§5) retains the unresolved outcome, the residuals and the\\nobligations still owed. A stop reaches no destination and discards none\\nof these (P4b, P5).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ACTIVATION.md#ACTIVATION%2F1.%20The%20step%2FTransitions\",\"start_line\":174}],\"statement\":\"Each transition binds applicable destination/affected-relation obligations; intake binds destination or prerequisite, exact state subject/basis, affected relation set/invariants. Composition is permitted only by §4 Refinement. Discovery may add obligations or invalidate claims; reestablish or withdraw invalid claims before reliance. Work outside attention stays open with material dependencies. Destination revision requires owning authority/re-entry and proves nothing about the prior destination. Completion requires sufficient evidence that current state meets applicable destination/acceptance; acceptance is decision-owner disposition. Empty worklists, counts and absent recorded counterexamples are insufficient. Unable-to-deliver steps stop with non-candidate_ready availability; halting or over-authority ambiguity yields blocked or escalated; refused admission/activation creates no step. Every stop names cause and retains unresolved outcome, residuals and obligations, reaching no destination. Progress is outcome/evidence-relative, not item count; discovery can increase work while progress occurs. Existing intake/work-state carriers suffice.\",\"uncertainty\":\"The complete availability and ambiguity algebras are deferred to unsupplied §3.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:7a295baafc455033cb84f85eea832881","key":895,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:32042b38168b865f15b179aa395cf70f\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:7a295baafc455033cb84f85eea832881\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":226,\"path\":\"standards/ACTIVATION.md\",\"quote\":\"The applicable declared requirements and the declared calculi of the\\ntenant's binding ([SPEC_METHOD §11](SPEC_METHOD.md#11-build-tenant-binding))\\ngovern which transformations and compositions are lawful; the calculi\\nselect no outcome. A\\nlawful construction can remain incomplete or fail to reach Z, and\\nlawfulness establishes neither delivery nor optimality. A proof about the\\noutcome that rests on premises retains those premises and its scope. A\\nselected construction may need to discover its path while performing and\\nevaluating work (P2, P3, P6).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ACTIVATION.md#ACTIVATION%2F1.%20The%20step%2FConstruction%20relation\",\"start_line\":218}],\"statement\":\"Bind A to actual workspace and its acquired account, external observations through owning interfaces, justified knowledge and unknowns; account may be stale/incomplete and is not the subject. Bind Z to the owning Product's governing WHAT across Intent/Product/Specification, with descriptions refining it and multiple realizations possible. Declared requirements/calculi govern lawful transformations/compositions but choose no outcome; lawful construction may fail or remain incomplete and proves neither delivery nor optimality. Premise-based proof retains premises/scope; paths may be discovered during work. Keep required conditions, observations and predictive models distinct: none establishes another, and model applicability/adequacy needs its own claim. Strategy serves Z within resources including context/attention/time/effort/computation/communication, feedback delay, uncertainty, integration and rework; planning/checking/coordination also cost. Measures state units/boundaries/composition and distinguish estimates/assumptions/observations. Incomparable objectives use owning tradeoff criteria. Granted actor/realization selects strategy with material rationale in existing records; superiority claims state objectives/comparison/assumptions. Context limits holding, attention limits use, frame selects step material/contract, and destination stays Z across activations.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:068ecccf42756560828730d225febf60","key":896,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:32042b38168b865f15b179aa395cf70f\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:068ecccf42756560828730d225febf60\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":296,\"path\":\"standards/ACTIVATION.md\",\"quote\":\"Diagnosis distinguishes four causes: a defective realisation, an\\ninadequate governing requirement or design, an inaccurate predictive\\nmodel, and insufficient observation. A prediction error alone does not\\ndecide whether the required outcome holds. A revised model does not erase\\nthe counterexample or by itself repair the realisation. Diagnosis preserves unresolved\\nalternatives and routes each supported repair to the owner of its cause;\\nthe intake label supplies no repair class and no permission. Severity\\ndescribes consequence; priority orders the response under the selected\\noutcome, dependencies, resources and authority. A bug list projects\\nexisting work state and creates no separate delivery or authority\\nmechanism (P1, P2, P5, P6).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ACTIVATION.md#ACTIVATION%2F1.%20The%20step%2FConstruction%20relation\",\"start_line\":286}],\"statement\":\"Compose only compatible preconditions/effects/results/authority, preserving applicable outer obligations across decomposition/delegation/concurrency/recursion. Local success establishes end-to-end success only with coverage, compatibility and outcome evidence; chain obligations/categorical demonstrations retain FOUNDATIONS §4 ownership. Feedback follows observation/comparison/diagnosis/authorized response/action/reobservation; bugs use ordinary change intake/delivery. Diagnose defective realization, inadequate requirement/design, inaccurate model or insufficient observation separately; prediction error proves no outcome, model revision erases no counterexample and repairs no realization by itself. Preserve unresolved alternatives; supported repair belongs to cause owner, labels grant no class/permission. Severity concerns consequence, priority orders under outcome/dependencies/resources/authority; bug lists create no separate mechanism. Preservation, evidence-based progress, termination and outcome satisfaction require distinct support; formal induction/termination claims give premises/argument but no universal termination proof is prerequisite to bounded work. Continuing work needs supported purpose, possibly uncertainty reduction/hypothesis testing; repetition alone is not progress. Failure/missing information/uncertain effects/exhaustion use owned continuation/repair/recovery/re-entry/yield/stop; resume reacquires reality, preserves valid progress and resolves effects sufficiently before dependent action. Maintenance may continue under mandate; delivery needs completion conditions. Core evaluation preserves failure, coverage gaps and uncertainty; proof/checking/testing/use establish only scoped claims and required unavailable proof remains owed. Candidate, property proof and accepted delivery are separate. Completion needs sufficient Z evidence; exhaustion proves neither achievement nor impossibility, and changing Z leaves former counterexamples intact. Existing carriers suffice; relation adds no ledger, role sequence, runtime, general solver, fixed organization, convergence guarantee or categorical-universality theorem. Domain strategy/configuration/mechanisms/additional assurance retain their owners.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:d6efae8b809e23432cdeed4d1b89fb3c","key":897,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:51712ba4356f75aa10803f984ec35302\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:d6efae8b809e23432cdeed4d1b89fb3c\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[\"Cost allowance and spend measurement are required where the governed question is a cost claim.\"],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":381,\"path\":\"standards/ACTIVATION.md\",\"quote\":\"- the construction and assessment authority: the applicable frame-set,\\n  semantic, evaluation, operation where material, and decision authority\\n  (FOUNDATIONS §2, authority kinds), and the grant: the operations\\n  permitted, the territory that may change, and the decisions reserved to\\n  others (P6);\\n- the available actor capability envelopes;\\n- the conditions that make the result stale or out of scope, and the\\n  conditions that require re-entry at an owning relation;\\n- where the governed question is a cost claim, the allowance and how\\n  spend will be measured (§6).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ACTIVATION.md#ACTIVATION%2F1.%20The%20step%2FIntake\",\"start_line\":372}],\"statement\":\"Intake names governed selected outcome/admitted prerequisite/experiment; exact workspace subject/basis and acquirable inputs by identity/hash or input commit; evaluation/family and core or core-mapped result algebra; bounded affected relations/invariants; accepted transformation-admission relations; computational/common-library machinery and bindings; frame-set, semantic, evaluation, material operation and decision authorities with permitted operations, mutable territory and reserved decisions; actor envelopes; staleness/out-of-scope/owner-re-entry conditions; and applicable cost allowance/measurement. Implementation folklore is not a source. Where design profile applies, its conservation/admission-completeness/reconstruction/computational-projection laws supply affected set, admission relations, invariants and dispositions; intake consumes these without creating another design package.\",\"uncertainty\":\"Referenced authority kinds, design laws and result refinements are not fully supplied.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:fbdbac5d5cd18262964a922c8c975e78","key":898,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:878ed078b22fb1ce473fd0d2699d4e73\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:fbdbac5d5cd18262964a922c8c975e78\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[\"A causally relevant seam may be excluded only when the basis establishes it cannot participate.\"],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":400,\"path\":\"standards/ACTIVATION.md\",\"quote\":\"A seam whose far side can causally affect,\\nor be affected by, the action is inside the cone unless the basis\\nestablishes that it cannot participate. Unrelated incompleteness outside\\nthe cone is recorded as repricing input and does not block the bounded\\nclaim. The cone is the seed set Z of §2; the context is its projection.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ACTIVATION.md#ACTIVATION%2F1.%20The%20step%2FExecution%20unit\",\"start_line\":396}],\"statement\":\"Include both sides of any seam able to affect or be affected by the action unless basis establishes nonparticipation. Record unrelated incompleteness outside the cone as repricing input without blocking the bounded claim. Context is a projection of this cone.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:6c5ef45849bc30da57280372375f1d9c","key":899,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:c175c5ee302c9e5c9c41a8555568a32f\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:095b668d8b756b7fc08853511607dac3\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:6c5ef45849bc30da57280372375f1d9c\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[\"An explicit human override of the exact contract is an alternative to deterministic admission.\"],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":435,\"path\":\"standards/ACTIVATION.md\",\"quote\":\"The admitted contract names one\\ndurable result and evidence surface; every result, withheld closure and\\nresidual obligation is recorded there before return, a conversation return\\nalone is not durable evidence, and if no such surface is authorised and\\navailable, admission refuses (P4b). Absent or rejected admission returns\\nthe missing work authority without execution, as `admission_refused` with\\nits cause ([§3 Admission and activation](#admission-and-activation)).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ACTIVATION.md#ACTIVATION%2F1.%20The%20step%2FAdmission\",\"start_line\":429}],\"statement\":\"Execution begins only after deterministic admission or explicit exact-contract human override. Drafts, carriers, lanes and active labels cannot self-certify it. Admitted results identify mechanism/authority, exact contract identity/digest, decision/evidence including override; absent coordinates leave drafted or rejected, and prose is insufficient. Admission validates against but does not admit its cited basis. Drafting/admitting/retaining creates or renews no unadmitted authority. Only admitted contracts activate steps; results, child completion, tool/model outputs, shared actors and lateral handoffs alone activate nothing and authorize no continuation. No separate turn/carrier/approval ceremony is implied. Name one available authorized durable result/evidence surface and record every result, withheld closure and residual obligation before return; chat alone is insufficient and absent surface refuses admission. Missing/rejected admission returns admission_refused with cause and missing work authority without execution. TICKETS §5 owns carrier choice.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:fc3eb108adf044c8bb0c6b2802533f93","key":900,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:451f63c242804b87ec1e73f8ecc74c3e\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:fc3eb108adf044c8bb0c6b2802533f93\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":480,\"path\":\"standards/ACTIVATION.md\",\"quote\":\"a true\\npredicate is `satisfied`; a false predicate is `falsified`, the\\nbasis-bound fact that makes it false being the counterexample; a missing\\nor ambiguous premise is `indeterminate`, or `out_of_frame` where the\\npremise needs a relation the frame does not declare, and never\\n`falsified`. An exclusion is the state of the excluded obligation after a\\n`falsified` applicability result: it is no result, the obligation's own\\nevaluation is not performed and maps to no core value, and the obligation\\nleaves the required coverage of a dependent conjunction under the cited\\nauthority of that applicability result. An obligation whose applicability is\\nunresolved stays in that required coverage. A predicate that its owner\\ndeclares as a disjunction that includes non-application, such as \\\"meets\\nthe axiom or does not apply\\\", may be `satisfied` because the obligation\\ndoes not apply; that `satisfied` is for the declared disjunction only and\\nnever counts toward the predicate that the obligation holds\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ACTIVATION.md#ACTIVATION%2F1.%20The%20step%2FApplicability\",\"start_line\":466}],\"statement\":\"Owning evaluation/scope predicates determine obligations from sufficient basis-bound facts. True applicability is satisfied and requires evaluation/result; false is falsified with its basis-bound counterexample and excludes only that obligation under cited authority. Missing/ambiguous premise is indeterminate, or out_of_frame if it needs an undeclared relation, never falsified. Exclusion has no obligation result/core value, removes only that obligation from conjunction coverage and waives no acceptance criterion; unresolved applicability remains in coverage and withholds dependent claim until evidence/owner decision resolves it. Owner-declared disjunction including non-application may be satisfied by exclusion, but that satisfaction belongs only to the disjunction, never the obligation-holds predicate. Frame/tool/family availability alone triggers no activation. Residual semantic applicability judgment retains judgment/evidence identity rather than masquerading as computation. Missing, stale, wrong-subject/basis or incapable required results cannot satisfy conjunction; other applicable constraints remain even when detected by only one evaluation. Finite declared qualification fixtures must distinguish true/false/unknown premises, missing/wrong-subject results and sufficient positive result; always-skip/always-activate rules fail those distinct expectations. Members/profiles/projects reuse this exclusion owner rather than redefining it.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:c9447a3d48a045813227fe42714e87a4","key":901,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:6df3862f885cf91fa2e0a1d3a1ea15aa\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:c9447a3d48a045813227fe42714e87a4\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":554,\"path\":\"standards/ACTIVATION.md\",\"quote\":\"A configuration is admitted by the smallest\\nexisting authority that owns the material decision the configuration\\nmakes. One configuration may derive from several governing owners; each\\nkeeps its own decision, and admitting the configuration creates no new\\nauthority over them. An explicitly bounded proxy admits a configuration\\nonly inside its existing grant (FOUNDATIONS §2 Authority kinds, Proxy\\nlimit). Which authority owns which decision is a binding of the method or\\nprofile that applies this rule; the executive configuration's binding is\\n[EXECUTIVE_BASELINE §16](EXECUTIVE_BASELINE.md#existing-authority-selects-the-configuration),\\nwhich refers here for the rule (P6, P2).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ACTIVATION.md#ACTIVATION%2F1.%20The%20step%2FConfiguration\",\"start_line\":545}],\"statement\":\"Derive allocation from operations, dependencies, available actor capabilities and assurance; these constrain but do not determine topology. Selecting design explains allocation, material resource limits under §6 and failure assumptions in existing design/frame/work records, with no separate carrier. Direct entry explains proportionally through intake, envelopes and stale/out-of-scope/re-entry conditions. Evaluate against task/dependencies/limits/authority/assurance, not labels/topology/familiar roles/coordinator presence. Preserve RF-009's distinct relation structures without additions or deletions. Frame selection grants no authority; every activation binds subject, result algebra, capability and admitted authority. Admission belongs to smallest existing authority owning the material decision; multiple owners retain decisions and no new authority is created. Proxies act only inside bounded grants; method/profile supplies actual owner binding.\",\"uncertainty\":\"RF-009's enumerated structures and §6 resource declaration law are not supplied.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:03b8201920ee4ab0caaa590792c81aad","key":902,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:6df3862f885cf91fa2e0a1d3a1ea15aa\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:03b8201920ee4ab0caaa590792c81aad\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":573,\"path\":\"standards/ACTIVATION.md\",\"quote\":\"The allocation, and every reconfiguration, preserves the\\nmaterial dependencies, the outstanding obligations, the effects,\\nincluding those of uncertain completion, the admitted authority and the\\nrequired independence. A reconfiguration is any change of allocation\\nduring the work, including actors redistributing work among themselves\\nand the changes §4 Reconfiguration selects after a result. An outstanding\\nobligation and the results that depend on it move with the work. An\\neffect of uncertain completion is resolved sufficiently for the next\\ndependent action before that action (§3 Effects, §5). Required\\nindependence keeps its authorship and evidence conditions\\n([EVALUATION §3](EVALUATION.md#3-independent-assessment)), which a fresh\\ncontext alone does not meet. An adaptive or self-organised arrangement is\\nexempt from none of these conditions (P4b, P5, P6).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ACTIVATION.md#ACTIVATION%2F1.%20The%20step%2FConfiguration\",\"start_line\":561}],\"statement\":\"Every allocation/reallocation, including adaptive self-redistribution, preserves material dependencies, outstanding obligations and dependent results, effects including uncertain completion, admitted authority and required independence. Resolve uncertain effects sufficiently before dependent action; fresh context alone does not meet independence's authorship/evidence conditions. Where change execution and multi-task delivery are separated, coordinator retains longer-term outcome and decides from sufficient bounded closed results, not task working contexts; missing information must be acquired through permitted inputs or further bounded evaluation, never presumed favorable. Compact results retain every delivery-material blocker/residual/stop; small size proves none absent. Adequacy and optimality are distinct: optimality requires objectives, constraints, comparison scope and comparative evidence; familiarity/persistence/self-organization are insufficient, and different objectives/models can favor different configurations.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:a59d7ac7072cc8a5d4d7244deb5cd87f","key":903,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:5a4be050afd6cab484eae2425fa439e5\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:ea44ff449da230ebcd91aa055503a19e\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:a59d7ac7072cc8a5d4d7244deb5cd87f\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":635,\"path\":\"standards/ACTIVATION.md\",\"quote\":\"no role name confers an operation\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ACTIVATION.md#ACTIVATION%2F1.%20The%20step%2FRoles%20and%20delegation\",\"start_line\":633},{\"end_line\":659,\"path\":\"standards/ACTIVATION.md\",\"quote\":\"Direct entry preserves\\nexecution-contract admission (Admission above), the smallest lawful\\ncarrier, the required assessment and the reserved decisions\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ACTIVATION.md#ACTIVATION%2F1.%20The%20step%2FRoles%20and%20delegation\",\"start_line\":655}],\"statement\":\"Where independent assessment supports promotion, the assessor evaluates the exact live subject, authority paths, proof and installed state, not the constructor's summary. Independence is claim-relative and imposes no actor count. Direct constructor entry requires one capable context with sufficient existing work authority, exact intake and operation grant; no coordinating activation is required solely for appointment. Configuration selects coordination when material contexts, authority, capability or required independence need it, never merely because of a role or frame name. Direct entry preserves admission, the smallest lawful carrier, required assessment and reserved decisions; it permits bounded work and condition-based recording, not self-acceptance at another owner's boundary.\",\"uncertainty\":\"The referenced configuration, admission and independence laws are not supplied in full.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:e6ad89a7ce5f2cd98d0aed19ada57b55","key":904,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:ea44ff449da230ebcd91aa055503a19e\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:5a4be050afd6cab484eae2425fa439e5\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:e6ad89a7ce5f2cd98d0aed19ada57b55\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":679,\"path\":\"standards/ACTIVATION.md\",\"quote\":\"The\\nrecording waives no condition that actually applies\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ACTIVATION.md#ACTIVATION%2F1.%20The%20step%2FRoles%20and%20delegation\",\"start_line\":666},{\"end_line\":691,\"path\":\"standards/ACTIVATION.md\",\"quote\":\"A material change to the operation, the\\nsubject, the territory, the authority or the validity conditions requires\\nthe affected binding to be resolved before effect.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ACTIVATION.md#ACTIVATION%2F1.%20The%20step%2FRoles%20and%20delegation\",\"start_line\":684}],\"statement\":\"Only when applicable law requires no independent assessment and reserves no acceptance may the grant-holding constructor record the satisfied bounded result, evaluated conditions and evidence in the existing durable result surface without adding a carrier, appointment, review or recreated design view solely for completion. Recording waives no applicable condition, reports no unperformed evaluation and disposes no other owner's boundary. Required assessment or reserved acceptance remains required; discovered insufficiency withholds the dependent effect and returns the question to its owner. Carriers and profiles add only their carrier binding. Actual role transitions are recorded in the existing work carrier; status change alone requires neither a new grant nor rehashing an unchanged subject. Material operation, subject, territory, authority or validity changes require affected binding resolution before effect. A sequence-wide grant never lifts a configuration's non-mutation restriction on its coordinating role, including the cited Executive restriction.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:9f0c0cbb43be87a216bc1aa38a4f7d7b","key":905,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:6e08c1219e2615bd98a4b4349eacb927\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:9f0c0cbb43be87a216bc1aa38a4f7d7b\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":714,\"path\":\"standards/ACTIVATION.md\",\"quote\":\"If Z, R, the required-edge semantics, the basis or the scope is not\\n   exact, or the closure is not finite and unique on the exact basis,\\n   activation returns `closure_unresolved` (§3, Admission and activation)\\n   and no step proceeds; it does not guess.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ACTIVATION.md#ACTIVATION%2F2.%20Context%20construction%20under%20an%20envelope\",\"start_line\":702}],\"statement\":\"The described procedure computes material closure of Z under R, then projects it to the selected context, recording excluded, external, unresolved, translated and invalidation-sensitive seams. Inexact Z, R, required-edge semantics, basis or scope, a closure not finite and unique on the exact basis, or projection gap or refusal returns closure_unresolved and permits no step. Material outside the closure stays out; adjacency or corpus presence is no inclusion reason. The method does not require proof that no undiscovered material relation exists.\",\"uncertainty\":\"AC-010 and AC-011 are referenced but their full definitions are outside the supplied source.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:82c73e8524f392e1dd0a5cc0ac08b228","key":906,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:6e08c1219e2615bd98a4b4349eacb927\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:c95cc0e07f26edab0dce96bc1cff9eaf\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:82c73e8524f392e1dd0a5cc0ac08b228\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"The actor's envelope declares context capacity.\"],\"exceptions\":[\"Without declared context capacity, this measurement is not required; the other cited finite-attention conditions still apply.\"],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":730,\"path\":\"standards/ACTIVATION.md\",\"quote\":\"The fit claim for a measured\\n   boundary and the step's fit judgment are distinct\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ACTIVATION.md#ACTIVATION%2F2.%20Context%20construction%20under%20an%20envelope\",\"start_line\":723},{\"end_line\":745,\"path\":\"standards/ACTIVATION.md\",\"quote\":\"Where B declares no context capacity, no measurement is\\n   required\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ACTIVATION.md#ACTIVATION%2F2.%20Context%20construction%20under%20an%20envelope\",\"start_line\":740}],\"statement\":\"Before reading, measure selected context in the declared capacity's unit, bytes or tokens, over the selected execution binding's boundary; record measurement, capacity and comparison. Fit covers only that boundary; outside context is not measured and receives no fit claim. The step's fit judgment requires recorded complete active inputs or a supported upper bound including host-supplied context; without either it is indeterminate unless a counterexample such as measured excess establishes falsified. A correct task result retains its bounded standing but cannot supply missing fit. This conditional measurement applies whatever question the step governs, is not a budget or universal gate, and proves fit only; adequate attention requires actual-use evidence. Other envelope dimensions and time, spend and resource limits retain their own laws.\",\"uncertainty\":\"The complete active-input judgment and adequate-attention criteria depend on referenced laws not supplied here.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:3efbee86bbc263684a4e487336514be7","key":907,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:a7bf2b374366f62d9330810c3c2636be\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:1e4bf2ddf108dcc3728f8fb9c3694873\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:3efbee86bbc263684a4e487336514be7\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":798,\"path\":\"standards/ACTIVATION.md\",\"quote\":\"Only material in the exact selected\\nbasis is acquired\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ACTIVATION.md#ACTIVATION%2F2.%20Context%20construction%20under%20an%20envelope\",\"start_line\":794},{\"end_line\":814,\"path\":\"standards/ACTIVATION.md\",\"quote\":\"No frame,\\nderived surface or acquisition carries a universal sufficiency claim\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ACTIVATION.md#ACTIVATION%2F2.%20Context%20construction%20under%20an%20envelope\",\"start_line\":803}],\"statement\":\"Acquire declared inputs by exact identity. Absence from the materialised view permits neither reading elsewhere nor concluding source absence. Acquisition is neither admission nor another actor stage and grants no role, operation or decision; effectful work still requires an admitted contract. Acquire a serving derived surface whose sources are current; for another task or a stale, missing or question-insufficient surface, acquire the deciding owner sections declared in the exact selected basis. Candidate sources, version-line selectors and another basis cannot substitute. Read the selected material and actual subject and follow needed material-source and coupled-obligation references. Sufficiency is for the named question and material relations, never universal. Before dependent action, name missing bindings: no available frame declaring evaluation needs yields out_of_frame; an absent or unverifiable exact required basis yields admission_refused(basis) at admission or activation_refusal(basis) at activation. Handle coupled material that does not fit through the fit procedure. A standalone surface can decide only questions its own source members own; questions owned elsewhere or joining several owners return out_of_frame naming owners and require those members at current digests or a surface declaring every owner.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:07c45c6f329ecb1030b732eb069f70f2","key":908,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:a7bf2b374366f62d9330810c3c2636be\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:3af2fdc9a53de92bc0500be7d49532ee\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:07c45c6f329ecb1030b732eb069f70f2\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[\"Historical workaround prose may remain only where current requirement, design, runtime or test still needs its constraint.\"],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":832,\"path\":\"standards/ACTIVATION.md\",\"quote\":\"It distinguishes semantic\\nlaw, observed evidence, inference and decision, and records every\\nassumption whose failure could change the result\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ACTIVATION.md#ACTIVATION%2F2.%20Context%20construction%20under%20an%20envelope\",\"start_line\":830},{\"end_line\":854,\"path\":\"standards/ACTIVATION.md\",\"quote\":\"Prompt text must project the current authority\\nreferences, obligations, contracts, boundaries, proof expectations and\\nfallback conditions the step needs.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ACTIVATION.md#ACTIVATION%2F2.%20Context%20construction%20under%20an%20envelope\",\"start_line\":845}],\"statement\":\"The actor or assigning authority selects one capable frame or declared active configuration. Activation binds exact subject and basis and loads declared material relations and evidence sources as the referenced packet, never an undifferentiated workspace dump. If no lawful frame/actor pairing exists, missing declared material relation or capability yields out_of_frame; otherwise the applicable activation_refusal cause governs. Implied context cannot sustain work. Evaluation distinguishes semantic law, observation, inference and decision and records every result-changing assumption. Prompt construction starts from the highest live authority surface needed, projects current authority references, obligations, contracts, boundaries, proof expectations, fallback conditions and acquisition-selected material, including raw owners when required. It names an upstream unresolved authority gap before reading fallback context and excludes obsolete workaround prose.\",\"uncertainty\":\"The packet shape, full activation-refusal causes and design/ODD/UX/ticket prompt specialisations are references, not supplied definitions.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:c8e3619cf85d2aabc901ea9b460f797f","key":909,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:1e4bf2ddf108dcc3728f8fb9c3694873\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:c8e3619cf85d2aabc901ea9b460f797f\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"Applies to derived surfaces under every method and selected carrier.\"],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":905,\"path\":\"standards/ACTIVATION.md\",\"quote\":\"It is current for a selected basis only while every source identity it\\n  names equals the identity of that source in the selected basis. A change\\n  to any of them makes it stale.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ACTIVATION.md#ACTIVATION%2F2.%20Context%20construction%20under%20an%20envelope%2FStaleness%20of%20derived%20surfaces\",\"start_line\":889}],\"statement\":\"A surface names the exact identity, such as path and digest, of every derivation source and every source whose change can change its content. It is current only while all named identities equal the selected basis identities; any change makes it stale. No stale surface is used as current for any question. Currentness is restored only by regeneration from selected-basis sources or explicit re-acceptance recording new source identities and a finding that content still matches; meanwhile deciding owners are acquired directly. Identity matches establish provenance alone, neither fidelity nor sufficiency. Selected-basis owners decide question-specific insufficiency and overreach; the surface never judges these about itself. Packaging and installation carriers refine identities and re-acceptance procedures while naming this subsection as owner; PRODUCT_DEFINITION §11 is identified as the released-carrier application.\",\"uncertainty\":\"The referenced carrier-specific re-acceptance procedure is not supplied.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:ee54a35b161f7a01b98adb1fe788e2c8","key":910,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:59e8abdb24124885d914c88740a00872\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:ee54a35b161f7a01b98adb1fe788e2c8\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":933,\"path\":\"standards/ACTIVATION.md\",\"quote\":\"each evaluation it\\nperformed returns one core value with its predicate and domain outcome,\\nand an evaluation it did not perform has no result.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ACTIVATION.md#ACTIVATION%2F3.%20Step%20results%20and%20disposition\",\"start_line\":920},{\"end_line\":945,\"path\":\"standards/ACTIVATION.md\",\"quote\":\"A profile that refines these values for its own units maps each of its\\nvalues to exactly one core value under FOUNDATIONS §4 Results and adds no\\ncore value.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ACTIVATION.md#ACTIVATION%2F3.%20Step%20results%20and%20disposition\",\"start_line\":943}],\"statement\":\"Every performed evaluation returns exactly one core value with predicate and domain outcome; an unperformed evaluation has no result. Every refinement value maps to exactly one core value for its own named predicate, which travels with it. Satisfied under one predicate cannot satisfy another. Consumers must not treat refused activation as step stop, availability as fitness or acceptance, carried ambiguity as resolution, or unknown effect as no effect. Profile refinements likewise map each value to one core value and add none.\",\"uncertainty\":\"The complete core algebra and conjunction law are not supplied; only the quoted local uses and mappings are represented.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:1d7f5255a336cf3ab1a4fadad7ecb015","key":911,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:967b396c83203d799b9da541efa92a8f\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:1d7f5255a336cf3ab1a4fadad7ecb015\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":968,\"path\":\"standards/ACTIVATION.md\",\"quote\":\"| `closure_unresolved` | the seed set Z, the relation family R, the required-edge semantics, the basis or the scope is not exact, or the material closure is not finite and unique on the exact basis (§2, step 1; AC-010), or the projection of the closure returns a gap or refusal (§2, step 2; AC-011); the outcome names the condition that fails and the basis coordinates that leave it open | invalid_basis |\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ACTIVATION.md#ACTIVATION%2F3.%20Step%20results%20and%20disposition%2FAdmission%20and%20activation\",\"start_line\":966},{\"end_line\":976,\"path\":\"standards/ACTIVATION.md\",\"quote\":\"A refused admission or activation creates no step, no\\nactivation of the step's frame and no work result\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ACTIVATION.md#ACTIVATION%2F3.%20Step%20results%20and%20disposition%2FAdmission%20and%20activation\",\"start_line\":971}],\"statement\":\"For lawful admission and activation: activated → satisfied only with admitted contract and admission evidence, exact Z/R/required-edge semantics/basis/scope, finite unique closure, selected-context projection and activated_frame. admission_refused(authority) → out_of_frame when no admission mechanism or explicit human override admits the exact contract, or no authorised available durable result/evidence surface exists; name missing authority or surface and owner. admission_refused(basis) → invalid_basis when cited outcome, prerequisite or experiment basis, or named exact subject/basis, cannot support the contract; name that basis. closure_unresolved → invalid_basis for closure/projection defects, naming failing condition and open basis coordinates. out_of_frame → out_of_frame when no frame/actor pairing declares a needed relation or capability, or no fit option fits context to an envelope. activation_refusal takes its cause, predicate and core value from REFERENCE_FRAME §5, without local remapping. Refusal creates no step, frame activation or work result; return it to assigning authority or declared result carrier and never record it as construction availability or a step's stop.\",\"uncertainty\":\"The full activation_refusal mapping is externally owned and unresolved in this excerpt.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:2de3f5bfe5cd4ebedabda1ab6109ed0d","key":912,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:fdffde11bee635b630b1f96f399dbd64\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:2de3f5bfe5cd4ebedabda1ab6109ed0d\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"Lawful activation occurred; causes known during admission or activation instead use admission/activation outcomes.\"],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":995,\"path\":\"standards/ACTIVATION.md\",\"quote\":\"| `candidate_ready` | satisfied | an exact candidate and its transition evidence are available |\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ACTIVATION.md#ACTIVATION%2F3.%20Step%20results%20and%20disposition%2FConstruction%20availability\",\"start_line\":990},{\"end_line\":1026,\"path\":\"standards/ACTIVATION.md\",\"quote\":\"A stop\\nwith both causes records both and takes `re_entry_requested(basis)`\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ACTIVATION.md#ACTIVATION%2F3.%20Step%20results%20and%20disposition%2FConstruction%20availability\",\"start_line\":1023}],\"statement\":\"The cause-selected mapping is total and exclusive after lawful activation; wording, timing and preference cannot change it. candidate_ready → satisfied when exact candidate and transition evidence are available, establishing availability only. refused → falsified when governing prohibition or owner-valid construction refusal defeats construction, with that prohibition/refusal as counterexample. incomplete → falsified for candidate availability when the step stops without output because required evaluation was unperformed or undecidable on admissible evidence, or execution ended first; stop basis and residuals identify which. re_entry_requested(authority) → out_of_frame for a needed material decision outside the grant, naming owner. re_entry_requested(basis) → invalid_basis when activated basis no longer supports work. Both re-entry causes are recorded when present, with basis taking precedence. Performed evaluations keep their own results, including indeterminate; planned unperformed evaluations have no result and remain work-state residuals naming unfinished capability or execution. Incomplete assessment never falsifies an unassessed criterion or the assessed subject.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:7702b85aec740d78fd28481bd1ee7494","key":913,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:ed56e674258c8d8e90c3046d72aaf499\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:7702b85aec740d78fd28481bd1ee7494\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1044,\"path\":\"standards/ACTIVATION.md\",\"quote\":\"| `accept` | the candidate closes its declared cone and preserves every affected governing relation | satisfied |\\n| `local_repair` | implementation or proof is locally defective while the governing relation remains coherent | falsified |\\n| `re_enter` | the governing outcome, a requirement, an identity, a lifecycle, an authority, a public contract or the accepted design must change | invalid_basis |\\n| `reject` | the candidate violates a governing relation or leaves an undisposed competing truth path | falsified |\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ACTIVATION.md#ACTIVATION%2F3.%20Step%20results%20and%20disposition%2FDisposition\",\"start_line\":1041},{\"end_line\":1064,\"path\":\"standards/ACTIVATION.md\",\"quote\":\"it prohibits repeating an\\nunchanged failed construction relation as if iteration alone could close\\nit\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ACTIVATION.md#ACTIVATION%2F3.%20Step%20results%20and%20disposition%2FDisposition\",\"start_line\":1062}],\"statement\":\"Only the decision owner disposes; an assessor may recommend, but recommendation is evidence, never disposition. accept → satisfied when the candidate closes its declared cone and preserves every affected governing relation. local_repair → falsified for local implementation/proof defect with coherent governing relation; the defect is the counterexample. re_enter → invalid_basis when governing outcome, requirement, identity, lifecycle, authority, public contract or accepted design must change; re-enter the owning relation because the construction/assessment basis cannot support acceptance. reject → falsified for a governing violation or undisposed competing truth path, which is the counterexample. A repair creates a new candidate with its own results. Global correctness conserves every affected global relation without requiring whole-product proof in each local action. Repeated rejection at one unchanged boundary requires reassessment of frame altitude, causal cone, common components, design-versus-code placement and authority sufficiency. No rejection threshold, mandatory round count or review state machine is imposed; unchanged failed construction cannot be repeated as if iteration alone closed it.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:65b952b856ed605cf94cd03865ee8ab8","key":914,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:af664c6b9353a038c00eff8d30c32886\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:65b952b856ed605cf94cd03865ee8ab8\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1080,\"path\":\"standards/ACTIVATION.md\",\"quote\":\"| `carried` | falsified | policy permits work to continue with the ambiguity open; the open ambiguity is the counterexample, and it stays a recorded residual that names the evidence or decision that would resolve it |\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ACTIVATION.md#ACTIVATION%2F3.%20Step%20results%20and%20disposition%2FAmbiguity%20outcome\",\"start_line\":1078},{\"end_line\":1089,\"path\":\"standards/ACTIVATION.md\",\"quote\":\"No outcome other than `resolved` maps to `satisfied`\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ACTIVATION.md#ACTIVATION%2F3.%20Step%20results%20and%20disposition%2FAmbiguity%20outcome\",\"start_line\":1087}],\"statement\":\"Record every ambiguity outcome. resolved → satisfied only for a recorded decision under policy permitting lawful probabilistic processing or human adjudication. carried → falsified for resolution when policy permits continuation with known open ambiguity; retain a residual naming resolving evidence or decision. escalated → out_of_frame when policy/risk appetite reserves decision to human authority absent from the step; name it. blocked → falsified when unresolved ambiguity and policy or hard stop halt work; name the halting condition and what lifts it. Carried and blocked are known openness, not evidence-indeterminate resolution. Preserve their domain details, and never support a dependent claim as if carried, escalated or blocked ambiguity were resolved.\",\"uncertainty\":\"The applicable ambiguity policy and risk appetite are not supplied.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:087fc00fc1b216c81376389c13956fb0","key":915,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:5a3dd9d1ad03a25d09bcc27c8ac5c6c1\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:087fc00fc1b216c81376389c13956fb0\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1105,\"path\":\"standards/ACTIVATION.md\",\"quote\":\"| `completed` | satisfied | evidence about the subject establishes that the intended effect occurred in full and that the effect has ended |\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ACTIVATION.md#ACTIVATION%2F3.%20Step%20results%20and%20disposition%2FEffects\",\"start_line\":1103},{\"end_line\":1126,\"path\":\"standards/ACTIVATION.md\",\"quote\":\"The residual does\\nnot weaken the counterexample, and the counterexample does not resolve\\nthe residual.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ACTIVATION.md#ACTIVATION%2F3.%20Step%20results%20and%20disposition%2FEffects\",\"start_line\":1121}],\"statement\":\"Use admitted evidence about the subject. completed → satisfied requires full intended effect and established end. not_effected → falsified requires evidence that the declared outcome is unattained and no later completion can attain it: examples include no effect beginning, an effect ending short, a bounded interval closing partly undone, or prior action destroying what the outcome needs; name any part that occurred. completion_unknown → indeterminate when neither other value is established, including lost response without observed counterexample or full effect observed while it may still act; name the deciding observation. Lost response, absent record or no context trace is not evidence of not_effected. End is established by subject evidence that action ceased or never began; if an effect began without established end, record the needed observation separately. End does not decide not_effected: a closed incomplete interval can falsify outcome while action continues. Counterexample and end residual remain independent. Before repetition or dependent action, reconcile uncertain completion sufficiently for that action; not_effected with unknown end licenses neither absence assumptions nor repetition.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:6525cc0df73c932979dece1296ccfcfd","key":916,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:f0c8f92d73a2b89efda429853c9a3bbe\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:af664c6b9353a038c00eff8d30c32886\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:6525cc0df73c932979dece1296ccfcfd\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1170,\"path\":\"standards/ACTIVATION.md\",\"quote\":\"A hard stop halts the work at its condition whatever the policy\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ACTIVATION.md#ACTIVATION%2F4.%20Totality%20and%20refinement\",\"start_line\":1165}],\"statement\":\"Name next moves in advance for every non-satisfied result and admitted condition class, including unknown. Applicable ambiguity policy and risk appetite choose ambiguity outcomes; this section states no default policy and names SPEC_METHOD §5 as its owner. Hard stops are not optional policy choices and halt at their condition regardless of risk appetite. Typical, non-exhaustive classes are violated invariant/guarantee, absent required authority surface, missing declared executional/operational capability, undeclared irreversible side effect and explicit human-approval gate. A declared ambiguity takes blocked; other cases take a transition stop. Adding algebra values does not solve hanging calls, unsatisfiable demands or lost post-effect responses.\",\"uncertainty\":\"The default ambiguity policy and the general transition-stop specification are outside this excerpt.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:b6ec6e46ff702a56297ab8ba287fc0fe","key":917,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:37b3d302abc5b3361220cc283757b68c\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:b6ec6e46ff702a56297ab8ba287fc0fe\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1208,\"path\":\"standards/ACTIVATION.md\",\"quote\":\"Coverage of the outer obligations, correctness of the local\\nimplications and legitimate authority are premises, not conclusions\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ACTIVATION.md#ACTIVATION%2F4.%20Totality%20and%20refinement%2FRefinement\",\"start_line\":1198},{\"end_line\":1243,\"path\":\"standards/ACTIVATION.md\",\"quote\":\"Faithful refinement, defined above, requires exact\\nsteps.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ACTIVATION.md#ACTIVATION%2F4.%20Totality%20and%20refinement%2FRefinement\",\"start_line\":1229}],\"statement\":\"Faithful refinement requires exact steps: each admitted input satisfying Pᵢ yields output satisfying Pᵢ₊₁, retains every applicable invariant, exposes other outcomes without coercion and satisfies the next step's domain/preconditions. Successful exact composition carries P₀ to Pₙ by induction, assuming outer-obligation coverage, valid local implications and legitimate authority; local passes do not establish those premises. Non-next-step transfer needs a declared adapter composed as a step or a specialised contract whose domain names the carried material and whose exact owner authority, context, basis, scope, preservation, loss, refusal and invalidation law are declared. Coupled required relations fit together in some step; unrelated obligations remain excluded; every affected seam includes its far side or explains nonparticipation. Every layer states and discharges preservation of the layer above. Refinement/rewrite requires a subject-owner licensing law, such as declared associativity, commutativity or equivalence; without declared laws only universally valid steps are admissible. Any unlicensed and non-universal step, and any refinement/rewrite relying on it, is inadmissible. Approximate steps state adequacy and an argued composite end-to-end bound; such composites are adequate only within that bound, never faithful. Fixed per-step tolerances alone do not establish composition bounds. A step neither exact nor approximate with the required adequacy and composite bound is inadmissible, as is reliance on it. Material-transition admission remains one complete semantic commit or none, including the cited ODD realisation.\",\"uncertainty\":\"Referenced preservation, typed-composition, ODD and profile laws are not supplied in full.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:4f0c805801fc411653ab405fb7d57b7e","key":918,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:bfe14a0ff0b9caef21ad7cbc62061481\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:4f0c805801fc411653ab405fb7d57b7e\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"A material transition is admitted.\"],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1300,\"path\":\"standards/ACTIVATION.md\",\"quote\":\"Admission\\nis one semantic commit of the complete transition, bound to its exact basis\\nidentity; failure or interruption admits the complete transition or none,\\nnever a subset.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ACTIVATION.md#ACTIVATION%2F4.%20Totality%20and%20refinement%2FComplete%20enclosing-relation%20admission\",\"start_line\":1290}],\"statement\":\"Derive and validate completeness from authoritative inputs; caller/owner assertions of completeness, validity, prior admission or authority do not establish truth. Bind one exact admission-valid authoritative basis through admission. If validity/currentness can advance after preflight, require the declared predecessor/currentness commit condition or effect-free re-entry into derivation and validation. Participating owners bind equal bases or a design-declared coherent composite; independently valid mixed-basis judgments cannot combine. Validate every participant and join before any effect. No subset or nested constituent becomes admitted truth; failure/interruption admits the entire transition or none. Direct, supported composite and nested realisations preserve this law; partial results cannot replace an owner's derivation/validation and competing same-scope paths cannot establish transition outside the governing relation. Same-basis reconstruction and replay exactly reproduce enclosing relation, basis identity and complete semantic outcome/refusal. The law is false for asserted-only completeness, omitted relevant participant/join/seam, unidentified/stale/incoherently mixed basis, advancing currentness without condition or effect-free re-entry, premature effect, exposed subset, differing reconstruction or remaining competing authority.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:79ce519f0672f0ebce6eb907b525d4fe","key":919,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:90da442170f46d6cdf3bca49e170cff2\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:79ce519f0672f0ebce6eb907b525d4fe\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"Cases fall within accepted design's supported input, state and operating or threat model.\"],\"exceptions\":[\"Named representative atomic-failure observations suffice only with a design-declared dominance or equivalence proof covering the complete partial-failure surface.\"],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1330,\"path\":\"standards/ACTIVATION.md\",\"quote\":\"| atomic publication failure | after validation succeeds, failure or interruption is observed at every materially distinct commit or publication boundary capable of exposing a subset, followed by fresh reconstruction showing the complete transition or none; named representative observations suffice only under a design-declared dominance or equivalence proof covering the complete partial-failure surface |\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ACTIVATION.md#ACTIVATION%2F4.%20Totality%20and%20refinement%2FStanding%20structural%20qualification\",\"start_line\":1330},{\"end_line\":1339,\"path\":\"standards/ACTIVATION.md\",\"quote\":\"Final-participant\\nvalidation failure does not substitute for post-validation atomic-failure\\nevidence.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ACTIVATION.md#ACTIVATION%2F4.%20Totality%20and%20refinement%2FStanding%20structural%20qualification\",\"start_line\":1333}],\"statement\":\"An excluded threat alone creates no acceptance predicate or defensive-work requirement; scope expansion returns to its owner, while supported malformed inputs, stale state and effect boundaries keep checks. Direct cases derive, validate and admit the complete relation once. Every supported composite/nested constituent and owner boundary obeys the same law; unsupported forms need design-grounded not_applicable and no weaker/competing path. Reachable forged identity, membership, equality or authority is refused without effect; exclusion requires owning authority, not helper inability. Unresolved participant/join/seam/relation identity is refused without effect. Stale input is refused; preflight-to-admission advancement causes effect-free re-entry. Incoherent multi-owner bases are refused without effect. Competing same-scope paths cannot establish transition. Fresh process/reconstruction and exact replay reproduce relation, basis and complete outcome/refusal. After successful validation, observe interruption/failure at every materially distinct commit/publication boundary capable of exposing subsets, then reconstruct all or none. An indivisible commit unit requires established boundary and observations immediately on both sides. Final-participant validation failure is not post-validation atomic-failure evidence. A standing claim is false if any owner/supported boundary is omitted, any distinct partial-failure boundary lacks observation or coverage proof, a weaker helper/manufactured refusal is used, or reconstruction omits complete semantic comparison.\",\"uncertainty\":\"No actual design, supported model or qualification observations are supplied.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:989e429cbf3348b9e0e6bfcc3e337195","key":920,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:1922d98a4b06f1a4a48edade05b0d465\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:7fe4bc4d420d2ffbab8ac5fcc89547c3\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:989e429cbf3348b9e0e6bfcc3e337195\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1373,\"path\":\"standards/ACTIVATION.md\",\"quote\":\"A preservation checkpoint may retain unfinished or unaccepted\\nwork under an existing exact operation grant\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ACTIVATION.md#ACTIVATION%2F5.%20Work%20state%20and%20restart\",\"start_line\":1364},{\"end_line\":1395,\"path\":\"standards/ACTIVATION.md\",\"quote\":\"The execution protocol of §1, §3 and this section is false if execution\\nproceeds from unreconstructable context\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ACTIVATION.md#ACTIVATION%2F5.%20Work%20state%20and%20restart\",\"start_line\":1389}],\"statement\":\"Resumption recovers applicable progress, checks every reused result's invalidators, reopens only affected support and reconciles uncertain effects before repetition/dependent action sufficiently for that action. It implies no idempotence: lawful next moves for uncertain effects are reconciliation, yield or stop, never blind repetition. Acceptance binds one exact checkpoint and does not enlarge outcome or affected relations; the next already-authorised bounded action needs no renewed human approval. A preservation checkpoint under an exact grant names parent/predecessor, included territory, concurrent-writer disposition and durable evidence location; it is neither acceptance, promotion nor publication. Restart from less than retained work states why repair is insufficient, surviving obligations/evidence and changed causal assumptions; reconstructability alone does not choose restart. Counts of paperwork, code, tests, commits or reviews alone are not progress. Finer categories must name and refine this owner, mapping each to progress, prerequisite work, non-progress evidence, churn or forecast revision; an unmappable category requires owner change. Execution protocol is false for unreconstructable context, constructor reports replacing required independent live evidence, proxy overreach, unrelated incompleteness blocking a closed cone, same-process proof of materially cross-process authority or rejected activity reported as accepted progress.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:a62337904a43c58b9847a7bd232d5c97","key":921,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:1922d98a4b06f1a4a48edade05b0d465\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:e3fd35bdac6bd4cd6baec77ead672074\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:c5b83e3a0a9998b11c480c9d9b26887b\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:c95cc0e07f26edab0dce96bc1cff9eaf\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:5b25bc7a2a279511eaa355c912e1a27b\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:e5c8b96517828a0f56dd887c29ace149\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:a62337904a43c58b9847a7bd232d5c97\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"Each foundation-family row applies only under its stated instance premises.\"],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1404,\"path\":\"standards/ACTIVATION.md\",\"quote\":\"They are conditions of the work this family governs, not\\ncommitments, and do not follow from finite capacity alone.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ACTIVATION.md#ACTIVATION%2F5.%20Work%20state%20and%20restart\",\"start_line\":1401},{\"end_line\":1582,\"path\":\"standards/ACTIVATION.md\",\"quote\":\"the default priority, the smallest supported product path first: SPEC_METHOD §8\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ACTIVATION.md#ACTIVATION%2F6.%20Cost%20and%20proportionality\",\"start_line\":1582}],\"statement\":\"The source's work-state/reuse family has extra premises a persistent workspace, b work spanning activations, c changing actors and d open-world effects. Its six rows are: work-state object, P3/P0 with a,b, pillars 2,5, carrier chosen by profile/realisation; workspace versus account, P0/P3/P4b/P6 with a,c, pillars 6,9, recovery observations chosen by resuming intake plus work state; effect reconciliation, P5/P6 with d, pillars 4,5, no added choice; checkpoint/progress, P2/P6 with b, pillar 5, projections chosen by consumer; closed handoff/reuse, P4b/P0/P6 with c, pillars 7,9, revising observations and other invalidation conditions declared by producer; transition evidence, P5/P6 with c, pillar 9, representation chosen by consumer. The proportionality/cost family has extra premises a selected outcome, b complexity-adding obligations, c a governed cost claim and d bounded-resource consumption. Its six rows are proportionality P2/P0 with b, pillars 6,7, once-per-family rationale by owning law; symbolic design P2/P0/P1 with b, pillars 4,6, no added choice; execution purpose P2/P0/P6 with b, pillars 7,9, no added choice; cost P0/P2 with c, pillar 8, allowance by activation and measurement boundary/unit by execution binding; resource limits P0/P5/P6/P2 with d, pillars 8,7, values and measurable units/boundaries by execution binding; delivery priority P2/P0 with a, pillars 1,5, SPEC_METHOD §8 chooses the smallest supported product path first and prioritises likelihood, impact, reversibility, dependency and delayed feedback without probability waiving hard stops. These are source-authored derivation accounts, not proofs performed here. P0 is labelled recovered; P1/P2/P3/P6 independent; P5 derived from P0/P6 with the open-world premise; P4b derived from P0/P2 with non-reacquirable step-produced facts. Instance premises are not commitments and do not follow from finite capacity alone. Consumer applications add no determination beyond their owning rule.\",\"uncertainty\":\"The external foundation standing and most listed consumer loci are not supplied.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:4e92b9cd9f9d8b0925f22464062d5ed0","key":922,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:1bbfea85ff18f82f399dc48f5698013b\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:1922d98a4b06f1a4a48edade05b0d465\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:4e92b9cd9f9d8b0925f22464062d5ed0\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1463,\"path\":\"standards/ACTIVATION.md\",\"quote\":\"Discarding an actor's private context resets nothing\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ACTIVATION.md#ACTIVATION%2F5.%20Work%20state%20and%20restart%2FThe%20workspace%20and%20an%20actor%27s%20account\",\"start_line\":1456},{\"end_line\":1476,\"path\":\"standards/ACTIVATION.md\",\"quote\":\"The recovery contract that applies, which is\\nthe resuming step's intake with the work state, determines which\\nobservations and which effect reconciliations the next dependent action\\nneeds.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ACTIVATION.md#ACTIVATION%2F5.%20Work%20state%20and%20restart%2FThe%20workspace%20and%20an%20actor%27s%20account\",\"start_line\":1471}],\"statement\":\"Record closed results and needed step-produced facts before returning. When current subject/authoritative inputs materially disagree with cached belief, retained summary or prior result, reconcile: current evidence corrects the account and undecided matters stay explicit unknowns. Stored accounts and past success never overrule contrary current evidence. Reliance on prior results requires current applicability and invalidator checks. Correct accounts within grant; required out-of-grant operation, territory or decision stops with re_entry_requested(authority) naming owner. Discarding private context changes neither workspace, valid work nor outstanding obligations. Missing context/memory/summary trace proves neither undone work, absent effect nor ended effect; retain completion_unknown or not_effected with end unresolved until subject evidence decides. Interrupted partial writes remain current material state and are assessed as they stand. Unperformed assessment has no result. No universal reset, full-history replay or additional carrier is required. Recovery intake plus work state determines needed observations/reconciliation. Handoff uses closed results without requiring private context and preserves validity and independence conditions.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:f93bc50003b5eebc948cd5e4582c3a21","key":923,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:e3fd35bdac6bd4cd6baec77ead672074\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:c5b83e3a0a9998b11c480c9d9b26887b\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:f93bc50003b5eebc948cd5e4582c3a21\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1525,\"path\":\"standards/ACTIVATION.md\",\"quote\":\"Rival authority,\\nuncertainty over failure classification and evidence uncertainty count only\\nwhere they leave materially distinct admissible semantic, authority,\\noutcome or acceptance interpretations\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ACTIVATION.md#ACTIVATION%2F6.%20Cost%20and%20proportionality\",\"start_line\":1511},{\"end_line\":1562,\"path\":\"standards/ACTIVATION.md\",\"quote\":\"a cost claim over transferred context\\ncounts the context transferred to every delegated actor, not only to the\\ncoordinator.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ACTIVATION.md#ACTIVATION%2F6.%20Cost%20and%20proportionality\",\"start_line\":1559}],\"statement\":\"Each constraint identifies removed semantic ambiguity and justifies its added reasoning complexity through sufficient contraction of admissible interpretations. Rival authority, failure-classification uncertainty and evidence uncertainty count only as material alternative interpretations, not independent benefits. Greater capability may enlarge the bounded relation resolvable but grants no authority, weakens no invariant and waives no acceptance. Detailed symbolic design is proportional when one bounded model within capacity resolves material alternatives; divergent implementation paths, states, tests, reviews and joins are counterfactual evidence of those alternatives, not another numerator. A prior design removing no material alternative is disproportionate, as are additions duplicating truth, adding reconciliation or expanding reasoning without materially reducing ambiguity. Existing obligations should absorb detail where ownership and meaning survive. Repeated acquisition, assembly, hashing, preparation, status, review and evidence generation require an identified change, decision or assurance need; repetition adds neither validity nor independence, reuse remains conditional, and materially outcome-affecting operational assumptions require cited UP-019 qualification. For governed cost claims, declare allowance, report measured or unmeasured spend, separate concealable cost components, and declare supported dimensions/workloads before qualification. Report volume is not model traffic. No universal quota, ticket/actor count or separate accounting carrier follows.\",\"uncertainty\":\"UP-019 qualification and the complete delivery-priority law are external references.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:72cf8c2aee0f860a96a4eb82f1f120df","key":924,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:c95cc0e07f26edab0dce96bc1cff9eaf\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:72cf8c2aee0f860a96a4eb82f1f120df\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"A limit is declared through intake, actor envelope or selected execution binding and its owning selected-frame scope.\"],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1623,\"path\":\"standards/ACTIVATION.md\",\"quote\":\"A context limit bounds the material held in active\\n  context at once, including material acquired during the activation\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ACTIVATION.md#ACTIVATION%2F6.%20Cost%20and%20proportionality%2FResource%20limits\",\"start_line\":1616},{\"end_line\":1639,\"path\":\"standards/ACTIVATION.md\",\"quote\":\"Pressure on a declared limit never licenses omitting or\\n  truncating a material obligation or input.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ACTIVATION.md#ACTIVATION%2F6.%20Cost%20and%20proportionality%2FResource%20limits\",\"start_line\":1624}],\"statement\":\"Declare each limit's value before the activation it bounds and specify unit and measurement boundary, including counted inputs, actors, processes and repeated reads. Measure in that unit/boundary where the served obligation needs measurement; outside consumption is recorded unmeasured and receives no limit claim. Separately report initial context bytes, cumulative acquired bytes including rereads, and the bound on simultaneously active material including later acquisitions; different-question measures remain separate. Before exceeding a limit, refine, sequence, reassign to fitting limits or stop with the applicable result naming the limit, such as incomplete when bounded execution ends first; keep unresolved outcome. Enlarging a limit re-enters its grant/binding owner. The execution binding supplies values and measurable units/boundaries, with a referenced build-tenant binding. Staying within limits proves no adequacy; larger limits give no authority or invariant waiver. No universal quota, budget or measurement gate follows.\",\"uncertainty\":\"No selected execution binding or actual limit values are supplied.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:27a1d4fcf6d84dedbc06b72c7e57a2e6","key":925,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:5b25bc7a2a279511eaa355c912e1a27b\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:27a1d4fcf6d84dedbc06b72c7e57a2e6\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1681,\"path\":\"standards/ACTIVATION.md\",\"quote\":\"Invalidation withdraws the result from direct reliance\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ACTIVATION.md#ACTIVATION%2F7.%20Closed%20result%20and%20reuse\",\"start_line\":1677},{\"end_line\":1713,\"path\":\"standards/ACTIVATION.md\",\"quote\":\"A reused judgment does not\\nsatisfy a separately required independent judgment\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ACTIVATION.md#ACTIVATION%2F7.%20Closed%20result%20and%20reuse\",\"start_line\":1704}],\"statement\":\"An unchanged consumer may reuse a result after checking exact applicability. Affectedness is described as dependencies D*(t) meeting impact cover I(Δ). Before reliance, invalidate results affected by material subject/input/evidence change capable of changing value, any changed bound basis coordinate, or occurrence of a declared revising observation. This applies even if subject bytes are unchanged, while preserving predecessor/successor links and demonstrably independent survivors. Invalidation withdraws direct reliance; retain_applicable separately governs retaining evidence on a new basis, and changed coordinates alone establish neither truth nor falsity. Source/task/actor condition changes are basis changes if bound there, otherwise material input changes; role/conversation/resumption changes alone invalidate nothing unless required actor conditions change. Domain triggers instantiate these three kinds, never a parallel list. Judgment continuity names basis/evidence; Return A Closed Result names inputs/observation. Reuse cannot satisfy a separately required independent judgment; an independent assessor acquires its own evidence and gives its own judgment, subject to the permission for shared valid mechanical evidence. Frame revision-coordinate need belongs to REFERENCE_FRAME §10, touched-result validity to this reuse law.\",\"uncertainty\":\"The exact impact-cover, retain_applicable, minimum closed-result shape and independence conditions are referenced but not fully supplied.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:9a841252191c00a2c7b5ef608c195b71","key":926,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:e5c8b96517828a0f56dd887c29ace149\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:9a841252191c00a2c7b5ef608c195b71\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[\"Affected risk may require whole-candidate proof after local change.\"],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1734,\"path\":\"standards/ACTIVATION.md\",\"quote\":\"Construction uses the cheapest focused proof capable of falsifying the\\nactive relation.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ACTIVATION.md#ACTIVATION%2F7.%20Closed%20result%20and%20reuse%2FTransition%20evidence\",\"start_line\":1727}],\"statement\":\"Construction uses the cheapest focused proof capable of falsifying the active relation. Expensive whole-candidate qualification occurs at a declared candidate boundary rather than every local edit, except where affected risk requires it. If loss of incidental process state is a material counterexample to durable/reconstructable authority, same-process proof alone cannot establish that claim: destroy or exclude incidental authority and compare reconstructed semantic outcomes. The evidence record includes all declared transition coordinates, any required integration proof and, conditionally, assessor recommendation and subsequent owner disposition.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:0aa0d0e81eabe53a1189a371c766eab0","key":927,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:9064eb4b0984f7fd1d567f3325b1ca5d\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:0aa0d0e81eabe53a1189a371c766eab0\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":29,\"path\":\"standards/ASSURANCE.md\",\"quote\":\"the profile that maps engagement roles and specialist\\nfamilies onto them is [EXECUTIVE_BASELINE](EXECUTIVE_BASELINE.md), tier 3,\\nand nothing here depends on it.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ASSURANCE.md#ASSURANCE\",\"start_line\":26}],\"statement\":\"ASSURANCE consumes FOUNDATIONS claim/evidence/judgment/authority and result/conjunction laws, REFERENCE_FRAME declarations/conjunction/translation/coverage, EVALUATION separation/assessment/acceptance/conformance, and ACTIVATION applicability/execution/proportionality/reuse. SPEC_METHOD owns the particular chain and change classes; PRODUCT_DEFINITION owns project bindings. The introduction locates the design profile's module-derived unit-proof law in ASSURANCE §§14–16 and ticket test-case authority in TICKETS §7, pre-empting neither. Testing and interface frames are §§7–13; the tier-3 Executive mapping does not govern this member through dependency. Every clause is stated to name its requiring P0–P6 principle.\",\"uncertainty\":\"The module-law ownership phrasing competes with the later taxonomy paragraph; the unsupplied owners cannot resolve it here.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:ce9ecee4c54bab5901552dab44ff2025","key":928,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:06901ce9bac058a7449da2d48cc0ae44\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:ce9ecee4c54bab5901552dab44ff2025\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[\"Constraints, governance rules and verification-infrastructure requirements may need evidence in addition to or instead of end-to-end scenarios.\"],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":64,\"path\":\"standards/ASSURANCE.md\",\"quote\":\"The failure alone does not show whether the realisation, the governing\\nclaim, the scenario's expected outcome or its observation is wrong\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ASSURANCE.md#ASSURANCE%2F1.%20Verification%20layers\",\"start_line\":61}],\"statement\":\"Requirements/design wording alone cannot verify operational capability. While no concrete scenario can be written, operational meaning is unverified, without deciding whether the claim is inadequate or means of stating/observing its outcome are missing; diagnosis locates the cause. Failure reports observed versus expected disagreement and establishes actual-behaviour disagreement only with supported observation binding. Failure alone does not locate error among realisation, governing claim, expected outcome and observation; localisation proceeds only as far as evidence supports. Scenarios primarily validate capability and other operational behaviour and never replace requirement categories or all other evidence.\",\"uncertainty\":\"The diagnostic, observation-binding and counterexample-localisation procedures are referenced outside the supplied detail.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:1cfc131a76df6f85742a5443d4bf5f5e","key":929,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:ad2911520dc8ffb9419df0fede4f0e57\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:1cfc131a76df6f85742a5443d4bf5f5e\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"Use each row only under its specified instance premises.\"],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":98,\"path\":\"standards/ASSURANCE.md\",\"quote\":\"the preference for a fresh sandbox, at \\\"should\\\": a policy choice of this member\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ASSURANCE.md#ASSURANCE%2F1.%20Verification%20layers%2FFoundation%20to%20law%3A%20assurance%20and%20testing\",\"start_line\":97}],\"statement\":\"The foundation table separately states: every executable proof surface declares authority and derives expected results from it, not implementation; project lanes map to one taxonomy before closure. Composed-product acceptance evidence comes through declared surfaces; substituted workers/transports prove only exercised relations and narrower green lanes do not prove a real external boundary. Required lanes reproduce from exact declared source boundary using checked-in fixtures, declared external acquisition or classification outside required closure; missing fixture is an unperformed evaluation, not product semantic failure. Every live requirement has written traceable test authority. Where meaningful behaviour is claimed, proof should be an ordered coherent-use sequence; significant paths are declared and exercised, with undeclared coverage unjudgeable and unexercised behaviour unproved. For an installable-system claim, decisive proof runs against installed development form as an external target; source checks cannot replace it, and a fresh sandbox is a should-level preference. When testing frames are selected, each binds exact claim, subject, path, population, oracle and falsifier; results stay claim-bound and combine only through declared relations. Labels, runners, counts and coverage measures confer no assurance; broader results do not make narrower laws true and narrower green results do not establish unexamined broader claims.\",\"uncertainty\":\"Detailed five significant paths, four ordinary frames and their complete declarations are referenced but not supplied.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:93cd36570856f72013f141f0e0562b0b","key":930,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:ad2911520dc8ffb9419df0fede4f0e57\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:93cd36570856f72013f141f0e0562b0b\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"Apply the relevant row's composition, runnable-product, users or designed-module premises.\"],\"exceptions\":[\"Path-sensitive mutation is a policy choice only where proportionate and safe.\"],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":105,\"path\":\"standards/ASSURANCE.md\",\"quote\":\"a reduced covering set is lawful only with a reason why the omitted interactions cannot change the claim, or with them kept as residuals\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ASSURANCE.md#ASSURANCE%2F1.%20Verification%20layers%2FFoundation%20to%20law%3A%20assurance%20and%20testing\",\"start_line\":100}],\"statement\":\"Path claims require two-sided evidence: required ordinary supported paths witnessed and each forbidden path absent/refused in production and assurance graphs; equal output through a forbidden path falsifies a path claim. Testing value concerns material combinations discriminated, not counts; reduced covering sets need a reason omitted interactions cannot change the claim or explicit residuals, and code coverage proves only visits. Assurance evaluates the owner-issued subject acquired through its owner surface, never parallel reconstructed owner state; missing owner projection remains a named undecided gap. Counterexamples persist until disposed and return to the earliest evidence-supported causal frontier; unique locus, joint set, unresolved alternatives and unbounded frontier remain distinct core-mapped forms, and localisation grants no repair. Interface chains keep contract sufficiency, boundary congruence, path realisation and user usability distinct; full usability requires all four and their conjunction. Each seam binds domains, available context, translation, current observation, actual path and diagnostic cause; local success cannot replace complete-path results. For design-governed boundaries, implementation and unit tests derive from accepted ontology/design/module authority; evidence feeds back without choosing semantic answers. Module-owned unit tests are authoritative for module proof and should trace ownership rather than helper shape; no lane means not closure-ready. Before module closure every lifecycle phase is answered, reasoned not_applicable or named gap; implementation proves only within its authority and gaps proceed only when governed.\",\"uncertainty\":\"The eight index terms, nine factors, four localisation mappings, twelve interface elements, six obligations, ten qualification cases, two module evidence chains and nine lifecycle items are referenced but not enumerated in the supplied source.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:1c17d94aebc89ec5fec96a2ee6b78af1","key":931,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:ad2911520dc8ffb9419df0fede4f0e57\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:1c17d94aebc89ec5fec96a2ee6b78af1\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":109,\"path\":\"standards/ASSURANCE.md\",\"quote\":\"The table accounts for §1 to §16.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ASSURANCE.md#ASSURANCE%2F1.%20Verification%20layers%2FFoundation%20to%20law%3A%20assurance%20and%20testing\",\"start_line\":109},{\"end_line\":131,\"path\":\"standards/ASSURANCE.md\",\"quote\":\"Each consumer applies the rule and decides nothing the owning section does\\nnot (P2, P6).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ASSURANCE.md#ASSURANCE%2F1.%20Verification%20layers%2FFoundation%20to%20law%3A%20assurance%20and%20testing\",\"start_line\":130}],\"statement\":\"Row provenance is retained as source claims, not established derivations: verification P2/P6 with runnable product+users, pillars 1,5,9; taxonomy P6/P2/P1 with runnable product, 4,9; composed acceptance P6/P1/P5 with runnable product+users+external boundaries, 8,9; portability P3/P6/P5 with external boundaries, 8,9; test authority/paths P6/P2 with composition, 1,5,9; installed proof P6/P3 with runnable product, 8,9; testing frames P0/P6/P1/P4a with composition, 3,7,9; path claims P6/P3/P5 with runnable product+composition, 4,9; combinations P2/P6/P5/P4a with composition, 3,9; subject acquisition P6/P1/P5 with runnable product, 6,9; localisation P5/P1/P4b with composition, 3,9; interfaces P0/P1/P4a/P5/P6 with composition+users, 4,7,9; module tests P6/P4b/P2 with designed modules, 4,9; lifecycle P2/P6/P5 with designed modules, 1,9. P0 is recovered, P1/P2/P3/P4a/P6 independent, P5 derived from P0/P6 with open-world premise, and P4b derived from P0/P2 with non-reacquirable step-produced facts. ASSURANCE's added choices include the three layers/product-owner scenarios; two proof authorities/context/terminology; sandbox modes; three portability forms; scenario bundle/five usual paths; fresh-sandbox preference; four ordinary frames/declarations; proportionate safe path mutation; eight index terms/nine factors; four localisation forms; interface identity/twelve elements/four claims/six obligations/ten cases; two module evidence chains/completeness/traceability; nine lifecycle items. Project chooses lane names; governing frame configuration or admitted authority selects testing/interface frames; scalar scores belong to Product/requirement/accepted-design authority. SPEC_METHOD owns chain, change re-entry and lifecycle markers; FOUNDATIONS owns observation binding and install/development roles; ACTIVATION owns diagnosis; TICKETS owns admitted test derivation; DESIGN_MODULE binds module terms and computational recurrence; EXECUTIVE_BASELINE maps roles/families. Consumer listings identify applications, not transferred ownership; merely naming a law is distinguished from applying it, and each consumer decides nothing beyond the owner.\",\"uncertainty\":\"Full standing and detailed referenced domain inventories remain outside the supplied excerpts.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:8c3f3bf2694e89b5c877cf9bfe75a242","key":932,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:2e29eb63656a6092cdf8daa41beaada3\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:433fbad86b733e2a1409c02021a25be1\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:8c3f3bf2694e89b5c877cf9bfe75a242\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":171,\"path\":\"standards/ASSURANCE.md\",\"quote\":\"Authority source is not execution breadth.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ASSURANCE.md#ASSURANCE%2F2.%20Testing%20strategy%20taxonomy\",\"start_line\":149},{\"end_line\":199,\"path\":\"standards/ASSURANCE.md\",\"quote\":\"Where a product or release\\nclaim depends on live probabilistic compute, semantic green, unit green,\\nmodule-integration green and harnessed-sandbox green are necessary and not\\nsufficient for live acceptance\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ASSURANCE.md#ASSURANCE%2F2.%20Testing%20strategy%20taxonomy\",\"start_line\":196}],\"statement\":\"Every executable proof surface declares authority. For ticketed work, admitted ticket and triage path are immediate authority; expected results derive from lawful re-entry and cited constitutional/realisation law, never current implementation behaviour. Conformance derives from governing design, module ownership, declared carrier inventory or equivalent, structural diagrams where present and boundary-local fail-closed law. Unit tests are conformance; module integration, negative and fail-closed tests may be conformance when their target is a designed boundary rather than user scenario. UAT derives from requirements, acceptance criteria, declared scenarios/use cases and product release/qualification claims. Direct source unit/helper/module-integration tests cannot alone close user acceptance or be called UAT. Harnessed UAT proves composition, orchestration, control, projection, archive and scenario wiring with deterministic reproducibility; live UAT proves the same scenario crosses the actual external probabilistic boundary and returns evidence through result, evaluation, provenance and projection surfaces. Live-dependent claims require more than necessary semantic/unit/integration/harnessed green results. Unit denotes conformance scope, integration breadth rather than authority, sandbox composed acceptance, harnessed/fake/recorded/deterministic non-live execution, and live actual external execution; a projection merely named live is insufficient. Every local lane label maps to this taxonomy before closure.\",\"uncertainty\":\"Module-derived unit-proof ownership is textually unsettled across the supplied sections.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:984f44328b8ff22b978be206672e8e52","key":933,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:3bc1331fd561438b3abf435cbe8f3166\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:984f44328b8ff22b978be206672e8e52\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":221,\"path\":\"standards/ASSURANCE.md\",\"quote\":\"Required closure lanes are reproducible from the declared source boundary\\n(P3, P6). A unit, semantic or\\nmodule-design conformance lane does not depend on an undeclared local path,\\na sibling workspace, an operator home directory or a mutable external\\nfixture.\\n\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ASSURANCE.md#ASSURANCE%2F2.%20Testing%20strategy%20taxonomy%2FFixture%20and%20proof%20portability\",\"start_line\":217},{\"end_line\":234,\"path\":\"standards/ASSURANCE.md\",\"quote\":\"A missing external fixture fails with a governed diagnostic that names the\\nfixture authority and the lane; it never masquerades as a product semantic\\nfailure\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ASSURANCE.md#ASSURANCE%2F2.%20Testing%20strategy%20taxonomy%2FFixture%20and%20proof%20portability\",\"start_line\":232}],\"statement\":\"Required closure lanes reproduce from the declared source boundary. Unit, semantic and module-design conformance lanes must not depend on an undeclared local path, sibling workspace, operator home directory or mutable external fixture. Missing external fixtures produce a governed diagnostic naming fixture authority and lane, never a product semantic failure.\",\"uncertainty\":\"The family consumer note's reference to a core value for an unperformed evaluation is retained separately as a textual tension.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:ef827f7709fbae8aa7a8fc67b6b9b176","key":934,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:12d92e8aac0a56903f7c6713bf136289\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:ef827f7709fbae8aa7a8fc67b6b9b176\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"A requirement is live.\"],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":252,\"path\":\"standards/ASSURANCE.md\",\"quote\":\"No live requirement is fully proved on\\ninformal operator confidence, ambient habit or an unlabelled test corpus\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ASSURANCE.md#ASSURANCE%2F3.%20Test%20authority\",\"start_line\":248}],\"statement\":\"Every live requirement has written, traceable test-case authority including full expected-result assertion provenance and predicate relationship to its owning obligation. Informal confidence, ambient habit, unlabelled tests and green labels cannot by themselves establish full proof or acceptance. Derivation from admitted work authority is delegated by reference to TICKETS §7.\",\"uncertainty\":\"The referenced ticket derivation and assertion/parallel-derivation laws are not fully supplied.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:71fbadfc84c94fbba2786125bd21803d","key":935,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:a53692f0d555aea884937662d5230e55\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:f9c245e92a9e876a8878777f5d99ecff\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:71fbadfc84c94fbba2786125bd21803d\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"A requirement claims meaningful system behaviour.\"],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":260,\"path\":\"standards/ASSURANCE.md\",\"quote\":\"Features are not proved by isolated assertions alone. Where a requirement\\nclaims meaningful system behaviour, the proving surface should be a scenario\\nbundle or an equivalent ordered set of test cases that exercises that\\nbehaviour through a coherent sequence rather than as disconnected\\nfragments (P2, P6).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ASSURANCE.md#ASSURANCE%2F4.%20Scenario%20bundle\",\"start_line\":256}],\"statement\":\"Isolated assertions alone do not prove features. The proving surface should use a scenario bundle or equivalent ordered cases exercising coherent behaviour. Scenarios and use cases force operational intent/design to expose boundaries, sequences, actors, controls and outcomes; the significant paths they identify must be exercised.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:7551d47b1944a843c562ddfc1e4faf82","key":936,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:b0b4ff2640d207bee8d1ebe2ff5163f3\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:7551d47b1944a843c562ddfc1e4faf82\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"The system has an installable or runnable development form.\"],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":285,\"path\":\"standards/ASSURANCE.md\",\"quote\":\"proof should prefer a fresh sandbox or equivalent isolated environment, an\\ninstalled or built development artifact, and execution through the same\\ndeclared entry, control and runtime surfaces the real product uses. Direct\\nsource-level or unit-level checks may stay useful; they do not replace\\ninstalled-dev proof of the system under test (P6; SPEC_METHOD §6 for the\\ninstall and development-product roles).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ASSURANCE.md#ASSURANCE%2F5.%20Installed%20dev%20proof\",\"start_line\":280}],\"statement\":\"The decisive lane runs against an installed development target, not solely the source tree. It should prefer fresh isolation, an installed/built artifact and the Product's declared entry/control/runtime surfaces. Useful source/unit checks do not replace this proof.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:3bb2f2ed3c0876f49db01b235382acff","key":937,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:f9c245e92a9e876a8878777f5d99ecff\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:3bb2f2ed3c0876f49db01b235382acff\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":304,\"path\":\"standards/ASSURANCE.md\",\"quote\":\"If the significant paths are not declared, scenario coverage cannot be\\njudged. If they are declared and not exercised, the behaviour is not fully\\nproved (P6; EVALUATION §1, a claim's scope cannot exceed its evaluated\\nevidence).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ASSURANCE.md#ASSURANCE%2F6.%20Significant%20path%20coverage\",\"start_line\":301}],\"statement\":\"The proving surface declares and exercises meaningful paths intentionally; exhaustive proof does not require every possible branch in every file. Undeclared paths make scenario coverage unjudgeable; declared but unexercised significant paths leave behaviour not fully proved. Claim scope cannot exceed evaluated evidence. The listed path classes are usual and relevance-dependent, not a universal exhaustive checklist.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:d8ac4e776c0b3c790d6cbf4644160d3d","key":938,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:2aa7efe612226c86a56903f07ffef6a4\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:a95cc4187253ab78a3b16b5c7c45e144\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:37c6c0adb01d42ea37f40ece5db0dad2\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:d8ac4e776c0b3c790d6cbf4644160d3d\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":325,\"path\":\"standards/ASSURANCE.md\",\"quote\":\"Producing an expected output through a bypass, an obsolete executor, a\\ntest-only seam, an undeclared fallback or a competing authority falsifies\\npath conformance even when the output value is equal (P6, P3).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ASSURANCE.md#ASSURANCE%2F7.%20Product%20testing%20frame%20set%2FTerms\",\"start_line\":323}],\"statement\":\"Files, suites, runners, fixtures, scenario labels, coverage percentages and actors do not become frames merely by existing. Authority stays within the exercised claim; counts, source coverage, duration and framework category do not enlarge it. Equal output through bypass, obsolete executor, test-only seam, undeclared fallback or competing authority falsifies path conformance. Cross-participant combinations cannot be mocked away and counted as unit evidence.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:9cfff93b30f99373281f0d72e5dc6bf7","key":939,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:5501995e5fa70ff1ab307cf852168870\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:2aa7efe612226c86a56903f07ffef6a4\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:9cfff93b30f99373281f0d72e5dc6bf7\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"Testing frames have been selected under governing configuration or admitted work authority.\"],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":385,\"path\":\"standards/ASSURANCE.md\",\"quote\":\"The fan-out assigns claims to evidence; it is neither an authority\\nhierarchy nor a claim that one frame decomposes into another. Evidence\\nmay relate through declared conjunction\\n([FOUNDATIONS §4 Conjunction of results](FOUNDATIONS.md#conjunction-of-results)),\\ntranslation (REFERENCE_FRAME §6), falsification and re-entry (P4a). A\\nbroader frame cannot make a module-owned\\nlaw true, and any number of narrower green frames cannot establish an\\nunevaluated Product composition or user outcome (EVALUATION §1, the weaker\\nproperty never substitutes for the claimed one).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ASSURANCE.md#ASSURANCE%2F7.%20Product%20testing%20frame%20set%2FThe%20set\",\"start_line\":377}],\"statement\":\"Frame selection is determined by evaluated claim, subject, path, population, oracle and falsification boundary, not runner kind. The four frames introduce no role, stage, authority or hierarchy and do not decompose into one another. Each claim is assigned congruent evidence: user outcome to UAT, runnable causal path to end to end, composition boundary to integration, module law to unit. Internal complexity sets unit evidence size/strategy, never eligibility. Broader evidence cannot make a module law true; arbitrarily many narrower successes cannot establish an unevaluated Product composition/outcome. Frame labels without declarations have no assurance value. Each core result retains its claim predicate; invalidation rows only instantiate material-input or basis changes under ACTIVATION §7, adding no other invalidator.\",\"uncertainty\":\"The referenced activation, frame-declaration and core-result owners are not supplied in full.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:0fd3f57e814042cb9f8f92db6d918479","key":940,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:9e6e1272a4d33627b22f146f2f8b9751\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:0fd3f57e814042cb9f8f92db6d918479\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":412,\"path\":\"standards/ASSURANCE.md\",\"quote\":\"| exclusions | source imports, private APIs, direct Product-state injection, test-only endpoints, hidden administrator capability, undeclared fixtures or substitutes, a test double at a boundary claimed as real or live, compatibility bypasses, and internal success substituted for the user outcome |\\n| result | one core result bound to the exact user-outcome claim, with witnessed paths, counterexamples, residual user populations and invalidation conditions |\\n| invalidation | a material change of Product, supported interface, user role, capability, configuration, dependency or substitution mode, data contract, runnable subject, acceptance meaning or ordinary path |\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ASSURANCE.md#ASSURANCE%2F7.%20Product%20testing%20frame%20set%2FUser-acceptance%20frame\",\"start_line\":410}],\"statement\":\"UAT obeys applicable Product/requirement outcomes, supported-interface, identity, UX, safety, persistence and release law, RF-001–017 and EVALUATION §§1,2,3,6,7. It has bounded evaluation authority only: no new Product meaning or acceptance ownership. Exclude source imports, private APIs, state injection, test-only endpoints, hidden administrator power, undeclared fixtures/substitutes, doubles at claimed real/live boundaries, compatibility bypasses and internal success substituted for user outcome. Return one exact-claim core result with witnessed paths, counterexamples, residual users and invalidators. Material changes to Product, interface, role, capability, configuration, dependency/substitution mode, data contract, runnable subject, acceptance meaning or ordinary path invalidate it.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:f182d82b176d62f66b0c56cde7058af7","key":941,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:9e6e1272a4d33627b22f146f2f8b9751\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:f182d82b176d62f66b0c56cde7058af7\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"Harnessed sandbox UAT is admitted, or a claim depends on real external compute or transport.\"],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":426,\"path\":\"standards/ASSURANCE.md\",\"quote\":\"Where harnessed sandbox UAT is admitted (§2), a deterministic, fake,\\nrecorded or injected external worker or transport limits the result to the\\ncomposed Product relations actually exercised; it does not prove that the\\nlive external boundary works. When a Product or release claim depends on\\nreal external compute or transport, live sandbox UAT is mandatory for that\\nclaim; unit, integration, semantic and end-to-end evidence that uses the\\nsubstitute, and harnessed UAT green, are not sufficient (P6, P5).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ASSURANCE.md#ASSURANCE%2F7.%20Product%20testing%20frame%20set%2FUser-acceptance%20frame\",\"start_line\":420}],\"statement\":\"Deterministic, fake, recorded or injected workers/transports restrict harnessed UAT results to exercised composed relations and prove no live boundary. A Product/release claim depending on real external compute/transport requires live sandbox UAT for that claim; substitute-based unit, integration, semantic, end-to-end evidence and harnessed UAT success are insufficient.\",\"uncertainty\":\"Section 2's admission conditions are outside the supplied source.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:b436359168d2b8bf3b9057c6d35643c7","key":942,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:74b38a1ed583949eef88dee3e98a862a\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:b436359168d2b8bf3b9057c6d35643c7\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":444,\"path\":\"standards/ASSURANCE.md\",\"quote\":\"| exclusions | source-only substitutes for runnable-Product claims, direct invocation below the supported entry, test doubles at claimed real boundaries, test-only routing, hidden retries or repair, omitted persistence or fresh-process boundaries, and equal output without path evidence |\\n| result | one core result bound to the exact end-to-end claim, with the exercised composition edges, unexercised material paths, counterexamples and residual combinations |\\n| invalidation | a material change of artifact, install, dependency, configuration, interface, owner, path, lifecycle, persistence, recovery, projection, test semantics or evidence population |\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ASSURANCE.md#ASSURANCE%2F7.%20Product%20testing%20frame%20set%2FEnd-to-end%20frame\",\"start_line\":442}],\"statement\":\"Governed by Product/accepted-design composition, exact-subject/assurance congruence, path singularity where required and lifecycle, authority, persistence, replay, recovery and release law. Observation may expose internals but cannot bypass, repair, replace or reinterpret the path. Exclude source-only runnable substitutes, below-entry calls, doubles at real boundaries, test routing, hidden retry/repair, omitted persistence/fresh-process boundaries and output without path evidence. Return an exact-claim core result with exercised edges, unexercised material paths, counterexamples and residual combinations. Material artifact/install/dependency/configuration/interface/owner/path/lifecycle/persistence/recovery/projection/test-semantics/evidence-population changes invalidate it. Expected output is necessary but insufficient; forbidden or obsolete paths falsify the claim. One process, many lines or an end-to-end label do not establish frame identity.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:5328bec6996a38bb5200c799b146c1f2","key":943,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:1c4c010033a4beec67d91c7c12d3f812\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:5328bec6996a38bb5200c799b146c1f2\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":467,\"path\":\"standards/ASSURANCE.md\",\"quote\":\"| exclusions | mocks or stubs that hide the claimed real contract, one-sided contract assertions, happy-path-only exchange, helper-call equivalence, flattened versions or states, and projection of a boundary result to the whole Product without a governing relation |\\n| result | one core result for the declared integration claim, with covered combinations, counterexamples, omitted interactions and invalidation conditions |\\n| invalidation | a material change of participant, interface, carrier, state, configuration, dependency, timing, failure, recovery or interaction population |\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ASSURANCE.md#ASSURANCE%2F7.%20Product%20testing%20frame%20set%2FIntegration%20frame\",\"start_line\":465}],\"statement\":\"Apply declared interface/composition law, complete participant admission, applicable atomicity/reconstruction and exact assurance boundaries. Boundary evaluation neither establishes an unevaluated Product outcome nor authorises substitution. Exclude mocks hiding real contracts, one-sided assertions, happy-path-only exchanges, helper equivalence, flattened versions/states and whole-Product projection without a governing relation. Return one integration core result with covered combinations, counterexamples, omissions and invalidators. Material participant/interface/carrier/state/configuration/dependency/timing/failure/recovery/population changes invalidate it.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:eef31a34ab52452efd05c6e5fc8f09d1","key":944,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:9873a2fcf1a72b9c6d82964e88b5d0b2\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:f36832f6941f8683b920fbd70d2f5ad7\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:eef31a34ab52452efd05c6e5fc8f09d1\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":490,\"path\":\"standards/ASSURANCE.md\",\"quote\":\"| authority | bounded local evidence only; a unit result has no Product, installed, integration, user-acceptance, architecture, path-selection or release authority |\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ASSURANCE.md#ASSURANCE%2F7.%20Product%20testing%20frame%20set%2FUnit%20frame\",\"start_line\":485},{\"end_line\":519,\"path\":\"standards/ASSURANCE.md\",\"quote\":\"No Product, user-outcome, installed-path, cross-module composition or\\nrelease claim may be closed from unit evidence, whatever the test count,\\nassertion count, source coverage, mutation score, runtime or historical\\npass rate. Treating unit green as broader assurance is a frame error (P6,\\nEVALUATION §1).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ASSURANCE.md#ASSURANCE%2F7.%20Product%20testing%20frame%20set%2FUnit%20frame\",\"start_line\":515}],\"statement\":\"Unit proof obeys DESIGN_MODULE ownership/proof law and accepted ontology, carriers, domain, sequence, state, algorithm and error relations. It excludes Product outcomes, cross-module composition, supported user paths, packaging/install, real external participants, orchestration topology, mocked-away interface behaviour, incidental branches/private layout, assertion counts and source coverage as broader assurance. Return one exact-law/module-population core result with counterexamples, residual combinations and invalidators. Material changes to ontology, carriers, boundary, law, algorithm, state space, numerical regime, implementation, oracle, generator or bounded population invalidate it. No unit metric or success closes Product, user, installed, composition or release claims or supplies architecture/path-selection authority.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:b9ca3999fb551a1483ac71f2ccaf7b23","key":945,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:9873a2fcf1a72b9c6d82964e88b5d0b2\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:f36832f6941f8683b920fbd70d2f5ad7\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:b9ca3999fb551a1483ac71f2ccaf7b23\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"A module has code.\"],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":513,\"path\":\"standards/ASSURANCE.md\",\"quote\":\"This frame does not waive the module-derived unit lane. It binds the lane\\nto module-owned law and the smallest congruent evidence population. Low\\ninternal combinatorial complexity justifies a small lane, not omission and\\nnot hundreds of implementation-shaped tests. Unit-test volume has no\\nindependent closure value (P2).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ASSURANCE.md#ASSURANCE%2F7.%20Product%20testing%20frame%20set%2FUnit%20frame\",\"start_line\":509}],\"statement\":\"Every coded module requires the design-owned module-derived unit lane; public contracts are eligible. Complexity determines proportional size/strategy and the smallest congruent population, not omission or large implementation-shaped suites. Independent oracles often discriminate algebras, calculations, transformations, parsers, reducers, state machines, decision tables, admission/conservation relations and bounded algorithms especially well. Repeating implementation or incidental branches yields weak/circular evidence. Predominantly composition, orchestration, configuration, persistence, ownership or user-interaction complexity needs evidence at its actual integration/end-to-end/UAT boundary; mocking it does not create unit evidence.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:9481253eff88964e304168d10a5ffcab","key":946,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:9998e713a60bf1ac244a0e611d7a518a\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:37c6c0adb01d42ea37f40ece5db0dad2\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:9481253eff88964e304168d10a5ffcab\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":575,\"path\":\"standards/ASSURANCE.md\",\"quote\":\"The activated frame declares the finite interaction population and why its\\ncovering set is adequate. Pairwise or other covering-array reduction is\\nlawful only where the basis explains why the omitted higher-order\\ninteractions cannot change the claim, or keeps them as residuals.\\nHigh-consequence authority, persistence, concurrency, recovery, migration\\nand historically failure-prone relations normally need explicit\\nhigher-strength combinations (P5, P2; REFERENCE_FRAME §8, interaction and\\nfailure coverage).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ASSURANCE.md#ASSURANCE%2F8.%20Combinatorial%20coverage%20and%20testing%20value\",\"start_line\":568}],\"statement\":\"Activated frames declare finite interaction populations and covering-set adequacy. Unit dimensions remain module-bounded; value normally rises with closed-domain internal complexity. Integration/end-to-end/UAT value can be multiplicative through composed pre/postconditions, authority, state, configuration, failure and recovery, but depends on interactions actually discriminated, not sunny-path interface count. Common Product factors include user role/capability, operation/composition, definition/owner/implementation/dependency, lifecycle/persisted state, configuration/version, process/continuation/retry/re-entry/recovery, success/refusal/malformed/partial-failure/rival cases, fresh process/replay/reconstruction/migration and visible outcome/projection. High-consequence authority, persistence, concurrency, recovery, migration and historically fragile relations normally need explicit higher-strength coverage. Code visitation metrics do not establish semantic combinations, authoritative selection, user coverage or rival-path absence.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:8ca2cf800e571c05d0fcc732b9b22a70","key":947,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:a95cc4187253ab78a3b16b5c7c45e144\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:3635e0d97a204bc786bfeff7cc2b76e4\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:8ca2cf800e571c05d0fcc732b9b22a70\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"A Product path claim is made.\"],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":591,\"path\":\"standards/ASSURANCE.md\",\"quote\":\"Every Product path claim needs two-sided evidence (P6, P3):\\n\\n1. required-path reachability: each required authoritative composition has\\n   an exact witness in the deployed, installed or otherwise runnable\\n   Product form through the supported ordinary path; and\\n2. forbidden-path exclusion: each material superseded, duplicate,\\n   fallback, bypass or otherwise forbidden production path is absent,\\n   unreachable or refused at its declared boundary.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ASSURANCE.md#ASSURANCE%2F9.%20Legitimate%20path%20and%20technical-debt%20erasure\",\"start_line\":584}],\"statement\":\"Every required authoritative composition needs an exact supported ordinary-path witness in the runnable Product. Every material superseded, duplicate, fallback, bypass or other forbidden production path must be absent, unreachable or refused at its declared boundary. Successor success proves no predecessor removal. No obsolete/bypass/fallback/rival path may remain reachable in scoped production closure; no obsolete assurance consumer may falsely prove closure or reintroduce removed production paths. A forbidden-path outcome falsifies the path claim.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:483cc88ad05fe0eb7c49c01025d59d2d","key":948,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:3635e0d97a204bc786bfeff7cc2b76e4\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:483cc88ad05fe0eb7c49c01025d59d2d\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"Path-sensitive mutation or sabotage is proportionate and safe.\"],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":630,\"path\":\"standards/ASSURANCE.md\",\"quote\":\"A Product outcome reached through a forbidden path is a falsified path\\nclaim, not a passing Product test. A negative-path test that mutates the\\nexact subject without isolation, restoration and subject revalidation\\ninvalidates its own assurance basis (P6, P3).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ASSURANCE.md#ASSURANCE%2F9.%20Legitimate%20path%20and%20technical-debt%20erasure\",\"start_line\":627}],\"statement\":\"Assurance includes checks that disabling the authoritative path prevents scenario success, restoring a rival produces refusal/detected counterexample, corrupting material interface/owner output is detected at its owning boundary, and removing an asserted obsolete path preserves accepted outcome except through the declared deletion relation. Negative tests mutating the exact subject without isolation, restoration and subject revalidation invalidate their own basis.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:1b2ac30da0a6a2e4e4e615c88bf8675d","key":949,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:5501995e5fa70ff1ab307cf852168870\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:2aa7efe612226c86a56903f07ffef6a4\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:1b2ac30da0a6a2e4e4e615c88bf8675d\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":645,\"path\":\"standards/ASSURANCE.md\",\"quote\":\"Each bound result states which\\npredicate it establishes; a result over a necessary condition does not\\nestablish the obligation, and the sufficiency of a conjunction is a claim\\nof its own ([FOUNDATIONS §4 Assertions and observation](FOUNDATIONS.md#assertions-and-observation))\\n(P6).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ASSURANCE.md#ASSURANCE%2F10.%20Testing%20evidence%20composition\",\"start_line\":641}],\"statement\":\"A shared execution can yield distinct UAT outcome, end-to-end path, integration seam evidence and module-algebra counterexamples. Claims combine only through declared REFERENCE_FRAME §6 relations and FOUNDATIONS conjunction, with each predicate retained. Necessary-condition evidence does not establish the obligation; conjunction sufficiency is a separate claim. Default responsibilities remain user outcome, complete authoritative runnable path, material participant composition and proportionate module-law evidence respectively. UAT alone may leave path singularity open; end-to-end alone may leave user populations/combinations open; integration/unit cannot substitute for either. When all are required, conflicts and missing results remain visible to the decision owner and cannot be hidden by aggregate success.\",\"uncertainty\":\"The imported conjunction law is referenced but not supplied in full.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:22148c158cb713686fbfa92935c91f0e","key":950,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:4a758d8b16a2d0014a7ecd1bc24c03f7\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:22148c158cb713686fbfa92935c91f0e\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"The assessed claim depends on owner-issued truth.\"],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":681,\"path\":\"standards/ASSURANCE.md\",\"quote\":\"Where the acquired observation cannot\\nseparate two admissible subjects on which the assessed predicate takes\\nopposite truth values, the frame returns further evidence, a justified\\nnarrower scope or `indeterminate`. The binding of the\\nobservation itself needs support\\n([FOUNDATIONS §4 Assertions and observation](FOUNDATIONS.md#assertions-and-observation),\\nObservation sufficiency) (P1, P6).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ASSURANCE.md#ASSURANCE%2F11.%20Assurance%20subject%20acquisition%20and%20evaluation\",\"start_line\":675}],\"statement\":\"Harnesses, fixtures, expected-value builders, proof scripts, evaluators and assessors cannot reconstruct parallel owner state from raw payloads/events/logs/filenames/labels/implementation fragments and treat it as the Product. Observation bindings require support. If admissible subjects with opposite predicate truth remain observationally indistinguishable, seek further evidence, justify narrower scope or return indeterminate. The semantic oracle derives independently from Product, requirement and accepted design, not mandatory trust in implementation. Missing owner projections/observable seams remain named assurance/design gaps; harnesses cannot fill them with rival semantics.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:6ab91f4366633eda3c92a8d81c3cb1c7","key":951,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:75d7ebdc57547aefb3f31ca6c91db8e4\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:6ab91f4366633eda3c92a8d81c3cb1c7\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":728,\"path\":\"standards/ASSURANCE.md\",\"quote\":\"One unique violated locus and a jointly established set\\nmap to `satisfied`. Unresolved alternative frontiers map to\\n`indeterminate`, naming the alternatives that further evidence must\\ndecide between. The fourth form is the core value `indeterminate` itself,\\nnaming the evidence a bounded frontier needs. The form travels with the\\nvalue as the domain outcome, so a joint set stays distinct from a unique\\nlocus and unresolved alternatives stay distinct from an unbounded\\nfrontier. Purpose and material relation: a localisation combines with\\nother results in the one core, and an unresolved causal explanation is\\nnever read as an established one (P5, P1, P6).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ASSURANCE.md#ASSURANCE%2F12.%20Counterexample%20localisation\",\"start_line\":719}],\"statement\":\"Exactly one frontier form is returned. Unique locus and jointly established minimal incomparable loci map to satisfied for the predicate that evidence establishes earliest violated loci; unresolved alternatives map to indeterminate naming alternatives, and unbounded frontier maps to indeterminate naming needed evidence. Preserve the domain form alongside the core value. Record subject, basis, frontier form/members, causal evidence, expected relations, observed counterexample and invalidated downstream claims. Do not choose an arbitrary owner from joint causes or convert alternatives into joint causes. Localisation grants no broader tests, compatibility repair, controller or upstream reinterpretation; scope/design change follows existing re-entry.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:559156728c4d119e6dd8afd94c0ef6a5","key":952,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:edbbabc8b2dc4636bae4930b21b2d9bb\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:559156728c4d119e6dd8afd94c0ef6a5\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"The composite refinement is activated.\"],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":767,\"path\":\"standards/ASSURANCE.md\",\"quote\":\"| result and relations | each activated claim returns a core result with its exact evidence, coverage, causal findings and residuals; shared evidence is referenced once; mandatory claims compose only through a declared same-basis or lawful-translation conjunction (FOUNDATIONS §4 Conjunction of results) to the named decision consumer |\\n| invalidation | a material change of contract, domain, participant, prompt or context, capability, callable path, configuration, translation, relevant workspace observation, lifecycle, oracle or evidence population invalidates the affected conclusions; unchanged valid evidence and owner rulings stay reusable |\\n| qualification | the representative sensitivity and refusal cases below, bound to actual subjects, actor envelopes and independently stated expected relations; mechanical source checks supply no semantic or live-user qualification |\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ASSURANCE.md#ASSURANCE%2F13.%20End-to-end%20interface%20integration%20frame\",\"start_line\":765}],\"statement\":\"Apply selected Product/requirement/design/interface law, REFERENCE_FRAME declaration/translation law, FOUNDATIONS conjunction and existing testing-owner law. Equal shape/output implies no equal meaning, provenance or authority. Owners retain semantic, operation, admission and reserved decisions; bounded evaluation grants construction only under an existing exact operation grant and returns closed results to the declared decision consumer. Evidence binds contracts/both sides, design relations plus unresolved realisation facts for design claims, or actual requests/context/responses, callables/configuration, owner validation, effects/observations and ordinary-caller outcomes for realised claims, with independent expectations and substitution limits. Access must not alter reviewed subjects; required independence is claim-relative. Exclude hidden context/privilege, rival contract truth, inferred authority, undeclared substitutes, private/test paths for ordinary claims, candidate-as-admission, fixture-as-user evidence and unsupported whole-Product/future claims. Each activated claim returns exact evidence, coverage, causal findings and residuals; shared evidence is referenced once and mandatory claims compose only through declared same-basis/lawful-translation conjunction. Material contract/domain/participant/prompt/context/capability/path/configuration/translation/workspace/lifecycle/oracle/population changes invalidate affected conclusions; unchanged valid evidence/rulings remain reusable. Mechanical source checks give no semantic or live-user qualification.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:71ea5193b224042ddb698669c9aff367","key":953,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:548e95b2ad0b13be8c12ff0b8188144c\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:71ea5193b224042ddb698669c9aff367\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":793,\"path\":\"standards/ASSURANCE.md\",\"quote\":\"The activation selects claims from the work's applicability (ACTIVATION §1)\\nand states the scope reason for each unselected claim; an unselected claim\\nhas no result. Design-only work\\ndoes not require unavailable runtime evidence and does not report runtime or\\nUAT satisfaction. An unknown material condition keeps its dependent claim\\nunresolved: the claim's result is never `satisfied` and names the\\ncondition as what would decide it\\n([FOUNDATIONS §4 Results](FOUNDATIONS.md#results), Standing); omission\\ncannot close it. A full end-to-end usability claim\\nneeds all four distinct results and their explicit conjunction\\n([FOUNDATIONS §4 Conjunction of results](FOUNDATIONS.md#conjunction-of-results)),\\nin which an unselected claim is uncovered coverage. Transport,\\nparse, admission, semantic satisfaction, operation completion and user\\nsuccess are not interchangeable (P5, P6).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ASSURANCE.md#ASSURANCE%2F13.%20End-to-end%20interface%20integration%20frame%2FClaim%20boundaries\",\"start_line\":780}],\"statement\":\"Activation selects applicable claims and records scope reasons for every unselected claim, which has no result. Design-only work can establish contract sufficiency without runtime, keeps realisability/context uncertainty explicit, requires no unavailable runtime evidence and claims no runtime/UAT satisfaction. Actual-composition claims acquire both sides/exchanges; design correspondence proves no implementation behaviour. Matching output on another path does not prove path realisation; internal or validator-aware fixture success does not prove usability. Unknown material conditions leave dependent claims unresolved, never satisfied, naming deciding conditions; omission does not close them. Full end-to-end usability requires four distinct results plus explicit conjunction; an unselected claim is uncovered. Transport, parse, admission, semantic satisfaction, operation completion and user success remain distinct.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:b2b07af384f391edf6ad3bc028b53f4e","key":954,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:edbbabc8b2dc4636bae4930b21b2d9bb\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:548e95b2ad0b13be8c12ff0b8188144c\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:b2b07af384f391edf6ad3bc028b53f4e\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"For every material seam.\"],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":808,\"path\":\"standards/ASSURANCE.md\",\"quote\":\"1. Bind the functional input domain, producer success postconditions,\\n   consumer preconditions, permitted effects, refusals and observable exit.\\n   Direct successful handoff requires the producer's guarantees to meet the\\n   consumer's preconditions. An interface may instead emit candidates:\\n   candidate output, later admission and semantic assessment stay distinct\\n   declared stages. A normal model refusal or an inadmissible candidate does\\n   not by itself falsify an adequately declared candidate interface; the\\n   exact promised outcome and refusal behaviour are evaluated (P4a, P5).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ASSURANCE.md#ASSURANCE%2F13.%20End-to-end%20interface%20integration%20frame%2FObligations\",\"start_line\":801}],\"statement\":\"Reuse existing truth surfaces; add only missing cross-interface relations, without making schemas/prompts/adapters/indexes/tests contract owners. Bind functional inputs, producer success guarantees, consumer preconditions, effects, refusals and exit; direct success requires guarantees to meet preconditions. Candidate output, admission and semantic assessment remain declared distinct stages; normal refusal/inadmissible candidates alone do not falsify an adequate candidate contract. Supply material actor obligations/domains through actual context/interface or an exactly locatable lawfully resolvable source. Bind material LLM role, instructions, context, tools and model/transport configuration. Generic governance access neither supplies Product-specific contracts nor authorises hidden-rule inference. Deterministic owners expose computed facts by reuse/proven equivalent projection; semantic actors judge meaning within that domain, without inferring reserved rulings, eligibility, authority or admission from responses/labels.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:1f7089dd48c486660f00d260f790349b","key":955,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:edbbabc8b2dc4636bae4930b21b2d9bb\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:1f7089dd48c486660f00d260f790349b\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"For every material seam and each later operation on a mutable workspace.\"],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":833,\"path\":\"standards/ASSURANCE.md\",\"quote\":\"4. Observe the relevant current mutable workspace for each later\\n   operation, and bind that observation separately from immutable\\n   authority, artifacts, history and prior candidates. Changed support\\n   invalidates dependent conclusions; unaffected accepted work stays\\n   reusable. A snapshot does not replace the current subject, and a change\\n   of actor alone is no reason to repeat still-valid work (P3, P4b;\\n   ACTIVATION §7).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ASSURANCE.md#ASSURANCE%2F13.%20End-to-end%20interface%20integration%20frame%2FObligations\",\"start_line\":827}],\"statement\":\"Preserve domain/time meaning through serialisation, parsing, normalisation and adaptation. Translation binds source/target coordinates, preserved meaning, accepted loss, provenance, governing owner and refusal conditions. Distinguish proposed/admitted/assessed/completed, active input/history and current validity/available bytes; equal wire shape proves no translation. Bind current workspace observations separately from immutable authority, artifacts, history and candidates; changed support invalidates dependencies while unaffected accepted work remains reusable. Snapshots cannot replace current subjects; actor changes alone do not justify repeating valid work. Follow actual callable paths/effect owners through selected exit and required fresh observation; hidden fallback, injection, repaired output, private entry or undeclared retry cannot support ordinary-path claims. Evaluation gives pure functions no new event lifecycle.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:083aefb645ddbce35914d5601c488325","key":956,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:edbbabc8b2dc4636bae4930b21b2d9bb\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:75d7ebdc57547aefb3f31ca6c91db8e4\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:4a758d8b16a2d0014a7ecd1bc24c03f7\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:083aefb645ddbce35914d5601c488325\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":849,\"path\":\"standards/ASSURANCE.md\",\"quote\":\"6. Preserve diagnostic cause through wrappers and projections. Apply §12:\\n   report the supported causal frontier, not merely the first log or clock\\n   occurrence. Keep the originating seam, bounded field or path, expected\\n   domain or basis, observed mismatch and evidence locator where available,\\n   with downstream symptoms, successful work and the declared continuation\\n   or block. Preserve joint causes, alternative frontiers and\\n   indeterminacy; do not invent a unique cause. Product redaction rules\\n   still govern sensitive content. Missing required diagnostic evidence\\n   stays a named gap. Return the smallest supported owner or re-entry;\\n   diagnosis grants no repair or retry (P5, P4b, P6).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ASSURANCE.md#ASSURANCE%2F13.%20End-to-end%20interface%20integration%20frame%2FObligations\",\"start_line\":840}],\"statement\":\"Preserve supported causal frontier through wrappers/projections, including available originating seam, bounded field/path, expected domain/basis, mismatch and evidence locator, downstream symptoms, successful work and declared continuation/block. Retain joint causes, alternatives and indeterminacy; invent no unique cause. Product redaction still applies; missing diagnostics remain named gaps. Return the smallest supported owner/re-entry; diagnosis authorises no repair/retry. Acquire facts from existing owner surfaces and use independent contract-derived oracles. Computed facts, contextual judgments and reserved owner rulings retain separate owners and validity scopes.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:95022a71f2e77b1f7fa1ed6b42b41055","key":957,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:548e95b2ad0b13be8c12ff0b8188144c\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:edbbabc8b2dc4636bae4930b21b2d9bb\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:95022a71f2e77b1f7fa1ed6b42b41055\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"An LLM-interface usability claim is selected.\"],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":865,\"path\":\"standards/ASSURANCE.md\",\"quote\":\"For an LLM-interface usability claim, clean-room LLM UAT is used, with the\\nordinary supplied context and permitted tools and without private\\nimplementation knowledge or fixture assistance. Expected outcomes are\\nrecorded before responses are inspected. The sunny case and the ordinary\\nambiguity and negative cases material to the claim are included.\\nSubstitutes are disclosed; replayed or fabricated responses prove only\\ntheir stated narrower relation, not live-provider usability. Responses are\\nnot edited, and nothing is silently retried until green. Live claims need\\nlive evidence under §2, not a new universal live-provider requirement\\nduring design (P6, P5; EVALUATION §3, expectations before exposure).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ASSURANCE.md#ASSURANCE%2F13.%20End-to-end%20interface%20integration%20frame%2FObligations\",\"start_line\":856}],\"statement\":\"Use clean-room LLM UAT with ordinary context/permitted tools and no private implementation knowledge or fixture help. Record expectations before inspecting responses and include material sunny, ordinary ambiguity and negative cases. Disclose substitutes; replay/fabrication proves only declared narrower relations. Do not edit responses or silently retry to success. Live claims require live evidence under §2; this is no universal live-provider requirement during design.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:ea837689e9c18791ae0472dc2b7b18ee","key":958,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:edbbabc8b2dc4636bae4930b21b2d9bb\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:ea837689e9c18791ae0472dc2b7b18ee\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":877,\"path\":\"standards/ASSURANCE.md\",\"quote\":\"An early sunny thread can establish bounded evidence while the unexercised\\nclaims stay open (the sequencing heuristic of SPEC_METHOD §8). This frame\\nadds no exhaustive-hardening prerequisite, scenario quota, controller,\\nruntime, generator, routine human approval, new ledger or automatic extra\\nagent. Existing authority selects proportionate assurance and any further\\noperation. The result returns, for each of the four claims, its core\\nresult or the scope reason it was not selected, the exact\\nexercised subject and path, the supported mismatch, retained work,\\nsubstitutions, residuals and invalidators in the existing work carrier; it\\nis neither acceptance nor a grant of the next action (P2, P6; ACTIVATION\\n§6).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ASSURANCE.md#ASSURANCE%2F13.%20End-to-end%20interface%20integration%20frame%2FObligations\",\"start_line\":867}],\"statement\":\"Early sunny evidence can be bounded while unexercised claims remain open. The frame creates no exhaustive-hardening prerequisite, quota, controller, runtime, generator, routine human approval, ledger or automatic agent. Existing authority chooses proportionate assurance/further operations. Existing work carriers retain each of four claim results or nonselection reasons, exact subject/path, supported mismatch, retained work, substitutions, residuals and invalidators. This return is neither acceptance nor permission for the next action.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:ffc4ab48c59085404a080488bc5582b5","key":959,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:fe7db12377fdd46a49a3d55fed08adb1\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:ffc4ab48c59085404a080488bc5582b5\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"Material computational composition or recurrence work.\"],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":900,\"path\":\"standards/ASSURANCE.md\",\"quote\":\"An identifiable complete-path result and its evidence return to the\\ndeclared decision consumer; a collection of local successes cannot replace\\nthat result. Design-only evidence establishes only the design claim; claims\\nabout actual work need observations on the selected path. Valid unchanged\\nresults are reused, and affected reassessment is activated on a material\\nchange of path, basis or workload. This is a bounded composition of\\nexisting frames, not a permanent actor, an extra frame family, a per-helper\\nreview or a separate accounting ledger (P4b, P2).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ASSURANCE.md#ASSURANCE%2F13.%20End-to-end%20interface%20integration%20frame%2FComputational%20whole-path%20evaluation\",\"start_line\":893}],\"statement\":\"Qualification challenges declared workload/operational assumptions while preserving independent scope, freshness and effect checks serving distinct obligations. Return an identifiable complete-path result/evidence to the decision consumer; local successes cannot replace it. Design evidence establishes only design claims; actual work needs selected-path observations. Reuse unchanged valid results and activate affected reassessment for material path/basis/workload changes. No permanent actor, new frame family, per-helper review or separate ledger is created.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:8af9d5fad94ce242ca3c8c63415bd01a","key":960,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:edbbabc8b2dc4636bae4930b21b2d9bb\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:548e95b2ad0b13be8c12ff0b8188144c\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:8af9d5fad94ce242ca3c8c63415bd01a\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"A representative qualification case is selected.\"],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":907,\"path\":\"standards/ASSURANCE.md\",\"quote\":\"These are representative source-contract discriminators: not an executed\\ntrial, a universal test quota or whole-Product qualification. Each selected\\ncase binds its own exact subject, oracle, evidence and claim scope (P6,\\nP5; EVALUATION §7).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ASSURANCE.md#ASSURANCE%2F13.%20End-to-end%20interface%20integration%20frame%2FQualification\",\"start_line\":904}],\"statement\":\"Cases are representative source-contract discriminators, not executed trials, quotas or whole-Product qualification; each binds exact subject/oracle/evidence/scope. Discriminate: ordinary usability of empty and nonempty eligible domains, with hidden required rules defeating sufficiency despite correct refusal; legitimate candidate refusal/filtering versus inadequate interfaces or violated success guarantees, with variability alone not failure; owner-defined eligibility/lifecycle versus available/equal-looking historical or same-response references; temporal/admission mismatch despite valid matching shapes; lost units/default/identity/order despite validation; hidden-rule fixture success versus unproved ordinary usability; forbidden-path equal output as falsified realisation; refresh affected workspace evidence while keeping unaffected valid work; retain originating causal frontier/uncertainty rather than symptoms or invented causes; design-only contract closure without inferred runtime/UAT satisfaction.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:17ffc1c606f4c8f7fc60bc0cda71db3a","key":961,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:5a33a4d8c03287f415271883ababd0f6\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:17ffc1c606f4c8f7fc60bc0cda71db3a\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"A new or materially changed realisation boundary is governed by a design profile.\"],\"exceptions\":[\"An unchanged realization_refactor cites the accepted relation and proves no material semantic-boundary delta without recreating evidence.\"],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":956,\"path\":\"standards/ASSURANCE.md\",\"quote\":\"When the\\ndesign's co-evolution condition holds, the two chains may proceed together\\nwithout making implementation semantic authority; design still owns the\\nstructural HOW. Where the design is not decision-complete, the relation is\\ndesign-gated at the smallest causally closed affected decision set and\\nretained implementation follows its acceptance. An unchanged\\n`realization_refactor` (SPEC_METHOD §4 Change classes) cites the accepted\\nrelation and proves no material semantic-boundary delta; it does not\\nrecreate the evidence (P2, P6).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ASSURANCE.md#ASSURANCE%2F14.%20Design-to-module%20evidence%20route\",\"start_line\":948}],\"statement\":\"Evidence feedback cannot select/accept semantic answers. Assertion and execution provenance remain separate; agreement may share error and disagreement requires diagnosis. When the design's co-evolution condition holds, chains may proceed together without implementation semantic authority; design owns structural HOW. Incomplete design gates retained implementation at acceptance of the smallest causally closed affected decision set. For probabilistic/agentic construction, ACTIVATION §1 owns accepted-design handoff into bounded construction, assessment, disposition, checkpoint and continuation; the profile supplies governing-frame, transformation-admission, invariant-reconstruction, computational-realisation and module evidence, not a second protocol.\",\"uncertainty\":\"The design co-evolution condition and referenced execution protocol are not supplied.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:e1447cff9c3d4e226d8b018f49859e36","key":962,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:5a33a4d8c03287f415271883ababd0f6\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:f36832f6941f8683b920fbd70d2f5ad7\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:e1447cff9c3d4e226d8b018f49859e36\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"Design-profile completeness, promotion or closure is claimed.\"],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":978,\"path\":\"standards/ASSURANCE.md\",\"quote\":\"- the final implementation is traceable to the accepted ontology;\\n- the final implementation is traceable to design and module boundary\\n  assets;\\n- unit tests are traceable to module ownership, not only to helper\\n  layout;\\n- implementation-first discoveries are reconciled into the ontology and\\n  the design's domain, sequence and state evidence before promotion or\\n  closure; and\\n- implementation may not compensate for an unrealised declared\\n  constructor by introducing a hidden controller or alternative authority\\n  path.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ASSURANCE.md#ASSURANCE%2F14.%20Design-to-module%20evidence%20route\",\"start_line\":968}],\"statement\":\"Implementation must trace to accepted ontology, design and module assets; tests to module ownership. Reconcile implementation-first discoveries into ontology and domain/sequence/state evidence before promotion/closure; hidden controllers or alternative authority cannot compensate for unrealised constructors. Implementation-discovered tests must re-express closure proof against ownership; module boundaries enable common audit without outranking constitutional truth/ratified design. Minimum chain: constitutional WHAT; accepted ontology; target design; target module assets and ontology-derived carriers; accepted domain/sequence/state projections with axiom evaluation; implementation; tests from the same ontology/boundary. With reference realisation: constitutional WHAT; reference design; accepted target ontology plus reference mapping; target design mapping; target module assets/carriers; accepted domain/sequence/state projections with axiom evaluation; implementation/tests from the same ontology. Jumping from design/code to tests without reconstructing module boundaries yields too-weak proof.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:453d61712f0e8102edd5b73e38e1f87d","key":963,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:f36832f6941f8683b920fbd70d2f5ad7\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:453d61712f0e8102edd5b73e38e1f87d\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"Unit tests are under the design profile.\"],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1050,\"path\":\"standards/ASSURANCE.md\",\"quote\":\"Canonical rule (P6): module-owned unit tests are authoritative for module\\nproof; broader integration, scenario and sandbox lanes remain downstream\\nproof families; transitional slice-gating tests may exist, but they do not\\nreplace module-derived unit proof. If a module has code but no\\nmodule-derived unit test lane, the module is not closure-ready under the\\ndesign profile. What such a lane claims, and what it never closes, is\\nthe unit frame of §7.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ASSURANCE.md#ASSURANCE%2F15.%20Module-derived%20unit%20tests\",\"start_line\":1044}],\"statement\":\"Tests should trace to accepted ontology and applicable entity/lifecycle/authority/function/effect/projection law, module design, active or equivalent carrier inventory, module-bounded domain/sequence/state projections and owned requirement families. They are not primarily authored from helper/private layout, incidental branches, temporary decomposition or mock convenience hiding contracts. Ask what ownership requires proving. Helper tests may exist but cannot be the canonical module proof. Broader integration/scenario/sandbox lanes remain downstream proof families, not substitutes. Transitional slice-gating does not replace the module lane; coded modules without it are not closure-ready. Design ownership does not extend to Product UAT/acceptance.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:e6d3c97522c9269a853e6ac6cbaa2ae6","key":964,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:32452eb024ac40cc77301d8270aacad9\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:e6d3c97522c9269a853e6ac6cbaa2ae6\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"For each governed boundary, before design-method closure.\"],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1089,\"path\":\"standards/ASSURANCE.md\",\"quote\":\"Each lifecycle phase takes one of the three answers that\\n[SPEC_METHOD §2 Operational lifecycle sufficiency](SPEC_METHOD.md#operational-lifecycle-sufficiency)\\nowns, applied here to design evidence: answered by the active design,\\nrequirement, release, deployment or telemetry surface; declared not\\napplicable with a reason; or recorded as a named `Gap:` or `Unanswered:`\\nitem, which in design evidence also names its owning follow-up. A phase\\nlist without answers, not-applicable reasons or named gaps is not\\ndesign-method evidence (P5, P6). The three are declared states of the\\ndesign evidence for a phase under that section, not result values; a\\nnamed gap is a residual\\n([FOUNDATIONS §2](FOUNDATIONS.md#2-ontology)) that remains until its\\nowning follow-up disposes it (P4b, P5).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ASSURANCE.md#ASSURANCE%2F16.%20Module%20lifecycle%20confirmation\",\"start_line\":1078}],\"statement\":\"Design evidence states or points to upstream intent/requirements, build/realisation, assurance/proof, release/packaging, deployment/install, live use/invocation, telemetry/projection/monitoring, retirement/revocation/supersession/decommission and lifecycle decision owner/source truth/authority. Each phase is answered by an active owning surface, reasoned not-applicable, or named Gap:/Unanswered: with owning follow-up. These are evidence states, not core results; bare phase lists are insufficient and named gaps persist until owner disposition. Implementation/tests/artifacts/fixtures confirm only within declared authority and cannot invent lifecycle authority. Missing release/deployment/live-use/telemetry/retirement truth permits proceeding only with explicitly governed gaps; local convention, precedent, mutable state, prompts or fixtures cannot close them.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:0277d995888cfc3dee81e9c49665eedf","key":965,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:8710247991b836d7b07fd776cf748e2c\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:7fd7c71247668ac4656ebb2663df6898\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:0277d995888cfc3dee81e9c49665eedf\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[\"An exact separately identified proof may establish a specified status for a declared fragment, model or relation; categorical status requires the referenced Formal fragment demonstration.\"],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":40,\"path\":\"standards/AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS.md\",\"quote\":\"`a_c` claims no universal applicability, logical completeness,\\nconsistency, decidability, soundness or category-theoretic status except\\nwhere an exact, separately identified proof establishes that claim for a\\ndeclared fragment, model or relation; for category-theoretic status that\\nproof is the demonstration of\\n[FOUNDATIONS §4](FOUNDATIONS.md#4-algebra), Formal fragment (P6).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS.md#AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS%2F1.%20Position\",\"start_line\":35}],\"statement\":\"No universal applicability, completeness, consistency, decidability, soundness or category-theoretic status is claimed without the specified proof. Principles derive the calculus; subject interpretation and accepted-model encoding are distinct downstream relations. Interpretation/encoding cannot redefine it; a layer becomes a released Product only through separately authorised acceptance and release.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:dab30bcdeb26e008088821a5d3a2e718","key":966,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:3dab7b4ae60847a9b5f77b8991c041fa\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:8710247991b836d7b07fd776cf748e2c\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:dab30bcdeb26e008088821a5d3a2e718\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":120,\"path\":\"standards/AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS.md\",\"quote\":\"Issuance of an exact `AxiomaticCalculusBasis` (§8) resolves the local routes\\nabove to absolute semantic addresses inside the selected immutable package\\nand records them under `derivation_basis.principle_refs`. Each address\\nidentifies the actual clause it uses; a mutable authoring locator is not a\\ndigest-bound derivation reference (P3).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS.md#AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS%2F1.%20Position%2FDerivation%20provenance\",\"start_line\":116}],\"statement\":\"Imported concepts retain owners; FOUNDATIONS owns result values/conjunction consumed by AC-007/019, and models/carriers/interpretations gain no ownership. No implicit method representation, carrier or downstream implementation is needed to interpret the calculus. Equal-spelled F_D/F_P/F_H terms create no identity, import or equivalence. Basis issuance binds actual immutable clauses, not mutable locators. Models, carriers, tools and successful applications cannot amend source principles or calculus.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:1babd59b4d9e109dda4bbbc62f9adaa0","key":967,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:8710247991b836d7b07fd776cf748e2c\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:1babd59b4d9e109dda4bbbc62f9adaa0\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":142,\"path\":\"standards/AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS.md\",\"quote\":\"`a_c` does not choose the subject vocabulary, decide which source\\ndeclarations are material, supply semantic acceptance, select a carrier,\\nexecute a model or prove that one interpretation is uniquely correct (P2,\\nP6).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS.md#AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS%2F1.%20Position%2FScope\",\"start_line\":139}],\"statement\":\"The calculus governs symbolic-model form: identities/types, exact relation endpoints, explicit constraints/latitude/residuals, typed traversals/judgments, closure/projection/overlay/transformation, subject preservation and separation of structural, semantic and authority claims. It chooses no vocabulary/materiality, provides no semantic acceptance, selects no carrier, executes no model and proves no unique interpretation.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:02fa9fa423e4ef87d23191b96a8dedbb","key":968,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:90c3d9660d33d96fa0e0932fb3cdc162\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:02fa9fa423e4ef87d23191b96a8dedbb\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":212,\"path\":\"standards/AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS.md\",\"quote\":\"Each consumer applies the rule and decides nothing the owning section does\\nnot (P2, P6).\\n\\nPurpose and material relation: an actor\\nstarted on this member sees which rules of the calculus follow from the\\nfoundations and which are choices, with the owner of each choice, so no\\nchoice is presented as derived (P6, P1).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS.md#AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS%2F1.%20Position%2FFoundation%20to%20law\",\"start_line\":206}],\"statement\":\"Preserve the nineteen row derivations and their standing: P1/P6+(i)→one-way derivation; P2/P6→scope/status limits; P3/P5+(i)→closed signature; P3/P4a→identity/typing; P6/P4b/P3→authority/basis; P5/P6→results/stops; P1/P6→latitude; P4b/P6→residual persistence; P0/P2/P4b→closure/projection; P3/P6→overlay; P4b/P3/P6→transformation; P6/P3→judgment separation; P4a/P3/P6+(iii)→typed functors/composition; P1/P6/P4b+(ii,iii)→interpretation; P3/P6+(ii)→layers; P3/P6→edition identity; P2/P6→application boundary; P0/P2/P4b/P6+(i,iii)→constraint surfaces; P6→law qualification. Owner choices remain explicit: this member owns a_c identities/name, eight record kinds/shapes, dual-cause refusal policy, edition shape/RFC8785/SHA-256/reference order and minimum ten qualification obligations with positive/refusal cases per law. Signatures own sorts/domains/kinds/qualifiers/symmetry, constraint judgment, residual domains, stop contracts and permitted functors; individual owners own composite bases, latitude, dispositions, overlays, transformations/preservation and operation authority. Applying evaluation/activation owns closure seeds/relation families; downstream subject authority owns interpretation/selection/acceptance/currentness, model-supplied semantic-subset decision contracts and application choices; owning Products govern downstream identity grammars/issuance and external Product status; release issues edition identity. Consumers apply only owning rules, not new decisions. References labelled provenance/import-only—including IDENTITY, RELEASE, EVALUATION acceptance, FOUNDATIONS latitude and profile-side declarations—must not become additional applications by connectivity.\",\"uncertainty\":\"Detailed consumer loci and several referenced laws are outside the supplied sections.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:beeb29585136268989faa46c0daac6f4","key":969,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:90c3d9660d33d96fa0e0932fb3cdc162\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:8710247991b836d7b07fd776cf748e2c\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:beeb29585136268989faa46c0daac6f4\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":180,\"path\":\"standards/AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS.md\",\"quote\":\"| P6 (independent) | By P6 a claim about this member holds only on evidence that tests each law, so a review or qualification of this member covers each law with positive and refusal cases, and no example, checker, model or carrier qualifies a law beyond the claim it evaluates | [§10](#10-conformance-obligations) | the ten obligations as the minimum coverage: this member; a policy of this member: each law is covered by positive and refusal cases | 9, 10 |\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS.md#AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS%2F1.%20Position%2FFoundation%20to%20law\",\"start_line\":180}],\"statement\":\"The table additionally states: every traversal uses exactly one deterministic-evaluation, probabilistic-construction or human-adjudication kind, distinct from actor/executor/domain operation and asserting no categorical functor; typed composition retains both identities and intermediate facts. Interpretation proposes without accepting; admitted records have exact provenance or model-local identification, evaluated declarations have dispositions, structural success only supports semantic review, and valid models satisfy all applicable laws. Encoding requires acceptance of the unchanged model; downstream success ratifies no upstream layer. Edition identity is an external record created after published bytes, binding bytes/derivation; downstream identities bind upstream identities and judgments remain outside judged identities. Applications' selections, constructions, acceptances, releases, imports/translations/specialisations remain external. Task constraint surfaces carry material closure, residuals blocking dependent work, no authority, and distinct validity/fidelity/sufficiency claims. Qualification covers every law with positive and refusal cases and never extends beyond evaluated claims.\",\"uncertainty\":\"These are supplied table summaries, not imported full definitions of AC-015–020 or sections 5–10.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:e1456caa8d379dd1775ef866f970f97d","key":970,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:756e46fcb645468c0a61b7d1af496ff1\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:d7d4d3087eb8ab6376c885fc78a46108\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:e1456caa8d379dd1775ef866f970f97d\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[\"A population may be empty only when the selected signature requires no member of that kind.\",\"A new fundamental family requires an explicit compatible calculus extension.\"],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":250,\"path\":\"standards/AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS.md\",\"quote\":\"Every `a_c` signature imports those identities unchanged. A model-family\\nsignature specialises their fields, value domains, reference domains and\\nadmissible kinds; it does not remove, rename, shadow or silently add a\\ncore record family. Another fundamental record family requires an explicit\\ncompatible calculus extension, never an extra subject sort (P3).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS.md#AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS%2F2.%20Signature\",\"start_line\":246}],\"statement\":\"Import all eight core identities unchanged; family signatures specialise fields/domains/kinds without removing, renaming, shadowing or silently adding families. Unknown kinds/fields require a new signature or explicit compatible extension, not implicit extension or extra subject sort. Populations are finite, total, disjoint and identity-unique; every record belongs exactly once and every external identity has exactly one declared reference domain/resolution. Hidden records, extra unpopulated families, duplicate identities or identities lacking local record/lawful external resolution refuse the model. Every identity-bearing scalar/collection element is checked by RefDomain_Sigma: exact family, semantic sort where applicable, and exact external kind/basis; never both local and external. Missing field domains, wrong families/sorts, ambiguous targets and dangling external identities refuse structural admission.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:a636807607103da35d50e686a7e1ef0d","key":971,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:d7d4d3087eb8ab6376c885fc78a46108\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:a636807607103da35d50e686a7e1ef0d\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":339,\"path\":\"standards/AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS.md\",\"quote\":\"The following subsections define the exact shapes of five of the eight\\ncore record families. `SemanticObject`, `TypedRelation`, `Constraint`,\\n`Latitude` and `Residual` populate `O`, `E`, `C`, `L` and `X`. The\\ntraversal record (§5), the transformation record (AC-013) and the judgment\\nrecord (AC-014) populate `V`, `T` and `J`. A traversal, transformation or\\njudgment is not placed in `O` merely by reifying its name as a semantic\\nobject. A subject model may independently represent the concept of a\\nrecord kind, but that representation does not satisfy the core population\\nlaw (P3, P1).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS.md#AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS%2F3.%20Typed%20records\",\"start_line\":331}],\"statement\":\"SemanticObject, TypedRelation, Constraint, Latitude and Residual populate O/E/C/L/X; traversal, transformation and judgment populate V/T/J. Reifying a record-kind name as an object does not place an operational record in O or satisfy its required core population. Independently representing record-kind concepts is permitted but distinct.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:a2da593a44299a0296006bd6fbbfe386","key":972,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:aca1e4de8dbbb05752a7c83155ab6025\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:a2da593a44299a0296006bd6fbbfe386\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"A predicate is not deterministically decidable.\"],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":410,\"path\":\"standards/AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS.md\",\"quote\":\"`kind` resolves one declared `ConstraintKind`; `judgment_kind` resolves\\none declared `JudgmentKind`. The owning signature defines the predicate\\nlanguage and how its result is judged. A predicate that is not\\ndeterministically decidable states the required probabilistic or human\\njudgment kind rather than pretending to be a machine proof (P6, P1).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS.md#AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS%2F3.%20Typed%20records%2FConstraint\",\"start_line\":406}],\"statement\":\"Declare the required probabilistic or human judgment kind instead of claiming machine proof. Both constraint and judgment kinds must resolve within the owning signature.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:9ffea98bf79d22387e9844cf86684c58","key":973,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:5e6bfac5ccaaebc55f824ebe3d10283c\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:9ffea98bf79d22387e9844cf86684c58\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[\"Competent authority explicitly dispositions the residual.\"],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":463,\"path\":\"standards/AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS.md\",\"quote\":\"Projection, compression, interpretation or encoding cannot erase a\\nresidual. It remains represented, is explicitly dispositioned by competent\\nauthority, or causes refusal (P4b, P6).\\n\\n`kind` resolves one declared `ResidualKind`. The owning signature defines\\nits lawful subject, uncertainty, consequence, re-entry and invalidation\\ndomains. An undeclared residual kind or value refuses structural admission\\n(P3).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS.md#AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS%2F3.%20Typed%20records%2FResidual\",\"start_line\":456}],\"statement\":\"Projection, compression, interpretation and encoding cannot erase residuals: retain them, record competent disposition or refuse. Undeclared residual kinds or values refuse structural admission.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:4728e957549dcf7ba472209200ee7240","key":974,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:8710247991b836d7b07fd776cf748e2c\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:4728e957549dcf7ba472209200ee7240\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":469,\"path\":\"standards/AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS.md\",\"quote\":\"The objects these laws govern are the records of §2, §3 and §5 and the\\nontology of FOUNDATIONS §2; where a law names identity, authority, basis\\nor residual, the definition is FOUNDATIONS' and the law is this member's.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS.md#AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS%2F4.%20Fundamental%20laws\",\"start_line\":467}],\"statement\":\"Fundamental laws govern records of sections 2, 3 and 5 and FOUNDATIONS §2 ontology. FOUNDATIONS retains definitions of identity, authority, basis and residual; this member owns the laws over them.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:4f4fa446b51db226ad2c5cc1372ccd63","key":975,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:d7d4d3087eb8ab6376c885fc78a46108\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:756e46fcb645468c0a61b7d1af496ff1\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:4f4fa446b51db226ad2c5cc1372ccd63\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":478,\"path\":\"standards/AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS.md\",\"quote\":\"Every admitted object, relation, constraint, latitude, residual,\\ntraversal, transformation specialisation and judgment belongs to one\\ndeclared signature. Every fundamental record also occurs exactly once in\\nthe total `Population_M` function under its declared `RecordKind_ac`.\\nMissing, duplicate, shadowed or unknown record kinds and populations fail\\nclosed (P3, P5).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS.md#AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS%2F4.%20Fundamental%20laws%2FAC-001%20Closed%20signature\",\"start_line\":473}],\"statement\":\"Every admitted fundamental record belongs to one declared signature and occurs exactly once under its declared core kind in total Population_M. Missing, duplicate, shadowed or unknown kinds/populations fail closed.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:332fd93a7e880aed559721bd71f8d122","key":976,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:d7d4d3087eb8ab6376c885fc78a46108\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:a581786e372e2577624fc3ed9d0583a0\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:332fd93a7e880aed559721bd71f8d122\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":492,\"path\":\"standards/AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS.md\",\"quote\":\"So an identity resolves one member under one type,\\ncontext, owner, scope and basis. That equal representations do not\\nestablish equal meaning is FOUNDATIONS §2, Representation. The `a_c`\\nbinding beside it: equal spelling, payload equality, position in any\\nstructure and carrier equality do not establish semantic identity (P3).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS.md#AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS%2F4.%20Fundamental%20laws%2FAC-002%20Scoped%20identity\",\"start_line\":488}],\"statement\":\"Every identity in I resolves one member under one type, context, owner, scope and basis. Owner maps to authority, type to kind, resolved member to denoted value; context/scope/basis are additional required coordinates permitted by IDENTITY §2. Equal spelling, payload, structural position or carrier does not establish semantic identity.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:7129023e981965054165cf62a95f4f64","key":977,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:d7d4d3087eb8ab6376c885fc78a46108\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:756e46fcb645468c0a61b7d1af496ff1\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:7129023e981965054165cf62a95f4f64\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":501,\"path\":\"standards/AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS.md\",\"quote\":\"Every referenced identity resolves exactly once in the applicable model or\\nthrough one explicit external relation. Resolution uses the exact\\n`RefDomain_Sigma(source_record_kind, field)` declaration across the\\nmodel's record populations. Dangling, duplicate, wrong-record-kind,\\nwrong-sort, wrong-basis, locally-and-externally ambiguous or\\nundeclared-field references refuse structural admission (P3, P5).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS.md#AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS%2F4.%20Fundamental%20laws%2FAC-003%20Reference%20closure\",\"start_line\":496}],\"statement\":\"Every reference resolves exactly once locally or through one explicit external relation using its exact RefDomain_Sigma declaration. Dangling, duplicate, wrong-kind, wrong-sort, wrong-basis, local/external ambiguous and undeclared-field references refuse structural admission; AC-007 separately determines the refusal's core value by cause.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:476958e66bedc4cdcb16fb3339d49b53","key":978,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:9d8d43c934e9fdbe3d228917333e3d48\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:476958e66bedc4cdcb16fb3339d49b53\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[\"Direction is immaterial only when the relation kind explicitly declares symmetry.\"],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":507,\"path\":\"standards/AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS.md\",\"quote\":\"A relation is lawful only when its kind admits the exact source and target\\nsorts and all required qualifiers are present. Direction is material\\nunless the relation kind explicitly declares symmetry (P4a, P3).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS.md#AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS%2F4.%20Fundamental%20laws%2FAC-004%20Relation%20typing\",\"start_line\":505}],\"statement\":\"Lawfulness requires exact admitted endpoint sorts and all required qualifiers; direction is material subject to explicit symmetry.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:04fbc67dd09700912ca073daf1815cf8","key":979,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:d7d4d3087eb8ab6376c885fc78a46108\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:ef0ffce7253e996c7f40fd2fb817d10e\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:aea0ac1826c9dc379a8b046db93f8e1d\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:0430c525dee26281ae235ebacc9459ab\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:04fbc67dd09700912ca073daf1815cf8\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":517,\"path\":\"standards/AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS.md\",\"quote\":\"Objects, relations, constraints, latitude, residuals, traversals,\\ntransformations, projections and judgments retain their declared semantic,\\noperation, evaluation and decision authority (the kinds of\\n[FOUNDATIONS §2 Authority kinds](FOUNDATIONS.md#authority-kinds)). What\\ncreates no authority is listed there; in `a_c` its instances are copying,\\ninterpreting, encoding, evaluating and transporting a record, none of\\nwhich transfers authority (P6, P4b).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS.md#AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS%2F4.%20Fundamental%20laws%2FAC-005%20Authority%20conservation\",\"start_line\":511}],\"statement\":\"All listed records and projections retain declared semantic, operation, evaluation and decision authority. Copying, interpreting, encoding, evaluating or transporting transfers none.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:b6c6e0da2959d0d95efeb8bc2d9fcde8","key":980,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:d7d4d3087eb8ab6376c885fc78a46108\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:5dd095b251a98fbf2b0a7ece590700f8\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:b6c6e0da2959d0d95efeb8bc2d9fcde8\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[\"Mixed bases require an explicit owned composite-basis record.\"],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":528,\"path\":\"standards/AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS.md\",\"quote\":\"Every result binds its exact basis under\\n[RF-005](REFERENCE_FRAME.md#rf-005-exact-basis-and-coordinates), which\\nowns the exact-basis rule for results; what a basis is, including that\\nmixed bases need an explicit composite relation, is FOUNDATIONS §2,\\nBasis. This law binds the same rule to every fundamental record and model\\nof `a_c`: each binds an exact basis, the composite-basis relation of a\\nmixed basis is an explicitly owned record, and individually valid\\ncoordinates do not create a coherent composite basis by proximity (P6, P3).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS.md#AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS%2F4.%20Fundamental%20laws%2FAC-006%20Basis%20coherence\",\"start_line\":521}],\"statement\":\"Every result, fundamental record and model binds an exact basis. Individually valid nearby coordinates do not constitute coherent composite basis. FOUNDATIONS defines Basis and RF-005 owns result exactness; AC-006 applies it to records/models.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:19845d8d9846ca93150b75f322968d4a","key":981,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:aca1e4de8dbbb05752a7c83155ab6025\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:5dd095b251a98fbf2b0a7ece590700f8\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:19845d8d9846ca93150b75f322968d4a\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"A constraint judgment is performed.\"],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":562,\"path\":\"standards/AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS.md\",\"quote\":\"A missing result is no value of this refinement: a judgment that was not\\nperformed has no closed result, is never `indeterminate`, and enters every\\nconjunction over it as a planned assessment without a closed result\\n(FOUNDATIONS §4 Results, Not performed).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS.md#AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS%2F4.%20Fundamental%20laws%2FAC-007%20Constraint%20and%20refusal\",\"start_line\":559}],\"statement\":\"For the predicate that the constraint holds for its governed subject on exact basis: holds→satisfied with established predicate; failed→falsified with named counterexample; undecidable admissible evidence→indeterminate naming deciding evidence; outside applies_to/context/scope requiring an undeclared relation→out_of_frame naming that relation and source-given owner; unsupported subject/basis→invalid_basis naming repair. No mapping raises standing or coerces failure, absence, indeterminacy, out-of-scope or invalid basis to satisfied. A judgment not performed has no closed result, is not indeterminate and enters conjunction as planned assessment without a result.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:2307746e6d2f9c79e0374143aac37e0e","key":982,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:5dd095b251a98fbf2b0a7ece590700f8\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:18a9318a44e9f56d1d45b6db418ee071\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:ef0ffce7253e996c7f40fd2fb817d10e\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:aea0ac1826c9dc379a8b046db93f8e1d\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:2307746e6d2f9c79e0374143aac37e0e\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"A closure, projection, structural admission, transformation application or interpretation is applied.\"],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":580,\"path\":\"standards/AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS.md\",\"quote\":\"| `hold` | indeterminate | the operation was applied and stops because evidence, an observation or a disposition it needs is not yet admitted, so the admissible evidence cannot decide whether it yields its result; its residual names what would decide |\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS.md#AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS%2F4.%20Fundamental%20laws%2FAC-007%20Constraint%20and%20refusal\",\"start_line\":577}],\"statement\":\"For the predicate that the operation yields its declared result on exact basis: declared result→satisfied, establishing availability of a proposed model/successor only, not acceptance/admission; hold→indeterminate when required evidence/observation/disposition is not yet admitted, naming what decides; gap→invalid_basis when a needed member/reference/resolution/declaration remains unresolved by its declared relation; refusal(constraint)→falsified for a demonstrated law/signature violation by what is judged or any refusal not naming a basis condition; refusal(basis)→invalid_basis for basis conditions without a demonstrated violation by what is judged. A resolved-to-no-target local/external reference is dangling and refuses, distinct from open external resolution. Basis-only causes include inexact seeds/relations/edge semantics/basis/scope, nonfinite/nonunique fixed points, unestablished input identity/basis/admission or mixed bases without composite relation. Refusal names its condition, admits no record/model/carrier and silently drops nothing.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:f46311c5c510106323843916505bbab5","key":983,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:5dd095b251a98fbf2b0a7ece590700f8\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:f46311c5c510106323843916505bbab5\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":610,\"path\":\"standards/AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS.md\",\"quote\":\"A basis mismatch inside a model or a record, a\\nrelation's qualifier record included, is mixed bases with no\\ncomposite-basis relation (AC-006): a coordinate of the model or record\\nbinds, or a reference in it resolves on, a basis that the governing basis\\nrelation does not admit, as a wrong-basis reference of AC-003 does. It is\\na condition of the basis, in the structural admission that judges that\\nmodel or record as in every other operation, and never a violated\\nconstraint of a signature, even where the signature declares the basis\\nrelation; a refusal that names only such a mismatch is `refusal(basis)`.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS.md#AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS%2F4.%20Fundamental%20laws%2FAC-007%20Constraint%20and%20refusal\",\"start_line\":602}],\"statement\":\"Cause is part of refusal value. A demonstrated violation by the judged record/model/carrier/transformation/application makes refusal(constraint), even with a basis condition; report the latter alongside as a separate invalid_basis result naming repair and the unsupported evaluation predicate, not the operation-outcome predicate. Known failure/counterexample survives conjunction. A defect in an input used as basis is a basis condition for that operation. Basis mismatch—including qualifier or wrong-basis reference—is always a basis condition, never signature-constraint violation, even when the signature declares the basis relation. Thus AC-001 violation may falsify model admission while invalidating the basis of projection over that model. Unapplied operations have no outcome. A gap stop is a closed invalid_basis result, distinct from missing-result conjunction gaps. Signature/traversal-specific stops map under §5. Unestablished closure/projection is invalid_basis for its predicate, as closure_unresolved is for its own activation predicate.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:44ffd00b6cf32480c5855703326533c2","key":984,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:d5f04a0892164371ab84d6dfd38ae088\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:44ffd00b6cf32480c5855703326533c2\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[\"An applicable latitude record or transformation relation permits the difference.\"],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":636,\"path\":\"standards/AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS.md\",\"quote\":\"Two values may differ lawfully only through an applicable latitude record\\nor transformation relation. An implementation preference, a probabilistic\\nchoice or a human presence is not implicit latitude. FOUNDATIONS §4 states\\nthe same rule for any two values; this law is its form over `L` and `T`\\n(P6, P1).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS.md#AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS%2F4.%20Fundamental%20laws%2FAC-008%20Explicit%20latitude\",\"start_line\":632}],\"statement\":\"Lawful differences require declared applicable latitude or transformation. Implementation preference, probabilistic choice and human presence supply no implicit latitude.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:f5c4c334932e96be059bb5d2221cf8f7","key":985,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:5e6bfac5ccaaebc55f824ebe3d10283c\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:d7d4d3087eb8ab6376c885fc78a46108\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:f5c4c334932e96be059bb5d2221cf8f7\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[\"Authorised disposition creates an exact successor model.\"],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":643,\"path\":\"standards/AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS.md\",\"quote\":\"Every material uncertainty, omission, translation loss, unresolved\\nboundary or unproven relation remains in `X` until an authorised\\ndisposition creates an exact successor model. Absence from a projection is\\nnot resolution (P4b).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS.md#AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS%2F4.%20Fundamental%20laws%2FAC-009%20Residual%20conservation\",\"start_line\":640}],\"statement\":\"Every material uncertainty, omission, translation loss, unresolved boundary and unproved relation remains in X until authorised successor disposition. Projection absence is not resolution.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:1d8a62267b3b3dafc71ca93d740aec0c","key":986,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:18a9318a44e9f56d1d45b6db418ee071\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:1d8a62267b3b3dafc71ca93d740aec0c\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":662,\"path\":\"standards/AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS.md\",\"quote\":\"The result is defined only when `Z`, `R`, required-edge semantics, basis\\nand scope are exact and the fixed point is finite and unique. Failure to\\nestablish those conditions returns a gap or refusal: `gap` where a\\ncondition is unresolved on the basis, otherwise `refusal(basis)`, because\\neach condition bears on the basis the closure acts on (AC-007). Least\\nclosure means least lawful record closure under `R`; it does not claim\\nglobally minimal prose, bytes, tokens, cost or cognitive effort.\\nACTIVATION §2 applies this closure to the construction of a step's context\\nunder an envelope.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS.md#AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS%2F4.%20Fundamental%20laws%2FAC-010%20Material%20closure\",\"start_line\":654}],\"statement\":\"Closure exists only with exact Z/R/required-edge semantics/basis/scope and finite unique fixed point. Unresolved required conditions return gap; otherwise failure to establish them returns refusal(basis). Least lawful closure claims no global minimum prose, bytes, tokens, cost or cognition. ACTIVATION §2 applies it to step context under an envelope.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:a144371527fe75591af0f1f0909d2a37","key":987,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:ef0ffce7253e996c7f40fd2fb817d10e\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:a144371527fe75591af0f1f0909d2a37\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":683,\"path\":\"standards/AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS.md\",\"quote\":\"A\\nprojection is not a new semantic owner. It is a reference, so the rule\\nthat no reference trims a required member to fit a carrier or budget,\\nstated at [FOUNDATIONS §4](FOUNDATIONS.md#4-algebra), Reference versus\\nbody, applies to it: here the required members are those of the material\\nclosure of `Z`, and a capability budget is one such budget. ACTIVATION §2\\napplies the projection to a step's context, and every projected frame of\\nthis corpus is one.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS.md#AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS%2F4.%20Fundamental%20laws%2FAC-011%20Projection\",\"start_line\":676}],\"statement\":\"Projection preserves selected meaning and contains closure with explicit seams. Failures inherited from closure/input model are gap or refusal(basis). It creates no semantic owner and may not trim required closure members for carrier, capability or other budgets. Step contexts and this corpus's projected frames are applications of this projection.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:76b6ddd45d61e125534fde31d894add1","key":988,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:af35b2208105298937667271bdb8b937\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:76b6ddd45d61e125534fde31d894add1\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":691,\"path\":\"standards/AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS.md\",\"quote\":\"Override,\\ndisambiguation, equivalence, specialisation or translation exists only as\\na typed relation with exact authority, direction, scope, basis,\\npreservation, loss, refusal and invalidation semantics (P3, P6).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS.md#AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS%2F4.%20Fundamental%20laws%2FAC-012%20Overlay\",\"start_line\":688}],\"statement\":\"Overlay cannot mutate its basis. Override, disambiguation, equivalence, specialisation and translation require typed relations with exact authority, direction, scope, basis, preservation, loss, refusal and invalidation semantics.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:19db1aae0ee7c9c3a56fd1e108ce1fb4","key":989,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:aea0ac1826c9dc379a8b046db93f8e1d\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:d7d4d3087eb8ab6376c885fc78a46108\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:19db1aae0ee7c9c3a56fd1e108ce1fb4\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[\"Cross-basis/signature migration has a separately identified specialisation with exact composite-basis and compatible signature-extension relations naming both sides.\"],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":738,\"path\":\"standards/AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS.md\",\"quote\":\"`domain_model` and `codomain_model` resolve exact content identities of\\nthe complete input and proposed successor models. Each model identity\\ncommits to its exact calculus basis, signature identity, complete finite\\n`Population_M`, complete `External_M`, exact external-resolution map and\\nselected model-content identity under the owning identity law. A mutable\\nlocator, a model-family name, a partial projection or a population digest\\nwithout the exact model identity refuses (P3).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS.md#AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS%2F4.%20Fundamental%20laws%2FAC-013%20Transformation\",\"start_line\":732}],\"statement\":\"t.traversal resolves one exact v; context, owner, scope, basis, operation authority, evidence, provenance and stop contract equal or lawfully restrict v, otherwise refuse. Domain/codomain identify complete exact models committing to calculus basis, signature, full populations/external identities/resolution map and owned content identity; mutable locators, family names, partial projections or population digests alone refuse. Ordinary transformations share domain/codomain/t/traversal basis and domain/codomain signature. Migration needs the stated separate specialisation. Changed basis or record kind forces removal/introduction and continuity only through exact migration, never preserved membership. Preservation_relation is exact typed equality binding both models/bases, record kinds, comparison domain, direction, authority, scope, evidence and equality law; equivalence/meaning preservation may relate removed/introduction but cannot preserve an identity.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:4a5e8ba91771df08f40095779fa84827","key":990,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:aea0ac1826c9dc379a8b046db93f8e1d\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:4a5e8ba91771df08f40095779fa84827\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"A lawful transformation is claimed.\"],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":794,\"path\":\"standards/AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS.md\",\"quote\":\"Local_b       = P_t disjoint_union R_t\\nLocal_b_prime = P_t disjoint_union N_t\\nN_t intersect Local_b = empty\\nR_t intersect Local_b_prime = empty\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS.md#AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS%2F4.%20Fundamental%20laws%2FAC-013%20Transformation\",\"start_line\":791}],\"statement\":\"Prove Local_b = P_t disjoint_union R_t; Local_b_prime = P_t disjoint_union N_t; N_t intersects no input identity and R_t no successor identity. Preserved records retain exact kind, identity, context, owner, scope and basis, with either byte identity under one exact shared canonical grammar or exact typed equality when no shared byte grammar exists. These are alternative proofs, not carrier selection. Changed fields/basis/kind, nominal identifier equality, equivalence or unbound preservation assertions refuse P_t. Every input identity is classified exactly once; every introduction is a complete lawful record in exactly one successor population; removals are absent. No silent dropping, retention or duplication.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:b88a03a9f063f44f5410608036b837ba","key":991,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:aea0ac1826c9dc379a8b046db93f8e1d\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:a0e0dad70524c698d0bec0c1bea7fe41\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:b88a03a9f063f44f5410608036b837ba\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"A lawful transformation is claimed.\"],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":856,\"path\":\"standards/AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS.md\",\"quote\":\"The two resolution tuples are exactly field-equal. A nominally equal\\nexternal identifier, an equivalent target, a changed target kind, a\\nchanged resolved target, a changed reference domain, a changed basis\\nrelation, a changed resolution basis or a missing witness cannot enter\\n`EP_t`. Every member of `ER_t` has its complete resolution only in the\\ndomain model; every member of `EN_t` has its complete resolution only in\\nthe codomain model. A changed external resolution is a removal followed by\\nintroduction of the new resolution coordinate and any separately declared\\ncontinuity relation; the referenced external identity may remain\\nunchanged, but the resolution is not preserved. Witnesses are total and\\nunique over `EP_t` and name no other resolution coordinate (P4b, P3).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS.md#AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS%2F4.%20Fundamental%20laws%2FAC-013%20Transformation\",\"start_line\":846}],\"statement\":\"Every external identity has exactly one exact resolution tuple; missing/ambiguous/extra tuples refuse. Prove E_b = EP_t disjoint_union ER_t; E_b_prime = EP_t disjoint_union EN_t; EN_t intersects no E_b and ER_t no E_b_prime. Each preserved tuple has exactly one total, exclusive witness binding both models/resolutions, equal decision and evidence, with field-exact equality. Nominal identity, equivalent targets, changes to target kind/target/reference domain/basis relation/resolution basis or missing witnesses cannot preserve. Removed tuples occur only in input, introduced only in successor. Changed resolution requires removal/introduction and separate continuity even if referenced external identity remains unchanged.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:2895bc98462c4a3918fb7ba245f0e6bf","key":992,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:ae