eration:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:29b723f9e1221b14158f69da70c9ab44","key":993,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:0430c525dee26281ae235ebacc9459ab\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:29b723f9e1221b14158f69da70c9ab44\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":905,\"path\":\"standards/AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS.md\",\"quote\":\"Issuing a judgment does not transform, rewrite, reissue or rename its\\nsubject. Promotion is an explicit relation between the unchanged subject\\nand its admission or acceptance judgment (P6, P3).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS.md#AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS%2F4.%20Fundamental%20laws%2FAC-014%20Judgment%20separation\",\"start_line\":903}],\"statement\":\"Judgment issuance never transforms, rewrites, reissues or renames the subject. Promotion is a separate explicit relation from unchanged subject to its admission/acceptance judgment.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:ac3e423f8745ec2d89ad5a518bbb0235","key":994,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:ad180a0b7eeeab223c0c1434f7a93e6a\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:cc99c053f518c955c093894ab174b704\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:a264d9c6baa9d13219958780b476cbb9\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:de2cfd132ecf92f2b6817d00d756fdd7\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:ac3e423f8745ec2d89ad5a518bbb0235\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":932,\"path\":\"standards/AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS.md\",\"quote\":\"A same-spelled term\\nowned by a profile, a realisation or a runtime is not imported by nominal\\nequality and does not specialise this record except through a declared\\nbinding under that owner's authority\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS.md#AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS%2F5.%20Traversals%20and%20functor%20kinds\",\"start_line\":929},{\"end_line\":988,\"path\":\"standards/AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS.md\",\"quote\":\"The actor, the executor, the domain operation and the functor kind are\\ndifferent coordinates. `Encode`, `Interpret`, `Serialize`, `Measure` and\\nother named domain operations are not aliases for `F_D`, `F_P` or `F_H`.\\nDifferent traversals may share one functor kind without sharing identity,\\nsemantics, inputs, outputs, authority or evidence (P3, P6).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS.md#AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS%2F5.%20Traversals%20and%20functor%20kinds\",\"start_line\":984}],\"statement\":\"Nominal equality does not import or specialise this member's traversal; specialisation requires a declared binding under the other owner's authority. Actor, executor, domain operation and functor kind remain distinct coordinates. Encode, Interpret, Serialize, Measure and other operations are not kind aliases. Sharing a kind implies no shared traversal identity, semantics, input, output, authority or evidence.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:1e7ffb16a7c106d6577d2c0841510a22","key":995,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:0a8a14f789f22c87c4dd9c92b92241f1\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:ad180a0b7eeeab223c0c1434f7a93e6a\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:1e7ffb16a7c106d6577d2c0841510a22\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"For every stop value and each cause refinement declared by the signature stop contract or traversal stop_states.\"],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":971,\"path\":\"standards/AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS.md\",\"quote\":\"Each refined value, whether the stop contract or a\\n`stop_states` declares it, names its parent value and its cause and maps\\nto its parent's core value: a value refined from `hold` to indeterminate,\\nfrom `gap` or `refusal(basis)` to invalid_basis, and from\\n`refusal(constraint)` to falsified. No refined value takes `satisfied`.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS.md#AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS%2F5.%20Traversals%20and%20functor%20kinds\",\"start_line\":960}],\"statement\":\"Each stop maps to exactly one existing core value, never satisfied. Further stops declare their single core mapping in the signature stop contract; traversal stop_states binds its exact mapping. Every refinement names parent and cause and keeps the parent's core value: hold -> indeterminate; gap and refusal(basis) -> invalid_basis; refusal(constraint) -> falsified. A different core value requires a different parent declared only by that parent's owning member; this member owns the four named stops. Neither contract nor stop_states raises standing or turns a violated constraint into mere evidential undecidability.\",\"uncertainty\":\"The full cause definitions in AC-007 are outside the supplied sections.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:cb1cfedd2477aafd0a91bde1c1fe8255","key":996,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:0a8a14f789f22c87c4dd9c92b92241f1\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:cb1cfedd2477aafd0a91bde1c1fe8255\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"For every functor application.\"],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1006,\"path\":\"standards/AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS.md\",\"quote\":\"Every functor application binds exactly one functor kind and one traversal\\nidentity. Applying any `F_*` kind without the bracketed traversal identity\\n`[v]` is incomplete (P3). Such an\\napplication violates this law, and its outcome is `refusal(constraint)`\\nunder AC-007; this sense of incomplete is not the construction-availability\\nvalue `incomplete` of a step\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS.md#AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS%2F5.%20Traversals%20and%20functor%20kinds%2FAC-015%20Functor%20classification\",\"start_line\":998}],\"statement\":\"Bind exactly one kind and one traversal identity. An F_* application lacking bracketed [v] violates AC-015 and yields refusal(constraint), whose supplied core mapping is falsified. Its descriptive incompleteness is not ACTIVATION's construction-availability value incomplete.\",\"uncertainty\":\"ACTIVATION's separate incomplete value is referenced but not defined here.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:156144cd35021180c3ce65144f296493","key":997,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:7f4b90a2ef961e06be982fbd06f043b5\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:156144cd35021180c3ce65144f296493\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"When two traversals are composed.\"],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1022,\"path\":\"standards/AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS.md\",\"quote\":\"Two traversals compose only when the first result type and judgment\\nsatisfy the second traversal's exact domain and preconditions (P4a):\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS.md#AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS%2F5.%20Traversals%20and%20functor%20kinds%2FAC-016%20Typed%20composition\",\"start_line\":1010},{\"end_line\":1022,\"path\":\"standards/AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS.md\",\"quote\":\"Composition retains both traversal identities, intermediate results,\\njudgments, evidence, authority, provenance and stop states. It cannot\\nflatten probabilistic proposal, deterministic evaluation and human\\ndecision into one undifferentiated operation.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS.md#AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS%2F5.%20Traversals%20and%20functor%20kinds%2FAC-016%20Typed%20composition\",\"start_line\":1017}],\"statement\":\"Composition is possible only if the first result type and judgment satisfy the second exact domain and preconditions. Preserve both identities, intermediate results, judgments, evidence, authority, provenance and stop states; probabilistic proposal, deterministic evaluation and human decision cannot be flattened. No universal F_P -> F_D -> F_H sequence is prescribed. FOUNDATIONS §3 P4a consumes this law.\",\"uncertainty\":\"The consuming P4a clause is not supplied.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:536772533e012544c08a88166035f581","key":998,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:0a8a14f789f22c87c4dd9c92b92241f1\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:536772533e012544c08a88166035f581\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"If a model claims categorical functor laws.\"],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":994,\"path\":\"standards/AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS.md\",\"quote\":\"\\\"Functor kind\\\" is an `a_c` term for this traversal classification. It does\\nnot by itself assert a category-theoretic functor. A model that claims\\ncategorical functor laws carries the demonstration that\\n[FOUNDATIONS §4](FOUNDATIONS.md#4-algebra), Formal fragment, requires of\\nevery categorical claim (P6, P1).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS.md#AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS%2F5.%20Traversals%20and%20functor%20kinds\",\"start_line\":990}],\"statement\":\"Functor-kind classification alone makes no category-theoretic assertion. A categorical claim carries the required Formal fragment demonstration; the supplied conformance discriminator further requires objects, arrows, arrow equality, identity, composition and demonstrated functor laws before such a claim.\",\"uncertainty\":\"FOUNDATIONS' full formal requirements are not supplied.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:00531a07612cbece29660d1a1407b43b","key":999,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:a6456d0051fb8cb6e9e734fa4c1a72ce\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:9740b41ae788ab183f1158a8c17b9c96\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:00531a07612cbece29660d1a1407b43b\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"For an exact-subject interpretation contract.\"],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1049,\"path\":\"standards/AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS.md\",\"quote\":\"- the exact `a_c` basis;\\n- the exact subject identity, inventory, and bytes or semantic addresses;\\n- the selected signature and any compatible extension relation;\\n- the mapping from subject declarations to every applicable model record\\n  population, including objects, relations, constraints, latitude,\\n  residuals, traversals, transformations and judgments;\\n- the interpreter identity, capability, provenance and stop states;\\n- the structural evaluation contract;\\n- the semantic selection and acceptance authority; and\\n- the source re-entry and invalidation rules.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS.md#AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS%2F6.%20Interpretation%20and%20models\",\"start_line\":1040},{\"end_line\":1056,\"path\":\"standards/AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS.md\",\"quote\":\"The proposed model `M_subject*` does not become accepted through\\nconstruction. Structural evaluation can prove closed shape, reference\\ntyping, identity derivation and basis coherence. It cannot prove that\\nprobabilistic semantic selection retained every material subject meaning.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS.md#AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS%2F6.%20Interpretation%20and%20models\",\"start_line\":1051}],\"statement\":\"The contract makes FOUNDATIONS §2 Interpretation exact for one subject and signature and declares every listed coordinate: exact calculus basis; subject identity, inventory and bytes or semantic addresses; signature and compatible extension; mapping to every applicable record population, including the eight named populations; interpreter identity, capability, provenance and stops; structural evaluation; semantic selection and acceptance authority; source re-entry and invalidation. Construction grants no acceptance. Structural proof of shape, references, identity or basis does not establish retention of every material meaning; semantic acceptance remains separate.\",\"uncertainty\":\"The cited FOUNDATIONS definition and full source-defined record schemas are absent.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:b797fc2dcdb04890b9e67570c161dcf7","key":1000,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:a6456d0051fb8cb6e9e734fa4c1a72ce\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:b797fc2dcdb04890b9e67570c161dcf7\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"For every admitted model record and every evaluated subject declaration.\"],\"exceptions\":[\"A record may be explicitly model-local under competent authority instead of mapping to exact subject provenance.\"],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1064,\"path\":\"standards/AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS.md\",\"quote\":\"Every admitted model record maps to exact subject provenance or is\\nexplicitly identified as model-local content under competent authority.\\nEvery evaluated subject declaration has a retained, omitted, residual,\\ninapplicable or refused disposition. Interpretation cannot treat absence\\nas immateriality without a recorded basis and authority (P1, P4b, P6).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS.md#AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS%2F6.%20Interpretation%20and%20models%2FAC-017%20Interpretation%20fidelity\",\"start_line\":1060}],\"statement\":\"Admitted records require exact subject provenance or the stated model-local exception. Every evaluated declaration receives retained, omitted, residual, inapplicable or refused disposition. Absence cannot be treated as immaterial without recorded basis and authority.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:d300d15f6f201f454e866e1e0923ecee","key":1001,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:9740b41ae788ab183f1158a8c17b9c96\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:d300d15f6f201f454e866e1e0923ecee\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"For every review, as owned by EVALUATION §2 and bound here to a_c.\"],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1075,\"path\":\"standards/AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS.md\",\"quote\":\"The separation of structural conformance from semantic fidelity, and the\\nrule that structural success is evidence for semantic review and no\\nsubstitute for it, are [EVALUATION §2](EVALUATION.md#2-separation)'s,\\nwhich owns them for every review.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS.md#AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS%2F6.%20Interpretation%20and%20models%2FAC-018%20Structural%20and%20semantic%20separation\",\"start_line\":1068}],\"statement\":\"Keep structural conformance separate from semantic fidelity. Structural success supports semantic review but cannot substitute for it; the owning rule remains EVALUATION's.\",\"uncertainty\":\"EVALUATION's wider review protocol is unavailable in these sections.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:2e4593574d36d7c661c98d909dcf641c","key":1002,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:67c220e7b0925f26c733270e399c4399\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:2e4593574d36d7c661c98d909dcf641c\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"When claiming M_b satisfies a_c[Sigma].\"],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1095,\"path\":\"standards/AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS.md\",\"quote\":\"1. `Sigma` and the exact `a_c` basis resolve;\\n2. every record satisfies AC-001 through AC-009;\\n3. every claimed closure, projection, overlay, transformation, judgment\\n   and composition satisfies its applicable law;\\n4. interpretation fidelity and residual dispositions bind the exact\\n   subject;\\n5. structural evaluation and semantic acceptance remain distinct and both\\n   required where claimed; and\\n6. all evidence, provenance, invalidation and re-entry coordinates\\n   resolve.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS.md#AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS%2F6.%20Interpretation%20and%20models%2FAC-019%20Valid%20model\",\"start_line\":1082}],\"statement\":\"Validity requires resolving Sigma and exact calculus basis; every record satisfying AC-001–AC-009; every claimed closure, projection, overlay, transformation, judgment and composition satisfying its applicable law; fidelity and residual dispositions binding the exact subject; distinct structural evaluation and semantic acceptance, both required where claimed; and resolution of every evidence, provenance, invalidation and re-entry coordinate. A checker may decide the structural subset. A generic checker cannot claim the semantic or authority subset unless the model supplies an exact lawful decision contract.\",\"uncertainty\":\"Several required laws and the decision-contract details are outside the supplied source.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:c492ecfd239c228de4087e08690c1521","key":1003,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:ef0db177bf46d1cab0da9336e9c1ccd2\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:6051ed012cfd01b86ac5f4b8f7d062f6\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:c492ecfd239c228de4087e08690c1521\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"When encoding a model or combining semantic-acceptance and carrier-admission results.\"],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1129,\"path\":\"standards/AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS.md\",\"quote\":\"Encoding requires `J_X.decision = accepted` and exact equality between the\\njudgment subject identity and digest and `M_X`; hold or refusal cannot be\\nencoded.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS.md#AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS%2F7.%20Layers\",\"start_line\":1118},{\"end_line\":1129,\"path\":\"standards/AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS.md\",\"quote\":\"`accepted` and\\n`admitted` map to satisfied, a hold maps as AC-007's `hold`, and `refuse`\\nis a `refusal` that takes its core value under AC-007 by its cause\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS.md#AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS%2F7.%20Layers\",\"start_line\":1124}],\"statement\":\"Encoding requires an accepted J_X whose subject identity and digest exactly equal unchanged M_X; hold and refusal cannot be encoded. Acceptance and admission answer distinct predicates, do not alter subject identity, and combine with other results only through core mappings: accepted/admitted -> satisfied; hold -> AC-007 hold; refuse -> cause-dependent AC-007 refusal. Withheld or refused judgments never count as accepted.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:d30cd1504c42d2325d859a28fdddaa01","key":1004,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:eae05dbe7bea9721fd387b0353bf6ffd\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:ef0db177bf46d1cab0da9336e9c1ccd2\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:6051ed012cfd01b86ac5f4b8f7d062f6\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:d30cd1504c42d2325d859a28fdddaa01\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1147,\"path\":\"standards/AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS.md\",\"quote\":\"`a_c`, `a_c.X` and `a_c.X.C` have independent content identities,\\njudgments, supersession relations and proof obligations (P3, P6):\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS.md#AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS%2F7.%20Layers%2FAC-020%20Layer%20and%20release%20separation\",\"start_line\":1133},{\"end_line\":1147,\"path\":\"standards/AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS.md\",\"quote\":\"An encoding failure does not change `a_c.X`. An interpretation failure\\ndoes not change `a_c`. A downstream success cannot ratify an upstream\\nlayer or basis. None of these layers is automatically an independently\\nreleased Product.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS.md#AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS%2F7.%20Layers%2FAC-020%20Layer%20and%20release%20separation\",\"start_line\":1142}],\"statement\":\"The three layers retain independent content identities, judgments, supersession and proof obligations. Calculus qualification tests internal coherence against its complete declared laws; interpretation proves fidelity to exact X; carrier qualification proves faithful canonical encoding of the accepted model. Encoding failure does not change the interpreted model, interpretation failure does not change the calculus, and downstream success cannot ratify upstream basis or layer. Product status belongs to an external authority selecting and releasing the layer, never follows automatically. SPEC_METHOD §6 applies this law to release lineage.\",\"uncertainty\":\"SPEC_METHOD's release-lineage application is not supplied.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:9c0dded7fd64c3451b20c76a2e1907d6","key":1005,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:c875cd254042a164528403012c2ce30f\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:9c0dded7fd64c3451b20c76a2e1907d6\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"For the source-defined AxiomaticCalculusBasis record.\"],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1173,\"path\":\"standards/AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS.md\",\"quote\":\"  kind: \\\"stdo.axiomatic-calculus-basis\\\",\\n  schema_version: 1,\\n  concept_identity: \\\"urn:stdo:concept:axiomatic-calculus:a-c\\\",\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS.md#AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS%2F8.%20Calculus%20identity\",\"start_line\":1159},{\"end_line\":1183,\"path\":\"standards/AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS.md\",\"quote\":\"The record uses RFC 8785 JSON Canonicalization Scheme bytes. Duplicate\\nobject names are rejected before canonicalisation.\\n`derivation_basis.principle_refs` is duplicate-free and sorted by\\nascending unsigned UTF-16 code units.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS.md#AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS%2F8.%20Calculus%20identity\",\"start_line\":1176}],\"statement\":\"The record has kind stdo.axiomatic-calculus-basis, schema_version 1 and concept_identity urn:stdo:concept:axiomatic-calculus:a-c. derivation_basis contains an absolute immutable package release_uri, manifest_sha256 and nonempty absolute semantic-address principle_refs. publication_basis contains the same release_uri, manifest_sha256, absolute member_uri within that release and member_sha256. Each digest field is 'sha256:' plus 64 lowercase hexadecimal characters. Reject duplicate object names before RFC 8785 JCS canonicalisation; principle_refs is duplicate-free and sorted ascending by unsigned UTF-16 code units. Identity is urn:stdo:axiomatic-calculus-basis:sha256: followed by sha256(JCS(AxiomaticCalculusBasis)).\",\"uncertainty\":\"No basis record is constructed or its identity calculated here.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:6cf469590dcb86f248b838a61ffebdba","key":1006,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:c875cd254042a164528403012c2ce30f\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:6cf469590dcb86f248b838a61ffebdba\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1202,\"path\":\"standards/AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS.md\",\"quote\":\"A principle reference outside the bound package, a\\nmissing or ambiguous clause, an extra undeclared premise reference, or a\\nmanifest or member digest mismatch invalidates the record (P3, P6).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS.md#AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS%2F8.%20Calculus%20identity\",\"start_line\":1200},{\"end_line\":1211,\"path\":\"standards/AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS.md\",\"quote\":\"The identity record is external to the member bytes and to the manifest\\nmember set whose digest it names. It is issued only after that set and its\\nmanifest are frozen\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS.md#AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS%2F8.%20Calculus%20identity\",\"start_line\":1204}],\"statement\":\"derivation_basis binds the complete finite governing-clause set identified by §1 Derivation provenance; recompute it when clauses change, never infer it from a hard-coded member count. Every reference resolves within publication_basis's exact package, with equal release_uri and manifest_sha256 across both roles; co-publication does not transfer premise ownership. publication_basis binds exact member bytes at a member_uri within its release. Every release_uri has immutable stdo://releases/v<version>-rc.<positive-ordinal>/ form. Acceptance is a verdict over that cut, not another identity; record presence grants no acceptance or release status. Outside-package references, missing/ambiguous clauses, extra undeclared premises and digest mismatches invalidate the record. Issue only after frozen member set and manifest; keep the record outside both hashed member set and member bytes. It may accompany them as external metadata, but neither member nor manifest embeds its identity or final bytes. The record hashes already-fixed coordinates without reverse dependency.\",\"uncertainty\":\"The actual §1 premise inventory and RELEASE issuance/acceptance rules are not supplied.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:ce17c463409bce89acbaf19cc7c4d4f0","key":1007,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:ef0db177bf46d1cab0da9336e9c1ccd2\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:6051ed012cfd01b86ac5f4b8f7d062f6\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:c875cd254042a164528403012c2ce30f\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:ce17c463409bce89acbaf19cc7c4d4f0\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"For downstream identities and dependencies on a released calculus.\"],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1221,\"path\":\"standards/AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS.md\",\"quote\":\"id(a_c.X) binds\\n  exact id(a_c)\\n  + exact subject basis id(X)\\n  + exact interpretation contract\\n  + selected model content identity\\n  + semantic-selection ledger identity and digest\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS.md#AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS%2F8.%20Calculus%20identity\",\"start_line\":1216},{\"end_line\":1237,\"path\":\"standards/AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS.md\",\"quote\":\"id(a_c.X.C) binds\\n  exact id(a_c.X)\\n  + exact carrier Product or cut\\n  + exact encoding profile\\n  + canonical carrier content identity\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS.md#AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS%2F8.%20Calculus%20identity\",\"start_line\":1233},{\"end_line\":1259,\"path\":\"standards/AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS.md\",\"quote\":\"A dependency on a released calculus binds that record's identity,\\nrelease, manifest digest and member digest. A mutable authoring copy or an\\nunissued record is never substituted for that exact basis (P3, P6).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS.md#AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS%2F8.%20Calculus%20identity\",\"start_line\":1257}],\"statement\":\"Interpreted identity binds at least exact calculus identity, subject basis identity, interpretation contract, selected model content identity and semantic-selection ledger identity/digest. Carrier identity binds at least exact interpreted identity, carrier Product or cut, encoding profile and canonical carrier content identity. Semantic acceptance points to unchanged interpreted identity/digest and stays external to both identities; encoding mechanically verifies that match and retains acceptance as evidence. Admission points to unchanged carrier identity/digest; admitted encoding is the external triple (a_c.X.C, J_X, D_C). Product acceptance/release likewise point to content-first identities. The owning Product defines downstream canonical grammar and issuance authority but cannot omit upstream identities or replace them with mutable locators. Publication binding is issued under RELEASE and AC-020 after exact package bytes exist, tying this member and §1 governing clauses to the same package. Released-calculus dependencies bind the issued record's identity, release, manifest and member digests; mutable authoring copies and unissued records cannot substitute.\",\"uncertainty\":\"Downstream canonical grammars and issuance authorities are intentionally delegated and not specified here.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:163b0001ea62bb43ef86be75053d861c","key":1008,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:eae05dbe7bea9721fd387b0353bf6ffd\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:ef0db177bf46d1cab0da9336e9c1ccd2\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:6051ed012cfd01b86ac5f4b8f7d062f6\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:163b0001ea62bb43ef86be75053d861c\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1270,\"path\":\"standards/AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS.md\",\"quote\":\"This member defines the generic relations `a_c.X` and `a_c.X.C`. It\\nselects, constructs, accepts or releases no concrete interpretation or\\ncarrier. A downstream authority owns its exact subject population,\\ninterpretation, carrier, judgments and Product or release status. The\\ndownstream identity is never embedded back into the calculus or its\\npublication basis (P2, P6).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS.md#AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS%2F9.%20Application%20boundary%2C%20imports%20and%20exclusions%2FApplication%20boundary\",\"start_line\":1265}],\"statement\":\"The member defines generic interpretation and carrier relations without selecting, constructing, accepting or releasing concrete instances. Downstream authority owns exact subject population, interpretation, carrier, judgments and Product/release status. Downstream identity is never embedded back in the calculus or publication basis.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:3ae0fd2275dfb35514c8ea0436ec864e","key":1009,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:62a4645dab80b6d4b815a54e56dda0f7\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:3ae0fd2275dfb35514c8ea0436ec864e\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"For a task projection from an interpreted subject.\"],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1307,\"path\":\"standards/AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS.md\",\"quote\":\"The task's declared subject and work boundary\\nare the seed set `Z`, with the dependency relation family `R` the task\\ndeclares, and the surface is `project(M_subject, Z, R)` (AC-011) over the\\nmaterial closure of AC-010.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS.md#AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS%2F9.%20Application%20boundary%2C%20imports%20and%20exclusions%2FConstraint%20surfaces\",\"start_line\":1292}],\"statement\":\"Use task subject/work boundary as seed Z and its declared dependency family R: project(M_subject,Z,R) under AC-011 over AC-010 material closure. Surface objects/meanings come from M_Z semantic objects with AC-002 identity and AC-017 provenance; predicates/dependencies from constraints and typed relations under AC-007/AC-004, sharing one premise record across several constraints without imposing tree shape or execution order; operations from closure traversals/transformations with preconditions and operation authority; results from constraint judgment kinds/outcomes mapped under AC-007; freedom from AC-008 latitude; authority retained per record under AC-005, with none granted by the surface; evidence from judgments and evidence/provenance/basis under AC-014/AC-006; unresolved conditions from AC-009 residuals and AC-011 Boundary_Z seams.\",\"uncertainty\":\"Full closure, projection, transformation and record laws referenced by the construction are absent.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:bc29837020eb7949f69242153f20442e","key":1010,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:62a4645dab80b6d4b815a54e56dda0f7\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:bc29837020eb7949f69242153f20442e\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"Whenever a constraint surface is used.\"],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1326,\"path\":\"standards/AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS.md\",\"quote\":\"A missing premise or an omitted\\n   obligation never becomes permission or a satisfied result (AC-007,\\n   AC-009).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS.md#AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS%2F9.%20Application%20boundary%2C%20imports%20and%20exclusions%2FConstraint%20surfaces\",\"start_line\":1324},{\"end_line\":1334,\"path\":\"standards/AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS.md\",\"quote\":\"It\\n   supplies no observation, effect grant or task context\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS.md#AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS%2F9.%20Application%20boundary%2C%20imports%20and%20exclusions%2FConstraint%20surfaces\",\"start_line\":1328}],\"statement\":\"Preserve each element's recorded standing as premise, derived consequence, policy choice, observation or unresolved claim; retain policy ownership and never turn preference into obligation. Construction/assurance elements keep their recorded kind among FOUNDATIONS' five support kinds: formula is not discharge, and externally assessed predicates retain establishing source, scope and evidence. A residual, hold, gap or unestablished external predicate retains source and required acquisition and blocks every dependent operation/result until its premise is established. Missing premises and omitted obligations grant neither permission nor satisfaction. A surface carries constraints and acquisition routes, not observations, effect grants or task context; ACTIVATION §2 acquisition obtains those from workspace and selected authoritative inputs, and workspace remains the reacquisition basis.\",\"uncertainty\":\"The five support-kind definitions and detailed acquisition protocol are not supplied.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:1d484a940190d107b663de97a84c2d8e","key":1011,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:62a4645dab80b6d4b815a54e56dda0f7\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:1d484a940190d107b663de97a84c2d8e\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"For source/basis binding, derived fidelity, qualification and ordinary entry.\"],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1352,\"path\":\"standards/AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS.md\",\"quote\":\"A projection from an\\n   interpretation bound to other subject bytes, or whose basis is not\\n   established, returns `refusal(basis)`, which is `invalid_basis`\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS.md#AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS%2F9.%20Application%20boundary%2C%20imports%20and%20exclusions%2FConstraint%20surfaces\",\"start_line\":1337},{\"end_line\":1359,\"path\":\"standards/AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS.md\",\"quote\":\"Ordinary entry\\nselects the current exact interpretation with its limits, and an earlier\\ninterpretation is identified as historical.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS.md#AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS%2F9.%20Application%20boundary%2C%20imports%20and%20exclusions%2FConstraint%20surfaces\",\"start_line\":1357}],\"statement\":\"Bind exact represented subject separately from calculus basis/signature. Different subject bytes or unestablished basis yield refusal(basis)=invalid_basis. The surface is a derived view of owning prose, not another owner; changing permitted/required work is a fidelity defect repaired at the causal source or derivation. Approximation declares adequacy relation and end-to-end bound. Structural validity may be checked mechanically, fidelity needs semantic judgment, and task sufficiency is shown only through actual use. Mechanical projection requires a separately selected checking contract; none of those claims grants operation or acceptance authority. This section itself selects, constructs and accepts no interpretation. Downstream authority owns the interpretation and its currency; ordinary entry selects the current exact interpretation with limits, marking earlier ones historical.\",\"uncertainty\":\"Detailed checking, adequacy and task-qualification contracts are delegated to absent owners.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:0033dcf64d245c5994c50c3b3b5717c5","key":1012,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:eae05dbe7bea9721fd387b0353bf6ffd\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:0033dcf64d245c5994c50c3b3b5717c5\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1379,\"path\":\"standards/AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS.md\",\"quote\":\"`a_c` is not (P2):\\n\\n- a representation or compression of its derivation source;\\n- a selected semantic model of any subject;\\n- a carrier profile or carrier instance;\\n- an executable language, interpreter, compiler implementation or\\n  runtime;\\n- a deterministic semantic assessor or theorem prover;\\n- a required storage topology of any shape;\\n- an ontology of any domain;\\n- an authority registry; or\\n- a claim that all governed systems share one vocabulary or relation set.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS.md#AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS%2F9.%20Application%20boundary%2C%20imports%20and%20exclusions%2FExclusions\",\"start_line\":1368}],\"statement\":\"a_c is none of: representation/compression of its derivation source; selected subject semantic model; carrier profile/instance; executable language, interpreter, compiler implementation or runtime; deterministic semantic assessor/theorem prover; required storage topology; domain ontology; authority registry; or assertion of a universal vocabulary/relation set across governed systems.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:6e85df03eb9d4a14635b7d034c5a03c9","key":1013,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:f2c25849cc6b1cd3bcf28e04dd63d98c\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:6e85df03eb9d4a14635b7d034c5a03c9\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"For review and qualification of the calculus member.\"],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1406,\"path\":\"standards/AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS.md\",\"quote\":\"No example, checker, model or carrier can qualify a law outside the exact\\nclaim it evaluates (P6; EVALUATION §1).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS.md#AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS%2F10.%20Conformance%20obligations\",\"start_line\":1405},{\"end_line\":1403,\"path\":\"standards/AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS.md\",\"quote\":\"10. one neutral toy model demonstrating that the calculus has no hidden\\n    derivation-source record, application-profile or carrier dependency.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS.md#AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS%2F10.%20Conformance%20obligations\",\"start_line\":1402}],\"statement\":\"Cover at least: closed signature, RecordKind_ac, populations, fields, value/reference domains; well-typed positive/refusal examples for every fundamental law; identity uniqueness and cross-context collisions; closure/projection/overlay/transformation/composition, including exact model identities, population partitions, basis equality and byte-or-typed-equality preservation refusal; strict operation/kind/actor/judgment separation; residual/authority conservation through interpretation/encoding; exact calculus-basis reconstruction; direct-coordinate, cross-family, wrong-family, duplicate-family and dangling-reference refusal cases for every fundamental record family; derivation/publication reconstruction with cyclic and same-carrier counterexamples; and one neutral toy model exposing no hidden derivation-source-record, application-profile or carrier dependency. No example, checker, model or carrier qualifies a law beyond its exact evaluated claim.\",\"uncertainty\":\"The referenced full signatures, record families and other laws are not supplied.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:0b405a4c5c09a168c6bd3e06950d17f2","key":1014,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:41bf874a29ce16378405f71ab8c8c333\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:ab6137fc418fad31d70ce554031e1867\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:0b405a4c5c09a168c6bd3e06950d17f2\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"For case execution, assessment and pass claims.\"],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":22,\"path\":\"standards/CONFORMANCE.md\",\"quote\":\"A run is not a pass; only an assessment\\nagainst the declared predicate establishes one. The presence of a case or\\ncoverage map is no execution or qualification evidence (P6).\\n\\nA case passes when the expected distinction is observed and no coerced\\nsuccess appears anywhere in the result\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/CONFORMANCE.md#CONFORMANCE\",\"start_line\":11}],\"statement\":\"A run alone is not a pass. Assessment against the declared predicate must observe the expected distinction without coerced success anywhere, returning satisfied for a pass. A case that cannot run with its declared subject is a planned evaluation not performed: it has no result and is explicitly recorded not run. Catalogue or coverage-map presence proves no execution or qualification. Core values and refinements retain their imported owners and mappings.\",\"uncertainty\":\"No run, assessment or pass is asserted by this interpretation.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:e33deb693488732932f68306ed532ff0","key":1015,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:3030c011fcddc60e3c15f2b18a635b9c\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:e33deb693488732932f68306ed532ff0\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"For the respective C-01–C-06 situations.\"],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":45,\"path\":\"standards/CONFORMANCE.md\",\"quote\":\"| C-01 No cost term | an activation whose governed question is capability fit, run without an allowance | ACTIVATION §6 | the activation refuses or records the missing allowance; the return reports spend or unavailability |\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/CONFORMANCE.md#CONFORMANCE%2F1.%20Counterexample%20cases\",\"start_line\":40}],\"statement\":\"C-01: capability-fit activation without allowance refuses or records missing allowance and reports spend/unavailability (ACTIVATION §6). C-02: for 40 rows labelled proven with literal PENDING fields, inspect underlying data and return falsified for rows, not satisfied for labels (EVALUATION §§2,4). C-03: eight from-scratch restarts repeating a method-stance defect require the restart proposal to explain why retained-work repair is insufficient; locate the defect at its owner and reprice it instead of rerunning (ACTIVATION §5). C-04: repeated unchanged-basis derivation at handoff requires counting per-handoff reads/derivations and replacing repetition with applicable reuse (ACTIVATION §7; FOUNDATIONS §4). C-05: parsing a 504.8 MB manifest for 182 entries requires declared exact-identity selective acquisition and counted transferred context without trimming required members (ACTIVATION §2). C-06: distinguish a 2.4 GB report's volume from model traffic in cost records (ACTIVATION §6).\",\"uncertainty\":\"The named local mechanisms are references; their full rules are not supplied.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:f4fd5c93d1c721a8100b12b9d8fc8c36","key":1016,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:3030c011fcddc60e3c15f2b18a635b9c\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:f4fd5c93d1c721a8100b12b9d8fc8c36\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"For the respective C-07–C-12 situations.\"],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":51,\"path\":\"standards/CONFORMANCE.md\",\"quote\":\"| C-07 Operational variable missed at intake | a provider permission profile that changed before activation | ACTIVATION §1 | the intake names operational variables; a change returns invalid_basis before effects |\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/CONFORMANCE.md#CONFORMANCE%2F1.%20Counterexample%20cases\",\"start_line\":46}],\"statement\":\"C-07: intake names operational variables; changed provider permission profile returns invalid_basis before effects (ACTIVATION §1). C-08: engine completeness amid Product-outcome regression is judged only against the selected outcome, which evidence surfaces cannot enlarge (SPEC_METHOD §3). C-09: a kernel deciding the worker's question requires declared boundary and re_enter at the owning misallocated relation (ODD §5; FOUNDATIONS §2 Work boundary). C-10: a fixture simplified around a kernel defect requires owner triage before repair, framework correction and fixture restoration (SPEC_METHOD §4). C-11: reviewer sign-off cannot close work whose stated condition is unmet; closure follows that condition and reviewer result is input only (EVALUATION §5). C-12: ticket/column/filename-only findings are judged by ambiguity removed, with carrier findings costed as churn (ACTIVATION §6).\",\"uncertainty\":\"The named local mechanisms are references; their full rules are not supplied.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:fc42a83a97b4d8b4814f10533814c611","key":1017,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:3b64cf3c4b6500bf2f4c5566de937a70\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:fc42a83a97b4d8b4814f10533814c611\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"For each applicable construction trial, with declarations before every run.\"],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":64,\"path\":\"standards/CONFORMANCE.md\",\"quote\":\"| T-04 Failure and missing assessment | one observed failure plus one required obligation with no assessment | both states survive; the composite cannot report success or erase the unassessed obligation |\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/CONFORMANCE.md#CONFORMANCE%2F2.%20Construction%20trials\",\"start_line\":60},{\"end_line\":72,\"path\":\"standards/CONFORMANCE.md\",\"quote\":\"Trials declare a per-actor context cap, the fit of\\n[ACTIVATION §2](ACTIVATION.md#2-context-construction-under-an-envelope),\\nand a total-work budget, a resource limit under\\n[ACTIVATION §6 Resource limits](ACTIVATION.md#resource-limits), before each\\nrun, include a required basis larger than the cap, count transferred context\\nacross every delegated actor, keep acceptance criteria independent of the\\nconstructing actor, and repeat probabilistic trials with varied task order.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/CONFORMANCE.md#CONFORMANCE%2F2.%20Construction%20trials\",\"start_line\":66}],\"statement\":\"T-01: basis exceeding one actor cap, tighter repeats and a coupled cannot-fit case preserve the outer contract through independently assessed refinement; cannot-fit yields out_of_frame or lawful escalation, never omission. T-02: sufficient but ambiguous small-feature intent has ambiguity resolved or explicit and meets independently owned acceptance. T-03: joining two valid bounded results preserves all inputs, constraints, judgments and evidence and refuses an incompatible producing-step composition boundary. T-04: observed failure and required unassessed obligation both survive without composite success. T-05: pause/context-clear/new actor recovers valid progress/basis and detects unsupported completion and needless restarts. T-06: revised requirement reopens affected claims and reuses unaffected results with explicit dependencies. T-07: structurally passing but behaviourally defective candidate is detected or evidential limits reported; structural green is not acceptance. T-08: sourced decision analysis with uncertainty/staleness keeps facts, assumptions, judgments and authority distinct and is independently assessable. Before every run declare per-actor cap/fit and total-work resource budget; include required basis larger than cap, count context across every delegate, keep acceptance independent of constructor and vary task order in probabilistic repeats.\",\"uncertainty\":\"ACTIVATION's fit and resource-limit definitions are referenced but not supplied.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:3d8ebdd8850ffba89e68cceadd9d7188","key":1018,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:1feeffc1b115acff77fce3a56823b82e\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:3d8ebdd8850ffba89e68cceadd9d7188\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"For R-01 and R-02; comparative obligations apply when an improvement is claimed.\"],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":79,\"path\":\"standards/CONFORMANCE.md\",\"quote\":\"| R-01 Fresh-context activation | a fresh actor given only this corpus performs a bounded activation on a declared subject; a comparative claim also selects an exact comparable baseline and runs the same task under matched acquisition conditions | the governing relations are recovered with fidelity judged independently; reconstruction cost, task completion and material errors are recorded; a comparative improvement claim has supporting matched evidence and any adverse difference is explained |\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/CONFORMANCE.md#CONFORMANCE%2F3.%20Recoverability\",\"start_line\":78}],\"statement\":\"R-01 gives a fresh actor only the corpus for bounded activation on a declared subject; governing-relation recovery has independently judged fidelity and records reconstruction cost, task completion and material errors. Comparative claims select an exact comparable baseline, run the same task under matched acquisition conditions, supply matched supporting evidence and explain adverse differences. R-02 repeats without validator folklore, author memory or whole-corpus loading and must succeed or truthfully return out_of_frame.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:f6146c61246179e2e1d818385f80d321","key":1019,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:d61f2a51196c61efb27445373af99579\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:f6146c61246179e2e1d818385f80d321\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"For discriminators 32, 33, 38, 42 and 43 and their CD-01–CD-03 actual-use cases.\"],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":101,\"path\":\"standards/CONFORMANCE.md\",\"quote\":\"Each needs actual use, a fresh constructor applying this\\ncorpus to a declared subject with the result assessed, in addition to the\\nlogical review of §5.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/CONFORMANCE.md#CONFORMANCE%2F4.%20Cases%20for%20method%20discriminators\",\"start_line\":87},{\"end_line\":97,\"path\":\"standards/CONFORMANCE.md\",\"quote\":\"the summary never overrules the workspace, discarding the prior context erases nothing in it, and a missing record of the effect leaves it completion_unknown, never absent\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/CONFORMANCE.md#CONFORMANCE%2F4.%20Cases%20for%20method%20discriminators\",\"start_line\":97}],\"statement\":\"These distinctions require fresh-constructor actual use on a declared subject with assessment in addition to textual logical review. CD-01 (32,33; ACTIVATION §1 Configuration, §3 Effects, §5; EXECUTIVE_BASELINE §16): peer actors without central coordinator or familiar responsibility names, alongside an installed release Executive, are judged by task, dependencies, limits, authority and assurance; labels/topology neither accept nor reject, and installed configuration retains its own scope. A handoff of uncertain external effect preserves outstanding obligations/dependent results, resolves completion before next dependent action and retains admitted authority/required independence; self-organisation provides no exemption. CD-02 (42,43; SPEC_METHOD §11 rules 1,2,4; EVALUATION §3): software and mixed human/software realisations of the same requirements each provide computational calculus, execution binding and evidence, judged by requirements rather than executor kind. A faster plan merging required independent assessments or automating a required human decision is falsified for each weakened obligation; output equality, cost and speed do not discharge losses. CD-03 (38; ACTIVATION §5 workspace/account, §3 Effects and Construction availability, §7): fresh actor reconciles stale summary with current subject/authoritative inputs, corrects account, retains applicable work and continues within grant; the out-of-grant disagreement stops with re_entry_requested(authority). Summary cannot override workspace; clearing context erases no workspace; missing effect record leaves completion_unknown, not absent.\",\"uncertainty\":\"Referenced operational owners are not supplied; the cases describe expected behaviour, not an executed workflow.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:78abb83318d9c5b9ad916affc7a23a49","key":1020,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:d61f2a51196c61efb27445373af99579\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:78abb83318d9c5b9ad916affc7a23a49\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"For each applicable positive, negative and unresolved assurance case.\"],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":110,\"path\":\"standards/CONFORMANCE.md\",\"quote\":\"The assurance relations require the candidate to demonstrate here the\\napplicable positive, negative and unresolved cases of a weak assertion, an\\ninsufficient observation, shared error, and change selection that retains\\nvalid evidence or invalidates affected evidence\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/CONFORMANCE.md#CONFORMANCE%2F4.%20Cases%20for%20method%20discriminators\",\"start_line\":103},{\"end_line\":117,\"path\":\"standards/CONFORMANCE.md\",\"quote\":\"a changed hash alone decides nothing\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/CONFORMANCE.md#CONFORMANCE%2F4.%20Cases%20for%20method%20discriminators\",\"start_line\":117}],\"statement\":\"Each applicable AR case requires its own exact execution and assessment record, with no catalogue-implied run/result. AR-01: each actual-use expectation set includes a necessary condition a wrong decision can satisfy; satisfied establishes only that condition, supplies no correct-frame-use claim and is excluded from benefit attribution, while falsified remains a failed run condition (FOUNDATIONS §4 Assertions and observation). AR-02: each set records two admissible returns, one correct, one incorrect, indistinguishable at the observation; grade indeterminate with that reason, never satisfied/falsified. A return matching neither is listed for diagnosis because item or return may be at fault. AR-03: expectation writer, actors and grader from one model family, with writer/actors reading shared owners, do not create independent evidence by agreement. Diagnose disagreement among ACTIVATION §1's four causes, including expectation error; assume no statistical independence from families/codebases; name donors/common dependencies of ported material (FOUNDATIONS §4 Parallel derivation). AR-04: for two changed and nine added owning sections, dependent curated frames, hashed expectation sets, interpretation and conservation readings whose validity dependencies meet impact cover are reassessed or invalidated until rebuilt; frames regenerate/tests rerun, and interpretation lacking added-section coverage stays invalidated. An expectation set with unchanged deciding sentences may remain with validity conditions stated; hash change alone decides nothing (FOUNDATIONS §4 Change impact, S_Δ and retain_applicable; ACTIVATION §7).\",\"uncertainty\":\"The four diagnostic causes and full formal assurance relations are not supplied.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:1d7b815850a2f4929340fe6736f876a7","key":1021,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:303a9298cdaede2eb7861c085d6b6788\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:1d7b815850a2f4929340fe6736f876a7\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"For each applicable coverage row, read against material member and consumer scope.\"],\"exceptions\":[\"Interpretation and optional-profile cases apply only when that surface or claim is selected; mere availability creates no implementation obligation.\"],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":137,\"path\":\"standards/CONFORMANCE.md\",\"quote\":\"Each applicable row is\\nread against the material member and consumer scope; an actual-use case\\nadds observed evidence and does not replace that reading. Required frame\\nresults carry the core result algebra or its mapped refinement. Cases\\nabout an interpretation or optional profile apply when that surface or\\nclaim is selected; availability alone creates no implementation obligation.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/CONFORMANCE.md#CONFORMANCE%2F5.%20Discriminator%20coverage\",\"start_line\":132},{\"end_line\":212,\"path\":\"standards/CONFORMANCE.md\",\"quote\":\"A coverage mapping states which cases can exercise a distinction. It is\\nnot a claim that those cases ran or passed. A selected case without a\\ncurrent assessment remains a planned evaluation without a closed result\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/CONFORMANCE.md#CONFORMANCE%2F5.%20Discriminator%20coverage\",\"start_line\":209}],\"statement\":\"Logical review constructs each situation against the text and finds the expected distinction, a counterexample or contradiction without running anything; its reviewer must meet EVALUATION §3 and result follows §4. Mechanical/structural checking does not establish this review, which supplies no actual-use evidence. Actual use adds evidence without replacing applicable textual reading. Required frame results carry core algebra or mapped refinement. Mapping denotes possible exercise, not execution/pass; a selected case without current assessment remains planned with no closed result.\",\"uncertainty\":\"Reviewer eligibility and review-result contracts are outside this source.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:97cdbd3cf78958e4b7d5ba6e6c993bba","key":1022,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:303a9298cdaede2eb7861c085d6b6788\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:97cdbd3cf78958e4b7d5ba6e6c993bba\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"For coverage discriminators 1–10; L-n is the corresponding logical-review check.\"],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":150,\"path\":\"standards/CONFORMANCE.md\",\"quote\":\"A blank field, generic referral, coarser grouping or whole-member preamble cannot supply a missing relation.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/CONFORMANCE.md#CONFORMANCE%2F5.%20Discriminator%20coverage\",\"start_line\":142}],\"statement\":\"1: show every claimed derivation's premises and argue independence rather than assume it (FOUNDATIONS §§1,3; EVALUATION §1; L-1 premises shown). 2: family arguments cover material inherited/edited rules and actual declared-family consumers or support no separate consumer; blank/generic/coarser/preamble substitutes cannot supply missing relations (FOUNDATIONS §3 tables/family index; every member family table). 3: a new introduction plus unchanged rival consumer rules is only correspondence; deciding consumers must use shared determination or justified refinement (FOUNDATIONS §§2,3; ACTIVATION §§1–7; EVALUATION §§3,5). 4: shorter text is no reduction witness; comparative claims compare actual deciding paths/acquisition with exact comparable baseline (FOUNDATIONS §3; README; shared owners). 5: shared-law use must preserve outcomes and necessary domain exception ownership; no universal reduction percentage/word decrease is needed (FOUNDATIONS §4 refinements, §2 imports; refining members). 6: outcome-driven contracts govern construction, evaluation, continuation, recovery and termination with independent cases and justified extra policies, without requiring optional typed-graph adoption (ACTIVATION §§1,4,5; ODD §1). 7: one successor law may conserve multiple predecessor claims without old partitions, but each material obligation/consumer binding is evaluated and bare links cannot replace meaning (RELEASE §9; work-carrier dispositions). 8: size reduction cannot erase material exceptions: valid disposition preserves required behaviour or obtains owning removal decision (same owners). 9: shared-law replacement retains material trigger, modal force, adoption conditions and exceptions, with noncircular owner/domain determination (FOUNDATIONS §2; referring members). 10: generic rules remain obtainable without optional-profile adoption; profile additions retain selection boundary (FOUNDATIONS §3; PROFILES §1; IDENTITY §2; ACTIVATION §1).\",\"uncertainty\":\"Most deciding owner clauses are referenced only; this preserves catalogue expectations, not independently reconstructed owner laws.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:753ee939a83aa72be258cae0482da5d3","key":1023,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:303a9298cdaede2eb7861c085d6b6788\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:753ee939a83aa72be258cae0482da5d3\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"For coverage discriminators 11–20; each uses its matching L-n check.\"],\"exceptions\":[\"For discriminator 18, an authorised successor relation may establish changed permitted work.\"],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":160,\"path\":\"standards/CONFORMANCE.md\",\"quote\":\"The changed permitted work is a fidelity defect unless an authorised successor relation establishes the change. Matching digests or valid schema do not repair it.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/CONFORMANCE.md#CONFORMANCE%2F5.%20Discriminator%20coverage\",\"start_line\":158}],\"statement\":\"11: promoting a helper requires a material distinction/independent boundary; names and shared machinery create no semantic/authority owner (DESIGN_MODULE §4; ACTIVATION §6). 12: a small interface proves no Markov sufficiency/independence; state assumptions/evidence and leave unsupported claims unresolved (IDENTITY §2; WORLD_MODEL §4; FOUNDATIONS §5). 13: a schema-passing model omitting a condition fails fidelity for affected decisions and cannot authorise source-prohibited work (AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS §6, AC-017/018; EVALUATION §2). 14: a faithful fragment proves only covered scope; whole-method claims require every material owned determination/dependency (same owners). 15: assess projected frames against source fidelity/task sufficiency; different encoding alone is no defect, changed obligations/permissions are (AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS §9; ACTIVATION §2). 16: unresolved premises retain dependencies and applicable stop/acquisition/refinement, never unrestricted freedom or permission grants (AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS §9, AC-009; ACTIVATION §1). 17: permit alternative solutions satisfying contract; internal strategy stays with worker (AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS §9, AC-008). 18: changing not-required to prohibited or preference to obligation is a fidelity defect absent authorised successor change; digest/schema agreement cannot repair it (EVALUATION §7; AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS AC-008, §9). 19: ordinary entry binds current source, signature, program, maps, instructions and evidence boundary and reproduces its route; older artifacts stay historical. Stale-input refusal contains failure without proving usable current publication or coverage (PRODUCT_DEFINITION §11; ACTIVATION §2; README). 20: structural agreement between information/representation establishes neither identical meaning nor semantic fidelity (EVALUATION §§2,6; AC-017/018; L-20 structure is not meaning).\",\"uncertainty\":\"Referenced ownership and selection details outside supplied sections remain unresolved.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:3d9561a870b75c43fc82c3816423d63e","key":1024,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:303a9298cdaede2eb7861c085d6b6788\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:3d9561a870b75c43fc82c3816423d63e\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"For coverage discriminators 21–30.\"],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":170,\"path\":\"standards/CONFORMANCE.md\",\"quote\":\"Plan membership does not authenticate the returned judgement. The misbound result cannot satisfy the assessment obligation.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/CONFORMANCE.md#CONFORMANCE%2F5.%20Discriminator%20coverage\",\"start_line\":164}],\"statement\":\"21: stable identity with changed content requires separate consideration of current state and old observation applicability (FOUNDATIONS §2 Object; IDENTITY §2; RF-005; ACTIVATION §7; L-21). 22: producer/consumer domain or precondition incompatibility is explicit; same-shaped fields do not validate a join (FOUNDATIONS §4; AC-004/016; T-03 and L-22). 23: retain authenticated A failure/citations and unresolved uncovered B; authenticate each planned assessment judgment against producer, subject, basis and evidence. B is required coverage outside planned assessments, not an omitted planned judgment (FOUNDATIONS §4 conjunction; T-04 and L-23). 24: plan membership cannot authenticate a wrong-subject judgment or satisfy its obligation (FOUNDATIONS §4 second input; EVALUATION §2; RF-005; L-24). 25: interdependent context exceeding capacity requires lawful narrowing, capable handoff or truthful stop preserving obligations (ACTIVATION §2 step 3, §4; RF-014; T-01). 26: byte-fit alone proves no adequacy; retain material dependencies, exclude irrelevant material and assess actual frame use (ACTIVATION §2 steps 2/3; EVALUATION §7; RF-003/004; L-26 plus frame qualification). 27: changed frame/task or answer-supplying instructions require exact tested packet and independent expectations; report narrower evidence, since rewritten trials or matching pins prove no current sufficiency (EVALUATION §§7,3; L-27). 28: fresh context is not independent authorship/authority; ported contributions retain authorship and contributors cannot independently accept them, though independent reviewers may share relevant common sources (EVALUATION §3; ACTIVATION §1 reconfiguration; L-28). 29: excluded frontier work stays open, with next-decision dependencies retained (ACTIVATION §1; RF-015; L-29). 30: discovery can enlarge frontier while improving knowledge; counts alone prove no progress. Revised destination needs owner decision and cannot prove original attainment (ACTIVATION §§1,5; L-30).\",\"uncertainty\":\"Referenced reference-frame and activation laws are not supplied in full.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:1420dbfd65af1b3b418845541d7234da","key":1025,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:303a9298cdaede2eb7861c085d6b6788\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:1420dbfd65af1b3b418845541d7234da\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"For coverage discriminators 31–40.\"],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":180,\"path\":\"standards/CONFORMANCE.md\",\"quote\":\"harmless explanatory metadata leaves a closed result reusable after the consumer's exact applicability check\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/CONFORMANCE.md#CONFORMANCE%2F5.%20Discriminator%20coverage\",\"start_line\":176}],\"statement\":\"31: a directly authorised task fitting a sufficient frame permits direct activation subject to separately required assessment, with no fixed role inventory/actor sequence (ACTIVATION §1; L-31). 32: peer/no-Executive/unfamiliar-role configurations are judged by task, dependencies, limits, authority and assurance; labels/topology neither reject nor accept; adopted configurations keep scope (ACTIVATION §1; EXECUTIVE_BASELINE §16; CD-01). 33: redistribution preserves obligations/dependencies, resolves material effect uncertainty before dependent action and retains authority/independence, with no self-organisation exemption (ACTIVATION §§1,3,5; CD-01). 34: adequacy differs from optimality; optimality requires objectives, constraints, comparison scope and evidence, with different models/objectives possibly favouring different configurations (ACTIVATION §1; L-34). 35: compact results must not hide delivery blockers; coordinator retains longer-term outcome and acquires next-decision information through permitted frame inputs, never assumes missing information favourable (ACTIVATION §§1,7; L-35). 36: changed dependencies/new invalidating evidence trigger applicability/validity checks before reuse even with unchanged bytes; keep demonstrably independent supported work. A declaration-preserving frame revision's harmless metadata permits reuse after exact consumer applicability check; new evidence bearing on closure or discovered out-of-family activation reopens results and consuming coverage before reliance (ACTIVATION §§7,1; EVALUATION §2; REFERENCE_FRAME §10; T-06 and L-36). 37: relevant rules without material context/authority are insufficient; activated frame binds contract, subject, evidence, capability and permitted effects (REFERENCE_FRAME §11; ACTIVATION §§1,2; L-37). 38: reconcile fresh-actor summary against current authoritative workspace, retain applicable work and stay within grant; cleared context proves no uncertain effect absent (ACTIVATION §§5,3; CD-03). 39: partial-write recovery uses current workspace/applicable state without erasing progress or inventing completed assessment (ACTIVATION §5; FOUNDATIONS §4 Not performed; T-05 and L-39). 40: parse/map success remains mechanical until independently sufficient semantic and practical evidence exists (EVALUATION §§2,7; AC-018/019; T-07 and L-40).\",\"uncertainty\":\"The cited operating protocols are retained as owner references, not executed or fully reconstructed.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:4134e710b8570da01b59731715bff40c","key":1026,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:303a9298cdaede2eb7861c085d6b6788\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:4134e710b8570da01b59731715bff40c\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"For coverage discriminators 41–52.\"],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":192,\"path\":\"standards/CONFORMANCE.md\",\"quote\":\"Failure, undecidability, non-performance and unknown effect completion never map to a higher standing.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/CONFORMANCE.md#CONFORMANCE%2F5.%20Discriminator%20coverage\",\"start_line\":187},{\"end_line\":192,\"path\":\"standards/CONFORMANCE.md\",\"quote\":\"An exact step preserves meaning. An approximate step states its adequacy relation and an end-to-end bound.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/CONFORMANCE.md#CONFORMANCE%2F5.%20Discriminator%20coverage\",\"start_line\":192}],\"statement\":\"41: proposed carrier/process law needs purpose/material justification or is unsupported overhead (ACTIVATION §6; SPEC_METHOD §4; TICKETS §5; L-41). 42: software, human and mixed tenants each supply calculus, execution binding and evidence; requirements decide fitness, executor kind does not. Preserve permitted adequate human processes using current records/direct observation without code or full event-history replay (SPEC_METHOD §11 rules 1,2,4; CD-02). 43: faster assessment-merging or human-decision automation fails conformance despite matching outputs/lower cost (SPEC_METHOD §11 rules 2,4; EVALUATION §3; CD-02). 44: each environment binding satisfies calculus laws; different stacks require no duplicate calculus, and actor identity decides neither operation kind nor authority (SPEC_METHOD §11 rules 2,5; L-44). 45: structural validation of a human-process model selects no automated executor and proves no execution fitness, which needs applicable evidence (SPEC_METHOD §11 rule 6; AC-018; L-45). 46: one locus owns a question; others refer or refine with mapping back, frame copies name owner, and precedence is no substitute (FOUNDATIONS §2 imports; PRODUCT_DEFINITION §11; L-46). 47: each owner-defined result maps declared predicate and meaning conditions to exactly one core value without raised standing; predicate/domain outcome travel with it. At 12:01, evidence of only three of five updates required by 12:00 is not_effected=falsified with two missing updates as counterexample and unknown ending as residual; lost response without counterexample is completion_unknown=indeterminate; neither repeats before reconciliation (FOUNDATIONS §4; ACTIVATION §3; result-defining members/profiles; L-47). 48: lifecycle/classification data remains distinct from admission/compliance/closure decisions; actual determination uses core contract, and data labels/core referrals cannot replace domain mappings (FOUNDATIONS §4; ACTIVATION §3; TICKETS §3; SPEC_METHOD §2; L-48). 49: compare required/permitted decisions on the same material case including modality, triggers, scope and exceptions; indicative grammar does not settle meaning. Superseded claims name replacement relation/owners and proposed replacements stay pending until accepted (RELEASE §9; work-carrier dispositions; L-49). 50: every result-returning frame carries core algebra or profile mapping (RF-012, §11; ACTIVATION §2; L-50). 51: categorical functor/join claims require objects, arrows, arrow equality, identity, composition and demonstrated laws before the claim; otherwise hypothesis (FOUNDATIONS §4; EVALUATION §6; AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS §5; L-51). 52: rewrite/refinement declares its permitting subject law; exact preserves meaning, approximate declares adequacy/end-to-end bound (ACTIVATION §4; L-52).\",\"uncertainty\":\"External result mappings are retained only where the supplied catalogue states them.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:5ed6aa456c7794319f1d53db541df8ea","key":1027,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:303a9298cdaede2eb7861c085d6b6788\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:5ed6aa456c7794319f1d53db541df8ea\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"For integrated assessment of the complete declared member set and material composition, including J53–J59.\"],\"exceptions\":[\"Existing applicable evidence may support several cases; no separate run per table row or complete fresh execution is required where governing assurance is established.\"],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":207,\"path\":\"standards/CONFORMANCE.md\",\"quote\":\"Supported inapplicability of a conditional obligation is recorded separately; it does not waive any applicable mandatory criterion.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/CONFORMANCE.md#CONFORMANCE%2F5.%20Discriminator%20coverage\",\"start_line\":203},{\"end_line\":207,\"path\":\"standards/CONFORMANCE.md\",\"quote\":\"Existing applicable evidence can support several cases; no separate run per table row is imposed.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/CONFORMANCE.md#CONFORMANCE%2F5.%20Discriminator%20coverage\",\"start_line\":205}],\"statement\":\"Review and acceptance remain distinct EVALUATION-owned acts; local success cannot discharge shared contradiction, unresolved owner decision or required-result gap. J53: separately satisfied members do not erase cross-member contradiction; assess shared owners/composition. J54: reviewer agreement supports a replacement proposal but dependent acceptance waits for exact owner replacement decision on work carrier; construction grant supplies none. J55: missing, stale or falsified required criteria withhold acceptance under conjunction while preserving components; favourable verdict cannot replace evidence; supported conditional inapplicability is separate and waives no applicable mandatory criterion. J56: control success alongside candidate-frame failure preserves applicable task judgment, proves neither fixture answer leakage nor removal of frame-use failure; benefit attribution and applicability corrections need their own claim/reason. J57: assess actual path from selected outcome through bounded work, observation, diagnosis and lawful continuation/closure, using independently specified actual-use expectations; prose alone proves no use. J58: join source obligation, interpreted predicate, observed subject and supported conclusion, exposing weak assertion, insufficient observation and shared error while retaining bounded standings. J59: supported repair impact selects reassessment, retains known failures and unknown coverage and combines new evidence with justified reuse; demonstrate both valid retention and missed-dependency/changed-oracle cases.\",\"uncertainty\":\"The full conjunction and acceptance protocols remain external references.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:26798f845a0e65ef33d8be6702ae4c99","key":1028,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:fa454c5f56bb19592ddc541d457f3689\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:26798f845a0e65ef33d8be6702ae4c99\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"For UC-1–UC-9; each has its corresponding L-UCn check, with UC-9 also exercised by CD-03.\"],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":234,\"path\":\"standards/CONFORMANCE.md\",\"quote\":\"Preservation alone proves no progress or termination. State the actual support for continuing or the unresolved stop; no generic termination proof is required merely to perform bounded work.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/CONFORMANCE.md#CONFORMANCE%2F5.%20Discriminator%20coverage%2FUniversal-construction%20and%20assurance%20discriminators\",\"start_line\":232}],\"statement\":\"UC-1: internal success with required end-to-end failure retains outer failure and diagnoses affected join; local completion proves no Z (ACTIVATION §1; FOUNDATIONS §4 preservation; EVALUATION §1). UC-2: lawful operations with unmet outcome constraints distinguish admissible construction from delivery; specification supplies Z, calculus/execution implies no satisfaction/acceptance (ACTIVATION §1 Binding A and Z; SPEC_METHOD §11). UC-3: bug labels do not decide implementation/requirement/observation cause or repair permission; use one intake/diagnosis, correct supported affected relation or acquire evidence and retain alternatives (ACTIVATION §1; SPEC_METHOD §4). UC-4: weakened Z needs owner decision/downstream re-entry and proves neither former Z nor erasure of original counterexample (ACTIVATION §1; SPEC_METHOD §4; FOUNDATIONS §4 parallel derivation). UC-5: predictive accuracy and normative outcome satisfaction are separate predicates/support, neither determining the other (ACTIVATION §1 three accounts/diagnosis). UC-6: select strategy within outcome constraints by material resource/risk/feedback tradeoffs, with no cost waiver; preserve incomparable alternatives and unsupported estimates (ACTIVATION §1; FOUNDATIONS §4 quantified assurance; EXECUTIVE_BASELINE Steel-thread). UC-7: invariant preservation alone proves no progress/termination; give actual continuation support or unresolved stop, without imposing generic termination proof for bounded work (ACTIVATION §1; FOUNDATIONS §3). UC-8: distinguish attempt termination, discovery, ongoing maintenance and delivery; elapsed work/count changes alone decide none (ACTIVATION §§1,6). UC-9: restart/disturbance contradicting cache requires current-subject reacquisition, affected-claim reopening, independent-work preservation and sufficient effect-uncertainty resolution before dependent action (ACTIVATION §§5,7; CD-03).\",\"uncertainty\":\"Owner definitions of A, Z and governing construction relations are not fully supplied.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:df657a33bd9b0a6128d8ff960a3cb057","key":1029,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:fa454c5f56bb19592ddc541d457f3689\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:df657a33bd9b0a6128d8ff960a3cb057\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"For AS-1–AS-6; each has L-ASn, with AS-2/3/6 also exercised by AR-01/02/03 respectively.\"],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":240,\"path\":\"standards/CONFORMANCE.md\",\"quote\":\"A universal soundness claim covers every admitted conclusion; a selected deterministic model retains its scope, and a probability claim needs its own distribution and evidence.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/CONFORMANCE.md#CONFORMANCE%2F5.%20Discriminator%20coverage%2FUniversal-construction%20and%20assurance%20discriminators\",\"start_line\":239}],\"statement\":\"AS-1: local success without postcondition-to-next-precondition preservation or final-property-to-Z coverage requires the missing argument, withholds unsupported end-to-end conclusion and retains local support (FOUNDATIONS §4 preservation). AS-2: correct histogram keys with wrong counts shows a key-only test's predicate limit; assertion provenance distinguishes necessary from sufficient, and faithful count assertion detects the count defect within scope (FOUNDATIONS §4 assertions; AR-01). AS-3: opposite-truth admissible states with identical observations preclude sound complete decision from those observations; acquire distinguishing evidence, justify narrower scope or return indeterminate, distinguishing unavailable observation from non-performance (same owner; AR-02). AS-4: implementation-copied expectations plus requirement digest prove neither assertion fidelity nor independent upstream derivation; supported local regression claims remain usable (FOUNDATIONS §4 parallel derivation). AS-5: where human/probabilistic checker soundly admits satisfied or indeterminate on identical observations, the model admits both; universal soundness covers all admitted conclusions, deterministic selection keeps scope, probability needs distribution/evidence (FOUNDATIONS §4 assertions). AS-6: differing actors agreeing through shared wrong interpretation/fixture/contribution do not supply independence; expose common causes and port authorship, and validate common expectation using its separate purpose/evidence (FOUNDATIONS §4 parallel derivation; AR-03).\",\"uncertainty\":\"Formal proofs, observation models and independence evidence are not present.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:8620e8322b06fc18bf8fb1f38f845b00","key":1030,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:fa454c5f56bb19592ddc541d457f3689\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:8620e8322b06fc18bf8fb1f38f845b00\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"For AS-7–AS-12 and all claims based on the listed finite models or case mappings.\"],\"exceptions\":[\"Applicable unchanged evidence may be retained where isolation and validity conditions are supported; full re-execution is not required solely because the subject changed.\"],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":246,\"path\":\"standards/CONFORMANCE.md\",\"quote\":\"Missing influence information cannot justify exclusion; new uncovered obligations generate work and mandatory gates remain applicable.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/CONFORMANCE.md#CONFORMANCE%2F5.%20Discriminator%20coverage%2FUniversal-construction%20and%20assurance%20discriminators\",\"start_line\":244},{\"end_line\":251,\"path\":\"standards/CONFORMANCE.md\",\"quote\":\"The listed cases are an assessment design. Their execution records bind\\ncurrent subjects and evidence independently. A mapped case never becomes\\na pass by its presence, and a mapping does not exempt a material owner or\\nconsumer from review (P6, P2).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/CONFORMANCE.md#CONFORMANCE%2F5.%20Discriminator%20coverage%2FUniversal-construction%20and%20assurance%20discriminators\",\"start_line\":248}],\"statement\":\"AS-7/L-AS7: multiplying miss rates or promoting injected-defect scores to whole-Product correctness requires model, justified dependence and calibration scope; unsupported quantification stays unresolved while bounded observations survive (FOUNDATIONS §4 quantified assurance). AS-8/L-AS8: finite successes/schema-valid formula are no universal preservation proof; formal obligation, discharged argument, structure and bounded execution retain distinct scopes, with bounded work allowed under governing conditions (FOUNDATIONS §4 formal representation; AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS §9 condition 1). AS-9/AR-04/L-AS9: changed governing requirements trigger owner-authorised reassessment of affected assertions/applicability; original evidence/counterexamples retain subjects (FOUNDATIONS §4 change impact; ACTIVATION §7). AS-10/L-AS10: impact includes material execution/validity dependencies, not just requirement-to-test provenance; missing influence cannot justify exclusion, uncovered obligations generate work and mandatory gates remain (FOUNDATIONS §4 change impact). AS-11/L-AS11: supported isolated repair permits unchanged applicable evidence plus affected reassessment, without automatic full rerun. AS-12/L-AS12: selection accounts for required assurance, residual uncertainty and total relevant cost; broader execution is available, and cheap selection/fixed full-suite habits prove neither adequacy nor efficiency (FOUNDATIONS §4 change impact/quantified assurance). Every case receives local logical review and actual-use evidence where its claim requires it; finite-model properties stay within declared model/population, mechanical validity grants no semantic fidelity or whole-Product conformance. Execution records independently bind current subjects/evidence; mapping neither proves pass nor exempts material owners/consumers from review.\",\"uncertainty\":\"Quantitative models, impact covers and actual evidence are not supplied.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:e9a6b9869d990f8f2d548d45abf9d559","key":1031,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:803107dc0e8102b1fc0c5d9126108f77\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:b53ecd7f95b44bc7ffed5180d491d116\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:ac55c80211cf131cf378a4be5f1205d3\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:e9a6b9869d990f8f2d548d45abf9d559\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"Where the optional profile governs a boundary.\"],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":26,\"path\":\"standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md\",\"quote\":\"It imports\\n[FOUNDATIONS](FOUNDATIONS.md), [ACTIVATION](ACTIVATION.md),\\n[EVALUATION](EVALUATION.md), [IDENTITY](IDENTITY.md),\\n[SPEC_METHOD](SPEC_METHOD.md), [ASSURANCE](ASSURANCE.md),\\n[TICKETS](TICKETS.md) and [RELEASE](RELEASE.md) by reference and defines\\nnone of their objects again\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md#DESIGN_MODULE\",\"start_line\":14},{\"end_line\":75,\"path\":\"standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md\",\"quote\":\"Every clause names the principle that requires it (P0 to P6, FOUNDATIONS\\n§3).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md#DESIGN_MODULE\",\"start_line\":74}],\"statement\":\"Import FOUNDATIONS, ACTIVATION, EVALUATION, IDENTITY, SPEC_METHOD, ASSURANCE, TICKETS and RELEASE by reference without redefining their objects. Ownership remains: proportionality at ACTIVATION §6; execution unit/seam at §1; complete enclosing-relation admission at §4; authority identity at IDENTITY §6; shared machinery at FOUNDATIONS §4; realisation core/non-goals at SPEC_METHOD §2; design-to-module evidence, module-derived tests and lifecycle confirmation at ASSURANCE §§14–16. ODD graph-execution and UX profiles refine/bound DESIGN_MODULE where their own scopes apply. Each profile clause names its requiring P0–P6 principle.\",\"uncertainty\":\"Imported owner definitions and the stated refining profiles are outside the supplied excerpts.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:df4241330cccefa8885f3fd52e4a94b1","key":1032,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:48509418a2bcdf06ca45005884f68544\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:df4241330cccefa8885f3fd52e4a94b1\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"For performed profile evaluations, design dispositions and record entries.\"],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":72,\"path\":\"standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md\",\"quote\":\"This member uses `not_applicable` in two senses. A\\n`not_applicable` record entry, in the entity-lifecycle matrix, for a\\ndiscovery category or for an unsupported admission form (§5), records an\\nexclusion: the excluded obligation has no result\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md#DESIGN_MODULE\",\"start_line\":62},{\"end_line\":72,\"path\":\"standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md\",\"quote\":\"A `not_applicable` axiom verdict (§7\\nCross-view axiom evaluation) is a value of a predicate declared as a\\ndisjunction that includes non-application, mapped there under the same\\nparagraph.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md#DESIGN_MODULE\",\"start_line\":67}],\"statement\":\"Performed evaluations return core values directly or via the two locally mapped refinements: §7 reconstruction decisions and cross-view axiom verdicts. Ontology/design verdicts are ACTIVATION §3 dispositions as specified by §7 Gate and retrospective work. Function-derivation dispositions, entity-lifecycle entries, discovery-category/unsupported-admission not_applicable entries, competing-path dispositions, IACS revision classes, reference mappings, two-part algorithmic-obligation dispositions and module roles are author-declared assessed records, not results, and map to no core value. Their evaluations return separate core values. A not_applicable record entry records an exclusion with no result for the excluded obligation under ACTIVATION applicability/core exclusions; a not_applicable axiom verdict is instead a mapped predicate value for a disjunction including non-application. Consumers must never combine record entries as results.\",\"uncertainty\":\"The two refinement mappings and referenced exclusion/disposition contracts are not supplied.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:753baaff60c88ef40bed775c0c4c6a2f","key":1033,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:803107dc0e8102b1fc0c5d9126108f77\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:634fd70c19c7707b7f5e7b83c30a4e6b\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:753baaff60c88ef40bed775c0c4c6a2f\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"For module boundaries, schema/carrier families, entity/record design and interface contracts under this profile.\"],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":123,\"path\":\"standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md\",\"quote\":\"A product decision that functionality is\\nrequired does not decide how many entities, functions, public operations,\\ncarriers or modules should exist\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md#DESIGN_MODULE%2F1.%20Purpose%20and%20position%2FPurpose\",\"start_line\":113},{\"end_line\":123,\"path\":\"standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md\",\"quote\":\"For a product governed by the\\ngraph-execution profile, this profile does not authorise replacing a graph\\nfunction, edge traversal or graph module with deterministic implementation\\nmodules; it governs the deterministic realisation shape inside or beneath\\nthose carriers\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md#DESIGN_MODULE%2F1.%20Purpose%20and%20position%2FPurpose\",\"start_line\":115}],\"statement\":\"The profile biases toward low coupling, modular composition, immutable typed carriers, total or nearly total semantic transforms and explicit effect boundaries, pursuing implementation discipline beyond passing code rather than language ideology. Every intermediate traversal should have a finite inspectable reasoning/implementation/evaluation/proof/refactor unit; modules are one tool, not the only possible bounded traversal. The profile governs ontology, architecture and module derivation after selected outcomes/capabilities, without replacing SPEC_METHOD constitutional authority or graph-native law. Required functionality does not determine entity/function/public-operation/carrier/module counts. For graph-profile Products, deterministic modules cannot replace graph functions, edge traversals or graph modules by this profile's authority; it governs deterministic shape within/beneath them. Scope includes the named boundary/schema/entity/interface forms and is not limited to one language/runtime.\",\"uncertainty\":\"The execution-unit and graph-native owners are referenced but not fully supplied.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:becbde218a0cd99ee0a3c6f95fae2dd3","key":1034,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:6448312e3a64306604f189415f61316f\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:becbde218a0cd99ee0a3c6f95fae2dd3\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"For implementations seeking to satisfy the profile.\"],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":134,\"path\":\"standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md\",\"quote\":\"A Python, Scala, TypeScript,\\nKotlin or Java implementation may each satisfy it if it keeps semantic law\\nin explicit carriers and transforms rather than hidden orchestration.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md#DESIGN_MODULE%2F1.%20Purpose%20and%20position%2FPosition\",\"start_line\":132}],\"statement\":\"Functional design discipline is required without requiring a functional language. The preferred shape says meaning should live in typed carriers/explicit transforms, imperative coordination should be subordinate to admitted truth, effects should be isolated to explicit boundary modules, and shared mutable state should be minimised and justified. Python, Scala, TypeScript, Kotlin and Java may each satisfy the discipline if semantic law remains explicit rather than hidden in orchestration.\",\"uncertainty\":\"These preference/should formulations are retained without upgrading each into an unconditional must.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:6bbecdffb0392835a99804e61c8db59f","key":1035,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:af6461c6cd976f9897df29c33b0d379b\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:e33b4c2ac78d7102c41dd630b46098a2\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:6bbecdffb0392835a99804e61c8db59f\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"The profile has been adopted for the boundary.\"],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":268,\"path\":\"standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md\",\"quote\":\"no profile choice is presented as following from the foundations (P6, P2).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md#DESIGN_MODULE%2F1.%20Purpose%20and%20position%2FFoundation%20to%20law\",\"start_line\":268}],\"statement\":\"Keep consequence, premise standing and added choice distinct. F17 owns its scope, functional preferences at should force, no-world-model-theory stance, two result refinements and record vocabulary, closure evaluators/fail-closed/ingress shape, Python rules and strict-pass requirement, ten Ontology terms/materiality/evidence, nineteen M(B) terms and sequencing predicates, frame items and reconstruction decisions, selection sources/dimensions, lifecycle matrices and should-normally readings, authority/admission design fields, Prime/IACS/promotion vocabulary, three views/stereotypes/evaluation columns, design gate, computational dispositions, six recommended module roles and binding, carrier/mutation/effect/dependency preferences, governance publication/drift categories, optimisation/review triggers, recurrence design-conformance refinement, review questions/checks, optional adoption-recording means and role-limited runtime identity defaults. These choices are not foundational deductions. Projects choose strict checker/configuration and composition/effect algebra; consumers choose substrate/evidence mechanism; exact-Product priorities/risk tolerances belong to the existing trade-off owner; Product owns workloads, acceptance limits and semantic-function domain outcomes; design authority accepts the Ontology; Product authority adopts boundary/rule family. Referenced owners retain core/non-goal, proportionality, invalidation/reuse, admission, authority-identity, bridge/migration, disposition, assurance, work-carrier and constitutional laws.\",\"uncertainty\":\"The cited owning bodies and several enumerated rule details are outside the supplied sections.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:ee583763e550898d871406d498843838","key":1036,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:af6461c6cd976f9897df29c33b0d379b\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:ee583763e550898d871406d498843838\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"An actor applies a foundation-to-law row to a governed boundary.\"],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":192,\"path\":\"standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md\",\"quote\":\"an entry of the design record, a `not_applicable` exclusion included, is not a result\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md#DESIGN_MODULE%2F1.%20Purpose%20and%20position%2FFoundation%20to%20law\",\"start_line\":192},{\"end_line\":216,\"path\":\"standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md\",\"quote\":\"identity generators, validators and normalisers that a runtime realisation publishes are defaults, which the owner of the identity can override\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md#DESIGN_MODULE%2F1.%20Purpose%20and%20position%2FFoundation%20to%20law\",\"start_line\":216}],\"statement\":\"Required functionality does not determine counts of entities, functions, operations, carriers or modules. Every performed evaluation returns an F3 core value directly or through its defined refinement; records, including exclusions, are not results. Modules bound traversal reasoning and are classified by recommended roles; the head's binding applies tier-2 assurance law unchanged. Semantic functions should be total or as close as language/problem allow; immutable typed values are preferred. Effects should be explicit at the edge, controllers should not hide semantic authority and coupling should be reduced through dependency shape. A boundary governing, observing or evaluating another actor publishes state, boundary and admissible routes, not strategy unless ratified responsibility includes strategy. Cleanup is lawful only when boundary-local and neutral in behaviour, authority, visibility and effect; leaving an opened boundary better is a should, and cross-boundary opportunities are owner repricing input. Credible recurrence triggers commonisation review, never automatic merge. Before closure, reconstruct the exact claim's function, reuse accepted evidence only under reuse law, and block closure for falsifying issues or applicable hard stops; outside-claim discoveries do not enlarge scope. Each interface family has one source truth consumed downstream; retaining an old authority path behind a new interface is bridge debt, while compatibility needs its own authority and proof. Review checks governing rules; unanswered required relations withhold conformance, and evidence-based diagnosis goes to the actual owner. Missing authority/observation alone proves neither excessive coupling nor imperative design. Prompt clauses enforcing design law need provenance and evidence of continued causal effect. Adoption applies consistently across the named boundary; partial adoption identifies boundary/rule family and cannot claim completion whose evidence was skipped. Consumer-bound ABG-role runtime identity generators, validators and normalisers may publish defaults only within that role; defaults confer no authority and the identity owner may override them.\",\"uncertainty\":\"Detailed later clauses, prompt checks, module roles, mutation justifications and runtime default surface kinds are referenced but not supplied.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:54bdcc9dcc60196021a5abe23c154b76","key":1037,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:97f087b604d6d9d05c50fbf4d552359b\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:54bdcc9dcc60196021a5abe23c154b76\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"This profile is used in a graph-execution-governed Product.\"],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":275,\"path\":\"standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md\",\"quote\":\"reviewers first ask whether the boundary is an\\noperative graph traversal (P6, P0).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md#DESIGN_MODULE%2F2.%20Graph-execution%20alignment%20and%20escalation\",\"start_line\":273},{\"end_line\":295,\"path\":\"standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md\",\"quote\":\"the boundary should be repriced against the graph-execution\\nprofile before claiming design-method closure.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md#DESIGN_MODULE%2F2.%20Graph-execution%20alignment%20and%20escalation\",\"start_line\":294}],\"statement\":\"Review first determines whether the boundary is an operative graph traversal. Product movement between typed asset states follows the outcome-traversal → graph-carrier → deterministic-realisation structure. If a deterministic module appears to own next work, target movement, traversal closure or the graph function being performed, the boundary should be repriced against graph execution before design-method closure.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:6de89eea3a2a2507e088821a99e5a482","key":1038,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:82e6156594202f0a9c804bce9d492a25\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:6de89eea3a2a2507e088821a99e5a482\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"The profile governs the boundary.\",\"A design or implementation change is proposed.\"],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":304,\"path\":\"standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md\",\"quote\":\"They are not optional heuristics. A\\nchange that improves local ergonomics, test output or static-checker\\noutput but fails one of them is not real progress under this profile.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md#DESIGN_MODULE%2F3.%20Boundary%20closure%20evaluators\",\"start_line\":302}],\"statement\":\"Each change should be judged against the three overriding evaluators; they are not optional heuristics. Local ergonomics, tests or static-checker improvements do not count as real progress when any evaluator fails.\",\"uncertainty\":\"The text combines should force with non-optional evaluator standing; both are retained without upgrading should to must.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:82497bc3b2f7d463d712a9456abc0b83","key":1039,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:82e6156594202f0a9c804bce9d492a25\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:82497bc3b2f7d463d712a9456abc0b83\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"A change affects a governed semantic boundary.\"],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":317,\"path\":\"standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md\",\"quote\":\"If meaning survives by reconstruction, the\\nseam is not closed.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md#DESIGN_MODULE%2F3.%20Boundary%20closure%20evaluators%2FAuthority%20seam%20closure\",\"start_line\":316}],\"statement\":\"Each change does not increase truth-surface count; existing duplicates/rivals should be reduced by seam-closure work. Each semantic boundary has one authoritative carrier or contract. Controllers must not reconstruct already-admitted truth; downstream surfaces must not silently rebuild source truth from raw artifacts; raw/open payloads are not trusted beyond ingress. Removing the authoritative carrier must fail closed: silent reconstruction of the same meaning demonstrates an unclosed seam.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:bf0181c38ecb32071eca4fa3879d0d81","key":1040,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:82e6156594202f0a9c804bce9d492a25\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:982faaba8542901a360f970f115eecef\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:bf0181c38ecb32071eca4fa3879d0d81\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"The module performs projection or query.\"],\"exceptions\":[\"A same-name, different-shape carrier divergence is lawful when an explicit migration design makes it lawful.\"],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":326,\"path\":\"standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md\",\"quote\":\"same-name but different-shape\\ncarriers fail closed unless an explicit migration design makes the\\ndivergence lawful; and negative tests cover structural drift, not only\\nmissing source truth.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md#DESIGN_MODULE%2F3.%20Boundary%20closure%20evaluators%2FAuthority%20seam%20closure\",\"start_line\":323}],\"statement\":\"Projection/query seam closure names the admitted carrier, runtime, event or source truth. Reconstructed catalogue, ownership, route, status or closure truth is structurally compared with the admitted source carrier before publication. Same-name/different-shape carriers otherwise fail closed. Negative tests cover structural drift as well as missing truth.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:42c67cf2ca006491ed1533dc74dfd900","key":1041,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:82e6156594202f0a9c804bce9d492a25\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:e14ea2ce604c9b38027bf09a26544d13\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:42c67cf2ca006491ed1533dc74dfd900\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"A governed change affects the slice.\"],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":338,\"path\":\"standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md\",\"quote\":\"Each change should collapse the slice to the few real identity-bearing\\ncarrier families (P3, P2).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md#DESIGN_MODULE%2F3.%20Boundary%20closure%20evaluators%2FEssential%20carrier%20consolidation\",\"start_line\":330}],\"statement\":\"Each change should consolidate the slice into its few real identity-bearing carrier families: declare IACS first, keep subordinate payloads subordinate by default and avoid fragment classes/interfaces/result records created only for typing, serialisation or convenience extraction. Progress means sharper/fewer carrier families, less duplicate authority and less boundary inflation; extra wrappers, branch-local peer types and public records merely mirroring payload detail do not establish progress.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:909b0356ea0855f0488642fb192f977c","key":1042,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:82e6156594202f0a9c804bce9d492a25\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:fb7c124a177ade36a4c47157ab72d44e\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:909b0356ea0855f0488642fb192f977c\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":352,\"path\":\"standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md\",\"quote\":\"The rule is the same: proof\\nfirst, enforcement second.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md#DESIGN_MODULE%2F3.%20Boundary%20closure%20evaluators%2FEnforcement%20after%20proof\",\"start_line\":351}],\"statement\":\"Typing, schemas, validators, contracts and codecs lock in an already-real seam. Parse, validate or construct first; explicitly admit and narrow; then enforce the proved shape with types/schemas. Relabelling an open payload, enveloping loose data without changing the authority path, casts, unchecked assertions and dynamic mutation do not supply closure. The evaluator is language-agnostic; strict Python checking, sealed algebraic types with schema parsing and compiler-enforced sums with decoding are examples, not a language mandate.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:0fc795b026b4d204d26e886a90c4ab97","key":1043,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:82e6156594202f0a9c804bce9d492a25\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:fb7c124a177ade36a4c47157ab72d44e\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:0fc795b026b4d204d26e886a90c4ab97\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"Input is foreign, dynamic or weakly typed.\"],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":364,\"path\":\"standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md\",\"quote\":\"The required\\nshape: receive foreign input; parse, validate or normalise it once;\\nconstruct local admitted carrier truth; consume only that local truth in\\nsemantic kernels.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md#DESIGN_MODULE%2F3.%20Boundary%20closure%20evaluators%2FIngress%20collapse\",\"start_line\":357}],\"statement\":\"Such input is lawful only at ingress and, once admitted, immediately becomes local carrier truth before semantic transforms. Required order: receive; parse/validate/normalise once; construct admitted local truth; consume only that truth in semantic kernels. Repeated parsing across modules, from_dict(...).to_dict() ceremony retaining open authority, loaders merely relabelling unvalidated JSON/maps and kernels inspecting open fragments are not lawful seam closure.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:287ccd9684a75fb6296f8b44761d0027","key":1044,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:fb7c124a177ade36a4c47157ab72d44e\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:287ccd9684a75fb6296f8b44761d0027\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"A project adopts this profile.\"],\"exceptions\":[\"Materially necessary mutable carrier state is allowed under the owning Immutable carriers rule and its required recorded justification.\",\"The explicit failure-carrier preference applies only where practical.\"],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":394,\"path\":\"standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md\",\"quote\":\"Both lists bind. A project that adopts this profile prefers the first\\nand avoids the second as an obligation of the profile, not as a\\ndescription of practice:\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md#DESIGN_MODULE%2F4.%20Functional%20bias%20and%20typing%2FFunctional%20bias%20without%20language%20mandate\",\"start_line\":385}],\"statement\":\"Binding preferences are immutable carriers over shared mutable objects; closed typed carriers over dictionaries/string protocols; one ingress parse/admission; explicit returns over hidden mutation; explicit failure carriers over ambient exception control where practical; small-transform composition over long controllers. Binding avoidances are a giant mutable workspace, orchestration owning semantic law, hidden coupling through globals/registries/service state, typed envelopes over open truth, dynamic semantic-centre mutation, helpers both deciding meaning and writing, and proxy interfaces retaining old authority. An avoided shape or forgone preference is nonconformant unless a profile rule permits departure and its required justification is recorded. Convenience permits none; preserve preference/avoidance modality rather than recasting every preference as an unconditional ban.\",\"uncertainty\":\"Full mutation-justification requirements are in an unsupplied owning clause.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:b7ae8d9d661e3ad2148b57b4a4356c50","key":1045,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:fb7c124a177ade36a4c47157ab72d44e\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:b7ae8d9d661e3ad2148b57b4a4356c50\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"The profile governs a Python boundary.\"],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":402,\"path\":\"standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md\",\"quote\":\"every function, method and\\ncallable surface has explicit parameter and return annotations; semantic\\ncarriers are closed and typed; and repo-authored tests, scripts and\\nsupport code are typed too, with no lower bar than production code.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md#DESIGN_MODULE%2F4.%20Functional%20bias%20and%20typing%2FPython%20typing\",\"start_line\":399}],\"statement\":\"All repo-authored Python, including every callable, test, script and support surface, has explicit parameter/return annotations and closed typed semantic carriers. Untyped def, implicit Any, semantic dict[str, Any]/Mapping[str, Any]/object carrier truth and unchecked JSON passed through layers with .get chains are not typed semantic design; semantic-centre dict[str, Any] is design debt. Use dataclass, TypedDict, Protocol, Literal, Enum or other closed forms; validate dynamic input and narrow it before transforms. A strict pass such as mypy --strict or an equivalent configuration is required. If the adopted boundary cannot check cleanly, it is not yet implementation-conformant.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:1574a126ebeadbf6af7741893cd5e9f5","key":1046,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:fdb10a62e0ecdba0beca462cc9d91a8d\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:0a1c7d24e8784721926afa9489f9c0e0\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:1574a126ebeadbf6af7741893cd5e9f5\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"A new or materially changed active semantic boundary is involved.\"],\"exceptions\":[\"A realization_refactor wholly inside an accepted boundary may cite the existing Ontology/design basis and prove no Ontology delta; unchanged evidence need not be re-authored or re-accepted.\"],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":435,\"path\":\"standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md\",\"quote\":\"Every new or materially changed active semantic boundary derives its\\nsemantic model from one accepted Ontology (P1, P6).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md#DESIGN_MODULE%2F5.%20Ontology-first%20design\",\"start_line\":430},{\"end_line\":472,\"path\":\"standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md\",\"quote\":\"Unaffected\\nmaintenance and unrelated boundaries do not freeze merely because one\\nsource digest changed (P2, P0).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md#DESIGN_MODULE%2F5.%20Ontology-first%20design\",\"start_line\":470}],\"statement\":\"Derive the semantic model from one accepted Ontology. Before promoting a changed entity, function, authority, effect, Prime-conformant carrier, module boundary, public operation or schema, produce a candidate slice and carry it through acceptance. Identify constitutional sources and accepting design authority, stable element/relation identities and a version/basis making source change, staleness and affected projections decidable. A governing-source reprice invalidates only affected relations/projections until impact reevaluation. Publish only affected semantic/structural deltas and projection impacts; unrelated maintenance does not freeze on a digest change. Code, tests, generated schemas and an implementing agent cannot self-ratify missing authority. Inventories of classes, schemas, endpoints, commands or carriers alone are not Ontologies.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:704111024ccf1ddaab7f3643b9882e77","key":1047,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:b8bc7d3a0ac93efb8d5099e60d3dfcad\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:17af2f81977b5a255c4155d8b1c3abd0\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:704111024ccf1ddaab7f3643b9882e77\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"Design sequencing is selected for a governed boundary.\"],\"exceptions\":[\"A disposable spike may provide evidence before acceptance without becoming the selected design.\"],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":514,\"path\":\"standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md\",\"quote\":\"Co-evolution is lawful only when `decision_complete(B)` holds:\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md#DESIGN_MODULE%2F5.%20Ontology-first%20design%2FProportional%20design%20sequencing\",\"start_line\":506}],\"statement\":\"Neither co-evolution nor design-gated sequencing is a global default. Proportionality selects material relations and the smallest affected gate; decision completeness tests admissibility. Design, implementation and tests may co-evolve only when decision-complete, with design owning HOW and reconciliation before promotion/closure. Prior acceptance is required before retained implementation would establish unresolved/contradictory relations or choose materially non-equivalent networks with durable consequences. A symbolic contraction's removed code/runtime/test/review/reconciliation space is counterfactual evidence, not an independent gate justification. A prior gate is warranted when semantic ambiguity concerning materially different durable architectures is removed and that contraction justifies reasoning load; it is disproportionate when no materially divergent alternative remains. Record the selected relation and basis in the existing work/design carrier, with no separate artifact required. Design still records and owns HOW before promotion/closure.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:d67aa4f13bf31c5c9fa7ebda2dc51a46","key":1048,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:b8bc7d3a0ac93efb8d5099e60d3dfcad\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:d67aa4f13bf31c5c9fa7ebda2dc51a46\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"Implementation supplies design feedback.\"],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":547,\"path\":\"standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md\",\"quote\":\"Repeated or\\ncross-cutting material surprises are evidence for diagnosis under\\n[ACTIVATION §1 Feedback and diagnosis](ACTIVATION.md#construction-relation),\\nnot a diagnosis.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md#DESIGN_MODULE%2F5.%20Ontology-first%20design%2FProportional%20design%20sequencing\",\"start_line\":538}],\"statement\":\"Implementation can counterexample, falsify constraints or expose ambiguity, but cannot select missing semantic answers, rewrite upstream truth to legalise itself or ratify decisions after establishing them. Newly exposed architectural ambiguity switches the smallest causally closed affected decision set to design-gated sequencing without retroactively invalidating unrelated work. Serial repairs are not acceptance. Repeated/cross-cutting surprises warrant diagnosis, not automatic reframing: a diagnosed underconstrained cut triggers one bounded design_reframe, with retained code provisional until acceptance; where accepted design is decision-complete and only realisation deviates, repair is realization_refactor regardless of recurrence.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:3ebec385c4ce0dde20cd0513d9b60c5e","key":1049,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:b8bc7d3a0ac93efb8d5099e60d3dfcad\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:17af2f81977b5a255c4155d8b1c3abd0\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:3ebec385c4ce0dde20cd0513d9b60c5e\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"Decision completeness or design-gate readiness is assessed.\"],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":600,\"path\":\"standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md\",\"quote\":\"Contradictory projections make the\\ndesign unsatisfiable and block promotion (P1, P5):\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md#DESIGN_MODULE%2F5.%20Ontology-first%20design%2FDecision-complete%20symbolic%20design\",\"start_line\":593}],\"statement\":\"Readiness for retained implementation without a prior gate holds exactly when decision-complete; a gate unable to reach it has not closed. Ontology, Prime contraction, IACS, target design, three views, public contracts, module boundaries, implementation and tests project one network at different reasoning altitudes. Their presence, names, plausibility or mechanical validity do not prove completeness. False decision_complete means underconstrained, including new semantic decisions forced into implementation, projection contradictions or multiple materially non-equivalent networks. Contradictions make design unsatisfiable and block promotion as a gate precondition, not a review-finding disposition. Existing Ontology/algebra/mappings/views may jointly carry the complete network without another document.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:2fc75893782a4078cfb9fcfd17f765d7","key":1050,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:a47b4123e6da5cd417b5ac30e436cd15\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:2fc75893782a4078cfb9fcfd17f765d7\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"A bounded local action affects a material design frame.\"],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":638,\"path\":\"standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md\",\"quote\":\"A result that changes a governing relation re-enters at that\\nrelation before acceptance\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md#DESIGN_MODULE%2F5.%20Ontology-first%20design%2FBounded%20frame%20conservation%20%28UP-017%29\",\"start_line\":632}],\"statement\":\"Declare all five frame items. Evaluate the result against every affected governing frame, preserve every applicable accepted relation and update only affected subordinate projections. Local action conserves governing truth; changed governing relations re-enter their own locus before acceptance. Open a subordinate frame only for a material distinction unresolved at governing altitude. Declared seams make the bounded set testable under ACTIVATION's seam law without a closure algorithm or recursive expansion through irrelevant relations. Local validity does not satisfy the law if any affected governing invariant is violated, duplicated or silently reinterpreted.\",\"uncertainty\":\"The supplied reconstruction clause distinguishes explicitly disposed duplication from unlawful undisposed duplication.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:007fbcac1a8b29af810c5fc56a7a874a","key":1051,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:a47b4123e6da5cd417b5ac30e436cd15\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:fdb10a62e0ecdba0beca462cc9d91a8d\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:e14ea2ce604c9b38027bf09a26544d13\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:007fbcac1a8b29af810c5fc56a7a874a\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"Functionality is discovered.\"],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":655,\"path\":\"standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md\",\"quote\":\"constitutional functionality\\n  -> candidate Ontology\\n  -> logical completeness\\n  -> whole-family Prime contraction\\n  -> accepted Ontology basis\\n  -> Irreducible Architectural Carrier Set\\n  -> target design and domain, sequence and state projections\\n  -> public contract and adapter projections\\n  -> implementation and test projections\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md#DESIGN_MODULE%2F5.%20Ontology-first%20design%2FBounded%20frame%20conservation%20%28UP-017%29\",\"start_line\":647}],\"statement\":\"A discovered verb, screen action, endpoint, command, ticket phrase or use case is behavioural evidence, not an architectural operation. It must not directly become public operation identity, peer carrier, module or implementation function. Preserve the declared order: constitutional functionality → candidate Ontology → logical completeness → whole-family Prime contraction → accepted Ontology basis → IACS → target design and domain/sequence/state projections → public-contract/adapter projections → implementation/test projections.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:4005f6617e3dff3a1f1752f5c7b4871c","key":1052,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:3f7e4abc35ea8e58b3115e97b533309b\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:4005f6617e3dff3a1f1752f5c7b4871c\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"The chosen substrate lacks a required native capability.\"],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":669,\"path\":\"standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md\",\"quote\":\"A missing\\nsubstrate capability remains an explicit design gap or triggers lawful\\nre-entry\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md#DESIGN_MODULE%2F5.%20Ontology-first%20design%2FNative%20constructability%20%28UP-002%29\",\"start_line\":663}],\"statement\":\"Semantic coherence does not make the design acceptable if the substrate cannot natively construct any required identity, relation, transition, authority boundary, effect, lifecycle, composition, publication or retirement behaviour. Keep the missing capability as an explicit design gap or lawful re-entry; reference bridges, adapters, filesystem runners, test doubles and promised features cannot hide it. The consumer chooses substrate and evidence mechanism.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:813326120e26a94cbd79684e35057116","key":1053,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:3f7e4abc35ea8e58b3115e97b533309b\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:813326120e26a94cbd79684e35057116\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"Before constructing a material generic capability, common mechanic or algorithm, selecting a material dependency, or retaining implementation of a newly exposed material generic subproblem.\"],\"exceptions\":[\"No package survey or ledger is required for a trivial helper whose choice cannot materially affect authority, Product behaviour, lifecycle cost or accepted design network.\"],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":789,\"path\":\"standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md\",\"quote\":\"It\\nis mandatory for material algorithms, common mechanics, new dependencies\\nand locally rebuilt foundation capabilities.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md#DESIGN_MODULE%2F5.%20Ontology-first%20design%2FCapability%20and%20foundation%20selection%20%28UP-023%29\",\"start_line\":784}],\"statement\":\"Perform a proportional selection pass under Shared machinery law. First describe capability without Product/domain/module/vendor/file/incumbent labels. Separate irreducible semantic or authority relations, retaining owner, role kind, subject, scope, basis and material lifecycle/refusal invariants, from supporting mechanics/foundations or explicitly assigned roles; factoring concerns relations and roles, not authorship. Evaluate applicable compositions from admitted project foundations; language/runtime/platform/standard library; accepted predecessor or immutable-lineage evidence; maintained external foundations where dependencies are permitted; and bounded local implementation. Re-enter recursively for newly exposed material generic subproblems before retaining them. This prior pass is distinct from post-pattern recurrence review.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:544c12863273b45c8e46f70f8596d30d","key":1054,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:3f7e4abc35ea8e58b3115e97b533309b\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:544c12863273b45c8e46f70f8596d30d\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"A bounded candidate population is discovered.\"],\"exceptions\":[\"An immaterial residual may remain when the record explains why it cannot change the decision.\"],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":712,\"path\":\"standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md\",\"quote\":\"Candidate discovery is bounded, reproducible and explicitly\\nnon-exhaustive.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md#DESIGN_MODULE%2F5.%20Ontology-first%20design%2FCapability%20and%20foundation%20selection%20%28UP-023%29\",\"start_line\":698}],\"statement\":\"For every candidate category record searched sources/collections, cutoff time, relevant version basis, applicability/inclusion criteria, material exclusions, predecessor/incumbent status, discovered candidates and residual unknowns. An unsearched category records reasoned not_applicable or a named gap. Discovery closes only on its declared basis/cutoff. A gap capable of materially altering the frontier prevents selection. A later applicable candidate that could materially alter the lawful frontier invalidates affected selection evidence and re-enters selection as newly acquired material evidence.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:191cdc88ba5b9412b7ae8851036c23f8","key":1055,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:3f7e4abc35ea8e58b3115e97b533309b\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:191cdc88ba5b9412b7ae8851036c23f8\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"Material admitted candidates are compared within the Product boundary and any owner-admitted migration strategy.\"],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":743,\"path\":\"standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md\",\"quote\":\"Unknown evidence\\nremains unknown and cannot be converted into a favourable score. A\\nuniversal scalar is not required.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md#DESIGN_MODULE%2F5.%20Ontology-first%20design%2FCapability%20and%20foundation%20selection%20%28UP-023%29\",\"start_line\":740}],\"statement\":\"Selection does not decide bounded evolution versus fundamental re-adoption or override SPEC_METHOD's rebuttable migration presumption; a working predecessor may constrain the migration candidate set. Discovery may start with incumbents, but selection has no source-order, familiarity, sunk-cost, local-code or dependency-count preference. Compare candidate compositions, not only packages, in one ledger/equivalent record over all decision-changing dimensions: fit/constructability; semantic or operation-authority leakage; adapter/integration/migration/deletion/future-code cost; licence/maintenance/security/upgrade/supply chain; package/runtime/startup/storage/operations cost; determinism/concurrency/failure/recovery/reconstruction/replay; proof/assurance burden; exit/replacement/reversibility. Hard authority, Product-contract, safety, security, licensing or native-constructability failure eliminates the candidate. Unknown remains unknown; no universal scalar is required. Materially incomparable lawful candidates form an explicit undominated frontier.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:8dc39335e5dab83860cb397358733bf5","key":1056,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:3f7e4abc35ea8e58b3115e97b533309b\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:8dc39335e5dab83860cb397358733bf5\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"Candidate dominance or final selection is considered on the current basis.\"],\"exceptions\":[\"A previously dominated candidate may become selectable when new evidence or a material dimension invalidates that dominance relation.\"],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":763,\"path\":\"standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md\",\"quote\":\"A material unknown\\nthat could reverse the relation prevents dominance and remains a gap.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md#DESIGN_MODULE%2F5.%20Ontology-first%20design%2FCapability%20and%20foundation%20selection%20%28UP-023%29\",\"start_line\":748}],\"statement\":\"A lawful composition dominates another only if every material dimension is comparable or evidenced non-discriminating, it is no worse on all comparable dimensions and strictly better on at least one. A potentially reversing material unknown prevents dominance and remains a gap. Dominated candidates cannot be selected; thus a local rebuild dominated by an existing lawful composition is inadmissible. Unused feature breadth alone proves no dominance and may add lifecycle cost. The existing trade-off owner may choose an undominated lawful composition only using declared exact-Product/basis priorities and risk tolerances, recording their resolution of the frontier. Unresolved priorities leave a design gap. Fewest dependencies, smallest edit/line count or richest features are not necessary selection criteria. Each rejected material candidate records decisive evidence or falsifier; unsupported preference is not closure.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:ae45b1528ee29cc61b2611b342cafbf5","key":1057,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:3f7e4abc35ea8e58b3115e97b533309b\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:094d58ecf1ad6d4feccfdf69b1667180\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:ae45b1528ee29cc61b2611b342cafbf5\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"A foundation or local implementation realises a declared relation.\"],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":777,\"path\":\"standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md\",\"quote\":\"Ownership belongs to the declared relation, not necessarily to locally\\nwritten code;\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md#DESIGN_MODULE%2F5.%20Ontology-first%20design%2FCapability%20and%20foundation%20selection%20%28UP-023%29\",\"start_line\":773}],\"statement\":\"Reuse does not automatically confer or transfer semantic, admission or other operation authority. A foundation may realise an explicitly assigned authority-bearing role only with accepted design preserving the relation's owner, role kind, subject, scope, basis and material lifecycle/refusal invariants. Capability, provenance and authorship cannot widen or remint the role. Irreducible Product/domain relations retain their owners across local, reused or composed realisation. Generic local code is lawful only when it wins the same comparison; it is not the default.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:67022075116b5c9cc3db47ddc1fa1883","key":1058,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:c27a10cb8a982f47cef70a74549cb00b\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:e14ea2ce604c9b38027bf09a26544d13\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:67022075116b5c9cc3db47ddc1fa1883\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"An identity-bearing entity or independently governed value family lies in the active boundary.\"],\"exceptions\":[\"Subordinate payloads/value objects inherit owner lifecycle and authority and need no peer row unless they pass the Promotion Test.\"],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":816,\"path\":\"standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md\",\"quote\":\"Every cell identifies a lawful function,\\ndeclares `not_applicable` with a reason, or names a `Gap:` or\\n`Unanswered:` item and owner. Silence is not logical-completeness evidence\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md#DESIGN_MODULE%2F5.%20Ontology-first%20design%2FEntity%20and%20lifecycle%20completeness\",\"start_line\":813}],\"statement\":\"Provide the matrix or an equivalent closed representation for every applicable entity/family. Every cell names a lawful function, reasoned not_applicable, or an owned Gap:/Unanswered: item; silence is insufficient. Create may mean declaration, construction, admission or materialisation. Read should normally be typed projection of authoritative truth; update should normally be admitted transition/new version rather than in-place semantic mutation; delete should normally be retirement, revocation, decommission or supersession where identity/history must remain true.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:e195f7fb2552db96186e1c1b050f29ef","key":1059,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:094d58ecf1ad6d4feccfdf69b1667180\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:e195f7fb2552db96186e1c1b050f29ef\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"An Ontology function or lifecycle transition crosses a semantic, authority, admission, effect, persistence or public boundary.\"],\"exceptions\":[\"Pure subordinate helpers inherit their owning function's authority envelope and need no peer authority row unless they cross a listed boundary.\"],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":844,\"path\":\"standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md\",\"quote\":\"One\\nowner may lawfully occupy more than one role only when the governing\\nauthority explicitly says so; role coincidence is not inferred from\\nimplementation convenience.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md#DESIGN_MODULE%2F5.%20Ontology-first%20design%2FAuthority%20model\",\"start_line\":839}],\"statement\":\"Supply an authority matrix or equivalent closed representation for every such crossing. Distinguish actor/capability from admitted authority, proposal from evaluation/verification/admission/execution/projection/retirement, attribution from permission, and domain meaning from runtime effects. Multiple roles may share an owner only when governing authority explicitly permits it. Composition cannot implicitly widen admitted input/constituent/current-basis authority. Delegation, elevation, transfer and retirement authority require a named typed transition and owning admission boundary carrying, not replacing, the explicit authority decision. Projections create no authority; downstream actor labels, capability strings or payload shape cannot reconstruct an authority witness.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:2873f488cae38fe475feb9f363749732","key":1060,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:d2d50ec064f37926a95bcc1bbbb51190\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:094d58ecf1ad6d4feccfdf69b1667180\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:2873f488cae38fe475feb9f363749732\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"Every consequential entity-transition domain; every material admission relation.\"],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":894,\"path\":\"standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md\",\"quote\":\"- the complete semantic commit unit and its decomposability: every\\n  materially distinct post-validation commit or publication boundary\\n  capable of exposing a subset, or a design-declared dominance or\\n  equivalence proof that named representative observations cover the\\n  complete partial-failure surface;\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md#DESIGN_MODULE%2F5.%20Ontology-first%20design%2FTransformation%20admission%20completeness%20%28UP-016%29\",\"start_line\":888}],\"statement\":\"The who-admits matrix alone is insufficient. Design evidence contains the complete relation and accepted design declares each admission owner/supported boundary; exact admission-valid basis identity, predecessor and currentness continuity through admission, including equal/coherent composite multi-owner basis; complete enclosing relation, participant identities and equality joins; refusal/effect boundaries; complete commit unit and decomposability, covering every distinct post-validation commit/publication boundary exposing a subset or a declared dominance/equivalence proof of representative coverage of the entire partial-failure surface; reconstruction with supported direct/composite/nested forms; and competing-path disposition. Bind ACTIVATION §4 admission and standing-test semantics, which remain owned there; qualification is per owner and supported boundary. Missing or downstream-invented fields/owners/boundaries, inferred basis continuity/partial-failure coverage/proof/reconstruction, or parser/helper/manufactured-refusal non-applicability falsify the obligation.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:99dc0eb8b4e500410422db5677903fcd","key":1061,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:d2d50ec064f37926a95bcc1bbbb51190\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:99dc0eb8b4e500410422db5677903fcd\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"Several paths or projections can affect admission.\"],\"exceptions\":[\"Disjoint authority scopes or entity identities are not a counterexample to singularity.\"],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":937,\"path\":\"standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md\",\"quote\":\"disjoint scopes or identities are not a\\ncounterexample\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md#DESIGN_MODULE%2F5.%20Ontology-first%20design%2FTransformation%20admission%20completeness%20%28UP-016%29\",\"start_line\":932}],\"statement\":\"Every competing path is explicitly related to the singular admission law. Equivalent paths may be constituents, replicas, replacements or deliberately independent realisations; disposition does not itself require deletion. Retaining a superseded responsibility requires a distinct supported purpose, not a label or existing test. A projection may produce a candidate, but every consequential result re-enters admission against its explicit predecessor basis; projection state is not self-authenticating evidence. The law is false when materially non-equivalent admission relations remain reachable for the same transition domain, entity identity, authority scope and predecessor basis; an equivalent competing implementation remains undisposed; or projection-triggered reaction authenticates admission from its own reconstruction.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:52b135c2e5bc6edbd4fbb6840c7c2045","key":1062,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:c568f26576d25f251810727e0b735e24\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:52b135c2e5bc6edbd4fbb6840c7c2045\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"Function derivation is performed; composition-law requirements apply where higher-order behaviour exists.\"],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":974,\"path\":\"standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md\",\"quote\":\"Every\\nretained result is reconciled into accepted design before promotion or\\ndesign-method closure. No private helper, loop, adapter or endpoint may\\nbecome an undeclared constructor\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md#DESIGN_MODULE%2F5.%20Ontology-first%20design%2FAtomic%20functions%20and%20higher-order%20composition\",\"start_line\":971}],\"statement\":\"Derive the smallest parameterised atomic families completing lifecycles. Variation only in entity/projection/transition kind, policy or subordinate payload should normally be a typed parameter or closed variant rather than a peer function. Every functionality row is derived by an admitted atom, derived by declared higher-order composition, deferred with owner/re-entry condition, excluded by current Product authority, or an explicit named unresolved gap. Name the governing composition/effect algebra and applicable identity, closure, associativity, cardinality, effect and authority-conservation laws; do not hide them in controller flow. Iterative discovery of composition/effects/implementation is allowed only under co_evolution_admissible; otherwise only a disposable spike crosses unresolved/contradictory/non-equivalent relations before acceptance. Reconcile every retained result into accepted design before promotion/closure. No private helper, loop, adapter or endpoint becomes an undeclared constructor.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:234e990eec8ef2504c3291a185e64b1e","key":1063,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:6814b648516f3fa537517748d3181520\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:982faaba8542901a360f970f115eecef\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:234e990eec8ef2504c3291a185e64b1e\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"A Prime atom or its realisation is proposed or used.\"],\"exceptions\":[\"An out-of-domain case may justify proposing another candidate atom for design admission.\"],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1002,\"path\":\"standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md\",\"quote\":\"An atom without a declared admitted domain remains a candidate\\natom; it cannot supply Prime acceptance or Prime-conformance to a\\nrealisation projection.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md#DESIGN_MODULE%2F5.%20Ontology-first%20design%2FPrime%20semantic%20atoms%20and%20admitted%20domain\",\"start_line\":1000}],\"statement\":\"Every accepted atom declares its admitted domain and governs every admitted instance within it. Later use composes/parameterises it, never locally forks, shadows, specialises or reinterprets it. An in-domain counterexample falsifies the shared atom and re-enters its design boundary, not feature-local replacement. An undeclared domain leaves the atom a candidate unable to supply Prime acceptance/conformance. One atom may project into several units and a unit may implement several atoms only with explicit mapping and no rival meaning/authority. Atomic-function Prime is not established until the complete candidate family is contracted.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:6d7bca73ffdf581232cbf35ad43e9fd8","key":1064,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:6814b648516f3fa537517748d3181520\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:982faaba8542901a360f970f115eecef\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:6d7bca73ffdf581232cbf35ad43e9fd8\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"Before promotion and whenever whole-family Prime is claimed.\"],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1030,\"path\":\"standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md\",\"quote\":\"A function-and-carrier-only pass does not\\nestablish whole-family Prime\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md#DESIGN_MODULE%2F5.%20Ontology-first%20design%2FWhole-family%20Prime%20contraction\",\"start_line\":1010}],\"statement\":\"Review every proposed identity, authority transition, lifecycle relation, topology, function, composition law, effect and closure law plus every realisation projection, not isolated atoms or only functions/carriers. Ask whether operations are typed parameters of one function, commands transitions of one entity, reads projections of one truth, implementations applications of one higher-order function; whether independent identity, authority, effect, lifecycle, reuse or public pattern-match semantics are introduced; whether all atom kinds entered contraction; whether every unit maps to accepted atoms; and whether any projection introduces/duplicates/reinterprets meaning or authority. Individually plausible functions are not Prime if one parameterised template plus closed variants carries identical meaning/authority. Contract visible recurrence during design; later recurrence review is no substitute.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:2c2c93d571e467b2ba56aea739edebc5","key":1065,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:6814b648516f3fa537517748d3181520\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:982faaba8542901a360f970f115eecef\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:2c2c93d571e467b2ba56aea739edebc5\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"Prime contraction occurs at a material semantic boundary.\"],\"exceptions\":[\"Work inside an accepted boundary cites the existing Prime basis rather than recreating it.\"],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1051,\"path\":\"standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md\",\"quote\":\"Contraction preserves root authority and every retained semantic relation.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md#DESIGN_MODULE%2F5.%20Ontology-first%20design%2FRecursive%20Prime%20and%20root%20conservation%20%28UP-003%29\",\"start_line\":1041}],\"statement\":\"Contract each candidate atom, then the whole resulting family. Local irreducibility or unit conformance does not prove global Prime if the family duplicates identity, authority, function, lifecycle, topology, effect or projection meaning. Preserve root authority and every retained semantic relation; fewer files/functions/operations/authoring surfaces cannot compensate for a new authority source/truth path. Evidence names the complete family; each stable identity, irreducible relation, admitted domain and falsification condition; whole-family contraction relation; before/after retained meaning and authority; accepted loss; and an explicit total map from every proposed projection to accepted atoms.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:2d796ed3d20c28db806d93b131d45ae1","key":1066,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:982faaba8542901a360f970f115eecef\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:fdb10a62e0ecdba0beca462cc9d91a8d\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:2d796ed3d20c28db806d93b131d45ae1\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"A design or implementation projection is produced.\"],\"exceptions\":[\"Implementation branches and test expectations need not each be enumerated by the Ontology, but must preserve it and trace through requirements plus accepted design.\"],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1077,\"path\":\"standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md\",\"quote\":\"Any intentional omission or flattening declares accepted loss and a\\nfailure condition\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md#DESIGN_MODULE%2F5.%20Ontology-first%20design%2FOntology%20projection\",\"start_line\":1066}],\"statement\":\"Each design projection identifies its Ontology source and preserved identity, relationship, lifecycle, authority, function or effect law. Intentional omissions/flattening declare accepted loss and a failure condition. Target design may add structural HOW but no rival semantics; implementation/tests trace through accepted design, never bypassing it. A public operation, sequence message, state transition, carrier or effect without trace through accepted design to accepted Ontology is ungrounded and cannot enter the active Product line.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:f8aacb2f5e9c9690fffc034ecc49ad9b","key":1067,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:6814b648516f3fa537517748d3181520\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:e14ea2ce604c9b38027bf09a26544d13\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:982faaba8542901a360f970f115eecef\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:f8aacb2f5e9c9690fffc034ecc49ad9b\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"Top-level realisation units are proposed.\"],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1129,\"path\":\"standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md\",\"quote\":\"Typed\\nclosure by itself is not sufficient reason to create a new top-level type.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md#DESIGN_MODULE%2F6.%20Prime%20law\",\"start_line\":1089}],\"statement\":\"Derive Prime atoms from logically complete candidate Ontology before proposing top-level units; whole-family evidence supports Ontology acceptance, and target design/IACS/modules/functions/schemas/tests project rather than originate accepted Prime meaning. Prime conformance applies to functions, classes, carriers, top-level schema records and modules. A unit is conformant only when projecting accepted atoms without adding, duplicating or reinterpreting semantic authority; topological/effect boundaries first need accepted atoms. Size and one-to-one atom correspondence are immaterial. Typical lawful grounds include new admitted-graph topology/branch, typed transformation, effect, validation/admission or projection boundary. Units solely shortening call sites without new semantics, aggregating unrelated behaviour, renaming old interfaces, wrapping data, hiding mutation/fallback/orchestration, naming non-authoritative payload variation, exposing internal detail, cosmetically mirroring carriers or multiplying types for typing discomfort are nonconformant. Prefer composition, existing lawful functions and fewer sharper boundaries/carrier families; line-count minimisation is not the aim.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:67026d03483e36b851f7202e1f1377d8","key":1068,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:6814b648516f3fa537517748d3181520\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:982faaba8542901a360f970f115eecef\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:67026d03483e36b851f7202e1f1377d8\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"Prime contraction and its governance cost are assessed.\"],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1143,\"path\":\"standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md\",\"quote\":\"contraction is not\\nsuccessful when it increases authority centres, maintained truth surfaces,\\nacceptance boundaries, dependency cycles, manually reconciled projections\\nor review burden.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md#DESIGN_MODULE%2F6.%20Prime%20law%2FBoundary%20and%20governance%20cost%20%28UP-005%29\",\"start_line\":1139}],\"statement\":\"Apply ACTIVATION proportionality to ambiguity removed versus reasoning complexity. Review cuts, realisation units, runtime modules and work items are distinct and may map many-to-one/one-to-many; administrative convenience does not force one-to-one decomposition. Contraction is not successful if authority centres, maintained truth surfaces, acceptance boundaries, dependency cycles, manual projection reconciliation or review burden increase. Evidence stays proportional to semantic change/risk; no artifact or review per concern is required.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:b024c556ee1ddae30e71b34641db0f54","key":1069,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:e14ea2ce604c9b38027bf09a26544d13\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:fdb10a62e0ecdba0beca462cc9d91a8d\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:b024c556ee1ddae30e71b34641db0f54\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"A schema, carrier family or typed public boundary is defined.\"],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1190,\"path\":\"standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md\",\"quote\":\"If the accepted Ontology\\nor IACS has not been declared, the schema is not yet design-method\\ncomplete under this profile.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md#DESIGN_MODULE%2F6.%20Prime%20law%2FIrreducible%20architectural%20carrier%20set\",\"start_line\":1179}],\"statement\":\"Derive IACS from accepted Ontology before naming subordinate payloads or implementation modules; it should precede helper result shapes/internal branch details. Cite accepted Ontology and function-derivation evidence; declare IACS; map every carrier to identity/lifecycle/function/authority/effect/projection law; distinguish authoritative from downstream; default all other shapes to subordinate/private unless promoted; reconcile typed implementation before closure. Carrier role examples do not justify branch-specific payload, persistence detail, read-model row or typing-only grouping as top-level. IACS is an Ontology projection, never its replacement or the first origin of semantic meaning. Absence of declared accepted Ontology or IACS prevents schema design-method completeness. Under co-evolution, evidence/code/tests may develop together but implementation cannot self-ratify discoveries; Ontology/IACS acceptance and reconciliation precede promotion/closure. Otherwise accept the affected unresolved/contradictory/non-equivalent relation before retained implementation establishes it.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:0feabdfe800fe6dd18c398e129f51e3c","key":1070,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:e14ea2ce604c9b38027bf09a26544d13\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:0feabdfe800fe6dd18c398e129f51e3c\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"A carrier is added, removed, merged or split.\"],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1213,\"path\":\"standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md\",\"quote\":\"The IACS is not numerically frozen.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md#DESIGN_MODULE%2F6.%20Prime%20law%2FIACS%20revision\",\"start_line\":1194}],\"statement\":\"Revision is lawful through accepted Ontology/design re-entry. Re-derive the whole IACS and classify every addition/removal/merge/split; rerun Promotion Test and Boundary Inflation checks over the full set; update every conformance/checker subject to the declared composite relation under EVALUATION's assurance-boundary congruence and freeze/revision law; reconcile implementation before promotion/closure. A prohibition without a lawful revision path is false. Revision is false if gates cover only new carriers, assurance retains weaker/obsolete subjects or reconciliation is absent before closure.\",\"uncertainty\":\"The external assurance-boundary congruence and freeze/revision law is referenced, not reproduced.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:952ca44d3b0bf010f21bfb5d7e6bbce9","key":1071,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:e14ea2ce604c9b38027bf09a26544d13\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:952ca44d3b0bf010f21bfb5d7e6bbce9\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"A subordinate payload is proposed as a top-level class, dataclass, TypedDict, enum or named schema record.\"],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1236,\"path\":\"standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md\",\"quote\":\"The burden of proof is on\\npromotion; designers and reviewers should assume a candidate type stays\\nsubordinate until an irreducible boundary is shown\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md#DESIGN_MODULE%2F6.%20Prime%20law%2FPromotion%20test\",\"start_line\":1234}],\"statement\":\"Justify an architectural boundary, not payload detail. Promotion is allowed only if at least one holds: authoritative source carrier; public/persisted contract; explicit public-outcome variant directly pattern-matched by consumers; reuse across several modules without semantic bleed; independent versioning/publication/admission. Promotion is unlawful for mere larger-carrier detail, one-use local field grouping, open-dictionary typing shim, private variation crossing no true interface, or cosmetic/local mirror. Without independent authority, independent reuse or direct pattern-match semantics, remain nested/private/local. Proof burden rests on promotion; designers/reviewers should presume subordination until irreducible need is shown. These grounds do not waive other Prime/IACS requirements.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:16d93bc7cbbcb3fb62b14c8de1c0c7f5","key":1072,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:e14ea2ce604c9b38027bf09a26544d13\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:16d93bc7cbbcb3fb62b14c8de1c0c7f5\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"Schema work or a schema/ticket's wide type family is considered.\"],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1256,\"path\":\"standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md\",\"quote\":\"Typed closure does not excuse Boundary\\nInflation.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md#DESIGN_MODULE%2F6.%20Prime%20law%2FBoundary%20inflation%20prohibition\",\"start_line\":1247}],\"statement\":\"Declare IACS, authoritative types, downstream projections, subordinate shapes and intentionally deferred promotions; a wide type inventory must distinguish IACS from subordinate payloads or it is design drift. Inflation is design debt, not progress: typing difficulty promotes payload peers, internal records become public without a new authoritative boundary, near-identical peers replace a sufficient single family, or one migration silently becomes parallel schema migrations. Typed closure supplies no excuse.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:52966e193d698210a9ee0d3617cbff74","key":1073,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:d64c3fd67483b1082f3765ec22d6a46f\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:fdb10a62e0ecdba0beca462cc9d91a8d\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:e14ea2ce604c9b38027bf09a26544d13\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:c19d38e4362efe35b2f5323c54192a62\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:52966e193d698210a9ee0d3617cbff74\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"A module boundary is reference-derived.\"],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1284,\"path\":\"standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md\",\"quote\":\"If a target realisation cannot show that derivation chain, it is not yet\\ndesign-method complete under this profile\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md#DESIGN_MODULE%2F6.%20Prime%20law%2FReference-derived%20module%20design\",\"start_line\":1283}],\"statement\":\"Name reference design surfaces; provide accepted target Ontology with disposition of reference entities/functions/lifecycle/authority/effects/projections; target design surfaces replacing/binding them; explicit preserved/reshaped/deferred/delivery-binding-demoted mapping; and target module assets including Ontology-derived IACS and three views. Demonstrate how the target boundary derives from reference design without importing incidental drift, delivery quirks, helper sprawl or accidental authority. Code comparison alone or an absent chain prevents design-method completeness.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:a1b8dbe93a865a2884956bcfab4d85b7","key":1074,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:c19d38e4362efe35b2f5323c54192a62\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:17af2f81977b5a255c4155d8b1c3abd0\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:a1b8dbe93a865a2884956bcfab4d85b7\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"A new or materially changed semantic or typed module boundary is promoted or claims design-method closure.\"],\"exceptions\":[\"Unchanged boundaries cite their accepted basis; local work with no material semantic-boundary delta does not recreate the gate.\"],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1309,\"path\":\"standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md\",\"quote\":\"Every new or materially changed semantic or typed module boundary carries\\none accepted Ontology and one complete three-view Mermaid design asset\\nbefore the boundary is promoted or claims design-method closure\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md#DESIGN_MODULE%2F7.%20Ontology%20and%20three-view%20design%20gate\",\"start_line\":1288}],\"statement\":\"Carry one accepted Ontology and the complete three-view asset before promotion/closure. Co-evolution may precede the gate only while its predicate holds; otherwise accept affected unresolved/contradictory/non-equivalent relations before retained implementation establishes them. All three views are required; a broad flowchart is no substitute. They are fidelity-checked projections, not decorative peers or independent truth surfaces.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:756a984e940b25cc22045cf9adc9e67a","key":1075,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:fdb10a62e0ecdba0beca462cc9d91a8d\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:c19d38e4362efe35b2f5323c54192a62\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:756a984e940b25cc22045cf9adc9e67a\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"A design asset covers an active boundary.\"],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1326,\"path\":\"standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md\",\"quote\":\"The design asset cites one accepted Ontology for the active boundary and\\nincludes or references its\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md#DESIGN_MODULE%2F7.%20Ontology%20and%20three-view%20design%20gate%2FOntology%20evidence\",\"start_line\":1313}],\"statement\":\"Include or reference entity/relationship inventory, invariant/cardinality law, lifecycle-completeness matrix, authority matrix, atomic/higher-order derivation matrix, applicable composition/effect algebra, whole-family Prime contraction with every accepted atom's domain and projection mapping, and explicit deferred/excluded/unresolved functionality. A boundary-bounded slice may derive from a wider accepted Product Ontology only with a parent citation and preservation of parent identity/relationship/lifecycle/authority/function law. Copying selected rows into an ungrounded local model creates a rival truth surface.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:7e4c0a078b9db1e70c8e37aa82c5bba7","key":1076,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:770fcc5357db9571656e4e89a8719021\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:a47b4123e6da5cd417b5ac30e436cd15\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:7e4c0a078b9db1e70c8e37aa82c5bba7\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"A declared bounded action and accepted material-frame basis are considered.\"],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1398,\"path\":\"standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md\",\"quote\":\"Sufficiency is bound to a declared action and its affected set; it is\\nnot a claim over an unbounded space of possible future changes, and the\\nperformance of any particular reviewer is not evidence either way\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md#DESIGN_MODULE%2F7.%20Ontology%20and%20three-view%20design%20gate%2FInvariant%20reconstruction%20sufficiency%20%28UP-018%29\",\"start_line\":1362}],\"statement\":\"Selected method basis plus accepted design must expose every governing relation in the causally closed affected set and support preserve/change/duplicate/violate decisions without dialogue, commentary, prior-worker memory or implementation folklore. Restating method decision law in design duplicates local method rather than satisfying the requirement. Sufficiency concerns the declared action/set, not all future changes or reviewer performance. Existing Ontology evidence, authority/admission/frame declarations, views and module mappings carry this durable reasoning state; no new package/artifact is required. Missing governing relations or inability to decide from the two inputs alone falsify sufficiency. If tested, use named cases with known governing relations/expected decisions and withhold conversational/folk-memory aids.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:77179ca186e4b0bebfdd68fc9add4fd2","key":1077,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:770fcc5357db9571656e4e89a8719021\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:77179ca186e4b0bebfdd68fc9add4fd2\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"An action is evaluated against one governing relation for admissibility in the acting frame on the current governing basis.\"],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1355,\"path\":\"standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md\",\"quote\":\"| preserves | leaves the relation intact and operates inside it | `satisfied` |\\n| changes | alters the relation itself, and therefore re-enters at that relation before acceptance | `invalid_basis` |\\n| duplicates | establishes an equivalent path that is explicitly disposed as a constituent, replica, replacement or deliberately independent realisation | `satisfied` |\\n| violates | contradicts the relation, or establishes an equivalent path that is left undisposed | `falsified` |\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md#DESIGN_MODULE%2F7.%20Ontology%20and%20three-view%20design%20gate%2FInvariant%20reconstruction%20sufficiency%20%28UP-018%29\",\"start_line\":1352}],\"statement\":\"Preserves leaves accepted relation intact and maps to satisfied. Changes alters the relation and requires re-entry at its locus before acceptance, mapping to invalid_basis. Duplicates is an equivalent path explicitly disposed as constituent/replica/replacement/deliberately independent realisation, mapping to satisfied. Violates contradicts or leaves an equivalent path undisposed, mapping to falsified. A change accepted in the acting frame instead of its owning locus is a violation regardless of delta size; disposition, not equivalence alone, separates lawful duplication from violation. Preserve the predicate, decision and core value together. If none of the four is reached, return the cause-selected core value, including indeterminate for insufficient admissible evidence and what would decide it. If the method/design pair itself is insufficient, that case falsifies the sufficiency law. A lawful re-entry change is neither an acting-frame acceptance nor a violation; a violation is not re-entry.\",\"uncertainty\":\"Other cause-to-core mappings are owned by the referenced result algebra.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:0df0c8fbeeca13749b3cdf1251414aa5","key":1078,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:9809bdb58b2f5e183372e40c53f99694\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:0df0c8fbeeca13749b3cdf1251414aa5\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"The domain view describes the active boundary.\"],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1412,\"path\":\"standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md\",\"quote\":\"IACS carriers and their Prime-atom projection\\nmappings; subordinate payloads; effect-edge-only payloads; downstream-only\\nprojections; deferred families outside the active slice; authoritative\\nversus downstream role; public versus module-local visibility; and\\ncomposition, containment, association and real variant-family structure.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md#DESIGN_MODULE%2F7.%20Ontology%20and%20three-view%20design%20gate%2FDomain%20model\",\"start_line\":1408}],\"statement\":\"Show domain identities/cardinalities rather than helper decomposition; ownership, invariants and lawful lifecycle relations; atomic families with crossing entity inputs/outputs; higher-order relations where they determine boundary shape; IACS/Prime mappings, subordinate and edge-only payloads, downstream-only projections and deferred out-of-slice families; authority/downstream roles, visibility, composition, containment, association and actual variants. Use the declared stereotype, visibility and relationship meanings.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:dcb6403868ce2165b137e83e259568ba","key":1079,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:b88eeaaa5be3aa8b3a9cb5bb26849eb0\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:9809bdb58b2f5e183372e40c53f99694\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:094d58ecf1ad6d4feccfdf69b1667180\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:dcb6403868ce2165b137e83e259568ba\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"The sequence view describes supported execution.\"],\"exceptions\":[\"A participant absent from the domain model is permitted only as an explicitly external actor.\"],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1437,\"path\":\"standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md\",\"quote\":\"Every\\nmessage also binds to an Ontology function and its admitted authority\\nrole; actor identity or call reachability alone does not authorise a\\nmessage\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md#DESIGN_MODULE%2F7.%20Ontology%20and%20three-view%20design%20gate%2FSequence%20model\",\"start_line\":1434}],\"statement\":\"Show admitted input to result/truthful stop and owner/required authority for every decision, admission, execution, projection and effect boundary. Where applicable show malformed input/output, retry, recursion, fan-out/fan-in, nested workflow and human escalation. Every participant is in the domain model or explicitly external. Every message binds to a declared carrier transform, graph/computation constructor, interpreter action or effect handler and also to an Ontology function/admitted authority role. No private loop, service method, plugin, shell or script silently substitutes for a workflow transition. Identity and reachability alone authorise nothing.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:e946efc34554a4a7466f884869678be2","key":1080,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:7f39de5452d3ee7ee736cf3e653ad621\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:e946efc34554a4a7466f884869678be2\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"The state view describes an active boundary.\"],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1448,\"path\":\"standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md\",\"quote\":\"Controller-local memory is not a lawful source of lifecycle truth when the\\nproduct declares replay, event, graph or carrier ownership\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md#DESIGN_MODULE%2F7.%20Ontology%20and%20three-view%20design%20gate%2FState%20model\",\"start_line\":1447}],\"statement\":\"Show the complete admitted lifecycle and all producible refusal/blocked/continuation/retry/escalation/terminal states. Every transition binds to an Ontology function and names its owning authority, admission, compiler, interpreter, event, projection or external act. Where Product declares replay/event/graph/carrier ownership, controller-local memory cannot be lifecycle truth.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:b3edab6c836a19d0a7e8ead6cccc099f","key":1081,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:b8eaf98796f24eef0b1f5239adcc90a4\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:c19d38e4362efe35b2f5323c54192a62\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:b3edab6c836a19d0a7e8ead6cccc099f\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"Cross-view evaluation is performed for the active boundary.\"],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1479,\"path\":\"standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md\",\"quote\":\"A\\nrelied-on `semantic_not_realized` constructor is a blocking gap; it may\\nnot be replaced by imperative glue in a plugin, shell, service, script or\\ntest harness\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md#DESIGN_MODULE%2F7.%20Ontology%20and%20three-view%20design%20gate%2FCross-view%20axiom%20evaluation\",\"start_line\":1476}],\"statement\":\"Evaluate every applicable Product, graph, language, runtime, handler and module axiom. Establish every view element's accepted-Ontology derivation; every functionality row's derived/deferred/excluded/gap disposition; domain existence of sequence participants and lifecycle carriers; declared semantic/effect boundaries for messages; admitted-truth derivation of transitions; explicit function/transition authority with no compositional widening; public operations as Ontology-function projections; no direct transition of raw probabilistic output to accepted/closed; handlers/plugins owning interiors only while runtime owns admission/events/continuation/closure; native types enforcing locally decidable relations; admission/semantic compilation owning global references/completeness/realisation gaps. For graph-native work, all batch/retry/recursion/nesting is visible in declared graph/compute algebra. A relied-on semantic_not_realized constructor blocks and cannot be replaced with imperative plugin/shell/service/script/test-harness glue.\",\"uncertainty\":\"The cross-view requirement that every participant be in the domain model is read together with the sequence clause's explicit external-actor exception.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:fc5ef9691cfed84bc643e603274c7120","key":1082,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:b8eaf98796f24eef0b1f5239adcc90a4\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:fc5ef9691cfed84bc643e603274c7120\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"One axiom is assessed on the exact Ontology/design basis.\"],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1501,\"path\":\"standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md\",\"quote\":\"| `pass` | the cited Ontology, view and enforcement evidence establishes that the design meets the axiom | `satisfied` |\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md#DESIGN_MODULE%2F7.%20Ontology%20and%20three-view%20design%20gate%2FCross-view%20axiom%20evaluation\",\"start_line\":1499},{\"end_line\":1516,\"path\":\"standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md\",\"quote\":\"an undecided or unevaluated\\naxiom is never read as a pass or a fail\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md#DESIGN_MODULE%2F7.%20Ontology%20and%20three-view%20design%20gate%2FCross-view%20axiom%20evaluation\",\"start_line\":1515}],\"statement\":\"For the exact-basis disjunction 'meets axiom OR axiom does not apply', pass maps to satisfied when cited Ontology/view/enforcement evidence establishes compliance. not_applicable maps to satisfied only when applicability is false on basis-bound facts, with a reason naming those facts and the excluding scope authority; it satisfies only the disjunction, never 'meets axiom'. An unresolved premise supports no not_applicable. fail maps to falsified only for an applicable axiom with a cited violating element/message/transition/authority path/enforcement counterexample. Record verdict and value together. If no refined verdict is reached, record cause-selected core value and what would decide: indeterminate for insufficient admissible evidence, including unresolved applicability with unmet axiom; out_of_frame for undeclared relation/evaluator capability; invalid_basis for unsupported Ontology/design basis. Unevaluated applicable axioms have no result. None of these is pass; exclusion is neither conformance nor failure, and undecided/unevaluated is neither pass nor fail.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:718e49a17ecda0c8f9633d2d5476674d","key":1083,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:17af2f81977b5a255c4155d8b1c3abd0\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:b8eaf98796f24eef0b1f5239adcc90a4\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:b8bc7d3a0ac93efb8d5099e60d3dfcad\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:718e49a17ecda0c8f9633d2d5476674d\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"A new or semantically changed boundary seeks promotion, publication or design-method closure.\"],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1554,\"path\":\"standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md\",\"quote\":\"a matrix in which every applicable axiom is\\n`pass` is evidence for the design authority, never the verdict, and a\\nstep that produced the pack establishes neither.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md#DESIGN_MODULE%2F7.%20Ontology%20and%20three-view%20design%20gate%2FGate%20and%20retrospective%20work\",\"start_line\":1543}],\"statement\":\"Both Ontology and design verdicts must be accepted before affected implementation/public contract/semantic carrier promotion or closure. A failed applicable axiom, missing functionality disposition, unresolved authority or blocking realisation gap keeps non-accepted. Acceptance consumes availability, decision-completeness assessment, axiom verdicts and cross-view proofs, and remains distinct from all of them. Passing matrices are evidence, never acceptance; pack production establishes neither assessment nor acceptance. Any non-satisfied axiom result, applicable axiom without result, or resultless axiom whose applicability is not established false keeps non-accepted: mandatory non-satisfied results/gaps cannot combine to satisfied. An absent Ontology, view, cross-view evaluation or either accepted verdict means not design-method complete and prevents promotion/publication/closure.\",\"uncertainty\":\"The other three acceptance dispositions and their mappings are referenced but not supplied.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:e8ada94da7eb2bcea0b90496d20adbac","key":1084,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:17af2f81977b5a255c4155d8b1c3abd0\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:b8bc7d3a0ac93efb8d5099e60d3dfcad\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:c19d38e4362efe35b2f5323c54192a62\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:e8ada94da7eb2bcea0b90496d20adbac\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"Co-evolving, unchanged-refactor or retrospective work is considered.\"],\"exceptions\":[\"An unchanged realization_refactor reuses the existing verdict on a no-delta proof.\"],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1588,\"path\":\"standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md\",\"quote\":\"Until the design gate is accepted it is provisional evidence: it does not\\nauthor semantic truth, earn publication authority, or satisfy promotion or\\nclosure.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md#DESIGN_MODULE%2F7.%20Ontology%20and%20three-view%20design%20gate%2FGate%20and%20retrospective%20work\",\"start_line\":1565}],\"statement\":\"For an unchanged realization_refactor, cite accepted Ontology/design basis, identify touched projections and prove no entity/relationship/lifecycle/authority/function/effect/public-semantics delta; reuse the verdict without new Ontology or acceptance ceremony. Under co_evolution_admissible, implementation may precede/develop with evidence and be retained after reconciliation, but remains provisional until acceptance and grants no semantics/publication/promotion/closure authority. Otherwise only disposable spikes cross unresolved/contradictory/non-equivalent relations before acceptance. Retrospective code may inform design; newly discovered material ambiguity/contradiction/non-equivalence falsifies decision completeness and activates the affected decision's gate. Promotion/closure wait for accepted Ontology, three views and evaluation. Evaluate code against prior authority, never rewrite design merely to rationalise unlawful shape. Keep assets boundary-bounded; unrelated bootstrap, test-harness, projection or delivery shapes added merely for apparent completeness are defects. Provisional work may continue only while co-evolution remains admissible.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:6864ea383512c4ce64c21e80b00f35a2","key":1085,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:1ffb0d473667cbcd448ccf239b30f413\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:6864ea383512c4ce64c21e80b00f35a2\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"A material realisation component is composed or used.\"],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1613,\"path\":\"standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md\",\"quote\":\"Use of a\\ncomponent outside its declared role set does not silently establish\\nidentity, admission, lifecycle, ordering, closure or projection truth\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md#DESIGN_MODULE%2F7.%20Ontology%20and%20three-view%20design%20gate%2FComputational%20realisation%20projection%20%28UP-019%29\",\"start_line\":1610}],\"statement\":\"Every material component declares its semantic and operational role set. Where a role bears authority, composition and use preserve its applicable IDENTITY §6 authority relation; that section supports rather than owns the role model. New operational responsibility and new semantic or authoritative roles are design changes requiring re-entry; behaviour already within an abstract declared role is ordinary variation. Out-of-role use establishes none of identity, admission, lifecycle, ordering, closure or projection truth.\",\"uncertainty\":\"The referenced authority relation is not fully supplied.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:1413d6b4bed3f4cfa7e2226694225411","key":1086,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:8e5e05d12a032d36a117b5f56176885c\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:1413d6b4bed3f4cfa7e2226694225411\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"At a material semantic boundary.\",\"For material producer-to-consumer paths and material algorithmic work.\"],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1628,\"path\":\"standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md\",\"quote\":\"Component-local success cannot establish the complete-path\\nclaim, and different names do not establish different computational\\nresponsibilities\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md#DESIGN_MODULE%2F7.%20Ontology%20and%20three-view%20design%20gate%2FComputational%20realisation%20projection%20%28UP-019%29\",\"start_line\":1626},{\"end_line\":1637,\"path\":\"standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md\",\"quote\":\"Bind\\nany acceptance limits and their owning authority before qualification;\\nlimits and workloads are Product-owned, not universal method constants.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md#DESIGN_MODULE%2F7.%20Ontology%20and%20three-view%20design%20gate%2FComputational%20realisation%20projection%20%28UP-019%29\",\"start_line\":1635}],\"statement\":\"Project the domain into its computational realisation and extend cross-view evaluation to prove they describe one system. Identify fact establishment, consuming operations, applicable basis and invalidators, effect boundaries, retained alternatives and accumulated work using ACTIVATION §§4 and 7; include method and assurance operations where material. Declare supported input dimensions, workload, growth and assumptions needed for the selected outcome; distinguish material startup, framework, external-computation, transport and assurance costs under ACTIVATION §6. Bind any acceptance limits and owner before qualification, challenge assumptions on representative supported paths and material growth, and observe work directly when elapsed time cannot locate it without repeating operations merely to count them. Existing design/proof surfaces suffice; no additional accounting system or fixed complexity is required. Local success and differing names cannot establish whole-path success or different computational responsibilities.\",\"uncertainty\":\"The referenced enclosing-relation, reuse and cost laws are not fully supplied.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:c0ad4a9cf9b78c5ee491576932d66d44","key":1087,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:8e5e05d12a032d36a117b5f56176885c\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:efb9ff5d3635a7b82d3288c918fc04d1\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:c0ad4a9cf9b78c5ee491576932d66d44\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"Computational similarity or a material algorithmic obligation in M(B) is present.\"],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1663,\"path\":\"standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md\",\"quote\":\"A materially non-equivalent law among\\nthose dimensions requires separation. Other differences justify separation\\nonly when evaluation shows that parameterisation or adaptation would\\nweaken ownership, authority, lifecycle, failure or operational\\nconstraints.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md#DESIGN_MODULE%2F7.%20Ontology%20and%20three-view%20design%20gate%2FComputational%20realisation%20projection%20%28UP-019%29\",\"start_line\":1658},{\"end_line\":1682,\"path\":\"standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md\",\"quote\":\"or a local realisation presents an existing accepted\\nrelation as newly owned local truth.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md#DESIGN_MODULE%2F7.%20Ontology%20and%20three-view%20design%20gate%2FComputational%20realisation%20projection%20%28UP-019%29\",\"start_line\":1681}],\"statement\":\"The subordinate projection cannot decide semantic identity, ownership or authority. Similarity yields a commonisation candidate, followed by semantic and operational equivalence evaluation, then reuse, a parameterised common relation or justified separation. Material non-equivalence in identity/key law, ownership, ordering, admissible mutation, consistency/concurrency, retention, failure, access policy, lifecycle or authority over truth requires separation; other differences justify it only if parameterisation/adaptation would weaken ownership, authority, lifecycle, failure or operational constraints. A difference alone does not discharge Prime contraction or recurrence review. Each material obligation in M(B) has both a semantic disposition (existing accepted relation, extension, new candidate relation) and realisation disposition (consume, implement locally, optimise, adapt, deliberately duplicate under stated non-semantic constraints). The law is falsified by materially equivalent domain-named implementations without semantic disposition, generic machinery becoming semantic authority, superficial commonisation despite incompatible identity/ordering/failure/ownership/lifecycle law, or local realisation presenting accepted relations as newly owned truth.\",\"uncertainty\":\"M(B) and the full Prime law are referenced but not defined in the supplied section.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:3765143e2625581e8b67a637c1cda9fd","key":1088,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:bb53ea665dafe38a1f8718f3b042739a\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:a46e77f57dce5d3691cc4fbe307267d5\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:3765143e2625581e8b67a637c1cda9fd\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1713,\"path\":\"standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md\",\"quote\":\"This is a theoretical justification, not an extra prerequisite. The rules\\nof this profile remain engineering law even where the Markov-object\\nconstruct is irrelevant, unavailable or still only candidate-class\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md#DESIGN_MODULE%2F8.%20Theoretical%20framing\",\"start_line\":1709}],\"statement\":\"The framing is optional theoretical justification, adds no prerequisite and expands no profile scope. The source's engineering rules remain applicable even when the Markov-object construct is irrelevant, unavailable or candidate-class.\",\"uncertainty\":\"No empirical or metaphysical validity of the framing is asserted.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:2da4e83034810764ae2685c55dc4f3cc","key":1089,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:d0ef4997ddb9eeaa35eecc22a937ba5e\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:2da4e83034810764ae2685c55dc4f3cc\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"This profile governs a realisation boundary.\"],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1719,\"path\":\"standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md\",\"quote\":\"modules should be\\nclassified by role (P0, P6). Recommended\\nroles are:\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md#DESIGN_MODULE%2F9.%20Module%20taxonomy\",\"start_line\":1717},{\"end_line\":1754,\"path\":\"standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md\",\"quote\":\"for a boundary this\\nprofile governs they read through the binding declared at the head of this\\nmember\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md#DESIGN_MODULE%2F9.%20Module%20taxonomy\",\"start_line\":1752}],\"statement\":\"Modules should be classified by role; the listed roles are recommendations. Design-to-module evidence, module-derived unit tests and module lifecycle confirmation remain ASSURANCE §§14–16 law, read through the member-head binding for a governed boundary.\",\"uncertainty\":\"ASSURANCE §§14–16 and the member-head binding are outside the supplied source.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:cc17887fb1919e5ec9783909dd017d3b","key":1090,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:bb53ea665dafe38a1f8718f3b042739a\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:7243c6a09744b0df33d05cde1696eb08\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:656e135dc87d3a38444515f4547a5002\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:cc17887fb1919e5ec9783909dd017d3b\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"A project uses the profile.\"],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1761,\"path\":\"standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md\",\"quote\":\"Projects using this profile prefer one algebraic primitive plus\\nprojections over several local decision systems, and prefer total\\nfunctions, closed enums, explicit state and deterministic folds\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md#DESIGN_MODULE%2F10.%20Realisation%20rules\",\"start_line\":1758}],\"statement\":\"Prefer one algebraic primitive with projections over several local decision systems, and prefer total functions, closed enums, explicit state and deterministic folds.\",\"uncertainty\":\"These are preferences, not unconditional prohibitions of every alternative.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:9c76879b511f6286c0d5200bc13ed9ca","key":1091,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:656e135dc87d3a38444515f4547a5002\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:9c76879b511f6286c0d5200bc13ed9ca\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"Values carry source truth.\"],\"exceptions\":[\"Mutation is materially necessary.\"],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1773,\"path\":\"standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md\",\"quote\":\"Mutable\\ncarrier state requires explicit justification when it is\\nperformance-critical, required by the host runtime or framework, or\\nmodelling a genuinely stateful boundary rather than semantic truth.\\nConvenience is not sufficient justification.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md#DESIGN_MODULE%2F10.%20Realisation%20rules%2FImmutable%20carriers\",\"start_line\":1769}],\"statement\":\"Source truth should use typed immutable values. Mutable carrier state requires explicit justification for performance-critical use, host runtime/framework requirements, or modelling a genuinely stateful boundary rather than semantic truth. Convenience is insufficient.\",\"uncertainty\":\"The general preference is distinguished from the stricter functional-claim checklist.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:5ad4980c7e77ba6192c94103a20c4b69","key":1092,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:7243c6a09744b0df33d05cde1696eb08\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:5ad4980c7e77ba6192c94103a20c4b69\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"A semantic function is realised under the profile.\"],\"exceptions\":[\"Totality is bounded by what the language and problem allow.\",\"Typed explicit failure is preferred when practical.\"],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1778,\"path\":\"standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md\",\"quote\":\"Semantic functions should be total or as close to total as the language\\nand problem allow\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md#DESIGN_MODULE%2F10.%20Realisation%20rules%2FTotality\",\"start_line\":1777},{\"end_line\":1792,\"path\":\"standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md\",\"quote\":\"They should avoid partial\\nfunctions that assume hidden preconditions, semantic `.get(...)` fallback\\nchains, and controller code that reconstructs missing truth from defaults\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md#DESIGN_MODULE%2F10.%20Realisation%20rules%2FTotality\",\"start_line\":1789}],\"statement\":\"Prefer totality, boundary rejection of invalid input, admitted carriers in semantic kernels, typed explicit failure, Result-like or closed outcome carriers, explicit validation and unsupported/rejected outcomes. Avoid hidden-precondition partial functions, semantic fallback chains and controller reconstruction from defaults. Product outcome values must remain distinct from method evaluation results.\",\"uncertainty\":\"FOUNDATIONS' full result algebra is not supplied.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:66c918f30ab03bea1d15410f703a5a9a","key":1093,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:a50aeb522de220e58f85fd64698e09f8\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:7243c6a09744b0df33d05cde1696eb08\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:66c918f30ab03bea1d15410f703a5a9a\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1805,\"path\":\"standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md\",\"quote\":\"If a function both decides the\\nsemantic meaning and directly performs the write, the design should be\\ntreated as suspect.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md#DESIGN_MODULE%2F10.%20Realisation%20rules%2FEffect%20edge\",\"start_line\":1803}],\"statement\":\"Effects should be explicit and isolated; kernels should not perform effects while deciding law. Prefer the ordered sequence: admit/parse authoritative input, transform to typed plan/outcome, apply edge effects from it, publish resulting events/projections downstream. A function deciding meaning and directly writing should be treated as suspect.\",\"uncertainty\":\"This paragraph states a preference and diagnostic, not an executed sequence.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:d866f783309419690a787460a3e5ae87","key":1094,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:43b972cd7d8a7223dd4bfa064cbaee31\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:656e135dc87d3a38444515f4547a5002\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:d0ef4997ddb9eeaa35eecc22a937ba5e\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:d866f783309419690a787460a3e5ae87\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1813,\"path\":\"standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md\",\"quote\":\"No controller, manager, service method, runtime loop or public wrapper\\nshould be the hidden semantic centre of the system\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md#DESIGN_MODULE%2F10.%20Realisation%20rules%2FNo%20semantic%20centre\",\"start_line\":1809}],\"statement\":\"Controllers, managers, service methods, runtime loops and public wrappers should not hide semantic meaning through procedural decisions, payload-fragment reconstruction, legacy/fallback rehydration, or ad hoc dictionaries and .get chains. Closure, identity, failure, next work and current truth should already be explicit in carriers, contracts or design modules.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:513ec2735804cb6072f4318e9f72e02c","key":1095,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:d0ef4997ddb9eeaa35eecc22a937ba5e\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:656e135dc87d3a38444515f4547a5002\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:7243c6a09744b0df33d05cde1696eb08\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:a50aeb522de220e58f85fd64698e09f8\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:513ec2735804cb6072f4318e9f72e02c\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1830,\"path\":\"standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md\",\"quote\":\"Reducing coupling\\nmeans reducing the number of places where meaning can be invented.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md#DESIGN_MODULE%2F10.%20Realisation%20rules%2FCoupling\",\"start_line\":1829}],\"statement\":\"Reduce coupling by dependency shape, not file count alone. The preferred displayed direction is carriers -> semantic kernels -> effect shells -> projections, rather than controllers -> service helpers -> mutable runtime state -> projections. Excess coupling includes many modules reading/mutating one object, projections inferring truth from implementation state, consumers silently rebuilding source truth from raw artifacts, or tests passing only because multiple modules duplicate meaning. Reduction means fewer places where meaning can be invented.\",\"uncertainty\":\"The arrow is retained as the source's preferred dependency direction, without inferring execution or authority from it.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:456bb380c84f99b58accbb280cbaf383","key":1096,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:71c5dc886f20ac28171b216ffc9f66b7\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:456bb380c84f99b58accbb280cbaf383\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"A boundary governs, observes, routes, audits or evaluates another actor, executor, builder or substrate.\"],\"exceptions\":[\"Imperative strategy is permitted when strategy ownership is explicitly part of the boundary's ratified responsibility.\",\"Assessment that reproduces another actor's judgment requires explicit ownership of that assessment boundary.\"],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1837,\"path\":\"standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md\",\"quote\":\"it publishes governance truth, not\\nimperative strategy law, unless strategy ownership is explicitly part of\\nthe boundary's ratified responsibility\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md#DESIGN_MODULE%2F10.%20Realisation%20rules%2FGovernance%20and%20strategy%20separation\",\"start_line\":1835}],\"statement\":\"Publish governance truth: current state, preserved structure, unmet pressure/unresolved identities, route eligibility, lawful edit/proof frontier, admitted policy identity and prior-turn/run continuity. Do not drift into replacement decision-engine behaviour through contexts, projections, prompts or route helpers. Imperative repair instructions, framework preferences disguised as observability, budgets/scores/counters/ratings recreating another actor's judgment, and hidden doctrine in prompts/reports/read models are unlawful absent the applicable explicit ownership exception.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:b7ae5ad2cec2fa10963d1de0c4164601","key":1097,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:3fa0f57bb318e19e8b76a27b4f5b3a61\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:b7ae5ad2cec2fa10963d1de0c4164601\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"A boundary is lawfully open for bounded work.\"],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1865,\"path\":\"standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md\",\"quote\":\"Opportunistic\\noptimisation is lawful only when it is boundary-local to the active design\\nor module surface; behaviour-preserving at the declared semantic boundary;\\nauthority-neutral, with no change to ownership of truth;\\nvisibility-neutral, with no silent promotion of subordinate payloads; and\\neffect-neutral, with no hidden expansion of runtime, persistence or\\nbootstrap doctrine.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md#DESIGN_MODULE%2F10.%20Realisation%20rules%2FOpportunistic%20optimisation\",\"start_line\":1859}],\"statement\":\"The opened area should be improved, subject to constitutional truth, ownership evidence and equivalence. Lawful optimisation must be boundary-local, behaviour-preserving, authority-neutral, visibility-neutral and effect-neutral. Removing local parser re-entry, consolidating local routes, improving a local algorithm/scan, or simplifying proof fixtures/tests without changing module claims can qualify. Cross-module lookup/index/cache/persistence repricing, changed public carriers/visibility/truth ownership, wider effects or observability doctrine, and performance changes to Product expectations require explicit design re-entry. Cross-boundary discoveries remain repricing inputs; admitted follow-up enters separately at the smallest lawful re-entry point. TICKETS, not this scope rule, owns follow-up recording and ticket closure effects.\",\"uncertainty\":\"SPEC_METHOD §4 and TICKETS mechanics are not supplied.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:b69ab0018ca7250bb2a3f26bedd03b0f","key":1098,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:efb9ff5d3635a7b82d3288c918fc04d1\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:b69ab0018ca7250bb2a3f26bedd03b0f\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"A pattern recurs across more than one processed boundary.\",\"The third-local-rebuild condition applies when such a rebuild is proposed.\"],\"exceptions\":[\"A third rebuild may remain boundary-specific when review explicitly records a do-not-commonise decision and rationale.\"],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1919,\"path\":\"standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md\",\"quote\":\"a third local rebuild\\nis not design-method conformant unless the active boundary consumes an\\nexisting reusable library or commonisation surface, extends that surface\\nbefore the local implementation lands, or review records an explicit\\ndo-not-commonise decision and why the pattern is still boundary-specific\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md#DESIGN_MODULE%2F10.%20Realisation%20rules%2FRecurrence%20extraction\",\"start_line\":1913},{\"end_line\":1931,\"path\":\"standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md\",\"quote\":\"shared names, fewer lines or\\nan unused common helper do not establish contraction\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md#DESIGN_MODULE%2F10.%20Realisation%20rules%2FRecurrence%20extraction\",\"start_line\":1930}],\"statement\":\"Treat recurrence as a commonisation candidate. TICKETS §6 owns the rule of two, third-rebuild threshold, commonisation order and library_usage/governing_library/library_rationale fields for every implementation migration ticket. For design conformance a third rebuild must consume a reusable surface, extend it before local implementation lands, or record the stated exception. Tenant-local authority-neutral reusable patterns should be extracted. Changes to ownership, public carriers, module boundaries or shared common law are separate design decisions. Commonisation closes only when the selected path consumes the accepted relation and superseded production responsibility is retired or satisfies SPEC_METHOD §7 retention. Compare removed work and maintained responsibilities across the path; names, line count and unused helpers prove no contraction.\",\"uncertainty\":\"The complete ticket commonisation order and retention relation are not supplied.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:322fc2834cfa982821e3f99d18b2c855","key":1099,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:dae69138fe6568c833436d0e22dc3ade\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:322fc2834cfa982821e3f99d18b2c855\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"A processed ticket applies the profile and claims design-method closure.\"],\"exceptions\":[\"The check may be part of normal verification; no separate artifact, round or reviewer is required.\"],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1953,\"path\":\"standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md\",\"quote\":\"whether any discovered\\nissue falsifies the current claim or an applicable hard stop\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md#DESIGN_MODULE%2F10.%20Realisation%20rules%2FPost-ticket%20design%20review\",\"start_line\":1952},{\"end_line\":2017,\"path\":\"standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md\",\"quote\":\"No processed ticket that applies this profile should claim\\ndesign-method closure until this bounded design check is complete.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md#DESIGN_MODULE%2F10.%20Realisation%20rules%2FPost-ticket%20design%20review\",\"start_line\":2016}],\"statement\":\"Check the accepted design basis and exact closure claim before claiming closure; implementation status alone is insufficient. Determine lawfulness under current design/module assets, inclusion of every causally applicable live requirement, accepted design relation and retained predecessor claim, competing/ambiguous acceptance-path authority, durable architectural foreclosure of an admitted Product outcome, and falsification of the claim or an applicable hard stop. Reconstruct the complete selected function rather than only revisiting previous findings. Hashes establish identity; headings/artifact presence establish location; tests establish only asserted properties. None supplies missing semantic relations or permits substitution of weaker claims. TICKETS retains status, closure, reopening, dependency and follow-up mechanics.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:261d15c2299b1622acf7bc5fabddcfaf","key":1100,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:dae69138fe6568c833436d0e22dc3ade\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:261d15c2299b1622acf7bc5fabddcfaf\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"Reuse of current accepted Ontology, design verdict or sufficient reconstruction evidence is proposed for an unchanged boundary.\"],\"exceptions\":[\"New or materially changed boundaries still require complete Ontology and three-view coverage.\"],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1987,\"path\":\"standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md\",\"quote\":\"Missing, stale or ambiguous coverage is not a\\nno-delta proof. A material changed relation or a new counterexample is an\\ninstance of that section's material input change: it requires affected\\nreconstruction and the applicable design gate, conserving supported\\nunaffected relations.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md#DESIGN_MODULE%2F10.%20Realisation%20rules%2FPost-ticket%20design%20review\",\"start_line\":1982}],\"statement\":\"Confirm exact scope, traces, applicability and absence of ACTIVATION §7 invalidators before reuse. The source states that §7 owns exactly three invalidators and no fourth. Governing-source repricing is changed basis invalidating only affected Ontology relations and downstream projections pending impact evaluation. A later applicable candidate that could materially alter the lawful frontier changes affected selection inputs; evidence or a material dimension defeating dominance changes that relation's inputs. A new role, conversation or review occurrence alone does not require evidence re-authoring or recreating views. Missing/stale/ambiguous coverage is no no-delta proof. Material relation changes and new counterexamples require affected reconstruction and the applicable gate while conserving supported unaffected relations.\",\"uncertainty\":\"The complete enumeration of ACTIVATION §7's three invalidators is not present; the supplied examples identify changed basis and material input change only.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:6e5438ed322a50f6da58813f56b5a9aa","key":1101,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:dae69138fe6568c833436d0e22dc3ade\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:7995901312b7127d206370b31b7cfb50\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:6e5438ed322a50f6da58813f56b5a9aa\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"The bounded design check discovers an issue or opportunity.\"],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1993,\"path\":\"standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md\",\"quote\":\"an issue that falsifies the current claim or an\\napplicable hard stop blocks the design-method closure claim, because that\\nclaim is then `falsified`, which never becomes `satisfied`\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md#DESIGN_MODULE%2F10.%20Realisation%20rules%2FPost-ticket%20design%20review\",\"start_line\":1989},{\"end_line\":2010,\"path\":\"standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md\",\"quote\":\"repricing inputs that do not automatically widen the subject, block its\\nbounded claim or require a follow-up ticket\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md#DESIGN_MODULE%2F10.%20Realisation%20rules%2FPost-ticket%20design%20review\",\"start_line\":2009}],\"statement\":\"A falsified current claim or applicable hard stop blocks design-method closure; falsified does not become satisfied and a hard stop is not waived. Current-promotion effects use EVALUATION §5: falsifying issue, competing/ambiguous authority, unlawful current boundary or omitted applicable requirement/design/predecessor claim, and durable architectural foreclosure supply its four domain triggers. Wording cannot narrow away active applicable authority. Absorb local clean-up/commonisation only when needed to make the claim true, preserve singular authority, satisfy accepted design or avoid foreclosure. Other clean-up, recurrence, generality and cross-boundary opportunities remain out-of-claim repricing inputs; they do not automatically widen scope, block the bounded claim or require follow-up. Owner-admitted repricing enters at the smallest lawful re-entry point; unclaimed future capability and optional clean-up are not implicit work.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:97cbead21573e99ce9db237e0afaa860","key":1102,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:f885e90230e4244ecb359d1703569deb\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:97cbead21573e99ce9db237e0afaa860\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":2029,\"path\":\"standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md\",\"quote\":\"Low\\ncoupling requires semantic non-bleed, not only small functions.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md#DESIGN_MODULE%2F10.%20Realisation%20rules%2FInterface%20bleed%20prohibition\",\"start_line\":2028}],\"statement\":\"No interface should bleed semantic authority into another family. Each family requires one authoritative source truth, downstream consumption of that truth and no new semantic centre created by crossing the interface boundary. Low coupling requires semantic non-bleed as well as small functions.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:e626d2e397a57828d3b9911b23974c32","key":1103,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:106b5875c771ed4e6863de75f3deb31a\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:e626d2e397a57828d3b9911b23974c32\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"A project uses this profile.\"],\"exceptions\":[\"Intentionally retained compatibility is an explicit feature with its own bounded authority and proof.\"],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":2042,\"path\":\"standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md\",\"quote\":\"If compatibility is intentionally retained, it is treated as\\nan explicit feature with its own bounded authority an