ote\":\"A prompt clause that exists to enforce design law\\nneeds provenance and a proof that the clause still causes or prevents the\\nintended behaviour\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md#DESIGN_MODULE%2F11.%20Review\",\"start_line\":2049}],\"statement\":\"Profile prompts follow ACTIVATION §2 prompt construction. Design-enforcing clauses need provenance and proof of continuing intended causal or preventive effect.\",\"uncertainty\":\"The external prompt-construction rule is not supplied.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:248bbacd0c259c74fffeb4898cbf2474","key":1105,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:0793e8125983d93adb20487fbf5a9458\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:248bbacd0c259c74fffeb4898cbf2474\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"Reviewing code under this profile.\"],\"exceptions\":[\"Python-specific checks apply to governed Python surfaces.\",\"Reference-to-target derivation checks apply when a reference realisation exists.\",\"Governance, optimisation, recurrence and ticket checks apply when their stated circumstances occur.\"],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":2068,\"path\":\"standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md\",\"quote\":\"Would removing the authoritative carrier make the system fail closed\\n   rather than silently rebuilding truth?\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md#DESIGN_MODULE%2F11.%20Review%2FDesign%20review%20questions\",\"start_line\":2067},{\"end_line\":2112,\"path\":\"standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md\",\"quote\":\"If the ticket is making a design-method closure claim, did the bounded\\n    design check cover the exact claim and applicable hard stops without\\n    automatically absorbing optional discovery?\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md#DESIGN_MODULE%2F11.%20Review%2FDesign%20review%20questions\",\"start_line\":2110}],\"statement\":\"Ask whether law resides in carriers rather than orchestration; steps transform admitted truth; effects are isolated; projections/reports cannot invent closure or same-name structurally different truth; mutation is justified, bounded and local; consumers can directly pattern-match carriers; proxies are not silently authoritative; removal of authority fails closed; new functions project accepted Prime atoms without convenience aggregation or rival authority; interfaces do not bleed; Python avoids Any/open dictionaries/untyped semantic definitions; IACS is declared; subordinate payloads remain justified as subordinate; promoted types pass the Promotion Test; typed closure avoids Boundary Inflation and parallel schema migrations; truth surfaces do not increase and duplicate truth is reduced; foreign/open payloads are not trusted past ingress; enforcement follows proof. Also ask whether governance publishes state/routes rather than strategy; reference design explicitly derives target design then module assets; module-domain projections faithfully show IACS, Prime mappings, payloads, visibility, ownership and deferred families; tests derive from ownership/assets; optimisation remains local, behaviour-preserving and authority-neutral; cross-boundary opportunities require owner-admitted re-entry; recurrence receives an explicit commonisation decision and third rebuild consumes/extends or records do-not-commonise; closure checks exact claims and hard stops without automatic optional work.\",\"uncertainty\":\"These are required review questions, not assertions that the reviewed properties hold.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:6df41135c9856299bf9ef53e0ecba6bb","key":1106,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:0793e8125983d93adb20487fbf5a9458\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:6df41135c9856299bf9ef53e0ecba6bb\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"Reviewing code under this 