ve design. That diagnosis requires evidence\\nthat meaning is held in orchestration or outside the declared carriers\\nand transforms\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md#DESIGN_MODULE%2F11.%20Review%2FDesign%20review%20questions\",\"start_line\":2204}],\"statement\":\"Withhold the dependent conformance claim, record the unanswered relation and deciding evidence needed, and diagnose the gap at its actual owner under ACTIVATION §1. Missing authority declarations or observations alone do not prove excessive coupling or imperative design; those diagnoses require evidence of meaning in orchestration or outside declared carriers/transforms.\",\"uncertainty\":\"An unanswered relation remains unresolved, not falsified by absence.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:9b6df9f105751a725de250491b07eeb6","key":1109,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:0793e8125983d93adb20487fbf5a9458\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:7243c6a09744b0df33d05cde1696eb08\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:656e135dc87d3a38444515f4547a5002\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:a50aeb522de220e58f85fd64698e09f8\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:9b6df9f105751a725de250491b07eeb6\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"A project claims functional bias, pure transforms, immutable carriers, single-owner truth or low-coupling realisation.\"],\"exceptions\":[\"Reference equivalence and explicit reference-to-target derivation apply when a reference exists.\",\"Identity creation ownership applies when identity is introduced.\",\"Optimisation, recurrence, cross-boundary, ticket and graph checks apply when their stated triggers occur.\"],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":2264,\"path\":\"standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md\",\"quote\":\"if identity is introduced, identity creation is explicitly owned by\\n      a declared ingress or effect boundary rather than hidden inside\\n      semantic helpers;\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md#DESIGN_MODULE%2F11.%20Review%2FFunctional%20realisation%20checklist\",\"start_line\":2262},{\"end_line\":2314,\"path\":\"standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md\",\"quote\":\"a negative proof shows that an imperative bypass, open-payload\\n      bypass or effect-edge erasure fails closed;\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md#DESIGN_MODULE%2F11.%20Review%2FFunctional%20realisation%20checklist\",\"start_line\":2313}],\"statement\":\"Explicitly check: constitutional WHAT is preserved within lawful HOW; one accepted Ontology derives entities, identities, relationships, invariants, lifecycle, authority, atomic functions, composition, effects and projections; every create/read/update/delete lifecycle question has a lawful function, reasoned not_applicable or owned gap; authority kinds are distinct; every functionality item is disposed without direct verb promotion; whole-family Prime contraction precedes peer promotion and records all atom domains/projection maps; IACS/views/contracts/adapters/code/tests are fidelity-checked Ontology projections. Check reference-boundary equivalence and design-to-design-to-module mapping before implementation where applicable, and proportional generic-foundation selection with discovery/frontier/roles/evidence. Implementation and tests derive from the same module assets; each truth surface has one owner; duplicate truth/reconstruction/rival paths decrease; functions consume admitted carriers and are pure for equal inputs; time/randomness/UUIDs/environment/process/filesystem/network/registries and shared mutable state are absent from the semantic centre; identity creation is ingress/effect-owned; carriers return new immutable values; local admitted truth does not re-enter parsers/validators/loaders; ingress rejects incomplete/invalid truth; defaults are ratified and carrier-owned; each function has one owner/responsibility. Algebra depends on carrier contracts, admission on validation, effects stay typed at edges without erasing truth into open objects; no function both decides meaning and performs effects; package/bootstrap/controller/adapter/runtime layers stay below the semantic centre; governance publishes facts, eligibility and provenance only. Require matching complete Mermaid views, complete cross-view matrix and explicit accepted verdict without bypassed gaps; module-owned tests; lawful local optimisation; explicit recurrence decisions, consumption/extension of available common surfaces or rationale for non-use; owner-admitted cross-boundary re-entry; bounded closure checks; negative fail-closed proof for imperative/open-payload/effect-erasure bypasses; graph-governed modules inside declared traversals and repricing when modules decide next work, closure, semantic target movement or graph identity; lifecycle confirmation with answers, reasoned non-applicability or named gaps and authority-grounded operational claims.\",\"uncertainty\":\"Checklist claims are represented as review obligations, not verified properties of any Product.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:5d6553b02acc8e50d097d190d40ea2d2","key":1110,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:0793e8125983d93adb20487fbf5a9458\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:5d6553b02acc8e50d097d190d40ea2d2\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"The hard gate is applied to a new or materially changed boundary.\"],\"exceptions\":[\"For an unchanged boundary, use the accepted basis plus evidence of no material semantic-boundary delta; no new Ontology, IACS, views, cross-view evaluation or unit-test lane is required.\"],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":2336,\"path\":\"standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md\",\"quote\":\"accepted Ontology before promotion or closure and, where\\n      design-gated, before retained implementation establishes an\\n      unresolved or contradictory relation or chooses a materially\\n      non-equivalent network;\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md#DESIGN_MODULE%2F11.%20Review%2FFunctional%20realisation%20checklist\",\"start_line\":2333},{\"end_line\":2364,\"path\":\"standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md\",\"quote\":\"For an unchanged boundary, the hard gate is the accepted basis plus\\nevidence of no material semantic-boundary delta; it does not require a new\\nOntology, IACS, three-view asset, cross-view evaluation or unit-test lane\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md#DESIGN_MODULE%2F11.%20Review%2FFunctional%20realisation%20checklist\",\"start_line\":2361}],\"statement\":\"The language-agnostic gate covers module, carrier, data-entity and realisation review. Require accepted Ontology before promotion/closure and, where design-gated, before retained implementation establishes unresolved/contradictory relations or materially non-equivalent networks; complete lifecycle/authority/function derivation; whole-family Prime, admitted domains, projection mappings and composition/effect algebra; proportional capability/foundation selection for material generic mechanics/dependencies with bounded discovery, frontier disposition and exact role/authority conservation; pure semantic functions; immutable carriers without shared mutable semantic state; one owner per truth; low admission/algebra/effect coupling; no hidden runtime authority; accepted domain/sequence/state projections; complete cross-view evaluation without bypassed gaps; specification equivalence and reference equivalence when present; lifecycle confirmation or named gaps; and negative proof for imperative/open bypass.\",\"uncertainty\":\"Named lifecycle gaps are expressly retained by the gate; they are not silently converted to resolved phases.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:5d83797a0b11e6e267bc65680e69d602","key":1111,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:0bfa7a9a55ccb9c21fe73b41be970541\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:bb53ea665dafe38a1f8718f3b042739a\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:5d83797a0b11e6e267bc65680e69d602\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"Product authority adopts the profile for a named boundary.\"],\"exceptions\":[\"Partial adoption may narrow scope but cannot omit evidence needed to audit, refactor or reconstruct a boundary while claiming completion.\"],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":2387,\"path\":\"standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md\",\"quote\":\"For\\nmigrations involving carrier closure, schema closure or governance\\nboundaries, projects should make the boundary closure evaluators (§3)\\nexplicit in the governing ADR or ticket rather than leaving them implicit\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md#DESIGN_MODULE%2F12.%20Adoption%20and%20relations%2FAdoption\",\"start_line\":2383},{\"end_line\":2403,\"path\":\"standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md\",\"quote\":\"When the new or\\nmaterially changed boundary has active implementation, the project also\\npublishes a module-derived unit test lane (ASSURANCE §15) before claiming\\nclosure for that change\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md#DESIGN_MODULE%2F12.%20Adoption%20and%20relations%2FAdoption\",\"start_line\":2400}],\"statement\":\"Apply adoption consistently across Ontology/architecture, design modules, runtime/execution kernels, prompts/reports, constructors/materialisers and projections/queries in the named boundary. Carrier/schema closure and governance migrations should state boundary closure evaluators explicitly in the governing ADR/ticket. Every new or materially changed adopted semantic boundary declares/cites accepted Ontology before completion, with change-proportionate lifecycle, authority, function derivation, whole-family Prime, atom domains, realisation maps and traceability. Schema/typed-carrier changes derive and reconcile IACS first; reference-derived changes publish reference-to-target derivation and Ontology-derived three views first; active implementation publishes a module-derived unit-test lane before closure. Partial adoption should explicitly name boundary and rule family.\",\"uncertainty\":\"Boundary closure evaluator details and ASSURANCE §15 are outside the supplied sections.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:1589dc243d3a3bbc15300f287fe54864","key":1112,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:178c7d7d9a8e9d339fe3d75171216d5f\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:bb53ea665dafe38a1f8718f3b042739a\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:1589dc243d3a3bbc15300f287fe54864\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"A Product is governed by the graph-execution profile.\",\"UX additions apply when the boundary realises a UX/UI surface.\"],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":2435,\"path\":\"standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md\",\"quote\":\"For products governed by the graph-execution profile, that profile decides\\nwhether the operative unit is an outcome traversal, graph function, GTL\\nmodule or ABG runtime boundary; this profile then governs the\\ndeterministic module structure that realises, evaluates, adapts or\\nprojects inside that boundary\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md#DESIGN_MODULE%2F12.%20Adoption%20and%20relations%2FRelationship%20to%20other%20members\",\"start_line\":2428}],\"statement\":\"ODD decides the operative graph unit; DESIGN_MODULE governs deterministic realisation/evaluation/adaptation/projection inside it. Load UX only for UX realisation; its render purity, reducer purity, effect membrane and AssetSurface binding add functional front/back consistency. Module lifecycle confirmation detects adequate lifecycle signal for build/review but does not decide release eligibility, exact-cut acceptance, selector promotion, installation policy or rollout; RELEASE and project-owned release/deployment/operational surfaces retain those decisions.\",\"uncertainty\":\"The other members' full operative laws are not supplied.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:5aed54c0690e67be3b33143e4c30ccd5","key":1113,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:e19911b2f9e025ddf9ca3741869cd84a\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:5aed54c0690e67be3b33143e4c30ccd5\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"The realisation is consumer-bound to the ABG role under graph execution.\"],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":2453,\"path\":\"standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md\",\"quote\":\"Their standing as\\ndefaults and the identity law of their override, its preservation\\nconditions and its publication surface are\\n[IDENTITY §7](IDENTITY.md#7-default-formats-and-overrides).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md#DESIGN_MODULE%2F12.%20Adoption%20and%20relations%2FIdentity%20defaults%20from%20a%20bound%20runtime%20realisation\",\"start_line\":2450}],\"statement\":\"Default publication is confined to the bound role's own runtime surfaces and default ODD kinds used by default F_D helpers; it extends no permission to other runtime realisations. Default standing, override identity law, preservation conditions and publication surface belong to IDENTITY §7.\",\"uncertainty\":\"IDENTITY §7's override requirements are unresolved in this source selection.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:64aba38f50a5e5fc7bb7eea6468712ec","key":1114,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:bb53ea665dafe38a1f8718f3b042739a\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:64aba38f50a5e5fc7bb7eea6468712ec\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"A boundary composes higher-order or effectful computation.\"],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":2464,\"path\":\"standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md\",\"quote\":\"the composition and effect algebra\\nthat remains required where a boundary composes higher-order or effectful\\ncomputation are stated once in\\n[SPEC_METHOD §2 Realisation shape](SPEC_METHOD.md#realisation-shape)\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md#DESIGN_MODULE%2F12.%20Adoption%20and%20relations%2FNon-goals\",\"start_line\":2460}],\"statement\":\"The profile does not mandate one programming language, elimination of all imperative code, monadic/category-theory vocabulary or custom algebraic replacement of every exception. These non-goals do not remove the composition and effect algebra required for higher-order/effectful computation; SPEC_METHOD §2 owns the full realisation-shape rule.\",\"uncertainty\":\"The complete required algebra and implementation shape are not supplied.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:7e5853a8f74dcbf6b25c4ab455ca8ef6","key":1115,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:68dd606198d8326413b678398e5e1a69\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:7e5853a8f74dcbf6b25c4ab455ca8ef6\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"A load-bearing claim is made; additional construction-kind requirements apply to recursive or repeated work.\"],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":19,\"path\":\"standards/EVALUATION.md\",\"quote\":\"Without these it is evidence discovery, not proof. Packaging, syntax,\\ncompilation, presence, invocation or local behaviour never substitutes for a\\nsemantic, authority-bearing, installed, release or end-to-end claim because\\nthe weaker property is easier to measure\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/EVALUATION.md#EVALUATION%2F1.%20Claims\",\"start_line\":16}],\"statement\":\"Before witness selection declare exact subject, property, basis, witness relation, excluded nearest weaker property and falsifier; otherwise the activity is evidence discovery, not proof. Packaging/syntax/compilation/presence/invocation/local behaviour cannot substitute for semantic, authority, installed, release or end-to-end claims. Repeated/recursive construction claims state preservation, progress, termination or outcome satisfaction and whether the witness predicate is the full obligation, a necessary condition or part of a sufficient conjunction. Expected answers require assertion provenance and execution requires execution provenance; a passing necessary-condition check establishes only that condition.\",\"uncertainty\":\"The external provenance and construction relations are not fully supplied.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:b7cc9fc03143a501d30178d33fa89e8d","key":1116,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:68dd606198d8326413b678398e5e1a69\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:b7cc9fc03143a501d30178d33fa89e8d\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"Assurance supports promotion or closure.\",\"Mechanical-enforcement requirements apply when mechanical enforcement is claimed.\"],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":44,\"path\":\"standards/EVALUATION.md\",\"quote\":\"a planned or\\nspecification-only harness is planned evidence, not observed verification,\\nand until both the predicate and such a witness are observed the claim\\nremains open or is explicitly downgraded to the planned property\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/EVALUATION.md#EVALUATION%2F1.%20Claims\",\"start_line\":41}],\"statement\":\"Checker/validator/harness/reviewer assurance binds the exact subject and authoritative composition relation. Single-file/carrier evidence proves only that boundary; cross-carrier satisfaction/conflict must be decided at the declared composite boundary. Mechanical-enforcement claims require a named executable/reproducible predicate and a witness reachable through the ordinary declared assurance path; until both are observed, the claim stays open or is explicitly downgraded to planned evidence.\",\"uncertainty\":\"No ordinary assurance path is instantiated by this interpretation.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:10dcb15d70ad06dd2880a8d89b96c387","key":1117,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:68dd606198d8326413b678398e5e1a69\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:10dcb15d70ad06dd2880a8d89b96c387\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":51,\"path\":\"standards/EVALUATION.md\",\"quote\":\"A claim's quantifier, population and scope cannot exceed its evaluated\\nevidence. Generalising a local defect or observation needs a declared\\ninference relation, the relevant comparable population, explicit\\ncounterexample treatment and governing evidence. Later counterevidence\\ninvalidates every dependent verdict until the claim-evidence relation is\\nsuperseded, withdrawn or requalified\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/EVALUATION.md#EVALUATION%2F1.%20Claims\",\"start_line\":46}],\"statement\":\"Quantifier, population and scope cannot outrun evaluated evidence. Generalisation needs a declared inference relation, comparable population, explicit counterexample treatment and governing evidence. Later counterevidence invalidates every dependent verdict until supersession, withdrawal or requalification of the claim-evidence relation. The source's boundary/quantifier rules are falsified by weaker/different-subject assurance, unevaluated composite closure from individual-carrier evidence, absent mechanical predicate/reachable witness, planned evidence reported as observed, unsupported generalisation, or dependent verdicts surviving material counterevidence without requalification.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:a5ac162b1e74e48acbabc21b8e36006a","key":1118,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:bc7e4c53bced59c7b790eb61fb0c25fa\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:a5ac162b1e74e48acbabc21b8e36006a\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"A consumer applies an F6 rule.\"],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":126,\"path\":\"standards/EVALUATION.md\",\"quote\":\"Each consumer applies the rule and decides nothing the owning section does\\nnot\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/EVALUATION.md#EVALUATION%2F1.%20Claims%2FFoundation%20to%20law%3A%20claims%2C%20evidence%2C%20assessment%20and%20acceptance\",\"start_line\":125}],\"statement\":\"The table's consumers apply, without expanding, the owning rule. Claim-composition authority declares composite boundaries; project assurance design declares ordinary assurance paths; claim authors declare generalisation inference/population; models supply checker decision contracts. TICKETS policy identifies required independent-assessment boundaries and a governing basis may add them; governing authority configures actor type/count, rounds, engines, prompts and orchestration. This member owns assessor pre-exposure expectations, no repair, post-exposure intervention and same-family default non-independence. Adopting profiles declare triage fields; Products own scales, priority/boundary/cutoff policies. Governing bases name acceptance boundary, interval and owner; work items own closing conditions; humans admit bounded proxy grants; hard-stop owners and ACTIVATION §4 determine non-waivability; RELEASE owns successor dispositions and evaluation, while current Product authority owns removals. Core result algebra and planned-but-unevaluated absence remain FOUNDATIONS family F3, not new F6 result values.\",\"uncertainty\":\"The table identifies external owners and consumer loci; their full definitions are not imported.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:3ae4349154a238306134ba5a46015bb9","key":1119,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:c069b37d4f1a0f0716eb0d9fe2891726\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:3ae4349154a238306134ba5a46015bb9\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[\"One actor may perform several roles if the record keeps them distinguishable.\"],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":153,\"path\":\"standards/EVALUATION.md\",\"quote\":\"A semantic change requires lawful re-entry and invalidates affected\\ndownstream acceptance. A broad digest may conservatively\\ninvalidate a review; it does not prove that every semantic relation\\nchanged\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/EVALUATION.md#EVALUATION%2F2.%20Separation\",\"start_line\":150}],\"statement\":\"Keep semantic basis, evidence basis and state projection distinct, and separately record law, observations, evaluator application and decision disposition. RF-007 and AC-018 add only frame/model bindings. Evidence change may invalidate a verdict without changed law; ACTIVATION §7 decides when, and required invalidation occurs before reliance. Projection change may stale a view without changing truth under ACTIVATION §2. Semantic change requires lawful re-entry and invalidates affected downstream acceptance. Broad digest change may conservatively invalidate review but proves only representation change, not change to every semantic relation.\",\"uncertainty\":\"External reuse and staleness tests are not fully supplied.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:493adf50070b0c80bf1a24c4d149aa8e","key":1120,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:c069b37d4f1a0f0716eb0d9fe2891726\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:68dd606198d8326413b678398e5e1a69\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:493adf50070b0c80bf1a24c4d149aa8e\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"A checker or other evidence surface is used to support a claim.\"],\"exceptions\":[\"A checker may claim a semantic or authority subset under an exact lawful model-supplied decision contract.\"],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":168,\"path\":\"standards/EVALUATION.md\",\"quote\":\"Evidence bound to a basis other than\\nthe evaluated one is excluded by basis; it is not admitted with a narrower\\nscope\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/EVALUATION.md#EVALUATION%2F2.%20Separation\",\"start_line\":165}],\"statement\":\"Structural success supplies evidence for semantic review and does not replace it. A checker decides the structural subset; semantic/authority claims require the stated contract. Valid parse, map, green test and historical judgment each establish only their own claim. Evidence on another basis is excluded, not admitted under a narrower scope; AC-018/AC-019 bind these distinctions to a_c records and validity.\",\"uncertainty\":\"The subject's referenced model laws are data and are not the selected calculus's operational application.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:c61f28a8dc747ab21a4b751803b15896","key":1121,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:82a1c0ef4b3ec237b1b9e89ac75fddb3\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:c61f28a8dc747ab21a4b751803b15896\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"Promotion requires independent assessment under TICKETS policy or an added governing-basis requirement.\"],\"exceptions\":[\"Shared mechanical evidence may be reused subject to ACTIVATION §7; the constructor's judgment may not.\",\"Outside method qualification an equivalent exact-subject relation sufficient for the claim may replace immutable identity.\"],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":191,\"path\":\"standards/EVALUATION.md\",\"quote\":\"The assessor records its\\nexpectations from the governing source before opening the candidate; it\\nreads the subject at that identity or relation, never a mutable working\\ntree; it makes no repair; it does not assess its\\nown authorship.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/EVALUATION.md#EVALUATION%2F3.%20Independent%20assessment\",\"start_line\":186}],\"statement\":\"Assess exact live subject, authority paths, proof and installed state, not constructor summaries. For method qualification freeze identity before material reference exposure; elsewhere stabilise exact subject. Record expectations from governing source before opening candidate; read that fixed subject rather than a mutable tree; make no repairs and assess no own authorship. Post-exposure revision is a declared intervention, either a method constituent with its own qualification boundary or a new qualification subject, and cannot retroactively pass the original frozen construction. This law prescribes no actor type/count, round count, engine, prompt or orchestration.\",\"uncertainty\":\"Required-assessment boundaries and method qualification's full protocol are not supplied.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:bb792864114a40c2a0bbe3c265517dc0","key":1122,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:82a1c0ef4b3ec237b1b9e89ac75fddb3\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:2bdf6340141f53f21c1781855206b707\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:bb792864114a40c2a0bbe3c265517dc0\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"An assessment is returned for required or planned assessment.\"],\"exceptions\":[\"No cryptographic or transport binding protocol is prescribed.\"],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":201,\"path\":\"standards/EVALUATION.md\",\"quote\":\"Membership in a plan authenticates nothing,\\nan unauthenticated result satisfies no required assessment, and a result\\nbound to another subject satisfies no planned assessment\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/EVALUATION.md#EVALUATION%2F3.%20Independent%20assessment\",\"start_line\":197}],\"statement\":\"Bind returned assessment to producer, subject, basis and evidence to authenticate it. Authentication establishes neither expected-answer assertion provenance nor run execution provenance; both remain separately required. Plan membership authenticates nothing. Unauthenticated results satisfy no required assessment and results bound to another subject satisfy no planned assessment.\",\"uncertainty\":\"The full FOUNDATIONS provenance and conjunction relations are not supplied.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:055ca0f16bfea4bc6a2a86d9af93ce78","key":1123,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:82a1c0ef4b3ec237b1b9e89ac75fddb3\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:055ca0f16bfea4bc6a2a86d9af93ce78\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[\"A reporter may assess a later repair only when its existing assessment grant, authorship relation and evidence independence permit.\",\"Same-model-family activations count as independent only if the claim's governing basis declares that policy.\"],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":224,\"path\":\"standards/EVALUATION.md\",\"quote\":\"A person\\nwho authored an adopted repair cannot supply its required independent\\nassessment by calling that authorship a finding\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/EVALUATION.md#EVALUATION%2F3.%20Independent%20assessment\",\"start_line\":222},{\"end_line\":240,\"path\":\"standards/EVALUATION.md\",\"quote\":\"the default where it is not\\nstated is that they are not independent.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/EVALUATION.md#EVALUATION%2F3.%20Independent%20assessment\",\"start_line\":239}],\"statement\":\"Reporting defects, counterexamples or already-required behaviour alone is not authorship. Adopted wording, design or policy, including particular repair directions, is authorship of that contribution; calling it a finding does not restore independence. Finding a defect grants no review authority. Reading the same governing sources is allowed, but a fresh context grants neither independence nor authority; self-review remains construction output. Received contributions retain their author's identity wherever carried, and that author's reading is not independent acceptance. Independence across actor families must be declared; absent a stated policy, two activations of one model family are not independent for semantic judgment.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:0eb494a45690f748eb48fa97cccfc7f7","key":1124,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:2bdf6340141f53f21c1781855206b707\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:0eb494a45690f748eb48fa97cccfc7f7\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"A review is returned.\"],\"exceptions\":[\"A review may recommend a disposition as evidence only.\"],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":259,\"path\":\"standards/EVALUATION.md\",\"quote\":\"it does not apply one. A finding\\nwithout evidence a consumer can chase is commentary.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/EVALUATION.md#EVALUATION%2F4.%20Review%20results\",\"start_line\":258}],\"statement\":\"Return one core result and required evidence record for each actually evaluated declared predicate. Explicitly name planned unperformed predicates without assigning any core value, including indeterminate or falsified. Recommendations are evidence, never applied dispositions. A finding lacking consumer-traceable evidence is commentary.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:2775926f6a7ac6cb34fc94bd901ad92e","key":1125,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:e5950994e1df5b915151a6b066232472\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:2bdf6340141f53f21c1781855206b707\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:2775926f6a7ac6cb34fc94bd901ad92e\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"A finding-level triage projection is made.\"],\"exceptions\":[\"For satisfied, another exact consumed result may separately supply a finding affecting priority or boundary effect.\"],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":290,\"path\":\"standards/EVALUATION.md\",\"quote\":\"| invalid_basis | a basis failure; triage `not_applicable`; invalidation evidence and basis-repair pressure | refuse to consume the result and return through the declared basis re-entry relation |\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/EVALUATION.md#EVALUATION%2F4.%20Review%20results%2FResult%20and%20triage%20projection\",\"start_line\":290}],\"statement\":\"The projection is total over core values, not over unperformed predicates: those have neither result nor triage. satisfied: explicit no-finding, triage not_applicable, evidence/residuals/invalidation retained; priority/boundary effect not_applicable unless another exact result supplies a finding. falsified: one or more exact findings, triage complete where supported and indeterminate fields where not; apply Product priority/boundary policy without mechanical severity-to-disposition mapping. indeterminate: partial finding/observation, indeterminate triage and exact gaps/residuals; preserve uncertainty or reactivate capable evaluation, never consume as satisfaction or closed finding. out_of_frame: undeclared material relation or missing evaluator capability, indeterminate triage with exact reconfiguration pressure; refine/reconfigure and keep unresolved, never consume as satisfaction or falsification. invalid_basis: basis failure, not_applicable triage, invalidation evidence and repair pressure; refuse consumption and use declared basis re-entry.\",\"uncertainty\":\"These are descriptions of source-defined results, not results returned by this interpretation.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:a221b251c7153a7a057780a22a4831b1","key":1126,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:e5950994e1df5b915151a6b066232472\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:82a1c0ef4b3ec237b1b9e89ac75fddb3\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:89222b77e50c83868d267c878c6103c4\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:a221b251c7153a7a057780a22a4831b1\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":301,\"path\":\"standards/EVALUATION.md\",\"quote\":\"The assessor returns to the decision owner, not to the constructor. It does\\nnot edit the candidate, direct the repair or authorise continuation\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/EVALUATION.md#EVALUATION%2F4.%20Review%20results%2FResult%20and%20triage%20projection\",\"start_line\":299}],\"statement\":\"Every configuration keeps severity, priority, boundary effect and disposition distinct even when Product policy maps values. A recommended disposition is evidence, not priority/boundary effect/disposition, and is never adopted mechanically. Profiles declare fields; Products bind scales. An adjacent out-of-claim observation returns separately with claim-relative triage not_applicable and exact repricing/re-entry pressure; the decision owner routes it to its declared owner without a claim-relative block or new review round from severity alone. The assessor returns to the decision owner, not constructor, and neither edits, directs repair nor authorises continuation. The rule applies to any assessor/owner; EXECUTIVE_BASELINE is an instance binding.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:ea0ba787374aa89f668720dc3919cb1a","key":1127,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:89222b77e50c83868d267c878c6103c4\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:ea0ba787374aa89f668720dc3919cb1a\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[\"A human decision may be exercised by an explicitly admitted bounded proxy.\"],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":322,\"path\":\"standards/EVALUATION.md\",\"quote\":\"for acceptance, a change a proxy cannot make re-enters at its owning\\nrelation\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/EVALUATION.md#EVALUATION%2F5.%20Acceptance\",\"start_line\":321}],\"statement\":\"Acceptance must be the owner's disposition over the unchanged subject and cannot be widened by recording it; it exhausts only its named instance and interval. Review approval, green labels, document/review counts and historical outcomes are not acceptance or work-item closure. A human may act directly or through an explicitly admitted bounded proxy; proxy identity remains distinct, grant contents belong to IDENTITY §6, absolute proxy limits to FOUNDATIONS §2, and changes beyond the proxy grant re-enter at their owning relation.\",\"uncertainty\":\"The full proxy-grant tuple and absolute limits are not supplied.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:bc716cae5de1560b004ad07068f1f0a6","key":1128,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:89222b77e50c83868d267c878c6103c4\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:bc716cae5de1560b004ad07068f1f0a6\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"The accepted subject is a successor.\"],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":332,\"path\":\"standards/EVALUATION.md\",\"quote\":\"A claim whose disposition is\\nunresolved cannot be qualified and so cannot be accepted; how the record\\nis evaluated is [RELEASE §9](RELEASE.md#9-successor-baseline-conservation-stdo-up-015).\\nAn intentionally removed disposition is a decision of the current Product\\nauthority, and its record is that decision\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/EVALUATION.md#EVALUATION%2F5.%20Acceptance\",\"start_line\":328}],\"statement\":\"Include the successor disposition record naming the exact immutable predecessor cut and one semantic disposition for every predecessor claim capable of affecting the successor. Unresolved claim dispositions cannot be qualified or accepted. Intentional removal is a current Product-authority decision recorded as such; RELEASE §9 owns record evaluation.\",\"uncertainty\":\"The complete disposition vocabulary and evaluation procedure are not supplied.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:a86beb01b7eb9e6a94f3e22b728e5e77","key":1129,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:7995901312b7127d206370b31b7cfb50\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:a86beb01b7eb9e6a94f3e22b728e5e77\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"At any promotion boundary a finding is consumed against the exact reviewed claim and applicable hard stops.\"],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":361,\"path\":\"standards/EVALUATION.md\",\"quote\":\"| a valid falsification of a mandatory claim governed by a non-waivable hard stop | the boundary blocks, whatever the assigned priority or the decision cutoff |\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/EVALUATION.md#EVALUATION%2F5.%20Acceptance%2FWhen%20a%20finding%20blocks%20promotion\",\"start_line\":359},{\"end_line\":366,\"path\":\"standards/EVALUATION.md\",\"quote\":\"Severity selects neither priority nor a block mechanically, and priority\\nneither erases severity nor waives a hard stop. The decision cutoff is the\\nadopting Product's policy; this member sets no cutoff\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/EVALUATION.md#EVALUATION%2F5.%20Acceptance%2FWhen%20a%20finding%20blocks%20promotion\",\"start_line\":364}],\"statement\":\"A finding can block only if it falsifies the claim, exposes competing/ambiguous acceptance-path authority, violates applicable active authority/safety/retained accepted behaviour, or establishes durable material architectural foreclosure of an admitted Product outcome. These are necessary, not all automatically sufficient. Valid falsification of a mandatory claim under a non-waivable hard stop blocks regardless of priority/cutoff. Otherwise the decision owner decides using exact affected claim, governed outcome/decision, hard stops and Product cutoff policy; below cutoff no automatic block follows and accepted residuals stay explicit. Findings meeting none do not block. Outside observations alone neither widen subject, block the bounded claim nor require another ticket, artifact, review round or implementation increment. Severity mechanically selects neither priority nor blocking; priority erases neither severity nor hard stops. This member sets no cutoff.\",\"uncertainty\":\"Product cutoff and particular hard stops are not instantiated.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:a10b3e71f1d4c97d3d48fd1b0b845e4d","key":1130,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:cae7dff6a99951473cac43cb9487326d\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:19e30cf61a7e6ca33b6b4f01e979cf51\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:a10b3e71f1d4c97d3d48fd1b0b845e4d\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"A conformance or equivalence claim is made.\"],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":413,\"path\":\"standards/EVALUATION.md\",\"quote\":\"An analogy or matching result\\nis insufficient. Evidence for one claim is not reported as a result for\\nanother\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/EVALUATION.md#EVALUATION%2F6.%20Conformance%20of%20realisations\",\"start_line\":409}],\"statement\":\"A weak Σ admitting materially different behaviour must declare latitude or be repaired before decision-complete design is claimed. No ladder rung implies another; conformance proves neither identical behaviour outside Σ nor equal cost. Semantic conformance uses the governing semantic basis as Σ. For a proposed span 𝒜 → ℐ and 𝒜 → 𝒞_H, keep conformance, semantic and computational equivalence separate. Categorical equivalence must meet all applicable FOUNDATIONS Formal-fragment items and additionally exhibit a quasi-inverse functor with natural isomorphisms from each composite to its identity functor on a stated domain. Analogy, matching output or passing conformance is insufficient for equivalence or preserved structure; evidence for one claim is not another's result.\",\"uncertainty\":\"The Formal fragment's definitions of categories, functors, 𝒜, ℐ and 𝒞_H are not supplied.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:7dbf6dcd8c36901e9d7ebdedeb2d25ef","key":1131,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:6d96b75770d3c078aeccf46c41c1bc6f\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:cae7dff6a99951473cac43cb9487326d\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:7dbf6dcd8c36901e9d7ebdedeb2d25ef\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"A layered derivation, reconstruction or frozen-result comparison is assessed.\"],\"exceptions\":[\"Exact current accepted basis and sufficient evidence may be reused after checking applicability and invalidation.\",\"An applicable separately held reference outcome is optional non-authoritative evidence; equivalence to it is required only when the governing basis requires it.\"],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":429,\"path\":\"standards/EVALUATION.md\",\"quote\":\"reconstructability requires a correct reconstruction route, not its\\nexecution at every use, grants no restart authority and does not excuse\\nstale success. The claim determines the reconstruction span; a local\\nselected function does not require recreating the whole subject.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/EVALUATION.md#EVALUATION%2F6.%20Conformance%20of%20realisations\",\"start_line\":426},{\"end_line\":444,\"path\":\"standards/EVALUATION.md\",\"quote\":\"A construction outside the declared competence or\\nconfiguration envelope cannot indict generic method sufficiency\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/EVALUATION.md#EVALUATION%2F6.%20Conformance%20of%20realisations\",\"start_line\":443}],\"statement\":\"Failure to derive a conformant next layer indicates an upper-layer defect: unclear, contradictory, underspecified, insufficiently concrete/decomposable, or polluted with accidental lower-layer detail. Producing an artifact while hiding major unresolved ambiguity is insufficient. Reconstruction scope follows the claim, grants no restart authority and excuses no stale success; new material counterexamples challenge affected relations. After freeze compare to the mandatory governing semantic basis. Lawful alternatives permitted by that basis pass; subjective similarity is insufficient. Byte/structural identity, unique derivation, determinism and incumbent equality are not generic comparison criteria. Out-of-envelope constructions cannot indict generic method sufficiency.\",\"uncertainty\":\"No competence envelope, frozen construction or reconstruction is evaluated here.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:3d421d7bc783da5307c013ca04e91296","key":1132,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:1d08ca4a4088f38ec8f6103c6776ca87\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:3d421d7bc783da5307c013ca04e91296\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"Returning a task that builds or assesses one successor member against its predecessor.\"],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":464,\"path\":\"standards/EVALUATION.md\",\"quote\":\"Relocation reported as reduction, or\\nconservation claimed from unchanged bytes, misreports the claim (§1, P1,\\nP6). The three heads stay separate in the return as the rungs of the\\nladder do above; a frame for a reconstruction task binds this\\ndistinction.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/EVALUATION.md#EVALUATION%2F6.%20Conformance%20of%20realisations%2FReturn%20of%20a%20reconstruction\",\"start_line\":460}],\"statement\":\"State each of semantic conservation, demonstrated reduction and mere relocation under separate heads with its own claim and evidence; claim none by byte or size measure. Read both texts against RELEASE §9 dispositions for conservation; trace the same deciding path in both versions under a declared cost measure and tradeoffs for reduction. Relocation without a traced path change is not reduction, and unchanged bytes do not establish conservation. Reconstruction task frames bind this separation.\",\"uncertainty\":\"RELEASE §9's complete conservation reading is external.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:195ecdea023e6febb1dd300ea03bab79","key":1133,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:37fb4b17481814bac5a73cccf5a35e94\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:195ecdea023e6febb1dd300ea03bab79\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":488,\"path\":\"standards/EVALUATION.md\",\"quote\":\"Evidence for one claim is never reported as a result for another\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/EVALUATION.md#EVALUATION%2F6.%20Conformance%20of%20realisations%2FFoundation%20to%20law%3A%20conformance%2C%20equivalence%20and%20qualification\",\"start_line\":488}],\"statement\":\"Several realisations may conform without unique derivation or incumbent equality. Material behavioural alternatives require owner-declared latitude or repair before decision-complete design is claimed. Conformance entails neither behaviour identity outside the specification nor equal cost. Each equivalence rung needs its own evidence; none implies another. Categorical equivalence additionally requires applicable Formal-fragment items, a quasi-inverse functor and natural isomorphisms on a stated domain; structure preservation is a further claim. The claim author owns domain, workloads and architecture H; the specification owner owns interpretation contract/latitude. Evidence cannot be relabelled as another claim's result.\",\"uncertainty\":\"Detailed rung definitions and applicable Formal-fragment requirements are referenced but not supplied.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:ec009b23a31867060820077168cb445e","key":1134,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:f35cd95bc2a52b766d1979572061b2cf\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:ec009b23a31867060820077168cb445e\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":489,\"path\":\"standards/EVALUATION.md\",\"quote\":\"Reconstruction of an accepted relation may reuse its exact current basis and sufficient evidence after checking applicability and invalidation; reconstructability requires a correct route, not its execution at every use, grants no restart authority and does not excuse stale success\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/EVALUATION.md#EVALUATION%2F6.%20Conformance%20of%20realisations%2FFoundation%20to%20law%3A%20conformance%2C%20equivalence%20and%20qualification\",\"start_line\":489},{\"end_line\":499,\"path\":\"standards/EVALUATION.md\",\"quote\":\"the reduction measure, its baselines and the traced paths: the candidate's design, declared before the trace\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/EVALUATION.md#EVALUATION%2F6.%20Conformance%20of%20realisations%2FFoundation%20to%20law%3A%20conformance%2C%20equivalence%20and%20qualification\",\"start_line\":499}],\"statement\":\"Failure of competent derivation indicates an upper-layer defect; hiding major unresolved ambiguity at a boundary is insufficient. Reconstruction span follows the claim. Reuse requires exact current basis, sufficient evidence and applicability/invalidation checks; reconstructability requires a correct route, not execution at every use, and grants neither restart authority nor stale success. New material counterexamples still challenge accepted relations. Conservation, demonstrated reduction and relocation need separate evidence; no byte/size measure proves any. RELEASE supplies conservation reading/dispositions, while candidate design declares reduction measures, baselines and traced paths before tracing.\",\"uncertainty\":\"Layer diagnoses and detailed conservation rules depend on unsupplied SPEC_METHOD and RELEASE sections.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:ed9313e92bf96dff5c1519cec82e9cad","key":1135,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:6a2c32a018781528793f87b832b7cdf2\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:37fb4b17481814bac5a73cccf5a35e94\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:ed9313e92bf96dff5c1519cec82e9cad\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"A frozen construction is being compared.\"],\"exceptions\":[\"Reference equivalence is required when the governing basis explicitly requires it.\"],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":490,\"path\":\"standards/EVALUATION.md\",\"quote\":\"after freeze, the evaluator compares the frozen result with the mandatory governing semantic basis. A separately held expected or reference outcome is optional and non-authoritative evidence; a lawful alternative construction the basis permits passes.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/EVALUATION.md#EVALUATION%2F6.%20Conformance%20of%20realisations%2FFoundation%20to%20law%3A%20conformance%2C%20equivalence%20and%20qualification\",\"start_line\":490}],\"statement\":\"Comparison uses the mandatory governing semantic basis. Separately held references are optional non-authoritative evidence; lawful alternatives permitted by the basis pass. Subjective similarity is insufficient. Byte/structural identity, uniqueness, determinism and incumbent equality are not generic criteria. Out-of-envelope construction cannot indict generic method sufficiency.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:56b9b5835adad2d84643919cd9b6ada0","key":1136,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:9b0624c77d9b5a044328250e6c6a92a3\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:56b9b5835adad2d84643919cd9b6ada0\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":498,\"path\":\"standards/EVALUATION.md\",\"quote\":\"counts the context transferred across every delegated actor, and keeps its acceptance criteria independent of the constructing actor\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/EVALUATION.md#EVALUATION%2F6.%20Conformance%20of%20realisations%2FFoundation%20to%20law%3A%20conformance%2C%20equivalence%20and%20qualification\",\"start_line\":498},{\"end_line\":497,\"path\":\"standards/EVALUATION.md\",\"quote\":\"A case passes when the expected distinction is observed and no coerced success appears anywhere in the result\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/EVALUATION.md#EVALUATION%2F6.%20Conformance%20of%20realisations%2FFoundation%20to%20law%3A%20conformance%2C%20equivalence%20and%20qualification\",\"start_line\":497}],\"statement\":\"Running a case is not passing it: only an independent assessor records a pass, requiring the expected distinction and no coerced success anywhere. A case impossible to run with its declared subject is explicitly not run, has no result and receives no core value; this revision receives no pass without its run and assessment. Before each bounded-construction run declare per-actor context cap and total-work budget, count context transferred across every delegated actor, and keep acceptance criteria independent of the constructor. The source locates these declarations in eight CONFORMANCE §2 trials, with context/resource measurement owned by ACTIVATION.\",\"uncertainty\":\"Required-basis-over-cap cases, varied task ordering for probabilistic repetition, case inventories and measurement procedures are cross-references, not supplied specifications.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:80de64c15f110e717d84d9bdec09bd3a","key":1137,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:a317b21a815ed3243d75442184df803b\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:80de64c15f110e717d84d9bdec09bd3a\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":553,\"path\":\"standards/EVALUATION.md\",\"quote\":\"9. Result-consumption test: can a declared consumer use the closed result\\n   without importing hidden frame context?\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/EVALUATION.md#EVALUATION%2F7.%20Qualification%20of%20frames%20and%20of%20the%20method%2FFrame%20qualification\",\"start_line\":552}],\"statement\":\"Minimum qualification asks nine questions: can competent actors produce declared-algebra results for representative in-domain evaluations; can fresh competent actors reconstruct activation from declared packets without hidden history; do material changes affect results where expected; do excluded unrelated changes leave results stable where expected; does stale/mismatched/ambiguous basis invalidate or refuse evaluation; does selection preserve semantic/decision authority and exact inherited operation authority for every material construction, transformation, admission, publication or mutation; are claimed representative historical/constructed violations detected; can the actor class hold and operate the frame within its envelope; and can a declared consumer use the closed result without hidden context. Qualification binds exact revision, actor envelope, evaluation family, basis class and evidence conditions, never a generically named unevaluated population.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:faea489c17c8647588549da9859b7250","key":1138,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:a317b21a815ed3243d75442184df803b\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:faea489c17c8647588549da9859b7250\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":575,\"path\":\"standards/EVALUATION.md\",\"quote\":\"A size measurement, or any byte or token\\nthreshold, establishes fit and nothing about attention; a frame that fits\\nis not thereby adequately attended.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/EVALUATION.md#EVALUATION%2F7.%20Qualification%20of%20frames%20and%20of%20the%20method%2FFrame%20qualification\",\"start_line\":571}],\"statement\":\"Fit and adequate attention are evaluated separately. Context fit uses ACTIVATION §2 step 3 measurement against capacity; other dimensions follow RF-014. Attention requires declared-class actors actually applying the frame to declared tasks/conditions, assessed against governing-source expectations recorded before results are opened, using an independent assessor where the claim requires one. Actual-use evidence binds revision, class, tasks and conditions and provides no universal attention score. Fit is necessary under finite attention but never qualifies attention. Time, spend and other limits belong to the selected execution binding under ACTIVATION §6. Logical review and unassessed runs do not supply actual-use evidence for the revision.\",\"uncertainty\":\"The other envelope dimensions, measurement procedures and independent-assessment applicability rules are not fully supplied.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:777aec27e778d4fc79023d2355d433e0","key":1139,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:6a2c32a018781528793f87b832b7cdf2\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:777aec27e778d4fc79023d2355d433e0\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"Generic method sufficiency is being qualified.\"],\"exceptions\":[\"Withholding until freeze is conditional on earlier exposure compromising reconstructive independence.\"],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":603,\"path\":\"standards/EVALUATION.md\",\"quote\":\"The constructor, freeze,\\nassessor, acceptance and release protocols are supplied by the governing\\nauthority; this member does not select a particular protocol for those\\nroles.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/EVALUATION.md#EVALUATION%2F7.%20Qualification%20of%20frames%20and%20of%20the%20method%2FMethod%20self-qualification\",\"start_line\":600}],\"statement\":\"A fresh competent constructor works within declared capability/context/configuration using only declared ordinary method, authority surfaces and trial subjects. An independently authorised evaluator has declared governing basis and comparison predicate. Material expected/reference outcomes, source exemplars, incumbents, author memory and ad hoc rescue are withheld until construction freezes wherever early exposure would compromise independence; comparison then evaluates the frozen result against the mandatory relation population under §6. RF-013 owns activation reconstructability; governing authority supplies constructor, freeze, assessor, acceptance and release protocols.\",\"uncertainty\":\"The source assigns protocol ownership but selects no concrete protocol.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:fa98d4349e639c24a91066e18be8e320","key":1140,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:6a2c32a018781528793f87b832b7cdf2\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:fa98d4349e639c24a91066e18be8e320\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":619,\"path\":\"standards/EVALUATION.md\",\"quote\":\"| material composition | a case requiring cross-frame execution declares composition, order where material, closure, failure and the conservation of semantic, operation and decision authority; a case not requiring composition stays uncomposed |\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/EVALUATION.md#EVALUATION%2F7.%20Qualification%20of%20frames%20and%20of%20the%20method%2FMethod%20self-qualification\",\"start_line\":619}],\"statement\":\"Required representative observations cover every claimed function/failure relation: declare derives a frame set from governed workspace, outcome, practices, capability envelopes, evaluation inventory, authority and residual boundary, refusing missing authority/evaluation basis; activate succeeds on exact subject/basis and capable actor, while stale, ambiguous, topology-mismatched, unauthorised or capability-incompatible cases refuse or return applicable closed pressure; evaluate exhibits satisfied, falsified, indeterminate, out_of_frame and invalid_basis, material sensitivity and established irrelevance stability; conjoin decides compatible closed results by declared rule, returns conflict for conflict, indeterminate for mandatory indeterminacy, invalid_basis for basis mismatch, and cause-appropriate declared veto/deferral outcomes without flattening frame meaning; translate preserves coordinates/provenance, states loss and refuses identity/basis/authority/equality mismatch; audit_coverage maps evaluation, interaction, semantic/operation/decision authority, failure, capability and required independent/assurance-independent coverage to capable frames or explicit residuals, never closing by artifact/actor count; revise produces declared deltas for historical failure, topology/evidence/capability changes and identifies every affected prior activation/result/conjunction/coverage claim; result consumption needs no hidden context or authority, otherwise output insufficiency is reconstructability failure; material composition declares composition, material order, closure, failure and authority conservation, while cases needing none stay uncomposed.\",\"uncertainty\":\"Full method-function definitions, closed-pressure algebra and cause-specific veto/deferral outcomes remain with referenced owners.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:8624e7e4ed5f315c8bf2e00db2d70af7","key":1141,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:6a2c32a018781528793f87b832b7cdf2\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:8624e7e4ed5f315c8bf2e00db2d70af7\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":629,\"path\":\"standards/EVALUATION.md\",\"quote\":\"an unevaluated function or branch stays open rather than\\ninheriting a whole-method verdict (P6; §1).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/EVALUATION.md#EVALUATION%2F7.%20Qualification%20of%20frames%20and%20of%20the%20method%2FMethod%20self-qualification\",\"start_line\":628}],\"statement\":\"A valid declaration and coverage result establish only declare and evaluated audit_coverage, with no implication for other relations. Each relation needs representative positive, boundary and falsifying cases. Every verdict states exact functions, revisions, actor envelopes, basis classes, result branches and evidence populations evaluated; unevaluated functions/branches remain open. Prior exemplars after freeze are optional comparison evidence, not mandatory answers unless the governing basis explicitly requires equivalence.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:c8d4abcb033916706ed7a1ea53788d96","key":1142,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:6a2c32a018781528793f87b832b7cdf2\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:c8d4abcb033916706ed7a1ea53788d96\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"Derived guidance has changed or a native, mechanical or operational claim is made.\"],\"exceptions\":[],\"gro