e-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:a5c248981dcf48ebaeee053e8dd9a9d8","key":1188,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:7aa04f0e75b58f269a74a0246551af0f\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:7afbe7f5297c074ec9d4d63e0240a1f4\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:a5c248981dcf48ebaeee053e8dd9a9d8\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"Executive disposes consumed results.\"],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1296,\"path\":\"standards/EXECUTIVE_BASELINE.md\",\"quote\":\"A repair creates\\na new candidate, and an affected review is reactivated against it.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/EXECUTIVE_BASELINE.md#EXECUTIVE_BASELINE%2F12.%20Complete%20engagement%20transition%2F7.%20Executive%20disposes%20and%20checkpoints\",\"start_line\":1284}],\"statement\":\"Verify every consumed result's current subject/basis, revalidate complete Product view and current MVP/release mandate, apply declared conjunction, assign priority, record promotion-boundary effect and act on exactly one disposition within grant. Repair creates a new candidate and reactivates affected review. Acceptance widens neither outcome nor authority to an unselected successor. Severity selects neither priority nor blocking, and priority waives no hard stop. EVALUATION §5 owns blocking; Executive records current-boundary determination. Unsupported technical assessments return through new/refined activation instead of silent rewriting.\",\"uncertainty\":\"The complete blocking conditions and disposition definitions remain external.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:54cf37fee2b9015e30d2a3894359a9fc","key":1189,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:7aa04f0e75b58f269a74a0246551af0f\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:de33d953ef86a7c2be96a9c8d96ca5fa\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:7afbe7f5297c074ec9d4d63e0240a1f4\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:54cf37fee2b9015e30d2a3894359a9fc\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"Promotion-boundary effect is determined.\"],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1320,\"path\":\"standards/EXECUTIVE_BASELINE.md\",\"quote\":\"| an unsupported or materially incomplete technical assessment | a capable evaluation is reactivated, or `indeterminate` is kept; Reviewer evidence is not rewritten |\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/EXECUTIVE_BASELINE.md#EXECUTIVE_BASELINE%2F12.%20Complete%20engagement%20transition%2FPromotion%20constraint%20projection\",\"start_line\":1320}],\"statement\":\"The EVALUATION §5 table is projected with Executive as decision owner over valid falsification of a mandatory non-waivable-hard-stop claim; other findings meeting any of its four conditions, including below-cutoff findings; findings meeting none; and observations outside exact evaluated claim. Executive determines blocking from exact affected claim, current Product mandate, hard stops and Product-owned cutoff policy. For unsupported or materially incomplete assessment, reactivate capable evaluation or retain indeterminate; never rewrite Reviewer evidence.\",\"uncertainty\":\"The four EVALUATION §5 conditions and their complete table are not included; no missing blocking outcome is invented.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:7a4279776384b52d8de7ffc14b6d5b65","key":1190,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:f0b2a89787d06e354d150881b25848f7\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:7a4279776384b52d8de7ffc14b6d5b65\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"A handoff projection is used.\"],\"exceptions\":[\"Direct engagement substitutes actual granting/result authority for Executive where no Executive activation exists.\"],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1349,\"path\":\"standards/EXECUTIVE_BASELINE.md\",\"quote\":\"| work result | Worker to Executive | result variant, exact subject if any, transition evidence, non-changes, each intended external effect with its ACTIVATION §3 Effects value (`completed`, `not_effected` or `completion_unknown`), residuals, stop basis | ACTIVATION §3, §5 and §7 |\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/EXECUTIVE_BASELINE.md#EXECUTIVE_BASELINE%2F13.%20Handoff%20projection\",\"start_line\":1333}],\"statement\":\"Minimum handoffs preserve: Executive→Worker exact intake/basis/cone, applicable grant/subject/write territory, frames, evidence, exclusions, stop/re-entry; activation relation→Executive attempted frame/subject/basis/actor, cause and failed predicate, evidence/reconfiguration pressure, no Worker result; Worker→Executive variant, subject if any, transition evidence, non-changes, every intended external effect with completed/not_effected/completion_unknown, residuals/stop basis; Executive→Reviewer exact subject/claim/composition/population/severity/authority/independence/invalidation; Reviewer→Executive verdict basis/evidence/findings/counterexamples/triage/residuals/invalidation, no priority/disposition; Executive or declared parent→capable specialist exact evaluation/subject/basis/material map/envelope/evidence/authority/dependencies/exclusions/consumer/invalidation; specialist→Executive/declared conjunction/exact parent closed result/activation/basis/evidence/source routes/residuals/invalidation, no implicit continuation; Executive→existing work authority and any next activation consumed results/triage/current mandate/priority/boundary effect/grant/disposition/checkpoint/residuals/already-authorised action. Owners remain REFERENCE_FRAME §5/§11, ACTIVATION §1/§3/§5/§7, EVALUATION §3/§4/§7, exact specialist owner and Product triage policy as applicable. Flattening across candidates, processes, episodes, configurations, populations or bases establishes no relation; declare needed equality/translation under REFERENCE_FRAME §6. Direct engagement retains the same coordinates and gains neither implicit Reviewer activation nor new decision authority.\",\"uncertainty\":\"Referenced owning-law details are not reproduced.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:01a4b8b4949e8b8a3c21007395025770","key":1191,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:eb37ce9d560740bee6081f30b5e7db1b\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:82f113a16ea802824461602cdcb694b0\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:ab9ace3a757b796239f24bcaa97089ea\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:7aa04f0e75b58f269a74a0246551af0f\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:01a4b8b4949e8b8a3c21007395025770\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"Evaluations are material to the selected outcome.\"],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1384,\"path\":\"standards/EXECUTIVE_BASELINE.md\",\"quote\":\"Executive visibility is not coverage.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/EXECUTIVE_BASELINE.md#EXECUTIVE_BASELINE%2F14.%20Coverage%20application\",\"start_line\":1380}],\"statement\":\"Executive owns exact method/project/work basis; cone/configuration challenged by Worker/Reviewer; generic-family configuration; conjunction, priority, promotion effect/disposition; checkpoint/continuation under existing authority; and missing-frame response under pressure from any frame. Worker covers bounded realisation/self-review and candidate/transition evidence. User-outcome and authoritative runnable-path evaluations use Worker execution/self-review and Reviewer where required; integration and module laws use Worker/Reviewer according to claim; obsolete/rival-path absence uses Worker deletion evidence and required exact-subject Reviewer challenge; independent assessment/triage uses Reviewer. Inputs respectively include complete current authority; execution-unit and design conservation law plus domain/identity/dependency/implementation/history; twelve-family declarations/acquisition/dispositions; accepted design and material foundation selection; exact identity/evidence; UAT Product/requirement/UX/identity/install/acceptance; end-to-end composition/authority/lifecycle/persistence/recovery/replay/negative reachability; integration participants/carriers/state/configuration/failure/recovery; unit ontology/carrier inventory/public contracts/algebra/calculation/state machines/invariants/module combinations; separate production and assurance/source closure graphs plus package/consumer/mutation/sabotage/reconstruction/history; live assurance and Product severity; exact closed mandatory results and Product triage; current Goals/Product/release; and REFERENCE_FRAME §8/§10. Every material evaluation needs capable frame, admissible evidence and semantic/decision owners; every material construction/transformation/admission/publication/mutation additionally needs existing operation owner and exact grant.\",\"uncertainty\":\"Detailed external testing and coverage laws remain referenced.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:e02b362cd44dd04b4d9c6f3f149dd804","key":1192,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:7e0e873e6fcb53c802e77f7e3547b545\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:7aa04f0e75b58f269a74a0246551af0f\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:e02b362cd44dd04b4d9c6f3f149dd804\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"A gap can change evaluation.\"],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1412,\"path\":\"standards/EXECUTIVE_BASELINE.md\",\"quote\":\"| 8. another frame required | only when questions 1 to 7 do not close the gap, a frame is added or revised |\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/EXECUTIVE_BASELINE.md#EXECUTIVE_BASELINE%2F15.%20Missing-frame%20and%20re-entry%20application\",\"start_line\":1407}],\"statement\":\"Apply all questions in order: correct declared frame activated; exact subject/basis; actor inside capability envelope including required independence; admissible evidence; missing material variable/invariant, asked only after required specialist inputs are verified supplied; missing conjunction/translation; wrong/incomplete family; need for another frame, adding/revising only if questions 1–7 do not close the gap. Discovery changing Product, requirement, identity, lifecycle, authority, public contract or accepted design requires re_enter to its existing owner. Enlarging Executive frame cannot repair an upstream authority gap.\",\"uncertainty\":\"Only the supplied diagnostic readings are interpreted; referenced full diagnostic law remains external.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:447c87af22c2e182ece4836856f55691","key":1193,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa4