r authorship/direction while retaining independence for that contribution; changed subject/basis inheriting prior verdict without applicability; coordinate flattening; unowned local axioms authority; profile as peer execution/independence/assurance constitution; silent method-law change; consumer architecture as universal; testing labels/runner replacing exact frame/subject/claim/population/oracle/path/falsifier; counts of tests/assertions/snapshots/lines/branches/functions as Product confidence/closure; implementation-shaped units as independent design/architecture/integration/install/user proof; mocking away interface/persistence/orchestration/authority/configuration/user complexity and counting unit coverage; helper tests as canonical module-algebra or Product-composition proof; equal output without authoritative path or with reachable rival; sunny path replacing population/strength justification/failure coverage/residuals; UAT unavailable user capabilities/information/setup/interfaces; harness/fixture/proof/expected builder reconstructing owner truth as subject; unsupported single-owner localisation despite joint/alternative/no bounded frontier or localisation authorising wider repair; mutation/sabotage/fixture/capture changing subject without isolation/restoration/revalidation; aggregate green hiding missing/conflicting testing results; family as required component/actor/service/file/runtime/stage/owner, omission for absent names or flattening distinct family/result relations; Reviewer priority/block/repair/activation; Executive collapsing severity, priority, frame result, boundary effect and disposition.\",\"uncertainty\":\"The external defect-reporting versus repair-authorship boundary remains referenced.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:37285ecd20b5e3e576c672fc172bb57a","key":1202,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:f8dada96e1fc49226a473a335e1d40b9\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:37285ecd20b5e3e576c672fc172bb57a\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"Baseline application to one exact outcome is claimed; only applicable branch obligations are evaluated.\"],\"exceptions\":[\"Project-defined configurations need not claim optional baseline conformance.\"],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1879,\"path\":\"standards/EXECUTIVE_BASELINE.md\",\"quote\":\"A project has applied this baseline to one outcome when\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/EXECUTIVE_BASELINE.md#EXECUTIVE_BASELINE%2F22.%20Closure\",\"start_line\":1806}],\"statement\":\"Application requires existing-authority admission/projection of exact basis; complete selected method including REFERENCE_FRAME governing; finite engagement frames available and activated only when applicable, neither hierarchy nor actors; refusal distinct from cause-selected single work result with single core mapping and declared consumer; review requirement determined by existing authority, coordinated activation by Executive and no unnecessary direct-branch activation; required review exact subject/population/verdict/triage/independence; Executive closed-result/triage consumption against full Product/current mandate with distinct severity/priority/result/boundary effect and existing disposition/continuation; every known material specialist evaluation/interaction covered or explicit residual; invalidation/rechart on frame/basis/capability/evidence/topology changes; exact existing-owner grant for material operation; no new execution authority/local constitution/actor topology/runtime/universal completeness; material testing claims assigned exact UAT/end-to-end/integration/unit or declared alternative; user claim binds user capability, exact Product, ordinary supported surface, environment/outcome; end-to-end binds runnable form and authoritative causal path, rejecting unknown/forbidden equal-output paths; material interface/Product factors have population, adequate strength, exercised matrix and residual combinations; unit law/public-contract evidence proportional to useful module-population discrimination rather than implementation size; positive runnable witnesses for required paths, production exclusion of obsolete/rival/fallback/bypass, assurance/source closure unable to supply false evidence or reintroduce removed paths, isolated test-only seams outside ordinary claims; counts/coverage/green do not replace Product/install/path/composition/user proof; assurance machinery preserves or revalidates subject; owner truth acquired at exact owner surface and checked with separately derived oracle without rival interpreter; counterexamples retain supported minimal unique/joint/alternative/indeterminate frontier; all twelve material families have declarations/acquisition and non-material/uncovered families authority-bound dispositions; every material seam preserves/translates identity/coordinate/basis/value-or-evidence/lifecycle/authority/provenance; no inferred consumer architecture/local topology/runtime/component roster.\",\"uncertainty\":\"Condition-based work-item closure itself remains owned by unsupplied TICKETS §7.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:0bfffaa859153d9ab5adc7608d6e4b74","key":1203,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:6ec8a2077a8e4407dbae4ef32cd2e567\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:bba66a69742d9ed73c7869959fc063e7\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:0bfffaa859153d9ab5adc7608d6e4b74\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":13,\"path\":\"standards/FOUNDATIONS.md\",\"quote\":\"A\\nrefinement names its owner here and never redefines it; a refinement of\\nresults maps each of its values into the core\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/FOUNDATIONS.md#FOUNDATIONS\",\"start_line\":11},{\"end_line\":40,\"path\":\"standards/FOUNDATIONS.md\",\"quote\":\"A premise is\\nnever presented as derived, and a hypothesis never as law\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/FOUNDATIONS.md#FOUNDATIONS%2F1.%20Vocabulary%20of%20standing\",\"start_line\":34}],\"statement\":\"Imported definitions are not redefined; refinements name their FOUNDATIONS owner and each refined result value maps into core. Recovered and independent commitments are adopted premises, derived commitments their consequences; premise cannot be presented as derived and hypothesis cannot be law. Foundational standing, result standing and successor disposition remain distinct. Every clause names its requiring principle P0–P6.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:bd18a3e2be5e6258fd5075b546049065","key":1204,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:7d30c17505ac92c5cce93774e45e6626\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:a31aad4a23047f64dc2ae6c9cc88ecd9\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:028479125fd2aebd66e8dbd97b743e8c\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:bd18a3e2be5e6258fd5075b546049065\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":71,\"path\":\"standards/FOUNDATIONS.md\",\"quote\":\"mixed bases need an explicit composite relation\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/FOUNDATIONS.md#FOUNDATIONS%2F2.%20Ontology\",\"start_line\":70},{\"end_line\":94,\"path\":\"standards/FOUNDATIONS.md\",\"quote\":\"actor capability may justify a different frame size or activation sequence and can neither waive an invariant nor widen authority\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/FOUNDATIONS.md#FOUNDATIONS%2F2.%20Ontology%2FFrame%20objects\",\"start_line\":88},{\"end_line\":196,\"path\":\"standards/FOUNDATIONS.md\",\"quote\":\"representation cannot create, widen or replace it\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/FOUNDATIONS.md#FOUNDATIONS%2F2.%20Ontology%2FThe%20frame%20tuple\",\"start_line\":195}],\"statement\":\"Equal representations do not establish equal meaning; object identity survives admissible state/encoding changes. Evidence availability creates neither semantic truth nor decision authority. Basis is immutable or has declared advancement detection and reevaluation conditions; mixed bases require explicit composition. Similar wording does not prove equal evaluation family, and equal names/values/shapes/locations/topological positions do not prove coordinate equality. Topology is preserved only if all material entities, relations, lifecycle spaces, authorities, capabilities, adjacencies and seams are preserved; changing any is topology mutation that may invalidate coordinates. Capability may change frame size/sequence but cannot waive invariants or widen authority. Declaration reuse does not prove activation correctness. Frame binding requires every material coordinate to resolve to exact source, subject, basis, authority, evidence route, actor envelope, result relation and invalidation condition; source-linked prose suffices and representation cannot create/widen/replace binding.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:abed4c1c4b36b626bcf41a7fbab69918","key":1205,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:cdbc87d83c3a1d696b268a09e5c6e022\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:abed4c1c4b36b626bcf41a7fbab69918\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":139,\"path\":\"standards/FOUNDATIONS.md\",\"quote\":\"Authority of any kind exists only by an\\nadmitted grant or an explicit authority decision of its owner, with an\\nidentifiable basis.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/FOUNDATIONS.md#FOUNDATIONS%2F2.%20Ontology%2FAuthority%20kinds\",\"start_line\":111}],\"statement\":\"Authority requires admitted grant or explicit owner decision on identifiable basis. Read-only evaluation declares no operation authority; effectful evaluation inherits exact owner grant rather than frame-created authority. Identity/capability/tools/access; names, labels, roles, capability strings, locators/paths; declaring/selecting/activating/executing frames or occupying roles; implementation reachability; evidence/payload shape or availability; checks/success/review/counts; copying/interpreting/encoding/evaluating/transporting/projecting/compressing/importing/acquiring; work-contract drafting/admission/retention beyond admitted contents; and composition/delegation/adapters/wrappers/registries create, widen, transfer or reconstruct no semantic/evaluation/operation/decision authority. The latter mechanisms may restrict or faithfully carry grants but cannot widen scope, add role, increase cardinality or change kind. Elevation, transfer, split, merge, proxy grant, revocation and retirement each require explicit authority decision and identifiable basis. Domain instances cite the shared rule rather than mint variants.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:06f050b8a9f247dd458576d82a7bbb88","key":1206,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:cdbc87d83c3a1d696b268a09e5c6e022\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:06f050b8a9f247dd458576d82a7bbb88\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"A human authority acts through a proxy.\"],\"exceptions\":[\"Direct human acceptance remains required wherever governing Product or release law requires it.\"],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":153,\"path\":\"standards/FOUNDATIONS.md\",\"quote\":\"A proxy acts only inside its existing grant.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/FOUNDATIONS.md#FOUNDATIONS%2F2.%20Ontology%2FAuthority%20kinds\",\"start_line\":144}],\"statement\":\"Proxy must be explicitly admitted, bounded and permitted by governing identity/authority law; proxy and human identities remain distinct. It cannot change outcome meaning, requirements, governing authority or accepted design: those re-enter owning relations. Proxy grants do not make constructor self-review independent, create unrelated runtime/domain authority or replace required direct human acceptance. IDENTITY §6 owns grant contents and ACTIVATION §1 owns allowable within-step decisions.\",\"uncertainty\":\"Grant-content and within-step decision laws are not supplied.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:ef800af0e0eda493751b06e26445b71a","key":1207,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:557308c7c90ed316b3c85ed43c6bcb23\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:ef800af0e0eda493751b06e26445b71a\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":247,\"path\":\"standards/FOUNDATIONS.md\",\"quote\":\"Equal version text does not collapse these objects. A selector or a\\nmutable carrier may move; a release cut never moves.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/FOUNDATIONS.md#FOUNDATIONS%2F2.%20Ontology%2FProduct%20lineage%20objects\",\"start_line\":245}],\"statement\":\"Do not call mutable source workspace a Product or confuse source project with immutable release cut/install. Builder role binds exact install without transferring meaning/authority or confusing authored Product. Product definition remains source authority rather than released artifact. Products may depend on products; installs may build successors or other products, as in bootstrap source→release P0→install P0→build P1 source→release P1. Candidate source, release subject, selector and cut remain distinct; co-location does not establish release membership and equal version text establishes no identity equality. Selectors/carriers may move, cuts never do.\",\"uncertainty\":\"SPEC_METHOD §6 and RELEASE §1/§2 applications and exact selector rules are external.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:79b83d4b8470d2cad73d7de4a87b0ef3","key":1208,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:b0d28fcdc19fd68081f6b530c2780343\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:79b83d4b8470d2cad73d7de4a87b0ef3\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"A member uses another member's defined concept.\"],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":333,\"path\":\"standards/FOUNDATIONS.md\",\"quote\":\"a missing\\nsource meaning, adoption or authority binding is an undeclared material\\nrelation, the ground of `out_of_frame`\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/FOUNDATIONS.md#FOUNDATIONS%2F2.%20Ontology%2FImports%20between%20members\",\"start_line\":329}],\"statement\":\"Use requires reference-only import, not redefinition. For each concept identify owner's name, owning textual section (not itself semantic authority), declared source bounded context or source member if none, target context/member, source→target direction and no loss. A collected declaration or point-of-use owning-section reference supplies these facts; proximity/equal spelling never imports. Changed, narrowed or lossy meaning is not import. Activation binds distinct member coordinates even under the same selected cut. Changes in member, basis, source declaration or adoption premise require fresh applicability. Missing source meaning, adoption or authority binding is reported before dependent reliance; dependent evaluation has out_of_frame ground. Changed member/basis with applicability unestablished has invalid_basis ground.\",\"uncertainty\":\"Full result algebra and external adoption laws are not supplied; the stated grounds remain distinct.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:52cda63f979e696f53343e22d355c775","key":1209,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:6fa6231a6a9a8b9b410e028e53f394b4\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:52cda63f979e696f53343e22d355c775\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[\"A Product may explicitly promote internal HOW into declared reusable structure within its authority.\"],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":469,\"path\":\"standards/FOUNDATIONS.md\",\"quote\":\"not theorems derived from finite capacity alone\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/FOUNDATIONS.md#FOUNDATIONS%2F3.%20Commitments\",\"start_line\":347}],\"statement\":\"Each commitment has exactly its stated standing; adopted domain premises are not derived from finite actor capacity. Particular rules need premises plus owned domain/policy choices; arguments create no authority. P0 deterministic checks/validation are evidence surfaces and may optimise/prove precise domain-local paths, but do not authorise framework/runtime absorption of domain strategy into constitutional law. Unconstrained probabilistic reasoning stays worker-internal and returns through boundary contracts, evidence, provenance and control truth. Prescribing strategy beyond that contract crosses authority. Profiles may bind the unit to a traversal unit as admissible external space under PROFILES §2. P4b records required non-reacquirable facts at their producing step, including authority, residual, judgment, frame-boundary, transition, successor-claim and referenced-evidence instances scoped by consumers. P5's named indeterminate/out_of_frame/invalid_basis values are declared result-family choices, not uniquely derived names.\",\"uncertainty\":\"External profiles, result family F3 and calculus applications are referenced only.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:6036a50c404c1098605eb4794356a85f","key":1210,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:2951160ca2da445ee90413367849a4a5\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:6036a50c404c1098605eb4794356a85f\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":498,\"path\":\"standards/FOUNDATIONS.md\",\"quote\":\"Feedback, a useful model and\\nlocally valid steps do not by themselves prove reachability, stability,\\noptimality or termination\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/FOUNDATIONS.md#FOUNDATIONS%2F3.%20Commitments%2FConstruction%20synthesis\",\"start_line\":496}],\"statement\":\"Finite capacity motivates bounded work while purpose, meaning, identity, compatibility, evidence and authority retain independent premises. Strategy selection and domain controls are owned added choices. Feedback, a useful model and locally valid steps alone prove neither reachability, stability, optimality nor termination.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:7801807b777b09db5cbd190fe14ca171","key":1211,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:e5540e29232bd5affc66513f588ca970\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:7801807b777b09db5cbd190fe14ca171\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"A material deciding-rule family is traced.\"],\"exceptions\":[\"Where no separate consumer applies, explicitly state that absence and its scope.\"],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":576,\"path\":\"standards/FOUNDATIONS.md\",\"quote\":\"A blank field or a generic referral establishes\\nneither coverage nor non-applicability.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/FOUNDATIONS.md#FOUNDATIONS%2F3.%20Commitments%2FFoundation%20to%20law\",\"start_line\":546}],\"statement\":\"Each material family has one table at its owning entry locus, starting labelled instance premises and one row per consequence. Premises name commitment standings and used instance premises; profiles also name imported families. Rule column links owner or explicitly marks external owning section, alternatively linked external consumers after table. Added-choice column contains only what premises leave open with owner or none, never the whole rule. Pillar cells are trace only: no premise, standing, choice ownership, axiom claim or finite-capacity derivation. Every family table has a consumer paragraph identifying row-specific linked loci or scoped absence; blanks/generic referrals prove neither coverage nor inapplicability. Tables and consumers add no determinations or records beyond owning rules. Consequences are arguments, not proofs of every clause; carriers, actor counts, numeric limits, optional adoption, release procedure and refinement values are owned choices. Index pillar cells union table-row contributions. Table pending traces no rules; pillar pending names no pillar. Partial traces cannot claim derivation of whole method.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:d17d4bd4d46053a9cfd6aee184eba224","key":1212,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:e5540e29232bd5affc66513f588ca970\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:d17d4bd4d46053a9cfd6aee184eba224\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":622,\"path\":\"standards/FOUNDATIONS.md\",\"quote\":\"| F22 | Assurance relations | [FOUNDATIONS §4 Assurance relations](#assurance-relations) | FOUNDATIONS §4 Preservation through construction, Assertions and observation, Parallel derivation and mutual assurance, Quantified assurance, Change impact and evidence reuse, Formal representation | 2, 3, 4, 6, 7, 9, 10 |\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/FOUNDATIONS.md#FOUNDATIONS%2F3.%20Commitments%2FFoundation%20to%20law\",\"start_line\":601}],\"statement\":\"Index mappings (family: table; accounted scope; pillars) are: F1 Frames/context: REFERENCE_FRAME §1; REFERENCE_FRAME, ACTIVATION §2, FOUNDATIONS frame objects/authority/disjointness/tuple; 1–9. F2 Transitions/steps/configuration: ACTIVATION §1; §1 construction and §4 plus SPEC_METHOD §8 excluding delivery priority; 1,3,4,5,6,7,8,9. F3 Results/combination: FOUNDATIONS Results; §4 and import result grounds, ACTIVATION §3, RF-012, AC-007, EVALUATION §4; 3,4,6,7,9. F4 State/resumption/reuse: ACTIVATION §5; §5/§7; 2,4,5,6,7,9. F5 Proportionality/cost: ACTIVATION §6; §6 and SPEC_METHOD §8 priority; 1,4,5,6,7,8,9. F6 Claims/evidence/assessment/acceptance: EVALUATION §1; §1–§5; 1,2,3,6,7,8,9. F7 Conformance/equivalence/qualification: EVALUATION §6; §6/§7 and CONFORMANCE; 1,3,4,6,7,8,9. F8 Identity: IDENTITY §1; IDENTITY; 1,2,6,7,8,9. F9 a_c: AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS §1; that member; 1,2,3,4,6,7,8,9,10. F10 Constitutional chain/outcome/build tenant: SPEC_METHOD §2; §1–§3/§6/§9–§11; 1,2,3,4,5,6,8,9. F11 Change/ambiguity: SPEC_METHOD §4; §4/§5/§7; 1,2,3,4,5,6,7,9. F12 Project binding: PRODUCT_DEFINITION §1; that member and imports excluding F3 grounds; 1,2,4,6,7,8,9. F13 Work carriers: TICKETS §5; TICKETS and POSTING_GUIDE §2/§7/§9; 1,2,3,4,6,7,8,9. F14 Assurance/testing: ASSURANCE §1; ASSURANCE; 1,3,4,5,6,7,8,9. F15 Release/successor: RELEASE §1; RELEASE and lineage objects; 1,2,3,6,7,8,9. F16 Engagement: EXECUTIVE_BASELINE §3; that profile; 1–9. F17 Software design: DESIGN_MODULE §1; that member; 1,2,3,4,5,6,7,9. F18 Outcome-driven development: ODD §1; ODD; 1–9. F19 Traversal occurrence: its Position; that member; 1,2,3,4,6,7,8,9,10. F20 UX: UX §1; UX; 1–9. F21 World model: WORLD_MODEL §1; that member; 1,2,3,5,6,8,9,10. F22 Assurance relations: FOUNDATIONS Assurance relations; preservation, assertions/observation, parallel derivation, quantified assurance, change/reuse, formal representation; 2,3,4,6,7,9,10. No-table reasons: standing/ontology/commitments/format supply premises; synthesis decides no outcome; work boundary is P0 object; accounts is distinction traced at SPEC_METHOD §11 by F10; hypotheses are not law; PROFILES owns family-import premises and indexes profile-owned traces; posting/writing conventions are guide-owned policy; glossary is locator; README/templates/schemas/plugins own no determination.\",\"uncertainty\":\"Index entries identify trace locations, not supplied rule bodies or verified coverage.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:22939679ef8b1bb28b95e0c45b220156","key":1213,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:03892680a0099e23b65aaa50c3aad6e6\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:22939679ef8b1bb28b95e0c45b220156\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":665,\"path\":\"standards/FOUNDATIONS.md\",\"quote\":\"An inaccessible or insufficient reference is a residual,\\nnot success.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/FOUNDATIONS.md#FOUNDATIONS%2F4.%20Algebra\",\"start_line\":651}],\"statement\":\"s₂∘s₁ exists only under P4a, carries both steps' produced facts and combines results under declared conjunction. RF-010 owns when composition law is necessary versus separate closed results supplied to one conjunction/decision rule. Every transformation records preserved, introduced and removed material, external resolution witnesses and residuals. A reference conserves a relation only if owner, exact selector, authenticity, availability and completeness support the same consuming decision; inaccessible/insufficient reference is residual, not success. Projection cannot trim required members for carrier/budget. Computational similarity only proposes commonisation, never adjudicates identity/authority; shared implementation preserves each instance's responsibility and binding.\",\"uncertainty\":\"Detailed conjunction, RF-010 and AC conservation/projection rules remain external.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:65fb7d175d956c3809dc59bf9ea38e30","key":1214,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:03892680a0099e23b65aaa50c3aad6e6\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:4bc9faf98ce709b8d6d49d1eb9109591\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:65fb7d175d956c3809dc59bf9ea38e30\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"A categorical claim is made about the method or a construction.\"],\"exceptions\":[\"Each demonstration component applies only insofar as relevant to that claim.\"],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":701,\"path\":\"standards/FOUNDATIONS.md\",\"quote\":\"A\\ncategorical statement without the demonstration it requires is a\\nhypothesis:\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/FOUNDATIONS.md#FOUNDATIONS%2F4.%20Algebra\",\"start_line\":694}],\"statement\":\"Establishment requires stated objects, arrows, arrow equality, identity for each object, associative composition and identity units; maps defined on objects and arrows and called functors only after identity/composition preservation is proved; laws/records/maps represented in a_c with premises, consequences and choices distinct, respecting AC-020 identity separation and EVALUATION §2 structural-check limits; supporting evidence and scope distinguishing mechanical checks, mathematical arguments and independently specified-oracle tests. Record unresolved matters separately, not as fourth support kind. EVALUATION §6 owns differences among conformance/equivalence/preservation; ACTIVATION §4 owns licensed refinement/rewrite preservation. Without required demonstration a categorical statement is hypothesis, not law. Definition alone asserts no categorical functor.\",\"uncertainty\":\"No required proof is supplied for H1.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:18384a8ca581c8c3e3797e8edb2654ec","key":1215,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:73f26e79b171732285e45607615def72\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:9f8b2905240c9cb93ab890acc6dd7e24\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:1e617d4a71ceb9be3d7c064bf93039d6\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:18384a8ca581c8c3e3797e8edb2654ec\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":750,\"path\":\"standards/FOUNDATIONS.md\",\"quote\":\"Only\\n`satisfied` establishes the predicate. `falsified` establishes that the\\npredicate fails and names the counterexample. `indeterminate`,\\n`out_of_frame` and `invalid_basis` establish neither, and each names what\\nwould decide: the evidence, the missing relation or capability with its\\nowner where the subject gives one, or the basis repair. By support for the\\npredicate, `satisfied` stands above each other value, and the other four\\nare not ordered among themselves.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/FOUNDATIONS.md#FOUNDATIONS%2F4.%20Algebra%2FResults\",\"start_line\":743},{\"end_line\":762,\"path\":\"standards/FOUNDATIONS.md\",\"quote\":\"- an evaluation that was not performed stays distinct from one whose\\n  evidence cannot decide: it has no\\n  [closed result](ACTIVATION.md#7-closed-result-and-reuse), and it is never mapped\\n  to `indeterminate` or to any other core value;\\n- an effect whose completion is unknown never maps to no effect or to\\n  completed.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/FOUNDATIONS.md#FOUNDATIONS%2F4.%20Algebra%2FResults\",\"start_line\":757}],\"statement\":\"Every performed evaluation returns one core value or exactly mapped refinement and records its evaluated predicate, core value and original domain outcome. Domain meaning remains with the defining member/profile/Product; consumers needing its distinctions read the domain outcome. Result standing concerns the predicate and differs from commitment standing: only satisfied establishes it, falsified establishes failure with its counterexample, and the other three establish neither and identify deciding evidence, missing relation/capability and its given owner, or basis repair. No mapping or refinement raises standing: failed/falsified or undecidable outcomes cannot become success; non-performance maps to no core value; unknown effect completion cannot become no effect or completion. Actors cannot report evaluations they did not perform. Failed, indeterminate, out-of-frame, out-of-scope and invalid-basis outcomes keep their declared outcomes rather than being coerced to satisfied.\",\"uncertainty\":\"Specific domain mappings, including out-of-scope outcomes, require their defining owners.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:6b49c45d399b17bfcb136b1123f7cc30","key":1216,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:9f8b2905240c9cb93ab890acc6dd7e24\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:6b49c45d399b17bfcb136b1123f7cc30\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"A finer vocabulary or further split by cause is defined.\"],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":790,\"path\":\"standards/FOUNDATIONS.md\",\"quote\":\"The refinement names the question it\\nanswers and the predicate its mapping is for, and maps every refined value\\nto exactly one core value. No outcome exists outside the core; a\\nrefinement adds no core value and keeps the pressure of `indeterminate`,\\n`out_of_frame` and `invalid_basis` explicit. Where a refined value would\\nmap to one of two core values according to its cause, the cause is part of\\nthe refined value and each resulting value maps once (P5, P1). A further\\nrefinement, by a member, profile, project or adopting Product, may split a\\nrefined value by cause. The parent-value rule governs every such split:\\neach child value names its parent value and its cause and keeps its\\nparent's core value; a child that needs a different core value needs a\\ndifferent parent value, which only the owner of the parent declares;\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/FOUNDATIONS.md#FOUNDATIONS%2F4.%20Algebra%2FResults\",\"start_line\":779}],\"statement\":\"Declare the question, mapping predicate and exactly one core value for every refined outcome, adding no core values and preserving explicit indeterminate, out_of_frame and invalid_basis pressure. Include cause in the refined value whenever cause changes its mapping. Each child names parent and cause and retains the parent's core value; only the parent owner may declare a different parent needed for a different mapping. A child cannot inherit satisfied from a non-satisfied parent. Mappings are stated where values are defined; ACTIVATION §3 owns admission, activation and step refinements.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:8b48c39043d255467adbb114760e24fb","key":1217,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:73f26e79b171732285e45607615def72\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:1e617d4a71ceb9be3d7c064bf93039d6\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:8b48c39043d255467adbb114760e24fb\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"Determining the boundary between undeclared capability, undecidable evidence and an unexercised declared capability.\"],\"exceptions\":[\"When undeclared relations/capabilities and insufficient evidence both apply, out_of_frame and indeterminate each have a lawful ground; the returned value must name its own ground.\",\"Failure to exercise a declared capability does not suppress a sufficient evaluation or applicable judgment supported without it.\"],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":832,\"path\":\"standards/FOUNDATIONS.md\",\"quote\":\"Where the\\n  claim also depends on an undeclared relation or capability,\\n  `out_of_frame` and `indeterminate` each have a lawful ground; the result\\n  names the value it returns and that ground, and this boundary excludes\\n  neither (P5).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/FOUNDATIONS.md#FOUNDATIONS%2F4.%20Algebra%2FResults\",\"start_line\":828},{\"end_line\":849,\"path\":\"standards/FOUNDATIONS.md\",\"quote\":\"In either case\\n  the unexercised part, B above, has no result: in every conjunction over\\n  it, it is a planned assessment without a closed result, and the known\\n  failure A survives with it\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/FOUNDATIONS.md#FOUNDATIONS%2F4.%20Algebra%2FResults\",\"start_line\":846}],\"statement\":\"A required material relation or evaluator capability absent from the activated frame grounds out_of_frame regardless of what was exercised; identify the missing item, its owner where supplied and reconfiguration pressure. A dependent term left undefined is an undeclared material relation because its meaning can change the result outside declared inputs. Evidence unable to decide grounds indeterminate and identifies deciding evidence as residual uncertainty. A declared but unexercised capability has no core value of its own. Return any independently sufficient evaluation or applicable judgment with evidence, verdict and residual uncertainty; an exercised part falsifying A in A and B remains falsified despite agreement. If no sufficient evaluation exists because the capability was not exercised, there is no evaluation result; construction availability carries incomplete and work state carries the capability residual. The unexercised part remains a planned-assessment gap in either case, and the step stop value never substitutes for the evaluation result.\",\"uncertainty\":\"The supplied source expressly permits either grounded value when missing declaration and undecidable evidence coexist.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:fc9cce78019b80f96eb89327c8253735","key":1218,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:065709d4630efac07de8bfd91abef267\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:fc9cce78019b80f96eb89327c8253735\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"The applicable subject-defined rule is invoked.\"],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":875,\"path\":\"standards/FOUNDATIONS.md\",\"quote\":\"for an evaluation that depends on a concept imported from another member, a missing source meaning, adoption or authority binding is a relation the frame does not declare, and a changed member or basis whose applicability is not re-established cannot support the evaluation\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/FOUNDATIONS.md#FOUNDATIONS%2F4.%20Algebra%2FResults\",\"start_line\":875},{\"end_line\":885,\"path\":\"standards/FOUNDATIONS.md\",\"quote\":\"a categorical claim is established only with its demonstration, and without it is a hypothesis\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/FOUNDATIONS.md#FOUNDATIONS%2F4.%20Algebra%2FResults\",\"start_line\":885}],\"statement\":\"Imported evaluation concepts require source meaning, adoption and authority binding; missing bindings ground out_of_frame, while changed member/basis applicability not re-established grounds invalid_basis. Composed steps exist only through typed composition and carry both steps' produced facts. Every transformation records preserved, introduced and removed facts, external witnesses and residuals, with fields owned by AC-013. A reference substitutes for a body only when it supports the same consuming decision; otherwise retain the shortfall as residual, never success, and do not trim required members for carrier or budget limits. Values may lawfully differ only by declared relation, not preference, probabilistic choice or human presence. Similar computation can propose shared machinery but establishes no identity or authority; each instance retains responsibility and binding. Categorical claims require demonstration or remain hypotheses. Consumers apply owner rules without adding decisions; RF-012, AC-007 and review rules add no core choices beyond lawful refinements.\",\"uncertainty\":\"The referenced import, composition, transformation and categorical-demonstration owners are not fully supplied.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:1bd11007d732232698faa6c92cff5322","key":1219,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:27e46433dafe1a605ba0856f6d082557\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:1bd11007d732232698faa6c92cff5322\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":950,\"path\":\"standards/FOUNDATIONS.md\",\"quote\":\"A conjunction with any item in the second or third input is never\\n`satisfied`. Its record names which kind of gap it has, not performed,\\nuncovered or both, and each item. An uncovered obligation is never\\nreported as satisfied or as an omitted planned assessment; a planned\\nassessment without a closed result is never reported as uncovered or as an\\n`indeterminate` component.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/FOUNDATIONS.md#FOUNDATIONS%2F4.%20Algebra%2FConjunction%20of%20results\",\"start_line\":945},{\"end_line\":991,\"path\":\"standards/FOUNDATIONS.md\",\"quote\":\"Every known failure (a `falsified` result with its\\ncounterexample), every planned assessment without a closed result and\\nevery uncovered obligation is carried with the composite and survives every\\njoin: combining conjunctions takes the union of known failures and of\\nplanned assessments without a closed result, and recomputes uncovered\\ncoverage over the combined obligations.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/FOUNDATIONS.md#FOUNDATIONS%2F4.%20Algebra%2FConjunction%20of%20results\",\"start_line\":981}],\"statement\":\"Any planned-assessment or uncovered-coverage gap prevents satisfied; record each item and its kind, never converting uncovered coverage into a satisfied or omitted planned assessment, or a missing planned result into uncovered coverage or an indeterminate component. Every join unions known failures and planned-assessment gaps and recomputes uncovered coverage over combined obligations. Agreement cannot discard a constraint or any contributor's material counterexample. Missing, wrong-subject, conflicted and indeterminate mandatory results remain unresolved, not replaced by aggregate satisfaction. Each component retains predicate and domain outcome; satisfaction of one predicate never satisfies another, and uncertain effects stay distinct from failures and undecided claims.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:6e5ce7bf7280bcc43b5470e25a49cb5e","key":1220,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:27e46433dafe1a605ba0856f6d082557\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:73f26e79b171732285e45607615def72\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:6e5ce7bf7280bcc43b5470e25a49cb5e\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"A held result or evaluation basis is stale, advanced, ambiguous, mismatched, or bound to another subject or basis.\"],\"exceptions\":[\"An evaluation may instead be reactivated on the current basis.\"],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":973,\"path\":\"standards/FOUNDATIONS.md\",\"quote\":\"- a component whose only held result is stale has no closed result\\n  applicable to the composite: on the basis the composite requires, its\\n  evaluation was not performed. It is a planned assessment without a\\n  closed result, in the second input, and a gap. Its stale value is\\n  neither counted as a returned result nor relabelled `invalid_basis` for\\n  the composite, and it stays in the record with its own basis;\\n- the declared basis relations disagree (Reported value below) only among\\n  returned results, each bound to the basis the composite requires of it,\\n  whose bases the declared rule requires to agree or to join in a coherent\\n  composite basis, and which do not.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/FOUNDATIONS.md#FOUNDATIONS%2F4.%20Algebra%2FConjunction%20of%20results\",\"start_line\":964}],\"statement\":\"A performed evaluation on an unsuitable subject/basis returns invalid_basis for its own predicate, which a receiving conjunction holds as a returned result. A component supported only by a stale held result has no performed evaluation on the composite-required basis and is a planned-assessment gap; retain its old result and original basis, but neither count it nor relabel it invalid_basis for the composite. Stale satisfied never contributes. Basis disagreement concerns only applicable returned results whose individually required bases fail the declared agreement or coherent-composition relation. Do not answer the same stale component both as a gap and as invalid_basis.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:6d05bf9f41c453fb97f3946485fd3b48","key":1221,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:27e46433dafe1a605ba0856f6d082557\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:efae46f9c8f159bf2892e36617e85953\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:6d05bf9f41c453fb97f3946485fd3b48\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1018,\"path\":\"standards/FOUNDATIONS.md\",\"quote\":\"Where\\nevery mandatory result\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/FOUNDATIONS.md#FOUNDATIONS%2F4.%20Algebra%2FConjunction%20of%20results\",\"start_line\":1017},{\"end_line\":1008,\"path\":\"standards/FOUNDATIONS.md\",\"quote\":\"Where a mandatory result is\\nnot `satisfied`, the conjunction\\nreports a non-satisfied value chosen by its declared rule from those\\nreturned; no universal order among the non-satisfied values exists, and\\nthe member or profile that applies the conjunction declares its own in\\nits declared rule.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/FOUNDATIONS.md#FOUNDATIONS%2F4.%20Algebra%2FConjunction%20of%20results\",\"start_line\":1003}],\"statement\":\"Satisfied requires every mandatory result satisfied with valid applicable evidence, agreeing declared basis relations, and no gaps; a material counterexample to a mandatory constraint or uncovered required obligation forbids success. If a mandatory returned result is non-satisfied, choose a non-satisfied returned value by the declared rule. If every mandatory returned result is satisfied but basis relations disagree, report invalid_basis and retain gaps by kind. If those results are satisfied, bases agree and a gap remains, report indeterminate for the composite predicate, retaining gap kinds without assigning that value to missing components. If every mandatory result is satisfied, bases agree and no gap remains, any material counterexample to a mandatory constraint falsifies the conjunction regardless of contributor; otherwise use the declared rule over mandatory results. Nonmandatory falsified results always remain recorded with their predicates. Conjunction transfers no contributor's semantic authority.\",\"uncertainty\":\"Which non-satisfied returned value prevails is intentionally left to the declared rule.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:2dcb3bcd1139544ed3ee32439c757dd3","key":1222,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:a69423fbd046a97b345dff84e7d2be8f\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:2dcb3bcd1139544ed3ee32439c757dd3\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"The corresponding assurance-family instance premises apply.\"],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1075,\"path\":\"standards/FOUNDATIONS.md\",\"quote\":\"the carrier, checker and projections: the tenant's a_c design under AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/FOUNDATIONS.md#FOUNDATIONS%2F4.%20Algebra%2FAssurance%20relations\",\"start_line\":1075},{\"end_line\":1090,\"path\":\"standards/FOUNDATIONS.md\",\"quote\":\"Each consumer applies the rule and decides nothing this section does not\\n(P2, P6).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/FOUNDATIONS.md#FOUNDATIONS%2F4.%20Algebra%2FAssurance%20relations\",\"start_line\":1089}],\"statement\":\"Writing a relation or implication does not discharge its obligation. The family table adds no deciding rule. Added choices remain with their stated owners: approximate-step adequacy/bounds with the step-law owner; nonsequential composition laws with construction design; Ω and interpretation with the obligation owner and assessor activation; admitted T and observation π with the assessment frame owner; path selection with the strategy owner and ported-material authorship with EVALUATION §3; risk policy/thresholds with the actor exercising admitted work authority under the adopting Product; dependency representation/selection with the realisation and mandatory gates with RELEASE §8 and the Product; formal carrier/checker/projections with tenant a_c design. Consumers add no decision. Unsupported confidence in triage, priority or testing-value uses stays unresolved; a failing scenario establishes behavioural disagreement only with supported observation binding. A representation recording support kinds is a derived view, not an additional rule consumer.\",\"uncertainty\":\"The external consumer clauses and their full authorisation conditions are not supplied.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:00778cb24c2863e75a90e9b35d043c23","key":1223,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:bcbce5d0a737828a451a5a279b5244d0\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:00778cb24c2863e75a90e9b35d043c23\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"A preservation, end-to-end, approximate, cross-account or categorical construction claim is made.\"],\"exceptions\":[\"If a preceding postcondition does not establish the next precondition, the missing condition may instead be acquired and justified.\"],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1125,\"path\":\"standards/FOUNDATIONS.md\",\"quote\":\"An end-to-end argument establishes the initial condition, each step's\\napplicable premises, compatibility at each composition boundary, and the\\nconnection from the final property to Z. The preceding postcondition\\nmust establish the next precondition, or the missing condition must be\\nacquired and justified. Concurrency, alternative branches and external effects\\nrequire their applicable composition law; a sequential drawing does not\\nestablish one. Local success alone establishes neither composition\\ncompatibility nor Z. Preservation is distinct from progress, termination\\nand the availability of a suitable next step (P4a, P2, P6).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/FOUNDATIONS.md#FOUNDATIONS%2F4.%20Algebra%2FPreservation%20through%20construction\",\"start_line\":1117},{\"end_line\":1134,\"path\":\"standards/FOUNDATIONS.md\",\"quote\":\"Exact transformations preserve the declared meaning. Approximate\\ntransformations state their adequacy relation and an established bound\\nfor the complete composition; local tolerances cannot be assumed to add or\\nto remain unchanged.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/FOUNDATIONS.md#FOUNDATIONS%2F4.%20Algebra%2FPreservation%20through%20construction\",\"start_line\":1127}],\"statement\":\"State domains, transition relation and retained/established properties, accounting for material outcomes, effects and assumptions. A success-only relation supplies no claim about refusal, failure, interruption or unknown effects; these follow Results and ACTIVATION result/authority/recovery contracts. Real execution conformance is separate. Establish initial condition, each step's premises, every boundary's compatibility and the final property's connection to Z. Concurrency, branches and external effects require applicable composition laws; local success or a sequential drawing is insufficient. Preservation establishes neither progress, termination nor a suitable next step. Exact transformation preserves declared meaning; approximation states adequacy and an established complete-composition bound, without assuming local tolerances add or remain fixed. Changes to governing meaning/outcome follow their owner and successor rules. Cross-account claims identify maps and preservation obligations; human, machine or mixed execution alone discharges none. Commuting-diagram, functor and equivalence claims require categorical demonstration.\",\"uncertainty\":\"The referenced per-step law, recovery contracts, successor rules and full categorical demonstration requirements are external to the supplied sections.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:a99d396d405b819b9d55d91c7e6ca53b","key":1224,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:8c9bb8ca53b69dcc2598cbba518b1faa\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:c6397a5cd31d7e801c41504d6a8621df\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:a99d396d405b819b9d55d91c7e6ca53b\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1151,\"path\":\"standards/FOUNDATIONS.md\",\"quote\":\"The interpretation\\nretains the obligation's scope, conditions, exceptions and permitted\\nalternatives. A source identifier or digest authenticates the selected\\ntext; it does not prove the interpretation faithful (P1, P3).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/FOUNDATIONS.md#FOUNDATIONS%2F4.%20Algebra%2FAssertions%20and%20observation\",\"start_line\":1148},{\"end_line\":1165,\"path\":\"standards/FOUNDATIONS.md\",\"quote\":\"These implications are conditional on Γ and Ω. Passing a check of a\\nnecessary condition does not establish the full obligation. A conjunction\\nrequires its own coverage and compatibility argument; a collection of\\npassing tests does not supply it by its count (P1, P6, P5).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/FOUNDATIONS.md#FOUNDATIONS%2F4.%20Algebra%2FAssertions%20and%20observation\",\"start_line\":1162}],\"statement\":\"Interpretation retains obligation scope, conditions, exceptions and permitted alternatives. Identifiers and digests authenticate text but prove no fidelity. State each assertion's scope and implication direction, conditional on Γ and Ω, with support and unresolved parts. Passing a necessary condition proves only that condition; a sufficient conjunction requires its own coverage and compatibility argument, not a count of passing checks. A relation admitting sound satisfied and indeterminate judgments need not decide every case. A restricted deterministic model keeps its scope and actual checker conformance requires a separate account.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:56a4dd0e5af1a903af6e882e9c39a92b","key":1225,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:c6397a5cd31d7e801c41504d6a8621df\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:56a4dd0e5af1a903af6e882e9c39a92b\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"Soundness or completeness of an observation-based checker is claimed.\"],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1205,\"path\":\"standards/FOUNDATIONS.md\",\"quote\":\"For all s, s' in Ω:\\n  π(s) = π(s')  implies  q_t(s) = q_t(s').\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/FOUNDATIONS.md#FOUNDATIONS%2F4.%20Algebra%2FAssertions%20and%20observation\",\"start_line\":1204},{\"end_line\":1215,\"path\":\"standards/FOUNDATIONS.md\",\"quote\":\"If two admissible cases have the same observation but opposite truth\\nvalues, that observation cannot support a sound complete decision between\\nthem; further evidence, a justified narrower scope or an indeterminate\\njudgment is required. In a classical set model this condition permits a\\npredicate on the image of π; it establishes neither an executable decision\\nprocedure nor its cost. Unknown effects and unavailable observations\\nretain their distinctions from falsehood and from an evaluation that was\\nnot performed (Results) (P3, P1, P5, P6).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/FOUNDATIONS.md#FOUNDATIONS%2F4.%20Algebra%2FAssertions%20and%20observation\",\"start_line\":1208}],\"statement\":\"Universal soundness covers every admitted conclusion, not a favourable run. Always deciding q_t correctly from π alone requires equal observations to imply equal q_t truth for every pair in Ω. Observationally identical cases of opposite truth require more evidence, justified narrower scope or indeterminate. The classical image predicate entails neither an executable procedure nor a cost. Instrument, actor or execution acquisition needs supported observation binding; an idealised π does not establish it. Until oracle fidelity is established, reported passes and failures remain observations, not established source-obligation satisfaction or falsification. A relation supplies no probabilities; probabilistic claims need their declared outcome distribution. Unknown effects, unavailable observations, non-performance and unresolved work/coverage remain distinct from falsehood and indeterminate judgments.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:8cab203eeebbfbbb4b0e04dba3065863","key":1226,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:17185edeb211602f3f2cb3d5ef889e0f\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:4530a9f715df287b4ea597f2bbf43a15\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:8cab203eeebbfbbb4b0e04dba3065863\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1247,\"path\":\"standards/FOUNDATIONS.md\",\"quote\":\"An implementation-derived test can be useful for regression or a stated\\nlocal property. Repeating the implementation's decision supplies no\\nindependent justification of its fidelity to an upstream obligation. A\\nshorter assertion path can be easier to inspect and execute than\\nconstruction; that is a supported design claim for the selected path, not\\na guarantee of correctness, coverage or independence. Valid distinct\\nimplementations can produce different outputs within the same acceptable\\nrelation; equality of outputs is not always the oracle (P1, P6).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/FOUNDATIONS.md#FOUNDATIONS%2F4.%20Algebra%2FParallel%20derivation%20and%20mutual%20assurance\",\"start_line\":1240},{\"end_line\":1265,\"path\":\"standards/FOUNDATIONS.md\",\"quote\":\"Repeating\\nevidence does not create a new independent observation. Agreement with\\nan incorrect common model cannot validate that model against the desired\\nreal-world outcome; validation of the governing expectations uses its\\ndeclared purpose and external observations through their owners, and\\nproposed corrections preserve counterexamples and follow the applicable\\nchange authority\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/FOUNDATIONS.md#FOUNDATIONS%2F4.%20Algebra%2FParallel%20derivation%20and%20mutual%20assurance\",\"start_line\":1258}],\"statement\":\"Claims require both relevant assertion and execution provenance; execution logs alone do not justify the expected answer and authentication establishes neither provenance. Implementation-derived checks may support regression or a declared local property but repetition supplies no independent upstream-fidelity justification. A shorter assertion path's inspectability/ease requires a supported selected-path design claim and guarantees no correctness, coverage or independence. Different acceptable outputs may satisfy one acceptable relation. Account for shared causes; different actors, model families or codebases do not establish statistical independence, porting retains authorship/common dependencies, and repeated evidence is not a new independent observation. Diagnose disagreement without presuming the faulty party. Common-model agreement does not validate that model against reality; validate governing expectations through declared purpose and owner-mediated external observations. Corrections preserve counterexamples and follow applicable change authority.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:aba4c529b647f9ceb3f37e9edb9582ab","key":1227,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:cc5f5776011ad47b85c4351075c214f5\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:aba4c529b647f9ceb3f37e9edb9582ab\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1296,\"path\":\"standards/FOUNDATIONS.md\",\"quote\":\"The denominator must be nonzero. E can include agreement, disagreement or other\\nobservations; its likelihood under both faulty and non-faulty conditions\\nmatters. The formula supplies no missing likelihood or prior, and a\\nnumerical posterior is no stronger than its model and evidence.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/FOUNDATIONS.md#FOUNDATIONS%2F4.%20Algebra%2FQuantified%20assurance\",\"start_line\":1293},{\"end_line\":1314,\"path\":\"standards/FOUNDATIONS.md\",\"quote\":\"Conditional terms require defined conditioning events; zero-probability\\nprefixes are handled without inventing a conditional value. Replacing\\nthose terms with `P(M_i | V, Γ)` requires conditional independence under\\nthe declared model. One minus the joint miss probability is the chance of\\nat least one detection under those same conditions; it is not the\\nprobability that the whole product is correct. Agreement does not\\nnecessarily increase confidence when shared causes or new information\\nchange the model (P6, P1).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/FOUNDATIONS.md#FOUNDATIONS%2F4.%20Algebra%2FQuantified%20assurance\",\"start_line\":1307}],\"statement\":\"The actor exercising admitted work authority selects assurance for stated risk, obligations and resource limits, identifying material consequences, coverage, uncertainty and conditions of action/acceptance. Additional evidence strengthens claims only within applicability/dependence accounts, not by test count or preference for more checks. Quantification declares population/uncertainty, priors, likelihoods, shared causes and calibration limits. Bayesian denominator must be nonzero; agreement/disagreement likelihoods under both faulty and non-faulty conditions matter, and formulas invent no missing inputs. Conditional miss terms need defined conditioning events; invent no conditional for zero-probability prefixes. Dropping previous-miss conditioning requires model-declared conditional independence. One minus joint miss is conditional chance of at least one detection, not whole-product correctness; agreement need not increase confidence. Sampled-case or injected-defect calibration applies only through a justified relationship to operational failures. Unsupported numeric confidence stays unresolved. Cheaper assurance cannot waive required safety, authority or acceptance conditions.\",\"uncertainty\":\"No numerical model, parameters, calibration evidence or instance threshold is supplied.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:3440722dd836b4e0c89176eddaba34d1","key":1228,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:5a25ded62c9539a0ed3a79b1b0ff63bb\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:3440722dd836b4e0c89176eddaba34d1\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"Selecting reassessments after a material change or proposing reuse on a new subject/basis.\"],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1352,\"path\":\"standards/FOUNDATIONS.md\",\"quote\":\"Excluding a check requires\\nsupported coverage of its material dependencies and a reason the change\\ncannot invalidate the intended reused claim; an absent edge is not\\nevidence of non-influence. Unknown impact widens reassessment or leaves\\nthe dependent assurance unresolved. New obligations or cases create\\nassessment work even when no existing check covers them. A mandatory\\ngate, an assessment that the governing policy requires irrespective of\\nselection ([RELEASE §8](RELEASE.md#8-acceptance)), remains applicable\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/FOUNDATIONS.md#FOUNDATIONS%2F4.%20Algebra%2FChange%20impact%20and%20evidence%20reuse\",\"start_line\":1344},{\"end_line\":1375,\"path\":\"standards/FOUNDATIONS.md\",\"quote\":\"The\\noriginal evidence keeps its original subject; a new applicability\\nrelation permits its use. A changed hash alone establishes neither\\ninvalidity nor equivalence. A corrected run is not an unchanged independent\\ntest of the correction: the corrected subject carries its own evidence.\\nKnown failures, unresolved coverage and their\\ncitations remain visible until a supported repair, a reassessment or an\\nauthorised change of obligation disposes of them\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/FOUNDATIONS.md#FOUNDATIONS%2F4.%20Algebra%2FChange%20impact%20and%20evidence%20reuse\",\"start_line\":1368}],\"statement\":\"Conservatively cover changes and affected dependents and each check's material transitive dependencies. Exclusion requires supported dependency coverage and a reason the change cannot invalidate the reused claim; absent edges prove no non-influence. Unknown impact widens reassessment or leaves assurance unresolved. Include selected checks, new obligations/cases and all applicable mandatory gates; selection produces no execution evidence and failed/indeterminate results retain standing. Retention establishes continuing claim/scope applicability, justified assertion/observation basis and unchanged dependencies or an established preservation relation. Keep evidence's original subject and add a new applicability relation; changed hashes alone establish neither invalidity nor equivalence. Corrected subjects carry their own evidence. Preserve failures, unresolved coverage and citations until supported repair, reassessment or authorised obligation change disposes of them. ACTIVATION §7's closed-result/handoff invalidators are changes Δ, with affectedness when D*(t) meets I(Δ).\",\"uncertainty\":\"The three referenced ACTIVATION invalidators are not enumerated in the supplied source.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:bc1a7162b60ad6b5e5d1107fae066671","key":1229,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:5a25ded62c9539a0ed3a79b1b0ff63bb\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:bc1a7162b60ad6b5e5d1107fae066671\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1385,\"path\":\"standards/FOUNDATIONS.md\",\"quote\":\"If a governing requirement changes, dependent expectations may need\\nauthorised revision as well as new execution. A correction in a\\nrefinement revisits the affected obligations and their links to both the\\nrequirement and the realisation. A correction in the realisation\\nreassesses the affected implementation and integration under the\\nstill-applicable obligations. These are semantic dependency boundaries,\\nnot file or directory boundaries. Recovery reacquires current reality and\\ninvalidates affected claims; it need not erase valid work or rerun every\\ncheck\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/FOUNDATIONS.md#FOUNDATIONS%2F4.%20Algebra%2FChange%20impact%20and%20evidence%20reuse\",\"start_line\":1377},{\"end_line\":1395,\"path\":\"standards/FOUNDATIONS.md\",\"quote\":\"The\\nrequired assurance, risk policy and mandatory gates constrain that\\noptimisation; a cheap selection that leaves a required obligation\\nuncovered is insufficient.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/FOUNDATIONS.md#FOUNDATIONS%2F4.%20Algebra%2FChange%20impact%20and%20evidence%20reuse\",\"start_line\":1392}],\"statement\":\"Governing-requirement changes may require authorised expectation revision and new execution; refinement corrections revisit affected obligations and links to requirements and realisation; realisation corrections reassess implementation/integration under still-applicable obligations. These are semantic dependency boundaries. Recovery reacquires current reality and invalidates affected claims without necessarily discarding valid work or rerunning everything. Applicable retained plus new evidence may establish assurance; account completeness differs from execution freshness. Consider impact-analysis, acquisition, execution and assessment costs together, distinguishing forecasts from measurements, under required assurance, risk policy and gates. Broad/uncertain impact, selection-model changes, applicable release rules or evidence of missed dependencies can justify wider testing. A full suite may have gaps; no universal cadence follows and no optimisation removes required gates. Failures enter diagnosis and authorised response; evidence acquisition may precede any justified repair.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:f84a69bbd01fa8d0465026ca2fdd13a7","key":1230,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:cffbc4e797362ee75c9acc3609227c21\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:f84a69bbd01fa8d0465026ca2fdd13a7\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"An interpretation or assessment of assurance relations is made.\"],\"exceptions\":[\"An unproved universal claim may remain unresolved while bounded construction and assurance proceed where governing conditions permit.\"],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1432,\"path\":\"standards/FOUNDATIONS.md\",\"quote\":\"Assessment of these assurance relations demonstrates the applicable\\npositive, negative and unresolved cases in [CONFORMANCE](CONFORMANCE.md),\\nincluding weak assertions, insufficient observations, shared error, and change selection\\nthat either retains valid evidence or invalidates affected evidence.\\nMathematical proof, exhaustive checks of a finite model, sampled tests and\\nobserved use retain their distinct scopes. Finite examples do not prove\\nthe universal implications above. An unproved universal claim can remain\\nunresolved while bounded construction and assurance proceed where their\\ngoverning conditions permit them (P5, P6).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/FOUNDATIONS.md#FOUNDATIONS%2F4.%20Algebra%2FFormal%20representation\",\"start_line\":1424}],\"statement\":\"Represent material obligations and dependencies with source-governed fidelity and projected-view conditions. Preserve all five support kinds; external predicates retain source, scope and required evidence and arbitrary truth labels discharge nothing. Demonstrate applicable positive, negative and unresolved conformance cases, including weak assertions, insufficient observations, shared error and valid-retention/affected-invalidation selections. Finite examples do not prove universal implications. Assess owners and consumers under referenced EVALUATION criteria while keeping source-semantics, formal-fidelity and actual-use evidence separate. These duties do not require theorem proving for every test.\",\"uncertainty\":\"Full AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS fidelity/view conditions, CONFORMANCE cases and EVALUATION criteria are not supplied.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:214af1ff643a1145604b2bb954729190","key":1231,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:a159dd754aa9500e917e52db5c007d60\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:19d24390af542ec401ed7241d9526db2\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:b333d837ab9e156928c31281a56e5a0e\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:214af1ff643a1145604b2bb954729190\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":35,\"path\":\"standards/GLOSSARY.md\",\"quote\":\"Repeated spellings in different rows are intentional. Equal spelling,\\nnearness in this index, a heading, or inclusion in this member creates no\\nidentity, inheritance, import, equivalence or authority (P1, P3, P6).\\nResolution follows\\n[PRODUCT_DEFINITION §5](PRODUCT_DEFINITION.md#5-bounded-context-semantic-resolution);\\nthis index supplies no fallback decision (P1, P5).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/GLOSSARY.md#GLOSSARY%2F1.%20Index%20contract\",\"start_line\":30},{\"end_line\":63,\"path\":\"standards/GLOSSARY.md\",\"quote\":\"A term without such an owning clause is not a valid row under §1, and\\nthis index carries no such row (P5, P6).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/GLOSSARY.md#GLOSSARY%2F2.%20Locator%20law\",\"start_line\":62}],\"statement\":\"Index entries neither define nor decide meaning, context, imports or relations. Equal spellings, proximity, headings and index inclusion establish no identity, inheritance, import, equivalence or authority; repeated spellings are intentional. Resolve through the cited owning clause, selected basis and occurrence scope under PRODUCT_DEFINITION §5, with no index fallback. An unresolved context/owner invalidates a row; a term lacking an owning clause is not a valid row. Imported concepts require the context's own import or stated owner relation, citing defining and relation clauses separately. Watching index path/digest for locator drift remains separate from watching deciding sources and confers no semantic ownership.\",\"uncertainty\":\"The complete selected basis and external resolution procedure are not present.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:1b8526b8f627ba367270a80d73cdfc63","key":1232,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:a6fe8a828fd36e326960c62ade24fc8b\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:49133917db2c94cb7000087a71f47c5e\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:3da2a4eb8c47933e4c6e745c16195ef2\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:9c1b5668d40aed2d3b34a1013a682eb4\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:a2f107acde99288ef9dd2a88dd1b0877\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:13b6172ff45e0c256887788162a4e35c\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:1b8526b8f627ba367270a80d73cdfc63\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":335,\"path\":\"standards/GLOSSARY.md\",\"quote\":\"A\\nrow here declares no context; a context holds one of these concepts only\\nby its own import, as §8 records for the concepts that REFERENCE_FRAME §1\\nimports (§2; P1, P3).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/GLOSSARY.md#GLOSSARY%2F16.%20Concepts%20of%20members%20without%20a%20declared%20context\",\"start_line\":332},{\"end_line\":374,\"path\":\"standards/GLOSSARY.md\",\"quote\":\"Equal\\nspelling across these rows establishes no equivalence (§1; P1, P3).\\nPurpose and material relation: an actor that read one sense into another\\nclause reconciled the two by itself; this index points each sense to its\\nowner.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/GLOSSARY.md#GLOSSARY%2F17.%20Labels%20with%20several%20senses\",\"start_line\":370}],\"statement\":\"Indexing creates no context or import. A context holds an indexed concept only through its own import. Every label occurrence takes meaning from its owning clause and qualifies the label or states its predicate. Equal spelling establishes no equivalence, and an actor may not silently reconcile distinct senses. Listed result, triage, absence, stop, disposition and status meanings remain distinct.\",\"uncertainty\":\"The owning clauses and import rules are mostly outside the supplied source.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:6ebce8f4dc21353dc32138ca75c10439","key":1233,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:592f428587096675d25235df24f32725\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:6ebce8f4dc21353dc32138ca75c10439\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":122,\"path\":\"standards/IDENTITY.md\",\"quote\":\"- no two live objects of the same kind may share the same identity within\\n  the same authority scope;\\n- aliasing across scopes remains explicit; and\\n- serialisation preserves enough hierarchy to prevent accidental\\n  collision.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/IDENTITY.md#IDENTITY%2F2.%20Core%20law%2FUniqueness\",\"start_line\":118}],\"statement\":\"Identity is unique within lawful scope: no two live objects of the same kind may share an identity within the same authority scope; cross-scope aliasing stays explicit; serialisation preserves sufficient hierarchy to prevent accidental collision. A naked string need not appear globally unique.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:969b8675a4a2f8bd8a3b36a5c83ff6bf","key":1234,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:592f428587096675d25235df24f32725\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:628ebb39e8881c3e537451819d0b33f2\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:969b8675a4a2f8bd8a3b36a5c83ff6bf\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":133,\"path\":\"standards/IDENTITY.md\",\"quote\":\"Identity is typed. Different kinds of thing should not be collapsed into\\none undifferentiated identity space. Examples of distinct identity kinds\\ninclude goal, intent, requirement, requirement_family,\\nacceptance_criterion, scenario, design_decision, published_function,\\ncarrier_surface, release, install, run, function_call, continuation and\\nevent. The method does not treat a family identity as if it were a\\nconcrete requirement identity, or a release version as if it were object\\nidentity (P3).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/IDENTITY.md#IDENTITY%2F2.%20Core%20law%2FType\",\"start_line\":126}],\"statement\":\"Identity is typed; different kinds should not collapse into an undifferentiated space. Illustrative kinds are goal, intent, requirement, requirement_family, acceptance_criterion, scenario, design_decision, published_function, carrier_surface, release, install, run, function_call, continuation and event. Family identity is not concrete requirement identity; release version is not object identity.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:fcee4639f49f2df0aa2fa55cc2f130ad","key":1235,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:592f428587096675d25235df24f32725\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:fcee4639f49f2df0aa2fa55cc2f130ad\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[\"Lifecycle stability does not require every identity to remain immutable forever.\"],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":142,\"path\":\"standards/IDENTITY.md\",\"quote\":\"Identity should remain stable for the governed lifecycle it serves. This\\ndoes not mean every identity is immutable forever. It means identity is\\nstable enough to support traceability, comparison, replay, publication\\nand supersession. If an identity changes, the method should make the\\nrelationship explicit rather than silently reusing the old identity for a\\ndifferent object (P3, P4b).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/IDENTITY.md#IDENTITY%2F2.%20Core%20law%2FStability\",\"start_line\":137}],\"statement\":\"Identity should remain stable enough for its governed lifecycle to support traceability, comparison, replay, publication and supersession. If it changes, the method should explicitly relate old and new identity rather than silently reuse the old identity for another object.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:16ee54c4effee94097cefa3650b14d94","key":1236,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:66dfe66094c11997c7f30e2adfcebb0c\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:56f840f046c75cbe5f578321eada0403\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:16ee54c4effee94097cefa3650b14d94\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":165,\"path\":\"standards/IDENTITY.md\",\"quote\":\"no work relies on it as\\nestablished, and a profile that uses such a construct states its\\nepistemic status (P5). Purpose and material relation: this law was\\ndecided only in the optional world-model profile, so a Product that does\\nnot adopt that profile had no rule for boundary claims, and the common\\nsingle ownership requirement, item 8, requires generic law to be\\navailable without an optional profile; [WORLD_MODEL §4](WORLD_MODEL.md#4-the-markov-object-construct)\\nrefines it.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/IDENTITY.md#IDENTITY%2F2.%20Core%20law%2FBoundaries%20and%20sufficiency%20claims\",\"start_line\":158}],\"statement\":\"A boundary claim names object, supporting evidence and basis and holds only as far as that evidence. Task sufficiency is task-bounded, not completeness; beyond-evidence claims remain undecided. No work relies on a statistical Markov boundary as established, and a profile using it states its epistemic status. Generic boundary law applies without adopting the optional world-model profile; WORLD_MODEL §4 refines it.\",\"uncertainty\":\"RF-003, the hypothesis law and the WORLD_MODEL refinement are not supplied.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:3190abadc066b96e52c293ef11094ab0","key":1237,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:592f428587096675d25235df24f32725\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:628ebb39e8881c3e537451819d0b33f2\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:3190abadc066b96e52c293ef11094ab0\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[\"Hierarchy is recommended where appropriate, and not every serialisation needs all four visible segments.\"],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":191,\"path\":\"standards/IDENTITY.md\",\"quote\":\"Identity should be made unique by hierarchy where appropriate. One useful\\ngeneral model is:\\n\\n```text\\nauthority / kind / value / revision\\n```\\n\\nNot every serialisation needs all four visible segments, but the semantic\\nmodel should be available (P3).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/IDENTITY.md#IDENTITY%2F4.%20Identity%20hierarchy\",\"start_line\":183}],\"statement\":\"Identity should be made unique through hierarchy where appropriate, and the semantic model should remain available even when serialisation omits visible segments.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:6544f5ceb505252cdb38e98868d0bc79","key":1238,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:0fa83fdec596671a1df9bd98f5348022\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:006ca6488f42ba4e76c541e522c13142\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:6544f5ceb505252cdb38e98868d0bc79\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":212,\"path\":\"standards/IDENTITY.md\",\"quote\":\"Those rules should optimise for uniqueness, replay\\nsafety and event-stream integrity. The engine should not impose\\ndomain-specific semantic grammar on domain-owned objects (P3, P6).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/IDENTITY.md#IDENTITY%2F5.%20Authority%20split%2FEngine-owned%20identity\",\"start_line\":210},{\"end_line\":222,\"path\":\"standards/IDENTITY.md\",\"quote\":\"The runtime may transport those identities, but it should not\\nsilently invent their meaning (P3, P6).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/IDENTITY.md#IDENTITY%2F5.%20Authority%20split%2FDomain-owned%20identity\",\"start_line\":221},{\"end_line\":39,\"path\":\"standards/IDENTITY.md\",\"quote\":\"The engine should carry identity safely. The domain should define\\nsemantic identity law for its own constitutional objects (P3, P6).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/IDENTITY.md#IDENTITY%2F1.%20Position\",\"start_line\":38}],\"statement\":\"The engine should safely carry identities and optimise its generation rules for uniqueness, replay safety and event-stream integrity. It should not impose semantic grammar on domain-owned objects. The domain should define its constitutional objects' semantic identity law; runtime transport is allowed but should not silently invent meaning.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:f1713246fccd921a058aa03efda29dcd","key":1239,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:413efc4ed18e10f86b5c76f1f98556e0\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:0ed41260452a87de6836fa5047cb79ce\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:f1713246fccd921a058aa03efda29dcd\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":64,\"path\":\"standards/IDENTITY.md\",\"quote\":\"composition, delegation and projection restrict it or carry it faithfully and never widen it.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/IDENTITY.md#IDENTITY%2F1.%20Position%2FFoundation%20to%20law\",\"start_line\":64},{\"end_line\":255,\"path\":\"standards/IDENTITY.md\",\"quote\":\"A direct or proxied decision preserves its source, subject and basis,\\nacting identity and mode, scope, change class, disposition and\\nsupersession. Recording a ruling cannot widen it. What a proxy can never\\ndecide is stated at\\n[FOUNDATIONS §2 Authority kinds](FOUNDATIONS.md#authority-kinds); for\\nauthority identity its instances are that proxy authority does not make\\nimplementer self-review independent\\n([EVALUATION §3](EVALUATION.md#3-independent-assessment)) and confers no\\nunrelated runtime or domain authority (P6, P4b).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/IDENTITY.md#IDENTITY%2F6.%20Authority%20identity%20and%20conservation%20%28STDO-UP-004%29\",\"start_line\":247}],\"statement\":\"Authority coordinates survive every carrier; composition, delegation and projection restrict or faithfully carry authority and never widen it. Capability, labels, reachability, actor identity and payload shape create none. Elevation, transfer, split, merge, proxy grant, revocation and retirement require explicit authority decisions with identifiable basis; a step-produced authority decision cannot be re-acquired as though newly supplied. Direct/proxied decisions preserve source, subject, basis, acting identity/mode, scope, change class, disposition and supersession. Recording cannot widen a ruling. Proxy authority neither makes implementer self-review independent nor grants unrelated runtime/domain authority.\",\"uncertainty\":\"FOUNDATIONS owns the complete authority-carrier and proxy-prohibition law; only supplied instances and table consequences are retained.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:f5a7d1f1ed7a57f2ffde296a2002b4e6","key":1240,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:487b998011fc8bbf86f5688efd791a52\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:f5a7d1f1ed7a57f2ffde296a2002b4e6\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"A bound runtime publishes identity defaults or a derived domain overrides them.\"],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":279,\"path\":\"standards/IDENTITY.md\",\"quote\":\"Derived domains may override identity format and structure for their own\\nkinds. An override is lawful only if it preserves (P3):\\n\\n- scoped uniqueness;\\n- explicit kind distinction;\\n- deterministic parsing or reading;\\n- non-aliasing between family and member identities; and\\n- stable downstream traceability.\\n\\nOverrides are published in domain authority. They do not exist only as\\nad hoc regex assumptions hidden in implementation code (P6, P3).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/IDENTITY.md#IDENTITY%2F7.%20Default%20formats%20and%20overrides%2FDerived%20domain%20overrides\",\"start_line\":269}],\"statement\":\"Runtime defaults are lawful only while derived domains may override them. An override is lawful only if it preserves scoped uniqueness, explicit kind distinction, deterministic parsing/reading, family/member non-aliasing and stable downstream traceability. It is published in domain authority, not only hidden as implementation regex assumptions.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:29b9540b790345ab654b8da879d63aa9","key":1241,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:487b998011fc8bbf86f5688efd791a52\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:3cbeb196d9da340381b2cca3bb1e434d\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:29b9540b790345ab654b8da879d63aa9\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"A domain overrides defaults of its bound runtime realisation.\"],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":293,\"path\":\"standards/IDENTITY.md\",\"quote\":\"At minimum, the domain should publish (P3, P6):\\n\\n- the identity kinds in scope;\\n- the serialisation or readable form used for those kinds;\\n- the scope or hierarchy that makes them unique; and\\n- the distinction between grouping identities and concrete executable or\\n  traceable identities.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/IDENTITY.md#IDENTITY%2F7.%20Default%20formats%20and%20overrides%2FOverride%20publication%20surface\",\"start_line\":287},{\"end_line\":308,\"path\":\"standards/IDENTITY.md\",\"quote\":\"The important rule is that identity overrides are visible in domain\\nauthority, auditable, and recoverable without reverse-engineering regexes\\nfrom implementation code (P6, P3).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/IDENTITY.md#IDENTITY%2F7.%20Default%20formats%20and%20overrides%2FOverride%20publication%20surface\",\"start_line\":306}],\"statement\":\"The override is published on a lawful domain-authority surface, visible, auditable and recoverable without reverse-engineering implementation regexes. At minimum the domain should publish scoped kinds, their serialisation/readable form, uniqueness scope/hierarchy and grouping versus concrete executable/traceable identity distinctions.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:2438fabfbaa9da02436f9cdb8e1799f1","key":1242,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:0d44548345ed4f30503f0de96135ec17\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:006ca6488f42ba4e76c541e522c13142\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:2438fabfbaa9da02436f9cdb8e1799f1\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[\"A family marker, display alias or prose heading may be first-class only when governing identity law declares it an identity of its own kind.\"],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":327,\"path\":\"standards/IDENTITY.md\",\"quote\":\"- a parser distinguishes concrete identity kinds from grouping labels;\\n- family markers, display aliases and prose headings are not promoted\\n  into executable or traceable object identities unless the governing\\n  identity law says they are first-class identities of their own kind;\\n  and\\n- acceptance criteria, test cases and similar subordinate identities are\\n  not collapsed into requirement identity merely because their readable\\n  form is derived from a requirement token.\\n\\nIf a domain needs family identities, it should publish them explicitly as\\n`requirement_family` identities rather than rely on string-shape\\naccidents (P3).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/IDENTITY.md#IDENTITY%2F8.%20Parsing\",\"start_line\":316}],\"statement\":\"Parsers distinguish concrete identity kinds from grouping labels. They do not promote family markers, display aliases or prose headings into executable/traceable identities merely from matching shape. Acceptance criteria, tests and similar subordinate identities do not collapse into requirement identity because their readable form derives from a requirement token. A domain needing family identities should explicitly publish requirement_family identities.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:c553c68c9ccb152eec79ea60464c1019","key":1243,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:159bec39f19aa215b9d76120e9fe9081\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:c553c68c9ccb152eec79ea60464c1019\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":67,\"path\":\"standards/IDENTITY.md\",\"quote\":\"object identity, release identity, publication or revision coordinates and mutable discovery selectors may relate and are not interchangeable; by P6 none grants the other's authority\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/IDENTITY.md#IDENTITY%2F1.%20Position%2FFoundation%20to%20law\",\"start_line\":67}],\"statement\":\"Object identity, release identity, publication/revision coordinates and mutable discovery selectors may relate but are not interchangeable; none grants another's authority.\",\"uncertainty\":\"RELEASE owns the detailed release identity forms.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:9a96e973784d4c08bba2de34d614afa1","key":1244,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:3cbeb196d9da340381b2cca3bb1e434d\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:9a96e973784d4c08bba2de34d614afa1\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"Defining or auditing an identity surface.\"],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":362,\"path\":\"standards/IDENTITY.md\",\"quote\":\"1. What authority owns this identity?\\n2. What kind of thing does this identity denote?\\n3. What scope makes it unique?\\n4. Is the identity stable enough for the governed lifecycle?\\n5. Is the readable form only convenience, or is it being over-trusted?\\n6. Can a parser distinguish families, members, aliases and revisions\\n   without ambiguity?\\n7. Is this an engine or runtime identity, a domain semantic identity, or\\n   a release identity?\\n\\nIf those questions cannot be answered, the identity surface is\\nunder-defined (P3).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/IDENTITY.md#IDENTITY%2F10.%20Minimum%20questions\",\"start_line\":351}],\"statement\":\"Ask all seven identity-surface questions: owner; kind; uniqueness scope; lifecycle stability; readability convenience versus over-trust; unambiguous family/member/alias/revision parsing; runtime/domain/release category. If they cannot be answered, the surface is under-defined.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:0243ccc6636a6da115e82f2c52146818","key":1245,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:0d44548345ed4f30503f0de96135ec17\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:3cbeb196d9da340381b2cca3bb1e434d\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:0243ccc6636a6da115e82f2c52146818\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":400,\"path\":\"standards/IDENTITY.md\",\"quote\":\"Implementations should prefer typed identity readers, explicit\\nidentity-kind distinctions, and source-of-authority parsing contracts.\\nThey should avoid broad regex mining as the real identity model, silent\\ncoercion between family identities and concrete identities, and leaking\\nengine identity grammar into domain semantics (P3, P1).\\n\\nIf a project currently relies on those patterns, the first lawful repair\\nis to contain the immediate bug. The enduring repair is to publish\\nexplicit identity law and move implementations onto it (P3, P0).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/IDENTITY.md#IDENTITY%2F12.%20Consequence%20for%20implementations\",\"start_line\":392}],\"statement\":\"Implementations should prefer typed readers, explicit kind distinctions and source-of-authority parsing contracts, and should avoid regex mining as the real model, silent family/concrete coercion and engine-grammar leakage into domain semantics. For a project relying on those patterns, the first lawful repair contains the immediate bug; the enduring repair publishes identity law and moves implementations onto it. This is the member's implementation policy, applied under project design authority.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:bde9ec48c6867bc876bb21bc31487f50","key":1246,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:d95615227f8fdfe4b3e7141e3ba237e3\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:dfebaec0e3fc6f2d93521655089f3a54\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:7401bbbf535fd5e1e16b14036ff56999\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:bde9ec48c6867bc876bb21bc31487f50\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"A product is claimed to be built using ODD.\"],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":45,\"path\":\"standards/ODD.md\",\"quote\":\"ODD is a programming paradigm, not only a documentation preference. Its form\\nis `product = typed asset/domain model + GTL-defined graph functions + ABG\\ntraversal-control runtime + governed projection/query surfaces`. A product\\nwhose constructive carrier stays hidden in imperative loops, local service\\nlogic or product-specific orchestration scripts is not yet built with this\\nprofile (P0, P6).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ODD.md#ODD%2F1.%20Position\",\"start_line\":40}],\"statement\":\"Using ODD means building a GTL/ABG domain product with typed assets/nodes, named published graph functions bound into a GTL module, ABG-owned traversal governance/runtime facts/provenance/continuation/re-entry, bounded cooperative commands/services returning evidence and control, and visible state projected over constructive history. Documents, graph sketches or helper scripts alone do not satisfy that meaning; a hidden imperative constructive carrier leaves it not yet built with the profile. Automation must remain within lawful manual traversal of the same graph.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:b0d11240cc715483f8e5eeffc405739e","key":1247,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:d95615227f8fdfe4b3e7141e3ba237e3\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:dfebaec0e3fc6f2d93521655089f3a54\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:b0d11240cc715483f8e5eeffc405739e\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":213,\"path\":\"standards/ODD.md\",\"quote\":\"The profile does not replace a product-specific domain method such as the\\nworld-model profile (WORLD_MODEL, tier 3). Where a product is both ODD and\\nworld-model-driven, this profile governs graph-native structure and ODD\\nproduct shape and the world-model profile governs world-model semantics,\\npublication and composition law. The two compose (P1, P4a).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ODD.md#ODD%2F2.%20Method%20role\",\"start_line\":209},{\"end_line\":237,\"path\":\"standards/ODD.md\",\"quote\":\"An agent that reads only this profile should understand the paradigm.\\nTo build one concrete product correctly it must then read the\\nproduct-specific method and the local authority surfaces (P1, P2).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ODD.md#ODD%2F3.%20Method%20composition\",\"start_line\":235}],\"statement\":\"SPEC_METHOD supplies general constitutional goals/intent/product/requirements/design/re-entry law. ODD supplies graph-native structure and product shape, not domain semantics or the current local line. Domain methods supply semantic law; local INTENT.md, PRODUCT.md, requirements and design supply the ratified local line, with GTL surfaces included for graph-native software development. When WORLD_MODEL is also adopted, it governs world-model semantics, publication and composition. A source-described builder must acquire the product-specific method and local authority surfaces to build correctly; ODD alone is insufficient.\",\"uncertainty\":\"The referenced general/domain methods and actual product surfaces are not supplied.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:5a4690f0232752aab9138c3ce46d9e4b","key":1248,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:a1ff9d15d7f9cef03b4fc72c204cdd04\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:7b9b61c944808f060ef20bc9a9b82c30\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:5a4690f0232752aab9138c3ce46d9e4b\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"A consumer selects an installed STDO distribution.\"],\"exceptions\":[\"A project-local copy is optional, not the default.\"],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":260,\"path\":\"standards/ODD.md\",\"quote\":\"The selected immutable RC is consumer authority. Installed bytes must\\nmatch that cut; mutable source and the moving version-line selector cannot\\nsilently repair, replace or outrank it. A mismatch is an adoption defect,\\nresolved by selecting and installing one complete released cut and not\\nby mixing source and installed members. When an installed distribution\\ndisagrees with its selected immutable release, the selected release wins\\nand the installation must be repaired. Mutable source authors a future\\ncut; it does not govern the installed consumer (P6, P3;\\n[RELEASE §4](RELEASE.md#4-selector-and-consumer-adoption)).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ODD.md#ODD%2F4.%20Method%20library%20classes\",\"start_line\":252}],\"statement\":\"Consumers select one complete immutable release, addressed by exact logical release URI and installed-manifest digest independently of machine-local store path. Mutable source governs no consumer before publication and explicit selection. Installed bytes must match the selected immutable RC; mutable source and moving selectors cannot silently repair, replace or outrank it. A mismatch is an adoption defect repaired by selecting/installing one complete released cut, never by mixing source and installed members; the selected release wins disagreement.\",\"uncertainty\":\"No installation or consumer basis has been inspected or qualified.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:fe28a79a719147ed8d286cb22fb57def","key":1249,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:4affde1b64c0d4f4480ba70fa8f30aea\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:eac7cf8a2799092be0571f0c747f7bb9\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:f688644e4a37c1669dd925477341038c\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:7401bbbf535fd5e1e16b14036ff56999\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:fe28a79a719147ed8d286cb22fb57def\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"Work occurs within one declared ODD vector or edge traversal.\"],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":319,\"path\":\"standards/ODD.md\",\"quote\":\"ABG may govern, invoke, observe and classify the traversal; it\\ndoes not own the worker's hidden constructive path. Whatever the traversal\\nboundary does not constrain remains worker-internal HOW: hidden LLM\\nreasoning, heuristic search, domain implementation strategy, tool-local\\nexecution detail and product-specific business choice (P0, P6).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ODD.md#ODD%2F5.%20Graph%20model%2FProbabilistic%20compute\",\"start_line\":315},{\"end_line\":117,\"path\":\"standards/ODD.md\",\"quote\":\"the worker cannot close the edge, emit runtime events, mutate ledgers or decide re-entry, because its output is a candidate until evaluated and its report is an observation, not authority\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ODD.md#ODD%2F1.%20Position%2FFoundation%20to%20law\",\"start_line\":117}],\"statement\":\"The vector declares admissible external space; unconstrained internal solution path remains worker HOW. ABG may govern, invoke, observe and classify, but neither it nor the framework thereby executes or owns the domain's internal strategy. Worker output remains a candidate until evaluated and a report remains observation: the worker cannot close an edge, emit runtime events, mutate ledgers or decide re-entry. Neither worker nor human receives ambient authority from F_P/F_H classification.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:2d1f9dc4af744e908391a605b4ae61d1","key":1250,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:8a952a4985c21b8548d5a4551258e042\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:4affde1b64c0d4f4480ba70fa8f30aea\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:bf756d2b9147004f7d63d89815cb85ca\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:2d1f9dc4af744e908391a605b4ae61d1\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"A graph function refines a published outer vector into an inner workflow.\"],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":399,\"path\":\"standards/ODD.md\",\"quote\":\"Preserved meaning: the outer vector stays the\\ncallable contract; the inner steps conserve it and every applicable\\ninvariant; and each inner function's input satisfies its declared domain\\nand preconditions, as AC-016 requires. Narrowed scope: one published outer\\nvector and its declared inner workflow, whose retained functions should\\ndeclare `environment.requires`, `environment.provides` and\\n`environment.carries` (§11.8); a later function's declared domain is its\\n`environment.requires`, which may require any typed binding available in\\nthe cumulative carried environment, not only the immediately previous\\noutput. Invalidation: a change to ACTIVATION §4, to §11.8, to the outer\\nvector or to a function's environment declaration invalidates the binding\\nuntil it is evaluated again (P4a, P4b, P1).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ODD.md#ODD%2F5.%20Graph%20model%2FGraph%20functions\",\"start_line\":388}],\"statement\":\"Inner steps conserve the outer callable contract and every applicable invariant; each input satisfies its declared domain and preconditions. Earlier outputs are read only through the declared adapter/environment contract, and each published inner boundary is governed by the loop as the outer boundary is. Retained functions should declare requires/provides/carries. Changes to ACTIVATION §4, §11.8, the outer vector or any function environment declaration invalidate the binding until re-evaluated.\",\"uncertainty\":\"The full AC-016 and §11.8 laws are not supplied.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:32256f5ce033f22e7326030b34f7c6a6","key":1251,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:7b9b61c944808f060ef20bc9a9b82c30\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:796a8085272464e74aa0b22d9354d8cb\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:32256f5ce033f22e7326030b34f7c6a6\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":419,\"path\":\"standards/ODD.md\",\"quote\":\"The graph-native product and the project built with it are distinct. The\\ninstalled product provides the method, the runtime and the carrier\\nsurfaces; it does not provide the target project's business domain. The\\ninstalled product must not assume prior knowledge of the target project's\\ndomain (P6, P3).\\n\\nA clean install means: install the graph-native ODD product; author the\\ntarget project's intent, product definition, requirements and realisation\\nroot; traverse the product graph to build the target project's domain\\noutputs (P0, P6).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ODD.md#ODD%2F6.%20Product%20boundary\",\"start_line\":410}],\"statement\":\"Installed builder and target project remain distinct. The installed product must not assume prior knowledge of the target domain. A source-defined clean install proceeds from installing the ODD product to authoring target intent, definition, requirements and realisation root, then traversing its graph to produce target-domain outputs. This sequence is represented, not performed.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:a77fa506f8de030c7cc6f3847a01b919","key":1252,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:7b9b61c944808f060ef20bc9a9b82c30\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:796a8085272464e74aa0b22d9354d8cb\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:a77fa506f8de030c7cc6f3847a01b919\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"The installed released product helps build a subsequent version of itself.\"],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":455,\"path\":\"standards/ODD.md\",\"quote\":\"Self-hosting is lawful only while the installed product in use stays\\ndistinct from the product under development. A released installed product\\nmay help build the next version of itself, but the two must not collapse\\ninto one mixed authority surface. The distinction is between the installed\\nreleased builder and the in-development product being built, the same\\nboundary one compiler release keeps when it builds the next (P6, P3).\\n\\nThe framework must preserve distinct territories, authority surfaces,\\nruntime state, and project-owned specification and build-tenant surfaces. If\\nautomation, runtime resolution or qualification silently merges those\\nsurfaces, the framework violates this profile (P6, P3).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ODD.md#ODD%2F7.%20Self-host%20boundary\",\"start_line\":445}],\"statement\":\"Self-hosting is lawful only while released installed builder and in-development product remain distinct, with distinct territories, authority surfaces, runtime state and project-owned specification/build-tenant surfaces. Automation, runtime resolution or qualification that silently merges them violates the profile.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:7b9da11004b859b57d63097f51a26b29","key":1253,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:84dcf51004fa90f680da8c7bf39066d9\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:dfebaec0e3fc6f2d93521655089f3a54\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:7b9da11004b859b57d63097f51a26b29\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"A capability layer is active in a concrete product.\"],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":481,\"path\":\"standards/ODD.md\",\"quote\":\"In one concrete product each active layer should bind explicitly to local\\ntyped assets or typed nodes, public graph-function carriers, the required\\ncarried environment, proof or closure surfaces, and projection or query\\nsurfaces. An audit should therefore distinguish clearly between shared\\nODD structural law and local product semantic bindings (P3, P6).\\n\\nA product that copies another product's local asset names without\\nsemantic need is not reusing the method; that is accidental doctrine\\ntransfer. A product that declares a capability in prose but does not bind\\nit into typed assets, graph functions and proof lanes has under-built that\\ncapability (P1, P2).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ODD.md#ODD%2F8.%20Responsibility%20layers%20and%20local%20binding\",\"start_line\":471}],\"statement\":\"Each active layer should explicitly bind local typed assets/nodes, public graph-function carriers, required carried environment, proof/closure surfaces and projection/query surfaces; audits should distinguish shared law from local semantics. Copying another product's asset names without semantic need is accidental doctrine transfer, not method reuse. A prose-only capability lacking typed assets, graph functions and proof lanes is under-built.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:b957ea37c43816a49d8a2b96d0adf1ae","key":1254,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:f410088881523b5ea81f03f38d542d3b\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:d95615227f8fdfe4b3e7141e3ba237e3\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:b957ea37c43816a49d8a2b96d0adf1ae\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"A product is governed under ODD.\"],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":498,\"path\":\"standards/ODD.md\",\"quote\":\"Products governed under this profile should be audited against it as the\\nshared constitutional surface. The audit should ask at minimum (P6):\\n\\n- which responsibility layer or capability class is being implemented;\\n- which local typed assets or nodes bind that capability into the product;\\n- which public graph functions carry the constructive transition;\\n- which proof or closure lane justifies the capability;\\n- which projected or query state is exposed without replacing ABG runtime\\n  truth;\\n- whether any product command, service or query surface is trying to\\n  replace ABG continuation with tenant-local orchestration;\\n- whether the execution-authority audit (§11.5B) proves that traversal\\n  loops, actor invocation, process supervision, retry and continuation,\\n  runtime events and closure folds remain owned by ABG.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ODD.md#ODD%2F9.%20Method%20governance%20and%20audit\",\"start_line\":485}],\"statement\":\"Products should be audited against the profile. At minimum the audit should identify capability layer, local typed bindings, public constructive functions, proof/closure lane, projected/query state preserving ABG truth, any tenant orchestration replacing ABG continuation, and whether the execution-authority audit establishes ABG ownership of loops, invocation, supervision, retry, continuation, events and closure.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:d7b17d2e9467471e447063c966c2a910","key":1255,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:f410088881523b5ea81f03f38d542d3b\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:d95615227f8fdfe4b3e7141e3ba237e3\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:d7b17d2e9467471e447063c966c2a910\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[\"Product-local work may remain local when it changes no shared structural law.\"],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":511,\"path\":\"standards/ODD.md\",\"quote\":\"Approved shared-pattern work must update this profile when it changes or\\nclarifies the reusable structural law; product-local work may stay local\\nwhen it changes no shared structural law. Grey work must not be silently\\nabsorbed into the line (P6, P2).\\n\\nAn implementation or design move that the current profile does not\\nclearly cover must be evaluated against this profile and resolved as one\\nof: compliant with the current profile; non-compliant with it; or valid\\nand worth incorporating into it. If the result is incorporation, the\\nimplementation is not fully approved until this profile is updated. If the\\nresult is non-compliance, the implementation should be repriced, repaired\\nor rejected, not normalised by repetition (P6).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ODD.md#ODD%2F9.%20Method%20governance%20and%20audit\",\"start_line\":500}],\"statement\":\"Approved changes or clarifications of reusable structural law must update the profile. Uncovered moves must be evaluated as compliant, non-compliant or valid/worth incorporating. Incorporation is not fully approved until the profile is updated; non-compliance should be repriced, repaired or rejected. Grey work cannot silently enter the line. Usage, repetition and drift confer no shared approval; shared law is ratified in the profile and local law in product authority surfaces.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:b2e3be0d4f22b02ccf66366d829ea3d9","key":1256,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:dfebaec0e3fc6f2d93521655089f3a54\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:68488250933586b7cf75d39d4f345fde\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:e8fba98a082000f2293a25bde2a6c895\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:7401bbbf535fd5e1e16b14036ff56999\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:b2e3be0d4f22b02ccf66366d829ea3d9\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[\"Existing projects and other ODD product types may use different layouts preserving the authority split.\"],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":565,\"path\":\"standards/ODD.md\",\"quote\":\"At\\nthe universal layer this profile commits to the authority split (one WHAT\\nsurface, one HOW relation, runtime owned by ABG, product owning domain\\nmeaning) and not to directory names; existing projects and other ODD\\nproduct types may use another layout that keeps the split (P6, P1).\\n\\nThe product definition's `reference_frame_bases` bindings carry the\\nevaluation-frame meaning of [REFERENCE_FRAME](REFERENCE_FRAME.md). An ABG\\nruntime `Frame`, attention frame, zoom frame or overlay frame stays an\\nABG-owned runtime contract in WHAT and HOW; its name does not enrol it in\\nthe project's collective evaluation frame set. A declared evaluation frame\\nmay inspect such a runtime frame as its exact subject or coordinate\\nwithout collapsing the two (P1, P3).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ODD.md#ODD%2F10.%20What%20an%20ODD%20product%20is\",\"start_line\":553}],\"statement\":\"Read ownership strictly: one WHAT surface, one HOW relation, ABG runtime ownership and product domain-meaning ownership; stdo_<label>.json binds actual locations. reference_frame_bases carries evaluation-frame meaning. ABG Frame/attention/zoom/overlay frames remain runtime contracts and are not enrolled as evaluation frames by name. An evaluation frame may inspect a runtime frame as exact subject or coordinate without collapsing their identities.\",\"uncertainty\":\"REFERENCE_FRAME's full evaluation-frame definition is not supplied.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:7235a36160028a0b495824fe7e14844b","key":1257,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:dfebaec0e3fc6f2d93521655089f3a54\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:d95615227f8fdfe4b3e7141e3ba237e3\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:7235a36160028a0b495824fe7e14844b\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"Assessing whether an ODD product is built correctly.\"],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":603,\"path\":\"standards/ODD.md\",\"quote\":\"An ODD product is built correctly only when every clause of this section\\nholds (P6).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ODD.md#ODD%2F11.%20Core%20law\",\"start_line\":602},{\"end_line\":140,\"path\":\"standards/ODD.md\",\"quote\":\"the clauses form a conjunction, and one failing or unestablished clause leaves the product not built correctly\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ODD.md#ODD%2F1.%20Position%2FFoundation%20to%20law\",\"start_line\":140}],\"statement\":\"Built-correctly status requires every §11 clause to hold. A failing or unestablished clause prevents that positive conclusion; unestablished is not thereby equated with falsified.\",\"uncertainty\":\"The supplied §11 text stops at §11.5C; no whole-profile conformance judgment is possible from this excerpt.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:85e060370f3efcfd1063203ab63e7920","key":1258,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:dfebaec0e3fc6f2d93521655089f3a54\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:845e0e60b60e69f173452f33a26b882d\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:85e060370f3efcfd1063203ab63e7920\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":611,\"path\":\"standards/ODD.md\",\"quote\":\"The product works over explicit typed assets or typed nodes. It does not\\nwork over one hidden project blob, one giant mutable workspace object or one\\nundocumented service payload. Concrete assets must bind explicitly into\\ntyped domain boundaries. Where an asset is a real produced or consumed boundary,\\nits `asset_surface` is declared (P3).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ODD.md#ODD%2F11.%20Core%20law%2F11.1%20Typed%20assets%20and%20nodes%20are%20explicit\",\"start_line\":607}],\"statement\":\"The product operates on explicit typed assets/nodes, not a hidden blob, giant mutable workspace object or undocumented service payload. Concrete assets must explicitly bind typed domain boundaries. Every actual produced/consumed boundary declares asset_surface.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:c800611d14a51e06a8f3c630cb012e95","key":1259,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:8a952a4985c21b8548d5a4551258e042\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:dfebaec0e3fc6f2d93521655089f3a54\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:66f74c8f29b280b5c3f16e2a8b3d89fe\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:c800611d14a51e06a8f3c630cb012e95\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":619,\"path\":\"standards/ODD.md\",\"quote\":\"Every operative constructive step is carried by one named `GraphFunction`\\nor one lawful graph-function composition. The real carrier is never left\\ninside orchestration loops, bespoke Python pipeline runners, controller\\nscripts, or service methods that only happen to call GTL-adjacent helpers\\n(P0, P4a).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ODD.md#ODD%2F11.%20Core%20law%2F11.2%20Graph%20functions%20are%20the%20primary%20constructive%20carrier\",\"start_line\":615}],\"statement\":\"Every operative constructive step has one named GraphFunction or one lawful graph-function composition. Its real carrier cannot remain hidden in orchestration loops, bespoke pipeline runners, controller scripts or service methods merely calling GTL-adjacent helpers.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:8c8f0068376299a9f2b6dd24b9b2d519","key":1260,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:dfebaec0e3fc6f2d93521655089f3a54\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:4affde1b64c0d4f4480ba70fa8f30aea\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:8a952a4985c21b8548d5a4551258e042\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:81f6906b71f893b3c94e1dfc03ff9522\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:8c8f0068376299a9f2b6dd24b9b2d519\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"Building operative ODD framework behaviour.\"],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":637,\"path\":\"standards/ODD.md\",\"quote\":\"Because this profile makes an edge traversal the unit of compute, an ODD\\nproduct must use that unit of compute to build its own operative framework\\nbehaviour. The required order is: declare the outcome\\ntraversal over typed assets; publish the declarative GTL/ABG carrier\\nstructure; implement only the minimal imperative adapter code that remains\\nnecessary (P0, P6).\\n\\nAn outcome traversal declares the governed movement before\\nimplementation: source asset type; target asset type; edge traversal or\\ngraph-function name; closure or evaluation obligation; lineage obligation;\\nambiguity or gap obligation; allowed `F_D`, `F_P` and `F_H` bindings. The\\ndeclarative carrier structure is GTL graph functions, typed nodes,\\nvectors, operator bindings, evaluator bindings, carrier schemas, policy\\ndeclarations, projection declarations and lineage ledger declarations\\n(P0, P3).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ODD.md#ODD%2F11.%20Core%20law%2F11.2A%20Outcome-first%20realisation%20order\",\"start_line\":623}],\"statement\":\"Use edge traversal to build operative framework behaviour, in order: declare outcome traversal over typed assets; publish declarative GTL/ABG carriers; implement only remaining necessary minimal imperative adapters. Before implementation declare source/target types, edge/function name, closure/evaluation, lineage, ambiguity/gap obligations and allowed F_D/F_P/F_H bindings. Declarative structure comprises graph functions, typed nodes/vectors, operator/evaluator bindings, carrier schemas, policy/projection declarations and lineage ledgers. Imperative-first behaviour later described in GTL is ODD-shaped but not yet ODD-built.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:516f470b439e7bc5b48e8980b3552c57","key":1261,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:39e42e814d731b3e0b9630ddf1b8e191\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:81f6906b71f893b3c94e1dfc03ff9522\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:8a952a4985c21b8548d5a4551258e042\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:516f470b439e7bc5b48e8980b3552c57\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":653,\"path\":\"standards/ODD.md\",\"quote\":\"The live line must publish a machine-readable function catalogue. At\\nminimum each retained function should expose its name, inputs, outputs,\\nintent, and public or helper role. A callable surface that exists only in\\nprose or in prompt memory leaves the product under-built (P6, P3).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ODD.md#ODD%2F11.%20Core%20law%2F11.3%20The%20function%20catalogue%20is%20published\",\"start_line\":650},{\"end_line\":661,\"path\":\"standards/ODD.md\",\"quote\":\"The product must publish the public graph-function carriers, the graph or\\ngraphs those carriers traverse, typed node and vector surfaces, and the\\nsemantic jobs or equivalent outer callable contracts bound to the public\\ncarrier. Callers are never bound directly to hidden inner vectors (P4a,\\nP3).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ODD.md#ODD%2F11.%20Core%20law%2F11.4%20The%20GTL%20module%20is%20the%20operative%20publication%20surface\",\"start_line\":657}],\"statement\":\"The live line must publish a machine-readable function catalogue; each retained function should expose at least name, inputs, outputs, intent and public/helper role. Prose/prompt-only callable surfaces leave the product under-built. Publish public carriers, traversed graphs, typed node/vector surfaces and bound semantic jobs/equivalent outer contracts. Publish live refined inner boundaries explicitly through lawful GTL surfaces; callers always bind the outer public contract, never hidden inner vectors.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:c1c278eb739607efb67b5f5a6e9a27fa","key":1262,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:dfebaec0e3fc6f2d93521655089f3a54\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:7401bbbf535fd5e1e16b14036ff56999\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:66f74c8f29b280b5c3f16e2a8b3d89fe\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:c1c278eb739607efb67b5f5a6e9a27fa\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"An application operates over GTL/ABG.\"],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":694,\"path\":\"standards/ODD.md\",\"quote\":\"The product may publish typed assets and evidence, execute one admitted\\nbounded constructive step, publish downstream read models or domain\\noverlays, and return control to ABG. The product must not own a hidden\\ncontinuation loop; carry multi-step controller memory across publish\\nboundaries; infer later steps locally instead of re-entering through ABG;\\ntreat public `next` and explicit graph-function continuation as rival\\nauthorities inside one controller; or build product-local orchestration\\nthat in effect replaces ABG (P6).\\n\\nAn application that replaces ABG continuation with tenant-local control\\nflow no longer behaves as an ODD application over GTL/ABG. It has drifted\\ninto a different architecture that only happens to publish some\\nODD-shaped artifacts (P6).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ODD.md#ODD%2F11.%20Core%20law%2F11.5A%20ABG%20owns%20continuation%20and%20re-entry\",\"start_line\":682}],\"statement\":\"The application is cooperative, not a replacement runtime. ABG owns continuation, publish-boundary re-entry, graph-call lifecycle and graph step selection. Product code must not hold hidden continuation loops, multi-step controller memory across publish boundaries, locally infer later steps instead of ABG re-entry, make public next and graph-function continuation rival authorities, or otherwise replace ABG orchestration. Replacing ABG continuation with tenant-local flow leaves the application outside ODD-over-GTL/ABG behaviour.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:f7895e8efa5c4265294019f19d6828c1","key":1263,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:38deb25eaedf22835dddaba18b4d70a8\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:7401bbbf535fd5e1e16b14036ff56999\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:f7895e8efa5c4265294019f19d6828c1\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"An ODD product changes runtime, start/iterate, worker transport, actor invocation, process supervision, plugin dispatch, event projection, closure, assurance, retry or continuation semantics.\"],\"exceptions\":[\"A different runtime realisation is lawful only under an explicitly ratified, non-overlapping runtime scope.\"],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":709,\"path\":\"standards/ODD.md\",\"quote\":\"An ODD product over GTL/ABG that changes runtime, `start` or `iterate`,\\nworker transport, actor invocation, process supervision, plugin dispatch,\\nevent projection, closure, assurance, retry or continuation semantics\\nmust include an execution-authority audit before activation and closure\\n(P6).\\n\\nThe audit must prove that exactly one execution authority exists for the\\naffected traversal. For a consumer using the GTL and ABG roles, that\\nauthority is the one consumer-bound realisation of the ABG role, including\\nwhen the realisation under change itself implements that role. A\\ndifferent realisation is lawful only under an explicitly ratified,\\nnon-overlapping runtime scope (P6, P3).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ODD.md#ODD%2F11.%20Core%20law%2F11.5B%20Execution%20authority%20audit\",\"start_line\":698}],\"statement\":\"Before activation and closure, include an execution-authority audit proving exactly one authority for the affected traversal: the consumer-bound ABG realisation, including when that realisation itself is changing.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:3c69bea007a66330117a898ef091b8e9","key":1264,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:38deb25eaedf22835dddaba18b4d70a8\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:7401bbbf535fd5e1e16b14036ff56999\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:dfebaec0e3fc6f2d93521655089f3a54\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:3c69bea007a66330117a898ef091b8e9\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"Conducting an execution-authority audit.\"],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":719,\"path\":\"standards/ODD.md\",\"quote\":\"| Traversal selection and vector advance | ABG | Declare graph functions, vectors, assets, and domain policy inputs | Product-local runner deciding the next traversal step |\\n| Actor invocation and process supervision | ABG | Provide actor bindings, prompts, payload adapters, and evidence adapters | Product-local worker `spawn`, `spawnSync`, `exec`, timeout, kill, or stdout/stderr supervision outside the ABG actor seam |\\n| Retry, correction, continuation, and re-entry | ABG | Publish bounded-step outputs and return control | Product-local retry loops, carry-over controller memory, or hidden `next` authority |\\n| Runtime event emission, append, replay, and projection | ABG | Map domain evidence into admitted event payloads | Direct event append, side ledger mutation, or projection reconstruction that bypasses ABG runtime truth |\\n| Closure fold and assurance gate | ABG, with product policy and gain inputs | Provide domain interpretation, evaluators, gap reasons, and policy weights | Worker self-report or product postflight directly closing the runtime unit |\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ODD.md#ODD%2F11.%20Core%20law%2F11.5B%20Execution%20authority%20audit\",\"start_line\":715}],\"statement\":\"Inventory at least all five authority surfaces. ABG owns selection/advance; invocation/supervision; retry/correction/continuation/re-entry; runtime events/append/replay/projection; and closure/assurance, with product policy/gain inputs. Product/plugin roles are declarations and policy inputs, actor bindings/prompts/payload/evidence adapters, bounded outputs and control return, admitted evidence payload mapping, and domain interpretation/evaluators/gap reasons/weights. Forbidden local substitutes include next-step runners; spawn/spawnSync/exec/timeout/kill/stdout-stderr supervision outside the ABG seam; retries/controller memory/hidden next; direct event append/side-ledger mutation/bypassing reconstruction; self-report or postflight closure. Include language/tenant-appropriate code, call-graph or static-surface review and name evidence ruling out hidden execution authority; artifact review alone is insufficient.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:e7f6aecf3b4af18e5ba857db2a632ac8","key":1265,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:7401bbbf535fd5e1e16b14036ff56999\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:38deb25eaedf22835dddaba18b4d70a8\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:e7f6aecf3b4af18e5ba857db2a632ac8\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"An audited surface admits a consequential entity transformation.\"],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":732,\"path\":\"standards/ODD.md\",\"quote\":\"Where these surfaces admit a consequential entity transformation, ABG's\\nadmission authority is the graph-native specialisation of transformation\\nadmission completeness, whose admission semantics\\n[ACTIVATION §4](ACTIVATION.md#complete-enclosing-relation-admission) owns;\\nthe software-design profile applies that law in\\n[DESIGN_MODULE, Transformation admission completeness](DESIGN_MODULE.md#transformation-admission-completeness-up-016).\\nABG's broader execution, supervision, retry and projection authority\\ncontinues to derive from this profile and is not thereby reclassified as\\nadmission authority. `F_P` and `F_H` are the ODD projections of the\\ncandidate-producer and human-adjudication roles, which this profile binds\\nto the source concepts of SPEC_METHOD §5 in\\n[§5 Probabilistic compute](#probabilistic-compute) (P6, P1).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ODD.md#ODD%2F11.%20Core%20law%2F11.5B%20Execution%20authority%20audit\",\"start_line\":721}],\"statement\":\"ABG admission authority is then the graph-native specialisation of transformation admission completeness owned by ACTIVATION §4 and applied by DESIGN_MODULE. Broader ABG execution, supervision, retry and projection authority still derives from ODD and is not reclassified as admission authority. F_P/F_H remain the declared ODD projections of candidate-production/human-adjudication roles.\",\"uncertainty\":\"The complete enclosing-relation admission semantics are referenced but not supplied.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:afc2518cce43b742b217c1e36fe5c7f1","key":1266,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:38deb25eaedf22835dddaba18b4d70a8\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:dfebaec0e3fc6f2d93521655089f3a54\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:afc2518cce43b742b217c1e36fe5c7f1\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"Any listed closure-preventing condition is present.\"],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":754,\"path\":\"standards/ODD.md\",\"quote\":\"Any of these conditions prevents closure (P6):\\n\\n- a downstream product contains its own `start` or `iterate` loop for an\\n  ABG traversal;\\n- product or plugin code supervises worker processes outside the ABG\\n  actor seam;\\n- product or plugin code constructs retry, continuation or re-entry state\\n  outside ABG;\\n- product or plugin code appends runtime events or mutates runtime ledgers\\n  without ABG admission;\\n- plugin output carries next-vector, closure, actor-invocation, process\\n  or runtime-event authority instead of evidence or policy input;\\n- two controllers can each claim authority for one traversal.\\n\\nWhen any is present, the product may be useful but is not currently\\nODD-correct over GTL/ABG (P6).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ODD.md#ODD%2F11.%20Core%20law%2F11.5B%20Execution%20authority%20audit\",\"start_line\":739}],\"statement\":\"Each condition independently prevents closure and leaves the product not currently ODD-correct over GTL/ABG: downstream start/iterate loop for ABG traversal; process supervision outside the ABG seam; retry/continuation/re-entry state outside ABG; runtime event/ledger mutation without admission; plugin output carrying next-vector/closure/invocation/process/event authority instead of evidence/policy; or two controllers able to claim one traversal. Utility does not remove this boundary.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:8a8d11bde606b97901b521d4a7b2769e","key":1267,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:34566a52e8fcda8cee3d666e0e57e8ae\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:39e42e814d731b3e0b9630ddf1b8e191\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:81f6906b71f893b3c94e1dfc03ff9522\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:7401bbbf535fd5e1e16b14036ff56999\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:8a8d11bde606b97901b521d4a7b2769e\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":775,\"path\":\"standards/ODD.md\",\"quote\":\"For an ODD product: function catalogue views must reconcile to the\\nadmitted GTL module or public carrier; asset ownership and start-target\\nviews must be derived from, or structurally compared against, the admitted\\ncarrier they expose; runtime status views must derive from ABG runtime\\nfacts, events, replay or projection truth; domain query overlays must fail\\nclosed when the carrier they describe is missing, stale or structurally\\ndivergent (P3, P6).\\n\\nName equality is not enough. A same-named graph function, node, carrier,\\npolicy or route with different inputs, outputs, vectors, declarations,\\nownership or closure law is a different truth surface until reconciled.\\nNegative proof for a projection must include structural drift, not only\\nmissing source truth (P3, P6).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ODD.md#ODD%2F11.%20Core%20law%2F11.5C%20Projection-source%20coherence\",\"start_line\":763}],\"statement\":\"Projections cannot redefine ABG facts or reconstruct alternate authority. Catalogue views reconcile to admitted module/public carrier; ownership/start-target views derive from or structurally compare against their admitted carrier; runtime views derive from ABG facts/events/replay/projection truth. Domain overlays fail closed on missing, stale or structurally divergent carriers. Same names with different inputs, outputs, vectors, declarations, ownership or closure law denote different truth surfaces until reconciled. Projection negative proof must include structural drift as well as missing truth.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:9a81c528871d81c068e977c18127c3d7","key":1268,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:ccf788aa3cfe567da2d3eff370213cba\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:eac7cf8a2799092be0571f0c747f7bb9\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:9a81c528871d81c068e977c18127c3d7\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"Applying the source-described ODD constructive evaluation loop.\"],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":125,\"path\":\"standards/ODD.md\",\"quote\":\"every closure decision and next-action selection is reproducible by replay from carriers that each reference their causal predecessors\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ODD.md#ODD%2F1.%20Position%2FFoundation%20to%20law\",\"start_line\":125},{\"end_line\":124,\"path\":\"standards/ODD.md\",\"quote\":\"no edge closes from an artifact, a worker report, process success or liveness alone; closure is a fold over admitted evidence, the workspace counts only through the ledger, and an evaluator attends only to admitted ledger rows reachable through declared lineage\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ODD.md#ODD%2F1.%20Position%2FFoundation%20to%20law\",\"start_line\":124}],\"statement\":\"Artifacts, reports, process success and liveness alone close no edge. Closure folds admitted evidence; workspace counts only through the ledger, and evaluation attends only to admitted ledger rows reachable through declared lineage. Every closure-relevant callout is admitted to immutable ledger/event log. Corrections append or supersede without rewriting and preserve corrected identity. Every closure decision and next-action selection is replay-reproducible from carriers naming causal predecessors. Model synthesis, gap discovery, next-action selection and action evaluation retain separate authorities; each design, ticket, module or proof names the function it implements or consumes.\",\"uncertainty\":\"Ledger fields, replay inputs and detailed A0–A16 contracts are absent.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:8b206fb7fb09173573d49b3ac0ff8085","key":1269,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:ccf788aa3cfe567da2d3eff370213cba\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:dd4c6b532dec6f332c60a24617ffac0a\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:8b206fb7fb09173573d49b3ac0ff8085\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"Selected-outcome-bounded work is evaluated for continuation or closure.\"],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":127,\"path\":\"standards/ODD.md\",\"quote\":\"every action binds the current gap to exact target assets and obligations before invocation, and only published lawful actions are ranked\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ODD.md#ODD%2F1.%20Position%2FFoundation%20to%20law\",\"start_line\":127},{\"end_line\":126,\"path\":\"standards/ODD.md\",\"quote\":\"such work returns control without failure classification, keeping the same edge and a replay-visible resume basis\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ODD.md#ODD%2F1.%20Position%2FFoundation%20to%20law\",\"start_line\":126}],\"statement\":\"Each action binds current gap to exact target assets/obligations before invocation; only published lawful actions are ranked. The selected outcome bounds the loop. After a terminal condition, no further material work is selected without another admitted basis. Reprice requests constitutional re-entry and selects nothing. Lawful but undecided work yields control without failure classification, preserving the same edge and replay-visible resume basis; yield differs from retry, block and timeout. Edge closure is evidence toward Product acceptance, not acceptance.\",\"uncertainty\":\"The supplied table does not enumerate terminal conditions, full yield protocol or all repricing relations.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:3add900aa6d324c8b551be4d5e28e6b1","key":1270,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:ccf788aa3cfe567da2d3eff370213cba\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:f410088881523b5ea81f03f38d542d3b\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:3add900aa6d324c8b551be4d5e28e6b1\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":128,\"path\":\"standards/ODD.md\",\"quote\":\"a closure decision answers the edge predicate and is not a disposition of ACTIVATION §3, which answers the acceptance predicate, so neither counts toward the other; selection data decides no predicate, so it maps to no core value, while each typed no-action decides that no published lawful action can be selected and maps by its cause, and a closure decision it follows keeps its own value for the edge predicate\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ODD.md#ODD%2F1.%20Position%2FFoundation%20to%20law\",\"start_line\":128}],\"statement\":\"Closure decisions form a closed sum type and evaluate_next is total. Every closure decision and audit outcome maps to exactly one core value for a named predicate, including cause when cause decides the value. Closure concerns an edge predicate; ACTIVATION disposition concerns acceptance; neither counts toward the other. Selection data has no core value because it decides no predicate. Typed no-action decides that no published lawful action can be selected and maps by cause; any preceding closure decision retains its own edge-predicate value. Product owns priority policy.\",\"uncertainty\":\"Seven closure decisions and the two no-action causes are referenced but not enumerated; no mappings beyond supplied audit mappings are invented.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:48aef1f78365210126a6b33c4abfc0bc","key":1271,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:dfebaec0e3fc6f2d93521655089f3a54\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:8a952a4985c21b8548d5a4551258e042\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:7b9b61c944808f060ef20bc9a9b82c30\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:48aef1f78365210126a6b33c4abfc0bc\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"Applying the foundation table's manual, negative-proof, installed-development or refinement-convergence rules.\"],\"exceptions\":[\"Dogfooding applies only to a product providing this profile's framework behaviour; installed-development decisive proof applies where an installable development form exists.\"],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":136,\"path\":\"standards/ODD.md\",\"quote\":\"negative evidence for a boundary exercises the supported authority path with that input invalidated and shows refusal before the prohibited effect\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ODD.md#ODD%2F1.%20Position%2FFoundation%20to%20law\",\"start_line\":136},{\"end_line\":139,\"path\":\"standards/ODD.md\",\"quote\":\"a refined inner chain closes the enclosing carrier only when the enclosing contract still holds after fold-back and zoomed and unzoomed views agree\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ODD.md#ODD%2F1.%20Position%2FFoundation%20to%20law\",\"start_line\":139}],\"statement\":\"Every automated move must be possible for an actor holding only declared surfaces; agentic artifacts take effect only through admission against deterministic criteria, and conformance evidence is not ratification. Negative evidence invalidates the real authority-bearing input on the supported path and demonstrates refusal before prohibited effect; manufactured refusal/event/gap/verdict proves nothing about that path, and source/package/install/runtime absence are distinct claims. Decisive proof uses an installable development form where one exists; isolation/proving-lane provisions remain recommendations. Refined inner chains close enclosing carriers only if outer contract survives fold-back and zoomed/unzoomed views agree. A live requirement without a proof witness keeps the enclosing carrier open until realised or owner-deferred/repriced out of the active branch. Scenario bundles should clarify boundary, assets, vectors, paths and closure evidence; products choose scenarios and appropriate witnesses.\",\"uncertainty\":\"Full manual sequence, negative-test mechanism, installed-development rule and zoom/scenario clauses are outside the supplied excerpt.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:d85d7c0e2275c3b5e5e973873dbd0768","key":1272,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:a5d43a54e9b6c1b4035264da5197bcbd\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:d95615227f8fdfe4b3e7141e3ba237e3\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:d85d7c0e2275c3b5e5e973873dbd0768\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"An actor enters ODD product construction.\"],\"exceptions\":[\"A product-specific domain method is acquired where one exists.\"],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":131,\"path\":\"standards/ODD.md\",\"quote\":\"an actor building an ODD product acquires the general method, the product's domain method where one exists, and its local authority surfaces before it acts, then identifies and declares the graph carrier and loop, and implements code last\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ODD.md#ODD%2F1.%20Position%2FFoundation%20to%20law\",\"start_line\":131}],\"statement\":\"The source-defined construction order acquires general method, applicable domain method and local authority surfaces before action; then declares graph carrier and loop; code comes last. The table attributes a fourteen-step sequence and two reading orders to the profile and retains 'usually' for consequences of skipping that order. This is interpreted workflow data, not an instruction executed here.\",\"uncertainty\":\"The fourteen steps and two reading orders are not supplied in full.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:374cee39d4ee6a55e3b616ea67490f35","key":1273,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:bcaa8a8d820aec2a089181d683a453df\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:43f24abc172ed34fa00c9cdc0a76989f\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:374cee39d4ee6a55e3b616ea67490f35\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[\"Further material work requires another admitted basis after a terminal or exhausted basis.\"],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":806,\"path\":\"standards/ODD.md\",\"quote\":\"The loop selects no further material work without another admitted basis\\nonce the selected outcome is accepted; an admitted prerequisite is\\ndischarged; an admitted experiment's stated decision is resolved; another\\nadmitted terminal condition is reached; or its governing basis or bound\\nis exhausted, rejected, withdrawn, superseded, repriced away or\\nfalsified. A `reprice` disposition requests lawful constitutional\\nre-entry; it neither performs the reprice nor selects the successor\\noutcome (P2, P6).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ODD.md#ODD%2F11.%20Core%20law%2F11.5D%20Constructive%20evaluation%20and%20yield%20loop\",\"start_line\":799}],\"statement\":\"Material work must remain within the selected outcome or an admitted bounded prerequisite/experiment. No further material selection occurs after outcome acceptance, prerequisite discharge, experiment decision resolution, another admitted terminal condition, or exhaustion/rejection/withdrawal/supersession/repricing-away/falsification of its basis or bound without another admitted basis. Reprice requests constitutional re-entry; it performs neither repricing nor successor-outcome selection. Graph/edge closure is evidence toward Product acceptance, never Product or release acceptance.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:b0940cfc51af17b04468a4a89e80b033","key":1274,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:bcaa8a8d820aec2a089181d683a453df\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:3c87e88b6006249dbc37ff1e00860b70\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:b0940cfc51af17b04468a4a89e80b033\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":899,\"path\":\"standards/ODD.md\",\"quote\":\"No CLI branch, prompt prose, postflight string, gap-dossier action list,\\nquery projection, service method or local operator summary may become a\\nrival source of traversal truth (P6).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ODD.md#ODD%2F11.%20Core%20law%2F11.5D%20Constructive%20evaluation%20and%20yield%20loop\",\"start_line\":897}],\"statement\":\"Every GTL/ABG ODD product must preserve one authoritative traversal-consequence surface: IntentLineage → ProductAssetModel → ObservationSnapshot → GapPressureRow → TargetObligationBinding → PriorityProjection → ConstructionIntent → AdmittedEvidence → EdgeFulfillmentLedger → EdgeClosureDecision → NextActionProjection, with selected outcome/admitted bounded-basis refs also feeding TargetObligationBinding. No CLI branch, prompt, postflight string, gap-dossier list, query, service or operator summary may rival it. Carrier renaming cannot alter this authority shape.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:3edcc5ab425726e72026e3dbafc3e583","key":1275,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:505ca2ca015711bae0650516cdea1113\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:3edcc5ab425726e72026e3dbafc3e583\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[\"Libraries may be shared; authority may not.\"],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1061,\"path\":\"standards/ODD.md\",\"quote\":\"A module that lets one of these\\nfunctions exercise another's authority creates a rival control surface\\nand violates A0 (P6).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ODD.md#ODD%2F11.%20Core%20law%2F11.5D%20Constructive%20evaluation%20and%20yield%20loop\",\"start_line\":1059}],\"statement\":\"synthesize_model may update desired/known typed asset truth only from event-backed lineage, prior model and admitted product truth; it cannot observe worksite, admit intent, invoke, close or select work. eval_gap only observes and emits gap pressure; it cannot admit intent, invoke, close or choose work. evaluate_action only folds admitted action evidence into ledger and closure decision; it cannot select the next graph action. evaluate_next may bind obligations, rank lawful published actions and publish next-action projection, but cannot admit intent or decide prior-action closure/yield/failure/repair except by consuming admitted EdgeClosureDecision. Designs, tickets, modules and proofs must identify the specific implemented/consumed function rather than merely say evaluator.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:9ff284b1890c988bbba45ed58f01c182","key":1276,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:3c87e88b6006249dbc37ff1e00860b70\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:505ca2ca015711bae0650516cdea1113\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:9ff284b1890c988bbba45ed58f01c182\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"Before every constructive action invocation.\"],\"exceptions\":[\"The admitted prerequisite/experiment reference is optional when the selected outcome alone is the basis.\"],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":875,\"path\":\"standards/ODD.md\",\"quote\":\"`ConstructionIntent` must cite the lineage, the\\nselected action and the `TargetObligationBinding` that preserve the exact\\nselected Product outcome and any admitted bounded-basis refs (P4b, P6).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ODD.md#ODD%2F11.%20Core%20law%2F11.5D%20Constructive%20evaluation%20and%20yield%20loop\",\"start_line\":873},{\"end_line\":980,\"path\":\"standards/ODD.md\",\"quote\":\"A3 Published action law. `evaluate_next` may rank only published lawful\\nactions from the action catalogue. If the desired action is unpublished,\\nthe lawful result is a typed no-action disposition, not a fallback to a\\nbroad executive graph or a local script (P6, P5).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ODD.md#ODD%2F11.%20Core%20law%2F11.5D%20Constructive%20evaluation%20and%20yield%20loop\",\"start_line\":977}],\"statement\":\"Bind current gap, exact target assets, obligations, required roles and evidence refs to the exact selected outcome and any admitted prerequisite/experiment before invocation. A broad edge satisfies a specific gap only if the binding proves its lawfulness for those assets. External/bootstrap intent seeds the model but cannot invent unpublished actions. After evaluate_next selects an already-published function/vector, a distinct admission step admits construction intent synthesized against model and gap, citing lineage, selected action and preserving target-binding authority refs. An unpublished desired action yields typed no-action, never a broad-graph/script fallback.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:c52d4ba7c96684710a5824835d4ae414","key":1277,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:5656d4fa0bbe717157f7717db2dae858\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:3c87e88b6006249dbc37ff1e00860b70\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:c52d4ba7c96684710a5824835d4ae414\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":947,\"path\":\"standards/ODD.md\",\"quote\":\"Every closure-relevant F_P callout that does work needs ledger admission.\\nEvaluator work is not outside F_P merely because it reads ledgers: it is\\nF_P work over governed ledger state, and its result must be admitted into\\nthe immutable ledger and event spine before it can affect closure, routing\\nor traversal. Corrections append or supersede ledger and event facts; they\\ndo not rewrite the governed history of work (P4b, P6, P3).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ODD.md#ODD%2F11.%20Core%20law%2F11.5D%20Constructive%20evaluation%20and%20yield%20loop\",\"start_line\":942}],\"statement\":\"Filesystem/process output, screen logs, worker artifacts and product files are observations, gaining authority only through typed evidence admission and folding into ledger/decision truth. W may change without being true; L may be true without containing all W. Closure and evaluation judge W only through L, and evaluator outputs affect traversal only after their own L/E admission. Every closure-relevant F_P callout needs admission; corrections append/supersede rather than rewrite history. Evaluators may attend only to admitted rows reachable through declared lineage, predecessor refs, target binding, policy and relevant event cursor; outside workspace facts, prose, archives, summaries and controller memory are excluded. Closure cannot follow raw artifact presence, worker report, process success or CLI summary. The fulfillment ledger records counts, obligation rows, materialization/liveness/admission refs and edge_converged; it never selects the next action.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:87e964c690e8cf793ed9b735d314cc7b","key":1278,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:505ca2ca015711bae0650516cdea1113\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:34ccd9efb88618a7ee79652a99297483\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:87e964c690e8cf793ed9b735d314cc7b\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[\"Unresolved post_reprice must return no_action(undeclared) pending separately admitted constitutional re-entry.\"],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1009,\"path\":\"standards/ODD.md\",\"quote\":\"On `post_reprice`, `evaluate_next` must return a typed no-action\\ndisposition while constitutional re-entry stays unresolved. The reprice\\ndecision cannot authorise a replacement action; work may be evaluated\\nagain only after lawful re-entry separately admits an exact selected\\nProduct outcome or bounded basis and supplies it through a new\\n`initial_selection` or a basis-bearing resume. Default graph following is\\nordinary, but it is still an `evaluate_next` decision and not hidden\\nsequential control (P5, P2, P6).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ODD.md#ODD%2F11.%20Core%20law%2F11.5D%20Constructive%20evaluation%20and%20yield%20loop\",\"start_line\":1002}],\"statement\":\"evaluate_next must be total. initial_selection uses current model/gap/binding/catalogue/policy. post_yield_resume resumes or yields the same lawful edge from replay-visible resume truth without failure classification. post_close_graph_continuation may choose the next edge or empty selection when complete. For post_retry/post_repair/post_reenter/post_block, select a higher-priority lawful action if one exists; otherwise follow the current edge if lawful; otherwise if authority is missing return a reprice-or-block typed no-action; otherwise block with typed no-action. These are selection outcomes, not evaluate_action closure decisions. Default following still passes through evaluate_next. Post-reprice work can be evaluated again only after separately admitted exact outcome/bounded basis enters new initial_selection or basis-bearing resume.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:fa193be1e4757a8b0db1d45bb74563e5","key":1279,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:34ccd9efb88618a7ee79652a99297483\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:fa193be1e4757a8b0db1d45bb74563e5\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[\"An earlier result stands for no-action only if it decided the same selection predicate on the current basis.\"],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1044,\"path\":\"standards/ODD.md\",\"quote\":\"Where the graph is complete and no action follows a closed edge, nothing\\nis refused and no selection determination is made: the empty selection is\\ninvocational data, and `close` keeps its own value for the edge predicate\\nunder A8.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ODD.md#ODD%2F11.%20Core%20law%2F11.5D%20Constructive%20evaluation%20and%20yield%20loop\",\"start_line\":1041}],\"statement\":\"Selected next action is invocational data, not a core result. Each typed no-action independently answers whether a lawful published action can be selected for this gap on this exact basis, retaining its domain outcome beside its core value. no_action(undeclared) maps to out_of_frame when catalogue lacks the action or no admitted basis declares a needed relation/capability/authority; it names the missing item and owner. no_action(basis) maps to invalid_basis when the current outcome/catalogue/policy cannot support the gap. On unresolved post_reprice, no_action(undeclared) names the undeclared outcome/bound and declaring re-entry. Prior closure results are selection evidence only and neither predicate's value counts toward the other. A next-action projection establishes availability only. Empty selection after a closed, complete graph is neither refusal nor selection determination.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:e6a40077693dbad532c0db3176a4e9ef","key":1280,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:34ccd9efb88618a7ee79652a99297483\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:e6a40077693dbad532c0db3176a4e9ef\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"Closure results use admitted evidence and exact edge basis.\"],\"exceptions\":[\"For re-enter or block with both undeclared and basis causes, record both and take the basis value.\"],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1154,\"path\":\"standards/ODD.md\",\"quote\":\"A decision with both causes records both and takes the\\n  `basis` value, as\\n  [ACTIVATION §3 Construction availability](ACTIVATION.md#construction-availability)\\n  decides for `re_entry_requested`.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ODD.md#ODD%2F11.%20Core%20law%2F11.5D%20Constructive%20evaluation%20and%20yield%20loop\",\"start_line\":1151},{\"end_line\":1163,\"path\":\"standards/ODD.md\",\"quote\":\"| `repair(implementation)` | falsified | the failing obligation row is the counterexample (P5, P6) |\\n| `repair(proof)` | indeterminate | the defect is in the proof, so the admitted evidence cannot decide the obligation; the decision's reason refs name the repaired proof that would decide (P5, P6) |\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ODD.md#ODD%2F11.%20Core%20law%2F11.5D%20Constructive%20evaluation%20and%20yield%20loop\",\"start_line\":1162}],\"statement\":\"Every closure decision is replay-visible with sufficient basis/reason refs. close→satisfied when admitted ledger evidence fulfills exact-basis obligations. yield→indeterminate when the edge stays lawful and admitted progress/waiting does not decide, with resume basis naming what would decide. retry(defeated)→falsified only when admissible evidence defeats this attempt while the action stays lawful; all other retry is retry(undecided)→indeterminate, naming the deciding re-attempt. Repair requires coherent governing relation/basis/binding and a local defect permitting repair of the same edge: repair(implementation)→falsified for admitted implementation failure with failing obligation counterexample; every other repair is repair(proof)→indeterminate with repaired proof needed to decide. re-enter requires upstream asset/governing-relation change: undeclared needed relation/capability/authority→out_of_frame, naming it and its owner; otherwise unsupporting/stale/substituted/unrepairable basis→invalid_basis. reprice→out_of_frame for an undeclared selected outcome/bound, naming it, owner and requested constitutional re-entry. block(undeclared)→out_of_frame and block(basis)→invalid_basis when the action leaves the edge unable to proceed for the respective cause. Cause comes from reproducible basis/reason refs and adds no decision or core value.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:79f94d493a029d6521aaf108a9dfb6b7","key":1281,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:34ccd9efb88618a7ee79652a99297483\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:bcaa8a8d820aec2a089181d683a453df\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:79f94d493a029d6521aaf108a9dfb6b7\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1187,\"path\":\"standards/ODD.md\",\"quote\":\"`repair(proof)` is `indeterminate`, because a\\ndefective proof leaves the edge's obligations undecided, while\\n`local_repair` is `falsified`, because the local defect defeats\\nacceptance of the candidate. `re-enter(undeclared)` is `out_of_frame`,\\nbecause the change needs a relation, capability or authority that no\\nadmitted basis declares, while `re_enter` is `invalid_basis`. Neither\\nvalue counts toward the other's predicate\\n([FOUNDATIONS §4 Conjunction of results](FOUNDATIONS.md#conjunction-of-results)).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ODD.md#ODD%2F11.%20Core%20law%2F11.5D%20Constructive%20evaluation%20and%20yield%20loop\",\"start_line\":1180}],\"statement\":\"Do not combine candidate availability, edge fulfillment, next-action selectability or candidate acceptance as each other's results. Closure repair is not ACTIVATION local_repair, and re-enter is not re_enter: proof repair is indeterminate versus local_repair falsified; undeclared re-entry is out_of_frame versus re_enter invalid_basis. In ODD §§11.5D, 16 and 19, disposition denotes a closure decision or, for typed no-action disposition, evaluate_next selection, never ACTIVATION §3 disposition. RELEASE §9 owns successor-claim dispositions. Repair/re-entry realization is a published graph action chosen by evaluate_next from admitted closure truth; evaluate_action's conceptual disposition does not itself invoke it.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:65f88736c75d216d95437c1781663b55","key":1282,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:bcaa8a8d820aec2a089181d683a453df\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:34ccd9efb88618a7ee79652a99297483\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:65f88736c75d216d95437c1781663b55\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1216,\"path\":\"standards/ODD.md\",\"quote\":\"A10 Liveness does not close semantic truth. Liveness observes activity,\\ninactivity, process state and interruption. It can support yield or a\\nliveness interruption; it cannot by itself declare semantic failure,\\nsemantic closure or requirement non-satisfaction (P6).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ODD.md#ODD%2F11.%20Core%20law%2F11.5D%20Constructive%20evaluation%20and%20yield%20loop\",\"start_line\":1213}],\"statement\":\"Yield requires the same edge/attempt to remain lawful, admitted progress/waiting, replay-visible resume basis and control return without failure classification. It preserves the current edge for long-running, bounded or partially productive work and is not retry, block, timeout or a local CLI loop. Liveness alone cannot establish semantic failure, closure, requirement non-satisfaction or retry(defeated). It can support yield or interruption.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:c362ca27a5d3f82579a232f3c4c9b55d","key":1283,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:bcaa8a8d820aec2a089181d683a453df\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:3c87e88b6006249dbc37ff1e00860b70\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:c362ca27a5d3f82579a232f3c4c9b55d\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"For every closure decision, next-action selection and governing admitted/replay-derived carrier or projection.\"],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1285,\"path\":\"standards/ODD.md\",\"quote\":\"A13 requires that the decision be reproducible from the inputs;\\nA13a requires that each governing carrier or projection carry the predecessor refs\\nthat make reproduction reachable without external joins. A broken\\npredecessor chain is non-replayable at the carrier level and therefore\\nfails A13 (P3, P4b).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ODD.md#ODD%2F11.%20Core%20law%2F11.5D%20Constructive%20evaluation%20and%20yield%20loop\",\"start_line\":1281}],\"statement\":\"Reproduction must use RuntimeEventLog, execution basis, event-backed IntentLineage, ProductAssetModel publication basis/event refs, selected outcome identity/admitted bounded refs, GapPressureRow, TargetObligationBinding, ActionCatalog, admitted evidence, ledger, closure decision, NextActionBasis and visible policy refs. Inability to reproduce signals hidden state. Each governing carrier must carry causal predecessor refs: outcome/bounded refs→binding; lineage→model→gap→binding→priority→selected-action projection→construction intent→evidence→ledger→closure decision→next-action basis→post-action projection. Both projection occurrences must be predecessor-reachable; the latter also uses fresh eval_gap. Construction intent preserves authority refs. Reproduction must be reachable without external joins; a broken chain fails replayability.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:7530f63a69d2def58781e476307c39e2","key":1284,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:bcaa8a8d820aec2a089181d683a453df\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:505ca2ca015711bae0650516cdea1113\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:790dc2b2d5efd074ca29cd1903ea9f8d\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:7530f63a69d2def58781e476307c39e2\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[\"Intentionally opaque internals remain one bounded action and may compute an internal result with local control flow.\"],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1297,\"path\":\"standards/ODD.md\",\"quote\":\"Once a refinement is published as graph structure,\\nthe loop governs it recursively (P4a, P0, P6).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ODD.md#ODD%2F11.%20Core%20law%2F11.5D%20Constructive%20evaluation%20and%20yield%20loop\",\"start_line\":1296}],\"statement\":\"Each published inner-vector boundary must obey all four functions with its own visible model, gap, binding, action, evidence, ledger, closure and next-action projection. Opaque internals may not publish, dispatch, retry, repair, re-enter or close graph work as a hidden traversal controller. ABG owns runtime truth/replay, graph-call lifecycle, actor/process supervision, continuation and re-entry mechanics. Product owns domain asset/catalogue meaning, gap interpretation and priority policy. DESIGN_MODULE tier 3 governs realization modules inside this split and may not fragment eval_gap/evaluate_next/evaluate_action into module-local authorities.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:c605bc5b18dab1b81be6bb05308fe283","key":1285,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:bcaa8a8d820aec2a089181d683a453df\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:505ca2ca015711bae0650516cdea1113\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:c605bc5b18dab1b81be6bb05308fe283\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"For any ticket, design, code module or proof touching the four functions, traversal, gap evaluation, selection, intent, worker invocation, evidence admission, fulfillment, liveness, closure, re-entry, public query or live proof.\"],\"exceptions\":[\"Unchanged accepted relations cite their accepted basis and are not proved again.\"],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1318,\"path\":\"standards/ODD.md\",\"quote\":\"the causally\\napplicable members of this axiom set and the constitutional equation below\\nare the controlling acceptance constraints for the selected Product\\noutcome and the affected published boundary. Unchanged accepted relations\\ncite their accepted basis and are not proved again. The axiom family\\nauthorises no horizontal realisation growth, creates no Product work and\\ndoes not widen the selected outcome (P6, P2).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ODD.md#ODD%2F11.%20Core%20law%2F11.5D%20Constructive%20evaluation%20and%20yield%20loop\",\"start_line\":1312}],\"statement\":\"Causally applicable axioms and the constitutional equation control acceptance for the selected outcome and affected published boundary; they authorize no horizontal realization growth, new Product work or outcome widening. Local checklists, test names, source-grep checks, CLI summaries and implementation notes cannot weaken them. A locally complete ticket leaving a rival traversal-consequence path requires lawful re-entry, keeping the gap as blocker, or separately bounded paydown under an independently selected outcome/prerequisite. Correctness requires the next-work decision to derive only from the equation, with U=(selected outcome, optional admitted bounded basis) causally reachable through binding and intent. The equation projects lineage, synthesizes model, observes gap, binds U, evaluates initial selection, distinctly admits intent, invokes and admits evidence, evaluates action, refreshes model/gap/binding, derives post-action basis and evaluates next; unresolved post_reprice returns typed no-action.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:e6546eb887397276a545ca257125284f","key":1286,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:bcaa8a8d820aec2a089181d683a453df\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:3c87e88b6006249dbc37ff1e00860b70\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:e6546eb887397276a545ca257125284f\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1353,\"path\":\"standards/ODD.md\",\"quote\":\"If any of them conflicts with the admitted `EdgeFulfillmentLedger`,\\n`EdgeClosureDecision` or `NextActionProjection`, the ledger, decision and\\nprojection chain wins. If that chain is absent, the edge has not\\nconstitutionally closed and the next action has not been constitutionally\\nselected (P6).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ODD.md#ODD%2F11.%20Core%20law%2F11.5D%20Constructive%20evaluation%20and%20yield%20loop\",\"start_line\":1349}],\"statement\":\"Gap dossiers, postflight/assurance reports, materialization manifests, liveness projections, run summaries, worker prose, screen/PTY transcripts, prompt packages, harness target arguments, source-grep tests, CLI output/branches, queries/gaps views and service outputs provide only evidence, diagnostics or read-model context; none independently closes an edge, selects work or routes retry/repair/re-entry. The admitted ledger/decision/projection chain prevails over conflicts; without it there is no constitutional edge closure or next-action selection. Public query may render read-only eval_gap/evaluate_action/evaluate_next outputs but cannot append events, invoke workers, admit intent, run evaluate_action or choose traversal itself.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:656097d9edf16213ad156725b8d7a02d","key":1287,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:c268d2b1bafeebb5b3c54ed7be08bb2e\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:656097d9edf16213ad156725b8d7a02d\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1439,\"path\":\"standards/ODD.md\",\"quote\":\"If the team cannot explain the manual traversal, the automation is not yet\\nmethod-safe. Automation that cannot be explained in these terms is ahead\\nof the method (P0, P6).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ODD.md#ODD%2F11.%20Core%20law%2F11.7%20Manual%20walkthrough%20must%20still%20be%20lawful\",\"start_line\":1437}],\"statement\":\"Automation must stay true to the manual process, which an operator using only declared surfaces should be able to follow. It cannot skip undeclared nodes, fabricate authority, collapse multiple constitutional transitions into an opaque step without declared refinement, depend on implementation-carrier knowledge the installed product should lack, or merge installed-builder and development-product authority during self-host work. Inability to explain manual traversal means automation is not yet method-safe.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:2bbbd963f7f6d5d24101d2e46322aece","key":1288,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:26c627c4204c2f1f3b1820e20d788928\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:2bbbd963f7f6d5d24101d2e46322aece\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1478,\"path\":\"standards/ODD.md\",\"quote\":\"A derived surface or projected frame of the general method may\\norient the agent to source precedence, lawful re-entry and traceability;\\nit must not be used to decide product-specific behaviour, which must come\\nfrom the current product authority packet (P6, P1).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ODD.md#ODD%2F11.%20Core%20law%2F11.7A%20Conforming%20agentic%20development\",\"start_line\":1475},{\"end_line\":1511,\"path\":\"standards/ODD.md\",\"quote\":\"The agentic coder\\nproduces the artifact; the declared admission gates it deterministically,\\nfail-closed and naming the violated rule, exactly as a typed asset is\\nenforced by its constructor (§11.1) (P6, P3).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ODD.md#ODD%2F11.%20Core%20law%2F11.7A%20Conforming%20agentic%20development\",\"start_line\":1508}],\"statement\":\"Agents work from the smallest sufficient declared packet with source refs, not stale memory or wholesale hidden context. Compression is prompt input, never deciding authority; generic derived frames may orient precedence/re-entry/traceability but product behavior must come from current Product authority. Produced work must have correct change class, traceability and admission. Tickets, change classifications, design derivations and execution contracts must pass existing SPEC_METHOD/TICKETS admission: deterministic, fail-closed and naming violated rules, never treating a drafted classification as automatic truth. F_P reasons/drafts/proposes; F_D decides artifact conformance. A passed admission and completed walkthrough are conformance evidence, not ratification; repeated use cannot amend shared method or constitutionalize grey work.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:a02f8650ace7202060462c5614e760e1","key":1289,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:26c627c4204c2f1f3b1820e20d788928\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:a02f8650ace7202060462c5614e760e1\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1492,\"path\":\"standards/ODD.md\",\"quote\":\"An agent that ignored the declared authority, relied on stale memory or\\nreasoned badly has produced agent error, not a method defect. Admission\\nrejects the malformed artifact either way, so a bad agent turn neither\\nbecomes law nor silently indicts the method (P6).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ODD.md#ODD%2F11.%20Core%20law%2F11.7A%20Conforming%20agentic%20development\",\"start_line\":1489}],\"statement\":\"A walkthrough stopping point is a method defect only when a competent, correctly configured agent using declared authority still cannot decide because an owning surface has ambiguity, a missing step, contradictory authority or undecidable change class; reprice that defect into its owner. Ignored authority, stale memory or bad reasoning is agent error instead; malformed artifacts are rejected either way. Process-followability proof is independent of automated runtime: external API overload or transport failure cannot prove process soundness, because runtime availability and process validity differ.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:826fc7a76dadb569901e7150bccebf2c","key":1290,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:b6360702187f5ffc1352d86f863767c8\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:826fc7a76dadb569901e7150bccebf2c\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"The specified identities apply to the boundary.\"],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1553,\"path\":\"standards/ODD.md\",\"quote\":\"No CLI, SDK, service, adapter, plugin, fixture, query or projection may\\nbecome a rival traversal controller. The consumer owns the concrete test\\nand evidence mechanism; this section owns the property that mechanism\\nmust prove (P6).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ODD.md#ODD%2F11.%20Core%20law%2F11.7B%20Real%20authority-path%20negative%20proof%20%28STDO-UP-010%29\",\"start_line\":1550}],\"statement\":\"Negative proof must not manufacture the refusal, blocked event, gap or verdict being tested. The supported path is public entry → admitted GTL composition owning topology → named GraphFunction callable contract → implementation/plugin limited to admitted seam → ABG traversal/event/continuation/replay truth → replay projection → typed Product outcome/continuation. CLI, SDK, service, adapter, plugin, fixture, query and projection cannot become rival controllers. The consumer chooses the concrete test/evidence mechanism; the section fixes the property it must prove.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:189251feeb02fd1ed1ffc48404549e03","key":1291,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:6fdea63aaeebf1d9349b481121a8bf88\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:0ca7e123739fe9e8cd201c94ddb48a7c\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:189251feeb02fd1ed1ffc48404549e03\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[\"A live requirement without an executable witness stops holding the enclosing carrier open when realized, explicitly deferred or explicitly repriced out of the active branch.\"],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1567,\"path\":\"standards/ODD.md\",\"quote\":\"A product that publishes graph functions without this cumulative\\nenvironment law has a line that is graph-shaped but structurally wrong\\n(P4a, P6).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ODD.md#ODD%2F11.%20Core%20law%2F11.8%20Cumulative%20environment%20law%20is%20mandatory\",\"start_line\":1565},{\"end_line\":1583,\"path\":\"standards/ODD.md\",\"quote\":\"For current product closure, live current requirements that lack an\\nexecutable proof witness keep the enclosing carrier open until they are\\nrealised, explicitly deferred, or explicitly repriced out of the active\\nbranch. For the active software line the immediate pressure is usually a\\nrealised testcase or archived test evidence, but the governing law is\\nproof-lane aware: the witness must be a governed realised proof surface\\nappropriate to the requirement class (P2, P6).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ODD.md#ODD%2F11.%20Core%20law%2F11.9%20Global%20convergence%20must%20be%20stable%20under%20zoom\",\"start_line\":1577}],\"statement\":\"Published graph functions must obey cumulative-environment law rather than last-output-to-next-input wiring; explicit requires/provides/carries declarations remain a should. Local green arcs alone do not establish global closure: refined chains must lawfully close, preserve coarse contracts and agree across zoom. Live current requirements lacking appropriate executable proof keep the enclosing carrier open subject only to realization, explicit deferral or explicit repricing out of the active branch.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:8941f78d61def12e4bb55b7a77459a89","key":1292,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:e22ced7f66cd72435a045f8206873289\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:1a237778b4d22a437e7c3d2c0bd6aca4\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:8941f78d61def12e4bb55b7a77459a89\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"Installed proof applies where an installable development form exists; mandatory graph-function construction applies where the product provides ODD framework behavior.\"],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1606,\"path\":\"standards/ODD.md\",\"quote\":\"Direct source checks stay useful and do not\\nreplace installed-dev proof (P6, P3).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ODD.md#ODD%2F13.%20Installed-dev%20rule\",\"start_line\":1605},{\"end_line\":1616,\"path\":\"standards/ODD.md\",\"quote\":\"The product should be developed through the same graph-native method it\\nclaims to provide. Where the product provides ODD framework behaviour, it\\nmust build that behaviour through ODD graph functions and must not merely\\npublish ODD-shaped artifacts after imperative execution has already\\ndecided the work.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ODD.md#ODD%2F14.%20Dogfooding%20rule\",\"start_line\":1612}],\"statement\":\"Direct source checks do not replace decisive isolated installed-dev proof. Developing the product through its own graph-native method is recommended generally. Building provided ODD framework behavior through ODD graph functions is mandatory; publishing ODD-shaped artifacts after imperative execution decided the work is prohibited.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:5f942b306e0c02de2cbd93edaa8c1e39","key":1293,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:bcaa8a8d820aec2a089181d683a453df\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:c268d2b1bafeebb5b3c54ed7be08bb2e\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:26c627c4204c2f1f3b1820e20d788928\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:6fdea63aaeebf1d9349b481121a8bf88\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:0ca7e123739fe9e8cd201c94ddb48a7c\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:4e9e4a92055d8fabb6a672153a494baa\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:5f942b306e0c02de2cbd93edaa8c1e39\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"Any listed failure is sufficient for violation of this profile.\"],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1635,\"path\":\"standards/ODD.md\",\"quote\":\"This profile is violated when any of these holds (P6):\\n\\n1. a claimed product step has no corresponding node or vector;\\n2. a graph function exists with no clear outer contract;\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ODD.md#ODD%2F16.%20Failure%20pattern\",\"start_line\":1632}],\"statement\":\"Violations are: a claimed step lacking node/vector; function lacking clear outer contract; automation not describable as manual traversal; installed-product dependence on authoring-carrier knowledge absent from clean targets; scenarios unable to name significant proving paths; closure without target-relative evidence; wiring bypassing cumulative environment; zoom disagreement; service-owned operative transition lacking published function outcome contract; workspace-first framework orchestration labeled GTL afterward; imperative closure/continuation/semantic-target movement/lineage truth outside declared graph-function, ABG or Product carriers; hidden execution authority in product/plugin for traversal, actor invocation, process supervision, retry, continuation, runtime events, projection or closure folds; flattening lawful yield into retry/block/timeout/local waiting/hidden CLI loop; query/postflight/service/operator decisions outside the constructive loop; or inability to follow the constitutional process end-to-end from declared authority, or acceptance of a constitutional artifact without deterministic admission.\",\"uncertainty\":\"The agentic inability condition is read with §11.7A's explicit distinction between qualified method defects and agent error.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:2125e46f9d04bd450fd69581a6ba0660","key":1294,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:e7edc30111d4c0953afc57895e74e66f\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:e185446f4b1c692b239122ba48b7c9d5\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:2125e46f9d04bd450fd69581a6ba0660\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1699,\"path\":\"standards/ODD.md\",\"quote\":\"The instruction does not mean starting from imperative scripts and adding\\nGTL words later, treating graph functions as documentation wrappers, or\\nletting service code become the hidden real carrier (P0, P6).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ODD.md#ODD%2F17.%20Invocation%20rule\",\"start_line\":1697},{\"end_line\":1779,\"path\":\"standards/ODD.md\",\"quote\":\"Operative framework behaviour must be built outcome-first: outcome\\ntraversals first, declarative GTL/ABG carrier structure second, minimal\\nimperative adapter code last.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ODD.md#ODD%2F20.%20Canonical%20compression\",\"start_line\":1777}],\"statement\":\"Outcome traversals precede declarative GTL/ABG structure, which precedes minimal imperative adapter code. The invocation sequence cannot be replaced by imperative scripts later relabeled GTL, graph functions used as documentation wrappers or service code acting as hidden carrier. The canonical compression owns no determination; a differing source section decides.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:48308cbbf0a5ce6617b54bcd60e8cf17","key":1295,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:bcaa8a8d820aec2a089181d683a453df\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:26c627c4204c2f1f3b1820e20d788928\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:48308cbbf0a5ce6617b54bcd60e8cf17\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"An LLM is ramping into an ODD product.\"],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1766,\"path\":\"standards/ODD.md\",\"quote\":\"If those questions cannot be answered quickly, the product is not yet\\nsufficiently ODD-shaped (P0, P2).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ODD.md#ODD%2F19.%20Ramp-up%20checklist\",\"start_line\":1765}],\"statement\":\"The LLM should quickly recover: semantic source-to-outcome chain; typed domain assets/nodes; public functions; catalogue and GTL locations; ABG/Product ownership split; projection/query lane; each projection's admitted source and structural-drift fail-closed behavior; proof execution authority has not escaped ABG; constructive loop; closure vocabulary and replay-visible yield; capability-closing proof surfaces; outer carrier kept open by live unproved requirements despite inner green lanes; and whether an agent can follow declared authority alone with deterministic artifact admission. If these cannot be answered quickly, the product is not yet sufficiently ODD-shaped.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:637bfbd64a2e3f39befb6556e0cdf81d","key":1296,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:43a55d217680888d5abfc84ed0225020\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:637bfbd64a2e3f39befb6556e0cdf81d\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":37,\"path\":\"standards/POSTING_GUIDE.md\",\"quote\":\"Use a post when the content is provisional, investigative, comparative,\\nargumentative or not yet ratified (P6).\\n\\nDo not use a post for live requirements, live design decisions or active\\nprocess law. Those belong in the applicable bound WHAT surfaces or the\\nratified design surfaces (P6, P3).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/POSTING_GUIDE.md#POSTING_GUIDE%2F2.%20Boundary\",\"start_line\":32}],\"statement\":\"Posts carry provisional, investigative, comparative, argumentative or unratified content. Live requirements, live design decisions and active process law belong in applicable bound WHAT or ratified design surfaces and must not be carried as posts. Location, visibility and Closed state cannot confer ticket, Product, requirement or design authority.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:a81ccd12dfc669f38c8bfd2f703ca2bb","key":1297,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:43a55d217680888d5abfc84ed0225020\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:39bdea0a1e0944501e86c53001a7d5cb\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:38b9914ee8bbc6790e310e2774932d74\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:a81ccd12dfc669f38c8bfd2f703ca2bb\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":147,\"path\":\"standards/POSTING_GUIDE.md\",\"quote\":\"1. State whether the post describes current reality, target direction or\\n   both (P1).\\n2. Keep findings separate from recommendations (P6).\\n3. Make claims with exact file or requirement references (P3, P6).\\n4. Do not present a post as if it were already ratified (P6).\\n5. Do not rewrite closed history by stealth. An open post may be revised\\n   in place; a closed post should normally be superseded by a new post\\n   (P4b, P3).\\n6. Keep each post to one bounded subject (P2).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/POSTING_GUIDE.md#POSTING_GUIDE%2F8.%20Posting%20rules\",\"start_line\":139}],\"statement\":\"Each post uses one listed category and the base template, with a MATRIX decision table replacing central free prose. It must identify current reality, target direction or both; separate findings from recommendations; support claims with exact file/requirement refs; avoid presenting itself as ratified; preserve closed history against stealth rewriting; and concern one bounded subject. Its subject should be short, specific and stable enough for later scanning. Default file carriers use the prescribed timestamp/category/subject filename; non-file carriers must retain equivalent identity/history fields. Status explicitly records discussion state.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:c311423d514f30b594396b52d39f68c0","key":1298,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:43a55d217680888d5abfc84ed0225020\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:c311423d514f30b594396b52d39f68c0\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":153,\"path\":\"standards/POSTING_GUIDE.md\",\"quote\":\"A post becomes consequential only when its content is explicitly adopted\\ninto a bound WHAT surface, ratified design or accepted implementation.\\nUntil then it is commentary, not law (P6).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/POSTING_GUIDE.md#POSTING_GUIDE%2F9.%20Ratification\",\"start_line\":151},{\"end_line\":161,\"path\":\"standards/POSTING_GUIDE.md\",\"quote\":\"A post that carries such evidence or proposes such a change does not\\nadopt it (§9) (P6).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/POSTING_GUIDE.md#POSTING_GUIDE%2F10.%20Shared%20method%20adoption\",\"start_line\":160}],\"statement\":\"Post content becomes consequential only through explicit adoption into bound WHAT, ratified design or accepted implementation. Closing a discussion is not adoption. Carrying incident/review evidence or proposing reusable method change does not adopt it; STDO-UP-012 propagation remains governed by SPEC_METHOD §6.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:4000129d15d7020acc4f090ed27f4ace","key":1299,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:8048859bf02f15f5c3158d9ca21e6198\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:c1ed13a1e7694716094389e56c921b63\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:4000129d15d7020acc4f090ed27f4ace\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[\"A directory may contain multiple definitions only when it contains multiple distinct product WHATs.\"],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":49,\"path\":\"standards/PRODUCT_DEFINITION.md\",\"quote\":\"Every product defined under this method publishes one JSON definition for\\neach distinct current product WHAT. Its conventional filename is\\n`stdo_<label>.json`; `stdo_default.json` is the default for a source\\nproject with one product definition. A directory may hold more than one\\ndefinition when it hosts more than one distinct product WHAT, and only\\nthen. Several build tenants realising the same WHAT are entries in one definition and\\nnever add definition files (P3).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/PRODUCT_DEFINITION.md#PRODUCT_DEFINITION%2F1.%20Overlay%20and%20layout%20independence\",\"start_line\":43}],\"statement\":\"Publish exactly one JSON definition per distinct current WHAT; additional tenants of the same WHAT are entries, never additional definitions. A definition identity may persist across successive releases; forks, replacements or independently governed WHATs require another definition_id. Immutable Product/release identities remain separate. Product-definition, immutable Product, bounded-context and tenant identity URIs remain subject to IDENTITY and owning authority; URI, filename, path, label or proximity creates/widens no identity or authority. Relative refs resolve from retrieval URI, not assumed source-project proximity. Overlay/schema/template own only locator/relation shape, never referenced content.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:0c48e88a1339f1f4399a7a4d739d609b","key":1300,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:8048859bf02f15f5c3158d9ca21e6198\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:0c48e88a1339f1f4399a7a4d739d609b\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"For every Product Definition.\"],\"exceptions\":[\"product.bounded_context is null if no separate enclosing context is claimed; sprint bindings are optional.\"],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":173,\"path\":\"standards/PRODUCT_DEFINITION.md\",\"quote\":\"- `composition`: explicit relations to other product definitions; and\\n- `$schema` and `kind`: the schema locator and the\\n  `stdo.product-definition` discriminator.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/PRODUCT_DEFINITION.md#PRODUCT_DEFINITION%2F2.%20Required%20definition%20relations\",\"start_line\":171}],\"statement\":\"Each definition contains product identity/display name/source locator/explicit enclosing context or null; constitution.stdo source repository, mutable discovery selector and exact installed basis/deterministic manifest digest; every non-STDO set in additional_authorities; basis-qualified entrypoints; agent_bootstrap entrypoint and marker-managed targets; local axioms/overrides/disambiguations with owner/target/basis/scope and applicable context resolution; one or more accepted reference_frame_bases with authorities/scopes; current what Intent/Product/specification bindings; how shared surfaces and one or more independent tenants; ticketing Goals/tickets/comments/optional sprints; explicit composition; $schema and kind=stdo.product-definition. Repeating source truth in JSON is non-conformant rival authority. product.bounded_context identifies only enclosing WHAT context, not an exhaustive registry or flattened subordinate/peer/composed/tenant/user/runtime namespace; local disambiguations name their exact contexts.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:661414fcc745a500d44dfd319f2c668a","key":1301,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:4650f9cc9cfd8d82c104f3c11bf25352\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:8048859bf02f15f5c3158d9ca21e6198\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:cd46ea3f9d64e23d695883c0d8fb98b2\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:661414fcc745a500d44dfd319f2c668a\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"The family consequences use the declared instance premises, not foundational commitments alone.\"],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":142,\"path\":\"standards/PRODUCT_DEFINITION.md\",\"quote\":\"Each consumer applies the rule and decides nothing the owning section does\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/PRODUCT_DEFINITION.md#PRODUCT_DEFINITION%2F1.%20Overlay%20and%20layout%20independence%2FFoundation%20to%20law%3A%20binding%20a%20project%20to%20the%20method\",\"start_line\":142}],\"statement\":\"F12 consequences preserve project-owned WHAT and layout without becoming part of the method; one locating definition per WHAT without repeated content; separate definition/Product/release/tenant/project identities and explicit verified composition; exactly one applicable discovered definition or fail closed; complete constitutional sufficiency without entrypoint replacement or design-invented Product meaning; one exact complete immutable release verified before use, owner acceptance of exact change plans, and fail-closed unverifiable state with prior state kept/recovered; exactly one context-qualified material meaning after authorized resolution; imports preserving owner meaning and authority, with changed applicability rebound and missing meaning/adoption/authority reported before reliance; Product-admitted frame engagement with availability/adoption/activation and frame/actor/lineage identities distinct; one tenant registry and separate Goals/ticket/comment authorities; one owner per law, members governing together as one release, source-condition/digest-preserving derived surfaces stale on source change, digest equality proving identity not fidelity; and bootstrap from the selected release template into existing surfaces without a rival local method root, with initial requirements from any legitimate constitutional input. Each consumer applies only its owner's rule. Widening Product scope to executable tool/runtime/realization requires separate explicit human authorization.\",\"uncertainty\":\"Detailed foundational standing, referenced rule implementations and external consumer loci are not supplied.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:3cd00d2e5e4fc68054cf3d1e4d17a19d","key":1302,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:cd46ea3f9d64e23d695883c0d8fb98b2\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:8048859bf02f15f5c3158d9ca21e6198\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:3cd00d2e5e4fc68054cf3d1e4d17a19d\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":216,\"path\":\"standards/PRODUCT_DEFINITION.md\",\"quote\":\"The STDO basis identifies one complete\\nimmutable RC cut and its exact installed-release manifest, never a\\nhand-selected subset. Each `constitution.entrypoints[]` member names the\\nbasis against which its URI resolves. Entry points are derived navigation\\nand can neither narrow nor replace a complete selected constitution (P3,\\nP6).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/PRODUCT_DEFINITION.md#PRODUCT_DEFINITION%2F3.%20Constitutional-set%20sufficiency\",\"start_line\":211}],\"statement\":\"The complete governing set must collectively recover all five dimensions for its scope. constitution.stdo.basis locates one complete immutable RC cut and exact installed manifest, never a selected subset; additional_authorities locates every additional set/source. Each entrypoint names its resolving basis and cannot narrow/replace the set. Product-meaning ontology belongs in or is cited by bound WHAT. Accepted realization design ontology has semantic-design authority only for its boundary, derives from WHAT and applicable methods, and cannot invent missing Product meaning.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:5924df7ef7c9d04b8c4ace6096e61f93","key":1303,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:af0ac7f76ba62dab9f89ee2789b6ecd2\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:22c3599132a83101cd9b734284661c93\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:5924df7ef7c9d04b8c4ace6096e61f93\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":256,\"path\":\"standards/PRODUCT_DEFINITION.md\",\"quote\":\"Plan hashing covers the acceptance object only: local installation status\\nand machine-local install paths are excluded. The canonical bytes are UTF-8\\nJSON with recursively sorted object keys, two-space indentation, LF line\\nendings and one final LF. Fleet order is deterministic discovery-path\\norder. These rules make a presented digest independently reproducible\\nrather than an opaque session token (P3, P6).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/PRODUCT_DEFINITION.md#PRODUCT_DEFINITION%2F4.%20Shared%20installed%20release%20basis%20and%20toolchain%20manager\",\"start_line\":251},{\"end_line\":375,\"path\":\"standards/PRODUCT_DEFINITION.md\",\"quote\":\"It uses the same\\ncanonical JSON hashing rule. Already-installed status supplies no\\nadditional authority and does not change the digest. Mutation requires\\nexplicit acceptance of this exact plan and re-derives it; possession of its\\ndigest alone grants no operation authority.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/PRODUCT_DEFINITION.md#PRODUCT_DEFINITION%2F4.%20Shared%20installed%20release%20basis%20and%20toolchain%20manager%2FExplicit%20complete%20consumer%20update\",\"start_line\":370}],\"statement\":\"Canonical plan hashing uses UTF-8 JSON, recursively sorted object keys, two-space indentation, LF endings and one final LF. Basis-only Adoption Plans exclude machine-local installation paths/status; fleet plans order by deterministic discovery path. Complete update uses the same serialization but additionally binds physical destinations/preimages and selected cohort/routes/source observations. Already-installed status changes neither its digest nor authority. Digest possession alone never grants operation authority; mutation requires explicit acceptance and exact re-derivation.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:6a399b88f8478abe19f44f96e05aac01","key":1304,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:f5ea64751cc1eb33ef2ae5a9bbc3b09a\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:395e42597f3b0df9d733f31d1b45bed9\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:6a399b88f8478abe19f44f96e05aac01\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":290,\"path\":\"standards/PRODUCT_DEFINITION.md\",\"quote\":\"`constitution.stdo.source.repository` identifies the transport source.\\n`constitution.stdo.selector` is a mutable `stdo://channels/<version>`\\ndiscovery selector whose alias semantics are owned by the release law (the\\n[RELEASE](RELEASE.md) member). Neither is operative authority.\\n`constitution.stdo.basis.uri` and `constitution.stdo.basis.manifest_sha256`\\nare the sole authored STDO selection for that Product Definition (P6, P3).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/PRODUCT_DEFINITION.md#PRODUCT_DEFINITION%2F4.%20Shared%20installed%20release%20basis%20and%20toolchain%20manager\",\"start_line\":285}],\"statement\":\"Only constitution.stdo.basis.uri and manifest_sha256 author STDO selection; transport repository and mutable channel selector do not. Every manager-owned component from configured store root downward must be a physical directory or regular file of declared type. Symlinks, junctions, reparse points, devices, sockets, other redirections/special entries fail closed. Verification inventories all entry types including directories, rejects entries not derived from exact manifest file paths and never follows unmanifested aliases. No cache, registry, checkout, alias, schema or agent file may silently replace the selected basis. Every case-insensitively parsed stdo: schema locator must name that same immutable cut before schema loading.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:d943d98743c2a82b22f2537ec2a8e570","key":1305,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:f5ea64751cc1eb33ef2ae5a9bbc3b09a\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:af0ac7f76ba62dab9f89ee2789b6ecd2\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:d943d98743c2a82b22f2537ec2a8e570\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":312,\"path\":\"standards/PRODUCT_DEFINITION.md\",\"quote\":\"- mutating `adopt` requires that exact prior plan digest as explicit\\n  acceptance, re-derives it before installation, installs only the bound\\n  target, rechecks the Product Definition bytes, and atomically changes\\n  only its basis and its basis-relative schema locator; any drift refuses\\n  mutation;\\n- `status`, `verify`, `list`, `manifest` and `resolve` are read-only with\\n  respect to Product Definitions; and\\n- fleet adoption emits, and requires explicit acceptance of, one aggregate\\n  plan digest over every per-definition plan; all fleet writes require\\n  explicit whole-selection authorisation and infer no composition or\\n  inheritance from directory nesting.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/PRODUCT_DEFINITION.md#PRODUCT_DEFINITION%2F4.%20Shared%20installed%20release%20basis%20and%20toolchain%20manager\",\"start_line\":302}],\"statement\":\"install admits one explicitly named immutable RC without changing definitions. sync installs/verifies only the selected exact basis and never consults selector. adopt --dry-run resolves annotated selector/immutable RC and presents cut/tag/commit/tree/manifest/current-definition-byte/plan digests without mutation. Mutating adopt requires exact prior plan acceptance, re-derives before installation, installs only bound target, rechecks definition bytes and atomically changes only basis and basis-relative schema; drift refuses. status/verify/list/manifest/resolve are definition-read-only. Fleet adoption requires accepted aggregate digest over every per-definition plan and whole-selection authorization for all writes; nesting implies neither composition nor inheritance. Missing cuts, moved immutable tags, tag/commit or manifest mismatches, missing/extra/changed members, ambiguous discovery, unaccepted/stale plans, URI escape, redirected store, undeclared entry types or malformed markers fail closed.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1f