ON%2F4.%20Shared%20installed%20release%20basis%20and%20toolchain%20manager\",\"start_line\":333}],\"statement\":\"agent_bootstrap embeds no other constitution; it names one basis-qualified entrypoint and marker-managed discovery blocks in local instruction files. Targets are portable relative paths resolved against product.source_project; absolute paths, parent traversal, redirection and escape fail closed. Fleet source projects stay within the explicitly authorized fleet root and every target is preflighted before first write. Replace exactly one correctly ordered marker span, preserving all outside bytes including trailing whitespace; append preserves old bytes as exact prefix. Bootstrap only routes to definition/exact basis/owners. Recursive discovery prunes exact names .git, .hg, .svn, .bzr, .venv, venv, node_modules, vendor, site-packages, build, dist, out, target, .gradle, .tox, .nox, .cache, .ruff_cache, .mypy_cache, .pytest_cache, __pycache__, .genesis and .stdo. A discovered definition cannot itself be a symlink. Pruning is not proof that excluded trees lack independently governed Products.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:526b32ceccd6ba011c3dee636a514469","key":1307,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:22c3599132a83101cd9b734284661c93\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:526b32ceccd6ba011c3dee636a514469\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[\"Newly staged immutable installs may remain unused after refusal/failure.\"],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":385,\"path\":\"standards/PRODUCT_DEFINITION.md\",\"quote\":\"Only the selected basis and schema, the existing\\ncomposition locators and contracts, and the selected native and install\\nlinks may change; historical installs and unrelated consumer content stay\\navailable and unchanged. It creates no consumer-local checker and changes\\nno Product meaning or local semantic map (P3, P6, P2).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/PRODUCT_DEFINITION.md#PRODUCT_DEFINITION%2F4.%20Shared%20installed%20release%20basis%20and%20toolchain%20manager%2FExplicit%20complete%20consumer%20update\",\"start_line\":381}],\"statement\":\"cohort-update first presents the complete plan without consumer effects; exact accepted plan is re-derived before mutation. Verify selected cohort dependency closure and each companion definition/release record/admitted members before reliance. Stage absent immutable installs, verify existing ones without in-place repair and preflight every consumer target. Changes are restricted to selected basis/schema, existing composition locators/contracts and selected native/install links; historical installs and unrelated content remain unchanged/available. No consumer-local checker, Product meaning change or local semantic-map change is created. adopt/sync/fleet keep their narrower contracts. Caller explicitly selects every native route and derived context; empty selection means selected none, not semantic absence.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:f6053c33585181fce7b2e775fd032b72","key":1308,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:22c3599132a83101cd9b734284661c93\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:f6053c33585181fce7b2e775fd032b72\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":402,\"path\":\"standards/PRODUCT_DEFINITION.md\",\"quote\":\"The operation requires an exclusive consumer\\nwrite scope during application. It claims no crash-atomic transaction\\nacross independent filesystem paths: abrupt process or host loss, or\\nunavailable rollback storage, requires recovery from the presented\\npreimages before the complete relation can be claimed (P5, P4b).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/PRODUCT_DEFINITION.md#PRODUCT_DEFINITION%2F4.%20Shared%20installed%20release%20basis%20and%20toolchain%20manager%2FExplicit%20complete%20consumer%20update\",\"start_line\":398}],\"statement\":\"For every selected derived context, missing/ambiguous/changed/unavailable program, map or source evidence holds the whole update before consumer effects. Only the source owner performs semantic re-entry; the manager cannot relabel old maps current. Source freshness proves integrity, not semantic conformance/verdict. After staging, recheck consumer preimages and source evidence; report completion only after verifying every selected resulting binding/companion. Pre-effect refusal retains prior state; caught application failure restores affected preimages and reports no completion. Application requires exclusive consumer write scope. No cross-path crash atomicity is claimed; process/host loss or unavailable rollback requires preimage recovery before claiming the complete relation.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:67ded2dedaec06fd2c8935476ae4ed37","key":1309,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:523af2ab7853a047877a596bb6f7f95e\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:22c3599132a83101cd9b734284661c93\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:67ded2dedaec06fd2c8935476ae4ed37\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"For operations with an intended external write effect, including install, sync, mutating adopt, fleet adoption and complete update.\"],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":440,\"path\":\"standards/PRODUCT_DEFINITION.md\",\"quote\":\"Abrupt process or\\n  host loss, where no caught failure establishes that the update fell\\n  short, is `completion_unknown` (`indeterminate`), never `completed` or\\n  `not_effected`. `completion_unknown`, and `not_effected` with its end\\n  not established, are effects of uncertain completion under\\n  [ACTIVATION §3 Effects](ACTIVATION.md#effects): recovery from the\\n  presented preimages reconciles them, as\\n  [ACTIVATION §5](ACTIVATION.md#5-work-state-and-restart) states, before\\n  any repetition or claim of the complete relation.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/PRODUCT_DEFINITION.md#PRODUCT_DEFINITION%2F4.%20Shared%20installed%20release%20basis%20and%20toolchain%20manager%2FExplicit%20complete%20consumer%20update\",\"start_line\":432}],\"statement\":\"For 'intended effect occurred', completed→satisfied requires evidence of the entire effect. Refusal before any effect with retained prior-state evidence is not_effected→falsified and ended. Caught application failure is also not_effected→falsified: the complete update fell short and no later part is applied, regardless of rollback verification. Verified restoration establishes the effect's end; unverified restoration or unavailable rollback leaves the end unestablished, recorded as a residual naming needed verification without changing falsified. Name unused newly staged installs as the part that did occur. Abrupt process/host loss without a caught failure establishing shortfall yields completion_unknown→indeterminate, never completed or not_effected. Reconcile unknown completion or unestablished end from presented preimages before repetition or complete-relation claims.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:376da32340c26bfdd9b306a4adff8b95","key":1310,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:523af2ab7853a047877a596bb6f7f95e\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:f5ea64751cc1eb33ef2ae5a9bbc3b09a\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:376da32340c26bfdd9b306a4adff8b95\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":468,\"path\":\"standards/PRODUCT_DEFINITION.md\",\"quote\":\"- Command without an intended effect. A command without an intended\\n  external effect, such as `verify` or `adopt --dry-run`, has no value\\n  under Effects, and its refusal maps by cause as above. A condition it\\n  reports about the subject it evaluates, such as a member that `verify`\\n  finds missing, extra or changed, is a counterexample to that command's\\n  own predicate, `falsified`, not a refusal.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/PRODUCT_DEFINITION.md#PRODUCT_DEFINITION%2F4.%20Shared%20installed%20release%20basis%20and%20toolchain%20manager%2FExplicit%20complete%20consumer%20update\",\"start_line\":463}],\"statement\":\"Refusal also answers whether the operation may apply its effect on its exact subject/basis. Before commencement this is admission/activation; afterward it is construction availability. Missing exact-plan acceptance or fleet whole-selection authorization is missing operation authority: admission_refused(authority)→out_of_frame, naming required acceptance/authorization and owner. Every other refusal listed by the source has a basis cause, including byte/preimage drift, stale plan, ambiguous discovery/no exact subject, integrity failures, path/locator/marker boundary failure and deficient derived evidence: admission_refused(basis) before beginning or re_entry_requested(basis) after, both invalid_basis, naming failed coordinates and applicable source owner. Commands without intended external effect have no Effects result; refusals still map by cause. A verify finding of a missing/extra/changed member is falsified for its own predicate, not a refusal. Refused/failed/unknown operations must not be combined as completed; known caught failure with unverified restoration must not be called undecided; missing acceptance must not be called defective basis.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:5c8e1a6c768fd13179a30007be1de6ba","key":1311,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:c92508f838e93201cd94c393f5aefdbd\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:5c8e1a6c768fd13179a30007be1de6ba\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"For every material term occurrence.\"],\"exceptions\":[\"An owning document/section/schema field/operation may explicitly declare a context for subordinate occurrences, avoiding repeated qualifiers when resolution is unique.\"],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":521,\"path\":\"standards/PRODUCT_DEFINITION.md\",\"quote\":\"1. identify the occurrence's governed scope and nearest explicit\\n   bounded-context declaration;\\n2. identify the exact selected basis and the authorities applicable to\\n   that context and scope;\\n3. collect the context-local definitions and the explicitly imported\\n   concept references admitted by those authorities and that basis;\\n4. apply every applicable owner-authorised override or disambiguation; and\\n5. admit the occurrence only when exactly one concept remains.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/PRODUCT_DEFINITION.md#PRODUCT_DEFINITION%2F5.%20Bounded-context%20semantic%20resolution\",\"start_line\":514}],\"statement\":\"A context exists only through owning-authority declaration of stable identity, owner, selected basis and semantic scope; a consumer defines inside it only through explicit owner relation. Resolve by scope/nearest explicit context, then exact basis/applicable authorities, then admitted local definitions/imported refs, then all applicable authorized overrides/disambiguations, admitting only one remaining concept. Equal spelling/capitalization/shape/location/nesting/actor/implementation establishes no equal meaning, identity, equivalence, inheritance or authority; differing spelling proves no difference. Filename, heading, index, glossary, schema value, URI, repository, prompt, actor or proximity cannot accidentally declare context. Relations require the semantic address or explicit authorized relation.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:c5cdad46bf308f2f8cc5c0085c8eb2d8","key":1312,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:c92508f838e93201cd94c393f5aefdbd\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:c5cdad46bf308f2f8cc5c0085c8eb2d8\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"Zero or multiple applicable concepts remain at a material boundary.\"],\"exceptions\":[\"A dependent evaluation returns indeterminate where admissible evidence also cannot decide the claim and supplies that ground; otherwise the undeclared selecting relation grounds out_of_frame.\"],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":540,\"path\":\"standards/PRODUCT_DEFINITION.md\",\"quote\":\"For an evaluation that depends on such an occurrence,\\nthe definition, import or disambiguation that would select one concept is\\na material relation its frame does not declare: the evaluation returns\\n`out_of_frame` and names that relation and its owner, or returns\\n`indeterminate` where the admissible evidence also cannot decide the\\nclaim and so gives that ground too, and in either case names the ground,\\nas [FOUNDATIONS §4 Results](FOUNDATIONS.md#results), Out of frame or\\nindeterminate, states (P5, P1).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/PRODUCT_DEFINITION.md#PRODUCT_DEFINITION%2F5.%20Bounded-context%20semantic%20resolution\",\"start_line\":533}],\"statement\":\"Zero concepts is unresolved meaning; multiple concepts is ambiguous meaning. Both fail closed for agents, designs, schemas, implementations, tests, translations and reviewers; none may choose by familiarity, frequency, recency, nominal match or context-free glossary fallback. Dependent evaluation names the missing definition/import/disambiguation relation and owner and returns the grounded out_of_frame or indeterminate outcome, not false. Glossary is only a locator to exact context-declaring/concept-owning clauses; it defines neither, repairs no declaration and supplies no shared default. Its indexed concept applies only through the selected semantic address or explicit target import.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:f963e68e752a5d0e893fc9744d0383c8","key":1313,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:54629b053141a69765f840b7f0c3f90c\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:f963e68e752a5d0e893fc9744d0383c8\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"For every cross-context relation.\"],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":563,\"path\":\"standards/PRODUCT_DEFINITION.md\",\"quote\":\"- the preserved meaning, changed meaning, loss and refusal conditions;\\n- the source and target semantic owners, without transferring either\\n  authority;\\n- the selected source and target bases, the governed scope and\\n  provenance; and\\n- its lifecycle and invalidation conditions.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/PRODUCT_DEFINITION.md#PRODUCT_DEFINITION%2F5.%20Bounded-context%20semantic%20resolution\",\"start_line\":558}],\"statement\":\"Require explicit owner authorization and a carrier naming exact source/target concept refs and context identities; kind; direction and material lawful inverse; preserved/changed meaning, loss/refusal conditions; both semantic owners without authority transfer; both selected bases; scope/provenance; lifecycle/invalidation. The owner is distinct from the owning clause resolved by a concept reference. Meaning change/narrowing/loss cannot be called import. Equivalence needs governing-authority equality, not spelling or opposite translations. Disambiguation neither equates concepts nor imports by itself. No kind widens authority. Specialisation additionally specifies exact target, preserved/narrowed meaning, excluded source instances and absent/lawful inverse; its label alone establishes nothing. The source relates these kinds to AC-012 without making that reference an executed calculus operation.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:4ae36210060079618b508c86edbd17f5","key":1314,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:b698ebbf7b1bde39a0a5b16677367aa6\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:4ae36210060079618b508c86edbd17f5\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":633,\"path\":\"standards/PRODUCT_DEFINITION.md\",\"quote\":\"An empty local array explicitly declares that no local entry of that kind\\nis bound for the product. Omission is not an equivalent declaration (P6,\\nP4b).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/PRODUCT_DEFINITION.md#PRODUCT_DEFINITION%2F6.%20Local%20constitutional%20binding\",\"start_line\":631}],\"statement\":\"Each local axiom/override/disambiguation must name decision URI, existing lawful authority, applicable overridden clause/resolved ambiguity and exact scope; file category or overlay listing grants no authority. Disambiguations additionally require exact lexical term, context identity, complete material candidate refs, resolves_to as one of those candidates, every selected semantic basis, and uri/authority/applies_to. Cross-context candidates require the resolution-owning carrier's complete import/translation/equivalence relation. Empty arrays explicitly bind no entries of that kind; omission is not equivalent.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:b237cbb2e0d6d2be4a743a5e3d6397bf","key":1315,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:24eaed2b3ae25fcb1bde979499653b21\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:6e2b00300849fee60f54d5d16d37822d\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:8048859bf02f15f5c3158d9ca21e6198\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:b237cbb2e0d6d2be4a743a5e3d6397bf\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":691,\"path\":\"standards/PRODUCT_DEFINITION.md\",\"quote\":\"An Agent Frame Activation does not mutate the overlay, and the overlay\\nregisters no agents, assigns no permanent frames and persists no temporary\\nactive frame configuration (P3, P0).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/PRODUCT_DEFINITION.md#PRODUCT_DEFINITION%2F7.%20Collective%20reference-frame%20basis\",\"start_line\":689}],\"statement\":\"reference_frame_bases is nonempty; every entry locates an accepted declaration, all lawful admitting authorities and exact governed Product/context/tenant/outcome/other scope. The referenced declaration, not JSON entry, owns frames, method/profile basis, outcome, binding rules, envelopes, grants, triggers, coverage, results and invalidation; the entry adopts no profile and creates no authority. Availability comes from cut inclusion, adoption only from Product authority and activation only from exact authorized actor/subject work instruction. Activation mutates no overlay; no agent registry, permanent frame assignment or temporary active configuration is persisted there. Frames and actors remain distinct, with no grant arising from actor name or broad frame beyond cited owners/exact activation. A domain/runtime carrier called Frame enters the collective set only through explicit declaration with required evaluation/authority relations.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:be18e2cae6424ee6897f6f89c48600c8","key":1316,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:24eaed2b3ae25fcb1bde979499653b21\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:be18e2cae6424ee6897f6f89c48600c8\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"The governed outcome crosses a chain of Products.\"],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":709,\"path\":\"standards/PRODUCT_DEFINITION.md\",\"quote\":\"Every directed\\nProduct-composition edge names its source and target roles, governing\\nauthority and contracts, lifecycle, evidence boundary, refusal and\\ninvalidation conditions. Common actors, repositories, files,\\nimplementations, outputs or tool access create no composition or identity\\nrelation (P3, P6).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/PRODUCT_DEFINITION.md#PRODUCT_DEFINITION%2F7.%20Collective%20reference-frame%20basis\",\"start_line\":704}],\"statement\":\"The frame basis records a Product-role map distinguishing mutable source projects, definitions, candidate checkpoints, cuts, released Products, installs, artifacts and dependent Products; each development-product role binds an exact install identity. Each directed composition edge names source/target roles, authority/contracts, lifecycle, evidence boundary, refusal and invalidation. Common actors/repos/files/implementations/outputs/tools create no composition or identity. The starter templates/PROJECT_REFERENCE_FRAME_BASIS_TEMPLATE.md is non-authoritative; adopting it requires replacing every placeholder with exact identities, owners, scopes, sources, grants, results and invalidation conditions and admitting the completed declaration under existing authority.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:9a70f805b1ebd57908ae5c8f29c02a5e","key":1317,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:1d16434fac1e65d9e2c7122fb8b5e138\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:71e0e361793d1a2f94d72888e297322b\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:9a70f805b1ebd57908ae5c8f29c02a5e\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[\"Specification may cite multiple surfaces; sprints are optional.\"],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":770,\"path\":\"standards/PRODUCT_DEFINITION.md\",\"quote\":\"Goals own the bounded work wave, ticket state stays ticket\\nauthority, and comments stay non-authoritative commentary (P6, P3). Which\\ncarrier a given work item takes is SPEC_METHOD §4 and the [TICKETS](TICKETS.md) member;\\nthis section binds where each carrier kind lives.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/PRODUCT_DEFINITION.md#PRODUCT_DEFINITION%2F8.%20WHAT%2C%20HOW%20and%20work%20carriers\",\"start_line\":767}],\"statement\":\"Intent and Product each have one canonical WHAT entrypoint; specification may locate multiple requirement/specification surfaces. Canonical how.build_tenants entries carry stable identities and root/design/implementation locations; an optional TENANT_REGISTRY.md is only companion/projection, never another identity/location authority. Common realization law requires explicit adoption across more than one tenant. Ticket lanes minimally include backlog, active and completed. Goals own work-wave truth, tickets own ticket state and comments remain commentary. This member binds locations, while SPEC_METHOD §4/TICKETS select the carrier for a particular work item.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:1f9f6efc8266d09773e8a011f2fc7f92","key":1318,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:ec08ef0caf1ef5504b20e94591bbea9d\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:1f9f6efc8266d09773e8a011f2fc7f92\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"A Product scope is requested.\"],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":780,\"path\":\"standards/PRODUCT_DEFINITION.md\",\"quote\":\"For a requested Product scope exactly one applicable definition is\\nselected; zero or several unresolved definitions fail closed, and a\\nsymlinked definition is refused (P6, P5).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/PRODUCT_DEFINITION.md#PRODUCT_DEFINITION%2F9.%20Recursive%20discovery%20and%20explicit%20composition\",\"start_line\":778}],\"statement\":\"Select exactly one applicable definition. Zero applicable definitions or several unresolved definitions fail closed; refuse a symlinked definition.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:595c7d81086874af431839d2265711eb","key":1319,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:ec08ef0caf1ef5504b20e94591bbea9d\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:8bdd42573e0cb3dc879df6ffa3bb6827\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:595c7d81086874af431839d2265711eb\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":803,\"path\":\"standards/PRODUCT_DEFINITION.md\",\"quote\":\"Resolution verifies both the locator and the expected identity. Moving a\\ndefinition requires a locator update and does not change its identity.\\nReplacing the content at the same locator with another definition identity\\nfails closed. When an edge binds exact immutable Product or release\\nversions, the cited relation and contracts also carry and verify those\\nidentities; the mutable definition identity cannot substitute for them\\n(P3, P5).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/PRODUCT_DEFINITION.md#PRODUCT_DEFINITION%2F9.%20Recursive%20discovery%20and%20explicit%20composition\",\"start_line\":797}],\"statement\":\"Directory nesting creates no implicit inheritance, ownership, composition or constitutional override; parent and child definitions remain independent until explicitly composed. Resolution verifies locator and expected target identity. Movement requires a locator update without identity change; replacement by a different identity at the same locator fails closed. Edges binding exact immutable Product or release versions also carry and verify those identities in their relation and contracts; a mutable definition identity cannot substitute.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:ce0f70d0f003874c6a1fd156454efe81","key":1320,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:d9ee38b33be5ec7706f3f3ad6cfcdc0c\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:ec08ef0caf1ef5504b20e94591bbea9d\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:8bdd42573e0cb3dc879df6ffa3bb6827\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:ce0f70d0f003874c6a1fd156454efe81\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"A discovered set claims conformance.\"],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":825,\"path\":\"standards/PRODUCT_DEFINITION.md\",\"quote\":\"- every composition target resolves to another product definition whose\\n  `product.definition_id` equals `target_definition_id`, and every\\n  relation and non-empty contract set resolves; and\\n- no two carriers claim authority for the same Product, tenant, ticket\\n  state or constitutional relation.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/PRODUCT_DEFINITION.md#PRODUCT_DEFINITION%2F9.%20Recursive%20discovery%20and%20explicit%20composition\",\"start_line\":821}],\"statement\":\"Every definition validates against its selected released schema; every required URI/fragment resolves within declared workspace/resolver boundaries; every product.definition_id is unique; every build-tenant identity is unique within its overlay; every governed scope has a resolvable applicable frame basis and overlapping bindings are reconciled by cited authority. Every local disambiguation binds one exact term, target context, complete material candidate set, selected concept, authority, basis and scope; resolves_to belongs to disambiguates and the referenced resolution carrier is congruent. Every material cross-context term seam uses explicit import, disambiguation, translation or equivalence, not nominal matching. Every composition target is another definition with the expected ID, and every relation and non-empty contract set resolves. No two carriers claim authority for the same Product, tenant, ticket state or constitutional relation.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:46e77f6a6710806e349bdb69689737a0","key":1321,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:d9ee38b33be5ec7706f3f3ad6cfcdc0c\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:46e77f6a6710806e349bdb69689737a0\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[\"Schema uri and uri-reference formats assert syntax only when the declared validator implements format assertion.\"],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":836,\"path\":\"standards/PRODUCT_DEFINITION.md\",\"quote\":\"Portable Draft 2020-12 JSON Schema validation establishes structural shape.\\nThe schema's `uri` and `uri-reference` formats are annotations unless the\\ndeclared validator implements format assertion. Conformance therefore\\nperforms an explicit RFC 3986 URI and URI-reference syntax check with an\\nassertion-capable validator, followed separately by resolution, fragment\\nexistence, selected-release identity, uniqueness across files,\\nconstitutional sufficiency, semantic-resolution and cross-context-relation\\ncompleteness, and authority-congruence checks. The structural subset and\\nthe semantic subset of these checks are distinct claims (EVALUATION §2;\\nP1, P6).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/PRODUCT_DEFINITION.md#PRODUCT_DEFINITION%2F9.%20Recursive%20discovery%20and%20explicit%20composition\",\"start_line\":827}],\"statement\":\"Conformance explicitly checks RFC 3986 URI and URI-reference syntax using an assertion-capable validator, then separately checks resolution, fragments, selected-release identity, cross-file uniqueness, constitutional sufficiency, semantic resolution, cross-context-relation completeness and authority congruence. Structural validation is not semantic conformance.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:459def3028b0204d0c862b7a4ff725b2","key":1322,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:ea41d0e99982e9880a7fa88c1f2c15a4\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:459def3028b0204d0c862b7a4ff725b2\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"No explicit cross-context relation is supplied.\"],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":849,\"path\":\"standards/PRODUCT_DEFINITION.md\",\"quote\":\"| `Frame` | the reference-frame-evaluation context (REFERENCE_FRAME §1) and a consumer-owned runtime carrier | remain distinct; nominal match cannot enrol the runtime carrier as an evaluation frame |\\n| `Owner` | a generic specialist evaluation family and a semantic or decision authority owner | remain distinct; the evaluation family acquires no owner authority |\\n| `Product` | an immutable released Product and a mutable Product Definition | remain distinct and select only through the occurrence's declared context |\\n| `Tenant` | an STDO build realisation and hosted, customer, account, runtime or data tenancy | remain distinct; build tenancy supplies no default for the other contexts |\\n| `User` | a Product role, human person, identity principal, account, actor, operator or data subject | unresolved until downstream authority defines or explicitly relates the applicable meanings |\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/PRODUCT_DEFINITION.md#PRODUCT_DEFINITION%2F10.%20Semantic-resolution%20conformance%20cases\",\"start_line\":845}],\"statement\":\"Frame: evaluation frame and consumer runtime carrier remain distinct; spelling cannot enrol the latter. Owner: specialist evaluation family and semantic/decision owner remain distinct without authority transfer. Product: immutable release and mutable definition remain distinct and selection uses the occurrence's declared context. Tenant: build realisation supplies no default for hosted/customer/account/runtime/data tenancy. User: Product role, person, principal, account, actor, operator and data subject remain unresolved until downstream authority defines or explicitly relates applicable meanings.\",\"uncertainty\":\"User is expressly unresolved, not false or interchangeable.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:s