est. Project constitutional authority is at what bindings; realisation/work at how and ticketing. Create no competing local methodology root and do not bind mutable or partial source as the immutable release. The resolved installed basis remains operative until explicit consumer adoption of another cut.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:e6c28515fab54d1546139bb7d8cdb4bc","key":1328,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:3add3b1f83bc954a23767c8b23298c71\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:e6c28515fab54d1546139bb7d8cdb4bc\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"Following the source-described bootstrap sequence.\"],\"exceptions\":[\"Local axiom, override and disambiguation collections may be explicitly empty.\",\"The sprint root is optional.\"],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1042,\"path\":\"standards/PRODUCT_DEFINITION.md\",\"quote\":\"7. Bind, or explicitly empty, the local axiom, override and\\n   disambiguation collections (§6).\\n8. Bind at least one accepted collective reference-frame basis, its\\n   admitting authorities and its exact governed scope (§7).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/PRODUCT_DEFINITION.md#PRODUCT_DEFINITION%2F12.%20Bootstrap\",\"start_line\":1039},{\"end_line\":1057,\"path\":\"standards/PRODUCT_DEFINITION.md\",\"quote\":\"14. Validate the JSON shape, assert URI and URI-reference syntax,\\n    synchronise and verify the exact installed basis, then resolve every\\n    URI and perform the cross-definition identity, composition,\\n    constitutional-sufficiency and authority-congruence checks.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/PRODUCT_DEFINITION.md#PRODUCT_DEFINITION%2F12.%20Bootstrap\",\"start_line\":1054}],\"statement\":\"The ordered sequence is: (1) install manager once, resolve one version-line selector and explicitly select one immutable RC; (2) install the complete cut and retain deterministic manifest digest; (3) copy its exact template to the named/default definition; (4) assign stable mutable-WHAT definition ID, source-project locator and bounded context, distinct from every immutable Product/release ID; (5) bind constitution.stdo.source, non-operative selector, exact basis URI/digest, additional authorities and basis-qualified entrypoints, confirming collective axioms/ontology/epistemology/taxonomy/semantics; (6) bind bootstrap entrypoint and portable targets relative to resolved product.source_project, preflight every target and install/refresh only marker-bounded discovery blocks; (7) bind or explicitly empty local axiom/override/disambiguation collections; (8) bind at least one accepted collective frame basis, admitting authorities and exact scope; (9) confirm/write Goals, run goals→intent→product and bind Intent/Product; (10) gather/derive/classify/bind live requirements without a co-equal rival; (11) bind at least one tenant with root/design/implementation and any shared realisation law; (12) bind Goals, ticket lanes, comments and optional sprint root; (13) explicitly bind every known composition edge with target ID, relation authority and non-empty contracts; (14) validate shape, assert URI syntax, synchronise/verify basis, resolve every URI and perform identity/composition/sufficiency/congruence checks.\",\"uncertainty\":\"This records the sequence as data; referenced §§3–8 and manager procedures are not fully supplied.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:1bd91a4885f4c18f623e47f2c4f876c6","key":1329,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:3add3b1f83bc954a23767c8b23298c71\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:1948ec4783ac3e1560e6eed4e2e68e9d\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:1bd91a4885f4c18f623e47f2c4f876c6\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"A bound requirement set has become the live constitutional surface.\"],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1062,\"path\":\"standards/PRODUCT_DEFINITION.md\",\"quote\":\"Once a bound requirement set is the live constitutional surface, no rival\\nmonolithic requirements document should remain co-equal authority with it. This\\nkeeps requirement truth structurally clear, derivable and non-monolithic\\nwithout prescribing its folder (P6, P2).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/PRODUCT_DEFINITION.md#PRODUCT_DEFINITION%2F12.%20Bootstrap\",\"start_line\":1059}],\"statement\":\"No rival monolithic requirements document should remain co-equal authority with the live bound set; this recommends clear, derivable, non-monolithic truth without prescribing a folder.\",\"uncertainty\":\"The concluding source uses 'should'; the bootstrap sequence separately says to bind without creating a co-equal rival.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:7c56e61d339051ba66423ab1f49f5bc8","key":1330,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:fcb3e9e8bb4e4ab57ffef14f92ab3625\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:a8af91d16de288148f9b593e559aa36d\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:d855004b5d8379de384a5375291dfc0c\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:7c56e61d339051ba66423ab1f49f5bc8\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[\"Core traversal records/F_D/F_P/F_H and generic ASSURANCE module are not restricted by this boundary.\"],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":14,\"path\":\"standards/PROFILES.md\",\"quote\":\"The core names no runtime, no carrier and no executor. Terms owned outside\\nthe core, by a profile or a realisation, never enter tier 1 or 2: graph, edge, vector, ledger, event\\nlog, worksite, HoG, Markov overlay, screen, entity cut, and the design\\nprofile's IACS and Prime.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/PROFILES.md#PROFILES%2F1.%20The%20boundary\",\"start_line\":11},{\"end_line\":50,\"path\":\"standards/PROFILES.md\",\"quote\":\"A worked application, a hello world or a data mapper is an external test\\nsubject; its particulars cannot become generic method functionality by\\nprecedent.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/PROFILES.md#PROFILES%2F1.%20The%20boundary\",\"start_line\":48}],\"statement\":\"Profile/realisation-owned graph, edge, vector, ledger, event log, worksite, HoG, Markov overlay, screen, entity cut, IACS and Prime do not enter tiers 1–2. A profile may bind core mechanisms to them through its declared binding. Worked applications, hello worlds and data mappers remain external test subjects; their particulars cannot become generic functionality by precedent.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:1af950f0c333c333ffc3ec34265c2a40","key":1331,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:fcb3e9e8bb4e4ab57ffef14f92ab3625\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:d855004b5d8379de384a5375291dfc0c\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:1af950f0c333c333ffc3ec34265c2a40\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"A profile uses generic core concepts/families or refines another profile.\"],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":46,\"path\":\"standards/PROFILES.md\",\"quote\":\"A profile that refines\\nanother profile declares the refinement in its lead; the refined profile\\nkeeps its rules, and the refining profile owns only what it adds (P1, P6).\\nPurpose and material relation:\\neach profile table cites the families it rests on without restating them,\\nso no generic rule gains a second owner in a profile and no choice a\\nprofile adds is presented as following from the foundations (P6, P1).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/PROFILES.md#PROFILES%2F1.%20The%20boundary\",\"start_line\":40}],\"statement\":\"Import every used tier-1/2 concept under FOUNDATIONS §2 and every generic family on which profile rules rest; restate none of the owner's rules. The FOUNDATIONS §3 family-table premise column names each imported family ID and its table section; profile rules rest on its consequences with their stated standing. Imported rules/choices retain owners. A refining profile declares refinement in its lead and owns only additions; added choices must not be presented as foundational consequences.\",\"uncertainty\":\"Exact import and family-table laws are referenced rather than supplied in full.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:82963b58de55a821add7109064d2df89","key":1332,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:f701f72fd1de2cad38030bb4061e3655\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:0c4adf064c8a053607896be69a4fb6ac\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:82963b58de55a821add7109064d2df89\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[\"Tier-3 profiles are constitutional method members when a project selects them.\"],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":73,\"path\":\"standards/README.md\",\"quote\":\"The constitutional method members of this corpus are its tier 1 and tier 2\\nstandards and, when a project selects them, its tier 3 profiles (P6, P3).\\n\\nEach clause names its foundational commitments under\\n[FOUNDATIONS §1](FOUNDATIONS.md#1-vocabulary-of-standing) and §3. The\\nowning members state the method in full. Frame excerpts and guides route\\nattention to those local owners and create no additional authority.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/README.md#STDO%20V3%2FDocuments\",\"start_line\":67}],\"statement\":\"Tiers 1–2 constitute method members, with selected tier-3 profiles. Each clause identifies foundational commitments. Owners state the method in full; guides/excerpts create no additional authority. Task frames copy owner sections byte for byte, record source digests and own no determination; digest mismatch makes them stale. ACTIVATION §2 owns when to read a frame or its owner sections.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:c0ec95c1e90e77cb7440998955f75b7a","key":1333,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:b6c2d02f1f961be2126e685d026c926b\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:c0ec95c1e90e77cb7440998955f75b7a\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[\"An explicitly bound and verified project-local copy remains possible, but is not the default.\"],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":145,\"path\":\"standards/README.md\",\"quote\":\"Installed bytes take their authority from the exact release cut, the product\\ndefinition's basis URI, the manifest digest and the member inventory\\n([PRODUCT_DEFINITION §4](PRODUCT_DEFINITION.md#4-shared-installed-release-basis-and-toolchain-manager),\\n[RELEASE §3](RELEASE.md#exact-cut-qualification)) (P3, P6). Neither the\\nmutable authoring head nor the moving version-line selector silently\\nreplaces that consumer basis\\n([RELEASE §4](RELEASE.md#4-selector-and-consumer-adoption)) (P6, P3).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/README.md#STDO%20V3%2FLibrary%20and%20installed%20basis\",\"start_line\":139}],\"statement\":\"The manager installs each complete immutable cut once in a shared versioned store and resolves logical release URIs. Definitions name basis by logical URI and manifest digest, not machine-local path. Installed-byte authority depends on exact cut, basis URI, digest and member inventory. Neither mutable head nor moving selector silently replaces consumer basis. Included calculus theory remains separate from subject models/encodings; the optional occurrence profile neither changes calculus nor selects a consumer; GLOSSARY never defines a shared default.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:8ed643a42f169ac68a10a8554401564e","key":1334,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:35f1f9ede029690551cd65423de48e25\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:395652cb307f9e3aec1351f1377975e4\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:8ed643a42f169ac68a10a8554401564e\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"Within the reference-frame-evaluation context under its exact publication basis.\"],\"exceptions\":[\"Other members/products may import or specialise relations under their own authority, without entering or amending this member.\"],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":72,\"path\":\"standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md\",\"quote\":\"It is engagement law only: it defines no application\\nprofile, role mapping, product-owned frame-basis binding, domain product,\\nspecification taxonomy, design ontology, runtime, workflow, adoption\\nrelation or assurance implementation. Other members and products may import or\\nspecialise its relations under their own authority, and that external\\nrelation neither enters nor amends this member (P2: an obligation stops\\nwhere its purpose stops).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md#REFERENCE_FRAME%2F1.%20The%20frame%20as%20the%20engagement%20unit\",\"start_line\":59}],\"statement\":\"This member governs finite actors' bounded reasoning/execution contexts over changing work only. It defines no application profile, role mapping, Product frame-basis binding, domain product, specification taxonomy, design ontology, runtime, workflow, adoption relation or assurance implementation. Same-spelled profile/product/role/runtime carriers are not imported by proximity or nominal match.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:c684a87bd17b43ae94f37544de5b6fd8","key":1335,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:aa239bec637e6fe48df5a9c006edecbb\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:35f1f9ede029690551cd65423de48e25\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:c684a87bd17b43ae94f37544de5b6fd8\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":118,\"path\":\"standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md\",\"quote\":\"Scope bounds what\\nthis member owns; a concept of those kinds that another member defines,\\nsuch as evaluation, basis, the activation step, the core results or\\nqualification, is imported here, and this member defines it no second\\ntime. A refinement this member states, such as the function outcomes of §5\\nor the coverage statuses of §8, names its owner in this table and maps\\nback to it. A frame or frame family that a profile or product declares in\\nthis context is that owner's specialisation under Scope above and is not\\nimported here (P1, P3, P6).\\nPurpose and material relation: each\\nconcept used here keeps one owning section, so its meaning cannot diverge\\nbetween that owner and this member (P1, P6).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md#REFERENCE_FRAME%2F1.%20The%20frame%20as%20the%20engagement%20unit%2FImports%20into%20this%20context\",\"start_line\":107}],\"statement\":\"Each declared import runs from its named source member to the frame context with no loss, ownership transfer or authority grant. Imported concepts are not defined a second time; local refinements name and map back to their owners. Profile/Product frame specialisations retain those owners and are not thereby imports into this member.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:6d0c22d64058db10ac83eec95c90af1e","key":1336,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:395652cb307f9e3aec1351f1377975e4\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:6f930ad8904d0b79e414891042c6c678\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:525a659feca950ea645bdcfeb6f5d581\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:f09c3ecfad4a4003e555be971583654b\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:6d0c22d64058db10ac83eec95c90af1e\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":271,\"path\":\"standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md\",\"quote\":\"9. Unknown and out-of-frame results are lawful pressure for\\n   reconfiguration; they are neither failed evaluations nor implied\\n   acceptance (P5).\\n10. Historical failures, resets and invisible violations are evidence for\\n    improving a frame declaration, an activation, an actor assignment or a\\n    frame set (P4b, P6).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md#REFERENCE_FRAME%2F2.%20Core%20claims\",\"start_line\":266}],\"statement\":\"No finite actor is presumed to hold the whole workspace actively. Useful frames are finite and sufficient for their declared family; evaluation determines attention. Human authority may select practical sets without a unique mechanical partition. Frames may overlap, compose, refine, restrict, translate or succeed; hierarchy is optional, and joint use need not compose coordinates. Coverage is relative to declared workspace/outcome/inventory/basis/time. Breadth, usefulness, actor or technology grants no semantic/operation/decision authority. Unknown and out-of-frame outcomes are lawful reconfiguration pressure, neither failed evaluations nor implied acceptance. Historical failures/resets/invisible violations inform improvements.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:38609855353355f3619df16853df027c","key":1337,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:395652cb307f9e3aec1351f1377975e4\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:38609855353355f3619df16853df027c\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":276,\"path\":\"standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md\",\"quote\":\"Every frame, declared or activated, obeys the following. The objects named\\nare defined in FOUNDATIONS §2.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md#REFERENCE_FRAME%2F3.%20Laws\",\"start_line\":275}],\"statement\":\"The RF laws apply to every frame, whether declared or activated; the named objects are defined by FOUNDATIONS §2.\",\"uncertainty\":\"The object definitions themselves are not supplied.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:c2b0ae3b009cf02d24e902813c04be28","key":1338,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:395652cb307f9e3aec1351f1377975e4\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:c2b0ae3b009cf02d24e902813c04be28\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":281,\"path\":\"standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md\",\"quote\":\"Every frame declares the evaluation family it supports. A frame with no\\ndeclared evaluation family has no testable sufficiency boundary (P2).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md#REFERENCE_FRAME%2F3.%20Laws%2FRF-001%20Evaluation%20relativity\",\"start_line\":280}],\"statement\":\"Every frame declares its supported evaluation family; without it there is no testable sufficiency boundary. A module/file/service/role/persona/prompt/lens without a declared evaluation relation is not a frame. An evaluation belongs only if its decided question is declared by that family at the frame's coordinates; similar wording, name or set membership is insufficient.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:2190333a4308711e660ca5ea211d26a2","key":1339,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:395652cb307f9e3aec1351f1377975e4\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:2190333a4308711e660ca5ea211d26a2\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"The frame is activated.\"],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":294,\"path\":\"standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md\",\"quote\":\"An activated frame contains a finite attention surface that fits the\\nselected actor's declared capability envelope. A frame that needs\\nundeclared ambient memory, conversation history or an effectively global\\nworkspace context is not reconstructable for that actor (P0). The fit is tested in\\n[ACTIVATION §2](ACTIVATION.md#2-context-construction-under-an-envelope),\\nwhich owns the measurement of the context's size and when it applies.\\nWhether the actor attends adequately to a frame that fits is a separate\\nquestion, answered by actual-use evidence under\\n[EVALUATION §7](EVALUATION.md#frame-qualification); a size measurement\\ndoes not answer it (P0, P6).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md#REFERENCE_FRAME%2F3.%20Laws%2FRF-002%20Finite%20attention\",\"start_line\":285}],\"statement\":\"The finite attention surface fits the selected actor's declared envelope. Dependence on undeclared ambient memory, conversation history or effectively global context makes it unreconstructable for that actor. ACTIVATION §2 owns size measurement and applicability. Fit does not establish adequate attention, which requires actual-use evidence under EVALUATION §7.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:c67dda01f027439a9665fa59926f0d92","key":1340,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:395652cb307f9e3aec1351f1377975e4\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:c67dda01f027439a9665fa59926f0d92\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[\"No proof that every undiscovered material relation is absent is required.\"],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":303,\"path\":\"standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md\",\"quote\":\"Every known relation whose lawful change can alter the evaluation result,\\nthe validity of the basis, the sufficiency of evidence, operation authority\\nor decision authority appears in the frame or enters through a declared\\nauthoritative input. Omitting a material relation makes the frame\\ninsufficient. The law does not require proving that no undiscovered\\nmaterial relation exists (P2; P0 with the open-world premise).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md#REFERENCE_FRAME%2F3.%20Laws%2FRF-003%20Material%20sufficiency\",\"start_line\":298}],\"statement\":\"Every known relation whose lawful change can alter the result, basis validity, evidence sufficiency, operation authority or decision authority must appear or enter through declared authoritative input. Omitting any such material relation makes the frame insufficient.\",\"uncertainty\":\"Undiscovered material relations remain possible.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:c17675317136ab594b5b51a3e3f8dfa1","key":1341,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:395652cb307f9e3aec1351f1377975e4\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:c17675317136ab594b5b51a3e3f8dfa1\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"A relation cannot affect the declared evaluation.\"],\"exceptions\":[\"Include it if needed to establish its irrelevance.\"],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":309,\"path\":\"standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md\",\"quote\":\"Relations that cannot affect the declared evaluation stay outside active\\nattention unless they are needed to establish that irrelevance. A frame\\ndoes not expand because adjacent workspace material exists (P2).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md#REFERENCE_FRAME%2F3.%20Laws%2FRF-004%20Irrelevance%20exclusion\",\"start_line\":307}],\"statement\":\"Keep irrelevant relations outside active attention; adjacent workspace material alone does not expand a frame.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:51f2fc5ecb0f0e16c818a3c2cea69927","key":1342,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:395652cb307f9e3aec1351f1377975e4\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:525a659feca950ea645bdcfeb6f5d581\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:51f2fc5ecb0f0e16c818a3c2cea69927\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[\"Applicable evidence is not subject to a blanket reuse prohibition.\"],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":324,\"path\":\"standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md\",\"quote\":\"Every result binds its exact subject, basis, coordinates and evidence\\nscope. An evaluation performed on a stale, advanced, ambiguous or mismatched\\nbasis that cannot support its required claim returns `invalid_basis` or\\nrequires reactivation. Apparent equality never substitutes for declared\\ncoordinate equality (P3, P1).\\n\\nAdvancement does not rewrite a historical result. Reliance on the new\\nsubject or basis requires an established applicability relation, and\\nreliance affected by the change is withdrawn until that relation is\\nestablished. [FOUNDATIONS Change impact and evidence reuse](FOUNDATIONS.md#change-impact-and-evidence-reuse)\\nand [ACTIVATION §7](ACTIVATION.md#7-closed-result-and-reuse) own that decision;\\nthis law supplies no blanket prohibition on reusing applicable evidence.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md#REFERENCE_FRAME%2F3.%20Laws%2FRF-005%20Exact%20basis%20and%20coordinates\",\"start_line\":313}],\"statement\":\"Every result binds exact subject, basis, coordinates and evidence scope. A stale, advanced, ambiguous or mismatched basis that cannot support the required claim produces invalid_basis or requires reactivation. Apparent equality cannot replace declared coordinate equality. Advancement does not rewrite history; new-subject/basis reliance requires an established applicability relation, with affected reliance withdrawn until established under the cited reuse owners.\",\"uncertainty\":\"The foundation table abbreviates the invalid-basis condition; this rule retains RF-005's explicit 'cannot support its required claim' qualification.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:3a7b10b7771dfce4841d2aa627ac60e8","key":1343,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:395652cb307f9e3aec1351f1377975e4\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:3a7b10b7771dfce4841d2aa627ac60e8\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":333,\"path\":\"standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md\",\"quote\":\"A frame carries and applies admitted authority. It does not mint, widen,\\ntransfer or reconstruct semantic, evaluation, operation or decision\\nauthority from anything that creates none. That list is\\n[FOUNDATIONS §2 Authority kinds](FOUNDATIONS.md#authority-kinds)'; its\\ninstances in a frame include actor identity, available capability,\\nevidence shape, implementation reachability and frame selection (P6).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md#REFERENCE_FRAME%2F3.%20Laws%2FRF-006%20Authority%20conservation\",\"start_line\":328}],\"statement\":\"Frames carry/apply admitted authority; they cannot mint, widen, transfer or reconstruct semantic/evaluation/operation/decision authority from actor identity, capability, evidence shape, implementation reachability, frame selection or other non-grants. Declaring/selecting/activating/executing a frame or naming a role grants none. Authority kinds may lawfully coincide but do not collapse by default; actor identity is distinct, and a human-authority proxy retains separate identity.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:37d8b1f1a87f085b2e3525bd7f1275be","key":1344,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:395652cb307f9e3aec1351f1377975e4\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:37d8b1f1a87f085b2e3525bd7f1275be\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[\"One actor may lawfully perform several roles, while the roles remain distinguishable.\"],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":343,\"path\":\"standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md\",\"quote\":\"The separation of semantic law, evidence, the evaluator's application\\nand the disposing decision authority is\\n[EVALUATION §2](EVALUATION.md#2-separation)'s. This law binds it to a\\nframe: a frame declaration keeps these roles distinguishable even when\\none actor lawfully performs several of them, and where the evaluation\\nperforms a material operation, the existing operation owner supplies the\\nexact grant as a further role the declaration keeps apart (P6).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md#REFERENCE_FRAME%2F3.%20Laws%2FRF-007%20Semantic%2C%20evidence%20and%20verdict%20separation\",\"start_line\":337}],\"statement\":\"Distinguish semantic law, observations/evidence, evaluator application and disposing decision authority. A material operation additionally requires the exact grant of its existing operation owner, kept distinct; read-only evaluation declares no operation authority. Evaluation applies declared invariants/evidence rules/result algebra and records every assumption whose failure could change the result.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:2191b6876217a38548a08ee5f64ff46e","key":1345,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:395652cb307f9e3aec1351f1377975e4\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:2191b6876217a38548a08ee5f64ff46e\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":350,\"path\":\"standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md\",\"quote\":\"Frames may share entities, variables, evidence or coordinates. Shared\\nmaterial establishes neither identical meaning nor identical basis,\\nauthority or result. Every cross-frame equality or translation an\\nevaluation uses is declared where it is used (P1, P3).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md#REFERENCE_FRAME%2F3.%20Laws%2FRF-008%20Overlap%20without%20identity%20collapse\",\"start_line\":347}],\"statement\":\"Shared entities, variables, evidence or coordinates establish no identical meaning, basis, authority or result. Declare every cross-frame equality or translation where the evaluation uses it.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:35f114800910899208895e02b7fdbb98","key":1346,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:395652cb307f9e3aec1351f1377975e4\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:6f930ad8904d0b79e414891042c6c678\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:35f114800910899208895e02b7fdbb98\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[\"Consumers may align distinct structures where the governed subject warrants it through declared relations.\"],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":365,\"path\":\"standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md\",\"quote\":\"Frames may relate through disjointness, overlap, refinement, restriction,\\ntranslation, temporal succession, composition or governance (§7). Parent\\nand child relations apply only where explicitly declared. Functional\\ndecomposition, communication, authority precedence, frame configuration,\\nsubject topology and evaluation dependency are distinct relation\\nstructures; a consumer may align them where the governed subject warrants\\nit and may not silently treat them as one hierarchy (P3, P1). Communication is the exchange of\\ninformation between frames, or between the actors activated on them. An\\nexchange by itself grants no authority, an instance of\\n[FOUNDATIONS §2 Authority kinds](FOUNDATIONS.md#authority-kinds), What\\ncreates no authority, and establishes neither a decomposition nor an\\nevaluation dependency (P6, P1).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md#REFERENCE_FRAME%2F3.%20Laws%2FRF-009%20No%20assumed%20hierarchy\",\"start_line\":354}],\"statement\":\"Parent/child relations require explicit declaration. Keep functional decomposition, communication, authority precedence, frame configuration, subject topology and evaluation dependency distinct; none is silently one hierarchy. Information exchange alone grants no authority and establishes neither decomposition nor evaluation dependency. There is no default frame topology; declare the relations evaluation and coverage require.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:f6f6e5e9870266e9893953a84cd9789a","key":1347,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:395652cb307f9e3aec1351f1377975e4\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:6f930ad8904d0b79e414891042c6c678\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:f6f6e5e9870266e9893953a84cd9789a\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"Composition law is required when governing evaluation combines internal variables, transports evidence/values between frames, or treats operations as one material execution relation.\"],\"exceptions\":[\"Independently activated evaluations may instead return closed results to one declared conjunction or decision rule.\"],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":378,\"path\":\"standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md\",\"quote\":\"Using several frames does not require composing their internal manifolds.\\nComposition law is required only when the governing evaluation combines\\ntheir internal variables, transports evidence or values across them, or\\ntreats their operations as one material execution relation. Independently\\nactivated evaluations may instead return closed results to one declared\\nconjunction or decision rule (P4a; §6).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md#REFERENCE_FRAME%2F3.%20Laws%2FRF-010%20Composition%20on%20demand\",\"start_line\":373}],\"statement\":\"Using several frames alone does not require composing their manifolds. Required material composition declares shared invariants, material effect/decision order, closure, failure, and conservation of semantic/operation/decision authority; its owner is the application. Result conjunction and choices left by its decision rule retain their separate owners.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:cb59a352de859457b9ff12d6584a65aa","key":1348,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:395652cb307f9e3aec1351f1377975e4\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:525a659feca950ea645bdcfeb6f5d581\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:cb59a352de859457b9ff12d6584a65aa\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"Topology or frame declarations change materially.\"],\"exceptions\":[\"A revision changing no frame declaration requires no new revision coordinate, but unchanged declaration alone does not establish continued result validity.\"],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":387,\"path\":\"standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md\",\"quote\":\"An activated frame declares the topology changes capable of invalidating\\nits coordinates or its materiality judgment. A detected material topology\\nmutation causes reevaluation, frame revision or recharting before the\\nprevious result is reused. Material revision of the frame itself\\ninvalidates for reuse every result bound to the prior revision coordinate;\\n§10 Revision actions states that rule (P3, P4b).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md#REFERENCE_FRAME%2F3.%20Laws%2FRF-011%20Topology%20mutation%20and%20recharting\",\"start_line\":382}],\"statement\":\"Activated frames declare topology invalidators of coordinates/materiality. Detected material mutation requires reevaluation, revision or recharting before reuse. Material frame revision creates a new coordinate and identifies affected activations/results/coverage; all results bound to the prior revision reopen until recorded re-check establishes independence from change or reevaluation occurs. Silence keeps none closed; ACTIVATION §7 governs reuse.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:f4730bbd4c1fe4c868f6333bd93598ca","key":1349,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:525a659feca950ea645bdcfeb6f5d581\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:395652cb307f9e3aec1351f1377975e4\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:f4730bbd4c1fe4c868f6333bd93598ca\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[\"Non-performance has no evaluation result; an ACTIVATION stop state is distinct.\"],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":402,\"path\":\"standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md\",\"quote\":\"that nothing is\\ncoerced to success; that a refinement adds no core value, keeps\\nindeterminate, out-of-frame and invalid-basis pressure explicit and raises\\nno result's standing; and that an evaluation not performed has no result,\\nits stop state being\\n[ACTIVATION §3](ACTIVATION.md#3-step-results-and-disposition). This law\\napplies them to every frame and defines none of them (P5).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md#REFERENCE_FRAME%2F3.%20Laws%2FRF-012%20Closed%20results\",\"start_line\":396}],\"statement\":\"Every performed evaluation returns exactly one closed declared-algebra result. Nothing is coerced to success. Refinements map to the five core values, add none, retain indeterminate/out-of-frame/invalid-basis pressure and raise no standing.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:026d41b6033b714bb3fdba3bdd70cc9d","key":1350,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:395652cb307f9e3aec1351f1377975e4\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:026d41b6033b714bb3fdba3bdd70cc9d\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"A fresh competent actor is inside the declared capability envelope.\"],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":409,\"path\":\"standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md\",\"quote\":\"A fresh competent actor inside the declared capability envelope can\\nreconstruct the activated evaluation from the frame declaration, the exact\\nsubject, the basis and the admissible inputs, without undocumented\\nconversational or historical context (P0 with the actor-change premise).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md#REFERENCE_FRAME%2F3.%20Laws%2FRF-013%20Reconstructable%20activation\",\"start_line\":406}],\"statement\":\"The fresh actor can reconstruct evaluation from declaration, exact subject/basis and admissible inputs without undocumented history. Supply one activated frame or declared active configuration, not an implied global reconstruction demand. Return through the declared result relation; internal reasoning may be actor-owned where permitted but replaces no evidence/provenance/authority. Every binding field resolves through stable identities/source references; paths, lines, counts, summaries and matching labels are not substitutes.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:5ddfb36dfc831829cdad6db9e910cdb9","key":1351,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:395652cb307f9e3aec1351f1377975e4\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:5ddfb36dfc831829cdad6db9e910cdb9\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"The material manifold exceeds the actor's capability envelope.\"],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":421,\"path\":\"standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md\",\"quote\":\"Frame adequacy includes actor usability. When the material manifold\\nexceeds an actor's capability envelope, the remedies are those of\\n[ACTIVATION §2](ACTIVATION.md#2-context-construction-under-an-envelope)\\nstep 3, which owns the list: among them selecting another actor, refining\\nthe frame into steps, sequencing activations and a lawful compression\\n(RF-017). Choosing among them is human authority's, exercised directly or\\nin advance through the grant; ACTIVATION §2 says which of them a step\\nselects itself and which re-enter the grant's owner. The actor may not\\nsilently omit material relations to fit its context (P0, P5).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md#REFERENCE_FRAME%2F3.%20Laws%2FRF-014%20Capability%20fit\",\"start_line\":413}],\"statement\":\"Adequacy includes actor usability. Remedies include another actor, refined frame/outer contract, sequenced activations, lawful compression or out_of_frame, as owned by ACTIVATION §2. Human authority chooses directly or through prior grant; within-grant refinement/sequencing/compression differs from re-entry to grant/envelope owners for another actor or larger envelope. Never silently omit material relations or silently grow beyond the envelope; capability cannot waive invariants or widen authority.\",\"uncertainty\":\"The complete remedy/admission mechanics remain with unsupplied ACTIVATION §2.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:b9fd1165d4046cb6d1d7168854f19ae3","key":1352,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:f09c3ecfad4a4003e555be971583654b\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:525a659feca950ea645bdcfeb6f5d581\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:b9fd1165d4046cb6d1d7168854f19ae3\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":428,\"path\":\"standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md\",\"quote\":\"Coverage and evaluation results retain known uncertainty. Unresolved\\nrelations, uncovered evaluations, contested evidence and unknown capability\\nstay explicit. Absence of a recorded counterexample is not evidence of\\nuniversal completeness (P4b, P6; open-world premise).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md#REFERENCE_FRAME%2F3.%20Laws%2FRF-015%20Residual%20uncertainty\",\"start_line\":425}],\"statement\":\"Keep unresolved relations, uncovered evaluations, contested evidence and unknown capability explicit. No recorded counterexample does not establish universal completeness. Without an independently established closed-domain completeness predicate, inventory self-inspection cannot establish that no material evaluation is undiscovered; coverage stays falsifiable with a residual boundary.\",\"uncertainty\":\"Unknown material evaluations remain possible.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:36bd0976400185dd8b332132481edbd2","key":1353,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:35f1f9ede029690551cd65423de48e25\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:395652cb307f9e3aec1351f1377975e4\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:6f930ad8904d0b79e414891042c6c678\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:36bd0976400185dd8b332132481edbd2\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":435,\"path\":\"standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md\",\"quote\":\"This member requires the declared relations and the observable outcomes.\\nIt requires no frame runtime, universal carrier, registry, controller,\\nprompt format, repository layout, collaboration topology, worker count or\\nsoftware framework (P2).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md#REFERENCE_FRAME%2F3.%20Laws%2FRF-016%20Implementation%20neutrality\",\"start_line\":432}],\"statement\":\"Require declared relations and observable outcomes, not a frame runtime, universal carrier, registry, controller, prompt format, repository layout, collaboration topology, worker count or software framework. Signatures describe relations rather than callable interfaces; minimal declarations specify least content in any conforming carrier.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:139360ff03e5463a11da99f422c2a429","key":1354,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:395652cb307f9e3aec1351f1377975e4\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:6f930ad8904d0b79e414891042c6c678\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:139360ff03e5463a11da99f422c2a429\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"Practice is compressed into frames or frames are merged.\"],\"exceptions\":[\"Neither a unique smallest frame nor a disjoint-minimum frame set is required.\"],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":446,\"path\":\"standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md\",\"quote\":\"A frame compresses accumulated practice when its declaration preserves the\\nmaterial distinctions and failure detections its evaluation family requires\\nwhile fitting its capability envelope. Compression does not require a\\nunique smallest frame. Intentional overlap is retained where it supplies\\nindependently activated evaluation, different capability fit, different\\nevidence altitude or useful fault detection. Frames are merged only when\\nthe merged frame preserves evaluation meaning, authority, capability fit\\nand proportional reasoning cost (P2, P0).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md#REFERENCE_FRAME%2F3.%20Laws%2FRF-017%20Proportional%20compression\",\"start_line\":439}],\"statement\":\"Preserve material distinctions and failure detection required by the family while fitting the envelope. Retain useful intentional overlap for independent activation, different fit/evidence altitude or fault detection. Merge only while preserving evaluation meaning, authority, fit and proportional reasoning cost. Record compression and its preservation argument; the promotion served decides whether independent assessment is required.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:cadc75a1cf3378a66d602626fb8a5a4f","key":1355,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:395652cb307f9e3aec1351f1377975e4\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:e12ad01daa78bc629c9782979e182c88\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:6f930ad8904d0b79e414891042c6c678\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:cadc75a1cf3378a66d602626fb8a5a4f\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"Frame-set contraction is considered.\"],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":460,\"path\":\"standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md\",\"quote\":\"Frame-set contraction asks a different\\nquestion: whether two frame declarations support the same evaluation\\nrelation without material difference in evidence, authority, capability\\nfit, evaluation or assurance independence, or failure detection. A frame\\nset is not contracted to a disjoint minimum because its material variables\\noverlap (P2; RF-017).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md#REFERENCE_FRAME%2F3.%20Laws%2FEngagement%20atom%20and%20semantic%20atom\",\"start_line\":455}],\"statement\":\"Ask whether declarations support the same evaluation relation without material difference in evidence, authority, capability fit, evaluation/assurance independence or failure detection. Overlapping variables alone do not justify contraction to a disjoint minimum; domain semantic contraction is a separate question.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:71d2860b6b21316097f26cb1ff0301c1","key":1356,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:6f930ad8904d0b79e414891042c6c678\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:71d2860b6b21316097f26cb1ff0301c1\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"Human authority declares an initial project frame set.\"],\"exceptions\":[\"Bottom-up reconstruction of the workspace is not required.\"],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":482,\"path\":\"standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md\",\"quote\":\"- the governed workspace and outcome;\\n- the known evaluation inventory;\\n- the selected frames and their capability envelopes;\\n- intentional overlaps and separately activated checks;\\n- known frame dependencies or translations;\\n- semantic, evaluation, operation where material, decision and acceptance\\n  authority;\\n- known exclusions and residual uncertainty; and\\n- the conditions for revision.\\n\\nHuman selection is a lawful source of method structure. It proves neither\\nthat the selected set is complete nor that the frames hold authority over\\nthe subject relations they inspect (P6; RF-006, RF-015).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md#REFERENCE_FRAME%2F4.%20Frame-set%20declaration\",\"start_line\":470}],\"statement\":\"Record workspace/outcome, known inventory, selected frames/envelopes, intentional overlaps/separately activated checks, known dependencies/translations, semantic/evaluation/material-operation/decision/acceptance authorities, exclusions/residuals and revision conditions. Human selection is lawful structure but proves neither completeness nor authority over inspected relations. A set need not be a partition, tree, stack or exhaustive ontology.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:4cc14bf50576199ada096fae3423dafa","key":1357,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:6f930ad8904d0b79e414891042c6c678\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:4cc14bf50576199ada096fae3423dafa\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"Selecting frames for known material evaluations E(W,G).\"],\"exceptions\":[\"No optimisation algorithm is prescribed; human authority may accept a non-minimal set for material risk reduction or better actor fit.\"],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":497,\"path\":\"standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md\",\"quote\":\"Frame-set selection is a constrained coverage problem. For the known\\nmaterial evaluations E(W, G) of workspace W and governed outcome G, a\\nselected frame set S meets the baseline coverage constraint when, for every\\nevaluation e in E(W, G), there is a frame F in S and an available actor a\\ninside F's capability envelope K_F such that F with a is capable of e (P2,\\nP0). Selection also weighs actor context and\\ncompetence; evaluation risk and consequence; acquisition and reasoning\\ncost; evidence availability; useful independently activated overlap;\\ntranslation and reconciliation cost; historical blind spots; and\\nreversibility when the set proves inadequate. No optimisation algorithm is\\nprescribed. Human authority may accept a non-minimal set where its added\\ncost buys material risk reduction or better actor fit (P2, P6).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md#REFERENCE_FRAME%2F4.%20Frame-set%20declaration%2FFrame-set%20selection\",\"start_line\":486}],\"statement\":\"Baseline coverage holds iff every known material evaluation e has some frame F in selected S and available actor a within K_F capable together of e. Also weigh context/competence, risk/consequence, acquisition/reasoning cost, evidence availability, useful separately activated overlap, translation/reconciliation cost, historical blind spots and reversibility.\",\"uncertainty\":\"This baseline criterion does not establish global completeness or waive other constraints.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:71ea59e012cb4e646b830f5ee32f9be7","key":1358,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:6f930ad8904d0b79e414891042c6c678\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:395652cb307f9e3aec1351f1377975e4\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:71ea59e012cb4e646b830f5ee32f9be7\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[\"Resource controls apply through an explicitly selected frame and its owning applicability/work scope; ACTIVATION §6 is the selection where cost itself is the governed question.\"],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":511,\"path\":\"standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md\",\"quote\":\"These considerations create no universal resource ledger, benchmark,\\nbudget or measurement gate: cost is selected, not universal, under\\n[ACTIVATION §6](ACTIVATION.md#6-cost-and-proportionality), which owns\\nresource limits, and these four are its instances in frame selection. In\\nframe selection a resource control applies only through an explicitly\\nselected frame and its owning applicability and work scope; ACTIVATION §6\\nis that selection where a cost claim is the governed question. The test\\nthat an activated frame's context fits the selected actor is RF-002's,\\ndistinct from the actor context that selection weighs, and\\n[ACTIVATION §2](ACTIVATION.md#2-context-construction-under-an-envelope)\\nowns its measurement and when the measurement applies. Frame selection\\ncannot waive another applicable semantic, authority, evidence or\\nindependence constraint (P2, P6).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md#REFERENCE_FRAME%2F4.%20Frame-set%20declaration%2FFrame-set%20selection\",\"start_line\":499}],\"statement\":\"Selection considerations create no universal resource ledger, benchmark, budget or measurement gate. RF-002 activation fit differs from context considered in selection, with measurement owned by ACTIVATION §2. Selection cannot waive applicable semantic, authority, evidence or independence constraints.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:4e793c96e26d585a42ad87df1ce54e92","key":1359,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:395652cb307f9e3aec1351f1377975e4\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:544a4e40a3d742a6d00a0bffa1b08fbd\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:4e793c96e26d585a42ad87df1ce54e92\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[\"Size measurement applies where the actor envelope declares context capacity; it establishes fit only, not a budget or universal gate.\"],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":157,\"path\":\"standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md\",\"quote\":\"The context starts as the material closure of the intake's seed set (the subject, outcome and affected relations it names) under that relation family, and a closure that is not finite and unique on the exact basis stops the step and is not guessed\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md#REFERENCE_FRAME%2F1.%20The%20frame%20as%20the%20engagement%20unit%2FFoundation%20to%20law\",\"start_line\":157},{\"end_line\":156,\"path\":\"standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md\",\"quote\":\"Where the envelope declares a context capacity, the selected context's size is measured before the actor reads it, over a stated boundary, and recorded with the capacity and the comparison; context outside the boundary is recorded as not measured.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md#REFERENCE_FRAME%2F1.%20The%20frame%20as%20the%20engagement%20unit%2FFoundation%20to%20law\",\"start_line\":156}],\"statement\":\"A frame specifies a finite relation, not a required carrier. Binding requires every material coordinate to resolve to exact source, subject, basis, authority, evidence route, actor envelope, result relation and invalidation; representation cannot create/widen/replace binding. Context starts from intake seed material closure; non-finite or non-unique closure on the exact basis stops as closure_unresolved rather than being guessed. Project closure to context with boundary seams recorded as excluded/external/unresolved/translated/invalidation-sensitive. Applicable context-size measurement precedes reading, records boundary/capacity/unit/comparison, and marks outside context unmeasured; capacity/unit belong to the envelope, while measured boundary and other resource limits belong to the selected execution binding.\",\"uncertainty\":\"Exact AC-010/AC-011 and activation stop rules are external references.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:ce41bce456cc94d18c6b96def727c7c6","key":1360,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:395652cb307f9e3aec1351f1377975e4\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:6f930ad8904d0b79e414891042c6c678\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:ce41bce456cc94d18c6b96def727c7c6\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":164,\"path\":\"standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md\",\"quote\":\"frame disjointness (structural), evaluation independence (procedural) and assurance independence (claim-relative) are three relations: disjoint frames need not be independently evaluated, independently activated evaluations need not be disjoint, and the unqualified word \\\"independent\\\" establishes none of them.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md#REFERENCE_FRAME%2F1.%20The%20frame%20as%20the%20engagement%20unit%2FFoundation%20to%20law\",\"start_line\":164}],\"statement\":\"Keep structural frame disjointness, procedural evaluation independence and claim-relative assurance independence distinct. Disjointness does not ensure independent evaluation; independent activation need not be disjoint; 'independent' alone establishes none. Separately activated evaluations may overlap in subject, manifold or evidence but neither consumes nor influences the other's unclosed working result. Assurance independence conditions belong to governing assurance law.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:343e8d4467dc9dc3a0e1a8ec2cc28a85","key":1361,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:395652cb307f9e3aec1351f1377975e4\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:343e8d4467dc9dc3a0e1a8ec2cc28a85\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"One frame supplies evidence or a value consumed inside another.\"],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":166,\"path\":\"standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md\",\"quote\":\"the translation declares source and target coordinates, preserved meaning, accepted loss, provenance, equality law and refusal conditions; a loss inside the accepted loss travels with the value as a residual\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md#REFERENCE_FRAME%2F1.%20The%20frame%20as%20the%20engagement%20unit%2FFoundation%20to%20law\",\"start_line\":166}],\"statement\":\"Declare source/target coordinates, preserved meaning, accepted loss, provenance, equality law and refusal conditions. Loss within accepted loss travels with the value as residual; the declarer owns accepted-loss and refusal choices.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:bac30652b6a413e7025fb22ec4cba3d7","key":1362,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:f09c3ecfad4a4003e555be971583654b\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:525a659feca950ea645bdcfeb6f5d581\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:bac30652b6a413e7025fb22ec4cba3d7\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":175,\"path\":\"standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md\",\"quote\":\"A refused activation performs no evaluation; `decision(holds)` assesses the composite predicate and is not its acceptance; a coverage status is a result of the audit, never of the covered evaluation, and an excluded row is met by its cited exclusion, never covered or performed\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md#REFERENCE_FRAME%2F1.%20The%20frame%20as%20the%20engagement%20unit%2FFoundation%20to%20law\",\"start_line\":175}],\"statement\":\"Activation, conjunction, translation outcomes and coverage statuses answer their own predicates. Refused activation performs no evaluation; decision(holds) assesses a composite predicate rather than accepting it. Coverage audit status is not the covered evaluation's result. An excluded row is met by its cited exclusion, not covered or performed. Each refinement maps to one core value.\",\"uncertainty\":\"Full function outcome and coverage-status enumerations are not supplied.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:f84467c5c84f2178eeb1fd8cc12bdd92","key":1363,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:f09c3ecfad4a4003e555be971583654b\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:6f930ad8904d0b79e414891042c6c678\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:f84467c5c84f2178eeb1fd8cc12bdd92\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":177,\"path\":\"standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md\",\"quote\":\"every material interaction is covered by one frame, a declared conjunction, a translation or a material composition. Every material evaluation identifies its semantic and decision authority and every material operation its existing operation authority; a frame set with an unresolved decision owner, or an effectful path without operation authority, is not closed\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md#REFERENCE_FRAME%2F1.%20The%20frame%20as%20the%20engagement%20unit%2FFoundation%20to%20law\",\"start_line\":177}],\"statement\":\"Coverage binds exact workspace/outcome/basis/inventory/frame-set/time, and material change may invalidate it. Derive inventory from every material available source and record provenance/materiality; artifact/file/operation/test/review/actor counts prove no coverage. Dimensions are lenses until instantiated as bounded evaluation families. Each ledger row records subject/basis, frames/envelope, authorities/evidence/dependencies/status/residual. Row coverage is insufficient for material interactions: cover each by a frame, declared conjunction, translation or material composition. Each evaluation identifies semantic/decision owners and each material operation its existing authority; unresolved decision ownership or unauthorised effectful paths prevent closure.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:d4f4cf0fbc11c136dc4b8c18567cb83a","key":1364,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:f09c3ecfad4a4003e555be971583654b\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:6f930ad8904d0b79e414891042c6c678\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:d4f4cf0fbc11c136dc4b8c18567cb83a\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"The named cases or risks are material to the governed outcome.\"],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":180,\"path\":\"standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md\",\"quote\":\"a frame set has operational full coverage for its declared tuple only when its eight conditions hold, among them that no unresolved frame-result conflict is hidden by aggregation and that uncovered and unknown residuals are explicit. The claim is relative to that tuple and is not a claim that no undiscovered evaluation exists\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md#REFERENCE_FRAME%2F1.%20The%20frame%20as%20the%20engagement%20unit%2FFoundation%20to%20law\",\"start_line\":180}],\"statement\":\"Cover known success, refusal, boundary, integration, recovery, reconstruction and competing-path cases where material. Historical failures remain inputs until a declared frame detects or excludes recurrence. Independently activated coverage uses a separate evaluation relation and declares additional assurance-independence conditions; a persona label establishes neither. Human authority chooses which evaluations require it, considering high consequence, weak observability, confirmation bias and historical local-proof masking. Operational full coverage requires all eight referenced conditions, including no aggregation-hidden result conflicts and explicit uncovered/unknown residuals; it is tuple-relative, not universal completeness. Exclusions retain cited governing authority.\",\"uncertainty\":\"Only some of the referenced eight operational-full-coverage conditions are supplied.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:0b3775d4561863199b0e282a4729c584","key":1365,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:544a4e40a3d742a6d00a0bffa1b08fbd\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:395652cb307f9e3aec1351f1377975e4\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:6f930ad8904d0b79e414891042c6c678\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:0b3775d4561863199b0e282a4729c584\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"Failures, resets, invisible violations or listed signals prompt diagnosis.\"],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":181,\"path\":\"standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md\",\"quote\":\"Diagnosis excludes activation, basis, capability, evidence, missing-relation, missing-conjunction and evaluation-family defects before it adds another frame\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md#REFERENCE_FRAME%2F1.%20The%20frame%20as%20the%20engagement%20unit%2FFoundation%20to%20law\",\"start_line\":181}],\"statement\":\"Treat failures and violations as persistent evidence for frame/activation/actor/set improvement. Diagnosis grants no repair authority. Before adding a frame, exclude activation, basis, capability, evidence, missing-relation, missing-conjunction and evaluation-family defects; the member owns the listed signals and eight-question diagnostic order.\",\"uncertainty\":\"The full signal list and eight-question order are referenced but absent.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:d18d271a4a59ebbb8f4247b42e4627ed","key":1366,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:395652cb307f9e3aec1351f1377975e4\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:05c1a265f04949108de6c22b4ed5d7b2\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:d18d271a4a59ebbb8f4247b42e4627ed\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"Acquiring and activating source-described frame context.\"],\"exceptions\":[\"Prefer a current derived surface where it serves the task; acquire deciding owner sections when the carrier is stale, missing or insufficient for the named question.\"],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":182,\"path\":\"standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md\",\"quote\":\"declared inputs are acquired by exact identity, and only from the exact selected basis: a declared input absent from the actor's view is neither licence to read elsewhere nor evidence that it is absent, and a candidate source, a moving selector or another basis is no substitute.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md#REFERENCE_FRAME%2F1.%20The%20frame%20as%20the%20engagement%20unit%2FFoundation%20to%20law\",\"start_line\":182}],\"statement\":\"Acquire declared inputs by exact identity only from the selected basis. Absence from view neither licences another source nor proves absence; candidate source, moving selector or other basis is no substitute. Acquisition is read-only and grants no role/operation/decision; return a missing binding with its outcome before dependent action. Activation binds reusable declaration to exact subject/basis and declared material/evidence inputs, never a workspace dump; reusable declaration proves no particular activation. If no available frame/actor pairing can lawfully evaluate, return out_of_frame or the refusal whose cause holds; do not proceed via implied context.\",\"uncertainty\":\"These are represented subject rules, not instructions to perform acquisition in this response.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:cf37c09404790f100abe5163f0b6a69c","key":1367,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:05c1a265f04949108de6c22b4ed5d7b2\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:395652cb307f9e3aec1351f1377975e4\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:cf37c09404790f100abe5163f0b6a69c\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[\"Historical workaround prose may be retained when a current surface still needs its constraint.\"],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":184,\"path\":\"standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md\",\"quote\":\"For a question another member owns, or one that joins the law of several owners, the step returns `out_of_frame` naming the owning members, and the question is decided from those members or from a derived surface whose declared sources include every owner\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md#REFERENCE_FRAME%2F1.%20The%20frame%20as%20the%20engagement%20unit%2FFoundation%20to%20law\",\"start_line\":184}],\"statement\":\"A derived surface/projected frame decides standalone only questions owned by its source members. Questions owned elsewhere or joining owners return out_of_frame naming them, then are decided from those owners or a surface declaring every owner. A prompt is a rendered contract over typed authority, not source law: it projects current needed authority references, obligations, contracts, boundaries, proof expectations, fallbacks and acquired material. Begin at the highest live authority needed and name unresolved upstream authority gaps before fallback context.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:92185f0eb12931bc814faf225fc58c65","key":1368,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:544a4e40a3d742a6d00a0bffa1b08fbd\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:35f1f9ede029690551cd65423de48e25\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:92185f0eb12931bc814faf225fc58c65\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":242,\"path\":\"standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md\",\"quote\":\"Each consumer applies the rule and decides nothing the owning section does\\nnot (P2, P6).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md#REFERENCE_FRAME%2F1.%20The%20frame%20as%20the%20engagement%20unit%2FFoundation%20to%20law\",\"start_line\":241}],\"statement\":\"Family-table consumers apply rules without deciding beyond their owning sections. Choice columns assign import selections, context identity, evaluation families, coordinate/equality laws, invalidators, packet/declaration fields, translations, composition and resource controls to their stated owners. Core claims and violation lists restate traced laws; adopting REFERENCE_FRAME infers no frame machinery, global context, universal completeness or domain authority. Rows for engagement atomicity, imports, proportional compression and high-risk coverage explicitly have no separate consumer; cited domain contraction or separate-assessor profiles do not thereby apply those rows.\",\"uncertainty\":\"The extensive consumer-locus index remains a reference index, not proof that downstream consumers conform.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:77ea8f86eff7f4650c02654a677d62e8","key":1369,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:9a8783a2b29a0621f74aa70f7d3ee135\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:77ea8f86eff7f4650c02654a677d62e8\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"Interpreting activate, conjoin or translate outcomes.\"],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":558,\"path\":\"standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md\",\"quote\":\"each outcome below maps\\nto exactly one core value for the predicate its function names, the value\\ntravels with that predicate and with the outcome, whose meaning stays here,\\nand an outcome named in the signatures above that would map to more than\\none core value according to its cause carries the cause in its name, as in\\n`activation_refusal(basis)` (P5, P6). Purpose and material relation: a consumer that combines these\\noutcomes with other results reads them in the one core, so a refusal, a\\nconflict or a loss outside the accepted loss is neither mistaken for\\nsuccess nor merged with an evaluation that was not performed.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md#REFERENCE_FRAME%2F5.%20Method%20functions\",\"start_line\":550}],\"statement\":\"Each refined outcome carries its function's predicate and exactly one core value while retaining its local meaning; causes distinguish otherwise ambiguous outcome names. Refusal, conflict and unaccepted loss cannot mean success or be merged with an unperformed evaluation. Evaluate returns result, evidence and residuals under RF-012 and closed-result reuse under ACTIVATION §7; EVALUATION §7 qualifies all functions.\",\"uncertainty\":\"The referenced core and qualification laws are not supplied in full.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:9dda8d87fa4a9dd01368fe7b0ba88ed4","key":1370,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:9a8783a2b29a0621f74aa70f7d3ee135\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:9dda8d87fa4a9dd01368fe7b0ba88ed4\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"Activating a frame for an evaluation, subject, basis and actor.\"],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":565,\"path\":\"standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md\",\"quote\":\"| | `activation_refusal(basis)` | the subject or basis is stale, advanced, ambiguous or mismatched (RF-005), a topology mismatch included: the subject's topology is not the topology basis the frame declares (RF-011) | `invalid_basis` |\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md#REFERENCE_FRAME%2F5.%20Method%20functions\",\"start_line\":565}],\"statement\":\"activated_frame maps to satisfied when the declaration binds the exact evaluation, subject, basis and actor. activation_refusal(capability) maps to out_of_frame when a needed capability is declared by the frame but absent from the selected actor's declared envelope; it names the capability and its owner where supplied. activation_refusal(authority) maps to out_of_frame when needed semantic, evaluation, operation or decision authority is not admitted, naming its owner. activation_refusal(basis) maps to invalid_basis for stale, advanced, ambiguous or mismatched subject/basis, including topology mismatch. If no actor-usable frame declares a needed material relation or capability, activate directly returns out_of_frame. Activation answers activation only; refusal performs no evaluation.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:795aeeba8ac6d2199f767995a1ae4c72","key":1371,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:9a8783a2b29a0621f74aa70f7d3ee135\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:db936e60348cd5ddfbe90eadaba01749\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:795aeeba8ac6d2199f767995a1ae4c72\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"Combining closed frame results under a declared decision rule.\"],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":568,\"path\":\"standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md\",\"quote\":\"| | `conflict` | the conjunction reports `falsified` while mandatory results for the same claim disagree, one `satisfied` and another `falsified`; the counterexample survives the join, and the disagreement stays unresolved for the decision authority | `falsified` |\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md#REFERENCE_FRAME%2F5.%20Method%20functions\",\"start_line\":568}],\"statement\":\"decision(holds) maps to satisfied when the core conjunction is satisfied. decision(fails) maps to falsified when the conjunction is falsified and no mandatory result for the same claim is satisfied. conflict also maps to falsified when mandatory results for the same claim include satisfied and falsified: its counterexample survives and disagreement remains unresolved for decision authority. indeterminate maps to indeterminate. Core out_of_frame or invalid_basis is returned directly, including basis mismatch, despite absent signature alternatives. Declared veto/deferral uses the outcome whose cause matches the core value or returns out_of_frame/invalid_basis directly. Planned assessments without closed results and required coverage without planned assessment are recorded beside the value, are not conjoin outcomes and map to no core value. decision(holds) is assessment, not acceptance.\",\"uncertainty\":\"The full core conjunction, veto and deferral laws are external.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:427ceb82a65bba0508d372d4c344b3aa","key":1372,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:9a8783a2b29a0621f74aa70f7d3ee135\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:a18aa4716c81ba6c7558cbd669733f84\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:427ceb82a65bba0508d372d4c344b3aa\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"Translating a value or evidence into target coordinates.\"],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":574,\"path\":\"standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md\",\"quote\":\"| | `refusal(basis)` | the source value or evidence binds a stale, advanced, ambiguous or mismatched basis or coordinate (RF-005) | `invalid_basis` |\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md#REFERENCE_FRAME%2F5.%20Method%20functions\",\"start_line\":574}],\"statement\":\"translated_value maps to satisfied when declared meaning is carried into target coordinates. declared_loss maps to satisfied only for loss inside declared accepted loss, carried as a residual. refusal(condition) maps to falsified for a declared refusal condition, loss outside accepted loss, or failed identity/equality under the declared equality law. refusal(authority) maps to out_of_frame when carried semantic/evaluation/operation/decision authority has a target-authority relation stated neither as preserved nor as a refusal condition, and names the owner. refusal(basis) maps to invalid_basis for stale, advanced, ambiguous or mismatched source basis/coordinate.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:27a7398a225e94af717f706231604326","key":1373,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:195629e9ad706d9544c0aecd154fcd87\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:27a7398a225e94af717f706231604326\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"Several frames independently evaluate the same subject.\"],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":607,\"path\":\"standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md\",\"quote\":\"They may overlap in subject, manifold or\\nevidence sources; neither evaluation consumes or influences the other's\\nunclosed working result.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md#REFERENCE_FRAME%2F6.%20Frames%20in%20conjunction%2FIndependently%20activated%20co-evaluation\",\"start_line\":605}],\"statement\":\"Separate activations return closed results. Subject, manifold and evidence sources may overlap, but neither evaluation may consume or influence the other's unclosed working result.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:db181f191ffdbb1a5dac45b0842ab1ad","key":1374,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:a18aa4716c81ba6c7558cbd669733f84\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:db181f191ffdbb1a5dac45b0842ab1ad\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"A frame supplies evidence or value consumed inside another.\"],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":632,\"path\":\"standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md\",\"quote\":\"where the\\ntranslation is represented in `a_c` it is recorded in the preservation,\\nintroduced, removed and residual fields of\\n[AC-013](AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS.md#ac-013-transformation). This section adds\\nonly the frame fields: the source and target coordinates, the\\nprovenance, the equality law and the refusal conditions.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md#REFERENCE_FRAME%2F6.%20Frames%20in%20conjunction%2FEvidence%20or%20coordinate%20translation\",\"start_line\":627}],\"statement\":\"Declare source/target coordinates, preserved meaning, accepted loss, provenance, equality law and refusal conditions. ACTIVATION §4 Refinement owns what preservation/loss must show and the licensing law. When represented in a_c, record preservation, introduced, removed and residual fields under AC-013; this frame section adds only coordinates, provenance, equality law and refusal conditions.\",\"uncertainty\":\"External refinement and transformation requirements are not supplied.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:e0cdcec5219c3da3ce40da738fa5be89","key":1375,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:cff170c9e1941f9081b9f3ff23444d52\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:8a4b3e0b01733e1d2848d3e37a77872b\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:a8dda0745628627da84c7c6f067aa78a\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:e0cdcec5219c3da3ce40da738fa5be89\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":667,\"path\":\"standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md\",\"quote\":\"No relation is the default universal frame topology. A project declares\\nonly the relations its evaluations and coverage claims need (P3, P2;\\nRF-009).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md#REFERENCE_FRAME%2F7.%20Frame%20relations\",\"start_line\":665}],\"statement\":\"No frame relation supplies a default universal topology. Declare only relations needed by evaluations and coverage claims. A possible future interaction does not require general composition law in every frame; governing/subordinate inheritance requires a real declared authority or decomposition relation.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:8c22c8fd8ffba2d3e4b2304076eda3b8","key":1376,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:72de70c8d4e8e6e465a75397655a737d\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:8c22c8fd8ffba2d3e4b2304076eda3b8\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"A material member of the coverage tuple changes.\"],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":680,\"path\":\"standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md\",\"quote\":\"Changing any material member may invalidate the\\ncoverage result; whether a change does is decided by\\n[ACTIVATION §7](ACTIVATION.md#7-closed-result-and-reuse): it does when it\\ncould change that result, as a material input change or a changed basis\\n(P3, P6).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md#REFERENCE_FRAME%2F8.%20Workspace%20coverage%2FCoverage%20basis\",\"start_line\":676}],\"statement\":\"Tuple change may invalidate coverage; under the referenced reuse rule it does when the change could alter the result as a material input change or changed basis.\",\"uncertainty\":\"Full reuse criteria are external.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:b399945fde2e348759ba69dfba761f8a","key":1377,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:7729b386c86d4a0bdcd75f325e1923cf\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:b399945fde2e348759ba69dfba761f8a\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"Sources are available and material; enumerated kinds apply where applicable.\"],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":697,\"path\":\"standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md\",\"quote\":\"The inventory records provenance and\\nmateriality. Artifact presence, file count, operation count, test count or\\nrepository reachability proves no evaluation coverage (P2, P6).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md#REFERENCE_FRAME%2F8.%20Workspace%20coverage%2FEvaluation%20inventory\",\"start_line\":695}],\"statement\":\"Derive inventory from every material available source, including goals/intent/product/requirements/accepted method; accepted design with ontology, identities, lifecycles, authorities and algorithms; implementation capabilities and observable behaviour; operational/release/security/safety/governance obligations; direct/indirect dependencies and seams; evidence/tests/scenarios/qualification/acceptance claims; tickets/check-ins/commentary/post-mortems/incidents/rejected candidates; long loops/resets/repeated repairs/rival paths; known capability limits/prior invisible violations; and applicable external law/contracts/standards. Record provenance and materiality. Artifact presence, file/operation/test counts and repository reachability establish no evaluation coverage.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:55c9994cf7b24ea9c775e92e5f650f79","key":1378,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:873d4a144c22169c04cc15288c18fb86\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:55c9994cf7b24ea9c775e92e5f650f79\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"For each evaluation.\"],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":721,\"path\":\"standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md\",\"quote\":\"| operation authority | the existing owner grant for construction, transformation, admission, publication or mutation where the evaluation performs one; otherwise none |\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md#REFERENCE_FRAME%2F8.%20Workspace%20coverage%2FCoverage%20ledger\",\"start_line\":721}],\"statement\":\"Ledger minimum: exact evaluation predicate; materiality provenance; exact subject/basis coordinate; capable selected frames; required actor competence/context; semantic owner; existing operation grant when construction/transformation/admission/publication/mutation occurs, otherwise none; decision owner; required observations/provenance; material frame/seam dependencies; status; uncertainty/exclusion/re-entry residual. covered → satisfied for capable evaluation on tuple without conflict; separately_covered → satisfied for separately activated frames each evaluating without conflict; excluded_by_authority → satisfied for cited governing exclusion; conditionally_covered → indeterminate when its condition is unestablished, naming condition and deciding evidence in residual; conflicted → falsified for unresolved covering frame/result/authority conflict, retaining its counterexample for decision authority; uncovered → falsified for absent capable evaluation and absent cited exclusion, that absence being counterexample; unknown → indeterminate when admissible evidence cannot decide coverage, including unknown capability or materiality.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:62c74dd5cb20c981f4d939391488197a","key":1379,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:873d4a144c22169c04cc15288c18fb86\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:db936e60348cd5ddfbe90eadaba01749\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:62c74dd5cb20c981f4d939391488197a\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":761,\"path\":\"standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md\",\"quote\":\"Where the coverage tuple itself is stale, advanced,\\nambiguous or mismatched, the audit returns `invalid_basis` (RF-005) and\\nassigns no status.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md#REFERENCE_FRAME%2F8.%20Workspace%20coverage%2FCoverage%20ledger\",\"start_line\":759}],\"statement\":\"Status/core values answer the audit coverage-obligation predicate, never the evaluated claim. Satisfied exclusion establishes obligation met by exclusion, not evaluation coverage or performance. In conjunction over the governed claim, an uncovered row denotes required coverage without a planned assessment, not a falsified component. A stale, advanced, ambiguous or mismatched tuple yields invalid_basis with no status. Conditional, conflicted, unknown and uncovered rows are not covered; cited exclusion is not failure.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:3b7739f40dfc9ac323ed11862dfd78b7","key":1380,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:873d4a144c22169c04cc15288c18fb86\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:8a4b3e0b01733e1d2848d3e37a77872b\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:3b7739f40dfc9ac323ed11862dfd78b7\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"Two covered relations interact in a way capable of changing the governed outcome.\"],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":771,\"path\":\"standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md\",\"quote\":\"Evaluation-row coverage is insufficient when two covered relations interact\\nin a way capable of changing the governed outcome. Every material\\ninteraction is covered by one frame, a declared conjunction, a translation\\nor a material composition evaluation (P4a, P2).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md#REFERENCE_FRAME%2F8.%20Workspace%20coverage%2FInteraction%20coverage\",\"start_line\":768}],\"statement\":\"Evaluation-row coverage alone is insufficient. Every material interaction requires coverage by one frame, declared conjunction, translation or material-composition evaluation.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:e46a6fbd8f999746bee3fe1acb55a311","key":1381,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:51a5f7e39586744f57d4c28f2d03a6d3\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:873d4a144c22169c04cc15288c18fb86\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:e46a6fbd8f999746bee3fe1acb55a311\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"Material evaluations or operations are present.\"],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":779,\"path\":\"standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md\",\"quote\":\"Every material evaluation identifies semantic and decision authority.\\nEvery material operation also identifies its existing construction,\\ntransformation, admission, publication or mutation authority. A frame set\\nwith broad observational reach, an unresolved decision owner or an\\neffectful path without operation authority is not closed (P6).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md#REFERENCE_FRAME%2F8.%20Workspace%20coverage%2FAuthority%20coverage\",\"start_line\":775}],\"statement\":\"Every material evaluation identifies semantic and decision authority; every material operation identifies its existing construction/transformation/admission/publication/mutation authority. Broad observational reach does not establish closure; unresolved decision ownership or an effectful path lacking operation authority prevents closure.\",\"uncertainty\":\"The source's compressed list includes broad observational reach alongside closure defects; read with the explicit authority requirements rather than as a prohibition on broad observation.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:e082a1571c8cfdcb578be43c3dfa5494","key":1382,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:7729b386c86d4a0bdcd75f325e1923cf\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:873d4a144c22169c04cc15288c18fb86\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:e082a1571c8cfdcb578be43c3dfa5494\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"Cases are material.\"],\"exceptions\":[\"A historical failure ceases to require this retained input treatment when a declared frame detects or excludes its recurrence.\"],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":786,\"path\":\"standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md\",\"quote\":\"Coverage includes known success, refusal, boundary, integration, recovery,\\nreconstruction and competing-path cases where they are material.\\nHistorical failures stay first-class coverage inputs until a declared frame\\ndetects or excludes their recurrence (P4b, P5).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md#REFERENCE_FRAME%2F8.%20Workspace%20coverage%2FFailure%20coverage\",\"start_line\":783}],\"statement\":\"Include known success, refusal, boundary, integration, recovery, reconstruction and competing-path cases. Historical failures remain first-class coverage inputs until declared detection or exclusion of recurrence.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:de56a53a390d109806e23d2950515b6e","key":1383,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:195629e9ad706d9544c0aecd154fcd87\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:873d4a144c22169c04cc15288c18fb86\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:de56a53a390d109806e23d2950515b6e\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"Human authority requires independent coverage for failures with high consequence, weak observability, strong confirmation bias or historical local proof masking.\"],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":795,\"path\":\"standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md\",\"quote\":\"Human authority may require independently activated frame coverage for\\nevaluations whose failure has high consequence, weak observability, strong\\nconfirmation bias or a history of local proof masking. Such coverage uses a\\nseparately activated evaluation relation and declares any additional\\nassurance-independence conditions. A persona label alone establishes\\nneither relation (P6).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md#REFERENCE_FRAME%2F8.%20Workspace%20coverage%2FHigh-risk%20separately%20activated%20coverage\",\"start_line\":790}],\"statement\":\"Human authority may impose independently activated coverage; risk characteristics do not themselves automatically impose it. Required coverage uses separate activation and declares additional assurance-independence conditions. A persona label alone establishes neither relation.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:7721e6cd2018dee36a8a3338008b260c","key":1384,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:51a5f7e39586744f57d4c28f2d03a6d3\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:72de70c8d4e8e6e465a75397655a737d\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:873d4a144c22169c04cc15288c18fb86\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:7721e6cd2018dee36a8a3338008b260c\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"Claiming operational full coverage for the declared tuple.\"],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":818,\"path\":\"standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md\",\"quote\":\"Operational full coverage is relative to its tuple. It is not a claim that\\nno undiscovered evaluation exists (P6; P0 with the open-world premise).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md#REFERENCE_FRAME%2F8.%20Workspace%20coverage%2FOperational%20full%20coverage\",\"start_line\":817}],\"statement\":\"Require: every known material evaluation covered by at least one capable frame; every material interaction with declared evaluation/conjunction/translation/composition; every evaluation with semantic and decision authority and every material operation with inherited operation authority; every mandatory claim with admissible evidence and refusal paths; required independently activated overlaps and assurance-independence conditions present; no unresolved frame-result conflict hidden by aggregation; exclusions citing governing authority; uncovered/unknown residuals explicit and compatible with the claim. Coverage remains tuple-relative and asserts no absence of undiscovered evaluations.\",\"uncertainty\":\"How universal coverage of known material evaluations accommodates exclusions and compatible uncovered residuals is not fully specified here.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:3fe82e7fcb1853b9ff7ee0eb34060490","key":1385,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:51a5f7e39586744f57d4c28f2d03a6d3\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:72de70c8d4e8e6e465a75397655a737d\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:3fe82e7fcb1853b9ff7ee0eb34060490\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[\"An independently established closed-domain completeness predicate may support exhaustive coverage within a finite formally closed domain.\"],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":829,\"path\":\"standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md\",\"quote\":\"Without an independently established closed-domain completeness predicate,\\na finite frame set cannot establish the absence of every undiscovered\\nmaterial evaluation by inspecting its own declared inventory. A finite,\\nformally closed domain may support exhaustive coverage relative to that\\ndomain and its completeness predicate; the result does not generalise\\nbeyond that boundary. Formal incompleteness results motivate this caution;\\nthey do not by themselves prove that a particular workspace or frame set is\\nincomplete (P0 with the open-world premise; P6).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md#REFERENCE_FRAME%2F9.%20Completeness%20boundary\",\"start_line\":822}],\"statement\":\"A finite inventory cannot self-establish absence of all undiscovered material evaluations without an independently established closed-domain completeness predicate. Exhaustive results stay within that domain; formal incompleteness results alone prove no particular workspace incomplete. Coverage remains falsifiable and externally challengeable through outside human knowledge, independent review, historical failures/predecessors, mutation/adversarial/counterexample search, live operation/user behaviour, adjacent-domain comparison and changed capability/law/dependencies/topology. Explicit residual boundary is required; metaphysical or universal completeness claims are forbidden.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:819de0f95d423af6af58de6104aeb7d3","key":1386,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:41719079da7311bbe57eb93d596d2793\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:819de0f95d423af6af58de6104aeb7d3\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"Any listed observation occurs.\"],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":844,\"path\":\"standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md\",\"quote\":\"These observations trigger frame diagnosis (P4b, P5):\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md#REFERENCE_FRAME%2F10.%20Discovery%20and%20revision%2FMissing-frame%20signals\",\"start_line\":844}],\"statement\":\"Trigger diagnosis for: a competent actor repeatedly missing a known material violation; local repair creating/duplicating another authority path; repeated resets after apparently valid local completion; long implementation loops without stable closure; passing proof with unbound claimed outcome; material failure visible only after broad integration; repeated context expansion without decidable question; same frame name used for different material relations; or topology mutation leaving prior verdicts apparently current. These signals trigger diagnosis, not an automatic new frame.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:8e70c6d81f47fc844f44d1a7c5087df2","key":1387,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:41719079da7311bbe57eb93d596d2793\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:58a83663d990ad5bb6ebf276fd62dec9\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:8e70c6d81f47fc844f44d1a7c5087df2\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"Determining whether the correct frame was activated.\"],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":880,\"path\":\"standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md\",\"quote\":\"Question 1 is answered by family inclusion, not by set membership. An\\nevaluation is within a frame's family when the question it decides is one\\nthe frame's declared evaluation family states, at the frame's declared\\ncoordinates (RF-001). Membership of the frame in the frame set, the frame's\\nname, a role label or similar wording of the question does not place an\\nevaluation in the frame's family; an activation of a frame on an evaluation\\noutside its family answers question 1 no, whatever the frame's standing in\\nthe set (P2, the evaluations determine the attention surface; P1, a name\\ncarries no meaning; the material relation drawn is evaluation-to-family\\ninclusion).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md#REFERENCE_FRAME%2F10.%20Discovery%20and%20revision%2FDiagnostic%20order\",\"start_line\":871}],\"statement\":\"Use the eight diagnosis questions in the declared order. Correct activation requires the decided question to belong to the declared evaluation family at declared coordinates. Frame-set membership, frame name, role label and similar wording do not establish inclusion. Activation outside the family answers the first question no regardless of frame standing. The order prevents difficulty alone from creating another frame.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:f724760c4324bd35d85965b491b27bf7","key":1388,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:c8d1bd7d867c78286170d056a942c518\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:4e34ff185f118a1294229a41556d8e43\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:873d4a144c22169c04cc15288c18fb86\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:f724760c4324bd35d85965b491b27bf7\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"Material frame revision or a change relevant to closed-result reuse.\"],\"exceptions\":[\"A recorded re-check demonstrates independence, or re-evaluation occurs on the new revision.\",\"A harmless explanatory clarification changing no material input and constituting no revising observation invalidates no result by itself.\"],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":905,\"path\":\"standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md\",\"quote\":\"Every prior closed result bound to the previous\\nrevision of a materially revised frame is bound to a mismatched coordinate\\n(RF-005) and is invalidated for reuse until it is re-checked against the\\nnew revision (RF-011; ACTIVATION §7). The revision record lists those\\nresults as reopened; a result leaves that list only by a recorded re-check\\nthat finds it demonstrably independent of the change, or by re-evaluation\\non the new revision. A material revision does not select which of the\\nresults bound to the prior revision it reopens, and silence does not keep\\na result closed (P3, P4b).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md#REFERENCE_FRAME%2F10.%20Discovery%20and%20revision%2FRevision%20actions\",\"start_line\":897}],\"statement\":\"Every material revision changes frame identity/revision coordinates and states which activations, results and coverage claims require reevaluation. Every closed result bound to the materially revised frame's prior revision is invalid for reuse and listed reopened, without selective omission or preservation by silence. Leaving the list requires recorded demonstrable independence or new-revision reevaluation. Unchanged declarations do not preserve result validity: ACTIVATION §7 may reopen results without revision, recorded in work state. Discovery of outside-family activation or newly acquired material admissible evidence reopens the result and every consuming ledger row/coverage claim, preserving demonstrably independent survivors. Even harmless clarification leaves reuse subject to the consumer's exact applicability check.\",\"uncertainty\":\"External materiality and reuse definitions are not supplied.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:2faf16470f6f8916f16340d74c5fd783","key":1389,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:1d204a797802b5261b6acecea9ea1275\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:2faf16470f6f8916f16340d74c5fd783\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":958,\"path\":\"standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md\",\"quote\":\"The actor may own its internal reasoning and search where the governing\\nmethod permits. It returns through the declared result relation. Hidden\\ninternal reasoning is no substitute for required evidence, provenance or\\nauthority (P6). Frame size is optimised for reliable evaluation, not for\\nmaximum context loading: a more capable actor may activate a broader frame\\nand a less capable one may use a lawful refinement sequence, and both\\npreserve the same material invariants and authority relations (P0, P2;\\nRF-014).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md#REFERENCE_FRAME%2F11.%20The%20activation%20packet\",\"start_line\":951}],\"statement\":\"Receive one activated frame or declared active configuration, not an implied duty to reconstruct all workspace context. Packet authority includes semantic, evaluation, decision and operation authority where material. Return through the declared result relation; internal reasoning cannot substitute for required evidence, provenance or authority. Optimise frame size for reliable evaluation; broader frames or lawful refinement sequences must preserve the same material invariants and authority relations.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:4297882b0b78ee43f3092f143a8fe0ca","key":1390,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:2d2745cd8eece9f0ad7fb3c267b65b08\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:4297882b0b78ee43f3092f143a8fe0ca\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"Resolving any activation-binding field.\"],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1002,\"path\":\"standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md\",\"quote\":\"Every field resolves through stable identities and source references.\\nPaths, line numbers, member counts, summaries and matching labels may aid\\nnavigation or diagnostics; they do not substitute for the declared identity\\nand basis (P3).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md#REFERENCE_FRAME%2F11.%20The%20activation%20packet%2FMinimal%20activation%20binding\",\"start_line\":999}],\"statement\":\"Every field resolves through stable identities and source references. Paths, line numbers, counts, summaries and matching labels aid navigation or diagnostics but cannot replace declared identity and basis.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:252268b328c82dc6cddbf21c3c05c791","key":1391,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:58a83663d990ad5bb6ebf276fd62dec9\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:51a5f7e39586744f57d4c28f2d03a6d3\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:873d4a144c22169c04cc15288c18fb86\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:252268b328c82dc6cddbf21c3c05c791\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"The practice supports a frame or coverage claim.\"],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1007,\"path\":\"standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md\",\"quote\":\"Each of the following is a violation of this member where it supports a\\nframe or coverage claim:\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md#REFERENCE_FRAME%2F12.%20Violations\",\"start_line\":1006}],\"statement\":\"Violations are: presumed omniscient complete frame; calling module/file/service/role/persona/prompt/lens a frame without evaluation relation; silently identifying decomposition, authority hierarchy and frame topology as one tree; requiring all active frames to compose pairwise; composition without material cross-frame evaluation; treating selection/visibility as semantic authority; flattening evidence across bases/coordinates into one observed/executed relation; satisfied instead of lawful indeterminate/out_of_frame/invalid_basis; coverage inferred from artifact/file/operation/test/review/actor count; silent growth beyond actor envelope; stale activation reuse after topology mutation without recharting; creating frames for every failure before excluding activation/basis/evidence/capability/evaluation defects; contracting overlap that supplies independent failure detection or materially different capability fit; or asserting a generic runtime/registry/controller/universal carrier is required.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:a37fd281e63c17ed91806ad0c4abebb7","key":1392,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:4e34ff185f118a1294229a41556d8e43\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:a37fd281e63c17ed91806ad0c4abebb7\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1143,\"path\":\"standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md\",\"quote\":\"The out_of_frame residual field carries what\\n[FOUNDATIONS §4 Results](FOUNDATIONS.md#results) requires an out_of_frame\\nresult to name, and reads `none` for any other result (P5).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md#REFERENCE_FRAME%2F13.%20Minimal%20declarations%2FMinimal%20evaluation%20result\",\"start_line\":1141}],\"statement\":\"The out_of_frame residual records missing relation or capability, owner and reconfiguration pressure as required by the external result law; it reads none for every other result.\",\"uncertainty\":\"Any additional requirements of FOUNDATIONS §4 remain external.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:1382ef52806bbf3f5dd8284f60147360","key":1393,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:51a5f7e39586744f57d4c28f2d03a6d3\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:58a83663d990ad5bb6ebf276fd62dec9\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:72de70c8d4e8e6e465a75397655a737d\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:1382ef52806bbf3f5dd8284f60147360\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"A project is said to operate under REFERENCE_FRAME.\"],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1163,\"path\":\"standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md\",\"quote\":\"8. no executable frame machinery, global context, universal completeness\\n   or domain authority is inferred from adopting this member (RF-016, §9).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md#REFERENCE_FRAME%2F14.%20Closure\",\"start_line\":1162}],\"statement\":\"Human authority declares workspace, outcome, inventory and frame set; every active frame is finite, evaluation/basis-bound, authority-safe and usable within its actor envelope; results preserve semantic/evidence/inference/decision distinctions; cross-frame conjunction/translation/composition exists only for material evaluation need; every known material evaluation/interaction maps to capable frame or explicit residual; operational full coverage names its exact tuple; topology/capability/evidence/history can trigger revision/recharting; adoption implies no executable machinery, global context, universal completeness or domain authority.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:a1f1a2b0bbc6098050ca44e0095eae1e","key":1394,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:47f5a07e664b149bf807f7c0c22cd554\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:99876a10de367b85603c3ed68656e593\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:a1f1a2b0bbc6098050ca44e0095eae1e\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[\"A product-local cut name may also be the Git tag name in a release source containing exactly one independently released project, subject to the declared profile.\"],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":39,\"path\":\"standards/RELEASE.md\",\"quote\":\"This member owns the release-publication bounded context\\n`urn:stdo:bounded-context:release-publication` under the selected complete\\nSTDO basis. It owns the identities and transitions used to qualify,\\npublish and select released cuts. It does not own Product meaning or\\nconsumer adoption; the consumer side of adoption is PRODUCT_DEFINITION §4\\n(P6, P3).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/RELEASE.md#RELEASE%2F1.%20Context%20and%20position\",\"start_line\":34}],\"statement\":\"Release-publication owns qualification/publication/selection identities and transitions under the selected complete basis, not Product meaning or consumer adoption. Live specification states current constitutional truth; release process evaluates/bounds/names/publishes/discovers one point-in-time cut. Product-local cut name is v<version>-rc.<n>; selector is v<version>, denoting greatest positive published RC ordinal for that project/line, not immutable identity or exact constitutional/dependency/evidence/replay basis. Equal local names do not merge projects. Bugs/features/regressions/blockers first receive intake class, lawful re-entry, scope, proof obligations and version-line disposition; an RC window permits no untriaged mutation. RELEASE introduces no result values: refused/stopped/fail-closed operations do not complete, and all begun intended effects report under ACTIVATION §3, never completed; invalid state, incomplete cohort or failed verification is a counterexample to its check predicate, reported in the core, never publication or qualification success.\",\"uncertainty\":\"Generic effect, triage and result laws are external.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:4ff637e5bcc0fe562498ba323222ef4b","key":1395,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:7b19e39be9fd85c952d4163c0c025b77\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:99876a10de367b85603c3ed68656e593\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:4ff637e5bcc0fe562498ba323222ef4b\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"Applying F15's stated instance premises.\"],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":150,\"path\":\"standards/RELEASE.md\",\"quote\":\"Each consumer applies the rule and decides nothing the owning section does\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/RELEASE.md#RELEASE%2F1.%20Context%20and%20position%2FFoundation%20to%20law%3A%20release%20and%20successor%20conservation\",\"start_line\":150}],\"statement\":\"Keep substrate, development product, source project, release cut, product, install, artifact and product definition distinct; mutable source workspace lacks fixed Product identity; builder install binds as development product and transfers no authored-Product meaning/authority; product definition belongs to source project, not released artifact. Candidate source, cut, subject and selector remain distinct; shared carrier grants no membership. FOUNDATIONS owns these taxonomies. RELEASE owns ref/name shapes, three phases, no second final cut, publication/advancement procedures, release surfaces, RC ordinal, cohort construction and disposition vocabulary; Product authority assigns namespaces/cohorts and accepts cuts/removals. Generic claims/acceptance belong to EVALUATION; triage/lineage application to SPEC_METHOD; adoption hashing/manager commands to PRODUCT_DEFINITION; same-version recovery requires separate law. F15 accounts for RELEASE §§1–9 and lineage objects; §10 decides nothing. Consumers apply only the owning rule's decisions, with no authority extension.\",\"uncertainty\":\"Detailed external consumer loci and underlying derivations are not available beyond the table's reports.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:e8ec6569341e0678ca071b6099ed239d","key":1396,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:99876a10de367b85603c3ed68656e593\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:e8ec6569341e0678ca071b6099ed239d\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"Assigning namespaces or publishing future refs.\"],\"exceptions\":[\"A declared unqualified profile remains available only while exactly one independently released project exists.\",\"Historical refs are conserved rather than retroactively renamed.\",\"The naming section permits another spelling only under a ref policy proving collision freedom and preserving the same distinctions.\"],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":186,\"path\":\"standards/RELEASE.md\",\"quote\":\"`<project>` is one explicit Project Release Namespace. It matches\\n`[a-z0-9]+(?:[-_][a-z0-9]+)*`, contains no slash, is unique within the\\nrelease source, and remains stable for the continuing release line. It is\\nassigned by the Product release authority. A directory name, display name,\\ndefinition label, package name or matching version cannot infer or\\nreassign it (P3, P6).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/RELEASE.md#RELEASE%2F2.%20Release%20identities%2FProject-qualified%20Git%20refs\",\"start_line\":181}],\"statement\":\"Namespace matches [a-z0-9]+(?:[-_][a-z0-9]+)*, has no slash, is release-source unique, stable along the continuing line and assigned only by Product release authority; directory/display/definition/package names and versions cannot infer/reassign it. Shared-source future ref shapes are refs/heads/rc/<project>/<version>, refs/tags/<project>/v<version>-rc.<n>, refs/tags/<project>/v<version>, refs/heads/release/<project>/<version>; future unqualified cuts/selectors are forbidden. A second independently released project requires qualification before either next cut. Allocated Stack namespaces are specification_methodology, axiom_indexer and stdo_representation; these distinguish refs without Product merger, dependency or composition implication.\",\"uncertainty\":\"The exact-shape requirement is read together with the expressly conditional alternative-spelling provision in Naming.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:0b982b881b71d6525cda727d903d6235","key":1397,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:99876a10de367b85603c3ed68656e593\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:0b982b881b71d6525cda727d903d6235\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"An immutable cut is published in a shared release source.\"],\"exceptions\":[\"The canonical root locator is . alone; at repository root the project-subtree tree equals the repository-root tree.\"],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":241,\"path\":\"standards/RELEASE.md\",\"quote\":\"A tag over a monorepo commit does not make sibling subtrees Product\\nmembers. Unrelated sibling bytes remain carrier state outside the declared\\nProduct subject. Conversely, a member inventory or payload digest without\\nthe qualified ref, commit, Project Subtree root and Project Subtree tree is\\nnot a complete reacquirable release identity (P3, P6).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/RELEASE.md#RELEASE%2F2.%20Release%20identities%2FProject-subtree%20release%20identity\",\"start_line\":237}],\"statement\":\"Bind namespace/owning Product authority, exact qualified ref/annotated tag object, peeled commit/repository-root tree, normalised repository-relative subtree root and its exact Git tree, declared member inventory/release claim bytes, and §9 predecessor/successor dispositions. Subtree root is a locator within exact commit, not Product identity: slash-separated exact tree-entry bytes with no leading/trailing slash, empty component, . component or .. component, except . alone for root. Moving source changes locator and cut identity without namespace reassignment. Commit tags confer no sibling membership; inventory/digest alone without qualified ref, commit, subtree root/tree is not complete reacquirable identity.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:4d2e05df9337bf1f515eaa6fd487e353","key":1398,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:99876a10de367b85603c3ed68656e593\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:4d2e05df9337bf1f515eaa6fd487e353\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"Project qualification or namespace transition.\"],\"exceptions\":[\"An additional archival ref may preserve reachability of the same historical tag object.\"],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":250,\"path\":\"standards/RELEASE.md\",\"quote\":\"Project qualification is prospective. Existing unqualified refs retain\\ntheir names, objects, peels and public links. A historical tag object may\\nremain reachable through an additional archival ref, but it is not\\nrecreated, re-annotated, moved or replaced. An immutable historical tag\\nremains the same object regardless of which preserving ref reaches it\\n(P3, P4b).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/RELEASE.md#RELEASE%2F2.%20Release%20identities%2FHistorical%20ref%20and%20public-URI%20conservation\",\"start_line\":245}],\"statement\":\"Qualification is prospective: preserve historical unqualified ref names, objects, peels and public links; never recreate/reannotate/move/replace historical tag objects. Product-local names and stdo://releases/v<version>-rc.<n>/ remain unchanged; project-qualified transport refs do not enter the logical URI. Resolution binds exact historical/qualified ref and fails closed if one project-local coordinate names distinct tag objects. Latest spans greatest positive ordinal over that project's historical and qualified cuts. First qualified publication creates qualified selector; old unqualified selector remains at its object, stops being current for shared source, and is not force-moved to imitate the namespace.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:32a4e150e00e879613789026392bfca6","key":1399,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:47f5a07e664b149bf807f7c0c22cd554\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:99876a10de367b85603c3ed68656e593\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:ab9e1240d741031d3f1aaabda745554e\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:32a4e150e00e879613789026392bfca6\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":280,\"path\":\"standards/RELEASE.md\",\"quote\":\"There is no second final cut after an accepted RC. Publication immediately\\nmakes the new highest ordinal discoverable through the version-line\\nselector; acceptance remains a verdict over the exact immutable RC rather\\nthan a second carrier. If any byte capable of affecting the Product or a\\nrelease-scoped claim changes, the project publishes and reviews a higher\\nimmutable RC cut instead (P3, P6).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/RELEASE.md#RELEASE%2F3.%20Phases\",\"start_line\":275}],\"statement\":\"Three phases: mutable candidate construction; immutable RC publication with monotonic selector advancement; exact-cut qualification, acceptance and explicit consumer adoption. Publication immediately advertises highest ordinal; acceptance is a verdict on that RC, not a second final cut/carrier. Any byte capable of affecting Product or release-scoped claim requires publication and review of a higher immutable RC.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:c125ea154ad5738ac7527dc85b3adaed","key":1400,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:47f5a07e664b149bf807f7c0c22cd554\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:99876a10de367b85603c3ed68656e593\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:c125ea154ad5738ac7527dc85b3adaed\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"Candidate construction precedes RC publication.\"],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":295,\"path\":\"standards/RELEASE.md\",\"quote\":\"The intended Product boundary, release-scoped claims, excluded\\nsource-project state and qualification basis become explicit before RC\\npublication. A material scope change is repriced instead of being silently\\nabsorbed (P2, P6).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/RELEASE.md#RELEASE%2F3.%20Phases%2FMutable%20candidate%20construction\",\"start_line\":292}],\"statement\":\"Mutable source is explicitly non-operative for released consumers. Before publication make intended Product boundary, release claims, excluded source state and qualification basis explicit. Reprice material scope change rather than silently absorbing it.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:648e49b07a4a8cfa74a05b5ab55a10f5","key":1401,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:47f5a07e664b149bf807f7c0c22cd554\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:99876a10de367b85603c3ed68656e593\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:648e49b07a4a8cfa74a05b5ab55a10f5\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"Publishing an immutable RC cut.\"],\"exceptions\":[\"Atomic push is conditioned here on transport support; coordinated cohorts impose mandatory atomicity separately.\",\"The release branch is optional.\"],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":326,\"path\":\"standards/RELEASE.md\",\"quote\":\"Each published RC tag is immutable. Further work increments `<n>` on the\\nsame version line when the intended line remains applicable. It does not\\nrequire a minor-version increment merely because review found a bounded\\nrepair. A published higher RC without matching selector advancement is an\\ninvalid, fail-closed release state; it never authorises resolution of the\\nolder cut as the version-line latest (P3, P5).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/RELEASE.md#RELEASE%2F3.%20Phases%2FImmutable%20RC%20publication\",\"start_line\":321}],\"statement\":\"In order: confirm triaged scope/lawful constitutional re-entry; declare exact Product subject/claim set; reconcile release-facing assets; run proportionate pre-RC qualification/operator checks; commit exact carrier; resolve/record namespace/subtree root/tree; in shared source create annotated immutable cut and annotated selector over same commit; atomically push carrier, RC branch, cut, selector and optional release branch where supported; remotely verify cut/selector/release branch resolve to highest published RC commit; record ref/subtree/identity/inventory evidence for reacquisition without mutable checkout. Tags never move. Increment RC ordinal on same line when applicable; bounded repair alone need not increment minor version. A higher published RC without matching selector advancement is invalid/fail-closed and cannot justify older-cut latest resolution.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:40039ecc91d296f1b8734651d2e970c7","key":1402,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:b6b525988325f2bf81fd5df06a4e1be9\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:99876a10de367b85603c3ed68656e593\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:40039ecc91d296f1b8734651d2e970c7\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"Qualifying or accepting an RC.\"],\"exceptions\":[\"Artifact presence can establish presence when presence is the exact claim.\"],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":351,\"path\":\"standards/RELEASE.md\",\"quote\":\"An RC is accepted only when the required exact-cut review and operator\\nchecks are complete and the human authority accepts that exact subject. If\\nreview requires any qualifying-byte change, the verdict remains attached\\nto the old RC and a higher RC is published. The selector already\\nadvertises the highest published RC; acceptance does not move it, rewrite\\nit or create another final carrier (P6, P3).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/RELEASE.md#RELEASE%2F3.%20Phases%2FExact-cut%20qualification\",\"start_line\":346}],\"statement\":\"Bind namespace, qualified immutable ref, annotated tag object, peeled commit, repository tree, subtree root/tree, member set, claim bytes, Product/release basis, each property/observation boundary, evidence subjects, owner verdicts/gaps and complete predecessor-successor relation. Evidence must match claim: source success proves neither packaged nor installed behaviour; packaging equivalence proves no semantic behaviour; artifact presence proves no usability except exact presence claims. Acceptance requires completed required exact-cut review/operator checks and human acceptance of exact subject. A qualifying-byte change leaves verdict on old RC and requires higher cut. Acceptance neither moves/rewrites selector nor creates final carrier.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:aa34c4f350eb3491be8f1cf2b6e84681","key":1403,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:99876a10de367b85603c3ed68656e593\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:47f5a07e664b149bf807f7c0c22cd554\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:aa34c4f350eb3491be8f1cf2b6e84681\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"Advancing a version-line selector for one namespace.\"],\"exceptions\":[\"Release branch updates apply only when that optional carrier is used.\",\"Atomic transport push is conditioned here on transport support.\"],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":374,\"path\":\"standards/RELEASE.md\",\"quote\":\"Advancement is refused when the target has no matching immutable annotated\\nRC tag, any higher ordinal already exists, the selector would move to a\\nlower RC, or the selector and release branch would not align to the same\\nhighest commit (P5).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/RELEASE.md#RELEASE%2F3.%20Phases%2FMonotonic%20version-line%20advancement\",\"start_line\":371}],\"statement\":\"Identify exact new cut/tag/ordinal/peel; confirm no higher ordinal; confirm selector absent or at lower ordinal on same project line; atomically create/force-update annotated selector to highest commit; align optional release branch; push complete carriers/refs atomically where supported; remotely verify highest peel and matching annotated immutable tag. Refuse missing matching annotated cut, existing higher ordinal, backward move or selector/release-branch misalignment. Forward movement is strictly ordinal-monotonic; repair defects with higher immutable RC, never moving old cut or rolling selector back. Selector means rc.latest; concrete RCs remain addressable.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:30020fa08b20607c8fcc93ce7d2e6ec3","key":1404,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:ab9e1240d741031d3f1aaabda745554e\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:99876a10de367b85603c3ed68656e593\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:30020fa08b20607c8fcc93ce7d2e6ec3\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"Resolving a channel or adopting its selected cut.\"],\"exceptions\":[\"A consumer may explicitly retain an older exact URI/digest using exact-basis operations such as sync, not a latest channel.\"],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":425,\"path\":\"standards/RELEASE.md\",\"quote\":\"Presentation and mutation are separate invocations. The read-only plan,\\nthe Adoption Plan of PRODUCT_DEFINITION §4, binds the current Product\\nDefinition bytes and basis to the target immutable cut, annotated tag\\nobject, peeled commit, tree and installed-manifest digest, then emits a\\ndeterministic plan digest. Mutation requires that exact digest as the\\noperator's acceptance and re-derives it before changing any Product\\nDefinition. Selector, target, manifest or definition drift invalidates the\\nacceptance. A fleet uses the same law with one aggregate digest over all\\nexact per-definition plans. Planning inside a mutating invocation is not\\nexternal presentation and cannot authorise itself. The plan's hashing rule\\nand the manager's command boundaries are PRODUCT_DEFINITION §4 (P6, P3).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/RELEASE.md#RELEASE%2F4.%20Selector%20and%20consumer%20adoption\",\"start_line\":415}],\"statement\":\"Selector answers only highest published cut, never consumer governing basis. Require annotated selector and distinct peeled commit; missing peeled ref fails closed, not lightweight fallback. Enumerate namespace RC tags including preserved historical ones; select greatest positive ordinal; require cut and selector annotated and peeling to same commit; fail closed for lag or other target. Refuse same-line channel target below current exact basis. Separate read-only presentation from mutation: bind current definition bytes/basis to exact target/tag object/peel/tree/manifest digest, emit deterministic plan digest, require operator acceptance of that exact digest, and rederive before any definition change. Selector/target/manifest/definition drift invalidates acceptance. Fleet acceptance binds aggregate digest over exact per-definition plans. Planning within mutation cannot self-authorise.\",\"uncertainty\":\"PRODUCT_DEFINITION owns unavailable hashing details and command boundaries.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:6524e5886176a9e9a93b4822d3737a7f","key":1405,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:99876a10de367b85603c3ed68656e593\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:6524e5886176a9e9a93b4822d3737a7f\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"Naming refs in a shared release source.\"],\"exceptions\":[\"Unqualified naming only under single-project or historical-conservation conditions.\",\"Alternative spelling requires the expressly qualifying ref policy.\"],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":447,\"path\":\"standards/RELEASE.md\",\"quote\":\"- candidate branch: `rc/example/3.0.0`;\\n- first immutable cut: `example/v3.0.0-rc.1`;\\n- second immutable cut: `example/v3.0.0-rc.2`;\\n- latest-release branch: `release/example/3.0.0`; and\\n- latest-published selector: `example/v3.0.0`.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/RELEASE.md#RELEASE%2F5.%20Naming\",\"start_line\":443}],\"statement\":\"Short shapes are rc/<project>/<version>, <project>/v<version>-rc.<n>, optional release/<project>/<version>, and <project>/v<version>. The example project/3.0.0 names illustrate successive rc.1/rc.2 with one latest selector; they do not allocate a namespace or identify actual releases.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:3e3acc97da4b39fb280cda88baaccb1c","key":1406,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:47f5a07e664b149bf807f7c0c22cd554\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:99876a10de367b85603c3ed68656e593\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:3e3acc97da4b39fb280cda88baaccb1c\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"An RC uses release-scoped surfaces.\"],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":472,\"path\":\"standards/RELEASE.md\",\"quote\":\"Before RC publication, each used surface is reconciled to the exact RC\\nsubject. After publication, changing one of those bytes creates a\\ndifferent candidate and therefore requires a higher RC tag. The\\nversion-line selector has no content-reconciliation phase because it adds\\nno new Product bytes (P3).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/RELEASE.md#RELEASE%2F6.%20Release-scoped%20assets%20and%20the%20Product%20subject%2FRelease-scoped%20assets\",\"start_line\":468}],\"statement\":\"Possible surfaces include release notes, release/installed-distribution manifests, dependency declarations, package/installed-carrier metadata, qualification receipts and branch/tag identity declarations. Reconcile every used surface to exact RC before publication. Any post-publication change to those bytes creates another candidate requiring higher RC. Selector adds no Product bytes and has no reconciliation phase. Exact version/RC identities belong in release carriers and consumer basis bindings; live constitutional version-label usage is governed by SPEC_METHOD's surface rule.\",\"uncertainty\":\"The complete external specification-surface rule is not supplied.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:3e238784a71fec598f7560d18eb70116","key":1407,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:99876a10de367b85603c3ed68656e593\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:b6b525988325f2bf81fd5df06a4e1be9\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:3e238784a71fec598f7560d18eb70116\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"Before qualification and after immutable publication.\"],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":495,\"path\":\"standards/RELEASE.md\",\"quote\":\"A repository commit carries those declared sets but does not make every\\nco-located file or sibling Project Subtree a Product member. The exact\\nProject Subtree tree and Product member inventory distinguish the subject\\nfrom the wider carrier. Once the immutable RC is published, no post-review\\ncarrier delta is admitted into that cut. Publication-caused ticket or\\nsource-work bookkeeping is recorded afterward on the continuing source\\nbranch and cannot move the immutable RC tag (P3, P6).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/RELEASE.md#RELEASE%2F6.%20Release-scoped%20assets%20and%20the%20Product%20subject%2FProduct%20subject%20and%20repository%20carrier\",\"start_line\":489}],\"statement\":\"Before qualification declare namespace/exact subtree root, exact Product member set or artifact, release claim surfaces, and co-located mutable source fields excluded from both. Commit co-location confers no Product membership; subtree tree and inventory delimit subject. Published RC admits no post-review carrier delta. Publication-caused tickets/source bookkeeping go afterward on continuing source branch and cannot move the cut.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:6b5aceb8067abd7ae80b76b21feadbf0","key":1408,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:fa247d55722088d1c8208111b982761e\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:6b5aceb8067abd7ae80b76b21feadbf0\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"A cohort is explicitly declared.\"],\"exceptions\":[\"A stale derived index may remain immutable history, but not accompany changed source as current cohort.\"],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":535,\"path\":\"standards/RELEASE.md\",\"quote\":\"The cohort is incomplete when a required member is missing, stale,\\ndifferently versioned, built from another source cut, or unable to\\nreproduce its declared source-member and digest closure. A change to any\\nsource member covered by the index invalidates the old derived candidate\\nfor the successor cohort. The index is regenerated, mechanically\\nvalidated, independently qualified where required, and released under the\\nsame new cut name. A stale index may remain immutable history; it cannot\\naccompany the changed source as the current cohort (P3, P5, P6).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/RELEASE.md#RELEASE%2F7.%20Coordinated%20release-matched%20asset%20cohorts\",\"start_line\":528}],\"statement\":\"Every required member uses exact <version>-rc.<n> suffix: cut/ref rendering adds v, embedded asset version does not. Qualification normalises only this leading marker and requires exact suffix equality. Equality establishes matching only, never Product/member/tag/acceptance/authority identity. Missing, stale, differently versioned, other-source-cut or nonreproducible source-member/digest closure makes cohort incomplete. Any covered source-member change invalidates old derived candidate for successor; regenerate, mechanically validate, independently qualify where required and release index under same new cut name.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:0badd5e9cf4303f9447a1e839a3f9fb3","key":1409,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:fa247d55722088d1c8208111b982761e\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:0badd5e9cf4303f9447a1e839a3f9fb3\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"Constructing and publishing a coordinated STDO cohort.\"],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":542,\"path\":\"standards/RELEASE.md\",\"quote\":\"Exact installed-manifest identity includes the annotated STDO tag object,\\nso a same-commit carrier containing both that identity and derived child\\nbytes would be self-referential. A coordinated STDO cohort therefore uses\\nthis bounded two-commit construction (P3, P5):\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/RELEASE.md#RELEASE%2F7.%20Coordinated%20release-matched%20asset%20cohorts%2FTwo-commit%20construction%20and%20one%20publication%20transaction\",\"start_line\":539}],\"statement\":\"Avoid tag-identity/derived-byte self-reference with ordered construction: A freezes corpus/plugin/release record/qualification bytes; create annotated STDO cut locally over A without push; install/verify exact local cut to obtain manifest identity for every derived Product/index; B freezes Axiom Indexer, STDO Representation, semantic index and cohort record; qualify B against exact local STDO tag before child tags; prepare annotated child cuts and all Product RC/selectors/optional release branches; mandatory post-tag/pre-push qualification checks every local tag object/peel, selector, RC/release branch, normalised version mapping, target commit and closed ref set, fetching/binding expected remote OID or absence for every destination; one atomic transaction publishes only qualified carrier branch and complete Product refs.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:bb1ef240d2f6e8bad0c2cf021c608fee","key":1410,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:fa247d55722088d1c8208111b982761e\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:bb1ef240d2f6e8bad0c2cf021c608fee\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"Publishing or remotely verifying a coordinated cohort.\"],\"exceptions\":[\"Later bookkeeping commits are allowed without moving immutable cohort tags.\"],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":575,\"path\":\"standards/RELEASE.md\",\"quote\":\"If the remote does not support atomic ref publication, publication\\nrefuses. The process has no sequential-push fallback. Every immutable cut\\ntag is create-only and therefore requires bound remote absence. Every\\nmutable carrier, RC branch, selector and release branch uses an explicit\\nper-ref compare-and-swap lease, such as\\n`--force-with-lease=<ref>:<expected-oid>`, in that same atomic\\ntransaction. A missing expected ref, unexpected existing tag or changed\\nremote object ID stops publication; the operator refetches and repeats\\ncomplete content and local-ref-graph qualification before constructing\\nanother push. A lease mismatch never falls back to an unguarded force, a\\npartial push or an in-place expectation update (P5, P3).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/RELEASE.md#RELEASE%2F7.%20Coordinated%20release-matched%20asset%20cohorts%2FTwo-commit%20construction%20and%20one%20publication%20transaction\",\"start_line\":565}],\"statement\":\"Refuse remote lacking atomic publication; no sequential fallback. Immutable tags are create-only with bound remote absence. Every mutable carrier/RC/selector/release ref uses explicit per-ref compare-and-swap lease in same atomic transaction. Missing expected ref, unexpected tag or changed OID stops publication; refetch and repeat full content/local-ref-graph qualification before another push. Never substitute unguarded force, partial push or in-place expectation update. Remote verification fails closed for any required ref absent, lightweight, differently versioned, wrong Product commit or selector/release-branch mismatch.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:828f4fda7e7b0daeb2cae99ded013b03","key":1411,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:fa247d55722088d1c8208111b982761e\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:b6b525988325f2bf81fd5df06a4e1be9\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:828f4fda7e7b0daeb2cae99ded013b03\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"Cohort qualification, recovery or change to cohort law.\"],\"exceptions\":[\"Historical same-version backfill only under separately authorised recovery law naming that exception.\"],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":603,\"path\":\"standards/RELEASE.md\",\"quote\":\"A historically published source cut may be the basis of a later\\nsame-version backfill only when separately authorised recovery law names\\nthat exception. Every recovered asset still binds the exact historical cut\\nand same cut name, and remote completeness remains mandatory. Recovery\\ncannot move the historical tag, add bytes to its Product subject, or be\\nrepresented as an atomic cohort that existed at the original publication.\\nNormal successor publication uses the atomic cohort process above (P3,\\nP6).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/RELEASE.md#RELEASE%2F7.%20Coordinated%20release-matched%20asset%20cohorts%2FQualification%20and%20recovery\",\"start_line\":596}],\"statement\":\"Content qualification binds exact A tag/manifest, B source tree, all Product target refs/version markers/inventories/index bytes/full source digest closure, establishing tagging requires no qualifying-byte change. After refs exist, local-ref qualification binds annotated objects, peels, targets, exact push set and all remote expectations/absences to unchanged content result. Post-publication verifies same relation remotely and refuses partial cohort. Authorised backfill must retain exact historical cut/name and complete remote set; it cannot move tag, add Product bytes or claim original atomic existence. Normal successors use atomic process. Adding/changing cohort law changes qualifying bytes and governs only a higher RC containing them, never retroactively an earlier cut.\",\"uncertainty\":\"No separate recovery law is supplied.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:1ed1593d106f7298a0b44f9ea4d6a821","key":1412,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:b6b525988325f2bf81fd5df06a4e1be9\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:47f5a07e664b149bf807f7c0c22cd554\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:ab9e1240d741031d3f1aaabda745554e\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:1ed1593d106f7298a0b44f9ea4d6a821\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"An RC is considered for acceptance.\"],\"exceptions\":[\"Independent exact-cut review applies where required.\",\"Release-blocking gaps may be addressed by explicit claim-scope narrowing.\",\"Retained evidence satisfies a gate only under the external validity conditions.\"],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":629,\"path\":\"standards/RELEASE.md\",\"quote\":\"Each criterion is a mandatory gate in the sense of\\n[FOUNDATIONS §4 Change impact and evidence reuse](FOUNDATIONS.md#change-impact-and-evidence-reuse):\\nit applies irrespective of any selection of checks after a change, and\\nretained evidence satisfies it only under the validity conditions stated\\nthere (P6).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/RELEASE.md#RELEASE%2F8.%20Acceptance%2FAcceptance%20criteria\",\"start_line\":625}],\"statement\":\"Acceptance may occur when pre-RC qualification passed for declared subject; required independent exact-cut review passed; required operator review completed; intended scope/successor relation stable; release assets accurately describe cut; every release-blocking gap, including EVALUATION §5 promotion blockers, closed or scope explicitly narrowed; and human Product authority accepted exact immutable RC. Each is mandatory regardless of selected post-change checks. Acceptance binds immutable identity and neither advances nor rolls back selector. Consumer adoption separately evaluates channel's exact latest target and mutates only after digest-bound plan acceptance.\",\"uncertainty\":\"External promotion-blocker and retained-evidence validity criteria are not supplied.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:632d538e4d8cc4c135962b3022730bec","key":1413,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:b6b525988325f2bf81fd5df06a4e1be9\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:632d538e4d8cc4c135962b3022730bec\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"A release claim depends on an external backend, transport or operator-facing service.\"],\"exceptions\":[\"The claim may be narrowed before acceptance instead of qualified against a healthy dependency.\"],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":649,\"path\":\"standards/RELEASE.md\",\"quote\":\"A clean skip caused by an unhealthy external dependency is an evaluation\\nnot performed, which has no result\\n([FOUNDATIONS §4 Results](FOUNDATIONS.md#results), Not performed). It may\\npreserve correct Product classification, but it cannot establish that the\\ndependent capability passed. The claim is either qualified against a\\nhealthy dependency or narrowed before acceptance (P6, P5).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/RELEASE.md#RELEASE%2F8.%20Acceptance%2FExternal%20qualification%20dependencies\",\"start_line\":644}],\"statement\":\"A dependency may remain outside Product for carrier/migration classification and still block dependent claim. A clean skip due to unhealthy dependency is unperformed evaluation with no result; correct classification does not establish capability passed. Qualify with healthy dependency or narrow claim before acceptance.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:883ea349cf4dac8dfad325c92f27ddc2","key":1414,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:d6c44732513e57f9b82a2af8b45fb479\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:b6b525988325f2bf81fd5df06a4e1be9\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:883ea349cf4dac8dfad325c92f27ddc2\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"A successor evolves predecessor semantic claims.\"],\"exceptions\":[\"Earlier conserved evidence may be reused when owning text and carrying consumer bindings are unchanged or the change demonstrably does not affect the claim.\"],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":686,\"path\":\"standards/RELEASE.md\",\"quote\":\"an obligation stays obligatory, a preference\\nstays a preference, and every permitted exception and scope condition\\nsurvives, or the claim is not conserved. A statement that a whole\\npackage's wording is equivalent establishes none of this for any claim\\n(P6, P1). A `conserved` disposition recorded\\nbefore this test applied is re-evaluated under it before the affected\\nclaim qualifies; until then its standing is `unresolved`.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/RELEASE.md#RELEASE%2F9.%20Successor%20baseline%20conservation%20%28STDO-UP-015%29\",\"start_line\":680}],\"statement\":\"Identify exact immutable predecessor; origin remains fixed for candidate. Every potentially affecting predecessor claim receives one semantic disposition. Retain/reassess evidence under change-impact law. Conservation compares same material case, scope and authority, must/may/prohibited outcomes, absent triggers/exceptions/prerequisites, owning text and consumer bindings, with discriminating counterexamples. Patch absence is not loss if successor-native behaviour is preserved; naming/code similarity is not conservation evidence. Indicative wording can bind; replacing must/shall alone neither conserves nor supersedes. Preserve obligation/preference force and every exception/scope condition. Package-wide equivalence proves no individual claim. Earlier conserved records predating this test must be reevaluated before qualification, remaining unresolved until then. Unresolved disposition blocks affected-claim qualification as a planned assessment without closed result; qualification records core value with each asserted disposition predicate, never treats disposition label as result.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:eeefedb5362e2ae467450f75059f1e76","key":1415,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:d6c44732513e57f9b82a2af8b45fb479\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:47f5a07e664b149bf807f7c0c22cd554\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:eeefedb5362e2ae467450f75059f1e76\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"A maintenance or support line may affect retained claims.\"],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":709,\"path\":\"standards/RELEASE.md\",\"quote\":\"Where a maintenance or support line may affect retained claims, the\\nrelease basis identifies the watched source, observation boundary,\\ninclusion policy and successor candidate. Relevant changes receive\\nsemantic disposition at material integration and exact-cut qualification.\\nThe consumer owns its record, branch strategy, comparison and proof\\nmechanism (P4b, P6).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/RELEASE.md#RELEASE%2F9.%20Successor%20baseline%20conservation%20%28STDO-UP-015%29\",\"start_line\":704}],\"statement\":\"Release basis names watched source, observation boundary, inclusion policy and successor candidate. Relevant changes receive semantic disposition at material integration and exact-cut qualification. Consumer owns record, branch strategy, comparison and proof mechanism. EVALUATION §5 owns acceptance requirements on the record and applies this section rather than becoming part of it.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:fc55efba4bbb738b20fa9951fd2d7476","key":1416,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:894323f233349c5a81fd1da1c9c828ba\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:7b52a0bef35a63b536af6e7f80726a0a\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:fc55efba4bbb738b20fa9951fd2d7476\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":35,\"path\":\"standards/SPEC_METHOD.md\",\"quote\":\"Its\\noverriding bias is declarative rather than imperative: the system should\\nprimarily declare truths, structures, interfaces, constraints and evidence\\nsurfaces, and let lawful processing derive and realise work from that\\ndeclared surface.\\nImperative procedure still exists and is subordinate to declared authority\\n(P6, P1).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/SPEC_METHOD.md#SPEC_METHOD%2F1.%20Position%20and%20identity%2FPosition\",\"start_line\":29}],\"statement\":\"Treat specification as constitutional source, enabling re-derivation, audit and correction under explicit authority. Declarative bias is a should: primarily declare truths, structures, interfaces, constraints and evidence surfaces for lawful derivation/realisation. Imperative procedure remains subordinate to declared authority. Constitutional examples use neutral capability/authority identities to demonstrate capabilities; consumer particulars are not precedent that becomes method law.\",\"uncertainty\":\"PROFILES §1's complete boundary is external.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:5637e9cc7786f756d51ea6126c79dc64","key":1417,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:7b52a0bef35a63b536af6e7f80726a0a\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:fc18dcf616a3cdc09fa46a6044df9951\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:5637e9cc7786f756d51ea6126c79dc64\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":73,\"path\":\"standards/SPEC_METHOD.md\",\"quote\":\"The authoritative split is strict: the surfaces bound as WHAT define WHAT;\\ndesign and realisation surfaces define HOW; no build tenant, design, code,\\ndefinition overlay or derived surface becomes co-equal constitutional\\nauthority with the bound WHAT (P6).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/SPEC_METHOD.md#SPEC_METHOD%2F1.%20Position%20and%20identity%2FProcess%20constitution\",\"start_line\":70}],\"statement\":\"Method owns process constitution; goals current overriding work concerns; intent domain direction; product-definition current mutable source-project definition; requirements live obligations derived from it; shared/tenant-local design concrete mechanisms. Product definition binds actual authority locations and tenant registry realisations under shared specification. Bound WHAT alone defines WHAT; design/realisation define HOW. Tenants, design, code, definition overlays and derived surfaces never become co-equal with WHAT. Conventional GOALS.md, INTENT.md, PRODUCT.md and specification/requirements/ require no relocation/duplication. Structured requirement families are preferred to an imperative monolithic catch-all; location itself is not constitutional.\",\"uncertainty\":\"Detailed binding and registry laws are external.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:c1e6d3b8caac4747375f043066a4aaee","key":1418,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:867a67ed8bb9b0e5119339afe287cda0\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:894323f233349c5a81fd1da1c9c828ba\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:c1e6d3b8caac4747375f043066a4aaee\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":98,\"path\":\"standards/SPEC_METHOD.md\",\"quote\":\"The expansion does not make the four owning\\nmembers independently selectable and does not reduce the released product\\nto four members: consumer authority remains one complete immutable released\\ncut with its exact member inventory ([RELEASE](RELEASE.md)).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/SPEC_METHOD.md#SPEC_METHOD%2F1.%20Position%20and%20identity%2FMethod%20identity\",\"start_line\":95}],\"statement\":\"Four named areas do not make their owning members independently selectable or reduce the released Product to four members. Consumer authority remains one complete immutable released cut with exact member inventory.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:8158197d8da8585102c28aac5025de46","key":1419,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:894323f233349c5a81fd1da1c9c828ba\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:7b52a0bef35a63b536af6e7f80726a0a\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:fc18dcf616a3cdc09fa46a6044df9951\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:8158197d8da8585102c28aac5025de46\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[\"Ambiguity blocking/escalation is policy under declared risk appetite except hard-stop prerequisite failures.\"],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":124,\"path\":\"standards/SPEC_METHOD.md\",\"quote\":\"The lifecycle is a governed disambiguation pipeline: each major\\nboundary reduces the space of lawful interpretations and surfaces major\\nambiguity explicitly; detection is mandatory; blocking or escalation is\\npolicy under declared risk appetite, except for hard-stop prerequisite\\nfailures (§5; ACTIVATION §4).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/SPEC_METHOD.md#SPEC_METHOD%2F1.%20Position%20and%20identity%2FCanonical%20statement\",\"start_line\":120}],\"statement\":\"The canonical statement routes each clause to its owner and decides nothing independently. Every Product publishes a layout-neutral routing definition locating constitution/local decisions/collective frame bases/WHAT/independent tenant HOW/work/composition, not rival truth. Material terms resolve under bounded context, owner, selected basis and scope; spelling creates no cross-context meaning/authority; explicit imports/translations/equivalences/disambiguations govern seams; zero or multiple applicable meanings fail closed. Requirements cover capabilities, guarantees, governance and verification; design records structural HOW. Major boundaries reduce lawful interpretations and explicitly detect ambiguity. Implementations never replace constitution. Scenarios supply end-to-end proof where capability claims need it. Design derives from requirements, requirements from goals/intent/product, code from requirements/design. Iteration cumulatively reprices; events/projection/delta reveal drift. Every live requirement family has design ownership, classification and downstream closure or explicit deferment; every design record grounds in requirements; shipping behaviour traces authority. Live surfaces change through supersession/withdrawal, never silent mutation. New intent follows real cases and gap analysis. Sprints price proof cost and force close review; they are no authority layer or concealment of drift.\",\"uncertainty\":\"Several owning sections and hard-stop definitions are not supplied.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:713e02d3a0f0c7f07f0a8fae201c0c0b","key":1420,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:26a8936b7793bf1681e921b95ed4987b\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:fc18dcf616a3cdc09fa46a6044df9951\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:713e02d3a0f0c7f07f0a8fae201c0c0b\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"Applying F10's owned-layer, layered-surface and realisation premises.\"],\"exceptions\":[\"Explicit deferment may substitute for downstream closure.\",\"Multiple conformant realisations may satisfy a layer.\",\"Explicit version labels may identify immutable release facts, selectors or clearly historical/superseded material.\"],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":164,\"path\":\"standards/SPEC_METHOD.md\",\"quote\":\"A realisation choice that no upper layer constrains belongs to design.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/SPEC_METHOD.md#SPEC_METHOD%2F2.%20The%20chain%2FFoundation%20to%20law%3A%20chain%2C%20outcome%20and%20build-tenant%20binding\",\"start_line\":164}],\"statement\":\"Declared specification governs; realisations/overlays/views realise, locate or project without co-equal authority. Each live requirement needs owning design decision and downstream closure or explicit deferment; behaviour traces authorising requirements/design and broken trace is drift. A layer is sufficient when a competent actor can derive a conformant next layer; derivation failure is an upper-layer defect. Unconstrained realisation choice belongs to design. Live constitutional surfaces are versioned history changed through supersession/withdrawal, never in place; current truth uses present tense, not version labels denoting recency. Use-exposed inexpressible constitutional conditions reprice the deficient surface or remain recorded governed debt; unanswered lifecycle phases remain recorded gaps. F10 identifies requirement categories/statuses, ADR fields/lifecycle/storage, Gap:/Unanswered: markers and conventional chain layout as domain choices, not consequences supplied by commitments alone.\",\"uncertainty\":\"Exact category/status values and detailed ADR/lifecycle rules are outside this excerpt.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:ae59b4848fba7e0f8c128ee183b93294","key":1421,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:26a8936b7793bf1681e921b95ed4987b\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:894323f233349c5a81fd1da1c9c828ba\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:ae59b4848fba7e0f8c128ee183b93294\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"Evaluating progress, closure, lineage or realisation shape under F10.\"],\"exceptions\":[\"Negative proof is needed where drift is plausible.\",\"Realisation-shape recommendations are scoped to boundaries governed by the design profile.\"],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":167,\"path\":\"standards/SPEC_METHOD.md\",\"quote\":\"A regression or unresolved gap falsifies the claim of the path it affects, so it blocks further promotion only on that path.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/SPEC_METHOD.md#SPEC_METHOD%2F2.%20The%20chain%2FFoundation%20to%20law%3A%20chain%2C%20outcome%20and%20build-tenant%20binding\",\"start_line\":167}],\"statement\":\"Progress is judged against one selected directly verifiable outcome per work wave; evidence evaluates but cannot select/enlarge/replace outcome. Growth requires admitted basis and ends with it; regression/unresolved gap blocks promotion only on affected path. Closure evidence includes authority trace, realisation proof, negative proof where drift plausible, and remaining open pressure, under external TICKETS/EVALUATION/ASSURANCE laws. Lineage objects remain distinct and consumers select one complete release; reusable method change retains one authority relation from evidence to realising consumer. Method terms resolve in declared bounded context. Under governing design profile, semantic steps should read as transforms over admitted truth with explicit edge effects; higher-order/effectful boundaries require explicit composition/effect algebra without mandatory vocabulary. Admission carriers, evidence categories, eight-step adoption chain and mechanics are expressly allocated policy/domain choices.\",\"uncertainty\":\"Full progress categories, growth admission, adoption chain and design-profile rules are external.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:9bc4f54f9b28de45003ef90119cc24f1","key":1422,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:26a8936b7793bf1681e921b95ed4987b\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:fc18dcf616a3cdc09fa46a6044df9951\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:9bc4f54f9b28de45003ef90119cc24f1\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"A build tenant binds obligations to a realisation.\"],\"exceptions\":[\"Only an obligation's owner can weaken it by changing WHAT at its owning layer.\"],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":172,\"path\":\"standards/SPEC_METHOD.md\",\"quote\":\"Only an obligation's owner can weaken it (P6), so a change that needs a weaker obligation is a change to the WHAT at its owning layer.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/SPEC_METHOD.md#SPEC_METHOD%2F2.%20The%20chain%2FFoundation%20to%20law%3A%20chain%2C%20outcome%20and%20build-tenant%20binding\",\"start_line\":172}],\"statement\":\"Different means may realise the same obligations; obligations decide fitness. Executor kind neither accepts nor rejects a realisation, human performance is not adjudication, convenient stack weakens nothing, and structural representation validation does not prove correct execution. Binding divides requirements calculus, computational calculus and execution environment, chosen as tenant design. Identify operations, outcome values mapped to core, resource measures/units/boundaries and obligation-required limits so finite actors can evaluate them. Calculus may serve wherever its laws hold regardless of executor. Multi-tenant development mechanics belong to project law. Construction steps, data meaning and execution remain three separate accounts; mappings state and discharge preservation under ACTIVATION Refinement and AC-013 when recorded in a_c, with joined accounts and environmental evidence owned by tenant binding.\",\"uncertainty\":\"Full §11, resource-limit law and three-account definitions are not supplied.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:f67740cf983b7a558cac5683f47a45b0","key":1423,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:fc18dcf616a3cdc09fa46a6044df9951\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:7b52a0bef35a63b536af6e7f80726a0a\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:f67740cf983b7a558cac5683f47a45b0\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[\"Projection need not replay a complete event stream if retained record is sufficient for Product obligations.\",\"Design chooses where/how required surfaces are realised unless the path itself is constitutional.\"],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":246,\"path\":\"standards/SPEC_METHOD.md\",\"quote\":\"This is the homeostatic loop. Every link is load-bearing. A break at any\\nlink, goals with no downstream repricing path, an unowned requirement, an\\nungrounded design record, code without a design decision, creates\\naccidental law (P6). Load-bearing means owned, not software: the links\\nCode, Events and Projection name responsibilities every realisation\\ncarries in the carrier its binding selects (§11), and no product owes a\\ncode base or an event store that its binding does not select (P2, P6).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/SPEC_METHOD.md#SPEC_METHOD%2F2.%20The%20chain%2FConstitutional%20chain\",\"start_line\":240}],\"statement\":\"Every chain link is owned and load-bearing; absent repricing path, unowned requirement, ungrounded design or code without design decision creates accidental law. ADR is a durable design record, not another constitutional layer. Code/Events/Projection are binding-selected responsibilities across software/human/mixed realisations, not universal codebase/event-store requirements. Goals keep temporary work focus out of deeper layers until intentional repricing. Present-tense Product Definition bridges direction to requirements, naming source-project terms/boundaries; it is neither immutable cut nor installed Product. Requirements state mandatory truth including capabilities/invariants/constraints/governance/verification, not merely visible features. Design chooses mechanisms, interfaces/topology/placement/carriers/entry-control/runtime wiring/lawful tenant boundaries; requirements may mandate delivered surfaces without deciding placement unless path is constitutional. Constitutional insufficiency re-enters at change-class-named layer.\",\"uncertainty\":\"Detailed change classes and §11 binding rules are only referenced.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:5cbf9d8d4fb3f1e5f672ae5af5261cd4","key":1424,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:f80d75c7a70cd53604f225c790e0cbea\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:5cbf9d8d4fb3f1e5f672ae5af5261cd4\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[\"Transitional paths may remain as explicitly retained compatibility features.\"],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":299,\"path\":\"standards/SPEC_METHOD.md\",\"quote\":\"It demands evidence for claims through scenarios, tests, events,\\nprojection and delta. It treats repricing as part of correctness: when\\nreality exposes a constitutional gap, the specification changes. It keeps\\nauthority directional while iterating: goals govern intent, intent governs\\nproduct definition, product definition governs requirements, requirements\\ngovern design, and requirements plus design govern code. It keeps the live\\noperative surface in the present tense only: once a new current reality is\\nestablished, transitional paths are erased from the live product unless\\nexplicitly retained as compatibility features. It treats derived artifacts,\\nindexes, trace matrices, reports, automation and generated views, as read\\nmodels, never as constitutional truth. If these claims do not hold, the\\nwork is not spec-driven.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/SPEC_METHOD.md#SPEC_METHOD%2F2.%20The%20chain%2FManifesto\",\"start_line\":288}],\"statement\":\"The method requires full constitutional requirements, code derivable from requirements/design, narrowing at major gates, evidence through scenarios/tests/events/projection/delta, and specification repricing when reality exposes a constitutional gap. Authority stays directional during iteration. Current operative truth is present-tense; obsolete transitions are erased subject to the compatibility exception. Derived artifacts, indexes, trace matrices, reports, automation and generated views are read models, never constitutional truth. Failure of these commitments excludes the spec-driven designation. Declarative truth/boundaries over imperative procedure remains a preference.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:bd239ac2a3bb35dd5712027f1279acac","key":1425,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:f80d75c7a70cd53604f225c790e0cbea\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:bd239ac2a3bb35dd5712027f1279acac\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"Any listed failure holds.\"],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":329,\"path\":\"standards/SPEC_METHOD.md\",\"quote\":\"The work is not spec-driven if any of these holds (P2, P6):\\n\\n1. Given goals, a competent team cannot derive a conformant intent surface.\\n2. Given intent, a competent team cannot derive a conformant\\n   product-definition surface.\\n3. Given product definition, a competent team cannot derive conformant\\n   requirements.\\n4. Given requirements, a competent team cannot derive a conformant design.\\n5. Given requirements and design, a competent team cannot derive conformant\\n   code.\\n6. A live requirement has no explicit status, category or owning design\\n   decision.\\n7. A live requirement has no downstream realisation or explicit deferment\\n   surface.\\n8. Code behaviour exists without requirement and design authority.\\n9. A live domain artifact is rewritten in place after becoming part of the\\n   live constitutional surface.\\n10. A capability claim has no operational evidence.\\n11. Drift is discovered, [Universal intake triage](#universal-intake-triage)\\n    locates its cause in the constitutional source, and that source is not\\n    repriced.\\n12. A major ambiguity at a constitutional or realisation boundary is neither\\n    recorded nor explicitly governed.\\n13. A material product, module, function, application, runtime surface or\\n    capability has no declared operational lifecycle signal and no recorded\\n    gap for unanswered release, deployment, live-use, telemetry or\\n    retirement questions.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/SPEC_METHOD.md#SPEC_METHOD%2F2.%20The%20chain%2FSpec-drivenness%20litmus\",\"start_line\":303}],\"statement\":\"Work is not spec-driven if a competent team cannot derive conformant intent from goals, product definition from intent, requirements from product, design from requirements, or code from requirements plus design; if any live requirement lacks explicit status, category, owning design decision, or both downstream realisation and explicit deferment; if code lacks requirement/design authority; if a live constitutional domain artifact is rewritten in place; if a capability lacks operational evidence; if triage attributes discovered drift to constitutional source that is not repriced; if major boundary ambiguity is neither recorded nor explicitly governed; or if a material product/module/function/application/runtime surface/capability has neither declared lifecycle signal nor recorded gap for unanswered release, deployment, live-use, telemetry or retirement questions.\",\"uncertainty\":\"These are exclusion conditions, not an independently sufficient acceptance test.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:98a9cd244a3564e45267d06050c629ba","key":1426,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:f8a1b1b5f801b47764b6f0c9f0a8473d\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:98a9cd244a3564e45267d06050c629ba\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":360,\"path\":\"standards/SPEC_METHOD.md\",\"quote\":\"A failure at any boundary is a specification defect of the upper layer. If\\nintent cannot be derived from goals, the goals surface is unclear,\\ncontradictory or not concrete enough to orient the next bounded wave of\\nwork. If product cannot be derived from intent, the intent surface is too\\nvague, contradictory or not concrete enough to guide realisation. If\\nrequirements cannot be derived from product, the product surface is\\nunderspecified, contradictory or not decomposable enough to govern\\nimplementation. If design cannot be derived from requirements, the\\nrequirement surface is underspecified, contradictory or polluted with\\naccidental implementation detail. If code cannot be derived from\\nrequirements plus design, the design surface is incomplete, ambiguous or\\nnot operational enough. ADRs and design documents are therefore not\\ndecorative explanation; they are the load-bearing bridge between\\nconstitutional truth and executable realisation.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/SPEC_METHOD.md#SPEC_METHOD%2F2.%20The%20chain%2FReconstruction%20litmus\",\"start_line\":347}],\"statement\":\"Specification-drivenness requires ordered reconstructability. Boundary failure is an upper-layer defect: goals unclear/contradictory/insufficiently concrete for the bounded wave; intent vague/contradictory/insufficiently concrete for realisation; product underspecified/contradictory/insufficiently decomposable; requirements underspecified/contradictory/polluted by accidental implementation detail; or design incomplete/ambiguous/insufficiently operational for code. ADRs/design documents are load-bearing. Sufficiency depends on ambiguity governance; accepted relations may be reused only on exact basis after applicability/invalidation checks. A local selected function's span excludes rebuilding the whole product. The litmus neither waives the design profile's material-change gate nor requires recreation of unchanged accepted views.\",\"uncertainty\":\"Detailed sufficiency, reconstruction-span and design-profile rules are externally owned.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:9fa440eca043b00545f8bfd145131721","key":1427,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:5901946aac03404c647b37dbf3bfb477\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:9fa440eca043b00545f8bfd145131721\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"A real use case, including scenario, deployment or external review, pressures the current model.\"],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":393,\"path\":\"standards/SPEC_METHOD.md\",\"quote\":\"The generative rule: a real use case (scenario, deployment, external review)\\nhits the current model; gap analysis identifies what the constitution cannot\\nexpress; if the gap is constitutional, not merely a missing implementation,\\nit re-enters at the layer its [change class](#change-classes) names, and\\nnew goals or intent are written where it changes the work wave, direction\\nor scope; the repriced surface then flows forward through the layers that\\nclass lists. New intents emerge from repeated, real use-case pressure\\nagainst the current model, not from abstract speculation; a gap becomes\\nintent only once it is concrete. Ad hoc coding pressure does not generate\\nintent; explicit gap analysis does. This is how the system stays alive\\ninstead of becoming a frozen constitution.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/SPEC_METHOD.md#SPEC_METHOD%2F2.%20The%20chain%2FRenewal%20path\",\"start_line\":383}],\"statement\":\"Explicit gap analysis identifies what the constitution cannot express. A constitutional gap, distinguished from missing implementation, re-enters at its change class's layer and flows forward through that class's layers. New goals/intent arise only where work-wave focus, direction or scope changes; intent emerges from concrete, repeated real-use pressure, not abstract speculation or ad hoc coding pressure. Requirements/design refine cumulatively, code is repeatedly re-derived, and implementation/testing/replay/scenario gaps feed repricing without reversing authority.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:7340b65094e8c49620520710fd9329fc","key":1428,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:0fba6006fc3beaeee2b2da0429d2ebd5\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:6aa1c6f8fac3acabc7f9abbc957c9418\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:b468f75bb4237ed72bce6a9a5f81fb40\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:9f2f38ea41a0381a444a2592fc8caaaa\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:d9ba6983a42a941491c1518a443a52cf\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:7340b65094e8c49620520710fd9329fc\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[\"Optional realisation detail may appear in intent when itself constitutional.\",\"Explicit version labels are reserved for immutable release facts, selector bindings, or clearly historical/superseded material.\"],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":441,\"path\":\"standards/SPEC_METHOD.md\",\"quote\":\"Constitutional specification is current-surface law and is written in the\\npresent tense. Dead law does not remain in active constitutional artifacts\\nfor historical comfort: what is no longer live is deleted, superseded or\\nmoved to commentary, and a migration wave does not justify preserving stale\\nconstitutional wording inside the live surface (P3). During a change wave\\nthe live constitutional surface is written in terms of the current truth\\nand the declared affected boundary; version-line branding such as `2.0` or\\n`3.0` is not used merely to indicate recency, and explicit version labels\\nare reserved for immutable release facts, selector bindings, or clearly\\nhistorical or superseded material (§6).\\n\\nBefore a downstream specification artifact is treated as complete, the\\nwhole affected span is checked: is the change class clear; is the re-entry\\npoint lawful for that class; can each downstream layer still be derived\\nfrom the upstream layer; do the active intent, product, requirements,\\ndesign and qualification surfaces still say the same thing in the affected\\nscope. If not, the gate is not closed (§4, consistency gate).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/SPEC_METHOD.md#SPEC_METHOD%2F2.%20The%20chain%2FSpecification%20surface%20rule\",\"start_line\":425}],\"statement\":\"Preserve each layer's role: goals do not replace requirements, intent excludes optional nonconstitutional implementation detail, product is not release notes, requirements carry explicit acceptance and material lifecycle obligations/gaps, and ADRs are not a second requirements surface. Live constitutional wording is present-tense current truth at its declared affected boundary; dead law is deleted, superseded or moved to commentary, even during migration. Recency alone does not justify version branding. Before treating a downstream artifact as complete, check the whole affected span for clear class, lawful re-entry, layer derivability and agreement among active intent/product/requirements/design/qualification; otherwise the gate stays open.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:7060523aab54cb2263e871fea4f08b18","key":1429,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:9f2f38ea41a0381a444a2592fc8caaaa\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:d9ba6983a42a941491c1518a443a52cf\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:7060523aab54cb2263e871fea4f08b18\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[\"Upstream constitutional constraints bind choices; constitutional necessity may require specific filenames, placement, paths or packaging.\"],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":459,\"path\":\"standards/SPEC_METHOD.md\",\"quote\":\"Requirements state what control or delivery surfaces must exist; design\\ndecides the concrete mechanism that realises them. If a technology stack,\\ncarrier or runtime is not already constrained by an upstream constitutional\\nsurface, choosing it is part of design, not a separate upstream authority\\n(P2, P1). A tenant's choice of stack, human process or\\ncombination is its execution binding, declared in that design under §11.\\nThe boundary matters especially for\\nagent-facing bootstrap and control surfaces: requirements may say that\\nauthoritative bootstrap or control surfaces must be present, carry bare\\naxioms and route to the canonical method; design decides whether those\\nsurfaces are entry documents, embedded blocks, standalone compiled\\nartifacts or another lawful topology (PRODUCT_DEFINITION §12). If\\nfilenames and placement are hardcoded in requirements without\\nconstitutional necessity, the requirement surface has absorbed design\\ndetail and made re-derivation harder.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/SPEC_METHOD.md#SPEC_METHOD%2F2.%20The%20chain%2FDesign%20rule\",\"start_line\":445}],\"statement\":\"Requirements specify required control/delivery surfaces; design chooses mechanisms, including stack/carrier/runtime and tenant execution binding unless upstream already constrains them. Agent-facing requirements may require authoritative bootstrap/control surfaces carrying bare axioms and routing to the canonical method; design chooses entry documents, embedded blocks, compiled artifacts or other lawful topology. Hardcoding filenames/placement without constitutional necessity absorbs design detail and impairs re-derivation.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:ada670a35c42e3e337876d3d22f42952","key":1430,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:55a257d3aa9a5758b48bd07e923451f9\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:ada670a35c42e3e337876d3d22f42952\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"The design profile governs the realisation boundary.\"],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":479,\"path\":\"standards/SPEC_METHOD.md\",\"quote\":\"Non-goals of that profile (P1, P4a): it does not require one specific programming language,\\nelimination of all imperative code, monadic or category-theory vocabulary,\\nor replacing every exception with a custom algebraic type. It does require\\nthat the implementation shape remain readable, modular and honest about\\nwhere meaning lives and where effects happen. Where a boundary composes\\nhigher-order functions or effectful computation, it does require an\\nexplicit composition and effect algebra with its applicable identity,\\nclosure, cardinality, effect and authority-conservation laws (FOUNDATIONS\\n§4 Composition). The vocabulary is optional; the law is not.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/SPEC_METHOD.md#SPEC_METHOD%2F2.%20The%20chain%2FRealisation%20shape\",\"start_line\":471}],\"statement\":\"Semantic steps should read as transforms over admitted truth, with explicit effects pushed to the edge. Meaning requiring inspection of orchestration, mutable workspace state, service methods or fallback defaults indicates excessive imperative coupling. Readability, modularity and honesty about meaning/effects are required. A boundary composing higher-order functions or effectful computation requires explicit composition/effect algebra with applicable identity, closure, cardinality, effect and authority-conservation laws.\",\"uncertainty\":\"The applicable algebra and profile-adoption rule are referenced but not fully supplied.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:4dea6098beebc338ba8d59c855575e72","key":1431,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:9f2f38ea41a0381a444a2592fc8caaaa\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:7d0a9c90f5f4ae3de1e1726cf6d1423f\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:4dea6098beebc338ba8d59c855575e72\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":525,\"path\":\"standards/SPEC_METHOD.md\",\"quote\":\"Every inherited or legacy requirement is classified as one of these, and\\nnothing live remains unclassified (P3):\\n\\n| Classification | Meaning | Action |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| Deferred | retained in the live surface as an explicit not-yet-operative or not-yet-realised obligation | keep with an honest deferment surface; do not present as current closure |\\n| Superseded | ownership has moved to a newer constitutional surface or design decision | add Implements and Supersedes to the governing design record |\\n| Active | remains live constitutional law in the current surface | has an owning design decision; write or update one |\\n| Orphaned | no longer part of the intended system | remove or explicitly supersede |\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/SPEC_METHOD.md#SPEC_METHOD%2F2.%20The%20chain%2FRequirement%20categories%20and%20classification\",\"start_line\":517}],\"statement\":\"Every live requirement family has explicit header Status and Category; either missing makes it incomplete. All four categories remain constitutional, not priority or user-facing labels. Scenarios validate capability meaning; not every requirement should become a marketed feature. Requirements should avoid premature concrete realisation choices; nonconstitutional path/filename/packaging choices belong to design. Every inherited/legacy requirement is classified: Deferred remains explicitly not-yet-operative/realised with honest deferment and no current-closure claim; Superseded transfers ownership and requires Implements/Supersedes in its governing design record; Active requires an owning design decision to be written/updated; Orphaned is removed or explicitly superseded. Nothing live remains unclassified.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:2e158804b1db370fa33015718caa8a6f","key":1432,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:7d0a9c90f5f4ae3de1e1726cf6d1423f\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:e4591f6921a4ff4e2ea685314fb47f04\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:1a5f8a4248ff79a871f4360d85c0c3f0\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:1b1081fd5b172df398ec35893fd08af7\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:2e158804b1db370fa33015718caa8a6f\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":544,\"path\":\"standards/SPEC_METHOD.md\",\"quote\":\"The lifecycle statuses (Active, Deferred, Superseded, Orphaned), the\\ncategories and the legacy classifications are declared states of a\\nrequirement, not results, and map to no core value. So are the other\\ndeclared classes of this member: the kinds of evidence of §3 (material\\nadvance, prerequisite readiness, preservation, regression), the old-path\\nclasses of §7 Required migration protocol, the inherited-material\\nclasses adopted, superseded, deferred and orphaned and the\\nimplementation classifications `carry_across`, `redundant` and `rewrite`\\nof §7 Fundamental migration, and the ADR `Status:` values of §10; the change\\nclasses are declared states under §4 Change classes. Each records\\na declared classification of its subject, not the answer to a predicate\\nthat an evaluation decides. An evaluation that reads them returns its own\\ncore value with its predicate under\\n[FOUNDATIONS §4 Results](FOUNDATIONS.md#results). Purpose and material\\nrelation: a declared state is never combined as an evaluation result, so\\na requirement marked Active, or evidence classed as material advance,\\ncannot stand in for a `satisfied` result, and a requirement marked\\nDeferred or Orphaned cannot stand in for a `falsified` one (P5, P1).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/SPEC_METHOD.md#SPEC_METHOD%2F2.%20The%20chain%2FRequirement%20categories%20and%20classification\",\"start_line\":527}],\"statement\":\"Requirement lifecycle/category/legacy classifications, evidence kinds, migration old-path classes, inherited-material classes, carry_across/redundant/rewrite, ADR statuses and change classes are declared states with no core-value mapping. They are never combined as evaluation results; evaluations return their own predicate-specific core value. Active/material advance does not mean satisfied; Deferred/Orphaned does not mean falsified.\",\"uncertainty\":\"The complete core-result algebra is outside the supplied source.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:b4f0737e7bf213100869faa6fb24c297","key":1433,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:7d0a9c90f5f4ae3de1e1726cf6d1423f\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:4db287e299d86eb8953d36f89d7b0b07\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:b4f0737e7bf213100869faa6fb24c297\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"The project evolves a released predecessor as a successor release.\"],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":560,\"path\":\"standards/SPEC_METHOD.md\",\"quote\":\"The legacy classification answers one question: what standing an\\ninherited requirement holds in the project's own live requirement\\nsurface. The disposition of a predecessor claim under\\n[RELEASE §9](RELEASE.md#9-successor-baseline-conservation-stdo-up-015)\\nanswers another: what a successor release does with a claim of the\\nreleased predecessor it evolves, a claim that qualification evaluates.\\nWhere a project's work is also such a successor, each predecessor claim\\ntakes its RELEASE §9 disposition by that section's predicates, and no\\nlifecycle status or legacy classification supplies or replaces it: a\\nrequirement marked Active may still be `superseded` where its meaning\\nchanged, Superseded names no accepted successor relation, and Orphaned\\nis not an intentional removal. Purpose and material relation: two\\nvocabularies with overlapping words would otherwise let a project-level\\nrecord stand in for a successor disposition that its owner has not made\\n(P6, P3).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/SPEC_METHOD.md#SPEC_METHOD%2F2.%20The%20chain%2FRequirement%20categories%20and%20classification\",\"start_line\":546}],\"statement\":\"Each predecessor claim requires its own RELEASE §9 disposition by that owner's predicates. Project lifecycle, legacy and migration-adoption classifications cannot supply or replace it. Active may coexist with successor superseded if meaning changed; Superseded establishes no accepted successor relation; Orphaned is not intentional removal.\",\"uncertainty\":\"RELEASE §9 predicates and disposition domain are not supplied.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:521de85724d3b3e4f8e3ac8f9a9611f8","key":1434,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:d8b080fae05d72da046074755cfaa758\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:9f2f38ea41a0381a444a2592fc8caaaa\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:d9ba6983a42a941491c1518a443a52cf\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:f696d7d5c8744e38d05c8d6dc1e2fd47\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:521de85724d3b3e4f8e3ac8f9a9611f8\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[\"A live requirement may have an explicit honest deferment surface instead of realised design/code/tests.\"],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":580,\"path\":\"standards/SPEC_METHOD.md\",\"quote\":\"Ownership: every live requirement family maps to one or more owning design\\ndecisions; every ADR or other design record grounds itself in requirements\\nthrough an explicit `Implements:` line.\\n\\nDownstream closure: no live requirement remains a free-floating statement\\nof intent; if it is live it is realised through the downstream chain or\\nexplicitly deferred with an honest surface that records the deferment, so\\nevery live requirement family has downstream closure, realised in design,\\ncode and tests or explicitly deferred. No shipping code or tests exist as\\nungoverned behaviour: behaviour that exists traces back to live\\nrequirements and the design decisions that authorise it. No hidden product\\nsurface is allowed; behaviour without trace authority is accidental law\\neven if it works.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/SPEC_METHOD.md#SPEC_METHOD%2F2.%20The%20chain%2FTrace%20closure%20and%20anti-drift\",\"start_line\":568}],\"statement\":\"Every live requirement family has one or more owning design decisions; every ADR/design record explicitly grounds requirements through Implements:. Live requirements close through design/code/tests or explicit honest deferment. All shipping code/tests trace to live requirements and authorising design; working untraced behaviour is still accidental law. Unowned requirements, ungrounded design, unrecorded deferment and ownerless code are drift; implementation-habit tests lock it in. Persistent event/projection delta is diagnosed by intake among code, requirement/design stack, predictive model or observation. Capability without a scenario has unverified operational meaning. Treating guarantees/governance/verification as features misclassifies them; in-place live-constitution correction corrupts history. A real-use gap inexpressible in requirements re-enters at Requirements or upstream according to class, not by a code hack.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:1349db414b8dc233b494faab235d1c6b","key":1435,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:ed7ff9285b162fceacac9fd577163485\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:1349db414b8dc233b494faab235d1c6b\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[\"Mutable implementation surfaces may be aggressively refactored while they retain that status.\",\"Retained superseded responsibility must satisfy the migration retention relation.\"],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":618,\"path\":\"standards/SPEC_METHOD.md\",\"quote\":\"Transitional implementation paths, migration\\nscaffolds and fallback behaviours have no permanent authority in the live\\nsurface: once superseded they are retired, and any retained responsibility\\nsatisfies the retention relation of §7 (closure criterion). The past is\\npreserved by version control, operational event history where present and\\nsuperseded constitutional artifacts. The method does not require shipping\\ncompatibility shims forever, and it does not allow silent mutation of live\\nconstitutional history.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/SPEC_METHOD.md#SPEC_METHOD%2F2.%20The%20chain%2FLive%20surface%20immutability\",\"start_line\":611}],\"statement\":\"Published live constitutional domain artifacts cannot be silently mutated in place. An incorrect artifact is superseded by a new version or withdrawn/deleted from the live surface. Superseded transitions, scaffolds and fallbacks retire unless retention is justified; they have no permanent authority and compatibility shims need not ship forever. History is preserved by version control, operational events where present and superseded artifacts.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:c25338f8b2a9b5a4eb114bee8b27c868","key":1436,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:7e3dd4056d50d0eb1d1209f1d770b654\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:b468f75bb4237ed72bce6a9a5f81fb40\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:9f2f38ea41a0381a444a2592fc8caaaa\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:d9ba6983a42a941491c1518a443a52cf\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:c25338f8b2a9b5a4eb114bee8b27c868\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"Lifecycle aspects materially affect product meaning or an obligation.\"],\"exceptions\":[\"No implementation mechanism for every phase and no release plan for every requirement is demanded.\"],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":654,\"path\":\"standards/SPEC_METHOD.md\",\"quote\":\"For product definition this means naming the current product boundary,\\nintended use context, release and install posture, live-use posture,\\nobservability posture, and retirement or supersession posture where those\\nmaterially affect the product's meaning. For requirements it means stating\\nany invariant obligation that governs build, assurance, release,\\ndeployment, live usage, telemetry, retirement, ownership, source truth,\\nauthority boundary or downstream interpretation; a requirement may defer a\\nphase only by naming the deferment and the surface that will own its later\\nresolution.\\n\\nThe rule is an ambiguity detector, not a demand that every requirement\\nbecome a release plan. Each phase has one of three answers, and this\\nsection owns them: the phase is answered by the surface; if a phase is\\nnot applicable, the surface says why; if it is unknown, a named gap such\\nas `Gap:` or `Unanswered:` is recorded.\\nSilent absence is not a valid lifecycle answer.\\n[ASSURANCE §16](ASSURANCE.md#16-module-lifecycle-confirmation) applies\\nthe three answers to the design evidence of a governed boundary. When the lifecycle signal is\\nmissing, downstream design may not fill the gap by local convention,\\nimplementation precedent, prompt prose or test fixture; it reprices the\\nappropriate constitutional surface or carries the ambiguity as explicit,\\ngoverned debt (§5).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/SPEC_METHOD.md#SPEC_METHOD%2F2.%20The%20chain%2FOperational%20lifecycle%20sufficiency\",\"start_line\":633}],\"statement\":\"Product names boundary, intended use, release/install, live-use, observability and retirement/supersession posture where material. Requirements state invariant build/assurance/release/deployment/use/telemetry/retirement/ownership/source-truth/authority/interpretation obligations. Product/requirements provide enough signal for design or explicitly record ambiguity. Deferral names both deferment and later resolution owner surface. Each phase is answered, reasoned not-applicable, or named unknown; silence is invalid. Missing signal requires constitutional repricing or explicit governed debt, never invention from convention, precedent, prompts or fixtures. These phase answers are declared states, map to no core value and cannot substitute for satisfied; consuming evaluation has its own predicate/result.\",\"uncertainty\":\"ASSURANCE §16 application and the full result calculus are not supplied.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:043cdc6259caea23bf33e58c4ae3c3ec","key":1437,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:7e174d80769b16059837b8b7bff5ce16\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:e4591f6921a4ff4e2ea685314fb47f04\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:043cdc6259caea23bf33e58c4ae3c3ec\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[\"An explicitly product-defined assurance capability may itself constitute product delivery; its evidence still does not author the claim.\"],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":709,\"path\":\"standards/SPEC_METHOD.md\",\"quote\":\"The exact bound outcome instance stops selecting later product-progress\\nwork when the owning authority accepts it; its witnesses remain regression\\nand preservation evidence. Acceptance exhausts only that instance and its\\ndeclared acceptance interval; it does not discharge an enduring guarantee,\\na recurring obligation or a broader product family beyond the accepted\\ninstance. Further work against the accepted instance is preservation, a\\nnamed bounded prerequisite for another admitted outcome, or a new change\\nrequiring lawful repricing; it is not additional progress against the\\naccepted instance (EVALUATION §5).\\n\\nSelecting the next unresolved outcome already defined by the product is a\\ngoals and work-sequencing decision. Changing an outcome's meaning or scope,\\nor introducing a new product outcome, requires lawful re-entry at the\\nproduct (§4).\\n\\nEvidence evaluates and constrains its bound product claim. Completion of a\\nproof surface, matrix, coverage ledger, inventory, design-method artifact,\\ntest suite or other evidence surface cannot by itself select, enlarge or\\nreplace the product outcome. If an assurance capability is explicitly\\ndefined as product behaviour, delivery of that capability is judged as\\nproduct progress; its evidence still does not author the claim. The same\\nartifact may be product output for one claim and evidence for another only\\nwhen those roles are declared separately (P6).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/SPEC_METHOD.md#SPEC_METHOD%2F3.%20Outcome%20conservation\",\"start_line\":687}],\"statement\":\"Judge progress and supported-path promotion against the same selected outcome. Only accepted material advance projects product progress; prerequisite readiness names its enabled obligation and remains bounded; preservation/repeated proof and regression are not new progress. Owner acceptance exhausts only the exact instance/interval, not enduring guarantees, recurrence or a broader family; witnesses persist for regression/preservation. Later work is preservation, a bounded prerequisite for another admitted outcome, or lawfully repriced change. Selecting an already-defined unresolved outcome is goals/sequencing; changed meaning/scope or a new outcome re-enters Product. Evidence completion cannot select, enlarge or replace the outcome. One artifact may be output for one claim and evidence for another only with separately declared roles.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:35843c2cceadd8426d8972b20231557c","key":1438,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:d1c14012a50c7c8714ad1601967bfdee\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:35843c2cceadd8426d8972b20231557c\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":738,\"path\":\"standards/SPEC_METHOD.md\",\"quote\":\"Admission or renewal of a prerequisite or experiment belongs to the\\nauthority owning the selected work wave, or its explicitly bounded proxy,\\nand is recorded in the existing durable goals or ticket authority. The\\nadmitted basis states its provisional bound and its exhaustion or\\nfalsification condition. Satisfaction of an experiment's stated\\ndecision-discriminating observation exhausts that experiment. Drafting or\\nvalidating a ticket or execution contract, retaining active status, or\\nholding a prior admission cannot create, extend or renew the basis\\n(ACTIVATION §1, Admission).\\n\\nAcceptance of the selected outcome, discharge of an admitted prerequisite,\\nor resolution of an admitted experiment's stated decision exhausts that\\nbasis. A basis or bound also ends when another admitted terminal condition\\nis reached or it is rejected, withdrawn, superseded, repriced away or\\nfalsified by evidence. Ended authority cannot be renewed by repair,\\ncontinuation, evidence, active ticket or run state, or prior admission;\\nfurther material work requires a new admission by the owning authority or\\nits explicitly bounded proxy (P6).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/SPEC_METHOD.md#SPEC_METHOD%2F3.%20Outcome%20conservation\",\"start_line\":721}],\"statement\":\"Prerequisite/experiment authority is only its provisional bound and grants no enlarged outcome, downstream work, promotion, closure or waiver of applicable design/safety/authority/release law. Admission/renewal belongs to the work-wave owner or explicitly bounded proxy and is recorded in existing durable goals/ticket authority with bound and exhaustion/falsification condition. Experiment observation satisfaction or decision resolution, prerequisite discharge, outcome acceptance, another admitted terminal condition, rejection, withdrawal, supersession, repricing-away or evidential falsification ends the basis. Ticket/contract drafting or validation, active status, repair, continuation, evidence, run state and prior admission cannot create, extend or renew it; further material work needs new owner/proxy admission.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:2589a0628cbe8376cff461453366ae45","key":1439,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:7e174d80769b16059837b8b7bff5ce16\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:d1c14012a50c7c8714ad1601967bfdee\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:2589a0628cbe8376cff461453366ae45\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[\"Independent work may proceed under its own admitted basis.\",\"Affected-path promotion may resume when regression/gap is repaired, repriced or accepted by the owning authority.\"],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":752,\"path\":\"standards/SPEC_METHOD.md\",\"quote\":\"Retention as supported product behaviour, required evidence, regression\\nprotection or bounded donor material confers no further growth authority.\\nConsumers own deletion, archival, quarantine and salvage mechanics. Salvage\\ncarries only the explicitly re-adopted semantics; it inherits neither the\\nenclosing work's authority, dependencies or completion claim nor its power\\nto select further work.\\n\\nA regression or unresolved gap blocks further promotion on the affected\\npath until repaired, repriced or accepted by the owning authority. It does\\nnot globally serialise independent work: parallel work may proceed under\\nits own admitted basis and cannot be laundered into the governed outcome's\\nprogress claim. Outcome success is necessary delivery evidence, not\\ncomplete product or release closure (§6).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/SPEC_METHOD.md#SPEC_METHOD%2F3.%20Outcome%20conservation\",\"start_line\":740}],\"statement\":\"Retention as supported behaviour, evidence, regression protection or bounded donor material grants no growth. Consumers own deletion/archive/quarantine/salvage mechanics; salvage inherits only explicitly re-adopted semantics, not enclosing authority, dependencies, completion or further-work selection. Regression or unresolved gap blocks the affected promotion path, without globally serialising independent authorised work or allowing its progress to be attributed to the governed outcome. Outcome success is necessary delivery evidence, not complete product/release closure.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:135ac9abfbed20bb0ca9722b85421d1b","key":1440,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:26bbc9cba5e07244353a82f9765fde0a\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:135ac9abfbed20bb0ca9722b85421d1b\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"A substantive change begins.\"],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":765,\"path\":\"standards/SPEC_METHOD.md\",\"quote\":\"Every substantive change begins with intake triage, an explicit declared\\nchange intent and a lawful re-entry point into the constitutional chain\\n(P4b, P2).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/SPEC_METHOD.md#SPEC_METHOD%2F4.%20Change%20management\",\"start_line\":763}],\"statement\":\"Every substantive change begins with intake triage, explicit declared change intent and lawful constitutional re-entry; the family table traces this route and creates no second decision path.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:70378bbc4fcfb78b6877101eca79e306","key":1441,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:13bc06c340699b069791c359438dbd42\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:70378bbc4fcfb78b6877101eca79e306\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":817,\"path\":\"standards/SPEC_METHOD.md\",\"quote\":\"Each consumer applies the rule and decides nothing the owning section does\\nnot (P2, P6).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/SPEC_METHOD.md#SPEC_METHOD%2F4.%20Change%20management%2FFoundation%20to%20law%3A%20change%20management%20and%20ambiguity\",\"start_line\":816}],\"statement\":\"F11 attributes ten consequences to premises: owning-layer re-entry rather than report labels; evidence-tested frames rather than names and diagnosis without repair authority; recorded exact-basis classification with distinct fact/judgment/ruling; unknowns withholding only dependent reliance and no assumption of no effect; obligation-conjunction closure rather than events/status; local visible bounded repayable proof deferral without sprint admission authority; recorded ambiguity with risk-policy blocking subject to hard stops; singular acceptance-path authority and downstream projections; shared-contract closure proof with persistent negative break evidence and owned retention; and no inherited authority absent explicit re-adoption. Domain/policy choices remain owned as stated: this member's six classes/four procedures/C-J-O order/material inputs, sprint requirements/triggers, ambiguity distinctions/narrowing, two migration strategies/presumption/old-path classes, inside-out order and implementation classes; project's declared risk policy; adopting profile's escrow suitability; and affected-product human authority's re-adoption selection. Consumers only apply owning rules, adding no decisions.\",\"uncertainty\":\"The table's foundation standing, external rule definitions and full consumer implementations are references, not independently established here.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:a04fe782b1dc51f2a7457923fa10199b","key":1442,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:fc60a58521409c90ecb8c28db3403f83\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:a04fe782b1dc51f2a7457923fa10199b\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":848,\"path\":\"standards/SPEC_METHOD.md\",\"quote\":\"Triage diagnoses among the four causes of\\n[ACTIVATION §1 Feedback and diagnosis](ACTIVATION.md#construction-relation),\\na defective realisation, an inadequate governing requirement or design, an\\ninaccurate predictive model, and insufficient observation, and routes each\\nsupported repair to the owner of its cause rather than inferring it from\\nthe intake label; severity and priority follow the policies that\\n[TICKETS](TICKETS.md) owns; a bug list projects existing work state. This\\nparagraph applies ACTIVATION §1 Feedback and diagnosis and states no\\nsecond relation (P2, P6).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/SPEC_METHOD.md#SPEC_METHOD%2F4.%20Change%20management%2FUniversal%20intake%20triage\",\"start_line\":840},{\"end_line\":867,\"path\":\"standards/SPEC_METHOD.md\",\"quote\":\"The frames' results combine under the one\\n[conjunction of results](FOUNDATIONS.md#conjunction-of-results): each\\nkeeps the diagnosis it evaluated as its predicate, a counterexample that\\none frame finds survives the join, and a frame planned and not applied\\nleaves its diagnosis open, never ruled out. Counterexample localisation\\napplies where required (ASSURANCE). This prescribes no reviewer count and no new\\nreview round; required independence stays intact. A diagnosis grants no\\nrepair effects and does not establish that governing meaning must change: a\\ncandidate may instead need correction under sufficient existing law (P6).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/SPEC_METHOD.md#SPEC_METHOD%2F4.%20Change%20management%2FUniversal%20intake%20triage\",\"start_line\":859}],\"statement\":\"Bug, feature, issue, regression, operator finding, release blocker and scenario failure enter the same triage; no label selects class or bypasses triage for code/tests/release. Evidence selection is S_Δ over I(Δ). Diagnose defective realisation, inadequate requirement/design, inaccurate predictive model or insufficient observation; route supported repair to cause owner, with TICKETS owning severity/priority and bug lists only projecting state. Triangulate the same subject/basis through the smallest sufficient applicable frame configuration, testing each diagnosis against its variables, relations and evidence. Preserve alternatives/uncertainty and identify the smallest lawful repair scope. Failure-exposing frame need not own the cause; renamed duplicate analysis adds no evidence. Conjunction preserves each predicate and any counterexample; unapplied planned frames leave diagnoses open. Required localisation/independence persists without prescribed reviewer count or new round. Diagnosis grants no effects and need not imply changed governing law.\",\"uncertainty\":\"Frame selection, conjunction, impact-cover calculus, localisation and severity/priority policies are externally owned.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:39274bb61b15eb6d83e18380e9326a65","key":1443,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:1a5f8a4248ff79a871f4360d85c0c3f0\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:39274bb61b15eb6d83e18380e9326a65\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":901,\"path\":\"standards/SPEC_METHOD.md\",\"quote\":\"Smaller changes may re-enter below Goals only if they explicitly assert\\nthat no upstream constitutional surface is changing. The absence of a\\ndeclared change class is process drift. A changed governing relation is\\naccepted only at its owner; accepting it inside the acting frame is a\\nviolation whatever the size of the delta (ACTIVATION §1).\\nTriage records the change intent, the class, the re-entry point and when\\ntriage occurred, wherever substantive work begins.\\n[TICKETS §4](TICKETS.md#change-class) records the class on the carrier.\\n\\nThe change classes are declared states of a change that intake triage\\nrecords, not results, and map to no core value. An evaluation that reads\\na declared class returns its own core value with its predicate under\\n[FOUNDATIONS §4 Results](FOUNDATIONS.md#results). A close classification\\nof [TICKETS §3](TICKETS.md#close-review) that names a layer, such as\\n`design_reframe`, is a result for its own predicate, mapped there, and\\ncarries the class at which the work re-enters as its domain outcome.\\nPurpose and material relation: a declared class is never combined as an\\nevaluation result, so a change classed `realization_refactor` cannot stand\\nin for a `satisfied` result that no upstream drift occurred (P5, P1).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/SPEC_METHOD.md#SPEC_METHOD%2F4.%20Change%20management%2FChange%20classes\",\"start_line\":883}],\"statement\":\"goal_reprice changes bounded-wave focus, enters Goals and flows through Intent/Product/Requirements/Design/Code/Evidence only where focus changes deeper truth. intent_reprice changes direction/scope, enters Intent and flows through Product onward. product_reprice changes current product realisation while intent stays stable, enters Product and flows through Requirements onward. requirement_reprice changes constitutional truth while direction stays stable, enters Requirements and flows through Design/Code/Evidence. design_reframe changes structure with intent/requirement truth stable, enters Design then Code/Evidence. realization_refactor changes local code/configuration/attributes without intended constitutional/structural change, enters only realised surface and must prove no upstream drift. Below-Goals entry explicitly asserts no upstream constitutional change. Missing class is process drift; only the governing relation's owner accepts a change regardless of delta size. Record intent/class/re-entry/time wherever substantive work begins. Declared classes are not core results; a ticket close-classification is instead its own predicate result carrying a re-entry class. realization_refactor alone does not prove satisfied no-drift.\",\"uncertainty\":\"Ticket close-classification mappings are not supplied.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:fcb91feedea31d05c522241794a0b50f","key":1444,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:e21989c4cfce457542b5b0140e63807c\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:fcb91feedea31d05c522241794a0b50f\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":924,\"path\":\"standards/SPEC_METHOD.md\",\"quote\":\"The explicitly selected source, worksite or qualification capability\\nproduces C over the exact request and desired outcome, the known targets\\nand effects, the operation grant and work lifetime, the product definition\\nand governing basis, the baseline and the available candidate, the declared\\nrelations, the accepted design and trace bindings, the evidence and the\\napplicable rules. Its output identifies the producer and procedure\\nrevision, the inputs, the result, the scope, the source routes, the\\nreproduction relation, the unknowns and the invalidators. A missing\\ncandidate or missing evidence is an input state, not a claim that nothing\\nchanged.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/SPEC_METHOD.md#SPEC_METHOD%2F4.%20Change%20management%2FComputed%20classification%20and%20treatment\",\"start_line\":915}],\"statement\":\"An explicitly selected source/worksite/qualification capability produces C from exact request/outcome, targets/effects, grant/lifetime, product/governing basis, baseline/available candidate, declared relations, accepted design/traces, evidence and rules. Output identifies producer/procedure revision, inputs/result/scope/source routes/reproduction relation/unknowns/invalidators. Missing candidate/evidence is not no-change. Expose in order: (1) authority traversal over explicit source/ownership/dependency/composition/projection declarations, reached owners/layers/exact bases, changed/unchanged/unknown relations, edges/frontier, including root/authority/grant changes despite equal public bytes; absent edges prove no irrelevance and uncertain materiality remains J; (2) full relevant serialised-member universe under owning declaration/projection, helpers/generated dependencies, additions/removals and every retained changed typed value/byte with exact before/after; rename is removal/addition unless owner supplies identity preservation, while missing candidate, incomplete enumeration, ambiguous identity or unavailable projection leaves affected delta unknown and membership equality proves no value equality; (3) changed bytes/relations joined to explicit accepted scope/traces/evidence, distinguishing covered/missing/stale/ambiguous/outside-scope, with filenames/listing/digest insufficient and semantic sufficiency remaining J; (4) only declared rules with sufficient facts, recording owners/predicates/consequences, smallest lawful re-entry/next action/evidence or assessment/reserved ruling/carrier lifetime, retaining conflicts/missing premises unresolved. Labels/filenames do not choose routes; settled rules require no invented J.\",\"uncertainty\":\"These are described operations, not traversals or computations performed by this interpretation.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:fac648e5b3488907530752fc5df04713","key":1445,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:e21989c4cfce457542b5b0140e63807c\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:fac648e5b3488907530752fc5df04713\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[\"A sufficient existing contract permits candidate rejection or local repair within its grant instead of changing governing meaning.\"],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":976,\"path\":\"standards/SPEC_METHOD.md\",\"quote\":\"A public delta or other nonconformance does not itself require changing\\nthe governing contract. If that contract remains sufficient for the\\nauthorised outcome, the candidate is rejected or locally repaired within\\nits grant. The actual governing owner is re-entered when the explicitly\\nselected desired outcome requires changed meaning or an applicable\\nassessment establishes governing insufficiency. C determines that\\nconsequence only from sufficient declared premises; unresolved intended\\nmeaning or necessity is J, and any reserved decision remains O. Candidate\\nbehaviour cannot author its own target law (P6).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/SPEC_METHOD.md#SPEC_METHOD%2F4.%20Change%20management%2FComputed%20classification%20and%20treatment\",\"start_line\":968}],\"statement\":\"Changed/unchanged/unknown relations, added/removed/retained-changed identities and covered/missing/stale/ambiguous/outside-scope evidence are computed facts, not evaluation core values. Covered/unchanged is not satisfied and consumed unknown remains unknown. Delta/nonconformance alone does not require contract repricing. Re-enter its actual owner when the selected desired outcome requires changed meaning or applicable assessment establishes governing insufficiency; C decides only with sufficient declared premises, intended-meaning/necessity uncertainty stays J and reserved ruling stays O. Candidate behaviour cannot author its own target law.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:84aec81396f0a308fd58aa6035a77e65","key":1446,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:e21989c4cfce457542b5b0140e63807c\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:84aec81396f0a308fd58aa6035a77e65\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[\"An existing bounded construction/evidence grant may permit a cheapest useful discriminator, including a first candidate, within its exact subject, territory, operations and stops; this implies no conformance.\"],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":992,\"path\":\"standards/SPEC_METHOD.md\",\"quote\":\"Unknown treatment withholds dependent reliance or promotion, not unrelated\\nauthorised work. An existing bounded construction or evidence grant may\\npermit the cheapest useful discriminator, including obtaining the first\\ncandidate, without asserting that the candidate is conformant; it carries\\nits own exact subject, territory, operations and stop conditions. The\\naffected C result is updated before dependent effects or promotion rely on\\nnewly available evidence. A mistaken route is corrected at its smallest\\naffected owner, preserving the original cause, the attempted subject, the\\nobserved effect state and valid progress. Retry requires the applicable\\noutcome, authority and safe-recovery conditions; an effect of uncertain\\ncompletion (`completion_unknown`, or `not_effected` with its end not\\nestablished, under [ACTIVATION §3 Effects](ACTIVATION.md#effects)) cannot\\nbe silently treated\\nas no effect, and is reconciled as ACTIVATION §5 states before any retry\\nor dependent action (P5).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/SPEC_METHOD.md#SPEC_METHOD%2F4.%20Change%20management%2FComputed%20classification%20and%20treatment\",\"start_line\":978}],\"statement\":\"Unknown treatment blocks dependent reliance/promotion, not unrelated authorised work. Update affected C before new evidence supports dependent effects/promotion. Correct mistaken routing at the smallest affected owner while preserving original cause, attempted subject, observed effect state and valid progress. Retry requires applicable outcome/authority/safe-recovery conditions; completion_unknown or not_effected with unestablished end is never silently no-effect and requires reconciliation before retry/dependence. New roles/conversations/resumptions reuse valid C after exact-applicability checks. Before reliance, invalidate affected claims when request, candidate, owner/root relation, projection, design trace/acceptance, applied rule, configuration, material evidence, basis or declared revising observation changes. Preserve predecessor/successor identities, changed inputs, surviving facts and affected J dependencies; recompute the wider frontier where independence is unproved. TICKETS owns carrier and recorded J/O continuity.\",\"uncertainty\":\"Exact effect reconciliation and reusable-result mechanics are deferred to ACTIVATION; J/O continuity to TICKETS.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:a9e1b594e1ce9f037c53ecb0497ba293","key":1447,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:ab6da5130acf85f9459ce4914e1db565\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:a9e1b594e1ce9f037c53ecb0497ba293\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1039,\"path\":\"standards/SPEC_METHOD.md\",\"quote\":\"The gate closes only under the closure condition that\\n[TICKETS §7 Condition-based closure and reuse](TICKETS.md#condition-based-closure-and-reuse)\\nowns, applied here with the obligations declared for the change span as\\nits required coverage. A material counterexample\\nto a mandatory constraint, a required judgment or ruling without a closed\\nresult, or an obligation that no evidence addresses keeps the gate from\\nclosing, and each stays recorded by kind (P5, P6). Reuse of the gate's\\nevidence and results is\\n[ACTIVATION §7](ACTIVATION.md#7-closed-result-and-reuse); TICKETS §7\\nrecords the work state on its carrier. A\\nreview event, a passing aggregate, a completed artifact or a status change\\ncannot substitute for that conjunction (EVALUATION §5).\\n\\nWhen a code and test mismatch appears during ticketed work, implementation\\nbehaviour is evidence but not authority. The mismatch is reconciled through\\nthe admitted ticket, its intake triage, its lawful re-entry point and the\\ngoverning requirement, design, module, carrier or closure surface.\\n[TICKETS §7](TICKETS.md#test-case-authority) defines the ticket-local\\ntest-case authority rule (ASSURANCE §3 states the test authority rule).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/SPEC_METHOD.md#SPEC_METHOD%2F4.%20Change%20management%2FConsistency%20gate\",\"start_line\":1021}],\"statement\":\"No closure while affected active surfaces disagree or proof of upstream sufficiency/downstream consistency/current intended tests and qualification is missing, even if one artifact looks correct. Required coverage is the declared change-span obligations under TICKETS §7 conjunction. Material mandatory-constraint counterexamples, required judgments/rulings without closed results and unevidenced obligations each remain recorded by kind and block closure. Review events, passing aggregates, completed artifacts and status changes do not substitute. Reuse follows ACTIVATION §7 and carrier state TICKETS §7. Ticketed code/test mismatches treat implementation as evidence, resolving through admitted ticket, triage, lawful re-entry and governing requirement/design/module/carrier/closure authority.\",\"uncertainty\":\"The full owned closure and test-case authority rules are outside this excerpt.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:d58de473edde27193e0511d6f801d6ee","key":1448,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:34a40dd5a86c3b8c493c9326a6d886d9\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:d58de473edde27193e0511d6f801d6ee\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1066,\"path\":\"standards/SPEC_METHOD.md\",\"quote\":\"A lawful sprint states at least: the goal or work wave it serves; the\\nupstream authority surfaces it depends on; the scope it admits; the\\nproduct, requirement, design, runtime, data-contract or governance\\nboundaries it excludes; the change classes it expects to contain; the\\nlocal proof or compliance debt, if any, that may be deferred during the\\nsprint; the closure trigger and closure law; and the paydown or repricing\\npath for debt discovered at close.\\n\\nSprints exist because proof cost is not uniform. For some work, especially\\nprojection-surface and user-interface iteration, proving every micro-change\\nbefore the next change can cost more than making the bounded change visible\\nand correcting it at close. That optimisation is lawful only when the\\ndeferred cost remains local, visible, bounded and repayable. Deferred\\ncompliance inside a sprint is escrow, not acceptance: it satisfies no\\nmethod, release or product closure until it is paid down, explicitly\\naccepted under the governing method, or repriced into the appropriate\\nupstream surface.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/SPEC_METHOD.md#SPEC_METHOD%2F4.%20Change%20management%2FSprint%20execution%20boundary\",\"start_line\":1050}],\"statement\":\"A lawful sprint states at least served goal/wave, upstream authority, admitted scope, excluded product/requirement/design/runtime/data-contract/governance boundaries, expected classes, deferrable local proof/compliance debt if any, closure trigger/law and close-debt paydown/repricing path. Proof-cost deferral is lawful only while local, visible, bounded and repayable; escrow is not acceptance or closure until paid down, explicitly accepted under governing method or repriced upstream. Close may be recommended for timebox expiry, reached scope, review becoming cheaper than accumulated iteration, unsafe review uncertainty or a container invalidated by gaps. Close is forensic reconciliation: compare work/evidence to authority, classify gaps, accept compliant work, open debt paydown and escalate drift lawfully. A discovered goal/intent/product/requirement/design/runtime/data-contract/governance/other truth change is not authorised by the manifest; split, escalate, reprice or explicitly carry paydown. TICKETS owns mechanics and a profile may determine escrow suitability.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:59812ff2f79db912676f8f20da14cf7e","key":1449,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:5b910fcb1a1702f5d09d1acaec26b473\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:59812ff2f79db912676f8f20da14cf7e\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"Substantive work begins.\"],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1096,\"path\":\"standards/SPEC_METHOD.md\",\"quote\":\"The triage fields are required wherever substantive work begins; a ticket\\nper change is not (P2, P4b; [TICKETS §1](TICKETS.md#1-work-carriers) owns\\nthe carrier model and\\n[TICKETS §5](TICKETS.md#carrier-selection) the selection of the smallest\\nlawful carrier).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/SPEC_METHOD.md#SPEC_METHOD%2F4.%20Change%20management%2FCarriers\",\"start_line\":1092}],\"statement\":\"Required lifetime determines the carrier and triage fields remain required wherever substantive work starts. A ticket per change is not required; TICKETS owns the smallest-lawful-carrier rule.\",\"uncertainty\":\"The complete TICKETS §5 selection rule is not supplied.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:d22325c21e5fcd7614c098ed2e15663c","key":1450,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:8454481b045e2d4a4564c3e00b3dca1d\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:d22325c21e5fcd7614c098ed2e15663c\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"A feature is introduced or changed.\"],\"exceptions\":[\"Design/implementation/tests may co-evolve only under the applicable conditions stated here.\"],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1128,\"path\":\"standards/SPEC_METHOD.md\",\"quote\":\"When a feature is introduced or changed: update goals if the current\\nbounded work wave or overriding concerns have changed; update intent if the\\npurpose or scope has changed; update product if the current product\\nrealisation, terms, boundaries or end-state shape have changed; update\\nrequirements so the invariant truths are explicit as a decomposition of the\\nproduct definition, including any lifecycle obligations or named lifecycle\\nambiguity gaps, and classify each new or changed requirement by category;\\nestablish or update design so it owns the governing structural HOW, where\\nunder the design profile its decision-completeness rule applies (design,\\nimplementation and tests may co-evolve only when its co-evolution predicate\\nholds, otherwise the smallest causally closed affected design set is\\naccepted before retained implementation establishes an unresolved,\\ncontradictory or materially non-equivalent relation;\\n[DESIGN_MODULE](DESIGN_MODULE.md)), and\\nwhere that profile does not apply design, implementation and tests may\\nco-evolve when upstream truth leaves no unresolved material design\\ndecision, and when such a decision remains the affected design is accepted\\nbefore retained implementation establishes it, ADRs being one valid design\\nform; write scenarios for capability claims that require operational proof\\nand define other evidence surfaces for non-capability requirements where\\nappropriate; prefer declarative expression of the problem and acceptance\\nsurface before adding imperative mechanism;\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/SPEC_METHOD.md#SPEC_METHOD%2F4.%20Change%20management%2FProcedures\",\"start_line\":1107}],\"statement\":\"After triage establishes a supported lawful class and affected span, update goals if wave/overriding concerns change; intent if purpose/scope changes; product if realisation/terms/boundaries/end-state changes; requirements with invariant decomposition, lifecycle obligations/gaps and category for each new/changed requirement; and design with governing structural HOW. Under the design profile, co-evolution requires its predicate, otherwise accept the smallest causally closed affected design set before retained implementation establishes unresolved/contradictory/materially nonequivalent relations. Outside the profile, co-evolution requires no unresolved material design decision; otherwise accept affected design first. ADRs are one design form. Write operational-proof scenarios for applicable capabilities and appropriate other evidence for non-capabilities; prefer declarative problem/acceptance expression. Check every reconstruction boundary, record/govern major ambiguity by declared risk appetite, develop under selected design, reconcile design/code/tests before promotion/closure, and verify reality through events/projection/delta.\",\"uncertainty\":\"The design profile's co-evolution predicate is not supplied.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:4cb82927e6f72966d6dd484c86cbf0af","key":1451,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:8454481b045e2d4a4564c3e00b3dca1d\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:4cb82927e6f72966d6dd484c86cbf0af\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"Bootstrapping a project or repricing requirements; alternatively, handling a real-use gap as specified.\"],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1155,\"path\":\"standards/SPEC_METHOD.md\",\"quote\":\"When bootstrapping a project or repricing a requirement surface: resolve\\nthe applicable product definition, verify its exact installed basis, load\\nits declared bootstrap entrypoint (PRODUCT_DEFINITION §12), then load the\\ngoals surface or the bound equivalent current work-wave carrier; perform\\nthe goals-to-intent step and write or confirm the intent surface; perform\\nthe intent-to-product step and write or confirm the product definition as\\nthe current bridge; gather requirement source material from the relevant\\nconstitutional inputs; perform the product-to-requirements step and write\\nthe resulting live surface under the requirement surface; store\\nrequirements as individual files or grouped families, whichever best\\npreserves clarity and avoids monolithic sprawl; make the requirement\\nsurface the sole live requirement authority before proceeding to design and\\ncode; prefer declarative structure over procedural workaround while shaping\\nthe new surface; record any major ambiguity that remains at the current\\nboundary before downstream realisation proceeds; only after that surface\\nexists should downstream design and implementation be treated as\\nconstitutionally grounded.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/SPEC_METHOD.md#SPEC_METHOD%2F4.%20Change%20management%2FProcedures\",\"start_line\":1139},{\"end_line\":1170,\"path\":\"standards/SPEC_METHOD.md\",\"quote\":\"When a real use case reveals a gap: enter\\n[Universal intake triage](#universal-intake-triage) first and keep the\\nclassification unresolved until the evidence supports a lawful change class;\\nthen write the scenario as the first\\nsubstantive project artifact for the gap so the pressure becomes concrete\\nand testable; run gap analysis to locate its cause under\\n[Universal intake triage](#universal-intake-triage), which keeps open what\\nthe evidence cannot yet separate; then re-enter at the layer the selected\\n[change class](#change-classes) names and flow forward from it, writing new\\ngoals or intent only where the work wave, direction or scope changes.\\nThe intake source does not change this rule: a bug report, feature request,\\nfailed test case, release blocker or operator observation still enters\\nthrough intake triage first, then follows the lawful change class selected\\nthere.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/SPEC_METHOD.md#SPEC_METHOD%2F4.%20Change%20management%2FProcedures\",\"start_line\":1157}],\"statement\":\"Bootstrap/repricing resolves product, verifies exact installed basis, loads declared bootstrap then goals/equivalent work-wave carrier, derives/confirms intent then product, gathers constitutional inputs and derives the live requirements surface. Individual files or grouped families are chosen for clarity without monolithic sprawl. Requirements become sole live requirement authority before design/code; declarative structure is preferred and remaining major ambiguity recorded before downstream realisation. Only then is downstream work treated as grounded. For a real-use gap, triage first leaves classification unresolved until evidence supports a class; scenario is the first substantive project artifact for the gap, followed by cause analysis preserving unresolved alternatives, selected re-entry and forward flow. New goals/intent require changed wave/direction/scope. Bug, feature, failed test, release blocker and operator origins do not bypass this sequence.\",\"uncertainty\":\"These procedures are represented as source data and have not been performed.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:798e38fd970990e85398f6ceec5b16a4","key":1452,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:286649052d4f3d74e1c0094c628bac34\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:21feeb8c6dd7e2109f1517741510bd3b\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:7a473adb85314975c9d0699a47c00191\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:798e38fd970990e85398f6ceec5b16a4\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1206,\"path\":\"standards/SPEC_METHOD.md\",\"quote\":\"Major ambiguity is always surfaced and governed; it may\\nnot remain hidden inside informal operator judgment, ambient precedent or\\nsilent model choice. At each major boundary the process detects and\\nrecords the major ambiguity that remains or is newly introduced; identifies\\nthe affected invariant, asset or decision boundary; records the decision\\ntaken if work proceeds; and records whether the ambiguity was resolved,\\ncarried forward, escalated or blocked. Those outcomes are `resolved`,\\n`carried`, `escalated` and `blocked` of\\n[ACTIVATION §3 Ambiguity outcome](ACTIVATION.md#ambiguity-outcome), which\\ngives each its core value for the predicate \\\"the declared ambiguity is\\nresolved on the exact basis\\\". Only `resolved` is `satisfied`, so a later\\nboundary rests no dependent claim on an ambiguity that is carried,\\nescalated or blocked as if it were resolved. Ambiguity detection is\\nmandatory; blocking is policy (P6, P5).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/SPEC_METHOD.md#SPEC_METHOD%2F5.%20Ambiguity%20governance%20and%20lifecycle\",\"start_line\":1193}],\"statement\":\"At every major boundary detect/record remaining or new major ambiguity, affected invariant/asset/decision boundary, decision if work proceeds, and resolved/carried/escalated/blocked outcome. No hidden major ambiguity in informal judgment, precedent or silent model choice. For the exact-basis resolution predicate only resolved maps to satisfied; dependent claims cannot treat carried/escalated/blocked as resolved. Detection is mandatory; blocking follows declared risk policy subject to hard stops. Profile runtime shorthands remain in their own contexts absent explicit import/translation. A missing lifecycle answer is a recorded gap, never silence.\",\"uncertainty\":\"Core mappings of carried, escalated and blocked and the hard-stop classes are referenced but not supplied.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:3ba3a22d134ffcadbac521ae4f33e8b7","key":1453,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:691f85265c6da81d5a46b1d99e177c71\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:3ba3a22d134ffcadbac521ae4f33e8b7\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1279,\"path\":\"standards/SPEC_METHOD.md\",\"quote\":\"Layer and release separation holds\\n([AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS §7](AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS.md#ac-020-layer-and-release-separation)):\\na calculus, its interpretation of a subject and its carrier encoding keep\\nindependent content identities, judgments, supersession relations and\\nproof obligations, and none is automatically an independently released\\nproduct. One constitutional surface and its version boundary for a project\\nare\\n[PRODUCT_DEFINITION §11](PRODUCT_DEFINITION.md#11-one-constitutional-surface-and-version-boundary).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/SPEC_METHOD.md#SPEC_METHOD%2F6.%20Lineage%20and%20release\",\"start_line\":1272}],\"statement\":\"Recursive/compositional building does not merge lineage identities: product definition is source-project present truth, not released artifact or builder. Only immutable v<version>-rc.<n> is exact operative release identity; the mutable line selector is neither exact dependency, evidence nor constitutional basis and cannot silently alter consumer selection. Cut identity/accepted feature boundary belongs to release metadata/evaluation rather than live specification. Shared realisation surfaces should express current truth by role/boundary/status rather than version line. Release mechanics and successor conservation remain RELEASE-owned. Calculus, subject interpretation and carrier encoding retain independent content identities, judgments, supersession and proof obligations; none automatically becomes an independently released product.\",\"uncertainty\":\"Full lineage definitions, release process, successor conservation and project version-boundary rules are external.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:71addd7f2a5168bd553d20759392075b","key":1454,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:7a15f604d594ccb443f28aaff58f7767\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:71addd7f2a5168bd553d20759392075b\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1304,\"path\":\"standards/SPEC_METHOD.md\",\"quote\":\"The chain states authority causality. It prescribes no intake workflow and\\nno artifact set (P2). An executable tool, runtime, carrier schema or\\nassurance implementation cannot enter the method merely because it\\naccompanies a method lesson; it requires its own Product authorisation\\n(P6). Other standards consume admitted law by reference (P3, P6), and a\\nconsumer selects a complete released version rather than mixing members from different cuts (P3;\\nthe release version boundary above,\\n[PRODUCT_DEFINITION §4](PRODUCT_DEFINITION.md#4-shared-installed-release-basis-and-toolchain-manager)).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/SPEC_METHOD.md#SPEC_METHOD%2F6.%20Lineage%20and%20release%2FShared%20method%20adoption%20and%20propagation%20%28STDO-UP-012%29\",\"start_line\":1297}],\"statement\":\"The adoption chain expresses authority causality, prescribing neither intake workflow nor artifact set. Accompanying tools, runtimes, schemas or assurance implementations require their own Product authorisation; a method lesson does not admit them. Other standards consume admitted law by reference. Consumers explicitly select one complete released version and cannot mix members from different cuts.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:0e9fc54392c5ebb72fe75eb47995b6d5","key":1455,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:ae116d98f8db6a1aeaa78cdaaeb00dfc\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:0e9fc54392c5ebb72fe75eb47995b6d5\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"A core interface changes.\"],\"exceptions\":[\"Bounded product-slice proof remains subject to the path-relative promotion rule.\"],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1328,\"path\":\"standards/SPEC_METHOD.md\",\"quote\":\"change the authoritative core contract first; ban bridge code for that\\ncontract family as an authoritative surface; audit every producer and every\\nconsumer of the impacted interface; migrate each producer and consumer to\\nthe new contract; chase every downstream effect until no superseded closure\\nlaw remains; run complete migration-closure proof only after the migration\\nwave is complete, bounded product-slice proof remaining governed by the\\npath-relative promotion rule below.\\n\\nThe rule exists because partial interface migration creates recurring\\ndrift: one producer writes the new contract while another still writes the\\nold; runtime reads one carrier while reporting or topology reads another;\\ncompatibility aliases silently remain authoritative; projections become a\\nsecond truth surface; tests go green while the architecture remains split.\\nDeclaring such a state complete is forbidden.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/SPEC_METHOD.md#SPEC_METHOD%2F7.%20Migration%2FCore%20interface%20migration\",\"start_line\":1315}],\"statement\":\"Change the authoritative contract first, prohibit authoritative bridge code for its family, audit and migrate every producer/consumer, and chase every downstream effect until no superseded closure law remains. Complete migration-closure proof comes after the completed migration wave. Split producer contracts, inconsistent runtime/reporting/topology carriers, authoritative aliases or second-truth projections cannot be declared complete despite green tests.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:8e3dfb050e69cb8cde954de777a4dd18","key":1456,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:0ac47d0a931c315a32966d607562e1c0\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:8e3dfb050e69cb8cde954de777a4dd18\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"Selecting a strategy for core-interface or major implementation replacement.\"],\"exceptions\":[\"The presumption does not require an unsafe or constitutionally inadmissible predecessor path, nor retention of internal/public mechanisms explicitly superseded by product authority.\"],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1361,\"path\":\"standards/SPEC_METHOD.md\",\"quote\":\"Where bounded evolution and fundamental re-adoption are both lawful and\\nfeasible, and a working predecessor can reach the admitted product outcome\\nwithout retaining competing or ambiguous authority, evolution on the\\nsupported product path is the rebuttable selection presumption. This does\\nnot require continuing an unsafe or constitutionally inadmissible\\npredecessor path; it conserves accepted predecessor semantics and product\\nfeedback, and it does not require preserving an internal implementation or\\npublic mechanism that product authority explicitly supersedes. When bounded\\nevolution includes a core-interface migration, it uses the inside-out\\nhard-break strategy; bounded evolution is a strategy-selection presumption,\\nnot a third strategy.\\n\\nFundamental re-adoption requires explicit selection by the human authority\\nowning the affected product boundary. The selection compares re-adoption\\nwith bounded evolution across product value, feedback latency, authority\\nrisk, reversibility, total cost and retained predecessor semantics, and\\nstates a bounded abort or re-entry condition. Implementation scale or\\narchitectural preference alone does not select re-adoption (P6, P2).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/SPEC_METHOD.md#SPEC_METHOD%2F7.%20Migration%2FConstitutional%20migration%20options\",\"start_line\":1344}],\"statement\":\"Prefer bounded evolution rebuttably only when both strategies are lawful/feasible and a working predecessor reaches the admitted outcome without competing/ambiguous authority. Core-interface evolution uses inside-out hard-break. Fundamental re-adoption requires explicit affected-product human-owner selection comparing product value, feedback latency, authority risk, reversibility, total cost and retained predecessor semantics, with bounded abort/re-entry condition. Scale or architectural preference alone cannot select it.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:98806585514a33e97ca8cc16fec61648","key":1457,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:ae116d98f8db6a1aeaa78cdaaeb00dfc\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:609c724f3e72ded60af13a3da3caf985\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:7e174d80769b16059837b8b7bff5ce16\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:98806585514a33e97ca8cc16fec61648\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[\"Residual superseded material outside the promoted path may be deferred only under all stated conditions.\"],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1399,\"path\":\"standards/SPEC_METHOD.md\",\"quote\":\"Product-slice promotion and complete migration closure are distinct claims.\\nAn intermediate product outcome may be promoted while its enclosing\\nmigration remains open only when the outcome's acceptance path has singular\\nauthority and the residual implementation satisfies the deferment rule\\nabove. That promotion neither closes the migration nor waives its final\\nretirement criteria. The slice's identity and acceptance criteria derive\\nfrom the product plus every causally applicable live requirement, accepted\\ndesign relation and retained predecessor claim; ticket or review wording\\ncannot narrow that authority away. Active migration status does not renew\\nan accepted slice's exhausted growth authority: work that only discharges\\nalready admitted removal, demotion and migration-closure proof obligations\\nmay continue within that existing bound without claiming further product\\nprogress; further material producer or consumer growth requires another\\nstill-live basis admitted under §3, and ticket activity alone is not that\\nbasis.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/SPEC_METHOD.md#SPEC_METHOD%2F7.%20Migration%2FConstitutional%20migration%20options\",\"start_line\":1385}],\"statement\":\"Both strategies prohibit proxy partial interfaces standing for the new contract in any acceptance path and silently authoritative bridges/fallbacks. Promotion requires singular authority over the full causal closure, not one successful trace; old/new admissibility for the same request/fact/identity/state/projection is competing authority and blocks it. Outside-path residuals may be deferred only when explicitly non-authoritative for the outcome or governing explicitly specified disjoint product/compatibility scope with deterministic routing, unable to falsify current/retained claims, and carrying bounded migration/qualification/release disposition. Tests detect leaks/prove, not plan migration. An intermediate slice can promote only with singular path authority and compliant residuals, leaving migration visibly open and retirement criteria intact. Slice identity/criteria include product plus every causally applicable live requirement, accepted design and retained predecessor claim; ticket/review wording cannot narrow them. Active migration does not renew accepted-slice growth; already-admitted removal/demotion/closure proof may continue within its bound without new progress claims, while producer/consumer growth requires another live admitted basis.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:55e52165c7371b0123ff8ac1a79873de","key":1458,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:ae116d98f8db6a1aeaa78cdaaeb00dfc\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:55e52165c7371b0123ff8ac1a79873de\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"Every core-interface migration.\"],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1422,\"path\":\"standards/SPEC_METHOD.md\",\"quote\":\"Every core interface migration explicitly declares: the exact affected\\nmigration scope; every explicitly excluded or disjoint product or\\ncompatibility scope and its deterministic routing relation; the new\\nauthoritative contract; the superseded contract or surface; the\\nauthoritative closure law for the new contract; the full set of producers\\nof the old and new contract; the full set of consumers of the old and new\\ncontract; and every projection, report, status surface and proof surface\\nthat derives from it. Every old path is then classified as `remove`,\\n`replace`, `re-authorize` or `temporary scaffolding`. Temporary scaffolding\\nis lawful only if it is explicitly non-authoritative and scheduled for\\nremoval before closure (P6, P4b).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/SPEC_METHOD.md#SPEC_METHOD%2F7.%20Migration%2FRequired%20migration%20protocol\",\"start_line\":1412}],\"statement\":\"Declare exact affected scope; every excluded/disjoint product or compatibility scope with deterministic routing; new authoritative and superseded contracts/surfaces; new closure law; full old/new producer and consumer sets; and every derived projection/report/status/proof surface. Classify every old path remove, replace, re-authorize or temporary scaffolding. Temporary scaffolding is lawful only when explicitly non-authoritative and scheduled for removal before closure.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:09e166869dc139b958255ff2f1784a78","key":1459,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:ae116d98f8db6a1aeaa78cdaaeb00dfc\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:09e166869dc139b958255ff2f1784a78\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"A core-interface migration.\"],\"exceptions\":[\"An explicit live-product compatibility feature may retain a deliberately specified, bounded path clearly identified as compatibility rather than current native truth.\"],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1435,\"path\":\"standards/SPEC_METHOD.md\",\"quote\":\"For a core interface migration: no compatibility alias remains\\nauthoritative; no fallback identity law remains as silent runtime\\nbehaviour; no bridge path participates in acceptance as if it were the new\\ncontract; no old reader or writer remains authoritative for the promoted\\noutcome once the new contract governs that outcome; no proxy or partial\\nimplementation of the new interface stands between old and new truth as if\\nit were completion. The only lawful exception is an explicit compatibility\\nfeature retained as part of the live product, whose compatibility path is\\nintentionally specified, explicitly bounded, and clearly identified as\\ncompatibility rather than current native truth (P3, P6).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/SPEC_METHOD.md#SPEC_METHOD%2F7.%20Migration%2FBridge%20prohibition\",\"start_line\":1426}],\"statement\":\"No authoritative compatibility alias, silent fallback identity law, bridge acceptance as new contract, old authoritative reader/writer for a newly governed promoted outcome, or proxy/partial interface pretending completion is lawful, subject only to the explicit compatibility-feature exception.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:e6881f6dc4b552fe84b2578e640e5373","key":1460,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:9cabea2f5cca79b57c9d7036eae01d55\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:ae116d98f8db6a1aeaa78cdaaeb00dfc\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:e6881f6dc4b552fe84b2578e640e5373\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1446,\"path\":\"standards/SPEC_METHOD.md\",\"quote\":\"If runtime, reporting, topology and proof\\ncan disagree about closure because they consume different carriers or\\ndifferent closure laws, the migration is incomplete; if a projection can\\nindependently close while the authoritative carrier is still open, the\\nmigration is incomplete; if the authoritative carrier can close while a\\nprojection still depends on an older law, the migration is incomplete.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/SPEC_METHOD.md#SPEC_METHOD%2F7.%20Migration%2FProjection%20discipline\",\"start_line\":1441}],\"statement\":\"Migration remains incomplete if runtime/reporting/topology/proof can disagree because of different carriers or closure laws, if a projection independently closes while its authoritative carrier is open, or if the carrier closes while a projection still depends on older law. Projections must not become second closure authority.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:13d2f5d834d4bcc045353a1ee34b4db9","key":1461,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:ae116d98f8db6a1aeaa78cdaaeb00dfc\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:0ac47d0a931c315a32966d607562e1c0\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:13d2f5d834d4bcc045353a1ee34b4db9\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"Inside-out hard-break migration.\"],\"exceptions\":[\"Downstream exploration may exist as isolated non-authoritative work.\"],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1463,\"path\":\"standards/SPEC_METHOD.md\",\"quote\":\"Inside-out hard-break migrations proceed from the new authoritative source\\ncarrier outward (P4b, P6). The full\\nbest-guess interface family is discovered before proof is used as closure\\nevidence, including producers, consumers, projections, prompts, reports,\\nwrappers, replay paths, ingest paths, bootstrap paths and proof surfaces.\\nAuthoritative producer and source-carrier work comes before downstream\\nconsumer, projection, prompt, dossier, report or review-surface hardening.\\nDownstream exploration may exist only as isolated non-authoritative work\\nand does not land in public runtime, projection, prompt, report or proof\\nentry points until the source carrier is published and admitted. A\\ndownstream projection ticket does not close while the source-carrier\\nticket it depends on is still open. Dependency direction reflects this\\norder explicitly so the ticket set exposes the migration wave from source\\ntruth to downstream read models.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/SPEC_METHOD.md#SPEC_METHOD%2F7.%20Migration%2FInside-out%20first%20sequencing\",\"start_line\":1450}],\"statement\":\"Discover the full best-guess family before closure use of proof, including producers/consumers/projections/prompts/reports/wrappers/replay/ingest/bootstrap/proof surfaces. Authoritative producers and source carrier precede downstream consumer/projection/prompt/dossier/report/review hardening. Isolated exploration cannot land in public runtime/projection/prompt/report/proof entrypoints until source publication and admission. A projection ticket cannot close before its depended-on source-carrier ticket; explicit dependency direction exposes source-to-read-model order.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:4f137c20b4486fdfb91837365d6ab918","key":1462,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:ae116d98f8db6a1aeaa78cdaaeb00dfc\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:4f137c20b4486fdfb91837365d6ab918\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"Each break in an inside-out interface-family migration.\"],\"exceptions\":[\"Explicitly specified, deterministically routed, non-overlapping product/compatibility scopes may coexist while migration stays open.\",\"Newly discovered affected interfaces leave the same wave only through explicit upward repricing.\"],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1483,\"path\":\"standards/SPEC_METHOD.md\",\"quote\":\"For each break: publish or admit the new deepest authoritative source\\ncarrier; deliberately sever one old authoritative seam; keep that seam\\nbroken; repair outward from source truth to consumers, then projections,\\nthen prompts and reports, then proof surfaces; run negative proof that the\\nsevered seam is rejected rather than merely unused. During the sequence,\\ntests may discover missed interfaces but do not replace the required\\ninterface inventory; newly discovered affected interfaces remain part of\\nthe same migration wave unless the work is explicitly repriced upward;\\nre-enabling the old seam through wrappers, fallbacks, projections or prompt\\npaths is a migration defect.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/SPEC_METHOD.md#SPEC_METHOD%2F7.%20Migration%2FHard-break%20discipline\",\"start_line\":1474}],\"statement\":\"The wave is an ordered set of hard breaks, not permission for competing dual truth over the same request/fact/identity/state/projection. For each break publish or admit the deepest new carrier, sever and keep broken an old authoritative seam, repair outward through consumers, projections, prompts/reports and proof surfaces, then negatively prove rejection rather than mere nonuse. Tests may find interfaces but cannot replace the inventory. Re-enabling the seam via wrappers, fallback, projection or prompts is a defect.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:f1eb19fb3644996efd2042b19357a74b","key":1463,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:ae116d98f8db6a1aeaa78cdaaeb00dfc\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:f1eb19fb3644996efd2042b19357a74b\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[\"Bounded slice proof may establish only the exact intermediate outcome allowed by path-relative promotion.\"],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1495,\"path\":\"standards/SPEC_METHOD.md\",\"quote\":\"Complete migration-closure proof is not valid while producers and\\nconsumers are split across old and new contracts. Bounded product-slice\\nproof may establish only the exact intermediate outcome permitted by the\\npath-relative promotion rule; it cannot establish migration closure (P6). Tests that pass only\\nbecause bridge-state semantics remain alive do not count as closure proof;\\ngreen local tests do not overrule a split architecture; migration-closure\\nproof belongs after migration, not during a partially migrated state;\\nper-break proof shows the severed old seam is rejected or fails closed\\nbefore downstream hardening can count as progress.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/SPEC_METHOD.md#SPEC_METHOD%2F7.%20Migration%2FProof-last%20rule\",\"start_line\":1487}],\"statement\":\"Complete migration proof is invalid while producers/consumers remain split across contracts; bridge-dependent passing tests and green local tests cannot establish closure. Slice proof is not migration proof. Per-break rejection/fail-closed evidence must precede counting downstream hardening as progress.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:a65538cbb247b950f076d02e84ee393b","key":1464,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:ae116d98f8db6a1aeaa78cdaaeb00dfc\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:a65538cbb247b950f076d02e84ee393b\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"Claiming completion across the declared affected scope.\"],\"exceptions\":[\"A superseded mechanism may remain for a distinct supported responsibility satisfying the retention burden.\"],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1522,\"path\":\"standards/SPEC_METHOD.md\",\"quote\":\"A core interface migration is complete across its declared affected scope\\nonly when every authoritative producer writes the new contract; every\\nauthoritative consumer reads the new contract; superseded authoritative\\npaths are retired unless justified for a distinct supported responsibility\\nunder the retention relation below; projections are downstream of the same\\nauthoritative truth rather than competing truth surfaces; runtime,\\nreporting, topology and proof share one closure law; and no temporary\\nscaffolding remains in the acceptance path. Until those conditions hold the\\nwork remains an active migration wave, not a completed refactor (P3, P6).\\n\\nRetention bears the burden. Each retained superseded mechanism identifies a\\ncurrent supported obligation, owner, purpose, execution scope and material\\ncost. Temporary compatibility or comparison work has an expiry or removal\\ntrigger; existing tests, an oracle label or nominal demotion do not justify\\nduplicate production responsibility. A required cold reconstruction route\\nor independent test oracle may serve an enduring distinct obligation\\nwithout an invented expiry. Where an obligation survives replacement, its\\nsurviving owner is identified; where it has no governing basis, no\\nreplacement guard is required. Retirement inside a closed affected cone\\ndoes not await unrelated whole-product closure (P2).\\n\\nAn accepted intermediate product slice within the wave names the slice it\\ncloses and keeps the enclosing migration visibly open; it does not project\\nslice acceptance as migration, qualification or release closure.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/SPEC_METHOD.md#SPEC_METHOD%2F7.%20Migration%2FClosure%20criterion\",\"start_line\":1499}],\"statement\":\"Completion requires every authoritative producer/consumer on the new contract, superseded paths retired or justified for distinct supported responsibility, projections downstream of the same truth, one runtime/reporting/topology/proof closure law, and no acceptance-path temporary scaffolding. Otherwise the wave stays active. Every retained mechanism identifies current obligation, owner, purpose, execution scope and material cost. Temporary compatibility/comparison needs expiry/removal trigger; tests, oracle labels or nominal demotion do not justify duplicate production responsibility. Enduring required cold reconstruction or independent oracle needs no invented expiry. Identify surviving obligation owners; with no governing basis no replacement guard is required. Retirement within a closed affected cone need not await unrelated whole-product closure. Accepted slices name their exact closure and keep enclosing migration visibly open, never projecting migration/qualification/release closure.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:5fa98b51c03c1b03746ade7ba3320eec","key":1465,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:4db287e299d86eb8953d36f89d7b0b07\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:5fa98b51c03c1b03746ade7ba3320eec\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[\"Inherited surfaces may be zeroed and rebuilt on the migration line.\",\"Prior implementation may be moved sideways as reference material.\"],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1570,\"path\":\"standards/SPEC_METHOD.md\",\"quote\":\"Performing a fundamental migration: declare the migration line and treat\\nthe prior line as source material; establish fresh constitutional surfaces\\nfor method, goals, intent, product, requirements and design; move the\\nprior implementation sideways if needed so it cannot continue as ambient\\nlive authority; classify inherited constitutional material as adopted,\\nsuperseded, deferred or orphaned; classify inherited implementation\\nmaterial as `carry_across`, `redundant` or `rewrite`; copy forward only\\nwhat is intentionally retained; re-derive downstream design and code from\\nthe new constitutional surfaces, not from ambient precedent. In a\\nfundamental migration `carry_across` does not mean automatic copy-forward\\nbut explicit re-adoption under the new line; direct runtime, projection,\\nprompt, proof or review dependence on the sideways implementation line is\\nbridge debt; proxy interfaces that partially imitate the target line while\\nstill depending on the sideways line are not lawful closure. This is a\\nlawful form of supersession, not a violation of live surface immutability\\n(§2), because the new line creates a new constitutional surface rather than\\nsilently mutating the old one.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/SPEC_METHOD.md#SPEC_METHOD%2F7.%20Migration%2FFundamental%20migration\",\"start_line\":1554}],\"statement\":\"Nothing carries forward by default. Explicitly re-adopt every retained statement/requirement/design/guide rule, intentionally locating it in the correct layer as recommended; old code/design are reference only unless re-derived/re-adopted. Absence means not-yet-adopted, without authority. Before reuse classify every inherited module/interface/carrier/projection/proof surface: carry_across is materially unchanged and intentionally adopted, redundant no longer needed, rewrite needed but rebuilt; unclassified implementation is a defect. Declare new line, establish fresh method/goals/intent/product/requirements/design, remove ambient old-line authority, classify constitutional material adopted/superseded/deferred/orphaned, copy only intentionally retained material, and re-derive from new truth. Direct runtime/projection/prompt/proof/review dependency on sideways implementation is bridge debt; partial proxies depending on it are not closure. The new surface is lawful supersession, not silent in-place mutation.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:2aa1221502366fbdd3fcbc7d98b8ccb7","key":1466,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:4db287e299d86eb8953d36f89d7b0b07\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:7d0a9c90f5f4ae3de1e1726cf6d1423f\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:2aa1221502366fbdd3fcbc7d98b8ccb7\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"Classifying inherited constitutional material and inherited requirements.\"],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1594,\"path\":\"standards/SPEC_METHOD.md\",\"quote\":\"The four classes of inherited constitutional material record the\\nadoption decision the new line takes on each inherited statement. For an\\ninherited requirement, the legacy classifications of\\n[§2 Requirement categories and classification](#requirement-categories-and-classification)\\nrecord a different thing: the standing of a requirement that is in the\\nlive surface. The two relate as follows, and are not one classification:\\n- an adopted requirement enters the live surface as Active, or as Deferred\\n  when it is adopted as an explicitly not-yet-operative obligation;\\n- a requirement whose adoption is deferred is not in the live surface: it\\n  has no legacy classification and no authority until it is adopted,\\n  because absence from the new surface means \\\"not yet adopted\\\";\\n- a superseded or orphaned inherited requirement takes Superseded or\\n  Orphaned, with that table's meanings.\\n\\nFor other inherited\\nconstitutional material the classes keep their names and the steps\\nabove. They are declared states of the new line's surfaces and, as §2\\nstates, none of them is or supplies the\\n[RELEASE §9](RELEASE.md#9-successor-baseline-conservation-stdo-up-015)\\ndisposition of a predecessor claim (P3, P6). Purpose and material\\nrelation: an inherited requirement in a migration falls under both this\\nstep and the legacy classification rule, and stating how the two records\\nrelate leaves no two records of one standing to reconcile (P3).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/SPEC_METHOD.md#SPEC_METHOD%2F7.%20Migration%2FFundamental%20migration\",\"start_line\":1572}],\"statement\":\"Adoption decision and live-requirement standing are distinct classifications. Adopted requirements enter Active, or Deferred when explicitly adopted as not-yet-operative. Deferred adoption leaves a requirement outside the live surface, with no legacy classification or authority until adoption. Superseded/orphaned inherited requirements take Superseded/Orphaned with the legacy table's meanings. Other inherited material retains its adoption-class names. None supplies a RELEASE §9 predecessor-claim disposition.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:4e6bd8863e893e76495bc8ea6eb2f349","key":1467,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:737fbdeb1271e076ee2a5b4f8cf1e047\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:4e6bd8863e893e76495bc8ea6eb2f349\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[\"Explicitly specified, deterministically routed, non-overlapping product/compatibility scopes may coexist while enclosing migration remains visibly open.\",\"At landing, a compatibility feature may remain only if named current behaviour, specification-justified, bounded and tested intentionally.\"],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1619,\"path\":\"standards/SPEC_METHOD.md\",\"quote\":\"When the wave lands across its declared affected scope: only the new\\ncurrent operative surface remains live for that scope; prior operative\\npaths for that scope are erased from the live product; the path taken to\\nget there survives only in version control, event history and superseded\\nrecords; mixed old and new operative models are not a stable end state. The\\nonly lawful exception is an explicit compatibility feature, which is named\\nas current product behaviour, justified in the specification, bounded in\\nscope and tested as an intentional feature. Otherwise the correct action is\\ndeletion, not passive preservation.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/SPEC_METHOD.md#SPEC_METHOD%2F7.%20Migration%2FTransformation%20wave\",\"start_line\":1611}],\"statement\":\"During the wave, mixed state exists only below the break boundary as explicitly non-authoritative plumbing; adapters/scaffolds must be named, bounded and outside acceptance paths, never competing authority over the same request/fact/identity/state/projection. On landing, only new current operative truth remains in the affected scope; erase prior operative paths and retain the route only in version control/events/superseded records. Mixed operative models are not a stable endpoint; absent the explicit compatibility exception, delete rather than passively preserve.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:3bd1f7fa7ba8463c5f76845a49eac0de","key":1468,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:730ea09d59cbd3d5c5d2f2393282f546\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:3bd1f7fa7ba8463c5f76845a49eac0de\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1681,\"path\":\"standards/SPEC_METHOD.md\",\"quote\":\"construction relation that the step serves, from the bound current state\\nto the destination through a selected strategy, feedback and the distinct\\nclaims of preservation, progress and completion, is\\n[ACTIVATION §1 Construction relation](ACTIVATION.md#construction-relation);\\nthis member applies it to delivery and correction (§4) and states no\\nsecond relation (P6). The\\nstep states its results in the core of\\n[FOUNDATIONS §4 Results](FOUNDATIONS.md#results) through the refinements\\nof [ACTIVATION §3](ACTIVATION.md#3-step-results-and-disposition): that a\\ncandidate is available, how each assessment of it came out, and the\\ndecision owner's disposition (`accept`, `local_repair`, `re_enter` or\\n`reject`) are separate results, so a candidate that is available or\\nassessed is not thereby accepted (P6). The selected computational relations\\nare drawn from the computational calculus of the tenant doing the work;\\nthe actors, tools and processes that carry out the step belong to that\\ntenant's execution environment, and the step's time, spend and other\\nresource limits are those of its execution binding (§11). The\\ndeclared work boundary of a probabilistic unit is FOUNDATIONS §2 (work\\nboundary) and §3 (P0); the complete enclosing-relation admission of a\\nmaterial transition and its standing structural qualification are\\nACTIVATION §4; proportionality is ACTIVATION §6. This member binds the\\ngeneric terms to its own: the selected outcome of a step is the product\\noutcome, prerequisite or experiment of §3; the owning relations are the\\nchain's layers; the re-entry conditions are the change classes of §4.\\n\\nDelivery priority applies the proportionality relation to the current\\nproduct outcome, likelihood, impact, reversibility, dependency and the cost\\nof delayed product feedback. Probability informs lawful priority; it does\\nnot waive authority, integrity, safety, retained release claims or another\\nhard stop. A probability stated for priority is a quantified claim under\\n[FOUNDATIONS §4 Quantified assurance](FOUNDATIONS.md#quantified-assurance);\\nunsupported numeric confidence stays unresolved (P6). The default priority is work that exposes or advances the\\nsmallest supported product path and its highest-value likely failures.\\nDefensive or prerequisite work that displaces that path identifies the\\naffected claim, evidence basis, bounded effort, return condition and\\nexpected product consequence. This is a priority relation, not a fixed\\nglobal execution sequence or a scheduling runtime (P2, P0).\\n\\nWhich frames carry construction, assessment and disposition, and which\\nconsumer receives a step's return, is set by the configuration that\\n[ACTIVATION §1 Configuration](ACTIVATION.md#configuration) derives from the\\ntask's operations, dependencies, actor capabilities and required\\nassurance; this member adds no role inventory, coordinator or sequence. A\\nstep's return goes to the consumer the configuration declares. Where the\\nconfiguration has a coordinator, the coordinator decides as\\n[ACTIVATION §1 Configuration](ACTIVATION.md#configuration), Coordination\\nacross tasks, states, within its decision grant, and selects the next\\nauthorised action. The executive configuration, with its Executive,\\nWorker and Reviewer frames, is one such configuration; the executive\\nbaseline profile owns it, and it governs where it is selected\\n([EXECUTIVE_BASELINE](EXECUTIVE_BASELINE.md)) (P0, P6).\\n\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/SPEC_METHOD.md#SPEC_METHOD%2F8.%20Bounded%20execution%20in%20this%20method\",\"start_line\":1631}],\"statement\":\"Availability or assessment is not acceptance. Computational relations come from the executing tenant's calculus; actors/tools/processes and resource limits come from its environment/binding. Bind generic outcome to §3 outcome/prerequisite/experiment, owning relations to chain layers and re-entry to §4 classes. Preservation/progress/completion remain distinct. Configuration derived from operations/dependencies/capabilities/assurance selects construction/assessment/disposition frames and return consumer; this member adds no role inventory, coordinator or sequence. If configured, a coordinator decides only within its grant and selects next authorised action. Executive/Worker/Reviewer is one profile-owned configuration governing only when selected.\",\"uncertainty\":\"ACTIVATION's admission, work-boundary, qualification, result and configuration definitions are not fully supplied.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:298322fa3715fb0d6e300e16b35a6cd5","key":1469,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:730ea09d59cbd3d5c5d2f2393282f546\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:298322fa3715fb0d6e300e16b35a6cd5\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1667,\"path\":\"standards/SPEC_METHOD.md\",\"quote\":\"Delivery priority applies the proportionality relation to the current\\nproduct outcome, likelihood, impact, reversibility, dependency and the cost\\nof delayed product feedback. Probability informs lawful priority; it does\\nnot waive authority, integrity, safety, retained release claims or another\\nhard stop. A probability stated for priority is a quantified claim under\\n[FOUNDATIONS §4 Quantified assurance](FOUNDATIONS.md#quantified-assurance);\\nunsupported numeric confidence stays unresolved (P6). The default priority is work that exposes or advances the\\nsmallest supported product path and its highest-value likely failures.\\nDefensive or prerequisite work that displaces that path identifies the\\naffected claim, evidence basis, bounded effort, return condition and\\nexpected product consequence. This is a priority relation, not a fixed\\nglobal execution sequence or a scheduling runtime (P2, P0).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/SPEC_METHOD.md#SPEC_METHOD%2F8.%20Bounded%20execution%20in%20this%20method\",\"start_line\":1656},{\"end_line\":1688,\"path\":\"standards/SPEC_METHOD.md\",\"quote\":\"Delivery is sequenced around the smallest real path from a supported entry\\nto a material outcome, established early and widened by increments chosen\\nfor consequential uncertainty, interface reach and failure impact; a\\npassing path establishes only the relations it exercised. This is a\\nsequencing heuristic for any realisation, not law; the baseline's\\nsteel-thread delivery governs its profile unchanged (P2).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/SPEC_METHOD.md#SPEC_METHOD%2F8.%20Bounded%20execution%20in%20this%20method\",\"start_line\":1683}],\"statement\":\"Priority considers current outcome, likelihood, impact, reversibility, dependencies and delayed-feedback cost. Probability cannot waive authority/integrity/safety/retained claims/hard stops; unsupported numeric confidence stays unresolved. Default priority exposes/advances the smallest supported product path and highest-value likely failures. Displacing defensive/prerequisite work identifies affected claim, evidence, bounded effort, return condition and expected product consequence. This is no fixed global sequence or scheduling runtime. Early small-path delivery and widening by consequential uncertainty/interface reach/failure impact is a heuristic, not law; passing proves only exercised relations and the selected baseline's steel-thread law remains unchanged.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:f84497a3720f8135304ca1165bf70840","key":1470,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:e9e4bace23b4c2d17586434a8f7540df\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:f84497a3720f8135304ca1165bf70840\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1698,\"path\":\"standards/SPEC_METHOD.md\",\"quote\":\"The rules that govern how constitutional claims are proved in practice are\\ntier-1 law: proof target identity and adequacy (EVALUATION §1); semantic,\\nevidence and projection separation (EVALUATION §2); assurance-boundary\\ncongruence and method qualification (EVALUATION §1, §3, §6 and §7).\\nVerification layers, the testing strategy taxonomy with fixture and proof\\nportability, test authority, scenario bundles, installed development proof\\nand significant path coverage are ASSURANCE §1 to §6 (P6).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/SPEC_METHOD.md#SPEC_METHOD%2F9.%20Evidence\",\"start_line\":1692}],\"statement\":\"Proof identity/adequacy, semantic-evidence-projection separation, assurance congruence and method qualification remain EVALUATION tier-1 law. Verification layers, test taxonomy/fixture/proof portability, test authority, scenarios, installed development proof and significant paths remain ASSURANCE-owned. Realisation-claim closure evidence includes authority trace, realisation proof, negative proof where drift is plausible and present-tense residual pressure; this section creates no additional closure condition.\",\"uncertainty\":\"Referenced EVALUATION, ASSURANCE and TICKETS closure law is not supplied in full.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:513d1dd23e9b3e777704177ed60e9b66","key":1471,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:1b1081fd5b172df398ec35893fd08af7\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:513d1dd23e9b3e777704177ed60e9b66\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[\"Superseded by: applies when superseded; Retained special case: applies when earlier behaviour is intentionally retained.\",\"A superseded ADR may be deleted only after explicit retirement.\"],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1729,\"path\":\"standards/SPEC_METHOD.md\",\"quote\":\"ADRs are append-only history. When a later ADR supersedes one, the earlier\\nADR stays in place with `Status: superseded` and `Superseded by:` naming\\nits successor; a superseded ADR is deleted only when it is explicitly\\nretired. When the scope of a shared or cross-tenant ADR narrows during\\nimplementation to one tenant, the ADR moves to that tenant's design\\nsurface and the move is recorded in the supersession chain (P4b, P3). This\\nsection owns ADR lifecycle and location; templates project its rules.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/SPEC_METHOD.md#SPEC_METHOD%2F10.%20Design%20records\",\"start_line\":1723}],\"statement\":\"Each ADR explicitly records Status active/superseded/retired, Implements requirement IDs, Derives from motivating intent/strategy, Supersedes prior ADR/doctrine, and conditional successor/retained-special-case fields. Write per decision boundary, not requirement file. Name any operational mechanism named by requirements; immediately reprice event-contract ADR when requirements expand event taxonomy. Append-only history keeps superseded ADRs with successor metadata until explicit retirement. A shared ADR narrowed to one tenant moves to that design surface with recorded supersession-chain move. Store at closest owning design surface, never comments/generated views/runtime archives/requirements folders. Filename convention is ADR-<local-id>-short-slug.md with local ID unique within owning adrs/ directory. Every layout records tenant identity/locations in product registry; templates project these owned rules.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:2e0f6c4d891336cfa028d7a57ccaf6fc","key":1472,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:c273a437cbb3bf7285b6040216d5722e\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:152d2a8a64bd069bdea1135af24a3c80\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:b24ab29ed2af1879ab09c354e892e5be\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:088223e4b5ad7c379a6722a6b1aca800\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:2e0f6c4d891336cfa028d7a57ccaf6fc\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"Every product built with the method.\"],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1828,\"path\":\"standards/SPEC_METHOD.md\",\"quote\":\"1. Realisations of one WHAT. One WHAT is realised by one or more\\n   independent build tenants, whatever the physical layout. The WHAT is\\n   constitutional and each tenant's realisation is HOW; a tenant-local\\n   realisation stays derivative until its governing truth is ratified in\\n   specification (§2). Each tenant binds the product's requirements\\n   calculus to a declared computational calculus and binds that calculus\\n   to a concrete execution environment. Both bindings are that tenant's\\n   design and realisation: they are declared in its existing design and\\n   realisation surfaces, chosen under the Design rule (§2) and recorded as\\n   design decisions (§10), and the method requires no further carrier. The\\n   tenant owns its binding, its realisation and their evidence; the WHAT\\n   keeps its meaning (P2, P6).\\n2. Selection. The execution environment may be a technology stack, a\\n   human process or a combination. Its selection stays within the\\n   requirements calculus, including every human decision that calculus\\n   requires: no choice of environment removes a required human decision or\\n   a required independent assessment. Author identity, actor identity and\\n   operation kind stay distinct, and none determines another. Who authored\\n   a tenant does not select its environment; one actor may perform\\n   operations of several kinds, each under its own grant; and an actor's\\n   identity neither decides the kind of an operation nor grants authority\\n   for it. A person performing an operation does not by that make it human\\n   adjudication: §5 states the admission that makes an operation human\\n   adjudication and how a person who decides under policy without it is\\n   governed. The same holds for every decision the requirements reserve to\\n   a human: the person the governing authority admits for it takes it, and\\n   a person's part elsewhere in the process does not (P6, P1).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/SPEC_METHOD.md#SPEC_METHOD%2F11.%20Build-tenant%20binding\",\"start_line\":1802}],\"statement\":\"One constitutional WHAT has one or more independent HOW tenants regardless of layout; tenant-local truth stays derivative until specification ratification. Each tenant declares both bindings in existing design/realisation and design decisions, with no new required carrier, owning means and evidence without changing WHAT. Selection must preserve every required human decision and independent assessment. Author identity, actor identity and operation kind are distinct and determine none of the others; operation kind includes what it does and required authority. One actor may perform multiple kinds only under each grant. Authorship is an independence condition under EVALUATION, not environment selection; identity grants no authority. Human participation alone is not human adjudication or another reserved human decision: the authority-admitted person must take that decision.\",\"uncertainty\":\"EVALUATION's full independence and identity definitions are not supplied.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:d8bf20d1063e242410b61c39f11d4248","key":1473,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:152d2a8a64bd069bdea1135af24a3c80\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:99af08784eea240f27b803be49f856e2\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:088223e4b5ad7c379a6722a6b1aca800\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:d8bf20d1063e242410b61c39f11d4248\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"Content and measurements are required insofar as material to served obligations.\"],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1856,\"path\":\"standards/SPEC_METHOD.md\",\"quote\":\"3. Material content. For the obligations it serves, the binding\\n   identifies:\\n   - the operations, each with its inputs, outputs, effects and outcome\\n     values; each outcome value maps to exactly one core value under\\n     [FOUNDATIONS §4 Results](FOUNDATIONS.md#results), and an intended\\n     external effect, one of uncertain completion included, is recorded as\\n     [ACTIVATION §3 Effects](ACTIVATION.md#effects) states;\\n   - the composition laws, and the transformations the calculus permits;\\n   - the resource measures;\\n   - the operational assumptions on which conformance depends, among them\\n     those about actors, tools, availability and failure.\\n\\n   Human effort, elapsed time, communication and machine resources are\\n   measured where a selected obligation needs them. Each measure states its\\n   unit and its boundary: what is counted, and where measurement starts and\\n   stops. A resource claim without its unit or its boundary supports no\\n   conformance claim. The size of a selected context is measured as\\n   [ACTIVATION §2](ACTIVATION.md#2-context-construction-under-an-envelope)\\n   step 3 measures it, against the capacity the binding declares for the\\n   actor. The law for declaring, measuring and honouring resource limits\\n   is [ACTIVATION §6 Resource limits](ACTIVATION.md#resource-limits), and\\n   this rule binds it: the values of a step's time, spend and other\\n   resource limits, and the units and boundaries the environment can\\n   measure, are those of the execution binding, stated before the\\n   activation they limit. Where a configuration states its resource limits\\n   and its assumptions about failure\\n   ([ACTIVATION §1 Configuration](ACTIVATION.md#configuration)), it takes\\n   them from this binding (P0, P2, P5).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/SPEC_METHOD.md#SPEC_METHOD%2F11.%20Build-tenant%20binding\",\"start_line\":1829}],\"statement\":\"Binding identifies operations with inputs/outputs/effects/outcome values, each outcome mapping to exactly one core value; intended external effects including uncertain completion are recorded under ACTIVATION. Declare composition laws/permitted transformations, resource measures and conformance assumptions about actors/tools/availability/failure. Measure human effort/time/communication/machine resources where an obligation needs them, with unit, counted scope and start/stop boundary; missing unit or boundary supports no conformance claim. Measure selected context against declared actor capacity under ACTIVATION §2. State time/spend/other limits and measurable units/boundaries before the limited activation; configuration takes limits/failure assumptions from this binding.\",\"uncertainty\":\"Core mappings, effect recording and context/resource measurement laws are external.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:6260d2954ce33a7ae588a5f5f41d6ae4","key":1474,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:152d2a8a64bd069bdea1135af24a3c80\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:b24ab29ed2af1879ab09c354e892e5be\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:6260d2954ce33a7ae588a5f5f41d6ae4\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1879,\"path\":\"standards/SPEC_METHOD.md\",\"quote\":\"4. Conformance evidence. The obligations of the requirements calculus\\n   decide fitness; the kind of executor alone neither accepts nor rejects a\\n   realisation. Evidence establishes how the bound realisation satisfies\\n   the required meaning and constraints, including the applicable\\n   authority, independence, failure and recovery conditions. Conformance is\\n   judged under\\n   [EVALUATION §6](EVALUATION.md#6-conformance-of-realisations), and two\\n   conforming tenants need not behave identically outside the contract.\\n   Each assessment returns a core value for its predicate, and the tenant's\\n   conformance is their\\n   [conjunction](FOUNDATIONS.md#conjunction-of-results), with the\\n   obligations of the requirements calculus as its required coverage. A\\n   convenient stack never weakens an obligation. An execution plan that\\n   merges two required independent assessments, or substitutes an\\n   automated result for a required human decision, is a counterexample to\\n   the obligation it weakens, so the binding's conformance for that\\n   obligation is `falsified`; in any run under such a plan the lost\\n   assessment or decision has no applicable closed result. Matching\\n   outputs, lower cost or a faster run do not discharge the lost\\n   independence or authority. A claim that a binding preserves categorical\\n   structure is a further claim: it meets the Formal fragment of\\n   [FOUNDATIONS §4](FOUNDATIONS.md#4-algebra) and stays distinct from\\n   conformance on the equivalence ladder of EVALUATION §6 (P6, P1, P4b).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/SPEC_METHOD.md#SPEC_METHOD%2F11.%20Build-tenant%20binding\",\"start_line\":1857}],\"statement\":\"Obligations, not executor kind, decide fitness. Evidence must establish required meaning/constraints including applicable authority, independence, failure and recovery; conformance is predicate-result conjunction covering the requirements calculus. Convenient stacks cannot weaken obligations. Merging required independent assessments or substituting automation for a required human decision falsifies conformance for the weakened obligation and leaves the lost assessment/decision without applicable closed result; matching output, cost or speed cannot discharge it. Categorical-structure preservation is a separate formal-fragment/equivalence-ladder claim. An a_c representation selects no executor and structural validation establishes no execution conformance; human-process models still require their own conformance evidence.\",\"uncertainty\":\"The full conjunction, equivalence ladder, formal fragment and structural/semantic separation law are external.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:f33a71885e9404e2196fe0a963185f30","key":1475,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:152d2a8a64bd069bdea1135af24a3c80\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:99af08784eea240f27b803be49f856e2\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:088223e4b5ad7c379a6722a6b1aca800\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:f33a71885e9404e2196fe0a963185f30\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1909,\"path\":\"standards/SPEC_METHOD.md\",\"quote\":\"7. Three accounts. The algorithmic, informational and computational\\n   accounts of a construction, which\\n   [FOUNDATIONS §2 Accounts of a construction](FOUNDATIONS.md#accounts-of-a-construction)\\n   defines, apply across the binding, from the requirements calculus\\n   through the computational calculus to the execution environment. The\\n   binding keeps the three accounts apart. A mapping from one account to\\n   another is a transformation: what it preserves, the law that licenses\\n   it, and whether it is exact or approximate with its adequacy relation\\n   and end-to-end bound, are stated and discharged under\\n   [ACTIVATION §4 Refinement](ACTIVATION.md#refinement), and where it is\\n   recorded in a_c its record is\\n   [AC-013](AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS.md#ac-013-transformation). The binding adds\\n   only which accounts the mapping joins and the evidence, in its\\n   execution environment, that discharges the preservation (P1, P0, P4a,\\n   P6).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/SPEC_METHOD.md#SPEC_METHOD%2F11.%20Build-tenant%20binding\",\"start_line\":1895}],\"statement\":\"A computational calculus may be reused across tenants/environments only where each binding satisfies and demonstrates its laws; different language/tool/team/person alone need not change calculus, and lawful executor replacement changes execution binding only. Keep algorithmic/informational/computational accounts distinct across requirements/calculus/environment. Cross-account mapping states preservation, licensing law, exactness or approximate adequacy/end-to-end bound and discharges them under refinement; an a_c record follows AC-013. Binding adds joined accounts and environmental preservation evidence. Major stack/admissibility ambiguity follows governance; binding changes enter triage/classification, while weakened obligations re-enter their WHAT owner. Construction uses the executing tenant's binding. Branches/copies/territories/review/merge mechanics are project local axioms or tenant design, not prescribed here; tenant-ticket independence/review remains TICKETS-owned.\",\"uncertainty\":\"Account definitions, refinement proof, AC-013 structure and multi-tenant ticket rules are not fully supplied.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:a657eea293b3715dc153f8f21ffd93d5","key":1476,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:89a8456fc34b22ab5de4993cf6bc5b8a\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:a657eea293b3715dc153f8f21ffd93d5\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":25,\"path\":\"standards/TICKETS.md\",\"quote\":\"same principles. The change classes a ticket records are\\n[SPEC_METHOD §4](SPEC_METHOD.md#change-classes), which is the triage target\\nof every clause here that names a class; the step side of admission is\\n[ACTIVATION §1](ACTIVATION.md#admission); the generic law of claims,\\nindependent assessment and acceptance is EVALUATION §1, §3 and §5; the\\ntesting law is ASSURANCE. This member defines none of those twice. Its\\nfamily table (F13) opens §5.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/TICKETS.md#TICKETS\",\"start_line\":19}],\"statement\":\"TICKETS mechanisms are tier-2 realisations whose clauses name requiring P0–P6 principles; mechanisms could differ under the same principles. Ticket class references target SPEC_METHOD §4; step-side admission remains ACTIVATION §1, claims/independence/acceptance EVALUATION, and testing ASSURANCE. TICKETS does not redefine those laws; F13 opens its §5.\",\"uncertainty\":\"Most owned TICKETS mechanics and its F13 table are outside the supplied sections.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:6d24971bf3681de5a602c0fa272d719e","key":1477,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:d2a79ed2fdb131ad2ae0e382dc22ee38\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:b643fdd62b3be8f761bafff726c6c232\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:6d24971bf3681de5a602c0fa272d719e\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":62,\"path\":\"standards/TICKETS.md\",\"quote\":\"A sprint may contain durable tickets, manifest-local iteration entries, or\\nboth. Tickets carry work items that need durable identity across sessions;\\nmanifest-local iteration entries carry small changes whose only independent\\nvalue is traceability inside the sprint. The sprint is the batch authority;\\nit does not erase the need for paydown tickets when close review finds debt\\nthat must survive past the sprint (P2, P4b).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/TICKETS.md#TICKETS%2F1.%20Work%20carriers%2FSprints\",\"start_line\":57}],\"statement\":\"A sprint may contain durable tickets, local iteration entries or both; use tickets for cross-session independent identity and local entries for small changes valued only for batch traceability. Batch authority does not create constitutional authority, remove explicit close review or erase paydown tickets for debt surviving the sprint.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:07dc0bb6aec13df34a9216d001a2bd04","key":1478,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:fd968916f08ade55608ac7b3f7f0511e\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:07dc0bb6aec13df34a9216d001a2bd04\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"A decision is recorded in a comment.\"],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":74,\"path\":\"standards/TICKETS.md\",\"quote\":\"A decision recorded in a\\ncomment takes its authority from the surface that owns the decision, once\\nit is adopted there ([POSTING_GUIDE §9](POSTING_GUIDE.md#9-ratification)),\\nand has none of its own (P6, P3).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/TICKETS.md#TICKETS%2F1.%20Work%20carriers%2FComments\",\"start_line\":71}],\"statement\":\"Comments are not task-status authority. A recorded decision gains authority only from adoption at its owning surface, not from the comment itself; POSTING_GUIDE owns post content, structure, discussion state and ratification.\",\"uncertainty\":\"POSTING_GUIDE details are not supplied.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:0028be625aa931e9fba8f5fd03cd2a3b","key":1479,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:04e341b6732269d66c8ea0de2a25c61d\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:0028be625aa931e9fba8f5fd03cd2a3b\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":99,\"path\":\"standards/TICKETS.md\",\"quote\":\"closure is checked against that same contract;\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/TICKETS.md#TICKETS%2F1.%20Work%20carriers%2FExecution%20contracts\",\"start_line\":97}],\"statement\":\"Contracts are neither a rival backlog nor a second planning surface. The described loop selects the smallest lawful carrier for the required lifetime, drafts one run contract, deterministically validates/admit-or-rejects its classification, records admitted work basis on the selected durable carrier including an event log when required, assembles applicable prompts from admitted work law rather than raw phrasing, and checks closure against the same criteria. Execution may follow admission in the same invocation; resulting state still undergoes proof, gap analysis and repricing.\",\"uncertainty\":\"The referenced ACTIVATION admission mechanism is not supplied in full.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:ca8f9016dcc43cc7f4a9c016658c23b5","key":1480,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:c91d96dbd8d81139a3066db234ad87a7\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:d852d15950483fab7f616afd7b72e49a\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:ca8f9016dcc43cc7f4a9c016658c23b5\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":116,\"path\":\"standards/TICKETS.md\",\"quote\":\"Milestone acceptance proves only its declared claim.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/TICKETS.md#TICKETS%2F1.%20Work%20carriers%2FMilestones%20and%20phase-scoped%20truth%20%28UP-006%29\",\"start_line\":108}],\"statement\":\"Accepted design does not satisfy implementation, installed proof, qualification or release. Ticket completion requires acceptance of every closure-bearing milestone under the condition-based closure rule for that milestone's own declared claim. Optional or deferred work requires explicit disposition and owner. Commentary and generated summaries cannot mutate milestone or ticket truth.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:7822fd19b7ca92f0a644d7b48616cc3c","key":1481,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:5f7af811df86c66a0f026fe690dc0a23\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:7822fd19b7ca92f0a644d7b48616cc3c\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":146,\"path\":\"standards/TICKETS.md\",\"quote\":\"their\\nabsence from the project tree is not absence from the governing method.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/TICKETS.md#TICKETS%2F2.%20Layout%20and%20authority%2FDefault%20layout\",\"start_line\":141}],\"statement\":\"The starter layout is stdo_default.json, specification/GOALS.md, .ai-workspace/sprints/, .ai-workspace/tickets/{backlog,active,completed}/ and .ai-workspace/comments/<agent-id>/. The applicable product definition resolves POSTING_GUIDE and TICKETS from its exact shared installed basis; their absence from the project tree does not establish method absence.\",\"uncertainty\":\"PRODUCT_DEFINITION §§1 and 4 and the installed basis are not supplied.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:7c43210a80c66f646f4b6b95fc6a1bb4","key":1482,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:d852d15950483fab7f616afd7b72e49a\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:5f7af811df86c66a0f026fe690dc0a23\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:6df0210aa0cfac994dc829752b179bc7\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:7c43210a80c66f646f4b6b95fc6a1bb4\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"A replacement carrier or growth capability is used.\"],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":177,\"path\":\"standards/TICKETS.md\",\"quote\":\"neither growth\\nchanges the authority or refusal laws\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/TICKETS.md#TICKETS%2F2.%20Layout%20and%20authority%2FCarrier%20substitution\",\"start_line\":176}],\"statement\":\"The selected local-file model remains valid. Other carriers need not reproduce its folders but must preserve ticket authority and refusal laws, including one durable record. A generated board remains a projection; a tracker holding tickets is lawful only through explicit product-definition rebinding with no rival surface left.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:ed7fcb9a0ad0e06093be964d92f2f027","key":1483,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:7da6fbd5a21c446b21dde647032e07d7\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:ed7fcb9a0ad0e06093be964d92f2f027\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":188,\"path\":\"standards/TICKETS.md\",\"quote\":\"Another bound carrier preserves the same identity, required\\nfields, history, closure law and one-truth relation\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/TICKETS.md#TICKETS%2F3.%20Sprint%20rules%2FOne%20durable%20record%20per%20sprint\",\"start_line\":184}],\"statement\":\"Each sprint has exactly one durable manifest. Alternative bound carriers preserve identity, required fields, history, closure law and one-truth relation. A local filename should contain a stable identifier and short slug; SPRINT-2026-04-30-process-navigator.md and SPRINT-2026-05-12-dashboard-density.md are recommendations, not mandated names.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:3555a2d6a76f0d89ba5ec1aee9596b4c","key":1484,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:7da6fbd5a21c446b21dde647032e07d7\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:3555a2d6a76f0d89ba5ec1aee9596b4c\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":196,\"path\":\"standards/TICKETS.md\",\"quote\":\"Each sprint manifest records at least `id`, `title`, `status`, `goal`,\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/TICKETS.md#TICKETS%2F3.%20Sprint%20rules%2FManifest%20fields\",\"start_line\":192}],\"statement\":\"Every manifest records at least id, title, status, goal, opened_at, updated_at, authority_refs, scope, excluded_boundaries, expected_change_classes, included_tickets or iterations, closure_trigger, closure_law, proof_surface, deferred_compliance, non_closure_conditions and paydown_policy. authority_refs names upstream governing surfaces. excluded_boundaries names prohibited changes, typically product truth, data contracts, runtime semantics, governance/closure law, public carrier shape and release criteria. deferred_compliance names intentionally deferred local proof/review/accessibility/screenshots/walkthrough/tests/design wording/trace cleanup. paydown_policy explains acceptance, ticketing, repricing or removal of debt during close review.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:6688df30f48157be13a737ab21f6770c","key":1485,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:7da6fbd5a21c446b21dde647032e07d7\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:d852d15950483fab7f616afd7b72e49a\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:5f68ddf5dc5c4ea4e2e1746d8627d2d6\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:6688df30f48157be13a737ab21f6770c\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"Work is proposed for sprint admission.\"],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":232,\"path\":\"standards/TICKETS.md\",\"quote\":\"It may not batch away intake triage:\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/TICKETS.md#TICKETS%2F3.%20Sprint%20rules%2FSprint%20admission\",\"start_line\":228}],\"statement\":\"Admission is permitted only with a reviewable manifest boundary: bounded scope, cited authority, expected change classes, explicit exclusions, closure law, non-closure conditions and deferred-compliance paydown policy. Repeated closure criteria may be batched; substantive included tickets still record lawful change_class and re_entry_point. Manifest-local iterations may rely on the sprint class only while inside scope and exclusions.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:6e2dc30966e14f48f80d41aae8b870b3","key":1486,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:7da6fbd5a21c446b21dde647032e07d7\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:6e2dc30966e14f48f80d41aae8b870b3\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"Local compliance proof is deferred.\"],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":244,\"path\":\"standards/TICKETS.md\",\"quote\":\"escrow satisfies no method, release or product closure until paid down,\\naccepted or repriced\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/TICKETS.md#TICKETS%2F3.%20Sprint%20rules%2FCompliance%20escrow\",\"start_line\":243}],\"statement\":\"Deferral requires a named proof/cleanup class, debt local to admitted sprint surface, expected correction cost below per-change proof cost, a short enough sprint for reviewability, and close review that classifies and pays down debt. Escrow is explicit and satisfies no method/release/product closure until paid down, accepted or repriced. When governing method permits, eligible classes may include screenshots/walkthrough capture, visual review, accessibility cleanup, UI interaction replay proof, design wording, trace and local realisation cleanup. Escrow must not hide new product truth, changed/new data contracts, runtime/governance/closure/provenance/evidence semantics, missing constructive carriers, changed public published-function/carrier contracts, or law changes requiring goal_reprice, intent_reprice, product_reprice, requirement_reprice or design_reframe. Such findings are recorded and exit through a standalone ticket, repricing action or sprint supersession.\",\"uncertainty\":\"The governing method's specific escrow permissions are not supplied.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:b4c2941a02a276667b4ff01ee25129cc","key":1487,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:7da6fbd5a21c446b21dde647032e07d7\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:0584fc4e2fd93e2660fcdd839ddc7ea2\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:b58b9bef6638581a1adfc8e2f24b5cd4\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:b4c2941a02a276667b4ff01ee25129cc\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"Sprint close review begins or closed status is proposed.\"],\"exceptions\":[\"Explicit local paydown debt may survive close only when governing method permits follow-up.\"],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":280,\"path\":\"standards/TICKETS.md\",\"quote\":\"A sprint may move to\\n`closed` only when every item and every debt entry is classified and the\\nresulting paydown or repricing work is durable.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/TICKETS.md#TICKETS%2F3.%20Sprint%20rules%2FClose%20review\",\"start_line\":275}],\"statement\":\"Close begins with status closing and freezes new iteration. Every included ticket/iteration is reviewed against the manifest; evidence durability is checked; changed surfaces are walked against cited authority; deferred compliance is classified; debt surviving review gets paydown tickets. Every item receives accepted, local_paydown, design_reframe, requirement_reprice, product_reprice or remove. Closure requires classification of every item and debt entry and durable resulting paydown/repricing work, not satisfied results for all. Hidden authority drift cannot be accepted.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:e3ab6c65957dce201048a29c7e8ed478","key":1488,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:b58b9bef6638581a1adfc8e2f24b5cd4\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:e3ab6c65957dce201048a29c7e8ed478\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":323,\"path\":\"standards/TICKETS.md\",\"quote\":\"cannot read remaining debt, needed repricing or\\nremoval as compliance\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/TICKETS.md#TICKETS%2F3.%20Sprint%20rules%2FClose%20review\",\"start_line\":322}],\"statement\":\"Classification must be against cited sprint authority and consume, while remaining separate from, the item's core review results. Local debt is the counterexample for local_paydown; its governing relation stays coherent, otherwise repricing is required. Repricing invalidates the cited authority's ability to support acceptance; its named layer is a declared re-entry fact accompanying the core value, not another result. Removal's reason is its counterexample and requires neither violated governing relation nor competing truth path; it therefore has no matching ACTIVATION disposition. Item/debt mappings add no core value or disposition and never turn debt, repricing or removal into compliance.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:343ed826595200dc88eaea35ae3b06fa","key":1489,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:d852d15950483fab7f616afd7b72e49a\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:343ed826595200dc88eaea35ae3b06fa\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":338,\"path\":\"standards/TICKETS.md\",\"quote\":\"without a co-equal\\nlocal copy\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/TICKETS.md#TICKETS%2F4.%20Ticket%20rules%2FOne%20durable%20record%20per%20ticket\",\"start_line\":332}],\"statement\":\"Every ticket has one durable authoritative record. Repository/external-tracker carriers are lawful only if they preserve the required contract, history, state transition, stable identity, searchability and closure semantics without a co-equal local copy. Local filenames should carry stable id and short slug; T-001-add-product-layer.md, B-002-fix-reset-manifest-id.md, S-003-evaluate-integration-capability.md and C-004-clean-up-trace-tags.md are recommended examples.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:130fc240ae84162f18d97a86d7ec5bbe","key":1490,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:2269e5c21dad5030dba9012113f88134\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:d852d15950483fab7f616afd7b72e49a\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:130fc240ae84162f18d97a86d7ec5bbe\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"The same admitted work genuinely has multiple tenant execution lines.\",\"Applies to backlog and active tickets.\"],\"exceptions\":[\"Completed tickets are not affected retroactively unless reopened or explicitly repriced.\",\"Upstream-only and single-tenant cases require no sibling duplicate.\"],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":385,\"path\":\"standards/TICKETS.md\",\"quote\":\"one ticket does not claim closure for more than one build-tenant\\nlifecycle;\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/TICKETS.md#TICKETS%2F4.%20Ticket%20rules%2FMulti-build-tenant%20independence\",\"start_line\":373}],\"statement\":\"Keep the upstream authority ticket separate and create one tenant-local ticket per build tenant, appending a tenant mnemonic to base id and filename. Each tenant independently owns status, proof, closure, repricing and reopening; another tenant's green status cannot hide blockers or false closure. Duplicates should record source_ticket and build_tenant. build_tenant identifies the product's how.build_tenants entry; path/display/tracker aliases substitute only when product definition binds them as identity. The unsuffixed base may remain upstream authority, while backlog/active multi-tenant execution and closure live on suffixed tickets. B-030 with B-030-T1 and B-030-T2 is illustrative.\",\"uncertainty\":\"Tenant identity and realisation semantics are imported from PRODUCT_DEFINITION §8.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:1bdb908077046a9ada4767f6e6a6f39d","key":1491,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:d852d15950483fab7f616afd7b72e49a\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:04e341b6732269d66c8ea0de2a25c61d\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:cb3b17a0446b24effc009acc33282fd6\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:1bdb908077046a9ada4767f6e6a6f39d\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":406,\"path\":\"standards/TICKETS.md\",\"quote\":\"Each ticket records at least `id`, `title`, `type`, `ticket_category`,\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/TICKETS.md#TICKETS%2F4.%20Ticket%20rules%2FRequired%20fields\",\"start_line\":389}],\"statement\":\"Every ticket records at least id, title, type, ticket_category, status, goal, change_intent, change_class, re_entry_point, triaged_at, created_at and updated_at. Recommended additional fields: priority, dependencies, links, intake_source, affected_boundary, source_ticket for duplication/derivation and build_tenant for tenant-local work. Migration tickets additionally carry migration_strategy and library_usage; consume/extend requires governing_library, none requires library_rationale. Tenant-local migration requires build_tenant and source_ticket when derived/duplicated upstream. For admission a runtime-drafted contract should also carry at least target_truth, superseded_truth when relevant, closure_law, evaluation_criteria, non_closure_conditions and proof_surface.\",\"uncertainty\":\"Recommended contract fields retain their 'should' modality.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:5e0e4e018c062383fa4b13d11eadbd40","key":1492,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:cb3b17a0446b24effc009acc33282fd6\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:5e0e4e018c062383fa4b13d11eadbd40\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"ticket_category is implementation_migration.\"],\"exceptions\":[\"Downstream exploratory work may occur while the source ticket is active, but is non-closure evidence until the source carrier is admitted and authoritative.\"],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":444,\"path\":\"standards/TICKETS.md\",\"quote\":\"the dependency chain runs `source carrier ->\\ndownstream consumers`, never the reverse.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/TICKETS.md#TICKETS%2F4.%20Ticket%20rules%2FInside-out%20sequencing\",\"start_line\":443}],\"statement\":\"Tickets publishing/admitting the authoritative source carrier are upstream. Tickets hardening prompts, projections, reports, dossiers, review surfaces and other consumers depend on them. A downstream ticket cannot close while its upstream source-carrier ticket remains open.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:0bc3b2171a6f4c0bfb3b00051d32cede","key":1493,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:a9a45cc30fc2d890d88c8a17834de609\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:a41b7a918702f428860acb628ab48df5\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:4f444a4cc883ac93d02be4653b6ab221\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:0bc3b2171a6f4c0bfb3b00051d32cede\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":466,\"path\":\"standards/TICKETS.md\",\"quote\":\"A ticket records the `change_class`\\ndeclared by intake triage,\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/TICKETS.md#TICKETS%2F4.%20Ticket%20rules%2FChange%20class\",\"start_line\":450}],\"statement\":\"Tickets record intake's declared class using SPEC_METHOD §4 classes. Type, category and class are independent dimensions: bug + implementation_migration + design_reframe is consistent. A spike should terminate in a more specific downstream ticket or an explicit decision that no further substantive change is required; exploratory status does not eliminate its current triage class.\",\"uncertainty\":\"The external class definitions are only partially described by the supplied text.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:ae3fd944b42d6fa764ff964cd1b9ab91","key":1494,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:5f68ddf5dc5c4ea4e2e1746d8627d2d6\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:a9a45cc30fc2d890d88c8a17834de609\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:ae3fd944b42d6fa764ff964cd1b9ab91\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"A bug's lawful re-entry class is being determined.\"],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":506,\"path\":\"standards/TICKETS.md\",\"quote\":\"Missing or ambiguous evidence leaves the affected\\ntreatment unknown; it is not proof that the governing layer itself is\\nabsent\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/TICKETS.md#TICKETS%2F4.%20Ticket%20rules%2FUpward%20propagation%20check\",\"start_line\":481}],\"statement\":\"Before realization_refactor, establish that current requirement and accepted realising design govern the affected behaviour and suffice for the authorized outcome; mere presence proves no coverage. Missing/ambiguous evidence leaves treatment unknown, not the layer absent. Candidate public violation does not select a new contract; governing-owner re-entry requires explicitly changed desired outcome or established insufficiency. Walk upward from realisation, checking each layer and stopping at the highest found missing/insufficient: requirement missing/insufficient → requirement_reprice and requirement owner; sufficient requirement but missing/insufficient design → design_reframe and Design; actual Goal/Intent/Product change → corresponding owner/class; sufficient requirement/design with implementation deviation → realization_refactor, repair or reject candidate. Unresolved meaning remains J and reserved choice remains O.\",\"uncertainty\":\"Full computed-classification algorithm and C/J/O annotation definitions are external.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:ea27f0256efd504f9a739e86f7e26624","key":1495,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:d852d15950483fab7f616afd7b72e49a\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:5f68ddf5dc5c4ea4e2e1746d8627d2d6\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:ea27f0256efd504f9a739e86f7e26624\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"Ticket concerns substantive work.\"],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":515,\"path\":\"standards/TICKETS.md\",\"quote\":\"The recorded values are those intake triage declared\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/TICKETS.md#TICKETS%2F4.%20Ticket%20rules%2FTriage%20metadata\",\"start_line\":514}],\"statement\":\"The ticket carries declared change_intent, lawful change_class, lawful re_entry_point and triaged_at; these are the values intake triage declared, not a later role's replacement classification.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:ba023f8d6a9166c13ec05d62f59e47f0","key":1496,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:1906988707368f41598a83175d808b93\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:0584fc4e2fd93e2660fcdd839ddc7ea2\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:a9a45cc30fc2d890d88c8a17834de609\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:52b796e9b8ce716db4e099c31df2b84e\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:03245c6904f417787ce80ebcc3bf7f00\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:b58b9bef6638581a1adfc8e2f24b5cd4\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:ba023f8d6a9166c13ec05d62f59e47f0\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":534,\"path\":\"standards/TICKETS.md\",\"quote\":\"a ticket marked `completed`, or a sprint marked `closed`, cannot stand in\\nfor a `satisfied` result\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/TICKETS.md#TICKETS%2F4.%20Ticket%20rules%2FStatus\",\"start_line\":533}],\"statement\":\"Ticket statuses including local additions, lanes, sprint statuses, migration_strategy, library_usage and recorded change_class are declared carrier states and map to no core value. Sprint-close classifications and debt outcomes are results mapped at close review. Evaluating a state produces a separate predicate-bearing core result; states must never be combined as evaluation results.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:b20d5dda90774bd929ad9c54056d062c","key":1497,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:d852d15950483fab7f616afd7b72e49a\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:1906988707368f41598a83175d808b93\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:5f7af811df86c66a0f026fe690dc0a23\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:b20d5dda90774bd929ad9c54056d062c\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":548,\"path\":\"standards/TICKETS.md\",\"quote\":\"completed tickets move to `ticketing.tickets.lanes.completed`, by default\\n`.ai-workspace/tickets/completed/`\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/TICKETS.md#TICKETS%2F4.%20Ticket%20rules%2FLanes\",\"start_line\":542}],\"statement\":\"Backlog tickets use ticketing.tickets.lanes.backlog, default .ai-workspace/tickets/backlog/; active tickets use .active, default .ai-workspace/tickets/active/; completed tickets move to .completed, default .ai-workspace/tickets/completed/. Lanes keep the live set small and searchable without moving deferred work into comments or goals.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:e4ab127f2a8eb3f31444faabe4a3caf8","key":1498,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:2d06b1088727674c5114bbd1b8f6a018\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:e4ab