674c5114bbd1b8f6a018\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:fd01bb70c1a76c3624381181e017d45c\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":617,\"path\":\"standards/TICKETS.md\",\"quote\":\"Each consumer applies the rule and decides nothing the owning section does\\nnot\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/TICKETS.md#TICKETS%2F5.%20From%20carrier%20to%20execution%2FFoundation%20to%20law%3A%20work%20carriers\",\"start_line\":616}],\"statement\":\"F13's eleven consequence groups concern lifetime-matched carriers, admitted execution basis, one authority chain, sprint escrow/close outcomes, recorded triage/upward re-entry, tenant-local lifecycles, migration proof/recurrence, independent verification and durable rulings, condition-based closure/test authority, semantic term resolution, and flexible carrier shape/bounded reading. Obligations surviving a run must be recorded before return; comment content is provisional until adopted into its owning surface and has its own discussion state. Member choices include carrier kinds/selection table, minimum fields/types/categories/statuses/lanes, offering sprints, escrow lists/result mappings, tenant suffixes, migration declarations/checklists/strategy/library values/thresholds/review questions/break order, four repricing states/predicate, five-step test reconciliation, recommended shapes/search defaults and bounded reading policy. Product definition owns carrier locations/rebinding and tenant registry; governing method owns whether debt may survive; POSTING_GUIDE owns post categories/structure/states. Admission step law, migration law, independent assessment/reuse, result conjunction/general test law and semantic resolution remain owned by the cited external sections. Consumers add no deciding authority. A credible recurrence requires review, not automatic commonisation or identity merging.\",\"uncertainty\":\"The table states derivations and ownership; their external foundation standing and unsupplied owner clauses are not independently established.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:f2b5a046de60125b47b849fe764feaad","key":1500,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:04e341b6732269d66c8ea0de2a25c61d\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:d852d15950483fab7f616afd7b72e49a\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:7da6fbd5a21c446b21dde647032e07d7\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:f2b5a046de60125b47b849fe764feaad\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"An execution is governed by the described method.\"],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":634,\"path\":\"standards/TICKETS.md\",\"quote\":\"then select the first matching row below.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/TICKETS.md#TICKETS%2F5.%20From%20carrier%20to%20execution%2FCarrier%20selection\",\"start_line\":624}],\"statement\":\"Every execution uses one run contract. Establish upstream work authority, then choose the first matching row, with local boundary equal to an admitted sprint when inside it, otherwise current run: (1) no authority → no admitted contract, no substitute-authority ticket, stop/re-enter; (2) exact admitted ticket → derive and reuse, no duplicate; (3) authority but no exact ticket and independent state/open obligation beyond local boundary → durable ticket plus contract, create/update only under ticket-state authority; (4) authority, no exact ticket, entirely inside admitted sprint with no post-close state → manifest plus local iteration, no durable ticket; (5) authority, no exact ticket or sprint and current-run completion without surviving independent state → intake-drafted contract, no durable ticket. Ticket-shaped fields create neither durable ticket identity nor lane state.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:c62d0418d5bdea87e8d7991cdf46a27e","key":1501,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:04e341b6732269d66c8ea0de2a25c61d\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:d852d15950483fab7f616afd7b72e49a\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:7da6fbd5a21c446b21dde647032e07d7\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:c62d0418d5bdea87e8d7991cdf46a27e\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":648,\"path\":\"standards/TICKETS.md\",\"quote\":\"Absence of a durable ticket neither requires nor authorises creating one.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/TICKETS.md#TICKETS%2F5.%20From%20carrier%20to%20execution%2FCarrier%20selection\",\"start_line\":641}],\"statement\":\"An exact product-authorized instruction may supply one-run upstream authority; generic requests and model-widened scope cannot. Durable creation/update requires selected surviving state and ticket-state authority. An explicit durable-record instruction from that authority selects durability but neither admits execution nor widens upstream authority. Admission mechanism/result-evidence surface are product-bound; admitted result coordinates are recorded on ticket/manifest when selected. Presence, lane, active status and admission prose without coordinates are not admission evidence; the contract remains drafted or rejected. Absent/rejected admission returns missing authority without execution. Before return, surviving obligations become sprint-local entries if their lifetime fits; otherwise durable tickets only under ticket-state authority. Without that authority, retain them in the named durable result/evidence surface or already-authorized enclosing carrier, mark closure withheld on ticket-state authority and return re-entry. No available durable result/evidence surface invokes referenced admission refusal. Execution and closure share categorization, criteria, proof and non-closure conditions; proof/gap analysis/repricing continue.\",\"uncertainty\":\"Exact admission coordinates and refusal procedure are defined by unsupplied ACTIVATION §1.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:5e1f079cefae95891733503796b73556","key":1502,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:04e341b6732269d66c8ea0de2a25c61d\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:5e1f079cefae95891733503796b73556\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[\"A human or mixed binding may select another durable carrier; a binding requiring an event log still requires that log.\"],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":700,\"path\":\"standards/TICKETS.md\",\"quote\":\"Admission validates a contract against its cited product outcome,\\nprerequisite or experiment basis and does not admit that basis\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/TICKETS.md#TICKETS%2F5.%20From%20carrier%20to%20execution%2FExecution%20contract%20admission\",\"start_line\":693}],\"statement\":\"Runtime flow should treat ticket/sprint entry/draft as admission candidate, never automatic truth; contracts carry at least drafted/admitted/rejected/superseded states. An admitted contract should be durably recorded for applicable prompt assembly and later closure on the same basis, with required event logs. Self-certification refusal belongs to ACTIVATION §1. Contract admission validates against the cited product outcome, prerequisite or experiment; it does not admit/renew that basis. Basis admission/renewal belongs to the selected goals-work-wave owner or explicitly bounded proxy and stays durably legible in existing goals/ticket authority. Active status, lane and admitted/retained contract never admit a growth basis.\",\"uncertainty\":\"External admission and basis-renewal laws are referenced rather than fully supplied.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:d87dbb955a1a963d3445c89b737eee35","key":1503,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:04e341b6732269d66c8ea0de2a25c61d\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:cb3b17a0446b24effc009acc33282fd6\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:d87dbb955a1a963d3445c89b737eee35\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[\"Residual implementation debt outside the claimed acceptance path is not by itself a non-closure condition.\"],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":722,\"path\":\"standards/TICKETS.md\",\"quote\":\"These conditions are not optional commentary;\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/TICKETS.md#TICKETS%2F5.%20From%20carrier%20to%20execution%2FEvaluation%20criteria%20and%20non-closure%20conditions\",\"start_line\":716}],\"statement\":\"A contract should expose progress/completion criteria and failures despite local green proof, minimally visible evaluation_criteria and non_closure_conditions as its local gain function. Typical migration failures are old authoritative normal execution in affected scope, accepted mixed old/new proof, proxy/partial acceptance implementation, reachable competing/ambiguous executable authority on the claimed acceptance path, or unreconciled ticket/product/proof wording. These are material execution conditions. Outside-path debt may be deferred only under SPEC_METHOD §7 path-relative authority and explicit disposition rules.\",\"uncertainty\":\"The exact external debt-deferral rule is not supplied; migration compatibility exceptions are retained separately.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:16b35c59a74c2c2d1e3e8f148db19a5d","key":1504,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:d852d15950483fab7f616afd7b72e49a\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:04e341b6732269d66c8ea0de2a25c61d\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:8f4f294b4aae61d03f01fb3afff526a8\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:16b35c59a74c2c2d1e3e8f148db19a5d\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[\"An unqualified term is permitted when cited product, re-entry surface, execution basis and affected scope select exactly one bounded-context meaning.\"],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":741,\"path\":\"standards/TICKETS.md\",\"quote\":\"An unresolved or multiply resolved material term blocks execution-contract\\nadmission and closure for the affected claim.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/TICKETS.md#TICKETS%2F5.%20From%20carrier%20to%20execution%2FBounded-context%20term%20binding\",\"start_line\":738}],\"statement\":\"Ticket/work-instruction terms follow PRODUCT_DEFINITION §5. Cross-context or materially competing meanings require citation of applicable product disambiguation or owner-authorized import/translation/equivalence/disambiguation carrier; referencing the relation may replace duplication. Prose, familiarity, matching glossary headings, tenant placement and comment context cannot select meaning or transfer authority. Unresolved/multiply resolved material terms block affected admission and closure. Opening/updating a ticket records pressure without curing it; resolution re-enters the owner of the missing context/relation.\",\"uncertainty\":\"External semantic-resolution machinery is not supplied.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:cefda19060e83350f9677a490ff2d8fa","key":1505,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:cb3b17a0446b24effc009acc33282fd6\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:52b796e9b8ce716db4e099c31df2b84e\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:03245c6904f417787ce80ebcc3bf7f00\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:cefda19060e83350f9677a490ff2d8fa\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"ticket_category is implementation_migration.\"],\"exceptions\":[\"No excluded/disjoint scope is satisfied by explicit declaration of absence, never silence.\"],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":798,\"path\":\"standards/TICKETS.md\",\"quote\":\"Both\\nare part of the ticket authority, not optional commentary.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/TICKETS.md#TICKETS%2F6.%20Implementation%20migration%2FDeclaration%20and%20checklist\",\"start_line\":748}],\"statement\":\"Require explicit declaration and hard live-Markdown checklist as ticket authority. Declaration names strategy, exact affected scope, every excluded/disjoint product or compatibility scope with deterministic routing, old/superseded and new/authoritative contracts, old/new producer and consumer sets, every derived projection/report/status/proof surface and closure law. Minimum checklist covers named scope/exclusions/routing/old/new paths/new producers/new consumers/projections; old authority removal or explicit demotion in scope; rejection of mixed-state closure evidence; removal/repricing of mixed-behaviour tests; recurrence review against libraries/commonisation; library usage with governing surface/rationale; one tenant lifecycle per backlog/active ticket with suffixed sibling work; and reconciled ticket/product/proof wording before closure. migration_strategy is inside_out_hard_break or fundamental_re_adoption; library_usage is none/consume/extend. consume/extend names governing_library; none explains in library_rationale that no reusable surface applies, the pattern remains boundary-specific, or no lawful recurrence/commonisation candidate yet exists.\",\"uncertainty\":\"SPEC_METHOD §7 owns the referenced migration law.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:098aaa4c8239a4529a21958cf3a07793","key":1506,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:cb3b17a0446b24effc009acc33282fd6\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:c91d96dbd8d81139a3066db234ad87a7\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:098aaa4c8239a4529a21958cf3a07793\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[\"An old path explicitly declared and justified in the ticket as retained compatibility may remain in affected scope.\",\"Deterministically routed non-overlapping scope outside affected scope retains its own current authority.\"],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":828,\"path\":\"standards/TICKETS.md\",\"quote\":\"a false closure claim is a\\nticket-method defect, not only a code defect\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/TICKETS.md#TICKETS%2F6.%20Implementation%20migration%2FClosure%20of%20a%20migration%20ticket\",\"start_line\":815}],\"statement\":\"Old authoritative normal execution inside affected scope blocks closure unless the retained-compatibility exception applies. No silently authoritative old path, mixed green tests, proxy or partial implementation establishes completion; compatibility is named as such rather than native truth and cannot be inferred from surviving code. A completed ticket whose checked items are false on the current tree must reopen or have an explicitly linked successor. Intermediate product-slice acceptance may occur under SPEC_METHOD §7 path-relative promotion, whose identity/criteria ticket wording cannot narrow. The migration ticket stays active until its checklist and final closure law hold. Active status renews no exhausted slice growth authority; bounded removal/demotion/closure-proof work may continue, but further material producer/consumer growth requires another basis admitted under SPEC_METHOD §3.\",\"uncertainty\":\"The exact promotion and continuing-work bounds are external.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:64f35c0b93871cb983302891c5b30194","key":1507,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:cb3b17a0446b24effc009acc33282fd6\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:52b796e9b8ce716db4e099c31df2b84e\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:64f35c0b93871cb983302891c5b30194\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":848,\"path\":\"standards/TICKETS.md\",\"quote\":\"Unclassified inherited implementation blocks closure\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/TICKETS.md#TICKETS%2F6.%20Implementation%20migration%2FStrategy%20requirements\",\"start_line\":848}],\"statement\":\"inside_out_hard_break requires a full best-guess interface inventory, deepest-source-outward break sequence, old seam intentionally severed by each break and expected negative proof per break. fundamental_re_adoption requires explicit human product-authority selection; comparison with bounded evolution across product value, feedback latency, authority risk, reversibility, total cost and retained predecessor semantics; bounded abort/re-entry; sideways reference/prior implementation boundary as source material; module/interface adjudication surface; and carry_across, redundant or rewrite classification of every inherited module/interface/carrier/projection/proof surface. Unclassified inherited implementation blocks closure.\",\"uncertainty\":\"The exact meanings of carry_across, redundant and rewrite are deferred to unsupplied SPEC_METHOD §7.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:1928a54747114176a43ff2cad892629a","key":1508,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:cb3b17a0446b24effc009acc33282fd6\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:03245c6904f417787ce80ebcc3bf7f00\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:1928a54747114176a43ff2cad892629a\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"Applies to every implementation migration ticket, irrespective of adopted profiles.\"],\"exceptions\":[\"A third local rebuild may proceed with consume, extend, or a linked explicit do-not-commonise design decision in library_rationale.\",\"Outside recurrence rules and current-claim hard stops, a discovered pattern is repricing input and blocks no bounded claim or requires no follow-up ticket unless its owning authority admits the follow-up.\"],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":879,\"path\":\"standards/TICKETS.md\",\"quote\":\"the second\\ncredible recurrence forces an explicit\\nlibrary or commonisation review; the third local rebuild is not acceptable\\nby default.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/TICKETS.md#TICKETS%2F6.%20Implementation%20migration%2FRecurring%20realisation%20and%20library%20declaration\",\"start_line\":858}],\"statement\":\"Second credible recurrence forces explicit library/commonisation review. If review establishes the same realisation pattern in two module boundaries or tickets, a third local rebuild blocks implementation absent a stated exception. Preferred order is boundary-local cleanup, then tenant-local reusable surface, then shared/common propagation only through separate design re-entry. DESIGN_MODULE adopters additionally apply §10's design-review/candidate refinement without a rival threshold. Patterns discovered during active work remain subject to these thresholds.\",\"uncertainty\":\"The external commonisation-candidate refinement is not supplied.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:1252fdc143839a7e388e18070a72ed83","key":1509,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:2269e5c21dad5030dba9012113f88134\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:cb3b17a0446b24effc009acc33282fd6\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:1252fdc143839a7e388e18070a72ed83\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"The same work item is processed across several tenants; backlog and active tickets are reviewed.\"],\"exceptions\":[\"Tenant-local reopening/repricing/successor work may require upstream change when the upstream source/product/design ticket itself must change.\"],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":890,\"path\":\"standards/TICKETS.md\",\"quote\":\"each tenant ticket has its\\nown proof surface and closure law;\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/TICKETS.md#TICKETS%2F6.%20Implementation%20migration%2FMulti-build-tenant%20review\",\"start_line\":885}],\"statement\":\"Review checks a separate suffixed ticket and named build_tenant for every tenant, separate proof surface/closure law, no substitution of one tenant's green proof for another's closure, and tenant-local reopening, repricing and successor work subject to the upstream-change exception.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:5dceae00d66efb38a2daa33befe53456","key":1510,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:cb3b17a0446b24effc009acc33282fd6\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:5dceae00d66efb38a2daa33befe53456\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"Core-interface or carrier migration for the recommended Functional Review Criteria section.\"],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":930,\"path\":\"standards/TICKETS.md\",\"quote\":\"Passing tests do not satisfy this section by themselves.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/TICKETS.md#TICKETS%2F6.%20Implementation%20migration%2FReview%20disambiguation\",\"start_line\":926}],\"statement\":\"Migration must be concrete enough that rename/adapter/wrapper/happy-path proof cannot claim source-truth replacement. A core-interface/carrier ticket should include ticket-specific Functional Review Criteria enabling review of: control-flow meaning replaced by admitted carrier/algebra/event truth; semantic centre actually reduced/removed rather than relocated; typed/closed carrier/contract/transition rather than open dict/string/config protocol; main step as pure admitted-truth transform rather than procedural law; effects at the edge; consumers directly reading admitted carrier rather than reconstructing from payloads/.get/defaults/text/legacy files; projections derived without independent closure authority; deterministic gates, if present, informing state without structurally blocking lawful constructive/probabilistic paths; and explicit reuse/extension where the pattern exists elsewhere. Tests alone do not suffice. Preserved semantic centres behind wrappers, adapter policy, old lists alongside algebra, fallback configuration or rehydrated dictionaries fail review despite green public behaviour.\",\"uncertainty\":\"Review questions retain their recommended framing and do not establish answers for any implementation.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:14d2020f8350f548659e9a6e0fa3b303","key":1511,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:f23081711b22632f373f64aaaeca6452\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:cb3b17a0446b24effc009acc33282fd6\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:14d2020f8350f548659e9a6e0fa3b303\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"Core-interface, carrier or authoritative-contract migration.\"],\"exceptions\":[\"A deferred interface names its successor ticket or stays unchecked.\",\"Compatibility shims qualify only if explicitly justified as retained compatibility.\"],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":965,\"path\":\"standards/TICKETS.md\",\"quote\":\"a checked box asserts truth on the current tree, not\\nintended direction;\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/TICKETS.md#TICKETS%2F6.%20Implementation%20migration%2FImpacted%20interface%20review%20checklist\",\"start_line\":956}],\"statement\":\"The checklist must exist before tests serve as closure evidence and name every relevant live interface. It should enumerate where present source-carrier builders; closure/register/projection builders; deepest semantic kernel/adapters; wrappers and bootstrap/replay/ingest/resume/query entrypoints; prompt/report/projection/read models; constructor/materialisation paths; proof lanes and negative fixtures. Each item states interface-specific closure, such as consuming admitted projection without helper authority, exposing read models without rebuilding missing publication, or avoiding independent closure from open payload aggregation. A false checked item makes the ticket not closure-ready. Hard-break checklists describe seam inventory before test closure evidence; re-adoption checklists explicitly cover inherited carried/dropped/rewritten modules/interfaces, never implicit carry-forward.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:8acfd522260deaead7f10fafbfb2f732","key":1512,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:cb3b17a0446b24effc009acc33282fd6\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:915b70c152b3bc925415246921bfbaad\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:8acfd522260deaead7f10fafbfb2f732\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"Migration touches a core interface; a closure map additionally applies when several old interfaces exist.\"],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":994,\"path\":\"standards/TICKETS.md\",\"quote\":\"Reviewers treat these as explicit defects:\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/TICKETS.md#TICKETS%2F6.%20Implementation%20migration%2FBreak%20order%20and%20break-to-closure%20map\",\"start_line\":987}],\"statement\":\"The ticket includes the source-outward ordered execution section and, for several old interfaces, the break-to-closure map. Explicit defects include typed wrappers retaining old semantic authority; a new carrier beside an old authoritative read model; proxies/partial implementations retaining old interfaces under new names; constructor/replay/ingest/resume/bootstrap/public-wrapper admission bypass; projections/tests passing without the new carrier; fallback invention of policy/identity/target/closure truth; and downstream proof passing while upstream source-carrier work remains open.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:ae1bdab94ab0979e0c0351ac0cddcdf1","key":1513,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:cb3b17a0446b24effc009acc33282fd6\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:f23081711b22632f373f64aaaeca6452\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:ae1bdab94ab0979e0c0351ac0cddcdf1\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[\"Explicitly specified retained compatibility permits an old path.\",\"Deterministically routed non-overlapping scope outside affected scope does not block migration merely because its path works.\"],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1023,\"path\":\"standards/TICKETS.md\",\"quote\":\"positive behaviour proof is not enough.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/TICKETS.md#TICKETS%2F6.%20Implementation%20migration%2FMixed-state%20negative%20proof\",\"start_line\":998}],\"statement\":\"Positive behaviour proof alone is insufficient. The proof surface should include at least one negative/structural proof that the old path cannot satisfy closure. Examples include rejecting a severed seam before downstream repair counts as progress; fail-closed advancement/closure/prompts/projection without new carrier; rejecting legacy payloads instead of rehydrating truth; deliberate old/new disagreement resolved to new truth or fail-closed; rejecting same-name but structurally different carrier/function/route/policy/projection; and closure proof independent of undeclared fixtures or mutable sibling workspaces. Old normal execution in affected scope or reachability on claimed acceptance path keeps the ticket open absent the compatibility exception. With an interface checklist, negative proof exercises named public consumers material to closure; bypassing one shim is insufficient when live authority already bypasses it through helpers/loaders/rebuild paths.\",\"uncertainty\":\"The 'should include' proof-count recommendation is not strengthened into a universal numerical obligation.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:862387e7e619d4cd1580b063dc8e5f40","key":1514,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:5709d600fd5dda035a513b9a6af281e8\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:8f4f294b4aae61d03f01fb3afff526a8\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:862387e7e619d4cd1580b063dc8e5f40\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1033,\"path\":\"standards/TICKETS.md\",\"quote\":\"a constructor's self-review is construction\\noutput\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/TICKETS.md#TICKETS%2F7.%20Authority%2C%20judgment%2C%20closure%20and%20state\",\"start_line\":1027}],\"statement\":\"The source assigns generic independent assessment to tier-1 EVALUATION §3, acceptance as decision-owner disposition and condition-based rather than reviewer-approved closure to EVALUATION §5, and closed-result reuse to ACTIVATION §7. Constructor self-review is construction output; this member states work-carrier consequences without taking ownership of those generic laws.\",\"uncertainty\":\"Full generic laws are absent from the supplied source.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:38057e1cf303c7d7af9c90187a2deee0","key":1515,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:5709d600fd5dda035a513b9a6af281e8\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:4d57b8a26f85d45964bb1e7f57caf9e8\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:04e341b6732269d66c8ea0de2a25c61d\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:d852d15950483fab7f616afd7b72e49a\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:38057e1cf303c7d7af9c90187a2deee0\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[\"Independent assessment is not required for every local implementation step.\",\"A governing basis may add independent-assessment boundaries.\"],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1091,\"path\":\"standards/TICKETS.md\",\"quote\":\"Self-review remains useful authoring evidence and cannot be relabelled as\\nindependent.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/TICKETS.md#TICKETS%2F7.%20Authority%2C%20judgment%2C%20closure%20and%20state%2FExecution%20and%20verification%20authority%20separation%20%28UP-007%29\",\"start_line\":1048}],\"statement\":\"Independent review is required at product, qualification, release and explicitly risk-bearing boundaries claiming it. Required reviews identify exact subject/basis/scope/exclusions/evidence/verdict/unresolved findings, and findings cite current authority plus code/proof paths rather than historical commentary alone. Human acceptance/rejection cannot make self-review independent. Claimed review supports promotion/closure only with durable exact subject/verdict traceability in existing ticket/commentary/qualification/release evidence; occurrence statements, unbound summaries and unavailable drafts are not verdicts. Verdicts stay within exact claim/hard stops; external EVALUATION §5 owns blocking findings and no trigger is added here. Human rulings receive durable disposition before the next affected acceptance boundary, keep source wording separate, and cannot be widened or discharged merely by opening a ticket. Where agentic construction applies, active work identifies selected basis, bounded affected relations, delegated construction/assessment authority and re-entry; references to existing design/evidence may suffice. Ticket state/prose/admitted contract cannot widen basis or replace required live-surface assessment. Existing ticket/commentary/commit/qualification/release carriers may hold transition evidence; no extra receipt, state, document, round or ceremony is required.\",\"uncertainty\":\"Independence protocol, finding hard stops and agentic execution semantics remain external.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:1749a5daeb057b2df05aa9ca3aeec6db","key":1516,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:aabfdedf155e1d5d7cde30038f43af26\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:4d57b8a26f85d45964bb1e7f57caf9e8\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:1749a5daeb057b2df05aa9ca3aeec6db\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[\"Required independent assessment must acquire sufficient exact evidence and supply its own independent judgment; reusing author J does not meet independence.\"],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1134,\"path\":\"standards/TICKETS.md\",\"quote\":\"a new\\nrole or conversation alone invalidates nothing.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/TICKETS.md#TICKETS%2F7.%20Authority%2C%20judgment%2C%20closure%20and%20state%2FRecorded%20judgment%20and%20owner-ruling%20continuity\",\"start_line\":1111}],\"statement\":\"Later roles/runs recover judgments and check applicability rather than reauthor unchanged conclusions. Changed material facts/evidence, declared revising observation or basis invalidate affected results; preserve originals and successor links, retaining only demonstrably independent results and reassessing affected scope. Current C may be referenced but unknown facts cannot become established premises by reuse. Owner rulings are reused without widening or asking unchanged authority again; new ambiguity or material decision change returns only the affected question to owner. J is not O; recording either creates no admission, acceptance, effects or continuation beyond grant. Results follow selected run/sprint/ticket and named evidence-surface lifetime, without a separate registry, ticket per judgment or extra approval ceremony.\",\"uncertainty\":\"Full C/J/O annotation and generic reuse definitions are external.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:a02d60f2393b5dc8a1a2b8225c6c1458","key":1517,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:da227221d3a03ed5c7408ecfff63e6d4\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:2306f4e60feb709f5c67ca75a73c1690\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:4d57b8a26f85d45964bb1e7f57caf9e8\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:a02d60f2393b5dc8a1a2b8225c6c1458\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1179,\"path\":\"standards/TICKETS.md\",\"quote\":\"An evaluation that was not performed has no result.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/TICKETS.md#TICKETS%2F7.%20Authority%2C%20judgment%2C%20closure%20and%20state%2FRecorded%20judgment%20and%20owner-ruling%20continuity\",\"start_line\":1172}],\"statement\":\"Repricing gives each affected obligation a retained/superseded/deferred/withdrawn disposition with owner and evidence in the same carrier; preserves surviving work, explains changed dependencies and does not copy unaffected history to parallel ledgers. Present owner decisions as short consequence deltas with original ruling separate; generic continuation does not accept undisclosed architecture/scope change. Performed repricing evaluation retains decision/state/evidence and all applicable failure grounds: established requires exact owner authority/evidence/conditions and surviving-obligation preservation; falsified requires a counterexample including exceeding grant or violating obligation; indeterminate retains undecided condition/needed evidence; out_of_frame retains undeclared material relation/capability; invalid_basis covers absent/stale/ambiguous/mismatched required basis. No performed evaluation means no result. Evaluation grants no decision authority; only authorized owner act changes state. Lawful deferral may satisfy repricing while delivery remains failed/outstanding. Unauthorized withdrawn cannot close; retention or satisfied repricing proves no delivery; supersession/deferral/withdrawal erase no unresolved obligation/evidence.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:da2ad442842cb8a26eac55511d93c834","key":1518,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:8f4f294b4aae61d03f01fb3afff526a8\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:c91d96dbd8d81139a3066db234ad87a7\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:d852d15950483fab7f616afd7b72e49a\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:da2ad442842cb8a26eac55511d93c834\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[\"Where applicable law requires neither independent review nor reserved acceptance, recording without review follows the referenced existing-carrier route; sprint-close and applicable design-profile law still apply.\"],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1215,\"path\":\"standards/TICKETS.md\",\"quote\":\"evidence presence alone is not satisfaction.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/TICKETS.md#TICKETS%2F7.%20Authority%2C%20judgment%2C%20closure%20and%20state%2FCondition-based%20closure%20and%20reuse\",\"start_line\":1188}],\"statement\":\"Completion requires every applicable declared obligation satisfied by valid exact-subject/basis/scope evidence, every required judgment/ruling present and applicable, and no active non-closure condition. Unknown applicability or insufficient evidence for a mandatory obligation withholds dependent claim; the existing owner decides reserved acceptance. This is the referenced conjunction with obligations as required coverage, and SPEC_METHOD applies it over change spans. Review evaluates conditions but is not the closing event. Unchanged obligations reuse valid evidence/J/O. Material counterexamples, changed evidence, declared J revising observations and changed basis invalidate affected claim/dependent results before further reliance. Unrelated observations remain bounded repricing input and neither automatically reopen satisfied claims nor expand work. Closure recording preserves exact evaluated scope, satisfied conditions, evidence and residuals.\",\"uncertainty\":\"Full conjunction and recording-without-review protocols are external.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:f51ce65446df591261a8f5b596bfcb6c","key":1519,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:e17862272f51f8550d5988e9dad8fcd0\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:d852d15950483fab7f616afd7b72e49a\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:5f68ddf5dc5c4ea4e2e1746d8627d2d6\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:f51ce65446df591261a8f5b596bfcb6c\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1261,\"path\":\"standards/TICKETS.md\",\"quote\":\"The code is never the arbiter of a\\ntest's expected result when code and test disagree\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/TICKETS.md#TICKETS%2F7.%20Authority%2C%20judgment%2C%20closure%20and%20state%2FTest%20case%20authority\",\"start_line\":1236}],\"statement\":\"Tests derive no authority from implementation. Acceptance predicates require an applicable supported entry/state and obligation under governing operating/threat model; existing tests authorize no excluded threat or superseded guard. Changed responsibility requires predicate audit and retirement of unsupported expectations under owner basis, without invented replacement guards. Live-authority conflict requires re-entry, not test waiver. For code/test mismatch after a ticket fix, reconcile in order: (1) ticket intent/class/re-entry/target/superseded truth/closure/evaluation/non-closure fields; (2) triage and lawful owner re-entry; (3) governing requirement/design/module/function/carrier/other authority; (4) test expectation; (5) implementation. Code may reveal stale/incomplete/narrow tests but cannot alone authorize expectation changes. Updating/removing a pre-repricing test requires named governing ticket and superseding authority change. Stale/ambiguous/under-authorized ticket re-enters triage before code or test is treated correct. A passing test is closure evidence only with expectation traced to admitted ticket and authority chain.\",\"uncertainty\":\"ASSURANCE §3's general law is not supplied.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:5b4e42ae0aa4932dd14cdf733059707b","key":1520,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:d852d15950483fab7f616afd7b72e49a\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:c91d96dbd8d81139a3066db234ad87a7\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:6df0210aa0cfac994dc829752b179bc7\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:ee3c8b088a7f0259a14a11460fb344f1\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:5b4e42ae0aa4932dd14cdf733059707b\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1275,\"path\":\"standards/TICKETS.md\",\"quote\":\"Contradiction between the owning ticket, its required milestones, the\\ncurrent goals or the cited acceptance evidence blocks closure.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/TICKETS.md#TICKETS%2F7.%20Authority%2C%20judgment%2C%20closure%20and%20state%2FOne-truth%20state%20projection%20and%20drift%20refusal%20%28UP-009%29\",\"start_line\":1272}],\"statement\":\"One work-state authority chain assigns bounded wave to goals, ticket state to ticket, subordinate milestone state to milestone authority, and realisation decisions to accepted design. Projection recency/visibility/repetition confers no truth. Contradictions among owning ticket, required milestones, current goals or cited acceptance evidence block closure. Superseded evidence remains history and must not appear as current acceptance.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:efbf0d91fb46f1e13701ebb98fcc489f","key":1521,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:75612f6702a23f4a631eb371f4aa0a2d\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:7c694b903339568539f5073b033755b9\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:efbf0d91fb46f1e13701ebb98fcc489f\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":126,\"path\":\"standards/TRAVERSAL_OCCURRENCE.md\",\"quote\":\"It defines no process scheduler, event-log carrier, state store, workspace\\nformat, rollback mechanism, actor topology or prospective reference-frame\\nprofile\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/TRAVERSAL_OCCURRENCE.md#TRAVERSAL_OCCURRENCE%2FScope\",\"start_line\":124}],\"statement\":\"The profile supplies none of the listed scheduler/log/store/workspace/rollback/topology/prospective-frame implementations. It is no universal execution theory and grants no mutation, admission, evaluation or decision authority. Availability does not imply adoption. Adopting Product owns subject interpretation, vocabulary mappings, authorities, requirements, design, implementation and evidence; those identities are not imported by this member.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1