on\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/TRAVERSAL_OCCURRENCE.md#TRAVERSAL_OCCURRENCE%2FPosition%2FFoundation%20to%20law\",\"start_line\":81}],\"statement\":\"F19 states: exact-basis ordinary a_c models add sorts/value domains, never record kinds; closed unknown/missing/mistyped elements refuse. Each exact application is immutable; changed-input reapplication creates a new occurrence and corrections append without erasure. Observations/events/projections describe rather than replace external subject reality; snapshot/rollback requires separate Product authorization. Effects require matching admitted grants, with functor/traversal/operation/executor/actor/grant/invocation distinct. Candidate, judgment, admitting event and materialized relation remain separate; precedence orders admitted facts without deciding authority. Cause requires admitted typed lineage; identity/causal subgraphs are acyclic so lineage walks reach first cause. Projection binds complete frontier; new event produces new frontier, never advances an old projection. Cut members share exactly one source frontier; successor equals that frontier plus exactly admitted event; missing/inconsistent members refuse; projection cannot be read beyond its frontier. Every judgment decision/stop and effect disposition for an effect-intending occurrence maps to exactly one core value for a named predicate. Undecidable effect outcome remains indeterminate; established non-attainment is falsified whether or not its end is established; no refusal maps to success.\",\"uncertainty\":\"Detailed owning clauses, complete domains and most exact result mappings are outside the supplied excerpt.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:fe68f70d8f59e774e342317d562f05f6","key":1523,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:b791117709f1f0565ea01a996a54f5e1\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:32e0954dfe17b0581711226c1b3cd946\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:2328163d8c2a7bea8aff888ec3f7378d\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:5422fc753f4b9ea1001d500422d352b2\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:fe68f70d8f59e774e342317d562f05f6\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":108,\"path\":\"standards/TRAVERSAL_OCCURRENCE.md\",\"quote\":\"Each consumer applies the rule and decides nothing the owning section does\\nnot\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/TRAVERSAL_OCCURRENCE.md#TRAVERSAL_OCCURRENCE%2FPosition%2FFoundation%20to%20law\",\"start_line\":107}],\"statement\":\"Profile policy owns closed sort/reference/event/relation/qualifier domains, occurrence identity inputs, acyclicity of identity/causal subgraphs, decision/stop/residual vocabulary and mappings, and exclusion of out_of_frame from constraint values. Product owns precedence/evaluators/authorities, admitted causal claims, event scope/frontier laws, compatible territory containment and adoption. AC-007 owns hold/gap/two refusal values, core mappings and causes; traversal-specific refinements retain parent core values. Internal consumer summaries state: defects against five closed populations refuse as falsified structural constraints; basis mismatch in model validation/structural admission carries refuse_invalid_basis; application_of targets exact application seed, corrects_event does not erase, missing seed retains hold; invokes_effect requires exact operation grant and authorized_by checks kind/target/territory; unauthorized/stale effect_readiness never dispatches; identity_depends_on and causal occurrence/event graphs are acyclic admitted cause; event_for follows declared scope law, frontier_contains is complete under one exact basis, projects_frontier binds one unchanged frontier. Named residuals include unresolved_cause, unresolved_scope, competing_lineage and stale_frontier. Not every framework event belongs to an occurrence. Representative examples/checkers are neither engines nor semantic authority. No other member applies this profile's rules; an adopting Product does. Consumers add no decisions beyond owning rules.\",\"uncertainty\":\"The referenced closed populations, judgment definitions, conformance items and refinements are not fully supplied.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:77343a3d5fd10f227cbb32e38e00e12a","key":1524,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:32e0954dfe17b0581711226c1b3cd946\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:77343a3d5fd10f227cbb32e38e00e12a\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"Signature instantiation or model validation is considered.\"],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":184,\"path\":\"standards/TRAVERSAL_OCCURRENCE.md\",\"quote\":\"Missing populations, hidden records, refs\\nambiguous between local and external, unknown record kinds and undeclared\\nfield domains refuse model validation\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/TRAVERSAL_OCCURRENCE.md#TRAVERSAL_OCCURRENCE%2FImported%20calculus%20boundary\",\"start_line\":182}],\"statement\":\"Instantiation is invalid on conflict in calculus basis, inherited field meaning, record shape, population, value/reference/relation domain, authority coordinate or refusal law. Only semantic objects use SemanticObject.value; all other families retain inherited exact record shapes/coordinates. Population_M_occ is total over and exactly equals RecordKind_ac; every fundamental record belongs to exactly one finite population and local identities are unique across the disjoint union. Every other I identity resolves once through declared external domain/basis. No new fundamental kind is added. RefDomain_Sigma_occurrence closes every identity-bearing value and inherited field to one exact local record-kind/sort or declared external target kind; qualified_field includes source sort/kind and full nested path, so same labels do not merge domains. Missing populations, hidden records, local/external ambiguity, unknown kinds and undeclared domains refuse validation.\",\"uncertainty\":\"Full inherited record definitions and the profile's finite reference-domain table are absent.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:72e73c43563bc9591ec0111273427edc","key":1525,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:32e0954dfe17b0581711226c1b3cd946\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:05cec91b956ed0b3ef183307afd15af2\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:5556c9d8858c4f3b77e26c5206499fb4\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:2328163d8c2a7bea8aff888ec3f7378d\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:e61e7e5c748d443c37e30a5b325aff71\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:0118bb401c0b96a292b49309470d55f2\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:84f335e3f21f357a51c35903945e92a1\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:d1e96f42414bc402e9fde726c0c23e81\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:dc23753029f4d1128dd4e2dbd634880a\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:38e3e0a9484edb3cff9134d451b16301\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:5422fc753f4b9ea1001d500422d352b2\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:67e19469f016aa9f5ab7518c55df3a03\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:b0dd17447a53aceb10e720510bed0a10\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:ddc9b5793eaf5a1b0c090b03651c4d48\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:bfbf00f6b8998d30c4bcb4dde0cacd45\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:dfd4d1a152e893c77ec96c35f826899e\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:17a43bd3fb2499f3995e928ea010d307\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:395a04117ba05d7d54dc87da66cda3f6\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:8406b4daa538a5ba8327a0943c030273\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:7ce6d5e8ef0b1f18effee52dfeeb907e\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:72e73c43563bc9591ec0111273427edc\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[\"Other auxiliary-domain values require a separately identified compatible signature extension.\"],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":243,\"path\":\"standards/TRAVERSAL_OCCURRENCE.md\",\"quote\":\"The value contract is closed: an\\nunknown field or a missing required field refuses structural admission\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/TRAVERSAL_OCCURRENCE.md#TRAVERSAL_OCCURRENCE%2FClosed%20semantic-object%20sorts\",\"start_line\":213}],\"statement\":\"Sigma_occurrence.Sort contains exactly the nineteen supplied core sort identities. Every row is a SemanticObject with exact id, sort, context, owner, scope and basis in addition to its closed value fields. Unknown or missing required fields refuse structural admission. Refs are exact scoped identities and content digests SHA-256; every _ref resolves exactly once under AC-003. Ref lists follow the owning signature's declared order and reject duplicates. Closed core observation_kind values are pre_effect/post_effect/external_observation; effect dispositions no_effect/completed_effect/partial_effect/refused_effect; scope classes occurrence_scoped/subject_scoped/authority_scoped. TraversalApplication, OperationKind and EffectOperation are identities, not executors. EffectOperation without exact in-model OperationKind or explicit compatible import refuses.\",\"uncertainty\":\"Reference-field target domains and compatible-extension rules beyond these statements remain external.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:4875623c9b7fe9ee860ce2de84c86380","key":1526,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:bfbf00f6b8998d30c4bcb4dde0cacd45\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:4875623c9b7fe9ee860ce2de84c86380\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[\"Non-claim-admission event kinds may carry claim fields only if a compatible extension explicitly declares them.\"],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":224,\"path\":\"standards/TRAVERSAL_OCCURRENCE.md\",\"quote\":\"`claim_ref_or_none` and `claim_judgment_ref_or_none` are both absent or\\nboth exact.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/TRAVERSAL_OCCURRENCE.md#TRAVERSAL_OCCURRENCE%2FClosed%20semantic-object%20sorts\",\"start_line\":221}],\"statement\":\"An event with scope independent of any occurrence gets no fictional occurrence merely to satisfy a total relation. Claim reference and claim-judgment reference are both absent or both exact. A claim-admission event requires both and a current source_frontier_ref. Other event kinds refuse the claim fields absent the explicit extension exception.\",\"uncertainty\":\"The closed event-kind population and extension details are not supplied.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:4e3c51a1091d82bfbde4a7afdce234a0","key":1527,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:51a45d4874435e678a2c688eedea647d\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:f4c1f471fd21f4717681cbba02bab5da\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f