on:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:1fac002a0d0acaf859ad0d6a1613903b\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":210,\"path\":\"standards/UX.md\",\"quote\":\"Those are valid concerns; they\\nbelong in product-local surfaces, not in this constitutional profile (P2).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/UX.md#UX%2F2.%20Role%20and%20composition%2FNon-goals\",\"start_line\":206}],\"statement\":\"UX profile does not supply styling/design-system specification, component library, brand/visual identity, wireframing/prototyping process, user-study method, stack ranking or framework recommendation. These valid concerns belong to Product-local surfaces.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:0139ae9e00673559bff5696e9bc13db9","key":1569,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:7a9d378573708e829488aa2ffbb49efa\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:593429f1fa25b744fdcf828e4235cd1c\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:c9843b48485016f674dd3003449d040f\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:0139ae9e00673559bff5696e9bc13db9\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"A Msg changes Product truth.\"],\"exceptions\":[\"UX-local messages may govern genuinely view-local expansion, sort, filter, focus and draft concerns.\"],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":239,\"path\":\"standards/UX.md\",\"quote\":\"If no\\nadmitted carrier exists for a product-truth-changing message, the UX\\nsurface is blocked until the carrier is authored or the requirement is\\nrepriced\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/UX.md#UX%2F3.%20Product%20truth%20and%20admitted%20carriers\",\"start_line\":214}],\"statement\":\"Every Product-truth-changing message maps to one admitted Product carrier. Such changes include asset writes/creation/moves/deletion; Context, selection authority, pinning/global state; session spawning/attachment/resumption; agent/job/workorder/graph-call/runtime-command dispatch; closure/approval/continuation/lineage/provenance/evidence; publishing/accepting/rejecting/superseding records. UX cannot become a hidden constructive carrier. Without an admitted carrier, surface is blocked until one is authored or requirement repriced.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:64a5a63086d9bef75b170a8d0c4c5208","key":1570,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:7a9d378573708e829488aa2ffbb49efa\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:c9843b48485016f674dd3003449d040f\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:64a5a63086d9bef75b170a8d0c4c5208\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"For a project selecting a realization stack.\"],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":296,\"path\":\"standards/UX.md\",\"quote\":\"Any\\nrealisation that preserves §4 to §8 is compliant with this profile.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/UX.md#UX%2F4.%20Process%20model%2FProcess%20model%20without%20stack%20mandate\",\"start_line\":265},{\"end_line\":318,\"path\":\"standards/UX.md\",\"quote\":\"A realisation is compliant with this profile when §4 to §10\\nhold under inspection and the §13 failure patterns are absent\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/UX.md#UX%2F4.%20Process%20model%2FRealisation%20discretion\",\"start_line\":311}],\"statement\":\"Project records chosen stack and short justification in design module. Each discretionary choice must preserve §4 Elm model and §6 membrane. Process model is non-negotiable, stack free within it; profile tests realizations and never ranks frameworks. One clause tests §4–§8; Realisation discretion tests §4–§10 under inspection plus absence of §13 failures. Source explicitly retains this difference for governing authority and refers to §15's stricter fail-closed selection. Reject view-owned state continuation, render effects, state mutation outside typed reducer, multi-step view state machines bypassing Msg, two-way binding without Msg, imperative DOM manipulation in render and handlers used as controllers. Non-normative examples are language-integrated reducers, typed reducer plus effect interpreter, reactive signals behind reducer with no external signal mutation, and server-rendered hypermedia using server derivation and request/response effect boundary; examples confer no compliance verdict.\",\"uncertainty\":\"Full §13 and §15 are absent; no implementation's compliance is evaluated.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:65fe28c7940fc5ec87e25232878bf53f","key":1571,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:7a9d378573708e829488aa2ffbb49efa\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:c9843b48485016f674dd3003449d040f\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:65fe28c7940fc5ec87e25232878bf53f\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[\"Sub algebra is required when subscribing to external or runtime events.\"],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":358,\"path\":\"standards/UX.md\",\"quote\":\"A lost or failed transport reply alone\\nestablishes neither completion nor non-completion.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/UX.md#UX%2F5.%20State%20transitions\",\"start_line\":322}],\"statement\":\"Surface declares State shape, Msg algebra, pure Update:(Msg,State)→(State,Cmd), Cmd algebra and conditional Sub algebra. State changes through typed Msg reduction. Each Cmd names effect kind, typed input, admitted carrier/external target, typed outcome Msg family covering every materially possible observed or unresolved result including success/failure, outcome-selection evidence and observations resolving uncertainty, and any required deterministic correlation among Cmd, invocation, outcome messages and replay. Outcome Msg represents available evidence; intended-effect meanings completed, not_effected, completion_unknown answer 'the intended effect occurred' without replacing Product message vocabulary. Lost/failed transport alone proves neither completion nor non-completion; sufficient independent observation may decide, otherwise Msg and State retain completion_unknown, correlation and missing observation. Reducer performs no I/O, side-channel logging or global mutation; runtime interprets effects at membrane.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:87673ea216f1bf2d4e3e4d3cc77989a8","key":1572,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:b3ee6d135ca780f28776d4755a5fbf1b\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:c9843b48485016f674dd3003449d040f\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:7a9d378573708e829488aa2ffbb49efa\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:87673ea216f1bf2d4e3e4d3cc77989a8\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":396,\"path\":\"standards/UX.md\",\"quote\":\"Recovery is an\\nexplicit Cmd/Msg interaction, not hidden membrane continuation\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/UX.md#UX%2F6.%20Effect%20membrane\",\"start_line\":372}],\"statement\":\"Effects are isolated to declared membrane. It interprets reducer-produced Cmd and returns outcomes through Msg; branching, conditional state derivation and multi-step business decisions belong in reducer. One declared Cmd is interpreted per effect. Unresolved outcome returns typed unresolved Msg without coercion to success/failure. Before repetition or dependent effect whose safety depends on outcome, Product observes owning state and follows referenced recovery with current authority/territory retained; recovery is explicit Cmd/Msg. Any useEffect/createEffect/onMount/subscribe/server-action or other handler belongs to membrane only when interpreting a declared Cmd. A handler deciding transitions violates the law; move that logic to reducer. Render, render helpers and reducer have no I/O, subscription or imperative platform manipulation.\",\"uncertainty\":\"Full ACTIVATION recovery law is referenced but absent.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:d01e00b8535fa22e955445eb22b82f1f","key":1573,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:7a9d378573708e829488aa2ffbb49efa\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:593429f1fa25b744fdcf828e4235cd1c\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:2baee2e53c0d830eab71c96035503953\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:d01e00b8535fa22e955445eb22b82f1f\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"When Product publishes typed AssetSurface contracts under graph-execution carrier law and Product design.\"],\"exceptions\":[\"Without AssetSurface, the design module names an equivalent typed contract and applies the same law.\"],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":422,\"path\":\"standards/UX.md\",\"quote\":\"Absence of an admitted\\ncontract blocks product-truth-changing UX actions\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/UX.md#UX%2F7.%20Carrier%20binding\",\"start_line\":400}],\"statement\":\"Bind one or more AssetSurface contracts as data sources/action targets. State derives from their projections without local asset-shape redeclaration. Truth-changing Msg variants map one-to-one to action-registry entries or documented projection wrappers with no hidden semantic change. UX-local variants remain local concerns. Selection emits Context update/equivalent consistent with selection contract. Writes use action registry, never direct file/service calls. Shared typed contract is ground truth on both sides; no admitted equivalent contract means truth-changing actions are blocked.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:bb790d5b5e9ac86b1c3fc329e73b2d63","key":1574,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:7a9d378573708e829488aa2ffbb49efa\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:593429f1fa25b744fdcf828e4235cd1c\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:5364ed6b537f501c3e9da24b34e62cd8\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:bb790d5b5e9ac86b1c3fc329e73b2d63\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"For source-described prompt construction for UI/operator-surface work.\"],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":435,\"path\":\"standards/UX.md\",\"quote\":\"If the prompt cannot identify that\\ncarrier and action path, the correct result is a block or re-entry, not\\nlocal UI invention\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/UX.md#UX%2F7.%20Carrier%20binding\",\"start_line\":424}],\"statement\":\"A UI/operator work prompt carries needed governing UX law using a current derived surface/projected frame where suitable, otherwise deciding sections directly, rather than requiring raw-member rediscovery. If work changes Product truth through UI, prompt names admitted carrier and action path; failure to identify them yields block/re-entry rather than local invention. This is a represented prompt-processing requirement, not an instruction to execute that workflow here.\",\"uncertainty\":\"Acquisition mechanics are owned by absent ACTIVATION §2.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:a4a1f3a0571c982d240915fb015df0ab","key":1575,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:c9843b48485016f674dd3003449d040f\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:7a9d378573708e829488aa2ffbb49efa\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:38bc94913c88b810c504dd4ecae182ca\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:a4a1f3a0571c982d240915fb015df0ab\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":456,\"path\":\"standards/UX.md\",\"quote\":\"A view does not:\\n\\n- decide on its own what the next state will be after a user event;\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/UX.md#UX%2F8.%20Continuation%20and%20replay\",\"start_line\":439}],\"statement\":\"Runtime owns continuation; view owns none. All transitions use declared Msg interpreted by reducer. View cannot independently decide next state, chain local updates without separate Msg emissions or hide inter-event state in refs, closures or module variables. A needed multi-step machine belongs in reducer State with explicit phase Msg; view projects the phase. Inability to replay behavior from Msg log against empty State indicates leaked view continuation.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:8c8a167c1fde72c63efa7c2fb21b751e","key":1576,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:38bc94913c88b810c504dd4ecae182ca\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:7a9d378573708e829488aa2ffbb49efa\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:8c8a167c1fde72c63efa7c2fb21b751e\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"Before a Product UX surface claims closure under the profile.\"],\"exceptions\":[\"A pure projection-only surface may use a no-effect proof.\"],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":498,\"path\":\"standards/UX.md\",\"quote\":\"`replay_passes` can coexist with `completion_unknown` for the\\neffect predicate\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/UX.md#UX%2F8.%20Continuation%20and%20replay%2FMsg-replay%20proof\",\"start_line\":460}],\"statement\":\"Require at least one executable replay proof per Product-meaningful interaction family, with all six declared proof components. Correctness depending on unrepresented DOM state; mutable refs/module variables/closures/timers/handler memory; network/file results bypassing Msg; or local state affecting Product after unmount/replay fails proof. Where effect may be unresolved, cover correlated unresolved Msg, retained State and recovery, including no outcome-dependent repeat before required observation. Reproducing that State proves only replay, never external completion: replay_passes and completion_unknown may coexist. Projection-only no-effect proof can be Msg log, final State and empty Cmd sequence.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:7598c50552d1d8f9cd86daf797a954a6","key":1577,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:7a9d378573708e829488aa2ffbb49efa\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:c9843b48485016f674dd3003449d040f\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:7598c50552d1d8f9cd86daf797a954a6\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[\"Out-of-render mutation is excepted from the cited §6 violation when part of declared membrane, such as a design-module-named imperative-interop platform handle.\"],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":519,\"path\":\"standards/UX.md\",\"quote\":\"- declares its consumed inputs explicitly;\\n- does not capture mutable state in closures across renders;\\n- does not read from sources outside its declared input.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/UX.md#UX%2F9.%20View%20shape\",\"start_line\":502}],\"statement\":\"View accepts typed State/props/context, returns typed ViewTree, declares every consumed input, captures no mutable cross-render closure state and reads no undeclared source. Function/component/template/server handler/signal expression/other framework shape is a recorded stack decision; constitutional State→ViewTree and no body side effects remain. An effect-handler-written ref read during rendering violates §6 unless covered by the narrow declared-membrane exception.\",\"uncertainty\":\"The membrane-handle exception does not expressly waive typed inputs, declared reads or replay requirements.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:b8ebcf3303ae97dad6b4b273f3cebbdf","key":1578,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:2baee2e53c0d830eab71c96035503953\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:7a9d378573708e829488aa2ffbb49efa\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:b8ebcf3303ae97dad6b4b273f3cebbdf\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"At every untrusted or out-of-process seam.\"],\"exceptions\":[\"UX-local types may describe view-local concerns but cannot shadow back-end types.\"],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":544,\"path\":\"standards/UX.md\",\"quote\":\"Runtime validation is mandatory at every untrusted or out-of-process seam\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/UX.md#UX%2F10.%20Type%20sharing\",\"start_line\":523}],\"statement\":\"Import UX-consumed/back-end shapes from shared front/back contract rather than redeclaring them; same package or contracts/ package is typical, not mandatory. Runtime validation is obligatory for HTTP/RPC responses, MCP payloads, file-loaded records, websocket/event streams, agent/worker outputs and URL/storage/clipboard/browser integration payloads. One typed-schema definition produces compile-time types and runtime validators; mechanism is project-local. Compile-time TypeScript alone is insufficient. View-local form drafts, sort enums and filter strings may have local types without shadowing back-end types.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:77b14a2cd014d3c961415d7c5150f1bc","key":1579,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:254e32e899936a647b4a4ae7b911dd86\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:f07b5194dc5c79f56d598c615a03f3b1\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:77b14a2cd014d3c961415d7c5150f1bc\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"The UX surface is the public face of a product capability.\"],\"exceptions\":[\"Accessibility is optional for internal-only debug surfaces, with the exemption recorded in the design module.\"],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":566,\"path\":\"standards/UX.md\",\"quote\":\"- semantic structure (heading levels, landmarks, lists, or\\n  platform-equivalent affordances);\\n- keyboard or platform-equivalent navigability for every action that has\\n  a pointer interaction;\\n- focus management on dynamic content changes;\\n- accessibility annotations for any custom interactive element that lacks\\n  a native semantic equivalent;\\n- colour contrast at the project's declared accessibility standard (WCAG\\n  AA is the recommended default for web).\\n\\nAccessibility is not optional for product capabilities. It is optional\\nfor internal-only debug surfaces, and the design module records the\\nexemption (P2, P6). This section is intentionally minimal. Projects with\\nstricter accessibility obligations (regulated industry, public-sector\\nprocurement) author a project-local accessibility refinement and cite it\\nfrom their design modules (P2).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/UX.md#UX%2F11.%20Accessibility%20minimum\",\"start_line\":551}],\"statement\":\"Declare semantic structure or platform equivalents; keyboard or platform-equivalent navigation for every pointer action; focus management for dynamic changes; annotations for every custom interactive element lacking native semantics; and contrast at the project's declared standard. WCAG AA is a recommended web default, not an unconditional mandate. Projects with stricter obligations author a local accessibility refinement and cite it from design modules.\",\"uncertainty\":\"Other supplied sections mention recorded public-surface exemptions; their relationship to this section's non-optional language is retained as a residual.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:df924d63a6cd5f43c2500101b50e3609","key":1580,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:ac03acbc25d43f1c4cec70fe0b4cab0a\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:f07b5194dc5c79f56d598c615a03f3b1\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:df924d63a6cd5f43c2500101b50e3609\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"Product authority adopts the profile for a project.\"],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":586,\"path\":\"standards/UX.md\",\"quote\":\"1. naming the profile in the project's UX-related design modules;\\n2. recording the realisation stack choice (§4 Realisation discretion) and\\n   the justification;\\n3. declaring the irreducible architectural carrier set and the structural\\n   carrier diagram the design profile requires (DESIGN_MODULE §6 and §7);\\n4. declaring the State, Msg, Update, Cmd and Sub shapes for each UX\\n   surface in the design module before implementation;\\n5. declaring the AssetSurface or equivalent typed-contract bindings (§7)\\n   the surface consumes and emits to;\\n6. naming the effect-membrane mechanism (§6) and the Cmd algebra it\\n   interprets;\\n7. naming the executable Msg-replay proof surface required by §8;\\n8. naming any §11 accessibility refinement the project requires;\\n9. noting any §9 view-shape or §6 effect-membrane exemptions explicitly.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/UX.md#UX%2F12.%20Adoption\",\"start_line\":573}],\"statement\":\"Record the profile name, chosen realisation stack and justification, irreducible architectural carrier set and required structural diagram, State/Msg/Update/Cmd/Sub shapes for each surface before implementation, consumed and emitted AssetSurface or equivalent typed-contract bindings, effect-membrane mechanism and interpreted Cmd algebra, executable Msg-replay proof surface, required accessibility refinements and explicit view-shape/effect-membrane exemptions.\",\"uncertainty\":\"The referenced UX §§1, 4, 6–9 and DESIGN_MODULE §§6–7 are not supplied in full.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:b2ee3ea9c8630dbf7cfb3340686a9952","key":1581,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:254e32e899936a647b4a4ae7b911dd86\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:ac03acbc25d43f1c4cec70fe0b4cab0a\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:b2ee3ea9c8630dbf7cfb3340686a9952\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"Any one trigger holds: reachable from product shell; used as proof for a ticket, requirement, design module, release or review; can mutate product truth; can spawn, attach, resume or dispatch work; or can change Context, selection authority, closure, continuation, evidence or provenance.\"],\"exceptions\":[\"A scaffold, prototype, debug pane or temporary proof surface can be exempt only with the specified record.\"],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":603,\"path\":\"standards/UX.md\",\"quote\":\"A UX surface is governed by this profile by default when any of these are\\ntrue (P6, P5):\\n\\n- it is reachable from the product shell;\\n- it is used as proof for a ticket, requirement, design module, release or\\n  review;\\n- it can mutate product truth;\\n- it can spawn, attach, resume or dispatch work;\\n- it can change Context, selection authority, closure, continuation,\\n  evidence or provenance.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/UX.md#UX%2F12.%20Adoption%2FScaffold%20and%20exemption\",\"start_line\":594}],\"statement\":\"Any listed trigger brings a surface under the profile by default.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:496aeeabaf67e1abe4e61c1a5030372a","key":1582,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:254e32e899936a647b4a4ae7b911dd86\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:f07b5194dc5c79f56d598c615a03f3b1\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:496aeeabaf67e1abe4e61c1a5030372a\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"A scaffold, prototype, debug pane or temporary proof surface claims exemption.\"],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":618,\"path\":\"standards/UX.md\",\"quote\":\"A scaffold, prototype, debug pane or temporary proof surface may be\\nexempt only when the design module or ticket records (P6, P4b):\\n\\n- the exemption scope;\\n- the permitted operations;\\n- whether mutation is forbidden or explicitly bounded;\\n- a visible scaffold or debug label where user-facing;\\n- the authoritative surface that will supersede it;\\n- the retirement condition and owning ticket;\\n- the non-closure condition preventing release if the scaffold remains.\\n\\nAn exempt scaffold cannot become the production UX by accumulation. It is\\nretired, repriced into a governed UX surface, or kept outside product\\nclosure (P4b, P6).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/UX.md#UX%2F12.%20Adoption%2FScaffold%20and%20exemption\",\"start_line\":605}],\"statement\":\"The design module or ticket must record scope, permitted operations, forbidden or explicitly bounded mutation, visible scaffold/debug label when user-facing, authoritative replacement, retirement condition and owning ticket, and a non-closure condition preventing release while the scaffold remains. An exempt scaffold cannot become production UX by accumulation: retire it, reprice it into governed UX or keep it outside product closure.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:cf0fd0fdd58e88c9c99baa48c55da5fa","key":1583,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:fba38b75e6777b991248c792e3cacb39\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:cf0fd0fdd58e88c9c99baa48c55da5fa\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"Any non-escrowable change appears during a UX sprint.\"],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":655,\"path\":\"standards/UX.md\",\"quote\":\"If one of those appears, the sprint records the finding and the work\\nexits the UX sprint path through standalone repricing or sprint\\nsupersession. The UX layer still does not become the hidden constructive\\ncarrier (P6; §3).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/UX.md#UX%2F12.%20Adoption%2FUX%20sprint%20compliance%20escrow\",\"start_line\":652}],\"statement\":\"Record the finding and exit the UX sprint path through standalone repricing or sprint supersession; the UX layer cannot become a hidden constructive carrier.\",\"uncertainty\":\"Generic escrow law and close mechanics belong to unsupplied TICKETS §3; SPEC_METHOD §4 admits this profile statement.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:271f649683d1a142747d6760e07ba7d6","key":1584,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:fba38b75e6777b991248c792e3cacb39\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:254e32e899936a647b4a4ae7b911dd86\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:271f649683d1a142747d6760e07ba7d6\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"UX sprint close is considered or claimed.\"],\"exceptions\":[\"Explicitly recorded exemptions can cover replay or accessibility closure obligations.\",\"Explicit local paydown tickets permit close only for debt local to UX realisation and only where the governing method allows follow-up.\"],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":658,\"path\":\"standards/UX.md\",\"quote\":\"A UX sprint should close when continued iteration is more expensive or\\nless trustworthy than review. Valid close triggers include (P2, P6):\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/UX.md#UX%2F12.%20Adoption%2FUX%20sprint%20compliance%20escrow\",\"start_line\":657},{\"end_line\":683,\"path\":\"standards/UX.md\",\"quote\":\"UX sprint close is a forensic walkthrough: it reviews each changed\\nscreen, state and product-meaningful interaction against the cited\\nauthority (P6). Each finding takes one of the six classifications of\\nTICKETS §3 Close review (`accepted`, `local_paydown`, `design_reframe`,\\n`requirement_reprice`, `product_reprice`, `remove`); for a UX finding,\\n`accepted` reads as compliant with this profile and the cited design,\\nand `local_paydown` as local UX debt captured by a paydown ticket (P6,\\nP5). The sprint may close with explicit local paydown tickets only where\\nthe debt is local to UX realisation and the governing method allows\\nfollow-up. It may not close while product-truth carrier gaps, hidden\\nstate continuation or authority drift remain unclassified (P6, P4b).\\n\\nClosure under this profile for a product UX surface still requires the\\n§8 Msg-replay proof and the §11 accessibility obligations unless an\\nexplicit exemption is recorded. The sprint can defer those obligations\\nduring iteration; it cannot erase them (P4b, P6).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/UX.md#UX%2F12.%20Adoption%2FUX%20sprint%20compliance%20escrow\",\"start_line\":668}],\"statement\":\"A sprint should close when further iteration is costlier or less trustworthy than review. Valid triggers include timebox expiry, too many changed states for casual review, obsolete screenshots/walkthroughs, interaction changes beyond polish, or reviewer uncertainty requiring reconciliation. Close reviews every changed screen, state and meaningful interaction against cited authority, classifying every finding as accepted, local_paydown, design_reframe, requirement_reprice, product_reprice or remove. Accepted means profile-and-design compliant; local_paydown means local UX debt captured by ticket. Unclassified carrier gaps, hidden state continuation or authority drift prohibit close. Replay and accessibility obligations may be deferred, never erased.\",\"uncertainty\":\"The six classifications are TICKETS-owned and are not mapped by the UX result section.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:43c97761547580e308eee89061745e79","key":1585,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:254e32e899936a647b4a4ae7b911dd86\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:fba38b75e6777b991248c792e3cacb39\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:43c97761547580e308eee89061745e79\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"Any listed failure pattern is present on a surface to which the profile applies.\"],\"exceptions\":[\"The source expressly conditions view-shape and accessibility failures on absence of recorded exemptions; scaffold failure refers to its required exemption record.\"],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":687,\"path\":\"standards/UX.md\",\"quote\":\"A UX surface violates this profile when any of these are true (P6, P5):\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/UX.md#UX%2F13.%20Failure%20patterns\",\"start_line\":687},{\"end_line\":725,\"path\":\"standards/UX.md\",\"quote\":\"Any of these is a violation of this profile. Repeated violations are not\\nnormalised by usage; they are repaired or the surface is repriced (P6,\\nP4b).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/UX.md#UX%2F13.%20Failure%20patterns\",\"start_line\":723}],\"statement\":\"Each independently constitutes a violation: render code directly mutates state/props/context; view-local cells carry product meaning rather than ephemera; effect-handler conditional logic decides transitions; multistep state machines live in views instead of reducers; render reads mutable refs outside the declared membrane; UX-local types shadow/redeclare backend types instead of importing shared contracts; selection/action emission writes file/network without AssetSurface action; unrecorded view-shape exemption; public-capability accessibility omitted without recorded exemption; two-way binding emits no typed Msg and bypasses reducer; Cmd logic implemented imperatively inside an effect handler; behaviour unreplayable from Msg log against empty State; truth-changing message lacks admitted carrier, graph function, runtime command or typed product contract; external data enters UX state without runtime validation; reachable, mutating or proof-used scaffold/debug surface lacks §12 exemption record; local ADR/convention/existing code weakens the profile; sprint claims closure with deferred proof, accessibility, carrier, scaffold or authority debt unclassified or un-ticketed. Repetition does not normalise violations: repair or reprice.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:fd17ddd967fe93010fb3428daeff289c","key":1586,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:254e32e899936a647b4a4ae7b911dd86\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:f07b5194dc5c79f56d598c615a03f3b1\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:fd17ddd967fe93010fb3428daeff289c\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"A UX surface review is performed under the profile.\",\"The sprint-specific question applies if the work used a UX sprint.\"],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":729,\"path\":\"standards/UX.md\",\"quote\":\"A UX surface review under this profile should answer (P6, P2):\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/UX.md#UX%2F14.%20Review%20questions\",\"start_line\":729},{\"end_line\":755,\"path\":\"standards/UX.md\",\"quote\":\"If any of these cannot be answered, the design module is incomplete (P6,\\nP5).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/UX.md#UX%2F14.%20Review%20questions\",\"start_line\":754}],\"statement\":\"Review should answer: State/Msg/Update; Cmd/Sub algebra; bound contracts; truth-changing messages' admitted carriers; membrane location and interpreted Cmds; provable View=f(State) purity; Msg-log replay proof; shared-contract import of all consumed types; runtime validation of all out-of-process payloads; documented view/membrane/accessibility/scaffold/debug exemptions; chosen stack's preservation of the Elm process model; non-ownership of replay continuation by the view; design-module carrier set and structural diagram for closure; and, if a sprint was used, classification of every deferred proof/accessibility/carrier/scaffold/authority finding. Any unanswerable question makes the design module incomplete.\",\"uncertainty\":\"Answerability is not an instruction to evaluate a particular surface here.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:2c4a61a3aee70ca6b01811102a83e20a","key":1587,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:0248d4f244332b39c63670566a866da5\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:2c4a61a3aee70ca6b01811102a83e20a\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"A surface review is evaluated on its exact basis.\"],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":783,\"path\":\"standards/UX.md\",\"quote\":\"| surface review | `design_module_incomplete` | invalid_basis | no counterexample of `violation` is found, and a §14 review question cannot be answered from the design module, so the design module, on which the review rests, cannot support the evaluation; the value names the unanswered question |\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/UX.md#UX%2F15.%20Results%20of%20this%20profile\",\"start_line\":783},{\"end_line\":808,\"path\":\"standards/UX.md\",\"quote\":\"Fail closed (§1 Authority). Where this profile is ambiguous for a case,\\nthe surface review applies the stricter interpretation and returns its\\nvalue under it; the ambiguity alone never yields `compliant`. Where the\\nambiguity leaves a term the review depends on undefined, so that no\\nstricter interpretation is fixed, the review returns\\n`out_of_frame` and names the term and its owner\\n([FOUNDATIONS §4 Results](FOUNDATIONS.md#results), Out of frame or\\nindeterminate, first case). A reprice or a scoped exemption, the other\\ntwo exits of §1 Authority, is a re-entry or a scope recorded in the\\ndesign module, not a value of this section (P5, P6).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/UX.md#UX%2F15.%20Results%20of%20this%20profile\",\"start_line\":799}],\"statement\":\"compliant→satisfied requires §§4–10 under inspection, no §13 failure and every §14 question answered from the design module. violation→falsified when a failure pattern, §4-rejected realisation or broken §§4–10 rule supplies a counterexample. design_module_incomplete→invalid_basis applies only with no violation counterexample and an unanswered design-module question, which is named. The source chooses the stricter §§4–10 test over the competing §§4–8 compliance test and retains the disagreement for authority. Ambiguity requires the stricter fixed interpretation; ambiguity alone cannot yield compliant. If an undefined required term prevents fixing a stricter interpretation, return out_of_frame naming term and owner. Repricing and scoped exemption are re-entry/scope, not results.\",\"uncertainty\":\"The two §4 tests and §1 authority are only described here, not supplied directly.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:3c52cb66f1e449df88a3c64d510a50f9","key":1588,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:0248d4f244332b39c63670566a866da5\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:3c52cb66f1e449df88a3c64d510a50f9\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"The relevant predicate is evaluated; closure obligations apply where product-UX closure is claimed.\"],\"exceptions\":[\"A recorded exemption can cover a closure obligation.\",\"Inside an open UX sprint closure is not claimed; deferred obligations are escrow.\"],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":789,\"path\":\"standards/UX.md\",\"quote\":\"| replay proof | `replay_passes` | satisfied | the proof reproduces its expected final State and ordered Cmd values on its injected deterministic values, and no dependency that §8 lists decides its correctness; reproducing an unresolved outcome proves replay only and does not establish external completion |\\n| replay proof | `replay_fails` | falsified | the proof diverges from its expected final State or Cmd values, or its correctness depends on something §8 lists; the divergence or the dependency is the counterexample |\\n| closure obligations | `closure_obligations_met` | satisfied | every product-meaningful interaction family carries its Msg-replay proof and the surface its accessibility declarations, or a recorded exemption covers the obligation |\\n| closure obligations | `closure_unproven` | falsified | an interaction family lacks its proof or the surface an accessibility declaration, with no recorded exemption; that family or obligation is the counterexample. Inside an open UX sprint closure is not claimed, and a deferred obligation is escrow under §12 |\\n| carrier admission | `carrier_admitted` | satisfied | each product-truth-changing message or action maps to an admitted carrier of §3 and binds under §7 to an AssetSurface contract where the product publishes one, otherwise to the equivalent typed contract its design module names |\\n| carrier admission | `carrier_missing` | falsified | a product-truth-changing message or action has no admitted carrier or typed contract (§13 pattern 13); that message or action is the counterexample |\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/UX.md#UX%2F15.%20Results%20of%20this%20profile\",\"start_line\":784}],\"statement\":\"For replay: replay_passes→satisfied iff injected deterministic values reproduce expected final State and ordered Cmds without a §8-prohibited correctness dependency; replay_fails→falsified for divergence or such a dependency, naming it. Replaying unresolved outcomes establishes replay only, not external completion. For closure: closure_obligations_met→satisfied requires every meaningful interaction family's proof and surface accessibility declarations or applicable recorded exemptions; closure_unproven→falsified identifies a missing uncovered proof/declaration. For carrier admission: carrier_admitted→satisfied requires every truth-changing message/action to map to a §3-admitted carrier and bind to the published AssetSurface contract, otherwise the equivalent typed contract named in the design module; carrier_missing→falsified identifies a message/action without admitted carrier or typed contract.\",\"uncertainty\":\"The §8 forbidden-dependency list and detailed carrier admission law are outside the supplied source.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:6e20b7347a459dd5ce10aec6a4e631b5","key":1589,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:0248d4f244332b39c63670566a866da5\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:6e20b7347a459dd5ce10aec6a4e631b5\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":797,\"path\":\"standards/UX.md\",\"quote\":\"Where none of these values applies, the evaluation returns a core value\\ndirectly under [FOUNDATIONS §4 Results](FOUNDATIONS.md#results):\\n`indeterminate` where the admissible evidence cannot decide its predicate,\\nnaming the evidence that would decide; `out_of_frame` where its claim\\nneeds a relation or capability that its frame does not declare; and\\n`invalid_basis` where its subject or basis cannot support it on a ground\\nother than `design_module_incomplete` (P5).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/UX.md#UX%2F15.%20Results%20of%20this%20profile\",\"start_line\":791},{\"end_line\":826,\"path\":\"standards/UX.md\",\"quote\":\"Two collisions are resolved here (P1): \\\"blocked\\\" for want of a carrier is\\nnot the ambiguity outcome `blocked` of\\n[ACTIVATION §3 Ambiguity outcome](ACTIVATION.md#ambiguity-outcome), and\\n`design_module_incomplete` is not the value `incomplete` of ACTIVATION §3\\nConstruction availability. An exempt scaffold is a recorded scope (§12),\\nnot a result; evaluations outside its recorded scope proceed under this\\nsection. The six close classifications of §12 belong to TICKETS §3 and are\\nnot mapped here (P6).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/UX.md#UX%2F15.%20Results%20of%20this%20profile\",\"start_line\":819}],\"statement\":\"Every mapping carries its own predicate, maps to exactly one core result and cannot raise standing or satisfy another predicate. Where no refinement applies, return indeterminate for undecidable admissible evidence and name deciding evidence; out_of_frame for undeclared required relation/capability; invalid_basis for unsupported subject/basis other than design_module_incomplete. Missing carrier yields carrier_missing for admission and violation for review; a construction step needing it stops with re_entry_requested(authority), naming carrier, design owner and re-entry to author it or reprice the requirement. This is distinct from ACTIVATION ambiguity blocked; design_module_incomplete is distinct from construction incomplete. Exempt scaffold is scope, not result; evaluations outside its scope use this algebra. TICKETS close classes are not mapped here.\",\"uncertainty\":\"ACTIVATION owns the construction-stop mapping; its full semantics are not supplied.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:7591b0904347dbfd5b315359981bf637","key":1590,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:3cd931c3ed7a9f280b50fe22580e8256\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:ea7976cc8986c83e51397ea3c9641497\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:7591b0904347dbfd5b315359981bf637\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"World-model publication occurs under this profile.\"],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":58,\"path\":\"standards/WORLD_MODEL.md\",\"quote\":\"Binding declared under PROFILES §1: where FOUNDATIONS §2 defines an Object as\\na subject with scoped identity, a boundary, current state and declared\\nmaterial relations, and P3 makes a boundary a claim with a proof\\nobligation, a world-model builder binds them to the published entity cut\\nof §6 and its admissibility test of §9. Direction: profile to tier 1;\\npreserved meaning: identity is declared and survives admissible change,\\nand the boundary carries its own proof; narrowed scope: world-model\\npublication under this profile, where admissible change is treatment\\nacross adjacent domains; invalidation: a change of §9 or of FOUNDATIONS\\n§2 Object or P3 re-evaluates the binding (P3, P1).\\n\\nEach clause names the principle that requires it (P0 to P6, FOUNDATIONS\\n§3), as [FOUNDATIONS §1](FOUNDATIONS.md#1-vocabulary-of-standing)\\nrequires.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/WORLD_MODEL.md#WORLD_MODEL\",\"start_line\":45}],\"statement\":\"The declared binding runs profile→tier 1: FOUNDATIONS Object's scoped identity, boundary, state and material relations, plus P3's boundary proof obligation, bind to published entity cut and §9 admissibility. Identity declaration and survival under admissible change, and boundary proof, are preserved; here change means treatment across adjacent domains. Changes to §9, FOUNDATIONS Object or P3 require re-evaluation. Clauses name their requiring principles. Imports include FOUNDATIONS, ACTIVATION, EVALUATION, IDENTITY, SPEC_METHOD, PRODUCT_DEFINITION, RELEASE and TICKETS under PROFILES §1, without redefining their objects; ODD is the graph-execution profile.\",\"uncertainty\":\"Imported members' complete definitions and principle laws are not supplied.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:72486bb276ace960c857fce268c8cd2d","key":1591,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:e39b94f9c23281964c94da96edfba0a6\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:87e03ae16d8303ea92b9eeaa8b53070b\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:5b76634cadf8409273f4834fa26ac392\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:72486bb276ace960c857fce268c8cd2d\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":82,\"path\":\"standards/WORLD_MODEL.md\",\"quote\":\"- domains are defined by bounded function and authority;\\n- records are intelligible only through function, provenance and\\n  treatment context;\\n- mappings are semantic treatments over governed meaning;\\n- catalogs and schemas are explanatory projections over deeper semantic\\n  structure;\\n- the world model traces authoritative source surfaces, records accepted\\n  semantic claims in ledgers, and publishes bounded semantic cuts;\\n- the published semantic layer gives probabilistic systems a governed\\n  substrate for reasoning and correspondence.\\n\\nThe profile builds inspectable, versioned, machine-reasonable domain truth\\n(P3, P6). §5 states each core claim in full.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/WORLD_MODEL.md#WORLD_MODEL%2F1.%20Position\",\"start_line\":70}],\"statement\":\"The profile claims institutional systems often retain values while losing interpretive context. Records require function, provenance and treatment context; mappings treat governed meaning; catalogs and schemas project deeper semantics. World-model work traces authoritative sources, records accepted semantic claims in ledgers and publishes bounded cuts as inspectable, versioned, machine-reasonable truth supporting probabilistic reasoning and correspondence.\",\"uncertainty\":\"These are source-authored position claims, not empirical findings established by this interpretation.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:05edc2bb536958e7d4723b01aa37d813","key":1592,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:3cd931c3ed7a9f280b50fe22580e8256\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:05edc2bb536958e7d4723b01aa37d813\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":92,\"path\":\"standards/WORLD_MODEL.md\",\"quote\":\"World-model work has two constitutional intents: build published domain\\nartifacts; and compose those artifacts into higher-order world models\\n(P2). Query, traversal and serving over\\nthose artifacts are important delivery concerns, but they do not define\\nthe constitutional identity of this profile. Those concerns may later be\\nrealised through a dedicated query or serving plane without changing the\\ntwo core intents (P2, P3).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/WORLD_MODEL.md#WORLD_MODEL%2F1.%20Position%2FConstitutional%20intents\",\"start_line\":86}],\"statement\":\"The two constitutional intents are building published domain artifacts and composing them into higher-order world models. Query, traversal and serving are delivery concerns, potentially later realised through a dedicated plane, without redefining those intents.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:a08f469245bf81fb372e57e187ffee08","key":1593,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:3cd931c3ed7a9f280b50fe22580e8256\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:e39b94f9c23281964c94da96edfba0a6\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:a08f469245bf81fb372e57e187ffee08\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":103,\"path\":\"standards/WORLD_MODEL.md\",\"quote\":\"- observe source systems before attempting to standardise them;\\n- comprehend enacted semantics before flattening them into schemas;\\n- treat domains as bounded functional surfaces, not as loose\\n  vocabularies;\\n- treat data as evidence of function, never as meaning in isolation;\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/WORLD_MODEL.md#WORLD_MODEL%2F1.%20Position%2FManifesto\",\"start_line\":99},{\"end_line\":131,\"path\":\"standards/WORLD_MODEL.md\",\"quote\":\"If these claims do not hold, the work is not genuinely\\nworld-model-driven (P6).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/WORLD_MODEL.md#WORLD_MODEL%2F1.%20Position%2FManifesto\",\"start_line\":130}],\"statement\":\"Observe before standardising; comprehend enacted meaning before schema flattening; use bounded functional domains and contextual data evidence; recover experts' implicit objects, boundaries, states, transitions, treatments and reference artifacts; materialise governed understanding rather than leave it in people/pipelines/detached documentation; provide conceptual knowledge beyond metadata; tether probabilistic reasoning before cross-domain alignment/comparison/interpretation; fully qualify names before deeper transformation; model cross-domain change through treatment/covariance/adjoint interpretation; publish immutable cuts with explicit supersession; compose without erasing local authority; keep probabilistic correspondence in epistemic overlays and compile accepted meaning where delivery needs volume; derive projections from the kernel without co-equal truth; permit generation only after descriptive grounding. Failure of these commitments excludes the source's world-model-driven characterisation.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:f9e16443b131c7de4e5d87a243cf2ab1","key":1594,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:3cd931c3ed7a9f280b50fe22580e8256\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:f9e16443b131c7de4e5d87a243cf2ab1\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"World-model work adopts this profile.\"],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":163,\"path\":\"standards/WORLD_MODEL.md\",\"quote\":\"Its instance premises hold where world-model work is done under this\\nprofile; they are adopted with it and do not follow from the foundations\\n(P1, P6):\\n\\n- I1: institutional source systems enact domain function and stay\\n  sovereign for operational truth; the builder observes them and replaces\\n  none of them;\\n- I2: records do not carry their own meaning, and the people who work with\\n  them already commit to the objects, implicitly in code paths, records\\n  and workflows, or explicitly in schemas and policy;\\n- I3: probabilistic systems can propose correspondences across domains,\\n  and delivery at volume needs deterministic execution;\\n- I4: some builders work over a representation space in which identity is\\n  a geometric direction.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/WORLD_MODEL.md#WORLD_MODEL%2F1.%20Position%2FFoundation%20to%20law\",\"start_line\":150}],\"statement\":\"F21 imports F2 transitions/refinement, F3 results, F8 identity, F9 a_c calculus and F12 method binding; similarly spelled profile ledgers/cuts/overlays/treatments/projections are not calculus records by spelling. Adopted, non-foundational premises are I1 source sovereignty/non-replacement, I2 context-dependent records and pre-existing human object commitments, I3 probabilistic correspondence with deterministic volume delivery, I4 some geometric identity spaces. The table attributes consequences as follows: P1/P6+I1/I2→derived semantic truth; P3/P6+F8/I2 and P1 naming→qualified discriminated entity cuts; P4b/P6/P3+I1→recoverable immutable provenance; P1/P4b+F2/F9→declared treatments and traceable subordinate projections; P1/P3+F12→owner-preserving imports and directional specialisation; P6/P5+F3→candidate construct/gate and run-specific falsification; P3/P6/P4b+F9/I4→space-bound, verified, traceable directions; P2/P6/P0+I3→epistemic control and deterministic compilation; P2/P5/P4a→bounded saturation, explicit gaps, sparse publication and authority-preserving composition; P2→bounded proof wedge; P5/P6+F3→predicate-specific result mappings and no result for unrun verification. The source labels P1/P2/P3/P4a/P6 independent, P0 recovered, P4b derived from P0/P2 given non-reacquirable step facts, and P5 derived from P0/P6 given open-world premises. Profile choices include constitutional intents/manifesto/evidence order, entity-cut surfaces and binding, append-only ledger and initial Git publication lane, five treatment fields and preferred projection order, Builder Project narrowing, working refinements/gate, mean-offset methods and exclusions/verification/publication/storage packages, plane split, preferred mesh, wedge/spec applicability and seven result refinements. Builder projects choose discrimination techniques; consumers choose carriers/layouts/schemas/storage; ACTIVATION owns treatment licensing and adequacy; FOUNDATIONS owns lineage concepts and hypothesis; PRODUCT_DEFINITION owns relation carrier coordinates.\",\"uncertainty\":\"These are authored derivation and ownership claims, not independently proved derivations.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:589fab888e77c55ec1ea41c6e2c4e469","key":1595,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:3cd931c3ed7a9f280b50fe22580e8256\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:589fab888e77c55ec1ea41c6e2c4e469\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"A consumer enters a foundation-to-law rule.\"],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":188,\"path\":\"standards/WORLD_MODEL.md\",\"quote\":\"Purpose and material relation: an actor started on\\nthis member sees which rules follow from the foundations and the imported\\nfamilies, and which are choices of this profile, the builder project or a\\nconsumer, with their owners, so no choice is presented as derived and no\\ncandidate construct as established (P6, P1).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/WORLD_MODEL.md#WORLD_MODEL%2F1.%20Position%2FFoundation%20to%20law\",\"start_line\":184},{\"end_line\":207,\"path\":\"standards/WORLD_MODEL.md\",\"quote\":\"Each consumer applies the rule and decides nothing the owning section does\\nnot (P2, P6).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/WORLD_MODEL.md#WORLD_MODEL%2F1.%20Position%2FFoundation%20to%20law\",\"start_line\":206}],\"statement\":\"Consumer links preserve ownership and add no decisions. Derived-semantic-layer consumers are Flow Observe, Materialisation and plane split; ODD/UX defer world-model semantics without applying those rules. Entity-cut consumers include world-model definition, working refinements, epistemic status, Markov discovery obligations, sparse materialisation, geometric specialisation/verification and result predicates. Ledger/publication consumers include immutable Markov cuts and overlay supersession. Treatment/projection consumers are Flow Relate and Project. Builder Project consumes directional specialisation; GLOSSARY only locates it. Epistemic-status consumers include CONFORMANCE discriminator 12, FOUNDATIONS hypothesis, effective blanket, Markov theory, verification-versus-formal-blanket distinction and promotion-gate results. Overlay-construction consumers include variance exclusion, overlay/Markov units, geometric materialisation and direction/publication/storage/null-peer/unrun-verification results. Plane rules are applied by builder alignment/compilation and tooling; Output decides nothing. Saturation/composition consumers include sparse refinements, Materialise/Compose and result predicates. The proof wedge is adopting-builder policy, merely inventoried by PROFILES. Result evaluations belong to §§9–11/14; FOUNDATIONS owns the core without applying profile rules. Uncited opening §4, effective blanket, design relation, remaining units, opening §9 and Output apply the stated consequences and name principles; this omission from rows adds no authority.\",\"uncertainty\":\"Some consumer loci and all external consumer texts are unavailable; their asserted roles are retained without invented endpoints.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:8d23af41793bdbd2560e4d0eb00742be","key":1596,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:3cd931c3ed7a9f280b50fe22580e8256\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:9732f555ffd02a5cb722940a58180d9b\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:71122f9461dadc023581a2b25fd7b04d\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:60576aa2140b8aef363512775cb7cbce\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:8d23af41793bdbd2560e4d0eb00742be\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"The selected complete method basis applies.\"],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":250,\"path\":\"standards/WORLD_MODEL.md\",\"quote\":\"The meanings are adopted unchanged for this profile's scope under the\\nselected complete method basis. Their owner in FOUNDATIONS §2 is\\nretained, and a change to either context, any cited concept or taxonomy\\nclause, or the selected method basis invalidates the import until it is\\nreevaluated. The GLOSSARY only locates those source-owned meanings. No\\nother same-spelled concept is imported by this declaration. For each\\nimport the source and target concept reference is the same listed\\nidentity; the relation expands applicability into the target context and\\nmints no alias or new semantic owner (P1, P6).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/WORLD_MODEL.md#WORLD_MODEL%2F2.%20Role%20and%20imports\",\"start_line\":242}],\"statement\":\"SPEC_METHOD owns general process constitution; this profile is the primary world-model method refinement for existing-system observation and bounded publication. Its four exact lineage imports preserve FOUNDATIONS ownership and meanings, use the same concept identities in source and target, expand applicability and mint no aliases. A change to either context, any cited concept/taxonomy clause or selected basis invalidates import until re-evaluation. Same-spelled alternatives are not imported; GLOSSARY only locates meanings. For products both graph-native and world-model-driven, graph execution governs execution shape/traversal/product-authoring structure while WORLD_MODEL governs semantics/publication/composition; the profiles compose.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:6d0906aff48ff44037b7c2798d660d5c","key":1597,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:43f89028fb972707e26975d939e746bb\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:71122f9461dadc023581a2b25fd7b04d\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:60576aa2140b8aef363512775cb7cbce\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:6d0906aff48ff44037b7c2798d660d5c\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"World-model construction under this profile, using the same selected complete method release containing both cited clauses.\"],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":298,\"path\":\"standards/WORLD_MODEL.md\",\"quote\":\"- loss and refusal: general Source Projects outside that narrower\\n  configuration are excluded; neither the installed builder Product nor\\n  its Install may be substituted for the mutable Builder Project;\\n- semantic owners: FOUNDATIONS retains the source concept; this profile\\n  owns the target specialisation and adds no authority over the source\\n  taxonomy;\\n- source and target basis: the same selected complete method release that\\n  contains both cited clauses;\\n- governed scope and provenance: world-model construction under this\\n  profile; this clause is the normative relation carrier; and\\n- lifecycle and invalidation: a change to either concept or context, the\\n  selected method basis, the builder configuration relation, or the\\n  governed scope invalidates the translation until the owning authorities\\n  reevaluate it; each is a named instance of a material input change or a\\n  changed basis under\\n  [ACTIVATION §7](ACTIVATION.md#7-closed-result-and-reuse).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/WORLD_MODEL.md#WORLD_MODEL%2F2.%20Role%20and%20imports%2FBuilder%20Project%20specialisation\",\"start_line\":283}],\"statement\":\"The source-to-target specialisation has no inverse, equivalence or universal claim that every Source Project is a Builder Project. Preserve mutable next-cut workspace meaning and distinction from Release Cut, Product, Install and Artifact. Exclude general Source Projects lacking builder configuration and refuse substitution of installed builder Product or Install. FOUNDATIONS retains source ownership; WORLD_MODEL owns only the target. This clause is the normative relation carrier. Changes to either concept/context, basis, builder configuration relation or governed scope invalidate translation until owning authorities re-evaluate.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:c649fcb5e526fa25d0efad10bba81227","key":1598,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:e39b94f9c23281964c94da96edfba0a6\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:c649fcb5e526fa25d0efad10bba81227\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":319,\"path\":\"standards/WORLD_MODEL.md\",\"quote\":\"A world model should make explicit:\\n\\n- what objects are treated as real in a bounded context;\\n- what boundaries make those objects coherent;\\n- what state and transition surfaces matter;\\n- what evidence supports those claims;\\n- what value lists or classifications govern interpretation;\\n- how adjacent domains reinterpret the objects;\\n- what co-varies across those domains;\\n- what is preserved, changed, aggregated, delayed or lost.\\n\\nA world model is not a replacement system of record; a central monolith\\nthat erases local semantics; a generic catalog entry; a copied data\\nwarehouse; or a schema registry pretending to be comprehension (P6).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/WORLD_MODEL.md#WORLD_MODEL%2F3.%20What%20a%20world%20model%20is\",\"start_line\":306}],\"statement\":\"A world model should expose bounded-context objects, coherent boundaries, relevant state/transitions, supporting evidence, governing value lists/classifications, adjacent-domain reinterpretations, covariance and what is preserved/changed/aggregated/delayed/lost. It is not a replacement system of record, local-semantics-erasing monolith, generic catalog entry, copied warehouse or schema registry standing in for comprehension.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:cb49542af66dc667797d11622780f453","key":1599,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:3cd931c3ed7a9f280b50fe22580e8256\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:e39b94f9c23281964c94da96edfba0a6\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:cb49542af66dc667797d11622780f453\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":335,\"path\":\"standards/WORLD_MODEL.md\",\"quote\":\"The profile should produce world models that are bounded, inspectable,\\nchallengeable, evidence-backed, versioned, composable,\\nprojection-capable and machine-reasonable (P2).\\nIf the profile is working, it should become possible to answer:\\n\\n- what object is this record evidence of;\\n- what boundary defines that object;\\n- what source evidence supports the claim;\\n- which source is locally authoritative;\\n- what treatment changed the meaning downstream;\\n- what relationship exists between two differently treated objects;\\n- what value list or classification was in force at the time;\\n- why a downstream figure is or is not explainable from upstream reality.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/WORLD_MODEL.md#WORLD_MODEL%2F3.%20What%20a%20world%20model%20is%2FObjectives\",\"start_line\":323}],\"statement\":\"The profile should produce bounded, inspectable, challengeable, evidence-backed, versioned, composable, projection-capable and machine-reasonable models. Successful use should enable explanation of a record's object and boundary, claim evidence, local source authority, downstream meaning-changing treatment, relations between differently treated objects, time-applicable classifications and downstream figures' explainability from upstream reality.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:0c563dc3de6305a9940b50e069fa71ee","key":1600,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:3cd931c3ed7a9f280b50fe22580e8256\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:87e03ae16d8303ea92b9eeaa8b53070b\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:0c563dc3de6305a9940b50e069fa71ee\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[\"Source code, rules and configuration are used when available; their availability is never a prerequisite to comprehension.\"],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":364,\"path\":\"standards/WORLD_MODEL.md\",\"quote\":\"The profile works from the strongest available explanatory surfaces\\n(P6). Preferred hierarchy:\\n\\n1. realised system behaviour and emitted records or events;\\n2. source code, rules and configuration when available;\\n3. interfaces and schemas;\\n4. large-scale observational data evidence;\\n5. documentation, catalogs and operator testimony.\\n\\nCode is a high-fidelity explanatory surface when available. Realised\\nbehaviour remains the broader truth surface because some systems are\\nproprietary, partially visible, or only intelligible through their\\noutputs and effects. The profile therefore never depends on code\\navailability as a prerequisite for comprehension (P6, P0).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/WORLD_MODEL.md#WORLD_MODEL%2F3.%20What%20a%20world%20model%20is%2FEvidence%20hierarchy\",\"start_line\":351}],\"statement\":\"Use strongest available explanatory surfaces, with preferred order: realised behaviour and emitted records/events; available code/rules/configuration; interfaces/schemas; large-scale observational data; documentation/catalogs/operator testimony. Code is high-fidelity when available, but realised behaviour is broader for proprietary, partially visible or output-intelligible systems.\",\"uncertainty\":\"This is a preference ordering, not a rule excluding lower-ranked evidence.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:61cdfada31c34e7af782e6f7c42803f5","key":1601,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:4945be8fe304fdd50b4910957a8aeb30\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:f0813b08ad22c7e3d02e681158434ded\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:c143b6f091bd0e5b8b35148ab55197eb\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:61cdfada31c34e7af782e6f7c42803f5\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":398,\"path\":\"standards/WORLD_MODEL.md\",\"quote\":\"- for any attribute basis over a domain (schema columns, SAE dictionary,\\n  feature set, vocabulary), the set of attributes that \\\"fire\\\" for an\\n  object is not a crisp partition, and overwriting attributes outside\\n  that apparent set still leaks partial identity transfer;\\n- the attributes that do fire have only partial alignment with the\\n  object's identity; each alone is insufficient, and the basis distributes\\n  object identity across many atoms.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/WORLD_MODEL.md#WORLD_MODEL%2F4.%20The%20Markov-object%20construct%2FEffective%20blanket\",\"start_line\":392},{\"end_line\":413,\"path\":\"standards/WORLD_MODEL.md\",\"quote\":\"This reading is a working hypothesis. Direction-level and behavioural\\nevidence can support an overlay without establishing the formal\\nconditional-independence condition for a Markov blanket. The construct\\nremains candidate-class under the promotion gate in Epistemic status\\nbelow (P6).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/WORLD_MODEL.md#WORLD_MODEL%2F4.%20The%20Markov-object%20construct%2FEffective%20blanket\",\"start_line\":409}],\"statement\":\"The profile rejects fixed-set blanket membership: for any domain attribute basis, firing attributes are not a crisp partition, outside-set overwrites leak partial identity transfer, and individually insufficient attributes distribute identity. Geometric direction and behavioural support do not establish statistical conditional independence; the reading remains a candidate hypothesis subject to the promotion gate.\",\"uncertainty\":\"The universal attribute-basis claims are source assertions at working-hypothesis standing.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:355727100cc727b27730d98329dc43d5","key":1602,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:f0813b08ad22c7e3d02e681158434ded\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:c143b6f091bd0e5b8b35148ab55197eb\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:ea7976cc8986c83e51397ea3c9641497\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:355727100cc727b27730d98329dc43d5\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"The construct or overlays built on it are in scope.\"],\"exceptions\":[\"The four refinements are not entity-cut admissibility conditions; §9 governs those.\"],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":421,\"path\":\"standards/WORLD_MODEL.md\",\"quote\":\"Four working refinements constrain how this profile treats Markov\\nobjects. They are adopted commitments of this profile at candidate\\nstanding, not formal closure of the construct. An application records\\nits own evidence for the boundaries and overlays it publishes; no\\nrefinement replaces the promotion gate (P3, P6).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/WORLD_MODEL.md#WORLD_MODEL%2F4.%20The%20Markov-object%20construct%2FFour%20working%20refinements\",\"start_line\":417},{\"end_line\":450,\"path\":\"standards/WORLD_MODEL.md\",\"quote\":\"They constrain the construct and overlays built on it. They are not\\nadmissibility conditions for entity cuts, which §9 governs (P3, P6).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/WORLD_MODEL.md#WORLD_MODEL%2F4.%20The%20Markov-object%20construct%2FFour%20working%20refinements\",\"start_line\":449}],\"statement\":\"Four candidate commitments apply: geometric identity survival under treatment, not set membership; schemas partially sense/fragment identity and published overlays expose the axis rather than attribute profile alone; invariant semantic identity, not core size, discriminates objecthood, allowing sparse invariants but excluding rich clusters with no context invariant; identity is mean/DC offset from a null peer rather than dominant variance, excluding principal-component/maximum-variance identity constructions. Applications record their own boundary/overlay evidence; no refinement constitutes formal closure or replaces promotion.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:2b74994fce881b68856a041e89a6676e","key":1603,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:f0813b08ad22c7e3d02e681158434ded\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:c143b6f091bd0e5b8b35148ab55197eb\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:ea7976cc8986c83e51397ea3c9641497\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:2b74994fce881b68856a041e89a6676e\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[\"Entity cuts do not inherit the construct's candidate status; they stand on their own §9 admissibility.\"],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":471,\"path\":\"standards/WORLD_MODEL.md\",\"quote\":\"Promotion gate. The experimental result that would promote the construct\\nfrom candidate to established is a direction-native\\nconditional-independence test: given the identity projection, residual\\nvariation along remaining components should be independent of the target\\nunder plausible treatments. Candidate standing persists without a\\nresult that meets this predicate on the claimed subject and basis. A\\nfailed run falsifies that run's predicate; it does not relocate the gate\\nor by itself falsify the construct (P6).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/WORLD_MODEL.md#WORLD_MODEL%2F4.%20The%20Markov-object%20construct%2FEpistemic%20status\",\"start_line\":464},{\"end_line\":483,\"path\":\"standards/WORLD_MODEL.md\",\"quote\":\"The\\nstatus is inherited downstream: tooling that materialises Markov-object\\noverlays under this profile should default to a candidate-class\\npublication kind and reserve any formally closed publication kind for\\ncuts backed by a real promotion-gate result (P6).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/WORLD_MODEL.md#WORLD_MODEL%2F4.%20The%20Markov-object%20construct%2FEpistemic%20status\",\"start_line\":479}],\"statement\":\"Adoption does not require established statistical Markov theory. Blanket claims remain candidate working commitments until a direction-native conditional-independence result meets its predicate for the exact subject and basis: given identity projection, residual variation in remaining components should be independent of the target under plausible treatments. No qualifying result preserves candidate standing; failed runs falsify only their run predicate without moving the gate or by themselves falsifying the construct. Published overlays are candidate-class, not certified blankets. Unadmitted candidate entities remain candidates; lawful published entity cuts do not. Downstream tooling should default to candidate-class publication and reserve formally closed kinds for real gate-backed cuts.\",\"uncertainty\":\"No statistical test procedure, threshold or actual run is supplied.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:9dd795b7f220bb262e1bad66da04fab1","key":1604,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:f0813b08ad22c7e3d02e681158434ded\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:3cd931c3ed7a9f280b50fe22580e8256\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:9dd795b7f220bb262e1bad66da04fab1\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"A Markov object is read as a candidate identity-bearing cut.\"],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":506,\"path\":\"standards/WORLD_MODEL.md\",\"quote\":\"This profile does not make established Markov-object theory a\\nprerequisite for all design work. The relation runs the other way: this\\nprofile gives one theoretical framing for why these boundary disciplines\\nare sound, and DESIGN_MODULE gives the general engineering law that\\nremains valid even outside world-model products (P2, P6).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/WORLD_MODEL.md#WORLD_MODEL%2F4.%20The%20Markov-object%20construct%2FRelation%20to%20the%20design%20profile\",\"start_line\":502}],\"statement\":\"Good boundary design should prefer the smallest lawful carrier set preserving real authority; subordinate payloads unless independently authoritative; resistance to promoting sensed fragments into peer objects without irreducible need; and strongly typed semantic boundaries rather than fuzzy, reconstructive or controller-owned identities. This is one theoretical account of DESIGN_MODULE's general engineering law, not an established-theory prerequisite for all design work.\",\"uncertainty\":\"DESIGN_MODULE §8's analogue account is not supplied.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:afc3bb1ec0c03489a37980558538497a","key":1605,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:e39b94f9c23281964c94da96edfba0a6\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:87e03ae16d8303ea92b9eeaa8b53070b\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:22a6fe3d61f766946bb29c4e77059644\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:63dba586b5a95104e1ecff3442d0c5f0\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:afc3bb1ec0c03489a37980558538497a\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":534,\"path\":\"standards/WORLD_MODEL.md\",\"quote\":\"Mappings are semantic treatments. Cross-domain transformation is not\\nplain structural rewrite. Every treatment declares preserved structure,\\nchanged meaning, loss, surplus and ambiguity (P1, P4b). A treatment is a refinement or\\nrewrite step of\\n[ACTIVATION §4 Refinement](ACTIVATION.md#refinement): what it preserves\\nand its licensing law are that section's, and a treatment that changes\\nmeaning is an approximate step with its adequacy relation. The five\\ndeclared fields are this profile's domain fields for that statement;\\npreserved structure is what the step preserves, and changed meaning,\\nloss, surplus and ambiguity state where and how it is not exact.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/WORLD_MODEL.md#WORLD_MODEL%2F5.%20Core%20claims\",\"start_line\":525},{\"end_line\":539,\"path\":\"standards/WORLD_MODEL.md\",\"quote\":\"Fully qualified naming is mandatory. Many cross-domain failures are\\npreventable naming collisions. Fully qualified naming removes aliasing,\\nso the remaining hard work is real semantic transformation; IDENTITY §2\\nstates the scoped identity it applies (P3, P1).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/WORLD_MODEL.md#WORLD_MODEL%2F5.%20Core%20claims\",\"start_line\":536}],\"statement\":\"Operational truth stays with enacting systems; the model derives semantics and externalises existing expert understanding. Data is constrained-function evidence and invalid in isolation from context. Every treatment declares preserved structure, changed meaning, loss, surplus and ambiguity; ACTIVATION owns refinement licensing, and meaning-changing treatments are approximate steps with adequacy relations. Fully qualified naming is mandatory. Changing classifications/code sets/value lists are governed temporal artifacts. API and schema contracts project structure/function and are not highest semantic authority. Canonical cuts should remain bounded semantic identities; probability belongs in epistemic overlays, distinct from accepted treatments, publications and compiled execution.\",\"uncertainty\":\"ACTIVATION's licensing and adequacy laws and IDENTITY's full naming law are external dependencies.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:543c97b6b3015ece3f038fe1f39c6945","key":1606,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:ea7976cc8986c83e51397ea3c9641497\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:0bbd894b080148e4f1a5c1c827e9d6f2\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:f0813b08ad22c7e3d02e681158434ded\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:543c97b6b3015ece3f038fe1f39c6945\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"Builder projects start from looser object candidates.\"],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":614,\"path\":\"standards/WORLD_MODEL.md\",\"quote\":\"Builder projects may\\nbegin with looser object candidates; world-model publication converges\\nthem into entity cuts, or explicitly leaves them as non-object artifacts\\nsuch as treatment surfaces, covariance edges or temporal reference\\nartifacts (P3, P5).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/WORLD_MODEL.md#WORLD_MODEL%2F6.%20Units\",\"start_line\":610}],\"statement\":\"Publication converges looser candidates into entity cuts or explicitly leaves them as non-object treatment, covariance or temporal-reference artifacts. Markov theory explains recovered boundaries rather than authorising invention of entities: institutional objects are already committed in code, records, workflows, schemas or policy. Optional geometric overlays add representation-substrate obligations without replacing ordinary recovery.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:47511a2009921ffa13605d5d2665b3cd","key":1607,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:d346a1dbfeb78b1415d50ab61ce48315\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:43f89028fb972707e26975d939e746bb\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:861bbbd5b7d29d5df06de8f92d683ed1\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:47511a2009921ffa13605d5d2665b3cd\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[\"Align, Compile and Serve/query are optional; Compile concerns actual execution needs and Serve/query depends on justified delivery needs.\"],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":641,\"path\":\"standards/WORLD_MODEL.md\",\"quote\":\"4. Assure. Qualify traced observations into lawful world-model claims.\\n   Assurance should make explicit what is being claimed; whether the\\n   claim is observed, derived, interpreted or composed; which source\\n   surfaces support it; which source is authoritative for which aspect of\\n   the claim; and what ambiguity or missingness remains.\\n5. Ledger. Write the accepted qualified claims into the attribute ledger.\\n   The ledger is append-only: new understanding is recorded as new\\n   qualified claims and later object cuts, not by mutating prior accepted\\n   entries in place.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/WORLD_MODEL.md#WORLD_MODEL%2F7.%20Flow\",\"start_line\":633},{\"end_line\":683,\"path\":\"standards/WORLD_MODEL.md\",\"quote\":\"14. Serve or query (optional). If delivery needs justify it, expose\\n    traversal or query capability over published domain artifacts and\\n    composed world models. This may remain filesystem-first in the\\n    low-volume lane or later move behind a dedicated query plane.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/WORLD_MODEL.md#WORLD_MODEL%2F7.%20Flow\",\"start_line\":680}],\"statement\":\"Observe strongest available behaviour/records/events/code/configuration/interfaces/schemas/docs/metadata; Trace source locators so later claims should re-enter concrete spans, fields, paths or records; Extract reviewable inventories and object/event/lifecycle/treatment/authority candidates and ambiguity registers, which are not yet the model; Assure should expose claim, observed/derived/interpreted/composed status, supporting sources, aspect-specific authority and gaps; Ledger accepted qualified claims append-only; Bound by function, authority, state and adjacency, rejecting schema-first or vocabulary-cluster modelling; Materialise ledger-derived cuts, permitting bounded, distinguishable, evidence-backed sparse publication; Relate treatments/covariance/adjoints/temporal references; Publish immutable cuts without overwriting, with Git/filesystem sufficient at low volume; Compose recursively, inspectably and boundedly without erasing local authority; optional Align yields epistemic candidates/rankings/ambiguities/mapping/anomaly suggestions, not published truth; Project tables, schema/API/event contracts, mapping documents, transformation specifications, covariant transforms, tests and applicable scaffolds from one kernel; optional Compile accepted understanding into deterministic jobs/plans/records/implementation, with scale execution recommended through compiled artifacts rather than per-row inference; optional Serve/query exposes published/composed models via filesystem or later query plane.\",\"uncertainty\":\"This records the source's staged procedure without performing any stage.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:9667dd7da8f793530d1e31bc3582e761","key":1608,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:ea7976cc8986c83e51397ea3c9641497\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:c143b6f091bd0e5b8b35148ab55197eb\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:9667dd7da8f793530d1e31bc3582e761\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"An entity cut is published.\"],\"exceptions\":[\"Outside a declared representation space, the boundary law is discharged semantically under §9.\"],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":702,\"path\":\"standards/WORLD_MODEL.md\",\"quote\":\"Every published entity cut is prompt-sufficient for reasoning (P3, P1). At minimum, the cut should make visible\\nidentity, boundary, authority, state, evidence, treatment, covariance and\\nambiguity. \\\"Make the effective blanket explicit\\\" means: state the\\nboundary at which the entity's identity survives reinterpretation, not\\nenumerate a set of member attribute columns. Attribute schemas are\\nevidence for identity, not identity itself. The boundary is\\ninterventional, not structural: the test is \\\"does this identity survive\\ntreatment across its adjacent domains?\\\", never \\\"which attributes are in\\nthe member set?\\\" (P3). Where a declared representation space exists, that\\nboundary takes its geometric form, the low-rank projection along which\\nidentity is preserved under treatment, and a Markov-object overlay should\\nthen expose both the distributed attribute evidence and the projection\\nthat recovers identity from it. Outside such a space the same law is\\ndischarged semantically under §9 (P3, P1).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/WORLD_MODEL.md#WORLD_MODEL%2F8.%20Representation%20and%20publication%2FRepresentation%20law\",\"start_line\":689}],\"statement\":\"Every published cut is prompt-sufficient for reasoning and should expose the eight surfaces. Boundary means identity survival under adjacent-domain treatment, not attribute membership; schemas evidence identity. In a declared representation space, the boundary takes low-rank geometric form, and overlays should expose evidence plus the identity-recovering projection.\",\"uncertainty\":\"Prompt sufficiency is asserted by the source; no concrete cut is assessed.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:b0bc9c23e790baec0adce490fdbc6117","key":1609,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:ea7976cc8986c83e51397ea3c9641497\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:861bbbd5b7d29d5df06de8f92d683ed1\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:3faa4fb493acae06174655ecb783af0f\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:87e03ae16d8303ea92b9eeaa8b53070b\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:b0bc9c23e790baec0adce490fdbc6117\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":727,\"path\":\"standards/WORLD_MODEL.md\",\"quote\":\"The entity cut is the immutable projection, not the mutable source of\\ntruth. \\\"Projection\\\" is literal: the cut selects one bounded identity and\\nboundary over the distributed evidence in the ledger, accompanied by that\\nevidence and the basis on which it was accepted; §9 states the\\nobligation, and §10 applies where the selection is expressed\\ngeometrically in a declared representation space (P3). The attribute\\nledger is the accepted semantic record over which the entity cut is\\nprojected. A single ledger state can support many different cuts at\\ndifferent identities, boundaries and context scopes; the cut records\\nwhich selection was taken, not that the ledger is the cut (P3, P1).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/WORLD_MODEL.md#WORLD_MODEL%2F8.%20Representation%20and%20publication%2FMaterialisation%20law\",\"start_line\":718},{\"end_line\":734,\"path\":\"standards/WORLD_MODEL.md\",\"quote\":\"Every accepted object attribute should therefore be recoverable through\\nthe object cut that contains it; the attribute-ledger entries that\\njustify it; the assurance basis that accepted those entries; and the\\ntraced source surfaces that support the assurance. No object attribute\\nshould exist without ledger support; no ledger entry should exist without\\nassurance; no assurance should exist without traceable source (P6, P4b).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/WORLD_MODEL.md#WORLD_MODEL%2F8.%20Representation%20and%20publication%2FMaterialisation%20law\",\"start_line\":729}],\"statement\":\"A materialised cut is builder-authored canonical object-level semantic truth, not a raw source emission or replacement operational source. Published artifacts should be versioned and explicitly superseded. The provenance sequence is source→tracing→assurance→attribute ledger→entity cut. A cut selects bounded identity/boundary with evidence and acceptance basis; one ledger state can support multiple identities, boundaries and contexts. Each accepted attribute should be recoverable through its cut, supporting entries, assurance and traced sources; attributes should not lack ledger support, entries assurance or assurance traceable sources. §10 applies only to geometric selections.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:4c7b0a90fa60d8145bf5f9b77532b172","key":1610,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:0a85925cde6108a838ebe8913e3afc63\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:861bbbd5b7d29d5df06de8f92d683ed1\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:4c7b0a90fa60d8145bf5f9b77532b172\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":749,\"path\":\"standards/WORLD_MODEL.md\",\"quote\":\"Published world-model truth should be immutable per cut; reviewable by\\ndiff; traceable to evidence; and superseded by explicit later cuts rather\\nthan silently overwritten (P4b, P3). The\\nfilesystem and Git are sufficient for the publication plane in the\\ninitial lane. A database, if introduced later, is a query-plane\\ncomplement rather than the constitutional publication authority. In other\\nwords: Git is the publication ledger; a database is the query plane\\n(P6). This publication ledger is distinct from the attribute ledger: the\\nattribute ledger records qualified semantic claims over object identity,\\nand the publication ledger records immutable published cuts of domain\\nartifacts and object projections. Both should remain append-only and\\nreplayable (P4b).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/WORLD_MODEL.md#WORLD_MODEL%2F8.%20Representation%20and%20publication%2FPublication%20law\",\"start_line\":738}],\"statement\":\"Published truth should be immutable per cut, diff-reviewable, evidence-traceable and explicitly superseded rather than silently overwritten. Both distinct ledgers should remain append-only and replayable. Initial publication can use filesystem and Git; a later database is a query complement, not constitutional publication authority.\",\"uncertainty\":\"Other clauses state cut immutability categorically; this clause's 'should' wording is preserved.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:2270f6f0a8397658c44c820d601390f7","key":1611,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:861bbbd5b7d29d5df06de8f92d683ed1\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:2270f6f0a8397658c44c820d601390f7\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":762,\"path\":\"standards/WORLD_MODEL.md\",\"quote\":\"The attribute ledger is the immediate semantic source of an entity cut\\n(P4b, P6). Every entry should be a fully\\nqualified claim, potentially including a value or measured quantity; a\\nrule or constraint; a classification; a topology or relation claim;\\nprovenance and authority information; and effective, observed and\\npublication coordinates. The ledger may be supported by one or more\\nevidence surfaces, including documents for declared semantics or policy,\\ncode for derivation logic or invariants, and data for observed state or\\nemitted values. The profile does not assume one source per attribute; it\\nassumes one lawful claim record per accepted attribute fact (P6, P3).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/WORLD_MODEL.md#WORLD_MODEL%2F8.%20Representation%20and%20publication%2FAttribute%20ledger%20law\",\"start_line\":753}],\"statement\":\"The ledger immediately supplies entity-cut semantics. Each entry should be fully qualified and may include quantities, rules, classifications, topology/relations, provenance/authority and effective/observed/publication coordinates. One or more document, code or data evidence surfaces may support it. The assumption is one lawful claim record per accepted attribute fact, not one source per attribute.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:281d36d42764e7a9f6c3ef113fb594ed","key":1612,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:43f89028fb972707e26975d939e746bb\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:ea7976cc8986c83e51397ea3c9641497\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:281d36d42764e7a9f6c3ef113fb594ed\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":769,\"path\":\"standards/WORLD_MODEL.md\",\"quote\":\"Entities are recovered, not invented. A builder project constructs an\\nentity cut by trawling authoritative source surfaces for the boundaries\\nthe operating model already commits to, then qualifying them into\\npublished truth (P3, P6).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/WORLD_MODEL.md#WORLD_MODEL%2F9.%20Entity%20cut%20construction\",\"start_line\":766}],\"statement\":\"Construct cuts by recovering already-committed operating-model boundaries from authoritative sources and qualifying them into published truth; do not invent entities.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:b3c0088fc257a097a3ca368c07361020","key":1613,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:ea7976cc8986c83e51397ea3c9641497\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:b3c0088fc257a097a3ca368c07361020\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":791,\"path\":\"standards/WORLD_MODEL.md\",\"quote\":\"An entity cut is admissible when its identity, boundary, authority,\\nstate, evidence, treatment, covariance and ambiguity are explicit,\\ntraceable, and discriminated from plausible alternatives at evidence\\naltitude proportional to the claim (P3, P6). That is\\nthe whole constitutional test. It binds what is true of a published cut;\\nit does not prescribe how a builder establishes it (P0).\\n\\n\\\"Explicit\\\" admits three lawful values on every surface: a stated value,\\nstated absence, or stated non-applicability with its reason. A cut whose\\nentity has no adjacent-domain treatment says so; it does not manufacture\\none. This keeps the predicate whole without adding evidence machinery\\n(P5).\\n\\nSparse first publication remains lawful. A unique, historical,\\nsingle-context, inaccessible or regulated entity is publishable when the\\ntest above holds and its residual ambiguity is declared. Absence of a\\ncomparison population, of repeated contexts, or of permission to\\nintervene is a bound on evidence altitude to be stated, not a bar to\\npublication (P5, P2).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/WORLD_MODEL.md#WORLD_MODEL%2F9.%20Entity%20cut%20construction%2FAdmissibility\",\"start_line\":773}],\"statement\":\"The whole constitutional test is explicit, traceable eight surfaces and discrimination from plausible alternatives at evidence altitude proportional to the claim, without prescribing builder technique. Each surface may state a value, absence, or non-applicability with reason. Missing adjacent treatment is stated, not manufactured. Sparse, unique, historical, single-context, inaccessible or regulated entities remain publishable when the test holds and residual ambiguity is declared. Missing comparison populations, repeated contexts or intervention permission bound evidence altitude and must be stated; they are not publication bars.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:3365dd1ac544a351a7b5e89b0cba8f9d","key":1614,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:ea7976cc8986c83e51397ea3c9641497\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:3365dd1ac544a351a7b5e89b0cba8f9d\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":799,\"path\":\"standards/WORLD_MODEL.md\",\"quote\":\"\\\"Discriminated from plausible alternatives\\\" means the cut states why\\nthis boundary rather than a nearby one the operating model would treat\\ndifferently. The claim carries its own discrimination; a stronger claim\\nneeds stronger discrimination (P3, P6). Techniques\\nthat serve this, none of them mandatory and none of them exhaustive:\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/WORLD_MODEL.md#WORLD_MODEL%2F9.%20Entity%20cut%20construction%2FDiscrimination\",\"start_line\":795},{\"end_line\":821,\"path\":\"standards/WORLD_MODEL.md\",\"quote\":\"The adjoint round-trip performs, at semantic altitude, the discrimination\\nthe geometric boundary test performs in a representation space. Where a\\nbuilder can intervene, interventional evidence discriminates more\\nstrongly than declarative evidence, and a cut should say which kind it\\nrests on (P6). Boundary is interventional in character, not structural.\\nA cut that states its boundary only as a set of source fields has made a\\nweaker claim than one that states the reinterpretations under which\\nidentity survives, and should be read as such (P3, P1).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/WORLD_MODEL.md#WORLD_MODEL%2F9.%20Entity%20cut%20construction%2FDiscrimination\",\"start_line\":814}],\"statement\":\"A cut explains why its boundary rather than a nearby operationally distinct boundary; stronger claims need stronger discrimination. Semantic adjoint round-trips perform the analogous role of geometric boundary tests. Where intervention is possible it discriminates more strongly than declaration, and cuts should state which evidence kind supports them. Field-set-only boundaries are weaker than boundaries naming identity-preserving reinterpretations and should be read accordingly.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:70b8c7847274309242ff23e2649d5c1a","key":1615,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:ea7976cc8986c83e51397ea3c9641497\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:70b8c7847274309242ff23e2649d5c1a\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"An entity cut is published or its identity/boundary revised.\"],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":833,\"path\":\"standards/WORLD_MODEL.md\",\"quote\":\"A published entity cut makes the eight admissibility surfaces (identity,\\nboundary, authority, state, evidence, treatment, covariance and\\nambiguity) visible and traceable, each as a stated value, stated absence\\nor stated non-applicability, and records the basis on which identity was\\ndiscriminated (P3, P6). Cuts are immutable: revising\\nidentity or boundary produces a new cut that supersedes the prior one\\n(P4b). Concrete carriers, layouts, schemas and storage topology are\\nconsumer realisation; this profile requires that the published surfaces\\nsurvive and does not select the form they are stored in (P0, P2).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/WORLD_MODEL.md#WORLD_MODEL%2F9.%20Entity%20cut%20construction%2FPublishing%20a%20cut\",\"start_line\":825}],\"statement\":\"Publish all eight surfaces visibly and traceably with lawful surface values and discrimination basis. Cuts are immutable: changed identity or boundary creates a superseding cut. Consumer-selected storage form must preserve all published surfaces.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:cea58e407335bf05c0a2f47ee5294eaa","key":1616,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:c143b6f091bd0e5b8b35148ab55197eb\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:4945be8fe304fdd50b4910957a8aeb30\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:cea58e407335bf05c0a2f47ee5294eaa\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"The builder operates in a declared learned representation, ledger embedding or equivalent metric space where identity is a geometric direction.\"],\"exceptions\":[\"Overlay construction is not required for ordinary institutional recovery.\"],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":847,\"path\":\"standards/WORLD_MODEL.md\",\"quote\":\"This law is the representation-substrate specialisation of §9. It\\napplies only where the builder operates over a declared representation\\nspace in which identity is a geometric direction (a learned\\nrepresentation, an embedding over ledger claims, or an equivalent metric\\nspace); it is not required for ordinary institutional recovery (P3, P2). Where it applies, a builder\\nproject constructs the overlay by a directional, interventional\\nprocedure. The steps below are both how the overlay is built and the\\nminimum structure that is stored when it is published. The declared\\nrepresentation space is part of the overlay: an identity direction is\\nuninterpretable without the space it lives in, and directions computed in\\ndifferent spaces do not compose (P3, P1).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/WORLD_MODEL.md#WORLD_MODEL%2F10.%20Markov-object%20overlay%20construction\",\"start_line\":837}],\"statement\":\"§10 specialises entity construction only on the stated representation substrate. Use the directional, interventional procedure and retain its minimum structure on publication. Representation space is part of the overlay; a direction without its space is uninterpretable and directions computed in different spaces do not compose.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:451cd0ee2923f8fcdbc314d0314002b7","key":1617,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:c143b6f091bd0e5b8b35148ab55197eb\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:861bbbd5b7d29d5df06de8f92d683ed1\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:451cd0ee2923f8fcdbc314d0314002b7\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"Overlay construction under §10 applies.\"],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":862,\"path\":\"standards/WORLD_MODEL.md\",\"quote\":\"For a candidate object, assemble attribute-ledger evidence across context\\nvariation together with evidence for at least one null peer (P3, P6):\\n\\n- multiple contexts in which the candidate is instantiated;\\n- a null-peer instance: a structurally similar thing that lacks the\\n  candidate's identity content, observed in the same contexts;\\n- paired ledger entries covering `(candidate, context)` and\\n  `(null, context)`, so identity-carrying signal can be separated from\\n  context-carrying signal.\\n\\nThe paired evidence is the raw material of the cut. The ledger entries\\nremain distributed; they are not the object (P3).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/WORLD_MODEL.md#WORLD_MODEL%2F10.%20Markov-object%20overlay%20construction%2FPaired%20evidence%20collection\",\"start_line\":851}],\"statement\":\"Collect candidate ledger evidence across multiple contexts and at least one structurally similar null peer lacking candidate identity content in the same contexts. Pair candidate/context and null/context entries to separate identity from context signal. Distributed ledger entries remain evidence, not the object.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:2ceb1add52ebdddc6a8f0396ca3f3941","key":1618,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:4945be8fe304fdd50b4910957a8aeb30\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:c143b6f091bd0e5b8b35148ab55197eb\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:2ceb1add52ebdddc6a8f0396ca3f3941\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"Overlay identity-direction extraction is performed.\"],\"exceptions\":[\"Supervised variants are admissible only when targeting mean offset rather than within-class variance.\"],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":878,\"path\":\"standards/WORLD_MODEL.md\",\"quote\":\"Derive the identity axis as a low-rank projection over the paired\\nevidence (P3, P1). The canonical\\nform is the mean offset\\n\\n`d(object) = μ(evidence_object) − μ(evidence_null)`\\n\\ntaken across contexts. Supervised variants (linear discriminant,\\nlogistic-regression normal, difference-in-conditional-means) are\\nadmissible when they target mean offset rather than within-class\\nvariance. Principal-component and maximum-variance constructions are not\\nadmissible as identity directions: they capture within-pair variation,\\nnot the identity offset. The identity direction is not an attribute\\ncolumn; it is a geometric combination over columns (P3).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/WORLD_MODEL.md#WORLD_MODEL%2F10.%20Markov-object%20overlay%20construction%2FIdentity-direction%20extraction\",\"start_line\":866}],\"statement\":\"Derive a low-rank projection over paired evidence, canonically d(object)=μ(evidence_object)−μ(evidence_null) across contexts. Linear-discriminant, logistic-regression-normal and difference-in-conditional-means variants may target mean offset. Principal-component and maximum-variance constructions are inadmissible identity directions regardless of verification; a direction is a geometric combination, not a column.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:b38667cfb0f492dd15b477a71ef11ba1","key":1619,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:c143b6f091bd0e5b8b35148ab55197eb\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:ea7976cc8986c83e51397ea3c9641497\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:b38667cfb0f492dd15b477a71ef11ba1\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"A candidate direction is considered for acceptance/publication.\"],\"exceptions\":[\"The underlying entity cut remains independently lawful and publishable without the overlay.\"],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":900,\"path\":\"standards/WORLD_MODEL.md\",\"quote\":\"A candidate identity direction is accepted only if projection along it\\npreserves object identity under held-out treatments. The builder records\\nat least one acceptable verification (P6, P3):\\n\\n- α-sweep: apply `x − α · d` on held-out contexts, and show the expected\\n  identity shift and its saturation behaviour;\\n- transplant: apply `x + α · d` to null-peer instances, and show identity\\n  acquisition;\\n- boundary test: overwrite attributes outside the projection support and\\n  show identity survives (this is what discriminates a geometric blanket\\n  from a set-membership blanket).\\n\\nA direction that has no acceptable verification is a candidate, not an\\naccepted overlay. Publishing an unverified direction violates the\\nRepresentation law (§8). The underlying entity cut remains lawful and\\npublishable without the overlay (P6, P3). Passing this battery establishes\\nthat a direction is verified for\\npublication under this profile; it does not establish a formally closed\\nMarkov blanket (§4 Epistemic status) (P6).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/WORLD_MODEL.md#WORLD_MODEL%2F10.%20Markov-object%20overlay%20construction%2FVerification%20by%20treatment\",\"start_line\":882}],\"statement\":\"Acceptance requires identity preservation under held-out treatment and at least one recorded acceptable verification: α-sweep x−α·d showing expected identity shift and saturation in held-out contexts; transplant x+α·d showing null-peer identity acquisition; or outside-projection-support overwrite showing survival. No acceptable verification leaves a candidate; publication then violates Representation law. Passing verifies publication, not formal Markov closure.\",\"uncertainty\":\"The results section additionally excludes acceptance when any recorded verification shows identity lost.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:e85d3edb1af4830dfe36055a1b108efa","key":1620,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:c143b6f091bd0e5b8b35148ab55197eb\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:e85d3edb1af4830dfe36055a1b108efa\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"The candidate appears in multiple contexts.\"],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":910,\"path\":\"standards/WORLD_MODEL.md\",\"quote\":\"For candidates that appear in multiple contexts, decompose the attribute\\nevidence into an invariant core, the attributes whose contribution to the\\nidentity direction is stable across ≥ N of N contexts, and a context\\ncoat, the attributes selected by the specific context, carrying\\ncontextual reinterpretation rather than identity per se (P3). Both are evidence. The core carries\\nidentity; the coat carries treatment. The coat to core ratio is a\\ncharacterisation, not a quality metric (P3, P1).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/WORLD_MODEL.md#WORLD_MODEL%2F10.%20Markov-object%20overlay%20construction%2FCore%20and%20coat%20decomposition\",\"start_line\":904}],\"statement\":\"Decompose evidence into invariant core, whose identity-direction contribution is stable across ≥ N of N contexts, and context-selected coat carrying reinterpretation. Both are evidence; core carries identity and coat treatment. Coat/core ratio characterises rather than measures quality.\",\"uncertainty\":\"The source does not define N or a numerical stability criterion.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:33056d281c51356bbc9fa66d7c0da0c4","key":1621,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:f0813b08ad22c7e3d02e681158434ded\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:c143b6f091bd0e5b8b35148ab55197eb\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:33056d281c51356bbc9fa66d7c0da0c4\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"Before overlay publication, an accepted Markov object is discriminated from incidental clusters.\"],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":926,\"path\":\"standards/WORLD_MODEL.md\",\"quote\":\"Before publication, discriminate an accepted Markov object from an\\nincidental attribute cluster by null-peer comparison (P3, P6):\\n\\n- is the candidate's core size in a range that null peers also hit? Yes\\n  is expected and acceptable; size is not diagnostic;\\n- are the identity-loaded attributes in the core unique to the candidate\\n  among its null peers? They should be;\\n- does the candidate's identity direction transfer more cleanly than a\\n  random diagonal in the representation? It should.\\n\\nFailure on the uniqueness and transfer tests means the cluster is not yet\\na lawful Markov object, even if its invariants are internally consistent\\n(P3, P5).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/WORLD_MODEL.md#WORLD_MODEL%2F10.%20Markov-object%20overlay%20construction%2FNull-peer%20discrimination\",\"start_line\":914}],\"statement\":\"Compare null peers before publication. Shared core-size range is expected and acceptable, not diagnostic. Identity-loaded core attributes should be unique among peers and direction transfer should be cleaner than a random diagonal. Failure of uniqueness or transfer leaves a cluster not yet lawful even with internally consistent invariants, as the result mapping makes explicit.\",\"uncertainty\":\"No operational uniqueness or transfer-quality threshold is specified.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:8f84391f7e2d89196e69e05a0c4c8657","key":1622,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:c143b6f091bd0e5b8b35148ab55197eb\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:8f84391f7e2d89196e69e05a0c4c8657\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"An overlay is published.\"],\"exceptions\":[\"Effective coordinate α is included where applicable.\"],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":944,\"path\":\"standards/WORLD_MODEL.md\",\"quote\":\"A published Markov-object overlay makes visible, at minimum (P6, P3):\\n\\n- representation space: the declared space and attribute basis the\\n  direction is expressed in, versioned so a later re-fit is detectable;\\n- identity direction: the projection (a representation-space vector or\\n  equivalent geometric description);\\n- attribute evidence: core and coat, traced to ledger entries;\\n- verification record: treatments used, outcomes observed, held-out\\n  contexts evaluated;\\n- boundary characterisation: the projection support on which identity was\\n  preserved under treatment;\\n- null-peer comparison: what similar things were tested, what was\\n  accepted, what was rejected;\\n- effective coordinate: α along the direction for this instance, where\\n  applicable.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/WORLD_MODEL.md#WORLD_MODEL%2F10.%20Markov-object%20overlay%20construction%2FOverlay%20publication\",\"start_line\":930}],\"statement\":\"Expose versioned declared space and attribute basis; vector/equivalent projection; core/coat evidence traced to ledger; verification treatments/outcomes/held-out contexts; identity-preserving projection support; null-peer tests and accept/reject decisions; and applicable α coordinate. Overlay projections are immutable. Revising directions for new contexts/evidence/refitted spaces creates supersession; any representation-space change supersedes every direction even if ledger entries did not change. Never mutate prior overlays in place.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:994211ec533b86e1bda12c84cfa5503f","key":1623,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:c143b6f091bd0e5b8b35148ab55197eb\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:994211ec533b86e1bda12c84cfa5503f\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"An overlay is stored.\"],\"exceptions\":[\"The supersession record identifies a replaced overlay if any.\"],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":969,\"path\":\"standards/WORLD_MODEL.md\",\"quote\":\"The stored overlay is not a row in a table and not a membership list. It\\nis a package attached to its entity cut (P4b, P6):\\n\\n- the declared representation space and its version;\\n- the geometric object (identity direction and projection support);\\n- the distributed evidence (pointers into the attribute ledger);\\n- the verification trace (treatments, contexts, outcomes);\\n- the provenance and authority record (who accepted, on what assurance\\n  basis);\\n- the supersession record (which overlay this replaces, if any).\\n\\nA storage layout that loses any of these surfaces is not a lawful\\nMarkov-object storage layout. Query planes and projection surfaces\\nderived from stored cuts are downstream conveniences and do not\\nsubstitute for this storage shape (P6, P4b).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/WORLD_MODEL.md#WORLD_MODEL%2F10.%20Markov-object%20overlay%20construction%2FStorage%20shape\",\"start_line\":955}],\"statement\":\"Store a package attached to the entity cut, not merely a table row or membership list: space/version, direction/support geometry, ledger evidence pointers, treatment/context/outcome verification trace, accepting authority and assurance provenance, and supersession record. Losing any surface makes storage unlawful; downstream query/projection conveniences cannot substitute.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:ef48b3baaece54c0462a945e43c3227e","key":1624,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:861bbbd5b7d29d5df06de8f92d683ed1\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:43f89028fb972707e26975d939e746bb\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:ea7976cc8986c83e51397ea3c9641497\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:ef48b3baaece54c0462a945e43c3227e\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":982,\"path\":\"standards/WORLD_MODEL.md\",\"quote\":\"World-model construction is iterative. Builder projects may work a\\nbounded source-object set repeatedly until the resulting attribute ledger\\nis judged sufficiently saturated for publication (P2, P5). Sufficient saturation means: materially important\\nattributes have traceable support; remaining gaps are explicit\\nambiguities rather than silent misses; and the resulting object cut is\\nstable enough to publish and supersede later if needed. Sparse first\\npublication remains lawful (§9 Admissibility); silent unsupported\\nattribute creation does not (P5, P6).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/WORLD_MODEL.md#WORLD_MODEL%2F11.%20Saturation%2C%20composition%20and%20projection%2FSaturation%20law\",\"start_line\":975}],\"statement\":\"Builders may repeatedly work a bounded source-object set until judged sufficiently saturated: material attributes have traceable support, remaining gaps are explicit ambiguities, and the cut is stable enough to publish and later supersede. Sparse publication remains lawful; silently creating unsupported attributes does not.\",\"uncertainty\":\"Materiality and publishable stability are bounded judgment criteria, not numeric thresholds supplied here.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:7c95156642b5160312dabfe668641621","key":1625,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:47e7639a8632c2097cf426c2201bade1\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:8b5b1ad1ac3b2d75baf19fd2e7853cdb\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:7c95156642b5160312dabfe668641621\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":994,\"path\":\"standards/WORLD_MODEL.md\",\"quote\":\"Do not build one central monolith first. Build local published domain\\nartifacts and their entity cuts, then stitch them (P4a, P6). Composition preserves fragment authority,\\nbounded-context meaning, treatment semantics, declared loss and\\nambiguity. Higher-order models are composed from published domain\\nartifacts; they do not erase them (P4a, P4b). The preferred end state is\\na federated world-model mesh rather than a single flattened enterprise\\nmodel. Detailed mesh topology may remain product-local while the line is\\nstill being developed; profile-level mesh law should be ratified only\\nonce the reusable node and edge model is stable (P2, P6).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/WORLD_MODEL.md#WORLD_MODEL%2F11.%20Saturation%2C%20composition%20and%20projection%2FComposition%20law\",\"start_line\":986}],\"statement\":\"Build local publications/cuts before stitching; do not start with a central monolith. Composition preserves fragment authority, bounded meaning, treatment semantics, declared loss and ambiguity without erasing artifacts. A federated mesh is preferred. Developing topology may remain Product-local; profile mesh law should be ratified only after reusable node/edge structure stabilises.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:e49477fb297a12cae90b9a790ff58392","key":1626,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:a7d93851d417c75f3d15373901149cb8\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:61857acd4f5f365bed011dce43b5991a\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:e49477fb297a12cae90b9a790ff58392\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[\"Trace temporal reference artifacts where applicable.\"],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1009,\"path\":\"standards/WORLD_MODEL.md\",\"quote\":\"Projection is downstream convenience, not semantic authority; the\\nsemantic kernel remains primary (P6, P1). All\\nprojections should remain traceable back to governing objects; evidence;\\ntreatments; covariance edges; adjoint mappings; and temporal reference\\nartifacts where applicable. Tables, schemas, APIs, mapping documents and\\ncovariant transforms are all publication forms over the same semantic\\nkernel (P1). Because an API usually carries more business semantics than\\na bare schema, the preferred structural order is\\n`world model -> API contract -> schema contract`. Query and traversal are\\nalso downstream-facing conveniences in this sense: they may be a\\nfirst-class delivery pillar without becoming the constitutional core of\\nthis profile (P6, P2).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/WORLD_MODEL.md#WORLD_MODEL%2F11.%20Saturation%2C%20composition%20and%20projection%2FProjection%20law\",\"start_line\":998}],\"statement\":\"All projections should trace governing objects, evidence, treatments, covariance, adjoints and applicable temporal references; the semantic kernel stays primary. Tables/schemas/APIs/mapping documents/covariant transforms publish the same kernel. Preferred order is world model→API contract→schema contract because APIs usually carry more business meaning. Query/traversal may be a first-class delivery pillar without constitutional-core status.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:ae253ab4693e6b16cb9d0ee3757bbc44","key":1627,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:fa21a8371950f5ec05eb0e10d057e58b\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:63dba586b5a95104e1ecff3442d0c5f0\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:ae253ab4693e6b16cb9d0ee3757bbc44\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1033,\"path\":\"standards/WORLD_MODEL.md\",\"quote\":\"LLMs and other probabilistic systems belong primarily on the semantic\\ncontrol plane. They should help with comprehension, candidate alignment,\\nambiguity reduction and correspondence ranking. They should not be the\\nrow-by-row execution engine for large-scale data movement when the\\nsemantic understanding has already been accepted and can be compiled\\n(P0, P2).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/WORLD_MODEL.md#WORLD_MODEL%2F12.%20Planes%2C%20proof%20and%20development%2FControl%20plane%20and%20data%20plane\",\"start_line\":1028}],\"statement\":\"Probabilistic systems belong primarily in semantic control and should aid comprehension, candidate alignment, ambiguity reduction and correspondence ranking. When semantic understanding is accepted and compilable, they should not execute large-scale data movement row by row.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:af4d42cdf5c8aaef62757a7d8f15012b","key":1628,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:3cd931c3ed7a9f280b50fe22580e8256\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:43f89028fb972707e26975d939e746bb\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:af4d42cdf5c8aaef62757a7d8f15012b\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[\"Compilation proof is additionally recommended where the line is mature enough.\"],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1054,\"path\":\"standards/WORLD_MODEL.md\",\"quote\":\"Adoption should not depend on winning the standardisation argument first\\n(P2). Preferred wedge:\\n\\n1. comprehend one bounded source slice;\\n2. publish one fragment;\\n3. stitch one adjacent fragment;\\n4. answer one painful question the incumbent pipeline cannot answer\\n   cleanly;\\n5. emit both conventional and covariant outputs side by side.\\n\\nThis is incremental semantic capture, not a demand for immediate central\\nconvergence. The proof obligation is practical: build the world model\\nonce, then show that the same semantic substrate can emit the legacy\\nartifacts the organisation expects and the richer covariant outputs the\\nprofile makes possible. Where the line is mature enough, the proof should\\nalso show that accepted semantic understanding can be compiled into\\ndeterministic executable pipelines without losing the traceability and\\nchallengeability of the governing world model (P2, P6).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/WORLD_MODEL.md#WORLD_MODEL%2F12.%20Planes%2C%20proof%20and%20development%2FProof%20law\",\"start_line\":1037}],\"statement\":\"Adoption should not await winning standardisation. Preferred incremental wedge: comprehend one bounded source slice, publish a fragment, stitch an adjacent fragment, answer a difficult incumbent-pipeline question, emit conventional and covariant outputs together. The practical obligation demonstrates both output classes from one semantic substrate rather than immediate central convergence. Mature lines should also demonstrate deterministic compilation retaining traceability and challengeability.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:f45cf1c11733a5c9de2ade15d6249cbe","key":1629,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:e39b94f9c23281964c94da96edfba0a6\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:4fde8cb332e23c5fd70f410d41046ae4\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:f45cf1c11733a5c9de2ade15d6249cbe\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[\"Simpler lines can use world model→application projections→implementation.\"],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1072,\"path\":\"standards/WORLD_MODEL.md\",\"quote\":\"The profile stands in parallel with spec-driven development.\\nSpecifications are usually normative; world models are usually\\ndescriptive. A sufficiently well-formed world model can therefore project\\nlarge parts of an application surface without requiring duplicated\\nsemantic re-authoring downstream (P2, P1). Preferred relationship:\\n\\n`world model -> epistemic correspondence overlay -> deterministic compiled artifacts -> implementation`\\n\\nFor simpler lines the shorter compression still holds:\\n`world model -> application projections -> implementation`. Use\\nnormative application specs where the problem is primarily user\\ninteraction, workflow choice, non-domain behaviour, or operational policy\\nbeyond the domain semantics themselves. Use the world model as the\\nsemantic substrate wherever the software is mainly an interface over\\nstable domain reality (P2, P1).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/WORLD_MODEL.md#WORLD_MODEL%2F12.%20Planes%2C%20proof%20and%20development%2FWorld-model-driven%20development\",\"start_line\":1058}],\"statement\":\"World-model development parallels spec-driven development: specifications are usually normative and models descriptive. Well-formed models can project application surfaces without duplicate semantic authoring. Preferred route is world model→epistemic correspondence overlay→deterministic compiled artifacts→implementation. Use normative application specs for primarily interaction, workflow choice, non-domain behaviour or extra-domain operational policy; use models as substrate where software mainly interfaces stable domain reality.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:a1aaeb99e7926336cea70b894a0a66b7","key":1630,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:3cd931c3ed7a9f280b50fe22580e8256\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:a1aaeb99e7926336cea70b894a0a66b7\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"The profile is working as intended.\"],\"exceptions\":[\"Inspectable Markov overlays apply where a representation space is selected; compiled execution artifacts apply where real volume must move safely.\"],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1092,\"path\":\"standards/WORLD_MODEL.md\",\"quote\":\"If the profile is working, the result is not just better metadata (P2). The result is:\\n\\n- published domain artifacts as the durable semantic publication units;\\n- composed world models built from those published artifacts;\\n- published entity cuts as the primary semantic units;\\n- inspectable Markov-object overlays where a representation space is\\n  selected;\\n- explicit treatment and covariance semantics;\\n- epistemic correspondence overlays grounded in the same semantic\\n  substrate;\\n- temporal reference artifacts for changing domain enumerations;\\n- familiar projections emitted from the same semantic substrate;\\n- deterministic compiled execution artifacts where the line must move\\n  real volume safely;\\n- a basis for AI reasoning over real institutional meaning.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/WORLD_MODEL.md#WORLD_MODEL%2F13.%20Output%20and%20companion%20surfaces%2FOutput\",\"start_line\":1078}],\"statement\":\"Expected outcomes are durable published domain artifacts, composed models, primary entity cuts, applicable inspectable Markov overlays, explicit treatment/covariance semantics, grounded epistemic correspondence overlays, temporal reference artifacts, familiar projections, applicable deterministic execution artifacts and a basis for AI reasoning over institutional meaning.\",\"uncertainty\":\"This is a conditional output account, not evidence that any output exists.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:8f15609107868a46253316769de572a2","key":1631,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:3cd931c3ed7a9f280b50fe22580e8256\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:f0813b08ad22c7e3d02e681158434ded\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:8f15609107868a46253316769de572a2\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1107,\"path\":\"standards/WORLD_MODEL.md\",\"quote\":\"The companion surfaces of this profile are local method owners (P6):\\n\\n- [SPEC_METHOD](SPEC_METHOD.md), the constitutional specification method;\\n- [RELEASE](RELEASE.md), the method for publishing immutable cuts and\\n  promoting version-line selectors for installed consumer bases;\\n- [TICKETS](TICKETS.md), the method for turning discovery into bounded\\n  execution work.\\n\\nResearch evidence can support or challenge a hypothesis, but it does not\\namend this profile or replace its promotion gate. Changes to the working\\ncommitments follow [SPEC_METHOD §4](SPEC_METHOD.md#4-change-management)\\nunder their governing authority (P6, P3).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/WORLD_MODEL.md#WORLD_MODEL%2F13.%20Output%20and%20companion%20surfaces%2FCompanion%20surfaces\",\"start_line\":1096}],\"statement\":\"SPEC_METHOD owns constitutional specification method; RELEASE owns immutable-cut publication and version-line selector promotion for installed bases; TICKETS owns bounded execution from discovery. Research can support/challenge hypotheses but neither amend this profile nor replace promotion. Working-commitment changes follow SPEC_METHOD §4 under governing authority.\",\"uncertainty\":\"The companion methods themselves are not supplied.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:10e8507728e994dda1cf9502e57a97a7","key":1632,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:fc9b41e078bad0f2e87fffa996874467\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:ea7976cc8986c83e51397ea3c9641497\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:861bbbd5b7d29d5df06de8f92d683ed1\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:10e8507728e994dda1cf9502e57a97a7\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"Cut admissibility or saturation is evaluated.\"],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1138,\"path\":\"standards/WORLD_MODEL.md\",\"quote\":\"| cut admissibility | `cut_admissible` | satisfied | each surface is a stated value, a stated absence or a stated non-applicability with its reason, is traced, and is discriminated at the stated altitude; a stated bound on evidence altitude with its residual ambiguity declared meets the test (sparse first publication) |\\n| cut admissibility | `cut_inadmissible` | falsified | a surface is neither a stated value, a stated absence nor a stated non-applicability, or is untraceable, or the admissible evidence shows the boundary undiscriminated from a plausible alternative; that surface or alternative is the counterexample |\\n| cut admissibility | `discrimination_undecided` | indeterminate | no counterexample of `cut_inadmissible` is found, and the admissible evidence cannot decide the discrimination the cut itself claims at its stated altitude; the value names the evidence that would decide |\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/WORLD_MODEL.md#WORLD_MODEL%2F14.%20Results%20of%20this%20profile\",\"start_line\":1136},{\"end_line\":1153,\"path\":\"standards/WORLD_MODEL.md\",\"quote\":\"| saturation | `saturated` | satisfied | the three conditions hold; the explicit gaps are carried as residuals |\\n| saturation | `not_saturated` | falsified | a condition fails, as where an attribute exists without traceable support (silent unsupported attribute creation) or a gap is a silent miss; that attribute or gap is the counterexample |\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/WORLD_MODEL.md#WORLD_MODEL%2F14.%20Results%20of%20this%20profile\",\"start_line\":1152}],\"statement\":\"Cut predicate: eight surfaces explicit/traced/discriminated at claim-proportional altitude. cut_admissible→satisfied for lawful stated value/absence/non-applicability with reason, tracing and discrimination, including declared evidence bounds and residual ambiguity; cut_inadmissible→falsified for missing lawful surface value, missing trace or evidence-established nondiscrimination, naming the surface/alternative; discrimination_undecided→indeterminate only without counterexample and with evidence unable to decide claimed discrimination, naming deciding evidence. Saturation predicate: material support, explicit gaps and stable publishable cut. saturated→satisfied when all three hold, carrying gaps as residuals; not_saturated→falsified when any fails, naming unsupported attribute, silent gap or other counterexample. Lawful absence/non-applicability is a surface value, not a non-satisfied result.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:19702389118902b5af6967860fcb6a12","key":1633,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:fc9b41e078bad0f2e87fffa996874467\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:c143b6f091bd0e5b8b35148ab55197eb\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:19702389118902b5af6967860fcb6a12\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"Direction acceptance is evaluated.\"],\"exceptions\":[\"Unrun verification has its own no-result rule when neither extraction_inadmissible nor representation_space_invalid applies.\"],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1143,\"path\":\"standards/WORLD_MODEL.md\",\"quote\":\"| direction acceptance | `direction_verified` | satisfied | the direction is built by an admissible extraction in its declared representation space, at least one acceptable verification is recorded with identity preserved under held-out treatment, and no recorded verification shows identity lost |\\n| direction acceptance | `extraction_inadmissible` | falsified | the direction is built by a principal-component or maximum-variance construction, which is not admissible as an identity direction, whatever its verification shows; that construction is the counterexample |\\n| direction acceptance | `verification_failed` | falsified | the extraction is admissible, and a recorded verification shows identity not preserved under held-out treatment; that verification is the counterexample |\\n| direction acceptance | `verification_inconclusive` | indeterminate | the extraction is admissible in a declared representation space, no recorded verification establishes an acceptable preservation or shows identity lost, and a recorded verification ran without establishing either; the value names the held-out treatment or verification that would decide |\\n| direction acceptance | `representation_space_invalid` | invalid_basis | no counterexample of `extraction_inadmissible` or `verification_failed` is found, and the overlay declares no representation space, or its direction is composed with directions computed in another space; that basis cannot support the evaluation (§10) |\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/WORLD_MODEL.md#WORLD_MODEL%2F14.%20Results%20of%20this%20profile\",\"start_line\":1139}],\"statement\":\"direction_verified→satisfied requires admissible extraction in declared space, at least one recorded acceptable held-out preservation and no recorded loss. extraction_inadmissible→falsified for principal-component/maximum-variance construction regardless of verification. verification_failed→falsified for admissible extraction with recorded held-out identity loss. verification_inconclusive→indeterminate requires admissible extraction and declared space, a verification that actually ran, no acceptable preservation or loss, and names deciding treatment/verification. representation_space_invalid→invalid_basis applies without extraction/verification counterexample when space is undeclared or directions from different spaces are composed.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:637f4ddfcfca7af8ce07988fb2aa3a08","key":1634,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:fc9b41e078bad0f2e87fffa996874467\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:c143b6f091bd0e5b8b35148ab55197eb\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:f0813b08ad22c7e3d02e681158434ded\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:637f4ddfcfca7af8ce07988fb2aa3a08\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"The corresponding publication, storage, null-peer or gate-run predicate is evaluated.\"],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1151,\"path\":\"standards/WORLD_MODEL.md\",\"quote\":\"| overlay publication | `published_verified` | satisfied | the published direction has a recorded acceptable verification |\\n| overlay publication | `published_unverified` | falsified | a direction with no acceptable verification is published, which violates §8 Representation law (§10 Verification by treatment); that publication is the counterexample |\\n| overlay storage | `storage_retained` | satisfied | the stored package retains the declared representation space and its version, the geometric object, the distributed evidence, the verification trace, the provenance and authority record, and the supersession record |\\n| overlay storage | `storage_lossy` | falsified | the stored layout loses one of those surfaces; the lost surface is the counterexample |\\n| null-peer discrimination | `null_peer_discriminated` | satisfied | the identity-loaded attributes in the candidate's core are unique to it among its null peers, and its identity direction transfers more cleanly than a random diagonal |\\n| null-peer discrimination | `not_yet_lawful` | falsified | the uniqueness test or the transfer test fails, so the cluster is not yet a lawful Markov object; the failing test is the counterexample |\\n| promotion gate | `gate_met` | satisfied | the run meets the test's predicate |\\n| promotion gate | `gate_not_met` | falsified | the run does not meet the test's predicate; it is the counterexample for that run only, and the construct's standing is unchanged |\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/WORLD_MODEL.md#WORLD_MODEL%2F14.%20Results%20of%20this%20profile\",\"start_line\":1144}],\"statement\":\"Publication: published_verified→satisfied for recorded acceptable verification; published_unverified→falsified for publishing without it. Storage: storage_retained→satisfied for all six package surfaces; storage_lossy→falsified naming any lost surface. Null-peer discrimination: null_peer_discriminated→satisfied for core-attribute uniqueness and cleaner-than-random-diagonal transfer; not_yet_lawful→falsified if either fails, naming the test. Promotion: gate_met→satisfied when that run meets the conditional-independence predicate; gate_not_met→falsified only that run, leaving construct standing unchanged. Construct candidate/established standings and candidate/formally-closed publication kinds are not results.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:c13043ee8d03febdce26cb6801fb6db9","key":1635,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:fc9b41e078bad0f2e87fffa996874467\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:c143b6f091bd0e5b8b35148ab55197eb\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:c13043ee8d03febdce26cb6801fb6db9\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1161,\"path\":\"standards/WORLD_MODEL.md\",\"quote\":\"Where none of these values applies, the evaluation returns a core value\\ndirectly under [FOUNDATIONS §4 Results](FOUNDATIONS.md#results):\\n`indeterminate` where the admissible evidence cannot decide its predicate,\\nnaming the evidence that would decide; `out_of_frame` where its claim\\nneeds a relation or capability that its frame does not declare; and\\n`invalid_basis` where its subject or basis cannot support it on a ground\\nother than `representation_space_invalid` (P5).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/WORLD_MODEL.md#WORLD_MODEL%2F14.%20Results%20of%20this%20profile\",\"start_line\":1155},{\"end_line\":1182,\"path\":\"standards/WORLD_MODEL.md\",\"quote\":\"A verification not run. Where no ground of `extraction_inadmissible` or\\n`representation_space_invalid` holds, a candidate direction whose\\nverification has not been run has no result for direction acceptance:\\nthe verification is the evaluation of that predicate, and it was not\\nperformed, so it has no\\nclosed result and is never mapped to\\n`indeterminate` or to any other core value\\n([FOUNDATIONS §4 Results](FOUNDATIONS.md#results), Not performed). The\\ndirection stays a candidate (§10 Verification by treatment). In every\\nconjunction over its acceptance, the unrun verification is a planned\\nassessment without a closed result\\n([FOUNDATIONS §4 Conjunction of results](FOUNDATIONS.md#conjunction-of-results),\\nGaps) where the verification was planned; where none was planned, the\\nobligation it would have discharged is uncovered coverage. A step whose output needed that verification and that stopped\\nwithout it ends `incomplete`, which\\n[ACTIVATION §3 Construction availability](ACTIVATION.md#construction-availability)\\nmaps for the predicate \\\"a candidate is available\\\", never to\\n`indeterminate`; the step's work state carries the unrun verification as\\na residual ([ACTIVATION §5](ACTIVATION.md#5-work-state-and-restart)).\\nPublishing the unverified direction is `published_unverified` (P5, P6).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/WORLD_MODEL.md#WORLD_MODEL%2F14.%20Results%20of%20this%20profile\",\"start_line\":1163}],\"statement\":\"Mappings preserve their own predicate and standing and combine only in the core. Where no refinement applies, indeterminate names evidence needed to decide, out_of_frame identifies required undeclared relation/capability, and invalid_basis covers unsupported subject/basis beyond representation_space_invalid. Without extraction-inadmissible or invalid-space grounds, unrun verification yields no direction-acceptance result, never indeterminate or another core value, and leaves the direction candidate. In conjunction it is a planned assessment without closed result if planned, otherwise uncovered coverage. A stopped construction needing that verification is incomplete for ACTIVATION's candidate-available predicate, never indeterminate, with unrun work retained as residual. Publishing it still yields published_unverified.\",\"uncertainty\":\"External conjunction and construction mappings are referenced but not fully supplied; no evaluation is performed here.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:ef14d5a239ea081eb07fd199222723e9","key":1636,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:07fe88a2a6a0523330a19d0977d0c575\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:ef14d5a239ea081eb07fd199222723e9\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":19,\"path\":\"standards/WRITING_GUIDE.md\",\"quote\":\"Write for a reader who is technically fluent and short on time (P0).\\n\\nState the claim. State the reason. Remove the performance around them\\n(P2).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/WRITING_GUIDE.md#WRITING_GUIDE%2F1.%20Core%20rule\",\"start_line\":16}],\"statement\":\"The guide prescribes claim and reason without performative framing for technically fluent, time-constrained readers.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:a098da04deeb218bd11d21f542cfa519","key":1637,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:07fe88a2a6a0523330a19d0977d0c575\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:a098da04deeb218bd11d21f542cfa519\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[\"One claim per sentence is qualified by 'when possible'; examples are permitted only when reducing ambiguity.\"],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":30,\"path\":\"standards/WRITING_GUIDE.md\",\"quote\":\"1. Prefer direct positive statements over contrast framing (P1).\\n2. Remove setup paragraphs that announce what a section will say (P2).\\n3. Use concrete nouns and verbs, not motivational or promotional\\n   language (P1).\\n4. Keep one claim per sentence when possible (P1, P6).\\n5. Prefer precise technical vocabulary over vague intensifiers (P1).\\n6. Use an example only when it reduces ambiguity (P2, P1).\\n7. Do not write filler transitions whose only purpose is tone (P2).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/WRITING_GUIDE.md#WRITING_GUIDE%2F2.%20Style%20rules\",\"start_line\":23}],\"statement\":\"Prefer direct positive statements and precise technical vocabulary; remove announcing setup paragraphs; use concrete nouns/verbs instead of promotional language; keep one claim per sentence when possible; restrict examples to ambiguity reduction; prohibit tone-only filler transitions.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:aa7d03e80d4ad21bcf9f70f6aa153add","key":1638,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:07fe88a2a6a0523330a19d0977d0c575\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:aa7d03e80d4ad21bcf9f70f6aa153add\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":48,\"path\":\"standards/WRITING_GUIDE.md\",\"quote\":\"Remove these habits (P2):\\n\\n- \\\"not X, but Y\\\"\\n- \\\"simply\\\"\\n- \\\"just\\\"\\n- \\\"clearly\\\"\\n- \\\"obviously\\\"\\n- \\\"powerful\\\"\\n- \\\"robust\\\"\\n- \\\"seamless\\\"\\n- \\\"game-changing\\\"\\n- generic reassurance\\n- dramatic phrasing\\n\\nThey usually add tone and no information (P2).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/WRITING_GUIDE.md#WRITING_GUIDE%2F3.%20Habits%20to%20remove\",\"start_line\":34}],\"statement\":\"Remove the habits 'not X, but Y', 'simply', 'just', 'clearly', 'obviously', 'powerful', 'robust', 'seamless', 'game-changing', generic reassurance and dramatic phrasing, which usually add tone without information.\",\"uncertainty\":\"The source characterises these as habits; this is not interpreted as a ban on quoting those words as data.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:8f2e89eaf5673550d57f7aadc0e19e45","key":1639,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:07fe88a2a6a0523330a19d0977d0c575\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:8f2e89eaf5673550d57f7aadc0e19e45\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":56,\"path\":\"standards/WRITING_GUIDE.md\",\"quote\":\"Good prose on these surfaces is factual, bounded, explicit about\\nauthority, explicit about uncertainty and easy to challenge (P6, P4b).\\n\\nA sentence that sounds polished and carries no new constraint or\\nobservation is cut (P2).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/WRITING_GUIDE.md#WRITING_GUIDE%2F4.%20Good%20prose\",\"start_line\":52}],\"statement\":\"Good prose is factual, bounded, explicit about authority/uncertainty and challengeable. Cut polished sentences carrying no new constraint or observation.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:7809a2b04932d8a3068e03b608804e1c","key":1640,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:07fe88a2a6a0523330a19d0977d0c575\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:7809a2b04932d8a3068e03b608804e1c\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":67,\"path\":\"standards/WRITING_GUIDE.md\",\"quote\":\"Bad prose on these surfaces (P6, P1):\\n\\n- implies conclusions instead of grounding them;\\n- repeats one claim in different words;\\n- mixes current reality with target intent without labelling the\\n  difference;\\n- explains basic concepts to an expert audience; or\\n- turns straightforward instructions into brand language.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/WRITING_GUIDE.md#WRITING_GUIDE%2F5.%20Bad%20prose\",\"start_line\":60}],\"statement\":\"Bad-prose criteria are ungrounded implied conclusions, paraphrastic repetition, unlabelled mixing of reality and intent, basic explanations to experts and branding of straightforward instructions.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:a10c1784de94fde3214bae53bc1061b7","key":1641,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:07fe88a2a6a0523330a19d0977d0c575\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:4fde8cb332e23c5fd70f410d41046ae4\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:a10c1784de94fde3214bae53bc1061b7\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":75,\"path\":\"standards/WRITING_GUIDE.md\",\"quote\":\"Method documents should sound constitutional. Requirements should sound\\nnormative. Design should sound structural. Commentary should sound\\nanalytical (P6).\\n\\nWhere the tone does not match the authority layer, rewrite it (P6).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/WRITING_GUIDE.md#WRITING_GUIDE%2F6.%20Tone%20and%20authority%20layer\",\"start_line\":71}],\"statement\":\"Method tone should be constitutional, requirements normative, design structural and commentary analytical. Rewrite tone that does not match its authority layer.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:139932c547bc26096522267c996ac63f","key":1642,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:4fde8cb332e23c5fd70f410d41046ae4\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:139932c547bc26096522267c996ac63f\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"A specification artifact is being written.\"],\"exceptions\":[\"Design detail belongs in constitutional layers only when the detail is itself constitutional.\"],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":92,\"path\":\"standards/WRITING_GUIDE.md\",\"quote\":\"When writing a specification artifact (P3, P6):\\n\\n- state the current live truth, not a narrated transition;\\n- keep each sentence in its right layer;\\n- remove stale law, as §9 states; and\\n- keep design detail out of constitutional layers unless the detail is\\n  itself constitutional.\\n\\nA sentence that sounds informative and changes no authority, constraint\\nor derivability is cut (P2, P6).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/WRITING_GUIDE.md#WRITING_GUIDE%2F7.%20Specification%20artifact%20practice\",\"start_line\":83}],\"statement\":\"State live truth rather than narrated transition, keep sentences in their proper layer, remove stale law and exclude nonconstitutional design detail from constitutional layers. Cut sentences changing no authority, constraint or derivability.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:30bc97765afac0653134bbb7193b2808","key":1643,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:4fde8cb332e23c5fd70f410d41046ae4\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:30bc97765afac0653134bbb7193b2808\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"A specification artifact is written or revised.\"],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":102,\"path\":\"standards/WRITING_GUIDE.md\",\"quote\":\"When writing or revising a specification artifact, ask (P2, P6):\\n\\n1. Can the next downstream layer derive from this?\\n2. Does this artifact state current truth rather than work in progress?\\n3. Does any sentence belong in a lower layer instead?\\n\\nIf any answer is wrong, rewrite or delete (P2).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/WRITING_GUIDE.md#WRITING_GUIDE%2F8.%20Layer%20checks\",\"start_line\":96}],\"statement\":\"Check downstream derivability, current truth rather than work in progress, and whether any sentence belongs lower. Rewrite or delete when an answer is wrong.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:e8ccda1eb6eb4166fd199d47e6dbf2ce","key":1644,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:4fde8cb332e23c5fd70f410d41046ae4\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:e8ccda1eb6eb4166fd199d47e6dbf2ce\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"Constitutional specification or current-surface writing is in scope.\"],\"exceptions\":[\"Explicit version labels are reserved for immutable release facts, selector bindings or clearly historical/superseded material.\"],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":113,\"path\":\"standards/WRITING_GUIDE.md\",\"quote\":\"The rule for current-surface writing, with its force, is the\\n[SPEC_METHOD §2 Specification surface rule](SPEC_METHOD.md#specification-surface-rule):\\nconstitutional specification is written in the present tense, material\\nthat is no longer live is deleted, superseded or moved to commentary, and\\nan explicit version label is reserved for an immutable release fact, a\\nselector binding, or clearly historical or superseded material (P3). This guide adds the writing practice:\\nduring a change wave prefer terms such as active, current, base, live,\\nshared and tenant-local (P3).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/WRITING_GUIDE.md#WRITING_GUIDE%2F9.%20Current-surface%20writing\",\"start_line\":106}],\"statement\":\"The guide attributes force to SPEC_METHOD §2: constitutional specification uses present tense; nonlive material is deleted, superseded or moved to commentary; version labels have the stated restricted uses. During change waves the guide prefers active, current, base, live, shared and tenant-local.\",\"uncertainty\":\"The owning SPEC_METHOD clause and release-boundary rules are not supplied.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:9f0e6083a5f10b71e7fd69d6ee46f749","key":1645,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:d4026128310a589d335a770c7ceb2679\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:9f0e6083a5f10b71e7fd69d6ee46f749\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"A JSON instance is checked against this schema.\"],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":19,\"path\":\"standards/schemas/installed-release-manifest.schema.json\",\"quote\":\"  \\\"required\\\": [\\n    \\\"kind\\\",\\n    \\\"schema_version\\\",\\n    \\\"release\\\",\\n    \\\"standards\