 frame result, boundary effect,\\nand disposition under [ACTIVATION §3](../ACTIVATION.md#disposition) remain distinct.\\n\\nThis template imposes no universal numeric scale. A project may bind `S0..Sn`\\nand `P0..Pn`, including a `P2` decision cutoff, only by defining their exact\\ndirection and effect here. When a finding blocks promotion, and that a\\ncutoff cannot waive a hard stop or turn an out-of-claim observation into a\\nblocker, is decided by `EVALUATION.md` section 5, When a finding blocks\\npromotion.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/templates/PROJECT_REFERENCE_FRAME_BASIS_TEMPLATE.md#Project%20Reference-Frame%20Basis%2FTechnical%20Triage%20And%20Promotion%20Policy\",\"start_line\":110}],\"statement\":\"Bind exact current Product/MVP or release mandate; Product-selected severity scale/direction/evidence criteria; priority scale/direction/assignment authority; current-boundary cutoff and decision owner's required disposition; Product-bound authority, safety, integrity and retained-claim hard stops owned by ACTIVATION section 4; claim-relative release-blocking/scope-narrowing rule; Reviewer fields/capability; and unsupported/indeterminate return route. Reviewer grades severity and returns evidence, affected claims, causal assessment where supportable, blast radius, workaround, repair complexity, regression risk, confidence and residual uncertainty. Under Executive profile, Executive assigns priority and boundary effect against the complete Product view/current mandate. Severity, priority, frame result, boundary effect and disposition remain distinct. No universal numeric scale is imposed. S0..Sn, P0..Pn and a P2 cutoff require exact declared direction/effect. A cutoff cannot waive hard stops or make out-of-claim observations blockers; governing promotion law is cited rather than reproduced.\",\"uncertainty\":\"Full hard-stop, disposition and promotion rules require the cited ACTIVATION and EVALU