nfiguration selects:\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/templates/PROJECT_REFERENCE_FRAME_BASIS_TEMPLATE.md#Project%20Reference-Frame%20Basis%2FExecutive%20Attention%2C%20Evaluation%2C%20And%20Action\",\"start_line\":126}],\"statement\":\"Record selected non-Executive configuration/coordinating role where applicable; exact governed outcome, current MVP/release mandate and basis lock; unresolved evaluation frontier/dependencies; attention/capability limits selecting next activations; closed-result, triage, priority, boundary-effect and residual ledger; conjunction/conflict rule; existing disposition and next-action authority. Executive selects the smallest dependency-ready set sufficient for the next decision, consumes closed results, preserves explicit residuals and chooses only already-authorized next actions. Its label supplies none of Product meaning, implementation, mutation, acceptance or publication authority.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:75b408b8bdb1508f4de60d4a1a8354aa","key":1670,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:ff5afa03a3b25dd926b9cbdb771c65a0\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:ffde74ec9ef3edc98acf5d94b8ee5f6b\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:fd824e786e3c2b80628328c7551a3b8d\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:75b408b8bdb1508f4de60d4a1a8354aa\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"Entry, coordination or continuation of represented constructive work.\"],\"exceptions\":[\"Executive-specific steps apply only under the adopted Executive profile.\"],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":164,\"path\":\"standards/templates/PROJECT_REFERENCE_FRAME_BASIS_TEMPLATE.md\",\"quote\":\"Bind the sufficient direct Writer path and the material conditions requiring\\ncoordination under the selected law. Direct entry still needs exact work\\nauthority, admission, operation scope and closure conditions. It does not add\\na ticket, coordinating appointment or review when none is applicable.\\n\\nFor coordinated work:\\n\\n```text\\nexisting authority\\n  -> Executive basis and outcome lock\\n  -> exact Worker, Reviewer, or specialist activation\\n  -> closed result and Reviewer technical triage where applicable\\n  -> Executive or declared conjunction\\n  -> Executive priority and boundary effect\\n  -> authorized disposition and next activation | stop | re-entry\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/templates/PROJECT_REFERENCE_FRAME_BASIS_TEMPLATE.md#Project%20Reference-Frame%20Basis%2FActivation%20And%20Return%20Topology\",\"start_line\":150},{\"end_line\":173,\"path\":\"standards/templates/PROJECT_REFERENCE_FRAME_BASIS_TEMPLATE.md\",\"quote\":\"No child result, tool output, model response, shared actor, or lateral handoff\\nactivates another frame or authorizes continuation by itself\\n(`ACTIVATION.md` section 1, Admission).\\n\\nExecutive performs no file or Git mutation. The same actor may construct only\\nafter entering a separately bound Writer activation with the inherited exact\\ngrant. Changing roles does not create authority or independent assessment.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/templates/PROJECT_REFERENCE_FRAME_BASIS_TEMPLATE.md#Project%20Reference-Frame%20Basis%2FActivation%20And%20Return%20Topology\",\"start_line\":167}],\"statement\":\"Bind a sufficient direct Writer path and material conditions requiring coordination. Direct entry requires exact work authority, admission, operation scope and closure conditions, without adding an inapplicable ticket, coordinating appointment or review. Coordinated topology is existing authority → basis/outcome lock → exact Worker/Reviewer/specialist activation → closed result plus applicable Reviewer triage → Executive or declared conjunction → priority/boundary effect → authorized disposition and next activation, stop or re-entry. Child results, tool outputs, model responses, shared actors and lateral handoffs cannot alone activate another frame or authorize continuation. Executive makes no file/Git mutation. Construction by the same actor requires separately bound Writer activation inheriting the exact grant; changing role creates neither authority nor independence.\",\"uncertainty\":\"Topology is represented as source-described order, not an executed traversal.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:f58a4a726f964ecf0570ce270d45dfab","key":1671,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:ff5afa03a3b25dd926b9cbdb771c65a0\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:aee67c6e9c16d6729f06f452277e5182\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:f58a4a726f964ecf0570ce270d45dfab\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"Coverage accounting, result reuse or closure of an exact claim.\"],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":203,\"path\":\"standards/templates/PROJECT_REFERENCE_FRAME_BASIS_TEMPLATE.md\",\"quote\":\"Coverage is complete only when every mandatory material evaluation and\\ninteraction is closed, or governing authority explicitly retains its residual\\nconsistently with the claim (`REFERENCE_FRAME.md` section 8, Operational full\\ncoverage). Record each material row's status in the values of that section's\\nCoverage ledger. A `residual` row is\\n`excluded_by_authority` where governing authority explicitly retains its\\nresidual consistently with the claim, and otherwise `conditionally_covered` or\\n`uncovered`. A `non_material` row is no material evaluation and takes no\\ncoverage status; its non-material evidence stays in the inventory above.\\nAvailable frame count and coordinator visibility are not coverage.\\n\\nReuse a valid result after checking its question, subject/basis, evidence and\\ninvalidators. Record reusable judgments and original owner rulings through the\\nexisting work carrier under TICKETS, separately from interpretation.\\nChanged material premises invalidate affected claims under the invalidators\\nof `ACTIVATION.md` section 7; a new role or session alone does not. Required independent assessments still supply their own\\njudgment. Closure requires satisfied applicable obligations, valid evidence,\\nrequired judgments/rulings and no active non-closure condition; review is not\\nitself the closing event.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/templates/PROJECT_REFERENCE_FRAME_BASIS_TEMPLATE.md#Project%20Reference-Frame%20Basis%2FCoverage%20And%20Residuals\",\"start_line\":185}],\"statement\":\"Record exact coverage tuple/evaluation interval; each material evaluation's capable activation or residual; interactions/Product-edge coverage; intentional overlap/independence; uncovered, conditional, conflicted, unknown, excluded and out-of-frame residuals; and exact-claim terminal closure predicate. Completeness requires every mandatory material evaluation and interaction closed or its residual explicitly retained by governing authority consistently with the claim. Use the cited Coverage ledger values: residual is excluded_by_authority only with that retention, otherwise conditionally_covered or uncovered. non_material takes no coverage status; retain its evidence in inventory. Frame count and coordinator visibility do not establish coverage. Reuse valid results only after checking question, subject/basis, evidence and invalidators; record reusable judgments/original owner rulings in the existing TICKETS work carrier separately from interpretation. Changed material premises invalidate affected claims; a new role/session alone does not. Required independent assessments supply their own judgments. Closure requires satisfied applicable obligations, valid evidence, required judgments/rulings and no active non-closure condition; review alone is not closure.\",\"uncertainty\":\"The full coverage ledger, invalidators and work-carrier law are referenced but not supplied.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:216f002f4e1754b0084972403baa9cbd","key":1672,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:ff5afa03a3b25dd926b9cbdb771c65a0\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:216f002f4e1754b0084972403baa9cbd\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"Before activation and disposition, and when material inputs or basis change.\"],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":218,\"path\":\"standards/templates/PROJECT_REFERENCE_FRAME_BASIS_TEMPLATE.md\",\"quote\":\"Revalidate before activation and disposition:\\n\\n- outcome lock: Goal, Product outcome, current MVP or release mandate,\\n  promotion policy, boundary, and re-entry class;\\n- basis lock: subject, checkpoint, authority, dependency, configuration,\\n  topology, evidence, and time;\\n- Product-role lock: Source Project, Product Definition, Development Product,\\n  Release Cut, Product, Install, Artifact, and dependency roles;\\n- authority lock: semantic, evaluation, operation, decision, acceptance, and\\n  publication owners and grants; and\\n- coverage-and-return lock: material evaluations, interactions, residuals, and\\n  declared result routes.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/templates/PROJECT_REFERENCE_FRAME_BASIS_TEMPLATE.md#Project%20Reference-Frame%20Basis%2FDrift%20Locks%2C%20Invalidation%2C%20And%20Revision\",\"start_line\":207},{\"end_line\":230,\"path\":\"standards/templates/PROJECT_REFERENCE_FRAME_BASIS_TEMPLATE.md\",\"quote\":\"Exact review checkpoints and released Products remain immutable under their\\nown lifecycle law. Their immutability does not make the Source Project building\\na successor immutable. A lawful mutation creates a new checkpoint and\\ninvalidates every affected prior result.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/templates/PROJECT_REFERENCE_FRAME_BASIS_TEMPLATE.md#Project%20Reference-Frame%20Basis%2FDrift%20Locks%2C%20Invalidation%2C%20And%20Revision\",\"start_line\":227}],\"statement\":\"Before activation and disposition revalidate outcome lock (Goal, Product outcome, current MVP/release mandate, promotion policy, boundary, re-entry class), basis lock (subject, checkpoint, authority, dependency, configuration, topology, evidence, time), Product-role lock (Source Project, Product Definition, Development Product, Release Cut, Product, Install, Artifact, dependency roles), authority lock (semantic, evaluation, operation, decision, acceptance, publication owners/grants), and coverage/return lock (material evaluations, interactions, residuals, result routes). List every invalidating method, Product, outcome, subject, checkpoint, candidate, dependency, composition-contract, actor, capability, evidence, authority, workspace or topology change as a named material-input/basis change affecting the basis or derived activations/results/conjunctions/coverage. Exact review checkpoints and released Products remain immutable under their lifecycle law; this does not freeze a successor-building Source Project. Lawful mutation creates a new checkpoint and invalidates every affected prior result.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:9753c804a30b6b5dae00195f364c02e9","key":1673,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:ff5afa03a3b25dd926b9cbdb771c65a0\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:9753c804a30b6b5dae00195f364c02e9\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"Source re-entry and use of derived surfaces.\"],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":242,\"path\":\"standards/templates/PROJECT_REFERENCE_FRAME_BASIS_TEMPLATE.md\",\"quote\":\"- exact governing source references:\\n- source resolution and freshness route:\\n- residual-to-source re-entry owners:\\n- ambiguous, missing, stale, or substituted-source refusal:\\n\\nPrompts, summaries, symbolic maps, compressions, and other projections are\\nderived surfaces under `ACTIVATION.md` section 2, Acquisition and Staleness of\\nderived surfaces, which state when one may be used and when the owning sources\\nare acquired instead. None replaces this accepted binding.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/templates/PROJECT_REFERENCE_FRAME_BASIS_TEMPLATE.md#Project%20Reference-Frame%20Basis%2FSource%20Re-Entry\",\"start_line\":234}],\"statement\":\"Declare exact governing sources, resolution/freshness route, residual-to-source re-entry owners and refusal for ambiguous, missing, stale or substituted source. Prompts, summaries, symbolic maps, compressions and other projections are derived surfaces subject to cited acquisition/staleness law; none replaces the accepted binding.\",\"uncertainty\":\"The precise conditions for using a derived surface instead of acquiring its owner are in unsupplied ACTIVATION section 2.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:ede4b1629d0f2b05e0711912ed988d1a","key":1674,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:e25baa19ab2bc02fc6f2e0012e576e53\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:ede4b1629d0f2b05e0711912ed988d1a\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"Filling a per-product overlay.\"],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":61,\"path\":\"standards/templates/README.md\",\"quote\":\"One definition represents one distinct product `WHAT`. Put multiple\\nindependent realizations of that same `WHAT` in `how.build_tenants`, not in\\nadditional definition files.\\n\\n`reference_frame_bases` is required and non-empty. Point each `uri` at the\\naccepted project frame-basis declaration already carried by Product,\\nrequirements, local constitutional authority, accepted design, or another\\nlawful surface. Bind every admitting authority and exact governed scope. The\\ndefault path uses `./specification/REFERENCE_FRAME_BASIS.md`; replace it when\\nthe owning project chooses another layout. Do not put agent identities or\\ntemporary frame activations in the Product Definition Overlay; their authorized\\nwork instruction or activation packet cites the applicable basis.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/templates/README.md#Standards%20Templates%2FProduct%20Definition%20Overlay\",\"start_line\":50},{\"end_line\":106,\"path\":\"standards/templates/README.md\",\"quote\":\"Set `product.bounded_context` to `null` when the product does not claim a\\nseparate enclosing bounded context. The field is not an exhaustive registry;\\nsubordinate, peer, composed, tenant, user, and runtime contexts remain in their\\nown authority and are related explicitly. Remove the illustrative\\ndisambiguation when it does not apply. Empty local-constitution and composition\\narrays are explicit declarations of none.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/templates/README.md#Standards%20Templates%2FProduct%20Definition%20Overlay\",\"start_line\":101}],\"statement\":\"One overlay defines one distinct WHAT; multiple independent realizations belong in how.build_tenants. Replace at least schema URI; definition identity/name/source locator/context while keeping definition identity distinct from immutable Product/release identities; STDO repository/non-operative channel/exact RC basis/digest; every additional authority, basis-qualified entrypoint, bootstrap target and local constitutional relation; retained disambiguation details; collective frame-basis URIs/admitting authorities/scopes; Intent/Product/specification URIs; common/tenant HOW; Goals/ticket/comment/optional sprint carriers; and composition edges with expected target identity, relation authority and at least one governing contract. reference_frame_bases must be nonempty, point to accepted lawful declarations and bind every admitting authority/exact scope. Agent identities and temporary activations belong in authorized instructions/packets citing the basis, not the overlay. Replace disambiguation for every material local resolution, or remove the example and retain empty when none; bind complete candidates/selected concept/carrier/authority/bases/context/scope. Cross-context meaning stays in the owning carrier. Use bounded_context null when no separate enclosing context is claimed; other contexts retain their authorities and explicit relations. Empty local-constitution and composition arrays declare none.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn: