 selected immutable constitutional set, unique definition/tenant identities, composition target identities/contracts, and evaluate constitutional sufficiency, semantic resolution, cross-context completeness and authority congruence under PRODUCT_DEFINITION section 9.\",\"uncertainty\":\"Section 9 is not supplied; this interpretation does not perform or establish conformance.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:018596afd4ca77fc51175aabca389d14","key":1676,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:e25baa19ab2bc02fc6f2e0012e576e53\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:018596afd4ca77fc51175aabca389d14\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"Use of the described toolchain operations on filled definitions.\"],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":124,\"path\":\"standards/templates/README.md\",\"quote\":\"For a filled definition, `stdo sync --definition <file>` installs and verifies\\nonly its already selected exact basis. Run\\n`stdo adopt --definition <file> --dry-run` to show the immutable cut currently\\nadvertised by its annotated version-line selector and its exact plan digest;\\napply with `--accept-plan-sha256 <digest>` in a separate invocation only after\\nexplicitly accepting that basis change. `stdo bootstrap --definition <file>`\\npreflights targets relative to `product.source_project` and refreshes only the\\ndeclared marker-bounded agent bootstrap. Fleet writes require `--all`; fleet\\nadoption also requires its separately presented aggregate plan digest.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/templates/README.md#Standards%20Templates%2FProduct%20Definition%20Overlay\",\"start_line\":116}],\"statement\":\"The schema URI uses the same exact logical release basis, contains no machine-local store path, and is resolved through the manager after installing the cut once; project-local .genesis is not required. Described sync installs/verifies only the already selected basis. Adopt dry-run displays the selector-advertised immutable cut and exact plan digest; applying requires a separate invocation with --accept-plan-sha256 <digest> after explicit acceptance of that basis change. Bootstrap preflights targets relative to source_project and refreshes only declared marker-bounded bootstrap content. Fleet writes require --all; fleet adoption additionally requires the separately presented aggregate plan digest.\",\"uncertainty\":\"Commands are interpreted as source-described operations and are not executed.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:10b51b2e016500063c1551a96b465175","key":1677,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:aa6df989dfeca63efc3780a3e046e7ba\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:10b51b2e016500063c1551a96b465175\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"The optional human-readable registry is maintained.\"],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":8,\"path\":\"standards/templates/build_tenants/TENANT_REGISTRY_TEMPLATE.md\",\"quote\":\"The Product Definition Overlay owns build-tenant identity and location. Keep\\nthis table consistent with that JSON or generate it from the definition. This\\nfile must not become a second tenant registry.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/templates/build_tenants/TENANT_REGISTRY_TEMPLATE.md#Tenant%20Registry\",\"start_line\":6},{\"end_line\":31,\"path\":\"standards/templates/build_tenants/TENANT_REGISTRY_TEMPLATE.md\",\"quote\":\"When `how.common` is non-empty, list those shared realization references here\\nfor readers. `common` is not itself a build tenant and must not appear as a\\ntenant identity.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/templates/build_tenants/TENANT_REGISTRY_TEMPLATE.md#Tenant%20Registry%2FShared%20Surface\",\"start_line\":29},{\"end_line\":49,\"path\":\"standards/templates/build_tenants/TENANT_REGISTRY_TEMPLATE.md\",\"quote\":\"Record the currently active realization focus explicitly in the table notes or\\nan adjacent short section when more than one tenant exists. The entry identity\\nmust match the corresponding `how.build_tenants[].id`.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/templates/build_tenants/TENANT_REGISTRY_TEMPLATE.md#Tenant%20Registry%2FRegistry\",\"start_line\":47}],\"statement\":\"Keep the registry consistent with canonical overlay JSON or generate it from that definition; it must not become a second registry. If how.common is nonempty, list its references for readers; common is not a tenant and cannot appear as a tenant identity. The illustrative table has Entry, Kind, Path, Status and Notes, with a replaceable Planned tenant candidate. Entry identity must match how.build_tenants[].id. With more than one tenant, explicitly record the active realization focus in notes or an adjacent short section. Planned, In Development, Paused, Released and Deprecated are suggested lifecycle states, not an exhaustive mandatory vocabulary.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:2bc1729d92c48ced46893912ce97ac5c","key":1678,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:8c5d50ef720aad00ae53060725c5d806\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:f1ae4372889c4213ac98c1d03a4317b8\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:6fc6053f339a829db593fa36aafd3835\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:f3ceb5e45f636cbf468d85358c2cad82\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:2bc1729d92c48ced46893912ce97ac5c\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[\"Tenant-local material may be moved to common when explicitly promoted.\"],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":5,\"path\":\"standards/templates/build_tenants/common/README_TEMPLATE.md\",\"quote\":\"Do not place tenant-specific implementation detail here unless it is explicitly promoted to common.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/templates/build_tenants/common/README_TEMPLATE.md#Common%20Build-Tenant%20Surfaces\",\"start_line\":5},{\"end_line\":5,\"path\":\"standards/templates/build_tenants/common/design/README_TEMPLATE.md\",\"quote\":\"Use this surface only for design law that genuinely applies across multiple build tenants.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/templates/build_tenants/common/design/README_TEMPLATE.md#Common%20Tenant%20Design\",\"start_line\":5},{\"end_line\":5,\"path\":\"standards/templates/build_tenants/variant/README_TEMPLATE.md\",\"quote\":\"Keep tenant-local design, tooling, traces, and implementation here unless they are explicitly promoted to `build_tenants/common/`.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/templates/build_tenants/variant/README_TEMPLATE.md#Tenant%20Root\",\"start_line\":5},{\"end_line\":7,\"path\":\"standards/templates/build_tenants/variant/design/README_TEMPLATE.md\",\"quote\":\"Resolve the governing method from the exact installed STDO basis in the\\napplicable Product Definition and use `build_tenants/common/design/` for shared\\nrealization law.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/templates/build_tenants/variant/design/README_TEMPLATE.md#Tenant%20Design\",\"start_line\":5}],\"statement\":\"Keep tenant-specific implementation details out of common unless explicitly promoted. Common design is only for law genuinely applying across multiple tenants. Keep tenant-local design, tooling, traces and implementation at its tenant root unless explicitly promoted to common. Tenant design resolves its governing method from the applicable exact installed basis and uses common/design for shared realization law.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:0a7edfee227faa41d2a12e50697e69f4","key":1679,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:f3ceb5e45f636cbf468d85358c2cad82\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:0a7edfee227faa41d2a12e50697e69f4\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"Declaring a tenant's adopted common surfaces.\"],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":18,\"path\":\"standards/templates/build_tenants/variant/design/README_TEMPLATE.md\",\"quote\":\"List the exact shared surfaces from `build_tenants/common/` that this tenant\\nadopts.\\n\\n- Shared design law under `build_tenants/common/design/`\\n- Shared qualification law under `build_tenants/common/qualification/` when it\\n  constrains tenant-local tests or evidence\\n\\nIf no common surface is currently adopted, say that explicitly.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/templates/build_tenants/variant/design/README_TEMPLATE.md#Tenant%20Design%2FAdopted%20Common%20Surfaces\",\"start_line\":11}],\"statement\":\"List exact adopted common surfaces, including shared design law and shared qualification law when it constrains tenant-local tests or evidence. Explicitly state when no common surface is adopted.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:5a977dc5bab12ecc5041456db988c3c6","key":1680,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:f3ceb5e45f636cbf468d85358c2cad82\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:5a977dc5bab12ecc5041456db988c3c6\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"Binding a tenant under the selected method's SPEC_METHOD section 11.\"],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":37,\"path\":\"standards/templates/build_tenants/variant/design/README_TEMPLATE.md\",\"quote\":\"A shared calculus may have several execution bindings. The actor's identity\\nselects neither a calculus nor an operation kind. Record any required\\nindependent assessment or human decision without replacing it with a matching\\noutput. Adopt a profile only through the existing authority that owns it.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/templates/build_tenants/variant/design/README_TEMPLATE.md#Tenant%20Design%2FComputational%20And%20Execution%20Binding\",\"start_line\":34}],\"statement\":\"Bind governing requirements/exact basis; computational calculus objects, operations, constraints and result meanings realizing them; concrete technology, human or mixed execution environment with capability/resource assumptions; calculus-to-environment binding including authority, evidence, effects, uncertainty and recovery; requirement/execution conformance evidence; remaining obligations, unsupported claims and owners. A shared calculus may have several execution bindings. Actor identity selects neither calculus nor operation kind. Record required independent assessments or human decisions without replacing them with matching output. Profile adoption requires the existing owning authority.\",\"uncertainty\":\"The selected method's complete section 11 and concrete execution bindings are not supplied.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:3f94e3cf32d9a66dea1b96e3f3528a42","key":1681,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:fe281fd3e8224c42a6242f5aa8d8994a\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:f1ae4372889c4213ac98c1d03a4317b8\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:3f94e3cf32d9a66dea1b96e3f3528a42\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":15,\"path\":\"standards/templates/build_tenants/common/design/README_TEMPLATE.md\",\"quote\":\"Cross-tenant Architecture Decision Records live under `design/adrs/`.\\n\\nADRs at this surface govern decisions that apply to two or more build tenants. Tenant-local decisions belong under `build_tenants/<tenant-path>/design/adrs/`, not here.\\n\\nADR conventions and frontmatter shape are defined in `SPEC_METHOD.md` section 10, Design records. See `design/adrs/README.md` for the full conventions and `design/adrs/ADR_TEMPLATE.md` for the canonical ADR shape.\\n\\nNumbering is local to this `adrs/` directory; cross-tenant ADR IDs do not share numbering with tenant-local ADR IDs.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/templates/build_tenants/common/design/README_TEMPLATE.md#Common%20Tenant%20Design%2FADRs\",\"start_line\":9},{\"end_line\":18,\"path\":\"standards/templates/build_tenants/common/design/adrs/README_TEMPLATE.md\",\"quote\":\"If the decision governs only one build tenant, write the ADR at that tenant's `build_tenants/<tenant-path>/design/adrs/` instead. The `<tenant-path>` is one or more segments per `SPEC_METHOD.md` section 10, Design records.\\n\\nIf the decision changes constitutional truth (intent / product / requirement), it does not belong in an ADR; re-enter through `SPEC_METHOD.md` section 4 intake triage and reprice the appropriate constitutional layer first.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/templates/build_tenants/common/design/adrs/README_TEMPLATE.md#Common%20Tenant%20ADRs%2FWhen%20to%20write%20a%20cross-tenant%20ADR\",\"start_line\":16},{\"end_line\":41,\"path\":\"standards/templates/build_tenants/common/design/adrs/README_TEMPLATE.md\",\"quote\":\"One ADR per decision boundary, not per requirement file. Cross-tenant scope is the constraint that distinguishes this folder from a tenant-local one: the decision must govern more than one tenant. If the scope narrows during implementation, move the ADR to the relevant tenant's `design/adrs/` and record the move in the supersession chain (`SPEC_METHOD.md` section 10).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/templates/build_tenants/common/design/adrs/README_TEMPLATE.md#Common%20Tenant%20ADRs%2FBoundary%20rule\",\"start_line\":41}],\"statement\":\"Common design/adrs holds one ADR per decision boundary governing more than one tenant, with directory-local numbering separate from tenant-local numbering. Listed reasons to write include cross-tenant governance, concrete realization of one or more cross-tenant requirements under specification/requirements, structural/interface choices tenants must comply with and supersession of a prior common decision. A one-tenant decision belongs at that tenant's design/adrs, with tenant-path one or more segments. If scope narrows during implementation, move to the relevant tenant and record the move in the supersession chain. A change to intent/product/requirement truth does not belong in an ADR: re-enter SPEC_METHOD section 4 intake triage and reprice the appropriate layer first. SPEC_METHOD section 10 owns conventions/frontmatter; the directory README/template supplies conventions/body.\",\"uncertainty\":\"The source list does not explicitly formalize whether its four write triggers are conjunctive; the mandatory more-than-one-tenant boundary is explicit.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:361db17015bb2942a0302ea8d33d0c54","key":1682,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:6695b345e496371ae633b24bae835eb2\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:f3ceb5e45f636cbf468d85358c2cad82\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:361db17015bb2942a0302ea8d33d0c54\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":47,\"path\":\"standards/templates/build_tenants/variant/design/README_TEMPLATE.md\",\"quote\":\"Tenant-local Architecture Decision Records live under `design/adrs/`.\\n\\nADRs are the durable design memory layer per `SPEC_METHOD.md` section 10, Design records. Use `design/adrs/ADR-NNN-short-slug.md` as the default filename pattern; namespace-prefixed local IDs are permitted when this tenant's design surface already uses them.\\n\\nCross-tenant decisions belong under `build_tenants/common/design/adrs/`, not here.\\n\\nSee `design/adrs/README.md` for the full ADR conventions and `design/adrs/ADR_TEMPLATE.md` for the canonical ADR shape.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/templates/build_tenants/variant/design/README_TEMPLATE.md#Tenant%20Design%2FADRs\",\"start_line\":41},{\"end_line\":18,\"path\":\"standards/templates/build_tenants/variant/design/adrs/README_TEMPLATE.md\",\"quote\":\"If the decision applies across two or more tenants, write the ADR at `build_tenants/common/design/adrs/` instead.\\n\\nIf the decision changes constitutional truth (intent / product / requirement), it does not belong in an ADR; re-enter through `SPEC_METHOD.md` section 4 intake triage and reprice the appropriate constitutional layer first.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/templates/build_tenants/variant/design/adrs/README_TEMPLATE.md#Tenant%20ADRs%2FWhen%20to%20write%20a%20tenant-local%20ADR\",\"start_line\":16},{\"end_line\":39,\"path\":\"standards/templates/build_tenants/variant/design/adrs/README_TEMPLATE.md\",\"quote\":\"One ADR per decision boundary, not per requirement file. The ADR question is: *what design choice makes these acceptance criteria true?* Multiple requirements may share one ADR; one requirement may be implemented by multiple ADRs.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/templates/build_tenants/variant/design/adrs/README_TEMPLATE.md#Tenant%20ADRs%2FBoundary%20rule\",\"start_line\":39}],\"statement\":\"Tenant design/adrs holds local durable design memory. Listed write reasons include governing only this tenant (single- or multi-segment path), concrete realization satisfying one or more declared requirements, structural/interface choices future maintainers need and supersession of a local decision. Decisions across two or more tenants belong in common/design/adrs. Constitutional truth changes require SPEC_METHOD section 4 intake and repricing first, not ADR authorship. Use one ADR per decision boundary asking what design makes acceptance criteria true, not per requirement file: multiple requirements may share an ADR and one requirement may have multiple ADRs. Default filename is ADR-NNN-short-slug.md; existing namespace-prefixed local conventions are permitted. The directory README/template and SPEC_METHOD section 10 own conventions.\",\"uncertainty\":\"The list of write triggers does not explicitly specify its Boolean combination; tenant scope and constitutional-change exclusions are explicit.\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:d89319c4b14028680900f563fbbb43e2","key":1683,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:fe281fd3e8224c42a6242f5aa8d8994a\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:d89319c4b14028680900f563fbbb43e2\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"Authoring a common ADR.\"],\"exceptions\":[\"Superseded by is omitted unless the ADR becomes superseded; absent replacement or retained behavior may be recorded as none.\"],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":10,\"path\":\"standards/templates/build_tenants/common/design/adrs/ADR_TEMPLATE.md\",\"quote\":\"| `Status:` | `active` |\\n| `Implements:` | `REQ-*` IDs this ADR makes true |\\n| `Derives from:` | `INT-*` or strategy/design doc that motivated the decision |\\n| `Supersedes:` | Prior ADR or doctrine this replaces, or `none` |\\n| `Superseded by:` | Successor ADR if this one becomes `superseded`, otherwise omit |\\n| `Retained special case:` | When earlier behavior is intentionally retained, or `none` |\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/templates/build_tenants/common/design/adrs/ADR_TEMPLATE.md#ADR-%3Clocal-id%3E%20%3CShort%20Decision%20Title%3E\",\"start_line\":5},{\"end_line\":35,\"path\":\"standards/templates/build_tenants/common/design/adrs/README_TEMPLATE.md\",\"quote\":\"- `Status:` `active` | `superseded` | `retired`\\n- `Implements:` REQ-* IDs this ADR makes true\\n- `Derives from:` INT-* or strategy document that motivated the decision\\n- `Supersedes:` prior ADR or doctrine this replaces (when applicable)\\n- `Superseded by:` successor ADR (when `Status:` is `superseded`)\\n- `Retained special case:` when earlier behavior is intentionally retained as a special case (when applicable)\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/templates/build_tenants/common/design/adrs/README_TEMPLATE.md#Common%20Tenant%20ADRs%2FFile%20shape\",\"start_line\":30}],\"statement\":\"Title shape is ADR-<local-id> <Short Decision Title>; filename ADR-<local-id>-short-slug.md. ID is unique within this directory, with local numbering independent of tenant ADRs; pick one convention and retain it. Numeric IDs are default; namespace prefixes are allowed when already used by the common design surface. Frontmatter carries Status active|superseded|retired, Implements REQ-* IDs and Derives from INT-* or motivating strategy document (the body template also says design document); Supersedes and Retained special case apply when relevant, with none illustrated; Superseded by identifies successor only when superseded. The starter illustrates active, not an accepted decision.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:1aa29aa8ae55043bffc2136f20e80036","key":1684,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:6695b345e496371ae633b24bae835eb2\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:1aa29aa8ae55043bffc2136f20e80036\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"Authoring a tenant-local ADR.\"],\"exceptions\":[\"Superseded by is omitted unless the ADR becomes superseded; absent replacement or retained behavior may be recorded as none.\"],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":10,\"path\":\"standards/templates/build_tenants/variant/design/adrs/ADR_TEMPLATE.md\",\"quote\":\"| `Status:` | `active` |\\n| `Implements:` | `REQ-*` IDs this ADR makes true |\\n| `Derives from:` | `INT-*` or strategy/design doc that motivated the decision |\\n| `Supersedes:` | Prior ADR or doctrine this replaces, or `none` |\\n| `Superseded by:` | Successor ADR if this one becomes `superseded`, otherwise omit |\\n| `Retained special case:` | When earlier behavior is intentionally retained, or `none` |\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/templates/build_tenants/variant/design/adrs/ADR_TEMPLATE.md#ADR-%3Clocal-id%3E%20%3CShort%20Decision%20Title%3E\",\"start_line\":5},{\"end_line\":33,\"path\":\"standards/templates/build_tenants/variant/design/adrs/README_TEMPLATE.md\",\"quote\":\"- `Status:` `active` | `superseded` | `retired`\\n- `Implements:` REQ-* IDs this ADR makes true\\n- `Derives from:` INT-* or strategy document that motivated the decision\\n- `Supersedes:` prior ADR or doctrine this replaces (when applicable)\\n- `Superseded by:` successor ADR (when `Status:` is `superseded`)\\n- `Retained special case:` when earlier behavior is intentionally retained as a special case (when applicable)\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/templates/build_tenants/variant/design/adrs/README_TEMPLATE.md#Tenant%20ADRs%2FFile%20shape\",\"start_line\":28}],\"statement\":\"Title shape is ADR-<local-id> <Short Decision Title>; filename ADR-<local-id>-short-slug.md. IDs are directory-unique; numeric IDs are default and existing namespace-prefixed tenant conventions such as ADR-GM-005 are permitted; choose and retain one convention. Frontmatter carries Status active|superseded|retired, Implements REQ-* IDs and Derives from INT-* or motivating strategy document (the body template also says design document). Supersedes and Retained special case apply when relevant, with none illustrated; Superseded by is required when superseded and otherwise omitted. The template's active is illustrative.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:39e524b5e56fe39175828267a8c0e4e0","key":1685,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:fe281fd3e8224c42a6242f5aa8d8994a\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:6695b345e496371ae633b24bae835eb2\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:39e524b5e56fe39175828267a8c0e4e0\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"Authoring the respective ADR body.\"],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":14,\"path\":\"standards/templates/build_tenants/common/design/adrs/ADR_TEMPLATE.md\",\"quote\":\"State the cross-tenant situation that demands a decision. Cite the requirements or strategy material that frames the choice. Identify the build tenants this decision is intended to govern. Keep this section to the constraints, not the answer.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/templates/build_tenants/common/design/adrs/ADR_TEMPLATE.md#ADR-%3Clocal-id%3E%20%3CShort%20Decision%20Title%3E%2FContext\",\"start_line\":14},{\"end_line\":14,\"path\":\"standards/templates/build_tenants/variant/design/adrs/ADR_TEMPLATE.md\",\"quote\":\"State the situation that demands a decision. Cite the requirements or strategy material that frames the choice. Keep this section to the constraints, not the answer.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/templates/build_tenants/variant/design/adrs/ADR_TEMPLATE.md#ADR-%3Clocal-id%3E%20%3CShort%20Decision%20Title%3E%2FContext\",\"start_line\":14},{\"end_line\":20,\"path\":\"standards/templates/build_tenants/common/design/adrs/ADR_TEMPLATE.md\",\"quote\":\"State the chosen design in present tense. One decision per ADR; split into multiple ADRs if the choice covers more than one decision boundary.\\n\\nName concrete mechanisms when requirements name them. If a requirement names an operational mechanism, this ADR must name that mechanism too.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/templates/build_tenants/common/design/adrs/ADR_TEMPLATE.md#ADR-%3Clocal-id%3E%20%3CShort%20Decision%20Title%3E%2FDecision\",\"start_line\":18},{\"end_line\":20,\"path\":\"standards/templates/build_tenants/variant/design/adrs/ADR_TEMPLATE.md\",\"quote\":\"State the chosen design in present tense. One decision per ADR; split into multiple ADRs if the choice covers more than one decision boundary.\\n\\nName concrete mechanisms when requirements name them. If a requirement names an operational mechanism, this ADR must name that mechanism too.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/templates/build_tenants/variant/design/adrs/ADR_TEMPLATE.md#ADR-%3Clocal-id%3E%20%3CShort%20Decision%20Title%3E%2FDecision\",\"start_line\":18}],\"statement\":\"Context states the situation demanding a decision and cites framing requirements/strategy, retaining constraints rather than the answer; common ADR context additionally identifies governed build tenants and cross-tenant situation. Decision states chosen design in present tense, one decision per ADR, splitting choices spanning multiple decision boundaries. Name concrete mechanisms named by requirements; an operational mechanism named in a requirement must also be named in the ADR.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:6e297e112d8f1acc798cd2c9005f4634","key":1686,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:fe281fd3e8224c42a6242f5aa8d8994a\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:6695b345e496371ae633b24bae835eb2\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:6e297e112d8f1acc798cd2c9005f4634\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"Authoring consequences and alternatives for the respective ADR.\"],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":30,\"path\":\"standards/templates/build_tenants/common/design/adrs/ADR_TEMPLATE.md\",\"quote\":\"Describe what becomes true once this decision is in force across the tenants it governs:\\n\\n- positive consequences the decision enables\\n- negative consequences or trade-offs the decision accepts\\n- downstream design or implementation work the decision requires in each affected tenant\\n- proof or qualification surfaces affected\\n- migration cost for tenants that previously diverged from the decision\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/templates/build_tenants/common/design/adrs/ADR_TEMPLATE.md#ADR-%3Clocal-id%3E%20%3CShort%20Decision%20Title%3E%2FConsequences\",\"start_line\":24},{\"end_line\":29,\"path\":\"standards/templates/build_tenants/variant/design/adrs/ADR_TEMPLATE.md\",\"quote\":\"Describe what becomes true once this decision is in force:\\n\\n- positive consequences the decision enables\\n- negative consequences or trade-offs the decision accepts\\n- downstream design or implementation work the decision requires\\n- proof or qualification surfaces affected\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/templates/build_tenants/variant/design/adrs/ADR_TEMPLATE.md#ADR-%3Clocal-id%3E%20%3CShort%20Decision%20Title%3E%2FConsequences\",\"start_line\":24},{\"end_line\":34,\"path\":\"standards/templates/build_tenants/common/design/adrs/ADR_TEMPLATE.md\",\"quote\":\"List the alternatives that were on the table, with one or two sentences on why each was rejected. Be specific enough that a future maintainer can recover the reasoning. Note any alternative that was kept lawful at the tenant-local level.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/templates/build_tenants/common/design/adrs/ADR_TEMPLATE.md#ADR-%3Clocal-id%3E%20%3CShort%20Decision%20Title%3E%2FAlternatives%20Considered\",\"start_line\":34},{\"end_line\":33,\"path\":\"standards/templates/build_tenants/variant/design/adrs/ADR_TEMPLATE.md\",\"quote\":\"List the alternatives that were on the table, with one or two sentences on why each was rejected. Be specific enough that a future maintainer can recover the reasoning.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/templates/build_tenants/variant/design/adrs/ADR_TEMPLATE.md#ADR-%3Clocal-id%3E%20%3CShort%20Decision%20Title%3E%2FAlternatives%20Considered\",\"start_line\":33}],\"statement\":\"Describe consequences once the decision is in force: positives, accepted negatives/trade-offs, required downstream design/implementation and affected proof/qualification surfaces. Common ADRs do this across governed tenants, specify work in each affected tenant and migration cost for prior divergence. List considered alternatives with one or two sentences explaining each rejection sufficiently for future recovery of reasoning; common ADRs additionally note alternatives kept lawful locally.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1f