tes/requirements/README_TEMPLATE.md\",\"quote\":\"- Write requirement families as separate `*.md` files.\\n- Every requirement family must declare `Family`, `Status`, and `Category`\\n  metadata in the header.\\n- `Status` must use the lifecycle vocabulary from `SPEC_METHOD.md`:\\n  `Active`, `Deferred`, `Superseded`, or `Orphaned`.\\n- `Category` must use the requirement-category vocabulary from\\n  `SPEC_METHOD.md`: `Capability`, `Constraint / Guarantee`, `Governance`, or\\n  `Verification`.\\n- Use deterministic REQ headers in the form `### REQ-...`.\\n- Replace `00-starter.md` with real project requirement families as the project becomes concrete.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/templates/requirements/README_TEMPLATE.md#Project%20Requirements%2FRules\",\"start_line\":10},{\"end_line\":11,\"path\":\"standards/templates/requirements/STARTER_REQUIREMENTS_TEMPLATE.md\",\"quote\":\"Replace this starter family with the first real project-specific requirement\\nfamily. If it is retained temporarily during bootstrap, keep it honestly\\nclassified as deferred rather than presenting it as active product truth.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/templates/requirements/STARTER_REQUIREMENTS_TEMPLATE.md#Starter%20Requirements%2FREQ-PROJ-STARTER-001%20Replace%20me\",\"start_line\":9}],\"statement\":\"Resolve governing references from the applicable exact installed basis. Write separate *.md family files; every header declares Family, Status and Category. Status is Active|Deferred|Superseded|Orphaned; Category is Capability|Constraint / Guarantee|Governance|Verification. Use deterministic ### REQ-... headers. Replace 00-starter.md as the project becomes concrete and replace the starter family with the first real project family. Temporary bootstrap retention must remain honestly deferred, never active product truth.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"latitude","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:1fce941e8faea6ef73cd8ab817709955","key":1691,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"allowed_variation\":{\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":52,\"path\":\"plugins/spec/references/GETTING_STARTED.md\",\"quote\":\"STDO constrains governed relations. It does not prescribe an actor count,\\nrepository layout, prompt construction engine, internal decomposition, search\\nprocedure, or tool sequence where those choices cannot change a governed\\nsemantic, authority, evidence, safety, or release property.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/plugins/spec/references/GETTING_STARTED.md#Using%20STDO%2FThe%20Operating%20Loop\",\"start_line\":49}],\"statements\":[\"Choose actor count, repository layout, prompt construction engine, internal decomposition, search procedure and tool sequence where these cannot change a governed semantic, authority, evidence, safety or release property.\"]},\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:479d3ef31228914c804610a63b669425\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"forbidden_variation\":{\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":52,\"path\":\"plugins/spec/references/GETTING_STARTED.md\",\"quote\":\"STDO constrains governed relations. It does not prescribe an actor count,\\nrepository layout, prompt construction engine, internal decomposition, search\\nprocedure, or tool sequence where those choices cannot change a governed\\nsemantic, authority, evidence, safety, or release property.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/plugins/spec/references/GETTING_STARTED.md#Using%20STDO%2FThe%20Operating%20Loop\",\"start_line\":49}],\"statements\":[\"Treat the stated implementation latitude as a waiver of governed properties.\"]},\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:1fce941e8faea6ef73cd8ab817709955\",\"invalidation\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:invalidation:source-or-interpretation-change\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"latitude","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:bab3fa913819f7c18dd1df600d621f39","key":1692,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"allowed_variation\":{\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":254,\"path\":\"standards/ACTIVATION.md\",\"quote\":\"Steel thread, phased (waterfall) delivery and iterative delivery are\\npossible strategies, each with its own costs, feedback delays, integration risks and rework.\\nThe selection belongs to the realisation and to the actor exercising the\\nadmitted work authority; its material rationale is stated in existing\\ndesign or work records, and a claim that one strategy is superior states\\nthe objectives, comparison and assumptions it depends on. No exhaustive\\noptimisation, universal numerical budget, scalar cost measure or preferred\\nstrategy is imposed by this relation or its consumers (P2, P5, P6).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ACTIVATION.md#ACTIVATION%2F1.%20The%20step%2FConstruction%20relation\",\"start_line\":247},{\"end_line\":271,\"path\":\"standards/ACTIVATION.md\",\"quote\":\"independent actions may\\nproceed concurrently where their dependencies, effects and authority\\npermit. Local success supplies end-to-end success only when the required\\ncoverage, composition compatibility and outcome evidence hold;\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ACTIVATION.md#ACTIVATION%2F1.%20The%20step%2FConstruction%20relation\",\"start_line\":268},{\"end_line\":304,\"path\":\"standards/ACTIVATION.md\",\"quote\":\"A formal induction or\\ntermination claim supplies its premises and argument; no universal\\ntermination proof is required before bounded work can begin, and where\\nsuch a proof is absent the claim stays within the available evidence.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ACTIVATION.md#ACTIVATION%2F1.%20The%20step%2FConstruction%20relation\",\"start_line\":301}],\"statements\":[\"Select steel-thread, phased/waterfall, iterative or other admissible strategies under owning criteria and admitted work authority.\",\"Proceed concurrently with independent actions where dependencies, effects and authority permit.\",\"Begin bounded work without a universal termination proof while limiting claims to available evidence.\"]},\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:32042b38168b865f15b179aa395cf70f\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"forbidden_variation\":{\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":254,\"path\":\"standards/ACTIVATION.md\",\"quote\":\"Steel thread, phased (waterfall) delivery and iterative delivery are\\npossible strategies, each with its own costs, feedback delays, integration risks and rework.\\nThe selection belongs to the realisation and to the actor exercising the\\nadmitted work authority; its material rationale is stated in existing\\ndesign or work records, and a claim that one strategy is superior states\\nthe objectives, comparison and assumptions it depends on. No exhaustive\\noptimisation, universal numerical budget, scalar cost measure or preferred\\nstrategy is imposed by this relation or its consumers (P2, P5, P6).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ACTIVATION.md#ACTIVATION%2F1.%20The%20step%2FConstruction%20relation\",\"start_line\":247},{\"end_line\":271,\"path\":\"standards/ACTIVATION.md\",\"quote\":\"independent actions may\\nproceed concurrently where their dependencies, effects and authority\\npermit. Local success supplies end-to-end success only when the required\\ncoverage, composition compatibility and outcome evidence hold;\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ACTIVATION.md#ACTIVATION%2F1.%20The%20step%2FConstruction%20relation\",\"start_line\":268},{\"end_line\":304,\"path\":\"standards/ACTIVATION.md\",\"quote\":\"A formal induction or\\ntermination claim supplies its premises and argument; no universal\\ntermination proof is required before bounded work can begin, and where\\nsuch a proof is absent the claim stays within the available evidence.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ACTIVATION.md#ACTIVATION%2F1.%20The%20step%2FConstruction%20relation\",\"start_line\":301}],\"statements\":[\"Claim strategy superiority without objectives, comparison and assumptions.\",\"Impose exhaustive optimization, a universal numerical budget, scalar cost measure or preferred strategy as a requirement of this relation or its consumers.\",\"Infer end-to-end success solely from local success.\"]},\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:bab3fa913819f7c18dd1df600d621f39\",\"invalidation\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:invalidation:source-or-interpretation-change\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"latitude","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:39642dc93dc5b157003625d7d50d534e","key":1693,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"allowed_variation\":{\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":512,\"path\":\"standards/ACTIVATION.md\",\"quote\":\"These conditions constrain a configuration without\\ndetermining it. One frame or several, fixed or adaptive allocation, a\\nhierarchy, peer coordination, or an arrangement that changes as actors\\nallocate work within their contracts may each be adequate. The method\\nprescribes no role inventory, hierarchy, coordinator or actor sequence\\n(P0, P2; [RF-016](REFERENCE_FRAME.md#rf-016-implementation-neutrality)).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ACTIVATION.md#ACTIVATION%2F1.%20The%20step%2FConfiguration\",\"start_line\":507},{\"end_line\":527,\"path\":\"standards/ACTIVATION.md\",\"quote\":\"Direct entry. A one-frame configuration is lawful. One directly\\nauthorised task that fits a sufficient frame may be entered directly, as\\nRoles and delegation below states, subject to any separately required\\nassessment (P0, P2).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ACTIVATION.md#ACTIVATION%2F1.%20The%20step%2FConfiguration\",\"start_line\":524}],\"statements\":[\"Use one or several frames, fixed or adaptive allocation, hierarchy, peer coordination or changing allocation when adequate to operations, dependencies, capabilities and assurance.\",\"Enter a directly authorized task through one sufficient frame, subject to separately required assessment.\",\"Select the Executive configuration where applicable without making it the method default.\"]},\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:6df3862f885cf91fa2e0a1d3a1ea15aa\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"forbidden_variation\":{\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":512,\"path\":\"standards/ACTIVATION.md\",\"quote\":\"These conditions constrain a configuration without\\ndetermining it. One frame or several, fixed or adaptive allocation, a\\nhierarchy, peer coordination, or an arrangement that changes as actors\\nallocate work within their contracts may each be adequate. The method\\nprescribes no role inventory, hierarchy, coordinator or actor sequence\\n(P0, P2; [RF-016](REFERENCE_FRAME.md#rf-016-implementation-neutrality)).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ACTIVATION.md#ACTIVATION%2F1.%20The%20step%2FConfiguration\",\"start_line\":507},{\"end_line\":527,\"path\":\"standards/ACTIVATION.md\",\"quote\":\"Direct entry. A one-frame configuration is lawful. One directly\\nauthorised task that fits a sufficient frame may be entered directly, as\\nRoles and delegation below states, subject to any separately required\\nassessment (P0, P2).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ACTIVATION.md#ACTIVATION%2F1.%20The%20step%2FConfiguration\",\"start_line\":524}],\"statements\":[\"Accept or reject configuration solely from labels, topology, coordinator presence or familiar roles.\",\"Derive authority from frame selection or decomposition position.\",\"Exempt adaptive or self-organized allocation from preservation or independence conditions.\"]},\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:39642dc93dc5b157003625d7d50d534e\",\"invalidation\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:invalidation:source-or-interpretation-change\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"latitude","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:d4a783d1ca1d567d3bd607a438612193","key":1694,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"allowed_variation\":{\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":647,\"path\":\"standards/ACTIVATION.md\",\"quote\":\"Inside a step, a proxy so declared may\\naccept preservation, require local repair, reject a violating candidate\\nand advance to the next already-authorised action\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ACTIVATION.md#ACTIVATION%2F1.%20The%20step%2FRoles%20and%20delegation\",\"start_line\":638}],\"statements\":[\"A configuration may allocate responsibilities beyond constructor, assessor and decision owner.\",\"One actor may occupy different roles across different claims if independence for the assessed claim is preserved; no actor count is prescribed.\",\"A declared bounded proxy may accept preservation, require local repair, reject a violating candidate and advance to the next already-authorised action within its limit.\",\"Human ceremony need not occur at every transition when governing basis, affected cone, decision envelope and re-entry conditions are already accepted.\"]},\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:5a4be050afd6cab484eae2425fa439e5\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa