ence to several of\\nthem; every result stays bound to its own claim. A label such as `UAT`,\\n`E2E`, `integration` or `unit` has no assurance value without the\\ncorresponding frame declaration (P1, P6).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ASSURANCE.md#ASSURANCE%2F7.%20Product%20testing%20frame%20set%2FThe%20set\",\"start_line\":387}],\"statements\":[\"Widening a result beyond its own claim or treating overlap as hierarchy or decomposition.\"]},\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:419bec8d8eda85ee63c6c1e71f08d142\",\"invalidation\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:invalidation:source-or-interpretation-change\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"latitude","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:9edbc4d059e57c8d771b2e22cab3af0a","key":1703,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"allowed_variation\":{\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":418,\"path\":\"standards/ASSURANCE.md\",\"quote\":\"It may be automated only when the\\nautomation faithfully occupies the declared user frame and gains no path or\\ncapability that user lacks. Automation can execute acceptance evidence; it\\ncannot assume acceptance authority (P6; EVALUATION §5).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ASSURANCE.md#ASSURANCE%2F7.%20Product%20testing%20frame%20set%2FUser-acceptance%20frame\",\"start_line\":415}],\"statements\":[\"Automated UAT only when automation faithfully occupies the declared user frame with no path or capability unavailable to that user.\"]},\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:9e6e1272a4d33627b22f146f2f8b9751\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"forbidden_variation\":{\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":418,\"path\":\"standards/ASSURANCE.md\",\"quote\":\"It may be automated only when the\\nautomation faithfully occupies the declared user frame and gains no path or\\ncapability that user lacks. Automation can execute acceptance evidence; it\\ncannot assume acceptance authority (P6; EVALUATION §5).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ASSURANCE.md#ASSURANCE%2F7.%20Product%20testing%20frame%20set%2FUser-acceptance%20frame\",\"start_line\":415}],\"statements\":[\"Automation assuming human or Product acceptance ownership.\"]},\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:9edbc4d059e57c8d771b2e22cab3af0a\",\"invalidation\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:invalidation:source-or-interpretation-change\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"latitude","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:2e10474d48337fc6e8c5c8fda2d8a055","key":1704,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"allowed_variation\":{\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":472,\"path\":\"standards/ASSURANCE.md\",\"quote\":\"A substitute or test double may support a deliberately narrower claim only\\nwhen its equivalence boundary and exclusions are explicit. Its result\\ncannot be promoted to evidence that the real participant or Product\\ncomposition was exercised (P6, EVALUATION §1).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ASSURANCE.md#ASSURANCE%2F7.%20Product%20testing%20frame%20set%2FIntegration%20frame\",\"start_line\":469}],\"statements\":[\"An admitted substitute/test double may support a deliberately narrower integration claim with explicit equivalence boundary and exclusions.\"]},\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:1c4c010033a4beec67d91c7c12d3f812\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"forbidden_variation\":{\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":472,\"path\":\"standards/ASSURANCE.md\",\"quote\":\"A substitute or test double may support a deliberately narrower claim only\\nwhen its equivalence boundary and exclusions are explicit. Its result\\ncannot be promoted to evidence that the real participant or Product\\ncomposition was exercised (P6, EVALUATION §1).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ASSURANCE.md#ASSURANCE%2F7.%20Product%20testing%20frame%20set%2FIntegration%20frame\",\"start_line\":469}],\"statements\":[\"Promoting substitute results to proof that real participants or Product composition were exercised.\"]},\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:2e10474d48337fc6e8c5c8fda2d8a055\",\"invalidation\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:invalidation:source-or-interpretation-change\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"latitude","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:df01f713900396fe4811463c7189058b","key":1705,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"allowed_variation\":{\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":542,\"path\":\"standards/ASSURANCE.md\",\"quote\":\"No universal scalar is required. A project may define one only through\\nProduct, requirement or accepted-design authority, and keeps the\\nunderlying coverage coordinates rather than flattening them into a score\\n(P1, P6). A project-defined scalar is a quantified claim under\\n[FOUNDATIONS §4 Quantified assurance](FOUNDATIONS.md#quantified-assurance)\\nand keeps its model and limits explicit (P6).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ASSURANCE.md#ASSURANCE%2F8.%20Combinatorial%20coverage%20and%20testing%20value\",\"start_line\":537},{\"end_line\":571,\"path\":\"standards/ASSURANCE.md\",\"quote\":\"Pairwise or other covering-array reduction is\\nlawful only where the basis explains why the omitted higher-order\\ninteractions cannot change the claim, or keeps them as residuals.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ASSURANCE.md#ASSURANCE%2F8.%20Combinatorial%20coverage%20and%20testing%20value\",\"start_line\":569}],\"statements\":[\"A project may define a scalar only under Product, requirement or accepted-design authority, retaining coverage coordinates and explicit quantified-assurance model/limits; no universal scalar is required.\",\"Pairwise or other covering-array reduction only when the basis explains why omitted higher-order interactions cannot change the claim or retains them as residuals.\"]},\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:9998e713a60bf1ac244a0e611d7a518a\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"forbidden_variation\":{\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":542,\"path\":\"standards/ASSURANCE.md\",\"quote\":\"No universal scalar is required. A project may define one only through\\nProduct, requirement or accepted-design authority, and keeps the\\nunderlying coverage coordinates rather than flattening them into a score\\n(P1, P6). A project-defined scalar is a quantified claim under\\n[FOUNDATIONS §4 Quantified assurance](FOUNDATIONS.md#quantified-assurance)\\nand keeps its model and limits explicit (P6).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ASSURANCE.md#ASSURANCE%2F8.%20Combinatorial%20coverage%20and%20testing%20value\",\"start_line\":537},{\"end_line\":571,\"path\":\"standards/ASSURANCE.md\",\"quote\":\"Pairwise or other covering-array reduction is\\nlawful only where the basis explains why the omitted higher-order\\ninteractions cannot change the claim, or keeps them as residuals.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ASSURANCE.md#ASSURANCE%2F8.%20Combinatorial%20coverage%20and%20testing%20value\",\"start_line\":569}],\"statements\":[\"Flattening underlying coverage coordinates into a score.\",\"Silently discarding potentially material higher-order interactions.\"]},\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:df01f713900396fe4811463c7189058b\",\"invalidation\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:invalidation:source-or-interpretation-change\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"latitude","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:82c5dec1d39b7c06ad22108b86b49f18","key":1706,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"allowed_variation\":{\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":613,\"path\":\"standards/ASSURANCE.md\",\"quote\":\"A test-only seam is lawful when it is isolated from the Product\\ndistribution, excluded from ordinary-path evidence and declared in the\\nassurance subject. Its presence outside the production graph is not a\\nproduction-path failure. A retained obsolete test or proof consumer stays\\nan assurance defect when it can falsely establish the claim or reintroduce\\nthe removed path (P6).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ASSURANCE.md#ASSURANCE%2F9.%20Legitimate%20path%20and%20technical-debt%20erasure\",\"start_line\":608}],\"statements\":[\"A test-only seam isolated from Product distribution, excluded from ordinary-path evidence and declared in the assurance subject; its existence outside production closure is not a production-path failure.\"]},\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:3635e0d97a204bc786bfeff7cc2b76e4\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"forbidden_variation\":{\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":613,\"path\":\"standards/ASSURANCE.md\",\"quote\":\"A test-only seam is lawful when it is isolated from the Product\\ndistribution, excluded from ordinary-path evidence and declared in the\\nassurance subject. Its presence outside the production graph is not a\\nproduction-path failure. A retained obsolete test or proof consumer stays\\nan assurance defect when it can falsely establish the claim or reintroduce\\nthe removed path (P6).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ASSURANCE.md#ASSURANCE%2F9.%20Legitimate%20path%20and%20technical-debt%20erasure\",\"start_line\":608}],\"statements\":[\"Retained obsolete test/proof consumers falsely establishing claims or reintroducing removed paths; these remain assurance defects.\"]},\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:82c5dec1d39b7c06ad22108b86b49f18\",\"invalidation\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:invalidation:source-or-interpretation-change\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"latitude","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:9513b6768e25dd79a583ce4b3a76db4a","key":1707,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"allowed_variation\":{\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":689,\"path\":\"standards/ASSURANCE.md\",\"quote\":\"After lawful acquisition, an independently derived oracle may evaluate the\\ngoverning claim. Generic assurance mechanics may compute bytes, digests,\\nordering, equality, set membership, completeness and conjunction over\\nowner-issued evidence. Those mechanics stay evidence evaluators: they\\ncannot mint owner carriers, choose the current history, select the\\nauthoritative path, interpret domain lifecycle or admission meaning, or\\nbecome a runtime fallback (P6; EVALUATION §2).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ASSURANCE.md#ASSURANCE%2F11.%20Assurance%20subject%20acquisition%20and%20evaluation\",\"start_line\":683}],\"statements\":[\"After lawful acquisition, independent oracles may evaluate claims and generic mechanics may compute bytes, digests, ordering, equality, set membership, completeness and conjunction over owner-issued evidence.\"]},\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:4a758d8b16a2d0014a7ecd1bc24c03f7\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"forbidden_variation\":{\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":689,\"path\":\"standards/ASSURANCE.md\",\"quote\":\"After lawful acquisition, an independently derived oracle may evaluate the\\ngoverning claim. Generic assurance mechanics may compute bytes, digests,\\nordering, equality, set membership, completeness and conjunction over\\nowner-issued evidence. Those mechanics stay evidence evaluators: they\\ncannot mint owner carriers, choose the current history, select the\\nauthoritative path, interpret domain lifecycle or admission meaning, or\\nbecome a runtime fallback (P6; EVALUATION §2).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ASSURANCE.md#ASSURANCE%2F11.%20Assurance%20subject%20acquisition%20and%20evaluation\",\"start_line\":683}],\"statements\":[\"Minting owner carriers, choosing current history, selecting authoritative paths, interpreting domain lifecycle/admission meaning or becoming runtime fallback.\"]},\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:9513b6768e25dd79a583ce4b3a76db4a\",\"invalidation\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:invalidation:source-or-interpretation-change\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"latitude","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:8a3aec8d6a58e7f291dcb78d737d9f87","key":1708,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"allowed_variation\":{\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":327,\"path\":\"standards/AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS.md\",\"quote\":\"The tuple is abstract. A carrier may use records, tables, terms, clauses,\\ncode or any other representation only when its encoding profile proves\\nthat every tuple relation is preserved or explicitly refused (P1, P4b).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS.md#AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS%2F2.%20Signature\",\"start_line\":325}],\"statements\":[\"Records, tables, terms, clauses, code or any other carrier representation only when its encoding profile proves every abstract tuple relation preserved or explicitly refused.\"]},\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:d7d4d3087eb8ab6376c885fc78a46108\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"forbidden_variation\":{\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":327,\"path\":\"standards/AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS.md\",\"quote\":\"The tuple is abstract. A carrier may use records, tables, terms, clauses,\\ncode or any other representation only when its encoding profile proves\\nthat every tuple relation is preserved or explicitly refused (P1, P4b).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS.md#AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS%2F2.%20Signature\",\"start_line\":325}],\"statements\":[\"Treating carrier choice as permission to lose tuple relations silently.\"]},\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:8a3aec8d6a58e7f291dcb78d737d9f87\",\"invalidation\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:invalidation:source-or-interpretation-change\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:sc