algorithm/layout choices may remain open only when every admitted choice is semantically equivalent under the accepted network.\"]},\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:b8bc7d3a0ac93efb8d5099e60d3dfcad\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"forbidden_variation\":{\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":593,\"path\":\"standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md\",\"quote\":\"Local algorithm and layout\\nchoices may remain open only when every admitted choice is semantically\\nequivalent under the accepted network.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md#DESIGN_MODULE%2F5.%20Ontology-first%20design%2FDecision-complete%20symbolic%20design\",\"start_line\":591}],\"statements\":[\"Leaving materially non-equivalent alternatives open while claiming decision completeness.\"]},\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:ec8f1b790535a28896e55e37688c766c\",\"invalidation\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:invalidation:source-or-interpretation-change\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"latitude","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:cd354dd2b53f05ba810044bf8fbf0f36","key":1721,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"allowed_variation\":{\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":913,\"path\":\"standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md\",\"quote\":\"A relation\\nmay lawfully require one actor, several signatures, a quorum, a human\\nstep-up, delegated proxy authority or jurisdictional partitioning, provided\\nits cardinality and adjudication law are declared\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md#DESIGN_MODULE%2F5.%20Ontology-first%20design%2FTransformation%20admission%20completeness%20%28UP-016%29\",\"start_line\":910},{\"end_line\":901,\"path\":\"standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md\",\"quote\":\"Unsupported composite or nested forms use\\n`not_applicable` only when accepted domain or design excludes the form and\\nthe boundary has no weaker or competing admission path\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md#DESIGN_MODULE%2F5.%20Ontology-first%20design%2FTransformation%20admission%20completeness%20%28UP-016%29\",\"start_line\":899}],\"statements\":[\"Multiple actors, stages or implementations may constitute or instantiate disjoint parts of one declared relation.\",\"One actor, multiple signatures, quorum, human step-up, delegated proxy authority or jurisdictional partitioning are lawful when cardinality and adjudication law are declared.\",\"Unsupported composite/nested forms may be not_applicable only when accepted domain/design excludes them and no weaker or competing admission path exists.\"]},\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:d2d50ec064f37926a95bcc1bbbb51190\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"forbidden_variation\":{\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":913,\"path\":\"standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md\",\"quote\":\"A relation\\nmay lawfully require one actor, several signatures, a quorum, a human\\nstep-up, delegated proxy authority or jurisdictional partitioning, provided\\nits cardinality and adjudication law are declared\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md#DESIGN_MODULE%2F5.%20Ontology-first%20design%2FTransformation%20admission%20completeness%20%28UP-016%29\",\"start_line\":910},{\"end_line\":901,\"path\":\"standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md\",\"quote\":\"Unsupported composite or nested forms use\\n`not_applicable` only when accepted domain or design excludes the form and\\nthe boundary has no weaker or competing admission path\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md#DESIGN_MODULE%2F5.%20Ontology-first%20design%2FTransformation%20admission%20completeness%20%28UP-016%29\",\"start_line\":899}],\"statements\":[\"Inferring singularity from a single component or inferring non-applicability from parser/helper/manufactured refusal.\"]},\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:cd354dd2b53f05ba810044bf8fbf0f36\",\"invalidation\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:invalidation:source-or-interpretation-change\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"latitude","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:7d73136c4ed185732ffc8a16f1f500a7","key":1722,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"allowed_variation\":{\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":966,\"path\":\"standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md\",\"quote\":\"This does not require monadic or category-theory vocabulary\\n(SPEC_METHOD §2 Realisation shape). A product under the graph-execution\\nprofile may bind the requirement to GTL composition and ABG\\ninterpretation; another product may use another explicit algebra.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md#DESIGN_MODULE%2F5.%20Ontology-first%20design%2FAtomic%20functions%20and%20higher-order%20composition\",\"start_line\":963}],\"statements\":[\"A graph-execution Product may bind composition to GTL and ABG interpretation; another Product may choose another explicit algebra.\",\"Monadic or category-theory terminology is not required.\"]},\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:c568f26576d25f251810727e0b735e24\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"forbidden_variation\":{\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":966,\"path\":\"standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md\",\"quote\":\"This does not require monadic or category-theory vocabulary\\n(SPEC_METHOD §2 Realisation shape). A product under the graph-execution\\nprofile may bind the requirement to GTL composition and ABG\\ninterpretation; another product may use another explicit algebra.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md#DESIGN_MODULE%2F5.%20Ontology-first%20design%2FAtomic%20functions%20and%20higher-order%20composition\",\"start_line\":963}],\"statements\":[\"Hiding applicable composition/effect/authority-conservation laws in controller flow.\"]},\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:7d73136c4ed185732ffc8a16f1f500a7\",\"invalidation\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:invalidation:source-or-interpretation-change\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"latitude","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:ac4f3c6a43f6a88e4d0c56f4bcf59250","key":1723,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"allowed_variation\":{\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1306,\"path\":\"standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md\",\"quote\":\"A project may ratify another text-native\\ndiagram format only when it preserves the same three distinct views and the\\nsame cross-view checks.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md#DESIGN_MODULE%2F7.%20Ontology%20and%20three-view%20design%20gate\",\"start_line\":1300}],\"statements\":[\"A project may ratify another text-native format only if it preserves the three distinct views and the same cross-view checks.\",\"Views may occupy one existing design surface and share one acceptance decision; three files, tickets, reviews or ceremonies are unnecessary.\"]},\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:c19d38e4362efe35b2f5323c54192a62\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"forbidden_variation\":{\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1306,\"path\":\"standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md\",\"quote\":\"A project may ratify another text-native\\ndiagram format only when it preserves the same three distinct views and the\\nsame cross-view checks.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md#DESIGN_MODULE%2F7.%20Ontology%20and%20three-view%20design%20gate\",\"start_line\":1300}],\"statements\":[\"Substituting one broad flowchart for the three models.\"]},\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:ac4f3c6a43f6a88e4d0c56f4bcf59250\",\"invalidation\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:invalidation:source-or-interpretation-change\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"latitude","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:fde6c6c5c675918b41720d99a9e6ec42","key":1724,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"allowed_variation\":{\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1610,\"path\":\"standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md\",\"quote\":\"A component may\\nlawfully hold several roles. Three cases are distinguished: behaviour\\nalready inside an abstract declared role is ordinary variation; a new\\noperational responsibility and a new semantic or authoritative role are\\neach design changes, and only those two require re-entry.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md#DESIGN_MODULE%2F7.%20Ontology%20and%20three-view%20design%20gate%2FComputational%20realisation%20projection%20%28UP-019%29\",\"start_line\":1606}],\"statements\":[\"One component may lawfully hold multiple declared roles.\",\"Behaviour already inside an abstract declared role is ordinary variation without design re-entry.\"]},\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:1ffb0d473667cbcd448ccf239b30f413\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"forbidden_variation\":{\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1610,\"path\":\"standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md\",\"quote\":\"A component may\\nlawfully hold several roles. Three cases are distinguished: behaviour\\nalready inside an abstract declared role is ordinary variation; a new\\noperational responsibility and a new semantic or authoritative role are\\neach design changes, and only those two require re-entry.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md#DESIGN_MODULE%2F7.%20Ontology%20and%20three-view%20design%20gate%2FComputational%20realisation%20projection%20%28UP-019%29\",\"start_line\":1606}],\"statements\":[\"Treating a new operational responsibility or new semantic/authoritative role as ordinary variation.\",\"Inferring semantic truth or authority from technological capability or out-of-role use.\"]},\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:fde6c6c5c675918b41720d99a9e6ec42\",\"invalidation\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:invalidation:source-or-interpretation-change\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"latitude","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:0dbacd20c7ae605e4d82a75cbeaf263f","key":1725,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"allowed_variation\":{\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1674,\"path\":\"standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md\",\"quote\":\"Isolation, substrate, performance, security and\\ndependency ownership are each lawful grounds for an independent\\nimplementation. The invariant is not that equivalent code is never\\nrebuilt; it is that a local realisation does not present an existing\\naccepted semantic or authoritative relation as newly owned local truth\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md#DESIGN_MODULE%2F7.%20Ontology%20and%20three-view%20design%20gate%2FComputational%20realisation%20projection%20%28UP-019%29\",\"start_line\":1669}],\"statements\":[\"Independent implementation for isolation, substrate, performance, security or dependency ownership.\",\"Consume, local implementation, optimisation, adaptation or deliberate duplication with stated non-semantic constraints and a semantic disposition.\"]},\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:8e5e05d12a032d36a117b5f56176885c\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"forbidden_variation\":{\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1674,\"path\":\"standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md\",\"quote\":\"Isolation, substrate, performance, security and\\ndependency ownership are each lawful grounds for an independent\\nimplementation. The invariant is not that equivalent code is never\\nrebuilt; it is that a local realisation does not present an existing\\naccepted semantic or authoritative relation as newly owned local truth\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md#DESIGN_MODULE%2F7.%20Ontology%20and%20three-view%20design%20gate%2FComputational%20realisation%20projection%20%28UP-019%29\",\"start_line\":1669}],\"statements\":[\"Presenting an existing accepted semantic or authoritative relation as newly owned local truth.\",\"Commonising superficial similarity despite materially non-equivalent governing laws.\"]},\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:0dbacd20c7ae605e4d82a75cbeaf263f\",\"invalidation\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:invalidation:source-or-interpretation-change\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"latitude","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:1421999cb80704265b31200c74a1f9e8","key":1726,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"allowed_variation\":{\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":2051,\"path\":\"standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md\",\"quote\":\"A worker may be told where to inspect and what\\ncontract to satisfy. A prompt clause that exists to enforce design law\\nneeds provenance and a proof that the clause still causes or prevents the\\nintended behaviour\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md#DESIGN_MODULE%2F11.%20Review\",\"start_line\":2048}],\"statements\":[\"Tell a worker where to inspect and which contract to satisfy.\"]},\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:0793e8125983d93adb20487fbf5a9458\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"forbidden_variation\":{\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":2051,\"path\":\"standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md\",\"quote\":\"A worker may be told where to inspect and what\\ncontract to satisfy. A prompt clause that exists to enforce design law\\nneeds provenance and a proof that the clause still causes or prevents the\\nintended behaviour\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md#DESIGN_MODULE%2F11.%20Review\",\"start_line\":2048}],\"statements\":[\"Using a design-law-enforcement clause without provenance and proof of its continuing intended effect.\"]},\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:1421999cb80704265b31200c74a1f9e8\",\"invalidation\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:invalidation:source-or-interpretation-change\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"latitude","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:1c6424f725783132568b617cf5b1c54d","key":1727,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"allowed_variation\":{\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":2408,\"path\":\"standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md\",\"quote\":\"Partial adoption is allowed, but the adopted boundary and adopted rule\\nfamily should be named explicitly. Partial adoption may narrow scope; it is\\nnot used to claim design-method completion while skipping the evidence\\nneeded to audit, refactor or reconstruct the realised boundary\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md#DESIGN_MODULE%2F12.%20Adoption%20and%20relations%2FAdoption\",\"start_line\":2405}],\"statements\":[\"Product authority may record adoption through ADR/design citation, agent-entry preference, migration-ticket review criteria and module taxonomy.\",\"Partial adoption may narrow scope; the boundary and rule family should be explicit.\"]},\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:0bfa7a9a55ccb9c21fe73b41be970541\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"forbidden_variation\":{\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":2408,\"path\":\"standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md\",\"quote\":\"Partial adoption is allowed, but the adopted boundary and adopted rule\\nfamily should be named explicitly. Partial adoption may narrow scope; it is\\nnot used to claim design-method completion while skipping the evidence\\nneeded to audit, refactor or reconstruct the realised boundary\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md#DESIGN_MODULE%2F12.%20Adoption%20and%20relations%2FAdoption\",\"start_line\":2405}],\"statements\":[\"Treating profile availability as adoption.\",\"Adding an adopter beyond Product authority.\",\"Claiming completion through partial adoption while omitting evidence required for audit, refactor or reconstruction.\"]},\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:1c6424f725783132568b617cf5b1c54d\",\"invalidation\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:invalidation:source-or-interpretation-change\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"latitude","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:a6307631ea1a3c76063a6bdc2607c453","key":1728,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"allowed_variation\":{\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":2462,\"path\":\"standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md\",\"quote\":\"What this profile does not require (one specific programming language,\\nelimination of all imperative code, monadic or category-theory vocabulary,\\nreplacing every exception with a custom algebraic type), what it does\\nrequire of implementation shape, and the composition and effect algebra\\nthat remains required where a boundary composes higher-order or effectful\\ncomputation are stated once in\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md#DESIGN_MODULE%2F12.%20Adoption%20and%20relations%2FNon-goals\",\"start_line\":2457}],\"statements\":[\"The profile leaves programming language, retention of some imperative code, use of monadic/category-theory terminology and treatment of individual exceptions unconstrained by the listed non-goals.\"]},\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:bb53ea665dafe38a1f8718f3b042739a\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"forbidden_variation\":{\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":2462,\"path\":\"standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md\",\"quote\":\"What this profile does not require (one specific programming language,\\nelimination of all imperative code, monadic or category-theory vocabulary,\\nreplacing every exception with a custom algebraic type), what it does\\nrequire of implementation shape, and the composition and effect algebra\\nthat remains required where a boundary composes higher-order or effectful\\ncomputation are stated once in\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md#DESIGN_MODULE%2F12.%20Adoption%20and%20relations%2FNon-goals\",\"start_line\":2457}],\"statements\":[\"Using those non-goals to waive required composition/effect algebra for higher-order or effectful boundaries.\"]},\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:a6307631ea1a3c76063a6bdc2607c453\",\"invalidation\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:invalidation:source-or-interpretation-change\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"latitude","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:078f244c8017f14de2c1a134cc95be7f","key":1729,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"allowed_variation\":{\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":137,\"path\":\"standards/EVALUATION.md\",\"quote\":\"One actor may lawfully perform\\nseveral; the record keeps them distinguishable.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/EVALUATION.md#EVALUATION%2F2.%20Separation\",\"start_line\":136},{\"end_line\":153,\"path\":\"standards/EVALUATION.md\",\"quote\":\"A broad digest may conservatively\\ninvalidate a review; it does not prove that every semantic relation\\nchanged\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/EVALUATION.md#EVALUATION%2F2.%20Separation\",\"start_line\":151}],\"statements\":[\"One actor may perform several evaluation roles with distinguishable records.\",\"A broad digest change may conservatively invalidate a review.\"]},\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:c069b37d4f1a0f0716eb0d9fe2891726\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"forbidden_variation\":{\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":137,\"path\":\"standards/EVALUATION.md\",\"quote\":\"One actor may lawfully perform\\nseveral; the record keeps them distinguishable.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/EVALUATION.md#EVALUATION%2F2.%20Separation\",\"start_line\":136},{\"end_line\":153,\"path\":\"standards/EVALUATION.md\",\"quote\":\"A broad digest may conservatively\\ninvalidate a review; it does not prove that every semantic relation\\nchanged\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/EVALUATION.md#EVALUATION%2F2.%20Separation\",\"start_line\":151}],\"statements\":[\"Conflating roles because one actor performs them.\",\"Inferring that every semantic relation changed from a broad digest change.\",\"Treating conservative digest invalidation as universally required.\"]},\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:078f244c8017f14de2c1a134cc95be7f\",\"invalidation\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:invalidation:source-or-interpretation-change\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"latitude","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:523a484ab6f6aa68dd6a9ce5de7a0dae","key":1730,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"allowed_variation\":{\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":443,\"path\":\"standards/EVALUATION.md\",\"quote\":\"A lawful alternative construction permitted by the basis\\npasses. Subjective similarity to the basis or the reference is insufficient\\nto establish conformance or equivalence. Byte or structural identity,\\nunique derivation, determinism and incumbent equality are not generic\\ncomparison criteria.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/EVALUATION.md#EVALUATION%2F6.%20Conformance%20of%20realisations\",\"start_line\":439}],\"statements\":[\"Multiple realisations may satisfy one specification.\",\"A lawful alternative allowed by the governing basis passes.\",\"Applicable separately held reference outcomes may be optional non-authoritative evidence.\",\"Accepted exact-current evidence may be reused after applicability/invalidation checks.\"]},\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:cae7dff6a99951473cac43cb9487326d\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:6d96b75770d3c078aeccf46c41c1bc6f\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"forbidden_variation\":{\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":443,\"path\":\"standards/EVALUATION.md\",\"quote\":\"A lawful alternative construction permitted by the basis\\npasses. Subjective similarity to the basis or the reference is insufficient\\nto establish conformance or equivalence. Byte or structural identity,\\nunique derivation, determinism and incumbent equality are not generic\\ncomparison criteria.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/EVALUATION.md#EVALUATION%2F6.%20Conformance%20of%20realisations\",\"start_line\":439}],\"statements\":[\"Generic demands for unique derivation, determinism, byte/structural identity or incumbent equality.\",\"Treating reference similarity as authority or sufficient proof.\",\"Hiding material ambiguity to claim sufficiency.\",\"Using reconstructability as restart authority or an excuse for stale success.\"]},\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:523a484ab6f6aa68dd6a9ce5de7a0dae\",\"invalidation\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:invalidation:source-or-interpretation-change\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"latitude","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:c07f0192470668c41fdb47e67e81b43f","key":1731,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"allowed_variation\":{\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":632,\"path\":\"standards/EVALUATION.md\",\"quote\":\"Qualification may\\nbe staged\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/EVALUATION.md#EVALUATION%2F7.%20Qualification%20of%20frames%20and%20of%20the%20method%2FMethod%20self-qualification\",\"start_line\":625}],\"statements\":[\"Qualification may be staged, with each verdict confined to the exact evaluated functions, branches and populations.\",\"Prior exemplars may be optional comparison evidence after freeze.\"]},\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:6a2c32a018781528793f87b832b7cdf2\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"forbidden_variation\":{\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":632,\"path\":\"standards/EVALUATION.md\",\"quote\":\"Qualification may\\nbe staged\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/EVALUATION.md#EVALUATION%2F7.%20Qualification%20of%20frames%20and%20of%20the%20method%2FMethod%20self-qualification\",\"start_line\":625}],\"statements\":[\"Giving unevaluated functions or branches a whole-method verdict.\",\"Treating exemplars as mandatory target answers without explicit governing-basis equivalence requirements.\"]},\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:c07f0192470668c41fdb47e67e81b43f\",\"invalidation\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:invalidation:source-or-interpretation-change\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"latitude","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:290d1db7d1479db3edb80c51444f57fb","key":1732,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"allowed_variation\":{\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":105,\"path\":\"standards/EXECUTIVE_BASELINE.md\",\"quote\":\"A project may adopt this profile or define another frame configuration\\n(§16).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/EXECUTIVE_BASELINE.md#EXECUTIVE_BASELINE%2F1.%20Canonical%20compression\",\"start_line\":98}],\"statements\":[\"A project may adopt this profile or define another frame configuration.\",\"Select the executive configuration where it fits; other configurations may use other names, frames or topology and are judged against their own tasks.\",\"A local axioms file may carry the authorised adoption decision.\"]},\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:495aa231497a5ecc0c35bbb322f4f213\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:668afb84e5d220dd4674a57a384862c4\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"forbidden_variation\":{\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":105,\"path\":\"standards/EXECUTIVE_BASELINE.md\",\"quote\":\"A project may adopt this profile or define another frame configuration\\n(§16).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/EXECUTIVE_BASELINE.md#EXECUTIVE_BASELINE%2F1.%20Canonical%20compression\",\"start_line\":98}],\"statements\":[\"Treating this configuration as the method default.\",\"Treating decision carriage as constitutional ownership.\",\"Treating departure from method law as local frame selection rather than a separate method basis or recorded non-conformance.\"]},\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:290d1db7d1479db3edb80c51444f57fb\",\"invalidation\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:invalidation:source-or-interpretation-change\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:acto