-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/FOUNDATIONS.md#FOUNDATIONS%2F4.%20Algebra%2FConjunction%20of%20results\",\"start_line\":1006}],\"statements\":[\"Invent a universal order among non-satisfied values.\",\"Override gap, counterexample, evidence-applicability or basis-agreement requirements.\",\"Transfer contributing evaluations' semantic authority.\"]},\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:c5bc9b87623c8a8367ee9497e255dcb0\",\"invalidation\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:invalidation:source-or-interpretation-change\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"latitude","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:ddb5f69df792e9cb05279f14eaa22c40","key":1750,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"allowed_variation\":{\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1056,\"path\":\"standards/FOUNDATIONS.md\",\"quote\":\"A tenant chooses its representation and execution within these obligations. The notation\\nstates proof obligations; writing an implication does not discharge it.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/FOUNDATIONS.md#FOUNDATIONS%2F4.%20Algebra%2FAssurance%20relations\",\"start_line\":1055}],\"statements\":[\"A tenant chooses representation and execution within the assurance obligations.\",\"The named owners choose adequacy relations, composition laws, domains, observation/evaluation relations, strategy paths, risk policies, dependency representations and formal carriers within their stated ownership.\"]},\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:a69423fbd046a97b345dff84e7d2be8f\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"forbidden_variation\":{\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1056,\"path\":\"standards/FOUNDATIONS.md\",\"quote\":\"A tenant chooses its representation and execution within these obligations. The notation\\nstates proof obligations; writing an implication does not discharge it.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/FOUNDATIONS.md#FOUNDATIONS%2F4.%20Algebra%2FAssurance%20relations\",\"start_line\":1055}],\"statements\":[\"Treat a written implication as discharged proof.\",\"Treat a family-table explanation as a separate deciding rule.\"]},\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:ddb5f69df792e9cb05279f14eaa22c40\",\"invalidation\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:invalidation:source-or-interpretation-change\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"latitude","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:b3174198149b79c0d1a6a740197f4d23","key":1751,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"allowed_variation\":{\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1270,\"path\":\"standards/FOUNDATIONS.md\",\"quote\":\"These relationships are recoverable from the existing sources, bindings\\nand evidence carriers. Shared derivations can be recorded once and applied\\nto a declared family. No new per-test document, parallel ledger, fixed\\nnumber of reviewers or prescribed provenance format is required (P6).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/FOUNDATIONS.md#FOUNDATIONS%2F4.%20Algebra%2FParallel%20derivation%20and%20mutual%20assurance\",\"start_line\":1267}],\"statements\":[\"Use different construction and assertion paths from a common obligation.\",\"Use implementation-derived tests for regression or a stated local property.\",\"Permit different outputs within the same acceptable relation.\",\"Recover provenance from existing sources, bindings and evidence carriers.\",\"Record shared derivations once for a declared family.\"]},\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:17185edeb211602f3f2cb3d5ef889e0f\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:4530a9f715df287b4ea597f2bbf43a15\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"forbidden_variation\":{\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1270,\"path\":\"standards/FOUNDATIONS.md\",\"quote\":\"These relationships are recoverable from the existing sources, bindings\\nand evidence carriers. Shared derivations can be recorded once and applied\\nto a declared family. No new per-test document, parallel ledger, fixed\\nnumber of reviewers or prescribed provenance format is required (P6).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/FOUNDATIONS.md#FOUNDATIONS%2F4.%20Algebra%2FParallel%20derivation%20and%20mutual%20assurance\",\"start_line\":1267}],\"statements\":[\"Infer independent fidelity from repeated implementation decisions.\",\"Infer correctness or statistical independence merely from agreement, actor diversity or repeated evidence.\"]},\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:b3174198149b79c0d1a6a740197f4d23\",\"invalidation\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:invalidation:source-or-interpretation-change\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"latitude","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:d0405f137dcf93be1ad9575c557b3219","key":1752,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"allowed_variation\":{\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1322,\"path\":\"standards/FOUNDATIONS.md\",\"quote\":\"Unsupported numeric\\nconfidence remains unresolved; qualitative evidence and stated limits\\nremain usable within the governing policy. No universal probability\\nthreshold is imposed and no probability estimate is required for every\\ntest. Required safety, authority and acceptance conditions cannot be\\nwaived by a cheaper assurance plan (P5, P6).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/FOUNDATIONS.md#FOUNDATIONS%2F4.%20Algebra%2FQuantified%20assurance\",\"start_line\":1317}],\"statements\":[\"Select required assurance under admitted work authority for stated risk, obligations and resources.\",\"Use qualitative evidence with stated limits within governing policy.\",\"Leave unsupported numeric confidence unresolved.\",\"Omit per-test probability estimates; the member imposes no universal probability threshold.\"]},\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:cc5f5776011ad47b85c4351075c214f5\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"forbidden_variation\":{\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1322,\"path\":\"standards/FOUNDATIONS.md\",\"quote\":\"Unsupported numeric\\nconfidence remains unresolved; qualitative evidence and stated limits\\nremain usable within the governing policy. No universal probability\\nthreshold is imposed and no probability estimate is required for every\\ntest. Required safety, authority and acceptance conditions cannot be\\nwaived by a cheaper assurance plan (P5, P6).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/FOUNDATIONS.md#FOUNDATIONS%2F4.%20Algebra%2FQuantified%20assurance\",\"start_line\":1317}],\"statements\":[\"Waive required safety, authority or acceptance conditions for a cheaper assurance plan.\",\"Invent missing priors, likelihoods or undefined conditional values.\",\"Treat detection probability as whole-product correctness.\"]},\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:d0405f137dcf93be1ad9575c557b3219\",\"invalidation\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:invalidation:source-or-interpretation-change\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"latitude","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:79e4a2e11bb608a5914708434f58e2f9","key":1753,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"allowed_variation\":{\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1344,\"path\":\"standards/FOUNDATIONS.md\",\"quote\":\"The representation of these dependencies is the tenant's choice; no\\nexhaustive graph database is required.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/FOUNDATIONS.md#FOUNDATIONS%2F4.%20Algebra%2FChange%20impact%20and%20evidence%20reuse\",\"start_line\":1343},{\"end_line\":1400,\"path\":\"standards/FOUNDATIONS.md\",\"quote\":\"full-suite execution remains available and may itself have\\ncoverage gaps. No universal full-suite cadence follows, and no\\noptimisation removes a separately required gate.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/FOUNDATIONS.md#FOUNDATIONS%2F4.%20Algebra%2FChange%20impact%20and%20evidence%20reuse\",\"start_line\":1398}],\"statements\":[\"Choose the dependency representation without an exhaustive graph database.\",\"Reuse evidence whose applicability and preservation conditions are established.\",\"Widen reassessment for broad/unknown impact, model changes, release rules or missed dependencies.\",\"Run the full suite, without assuming it covers everything or imposing a universal cadence.\",\"Acquire diagnostic evidence before repair is justified.\"]},\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:5a25ded62c9539a0ed3a79b1b0ff63bb\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"forbidden_variation\":{\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1344,\"path\":\"standards/FOUNDATIONS.md\",\"quote\":\"The representation of these dependencies is the tenant's choice; no\\nexhaustive graph database is required.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/FOUNDATIONS.md#FOUNDATIONS%2F4.%20Algebra%2FChange%20impact%20and%20evidence%20reuse\",\"start_line\":1343},{\"end_line\":1400,\"path\":\"standards/FOUNDATIONS.md\",\"quote\":\"full-suite execution remains available and may itself have\\ncoverage gaps. No universal full-suite cadence follows, and no\\noptimisation removes a separately required gate.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/FOUNDATIONS.md#FOUNDATIONS%2F4.%20Algebra%2FChange%20impact%20and%20evidence%20reuse\",\"start_line\":1398}],\"statements\":[\"Exclude a check merely because no dependency edge is recorded.\",\"Remove a mandatory gate through selection or cost optimisation.\",\"Treat selection as execution evidence.\",\"Treat a changed hash alone as invalidity or equivalence.\"]},\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:79e4a2e11bb608a5914708434f58e2f9\",\"invalidation\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:invalidation:source-or-interpretation-change\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"latitude","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:492bc2fd0a13ff0d85c76bb5f54252ca","key":1754,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"allowed_variation\":{\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":36,\"path\":\"standards/IDENTITY.md\",\"quote\":\"- the same literal token may be lawful in different scopes when its\\n  authority and kind differ;\\n- one string format is not sufficient to define identity across all\\n  products and runtime surfaces; and\\n- a human-readable form may help recognition, but readability is\\n  secondary to uniqueness and stable governed meaning.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/IDENTITY.md#IDENTITY%2F1.%20Position\",\"start_line\":31},{\"end_line\":179,\"path\":\"standards/IDENTITY.md\",\"quote\":\"- a GUID is lawful even when it carries no human meaning;\\n- a readable identity is lawful only if it still preserves uniqueness in\\n  scope; and\\n- no reader should infer that a readable identity is safer or more\\n  authoritative than an opaque one merely because it looks meaningful.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/IDENTITY.md#IDENTITY%2F3.%20Readable%20and%20opaque%20identity\",\"start_line\":175}],\"statements\":[\"Opaque GUID/UUID identity without human meaning.\",\"Readable identity only while preserving scoped uniqueness.\",\"Hybrid readable/opaque identity.\",\"Reuse of a literal token in different scopes when authority and kind differ.\"]},\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:592f428587096675d25235df24f32725\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"forbidden_variation\":{\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":36,\"path\":\"standards/IDENTITY.md\",\"quote\":\"- the same literal token may be lawful in different scopes when its\\n  authority and kind differ;\\n- one string format is not sufficient to define identity across all\\n  products and runtime surfaces; and\\n- a human-readable form may help recognition, but readability is\\n  secondary to uniqueness and stable governed meaning.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/IDENTITY.md#IDENTITY%2F1.%20Position\",\"start_line\":31},{\"end_line\":179,\"path\":\"standards/IDENTITY.md\",\"quote\":\"- a GUID is lawful even when it carries no human meaning;\\n- a readable identity is lawful only if it still preserves uniqueness in\\n  scope; and\\n- no reader should infer that a readable identity is safer or more\\n  authoritative than an opaque one merely because it looks meaningful.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/IDENTITY.md#IDENTITY%2F3.%20Readable%20and%20opaque%20identity\",\"start_line\":175}],\"statements\":[\"Treating one string format as sufficient across all products/runtime surfaces.\",\"Inferring greater safety or authority merely from readability; the source states this as a should-not recommendation.\"]},\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:492bc2fd0a13ff0d85c76bb5f54252ca\",\"invalidation\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:invalidation:source-or-interpretation-change\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"latitude","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:43819086a3272e57931e4ad5d685f4b1","key":1755,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"allowed_variation\":{\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":110,\"path\":\"standards/IDENTITY.md\",\"quote\":\"Optional\\nadditional coordinates may include parent scope, revision, publication\\nversion and temporal coordinates (P3).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/IDENTITY.md#IDENTITY%2F2.%20Core%20law%2FScoped%20identity\",\"start_line\":108}],\"statements\":[\"Additional coordinates may include parent scope, revision, publication version and temporal coordinates.\"]},\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:592f428587096675d25235df24f32725\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"forbidden_variation\":{\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":110,\"path\":\"standards/IDENTITY.md\",\"quote\":\"Optional\\nadditional coordinates may include parent scope, revision, publication\\nversion and temporal coordinates (P3).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/IDENTITY.md#IDENTITY%2F2.%20Core%20law%2FScoped%20identity\",\"start_line\":108}],\"statements\":[]},\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:43819086a3272e57931e4ad5d685f4b1\",\"invalidation\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:invalidation:source-or-interpretation-change\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"latitude","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:d7d6a6e6a536dfc002cf75323b9989ae","key":1756,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"allowed_variation\":{\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":245,\"path\":\"standards/IDENTITY.md\",\"quote\":\"Human authority may act directly or through an explicitly admitted\\nbounded proxy. Proxy actor identity and human-authority identity remain\\ndistinct; a profile's own surfaces may project the human-authority\\nrelation under that profile's term (PROFILES).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/IDENTITY.md#IDENTITY%2F6.%20Authority%20identity%20and%20conservation%20%28STDO-UP-004%29\",\"start_line\":240}],\"statements\":[\"Human authority may act directly or through an explicitly admitted bounded proxy.\",\"A profile may project the human-authority relation on its own surfaces under its own term.\"]},\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:413efc4ed18e10f86b5c76f1f98556e0\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:0ed41260452a87de6836fa5047cb79ce\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"forbidden_variation\":{\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":245,\"path\":\"standards/IDENTITY.md\",\"quote\":\"Human authority may act directly or through an explicitly admitted\\nbounded proxy. Proxy actor identity and human-authority identity remain\\ndistinct; a profile's own surfaces may project the human-authority\\nrelation under that profile's term (PROFILES).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/IDENTITY.md#IDENTITY%2F6.%20Authority%20identity%20and%20conservation%20%28STDO-UP-004%29\",\"start_line\":240}],\"statements\":[\"Collapsing proxy actor identity into human-authority identity.\",\"Widening a ruling by recording it.\",\"Treating proxy self-review as independent or conferring unrelated runtime/domain authority.\"]},\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:d7d6a6e6a536dfc002cf75323b9989ae\",\"invalidation\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:invalidation:source-or-interpretation-change\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"latitude","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:7c40146fda5bfd9091fa7985425f5946","key":1757,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"allowed_variation\":{\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":304,\"path\":\"standards/IDENTITY.md\",\"quote\":\"Suitable publication surfaces include (P6, P3):\\n\\n- the product definition (conventionally `PRODUCT.md`) for the active\\n  identity kinds and their governed role;\\n- requirement surfaces for obligations around identity stability or\\n  uniqueness;\\n- design or ADR surfaces for parsing, serialisation or normalisation\\n  rules; and\\n- a dedicated identity registry surface, such as a project's own\\n  `IDENTITY.md`, when the domain has enough complexity to justify one.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/IDENTITY.md#IDENTITY%2F7.%20Default%20formats%20and%20overrides%2FOverride%20publication%20surface\",\"start_line\":295}],\"statements\":[\"Product definition, conventionally PRODUCT.md, for active identity kinds and governed role.\",\"Requirement surfaces for stability/uniqueness obligations.\",\"Design or ADR surfaces for parsing, serialisation or normalisation rules.\",\"Dedicated project identity registry, such as IDENTITY.md, when domain complexity justifies it.\"]},\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:487b998011fc8bbf86f5688efd791a52\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"forbidden_variation\":{\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":304,\"path\":\"standards/IDENTITY.md\",\"quote\":\"Suitable publication surfaces include (P6, P3):\\n\\n- the product definition (conventionally `PRODUCT.md`) for the active\\n  identity kinds and their governed role;\\n- requirement surfaces for obligations around identity stability or\\n  uniqueness;\\n- design or ADR surfaces for parsing, serialisation or normalisation\\n  rules; and\\n- a dedicated identity registry surface, such as a project's own\\n  `IDENTITY.md`, when the domain has enough complexity to justify one.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/IDENTITY.md#IDENTITY%2F7.%20Default%20formats%20and%20overrides%2FOverride%20publication%20surface\",\"start_line\":295}],\"statements\":[\"An override existing only as implementation-code inference or hidden regex assumptions.\"]},\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:7c40146fda5bfd9091fa7985425f5946\",\"invalidation\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:invalidation:source-or-interpretation-change\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"latitude","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:db1bee36a452fd10ba89dd0771cabc47","key":1758,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"allowed_variation\":{\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":378,\"path\":\"standards/IDENTITY.md\",\"quote\":\"- runtime event identities generated as UUIDs by a consumer-bound runtime\\n  realisation;\\n- requirement identities such as `REQ-F-CAPABILITY-001` when the domain\\n  defines them as concrete `requirement` identities;\\n- family identities such as `REQ-F-CAPABILITY` when the domain defines\\n  them separately as `requirement_family`; and\\n- acceptance-criterion identities such as `REQ-F-CAPABILITY-001-AC-01`\\n  when the domain defines them as a separate `acceptance_criterion`\\n  identity kind.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/IDENTITY.md#IDENTITY%2F11.%20Examples%2FLawful\",\"start_line\":370},{\"end_line\":388,\"path\":\"standards/IDENTITY.md\",\"quote\":\"- treating `REQ-F-CAPABILITY-*` or `REQ-F-CAPABILITY` as a concrete\\n  requirement merely because a broad regex matched it;\\n- using release version as the identity of every live source object; and\\n- assuming a readable string is globally unique without its authority\\n  and kind.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/IDENTITY.md#IDENTITY%2F11.%20Examples%2FUnlawful\",\"start_line\":384}],\"statements\":[\"Consumer-bound runtime realisation generates event UUIDs.\",\"REQ-F-CAPABILITY-001 when domain law defines concrete requirement kind.\",\"REQ-F-CAPABILITY when separately defined as requirement_family.\",\"REQ-F-CAPABILITY-001-AC-01 when separately defined as acceptance_criterion.\"]},\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:592f428587096675d25235df24f32725\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:0d44548345ed4f30503f0de96135ec17\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"forbidden_variation\":{\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":378,\"path\":\"standards/IDENTITY.md\",\"quote\":\"- runtime event identities generated as UUIDs by a consumer-bound runtime\\n  realisation;\\n- requirement identities such as `REQ-F-CAPABILITY-001` when the domain\\n  defines them as concrete `requirement` identities;\\n- family identities such as `REQ-F-CAPABILITY` when the domain defines\\n  them separately as `requirement_family`; and\\n- acceptance-criterion identities such as `REQ-F-CAPABILITY-001-AC-01`\\n  when the domain defines them as a separate `acceptance_criterion`\\n  identity kind.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/IDENTITY.md#IDENTITY%2F11.%20Examples%2FLawful\",\"start_line\":370},{\"end_line\":388,\"path\":\"standards/IDENTITY.md\",\"quote\":\"- treating `REQ-F-CAPABILITY-*` or `REQ-F-CAPABILITY` as a concrete\\n  requirement merely because a broad regex matched it;\\n- using release version as the identity of every live source object; and\\n- assuming a readable string is globally unique without its authority\\n  and kind.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/IDENTITY.md#IDENTITY%2F11.%20Examples%2FUnlawful\",\"start_line\":384}],\"statements\":[\"Treating REQ-F-CAPABILITY-* or REQ-F-CAPABILITY as a concrete requirement merely because a broad regex matched.\",\"Using release version as every live source object's identity.\",\"Assuming readable-string global uniqueness without authority and kind.\"]},\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:db1bee36a452fd10ba89dd0771cabc47\",\"invalidation\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:invalidation:source-or-interpretation-change\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"latitude","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:fb513bb2968c08523e41030284666a96","key":1759,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"allowed_variation\":{\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":65,\"path\":\"standards/ODD.md\",\"quote\":\"A consumer binds the roles to concrete conforming realisations in its own\\nProduct, requirements, design and immutable dependency identity. A\\nconsumer, a reference realisation or a historical product may prove or\\nfalsify conformance; none of them supplies method authority (P6).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ODD.md#ODD%2F1.%20Position\",\"start_line\":62}],\"statements\":[\"Consumers bind GTL/ABG roles to concrete conforming realisations in their Product, requirements, design and immutable dependency identity.\",\"Consumer, reference realisation or historical product may prove or falsify conformance.\"]},\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:d95615227f8fdfe4b3e7141e3ba237e3\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:b45635a1f0ea19b2701d9a88aa71857a\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:7401bbbf535fd5e1e16b14036ff56999\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"forbidden_variation\":{\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":65,\"path\":\"standards/ODD.md\",\"quote\":\"A consumer binds the roles to concrete conforming realisations in its own\\nProduct, requirements, design and immutable dependency identity. A\\nconsumer, a reference realisation or a historical product may prove or\\nfalsify conformance; none of them supplies method authority (P6).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ODD.md#ODD%2F1.%20Position\",\"start_line\":62}],\"statements\":[\"Requiring a particular repository, package, vendor or implementation merely from the role names.\",\"Treating consumer/reference/historical evidence as method authority.\"]},\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:fb513bb2968c08523e41030284666a96\",\"invalidation\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:invalidation:source-or-interpretation-change\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"latitude","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:ef8c4e09ed20baa54d59e50231f416a6","key":1760,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"allowed_variation\":{\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":438,\"path\":\"standards/ODD.md\",\"quote\":\"- its constitutional surfaces under SPEC_METHOD, where `GOALS.md`,\\n  `INTENT.md`, `PRODUCT.md` and `requirements/` are the default\\n  software-development scaffold and not mandatory names;\\n- one or more realisation roots bound through `how.build_tenants`, where\\n  `build_tenants/` is the default root name for software-development ODD\\n  products and existing projects and other domain types may use their own\\n  locations;\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ODD.md#ODD%2F6.%20Product%20boundary\",\"start_line\":432},{\"end_line\":557,\"path\":\"standards/ODD.md\",\"quote\":\"existing projects and other ODD\\nproduct types may use another layout that keeps the split (P6, P1).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ODD.md#ODD%2F10.%20What%20an%20ODD%20product%20is\",\"start_line\":556}],\"statements\":[\"Existing projects and other domain types use their own constitutional and realisation locations.\",\"GOALS.md, INTENT.md, PRODUCT.md, requirements/, specification/ and build_tenants/ are software-development defaults, not universal mandatory names.\",\"Alternate layout retains one WHAT surface, one HOW relation, ABG runtime ownership and product domain meaning.\"]},\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:796a8085272464e74aa0b22d9354d8cb\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:dfebaec0e3fc6f2d93521655089f3a54\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:68488250933586b7cf75d39d4f345fde\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:e8fba98a082000f2293a25bde2a6c895\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"forbidden_variation\":{\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":438,\"path\":\"standards/ODD.md\",\"quote\":\"- its constitutional surfaces under SPEC_METHOD, where `GOALS.md`,\\n  `INTENT.md`, `PRODUCT.md` and `requirements/` are the default\\n  software-development scaffold and not mandatory names;\\n- one or more realisation roots bound through `how.build_tenants`, where\\n  `build_tenants/` is the default root name for software-development ODD\\n  products and existing projects and other domain types may use their own\\n  locations;\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ODD.md#ODD%2F6.%20Product%20boundary\",\"start_line\":432},{\"end_line\":557,\"path\":\"standards/ODD.md\",\"quote\":\"existing projects and other ODD\\nproduct types may use another layout that keeps the split (P6, P1).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ODD.md#ODD%2F10.%20What%20an%20ODD%20product%20is\",\"start_line\":556}],\"statements\":[\"Substituting directory-name coincidence for the declared authority split.\"]},\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:ef8c4e09ed20baa54d59e50231f416a6\",\"invalidation\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:invalidation:source-or-interpretation-change\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"latitude","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:adf3cf48718ef9b713153c5d595685cd","key":1761,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"allowed_variation\":{\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":646,\"path\":\"standards/ODD.md\",\"quote\":\"Imperative adapter code is lawful only where it transports or persists\\nfacts: file or network IO; CLI or API transport; event persistence;\\nruntime invocation; projection rendering; tool execution already admitted\\nby a declared traversal. Imperative code must not own domain meaning,\\nsemantic target movement, step selection, closure semantics, lineage truth\\nor constructive workflow truth. Framework behaviour implemented\\nimperatively first and only later described in GTL vocabulary is\\nODD-shaped but not yet ODD-built (P6, P0).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ODD.md#ODD%2F11.%20Core%20law%2F11.2A%20Outcome-first%20realisation%20order\",\"start_line\":639}],\"statements\":[\"Imperative adapters transport or persist facts through file/network IO, CLI/API transport, event persistence, runtime invocation, projection rendering or tool execution already admitted by a declared traversal.\"]},\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:dfebaec0e3fc6f2d93521655089f3a54\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:81f6906b71f893b3c94e1dfc03ff9522\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"forbidden_variation\":{\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":646,\"path\":\"standards/ODD.md\",\"quote\":\"Imperative adapter code is lawful only where it transports or persists\\nfacts: file or network IO; CLI or API transport; event persistence;\\nruntime invocation; projection rendering; tool execution already admitted\\nby a declared traversal. Imperative code must not own domain meaning,\\nsemantic target movement, step selection, closure semantics, lineage truth\\nor constructive workflow truth. Framework behaviour implemented\\nimperatively first and only later described in GTL vocabulary is\\nODD-shaped but not yet ODD-built (P6, P0).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ODD.md#ODD%2F11.%20Core%20law%2F11.2A%20Outcome-first%20realisation%20order\",\"start_line\":639}],\"statements\":[\"Imperative ownership of domain meaning, semantic target movement, step selection, closure semantics, lineage truth or constructive workflow truth.\"]},\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:adf3cf48718ef9b713153c5d595685cd\",\"invalidation\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:invalidation:source-or-interpretation-change\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"latitude","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:f2ba16f3218940086ce79bcfc5cd16a0","key":1762,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"allowed_variation\":{\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":689,\"path\":\"standards/ODD.md\",\"quote\":\"The product may publish typed assets and evidence, execute one admitted\\nbounded constructive step, publish downstream read models or domain\\noverlays, and return control to ABG. The product must not own a hidden\\ncontinuation loop; carry multi-step controller memory across publish\\nboundaries; infer later steps locally instead of re-entering through ABG;\\ntreat public `next` and explicit graph-function continuation as rival\\nauthorities inside one controller; or build product-local orchestration\\nthat in effect replaces ABG (P6).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ODD.md#ODD%2F11.%20Core%20law%2F11.5A%20ABG%20owns%20continuation%20and%20re-entry\",\"start_line\":682}],\"statements\":[\"Publish typed assets/evidence, execute one admitted bounded constructive step, publish downstream read models/domain overlays and return control to ABG.\"]},\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:dfebaec0e3fc6f2d93521655089f3a54\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"forbidden_variation\":{\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":689,\"path\":\"standards/ODD.md\",\"quote\":\"The product may publish typed assets and evidence, execute one admitted\\nbounded constructive step, publish downstream read models or domain\\noverlays, and return control to ABG. The product must not own a hidden\\ncontinuation loop; carry multi-step controller memory across publish\\nboundaries; infer later steps locally instead of re-entering through ABG;\\ntreat public `next` and explicit graph-function continuation as rival\\nauthorities inside one controller; or build product-local orchestration\\nthat in effect replaces ABG (P6).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ODD.md#ODD%2F11.%20Core%20law%2F11.5A%20ABG%20owns%20continuation%20and%20re-entry\",\"start_line\":682}],\"statements\":[\"Hidden continuation loops, controller memory across publish boundaries, locally inferred later steps, rival next/continuation authorities or product orchestration replacing ABG.\"]},\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:f2ba16f3218940086ce79bcfc5cd16a0\",\"invalidation\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:invalidation:source-or-interpretation-change\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"latitude","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:0ac502d01ad973f25cd6e025e7d59f5f","key":1763,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"allowed_variation\":{\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":598,\"path\":\"standards/ODD.md\",\"quote\":\"Service or query layers may own transport, sessions, routing,\\nbrowser-safe projection and API surfaces. They own neither runtime truth\\nnor continuation truth. The real constructive carrier is never hidden\\nbehind the word service (P6).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ODD.md#ODD%2F10.%20What%20an%20ODD%20product%20is%2FQuery%20and%20service%20layers\",\"start_line\":595},{\"end_line\":761,\"path\":\"standards/ODD.md\",\"quote\":\"Projection and query lanes are downstream read models over admitted\\ncarrier, runtime, event or source truth. They may summarise, index,\\nfilter or render that truth; they must not reconstruct an alternate\\nauthority surface beside the admitted carrier (P3, P6).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ODD.md#ODD%2F11.%20Core%20law%2F11.5C%20Projection-source%20coherence\",\"start_line\":758}],\"statements\":[\"Service/query ownership of transport, sessions, routing, browser-safe projection and APIs.\",\"Summarising, indexing, filtering or rendering admitted truth.\"]},\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:66f74c8f29b280b5c3f16e2a8b3d89fe\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:34566a52e8fcda8cee3d666e0e57e8ae\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"forbidden_variation\":{\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":598,\"path\":\"standards/ODD.md\",\"quote\":\"Service or query layers may own transport, sessions, routing,\\nbrowser-safe projection and API surfaces. They own neither runtime truth\\nnor continuation truth. The real constructive carrier is never hidden\\nbehind the word service (P6).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ODD.md#ODD%2F10.%20What%20an%20ODD%20product%20is%2FQuery%20and%20service%20layers\",\"start_line\":595},{\"end_line\":761,\"path\":\"standards/ODD.md\",\"quote\":\"Projection and query lanes are downstream read models over admitted\\ncarrier, runtime, event or source truth. They may summarise, index,\\nfilter or render that truth; they must not reconstruct an alternate\\nauthority surface beside the admitted carrier (P3, P6).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ODD.md#ODD%2F11.%20Core%20law%2F11.5C%20Projection-source%20coherence\",\"start_line\":758}],\"statements\":[\"Owning runtime or continuation truth.\",\"Hiding the real constructive carrier behind a service label.\",\"Reconstructing an alternate authority surface beside the admitted carrier.\"]},\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:0ac502d01ad973f25cd6e025e7d59f5f\",\"invalidation\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:invalidation:source-or-interpretation-change\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"latitude","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:af0d9fe4bcb48db3d389eb59ae182301","key":1764,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"allowed_variation\":{\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1068,\"path\":\"standards/ODD.md\",\"quote\":\"A5 F_P freedom, F_D authority. F_P may inspect, discover, reason, draft,\\ntransform and propose within the bounded action. F_P must not close the\\nedge, emit runtime events, mutate ledgers or decide re-entry. F_D, ABG and\\nproduct admission own durable evidence and closure truth (P0, P6). An F_P\\nworker must not be given an F_D-authored semantic extraction recipe when\\nthe edge requires F_P judgment (P0, P6).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ODD.md#ODD%2F11.%20Core%20law%2F11.5D%20Constructive%20evaluation%20and%20yield%20loop\",\"start_line\":1063}],\"statements\":[\"Use framework-independent carrier names while preserving the authority shape.\",\"Share underlying libraries across the four functions without sharing authority.\",\"F_P may inspect, discover, reason, draft, transform and propose inside the bounded action.\",\"Opaque internal realization may use local control flow to compute its bounded internal result.\"]},\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:bcaa8a8d820aec2a089181d683a453df\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:505ca2ca015711bae0650516cdea1113\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"forbidden_variation\":{\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1068,\"path\":\"standards/ODD.md\",\"quote\":\"A5 F_P freedom, F_D authority. F_P may inspect, discover, reason, draft,\\ntransform and propose within the bounded action. F_P must not close the\\nedge, emit runtime events, mutate ledgers or decide re-entry. F_D, ABG and\\nproduct admission own durable evidence and closure truth (P0, P6). An F_P\\nworker must not be given an F_D-authored semantic extraction recipe when\\nthe edge requires F_P judgment (P0, P6).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ODD.md#ODD%2F11.%20Core%20law%2F11.5D%20Constructive%20evaluation%20and%20yield%20loop\",\"start_line\":1063}],\"statements\":[\"F_P closing edges, emitting runtime events, mutating ledgers or deciding re-entry.\",\"Giving an F_P worker an F_D-authored semantic extraction recipe when the edge requires F_P judgment.\",\"Using opaque internals as hidden graph-work traversal authority.\"]},\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:af0d9fe4bcb48db3d389eb59ae182301\",\"invalidation\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:invalidation:source-or-interpretation-change\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"latitude","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:ab41f54eebcb75f461a3914e18b38f0c","key":1765,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"allowed_variation\":{\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1429,\"path\":\"standards/ODD.md\",\"quote\":\"Automation may make this faster, safer or more repeatable; it may not\\ninvent a different process. Automation is lawful when it renders prompts,\\nscaffolds artifacts, selects the next traversal step, runs workers,\\ncollects evidence and assesses closure.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ODD.md#ODD%2F11.%20Core%20law%2F11.7%20Manual%20walkthrough%20must%20still%20be%20lawful\",\"start_line\":1426}],\"statements\":[\"Make the same declared process faster, safer or more repeatable.\",\"Render prompts, scaffold artifacts, select traversal steps, run workers, collect evidence and assess closure within declared authority.\"]},\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:c268d2b1bafeebb5b3c54ed7be08bb2e\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"forbidden_variation\":{\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1429,\"path\":\"standards/ODD.md\",\"quote\":\"Automation may make this faster, safer or more repeatable; it may not\\ninvent a different process. Automation is lawful when it renders prompts,\\nscaffolds artifacts, selects the next traversal step, runs workers,\\ncollects evidence and assesses closure.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ODD.md#ODD%2F11.%20Core%20law%2F11.7%20Manual%20walkthrough%20must%20still%20be%20lawful\",\"start_line\":1426}],\"statements\":[\"Invent a different process or any of the undeclared authority/refinement/self-host collapses specified by the manual-fidelity rule.\"]},\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:ab41f54eebcb75f461a3914e18b38f0c\",\"invalidation\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:invalidation:source-or-interpretation-change\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"latitude","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:95b5c86f599ead19f4ca6ad9d836ed32","key":1766,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"allowed_variation\":{\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":55,\"path\":\"standards/POSTING_GUIDE.md\",\"quote\":\"An existing project may bind another directory, a repository resource, a\\nmessage board, an API collection or a product-scoped query instead. The\\nbound carrier must preserve the distinction between commentary and\\nauthority that this guide draws. Its location and its visibility cannot\\nturn a post into ticket, Product, requirement or design truth (P6, P3).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/POSTING_GUIDE.md#POSTING_GUIDE%2F3.%20Location\",\"start_line\":51}],\"statements\":[\"An existing project may bind another directory, repository resource, message board, API collection or product-scoped query.\"]},\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:39bdea0a1e0944501e86c53001a7d5cb\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"forbidden_variation\":{\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":55,\"path\":\"standards/POSTING_GUIDE.md\",\"quote\":\"An existing project may bind another directory, a repository resource, a\\nmessage board, an API collection or a product-scoped query instead. The\\nbound carrier must preserve the distinction between commentary and\\nauthority that this guide draws. Its location and its visibility cannot\\nturn a post into ticket, Product, requirement or design truth (P6, P3).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/POSTING_GUIDE.md#POSTING_GUIDE%2F3.%20Location\",\"start_line\":51}],\"statements\":[\"Letting carrier location or visibility convert commentary into ticket, Product, requirement or design truth.\"]},\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:95b5c86f599ead19f4ca6ad9d836ed32\",\"invalidation\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:invalidation:source-or-interpretation-change\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"latitude","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:92e50e798ba7377c04a2d9cee186a094","key":1767,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"allowed_variation\":{\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":131,\"path\":\"standards/POSTING_GUIDE.md\",\"quote\":\"An update to\\nan open post keeps the original `Date` as the first publication time and\\nadds or updates `Updated` when useful (P3, P4b).\\n\\nUpdating a `Closed` post is discouraged. Prefer a new post when a later\\nchange would materially alter a closed conclusion, reopen an old\\ndispute or start a new bounded subject (P4b, P3).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/POSTING_GUIDE.md#POSTING_GUIDE%2F7.%20Discussion%20state%20and%20mutability\",\"start_line\":125}],\"statements\":[\"Update the same Draft/Open post within its bounded discussion to correct mistakes, incorporate replies, refine recommendations, reprice confidence or add same-subject evidence.\",\"Keep original Date as first publication time; add/update Updated when useful.\",\"Prefer a new post for materially changing a closed conclusion, reopening a dispute or starting a new subject; Closed updates are discouraged, not absolutely prohibited.\"]},\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:43a55d217680888d5abfc84ed0225020\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:38b9914ee8bbc6790e310e2774932d74\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"forbidden_variation\":{\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":131,\"path\":\"standards/POSTING_GUIDE.md\",\"quote\":\"An update to\\nan open post keeps the original `Date` as the first publication time and\\nadds or updates `Updated` when useful (P3, P4b).\\n\\nUpdating a `Closed` post is discouraged. Prefer a new post when a later\\nchange would materially alter a closed conclusion, reopen an old\\ndispute or start a new bounded subject (P4b, P3).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/POSTING_GUIDE.md#POSTING_GUIDE%2F7.%20Discussion%20state%20and%20mutability\",\"start_line\":125}],\"statements\":[\"Treating discussion closure as constitutional adoption.\",\"Stealth rewriting of closed history.\"]},\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:92e50e798ba7377c04a2d9cee186a094\",\"invalidation\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:invalidation:source-or-interpretation-change\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"latitude","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:43407be1aa698f8ce292fb285ef4ad83","key":1768,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"allowed_variation\":{\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":77,\"path\":\"standards/PRODUCT_DEFINITION.md\",\"quote\":\"The directory containing a definition is its definition root. Relative URI\\nreferences resolve against the definition file's retrieval URI. The\\n`product.source_project` reference identifies the source-project root and\\nmay resolve to the definition root or elsewhere. File proximity creates no\\nauthority (P6).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/PRODUCT_DEFINITION.md#PRODUCT_DEFINITION%2F1.%20Overlay%20and%20layout%20independence\",\"start_line\":73}],\"statements\":[\"Keep the definition identity stable while authoring successive releases.\",\"Locate source_project at the definition root or elsewhere.\",\"Use multiple definitions in one directory only for distinct WHATs.\"]},\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:8048859bf02f15f5c3158d9ca21e6198\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:c1ed13a1e7694716094389e56c921b63\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"forbidden_variation\":{\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":77,\"path\":\"standards/PRODUCT_DEFINITION.md\",\"quote\":\"The directory containing a definition is its definition root. Relative URI\\nreferences resolve against the definition file's retrieval URI. The\\n`product.source_project` reference identifies the source-project root and\\nmay resolve to the definition root or elsewhere. File proximity creates no\\nauthority (P6).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/PRODUCT_DEFINITION.md#PRODUCT_DEFINITION%2F1.%20Overlay%20and%20layout%20independence\",\"start_line\":73}],\"statements\":[\"Adding definition files merely for more tenants of one WHAT.\",\"Repurposing definition identity as release identity.\",\"Inferring authority from file proximity.\"]},\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:43407be1aa698f8ce292fb285ef4ad83\",\"invalidation\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:invalidation:source-or-interpretation-change\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"latitude","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:153a3bc43988ccb652870954a8f44fb0","key":1769,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"allowed_variation\":{\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":207,\"path\":\"standards/PRODUCT_DEFINITION.md\",\"quote\":\"These are sufficiency dimensions of the complete set, not filename classes,\\nrequired folders or a one-document-per-dimension partition. One document\\nmay cover several dimensions and one dimension may be distributed across\\nseveral owning documents (P2).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/PRODUCT_DEFINITION.md#PRODUCT_DEFINITION%2F3.%20Constitutional-set%20sufficiency\",\"start_line\":204}],\"statements\":[\"One document may cover several sufficiency dimensions.\",\"One dimension may be distributed among multiple owning documents.\"]},\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:cd46ea3f9d64e23d695883c0d8fb98b2\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"forbidden_variation\":{\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":207,\"path\":\"standards/PRODUCT_DEFINITION.md\",\"quote\":\"These are sufficiency dimensions of the complete set, not filename classes,\\nrequired folders or a one-document-per-dimension partition. One document\\nmay cover several dimensions and one dimension may be distributed across\\nseveral owning documents (P2).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/PRODUCT_DEFINITION.md#PRODUCT_DEFINITION%2F3.%20Constitutional-set%20sufficiency\",\"start_line\":204}],\"statements\":[\"Treating the five dimensions as mandatory filenames, folders or a one-document-per-dimension partition.\",\"Replacing a complete constitution with entrypoint navigation.\"]},\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:153a3bc43988ccb652870954a8f44fb0\",\"invalidation\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:invalidation:source-or-interpretation-change\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"latitude","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:bbfb178140f876451d78f7344dcf3458","key":1770,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"allowed_variation\":{\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":277,\"path\":\"standards/PRODUCT_DEFINITION.md\",\"quote\":\"The store may live at any machine-local path. Its registry maps logical\\nrelease URIs to installed paths and manifest digests and owns neither\\nProduct selection nor method meaning. A consumer repository therefore needs\\nno project-local standards copy and no prescribed folder structure, and\\nseveral Product Definitions on one machine may select different installed\\ncuts concurrently (P3, P6).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/PRODUCT_DEFINITION.md#PRODUCT_DEFINITION%2F4.%20Shared%20installed%20release%20basis%20and%20toolchain%20manager\",\"start_line\":272}],\"statements\":[\"Place the shared release store at any machine-local path.\",\"Let multiple definitions select different installed cuts concurrently.\",\"Use consumer repositories without project-local standards copies or prescribed folder structures.\"]},\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:f5ea64751cc1eb33ef2ae5a9bbc3b09a\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:395e42597f3b0df9d733f31d1b45bed9\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"forbidden_variation\":{\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":277,\"path\":\"standards/PRODUCT_DEFINITION.md\",\"quote\":\"The store may live at any machine-local path. Its registry maps logical\\nrelease URIs to installed paths and manifest digests and owns neither\\nProduct selection nor method meaning. A consumer repository therefore needs\\nno project-local standards copy and no prescribed folder structure, and\\nseveral Product Definitions on one machine may select different installed\\ncuts concurrently (P3, P6).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/PRODUCT_DEFINITION.md#PRODUCT_DEFINITION%2F4.%20Shared%20installed%20release%20basis%20and%20toolchain%20manager\",\"start_line\":272}],\"statements\":[\"Letting registry location choose Product basis or method meaning.\",\"Using redirection or special entries in manager-owned storage.\"]},\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:bbfb178140f876451d78f7344dcf3458\",\"invalidation\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:invalidation:source-or-interpretation-change\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"latitude","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:fbcb473c1e6f60f222384dd6e39e8683","key":1771,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"allowed_variation\":{\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":719,\"path\":\"standards/PRODUCT_DEFINITION.md\",\"quote\":\"An accepted Project Reference-Frame Basis may be expressed entirely as\\nsource-linked prose. The starter at\\n`templates/PROJECT_REFERENCE_FRAME_BASIS_TEMPLATE.md` projects this binding\\nlaw into one copyable shape. The template is not authority, and no schema,\\naxiomatic representation, prompt framework or runtime frame engine is\\nneeded to use the method. An adopting Product replaces every placeholder\\nwith its own exact identities, owners, scopes, sources, grants, results and\\ninvalidation conditions, then admits that completed declaration under\\nexisting authority (P2, P6).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/PRODUCT_DEFINITION.md#PRODUCT_DEFINITION%2F7.%20Collective%20reference-frame%20basis\",\"start_line\":711}],\"statements\":[\"Express an accepted frame basis entirely as source-linked prose.\",\"Adopt an available profile or define a project configuration through Product authority.\",\"Several agents may activate overlapping frame subsets; one agent may activate different frames over time.\",\"Use the method without a schema, axiomatic representation, prompt framework or runtime frame engine.\"]},\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:24eaed2b3ae25fcb1bde979499653b21\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:6e2b00300849fee60f54d5d16d37822d\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"forbidden_variation\":{\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":719,\"path\":\"standards/PRODUCT_DEFINITION.md\",\"quote\":\"An accepted Project Reference-Frame Basis may be expressed entirely as\\nsource-linked prose. The starter at\\n`templates/PROJECT_REFERENCE_FRAME_BASIS_TEMPLATE.md` projects this binding\\nlaw into one copyable shape. The template is not authority, and no schema,\\naxiomatic representation, prompt framework or runtime frame engine is\\nneeded to use the method. An adopting Product replaces every placeholder\\nwith its own exact identities, owners, scopes, sources, grants, results and\\ninvalidation conditions, then admits that completed declaration under\\nexisting authority (P2, P6).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/PRODUCT_DEFINITION.md#PRODUCT_DEFINITION%2F7.%20Collective%20reference-frame%20basis\",\"start_line\":711}],\"statements\":[\"Treating a starter template as authority.\",\"Including a runtime/domain Frame through nominal matching.\",\"Inferring grants from an actor name or broad frame.\"]},\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:fbcb473c1e6f60f222384dd6e39e8683\",\"invalidation\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:invalidation:source-or-interpretation-change\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"latitude","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:1cb9abf9c184ca87bf440b93f2749874","key":1772,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"allowed_variation\":{\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":768,\"path\":\"standards/PRODUCT_DEFINITION.md\",\"quote\":\"These bindings may resolve to directories,\\nrepository resources, tracker collections, API endpoints or product-scoped\\nqueries. Goals own the bounded work wave, ticket state stays ticket\\nauthority, and comments stay non-authoritative commentary (P6, P3).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/PRODUCT_DEFINITION.md#PRODUCT_DEFINITION%2F8.%20WHAT%2C%20HOW%20and%20work%20carriers\",\"start_line\":765}],\"statements\":[\"Resolve work bindings to directories, repository resources, tracker collections, API endpoints or product-scoped queries.\",\"Keep a human-readable or generated TENANT_REGISTRY.md companion.\",\"Bind optional sprint execution-batch manifests.\"]},\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:71e0e361793d1a2f94d72888e297322b\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"forbidden_variation\":{\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":768,\"path\":\"standards/PRODUCT_DEFINITION.md\",\"quote\":\"These bindings may resolve to directories,\\nrepository resources, tracker collections, API endpoints or product-scoped\\nqueries. Goals own the bounded work wave, ticket state stays ticket\\nauthority, and comments stay non-authoritative commentary (P6, P3).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/PRODUCT_DEFINITION.md#PRODUCT_DEFINITION%2F8.%20WHAT%2C%20HOW%20and%20work%20carriers\",\"start_line\":765}],\"statements\":[\"Making the registry companion a second tenant identity/location authority.\",\"Converting comments into authoritative work truth through carrier substitution.\"]},\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:1cb9abf9c184ca87bf440b93f2749874\",\"invalidation\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:invalidation:source-or-interpretation-change\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"latitude","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:b1edb5413619f5c0f143973e9579e3f7","key":1773,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"allowed_variation\":{\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1006,\"path\":\"standards/PRODUCT_DEFINITION.md\",\"quote\":\"This is a starter topology, not a conformance requirement. A monorepo may\\nplace several `stdo_<label>.json` definitions at one root and bind each to\\na different WHAT. A hierarchical repository may place one or more\\ndefinitions at any nested project root. Recursive discovery (§9) finds both\\nshapes; explicit composition, never directory nesting, relates their\\nproducts (P3, P2).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/PRODUCT_DEFINITION.md#PRODUCT_DEFINITION%2F12.%20Bootstrap\",\"start_line\":1001}],\"statements\":[\"Bind an existing layout without moving, renaming or duplicating authority or realisation surfaces.\",\"Place several named definitions at one monorepo root, each binding a different WHAT.\",\"Place one or more definitions at any nested project root.\",\"Use an explicitly bound and verified project-local exact release copy.\"]},\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:3add3b1f83bc954a23767c8b23298c71\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:1948ec4783ac3e1560e6eed4e2e68e9d\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:ec08ef0caf1ef5504b20e94591bbea9d\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"forbidden_variation\":{\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1006,\"path\":\"standards/PRODUCT_DEFINITION.md\",\"quote\":\"This is a starter topology, not a conformance requirement. A monorepo may\\nplace several `stdo_<label>.json` definitions at one root and bind each to\\na different WHAT. A hierarchical repository may place one or more\\ndefinitions at any nested project root. Recursive discovery (§9) finds both\\nshapes; explicit composition, never directory nesting, relates their\\nproducts (P3, P2).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/PRODUCT_DEFINITION.md#PRODUCT_DEFINITION%2F12.%20Bootstrap\",\"start_line\":1001}],\"statements\":[\"Treat starter paths/topology as universal conformance law.\",\"Infer product composition from directory nesting.\",\"Select a local release copy by file proximity.\"]},\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:b1edb5413619f5c0f143973e9579e3f7\",\"invalidation\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:invalidation:source-or-interpretation-change\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"latitude","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:2689345674e6401396f71c5d6553b361","key":1774,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"allowed_variation\":{\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1016,\"path\":\"standards/PRODUCT_DEFINITION.md\",\"quote\":\"A project need not start with a complete `requirements/` tree on day zero.\\nRequirements may be sourced from any legitimate constitutional input\\nregardless of its path, including `GOALS.md`, `INTENT.md`, `PRODUCT.md`,\\nexisting requirement documents, imported standards or policy material,\\nprior project versions, and migration or repricing source material. Most\\nprojects begin by deriving `INTENT.md` from `GOALS.md`, then `PRODUCT.md`\\nfrom `INTENT.md`, then the first requirement surface from the product\\ndefinition; that is the usual starting point, not the only lawful source\\n(P2).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/PRODUCT_DEFINITION.md#PRODUCT_DEFINITION%2F12.%20Bootstrap\",\"start_line\":1008}],\"statements\":[\"Begin without a complete requirements tree.\",\"Source requirements from any legitimate constitutional input regardless of path, including Goals, Intent, Product, requirements, imported standards/policies, prior versions and migration/repricing sources.\",\"Use Goals→Intent→Product→requirements as the usual starting derivation without treating it as the only lawful source.\"]},\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:3add3b1f83bc954a23767c8b23298c71\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:1948ec4783ac3e1560e6eed4e2e68e9d\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"forbidden_variation\":{\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1016,\"path\":\"standards/PRODUCT_DEFINITION.md\",\"quote\":\"A project need not start with a complete `requirements/` tree on day zero.\\nRequirements may be sourced from any legitimate constitutional input\\nregardless of its path, including `GOALS.md`, `INTENT.md`, `PRODUCT.md`,\\nexisting requirement documents, imported standards or policy material,\\nprior project versions, and migration or repricing source material. Most\\nprojects begin by deriving `INTENT.md` from `GOALS.md`, then `PRODUCT.md`\\nfrom `INTENT.md`, then the first requirement surface from the product\\ndefinition; that is the usual starting point, not the only lawful source\\n(P2).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/PRODUCT_DEFINITION.md#PRODUCT_DEFINITION%2F12.%20Bootstrap\",\"start_line\":1008}],\"statements\":[\"Treat the usual derivation as the only lawful requirement source.\"]},\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:2689345674e6401396f71c5d6553b361\",\"invalidation\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:invalidation:source-or-interpretation-change\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"latitude","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:061280c8eb59900be15282741a29bb12","key":1775,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"allowed_variation\":{\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":77,\"path\":\"standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md\",\"quote\":\"Substrate. A reference frame may be represented in prose, structured data,\\na prompt, a design asset, a typed carrier, a runtime context or any other\\nform its consumer selects. No class, aggregate, actor, controller, service,\\nregistry, graph or frame engine is required (P2; RF-016).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md#REFERENCE_FRAME%2F1.%20The%20frame%20as%20the%20engagement%20unit\",\"start_line\":74}],\"statements\":[\"Represent a frame in prose, structured data, a prompt, design asset, typed carrier, runtime context or another consumer-selected form.\"]},\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:395652cb307f9e3aec1351f1377975e4\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"forbidden_variation\":{\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":77,\"path\":\"standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md\",\"quote\":\"Substrate. A reference frame may be represented in prose, structured data,\\na prompt, a design asset, a typed carrier, a runtime context or any other\\nform its consumer selects. No class, aggregate, actor, controller, service,\\nregistry, graph or frame engine is required (P2; RF-016).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md#REFERENCE_FRAME%2F1.%20The%20frame%20as%20the%20engagement%20unit\",\"start_line\":74}],\"statements\":[\"Require a class, aggregate, actor, controller, service, registry, graph or frame engine merely because a reference frame is used.\"]},\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:061280c8eb59900be15282741a29bb12\",\"invalidation\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:invalidation:source-or-interpretation-change\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"latitude","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:bca8585335335db1ad3e5b5508a69dde","key":1776,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"allowed_variation\":{\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":360,\"path\":\"standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md\",\"quote\":\"Frames may relate through disjointness, overlap, refinement, restriction,\\ntranslation, temporal succession, composition or governance (§7). Parent\\nand child relations apply only where explicitly declared. Functional\\ndecomposition, communication, authority precedence, frame configuration,\\nsubject topology and evaluation dependency are distinct relation\\nstructures; a consumer may align them where the governed subject warrants\\nit and may not silently treat them as one hierarchy\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md#REFERENCE_FRAME%2F3.%20Laws%2FRF-009%20No%20assumed%20hierarchy\",\"start_line\":354}],\"statements\":[\"Declare disjointness, overlap, refinement, restriction, translation, temporal succession, composition or governance.\",\"Align distinct relation structures where the governed subject warrants it.\",\"Declare parent/child relations explicitly.\"]},\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:395652cb307f9e3aec1351f1377975e4\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:6f930ad8904d0b79e414891042c6c678\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"forbidden_variation\":{\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":360,\"path\":\"standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md\",\"quote\":\"Frames may relate through disjointness, overlap, refinement, restriction,\\ntranslation, temporal succession, composition or governance (§7). Parent\\nand child relations apply only where explicitly declared. Functional\\ndecomposition, communication, authority precedence, frame configuration,\\nsubject topology and evaluation dependency are distinct relation\\nstructures; a consumer may align them where the governed subject warrants\\nit and may not silently treat them as one hierarchy\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md#REFERENCE_FRAME%2F3.%20Laws%2FRF-009%20No%20assumed%20hierarchy\",\"start_line\":354}],\"statements\":[\"Silently collapse distinct structures into one hierarchy.\",\"Infer authority, decomposition or evaluation dependency from communication alone.\"]},\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:bca8585335335db1ad3e5b5508a69dde\",\"invalidation\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:invalidation:source-or-interpretation-change\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"latitude","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:14662180e149f6310ab908b213970fd5","key":1777,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"allowed_variation\":{\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":468,\"path\":\"standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md\",\"quote\":\"Human authority may declare an initial project frame set from accumulated\\ndevelopment practice, known failure modes, domain expertise, the governed\\noutcome's risk and knowledge of the available agents and other actors. The\\ndeclaration need not reconstruct the set from the workspace bottom up (P6,\\nP2). It records:\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md#REFERENCE_FRAME%2F4.%20Frame-set%20declaration\",\"start_line\":464}],\"statements\":[\"Human authority may declare an initial set from accumulated practice, known failure modes, domain expertise, outcome risk and knowledge of available actors.\",\"Declare without reconstructing the workspace bottom up.\"]},\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:6f930ad8904d0b79e414891042c6c678\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"forbidden_variation\":{\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":468,\"path\":\"standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md\",\"quote\":\"Human authority may declare an initial project frame set from accumulated\\ndevelopment practice, known failure modes, domain expertise, the governed\\noutcome's risk and knowledge of the available agents and other actors. The\\ndeclaration need not reconstruct the set from the workspace bottom up (P6,\\nP2). It records:\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md#REFERENCE_FRAME%2F4.%20Frame-set%20declaration\",\"start_line\":464}],\"statements\":[\"Treat human selection as proof of completeness or authority over inspected subject relations.\"]},\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:14662180e149f6310ab908b213970fd5\",\"invalidation\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:invalidation:source-or-interpretation-change\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"latitude","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:be6781431fc5cc08ad0492d9ccf05762","key":1778,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"allowed_variation\":{\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":894,\"path\":\"standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md\",\"quote\":\"A revision may (P4b): clarify activation or\\nevidence acquisition; change the capability envelope; add or remove a\\nmaterial relation; split an overloaded frame; merge duplicative frames\\nwhere capability and authority stay sound; add intentional overlap; add or\\nrevise a conjunction or translation; retire a frame whose evaluation family\\nis no longer material; or revise the project evaluation inventory. Every\\nmaterial revision changes frame identity or revision coordinates and states\\nwhich prior activations, results and coverage claims require reevaluation\\n(P3, P4b).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md#REFERENCE_FRAME%2F10.%20Discovery%20and%20revision%2FRevision%20actions\",\"start_line\":886}],\"statements\":[\"Clarify activation or evidence acquisition; change capability envelope; add/remove material relation; split overloaded frame; merge duplicative frames where capability and authority remain sound; add intentional overlap; add/revise conjunction or translation; retire a frame whose family is no longer material; revise evaluation inventory.\"]},\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:c8d1bd7d867c78286170d056a942c518\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"forbidden_variation\":{\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":894,\"path\":\"standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md\",\"quote\":\"A revision may (P4b): clarify activation or\\nevidence acquisition; change the capability envelope; add or remove a\\nmaterial relation; split an overloaded frame; merge duplicative frames\\nwhere capability and authority stay sound; add intentional overlap; add or\\nrevise a conjunction or translation; retire a frame whose evaluation family\\nis no longer material; or revise the project evaluation inventory. Every\\nmaterial revision changes frame identity or revision coordinates and states\\nwhich prior activations, results and coverage claims require reevaluation\\n(P3, P4b).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md#REFERENCE_FRAME%2F10.%20Discovery%20and%20revision%2FRevision%20actions\",\"start_line\":886}],\"statements\":[\"Using revision discretion to leave prior-coordinate results silently closed or selectively exempt them from required reopening.\"]},\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:be6781431fc5cc08ad0492d9ccf05762\",\"invalidation\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:invalidation:source-or-interpretation-change\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"latitude","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:6f9eb4f16ef90354be432ccfc0a60be5","key":1779,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"allowed_variation\":{\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":958,\"path\":\"standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md\",\"quote\":\"The actor may own its internal reasoning and search where the governing\\nmethod permits. It returns through the declared result relation. Hidden\\ninternal reasoning is no substitute for required evidence, provenance or\\nauthority (P6). Frame size is optimised for reliable evaluation, not for\\nmaximum context loading: a more capable actor may activate a broader frame\\nand a less capable one may use a lawful refinement sequence, and both\\npreserve the same material invariants and authority relations (P0, P2;\\nRF-014).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md#REFERENCE_FRAME%2F11.%20The%20activation%20packet\",\"start_line\":951}],\"statements\":[\"Actor ownership of internal reasoning/search where governing method permits.\",\"Broader frame for a more capable actor or lawful refinement sequence for a less capable actor, preserving the same material invariants and authority relations.\"]},\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:1d204a797802b5261b6acecea9ea1275\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"forbidden_variation\":{\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":958,\"path\":\"standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md\",\"quote\":\"The actor may own its internal reasoning and search where the governing\\nmethod permits. It returns through the declared result relation. Hidden\\ninternal reasoning is no substitute for required evidence, provenance or\\nauthority (P6). Frame size is optimised for reliable evaluation, not for\\nmaximum context loading: a more capable actor may activate a broader frame\\nand a less capable one may use a lawful refinement sequence, and both\\npreserve the same material invariants and authority relations (P0, P2;\\nRF-014).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md#REFERENCE_FRAME%2F11.%20The%20activation%20packet\",\"start_line\":951}],\"statements\":[\"Substituting hidden reasoning for required evidence, provenance or authority.\",\"Treating maximum context loading as the optimisation objective.\"]},\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:6f9eb4f16ef90354be432ccfc0a60be5\",\"invalidation\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:invalidation:source-or-interpretation-change\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"latitude","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:2c19842dd5a3860262af27ec33a105f8","key":1780,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"allowed_variation\":{\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":965,\"path\":\"standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md\",\"quote\":\"It may be written in Markdown, structured data, a\\nprompt or another consumer-selected carrier without changing the relation\\n(P0, RF-016).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md#REFERENCE_FRAME%2F11.%20The%20activation%20packet%2FMinimal%20activation%20binding\",\"start_line\":963}],\"statements\":[\"Markdown, structured data, prompt or another consumer-selected carrier preserving the activation relation.\"]},\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:2d2745cd8eece9f0ad7fb3c267b65b08\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"forbidden_variation\":{\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":965,\"path\":\"standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md\",\"quote\":\"It may be written in Markdown, structured data, a\\nprompt or another consumer-selected carrier without changing the relation\\n(P0, RF-016).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md#REFERENCE_FRAME%2F11.%20The%20activation%20packet%2FMinimal%20activation%20binding\",\"start_line\":963}],\"statements\":[\"Replacing declared identity/basis with paths, line numbers, counts, summaries or matching labels.\"]},\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:2c19842dd5a3860262af27ec33a105f8\",\"invalidation\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:invalidation:source-or-interpretation-change\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"latitude","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:bf24d04744758d0382b614a9fac2333a","key":1781,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"allowed_variation\":{\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":290,\"path\":\"standards/RELEASE.md\",\"quote\":\"- bounded fixes are allowed after intake triage;\\n- qualification and operator review may continue;\\n- release notes may remain draft until RC publication;\\n- the RC branch may move; and\\n- mutable source is explicitly non-operative for released consumers.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/RELEASE.md#RELEASE%2F3.%20Phases%2FMutable%20candidate%20construction\",\"start_line\":286}],\"statements\":[\"Bounded fixes after intake triage.\",\"Continued qualification/operator review.\",\"Draft release notes until RC publication.\",\"Movement of RC branch.\"]},\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:47f5a07e664b149bf807f7c0c22cd554\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:99876a10de367b85603c3ed68656e593\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"forbidden_variation\":{\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":290,\"path\":\"standards/RELEASE.md\",\"quote\":\"- bounded fixes are allowed after intake triage;\\n- qualification and operator review may continue;\\n- release notes may remain draft until RC publication;\\n- the RC branch may move; and\\n- mutable source is explicitly non-operative for released consumers.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/RELEASE.md#RELEASE%2F3.%20Phases%2FMutable%20candidate%20construction\",\"start_line\":286}],\"statements\":[\"Treating mutable candidate source as operative for released consumers.\",\"Silently absorbing material scope changes.\"]},\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:bf24d04744758d0382b614a9fac2333a\",\"invalidation\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:invalidation:source-or-interpretation-change\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"latitude","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:6a8919017b2ccaab60fd41d901201f25","key":1782,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"allowed_variation\":{\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":453,\"path\":\"standards/RELEASE.md\",\"quote\":\"The unqualified profile remains lawful only under the single-project and\\nhistorical-conservation conditions of §2. Projects may choose another\\nspelling only in a release source whose ref policy proves collision\\nfreedom and preserves the same project namespace, mutable carrier,\\nimmutable cut and mutable selector distinctions (P3).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/RELEASE.md#RELEASE%2F5.%20Naming\",\"start_line\":449}],\"statements\":[\"Another spelling only where release-source ref policy proves collision freedom and preserves namespace, mutable carrier, immutable cut and mutable selector distinctions.\",\"Unqualified profile only under declared single-project or historical-conservation conditions.\"]},\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:99876a10de367b85603c3ed68656e593\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"forbidden_variation\":{\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":453,\"path\":\"standards/RELEASE.md\",\"quote\":\"The unqualified profile remains lawful only under the single-project and\\nhistorical-conservation conditions of §2. Projects may choose another\\nspelling only in a release source whose ref policy proves collision\\nfreedom and preserves the same project namespace, mutable carrier,\\nimmutable cut and mutable selector distinctions (P3).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/RELEASE.md#RELEASE%2F5.%20Naming\",\"start_line\":449}],\"statements\":[\"Using alternative spelling to erase project namespace or mutability/immutability distinctions.\"]},\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:6a8919017b2ccaab60fd41d901201f25\",\"invalidation\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:invalidation:source-or-interpretation-change\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"latitude","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:3252fd9c83e4a4788a6bf098f110c7e3","key":1783,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"allowed_variation\":{\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":82,\"path\":\"standards/SPEC_METHOD.md\",\"quote\":\"In the default scaffold `requirements/` is a folder under `specification/`.\\nRequirements may instead be stored at any location the product definition\\nbinds, as individual files or grouped into requirement families. The default\\nshape exists to avoid collapsing the constitutional surface into one\\nmonolithic requirements document, not to make folder placement\\nconstitutional. This is one expression of the declarative bias: declaring\\nrequirement structure and family boundaries is preferred over maintaining\\none imperative catch-all document (P2).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/SPEC_METHOD.md#SPEC_METHOD%2F1.%20Position%20and%20identity%2FProcess%20constitution\",\"start_line\":75}],\"statements\":[\"Requirements at any location bound by Product Definition, as individual files or grouped requirement families.\",\"Existing file layouts without moving or duplicating files merely to match conventional names.\"]},\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:7b52a0bef35a63b536af6e7f80726a0a\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"forbidden_variation\":{\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":82,\"path\":\"standards/SPEC_METHOD.md\",\"quote\":\"In the default scaffold `requirements/` is a folder under `specification/`.\\nRequirements may instead be stored at any location the product definition\\nbinds, as individual files or grouped into requirement families. The default\\nshape exists to avoid collapsing the constitutional surface into one\\nmonolithic requirements document, not to make folder placement\\nconstitutional. This is one expression of the declarative bias: declaring\\nrequirement structure and family boundaries is preferred over maintaining\\none imperative catch-all document (P2).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/SPEC_METHOD.md#SPEC_METHOD%2F1.%20Position%20and%20identity%2FProcess%20constitution\",\"start_line\":75}],\"statements\":[\"Treating conventional folder placement as constitutional authority.\",\"Promoting a definition overlay or derived surface to co-equal WHAT authority.\"]},\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:3252fd9c83e4a4788a6bf098f110c7e3\",\"invalidation\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:invalidation:source-or-interpretation-change\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"latitude","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:bb86620c09d7a7cfbb776582c90c81e4","key":1784,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"allowed_variation\":{\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":345,\"path\":\"standards/SPEC_METHOD.md\",\"quote\":\"Different designs may satisfy the same\\nrequirements and different codebases the same design.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/SPEC_METHOD.md#SPEC_METHOD%2F2.%20The%20chain%2FReconstruction%20litmus\",\"start_line\":344},{\"end_line\":371,\"path\":\"standards/SPEC_METHOD.md\",\"quote\":\"this litmus applies them to the method's own chain, where the span of a\\nlocal selected function excludes recreating the whole product. The design\\nprofile owns design-view coverage, its material-change gate and\\nunchanged-boundary reuse; this litmus neither waives that gate nor requires\\nrecreating unchanged accepted views ([DESIGN_MODULE](DESIGN_MODULE.md)).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/SPEC_METHOD.md#SPEC_METHOD%2F2.%20The%20chain%2FReconstruction%20litmus\",\"start_line\":367}],\"statements\":[\"Different designs may satisfy the same requirements and different codebases the same design.\",\"Reuse an accepted relation on its exact basis after applicability and invalidation checks.\",\"A selected local function need not reconstruct the whole product or unchanged accepted design views.\"]},\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:f8a1b1b5f801b47764b6f0c9f0a8473d\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"forbidden_variation\":{\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":345,\"path\":\"standards/SPEC_METHOD.md\",\"quote\":\"Different designs may satisfy the same\\nrequirements and different codebases the same design.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/SPEC_METHOD.md#SPEC_METHOD%2F2.%20The%20chain%2FReconstruction%20litmus\",\"start_line\":344},{\"end_line\":371,\"path\":\"standards/SPEC_METHOD.md\",\"quote\":\"this litmus applies them to the method's own chain, where the span of a\\nlocal selected function excludes recreating the whole product. The design\\nprofile owns design-view coverage, its material-change gate and\\nunchanged-boundary reuse; this litmus neither waives that gate nor requires\\nrecreating unchanged accepted views ([DESIGN_MODULE](DESIGN_MODULE.md)).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/SPEC_METHOD.md#SPEC_METHOD%2F2.%20The%20chain%2FReconstruction%20litmus\",\"start_line\":367}],\"statements\":[\"Treating sufficiency as determinism.\",\"Hiding major ambiguity to cross a boundary.\",\"Waiving the applicable design-profile material-change gate.\"]},\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:bb86620c09d7a7cfbb776582c90c81e4\",\"invalidation\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:invalidation:source-or-interpretation-change\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"latitude","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:33ea0af40239189e31cd4dfb33227f30","key":1785,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"allowed_variation\":{\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":450,\"path\":\"standards/SPEC_METHOD.md\",\"quote\":\"If a technology stack,\\ncarrier or runtime is not already constrained by an upstream constitutional\\nsurface, choosing it is part of design, not a separate upstream authority\\n(P2, P1). A tenant's choice of stack, human process or\\ncombination is its execution binding, declared in that design under §11.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/SPEC_METHOD.md#SPEC_METHOD%2F2.%20The%20chain%2FDesign%20rule\",\"start_line\":446}],\"statements\":[\"Design chooses stack, carrier, runtime or human/mixed process where upstream constitutional law leaves it open.\",\"Bootstrap/control topology may use entry documents, embedded blocks, standalone compiled artifacts or another lawful arrangement.\"]},\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:d9ba6983a42a941491c1518a443a52cf\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"forbidden_variation\":{\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":450,\"path\":\"standards/SPEC_METHOD.md\",\"quote\":\"If a technology stack,\\ncarrier or runtime is not already constrained by an upstream constitutional\\nsurface, choosing it is part of design, not a separate upstream authority\\n(P2, P1). A tenant's choice of stack, human process or\\ncombination is its execution binding, declared in that design under §11.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/SPEC_METHOD.md#SPEC_METHOD%2F2.%20The%20chain%2FDesign%20rule\",\"start_line\":446}],\"statements\":[\"Treating mechanism choice as a separate upstream authority.\",\"Hardcoding mechanism detail in requirements without constitutional necessity.\"]},\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:33ea0af40239189e31cd4dfb33227f30\",\"invalidation\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:invalidation:source-or-interpretation-change\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"latitude","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:b8e9b573c0411808e8c9624c7d84341d","key":1786,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"allowed_variation\":{\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":479,\"path\":\"standards/SPEC_METHOD.md\",\"quote\":\"Non-goals of that profile (P1, P4a): it does not require one specific programming language,\\nelimination of all imperative code, monadic or category-theory vocabulary,\\nor replacing every exception with a custom algebraic type. It does require\\nthat the implementation shape remain readable, modular and honest about\\nwhere meaning lives and where effects happen. Where a boundary composes\\nhigher-order functions or effectful computation, it does require an\\nexplicit composition and effect algebra with its applicable identity,\\nclosure, cardinality, effect and authority-conservation laws (FOUNDATIONS\\n§4 Composition). The vocabulary is optional; the law is not.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/SPEC_METHOD.md#SPEC_METHOD%2F2.%20The%20chain%2FRealisation%20shape\",\"start_line\":471}],\"statements\":[\"No particular language is required.\",\"Imperative code may remain.\",\"Monadic/category-theory vocabulary is optional.\",\"Not every exception needs a custom algebraic type.\"]},\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:55a257d3aa9a5758b48bd07e923451f9\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"forbidden_variation\":{\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":479,\"path\":\"standards/SPEC_METHOD.md\",\"quote\":\"Non-goals of that profile (P1, P4a): it does not require one specific programming language,\\nelimination of all imperative code, monadic or category-theory vocabulary,\\nor replacing every exception with a custom algebraic type. It does require\\nthat the implementation shape remain readable, modular and honest about\\nwhere meaning lives and where effects happen. Where a boundary composes\\nhigher-order functions or effectful computation, it does require an\\nexplicit composition and effect algebra with its applicable identity,\\nclosure, cardinality, effect and authority-conservation laws (FOUNDATIONS\\n§4 Composition). The vocabulary is optional; the law is not.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/SPEC_METHOD.md#SPEC_METHOD%2F2.%20The%20chain%2FRealisation%20shape\",\"start_line\":471}],\"statements\":[\"Using optional vocabulary as grounds to omit required composition/effect laws.\",\"Obscuring meaning or effects at a governed boundary.\"]},\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:b8e9b573c0411808e8c9624c7d84341d\",\"invalidation\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:invalidation:source-or-interpretation-change\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"latitude","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:ac32d74748f2303f114055474b11e36d","key":1787,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"allowed_variation\":{\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1234,\"path\":\"standards/SPEC_METHOD.md\",\"quote\":\"The default governance model: ambiguity\\nmay be carried or decided by lawful probabilistic processing when project\\npolicy allows it; it may be escalated to explicit human adjudication when\\nproject policy requires it; the threshold between those actions is\\ndetermined by declared risk appetite, not by silent convenience. Projects\\nmay therefore choose different ambiguity-handling policies: a lower risk\\nappetite escalates more major ambiguity to explicit human judgment; a\\nhigher one permits more bounded probabilistic decision-making. In either\\ncase the ambiguity and the decision are recorded.\\n\\nThe hard stops of [ACTIVATION §4](ACTIVATION.md#4-totality-and-refinement)\\nhold regardless of risk appetite. The method is therefore not \\\"eliminate\\nall ambiguity before work\\\"; it is \\\"make ambiguity visible, govern it\\nexplicitly, and reduce it progressively until downstream realisation is\\nsufficiently constrained\\\".\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/SPEC_METHOD.md#SPEC_METHOD%2F5.%20Ambiguity%20governance%20and%20lifecycle\",\"start_line\":1220}],\"statements\":[\"Projects choose different declared risk appetites and ambiguity policies.\",\"Policy may permit bounded probabilistic carrying/decision or require escalation to admitted human adjudication.\",\"Progressive reduction, rather than elimination of all ambiguity before work, is permitted.\"]},\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:286649052d4f3d74e1c0094c628bac34\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:21feeb8c6dd7e2109f1517741510bd3b\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:7a473adb85314975c9d0699a47c00191\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"forbidden_variation\":{\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1234,\"path\":\"standards/SPEC_METHOD.md\",\"quote\":\"The default governance model: ambiguity\\nmay be carried or decided by lawful probabilistic processing when project\\npolicy allows it; it may be escalated to explicit human adjudication when\\nproject policy requires it; the threshold between those actions is\\ndetermined by declared risk appetite, not by silent convenience. Projects\\nmay therefore choose different ambiguity-handling policies: a lower risk\\nappetite escalates more major ambiguity to explicit human judgment; a\\nhigher one permits more bounded probabilistic decision-making. In either\\ncase the ambiguity and the decision are recorded.\\n\\nThe hard stops of [ACTIVATION §4](ACTIVATION.md#4-totality-and-refinement)\\nhold regardless of risk appetite. The method is therefore not \\\"eliminate\\nall ambiguity before work\\\"; it is \\\"make ambiguity visible, govern it\\nexplicitly, and reduce it progressively until downstream realisation is\\nsufficiently constrained\\\".\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/SPEC_METHOD.md#SPEC_METHOD%2F5.%20Ambiguity%20governance%20and%20lifecycle\",\"start_line\":1220}],\"statements\":[\"Silent convenience as the threshold.\",\"Unrecorded ambiguity or decision.\",\"Waiving ACTIVATION hard stops through risk appetite.\",\"Treating carried, escalated or blocked ambiguity as resolved.\"]},\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:ac32d74748f2303f114055474b11e36d\",\"invalidation\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:invalidation:source-or-interpretation-change\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"latitude","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:68078262b8e15be81036b1aabe3f93ae","key":1788,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"allowed_variation\":{\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1753,\"path\":\"standards/SPEC_METHOD.md\",\"quote\":\"ADRs are stored at the design surface that owns the decision; an `adrs/`\\nsubdirectory is the default scaffold, not a mandatory location (P3). Tenant-local build-tenant ADRs go to the\\napplicable tenant design surface bound by the product definition, by\\ndefault `build_tenants/<tenant-path>/design/adrs/`; shared or cross-tenant\\nADRs to the applicable common surface, by default\\n`build_tenants/common/design/adrs/`; non-tenanted or project-local ADRs to\\n`<governing-design-surface>/adrs/`. In the default scaffold `<tenant-path>`\\nis one or more path segments beneath `build_tenants/`; both\\ncapability-oriented `<product-family>/<realization-variant>` paths and\\nsingle-label `<realization-variant>` paths are lawful, the former is the\\nrecommended default, existing or alternative layouts remain conformant and\\nneed no migration, and in every layout the product's tenant registry entry\\nrecords the tenant identity and locations used (PRODUCT_DEFINITION §1).\\nThe governing design surface is the closest design surface whose authority\\nowns the decision. ADRs are not placed in comments, generated views,\\nruntime archives or requirement folders. The filename convention is\\n`ADR-<local-id>-short-slug.md`, the local identifier unique within the\\nowning `adrs/` directory; numeric identifiers such as `ADR-001-...` are the\\ndefault, and namespace-prefixed identifiers such as `ADR-GM-005-...` are\\nallowed when the owning design surface already uses them. A `REGISTRY.md`\\nindex alongside the ADR files is recommended for tooling and review and is\\nnot required: the constitutional source remains each ADR file, and a\\nregistry is a read model that may drift unless tooling maintains it.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/SPEC_METHOD.md#SPEC_METHOD%2F10.%20Design%20records\",\"start_line\":1731}],\"statements\":[\"adrs/ is a default scaffold, not mandatory.\",\"Default tenant-local location is build_tenants/<tenant-path>/design/adrs/; shared location build_tenants/common/design/adrs/; project/non-tenanted location <governing-design-surface>/adrs/.\",\"Tenant paths may use multiple segments <product-family>/<realization-variant> (recommended default) or a single <realization-variant>; existing/alternative layouts remain conformant without migration.\",\"Numeric IDs are default; namespace-prefixed IDs are allowed where already used by the owning design surface.\",\"REGISTRY.md alongside ADRs is recommended but optional.\"]},\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:1b1081fd5b172df398ec35893fd08af7\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"forbidden_variation\":{\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1753,\"path\":\"standards/SPEC_METHOD.md\",\"quote\":\"ADRs are stored at the design surface that owns the decision; an `adrs/`\\nsubdirectory is the default scaffold, not a mandatory location (P3). Tenant-local build-tenant ADRs go to the\\napplicable tenant design surface bound by the product definition, by\\ndefault `build_tenants/<tenant-path>/design/adrs/`; shared or cross-tenant\\nADRs to the applicable common surface, by default\\n`build_tenants/common/design/adrs/`; non-tenanted or project-local ADRs to\\n`<governing-design-surface>/adrs/`. In the default scaffold `<tenant-path>`\\nis one or more path segments beneath `build_tenants/`; both\\ncapability-oriented `<product-family>/<realization-variant>` paths and\\nsingle-label `<realization-variant>` paths are lawful, the former is the\\nrecommended default, existing or alternative layouts remain conformant and\\nneed no migration, and in every layout the product's tenant registry entry\\nrecords the tenant identity and locations used (PRODUCT_DEFINITION §1).\\nThe governing design surface is the closest design surface whose authority\\nowns the decision. ADRs are not placed in comments, generated views,\\nruntime archives or requirement folders. The filename convention is\\n`ADR-<local-id>-short-slug.md`, the local identifier unique within the\\nowning `adrs/` directory; numeric identifiers such as `ADR-001-...` are the\\ndefault, and namespace-prefixed identifiers such as `ADR-GM-005-...` are\\nallowed when the owning design surface already uses them. A `REGISTRY.md`\\nindex alongside the ADR files is recommended for tooling and review and is\\nnot required: the constitutional source remains each ADR file, and a\\nregistry is a read model that may drift unless tooling maintains it.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/SPEC_METHOD.md#SPEC_METHOD%2F10.%20Design%20records\",\"start_line\":1731}],\"statements\":[\"Moving authority from ADR files to a registry.\",\"Placing ADRs in comments, generated views, runtime archives or requirement folders.\",\"Treating a default or recommendation as a mandatory migration.\"]},\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:68078262b8e15be81036b1aabe3f93ae\",\"invalidation\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:invalidation:source-or-interpretation-change\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"latitude","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:66e6caf2402df01dfdb9b83c7f8b0a02","key":1789,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"allowed_variation\":{\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1791,\"path\":\"standards/SPEC_METHOD.md\",\"quote\":\"- A generic procedure is a method procedure whose scope is independent of\\n  the selected execution environment. It and its projections preserve the\\n  bindings Rule 2 permits: code, an event stream or reconstruction from a\\n  complete history is required only where the governing obligations or\\n  the selected execution binding require it, and an adequate human\\n  process using current records and direct observation is a permitted\\n  execution binding of a generic procedure that requires none of them\\n  (P1, P6).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/SPEC_METHOD.md#SPEC_METHOD%2F11.%20Build-tenant%20binding\",\"start_line\":1784},{\"end_line\":1864,\"path\":\"standards/SPEC_METHOD.md\",\"quote\":\"two\\n   conforming tenants need not behave identically outside the contract.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/SPEC_METHOD.md#SPEC_METHOD%2F11.%20Build-tenant%20binding\",\"start_line\":1863}],\"statements\":[\"A conforming tenant may use software, human process or both.\",\"A generic procedure requiring neither code, event stream nor complete-history reconstruction may use adequate human process with current records and direct observation.\",\"Two conforming tenants may differ outside their contract.\",\"Calculus reuse is permitted when each binding satisfies and demonstrates its laws.\",\"Project law or tenant design selects multi-tenant development/merge mechanics.\"]},\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:c273a437cbb3bf7285b6040216d5722e\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:152d2a8a64bd069bdea1135af24a3c80\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:088223e4b5ad7c379a6722a6b1aca800\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"forbidden_variation\":{\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1791,\"path\":\"standards/SPEC_METHOD.md\",\"quote\":\"- A generic procedure is a method procedure whose scope is independent of\\n  the selected execution environment. It and its projections preserve the\\n  bindings Rule 2 permits: code, an event stream or reconstruction from a\\n  complete history is required only where the governing obligations or\\n  the selected execution binding require it, and an adequate human\\n  process using current records and direct observation is a permitted\\n  execution binding of a generic procedure that requires none of them\\n  (P1, P6).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/SPEC_METHOD.md#SPEC_METHOD%2F11.%20Build-tenant%20binding\",\"start_line\":1784},{\"end_line\":1864,\"path\":\"standards/SPEC_METHOD.md\",\"quote\":\"two\\n   conforming tenants need not behave identically outside the contract.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/SPEC_METHOD.md#SPEC_METHOD%2F11.%20Build-tenant%20binding\",\"start_line\":1863}],\"statements\":[\"Selecting an environment that removes required human decisions or independent assessments.\",\"Requiring code, event streams or complete-history reconstruction merely because the procedure is generic.\",\"Treating executor identity, participation, convenience or structural validation as authority/conformance.\",\"Weakening WHAT as a tenant-local choice.\"]},\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:66e6caf2402df01dfdb9b83c7f8b0a02\",\"invalidation\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:invalidation:source-or-interpretation-change\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"latitude","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:310fb8c8cecb28797bb176c5d6cd1561","key":1790,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"allowed_vari