not internal debug tools,\\nwith the scope recorded in the design module (P2, P6).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/UX.md#UX%2F12.%20Adoption\",\"start_line\":588}],\"statements\":[\"Adopt the profile only for selected project UX surfaces, such as production UI, with scope recorded in the design module.\"]},\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:ac03acbc25d43f1c4cec70fe0b4cab0a\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:254e32e899936a647b4a4ae7b911dd86\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"forbidden_variation\":{\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":590,\"path\":\"standards/UX.md\",\"quote\":\"Adoption is per project. A project may adopt this profile only for some\\nUX surfaces, for example the production UI but not internal debug tools,\\nwith the scope recorded in the design module (P2, P6).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/UX.md#UX%2F12.%20Adoption\",\"start_line\":588}],\"statements\":[]},\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:a315f37867fff54223235c4be408071d\",\"invalidation\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:invalidation:source-or-interpretation-change\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"latitude","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:3e1595e9f8cb57b1afa03d8b1a56f155","key":1814,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"allowed_variation\":{\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":650,\"path\":\"standards/UX.md\",\"quote\":\"A UX sprint may escrow (P2, P4b):\\n\\n- screenshots or walkthrough capture;\\n- visual review;\\n- copy, spacing, density and layout cleanup;\\n- accessibility review and remediation;\\n- Msg-replay proof updates for product-meaningful interaction families;\\n- design-module wording cleanup;\\n- trace cleanup between changed UX states and governing authority.\\n\\nA UX sprint may not escrow (P6):\\n\\n- product-truth-changing Msg variants that lack an admitted carrier;\\n- new or changed AssetSurface contracts or equivalent typed product\\n  contracts;\\n- new navigation, information architecture or selection authority that\\n  changes product meaning;\\n- runtime, governance, closure, continuation, lineage, provenance or\\n  evidence semantics;\\n- release criteria or method law.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/UX.md#UX%2F12.%20Adoption%2FUX%20sprint%20compliance%20escrow\",\"start_line\":631}],\"statements\":[\"During a short iteration window when per-change proof costs more than expected correction, escrow screenshots/walkthroughs, visual review, copy/spacing/density/layout cleanup, accessibility review/remediation, meaningful-interaction Msg-replay proof updates, design-module wording cleanup and trace cleanup between changed states and authority.\"]},\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:fba38b75e6777b991248c792e3cacb39\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"forbidden_variation\":{\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":650,\"path\":\"standards/UX.md\",\"quote\":\"A UX sprint may escrow (P2, P4b):\\n\\n- screenshots or walkthrough capture;\\n- visual review;\\n- copy, spacing, density and layout cleanup;\\n- accessibility review and remediation;\\n- Msg-replay proof updates for product-meaningful interaction families;\\n- design-module wording cleanup;\\n- trace cleanup between changed UX states and governing authority.\\n\\nA UX sprint may not escrow (P6):\\n\\n- product-truth-changing Msg variants that lack an admitted carrier;\\n- new or changed AssetSurface contracts or equivalent typed product\\n  contracts;\\n- new navigation, information architecture or selection authority that\\n  changes product meaning;\\n- runtime, governance, closure, continuation, lineage, provenance or\\n  evidence semantics;\\n- release criteria or method law.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/UX.md#UX%2F12.%20Adoption%2FUX%20sprint%20compliance%20escrow\",\"start_line\":631}],\"statements\":[\"Escrowing truth-changing Msg variants lacking admitted carriers; new/changed AssetSurface or equivalent typed product contracts; navigation/information architecture/selection authority changing product meaning; runtime/governance/closure/continuation/lineage/provenance/evidence semantics; release criteria or method law.\",\"Weakening the UX process model or erasing eventual replay/accessibility obligations through escrow.\"]},\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:3e1595e9f8cb57b1afa03d8b1a56f155\",\"invalidation\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:invalidation:source-or-interpretation-change\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"latitude","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:1ab5f8d91663a76f3eb11954836bb05f","key":1815,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"allowed_variation\":{\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":812,\"path\":\"standards/WORLD_MODEL.md\",\"quote\":\"Techniques\\nthat serve this, none of them mandatory and none of them exhaustive:\\n\\n- cross-context invariance: separate what holds wherever the entity\\n  appears from what a particular context adds, where multiple contexts\\n  exist;\\n- null-peer comparison: name a structurally similar entity the operating\\n  model treats differently, and state what separates them;\\n- adjoint round-trip: interpret the entity through an adjacent domain's\\n  treatment surface and back through its adjoint mapping, and show the\\n  identity claim survives;\\n- transplant: show what a neighbouring entity would have to acquire to be\\n  treated as this one;\\n- coat stripping: vary or remove contextual claims and show identity\\n  survives; vary an identity claim and show it does not.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/WORLD_MODEL.md#WORLD_MODEL%2F9.%20Entity%20cut%20construction%2FDiscrimination\",\"start_line\":798}],\"statements\":[\"Use nonmandatory, nonexhaustive discrimination techniques: invariance across multiple existing contexts; structurally similar but operationally distinct null peers; adjacent treatment and adjoint interpret-back preserving identity; transplant of identity requirements to a neighbour; coat stripping that preserves identity when context varies but not when identity claims vary.\"]},\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:ea7976cc8986c83e51397ea3c9641497\",\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:43f89028fb972707e26975d939e746bb\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"forbidden_variation\":{\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":812,\"path\":\"standards/WORLD_MODEL.md\",\"quote\":\"Techniques\\nthat serve this, none of them mandatory and none of them exhaustive:\\n\\n- cross-context invariance: separate what holds wherever the entity\\n  appears from what a particular context adds, where multiple contexts\\n  exist;\\n- null-peer comparison: name a structurally similar entity the operating\\n  model treats differently, and state what separates them;\\n- adjoint round-trip: interpret the entity through an adjacent domain's\\n  treatment surface and back through its adjoint mapping, and show the\\n  identity claim survives;\\n- transplant: show what a neighbouring entity would have to acquire to be\\n  treated as this one;\\n- coat stripping: vary or remove contextual claims and show identity\\n  survives; vary an identity claim and show it does not.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/WORLD_MODEL.md#WORLD_MODEL%2F9.%20Entity%20cut%20construction%2FDiscrimination\",\"start_line\":798}],\"statements\":[]},\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:1ab5f8d91663a76f3eb11954836bb05f\",\"invalidation\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:invalidation:source-or-interpretation-change\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"latitude","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:7a20be09f4475da13ae2ab80a101671a","key":1816,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"allowed_variation\":{\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":833,\"path\":\"standards/WORLD_MODEL.md\",\"quote\":\"Concrete carriers, layouts, schemas and storage topology are\\nconsumer realisation; this profile requires that the published surfaces\\nsurvive and does not select the form they are stored in (P0, P2).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/WORLD_MODEL.md#WORLD_MODEL%2F9.%20Entity%20cut%20construction%2FPublishing%20a%20cut\",\"start_line\":831}],\"statements\":[\"Consumers choose concrete carriers, layouts, schemas and storage topology while preserving required published surfaces.\"]},\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:ea7976cc8986c83e51397ea3c9641497\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"forbidden_variation\":{\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":833,\"path\":\"standards/WORLD_MODEL.md\",\"quote\":\"Concrete carriers, layouts, schemas and storage topology are\\nconsumer realisation; this profile requires that the published surfaces\\nsurvive and does not select the form they are stored in (P0, P2).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/WORLD_MODEL.md#WORLD_MODEL%2F9.%20Entity%20cut%20construction%2FPublishing%20a%20cut\",\"start_line\":831}],\"statements\":[\"Storage form that fails to preserve the required published surfaces.\"]},\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:7a20be09f4475da13ae2ab80a101671a\",\"invalidation\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:invalidation:source-or-interpretation-change\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"latitude","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:08a5e40040855892e87a9729ab1ae27e","key":1817,"owner":"urn:a-