:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"residuals","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:13f62a518ffef2c0ee0486da0910cb71","key":1836,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"consequence\":\"Preserve the distinction between Product-level test authority and design/module authority, but leave exact ownership of the module-derived unit-proof law unresolved; do not merge or select an owner silently.\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:13f62a518ffef2c0ee0486da0910cb71\",\"invalidation\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:invalidation:source-or-interpretation-change\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:residual-kind:authored-uncertainty\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"re_entry\":[],\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"subject\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:2e29eb63656a6092cdf8daa41beaada3\",\"uncertainty\":{\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":25,\"path\":\"standards/ASSURANCE.md\",\"quote\":\"The\\ndesign profile's module-derived unit-proof law (its 6A to 6C) is §14 to\\n§16\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ASSURANCE.md#ASSURANCE\",\"start_line\":22},{\"end_line\":140,\"path\":\"standards/ASSURANCE.md\",\"quote\":\"Module-derived unit-proof law stays owned by the design profile (the\\nDESIGN_MODULE member); the shared context does not merge the two authority\\nsources\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ASSURANCE.md#ASSURANCE%2F2.%20Testing%20strategy%20taxonomy\",\"start_line\":138}],\"statement\":\"The introduction locates this law in ASSURANCE §§14–16, while the taxonomy says it remains owned by DESIGN_MODULE. This might distinguish written law from profile-object binding, but the absent sections do not establish that reconciliation.\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"residuals","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:f0b81c3f24db29c87de63cf31572e1b2","key":1837,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"consequence\":\"Retain every table row's stated claim, modality and source-owner distinction without fabricating inventories, mappings, evidence, consumer endpoints or complete application semantics.\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:f0b81c3f24db29c87de63cf31572e1b2\",\"invalidation\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:invalidation:source-or-interpretation-change\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:residual-kind:authored-uncertainty\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"re_entry\":[],\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"subject\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:ad2911520dc8ffb9419df0fede4f0e57\",\"uncertainty\":{\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":109,\"path\":\"standards/ASSURANCE.md\",\"quote\":\"The table accounts for §1 to §16.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ASSURANCE.md#ASSURANCE%2F1.%20Verification%20layers%2FFoundation%20to%20law%3A%20assurance%20and%20testing\",\"start_line\":109},{\"end_line\":113,\"path\":\"standards/ASSURANCE.md\",\"quote\":\"Consumers of these rows, where an actor enters them (FOUNDATIONS §3\\nFoundation to law, Consumers), one list per row, each consumer linked to\\nits own locus:\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ASSURANCE.md#ASSURANCE%2F1.%20Verification%20layers%2FFoundation%20to%20law%3A%20assurance%20and%20testing\",\"start_line\":111}],\"statement\":\"ASSURANCE §§4–16 and most foundation/consumer targets are absent. The table references but does not enumerate several testing, localisation, interface, module and lifecycle inventories. Consumer lists at 115–128 identify application versus mere reference, including cases with no separate consumer; their detailed cross-file topology is not materialised.\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"residuals","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:b20cc795230d5b90d3c2a73c9209d97e","key":1838,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"consequence\":\"Retain missing fixture as unperformed evaluation, with a governed fixture/lane diagnostic and no product semantic-failure inference. Do not assign it an invented core value.\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:b20cc795230d5b90d3c2a73c9209d97e\",\"invalidation\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:invalidation:source-or-interpretation-change\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:residual-kind:authored-uncertainty\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"re_entry\":[],\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"subject\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:1cfc131a76df6f85742a5443d4bf5f5e\",\"uncertainty\":{\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":95,\"path\":\"standards/ASSURANCE.md\",\"quote\":\"a missing fixture means the evaluation was not performed, so it is reported as such, never as a product semantic failure.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ASSURANCE.md#ASSURANCE%2F1.%20Verification%20layers%2FFoundation%20to%20law%3A%20assurance%20and%20testing\",\"start_line\":95},{\"end_line\":118,\"path\":\"standards/ASSURANCE.md\",\"quote\":\"a missing fixture is reported as an evaluation not performed, in the core value of FOUNDATIONS §4 Results that this paragraph applies\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ASSURANCE.md#ASSURANCE%2F1.%20Verification%20layers%2FFoundation%20to%20law%3A%20assurance%20and%20testing\",\"start_line\":118}],\"statement\":\"The consumer note mentions a core value for an evaluation not performed, whereas the supplied ACTIVATION rules expressly give unperformed evaluations no result. The note does not specify a value or a different predicate that would resolve this wording tension.\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"residuals","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:f68b9ddf131b24aaa1e987cc1cd79abd","key":1839,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"consequence\":\"Retain only locally stated consequences; activation, applicability, live/harnessed admission, co-evolution, lifecycle and conjunction requirements cannot be fully reconstructed or treated as discharged from this excerpt.\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:f68b9ddf131b24aaa1e987cc1cd79abd\",\"invalidation\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:invalidation:source-or-interpretation-change\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:residual-kind:authored-uncertainty\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"re_entry\":[],\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"subject\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:5501995e5fa70ff1ab307cf852168870\",\"uncertainty\":{\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":350,\"path\":\"standards/ASSURANCE.md\",\"quote\":\"and each activation is decided by ACTIVATION §1 (Applicability). The kind\\nof runner does not select the frame; the evaluated claim, subject, path,\\npopulation, oracle and falsification boundary do (P6, P2). Each frame's `invalidation` row,\\nhere and in §13, lists named instances of the material input change or\\nthe changed basis of\\n[ACTIVATION §7](ACTIVATION.md#7-closed-result-and-reuse); it adds no\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ASSURANCE.md#ASSURANCE%2F7.%20Product%20testing%20frame%20set%2FThe%20set\",\"start_line\":345}],\"statement\":\"ASSURANCE §§1–3, later §13 details beyond these supplied sections, P0–P6, FOUNDATIONS, REFERENCE_FRAME, ACTIVATION, EVALUATION, PRODUCT_DEFINITION, DESIGN_MODULE, SPEC_METHOD and RELEASE are cited without their complete governing clauses. Graph discovery cannot supply them.\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"residuals","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:a483ef800cc2da9fd5eb45d34eaeab85","key":1840,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"consequence\":\"Do not fabricate resolved clause identities, full imported definitions, generic functor contracts or conformance coverage. The source's calculus is not equated with the selected published interpretation basis.\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:a483ef800cc2da9fd5eb45d34eaeab85\",\"invalidation\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:invalidation:source-or-interpretation-change\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:residual-kind:authored-uncertainty\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"re_entry\":[],\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"subject\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:3dab7b4ae60847a9b5f77b8991c041fa\",\"uncertainty\":{\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":105,\"path\":\"standards/AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS.md\",\"quote\":\"This member owns the calculus-specific definitions and specialisations of\\n`a_c`. Its imported concepts keep their owners: in particular,\\n[FOUNDATIONS Results](FOUNDATIONS.md#results) and\\n[Conjunction of results](FOUNDATIONS.md#conjunction-of-results) own the result\\nvalues and combination law consumed by AC-007 and AC-019. No calculus model,\\ncarrier or interpretation becomes another owner of those laws. A consumer\\nneeds no implicit representation of the method, particular carrier or\\ndownstream implementation to interpret the calculus (P1, P6).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS.md#AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS%2F1.%20Position%2FDerivation%20provenance\",\"start_line\":98}],\"statement\":\"FOUNDATIONS ontology/results/conjunction/principles, referenced IDENTITY and reference-frame laws, the exact AxiomaticCalculusBasis identity record, and full calculus §§5–10/AC-015–020 are not supplied. Table summaries establish only the meanings expressly stated here.\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"residuals","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:f5777e8fe793ea178f0077a322b9c88b","key":1841,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"consequence\":\"Keep consumer routing as qualified source-reentry information, not asserted external governing endpoints. No consumer obtains decisions beyond its owner; the numbered row/pillar annotations are documentation coordinates, not authority.\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:f5777e8fe793ea178f0077a322b9c88b\",\"invalidation\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:invalidation:source-or-interpretation-change\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:residual-kind:authored-uncertainty\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"re_entry\":[],\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"subject\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:90c3d9660d33d96fa0e0932fb3cdc162\",\"uncertainty\":{\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":184,\"path\":\"standards/AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS.md\",\"quote\":\"Consumers of these rows, where an actor enters them (FOUNDATIONS §3\\nFoundation to law, Consumers), one list per row, each consumer linked to\\nits own locus:\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS.md#AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS%2F1.%20Position%2FFoundation%20to%20law\",\"start_line\":182}],\"statement\":\"The source names consumer routes not fully supplied: position→§8 and ODD/TRAVERSAL_OCCURRENCE/WORLD_MODEL F9 tables; scope→SPEC_METHOD §11 rule 6; signature→TRAVERSAL_OCCURRENCE imported/sort/stop clauses and AC-007/019; identity/typing→constraint surfaces and CONFORMANCE discriminator 22; authority/basis→AC-007/019 and surfaces; stops→TRAVERSAL_OCCURRENCE and AC-010/011/013/015, §§6–7, surfaces; latitude→surfaces and CONFORMANCE 17–18; residuals→surfaces, AC-013 and CONFORMANCE 16; closure→ACTIVATION §§2–3, surfaces and distinct TRAVERSAL_OCCURRENCE Projection; overlay→PRODUCT_DEFINITION §5 and AC-019; transformation→FOUNDATIONS accounting, REFERENCE_FRAME translation, SPEC_METHOD §11 rule 7 and surfaces; judgment→surfaces and §§7–8; traversal→ACTIVATION refinement, TRAVERSAL_OCCURRENCE stop/occurrence laws, ODD terminology/graph functions, PROFILES §1, CONFORMANCE 22/51, AC-013/007; interpretation→EVALUATION §2, SPEC_METHOD §11, TRAVERSAL_OCCURRENCE, CONFORMANCE 13/14/20/40/45, §§7–8 and surfaces; layers→SPEC_METHOD §6, FOUNDATIONS formal fragment and §8; identity→TRAVERSAL_OCCURRENCE closed signature; application→§5, surfaces and §8; surfaces→ACTIVATION acquisition and CONFORMANCE 15–18; conformance→no separate consumer. Provenance/import-only qualifications remain in force. Pillar sets for these nineteen rows are respectively {6,10},{10},{3,10},{2,3,10},{9,10},{3,9,10},{6,10},{9,10},{7,10},{2,10},{3,4,10},{9,10},{4,8,10},{6,10},{6,10},{2,10},{1,10},{7,10},{9,10}; pillar definitions and target clauses are unavailable.\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"residuals","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa4