52b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"residuals","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:c7a0398e651d47c3f2f9b2820484620f","key":1856,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"consequence\":\"Keep broad frame-conservation wording and the later explicit disposed-duplication rule visible. Lawful disposed paths must not be silently classified as violations merely from equivalence; the interpretation does not claim a general resolution beyond the stated conditions.\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:c7a0398e651d47c3f2f9b2820484620f\",\"invalidation\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:invalidation:source-or-interpretation-change\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:residual-kind:authored-uncertainty\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"re_entry\":[],\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"subject\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:2fc75893782a4078cfb9fcfd17f765d7\",\"uncertainty\":{\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":638,\"path\":\"standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md\",\"quote\":\"The law is false if a change is\\nlocally valid inside the selected frame but violates, duplicates or\\nsilently reinterprets an invariant in any affected governing frame.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md#DESIGN_MODULE%2F5.%20Ontology-first%20design%2FBounded%20frame%20conservation%20%28UP-017%29\",\"start_line\":636},{\"end_line\":1362,\"path\":\"standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md\",\"quote\":\"The\\nboundary between duplicates and violates is disposition, not equivalence:\\nan equivalent path is lawful when disposed and a defect when not\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md#DESIGN_MODULE%2F7.%20Ontology%20and%20three-view%20design%20gate%2FInvariant%20reconstruction%20sufficiency%20%28UP-018%29\",\"start_line\":1359}],\"statement\":\"The frame clause broadly names duplicated invariants as falsifiers, while reconstruction explicitly accepts disposed equivalent paths. The text does not formally distinguish invariant duplication from path duplication.\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"residuals","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:c39df9ada4cce71320a97a5f589bffc6","key":1857,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"consequence\":\"Retain design declaration fields and per-owner/per-boundary qualification applicability; do not instantiate qualification, manufacture an admission evaluator or infer missing operational checks.\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:c39df9ada4cce71320a97a5f589bffc6\",\"invalidation\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:invalidation:source-or-interpretation-change\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:residual-kind:authored-uncertainty\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"re_entry\":[],\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"subject\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:d2d50ec064f37926a95bcc1bbbb51190\",\"uncertainty\":{\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":901,\"path\":\"s