 override format, preservation test or publication mechanism is supplied.\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:e47359d7699fa7bde3fe014f4f7b1492\",\"invalidation\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:invalidation:source-or-interpretation-change\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:residual-kind:authored-uncertainty\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"re_entry\":[],\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"subject\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:5aed54c0690e67be3b33143e4c30ccd5\",\"uncertainty\":{\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":2453,\"path\":\"standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md\",\"quote\":\"[IDENTITY §7](IDENTITY.md#7-default-formats-and-overrides).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/DESIGN_MODULE.md#DESIGN_MODULE%2F12.%20Adoption%20and%20relations%2FIdentity%20defaults%20from%20a%20bound%20runtime%20realisation\",\"start_line\":2453}],\"statement\":\"IDENTITY §7 owns default standing, override law, preservation and publication but is not supplied.\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"residuals","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:fcce2db4a0e8b77083d91e6f7833b1a5","key":1866,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"consequence\":\"Premises, policy owners and non-expansion are represented, while the detailed proof-table structure, pillar indexing and complete row-to-consumer hyperlink incidence remain source-reentry material rather than operative derivations or fabricated endpoints.\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:fcce2db4a0e8b77083d91e6f7833b1a5\",\"invalidation\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:invalidation:source-or-interpretation-change\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:residual-kind:authored-uncertainty\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"re_entry\":[],\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"subject\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:bc7e4c53bced59c7b790eb61fb0c25fa\",\"uncertainty\":{\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":105,\"path\":\"standards/EVALUATION.md\",\"quote\":\"Consumers of these rows, where an actor enters them (FOUNDATIONS §3\\nFoundation to law, Consumers), one list per row, each consumer linked to\\nits own locus:\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/EVALUATION.md#EVALUATION%2F1.%20Claims%2FFoundation%20to%20law%3A%20claims%2C%20evidence%2C%20assessment%20and%20acceptance\",\"start_line\":103},{\"end_line\":126,\"path\":\"standards/EVALUATION.md\",\"quote\":\"Each consumer applies the rule and decides nothing the owning section does\\nnot\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/EVALUATION.md#EVALUATION%2F1.%20Claims%2FFoundation%20to%20law%3A%20claims%2C%20evidence%2C%20assessment%20and%20acceptance\",\"start_line\":125}],\"statement\":\"The table references external consumer loci in RELEASE, ASSURANCE, ACTIVATION, AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS, EXECUTIVE_BASELINE, CONFORMANCE, REFERENCE_FRAME, PRODUCT_DEFINITION, TICKETS, IDENTITY, SPEC_METHOD and FOUNDATIONS, plus later EVALUATION qualification sections. Their full content and the foundational standing calculus are outside this selection.\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"residuals","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:88e6bc85d5158d865493b6edb0b18f95","key":1867,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"consequence\":\"The five core-value cases and their refusal/consumption distinctions are described, but no review is run, triage computed, result conjoined, authority exercised or disposition applied. The finite schema does not provide an executable result-projection or review protocol.\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:88e6bc85d5158d865493b6edb0b18f95\",\"invalidation\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:invalidation:source-or-interpretation-change\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:residual-kind:authored-uncertainty\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"re_entry\":[],\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"subject\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:2775926f6a7ac6cb34fc94bd901ad92e\",\"uncertainty\":{\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":282,\"path\":\"standards/EVALUATION.md\",\"quote\":\"The projection of the finding-level triage payload is total over the core\\nvalues of [FOUNDATIONS §4, Results](FOUNDATIONS.md#results).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/EVALUATION.md#EVALUATION%2F4.%20Review%20results%2FResult%20and%20triage%20projection\",\"start_line\":277}],\"statement\":\"Operational judgment, traversal and transformation detail exceeds descriptive records; FOUNDATIONS' complete result and conjunction algebra is not supplied.\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"residuals","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:5f71a3e07b823c1eb1f36e5463b70568","key":1868,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"consequence\":\"The additional quasi-inverse/natural-isomorphism requirement is retained without asserting category/functor validity or categorical equivalence for any subject.\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:5f71a3e07b823c1eb1f36e5463b70568\",\"invalidation\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:invalidation:source-or-interpretation-change\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:residual-kind:authored-uncertainty\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"re_entry\":[],\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"subject\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:19e30cf61a7e6ca33b6b4f01e979cf51\",\"uncertainty\":{\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":409,\"path\":\"standards/EVALUATION.md\",\"quote\":\"This rung adds one\\nrequirement of its own to those items: a quasi-inverse functor, and\\nnatural isomorphisms between each composite of the functor with its\\nquasi-inverse and the identity functor, on a stated domain.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/EVALUATION.md#EVALUATION%2F6.%20Conformance%20of%20realisations\",\"start_line\":406}],\"statement\":\"The categories, maps, symbols and applicable Formal-fragment obligations belong to an unsupplied FOUNDATIONS section; the schema does not encode their full mathematical proof objects.\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"residuals","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:99aa24329a3dbcea2ac3e4affbcbc79a","key":1869,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"consequence\":\"Interpretation retains stated rules and consumer restrictions but cannot establish full equivalence definitions, formal categorical obligations, trial inventories or linked consumers' complete law.\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:99aa24329a3dbcea2ac3e4affbcbc79a\",\"invalidation\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:invalidation:source-or-interpretation-change\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:residual-kind:authored-uncertainty\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"re_entry\":[],\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"subject\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:acdfc80f32db9748da683d36150a1900\",\"uncertainty\":{\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":524,\"path\":\"standards/EVALUATION.md\",\"quote\":\"Each consumer applies the rule and decides nothing the owning section does\\nnot (P2, P6).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/EVALUATION.md#EVALUATION%2F6.%20Conformance%20of%20realisations%2FFoundation%20to%20law%3A%20conformance%2C%20equivalence%20and%20qualification\",\"start_line\":523}],\"statement\":\"The thirteen consumer lists point to unsupplied FOUNDATIONS, SPEC_METHOD, CONFORMANCE, ASSURANCE, ACTIVATION, REFERENCE_FRAME, AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS, PRODUCT_DEFINITION, RELEASE and Executive sections. Their local assertions include tenant conformance without outside-contract identity, structure-preservation claims separate from conformance, no second profile qualification process, digest identity without semantic authority, no unassessed actual-use evidence and no unrun case pass. The exact cross-file applications, discriminator inventories and owning procedures remain unresolved. The prose saying CONFORMANCE cases are choices in the 'last two rows' is ambiguous after the table's reconstruction-return row; no row reassignment is inferred.\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"residuals","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:4981d58fded6bed098dd98cc93c85240","key":1870,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"consequence\":\"Named operations, result distinctions, representative tests and source falsifiers are retained descriptively; no executable function, proof or assessment is created.\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:4981d58fded6bed098dd98cc93c85240\",\"invalidation\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:invalidation:source-or-interpretation-change\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:residual-kind:authored-uncertainty\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"re_entry\":[],\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"subject\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:fa98d4349e639c24a91066e18be8e320\",\"uncertainty\":{\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":607,\"path\":\"standards/EVALUATION.md\",\"quote\":\"The qualification population is every function and failure relation the\\nmethod claims (REFERENCE_FRAME §5), each with its required representative\\nobservations (P6):\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/EVALUATION.md#EVALUATION%2F7.%20Qualification%20of%20frames%20and%20of%20the%20method%2FMethod%20self-qualification\",\"start_line\":605}],\"statement\":\"The table states representative observations rather than complete formal method-function definitions. Full closed-pressure domains, conjunction veto/deferral causes, activation reconstruction and post-exposure revision classifications reside in unsupplied owners. The five-family schema does not encode these as executable judgments, traversals or transformations.\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"residuals","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:d2ce43bf92202b214d7ef3e19903fd2f","key":1871,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"consequence\":\"Ownership is retained without importing unsupplied definitions or treating this optional profile as an independent execution or acceptance authority.\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:d2ce43bf92202b214d7ef3e19903fd2f\",\"invalidation\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:invalidation:source-or-interpretation-change\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:residual-kind:authored-uncertainty\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"re_entry\":[],\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"subject\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:363fd61e6242c3dcc4ebf0264109f1a4\",\"uncertainty\":{\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":139,\"path\":\"standards/EXECUTIVE_BASELINE.md\",\"quote\":\"Where this profile conflicts with an owning\\nclause, the owning clause controls and this profile requires revision (P6).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/EXECUTIVE_BASELINE.md#EXECUTIVE_BASELINE%2F2.%20Status%20and%20authority%20boundary\",\"start_line\":138}],\"statement\":\"The owner table identifies authoritative locations without supplying their complete content: frame principles/outcomes, core algebra, admission/delegation, bounded-frame conservation, independent-review triggers, exact assurance populations, design-derived unit proof, foundation selection, testing populations, identity/proxy grants and release acceptance. No conflict determination or inherited permission is inferred from the citations.\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"residuals","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:bb3fa85caf602935096a029b6b896ffc","key":1872,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"consequence\":\"The nineteen-row trace is retained as source-authored rationale and ownership data, with its material consequences represented; detailed consumer inventory is not expanded into fabricated local endpoints or claimed complete proofs.\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\"