bd71","key":1883,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"consequence\":\"Retain operational meanings as concepts and constraints only. No source-defined judgment, traversal, transformation, categorical proof or runtime procedure is instantiated; temporal execution, proof objects and complete result functions require source re-entry beyond this schema.\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:669338821fb8c6e276f92052a33fbd71\",\"invalidation\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:invalidation:source-or-interpretation-change\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:residual-kind:authored-uncertainty\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"re_entry\":[],\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"subject\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:03892680a0099e23b65aaa50c3aad6e6\",\"uncertainty\":{\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":647,\"path\":\"standards/FOUNDATIONS.md\",\"quote\":\"Every transformation records what it preserved,\\nintroduced and removed, its external resolution witnesses and its residuals\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/FOUNDATIONS.md#FOUNDATIONS%2F4.%20Algebra\",\"start_line\":644},{\"end_line\":688,\"path\":\"standards/FOUNDATIONS.md\",\"quote\":\"its laws, records and maps are represented in a_c\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/FOUNDATIONS.md#FOUNDATIONS%2F4.%20Algebra\",\"start_line\":677}],\"statement\":\"The five active authoring families express descriptive requirements but do not encode or execute the source's full operational calculus, proof population or transition semantics.\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"residuals","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:c4d80154dffd81d64715e46f40ccf8bd","key":1884,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"consequence\":\"Retain the supplied rules and named owners without inventing external procedures, mappings, acceptance boundaries or proofs. Detailed consumer enumeration remains source-reentry material rather than an instantiated dependency graph.\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:c4d80154dffd81d64715e46f40ccf8bd\",\"invalidation\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:invalidation:source-or-interpretation-change\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:residual-kind:authored-uncertainty\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"re_entry\":[],\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"subject\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:065709d4630efac07de8bfd91abef267\",\"uncertainty\":{\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":894,\"path\":\"standards/FOUNDATIONS.md\",\"quote\":\"RF-012 in [REFERENCE_FRAME §3](REFERENCE_FRAME.md#rf-012-closed-results),\\nAC-007 in\\n[AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS §4](AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS.md#ac-007-constraint-and-refusal)\\nand [EVALUATION §4](EVALUATION.md#4-review-results) apply the first row's\\nalgebra to frames, constraints and reviews and add no choice of their own\\nbeyond any refinement they map under the fifth row;\\n[ACTIVATION §3](ACTIVATION.md#3-step-results-and-disposition) holds the\\nstep's refinements of the fifth row and the stop state of the seventh.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/FOUNDATIONS.md#FOUNDATIONS%2F4.%20Algebra%2FResults\",\"start_line\":887},{\"end_line\":907,\"path\":\"standards/FOUNDATIONS.md\",\"quote\":\"where a refusal keeps its predicate and `refusal(basis)` is a closed result, not a gap\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/FOUNDATIONS.md#FOUNDATIONS%2F4.%20Algebra%2FResults\",\"start_line\":907}],\"statement\":\"P0–P6 derivations, earlier ontology/Basis/import rules, ACTIVATION refinements/recovery, RF-010/RF-012, AC-007/AC-011/AC-013, EVALUATION acceptance and other consumer owners are not supplied in full. The consumer register also names local applications not separately modelled: state/classification evaluations have their own predicates; cross-view verdicts retain non-applicability versus satisfaction; clean skips, unrun checks and unresolved release dispositions have no results; refusal(basis) is a closed result rather than a gap; uncovered coverage is not a falsified component; partial_effect residuals survive joins; a failed run falsifies only its own predicate; an audit of a stale coverage tuple may return invalid_basis for that audit; passing matrices or produced packs do not themselves constitute verdicts; usability requires four named results and explicit conjunction; cooperating frames may conjoin without composing; contraction records total projection-to-accepted-atom mapping; intentional ontology omission/flattening declares accepted loss and a failure condition. The external details of those predicates, four results, mappings and demonstrations remain unresolved.\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"residuals","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:9055ac39b3ef8094ec7143ece890f121","key":1885,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"consequence\":\"Use the family table only for the obligations and ownership it states. Do not infer validity, an admitted assessment, mandatory-gate satisfaction, independent authorship or qualified runtime behaviour from a citation.\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:9055ac39b3ef8094ec7143ece890f121\",\"invalidation\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:invalidation:source-or-interpretation-change\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:residual-kind:authored-uncertainty\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"re_entry\":[],\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"subject\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:a69423fbd046a97b345dff84e7d2be8f\",\"uncertainty\":{\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1047,\"path\":\"standards/FOUNDATIONS.md\",\"quote\":\"For a deciding rule, use [Preservation through construction](#preservation-through-construction),\\n[Assertions and observation](#assertions-and-observation),\\n[Parallel derivation and mutual assurance](#parallel-derivation-and-mutual-assurance),\\n[Quantified assurance](#quantified-assurance), or\\n[Change impact and evidence reuse](#change-impact-and-evidence-reuse).\\nThe family table below explains those owners and adds no separate decision.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/FOUNDATIONS.md#FOUNDATIONS%2F4.%20Algebra%2FAssurance%20relations\",\"start_line\":1042}],\"statement\":\"The supplied family table describes consequences and ownership but does not supply full commitment derivations, intake authority, source-owned per-step laws, ported-contribution authorship, release gates, conformance demonstration cases AR-01 to AR-04, or execution/checker mechanisms. Its row-to-consumer links and pillar annotations are not expanded as separate executable or governing dependencies.\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"residuals","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:80dbe7ea44136a4d4b84944f4b6f1512","key":1886,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"consequence\":\"Universal implications, checking relations, probabilities, transformation claims and source-defined judgment/traversal meanings remain descriptive obligations. No proof, instance judgment, runtime operation or support-kind certification is produced.\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:80dbe7ea44136a4d4b84944f4b6f1512\",\"invalidation\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:invalidation:source-or-interpretation-change\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:residual-kind:authored-uncertainty\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"re_entry\":[],\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"subject\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:cffbc4e797362ee75c9acc3609227c21\",\"uncertainty\":{\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1422,\"path\":\"standards/FOUNDATIONS.md\",\"quote\":\"An external predicate retains the source, scope and evidence required to\\nestablish it; an arbitrary truth label does not discharge the obligation.\\nNo particular proof assistant, probability library or execution engine is\\nselected (P1, P6).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/FOUNDATIONS.md#FOUNDATIONS%2F4.%20Algebra%2FFormal%20representation\",\"start_line\":1419}],\"statement\":\"The five active record families can retain formulas, modal requirements and dependency descriptions but cannot fully represent proof terms, all admitted checker conclusions, runtime traces, evidence payloads or the operational process of qualification. AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS §6/Constraint surfaces, EVALUATION §6–§7 and CONFORMANCE are unresolved source dependencies.\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"residuals","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:0377c5f2adcb98a8e8e1c49c4ceeb08b","key":1887,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"consequence\":\"Preserve all four hypotheses as candidates for falsification, without equating them to laws, establishing equivalence or asserting runtime composition.\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:0377c5f2adcb98a8e8e1c49c4ceeb08b\",\"invalidation\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:invalidation:source-or-interpretation-change\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:residual-kind:authored-uncertainty\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"re_entry\":[],\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"subject\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:44f67134d32e1310c5a17534a999d67f\",\"uncertainty\":{\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1452,\"path\":\"standards/FOUNDATIONS.md\",\"quote\":\"Not law; carried for falsification: categorical equivalence of 𝒜 and ℐ under\\nsome reformulation; universal algorithmic capture of meaning; the statistical\\nMarkov boundary (candidate status under\\n[WORLD_MODEL §4](WORLD_MODEL.md#epistemic-status));\\ntraversal composition laws of any runtime.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/FOUNDATIONS.md#FOUNDATIONS%2F5.%20Hypotheses\",\"start_line\":1448}],\"statement\":\"𝒜, ℐ, the contemplated reformulation, full meaning-capture claim, Markov-boundary epistemic conditions and any specific runtime composition law are not defined in the supplied section.\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"residuals","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:2fb8c9f10228a95ffdc540fb752a1e8d","key":1888,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"consequence\":\"Catalog entries remain source-linked locator categories. Missing semantic definitions, import declarations, authority bindings, result mappings and resolution decisions must be re-entered at their actual owners; none are inferred from labels or discovery edges.\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:2fb8c9f10228a95ffdc540fb752a1e8d\",\"invalidation\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:invalidation:source-or-interpretation-change\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:residual-kind:authored-uncertainty\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"re_entry\":[],\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"subject\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:a159dd754aa9500e917e52db5c007d60\",\"uncertainty\":{\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":15,\"path\":\"standards/GLOSSARY.md\",\"quote\":\"This member contains no semantic definition. It declares no bounded\\ncontext, concept, import, translation, equivalence, disambiguation or\\nauthority. It is a non-deciding index into the clauses that own those\\nmeanings in the selected complete STDO basis (P6, P1).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/GLOSSARY.md#GLOSSARY%2F1.%20Index%20contract\",\"start_line\":12},{\"end_line\":24,\"path\":\"standards/GLOSSARY.md\",\"quote\":\"§2 states how a row records a concept that a context holds by import, and\\na concept whose member declares no bounded context for it.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/GLOSSARY.md#GLOSSARY%2F1.%20Index%20contract\",\"start_line\":23}],\"statement\":\"Most owning clauses indexed across Method identity, Axiomatic calculus, Semantic resolution, Product-definition routing, Release publication, Reference-frame evaluation, Build tenancy, Recursive product, Product assurance, Ambiguity governance, World model, Graph-native ODD and Traversal occurrence are outside the supplied source. GLOSSARY §16–§17 are also absent. The shared labels and outcome lists do not disclose complete definitions or core mappings.\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"residuals","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:0e609728c2e5f94237aa5a0d21ab8efa","key":1889,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"consequence\":\"Do not infer context imports, outcome mappings or frame capabilities from the catalog alone. Explicit local owner links to Results and Conjunction remain non-deciding locators.\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:0e609728c2e5f94237aa5a0d21ab8efa\",\"invalidation\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:invalidation:source-or-interpretation-change\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:residual-kind:authored-uncertainty\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"re_entry\":[],\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"subject\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:5a10a0f1f401ec83baeec723320f3ada\",\"uncertainty\":{\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":170,\"path\":\"standards/GLOSSARY.md\",\"quote\":\"A row for an imported concept cites\\nits owning section as owning concept clause and the import declaration as\\nrelation clause (§2; P1, P6).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/GLOSSARY.md#GLOSSARY%2F8.%20Reference-frame%20evaluation\",\"start_line\":168}],\"statement\":\"External imported-owner definitions and refinements are unavailable. Secondary relations remain locators: Frame → REFERENCE_FRAME §1; Frame Tuple → minimal-frame-declaration; Activated Frame → activation packet; Frame-Set Declaration → PRODUCT_DEFINITION §7; Activation Packet → ACTIVATION §1; Actor Identity → SPEC_METHOD §11; Communication → ACTIVATION configuration; activate and coverage statuses → FOUNDATIONS Results; conjoin → Conjunction; translate → evidence-or-coordinate-translation; size measurement → RF-002; admission/activation → method functions; ambiguity → SPEC_METHOD §5; Closed Result → RF-012. The row grouping 'not performed ...; refinement of the core' is read as grouped indexed terms, not a claim that non-performance is a core refinement, because the explicitly cited Results owner forbids any such mapping.\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"residuals","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:eef61d5f2765113f52df564ceb368867","key":1890,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"consequence\":\"The inventories retain named terms, source owners, explicit distinctions and relation locators only. 'none' means no relation clause listed, not proof that no relationship exists. No full external definitions or result mappings are fabricated.\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:eef61d5f2765113f52df564ceb368867\",\"invalidation\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:invalidation:source-or-interpretation-change\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:residual-kind:authored-uncertainty\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"re_entry\":[],\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"subject\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:a6fe8a828fd36e326960c62ade24fc8b\",\"uncertainty\":{\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":338,\"path\":\"standards/GLOSSARY.md\",\"quote\":\"| Indexed term | Source context | Owning concept clause | Relation clause |\\n|---|---|---|---|\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/GLOSSARY.md#GLOSSARY%2F16.%20Concepts%20of%20members%20without%20a%20declared%20context\",\"start_line\":337}],\"statement\":\"Most FOUNDATIONS, ACTIVATION, EVALUATION, CONFORMANCE, PROFILES, DESIGN_MODULE and UX owning clauses and referenced glossary §§2, 5 and 8 are not supplied.\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"residuals","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:219df7d6fb1a39fec3c630ed20d87add","key":1891,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"consequence\":\"The listed uses remain distinct clause-owned senses; no shared result algebra, admission rule or template workflow is inferred or executed from matching labels.\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:219df7d6fb1a39fec3c630ed20d87add\",\"invalidation\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:invalidation:source-or-interpretation-change\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:residual-kind:authored-uncertainty\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"re_entry\":[],\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"subject\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:13b6172ff45e0c256887788162a4e35c\",\"uncertainty\":{\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":376,\"path\":\"standards/GLOSSARY.md\",\"quote\":\"| Label | Where this use occurs (locator, not a definition) | Owning clause |\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/GLOSSARY.md#GLOSSARY%2F17.%20Labels%20with%20several%20senses\",\"start_line\":376}],\"statement\":\"The section expressly supplies locators rather than definitions; most owning clauses and the referenced basis-inventory template are absent.\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"residuals","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:b0143bab9f9fe7420809442402f96c47","key":1892,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"consequence\":\"IDENTITY's stated law and owner boundaries are retained without restating absent Object/Authority/Basis definitions, calculus-edition identity, release forms, RF-003 or WORLD_MODEL refinement.\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:b0143bab9f9fe7420809442402f96c47\",\"invalidation\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:invalidation:source-or-interpretation-change\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:residual-kind:authored-uncertainty\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"re_entry\":[],\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"subject\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:856015343871c433411a25f5b43fe66d\",\"uncertainty\":{\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":20,\"path\":\"standards/IDENTITY.md\",\"quote\":\"The identity\\nof one calculus edition is\\n[AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS §8](AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS.md#8-calculus-identity), which\\nthis member does not restate. Release identity, its names and its forms are\\nthe release law of [RELEASE](RELEASE.md); this member states only the\\nboundary between it and object identity.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/IDENTITY.md#IDENTITY\",\"start_line\":15}],\"statement\":\"External owning definitions and laws are not provided; graph discovery cannot substitute for them.\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"residuals","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:7c6f641adf802c5ecbe9f0130a1b32a7","key":1893,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"consequence\":\"No proof of derivation or governing edge to an unavailable endpoint is asserted. Detailed routing can be re-entered at lines 58–69 and 81–92. Explicit negative routing remains meaningful: readability and release-boundary rows have only named local consumers; minimum questions and implementation policy have no separate consumer; RELEASE and SPEC_METHOD references do not imply application of the release-boundary row.\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:7c6f641adf802c5ecbe9f0130a1b32a7\",\"invalidation\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:invalidation:source-or-interpretation-change\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:residual-kind:authored-uncertainty\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"re_entry\":[],\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"subject\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:8b02973e1156879c7d2e0e2a6c603ecd\",\"uncertainty\":{\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":92,\"path\":\"standards/IDENTITY.md\",\"quote\":\"- Row 11, the minimum questions: no separate consumer applies. The questions are asked by whoever defines or audits an identity surface, each applying a rule traced above; the seven questions are this member's choice, and no section of another member names them.\\n- Row 12, the consequence for implementations: no separate consumer applies. The preference for typed readers and the two-step repair are a policy of this member for implementations; a project that repairs an implementation applies them under its own design authority, and no section of another member names this section.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/IDENTITY.md#IDENTITY%2F1.%20Position%2FFoundation%20to%20law\",\"start_line\":91}],\"statement\":\"The five-family representation does not fully materialise the table's pillar annotations and all clause-level consumer loci. Most underlying principle and consumer sections are unavailable.\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"residuals","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:3981582eccc22451ee481ec382596565","key":1894,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"consequence\":\"All listed grant contents are preserved without imposing an invented nine-field schema or dropping a listed content item.\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:3981582eccc22451ee481ec382596565\",\"invalidation\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:invalidation:source-or-interpretation-change\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:residual-kind:authored-uncertainty\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"re_entry\":[],\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"subject\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:0ed41260452a87de6836fa5047cb79ce\",\"uncertainty\":{\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":245,\"path\":\"standards/IDENTITY.md\",\"quote\":\"A proxy grant names its\\ngrantor, actor, subject, scope, permitted and excluded decisions,\\nvalidity, delegation rights, revocation and provenance (P6, P3).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/IDENTITY.md#IDENTITY%2F6.%20Authority%20identity%20and%20conservation%20%28STDO-UP-004%29\",\"start_line\":243},{\"end_line\":64,\"path\":\"standards/IDENTITY.md\",\"quote\":\"the nine grant fields: this section\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/IDENTITY.md#IDENTITY%2F1.%20Position%2FFoundation%20to%20law\",\"start_line\":64}],\"statement\":\"The derivation table says nine grant fields, while the prose separately names permitted and excluded decisions; it does not specify whether those share one field.\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"residuals","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:69891765879f76a53a3e78fcc6ecc515","key":1895,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"consequence\":\"All table topics' material rules are retained in concepts/constraints, but the exact row-by-row derivation proof, pillar assignment and full consumer network require source re-entry. Consumer references are applications, not new authority. The table's explicit no-separate-consumer statements are not converted into universal non-dependency claims.\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:69891765879f76a53a3e78fcc6ecc515\",\"invalidation\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:invalidation:source-or-interpretation-change\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:residual-kind:authored-uncertainty\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"re_entry\":[],\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"subject\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:a5d43a54e9b6c1b4035264da5197bcbd\",\"uncertainty\":{\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":173,\"path\":\"standards/ODD.md\",\"quote\":\"Each consumer applies the rule and decides nothing the owning section does\\nnot (P2, P6).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ODD.md#ODD%2F1.%20Position%2FFoundation%20to%20law\",\"start_line\":172},{\"end_line\":192,\"path\":\"standards/ODD.md\",\"quote\":\"Whether a product is built correctly is decided by §11,\\n  and whether a move complies by the audit of §9.\\n- §20 is a compression of this member and owns no determination (§20).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ODD.md#ODD%2F1.%20Position%2FFoundation%20to%20law\",\"start_line\":190}],\"statement\":\"The 25-row table and consumer inventory at lines 116–170 exceed the compact relation projection. Many cited internal clauses and external sections are not supplied, including exact failure-pattern/checklist contents and their detailed application loci.\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"residuals","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:9b72eac523a422586e3226aab5de4605","key":1896,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"consequence\":\"No complete closure algebra, evaluator, replay engine or transition system is constructed. Yield/retry/block/timeout, selection/no-action, edge closure and Product acceptance remain distinct. The known audit mappings are preserved; unknown closure mappings remain unresolved.\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:9b72eac523a422586e3226aab5de4605\",\"invalidation\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:invalidation:source-or-interpretation-change\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:residual-kind:authored-uncertainty\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"re_entry\":[],\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"subject\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:ccf788aa3cfe567da2d3eff370213cba\",\"uncertainty\":{\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":128,\"path\":\"standards/ODD.md\",\"quote\":\"the seven closure decisions, their causes, the two causes of a typed no-action and the default of graph following in A4\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ODD.md#ODD%2F1.%20Position%2FFoundation%20to%20law\",\"start_line\":128}],\"statement\":\"§11.5D/A0–A16, its seven closure decisions, no-action causes, ledger fields, causal carrier schemas, replay inputs, terminal conditions and constitutional equation are not supplied. Five active families cannot instantiate their operational semantics.\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"residuals","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:2400fe534819e7d5231ccdc2a97ed229","key":1897,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"consequence\":\"Source-to-target binding directions and supplied preservation/invalidation conditions are retained. Full semantic equivalence or lawfulness of the specialisations is not certified, and ODD shorthands are not identified with a_c functor kinds.\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:2400fe534819e7d5231ccdc2a97ed229\",\"invalidation\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:invalidation:source-or-interpretation-change\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:residual-kind:authored-uncertainty\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"re_entry\":[],\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"subject\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:4017b7e5758fd54465a17101f370d214\",\"uncertainty\":{\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":350,\"path\":\"standards/ODD.md\",\"quote\":\"The source concepts and their\\ncontext are owned by\\n[SPEC_METHOD §5](SPEC_METHOD.md#5-ambiguity-governance-and-lifecycle); this\\nprofile owns the targets in the graph-native ODD context (P1, P6).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ODD.md#ODD%2F5.%20Graph%20model%2FProbabilistic%20compute\",\"start_line\":347}],\"statement\":\"FOUNDATIONS P0, SPEC_METHOD §5 and PROFILES §§1–2 are referenced but absent; the selected complete STDO release is a subject-side binding condition, not independently established here.\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"residuals","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:cfe4e71e7ef2362366b715a213e6d7e9","key":1898,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"consequence\":\"The declared environment contract, outer-contract conservation and invalidation rules are retained, without inventing missing adapter semantics or evaluating any refinement.\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:cfe4e71e7ef2362366b715a213e6d7e9\",\"invalidation\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:invalidation:source-or-interpretation-change\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:residual-kind:authored-uncertainty\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"re_entry\":[],\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"subject\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:31591c3d84d1ea89565004b1b7295b63\",\"uncertainty\":{\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":386,\"path\":\"standards/ODD.md\",\"quote\":\"This profile declares the\\ncumulative carried environment of\\n[§11.8](#118-cumulative-environment-law-is-mandatory) as that specialised\\ncontract; §11.8 is conserved as profile law and is not generalised into\\nthe core.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ODD.md#ODD%2F5.%20Graph%20model%2FGraph%20functions\",\"start_line\":382}],\"statement\":\"ACTIVATION §4, ODD §11.8 and AC-016 are absent; only their explicitly quoted binding consequences are available.\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"residuals","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:e80a267ad58c8acd89f9ca524275e7dd","key":1899,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"consequence\":\"The universal correctness prerequisite is retained without claiming this excerpt enumerates every clause or establishes any product's correctness.\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:e80a267ad58c8acd89f9ca524275e7dd\",\"invalidation\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:invalidation:source-or-interpretation-change\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:residual-kind:authored-uncertainty\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"re_entry\":[],\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"subject\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:7235a36160028a0b495824fe7e14844b\",\"uncertainty\":{\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":603,\"path\":\"standards/ODD.md\",\"quote\":\"An ODD product is built correctly only when every clause of this section\\nholds (P6).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ODD.md#ODD%2F11.%20Core%20law\",\"start_line\":602}],\"statement\":\"Later §11 clauses, beginning with §11.5D, are discovery references or table summaries rather than supplied full source.\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"residuals","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:ae0f3ba4360641916575e2467f9d402c","key":1900,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"consequence\":\"ABG admission specialisation remains conditional and distinct from broader execution authority. No consequential transformation is admitted or executed by this interpretation.\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:ae0f3ba4360641916575e2467f9d402c\",\"invalidation\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:invalidation:source-or-interpretation-change\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:residual-kind:authored-uncertainty\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"re_entry\":[],\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"subject\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:e7f6aecf3b4af18e5ba857db2a632ac8\",\"uncertainty\":{\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":729,\"path\":\"standards/ODD.md\",\"quote\":\"ABG's\\nadmission authority is the graph-native specialisation of transformation\\nadmission completeness, whose admission semantics\\n[ACTIVATION §4](ACTIVATION.md#complete-enclosing-relation-admission) owns;\\nthe software-design profile applies that law in\\n[DESIGN_MODULE, Transformation admission completeness](DESIGN_MODULE.md#transformation-admission-completeness-up-016).\\nABG's broader execution, supervision, retry and projection authority\\ncontinues to derive from this profile and is not thereby reclassified as\\nadmission authority.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ODD.md#ODD%2F11.%20Core%20law%2F11.5B%20Execution%20authority%20audit\",\"start_line\":721}],\"statement\":\"The complete transformation admission semantics and DESIGN_MODULE application are not supplied; their full admission prerequisites cannot be recovered from the audit reference alone.\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"residuals","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:8771158db9cf8fc172f223a7b4dc8d1b","key":1901,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"consequence\":\"Retain the nonconvergence guarantee and obligation to distinguish four causes, but do not invent those causes or extend the imported outcome/result/acceptance law beyond the supplied descriptions.\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:8771158db9cf8fc172f223a7b4dc8d1b\",\"invalidation\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:invalidation:source-or-interpretation-change\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:residual-kind:authored-uncertainty\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"re_entry\":[],\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"subject\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:bcaa8a8d820aec2a089181d683a453df\",\"uncertainty\":{\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":788,\"path\":\"standards/ODD.md\",\"quote\":\"[ACTIVATION §1 Feedback and diagnosis](ACTIVATION.md#construction-relation):\\nit corrects towards the required conditions as observations arrive,\\nguarantees neither convergence nor the adequacy of those conditions, and\\nits diagnoses distinguish the four causes named there (P2, P6).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ODD.md#ODD%2F11.%20Core%20law%2F11.5D%20Constructive%20evaluation%20and%20yield%20loop\",\"start_line\":785}],\"statement\":\"ACTIVATION's four diagnostic causes, FOUNDATIONS result/conjunction law, SPEC_METHOD outcome conservation and RELEASE successor-claim law are referenced but not supplied.\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"residuals","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:ed278e5e89facf7f0489beef99fe12e6","key":1902,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"consequence\":\"The interpretation preserves obligations and ordered data dependencies without executing a transition, proving totality, admitting a ledger row or asserting that any edge closed. The actual runtime/program semantics remain outside these record families.\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:ed278e5e89facf7f0489beef99fe12e6\",\"invalidation\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:invalidation:source-or-interpretation-change\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:residual-kind:authored-uncertainty\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"re_entry\":[],\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"subject\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:c605bc5b18dab1b81be6bb05308fe283\",\"uncertainty\":{\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1401,\"path\":\"standards/ODD.md\",\"quote\":\"The implementation is correct only when the next work decision is derived\\nfrom that equation, `U` stays causally reachable through the target\\nbinding and the construction intent, and no other path can decide what\\nwork happens next (P6, P2).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ODD.md#ODD%2F11.%20Core%20law%2F11.5D%20Constructive%20evaluation%20and%20yield%20loop\",\"start_line\":1398}],\"statement\":\"The source defines an operational equation, causal carrier graph and function authority protocol. The finite schema describes these as data but does not encode executable judgments, traversals, transformations or machine-checkable totality proofs.\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"residuals","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:7cfe26945776ae0881a6c727704036de","key":1903,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"consequence\":\"Preserve the obligation to use deterministic fail-closed admission and the F_P/F_D distinction, without claiming an artifact passes or reconstructing missing gate criteria.\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:7cfe26945776ae0881a6c727704036de\",\"invalidation\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:invalidation:source-or-interpretation-change\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:residual-kind:authored-uncertainty\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"re_entry\":[],\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"subject\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:26c627c4204c2f1f3b1820e20d788928\",\"uncertainty\":{\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1507,\"path\":\"standards/ODD.md\",\"quote\":\"This profile does not declare the artifact rules again: tickets,\\nchange-class declarations, design-module derivations and execution\\ncontracts are admitted under SPEC_METHOD and TICKETS, which already require\\na drafted classification to be admitted or rejected against deterministic\\ncriteria rather than taken as automatic truth.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ODD.md#ODD%2F11.%20Core%20law%2F11.7A%20Conforming%20agentic%20development\",\"start_line\":1503}],\"statement\":\"SPEC_METHOD, TICKETS, ACTIVATION acquisition/standalone scope and ODD §9 shared-method change rules are absent.\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"residuals","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:c9bcbe499ecd7588576266018487db15","key":1904,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"consequence\":\"Only the supplied installed-form condition, isolation requirement and recommended proving lane are interpreted; full assurance qualification is not assessed.\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:c9bcbe499ecd7588576266018487db15\",\"invalidation\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:invalidation:source-or-interpretation-change\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:residual-kind:authored-uncertainty\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"re_entry\":[],\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"subject\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:e22ced7f66cd72435a045f8206873289\",\"uncertainty\":{\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1608,\"path\":\"standards/ODD.md\",\"quote\":\"[ASSURANCE §5 Installed dev proof](ASSURANCE.md#5-installed-dev-proof), which\\nowns it.\",\"secti