te legitimate inputs rather than infer exclusive sourcing.\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:4211e5c46d53ccb42aca3b463fac82cc\",\"invalidation\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:invalidation:source-or-interpretation-change\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:residual-kind:authored-uncertainty\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"re_entry\":[],\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"subject\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:e6c28515fab54d1546139bb7d8cdb4bc\",\"uncertainty\":{\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1016,\"path\":\"standards/PRODUCT_DEFINITION.md\",\"quote\":\"that is the usual starting point, not the only lawful source\\n(P2).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/PRODUCT_DEFINITION.md#PRODUCT_DEFINITION%2F12.%20Bootstrap\",\"start_line\":1015},{\"end_line\":1044,\"path\":\"standards/PRODUCT_DEFINITION.md\",\"quote\":\"9. Write or confirm the current Goals carrier, run the goals to intent to\\n   product steps, and bind the resulting Intent and Product entrypoints.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/PRODUCT_DEFINITION.md#PRODUCT_DEFINITION%2F12.%20Bootstrap\",\"start_line\":1043}],\"statement\":\"Manager/schema/template details and §§3–8 are absent. The ordered instruction to run goals→intent→product coexists with express non-exclusivity of requirement sources; whether any bootstrap step itself can be substituted is not resolved here.\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"residuals","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:82c4589d5f889eb745eb3eb63ea47040","key":1919,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"consequence\":\"Preserve declared coordinates and ownership restrictions without inventing a full import calculus or treating an index as its owner.\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:82c4589d5f889eb745eb3eb63ea47040\",\"invalidation\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:invalidation:source-or-interpretation-change\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:residual-kind:authored-uncertainty\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"re_entry\":[],\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"subject\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:1af950f0c333c333ffc3ec34265c2a40\",\"uncertainty\":{\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":36,\"path\":\"standards/PROFILES.md\",\"quote\":\"[FOUNDATIONS §2 Imports between members](FOUNDATIONS.md#imports-between-members),\\nwhich states what an import is, and restates none of that member's rules.\\nIts family table, in the format of\\n[FOUNDATIONS §3 Foundation to law](FOUNDATIONS.md#foundation-to-law),\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/PROFILES.md#PROFILES%2F1.%20The%20boundary\",\"start_line\":33}],\"statement\":\"FOUNDATIONS §§2–3 and the referenced PRODUCT_DEFINITION/UX/ODD binding owners are not fully present.\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"residuals","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:3913f64130bd5b5b0f5b9f0f73c83b22","key":1920,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"consequence\":\"The ODD and occurrence descriptions remain indexed profile roles; no graph runtime, traversal history or model-family signature is instantiated or completed.\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:3913f64130bd5b5b0f5b9f0f73c83b22\",\"invalidation\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:invalidation:source-or-interpretation-change\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:residual-kind:authored-uncertainty\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"re_entry\":[],\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"subject\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:d9237cdda330747e7521d91a94f9903d\",\"uncertainty\":{\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":67,\"path\":\"standards/PROFILES.md\",\"quote\":\"Where another member says that\\nthis section keeps the ODD binding, the binding is the one ODD states and\\nthis section indexes (P0, P1).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/PROFILES.md#PROFILES%2F2.%20Graph%20execution\",\"start_line\":65}],\"statement\":\"ODD's full bindings, cumulative environment law, ownership layers and TRAVERSAL_OCCURRENCE OP-001–007 are external.\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"residuals","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:4a717f0c11a5dd6558336b2db4d1f1c7","key":1921,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"consequence\":\"Design obligations are retained as named binding domains and owner routes, without reconstructing their admission, gate or cost algorithms.\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:4a717f0c11a5dd6558336b2db4d1f1c7\",\"invalidation\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:invalidation:source-or-interpretation-change\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:residual-kind:authored-uncertainty\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"re_entry\":[],\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"subject\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:bff1d9cf01a51b82efe1da37919b576e\",\"uncertainty\":{\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":85,\"path\":\"standards/PROFILES.md\",\"quote\":\"The per-boundary cost of the derivation chain is\\ndecided there (DESIGN_MODULE §5 Proportional design sequencing, §7 Gate\\nand retrospective work) (P2, P0).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/PROFILES.md#PROFILES%2F3.%20Software%20design\",\"start_line\":83}],\"statement\":\"DESIGN_MODULE, ASSURANCE §§14–16 and SPEC_METHOD §2 are indexed rather than supplied.\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"residuals","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:9950f8c923bd0355176b6a41597090e9","key":1922,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"consequence\":\"Preserve the conditional design refinement and one-core-value mapping, without inventing result values, equivalent contracts, exemptions or escrow transitions.\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:9950f8c923bd0355176b6a41597090e9\",\"invalidation\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:invalidation:source-or-interpretation-change\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:residual-kind:authored-uncertainty\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"re_entry\":[],\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"subject\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:7bad658d82a142e3a12d7ef3dd5f3e8e\",\"uncertainty\":{\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":100,\"path\":\"standards/PROFILES.md\",\"quote\":\"and its refinements of the core result algebra, each value mapped to one\\ncore value (UX §15). Its binding of TICKETS §3's generalised escrow terms\\nis declared in its lead (P6, P2).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/PROFILES.md#PROFILES%2F4.%20UX\",\"start_line\":98}],\"statement\":\"UX's detailed laws, result map and TICKETS escrow terms are absent.\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"residuals","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:23ba4c0384566d40276af158098b0f23","key":1923,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"consequence\":\"Keep Markov-object status candidate and core non-dependence explicit; no promotion or published entity cut is asserted.\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:23ba4c0384566d40276af158098b0f23\",\"invalidation\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:invalidation:source-or-interpretation-change\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:residual-kind:authored-uncertainty\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"re_entry\":[],\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"subject\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:3a7dbc4ecae4b3f5cc41c0adb447df38\",\"uncertainty\":{\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":108,\"path\":\"standards/PROFILES.md\",\"quote\":\"the Markov-object construct at candidate status\\nwith its effective blanket, working refinements, epistemic status and\\npromotion gate;\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/PROFILES.md#PROFILES%2F5.%20World%20model\",\"start_line\":106}],\"statement\":\"The construct, promotion gate, entity-cut laws and result mappings are indexed but not defined in the supplied source.\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"residuals","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:aadd7a40a6d323cef4a474470eb6d569","key":1924,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"consequence\":\"Do not activate Executive, Worker, Reviewer or specialist roles or infer authority from their names.\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:aadd7a40a6d323cef4a474470eb6d569\",\"invalidation\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:invalidation:source-or-interpretation-change\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:residual-kind:authored-uncertainty\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"re_entry\":[],\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"subject\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:fc43c65ddaf2dfc761ac15a3bf6c1f3e\",\"uncertainty\":{\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":130,\"path\":\"standards/PROFILES.md\",\"quote\":\"Its frame names\\nbind the responsibilities that configuration allocates under\\n[ACTIVATION §1 Roles and delegation](ACTIVATION.md#roles-and-delegation),\\nnot roles imported by spelling, as its lead declares (P1, P6).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/PROFILES.md#PROFILES%2F6.%20Engagement%20baseline\",\"start_line\":127}],\"statement\":\"Configuration duties and delegation grants belong to unsupplied EXECUTIVE_BASELINE and ACTIVATION sections.\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"residuals","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:af7151d83677854f43a45ebf04bac60a","key":1925,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"consequence\":\"Keep route order and purposes as a navigation concept rather than fabricated governing edges to absent endpoints.\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:af7151d83677854f43a45ebf04bac60a\",\"invalidation\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:invalidation:source-or-interpretation-change\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:residual-kind:authored-uncertainty\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"re_entry\":[],\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"subject\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:0b861da646df218c18f157e8c069d3be\",\"uncertainty\":{\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":12,\"path\":\"standards/README.md\",\"quote\":\"| You want to | Read, in order |\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/README.md#STDO%20V3%2FRoutes\",\"start_line\":12}],\"statement\":\"Most linked target sections are not supplied. Read-order guidance does not establish their full semantics, authority grants or successful operation.\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"residuals","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:cfa5cc5df717125ca68075a9625e2003","key":1926,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"consequence\":\"Catalogue entries retain named roles and tasks, while detailed external schemas, checklists, case discriminators, acceptance predicates and task-frame bodies remain unresolved.\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:cfa5cc5df717125ca68075a9625e2003\",\"invalidation\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:invalidation:source-or-interpretation-change\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:residual-kind:authored-uncertainty\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"re_entry\":[],\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"subject\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:f701f72fd1de2cad38030bb4061e3655\",\"uncertainty\":{\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":73,\"path\":\"standards/README.md\",\"quote\":\"The\\nowning members state the method in full. Frame excerpts and guides route\\nattention to those local owners and create no additional authority.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/README.md#STDO%20V3%2FDocuments\",\"start_line\":71}],\"statement\":\"The compact ownership catalogue and task list do not contain the full referenced documents. Aggregating their descriptions loses standalone record granularity, not ownership boundaries.\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"residuals","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:08d2403864c1def8a23ed42e82cf4a5f","key":1927,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"consequence\":\"Use only the stated import inventory, direction, no-loss and no-authority properties; do not invent tuple-component meanings or external authority/result definitions.\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:08d2403864c1def8a23ed42e82cf4a5f\",\"invalidation\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:invalidation:source-or-interpretation-change\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:residual-kind:authored-uncertainty\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"re_entry\":[],\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"subject\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:aa239bec637e6fe48df5a9c006edecbb\",\"uncertainty\":{\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":85,\"path\":\"standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md\",\"quote\":\"under the import rule\\nof [FOUNDATIONS §2](FOUNDATIONS.md#imports-between-members), which states\\nwhat an import is, its direction and loss, and that it transfers no\\nownership and confers no authority.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md#REFERENCE_FRAME%2F1.%20The%20frame%20as%20the%20engagement%20unit%2FImports%20into%20this%20context\",\"start_line\":82}],\"statement\":\"The source names imported objects, tuple, authority kinds, results, activation and qualification but does not supply their full owner definitions.\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"residuals","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:dc81344e0d43414be0ff8b3e1cbfac03","key":1928,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"consequence\":\"The five-family interpretation preserves substantive frame conditions and owner boundaries as concepts/constraints, but does not claim formal derivation, execute functions or materialize every row-to-pillar and row-to-consumer edge. The exact table remains the re-entry source for these details.\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:dc81344e0d43414be0ff8b3e1cbfac03\",\"invalidation\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:invalidation:source-or-interpretation-change\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:residual-kind:authored-uncertainty\",\"own