"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"consequence\":\"Retain the supplied signatures and mappings without implementing the external conjunction, qualification, result reuse or activation laws, or treating names as executable interfaces.\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:137b306920d8c1eaed74f4c1ad9937b8\",\"invalidation\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:invalidation:source-or-interpretation-change\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:residual-kind:authored-uncertainty\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"re_entry\":[],\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"subject\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:9a8783a2b29a0621f74aa70f7d3ee135\",\"uncertainty\":{\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":546,\"path\":\"standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md\",\"quote\":\"`declare` is §4; `activate` and `evaluate` are ACTIVATION §1 and §2;\\n`evaluate` returns its result under RF-012, and the closed result is\\nreturned and reused under ACTIVATION §7; `conjoin` and `translate` are §6;\\n`audit_coverage` is §8, which maps the statuses of its ledger to the core;\\n`revise` is §10. EVALUATION §7 qualifies each.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md#REFERENCE_FRAME%2F5.%20Method%20functions\",\"start_line\":542}],\"statement\":\"REFERENCE_FRAME §4 and RF laws, ACTIVATION §§1–7, FOUNDATIONS core/conjunction and EVALUATION §7 are referenced but not supplied in full. Their complete operational and applicability semantics remain unresolved.\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"residuals","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:2392f6ae07d1ebdfb2c5edf26533e717","key":1932,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"consequence\":\"Translation remains meaningful source data with declaration and refusal requirements; no operational transformation record, preservation proof or licensing judgment is produced.\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:2392f6ae07d1ebdfb2c5edf26533e717\",\"invalidation\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:invalidation:source-or-interpretation-change\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:residual-kind:authored-uncertainty\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"re_entry\":[],\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"subject\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:db181f191ffdbb1a5dac45b0842ab1ad\",\"uncertainty\":{\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":630,\"path\":\"standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md\",\"quote\":\"[ACTIVATION §4, Refinement](ACTIVATION.md#refinement), and where the\\ntranslation is represented in `a_c` it is recorded in the preservation,\\nintroduced, removed and residual fields of\\n[AC-013](AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS.md#ac-013-transformation).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md#REFERENCE_FRAME%2F6.%20Frames%20in%20conjunction%2FEvidence%20or%20coordinate%20translation\",\"start_line\":627}],\"statement\":\"The five active families do not instantiate source-defined AC-013 transformations, and the referenced preservation/refinement law is absent. Its operational fields and proof obligations are described but not discharged.\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"residuals","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:56a436c3f925c81722e19ab4fd278516","key":1933,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"consequence\":\"No prohibition on broad observation or closure verdict is inferred; the exact sentence is retained for re-entry alongside explicit semantic, decision and operation authority requirements.\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:56a436c3f925c81722e19ab4fd278516\",\"invalidation\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:invalidation:source-or-interpretation-change\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:residual-kind:authored-uncertainty\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"re_entry\":[],\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"subject\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:e46a6fbd8f999746bee3fe1acb55a311\",\"uncertainty\":{\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":779,\"path\":\"standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md\",\"quote\":\"A frame set\\nwith broad observational reach, an unresolved decision owner or an\\neffectful path without operation authority is not closed (P6).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md#REFERENCE_FRAME%2F8.%20Workspace%20coverage%2FAuthority%20coverage\",\"start_line\":777}],\"statement\":\"The list's grammar could read broad observational reach itself as a closure defect, or as reach insufficient without resolved authorities. The surrounding requirements support the latter but do not explicitly rewrite the sentence.\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"residuals","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:11a8b880b9a03536f435829c04b78d9c","key":1934,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"consequence\":\"Keep every condition and exclusion/status distinction without inventing a quantifier restriction or declaring full coverage for any subject.\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:11a8b880b9a03536f435829c04b78d9c\",\"invalidation\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:invalidation:source-or-interpretation-change\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:residual-kind:authored-uncertainty\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"re_entry\":[],\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"subject\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:7721e6cd2018dee36a8a3338008b260c\",\"uncertainty\":{\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":815,\"path\":\"standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md\",\"quote\":\"7. excluded evaluations cite their governing authority; and\\n8. uncovered and unknown residuals are explicit and compatible with the\\n   claim.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md#REFERENCE_FRAME%2F8.%20Workspace%20coverage%2FOperational%20full%20coverage\",\"start_line\":813}],\"statement\":\"Item 1 universally requires coverage of known material evaluations, while items 7–8 admit cited exclusions and claim-compatible uncovered/unknown residuals. The exact reconciliation of these scopes is not expressly defined in this excerpt.\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"residuals","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:2d5df7c51655ba103f5f409df9414398","key":1935,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"consequence\":\"Use only the import meanings expressly reported here; do not supply missing effect algebras, adoption hashing, calculus identity requirements, generic acceptance rules or lineage definitions from discovery nodes.\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:2d5df7c51655ba103f5f409df9414398\",\"invalidation\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:invalidation:source-or-interpretation-change\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:residual-kind:authored-uncertainty\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"re_entry\":[],\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"subject\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:47f5a07e664b149bf807f7c0c22cd554\",\"uncertainty\":{\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":30,\"path\":\"standards/RELEASE.md\",\"quote\":\"it defines none of those twice. Git, tag, branch, the `stdo://` URI forms\\nand the Product names of the Specification Stack are this Product's\\nrealisation and toolchain terms. Every clause names the principle that\\nrequires it (P0 to P6, FOUNDATIONS §3).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/RELEASE.md#RELEASE\",\"start_line\":27}],\"statement\":\"RELEASE imports FOUNDATIONS lineage/results, ACTIVATION effects, IDENTITY, EVALUATION claims/acceptance, AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS layers/identity, SPEC_METHOD lineage and PRODUCT_DEFINITION installed-basis/adoption/toolchain law. Most owning text is absent; Product-specific Git/URI terms are not universal calculus requirements.\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"residuals","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:8a769aed52e5cb076ee63993b475facf","key":1936,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"consequence\":\"The consumer list supplies reported directed applications, not independently verified governing edges to absent endpoints. Detailed consumer loci, numerical policy inventories and pillar assignments remain source-linked residual detail.\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:8a769aed52e5cb076ee63993b475facf\",\"invalidation\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:invalidation:source-or-interpretation-change\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:residual-kind:authored-uncertainty\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"re_entry\":[],\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"subject\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:7b19e39be9fd85c952d4163c0c025b77\",\"uncertainty\":{\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":151,\"path\":\"standards/RELEASE.md\",\"quote\":\"Each consumer applies the rule and decides nothing the owning section does\\nnot (P2, P6).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/RELEASE.md#RELEASE%2F1.%20Context%20and%20position%2FFoundation%20to%20law%3A%20release%20and%20successor%20conservation\",\"start_line\":150}],\"statement\":\"F15 reports consumers in SPEC_METHOD, EXECUTIVE_BASELINE, WORLD_MODEL, ODD, IDENTITY, PRODUCT_DEFINITION, ACTIVATION, AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS, FOUNDATIONS, EVALUATION, TICKETS and CONFORMANCE, plus internal release clauses. It explicitly reports no separate consumer for external-dependency and support-line rows, and restricts operation-result consumers to this member; Product Definition maps its manager effects independently. Other reports include mandatory acceptance gates regardless of selected checks; digest-bound adopt versus selector-free sync; complete companion/dependency closure; unresolved successor disposition blocking acceptance; lifecycle, migration, commitment standing, repricing and work-carrier presence not supplying semantic disposition. Those external loci are not available to verify or expand.\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"residuals","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:f7acb7db8b6d2d18c61ee2aa4d8b623c","key":1937,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"consequence\":\"No exact mandatory bundle or automatic version-line threshold is invented; bounded repair may remain on a line only where that line remains applicable.\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:f7acb7db8b6d2d18c61ee2aa4d8b623c\",\"invalidation\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:invalidation:source-or-interpretation-change\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:residual-kind:authored-uncertainty\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"re_entry\":[],\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"subject\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:47f5a07e664b149bf807f7c0c22cd554\",\"uncertainty\":{\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":721,\"path\":\"standards/RELEASE.md\",\"quote\":\"- What exact qualification bundle is mandatory for each Product class?\\n- What version-line compatibility rule requires a new `<version>` rather\\n  than a higher RC ordinal?\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/RELEASE.md#RELEASE%2F10.%20Open%20questions\",\"start_line\":719}],\"statement\":\"The source explicitly leaves undecided each Product class's exact mandatory qualification bundle and the compatibility rule requiring a new version rather than higher RC ordinal.\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"residuals","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:dd73635b5a53a1076c9f4774f208b086","key":1938,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"consequence\":\"Preserve the table's thirteen consequences and policy/owner distinctions as descriptions, without asserting external endpoint contents, executing account mappings, or proving derivations. Canonical statement adds no independent law; §8's step binding remains externally owned.\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:dd73635b5a53a1076c9f4774f208b086\",\"invalidation\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:invalidation:source-or-interpretation-change\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:residual-kind:authored-uncertainty\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"re_entry\":[],\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"subject\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:26a8936b7793bf1681e921b95ed4987b\",\"uncertainty\":{\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":184,\"path\":\"standards/SPEC_METHOD.md\",\"quote\":\"The table accounts for §1 to §3, §6 and §9 to §11. §1 Canonical statement\\ndecides nothing of its own: each clause names its owning section. §8\\nbinds the step of ACTIVATION to this method's terms; its delivery\\npriority is accounted for by family F5 at ACTIVATION §6, and the rest of\\nit by family F2 at ACTIVATION §1, whose paragraph after its table names\\nthe rows §8 applies and the families that trace its statement of the\\nstep's results and its use of the tenant's binding.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/SPEC_METHOD.md#SPEC_METHOD%2F2.%20The%20chain%2FFoundation%20to%20law%3A%20chain%2C%20outcome%20and%20build-tenant%20binding\",\"start_line\":178}],\"statement\":\"F10 reports consumers in ASSURANCE, DESIGN_MODULE, ODD, TICKETS, CONFORMANCE, WRITING_GUIDE, RELEASE, IDENTITY, PRODUCT_DEFINITION, POSTING_GUIDE, ACTIVATION and FOUNDATIONS plus internal method sections. Reports distinguish truth layers, trace every branch/test expectation, deny lifecycle labels admission/compliance/closure, apply inherited requirement status, bind execution as design, preserve present-tense/supersession, confirm lifecycle, deny ticket activity growth admission, keep posting distinct from adoption and execution kind distinct from operation kind. Evidence-closure and three-account mapping rows expressly have no separate consumer; their closure/evidence/refinement laws belong elsewhere. Exact category/status values, ADR defaults, lifecycle phases, progress categories, eight adoption steps, §11 details, discriminator contents, consumer loci and pillar associations are not fully represented or supplied as owning text.\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"residuals","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:64d3e270a4cf0b122627e1daadd41469","key":1939,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"consequence\":\"Retain only the stated sufficiency, reuse and local-span boundaries; no complete reconstruction proof, profile adoption or design-view acceptance is inferred.\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:64d3e270a4cf0b122627e1daadd41469\",\"invalidation\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:invalidation:source-or-interpretation-change\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:residual-kind:authored-uncertainty\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"re_entry\":[],\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"subject\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:f8a1b1b5f801b47764b6f0c9f0a8473d\",\"uncertainty\":{\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":371,\"path\":\"standards/SPEC_METHOD.md\",\"quote\":\"Reconstruction sufficiency depends on ambiguity governance (§5). The\\nhidden-ambiguity limit, reuse of an accepted relation's evidence, what\\nreconstructability requires and grants, and the reconstruction span are\\nstated once at\\n[EVALUATION §6 Layered sufficiency](EVALUATION.md#6-conformance-of-realisations);\\nthis litmus applies them to the method's own chain, where the span of a\\nlocal selected function excludes recreating the whole product. The design\\nprofile owns design-view coverage, its material-change gate and\\nunchanged-boundary reuse; this litmus neither waives that gate nor requires\\nrecreating unchanged accepted views ([DESIGN_MODULE](DESIGN_MODULE.md)).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/SPEC_METHOD.md#SPEC_METHOD%2F2.%20The%20chain%2FReconstruction%20litmus\",\"start_line\":362}],\"statement\":\"EVALUATION §6 and DESIGN_MODULE supply unprovided definitions, profile applicability, coverage, material-change and reuse predicates; P1/P2 foundations are cited but not established here.\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"residuals","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:d44be09f72a5969bd4eab00a712aca0d","key":1940,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"consequence\":\"Declared states remain distinct from evaluation results and successor dispositions; no missing core value or successor predicate is invented.\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:d44be09f72a5969bd4eab00a712aca0d\",\"invalidation\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:invalidation:source-or-interpretation-change\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:residual-kind:authored-uncertainty\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"re_entry\":[],\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"subject\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:2e158804b1db370fa33015718caa8a6f\",\"uncertainty\":{\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":544,\"path\":\"standards/SPEC_METHOD.md\",\"quote\":\"An evaluation that reads them returns its own\\ncore value with its predicate under\\n[FOUNDATIONS §4 Results](FOUNDATIONS.md#results). Purpose and material\\nrelation: a declared state is never combined as an evaluation result, so\\na requirement marked Active, or evidence classed as material advance,\\ncannot stand in for a `satisfied` result, and a requirement marked\\nDeferred or Orphaned cannot stand in for a `falsified` one (P5, P1).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/SPEC_METHOD.md#SPEC_METHOD%2F2.%20The%20chain%2FRequirement%20categories%20and%20classification\",\"start_line\":538},{\"end_line\":554,\"path\":\"standards/SPEC_METHOD.md\",\"quote\":\"Where a project's work is also such a successor, each predecessor claim\\ntakes its RELEASE §9 disposition by that section's predicates, and no\\nlifecycle status or legacy classification supplies or replaces it:\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/SPEC_METHOD.md#SPEC_METHOD%2F2.%20The%20chain%2FRequirement%20categories%20and%20classification\",\"start_line\":552}],\"statement\":\"FOUNDATIONS §4 result algebra and RELEASE §9 dispositions are not supplied. Overlapping words do not resolve these distinct domains.\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"residuals","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:9a79ece18a239dcfa3dac205d2ab7e42","key":1941,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"consequence\":\"The consumer catalogue is retained as source re-entry rather than fabricated local endpoints. Its links add no authority or second decision path, and its reported derivations are not proved by this interpretation.\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:9a79ece18a239dcfa3dac205d2ab7e42\",\"invalidation\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:invalidation:source-or-interpretation-change\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:residual-kind:authored-uncertainty\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"re_entry\":[],\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"subject\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:13bc06c340699b069791c359438dbd42\",\"uncertainty\":{\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":803,\"path\":\"standards/SPEC_METHOD.md\",\"quote\":\"The standing of these consequences is stated in\\n[FOUNDATIONS §3 Foundation to law](FOUNDATIONS.md#foundation-to-law).\\nThe table accounts for §4, §5 and §7.\\n\\nConsumers of these rows, where an actor enters them (FOUNDATIONS §3\\nFoundation to law, Consumers), one list per row, each consumer linked to\\nits own locus:\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/SPEC_METHOD.md#SPEC_METHOD%2F4.%20Change%20management%2FFoundation%20to%20law%3A%20change%20management%20and%20ambiguity\",\"start_line\":797},{\"end_line\":806,\"path\":\"standards/SPEC_METHOD.md\",\"quote\":\"- Row 2, the triangulation: no separate consumer applies. The frames that test a diagnosis are selected under REFERENCE_FRAME §5 and §6, as the choice column states; the four causes a diagnosis distinguishes are [ACTIVATION §1 Construction relation](ACTIVATION.md#construction-relation)'s, Feedback and diagnosis, which names this section as its consumer; and localisation of a counterexample is [ASSURANCE §12](ASSURANCE.md#12-counterexample-localisation)'s, which this section applies.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/SPEC_METHOD.md#SPEC_METHOD%2F4.%20Change%20management%2FFoundation%20to%20law%3A%20change%20management%20and%20ambiguity\",\"start_line\":806}],\"statement\":\"Lines 805–814 explicitly catalogue consumers: local chain/renewal/litmus/trace/outcome/execution/binding/classification/surface/lifecycle/immutability rules; TICKETS §§1,3–7; ACTIVATION §§1,4,7; RELEASE §§1,3; ASSURANCE §§2,12,14; DESIGN_MODULE §§5,10 and post-ticket review; FOUNDATIONS construction/parallel-assurance clauses; ODD §§5,11.5B,11.7A and family table; UX §§1,12 and family table; CONFORMANCE case C-10/discriminator 41; EXECUTIVE_BASELINE §5; and PRODUCT_DEFINITION §8. External rule bodies and linked anchors are absent. Row 2 states no separate consumer; row 5 likewise identifies no additional separate consumer beyond its stated application. Full consumer-level operational interpretation remains unresolved.\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"residuals","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:5058ff1a86b4ff565f9ea88d1c3e2b6d","key":1942,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"consequence\":\"Ordered traversal, delta enumeration, coverage joins and rule treatment are retained descriptively. No actual traversal, computation, core evaluation, repair, retry or continuity decision is represented as performed.\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:5058ff1a86b4ff565f9ea88d1c3e2b6d\",\"invalidation\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:invalidation:source-or-interpretation-change\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:residual-kind:authored-uncertainty\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"re_entry\":[],\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"subject\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:e21989c4cfce457542b5b0140e63807c\",\"uncertainty\":{\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":934,\"path\":\"standards/SPEC_METHOD.md\",\"quote\":\"The computed result exposes four things, in this order:\\n\\n1. Authority traversal. Follow the explicit source, ownership, dependency,\\n   composition and projection declarations from the affected targets and\\n   effects. Identify each reached layer and owner, its exact basis and its\\n   changed, unchanged or unknown relation, the traversed edges and the\\n   unresolved frontier. Include root, authority and grant changes even when\\n   public bytes are equal. An absent edge does not prove irrelevance;\\n   undeclared or semantically uncertain materiality remains J.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/SPEC_METHOD.md#SPEC_METHOD%2F4.%20Change%20management%2FComputed%20classification%20and%20treatment\",\"start_line\":926},{\"end_line\":1008,\"path\":\"standards/SPEC_METHOD.md\",\"quote\":\"[TICKETS §7](TICKETS.md#recorded-judgment-and-owner-ruling-continuity) owns\\nthe existing carrier and the recorded J and O continuity rules.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/SPEC_METHOD.md#SPEC_METHOD%2F4.%20Change%20management%2FComputed%20classification%20and%20treatment\",\"start_line\":1007}],\"statement\":\"The five active families cannot encode executable traversal/frontier state, complete serialised deltas, effect reconciliation or C/J/O continuity proofs. ACTIVATION §§3,5,7, FOUNDATIONS result algebra and TICKETS §7 remain external dependencies.\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"residuals","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:1d88ae1caff5c37b0a3ded23445b91d1","key":1943,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"consequence\":\"Known closure blockers remain explicit; satisfying their negations is not asserted sufficient for closure without the owning rule.\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:1d88ae1caff5c37b0a3ded23445b91d1\",\"invalidation\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:invalidation:source-or-interpretation-change\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:residual-kind:authored-uncertainty\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"re_entry\":[],\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"subject\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:ab6da5130acf85f9459ce4914e1db565\",\"uncertainty\":{\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1024,\"path\":\"standards/SPEC_METHOD.md\",\"quote\":\"The gate closes only under the closure condition that\\n[TICKETS §7 Condition-based closure and reuse](TICKETS.md#condition-based-closure-and-reuse)\\nowns, applied here with the obligations declared for the change span as\\nits required coverage.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/SPEC_METHOD.md#SPEC_METHOD%2F4.%20Change%20management%2FConsistency%20gate\",\"start_line\":1021}],\"statement\":\"TICKETS §7 conjunction/closure, ACTIVATION §7 reuse, EVALUATION §5 acceptance and ASSURANCE/TICKETS test authority are referenced but not supplied in full.\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"residuals","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:a0135d732d1a3b7b2c986891dfb9ba7a","key":1944,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"consequence\":\"Only the explicit resolved-to-satisfied mapping is retained; other outcomes are not collapsed into false. The person's policy-governed role is preserved without silently rewriting the source's non-human definition.\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:a0135d732d1a3b7b2c986891dfb9ba7a\",\"invalidation\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:invalidation:source-or-interpretation-change\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:residual-kind:authored-uncertainty\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"re_entry\":[],\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"subject\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:286649052d4f3d74e1c0094c628bac34\",\"uncertainty\":{\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1205,\"path\":\"standards/SPEC_METHOD.md\",\"quote\":\"Those outcomes are `resolved`,\\n`carried`, `escalated` and `blocked` of\\n[ACTIVATION §3 Ambiguity outcome](ACTIVATION.md#ambiguity-outcome), which\\ngives each its core value for the predicate \\\"the declared ambiguity is\\nresolved on the exact basis\\\". Only `resolved` is `satisfied`, so a later\\nboundary rests no dependent claim on an ambiguity that is carried,\\nescalated or blocked as if it were resolved.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/SPEC_METHOD.md#SPEC_METHOD%2F5.%20Ambiguity%20governance%20and%20lifecycle\",\"start_line\":1199},{\"end_line\":1219,\"path\":\"standards/SPEC_METHOD.md\",\"quote\":\"a person who carries or decides a\\ndeclared ambiguity where policy permits it, without that admission, acts\\nunder the policy and recording that govern lawful probabilistic\\nprocessing;\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/SPEC_METHOD.md#SPEC_METHOD%2F5.%20Ambiguity%20governance%20and%20lifecycle\",\"start_line\":1216}],\"statement\":\"ACTIVATION §3 mappings and §4 hard stops are absent. There is a terminology tension between defining lawful probabilistic processing as non-human and applying its policy/recording to human decisions lacking adjudication admission; the text specifies common governance without fully resolving category membership.\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"residuals","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:6a8cb125ea6995c05457f68db401c309","key":1945,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"consequence\":\"Named lineage roles and explicit identity separations are retained without inventing object definitions or release procedures.\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:6a8cb125ea6995c05457f68db401c309\",\"invalidation\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:invalidation:source-or-interpretation-change\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:residual-kind:authored-uncertainty\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"re_entry\":[],\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"subject\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:691f85265c6da81d5a46b1d99e177c71\",\"uncertainty\":{\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1247,\"path\":\"standards/SPEC_METHOD.md\",\"quote\":\"The roles are distinct objects with distinct identities,\\nsubstrate, development product, source project, release cut, product,\\ninstall, artifact and product definition, defined once in FOUNDATIONS §2\\n(product lineage objects) with their governing rules and the compiler\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/SPEC_METHOD.md#SPEC_METHOD%2F6.%20Lineage%20and%20release\",\"start_line\":1244}],\"statement\":\"FOUNDATIONS §2 lineage definitions, RELEASE §§2–9 publication/selection/successor rules, PRODUCT_DEFINITION §11 version boundary and AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS AC-020 are external. The subject's calculus reference does not amend the workflow's selected calculus basis.\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"residuals","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:18165b7a8d37152d5d7049969fd0559c","key":1946,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"consequence\":\"The bounded step, result distinctions, configuration and priority limits remain descriptions. No step admission, effect, accepted checkpoint, scheduling runtime or conformance result is inferred.\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:18165b7a8d37152d5d7049969fd0559c\",\"invalidation\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:invalidation:source-or-interpretation-change\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:residual-kind:authored-uncertainty\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"re_entry\":[],\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"subject\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:730ea09d59cbd3d5c5d2f2393282f546\",\"uncertainty\":{\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1636,\"path\":\"standards/SPEC_METHOD.md\",\"quote\":\"The\\nconstruction relation that the step serves, from the bound current state\\nto the destination through a selected strategy, feedback and the distinct\\nclaims of preservation, progress and completion, is\\n[ACTIVATION §1 Construction relation](ACTIVATION.md#construction-relation);\\nthis member applies it to delivery and correction (§4) and states no\\nsecond relation (P6).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/SPEC_METHOD.md#SPEC_METHOD%2F8.%20Bounded%20execution%20in%20this%20method\",\"start_line\":1630}],\"statement\":\"ACTIVATION's execution/construction, admission, results, effects, work envelopes, qualification, proportionality, configuration and reuse require unavailable definitions. FOUNDATIONS quantified assurance and EXECUTIVE_BASELINE steel-thread/executive-profile law are likewise unresolved. Operational transition/proof detail exceeds the active families.\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"residuals","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:b5456d120d8cabbd5b9ca2b3e62f8442","key":1947,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"consequence\":\"The local evidence list is preserved without claiming proof adequacy, qualified method or completed closure.\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:b5456d120d8cabbd5b9ca2b3e62f8442\",\"invalidation\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:invalidation:source-or-interpretation-change\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:residual-kind:authored-uncertainty\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"re_entry\":[],\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"subject\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:e9e4bace23b4c2d17586434a8f7540df\",\"uncertainty\":{\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1698,\"path\":\"standards/SPEC_METHOD.md\",\"quote\":\"The rules that govern how constitutional claims are proved in practice are\\ntier-1 law: proof target identity and adequacy (EVALUATION §1); semantic,\\nevidence and projection separation (EVALUATION §2); assurance-boundary\\ncongruence and method qualification (EVALUATION §1, §3, §6 and §7).\\nVerification layers, the testing strategy taxonomy with fixture and proof\\nportability, test authority, scenario bundles, installed development proof\\nand significant path coverage are ASSURANCE §1 to §6 (P6).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/SPEC_METHOD.md#SPEC_METHOD%2F9.%20Evidence\",\"start_line\":1692}],\"statement\":\"EVALUATION's proof/qualification law, ASSURANCE's testing law and TICKETS §7 closure are named dependencies whose full meanings cannot be reconstructed from the supplied references.\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"residuals","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:071410b2775e0c239bbfaa67441e50e7","key":1948,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"consequence\":\"Binding laws, explicit counterexample outcomes and permissible environments are retained. No concrete tenant, executable calculus, transformation proof, actor authority or conformance acceptance is instantiated.\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:071410b2775e0c239bbfaa67441e50e7\",\"invalidation\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:invalidation:source-or-interpretation-change\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:residual-kind:authored-uncertainty\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"re_entry\":[],\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"subject\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:152d2a8a64bd069bdea1135af24a3c80\",\"uncertainty\":{\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1894,\"path\":\"standards/SPEC_METHOD.md\",\"quote\":\"6. Representation. A representation of the requirements calculus or of a\\n   binding in a_c, the axiomatic calculus of\\n   [AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS](AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS.md), prescribes no executor and\\n   does not establish execution conformance by structural validation alone\\n   ([AC-018](AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS.md#ac-018-structural-and-semantic-separation)).\\n   An a_c model of a human process that passes structural validation\\n   neither selects an automated executor nor shows that the process meets\\n   its requirements; execution conformance needs its own evidence under\\n   rule 4 (P1, P6).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/SPEC_METHOD.md#SPEC_METHOD%2F11.%20Build-tenant%20binding\",\"start_line\":1886},{\"end_line\":1908,\"path\":\"standards/SPEC_METHOD.md\",\"quote\":\"A mapping from one account to\\n   another is a transformation: what it preserves, the law that licenses\\n   it, and whether it is exact or approximate with its adequacy relation\\n   and end-to-end bound, are stated and discharged under\\n   [ACTIVATION §4 Refinement](ACTIVATION.md#refinement), and where it is\\n   recorded in a_c its record is\\n   [AC-013](AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS.md#ac-013-transformation). The binding adds\\n   only which accounts the mapping joins and the evidence, in its\\n   execution environment, that discharges the preservation\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/SPEC_METHOD.md#SPEC_METHOD%2F11.%20Build-tenant%20binding\",\"start_line\":1900}],\"statement\":\"The full computational/result algebra, construction accounts, identity/independence definitions, effect and resource protocols, EVALUATION conformance/equivalence ladder, refinement proof, AC-013/AC-018, product registry/local axioms and TICKETS tenant-review rules are external. This finite schema retains mappings and obligations descriptively, without executable transformations or full proof objects.\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"residuals","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:96d9941490225a72df95aab37adee3e2","key":1949,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"consequence\":\"TICKETS ownership is represented without treating the overview or discovery nodes as the missing operational rules.\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:96d9941490225a72df95aab37adee3e2\",\"invalidation\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:invalidation:source-or-interpretation-change\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:residual-kind:authored-uncertainty\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"re_entry\":[],\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"subject\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:89a8456fc34b22ab5de4993cf6bc5b8a\",\"uncertainty\":{\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":25,\"path\":\"standards/TICKETS.md\",\"quote\":\"the step side of admission is\\n[ACTIVATION §1](ACTIVATION.md#admission); the generic law of claims,\\nindependent assessment and acceptance is EVALUATION §1, §3 and §5; the\\ntesting law is ASSURANCE. This member defines none of those twice. Its\\nfamily table (F13) opens §5.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/TICKETS.md#TICKETS\",\"start_line\":21}],\"statement\":\"Only the overview and initial carrier sections are supplied. Execution contracts, layout authority, detailed sprint/ticket rules, admission, continuity, closure, tests, migration review, one-truth projection, operating mode and F13 are named but their bodies are absent; their discovery nodes do not supply semantics.\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"residuals","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:c64a7878dc07b9cfe6052610f1ac7dd0","key":1950,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"consequence\":\"Comments remain non-authoritative carriers until adoption at their decision-owning surface; no ratification procedure or discussion-state domain is invented.\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:c64a7878dc07b9cfe6052610f1ac7dd0\",\"invalidation\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:invalidation:source-or-interpretation-change\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:residual-kind:authored-uncertainty\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"re_entry\":[],\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"subject\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:fd968916f08ade55608ac7b3f7f0511e\",\"uncertainty\":{\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":74,\"path\":\"standards/TICKETS.md\",\"quote\":\"A comment\\nis a post of [POSTING_GUIDE](POSTING_GUIDE.md), which states what it\\ncarries, its structure and its discussion state. A decision recorded in a\\ncomment takes its authority from the surface that owns the decision, once\\nit is adopted there ([POSTING_GUIDE §9](POSTING_GUIDE.md#9-ratification)),\\nand has none of its own (P6, P3).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/TICKETS.md#TICKETS%2F1.%20Work%20carriers%2FComments\",\"start_line\":69}],\"statement\":\"POSTING_GUIDE's content, structure, discussion-state and §9 ratification rules are not supplied.\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"residuals","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:819a7ab4c64fe06c95d600f344682321","key":1951,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"consequence\":\"Retain cited owners and consumer roles without reconstructing their laws or assigning graph-discovered authority. Exact application needs source re-entry at those owners.\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:819a7ab4c64fe06c95d600f344682321\",\"invalidation\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:invalidation:source-or-interpretation-change\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:residual-kind:authored-uncertainty\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"re_entry\":[],\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"subject\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:2d06b1088727674c5114bbd1b8f6a018\",\"uncertainty\":{\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":614,\"path\":\"standards/TICKETS.md\",\"quote\":\"Consumers of these rows, where an actor enters them\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/TICKETS.md#TICKETS%2F5.%20From%20carrier%20to%20execution%2FFoundation%20to%20law%3A%20work%20carriers\",\"start_line\":600}],\"statement\":\"The table's linked consumers/owners are not supplied in full. Routes include SPEC_METHOD carrier selection/change classes/sprint boundary/computed classification/consistency/evidence/build tenancy; PRODUCT_DEFINITION binding, tenant registry, semantic resolution and bootstrap; ACTIVATION admission/reuse/acquisition; ODD manual-walkthrough admission; CONFORMANCE discriminators 41 and 48; UX escrow/results/family table; DESIGN_MODULE recurrence; EVALUATION independence/acceptance; EXECUTIVE_BASELINE reviewer/evaluation/independence/closure; ASSURANCE test authority; and POSTING_GUIDE boundary/discussion/ratification. Internal recommended-shape, judgment, status, triage, recurrence, milestone and closure consumers are described but not operationally traversed. Term binding and carrier-shape/bounded-reading rows expressly have no separate external consumer.\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"residuals","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:ccbbaa344637c84b5fb036d09cd46f58","key":1952,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"consequence\":\"Carrier selection and persistence requirements are retained, but no admission result, execution authorization or evidence sufficiency is inferred.\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:ccbbaa344637c84b5fb036d09cd46f58\",\"invalidation\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:invalidation:source-or-interpretation-change\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:residual-kind:authored-uncertainty\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"re_entry\":[],\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"subject\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:c62d0418d5bdea87e8d7991cdf46a27e\",\"uncertainty\":{\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":662,\"path\":\"standards/TICKETS.md\",\"quote\":\"the coordinates an admitted result carries,\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/TICKETS.md#TICKETS%2F5.%20From%20carrier%20to%20execution%2FCarrier%20selection\",\"start_line\":654}],\"statement\":\"ACTIVATION §1 owns exact coordinates, admission-start conditions, self-certification refusal, result recording and no-durable-surface refusal; the supplied text refers to these without their full schema or procedure.\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"residuals","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:1772fa7f06fffd1e613e3d7470e87796","key":1953,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"consequence\":\"Intermediate acceptance, continuing cleanup and further growth remain distinct; no slice acceptance or growth permission is manufactured.\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:1772fa7f06fffd1e613e3d7470e87796\",\"invalidation\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:invalidation:source-or-interpretation-change\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:residual-kind:authored-uncertainty\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"re_entry\":[],\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"subject\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:098aaa4c8239a4529a21958cf3a07793\",\"uncertainty\":{\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":828,\"path\":\"standards/TICKETS.md\",\"quote\":\"may continue within the bound SPEC_METHOD §7 states,\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/TICKETS.md#TICKETS%2F6.%20Implementation%20migration%2FClosure%20of%20a%20migration%20ticket\",\"start_line\":826}],\"statement\":\"SPEC_METHOD §7's path-relative slice identity, acceptance criteria, cleanup bounds and compatibility law, and §3's renewed-growth admission, are not supplied. Strategy classification definitions and DESIGN_MODULE candidate refinements also remain reference dependencies.\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"residuals","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:928d6272013e103fa46c70a33b0a136d","key":1954,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"consequence\":\"The five-family representation describes judgment records, reuse/invalidation and result mappings but performs no evaluation, ownership decision, successor construction or authority effect.\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:928d6272013e103fa46c70a33b0a136d\",\"invalidation\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:invalidation:source-or-interpretation-change\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:residual-kind:authored-uncertainty\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"re_entry\":[],\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"subject\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:2306f4e60feb709f5c67ca75a73c1690\",\"uncertainty\":{\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1174,\"path\":\"standards/TICKETS.md\",\"quote\":\"the\\nstate changes only through the owner's authorised act.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/TICKETS.md#TICKETS%2F7.%20Authority%2C%20judgment%2C%20closure%20and%20state%2FRecorded%20judgment%20and%20owner-ruling%20continuity\",\"start_line\":1173}],\"statement\":\"Source-defined judgments and acts have operational identity, applicability and evidence semantics that are not instantiated by this finite author schema. Full reuse, independence and C/J/O annotations require the referenced external sections.\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"residuals","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:cd9d2732ff3613b9f2cf4dad307faa7e","key":1955,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"consequence\":\"The source examples remain re-entry material for exact artifact reconstruction. Their ids, timestamps, links and unchecked boxes confer no admission, truth, completed work or instantiated Product.\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:cd9d2732ff3613b9f2cf4dad307faa7e\",\"invalidation\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:invalidation:source-or-interpretation-change\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:residual-kind:authored-uncertainty\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"re_entry\":[],\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"subject\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:ce6b4d3f0699e02cd1c718d0569a04d0\",\"uncertainty\":{\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1281,\"path\":\"standards/TICKETS.md\",\"quote\":\"These shapes are the recommended carriers\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/TICKETS.md#TICKETS%2F8.%20Recommended%20shapes\",\"start_line\":1279}],\"statement\":\"The compact records preserve template roles, example intent, scoped exclusions, closure policy and checklist meaning rather than reproducing every timestamp, placeholder link, function name and Markdown formatting token. The examples are not declared exhaustive serialization schemas.\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"residuals","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:14960db729ef75f8e2b40c858171be92","key":1956,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"consequence\":\"Treat imports and profile-local names as references only; do not equate the subject's imported calculus with the workflow-selected published basis or infer operational authority.\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:14960db729ef75f8e2b40c858171be92\",\"invalidation\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:invalidation:source-or-interpretation-change\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:residual-kind:authored-uncertainty\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"re_entry\":[],\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"subject\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:75612f6702a23f4a631eb371f4aa0a2d\",\"uncertainty\":{\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":17,\"path\":\"standards/TRAVERSAL_OCCURRENCE.md\",\"quote\":\"imports [AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS](AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS.md) by reference\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/TRAVERSAL_OCCURRENCE.md#TRAVERSAL_OCCURRENCE\",\"start_line\":5}],\"statement\":\"PROFILES §1; AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS signature/RecordKind_ac/Population_M, typed records, AC-003, F_D/F_P/F_H, AC-0