sidual and no-further-effect boundary.\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:3002c7640357f891cf3da0d8ffa3abee\",\"invalidation\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:invalidation:source-or-interpretation-change\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:residual-kind:authored-uncertainty\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"re_entry\":[],\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"subject\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:3ca062201e6a5ccdee3b35eaf3990229\",\"uncertainty\":{\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1344,\"path\":\"standards/TRAVERSAL_OCCURRENCE.md\",\"quote\":\"- `partial_effect` binds one dispatched invocation, a bounded\\n  post-observation, bounded evidence, the `partial_effect` residual and\\n  stop, and explicit re-entry before any further effect;\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/TRAVERSAL_OCCURRENCE.md#TRAVERSAL_OCCURRENCE%2FMutable-subject%20effect%20relation\",\"start_line\":1342},{\"end_line\":972,\"path\":\"standards/TRAVERSAL_OCCURRENCE.md\",\"quote\":\"the bounded post-observation that the\\n  [effect law](#mutable-subject-effect-relation) requires is not yet\\n  acquired\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/TRAVERSAL_OCCURRENCE.md#TRAVERSAL_OCCURRENCE%2FClosed%20constraint%2C%20judgment%2C%20residual%20and%20stop%20kinds\",\"start_line\":970}],\"statement\":\"The source requires a bounded post-observation in partial-effect dispositions while describing undecided partial effects before that observation is acquired. It does not fully specify the intermediate record/admission stage in these sections.\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a