on:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"residuals","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:c2ec0865664863227c927e26a934a980","key":1964,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"consequence\":\"Keep no-dispatch and re-observation requirements, but do not collapse stale, hold, refusal and invalid_basis into one outcome or invent an extra refusal mapping.\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:c2ec0865664863227c927e26a934a980\",\"invalidation\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:invalidation:source-or-interpretation-change\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:residual-kind:authored-uncertainty\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"re_entry\":[],\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"subject\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:cab2df421b136e58a2959f119f2aac4b\",\"uncertainty\":{\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":1658,\"path\":\"standards/TRAVERSAL_OCCURRENCE.md\",\"quote\":\"16. refusal on a stale pre-effect observation and on grant currentness;\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/TRAVERSAL_OCCURRENCE.md#TRAVERSAL_OCCURRENCE%2FConformance%20obligations\",\"start_line\":1658},{\"end_line\":818,\"path\":\"standards/TRAVERSAL_OCCURRENCE.md\",\"quote\":\"| `pre_effect_current` | `EffectSubject` | `effect_readiness` | `stale` plus `hold` and `stale_currentness` | `hold` plus `stale_currentness` |\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/TRAVERSAL_OCCURRENCE.md#TRAVERSAL_OCCURRENCE%2FClosed%20constraint%2C%20judgment%2C%20residual%20and%20stop%20kinds\",\"start_line\":818}],\"statement\":\"The review checklist says refusal on stale currentness; the exact predicate table says stale plus hold and stale_currentness. 'Refusal' may be broader no-start language there, but that reading is not silently imposed.\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"residuals","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:e35a5b24e8b8d558ee3002917244b2ba","key":1965,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"consequence\":\"Retain named roles and explicit bindings only. Do not fabricate unseen replay/result refinements, exemption records, escrow inventories, carrier semantics or cross-file graph endpoints.\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:e35a5b24e8b8d558ee3002917244b2ba\",\"invalidation\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:invalidation:source-or-interpretation-change\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:residual-kind:authored-uncertainty\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"re_entry\":[],\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"subject\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:5364ed6b537f501c3e9da24b34e62cd8\",\"uncertainty\":{\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":44,\"path\":\"standards/UX.md\",\"quote\":\"the refined result values of §15.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/UX.md#UX\",\"start_line\":27}],\"statement\":\"UX §11–§15, core result algebra, ambiguity governance, Product adoption, graph-execution carriers and much of the upstream law are referenced but not supplied.\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"residuals","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:3df5bc0ae93f7a2968cfb897d48c9b0e","key":1966,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"consequence\":\"Preserve stated owner, standing, consequence and consumer direction while leaving missing enumerations and derivations open to source re-entry.\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:3df5bc0ae93f7a2968cfb897d48c9b0e\",\"invalidation\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:invalidation:source-or-interpretation-change\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:residual-kind:authored-uncertainty\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"re_entry\":[],\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"subject\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:efa832cfabb5bfc3cc21ed6c8f386c61\",\"uncertainty\":{\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":141,\"path\":\"standards/UX.md\",\"quote\":\"which are choices of this profile, the product or the\\nproject, with their owners, so no choice is presented as derived\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/UX.md#UX%2F1.%20Position%2FFoundation%20to%20law\",\"start_line\":137}],\"statement\":\"The table refers to five accessibility declarations, five default-governance conditions, escrowable/non-escrowable items, close triggers, six close classifications and four result refinements without supplying their complete inventories. Foundation principle definitions and consequence standing are imported.\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"residuals","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:f007e4ecc4fc9d57d844d621d6b8a797","key":1967,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"consequence\":\"Retain both tests and the expressly stated stricter fail-closed policy; do not certify compliance or silently equate the scopes. Governing-authority ambiguity remains.\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:f007e4ecc4fc9d57d844d621d6b8a797\",\"invalidation\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:invalidation:source-or-interpretation-change\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:residual-kind:authored-uncertainty\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"re_entry\":[],\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"subject\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:64a5a63086d9bef75b170a8d0c4c5208\",\"uncertainty\":{\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":273,\"path\":\"standards/UX.md\",\"quote\":\"This\\ntest differs from the test of §4 Realisation discretion;\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/UX.md#UX%2F4.%20Process%20model%2FProcess%20model%20without%20stack%20mandate\",\"start_line\":270},{\"end_line\":318,\"path\":\"standards/UX.md\",\"quote\":\"This test differs from the test of §4 Process model without stack\\nmandate;\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/UX.md#UX%2F4.%20Process%20model%2FRealisation%20discretion\",\"start_line\":314}],\"statement\":\"§4–§8 preservation and §4–§10 inspection with no §13 failure pattern are expressly different tests; full deciding §15 and failure inventory §13 are outside this source.\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"residuals","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:715076004740c027e9cf8bd8445893e3","key":1968,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"consequence\":\"Retain non-optional public accessibility, the explicit internal-debug exception and later recorded-exemption language without inventing the authority or full permissible scope of a public exemption.\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:715076004740c027e9cf8bd8445893e3\",\"invalidation\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:invalidation:source-or-interpretation-change\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:residual-kind:authored-uncertainty\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"re_entry\":[],\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"subject\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:77b14a2cd014d3c961415d7c5150f1bc\",\"uncertainty\":{\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":563,\"path\":\"standards/UX.md\",\"quote\":\"Accessibility is not optional for product capabilities. It is optional\\nfor internal-only debug surfaces, and the design module records the\\nexemption (P2, P6).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/UX.md#UX%2F11.%20Accessibility%20minimum\",\"start_line\":561},{\"end_line\":683,\"path\":\"standards/UX.md\",\"quote\":\"Closure under this profile for a product UX surface still requires the\\n§8 Msg-replay proof and the §11 accessibility obligations unless an\\nexplicit exemption is recorded. The sprint can defer those obligations\\nduring iteration; it cannot erase them (P4b, P6).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/UX.md#UX%2F12.%20Adoption%2FUX%20sprint%20compliance%20escrow\",\"start_line\":680}],\"statement\":\"§11 calls accessibility non-optional for product capabilities while §12 and result/failure clauses recognise recorded exemptions. Their complete reconciliation is not supplied.\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"residuals","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:8fb205e73dedb4631bad2a2828619fc2","key":1969,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"consequence\":\"The local result predicates and stricter-test choice are recorded, but exact replay exclusions, carrier admission mechanics, adoption authority and external construction mappings cannot be reconstructed.\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:8fb205e73dedb4631bad2a2828619fc2\",\"invalidation\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:invalidation:source-or-interpretation-change\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:residual-kind:authored-uncertainty\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"re_entry\":[],\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"subject\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:0248d4f244332b39c63670566a866da5\",\"uncertainty\":{\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":781,\"path\":\"standards/UX.md\",\"quote\":\"The first part is the stricter of the two compliance tests of §4, which disagree: §4 Process model without stack mandate counts a realisation that preserves §4 to §8 as compliant. The tests differ in scope; this mapping applies the stricter under the fail-closed rule of §1 Authority and retains the ambiguity for the governing authority.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/UX.md#UX%2F15.%20Results%20of%20this%20profile\",\"start_line\":781},{\"end_line\":784,\"path\":\"standards/UX.md\",\"quote\":\"and no dependency that §8 lists decides its correctness; reproducing an unresolved outcome proves replay only and does not establish external completion\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/UX.md#UX%2F15.%20Results%20of%20this%20profile\",\"start_line\":784}],\"statement\":\"UX §§1–10 and referenced FOUNDATIONS, ACTIVATION, DESIGN_MODULE, SPEC_METHOD and TICKETS rules are outside this source set.\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"residuals","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:2d75603f61e3dfc65b320a3d2de1dd3a","key":1970,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"consequence\":\"Preserve authored premise provenance and local consumer claims without treating unavailable family definitions as proved or materialising external graph endpoints. Profile-specific terms remain distinct from similarly spelled calculus records.\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:2d75603f61e3dfc65b320a3d2de1dd3a\",\"invalidation\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:invalidation:source-or-interpretation-change\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:residual-kind:authored-uncertainty\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"re_entry\":[],\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"subject\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:f9e16443b131c7de4e5d87a243cf2ab1\",\"uncertainty\":{\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":149,\"path\":\"standards/WORLD_MODEL.md\",\"quote\":\"The family imports\\nfive families under [PROFILES §1](PROFILES.md#1-the-boundary): F2,\\ntransitions, steps and configuration, for refinement\\n([ACTIVATION §4](ACTIVATION.md#4-totality-and-refinement)); F3,\\nresults and their combination\\n([FOUNDATIONS §4 Results](FOUNDATIONS.md#results)); F8, identity\\n([IDENTITY §1](IDENTITY.md#1-position)); F9, the `a_c` calculus\\n([AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS §1](AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS.md#1-position)); and F12,\\nbinding a project to the method\\n([PRODUCT_DEFINITION §1](PRODUCT_DEFINITION.md#1-overlay-and-layout-independence)). This\\nprofile's ledgers, cuts, overlays, treatments and projections are its own\\nconcepts and are not the calculus's records of similar name by spelling.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/WORLD_MODEL.md#WORLD_MODEL%2F1.%20Position%2FFoundation%20to%20law\",\"start_line\":138}],\"statement\":\"Imported family laws, principle standing, relation carriers, reuse rules and external consumer clauses are cited rather than supplied. The foundation table's pillar numbers are source indexing metadata, not separately modelled logical dependencies.\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"residuals","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:2fa771b785a2ed38806ef14ec3afe9c3","key":1971,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"consequence\":\"Retain the gate predicate and exact-subject/basis requirement without choosing a statistical estimator, intervention protocol, significance threshold or evidence-acceptance rule.\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:2fa771b785a2ed38806ef14ec3afe9c3\",\"invalidation\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:invalidation:source-or-interpretation-change\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:residual-kind:authored-uncertainty\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"re_entry\":[],\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"subject\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:2b74994fce881b68856a041e89a6676e\",\"uncertainty\":{\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":469,\"path\":\"standards/WORLD_MODEL.md\",\"quote\":\"The experimental result that would promote the construct\\nfrom candidate to established is a direction-native\\nconditional-independence test: given the identity projection, residual\\nvariation along remaining components should be independent of the target\\nunder plausible treatments. Candidate standing persists without a\\nresult that meets this predicate on the claimed subject and basis.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/WORLD_MODEL.md#WORLD_MODEL%2F4.%20The%20Markov-object%20construct%2FEpistemic%20status\",\"start_line\":464}],\"statement\":\"The formal statistical condition is described, but a reproducible test implementation and acceptance thresholds are not specified.\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"residuals","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:96192281e86b26fc0798f301e9c11e86","key":1972,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"consequence\":\"The staged flow, provenance and optionality are descriptive concepts/constraints. No executable state machine, transformation, traversal, assessment run or accepted artifact is created.\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:96192281e86b26fc0798f301e9c11e86\",\"invalidation\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:invalidation:source-or-interpretation-change\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:residual-kind:authored-uncertainty\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"re_entry\":[],\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"subject\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:d346a1dbfeb78b1415d50ab61ce48315\",\"uncertainty\":{\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":618,\"path\":\"standards/WORLD_MODEL.md\",\"quote\":\"The profile proceeds through these stages (P4b, P6):\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/WORLD_MODEL.md#WORLD_MODEL%2F7.%20Flow\",\"start_line\":618}],\"statement\":\"The five active families preserve procedural meaning but do not encode operational scheduling, executable transitions, compilation implementations or proof objects.\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"residuals","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:3658bca5099b6abf13a9b21a3a7c7a24","key":1973,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"consequence\":\"Keep the exact ≥ N of N expression; do not invent an adjustable proportion or numerical stability threshold.\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:3658bca5099b6abf13a9b21a3a7c7a24\",\"invalidation\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:invalidation:source-or-interpretation-change\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:residual-kind:authored-uncertainty\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"re_entry\":[],\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"subject\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:e85d3edb1af4830dfe36055a1b108efa\",\"uncertainty\":{\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":908,\"path\":\"standards/WORLD_MODEL.md\",\"quote\":\"For candidates that appear in multiple contexts, decompose the attribute\\nevidence into an invariant core, the attributes whose contribution to the\\nidentity direction is stable across ≥ N of N contexts, and a context\\ncoat, the attributes selected by the specific context, carrying\\ncontextual reinterpretation rather than identity per se (P3).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/WORLD_MODEL.md#WORLD_MODEL%2F10.%20Markov-object%20overlay%20construction%2FCore%20and%20coat%20decomposition\",\"start_line\":904}],\"statement\":\"N and the operational meaning of stable contribution are not defined here; literally the expression spans all N counted contexts.\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"residuals","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:96794a30fa88f491753469f6bd9b133e","key":1974,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"consequence\":\"Retain the guide's practical recommendations and attributed rules without importing absent layer constitution, release semantics or commentary authority.\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:96794a30fa88f491753469f6bd9b133e\",\"invalidation\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:invalidation:source-or-interpretation-change\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:residual-kind:authored-uncertainty\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"re_entry\":[],\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"subject\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:07fe88a2a6a0523330a19d0977d0c575\",\"uncertainty\":{\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":11,\"path\":\"standards/WRITING_GUIDE.md\",\"quote\":\"Consumes [SPEC_METHOD §2](SPEC_METHOD.md#2-the-chain)\\n(the chain, its layers and the specification surface rule) and\\n[§6](SPEC_METHOD.md#6-lineage-and-release) (the release version boundary),\\nand [POSTING_GUIDE](POSTING_GUIDE.md) (the commentary layer); defines none\\nof them.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/WRITING_GUIDE.md#WRITING_GUIDE\",\"start_line\":7}],\"statement\":\"SPEC_METHOD §§2/6 and POSTING_GUIDE are external references with no supplied full text.\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"residuals","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:863b4bbbda1cc74ae861df95cac68a2b","key":1975,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"consequence\":\"Do not infer semantic correctness or installed qualification from schema conformity. Additional checks would be needed for actual bytes/Git references, count equality, unique member paths, sorting, digest computation and coordinate agreement.\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:863b4bbbda1cc74ae861df95cac68a2b\",\"invalidation\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:invalidation:source-or-interpretation-change\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:residual-kind:authored-uncertainty\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author\",\"re_entry\":[],\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"],\"subject\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:d4026128310a589d335a770c7ceb2679\",\"uncertainty\":{\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":5,\"path\":\"standards/schemas/installed-release-manifest.schema.json\",\"quote\":\"  \\\"description\\\": \\\"Deterministic identity and exact installed-member inventory for one immutable STDO RC cut.\\\",\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/schemas/installed-release-manifest.schema.json#preamble\",\"start_line\":5},{\"end_line\":240,\"path\":\"standards/schemas/installed-release-manifest.schema.json\",\"quote\":\"        \\\"member_count\\\": {\\n          \\\"type\\\": \\\"integer\\\",\\n          \\\"minimum\\\": 0\\n        },\\n        \\\"member_set_sha256\\\": {\\n          \\\"$ref\\\": \\\"#/$defs/sha256\\\"\\n        },\\n        \\\"members\\\": {\\n          \\\"type\\\": \\\"array\\\",\\n          \\\"items\\\": {\\n            \\\"$ref\\\": \\\"#/$defs/member\\\"\\n          },\\n          \\\"uniqueItems\\\": true\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/schemas/installed-release-manifest.schema.json#preamble\",\"start_line\":228}],\"statement\":\"The description promises exact inventory, but the schema expresses structural syntax rather than content verification, cross-field equalities or a digest algorithm. No manifest instance or external validation procedure is supplied.\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal","family":"residuals","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:f2abcd9b735cc126b1d826d543f6e063","key":1976,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:basis\",\"consequence\":\"Retain schema constraints and separate conformance obligations without asserting validation, filesystem safety, authority or semantic acceptance.\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:record:f2abcd9b735cc126b1d826d543f6e063\",\"invalidation\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:invalidation:source-or-interpretation-change\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:0657852b6fd1fa48457c3f7d:residual